[{"id":"b256","title":"水壩地震動力分析","titleEn":"Seismic dynamic analysis of dams","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課把混凝土水壩的線性模態示意與土石壩孔壓機制分開，從質量、剛度、阻尼及地震輸入逐步走向水庫互制、接縫與數值收斂。十個單元均有原創計算與明確邊界，要求學徒追蹤同時刻、同座標和相同物理定義，不以單一週期或峰值吻合宣告整壩耐震合格。","summaryEn":"The course separates linear concrete-dam modal illustrations from embankment pore-pressure mechanisms. It moves through mass, stiffness, damping and forcing to reservoir interaction, joints and numerical convergence. Ten original calculations require consistent time, coordinates and physical definitions; matching one period or peak never establishes complete seismic adequacy.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-hydraulics","subcategoryTitle":"壩工監測、溢洪與壓力水路","subcategoryTitleEn":"Dam monitoring, spillways and pressure waterways","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-hydraulics","learningTags":["water","water-hydraulics","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-hydraulic","architectureNodes":[["模態質量與週期","Modal mass and period"],["阻尼係數與耗能","Damping coefficient and dissipation"],["反應譜位移換算","Spectral displacement conversion"],["同步位移與接縫","Synchronized displacement and joints"],["土壩孔壓與有效應力","Embankment pore pressure and effective stress"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-hydraulic","labels":["模態質量與週期","阻尼係數與耗能","反應譜位移換算","同步位移與接縫","土壩孔壓與有效應力"],"labelsEn":["Modal mass and period","Damping coefficient and dissipation","Spectral displacement conversion","Synchronized displacement and joints","Embankment pore pressure and effective stress"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創敏感度：選定模態質量50000000kg與線性剛度2000000000N/m，週期T=2π√(m/k)=0.9935s。只把剛度增加10%至2200000000N/m、質量不變，週期變成0.9472s，約減少4.65%，不是減少10%。這項計算僅隔離剛度影響，沒有證明實際壩體可用補強達到此值；基礎、水庫、接縫與阻尼也可能同時改變。學徒需先寫出廣義座標和校準方法，再比較週期、模態形狀與應力位置是否一起合理。即使週期縮短，地震需求可能因輸入譜形改變而升高或降低，不能直接推論風險同步下降。","textEn":"Original sensitivity: selected modal mass50000000kg and stiffness2000000000N/m give T=2π√(m/k)=0.9935s. Increase only stiffness by10% to2200000000N/m at unchanged mass; period becomes0.9472s, about4.65% shorter rather than10%. This isolates stiffness and does not establish that a real retrofit can achieve the assumed change. Foundation, reservoir, joints and damping may also vary. Define the generalized coordinate and calibration evidence before comparing period, mode shape and stress location together. Even a shorter period can increase or decrease seismic demand depending on the forcing spectrum; it cannot directly establish a corresponding reduction in risk.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b256-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「模態質量與週期」與「慣性力與加速度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Modal mass and period\" and \"Inertia and acceleration definition\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b256-v15-01","title":"模態質量與週期：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Modal mass and period: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「模態質量與週期」如何影響水壩地震動力分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Modal mass and period” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic dynamic analysis of dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水壩地震反應不是把整座重量直接乘一個係數，首先要理解材料剛度、基礎與水庫如何形成振動模態。單自由度模型只代表已選定的廣義座標，其質量和剛度必須成對校準；不同模態參與程度不同，第一週期吻合也不能證明全部壩體應力分布正確。 假設線性模態質量m=50000000kg、剛度k=2000000000N/m，ω=√(k/m)=6.325rad/s，T=2π/ω=0.9935s。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「模態質量與週期」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Dam response begins with how stiffness, foundation and reservoir interactions form vibration modes rather than multiplying total weight by one coefficient. A single degree of freedom represents a chosen generalized coordinate whose mass and stiffness must be calibrated together. Matching the first period does not establish the correctness of higher modes or the complete spatial stress distribution. Assume linear modal mass50000000kg and stiffness2000000000N/m. ω=√(k/m)=6.325rad/s and T=2π/ω=0.9935s, for this generalized coordinate only. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Modal mass and period” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「第一振動週期吻合即可證明整座水壩的地震應力全部正確。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Matching the first natural period proves that every earthquake stress in the dam is correct.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「模態質量與週期」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Modal mass and period”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-01-k1","title":"模態質量與週期","titleEn":"Modal mass and period","text":"水壩地震反應不是把整座重量直接乘一個係數，首先要理解材料剛度、基礎與水庫如何形成振動模態。單自由度模型只代表已選定的廣義座標，其質量和剛度必須成對校準；不同模態參與程度不同，第一週期吻合也不能證明全部壩體應力分布正確。","textEn":"Dam response begins with how stiffness, foundation and reservoir interactions form vibration modes rather than multiplying total weight by one coefficient. A single degree of freedom represents a chosen generalized coordinate whose mass and stiffness must be calibrated together.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：第一振動週期吻合即可證明整座水壩的地震應力全部正確。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Matching the first natural period proves that every earthquake stress in the dam is correct. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模態質量與週期」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Modal mass and period\" is correct?","options":["第一振動週期吻合即可證明整座水壩的地震應力全部正確。","水壩地震反應不是把整座重量直接乘一個係數，首先要理解材料剛度、基礎與水庫如何形成振動模態。","地表峰值加速度就是壩體每一點在同一時刻的絕對加速度。"],"optionsEn":["Matching the first natural period proves that every earthquake stress in the dam is correct.","Dam response begins with how stiffness, foundation and reservoir interactions form vibration modes rather than multiplying total weight by one coefficient.","Surface peak acceleration equals the simultaneous absolute acceleration at every point of the dam."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水壩地震反應不是把整座重量直接乘一個係數，首先要理解材料剛度、基礎與水庫如何形成振動模態。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Dam response begins with how stiffness, foundation and reservoir interactions form vibration modes rather than multiplying total weight by one coefficient. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b256-v15-02","title":"模態質量與週期：定量估算","titleEn":"Modal mass and period: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「模態質量與週期」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Modal mass and period” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設線性模態質量m=50000000kg、剛度k=2000000000N/m，ω=√(k/m)=6.325rad/s，T=2π/ω=0.9935s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume linear modal mass50000000kg and stiffness2000000000N/m. ω=√(k/m)=6.325rad/s and T=2π/ω=0.9935s, for this generalized coordinate only. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在自由體圖上說明廣義座標與質量正規化，核對剛度及質量是否使用同一模態定義。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Define the generalized coordinate and mass normalization and check consistent stiffness and mass conventions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設線性模態質量m=50000000kg、剛度k=2000000000N/m，ω=√(k/m)=6.325rad/s，T=2π/ω=0.9935s。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume linear modal mass50000000kg and stiffness2000000000N/m. ω=√(k/m)=6.325rad/s and T=2π/ω=0.9935s, for this generalized coordinate only.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「模態質量與週期」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Modal mass and period\", which statement holds?","options":["共振穩態放大係數可直接乘所有地震峰值作為真實反應。","瑞利阻尼只要在兩個頻率匹配就會在所有頻率保持同樣阻尼比。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["The steady resonant magnification can directly multiply every earthquake peak to give the actual response.","Rayleigh damping fitted at two frequencies has the same damping ratio at every frequency.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b256-v15-03","title":"模態質量與週期：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Modal mass and period: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「模態質量與週期」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Modal mass and period” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在自由體圖上說明廣義座標與質量正規化，核對剛度及質量是否使用同一模態定義。將解析週期與有限元素特徵值及環境振動資料比較，保留水位和溫度條件，不只調整一個參數湊合。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Define the generalized coordinate and mass normalization and check consistent stiffness and mass conventions. Compare the analytical period with eigenvalue and ambient-vibration evidence while retaining water-level and temperature conditions rather than tuning one parameter merely to force agreement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在自由體圖上說明廣義座標與質量正規化，核對剛度及質量是否使用同一模態定義。將解析週期與有限元素特徵值及環境振動資料比較，保留水位和溫度條件，不只調整一個參數湊合。","observationEn":"Site practice: Define the generalized coordinate and mass normalization and check consistent stiffness and mass conventions. Compare the analytical period with eigenvalue and ambient-vibration evidence while retaining water-level and temperature conditions rather than tuning one parameter merely to force agreement.","failure":"注意干擾：模態質量誤用總壩重會讓週期和慣性力同時錯位，固定基礎假設也可能高估剛度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using total dam mass as modal mass distorts both period and inertia, while an unrealistically fixed foundation may overstate stiffness. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在自由體圖上說明廣義座標與質量正規化，核對剛度及質量是否使用同一模態定義。將解析週期與有限元素特徵值及環境振動資料比較，保留水位和溫度條件，不只調整一個參數湊合。","textEn":"Define the generalized coordinate and mass normalization and check consistent stiffness and mass conventions. Compare the analytical period with eigenvalue and ambient-vibration evidence while retaining water-level and temperature conditions rather than tuning one parameter merely to force agreement.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在自由體圖上說明廣義座標與質量正規化，核對剛度及質量是否使用同一模態定義。將解析週期與有限元素特徵值及環境振動資料比較，保留水位和溫度條件，不只調整一個參數湊合。","textEn":"Define the generalized coordinate and mass normalization and check consistent stiffness and mass conventions. Compare the analytical period with eigenvalue and ambient-vibration evidence while retaining water-level and temperature conditions rather than tuning one parameter merely to force agreement.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「模態質量與週期」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Modal mass and period\"?","options":["在自由體圖上說明廣義座標與質量正規化，核對剛度及質量是否使用同一模態定義。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","接縫最大張開永遠等於兩側各自最大位移的平方和平方根。"],"optionsEn":["Define the generalized coordinate and mass normalization and check consistent stiffness and mass conventions.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Maximum joint opening always equals the root-sum-square of each side's individual peak displacement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在自由體圖上說明廣義座標與質量正規化，核對剛度及質量是否使用同一模態定義。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Define the generalized coordinate and mass normalization and check consistent stiffness and mass conventions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b256-v15-04","title":"模態質量與週期：失效診斷","titleEn":"Modal mass and period: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「模態質量與週期」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Modal mass and period” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"模態質量誤用總壩重會讓週期和慣性力同時錯位，固定基礎假設也可能高估剛度。第一週期接近量測時，局部接縫、壩肩或高階反應仍可能沒有被描述。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using total dam mass as modal mass distorts both period and inertia, while an unrealistically fixed foundation may overstate stiffness. A matching first period can still leave joints, abutments and higher-mode responses poorly represented. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設線性模態質量m=50000000kg、剛度k=2000000000N/m，ω=√(k/m)=6.325rad/s，T=2π/ω=0.9935s。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume linear modal mass50000000kg and stiffness2000000000N/m. ω=√(k/m)=6.325rad/s and T=2π/ω=0.9935s, for this generalized coordinate only.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「第一振動週期吻合即可證明整座水壩的地震應力全部正確。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Matching the first natural period proves that every earthquake stress in the dam is correct.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"模態質量誤用總壩重會讓週期和慣性力同時錯位，固定基礎假設也可能高估剛度。第一週期接近量測時，局部接縫、壩肩或高階反應仍可能沒有被描述。","textEn":"Using total dam mass as modal mass distorts both period and inertia, while an unrealistically fixed foundation may overstate stiffness. A matching first period can still leave joints, abutments and higher-mode responses poorly represented.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模態質量與週期」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Modal mass and period\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","模態質量誤用總壩重會讓週期和慣性力同時錯位，固定基礎假設也可能高估剛度。","地表峰值加速度就是壩體每一點在同一時刻的絕對加速度。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using total dam mass as modal mass distorts both period and inertia, while an unrealistically fixed foundation may overstate stiffness.","Surface peak acceleration equals the simultaneous absolute acceleration at every point of the dam."],"answer":1,"explanation":"模態質量誤用總壩重會讓週期和慣性力同時錯位，固定基礎假設也可能高估剛度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using total dam mass as modal mass distorts both period and inertia, while an unrealistically fixed foundation may overstate stiffness. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b256-v15-05","title":"慣性力與加速度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Inertia and acceleration definition: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「慣性力與加速度」如何影響水壩地震動力分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Inertia and acceleration definition” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic dynamic analysis of dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"慣性力跟質量及相應的絕對加速度有關，但地表峰值、基岩輸入與結構反應不是同一數據。等效靜力只提供量級，不能代替時變相位與變形計算；三方向輸入還要保持坐標一致，避免把不同時刻峰值任意拼成實際不存在的受力狀態。 假設所選質量50000000kg瞬時絕對加速度0.20g，F=ma=98.10MN；此數值不是由地表PGA自動得到的壩體反應。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「慣性力與加速度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Inertia depends on mass and its corresponding absolute acceleration, but surface peak, bedrock input and structural response are different quantities. Equivalent static force gives a scale rather than temporal phase or deformation. Three-component inputs also require consistent coordinates, and unrelated peaks must not be assembled into a force state that never occurred in the actual time history. Assume selected mass50000000kg has instantaneous absolute acceleration0.20g. F=ma=98.10MN, not a dam response automatically inferred from surface PGA. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Inertia and acceleration definition” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「地表峰值加速度就是壩體每一點在同一時刻的絕對加速度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Surface peak acceleration equals the simultaneous absolute acceleration at every point of the dam.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「慣性力與加速度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Inertia and acceleration definition”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-05-k1","title":"慣性力與加速度","titleEn":"Inertia and acceleration definition","text":"慣性力跟質量及相應的絕對加速度有關，但地表峰值、基岩輸入與結構反應不是同一數據。等效靜力只提供量級，不能代替時變相位與變形計算；三方向輸入還要保持坐標一致，避免把不同時刻峰值任意拼成實際不存在的受力狀態。","textEn":"Inertia depends on mass and its corresponding absolute acceleration, but surface peak, bedrock input and structural response are different quantities. Equivalent static force gives a scale rather than temporal phase or deformation.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：地表峰值加速度就是壩體每一點在同一時刻的絕對加速度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Surface peak acceleration equals the simultaneous absolute acceleration at every point of the dam. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「慣性力與加速度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Inertia and acceleration definition\" is correct?","options":["地表峰值加速度就是壩體每一點在同一時刻的絕對加速度。","阻尼設得越大就一定越接近真實水壩的地震反應。","慣性力跟質量及相應的絕對加速度有關，但地表峰值、基岩輸入與結構反應不是同一數據。"],"optionsEn":["Surface peak acceleration equals the simultaneous absolute acceleration at every point of the dam.","A larger damping value always makes the predicted dam earthquake response more realistic.","Inertia depends on mass and its corresponding absolute acceleration, but surface peak, bedrock input and structural response are different quantities."],"answer":2,"explanation":"慣性力跟質量及相應的絕對加速度有關，但地表峰值、基岩輸入與結構反應不是同一數據。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Inertia depends on mass and its corresponding absolute acceleration, but surface peak, bedrock input and structural response are different quantities. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b256-v15-06","title":"慣性力與加速度：定量估算","titleEn":"Inertia and acceleration definition: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「慣性力與加速度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Inertia and acceleration definition” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設所選質量50000000kg瞬時絕對加速度0.20g，F=ma=98.10MN；此數值不是由地表PGA自動得到的壩體反應。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume selected mass50000000kg has instantaneous absolute acceleration0.20g. F=ma=98.10MN, not a dam response automatically inferred from surface PGA. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分欄記錄輸入點、反應點、單位及坐標方向，確認g已乘9.81m/s²。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record input and response locations, units and axes separately, converting g to9.81m/s².","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設所選質量50000000kg瞬時絕對加速度0.20g，F=ma=98.10MN；此數值不是由地表PGA自動得到的壩體反應。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume selected mass50000000kg has instantaneous absolute acceleration0.20g. F=ma=98.10MN, not a dam response automatically inferred from surface PGA.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「慣性力與加速度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Inertia and acceleration definition\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","任何加速度峰值除以頻率平方都一定得到正確的反應譜位移。","水庫對水壩動力的作用就是把全部庫水重量加到壩體質量。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Any acceleration peak divided by frequency squared necessarily gives the correct spectral displacement.","Reservoir interaction simply adds the mass of all stored water to the dam."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b256-v15-07","title":"慣性力與加速度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Inertia and acceleration definition: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「慣性力與加速度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Inertia and acceleration definition” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分欄記錄輸入點、反應點、單位及坐標方向，確認g已乘9.81m/s²。以同時刻的加速度與支承反力檢查動力平衡，並區分絕對和相對加速度，不拿不相干峰值作平衡驗算。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record input and response locations, units and axes separately, converting g to9.81m/s². Check dynamic balance using simultaneous accelerations and support reactions and distinguish absolute from relative acceleration instead of combining unrelated individual peak values for equilibrium. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分欄記錄輸入點、反應點、單位及坐標方向，確認g已乘9.81m/s²。以同時刻的加速度與支承反力檢查動力平衡，並區分絕對和相對加速度，不拿不相干峰值作平衡驗算。","observationEn":"Site practice: Record input and response locations, units and axes separately, converting g to9.81m/s². Check dynamic balance using simultaneous accelerations and support reactions and distinguish absolute from relative acceleration instead of combining unrelated individual peak values for equilibrium.","failure":"注意干擾：把相對加速度當成絕對值可能漏掉地盤運動，三方向最大值不同時發生又會製造過大合力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating relative acceleration as absolute omits ground motion, while asynchronous directional peaks can create an excessive resultant. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分欄記錄輸入點、反應點、單位及坐標方向，確認g已乘9.81m/s²。以同時刻的加速度與支承反力檢查動力平衡，並區分絕對和相對加速度，不拿不相干峰值作平衡驗算。","textEn":"Record input and response locations, units and axes separately, converting g to9.81m/s². Check dynamic balance using simultaneous accelerations and support reactions and distinguish absolute from relative acceleration instead of combining unrelated individual peak values for equilibrium.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分欄記錄輸入點、反應點、單位及坐標方向，確認g已乘9.81m/s²。以同時刻的加速度與支承反力檢查動力平衡，並區分絕對和相對加速度，不拿不相干峰值作平衡驗算。","textEn":"Record input and response locations, units and axes separately, converting g to9.81m/s². Check dynamic balance using simultaneous accelerations and support reactions and distinguish absolute from relative acceleration instead of combining unrelated individual peak values for equilibrium.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「慣性力與加速度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Inertia and acceleration definition\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","分欄記錄輸入點、反應點、單位及坐標方向，確認g已乘9.81m/s²。","動力程式成功跑完且每週期有足夠點數就不必再查收斂。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Record input and response locations, units and axes separately, converting g to9.81m/s².","A completed dynamic run with many points per period never needs a convergence assessment."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分欄記錄輸入點、反應點、單位及坐標方向，確認g已乘9.81m/s²。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record input and response locations, units and axes separately, converting g to9.81m/s². Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b256-v15-08","title":"慣性力與加速度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Inertia and acceleration definition: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「慣性力與加速度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Inertia and acceleration definition” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把相對加速度當成絕對值可能漏掉地盤運動，三方向最大值不同時發生又會製造過大合力。反之僅用輸入PGA代表結構加速度，可能漏掉共振放大。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating relative acceleration as absolute omits ground motion, while asynchronous directional peaks can create an excessive resultant. Conversely, using input PGA for structural acceleration can miss amplification caused by resonant response of the selected mode. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設所選質量50000000kg瞬時絕對加速度0.20g，F=ma=98.10MN；此數值不是由地表PGA自動得到的壩體反應。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: F=ma=98.10MN, not a dam response automatically inferred from surface PGA.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「地表峰值加速度就是壩體每一點在同一時刻的絕對加速度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Surface peak acceleration equals the simultaneous absolute acceleration at every point of the dam.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把相對加速度當成絕對值可能漏掉地盤運動，三方向最大值不同時發生又會製造過大合力。反之僅用輸入PGA代表結構加速度，可能漏掉共振放大。","textEn":"Treating relative acceleration as absolute omits ground motion, while asynchronous directional peaks can create an excessive resultant. Conversely, using input PGA for structural acceleration can miss amplification caused by resonant response of the selected mode.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「慣性力與加速度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Inertia and acceleration definition\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","阻尼設得越大就一定越接近真實水壩的地震反應。","把相對加速度當成絕對值可能漏掉地盤運動，三方向最大值不同時發生又會製造過大合力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A larger damping value always makes the predicted dam earthquake response more realistic.","Treating relative acceleration as absolute omits ground motion, while asynchronous directional peaks can create an excessive resultant."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把相對加速度當成絕對值可能漏掉地盤運動，三方向最大值不同時發生又會製造過大合力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating relative acceleration as absolute omits ground motion, while asynchronous directional peaks can create an excessive resultant. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b256-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「阻尼係數與耗能」與「諧波放大與歷時」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Damping coefficient and dissipation\" and \"Harmonic magnification versus history\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b256-v15-09","title":"阻尼係數與耗能：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Damping coefficient and dissipation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「阻尼係數與耗能」如何影響水壩地震動力分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Damping coefficient and dissipation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic dynamic analysis of dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"阻尼比是相對臨界阻尼的比例，實體耗能可包含材料、接縫和基礎輻射，不應任意重複加入。線性黏滯模型便於分析但不能代表所有開裂摩擦機制，且校準模態與頻率範圍必須明示；增加阻尼使數值變小不等於取得可靠設計。 假設m=50000000kg、k=2000000000N/m、ζ=0.05，c=2ζ√(km)=31622776.6N·s/m；只代表線性黏滯阻尼。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「阻尼係數與耗能」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Damping ratio is relative to critical damping, while physical dissipation can include material, joints and radiation into the foundation. These effects must not be counted twice. Linear viscous damping is convenient but does not represent every cracking or friction mechanism, and calibration needs a specified modal and frequency range rather than an arbitrary value chosen to reduce response. Assume m=50000000kg,k=2000000000N/m and ζ=0.05. c=2ζ√(km)=31622776.6N·s/m, representing linear viscous damping only. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Damping coefficient and dissipation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「阻尼設得越大就一定越接近真實水壩的地震反應。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A larger damping value always makes the predicted dam earthquake response more realistic.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「阻尼係數與耗能」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Damping coefficient and dissipation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-09-k1","title":"阻尼係數與耗能","titleEn":"Damping coefficient and dissipation","text":"阻尼比是相對臨界阻尼的比例，實體耗能可包含材料、接縫和基礎輻射，不應任意重複加入。線性黏滯模型便於分析但不能代表所有開裂摩擦機制，且校準模態與頻率範圍必須明示；增加阻尼使數值變小不等於取得可靠設計。","textEn":"Damping ratio is relative to critical damping, while physical dissipation can include material, joints and radiation into the foundation. These effects must not be counted twice.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：阻尼設得越大就一定越接近真實水壩的地震反應。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A larger damping value always makes the predicted dam earthquake response more realistic. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「阻尼係數與耗能」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Damping coefficient and dissipation\" is correct?","options":["阻尼比是相對臨界阻尼的比例，實體耗能可包含材料、接縫和基礎輻射，不應任意重複加入。","阻尼設得越大就一定越接近真實水壩的地震反應。","共振穩態放大係數可直接乘所有地震峰值作為真實反應。"],"optionsEn":["Damping ratio is relative to critical damping, while physical dissipation can include material, joints and radiation into the foundation.","A larger damping value always makes the predicted dam earthquake response more realistic.","The steady resonant magnification can directly multiply every earthquake peak to give the actual response."],"answer":0,"explanation":"阻尼比是相對臨界阻尼的比例，實體耗能可包含材料、接縫和基礎輻射，不應任意重複加入。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Damping ratio is relative to critical damping, while physical dissipation can include material, joints and radiation into the foundation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b256-v15-10","title":"阻尼係數與耗能：定量估算","titleEn":"Damping coefficient and dissipation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「阻尼係數與耗能」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Damping coefficient and dissipation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設m=50000000kg、k=2000000000N/m、ζ=0.05，c=2ζ√(km)=31622776.6N·s/m；只代表線性黏滯阻尼。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume m=50000000kg,k=2000000000N/m and ζ=0.05. c=2ζ√(km)=31622776.6N·s/m, representing linear viscous damping only. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：列出材料阻尼、邊界吸收和接觸摩擦的實作位置，檢查同一耗能是否重複計算。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map material damping, absorbing boundaries and contact friction to check duplicate dissipation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設m=50000000kg、k=2000000000N/m、ζ=0.05，c=2ζ√(km)=31622776.6N·s/m；只代表線性黏滯阻尼。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume m=50000000kg,k=2000000000N/m and ζ=0.05. c=2ζ√(km)=31622776.6N·s/m, representing linear viscous damping only.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「阻尼係數與耗能」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Damping coefficient and dissipation\", which statement holds?","options":["瑞利阻尼只要在兩個頻率匹配就會在所有頻率保持同樣阻尼比。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","接縫最大張開永遠等於兩側各自最大位移的平方和平方根。"],"optionsEn":["Rayleigh damping fitted at two frequencies has the same damping ratio at every frequency.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Maximum joint opening always equals the root-sum-square of each side's individual peak displacement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b256-v15-11","title":"阻尼係數與耗能：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Damping coefficient and dissipation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「阻尼係數與耗能」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Damping coefficient and dissipation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"列出材料阻尼、邊界吸收和接觸摩擦的實作位置，檢查同一耗能是否重複計算。以自由衰減或頻率反應資料校核，另做阻尼敏感度，保存反應改變原因而非只報最小應力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map material damping, absorbing boundaries and contact friction to check duplicate dissipation. Compare free-decay or frequency-response evidence and perform damping sensitivity, explaining changed response rather than reporting only the smallest calculated stress from a favorable parameter choice. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：列出材料阻尼、邊界吸收和接觸摩擦的實作位置，檢查同一耗能是否重複計算。以自由衰減或頻率反應資料校核，另做阻尼敏感度，保存反應改變原因而非只報最小應力。","observationEn":"Site practice: Map material damping, absorbing boundaries and contact friction to check duplicate dissipation. Compare free-decay or frequency-response evidence and perform damping sensitivity, explaining changed response rather than reporting only the smallest calculated stress from a favorable parameter choice.","failure":"注意干擾：同時採很大材料阻尼和強吸收邊界可能過度消能，掩蓋壩肩需求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Large material damping combined with strongly absorbing boundaries can remove excessive energy and hide abutment demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"列出材料阻尼、邊界吸收和接觸摩擦的實作位置，檢查同一耗能是否重複計算。以自由衰減或頻率反應資料校核，另做阻尼敏感度，保存反應改變原因而非只報最小應力。","textEn":"Map material damping, absorbing boundaries and contact friction to check duplicate dissipation. Compare free-decay or frequency-response evidence and perform damping sensitivity, explaining changed response rather than reporting only the smallest calculated stress from a favorable parameter choice.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"列出材料阻尼、邊界吸收和接觸摩擦的實作位置，檢查同一耗能是否重複計算。以自由衰減或頻率反應資料校核，另做阻尼敏感度，保存反應改變原因而非只報最小應力。","textEn":"Map material damping, absorbing boundaries and contact friction to check duplicate dissipation. Compare free-decay or frequency-response evidence and perform damping sensitivity, explaining changed response rather than reporting only the smallest calculated stress from a favorable parameter choice.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「阻尼係數與耗能」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Damping coefficient and dissipation\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","土石壩的孔壓變化可直接用混凝土線彈性振子的阻尼比完全代表。","列出材料阻尼、邊界吸收和接觸摩擦的實作位置，檢查同一耗能是否重複計算。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Embankment pore-pressure change is fully represented by the damping ratio of a linear concrete oscillator.","Map material damping, absorbing boundaries and contact friction to check duplicate dissipation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"列出材料阻尼、邊界吸收和接觸摩擦的實作位置，檢查同一耗能是否重複計算。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map material damping, absorbing boundaries and contact friction to check duplicate dissipation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b256-v15-12","title":"阻尼係數與耗能：失效診斷","titleEn":"Damping coefficient and dissipation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「阻尼係數與耗能」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Damping coefficient and dissipation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"同時採很大材料阻尼和強吸收邊界可能過度消能，掩蓋壩肩需求。把小振幅試驗阻尼直接外推到嚴重開裂狀態，也會忽略隨振幅改變的機制。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Large material damping combined with strongly absorbing boundaries can remove excessive energy and hide abutment demand. Extending small-amplitude damping into severe cracking also overlooks mechanisms that change as deformation amplitude grows during shaking. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設m=50000000kg、k=2000000000N/m、ζ=0.05，c=2ζ√(km)=31622776.6N·s/m；只代表線性黏滯阻尼。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume m=50000000kg,k=2000000000N/m and ζ=0.05. c=2ζ√(km)=31622776.6N·s/m, representing linear viscous damping only.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「阻尼設得越大就一定越接近真實水壩的地震反應。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A larger damping value always makes the predicted dam earthquake response more realistic.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"同時採很大材料阻尼和強吸收邊界可能過度消能，掩蓋壩肩需求。把小振幅試驗阻尼直接外推到嚴重開裂狀態，也會忽略隨振幅改變的機制。","textEn":"Large material damping combined with strongly absorbing boundaries can remove excessive energy and hide abutment demand. Extending small-amplitude damping into severe cracking also overlooks mechanisms that change as deformation amplitude grows during shaking.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「阻尼係數與耗能」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Damping coefficient and dissipation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["同時採很大材料阻尼和強吸收邊界可能過度消能，掩蓋壩肩需求。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","共振穩態放大係數可直接乘所有地震峰值作為真實反應。"],"optionsEn":["Large material damping combined with strongly absorbing boundaries can remove excessive energy and hide abutment demand.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The steady resonant magnification can directly multiply every earthquake peak to give the actual response."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同時採很大材料阻尼和強吸收邊界可能過度消能，掩蓋壩肩需求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Large material damping combined with strongly absorbing boundaries can remove excessive energy and hide abutment demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b256-v15-13","title":"諧波放大與歷時：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Harmonic magnification versus history: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「諧波放大與歷時」如何影響水壩地震動力分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Harmonic magnification versus history” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic dynamic analysis of dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"共振概念可用持續正弦力說明，但地震是有限時間且頻率不斷改變的訊號，兩者反應不能混用。線性振子的穩態放大取決於頻率比及阻尼，建立穩態需要時間；脈衝、非線性接縫和頻率漂移可能使真正峰值與簡式大不相同。 假設線性受迫穩態、頻率比r=1、ζ=0.05，R=1/√[(1−r²)²+(2ζr)²]=10；非地震歷時放大保證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「諧波放大與歷時」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Sustained sinusoidal force illustrates resonance, but earthquakes have finite duration and changing frequency content. Their responses are not interchangeable. Steady harmonic amplification depends on frequency ratio and damping and takes time to develop. Pulses, nonlinear joints and frequency shifts can make actual peaks substantially different from the simplified forced-oscillator value even when its natural period is known. Assume linear steady forced response with frequency ratio r=1 and ζ=0.05. R=1/√[(1−r²)²+(2ζr)²]=10, not an earthquake amplification guarantee. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Harmonic magnification versus history” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「共振穩態放大係數可直接乘所有地震峰值作為真實反應。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The steady resonant magnification can directly multiply every earthquake peak to give the actual response.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「諧波放大與歷時」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Harmonic magnification versus history”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-13-k1","title":"諧波放大與歷時","titleEn":"Harmonic magnification versus history","text":"共振概念可用持續正弦力說明，但地震是有限時間且頻率不斷改變的訊號，兩者反應不能混用。線性振子的穩態放大取決於頻率比及阻尼，建立穩態需要時間；脈衝、非線性接縫和頻率漂移可能使真正峰值與簡式大不相同。","textEn":"Sustained sinusoidal force illustrates resonance, but earthquakes have finite duration and changing frequency content. Their responses are not interchangeable.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：共振穩態放大係數可直接乘所有地震峰值作為真實反應。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The steady resonant magnification can directly multiply every earthquake peak to give the actual response. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「諧波放大與歷時」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Harmonic magnification versus history\" is correct?","options":["共振穩態放大係數可直接乘所有地震峰值作為真實反應。","共振概念可用持續正弦力說明，但地震是有限時間且頻率不斷改變的訊號，兩者反應不能混用。","任何加速度峰值除以頻率平方都一定得到正確的反應譜位移。"],"optionsEn":["The steady resonant magnification can directly multiply every earthquake peak to give the actual response.","Sustained sinusoidal force illustrates resonance, but earthquakes have finite duration and changing frequency content.","Any acceleration peak divided by frequency squared necessarily gives the correct spectral displacement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"共振概念可用持續正弦力說明，但地震是有限時間且頻率不斷改變的訊號，兩者反應不能混用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Sustained sinusoidal force illustrates resonance, but earthquakes have finite duration and changing frequency content. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b256-v15-14","title":"諧波放大與歷時：定量估算","titleEn":"Harmonic magnification versus history: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「諧波放大與歷時」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Harmonic magnification versus history” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設線性受迫穩態、頻率比r=1、ζ=0.05，R=1/√[(1−r²)²+(2ζr)²]=10；非地震歷時放大保證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume linear steady forced response with frequency ratio r=1 and ζ=0.05. R=1/√[(1−r²)²+(2ζr)²]=10, not an earthquake amplification guarantee. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：畫出多個頻率比的反應曲線，標明以靜態位移為分母的定義。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot response over several frequency ratios and state that magnification is relative to static displacement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設線性受迫穩態、頻率比r=1、ζ=0.05，R=1/√[(1−r²)²+(2ζr)²]=10；非地震歷時放大保證。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume linear steady forced response with frequency ratio r=1 and ζ=0.05. R=1/√[(1−r²)²+(2ζr)²]=10, not an earthquake amplification guarantee.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「諧波放大與歷時」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Harmonic magnification versus history\", which statement holds?","options":["水庫對水壩動力的作用就是把全部庫水重量加到壩體質量。","動力程式成功跑完且每週期有足夠點數就不必再查收斂。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Reservoir interaction simply adds the mass of all stored water to the dam.","A completed dynamic run with many points per period never needs a convergence assessment.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b256-v15-15","title":"諧波放大與歷時：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Harmonic magnification versus history: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「諧波放大與歷時」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Harmonic magnification versus history” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"畫出多個頻率比的反應曲線，標明以靜態位移為分母的定義。再輸入短脈衝與有限週期正弦比較建立時間，檢查模型仍線性時兩種結果為何不同，不把穩態峰值直接當地震需求。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot response over several frequency ratios and state that magnification is relative to static displacement. Compare a short pulse and finite-cycle sinusoid to show buildup time, explaining their differences within the linear model rather than directly using the steady peak as earthquake demand. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出多個頻率比的反應曲線，標明以靜態位移為分母的定義。再輸入短脈衝與有限週期正弦比較建立時間，檢查模型仍線性時兩種結果為何不同，不把穩態峰值直接當地震需求。","observationEn":"Site practice: Plot response over several frequency ratios and state that magnification is relative to static displacement. Compare a short pulse and finite-cycle sinusoid to show buildup time, explaining their differences within the linear model rather than directly using the steady peak as earthquake demand.","failure":"注意干擾：地震短脈衝未必有時間建立穩態，直接套十倍可能高估；若忽略結構頻率變化或其他模態，也可能漏掉另一時間段的放大。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A short pulse may not build steady resonance, making direct tenfold scaling excessive. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"畫出多個頻率比的反應曲線，標明以靜態位移為分母的定義。再輸入短脈衝與有限週期正弦比較建立時間，檢查模型仍線性時兩種結果為何不同，不把穩態峰值直接當地震需求。","textEn":"Plot response over several frequency ratios and state that magnification is relative to static displacement. Compare a short pulse and finite-cycle sinusoid to show buildup time, explaining their differences within the linear model rather than directly using the steady peak as earthquake demand.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出多個頻率比的反應曲線，標明以靜態位移為分母的定義。再輸入短脈衝與有限週期正弦比較建立時間，檢查模型仍線性時兩種結果為何不同，不把穩態峰值直接當地震需求。","textEn":"Plot response over several frequency ratios and state that magnification is relative to static displacement. Compare a short pulse and finite-cycle sinusoid to show buildup time, explaining their differences within the linear model rather than directly using the steady peak as earthquake demand.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「諧波放大與歷時」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Harmonic magnification versus history\"?","options":["畫出多個頻率比的反應曲線，標明以靜態位移為分母的定義。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","第一振動週期吻合即可證明整座水壩的地震應力全部正確。"],"optionsEn":["Plot response over several frequency ratios and state that magnification is relative to static displacement.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Matching the first natural period proves that every earthquake stress in the dam is correct."],"answer":0,"explanation":"畫出多個頻率比的反應曲線，標明以靜態位移為分母的定義。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot response over several frequency ratios and state that magnification is relative to static displacement. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b256-v15-16","title":"諧波放大與歷時：失效診斷","titleEn":"Harmonic magnification versus history: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「諧波放大與歷時」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Harmonic magnification versus history” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"地震短脈衝未必有時間建立穩態，直接套十倍可能高估；若忽略結構頻率變化或其他模態，也可能漏掉另一時間段的放大。單一數值無法替代完整歷時檢查。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A short pulse may not build steady resonance, making direct tenfold scaling excessive. Ignoring frequency change or additional modes can instead miss amplification later in the record, so one factor cannot replace evaluation of the full time history. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設線性受迫穩態、頻率比r=1、ζ=0.05，R=1/√[(1−r²)²+(2ζr)²]=10；非地震歷時放大保證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: R=1/√[(1−r²)²+(2ζr)²]=10, not an earthquake amplification guarantee.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「共振穩態放大係數可直接乘所有地震峰值作為真實反應。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The steady resonant magnification can directly multiply every earthquake peak to give the actual response.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"地震短脈衝未必有時間建立穩態，直接套十倍可能高估；若忽略結構頻率變化或其他模態，也可能漏掉另一時間段的放大。單一數值無法替代完整歷時檢查。","textEn":"A short pulse may not build steady resonance, making direct tenfold scaling excessive. Ignoring frequency change or additional modes can instead miss amplification later in the record, so one factor cannot replace evaluation of the full time history.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「諧波放大與歷時」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Harmonic magnification versus history\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","地震短脈衝未必有時間建立穩態，直接套十倍可能高估；若忽略結構頻率變化或其他模態，也可能漏掉另一時間段的放大。","任何加速度峰值除以頻率平方都一定得到正確的反應譜位移。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A short pulse may not build steady resonance, making direct tenfold scaling excessive.","Any acceleration peak divided by frequency squared necessarily gives the correct spectral displacement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"地震短脈衝未必有時間建立穩態，直接套十倍可能高估；若忽略結構頻率變化或其他模態，也可能漏掉另一時間段的放大。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A short pulse may not build steady resonance, making direct tenfold scaling excessive. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b256-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「反應譜位移換算」與「瑞利阻尼頻帶」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Spectral displacement conversion\" and \"Rayleigh damping frequency band\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b256-v15-17","title":"反應譜位移換算：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Spectral displacement conversion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「反應譜位移換算」如何影響水壩地震動力分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Spectral displacement conversion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic dynamic analysis of dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"擬加速度反應譜與位移譜在同一線性振子和阻尼下可由角頻率換算，但擬加速度不是任意量測絕對加速度峰值。譜值忽略不同模態峰值發生時間，合成規則需另外選擇；先確認譜的定義與單位，才有資格比較位移和接縫需求。 假設同一線性振子週期T=1s、擬譜加速度Sa=0.40g，Sd=Sa/(2π/T)²=0.09940m；阻尼定義保持一致。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「反應譜位移換算」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pseudo-spectral acceleration and spectral displacement convert through angular frequency for the same linear oscillator and damping. Pseudo-acceleration is not an arbitrary measured absolute-acceleration peak. Spectra also omit the timing of different modal maxima, requiring separate combination rules. Definitions and units must therefore be checked before comparing converted displacement with joint or deformation demands. Assume the same linear oscillator has T=1s and pseudo-spectral acceleration Sa=0.40g. Sd=Sa/(2π/T)²=0.09940m at consistently defined damping. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Spectral displacement conversion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「任何加速度峰值除以頻率平方都一定得到正確的反應譜位移。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any acceleration peak divided by frequency squared necessarily gives the correct spectral displacement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「反應譜位移換算」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Spectral displacement conversion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-17-k1","title":"反應譜位移換算","titleEn":"Spectral displacement conversion","text":"擬加速度反應譜與位移譜在同一線性振子和阻尼下可由角頻率換算，但擬加速度不是任意量測絕對加速度峰值。譜值忽略不同模態峰值發生時間，合成規則需另外選擇；先確認譜的定義與單位，才有資格比較位移和接縫需求。","textEn":"Pseudo-spectral acceleration and spectral displacement convert through angular frequency for the same linear oscillator and damping. Pseudo-acceleration is not an arbitrary measured absolute-acceleration peak.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任何加速度峰值除以頻率平方都一定得到正確的反應譜位移。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any acceleration peak divided by frequency squared necessarily gives the correct spectral displacement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「反應譜位移換算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Spectral displacement conversion\" is correct?","options":["任何加速度峰值除以頻率平方都一定得到正確的反應譜位移。","瑞利阻尼只要在兩個頻率匹配就會在所有頻率保持同樣阻尼比。","擬加速度反應譜與位移譜在同一線性振子和阻尼下可由角頻率換算，但擬加速度不是任意量測絕對加速度峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Any acceleration peak divided by frequency squared necessarily gives the correct spectral displacement.","Rayleigh damping fitted at two frequencies has the same damping ratio at every frequency.","Pseudo-spectral acceleration and spectral displacement convert through angular frequency for the same linear oscillator and damping."],"answer":2,"explanation":"擬加速度反應譜與位移譜在同一線性振子和阻尼下可由角頻率換算，但擬加速度不是任意量測絕對加速度峰值。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pseudo-spectral acceleration and spectral displacement convert through angular frequency for the same linear oscillator and damping. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b256-v15-18","title":"反應譜位移換算：定量估算","titleEn":"Spectral displacement conversion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「反應譜位移換算」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Spectral displacement conversion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設同一線性振子週期T=1s、擬譜加速度Sa=0.40g，Sd=Sa/(2π/T)²=0.09940m；阻尼定義保持一致。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume the same linear oscillator has T=1s and pseudo-spectral acceleration Sa=0.40g. Sd=Sa/(2π/T)²=0.09940m at consistently defined damping. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對輸入是擬譜加速度或絕對加速度譜，將g與角頻率的轉換逐步寫出。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Identify pseudo-spectral versus absolute-acceleration input and show conversion from g and period to angular frequency.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設同一線性振子週期T=1s、擬譜加速度Sa=0.40g，Sd=Sa/(2π/T)²=0.09940m；阻尼定義保持一致。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume the same linear oscillator has T=1s and pseudo-spectral acceleration Sa=0.40g. Sd=Sa/(2π/T)²=0.09940m at consistently defined damping.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「反應譜位移換算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Spectral displacement conversion\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","接縫最大張開永遠等於兩側各自最大位移的平方和平方根。","土石壩的孔壓變化可直接用混凝土線彈性振子的阻尼比完全代表。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Maximum joint opening always equals the root-sum-square of each side's individual peak displacement.","Embankment pore-pressure change is fully represented by the damping ratio of a linear concrete oscillator."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b256-v15-19","title":"反應譜位移換算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Spectral displacement conversion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「反應譜位移換算」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Spectral displacement conversion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對輸入是擬譜加速度或絕對加速度譜，將g與角頻率的轉換逐步寫出。用同一歷時振子直接求位移峰值對照，確認週期及阻尼一致，並保留多模態合成方法的另行說明。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Identify pseudo-spectral versus absolute-acceleration input and show conversion from g and period to angular frequency. Compare with direct oscillator displacement from the same record at matching period and damping, documenting the separate method used for multiple-mode combination. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：核對輸入是擬譜加速度或絕對加速度譜，將g與角頻率的轉換逐步寫出。用同一歷時振子直接求位移峰值對照，確認週期及阻尼一致，並保留多模態合成方法的另行說明。","observationEn":"Site practice: Identify pseudo-spectral versus absolute-acceleration input and show conversion from g and period to angular frequency. Compare with direct oscillator displacement from the same record at matching period and damping, documenting the separate method used for multiple-mode combination.","failure":"注意干擾：將Hz直接當rad/s會使位移差數十倍，不同阻尼譜混用又會改變需求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using hertz as radians per second changes displacement by a large factor, and mixing damping definitions changes demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對輸入是擬譜加速度或絕對加速度譜，將g與角頻率的轉換逐步寫出。用同一歷時振子直接求位移峰值對照，確認週期及阻尼一致，並保留多模態合成方法的另行說明。","textEn":"Identify pseudo-spectral versus absolute-acceleration input and show conversion from g and period to angular frequency. Compare with direct oscillator displacement from the same record at matching period and damping, documenting the separate method used for multiple-mode combination.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"核對輸入是擬譜加速度或絕對加速度譜，將g與角頻率的轉換逐步寫出。用同一歷時振子直接求位移峰值對照，確認週期及阻尼一致，並保留多模態合成方法的另行說明。","textEn":"Identify pseudo-spectral versus absolute-acceleration input and show conversion from g and period to angular frequency. Compare with direct oscillator displacement from the same record at matching period and damping, documenting the separate method used for multiple-mode combination.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「反應譜位移換算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Spectral displacement conversion\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","核對輸入是擬譜加速度或絕對加速度譜，將g與角頻率的轉換逐步寫出。","地表峰值加速度就是壩體每一點在同一時刻的絕對加速度。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Identify pseudo-spectral versus absolute-acceleration input and show conversion from g and period to angular frequency.","Surface peak acceleration equals the simultaneous absolute acceleration at every point of the dam."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對輸入是擬譜加速度或絕對加速度譜，將g與角頻率的轉換逐步寫出。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Identify pseudo-spectral versus absolute-acceleration input and show conversion from g and period to angular frequency. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b256-v15-20","title":"反應譜位移換算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Spectral displacement conversion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「反應譜位移換算」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Spectral displacement conversion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將Hz直接當rad/s會使位移差數十倍，不同阻尼譜混用又會改變需求。即使單模態位移正確，各模態峰值同號相加仍可能不代表任何真實時刻。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using hertz as radians per second changes displacement by a large factor, and mixing damping definitions changes demand. Even correct individual modal displacements need not occur with equal signs at one actual instant. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設同一線性振子週期T=1s、擬譜加速度Sa=0.40g，Sd=Sa/(2π/T)²=0.09940m；阻尼定義保持一致。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Sd=Sa/(2π/T)²=0.09940m at consistently defined damping.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任何加速度峰值除以頻率平方都一定得到正確的反應譜位移。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any acceleration peak divided by frequency squared necessarily gives the correct spectral displacement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將Hz直接當rad/s會使位移差數十倍，不同阻尼譜混用又會改變需求。即使單模態位移正確，各模態峰值同號相加仍可能不代表任何真實時刻。","textEn":"Using hertz as radians per second changes displacement by a large factor, and mixing damping definitions changes demand. Even correct individual modal displacements need not occur with equal signs at one actual instant.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「反應譜位移換算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Spectral displacement conversion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","瑞利阻尼只要在兩個頻率匹配就會在所有頻率保持同樣阻尼比。","將Hz直接當rad/s會使位移差數十倍，不同阻尼譜混用又會改變需求。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Rayleigh damping fitted at two frequencies has the same damping ratio at every frequency.","Using hertz as radians per second changes displacement by a large factor, and mixing damping definitions changes demand."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將Hz直接當rad/s會使位移差數十倍，不同阻尼譜混用又會改變需求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using hertz as radians per second changes displacement by a large factor, and mixing damping definitions changes demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b256-v15-21","title":"瑞利阻尼頻帶：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rayleigh damping frequency band: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「瑞利阻尼頻帶」如何影響水壩地震動力分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rayleigh damping frequency band” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic dynamic analysis of dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"質量與剛度比例阻尼可在兩個指定模態匹配目標，但頻帶之外不會維持同一比例。低頻受質量項控制、高頻受剛度項控制，網格細化加入高頻模態可能造成過度衰減；應檢查整段頻率曲線，不能只驗算兩個校準點就認為全部動力都一致。 假設兩模態1與3Hz均ζ=0.05，C=αM+βK得α=0.47124s⁻¹、β=0.0039789s；在2Hz時ζ=0.04375。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「瑞利阻尼頻帶」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mass- and stiffness-proportional damping can match a target at two selected modes but does not maintain that ratio outside them. The mass term dominates low frequency and stiffness term high frequency, so refinement can add excessively damped modes. Examine the full curve instead of assuming that agreement at two calibration points establishes consistent damping throughout the dynamic model. Assume target damping0.05 at1 and3Hz. C=αM+βK gives α=0.47124s⁻¹,β=0.0039789s; at2Hz the damping ratio is0.04375. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rayleigh damping frequency band” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「瑞利阻尼只要在兩個頻率匹配就會在所有頻率保持同樣阻尼比。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Rayleigh damping fitted at two frequencies has the same damping ratio at every frequency.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「瑞利阻尼頻帶」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rayleigh damping frequency band”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-21-k1","title":"瑞利阻尼頻帶","titleEn":"Rayleigh damping frequency band","text":"質量與剛度比例阻尼可在兩個指定模態匹配目標，但頻帶之外不會維持同一比例。低頻受質量項控制、高頻受剛度項控制，網格細化加入高頻模態可能造成過度衰減；應檢查整段頻率曲線，不能只驗算兩個校準點就認為全部動力都一致。","textEn":"Mass- and stiffness-proportional damping can match a target at two selected modes but does not maintain that ratio outside them. The mass term dominates low frequency and stiffness term high frequency, so refinement can add excessively damped modes.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：瑞利阻尼只要在兩個頻率匹配就會在所有頻率保持同樣阻尼比。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Rayleigh damping fitted at two frequencies has the same damping ratio at every frequency. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「瑞利阻尼頻帶」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rayleigh damping frequency band\" is correct?","options":["質量與剛度比例阻尼可在兩個指定模態匹配目標，但頻帶之外不會維持同一比例。","瑞利阻尼只要在兩個頻率匹配就會在所有頻率保持同樣阻尼比。","水庫對水壩動力的作用就是把全部庫水重量加到壩體質量。"],"optionsEn":["Mass- and stiffness-proportional damping can match a target at two selected modes but does not maintain that ratio outside them.","Rayleigh damping fitted at two frequencies has the same damping ratio at every frequency.","Reservoir interaction simply adds the mass of all stored water to the dam."],"answer":0,"explanation":"質量與剛度比例阻尼可在兩個指定模態匹配目標，但頻帶之外不會維持同一比例。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mass- and stiffness-proportional damping can match a target at two selected modes but does not maintain that ratio outside them. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b256-v15-22","title":"瑞利阻尼頻帶：定量估算","titleEn":"Rayleigh damping frequency band: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「瑞利阻尼頻帶」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rayleigh damping frequency band” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設兩模態1與3Hz均ζ=0.05，C=αM+βK得α=0.47124s⁻¹、β=0.0039789s；在2Hz時ζ=0.04375。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume target damping0.05 at1 and3Hz. C=αM+βK gives α=0.47124s⁻¹,β=0.0039789s; at2Hz the damping ratio is0.04375. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在模型使用的最低到最高頻率畫阻尼曲線，標出兩個校準模態及中間值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot damping over the model’s relevant frequency range, marking calibration modes and intermediate values.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設兩模態1與3Hz均ζ=0.05，C=αM+βK得α=0.47124s⁻¹、β=0.0039789s；在2Hz時ζ=0.04375。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume target damping0.05 at1 and3Hz. C=αM+βK gives α=0.47124s⁻¹,β=0.0039789s; at2Hz the damping ratio is0.04375.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「瑞利阻尼頻帶」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rayleigh damping frequency band\", which statement holds?","options":["動力程式成功跑完且每週期有足夠點數就不必再查收斂。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","第一振動週期吻合即可證明整座水壩的地震應力全部正確。"],"optionsEn":["A completed dynamic run with many points per period never needs a convergence assessment.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Matching the first natural period proves that every earthquake stress in the dam is correct."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b256-v15-23","title":"瑞利阻尼頻帶：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rayleigh damping frequency band: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「瑞利阻尼頻帶」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rayleigh damping frequency band” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在模型使用的最低到最高頻率畫阻尼曲線，標出兩個校準模態及中間值。網格改變後重新檢查新增高頻耗能，並確認剛度項採初始或更新剛度，避免非線性時含義悄悄改變。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot damping over the model’s relevant frequency range, marking calibration modes and intermediate values. Recheck high-frequency dissipation after mesh changes and identify whether the stiffness term uses initial or updated stiffness, preventing an unnoticed change of meaning in nonlinear calculations. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在模型使用的最低到最高頻率畫阻尼曲線，標出兩個校準模態及中間值。網格改變後重新檢查新增高頻耗能，並確認剛度項採初始或更新剛度，避免非線性時含義悄悄改變。","observationEn":"Site practice: Plot damping over the model’s relevant frequency range, marking calibration modes and intermediate values. Recheck high-frequency dissipation after mesh changes and identify whether the stiffness term uses initial or updated stiffness, preventing an unnoticed change of meaning in nonlinear calculations.","failure":"注意干擾：高頻過度阻尼可能抹掉局部衝擊或接觸反應，低頻質量阻尼也可能對近剛體運動產生不合理耗能。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Excessive high-frequency damping erases local impact or contact response, while low-frequency mass damping may dissipate near-rigid movement unrealistically. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在模型使用的最低到最高頻率畫阻尼曲線，標出兩個校準模態及中間值。網格改變後重新檢查新增高頻耗能，並確認剛度項採初始或更新剛度，避免非線性時含義悄悄改變。","textEn":"Plot damping over the model’s relevant frequency range, marking calibration modes and intermediate values. Recheck high-frequency dissipation after mesh changes and identify whether the stiffness term uses initial or updated stiffness, preventing an unnoticed change of meaning in nonlinear calculations.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在模型使用的最低到最高頻率畫阻尼曲線，標出兩個校準模態及中間值。網格改變後重新檢查新增高頻耗能，並確認剛度項採初始或更新剛度，避免非線性時含義悄悄改變。","textEn":"Plot damping over the model’s relevant frequency range, marking calibration modes and intermediate values. Recheck high-frequency dissipation after mesh changes and identify whether the stiffness term uses initial or updated stiffness, preventing an unnoticed change of meaning in nonlinear calculations.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「瑞利阻尼頻帶」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rayleigh damping frequency band\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","阻尼設得越大就一定越接近真實水壩的地震反應。","在模型使用的最低到最高頻率畫阻尼曲線，標出兩個校準模態及中間值。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A larger damping value always makes the predicted dam earthquake response more realistic.","Plot damping over the model’s relevant frequency range, marking calibration modes and intermediate values."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在模型使用的最低到最高頻率畫阻尼曲線，標出兩個校準模態及中間值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot damping over the model’s relevant frequency range, marking calibration modes and intermediate values. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b256-v15-24","title":"瑞利阻尼頻帶：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rayleigh damping frequency band: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「瑞利阻尼頻帶」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rayleigh damping frequency band” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"高頻過度阻尼可能抹掉局部衝擊或接觸反應，低頻質量阻尼也可能對近剛體運動產生不合理耗能。只報兩點匹配，無法看出頻帶外的數值偏差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Excessive high-frequency damping erases local impact or contact response, while low-frequency mass damping may dissipate near-rigid movement unrealistically. Reporting only two fitted points hides numerical behavior outside the calibration band of the model. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設兩模態1與3Hz均ζ=0.05，C=αM+βK得α=0.47124s⁻¹、β=0.0039789s；在2Hz時ζ=0.04375。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: C=αM+βK gives α=0.47124s⁻¹,β=0.0039789s; at2Hz the damping ratio is0.04375.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「瑞利阻尼只要在兩個頻率匹配就會在所有頻率保持同樣阻尼比。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Rayleigh damping fitted at two frequencies has the same damping ratio at every frequency.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高頻過度阻尼可能抹掉局部衝擊或接觸反應，低頻質量阻尼也可能對近剛體運動產生不合理耗能。只報兩點匹配，無法看出頻帶外的數值偏差。","textEn":"Excessive high-frequency damping erases local impact or contact response, while low-frequency mass damping may dissipate near-rigid movement unrealistically. Reporting only two fitted points hides numerical behavior outside the calibration band of the model.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「瑞利阻尼頻帶」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rayleigh damping frequency band\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["高頻過度阻尼可能抹掉局部衝擊或接觸反應，低頻質量阻尼也可能對近剛體運動產生不合理耗能。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","水庫對水壩動力的作用就是把全部庫水重量加到壩體質量。"],"optionsEn":["Excessive high-frequency damping erases local impact or contact response, while low-frequency mass damping may dissipate near-rigid movement unrealistically.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Reservoir interaction simply adds the mass of all stored water to the dam."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高頻過度阻尼可能抹掉局部衝擊或接觸反應，低頻質量阻尼也可能對近剛體運動產生不合理耗能。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Excessive high-frequency damping erases local impact or contact response, while low-frequency mass damping may dissipate near-rigid movement unrealistically. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b256-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「附加水質量與週期」與「同步位移與接縫」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Added water mass and period\" and \"Synchronized displacement and joints\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b256-v15-25","title":"附加水質量與週期：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Added water mass and period: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「附加水質量與週期」如何影響水壩地震動力分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Added water mass and period” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic dynamic analysis of dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水庫動壓可能與壩體運動耦合，簡化附加質量僅在已指定形狀與頻率條件下代表某種等效作用。不能把整個水庫重量直接加到壩上，亦不能忽略可壓縮性、邊界吸收或水位改變；本單元固定剛度，只檢查一個假設附加量如何改變週期。 假設原模態m=50000000kg、附加水質量20000000kg、k=2000000000N/m，T=2π√[(m+ma)/k]=1.1755s。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「附加水質量與週期」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Reservoir pressure can couple with dam movement, while an added-mass approximation represents an equivalent effect only under stated geometry and frequency conditions. The entire reservoir mass cannot be attached to the dam, nor can compressibility, absorption and water-level change always be ignored. This unit holds stiffness fixed to isolate the period effect of one assumed modal addition. Assume modal mass50000000kg,added water mass20000000kg and unchanged stiffness2000000000N/m. T=2π√[(m+ma)/k]=1.1755s for this assumed approximation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Added water mass and period” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「水庫對水壩動力的作用就是把全部庫水重量加到壩體質量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reservoir interaction simply adds the mass of all stored water to the dam.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「附加水質量與週期」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Added water mass and period”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-25-k1","title":"附加水質量與週期","titleEn":"Added water mass and period","text":"水庫動壓可能與壩體運動耦合，簡化附加質量僅在已指定形狀與頻率條件下代表某種等效作用。不能把整個水庫重量直接加到壩上，亦不能忽略可壓縮性、邊界吸收或水位改變；本單元固定剛度，只檢查一個假設附加量如何改變週期。","textEn":"Reservoir pressure can couple with dam movement, while an added-mass approximation represents an equivalent effect only under stated geometry and frequency conditions. The entire reservoir mass cannot be attached to the dam, nor can compressibility, absorption and water-level change always be ignored.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水庫對水壩動力的作用就是把全部庫水重量加到壩體質量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reservoir interaction simply adds the mass of all stored water to the dam. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「附加水質量與週期」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Added water mass and period\" is correct?","options":["水庫對水壩動力的作用就是把全部庫水重量加到壩體質量。","水庫動壓可能與壩體運動耦合，簡化附加質量僅在已指定形狀與頻率條件下代表某種等效作用。","接縫最大張開永遠等於兩側各自最大位移的平方和平方根。"],"optionsEn":["Reservoir interaction simply adds the mass of all stored water to the dam.","Reservoir pressure can couple with dam movement, while an added-mass approximation represents an equivalent effect only under stated geometry and frequency conditions.","Maximum joint opening always equals the root-sum-square of each side's individual peak displacement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水庫動壓可能與壩體運動耦合，簡化附加質量僅在已指定形狀與頻率條件下代表某種等效作用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Reservoir pressure can couple with dam movement, while an added-mass approximation represents an equivalent effect only under stated geometry and frequency conditions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b256-v15-26","title":"附加水質量與週期：定量估算","titleEn":"Added water mass and period: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「附加水質量與週期」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Added water mass and period” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設原模態m=50000000kg、附加水質量20000000kg、k=2000000000N/m，T=2π√[(m+ma)/k]=1.1755s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume modal mass50000000kg,added water mass20000000kg and unchanged stiffness2000000000N/m. T=2π√[(m+ma)/k]=1.1755s for this assumed approximation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：明列附加質量的推導範圍與所代表模態，與流固耦合模型在多個水位下比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: State the added-mass derivation and represented mode and compare coupled calculations at several levels.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設原模態m=50000000kg、附加水質量20000000kg、k=2000000000N/m，T=2π√[(m+ma)/k]=1.1755s。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume modal mass50000000kg,added water mass20000000kg and unchanged stiffness2000000000N/m. T=2π√[(m+ma)/k]=1.1755s for this assumed approximation.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「附加水質量與週期」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Added water mass and period\", which statement holds?","options":["土石壩的孔壓變化可直接用混凝土線彈性振子的阻尼比完全代表。","地表峰值加速度就是壩體每一點在同一時刻的絕對加速度。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Embankment pore-pressure change is fully represented by the damping ratio of a linear concrete oscillator.","Surface peak acceleration equals the simultaneous absolute acceleration at every point of the dam.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b256-v15-27","title":"附加水質量與週期：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Added water mass and period: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「附加水質量與週期」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Added water mass and period” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"明列附加質量的推導範圍與所代表模態，與流固耦合模型在多個水位下比較。檢查水庫邊界是否過近造成反射，保存原質量和附加量分項，不把週期延長全歸因於材料變軟。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"State the added-mass derivation and represented mode and compare coupled calculations at several levels. Check artificial reflection from nearby reservoir boundaries, retaining structural and water contributions separately rather than attributing every period increase to softened dam material. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：明列附加質量的推導範圍與所代表模態，與流固耦合模型在多個水位下比較。檢查水庫邊界是否過近造成反射，保存原質量和附加量分項，不把週期延長全歸因於材料變軟。","observationEn":"Site practice: State the added-mass derivation and represented mode and compare coupled calculations at several levels. Check artificial reflection from nearby reservoir boundaries, retaining structural and water contributions separately rather than attributing every period increase to softened dam material.","failure":"注意干擾：直接加整個水庫質量會嚴重扭曲週期，人工反射又可能假造動壓峰值。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Attaching the entire reservoir mass grossly distorts period, and artificial reflections create spurious pressure peaks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"明列附加質量的推導範圍與所代表模態，與流固耦合模型在多個水位下比較。檢查水庫邊界是否過近造成反射，保存原質量和附加量分項，不把週期延長全歸因於材料變軟。","textEn":"State the added-mass derivation and represented mode and compare coupled calculations at several levels. Check artificial reflection from nearby reservoir boundaries, retaining structural and water contributions separately rather than attributing every period increase to softened dam material.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"明列附加質量的推導範圍與所代表模態，與流固耦合模型在多個水位下比較。檢查水庫邊界是否過近造成反射，保存原質量和附加量分項，不把週期延長全歸因於材料變軟。","textEn":"State the added-mass derivation and represented mode and compare coupled calculations at several levels. Check artificial reflection from nearby reservoir boundaries, retaining structural and water contributions separately rather than attributing every period increase to softened dam material.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「附加水質量與週期」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Added water mass and period\"?","options":["明列附加質量的推導範圍與所代表模態，與流固耦合模型在多個水位下比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","共振穩態放大係數可直接乘所有地震峰值作為真實反應。"],"optionsEn":["State the added-mass derivation and represented mode and compare coupled calculations at several levels.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The steady resonant magnification can directly multiply every earthquake peak to give the actual response."],"answer":0,"explanation":"明列附加質量的推導範圍與所代表模態，與流固耦合模型在多個水位下比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"State the added-mass derivation and represented mode and compare coupled calculations at several levels. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b256-v15-28","title":"附加水質量與週期：失效診斷","titleEn":"Added water mass and period: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「附加水質量與週期」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Added water mass and period” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"直接加整個水庫質量會嚴重扭曲週期，人工反射又可能假造動壓峰值。僅因空庫與滿庫週期不同就判定結構劣化，會把正常流固互制當成損傷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Attaching the entire reservoir mass grossly distorts period, and artificial reflections create spurious pressure peaks. Declaring deterioration solely from empty- versus full-reservoir period differences mistakes normal fluid-structure interaction for structural damage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設原模態m=50000000kg、附加水質量20000000kg、k=2000000000N/m，T=2π√[(m+ma)/k]=1.1755s。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: T=2π√[(m+ma)/k]=1.1755s for this assumed approximation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水庫對水壩動力的作用就是把全部庫水重量加到壩體質量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reservoir interaction simply adds the mass of all stored water to the dam.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"直接加整個水庫質量會嚴重扭曲週期，人工反射又可能假造動壓峰值。僅因空庫與滿庫週期不同就判定結構劣化，會把正常流固互制當成損傷。","textEn":"Attaching the entire reservoir mass grossly distorts period, and artificial reflections create spurious pressure peaks. Declaring deterioration solely from empty- versus full-reservoir period differences mistakes normal fluid-structure interaction for structural damage.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「附加水質量與週期」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Added water mass and period\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","直接加整個水庫質量會嚴重扭曲週期，人工反射又可能假造動壓峰值。","接縫最大張開永遠等於兩側各自最大位移的平方和平方根。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Attaching the entire reservoir mass grossly distorts period, and artificial reflections create spurious pressure peaks.","Maximum joint opening always equals the root-sum-square of each side's individual peak displacement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"直接加整個水庫質量會嚴重扭曲週期，人工反射又可能假造動壓峰值。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Attaching the entire reservoir mass grossly distorts period, and artificial reflections create spurious pressure peaks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b256-v15-29","title":"同步位移與接縫：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Synchronized displacement and joints: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「同步位移與接縫」如何影響水壩地震動力分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Synchronized displacement and joints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic dynamic analysis of dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"接縫張開由相鄰部位同一時刻的相對位移決定，而不是兩個獨立最大值相減或平方和。坐標方向和局部法向需先定義，剛體平移應在相減時消除；縫面接觸、止水材料與剪切交互作用則需另建模型，位移量本身不代表水密性。 假設同時刻沿接縫法向位移u1=12mm、u2=−8mm，相對張開u1−u2=20mm；不是各自峰值的非同步組合。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「同步位移與接縫」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Joint opening comes from simultaneous relative displacement, not subtraction or quadrature of unrelated extrema. Coordinate direction and local normal must be defined so common rigid translation cancels. Contact, waterstop response and combined shear require additional models; a displacement difference alone does not establish watertightness or allowable joint performance during an earthquake. Assume simultaneous normal displacements u1=12mm and u2=−8mm. Relative opening is20mm, rather than a combination of nonconcurrent individual maxima. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Synchronized displacement and joints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「接縫最大張開永遠等於兩側各自最大位移的平方和平方根。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Maximum joint opening always equals the root-sum-square of each side's individual peak displacement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「同步位移與接縫」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Synchronized displacement and joints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-29-k1","title":"同步位移與接縫","titleEn":"Synchronized displacement and joints","text":"接縫張開由相鄰部位同一時刻的相對位移決定，而不是兩個獨立最大值相減或平方和。坐標方向和局部法向需先定義，剛體平移應在相減時消除；縫面接觸、止水材料與剪切交互作用則需另建模型，位移量本身不代表水密性。","textEn":"Joint opening comes from simultaneous relative displacement, not subtraction or quadrature of unrelated extrema. Coordinate direction and local normal must be defined so common rigid translation cancels.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：接縫最大張開永遠等於兩側各自最大位移的平方和平方根。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Maximum joint opening always equals the root-sum-square of each side's individual peak displacement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「同步位移與接縫」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Synchronized displacement and joints\" is correct?","options":["接縫最大張開永遠等於兩側各自最大位移的平方和平方根。","動力程式成功跑完且每週期有足夠點數就不必再查收斂。","接縫張開由相鄰部位同一時刻的相對位移決定，而不是兩個獨立最大值相減或平方和。"],"optionsEn":["Maximum joint opening always equals the root-sum-square of each side's individual peak displacement.","A completed dynamic run with many points per period never needs a convergence assessment.","Joint opening comes from simultaneous relative displacement, not subtraction or quadrature of unrelated extrema."],"answer":2,"explanation":"接縫張開由相鄰部位同一時刻的相對位移決定，而不是兩個獨立最大值相減或平方和。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Joint opening comes from simultaneous relative displacement, not subtraction or quadrature of unrelated extrema. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b256-v15-30","title":"同步位移與接縫：定量估算","titleEn":"Synchronized displacement and joints: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「同步位移與接縫」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Synchronized displacement and joints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設同時刻沿接縫法向位移u1=12mm、u2=−8mm，相對張開u1−u2=20mm；不是各自峰值的非同步組合。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume simultaneous normal displacements u1=12mm and u2=−8mm. Relative opening is20mm, rather than a combination of nonconcurrent individual maxima. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先把兩側位移轉到同一局部法向與時鐘，再逐時刻求差並找峰值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Transform both records to one local normal and synchronized clock, then difference each time step before locating the peak.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設同時刻沿接縫法向位移u1=12mm、u2=−8mm，相對張開u1−u2=20mm；不是各自峰值的非同步組合。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume simultaneous normal displacements u1=12mm and u2=−8mm. Relative opening is20mm, rather than a combination of nonconcurrent individual maxima.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「同步位移與接縫」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Synchronized displacement and joints\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","第一振動週期吻合即可證明整座水壩的地震應力全部正確。","阻尼設得越大就一定越接近真實水壩的地震反應。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Matching the first natural period proves that every earthquake stress in the dam is correct.","A larger damping value always makes the predicted dam earthquake response more realistic."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b256-v15-31","title":"同步位移與接縫：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Synchronized displacement and joints: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「同步位移與接縫」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Synchronized displacement and joints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先把兩側位移轉到同一局部法向與時鐘，再逐時刻求差並找峰值。另列剪切滑移、接觸壓和止水變形，檢查剛體平移能否抵銷，保留真正控制時刻供受力與漏水判讀。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Transform both records to one local normal and synchronized clock, then difference each time step before locating the peak. Record shear, contact pressure and waterstop deformation separately, checking cancellation of rigid translation and retaining the actual controlling instant for interpretation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：先把兩側位移轉到同一局部法向與時鐘，再逐時刻求差並找峰值。另列剪切滑移、接觸壓和止水變形，檢查剛體平移能否抵銷，保留真正控制時刻供受力與漏水判讀。","observationEn":"Site practice: Transform both records to one local normal and synchronized clock, then difference each time step before locating the peak. Record shear, contact pressure and waterstop deformation separately, checking cancellation of rigid translation and retaining the actual controlling instant for interpretation.","failure":"注意干擾：時鐘偏移會把原本同步移動變成假張開，法向反轉又可能讓共同平移加倍。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Clock offsets make common movement appear as opening, and reversed normals can double rigid translation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先把兩側位移轉到同一局部法向與時鐘，再逐時刻求差並找峰值。另列剪切滑移、接觸壓和止水變形，檢查剛體平移能否抵銷，保留真正控制時刻供受力與漏水判讀。","textEn":"Transform both records to one local normal and synchronized clock, then difference each time step before locating the peak. Record shear, contact pressure and waterstop deformation separately, checking cancellation of rigid translation and retaining the actual controlling instant for interpretation.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"先把兩側位移轉到同一局部法向與時鐘，再逐時刻求差並找峰值。另列剪切滑移、接觸壓和止水變形，檢查剛體平移能否抵銷，保留真正控制時刻供受力與漏水判讀。","textEn":"Transform both records to one local normal and synchronized clock, then difference each time step before locating the peak. Record shear, contact pressure and waterstop deformation separately, checking cancellation of rigid translation and retaining the actual controlling instant for interpretation.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「同步位移與接縫」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Synchronized displacement and joints\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","先把兩側位移轉到同一局部法向與時鐘，再逐時刻求差並找峰值。","任何加速度峰值除以頻率平方都一定得到正確的反應譜位移。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Transform both records to one local normal and synchronized clock, then difference each time step before locating the peak.","Any acceleration peak divided by frequency squared necessarily gives the correct spectral displacement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"先把兩側位移轉到同一局部法向與時鐘，再逐時刻求差並找峰值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Transform both records to one local normal and synchronized clock, then difference each time step before locating the peak. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b256-v15-32","title":"同步位移與接縫：失效診斷","titleEn":"Synchronized displacement and joints: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「同步位移與接縫」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Synchronized displacement and joints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"時鐘偏移會把原本同步移動變成假張開，法向反轉又可能讓共同平移加倍。只取單側峰值會錯過兩側反向運動，低估止水和接觸介面的真正需求。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Clock offsets make common movement appear as opening, and reversed normals can double rigid translation. A one-sided peak can miss opposing movements and understate the actual demand on waterstops and contact interfaces between neighboring blocks. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設同時刻沿接縫法向位移u1=12mm、u2=−8mm，相對張開u1−u2=20mm；不是各自峰值的非同步組合。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Relative opening is20mm, rather than a combination of nonconcurrent individual maxima.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「接縫最大張開永遠等於兩側各自最大位移的平方和平方根。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Maximum joint opening always equals the root-sum-square of each side's individual peak displacement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"時鐘偏移會把原本同步移動變成假張開，法向反轉又可能讓共同平移加倍。只取單側峰值會錯過兩側反向運動，低估止水和接觸介面的真正需求。","textEn":"Clock offsets make common movement appear as opening, and reversed normals can double rigid translation. A one-sided peak can miss opposing movements and understate the actual demand on waterstops and contact interfaces between neighboring blocks.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「同步位移與接縫」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Synchronized displacement and joints\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","動力程式成功跑完且每週期有足夠點數就不必再查收斂。","時鐘偏移會把原本同步移動變成假張開，法向反轉又可能讓共同平移加倍。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A completed dynamic run with many points per period never needs a convergence assessment.","Clock offsets make common movement appear as opening, and reversed normals can double rigid translation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"時鐘偏移會把原本同步移動變成假張開，法向反轉又可能讓共同平移加倍。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Clock offsets make common movement appear as opening, and reversed normals can double rigid translation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b256-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「時間步與高頻解析」與「土壩孔壓與有效應力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Timestep and high-frequency resolution\" and \"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b256-v15-33","title":"時間步與高頻解析：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Timestep and high-frequency resolution: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「時間步與高頻解析」如何影響水壩地震動力分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Timestep and high-frequency resolution” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic dynamic analysis of dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"動力積分步長要解析關心的短週期，但每週期點數只是起點，不是收斂證明。輸入記錄取樣、內插方法、積分演算法和非線性接觸都可能施加更嚴限制；縮小步長後應比較峰值、相位及能量，而不是只確認程式沒有發散或報錯。 假設最短關注週期0.20s、積分步長0.005s，點數T/Δt=40；不能由此保證輸入頻寬或接觸反應已解析。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「時間步與高頻解析」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A dynamic timestep must resolve relevant short periods, but points per cycle are only an initial check, not proof of convergence. Input sampling, interpolation, integration algorithm and nonlinear contact may impose stricter limits. Refinement should compare peaks, phase and energy rather than merely confirming that software completes without numerical divergence or reported errors. Assume the shortest relevant period0.20s and timestep0.005s. T/Δt=40points per cycle, without guaranteeing input bandwidth or resolved contact response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Timestep and high-frequency resolution” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「動力程式成功跑完且每週期有足夠點數就不必再查收斂。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A completed dynamic run with many points per period never needs a convergence assessment.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「時間步與高頻解析」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Timestep and high-frequency resolution”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-33-k1","title":"時間步與高頻解析","titleEn":"Timestep and high-frequency resolution","text":"動力積分步長要解析關心的短週期，但每週期點數只是起點，不是收斂證明。輸入記錄取樣、內插方法、積分演算法和非線性接觸都可能施加更嚴限制；縮小步長後應比較峰值、相位及能量，而不是只確認程式沒有發散或報錯。","textEn":"A dynamic timestep must resolve relevant short periods, but points per cycle are only an initial check, not proof of convergence. Input sampling, interpolation, integration algorithm and nonlinear contact may impose stricter limits.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：動力程式成功跑完且每週期有足夠點數就不必再查收斂。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A completed dynamic run with many points per period never needs a convergence assessment. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「時間步與高頻解析」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Timestep and high-frequency resolution\" is correct?","options":["動力積分步長要解析關心的短週期，但每週期點數只是起點，不是收斂證明。","動力程式成功跑完且每週期有足夠點數就不必再查收斂。","土石壩的孔壓變化可直接用混凝土線彈性振子的阻尼比完全代表。"],"optionsEn":["A dynamic timestep must resolve relevant short periods, but points per cycle are only an initial check, not proof of convergence.","A completed dynamic run with many points per period never needs a convergence assessment.","Embankment pore-pressure change is fully represented by the damping ratio of a linear concrete oscillator."],"answer":0,"explanation":"動力積分步長要解析關心的短週期，但每週期點數只是起點，不是收斂證明。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A dynamic timestep must resolve relevant short periods, but points per cycle are only an initial check, not proof of convergence. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b256-v15-34","title":"時間步與高頻解析：定量估算","titleEn":"Timestep and high-frequency resolution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「時間步與高頻解析」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Timestep and high-frequency resolution” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設最短關注週期0.20s、積分步長0.005s，點數T/Δt=40；不能由此保證輸入頻寬或接觸反應已解析。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume the shortest relevant period0.20s and timestep0.005s. T/Δt=40points per cycle, without guaranteeing input bandwidth or resolved contact response. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：使用相同物理模型分別減半步長，對照位移峰值、加速度與能量殘差，另檢查原始輸入取樣率。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Halve the timestep with unchanged physics and compare displacement peaks, acceleration and energy residuals while checking original input sampling.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設最短關注週期0.20s、積分步長0.005s，點數T/Δt=40；不能由此保證輸入頻寬或接觸反應已解析。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume the shortest relevant period0.20s and timestep0.005s. T/Δt=40points per cycle, without guaranteeing input bandwidth or resolved contact response.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「時間步與高頻解析」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Timestep and high-frequency resolution\", which statement holds?","options":["地表峰值加速度就是壩體每一點在同一時刻的絕對加速度。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","共振穩態放大係數可直接乘所有地震峰值作為真實反應。"],"optionsEn":["Surface peak acceleration equals the simultaneous absolute acceleration at every point of the dam.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","The steady resonant magnification can directly multiply every earthquake peak to give the actual response."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b256-v15-35","title":"時間步與高頻解析：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Timestep and high-frequency resolution: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「時間步與高頻解析」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Timestep and high-frequency resolution” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"使用相同物理模型分別減半步長，對照位移峰值、加速度與能量殘差，另檢查原始輸入取樣率。不要以內插創造原記錄沒有的高頻證據，並把未收斂局部反應獨立標示。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Halve the timestep with unchanged physics and compare displacement peaks, acceleration and energy residuals while checking original input sampling. Interpolation cannot create missing high-frequency evidence; flag local responses that remain unconverged rather than hiding them in global averages. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：使用相同物理模型分別減半步長，對照位移峰值、加速度與能量殘差，另檢查原始輸入取樣率。不要以內插創造原記錄沒有的高頻證據，並把未收斂局部反應獨立標示。","observationEn":"Site practice: Halve the timestep with unchanged physics and compare displacement peaks, acceleration and energy residuals while checking original input sampling. Interpolation cannot create missing high-frequency evidence; flag local responses that remain unconverged rather than hiding them in global averages.","failure":"注意干擾：程式穩定仍可能有顯著相位誤差，粗步長也會漏掉短促接觸力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A stable computation can retain serious phase error and miss brief contact forces. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"使用相同物理模型分別減半步長，對照位移峰值、加速度與能量殘差，另檢查原始輸入取樣率。不要以內插創造原記錄沒有的高頻證據，並把未收斂局部反應獨立標示。","textEn":"Halve the timestep with unchanged physics and compare displacement peaks, acceleration and energy residuals while checking original input sampling. Interpolation cannot create missing high-frequency evidence; flag local responses that remain unconverged rather than hiding them in global averages.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"使用相同物理模型分別減半步長，對照位移峰值、加速度與能量殘差，另檢查原始輸入取樣率。不要以內插創造原記錄沒有的高頻證據，並把未收斂局部反應獨立標示。","textEn":"Halve the timestep with unchanged physics and compare displacement peaks, acceleration and energy residuals while checking original input sampling. Interpolation cannot create missing high-frequency evidence; flag local responses that remain unconverged rather than hiding them in global averages.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「時間步與高頻解析」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Timestep and high-frequency resolution\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","瑞利阻尼只要在兩個頻率匹配就會在所有頻率保持同樣阻尼比。","使用相同物理模型分別減半步長，對照位移峰值、加速度與能量殘差，另檢查原始輸入取樣率。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Rayleigh damping fitted at two frequencies has the same damping ratio at every frequency.","Halve the timestep with unchanged physics and compare displacement peaks, acceleration and energy residuals while checking original input sampling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"使用相同物理模型分別減半步長，對照位移峰值、加速度與能量殘差，另檢查原始輸入取樣率。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Halve the timestep with unchanged physics and compare displacement peaks, acceleration and energy residuals while checking original input sampling. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b256-v15-36","title":"時間步與高頻解析：失效診斷","titleEn":"Timestep and high-frequency resolution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「時間步與高頻解析」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Timestep and high-frequency resolution” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"程式穩定仍可能有顯著相位誤差，粗步長也會漏掉短促接觸力。把稀疏輸入內插成密集資料看似解析度提高，實際卻沒有補回缺失的地震頻率內容。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A stable computation can retain serious phase error and miss brief contact forces. Interpolating sparse input into many samples looks more resolved but does not restore earthquake frequencies absent from the original measured record. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設最短關注週期0.20s、積分步長0.005s，點數T/Δt=40；不能由此保證輸入頻寬或接觸反應已解析。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: T/Δt=40points per cycle, without guaranteeing input bandwidth or resolved contact response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「動力程式成功跑完且每週期有足夠點數就不必再查收斂。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A completed dynamic run with many points per period never needs a convergence assessment.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"程式穩定仍可能有顯著相位誤差，粗步長也會漏掉短促接觸力。把稀疏輸入內插成密集資料看似解析度提高，實際卻沒有補回缺失的地震頻率內容。","textEn":"A stable computation can retain serious phase error and miss brief contact forces. Interpolating sparse input into many samples looks more resolved but does not restore earthquake frequencies absent from the original measured record.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「時間步與高頻解析」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Timestep and high-frequency resolution\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["程式穩定仍可能有顯著相位誤差，粗步長也會漏掉短促接觸力。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","土石壩的孔壓變化可直接用混凝土線彈性振子的阻尼比完全代表。"],"optionsEn":["A stable computation can retain serious phase error and miss brief contact forces.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Embankment pore-pressure change is fully represented by the damping ratio of a linear concrete oscillator."],"answer":0,"explanation":"程式穩定仍可能有顯著相位誤差，粗步長也會漏掉短促接觸力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A stable computation can retain serious phase error and miss brief contact forces. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b256-v15-37","title":"土壩孔壓與有效應力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「土壩孔壓與有效應力」如何影響水壩地震動力分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seismic dynamic analysis of dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"土石壩可能發生循環孔壓增加及強度改變，這與混凝土線彈性振子是不同機制。有效應力下降需以相同應力路徑和時間的資料計算，孔壓比接近某值也不能單獨宣告整座壩已液化；殘餘強度、震後排水與永久變形仍需專門材料和穩定分析。 假設初有效垂直應力100kPa、總應力固定而超額孔壓增60kPa，ru=0.60，剩餘有效應力40kPa；非液化整體判定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「土壩孔壓與有效應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Embankments can develop cyclic pore pressure and altered strength, mechanisms distinct from a linear concrete oscillator. Effective-stress reduction needs matching stress paths and times. A pore-pressure ratio alone cannot declare the entire dam liquefied; residual strength, post-earthquake drainage and permanent deformation still require appropriate material testing and stability analysis rather than transfer of concrete-dam assumptions. Assume initial effective vertical stress100kPa and excess pore-pressure rise60kPa at fixed total stress. ru=0.60 and remaining effective stress40kPa, not a global liquefaction verdict. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「土石壩的孔壓變化可直接用混凝土線彈性振子的阻尼比完全代表。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Embankment pore-pressure change is fully represented by the damping ratio of a linear concrete oscillator.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「土壩孔壓與有效應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-37-k1","title":"土壩孔壓與有效應力","titleEn":"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress","text":"土石壩可能發生循環孔壓增加及強度改變，這與混凝土線彈性振子是不同機制。有效應力下降需以相同應力路徑和時間的資料計算，孔壓比接近某值也不能單獨宣告整座壩已液化；殘餘強度、震後排水與永久變形仍需專門材料和穩定分析。","textEn":"Embankments can develop cyclic pore pressure and altered strength, mechanisms distinct from a linear concrete oscillator. Effective-stress reduction needs matching stress paths and times.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：土石壩的孔壓變化可直接用混凝土線彈性振子的阻尼比完全代表。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Embankment pore-pressure change is fully represented by the damping ratio of a linear concrete oscillator. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「土壩孔壓與有效應力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress\" is correct?","options":["土石壩的孔壓變化可直接用混凝土線彈性振子的阻尼比完全代表。","土石壩可能發生循環孔壓增加及強度改變，這與混凝土線彈性振子是不同機制。","第一振動週期吻合即可證明整座水壩的地震應力全部正確。"],"optionsEn":["Embankment pore-pressure change is fully represented by the damping ratio of a linear concrete oscillator.","Embankments can develop cyclic pore pressure and altered strength, mechanisms distinct from a linear concrete oscillator.","Matching the first natural period proves that every earthquake stress in the dam is correct."],"answer":1,"explanation":"土石壩可能發生循環孔壓增加及強度改變，這與混凝土線彈性振子是不同機制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Embankments can develop cyclic pore pressure and altered strength, mechanisms distinct from a linear concrete oscillator. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b256-v15-38","title":"土壩孔壓與有效應力：定量估算","titleEn":"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「土壩孔壓與有效應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設初有效垂直應力100kPa、總應力固定而超額孔壓增60kPa，ru=0.60，剩餘有效應力40kPa；非液化整體判定。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume initial effective vertical stress100kPa and excess pore-pressure rise60kPa at fixed total stress. ru=0.60 and remaining effective stress40kPa, not a global liquefaction verdict. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將孔壓與總應力歷時同步，核對初始有效應力和超額孔壓的基準。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronize pore-pressure and total-stress histories, checking initial effective stress and the excess-pressure reference.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設初有效垂直應力100kPa、總應力固定而超額孔壓增60kPa，ru=0.60，剩餘有效應力40kPa；非液化整體判定。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume initial effective vertical stress100kPa and excess pore-pressure rise60kPa at fixed total stress. ru=0.60 and remaining effective stress40kPa, not a global liquefaction verdict.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「土壩孔壓與有效應力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress\", which statement holds?","options":["阻尼設得越大就一定越接近真實水壩的地震反應。","任何加速度峰值除以頻率平方都一定得到正確的反應譜位移。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["A larger damping value always makes the predicted dam earthquake response more realistic.","Any acceleration peak divided by frequency squared necessarily gives the correct spectral displacement.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b256-v15-39","title":"土壩孔壓與有效應力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「土壩孔壓與有效應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將孔壓與總應力歷時同步，核對初始有效應力和超額孔壓的基準。比較不同土層的循環試驗與震後強度，記錄局部高孔壓位置和排水路徑，避免把單點比值推廣到所有壩體材料。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronize pore-pressure and total-stress histories, checking initial effective stress and the excess-pressure reference. Compare layer-specific cyclic tests and post-shaking strength, mapping local high pressures and drainage routes without extending one point ratio to every material in the dam. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將孔壓與總應力歷時同步，核對初始有效應力和超額孔壓的基準。比較不同土層的循環試驗與震後強度，記錄局部高孔壓位置和排水路徑，避免把單點比值推廣到所有壩體材料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Synchronize pore-pressure and total-stress histories, checking initial effective stress and the excess-pressure reference. Compare layer-specific cyclic tests and post-shaking strength, mapping local high pressures and drainage routes without extending one point ratio to every material in the dam.","failure":"注意干擾：把總孔壓誤當超額孔壓會高估累積，忽略總應力變動則可能誤判有效應力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using total pressure instead of excess pressure overstates accumulation, while omitted total-stress variation misstates effective stress. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將孔壓與總應力歷時同步，核對初始有效應力和超額孔壓的基準。比較不同土層的循環試驗與震後強度，記錄局部高孔壓位置和排水路徑，避免把單點比值推廣到所有壩體材料。","textEn":"Synchronize pore-pressure and total-stress histories, checking initial effective stress and the excess-pressure reference. Compare layer-specific cyclic tests and post-shaking strength, mapping local high pressures and drainage routes without extending one point ratio to every material in the dam.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將孔壓與總應力歷時同步，核對初始有效應力和超額孔壓的基準。比較不同土層的循環試驗與震後強度，記錄局部高孔壓位置和排水路徑，避免把單點比值推廣到所有壩體材料。","textEn":"Synchronize pore-pressure and total-stress histories, checking initial effective stress and the excess-pressure reference. Compare layer-specific cyclic tests and post-shaking strength, mapping local high pressures and drainage routes without extending one point ratio to every material in the dam.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「土壩孔壓與有效應力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress\"?","options":["將孔壓與總應力歷時同步，核對初始有效應力和超額孔壓的基準。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","水庫對水壩動力的作用就是把全部庫水重量加到壩體質量。"],"optionsEn":["Synchronize pore-pressure and total-stress histories, checking initial effective stress and the excess-pressure reference.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Reservoir interaction simply adds the mass of all stored water to the dam."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將孔壓與總應力歷時同步，核對初始有效應力和超額孔壓的基準。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronize pore-pressure and total-stress histories, checking initial effective stress and the excess-pressure reference. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b256-v15-40","title":"土壩孔壓與有效應力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"prerequisiteIds":["b256-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「土壩孔壓與有效應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把總孔壓誤當超額孔壓會高估累積，忽略總應力變動則可能誤判有效應力。局部弱層即使不控制平均值，也可能形成永久變形路徑，不能只看整壩平均反應。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using total pressure instead of excess pressure overstates accumulation, while omitted total-stress variation misstates effective stress. A local weak layer can govern permanent deformation despite a modest average ratio across the wider dam body. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設初有效垂直應力100kPa、總應力固定而超額孔壓增60kPa，ru=0.60，剩餘有效應力40kPa；非液化整體判定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume initial effective vertical stress100kPa and excess pore-pressure rise60kPa at fixed total stress. ru=0.60 and remaining effective stress40kPa, not a global liquefaction verdict.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「土石壩的孔壓變化可直接用混凝土線彈性振子的阻尼比完全代表。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Embankment pore-pressure change is fully represented by the damping ratio of a linear concrete oscillator.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b256-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把總孔壓誤當超額孔壓會高估累積，忽略總應力變動則可能誤判有效應力。局部弱層即使不控制平均值，也可能形成永久變形路徑，不能只看整壩平均反應。","textEn":"Using total pressure instead of excess pressure overstates accumulation, while omitted total-stress variation misstates effective stress. A local weak layer can govern permanent deformation despite a modest average ratio across the wider dam body.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]},{"id":"b256-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「土壩孔壓與有效應力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Embankment pore pressure and effective stress\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把總孔壓誤當超額孔壓會高估累積，忽略總應力變動則可能誤判有效應力。","第一振動週期吻合即可證明整座水壩的地震應力全部正確。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using total pressure instead of excess pressure overstates accumulation, while omitted total-stress variation misstates effective stress.","Matching the first natural period proves that every earthquake stress in the dam is correct."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把總孔壓誤當超額孔壓會高估累積，忽略總應力變動則可能誤判有效應力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using total pressure instead of excess pressure overstates accumulation, while omitted total-stress variation misstates effective stress. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-dam-dynamics","v15s-embankment-seismic","v6-hoover-history","v15s-sisk-history"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b257","title":"水力模型縮尺試驗","titleEn":"Scale-model testing of hydraulic structures","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以非扭曲自由水面重力模型為主軸，逐步推導幾何、速度、流量、時間、壓力與合力比例，再檢查雷諾數、韋伯數及量測誤差無法自動相似的部分。十個單元要求先說明研究目的與控制尺度，再判斷哪些結果可量化放大，哪些只能定性比較，避免以模型照片漂亮取代實驗驗證。","summaryEn":"An undistorted gravity-driven free-surface model provides the main thread. Units derive geometry, velocity, discharge, time, pressure and force scales, then examine Reynolds and Weber mismatches and measurement uncertainty. Apprentices define the question and controlling length before deciding which results support quantitative extrapolation and which allow only qualitative comparison.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-hydraulics","subcategoryTitle":"壩工監測、溢洪與壓力水路","subcategoryTitleEn":"Dam monitoring, spillways and pressure waterways","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-hydraulics","learningTags":["water","water-hydraulics","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-hydraulic","architectureNodes":[["幾何比例與控制長度","Geometry ratio and reference length"],["總流量縮尺次方","Total-discharge scale exponent"],["壓力尺度與氣泡","Pressure scale and air effects"],["韋伯數與表面張力","Weber number and surface tension"],["重複試驗與代表性","Replicates and representativeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-hydraulic","labels":["幾何比例與控制長度","總流量縮尺次方","壓力尺度與氣泡","韋伯數與表面張力","重複試驗與代表性"],"labelsEn":["Geometry ratio and reference length","Total-discharge scale exponent","Pressure scale and air effects","Weber number and surface tension","Replicates and representativeness"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創縮尺敏感度：原型總流量1000m³/s，長度比例40，依佛祿相似Qm=1000/40^(5/2)=0.09882m³/s。若為節省實驗空間把比例增加10%至44，原型保持不變，所需模型流量降為1000/44^(5/2)=0.07787m³/s，約減少21.20%，並不是只減少10%。此時模型尺度更小，黏滯和表面張力相對影響反而更值得查核。學徒應重算速度、時間、感測器量程與誤差放大，確認試驗台是否能穩定提供較小流量。不能只因用水減少就認為改尺度必然改善研究品質。","textEn":"Original scale sensitivity: a prototype discharge of1000m³/s with length ratio40 requires Qm=1000/40^(5/2)=0.09882m³/s under Froude similarity. Increasing the ratio by10% to44 to save laboratory space while retaining the same prototype reduces flow to1000/44^(5/2)=0.07787m³/s, about21.20% rather than10%. The smaller model makes relative viscous and capillary effects more important to check. Recalculate velocity, timing, sensor range and uncertainty amplification, then verify that the rig can reliably provide the lower discharge. Reduced water demand alone does not establish that the revised scale improves the quality of the experiment.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b257-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「幾何比例與控制長度」與「重力流速度比例」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Geometry ratio and reference length\" and \"Velocity scaling for gravity flow\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b257-v15-01","title":"幾何比例與控制長度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Geometry ratio and reference length: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「幾何比例與控制長度」如何影響水力模型縮尺試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Geometry ratio and reference length” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Scale-model testing of hydraulic structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"縮尺試驗先決定要研究的水理現象，再選控制長度及完整幾何範圍，不能只把外觀縮小就認為等價。非扭曲模型各方向採同一比例，局部粗糙、縫隙與邊界若無法製作應記錄；改用垂直水平不同比例時，速度與輸砂關係必須重新推導。 假設原型與模型長度比λL=40，原型水深8m及長80m，模型分別0.20m與2m；所有方向採同一比例。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「幾何比例與控制長度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A model starts with the physical question, reference length and geometric domain rather than visual miniaturization. An undistorted model uses one ratio in all directions, documenting roughness, gaps or boundaries that cannot be reproduced. Different vertical and horizontal scales require rederived velocity and sediment relationships, so they cannot be introduced quietly while retaining undistorted-model formulas. Assume prototype-to-model length ratio40. Prototype depth8m and length80m become0.20m and2m, with the same ratio in every direction. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Geometry ratio and reference length” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要模型外觀像原型就可以忽略局部縫隙與尺度方向差異。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Visual similarity alone permits ignoring gaps and differences between horizontal and vertical scales.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「幾何比例與控制長度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Geometry ratio and reference length”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-01-k1","title":"幾何比例與控制長度","titleEn":"Geometry ratio and reference length","text":"縮尺試驗先決定要研究的水理現象，再選控制長度及完整幾何範圍，不能只把外觀縮小就認為等價。非扭曲模型各方向採同一比例，局部粗糙、縫隙與邊界若無法製作應記錄；改用垂直水平不同比例時，速度與輸砂關係必須重新推導。","textEn":"A model starts with the physical question, reference length and geometric domain rather than visual miniaturization. An undistorted model uses one ratio in all directions, documenting roughness, gaps or boundaries that cannot be reproduced.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要模型外觀像原型就可以忽略局部縫隙與尺度方向差異。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Visual similarity alone permits ignoring gaps and differences between horizontal and vertical scales. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「幾何比例與控制長度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Geometry ratio and reference length\" is correct?","options":["只要模型外觀像原型就可以忽略局部縫隙與尺度方向差異。","縮尺試驗先決定要研究的水理現象，再選控制長度及完整幾何範圍，不能只把外觀縮小就認為等價。","佛祿相似要求速度與模型長度使用完全相同的縮小倍數。"],"optionsEn":["Visual similarity alone permits ignoring gaps and differences between horizontal and vertical scales.","A model starts with the physical question, reference length and geometric domain rather than visual miniaturization.","Froude similarity requires velocity to use exactly the same reduction factor as length."],"answer":1,"explanation":"縮尺試驗先決定要研究的水理現象，再選控制長度及完整幾何範圍，不能只把外觀縮小就認為等價。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A model starts with the physical question, reference length and geometric domain rather than visual miniaturization. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b257-v15-02","title":"幾何比例與控制長度：定量估算","titleEn":"Geometry ratio and reference length: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「幾何比例與控制長度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Geometry ratio and reference length” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設原型與模型長度比λL=40，原型水深8m及長80m，模型分別0.20m與2m；所有方向採同一比例。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume prototype-to-model length ratio40. Prototype depth8m and length80m become0.20m and2m, with the same ratio in every direction. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把原型及模型坐標、邊界和粗糙尺寸列成對照表，實測關鍵斷面而非只看製圖尺寸。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Tabulate prototype and model coordinates, boundaries and roughness, measuring critical sections rather than relying only on drawings.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設原型與模型長度比λL=40，原型水深8m及長80m，模型分別0.20m與2m；所有方向採同一比例。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume prototype-to-model length ratio40. Prototype depth8m and length80m become0.20m and2m, with the same ratio in every direction.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「幾何比例與控制長度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Geometry ratio and reference length\", which statement holds?","options":["只要事後修改時間軸就能補救試驗時未縮尺的閥門動作。","縮尺合力只需要跟長度成正比而不必考慮受壓面積。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Rescaling the recorded time axis repairs any valve motion that was not correctly scaled during the test.","Model force scales only linearly with length and does not depend on loaded area.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b257-v15-03","title":"幾何比例與控制長度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Geometry ratio and reference length: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「幾何比例與控制長度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Geometry ratio and reference length” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把原型及模型坐標、邊界和粗糙尺寸列成對照表，實測關鍵斷面而非只看製圖尺寸。確認是否有扭曲尺度，將無法按比例製作的縫隙獨立標出，說明可能影響哪一項觀察量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Tabulate prototype and model coordinates, boundaries and roughness, measuring critical sections rather than relying only on drawings. Identify any distorted scale and separately mark gaps that cannot be reproduced, explaining which observed quantities their mismatch could influence. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把原型及模型坐標、邊界和粗糙尺寸列成對照表，實測關鍵斷面而非只看製圖尺寸。確認是否有扭曲尺度，將無法按比例製作的縫隙獨立標出，說明可能影響哪一項觀察量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Tabulate prototype and model coordinates, boundaries and roughness, measuring critical sections rather than relying only on drawings. Identify any distorted scale and separately mark gaps that cannot be reproduced, explaining which observed quantities their mismatch could influence.","failure":"注意干擾：微小閘縫若在模型被封死會改變漏流，轉角磨圓則可能改變分離。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Closing a tiny modeled gate gap changes leakage, while rounded corners alter separation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把原型及模型坐標、邊界和粗糙尺寸列成對照表，實測關鍵斷面而非只看製圖尺寸。確認是否有扭曲尺度，將無法按比例製作的縫隙獨立標出，說明可能影響哪一項觀察量。","textEn":"Tabulate prototype and model coordinates, boundaries and roughness, measuring critical sections rather than relying only on drawings. Identify any distorted scale and separately mark gaps that cannot be reproduced, explaining which observed quantities their mismatch could influence.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把原型及模型坐標、邊界和粗糙尺寸列成對照表，實測關鍵斷面而非只看製圖尺寸。確認是否有扭曲尺度，將無法按比例製作的縫隙獨立標出，說明可能影響哪一項觀察量。","textEn":"Tabulate prototype and model coordinates, boundaries and roughness, measuring critical sections rather than relying only on drawings. Identify any distorted scale and separately mark gaps that cannot be reproduced, explaining which observed quantities their mismatch could influence.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「幾何比例與控制長度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Geometry ratio and reference length\"?","options":["把原型及模型坐標、邊界和粗糙尺寸列成對照表，實測關鍵斷面而非只看製圖尺寸。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","重力相似已經自動保證液滴尺寸與曝氣程度都能直接放大。"],"optionsEn":["Tabulate prototype and model coordinates, boundaries and roughness, measuring critical sections rather than relying only on drawings.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Gravity similarity automatically makes droplet size and air entrainment directly scalable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把原型及模型坐標、邊界和粗糙尺寸列成對照表，實測關鍵斷面而非只看製圖尺寸。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Tabulate prototype and model coordinates, boundaries and roughness, measuring critical sections rather than relying only on drawings. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b257-v15-04","title":"幾何比例與控制長度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Geometry ratio and reference length: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「幾何比例與控制長度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Geometry ratio and reference length” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"微小閘縫若在模型被封死會改變漏流，轉角磨圓則可能改變分離。外觀相似但垂直尺度偷偷不同時，原本的相似律不再適用，結果仍可能看起來很合理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Closing a tiny modeled gate gap changes leakage, while rounded corners alter separation. A visually similar model with an undisclosed vertical-scale change violates the original similarity assumptions even when its output appears plausible. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設原型與模型長度比λL=40，原型水深8m及長80m，模型分別0.20m與2m；所有方向採同一比例。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Prototype depth8m and length80m become0.20m and2m, with the same ratio in every direction.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要模型外觀像原型就可以忽略局部縫隙與尺度方向差異。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Visual similarity alone permits ignoring gaps and differences between horizontal and vertical scales.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"微小閘縫若在模型被封死會改變漏流，轉角磨圓則可能改變分離。外觀相似但垂直尺度偷偷不同時，原本的相似律不再適用，結果仍可能看起來很合理。","textEn":"Closing a tiny modeled gate gap changes leakage, while rounded corners alter separation. A visually similar model with an undisclosed vertical-scale change violates the original similarity assumptions even when its output appears plausible.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「幾何比例與控制長度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Geometry ratio and reference length\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","微小閘縫若在模型被封死會改變漏流，轉角磨圓則可能改變分離。","佛祿相似要求速度與模型長度使用完全相同的縮小倍數。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Closing a tiny modeled gate gap changes leakage, while rounded corners alter separation.","Froude similarity requires velocity to use exactly the same reduction factor as length."],"answer":1,"explanation":"微小閘縫若在模型被封死會改變漏流，轉角磨圓則可能改變分離。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Closing a tiny modeled gate gap changes leakage, while rounded corners alter separation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b257-v15-05","title":"重力流速度比例：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Velocity scaling for gravity flow: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「重力流速度比例」如何影響水力模型縮尺試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Velocity scaling for gravity flow” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Scale-model testing of hydraulic structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"自由水面重力主導時以佛祿數相等建立速度比例，必須確認原型與模型使用相同重力場。此時速度不是隨長度線性縮小，且黏滯或表面張力主導的小尺度區仍可能失真；同一速度比例也不能無條件套到加壓水錘或可壓縮氣流。 假設λL=40且佛祿相似，原型速度8m/s，模型Vm=8/√40=1.2649m/s；不保證雷諾相似。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「重力流速度比例」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For gravity-dominated free surfaces, equal Froude numbers determine velocity scaling under equal gravity. Velocity does not shrink linearly with length, and small viscous or capillary regions may remain distorted. The same relation cannot automatically describe pressurized water hammer or compressible air, whose controlling physics and required similarity parameters differ from the chosen free-surface experiment. Assume length ratio40 and Froude similarity. Prototype velocity8m/s gives Vm=8/√40=1.2649m/s, without guaranteeing Reynolds similarity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Velocity scaling for gravity flow” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「佛祿相似要求速度與模型長度使用完全相同的縮小倍數。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Froude similarity requires velocity to use exactly the same reduction factor as length.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「重力流速度比例」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Velocity scaling for gravity flow”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-05-k1","title":"重力流速度比例","titleEn":"Velocity scaling for gravity flow","text":"自由水面重力主導時以佛祿數相等建立速度比例，必須確認原型與模型使用相同重力場。此時速度不是隨長度線性縮小，且黏滯或表面張力主導的小尺度區仍可能失真；同一速度比例也不能無條件套到加壓水錘或可壓縮氣流。","textEn":"For gravity-dominated free surfaces, equal Froude numbers determine velocity scaling under equal gravity. Velocity does not shrink linearly with length, and small viscous or capillary regions may remain distorted.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：佛祿相似要求速度與模型長度使用完全相同的縮小倍數。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Froude similarity requires velocity to use exactly the same reduction factor as length. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「重力流速度比例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Velocity scaling for gravity flow\" is correct?","options":["佛祿相似要求速度與模型長度使用完全相同的縮小倍數。","總流量與每米寬度流量在縮尺模型都使用同一比例次方。","自由水面重力主導時以佛祿數相等建立速度比例，必須確認原型與模型使用相同重力場。"],"optionsEn":["Froude similarity requires velocity to use exactly the same reduction factor as length.","Total discharge and discharge per unit width use the same scaling exponent.","For gravity-dominated free surfaces, equal Froude numbers determine velocity scaling under equal gravity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"自由水面重力主導時以佛祿數相等建立速度比例，必須確認原型與模型使用相同重力場。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For gravity-dominated free surfaces, equal Froude numbers determine velocity scaling under equal gravity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b257-v15-06","title":"重力流速度比例：定量估算","titleEn":"Velocity scaling for gravity flow: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「重力流速度比例」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Velocity scaling for gravity flow” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設λL=40且佛祿相似，原型速度8m/s，模型Vm=8/√40=1.2649m/s；不保證雷諾相似。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume length ratio40 and Froude similarity. Prototype velocity8m/s gives Vm=8/√40=1.2649m/s, without guaranteeing Reynolds similarity. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分別用原型與模型水深計算佛祿數，查核速度量測位置是否對應。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compute Froude numbers independently using corresponding depths and velocity locations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設λL=40且佛祿相似，原型速度8m/s，模型Vm=8/√40=1.2649m/s；不保證雷諾相似。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume length ratio40 and Froude similarity. Prototype velocity8m/s gives Vm=8/√40=1.2649m/s, without guaranteeing Reynolds similarity.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「重力流速度比例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Velocity scaling for gravity flow\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","重力壓力比例正確就表示空化與封閉氣泡壓縮也完全相似。","模型主流雷諾數高就可以證明每個細縫和近壁區都與原型相似。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Correct gravity-pressure scaling proves that cavitation and trapped-air compression are also fully similar.","A high main-flow Reynolds number proves similarity in every small gap and near-wall region."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b257-v15-07","title":"重力流速度比例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Velocity scaling for gravity flow: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「重力流速度比例」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Velocity scaling for gravity flow” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分別用原型與模型水深計算佛祿數，查核速度量測位置是否對應。再估黏滯與表面張力影響範圍，區分局部薄水層和主要流區，不以整體相似掩蓋小尺度區域的失真。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compute Froude numbers independently using corresponding depths and velocity locations. Estimate where viscosity and surface tension matter, separating thin local layers from the main flow rather than hiding small-scale distortion behind a matching global similarity parameter. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分別用原型與模型水深計算佛祿數，查核速度量測位置是否對應。再估黏滯與表面張力影響範圍，區分局部薄水層和主要流區，不以整體相似掩蓋小尺度區域的失真。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compute Froude numbers independently using corresponding depths and velocity locations. Estimate where viscosity and surface tension matter, separating thin local layers from the main flow rather than hiding small-scale distortion behind a matching global similarity parameter.","failure":"注意干擾：將速度也縮小四十倍會使流態和波速錯位，僅調整入流直到外觀看似相同也可能改變水深。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reducing velocity fortyfold misrepresents flow regime and wave propagation, while adjusting inflow merely to match appearance may change depth. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分別用原型與模型水深計算佛祿數，查核速度量測位置是否對應。再估黏滯與表面張力影響範圍，區分局部薄水層和主要流區，不以整體相似掩蓋小尺度區域的失真。","textEn":"Compute Froude numbers independently using corresponding depths and velocity locations. Estimate where viscosity and surface tension matter, separating thin local layers from the main flow rather than hiding small-scale distortion behind a matching global similarity parameter.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分別用原型與模型水深計算佛祿數，查核速度量測位置是否對應。再估黏滯與表面張力影響範圍，區分局部薄水層和主要流區，不以整體相似掩蓋小尺度區域的失真。","textEn":"Compute Froude numbers independently using corresponding depths and velocity locations. Estimate where viscosity and surface tension matter, separating thin local layers from the main flow rather than hiding small-scale distortion behind a matching global similarity parameter.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「重力流速度比例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Velocity scaling for gravity flow\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","分別用原型與模型水深計算佛祿數，查核速度量測位置是否對應。","模型讀值誤差很小所以換算回原型後可以完全忽略不計。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compute Froude numbers independently using corresponding depths and velocity locations.","A small model reading error can be ignored completely after conversion to prototype scale."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分別用原型與模型水深計算佛祿數，查核速度量測位置是否對應。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compute Froude numbers independently using corresponding depths and velocity locations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b257-v15-08","title":"重力流速度比例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Velocity scaling for gravity flow: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「重力流速度比例」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Velocity scaling for gravity flow” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將速度也縮小四十倍會使流態和波速錯位，僅調整入流直到外觀看似相同也可能改變水深。局部黏性控制區即使佛祿數正確，壓力和渦流仍未必可直接放大。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reducing velocity fortyfold misrepresents flow regime and wave propagation, while adjusting inflow merely to match appearance may change depth. Locally viscous regions can still have unrepresentative pressures and vortices despite equal Froude numbers. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設λL=40且佛祿相似，原型速度8m/s，模型Vm=8/√40=1.2649m/s；不保證雷諾相似。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Prototype velocity8m/s gives Vm=8/√40=1.2649m/s, without guaranteeing Reynolds similarity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「佛祿相似要求速度與模型長度使用完全相同的縮小倍數。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Froude similarity requires velocity to use exactly the same reduction factor as length.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將速度也縮小四十倍會使流態和波速錯位，僅調整入流直到外觀看似相同也可能改變水深。局部黏性控制區即使佛祿數正確，壓力和渦流仍未必可直接放大。","textEn":"Reducing velocity fortyfold misrepresents flow regime and wave propagation, while adjusting inflow merely to match appearance may change depth. Locally viscous regions can still have unrepresentative pressures and vortices despite equal Froude numbers.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「重力流速度比例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Velocity scaling for gravity flow\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","總流量與每米寬度流量在縮尺模型都使用同一比例次方。","將速度也縮小四十倍會使流態和波速錯位，僅調整入流直到外觀看似相同也可能改變水深。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Total discharge and discharge per unit width use the same scaling exponent.","Reducing velocity fortyfold misrepresents flow regime and wave propagation, while adjusting inflow merely to match appearance may change depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將速度也縮小四十倍會使流態和波速錯位，僅調整入流直到外觀看似相同也可能改變水深。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reducing velocity fortyfold misrepresents flow regime and wave propagation, while adjusting inflow merely to match appearance may change depth. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b257-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「總流量縮尺次方」與「時間縮尺與記錄」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Total-discharge scale exponent\" and \"Time scaling and recording\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b257-v15-09","title":"總流量縮尺次方：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Total-discharge scale exponent: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「總流量縮尺次方」如何影響水力模型縮尺試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Total-discharge scale exponent” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Scale-model testing of hydraulic structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"總流量是斷面面積乘速度，非扭曲重力模型的面積按長度平方、速度按平方根縮放，因此總流量有不同次方。單位寬度流量另有分母，兩者不能混用；量測管路與模型入口也需一致，旁通或溢流未記錄會破壞整體收支。 假設λL=40、原型總Q=1000m³/s，模型Qm=Qp/λL^(5/2)=0.09882m³/s；不是單位寬度流量比例。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「總流量縮尺次方」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Total discharge combines cross-sectional area with velocity. An undistorted gravity model scales area with length squared and velocity with its square root, producing a distinct exponent. Unit-width discharge has a different denominator and cannot use the same rule. Measurement piping, bypasses and overflow must also match the model boundary to preserve the water balance. Assume length ratio40 and prototype total discharge1000m³/s. Model Qm=Qp/λL^(5/2)=0.09882m³/s, distinct from unit-width discharge scaling. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Total-discharge scale exponent” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「總流量與每米寬度流量在縮尺模型都使用同一比例次方。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Total discharge and discharge per unit width use the same scaling exponent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「總流量縮尺次方」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Total-discharge scale exponent”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-09-k1","title":"總流量縮尺次方","titleEn":"Total-discharge scale exponent","text":"總流量是斷面面積乘速度，非扭曲重力模型的面積按長度平方、速度按平方根縮放，因此總流量有不同次方。單位寬度流量另有分母，兩者不能混用；量測管路與模型入口也需一致，旁通或溢流未記錄會破壞整體收支。","textEn":"Total discharge combines cross-sectional area with velocity. An undistorted gravity model scales area with length squared and velocity with its square root, producing a distinct exponent.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：總流量與每米寬度流量在縮尺模型都使用同一比例次方。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Total discharge and discharge per unit width use the same scaling exponent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「總流量縮尺次方」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Total-discharge scale exponent\" is correct?","options":["總流量是斷面面積乘速度，非扭曲重力模型的面積按長度平方、速度按平方根縮放，因此總流量有不同次方。","總流量與每米寬度流量在縮尺模型都使用同一比例次方。","只要事後修改時間軸就能補救試驗時未縮尺的閥門動作。"],"optionsEn":["Total discharge combines cross-sectional area with velocity.","Total discharge and discharge per unit width use the same scaling exponent.","Rescaling the recorded time axis repairs any valve motion that was not correctly scaled during the test."],"answer":0,"explanation":"總流量是斷面面積乘速度，非扭曲重力模型的面積按長度平方、速度按平方根縮放，因此總流量有不同次方。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Total discharge combines cross-sectional area with velocity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b257-v15-10","title":"總流量縮尺次方：定量估算","titleEn":"Total-discharge scale exponent: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「總流量縮尺次方」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Total-discharge scale exponent” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設λL=40、原型總Q=1000m³/s，模型Qm=Qp/λL^(5/2)=0.09882m³/s；不是單位寬度流量比例。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume length ratio40 and prototype total discharge1000m³/s. Model Qm=Qp/λL^(5/2)=0.09882m³/s, distinct from unit-width discharge scaling. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從面積與速度比例逐步推導流量次方，確認資料標示總流量或每米寬度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Derive the exponent from area and velocity and label total versus per-width discharge.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設λL=40、原型總Q=1000m³/s，模型Qm=Qp/λL^(5/2)=0.09882m³/s；不是單位寬度流量比例。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume length ratio40 and prototype total discharge1000m³/s. Model Qm=Qp/λL^(5/2)=0.09882m³/s, distinct from unit-width discharge scaling.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「總流量縮尺次方」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Total-discharge scale exponent\", which statement holds?","options":["縮尺合力只需要跟長度成正比而不必考慮受壓面積。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","重力相似已經自動保證液滴尺寸與曝氣程度都能直接放大。"],"optionsEn":["Model force scales only linearly with length and does not depend on loaded area.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Gravity similarity automatically makes droplet size and air entrainment directly scalable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b257-v15-11","title":"總流量縮尺次方：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Total-discharge scale exponent: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「總流量縮尺次方」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Total-discharge scale exponent” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從面積與速度比例逐步推導流量次方，確認資料標示總流量或每米寬度。以獨立容積時間法查核流量計，記錄旁通與回流，並將校正範圍對照實際模型所需的小流量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Derive the exponent from area and velocity and label total versus per-width discharge. Check the flow meter independently by volume and time, recording bypass and recirculation and comparing its calibration range with the small discharge actually required by the model. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：從面積與速度比例逐步推導流量次方，確認資料標示總流量或每米寬度。以獨立容積時間法查核流量計，記錄旁通與回流，並將校正範圍對照實際模型所需的小流量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Derive the exponent from area and velocity and label total versus per-width discharge. Check the flow meter independently by volume and time, recording bypass and recirculation and comparing its calibration range with the small discharge actually required by the model.","failure":"注意干擾：把每米流量的次方用在總流量會差一個長度比例，低流量儀器超出校正範圍又會加深誤差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using the unit-width exponent for total discharge introduces an entire length-scale error, compounded if the meter operates outside calibration. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從面積與速度比例逐步推導流量次方，確認資料標示總流量或每米寬度。以獨立容積時間法查核流量計，記錄旁通與回流，並將校正範圍對照實際模型所需的小流量。","textEn":"Derive the exponent from area and velocity and label total versus per-width discharge. Check the flow meter independently by volume and time, recording bypass and recirculation and comparing its calibration range with the small discharge actually required by the model.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"從面積與速度比例逐步推導流量次方，確認資料標示總流量或每米寬度。以獨立容積時間法查核流量計，記錄旁通與回流，並將校正範圍對照實際模型所需的小流量。","textEn":"Derive the exponent from area and velocity and label total versus per-width discharge. Check the flow meter independently by volume and time, recording bypass and recirculation and comparing its calibration range with the small discharge actually required by the model.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「總流量縮尺次方」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Total-discharge scale exponent\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","重複三次結果很接近就代表所有未測工況與系統偏差都已驗證。","從面積與速度比例逐步推導流量次方，確認資料標示總流量或每米寬度。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Three closely agreeing repeats validate every untested condition and eliminate systematic bias.","Derive the exponent from area and velocity and label total versus per-width discharge."],"answer":2,"explanation":"從面積與速度比例逐步推導流量次方，確認資料標示總流量或每米寬度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Derive the exponent from area and velocity and label total versus per-width discharge. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b257-v15-12","title":"總流量縮尺次方：失效診斷","titleEn":"Total-discharge scale exponent: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「總流量縮尺次方」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Total-discharge scale exponent” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把每米流量的次方用在總流量會差一個長度比例，低流量儀器超出校正範圍又會加深誤差。水面看似接近時，仍可能因錯誤流量造成錯誤能量與消能判讀。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using the unit-width exponent for total discharge introduces an entire length-scale error, compounded if the meter operates outside calibration. Similar-looking water levels can still conceal incorrect energy and dissipation because the delivered discharge is wrong. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設λL=40、原型總Q=1000m³/s，模型Qm=Qp/λL^(5/2)=0.09882m³/s；不是單位寬度流量比例。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Model Qm=Qp/λL^(5/2)=0.09882m³/s, distinct from unit-width discharge scaling.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「總流量與每米寬度流量在縮尺模型都使用同一比例次方。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Total discharge and discharge per unit width use the same scaling exponent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把每米流量的次方用在總流量會差一個長度比例，低流量儀器超出校正範圍又會加深誤差。水面看似接近時，仍可能因錯誤流量造成錯誤能量與消能判讀。","textEn":"Using the unit-width exponent for total discharge introduces an entire length-scale error, compounded if the meter operates outside calibration. Similar-looking water levels can still conceal incorrect energy and dissipation because the delivered discharge is wrong.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「總流量縮尺次方」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Total-discharge scale exponent\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把每米流量的次方用在總流量會差一個長度比例，低流量儀器超出校正範圍又會加深誤差。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要事後修改時間軸就能補救試驗時未縮尺的閥門動作。"],"optionsEn":["Using the unit-width exponent for total discharge introduces an entire length-scale error, compounded if the meter operates outside calibration.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Rescaling the recorded time axis repairs any valve motion that was not correctly scaled during the test."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把每米流量的次方用在總流量會差一個長度比例，低流量儀器超出校正範圍又會加深誤差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using the unit-width exponent for total discharge introduces an entire length-scale error, compounded if the meter operates outside calibration. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b257-v15-13","title":"時間縮尺與記錄：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Time scaling and recording: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「時間縮尺與記錄」如何影響水力模型縮尺試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Time scaling and recording” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Scale-model testing of hydraulic structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"重力模型的時間比例由長度除速度得到，原型漫長變化會在模型較短時間內發生。儀器取樣率、閥門運動與入流變化需同步配合，不能只縮放最後結果而保留原型的操作時間；資料對齊也應記錄起始事件，避免把時間偏移誤認為物理遲滯。 假設λL=40，原型事件120s，模型時間tm=120/√40=18.974s；只適用所選重力相似過程。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「時間縮尺與記錄」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Gravity-model time follows length divided by velocity, compressing long prototype changes into shorter experiments. Sampling, actuator movement and inflow variation must be synchronized accordingly, rather than scaling outputs while retaining prototype operating duration. Records also require a defined start event so clock offsets are not mistaken for physical lag in the measured hydraulic response. Assume length ratio40 and prototype duration120s. Model tm=120/√40=18.974s, applying only to the selected gravity-similar process. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Time scaling and recording” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要事後修改時間軸就能補救試驗時未縮尺的閥門動作。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Rescaling the recorded time axis repairs any valve motion that was not correctly scaled during the test.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「時間縮尺與記錄」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Time scaling and recording”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-13-k1","title":"時間縮尺與記錄","titleEn":"Time scaling and recording","text":"重力模型的時間比例由長度除速度得到，原型漫長變化會在模型較短時間內發生。儀器取樣率、閥門運動與入流變化需同步配合，不能只縮放最後結果而保留原型的操作時間；資料對齊也應記錄起始事件，避免把時間偏移誤認為物理遲滯。","textEn":"Gravity-model time follows length divided by velocity, compressing long prototype changes into shorter experiments. Sampling, actuator movement and inflow variation must be synchronized accordingly, rather than scaling outputs while retaining prototype operating duration.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要事後修改時間軸就能補救試驗時未縮尺的閥門動作。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Rescaling the recorded time axis repairs any valve motion that was not correctly scaled during the test. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「時間縮尺與記錄」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Time scaling and recording\" is correct?","options":["只要事後修改時間軸就能補救試驗時未縮尺的閥門動作。","重力模型的時間比例由長度除速度得到，原型漫長變化會在模型較短時間內發生。","重力壓力比例正確就表示空化與封閉氣泡壓縮也完全相似。"],"optionsEn":["Rescaling the recorded time axis repairs any valve motion that was not correctly scaled during the test.","Gravity-model time follows length divided by velocity, compressing long prototype changes into shorter experiments.","Correct gravity-pressure scaling proves that cavitation and trapped-air compression are also fully similar."],"answer":1,"explanation":"重力模型的時間比例由長度除速度得到，原型漫長變化會在模型較短時間內發生。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Gravity-model time follows length divided by velocity, compressing long prototype changes into shorter experiments. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b257-v15-14","title":"時間縮尺與記錄：定量估算","titleEn":"Time scaling and recording: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「時間縮尺與記錄」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Time scaling and recording” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設λL=40，原型事件120s，模型時間tm=120/√40=18.974s；只適用所選重力相似過程。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume length ratio40 and prototype duration120s. Model tm=120/√40=18.974s, applying only to the selected gravity-similar process. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把入流、閥位與量測通道放在共同時間軸，明列原型與模型的換算。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align inflow, valve position and sensor channels on a common clock and document both time scales.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設λL=40，原型事件120s，模型時間tm=120/√40=18.974s；只適用所選重力相似過程。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume length ratio40 and prototype duration120s. Model tm=120/√40=18.974s, applying only to the selected gravity-similar process.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「時間縮尺與記錄」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Time scaling and recording\", which statement holds?","options":["模型主流雷諾數高就可以證明每個細縫和近壁區都與原型相似。","模型讀值誤差很小所以換算回原型後可以完全忽略不計。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["A high main-flow Reynolds number proves similarity in every small gap and near-wall region.","A small model reading error can be ignored completely after conversion to prototype scale.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b257-v15-15","title":"時間縮尺與記錄：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Time scaling and recording: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「時間縮尺與記錄」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Time scaling and recording” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把入流、閥位與量測通道放在共同時間軸，明列原型與模型的換算。以可辨識水波事件校核時鐘和觸發延遲，檢查最快變化是否仍有足夠資料，不讓儀器更新頻率主導試驗結果。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align inflow, valve position and sensor channels on a common clock and document both time scales. Check triggers against an identifiable wave event and verify resolution of the fastest changes so instrument refresh limits do not govern the apparent experimental response. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把入流、閥位與量測通道放在共同時間軸，明列原型與模型的換算。以可辨識水波事件校核時鐘和觸發延遲，檢查最快變化是否仍有足夠資料，不讓儀器更新頻率主導試驗結果。","observationEn":"Site practice: Align inflow, valve position and sensor channels on a common clock and document both time scales. Check triggers against an identifiable wave event and verify resolution of the fastest changes so instrument refresh limits do not govern the apparent experimental response.","failure":"注意干擾：閥門動作沒有縮時會讓模型充水過慢，取樣頻率不足又會漏掉短峰值。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An unscaled actuator duration makes filling too slow, and sparse sampling misses short peaks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把入流、閥位與量測通道放在共同時間軸，明列原型與模型的換算。以可辨識水波事件校核時鐘和觸發延遲，檢查最快變化是否仍有足夠資料，不讓儀器更新頻率主導試驗結果。","textEn":"Align inflow, valve position and sensor channels on a common clock and document both time scales. Check triggers against an identifiable wave event and verify resolution of the fastest changes so instrument refresh limits do not govern the apparent experimental response.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把入流、閥位與量測通道放在共同時間軸，明列原型與模型的換算。以可辨識水波事件校核時鐘和觸發延遲，檢查最快變化是否仍有足夠資料，不讓儀器更新頻率主導試驗結果。","textEn":"Align inflow, valve position and sensor channels on a common clock and document both time scales. Check triggers against an identifiable wave event and verify resolution of the fastest changes so instrument refresh limits do not govern the apparent experimental response.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「時間縮尺與記錄」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Time scaling and recording\"?","options":["把入流、閥位與量測通道放在共同時間軸，明列原型與模型的換算。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要模型外觀像原型就可以忽略局部縫隙與尺度方向差異。"],"optionsEn":["Align inflow, valve position and sensor channels on a common clock and document both time scales.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Visual similarity alone permits ignoring gaps and differences between horizontal and vertical scales."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把入流、閥位與量測通道放在共同時間軸，明列原型與模型的換算。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align inflow, valve position and sensor channels on a common clock and document both time scales. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b257-v15-16","title":"時間縮尺與記錄：失效診斷","titleEn":"Time scaling and recording: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「時間縮尺與記錄」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Time scaling and recording” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"閥門動作沒有縮時會讓模型充水過慢，取樣頻率不足又會漏掉短峰值。事後把時間軸乘比例，不能補回試驗當時沒有正確重現的邊界變化。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An unscaled actuator duration makes filling too slow, and sparse sampling misses short peaks. Multiplying the time axis afterward cannot restore boundary changes that were not correctly reproduced while the physical experiment was running. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設λL=40，原型事件120s，模型時間tm=120/√40=18.974s；只適用所選重力相似過程。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Model tm=120/√40=18.974s, applying only to the selected gravity-similar process.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要事後修改時間軸就能補救試驗時未縮尺的閥門動作。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Rescaling the recorded time axis repairs any valve motion that was not correctly scaled during the test.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"閥門動作沒有縮時會讓模型充水過慢，取樣頻率不足又會漏掉短峰值。事後把時間軸乘比例，不能補回試驗當時沒有正確重現的邊界變化。","textEn":"An unscaled actuator duration makes filling too slow, and sparse sampling misses short peaks. Multiplying the time axis afterward cannot restore boundary changes that were not correctly reproduced while the physical experiment was running.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「時間縮尺與記錄」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Time scaling and recording\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","閥門動作沒有縮時會讓模型充水過慢，取樣頻率不足又會漏掉短峰值。","重力壓力比例正確就表示空化與封閉氣泡壓縮也完全相似。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","An unscaled actuator duration makes filling too slow, and sparse sampling misses short peaks.","Correct gravity-pressure scaling proves that cavitation and trapped-air compression are also fully similar."],"answer":1,"explanation":"閥門動作沒有縮時會讓模型充水過慢，取樣頻率不足又會漏掉短峰值。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An unscaled actuator duration makes filling too slow, and sparse sampling misses short peaks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b257-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「壓力尺度與氣泡」與「合力尺度與量測」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pressure scale and air effects\" and \"Force scaling and measurement\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b257-v15-17","title":"壓力尺度與氣泡：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pressure scale and air effects: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「壓力尺度與氣泡」如何影響水力模型縮尺試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pressure scale and air effects” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Scale-model testing of hydraulic structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"相同液體密度與重力下，重力壓力尺度隨長度比例改變，但絕對氣壓不會自動跟著縮小。模型氣泡、負壓和空化可能因此偏離原型，尤其局部高速與衝擊區；靜水或重力動壓的可放大性不能被解釋成所有瞬態壓力都相似。 假設λL=40、同密度重力壓力原型60kPa，模型壓力1.50kPa；此為表壓重力尺度，不代表絕對氣壓也縮四十倍。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壓力尺度與氣泡」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"At matched liquid density and gravity, gravity-pressure scale follows length, but ambient absolute pressure does not automatically scale. Air bubbles, suction and cavitation can therefore differ from the prototype, especially in high-speed or impact regions. Scaling hydrostatic or gravity-dominated pressure does not establish similarity of every transient pressure mechanism within the same apparatus. Assume length ratio40 and matched density. Prototype gravity gauge pressure60kPa scales to1.50kPa, without scaling ambient absolute air pressure fortyfold. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pressure scale and air effects” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「重力壓力比例正確就表示空化與封閉氣泡壓縮也完全相似。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Correct gravity-pressure scaling proves that cavitation and trapped-air compression are also fully similar.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「壓力尺度與氣泡」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pressure scale and air effects”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-17-k1","title":"壓力尺度與氣泡","titleEn":"Pressure scale and air effects","text":"相同液體密度與重力下，重力壓力尺度隨長度比例改變，但絕對氣壓不會自動跟著縮小。模型氣泡、負壓和空化可能因此偏離原型，尤其局部高速與衝擊區；靜水或重力動壓的可放大性不能被解釋成所有瞬態壓力都相似。","textEn":"At matched liquid density and gravity, gravity-pressure scale follows length, but ambient absolute pressure does not automatically scale. Air bubbles, suction and cavitation can therefore differ from the prototype, especially in high-speed or impact regions.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：重力壓力比例正確就表示空化與封閉氣泡壓縮也完全相似。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Correct gravity-pressure scaling proves that cavitation and trapped-air compression are also fully similar. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壓力尺度與氣泡」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pressure scale and air effects\" is correct?","options":["重力壓力比例正確就表示空化與封閉氣泡壓縮也完全相似。","縮尺合力只需要跟長度成正比而不必考慮受壓面積。","相同液體密度與重力下，重力壓力尺度隨長度比例改變，但絕對氣壓不會自動跟著縮小。"],"optionsEn":["Correct gravity-pressure scaling proves that cavitation and trapped-air compression are also fully similar.","Model force scales only linearly with length and does not depend on loaded area.","At matched liquid density and gravity, gravity-pressure scale follows length, but ambient absolute pressure does not automatically scale."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相同液體密度與重力下，重力壓力尺度隨長度比例改變，但絕對氣壓不會自動跟著縮小。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"At matched liquid density and gravity, gravity-pressure scale follows length, but ambient absolute pressure does not automatically scale. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b257-v15-18","title":"壓力尺度與氣泡：定量估算","titleEn":"Pressure scale and air effects: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「壓力尺度與氣泡」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pressure scale and air effects” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設λL=40、同密度重力壓力原型60kPa，模型壓力1.50kPa；此為表壓重力尺度，不代表絕對氣壓也縮四十倍。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume length ratio40 and matched density. Prototype gravity gauge pressure60kPa scales to1.50kPa, without scaling ambient absolute air pressure fortyfold. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：記錄壓力是表壓或絕對壓力並核對零點，區分慢變重力壓與短時衝擊。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Label gauge versus absolute pressure and verify zero, separating slow gravity loading from brief impact.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設λL=40、同密度重力壓力原型60kPa，模型壓力1.50kPa；此為表壓重力尺度，不代表絕對氣壓也縮四十倍。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume length ratio40 and matched density. Prototype gravity gauge pressure60kPa scales to1.50kPa, without scaling ambient absolute air pressure fortyfold.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「壓力尺度與氣泡」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pressure scale and air effects\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","重力相似已經自動保證液滴尺寸與曝氣程度都能直接放大。","重複三次結果很接近就代表所有未測工況與系統偏差都已驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Gravity similarity automatically makes droplet size and air entrainment directly scalable.","Three closely agreeing repeats validate every untested condition and eliminate systematic bias."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b257-v15-19","title":"壓力尺度與氣泡：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pressure scale and air effects: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「壓力尺度與氣泡」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pressure scale and air effects” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"記錄壓力是表壓或絕對壓力並核對零點，區分慢變重力壓與短時衝擊。觀察氣泡和通氣路徑，將空化相關區域單獨標註，必要時以不同尺度或專門裝置檢驗未相似的機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Label gauge versus absolute pressure and verify zero, separating slow gravity loading from brief impact. Observe bubbles and ventilation paths, flag cavitation-sensitive regions and use alternative scales or specialized facilities where needed to examine mechanisms not represented by the chosen similitude. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：記錄壓力是表壓或絕對壓力並核對零點，區分慢變重力壓與短時衝擊。觀察氣泡和通氣路徑，將空化相關區域單獨標註，必要時以不同尺度或專門裝置檢驗未相似的機制。","observationEn":"Site practice: Label gauge versus absolute pressure and verify zero, separating slow gravity loading from brief impact. Observe bubbles and ventilation paths, flag cavitation-sensitive regions and use alternative scales or specialized facilities where needed to examine mechanisms not represented by the chosen similitude.","failure":"注意干擾：封閉空氣團的壓縮在模型可能比原型更顯著，直接放大尖峰會誤判結構荷載。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Trapped-air compression can be disproportionately important in the model, making direct scaling of peaks misleading. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"記錄壓力是表壓或絕對壓力並核對零點，區分慢變重力壓與短時衝擊。觀察氣泡和通氣路徑，將空化相關區域單獨標註，必要時以不同尺度或專門裝置檢驗未相似的機制。","textEn":"Label gauge versus absolute pressure and verify zero, separating slow gravity loading from brief impact. Observe bubbles and ventilation paths, flag cavitation-sensitive regions and use alternative scales or specialized facilities where needed to examine mechanisms not represented by the chosen similitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"記錄壓力是表壓或絕對壓力並核對零點，區分慢變重力壓與短時衝擊。觀察氣泡和通氣路徑，將空化相關區域單獨標註，必要時以不同尺度或專門裝置檢驗未相似的機制。","textEn":"Label gauge versus absolute pressure and verify zero, separating slow gravity loading from brief impact. Observe bubbles and ventilation paths, flag cavitation-sensitive regions and use alternative scales or specialized facilities where needed to examine mechanisms not represented by the chosen similitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「壓力尺度與氣泡」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pressure scale and air effects\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","記錄壓力是表壓或絕對壓力並核對零點，區分慢變重力壓與短時衝擊。","佛祿相似要求速度與模型長度使用完全相同的縮小倍數。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Label gauge versus absolute pressure and verify zero, separating slow gravity loading from brief impact.","Froude similarity requires velocity to use exactly the same reduction factor as length."],"answer":1,"explanation":"記錄壓力是表壓或絕對壓力並核對零點，區分慢變重力壓與短時衝擊。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Label gauge versus absolute pressure and verify zero, separating slow gravity loading from brief impact. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b257-v15-20","title":"壓力尺度與氣泡：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pressure scale and air effects: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「壓力尺度與氣泡」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pressure scale and air effects” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"封閉空氣團的壓縮在模型可能比原型更顯著，直接放大尖峰會誤判結構荷載。把表壓負值當成低於蒸氣壓，亦會在沒有絕對壓力基準時錯判空化。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Trapped-air compression can be disproportionately important in the model, making direct scaling of peaks misleading. A negative gauge reading also cannot establish pressure below vapor pressure without the corresponding absolute-pressure reference. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設λL=40、同密度重力壓力原型60kPa，模型壓力1.50kPa；此為表壓重力尺度，不代表絕對氣壓也縮四十倍。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Prototype gravity gauge pressure60kPa scales to1.50kPa, without scaling ambient absolute air pressure fortyfold.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「重力壓力比例正確就表示空化與封閉氣泡壓縮也完全相似。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Correct gravity-pressure scaling proves that cavitation and trapped-air compression are also fully similar.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"封閉空氣團的壓縮在模型可能比原型更顯著，直接放大尖峰會誤判結構荷載。把表壓負值當成低於蒸氣壓，亦會在沒有絕對壓力基準時錯判空化。","textEn":"Trapped-air compression can be disproportionately important in the model, making direct scaling of peaks misleading. A negative gauge reading also cannot establish pressure below vapor pressure without the corresponding absolute-pressure reference.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「壓力尺度與氣泡」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pressure scale and air effects\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","縮尺合力只需要跟長度成正比而不必考慮受壓面積。","封閉空氣團的壓縮在模型可能比原型更顯著，直接放大尖峰會誤判結構荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Model force scales only linearly with length and does not depend on loaded area.","Trapped-air compression can be disproportionately important in the model, making direct scaling of peaks misleading."],"answer":2,"explanation":"封閉空氣團的壓縮在模型可能比原型更顯著，直接放大尖峰會誤判結構荷載。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Trapped-air compression can be disproportionately important in the model, making direct scaling of peaks misleading. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b257-v15-21","title":"合力尺度與量測：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Force scaling and measurement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「合力尺度與量測」如何影響水力模型縮尺試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Force scaling and measurement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Scale-model testing of hydraulic structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"壓力積分成合力時還要乘面積，所以同密度重力模型的力比例是長度三次方。量測裝置的剛度、頻率和支架阻流可能改變原本流場，模型力很小時摩擦和纜線也可能重要；不能僅因荷重元件讀值穩定就認為力傳遞已被完整量到。 假設λL=40、原型重力主導合力2MN，模型Fm=2000000/40³=31.25N；未處理感測器動態或氣泡衝擊。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「合力尺度與量測」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Integrating pressure over area gives a cubic length scale for force under matched-density gravity similarity. Sensor stiffness, natural frequency and support blockage can alter the flow, and friction or cables become significant when model forces are small. Stable readings alone do not establish that the complete intended load path reaches the calibrated measuring device. Assume length ratio40 and prototype gravity-dominated force2MN. Model Fm=2000000/40³=31.25N, excluding sensor dynamics and air-impact scaling. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Force scaling and measurement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「縮尺合力只需要跟長度成正比而不必考慮受壓面積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Model force scales only linearly with length and does not depend on loaded area.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「合力尺度與量測」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Force scaling and measurement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-21-k1","title":"合力尺度與量測","titleEn":"Force scaling and measurement","text":"壓力積分成合力時還要乘面積，所以同密度重力模型的力比例是長度三次方。量測裝置的剛度、頻率和支架阻流可能改變原本流場，模型力很小時摩擦和纜線也可能重要；不能僅因荷重元件讀值穩定就認為力傳遞已被完整量到。","textEn":"Integrating pressure over area gives a cubic length scale for force under matched-density gravity similarity. Sensor stiffness, natural frequency and support blockage can alter the flow, and friction or cables become significant when model forces are small.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：縮尺合力只需要跟長度成正比而不必考慮受壓面積。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Model force scales only linearly with length and does not depend on loaded area. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「合力尺度與量測」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Force scaling and measurement\" is correct?","options":["壓力積分成合力時還要乘面積，所以同密度重力模型的力比例是長度三次方。","縮尺合力只需要跟長度成正比而不必考慮受壓面積。","模型主流雷諾數高就可以證明每個細縫和近壁區都與原型相似。"],"optionsEn":["Integrating pressure over area gives a cubic length scale for force under matched-density gravity similarity.","Model force scales only linearly with length and does not depend on loaded area.","A high main-flow Reynolds number proves similarity in every small gap and near-wall region."],"answer":0,"explanation":"壓力積分成合力時還要乘面積，所以同密度重力模型的力比例是長度三次方。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Integrating pressure over area gives a cubic length scale for force under matched-density gravity similarity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b257-v15-22","title":"合力尺度與量測：定量估算","titleEn":"Force scaling and measurement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「合力尺度與量測」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Force scaling and measurement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設λL=40、原型重力主導合力2MN，模型Fm=2000000/40³=31.25N；未處理感測器動態或氣泡衝擊。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume length ratio40 and prototype gravity-dominated force2MN. Model Fm=2000000/40³=31.25N, excluding sensor dynamics and air-impact scaling. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以已知方向和位置的砝碼校核整套力傳遞路徑，記錄支架自振頻率及零漂。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Calibrate the full load path using known weights and positions, recording support frequency and zero drift.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設λL=40、原型重力主導合力2MN，模型Fm=2000000/40³=31.25N；未處理感測器動態或氣泡衝擊。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume length ratio40 and prototype gravity-dominated force2MN. Model Fm=2000000/40³=31.25N, excluding sensor dynamics and air-impact scaling.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「合力尺度與量測」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Force scaling and measurement\", which statement holds?","options":["模型讀值誤差很小所以換算回原型後可以完全忽略不計。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","只要模型外觀像原型就可以忽略局部縫隙與尺度方向差異。"],"optionsEn":["A small model reading error can be ignored completely after conversion to prototype scale.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Visual similarity alone permits ignoring gaps and differences between horizontal and vertical scales."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b257-v15-23","title":"合力尺度與量測：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Force scaling and measurement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「合力尺度與量測」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Force scaling and measurement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以已知方向和位置的砝碼校核整套力傳遞路徑，記錄支架自振頻率及零漂。比較壓力積分與總力感測器結果，檢查水流是否繞過或推到未量測的支架，不只校正單顆感測元件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Calibrate the full load path using known weights and positions, recording support frequency and zero drift. Compare integrated pressure with measured resultant and check whether water loads bypass the sensor or act on unmeasured supports rather than calibrating only the isolated transducer. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以已知方向和位置的砝碼校核整套力傳遞路徑，記錄支架自振頻率及零漂。比較壓力積分與總力感測器結果，檢查水流是否繞過或推到未量測的支架，不只校正單顆感測元件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calibrate the full load path using known weights and positions, recording support frequency and zero drift. Compare integrated pressure with measured resultant and check whether water loads bypass the sensor or act on unmeasured supports rather than calibrating only the isolated transducer.","failure":"注意干擾：支架摩擦可能承擔部分荷重，使感測器低估；共振則可能放大短峰值。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Support friction can carry load away from the sensor, while resonance amplifies short peaks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以已知方向和位置的砝碼校核整套力傳遞路徑，記錄支架自振頻率及零漂。比較壓力積分與總力感測器結果，檢查水流是否繞過或推到未量測的支架，不只校正單顆感測元件。","textEn":"Calibrate the full load path using known weights and positions, recording support frequency and zero drift. Compare integrated pressure with measured resultant and check whether water loads bypass the sensor or act on unmeasured supports rather than calibrating only the isolated transducer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以已知方向和位置的砝碼校核整套力傳遞路徑，記錄支架自振頻率及零漂。比較壓力積分與總力感測器結果，檢查水流是否繞過或推到未量測的支架，不只校正單顆感測元件。","textEn":"Calibrate the full load path using known weights and positions, recording support frequency and zero drift. Compare integrated pressure with measured resultant and check whether water loads bypass the sensor or act on unmeasured supports rather than calibrating only the isolated transducer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「合力尺度與量測」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Force scaling and measurement\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","總流量與每米寬度流量在縮尺模型都使用同一比例次方。","以已知方向和位置的砝碼校核整套力傳遞路徑，記錄支架自振頻率及零漂。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Total discharge and discharge per unit width use the same scaling exponent.","Calibrate the full load path using known weights and positions, recording support frequency and zero drift."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以已知方向和位置的砝碼校核整套力傳遞路徑，記錄支架自振頻率及零漂。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Calibrate the full load path using known weights and positions, recording support frequency and zero drift. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b257-v15-24","title":"合力尺度與量測：失效診斷","titleEn":"Force scaling and measurement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「合力尺度與量測」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Force scaling and measurement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"支架摩擦可能承擔部分荷重，使感測器低估；共振則可能放大短峰值。兩種偏差都能在靜態校正看似良好時出現，必須查核水中實際動態條件。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Support friction can carry load away from the sensor, while resonance amplifies short peaks. Both errors can occur despite satisfactory static calibration and require examination under the actual submerged dynamic conditions of the experiment. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設λL=40、原型重力主導合力2MN，模型Fm=2000000/40³=31.25N；未處理感測器動態或氣泡衝擊。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Model Fm=2000000/40³=31.25N, excluding sensor dynamics and air-impact scaling.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「縮尺合力只需要跟長度成正比而不必考慮受壓面積。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Model force scales only linearly with length and does not depend on loaded area.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"支架摩擦可能承擔部分荷重，使感測器低估；共振則可能放大短峰值。兩種偏差都能在靜態校正看似良好時出現，必須查核水中實際動態條件。","textEn":"Support friction can carry load away from the sensor, while resonance amplifies short peaks. Both errors can occur despite satisfactory static calibration and require examination under the actual submerged dynamic conditions of the experiment.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「合力尺度與量測」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Force scaling and measurement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["支架摩擦可能承擔部分荷重，使感測器低估；共振則可能放大短峰值。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","模型主流雷諾數高就可以證明每個細縫和近壁區都與原型相似。"],"optionsEn":["Support friction can carry load away from the sensor, while resonance amplifies short peaks.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A high main-flow Reynolds number proves similarity in every small gap and near-wall region."],"answer":0,"explanation":"支架摩擦可能承擔部分荷重，使感測器低估；共振則可能放大短峰值。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Support friction can carry load away from the sensor, while resonance amplifies short peaks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b257-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「雷諾數與黏滯失真」與「韋伯數與表面張力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Reynolds number and viscous distortion\" and \"Weber number and surface tension\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b257-v15-25","title":"雷諾數與黏滯失真：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Reynolds number and viscous distortion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「雷諾數與黏滯失真」如何影響水力模型縮尺試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Reynolds number and viscous distortion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Scale-model testing of hydraulic structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"使用同一水體且採佛祿相似時，模型速度和長度都變小，雷諾數不能同時保持。主要流區可能仍是紊流，但薄水層、近壁與小縫可能受黏滯控制；不能用一個全域雷諾數宣稱所有局部現象相似，應檢查尺寸改變後結果是否穩定。 假設ν=10⁻⁶m²/s，以水深為控制長度，模型V=8/√40m/s、h=0.20m，Re≈252982；原型V=8m/s、h=8m，Re=64000000。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「雷諾數與黏滯失真」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"With the same fluid under Froude similarity, both velocity and length decrease, so Reynolds number is not preserved. Main flow may remain turbulent while thin layers, walls and gaps become viscosity-sensitive. One global Reynolds number cannot qualify every local phenomenon; comparing more than one scale helps determine whether the measured result depends on the altered viscous regime. Assumeν=10⁻⁶m²/s, using depth as the reference length. Model V=8/√40m/s,h=0.20m gives Re≈252982; prototype V=8m/s,h=8m gives Re=64000000. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Reynolds number and viscous distortion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「模型主流雷諾數高就可以證明每個細縫和近壁區都與原型相似。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A high main-flow Reynolds number proves similarity in every small gap and near-wall region.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「雷諾數與黏滯失真」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Reynolds number and viscous distortion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-25-k1","title":"雷諾數與黏滯失真","titleEn":"Reynolds number and viscous distortion","text":"使用同一水體且採佛祿相似時，模型速度和長度都變小，雷諾數不能同時保持。主要流區可能仍是紊流，但薄水層、近壁與小縫可能受黏滯控制；不能用一個全域雷諾數宣稱所有局部現象相似，應檢查尺寸改變後結果是否穩定。","textEn":"With the same fluid under Froude similarity, both velocity and length decrease, so Reynolds number is not preserved. Main flow may remain turbulent while thin layers, walls and gaps become viscosity-sensitive.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模型主流雷諾數高就可以證明每個細縫和近壁區都與原型相似。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A high main-flow Reynolds number proves similarity in every small gap and near-wall region. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「雷諾數與黏滯失真」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Reynolds number and viscous distortion\" is correct?","options":["模型主流雷諾數高就可以證明每個細縫和近壁區都與原型相似。","使用同一水體且採佛祿相似時，模型速度和長度都變小，雷諾數不能同時保持。","重力相似已經自動保證液滴尺寸與曝氣程度都能直接放大。"],"optionsEn":["A high main-flow Reynolds number proves similarity in every small gap and near-wall region.","With the same fluid under Froude similarity, both velocity and length decrease, so Reynolds number is not preserved.","Gravity similarity automatically makes droplet size and air entrainment directly scalable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"使用同一水體且採佛祿相似時，模型速度和長度都變小，雷諾數不能同時保持。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"With the same fluid under Froude similarity, both velocity and length decrease, so Reynolds number is not preserved. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b257-v15-26","title":"雷諾數與黏滯失真：定量估算","titleEn":"Reynolds number and viscous distortion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雷諾數與黏滯失真」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Reynolds number and viscous distortion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設ν=10⁻⁶m²/s，以水深為控制長度，模型V=8/√40m/s、h=0.20m，Re≈252982；原型V=8m/s、h=8m，Re=64000000。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assumeν=10⁻⁶m²/s, using depth as the reference length. Model V=8/√40m/s,h=0.20m gives Re≈252982; prototype V=8m/s,h=8m gives Re=64000000. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用真正控制局部現象的長度估雷諾數，記錄水溫對黏度的影響，不能只選最大池寬。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Estimate Reynolds number using lengths controlling the local mechanism and record temperature-dependent viscosity rather than automatically choosing maximum basin width.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設ν=10⁻⁶m²/s，以水深為控制長度，模型V=8/√40m/s、h=0.20m，Re≈252982；原型V=8m/s、h=8m，Re=64000000。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assumeν=10⁻⁶m²/s, using depth as the reference length. Model V=8/√40m/s,h=0.20m gives Re≈252982; prototype V=8m/s,h=8m gives Re=64000000.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「雷諾數與黏滯失真」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Reynolds number and viscous distortion\", which statement holds?","options":["重複三次結果很接近就代表所有未測工況與系統偏差都已驗證。","佛祿相似要求速度與模型長度使用完全相同的縮小倍數。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Three closely agreeing repeats validate every untested condition and eliminate systematic bias.","Froude similarity requires velocity to use exactly the same reduction factor as length.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b257-v15-27","title":"雷諾數與黏滯失真：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Reynolds number and viscous distortion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「雷諾數與黏滯失真」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Reynolds number and viscous distortion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用真正控制局部現象的長度估雷諾數，記錄水溫對黏度的影響，不能只選最大池寬。比較至少兩尺度的壓損、分離或薄層行為，保留不能可靠外推的區域與觀察量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Estimate Reynolds number using lengths controlling the local mechanism and record temperature-dependent viscosity rather than automatically choosing maximum basin width. Compare losses, separation or thin layers at multiple scales and retain explicit limits for quantities that cannot be reliably extrapolated. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用真正控制局部現象的長度估雷諾數，記錄水溫對黏度的影響，不能只選最大池寬。比較至少兩尺度的壓損、分離或薄層行為，保留不能可靠外推的區域與觀察量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Estimate Reynolds number using lengths controlling the local mechanism and record temperature-dependent viscosity rather than automatically choosing maximum basin width. Compare losses, separation or thin layers at multiple scales and retain explicit limits for quantities that cannot be reliably extrapolated.","failure":"注意干擾：大水槽的全域雷諾數很高仍可能有層流閘縫，若把局部漏流按紊流比例放大，會算錯。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A high basin-scale Reynolds number can coexist with a laminar gate gap, invalidating turbulent leakage scaling. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用真正控制局部現象的長度估雷諾數，記錄水溫對黏度的影響，不能只選最大池寬。比較至少兩尺度的壓損、分離或薄層行為，保留不能可靠外推的區域與觀察量。","textEn":"Estimate Reynolds number using lengths controlling the local mechanism and record temperature-dependent viscosity rather than automatically choosing maximum basin width. Compare losses, separation or thin layers at multiple scales and retain explicit limits for quantities that cannot be reliably extrapolated.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用真正控制局部現象的長度估雷諾數，記錄水溫對黏度的影響，不能只選最大池寬。比較至少兩尺度的壓損、分離或薄層行為，保留不能可靠外推的區域與觀察量。","textEn":"Estimate Reynolds number using lengths controlling the local mechanism and record temperature-dependent viscosity rather than automatically choosing maximum basin width. Compare losses, separation or thin layers at multiple scales and retain explicit limits for quantities that cannot be reliably extrapolated.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「雷諾數與黏滯失真」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Reynolds number and viscous distortion\"?","options":["用真正控制局部現象的長度估雷諾數，記錄水溫對黏度的影響，不能只選最大池寬。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要事後修改時間軸就能補救試驗時未縮尺的閥門動作。"],"optionsEn":["Estimate Reynolds number using lengths controlling the local mechanism and record temperature-dependent viscosity rather than automatically choosing maximum basin width.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Rescaling the recorded time axis repairs any valve motion that was not correctly scaled during the test."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用真正控制局部現象的長度估雷諾數，記錄水溫對黏度的影響，不能只選最大池寬。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Estimate Reynolds number using lengths controlling the local mechanism and record temperature-dependent viscosity rather than automatically choosing maximum basin width. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b257-v15-28","title":"雷諾數與黏滯失真：失效診斷","titleEn":"Reynolds number and viscous distortion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雷諾數與黏滯失真」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Reynolds number and viscous distortion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"大水槽的全域雷諾數很高仍可能有層流閘縫，若把局部漏流按紊流比例放大，會算錯。溫度變化又可能在同一模型內改變黏度，使重複試驗不完全可比。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A high basin-scale Reynolds number can coexist with a laminar gate gap, invalidating turbulent leakage scaling. Water-temperature changes also alter viscosity between repeated tests, so nominally identical geometry and discharge need not give directly comparable local behavior. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設ν=10⁻⁶m²/s，以水深為控制長度，模型V=8/√40m/s、h=0.20m，Re≈252982；原型V=8m/s、h=8m，Re=64000000。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Model V=8/√40m/s,h=0.20m gives Re≈252982; prototype V=8m/s,h=8m gives Re=64000000.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模型主流雷諾數高就可以證明每個細縫和近壁區都與原型相似。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A high main-flow Reynolds number proves similarity in every small gap and near-wall region.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"大水槽的全域雷諾數很高仍可能有層流閘縫，若把局部漏流按紊流比例放大，會算錯。溫度變化又可能在同一模型內改變黏度，使重複試驗不完全可比。","textEn":"A high basin-scale Reynolds number can coexist with a laminar gate gap, invalidating turbulent leakage scaling. Water-temperature changes also alter viscosity between repeated tests, so nominally identical geometry and discharge need not give directly comparable local behavior.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雷諾數與黏滯失真」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Reynolds number and viscous distortion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","大水槽的全域雷諾數很高仍可能有層流閘縫，若把局部漏流按紊流比例放大，會算錯。","重力相似已經自動保證液滴尺寸與曝氣程度都能直接放大。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A high basin-scale Reynolds number can coexist with a laminar gate gap, invalidating turbulent leakage scaling.","Gravity similarity automatically makes droplet size and air entrainment directly scalable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"大水槽的全域雷諾數很高仍可能有層流閘縫，若把局部漏流按紊流比例放大，會算錯。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A high basin-scale Reynolds number can coexist with a laminar gate gap, invalidating turbulent leakage scaling. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b257-v15-29","title":"韋伯數與表面張力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Weber number and surface tension: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「韋伯數與表面張力」如何影響水力模型縮尺試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Weber number and surface tension” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Scale-model testing of hydraulic structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"表面張力對小尺度水舌、液滴與薄膜相對重要，重力縮尺通常不會保留慣性與表面張力之比。模型看見的破碎、噴濺或氣泡大小可能因此失真，不能以外觀照片當定量證據；若研究問題正是這些現象，需要另選尺度或承認觀察僅能定性。 假設ρ=1000kg/m³、σ=0.072N/m、模型V²=1.6m²/s²、L=0.20m，We=ρV²L/σ=4444.4；原型值是其1600倍。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「韋伯數與表面張力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Surface tension matters disproportionately for small jets, drops and films, and gravity scaling generally does not preserve its ratio to inertia. Breakup, spray and bubble size can therefore be distorted, making photographs insufficient quantitative evidence. If these phenomena are the study objective, a different scale or explicit qualitative limitation is needed rather than assuming visual similarity guarantees the physics. Assumeρ=1000kg/m³,σ=0.072N/m,model V²=1.6m²/s² and L=0.20m. We=4444.4; the corresponding prototype value is1600times larger. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Weber number and surface tension” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「重力相似已經自動保證液滴尺寸與曝氣程度都能直接放大。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Gravity similarity automatically makes droplet size and air entrainment directly scalable.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「韋伯數與表面張力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Weber number and surface tension”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-29-k1","title":"韋伯數與表面張力","titleEn":"Weber number and surface tension","text":"表面張力對小尺度水舌、液滴與薄膜相對重要，重力縮尺通常不會保留慣性與表面張力之比。模型看見的破碎、噴濺或氣泡大小可能因此失真，不能以外觀照片當定量證據；若研究問題正是這些現象，需要另選尺度或承認觀察僅能定性。","textEn":"Surface tension matters disproportionately for small jets, drops and films, and gravity scaling generally does not preserve its ratio to inertia. Breakup, spray and bubble size can therefore be distorted, making photographs insufficient quantitative evidence.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：重力相似已經自動保證液滴尺寸與曝氣程度都能直接放大。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Gravity similarity automatically makes droplet size and air entrainment directly scalable. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「韋伯數與表面張力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Weber number and surface tension\" is correct?","options":["重力相似已經自動保證液滴尺寸與曝氣程度都能直接放大。","模型讀值誤差很小所以換算回原型後可以完全忽略不計。","表面張力對小尺度水舌、液滴與薄膜相對重要，重力縮尺通常不會保留慣性與表面張力之比。"],"optionsEn":["Gravity similarity automatically makes droplet size and air entrainment directly scalable.","A small model reading error can be ignored completely after conversion to prototype scale.","Surface tension matters disproportionately for small jets, drops and films, and gravity scaling generally does not preserve its ratio to inertia."],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面張力對小尺度水舌、液滴與薄膜相對重要，重力縮尺通常不會保留慣性與表面張力之比。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Surface tension matters disproportionately for small jets, drops and films, and gravity scaling generally does not preserve its ratio to inertia. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b257-v15-30","title":"韋伯數與表面張力：定量估算","titleEn":"Weber number and surface tension: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「韋伯數與表面張力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Weber number and surface tension” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設ρ=1000kg/m³、σ=0.072N/m、模型V²=1.6m²/s²、L=0.20m，We=ρV²L/σ=4444.4；原型值是其1600倍。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assumeρ=1000kg/m³,σ=0.072N/m,model V²=1.6m²/s² and L=0.20m. We=4444.4; the corresponding prototype value is1600times larger. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先指定表面張力影響的局部長度，記錄水質、溫度及表面污染，查核材料是否改變潤濕。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Define the local length relevant to surface tension and record temperature, water condition and contamination, checking altered wetting on model materials.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設ρ=1000kg/m³、σ=0.072N/m、模型V²=1.6m²/s²、L=0.20m，We=ρV²L/σ=4444.4；原型值是其1600倍。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assumeρ=1000kg/m³,σ=0.072N/m,model V²=1.6m²/s² and L=0.20m. We=4444.4; the corresponding prototype value is1600times larger.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「韋伯數與表面張力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Weber number and surface tension\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","只要模型外觀像原型就可以忽略局部縫隙與尺度方向差異。","總流量與每米寬度流量在縮尺模型都使用同一比例次方。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Visual similarity alone permits ignoring gaps and differences between horizontal and vertical scales.","Total discharge and discharge per unit width use the same scaling exponent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b257-v15-31","title":"韋伯數與表面張力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Weber number and surface tension: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「韋伯數與表面張力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Weber number and surface tension” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先指定表面張力影響的局部長度，記錄水質、溫度及表面污染，查核材料是否改變潤濕。比較不同尺度水舌破裂和噴濺，將可量化水位與只宜定性解讀的液滴外觀分開。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Define the local length relevant to surface tension and record temperature, water condition and contamination, checking altered wetting on model materials. Compare jet breakup and spray across scales, separating quantitatively useful levels from droplet appearances that support only qualitative interpretation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：先指定表面張力影響的局部長度，記錄水質、溫度及表面污染，查核材料是否改變潤濕。比較不同尺度水舌破裂和噴濺，將可量化水位與只宜定性解讀的液滴外觀分開。","observationEn":"Site practice: Define the local length relevant to surface tension and record temperature, water condition and contamination, checking altered wetting on model materials. Compare jet breakup and spray across scales, separating quantitatively useful levels from droplet appearances that support only qualitative interpretation.","failure":"注意干擾：模型小液滴可能被表面張力束縛，原型卻更易破碎，直接按照片估曝氣會偏差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Small model droplets can remain surface-tension-bound where prototype flow breaks up, biasing air-entrainment estimates from imagery. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先指定表面張力影響的局部長度，記錄水質、溫度及表面污染，查核材料是否改變潤濕。比較不同尺度水舌破裂和噴濺，將可量化水位與只宜定性解讀的液滴外觀分開。","textEn":"Define the local length relevant to surface tension and record temperature, water condition and contamination, checking altered wetting on model materials. Compare jet breakup and spray across scales, separating quantitatively useful levels from droplet appearances that support only qualitative interpretation.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"先指定表面張力影響的局部長度，記錄水質、溫度及表面污染，查核材料是否改變潤濕。比較不同尺度水舌破裂和噴濺，將可量化水位與只宜定性解讀的液滴外觀分開。","textEn":"Define the local length relevant to surface tension and record temperature, water condition and contamination, checking altered wetting on model materials. Compare jet breakup and spray across scales, separating quantitatively useful levels from droplet appearances that support only qualitative interpretation.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「韋伯數與表面張力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Weber number and surface tension\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","先指定表面張力影響的局部長度，記錄水質、溫度及表面污染，查核材料是否改變潤濕。","重力壓力比例正確就表示空化與封閉氣泡壓縮也完全相似。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Define the local length relevant to surface tension and record temperature, water condition and contamination, checking altered wetting on model materials.","Correct gravity-pressure scaling proves that cavitation and trapped-air compression are also fully similar."],"answer":1,"explanation":"先指定表面張力影響的局部長度，記錄水質、溫度及表面污染，查核材料是否改變潤濕。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Define the local length relevant to surface tension and record temperature, water condition and contamination, checking altered wetting on model materials. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b257-v15-32","title":"韋伯數與表面張力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Weber number and surface tension: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「韋伯數與表面張力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Weber number and surface tension” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"模型小液滴可能被表面張力束縛，原型卻更易破碎，直接按照片估曝氣會偏差。加入界面活性物質改變張力時，也可能連帶改變氣泡與量測條件，不能當簡單修補。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Small model droplets can remain surface-tension-bound where prototype flow breaks up, biasing air-entrainment estimates from imagery. Surfactant adjustments also change bubbles and measurement conditions and cannot be treated as an uncomplicated correction to all scale effects. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設ρ=1000kg/m³、σ=0.072N/m、模型V²=1.6m²/s²、L=0.20m，We=ρV²L/σ=4444.4；原型值是其1600倍。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: We=4444.4; the corresponding prototype value is1600times larger.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「重力相似已經自動保證液滴尺寸與曝氣程度都能直接放大。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Gravity similarity automatically makes droplet size and air entrainment directly scalable.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"模型小液滴可能被表面張力束縛，原型卻更易破碎，直接按照片估曝氣會偏差。加入界面活性物質改變張力時，也可能連帶改變氣泡與量測條件，不能當簡單修補。","textEn":"Small model droplets can remain surface-tension-bound where prototype flow breaks up, biasing air-entrainment estimates from imagery. Surfactant adjustments also change bubbles and measurement conditions and cannot be treated as an uncomplicated correction to all scale effects.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「韋伯數與表面張力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Weber number and surface tension\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","模型讀值誤差很小所以換算回原型後可以完全忽略不計。","模型小液滴可能被表面張力束縛，原型卻更易破碎，直接按照片估曝氣會偏差。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A small model reading error can be ignored completely after conversion to prototype scale.","Small model droplets can remain surface-tension-bound where prototype flow breaks up, biasing air-entrainment estimates from imagery."],"answer":2,"explanation":"模型小液滴可能被表面張力束縛，原型卻更易破碎，直接按照片估曝氣會偏差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Small model droplets can remain surface-tension-bound where prototype flow breaks up, biasing air-entrainment estimates from imagery. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b257-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「讀值誤差的放大」與「重複試驗與代表性」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Scaling measurement uncertainty\" and \"Replicates and representativeness\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b257-v15-33","title":"讀值誤差的放大：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Scaling measurement uncertainty: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「讀值誤差的放大」如何影響水力模型縮尺試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Scaling measurement uncertainty” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Scale-model testing of hydraulic structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"模型的微小讀值誤差放回原型後也按相應比例放大，不能以數字小就忽略。讀值重複性、共同零點及尺度製造誤差屬不同分量，必須說明相關性後再合成；原型結果的小數位應反映證據，而不是把模型儀器的每一位都乘出來展示。 假設模型水位標準不確定度0.0005m、λL=40且比例視為精確，原型相應標準不確定度0.020m；未含尺度本身誤差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「讀值誤差的放大」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Small model reading errors grow under prototype scaling and cannot be dismissed by their absolute size. Repeatability, coherent zero offset and fabrication-scale error are distinct components requiring stated correlations before combination. Reported prototype precision should follow the evidence, not every digit produced by multiplying an instrument display by the geometric ratio in a spreadsheet. Assume model level standard uncertainty0.0005m and exact length ratio40. Prototype-equivalent uncertainty is0.020m, excluding uncertainty in the scale itself. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Scaling measurement uncertainty” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「模型讀值誤差很小所以換算回原型後可以完全忽略不計。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small model reading error can be ignored completely after conversion to prototype scale.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「讀值誤差的放大」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Scaling measurement uncertainty”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-33-k1","title":"讀值誤差的放大","titleEn":"Scaling measurement uncertainty","text":"模型的微小讀值誤差放回原型後也按相應比例放大，不能以數字小就忽略。讀值重複性、共同零點及尺度製造誤差屬不同分量，必須說明相關性後再合成；原型結果的小數位應反映證據，而不是把模型儀器的每一位都乘出來展示。","textEn":"Small model reading errors grow under prototype scaling and cannot be dismissed by their absolute size. Repeatability, coherent zero offset and fabrication-scale error are distinct components requiring stated correlations before combination.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模型讀值誤差很小所以換算回原型後可以完全忽略不計。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small model reading error can be ignored completely after conversion to prototype scale. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「讀值誤差的放大」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Scaling measurement uncertainty\" is correct?","options":["模型的微小讀值誤差放回原型後也按相應比例放大，不能以數字小就忽略。","模型讀值誤差很小所以換算回原型後可以完全忽略不計。","重複三次結果很接近就代表所有未測工況與系統偏差都已驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Small model reading errors grow under prototype scaling and cannot be dismissed by their absolute size.","A small model reading error can be ignored completely after conversion to prototype scale.","Three closely agreeing repeats validate every untested condition and eliminate systematic bias."],"answer":0,"explanation":"模型的微小讀值誤差放回原型後也按相應比例放大，不能以數字小就忽略。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Small model reading errors grow under prototype scaling and cannot be dismissed by their absolute size. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b257-v15-34","title":"讀值誤差的放大：定量估算","titleEn":"Scaling measurement uncertainty: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「讀值誤差的放大」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Scaling measurement uncertainty” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設模型水位標準不確定度0.0005m、λL=40且比例視為精確，原型相應標準不確定度0.020m；未含尺度本身誤差。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume model level standard uncertainty0.0005m and exact length ratio40. Prototype-equivalent uncertainty is0.020m, excluding uncertainty in the scale itself. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分開估水位零偏、讀值散布及模型尺寸誤差，說明哪些為共同分量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Estimate level bias, reading scatter and fabrication error separately, identifying shared components.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設模型水位標準不確定度0.0005m、λL=40且比例視為精確，原型相應標準不確定度0.020m；未含尺度本身誤差。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume model level standard uncertainty0.0005m and exact length ratio40. Prototype-equivalent uncertainty is0.020m, excluding uncertainty in the scale itself.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「讀值誤差的放大」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Scaling measurement uncertainty\", which statement holds?","options":["佛祿相似要求速度與模型長度使用完全相同的縮小倍數。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","只要事後修改時間軸就能補救試驗時未縮尺的閥門動作。"],"optionsEn":["Froude similarity requires velocity to use exactly the same reduction factor as length.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Rescaling the recorded time axis repairs any valve motion that was not correctly scaled during the test."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b257-v15-35","title":"讀值誤差的放大：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Scaling measurement uncertainty: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「讀值誤差的放大」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Scaling measurement uncertainty” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分開估水位零偏、讀值散布及模型尺寸誤差，說明哪些為共同分量。以獨立控制點檢核高程，將量測及尺度不確定度傳播到原型結果，按有效精度四捨五入，不使用無依據的小數位。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Estimate level bias, reading scatter and fabrication error separately, identifying shared components. Check elevations against independent control, propagate measurement and scale uncertainty to prototype results and round to defensible precision rather than retaining unsupported decimal places. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分開估水位零偏、讀值散布及模型尺寸誤差，說明哪些為共同分量。以獨立控制點檢核高程，將量測及尺度不確定度傳播到原型結果，按有效精度四捨五入，不使用無依據的小數位。","observationEn":"Site practice: Estimate level bias, reading scatter and fabrication error separately, identifying shared components. Check elevations against independent control, propagate measurement and scale uncertainty to prototype results and round to defensible precision rather than retaining unsupported decimal places.","failure":"注意干擾：水位零偏在所有測點共同存在時不會靠平均消失，尺度錯誤還可能同時影響水深和流量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A shared level offset survives averaging, and incorrect scale can affect both depth and discharge. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分開估水位零偏、讀值散布及模型尺寸誤差，說明哪些為共同分量。以獨立控制點檢核高程，將量測及尺度不確定度傳播到原型結果，按有效精度四捨五入，不使用無依據的小數位。","textEn":"Estimate level bias, reading scatter and fabrication error separately, identifying shared components. Check elevations against independent control, propagate measurement and scale uncertainty to prototype results and round to defensible precision rather than retaining unsupported decimal places.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分開估水位零偏、讀值散布及模型尺寸誤差，說明哪些為共同分量。以獨立控制點檢核高程，將量測及尺度不確定度傳播到原型結果，按有效精度四捨五入，不使用無依據的小數位。","textEn":"Estimate level bias, reading scatter and fabrication error separately, identifying shared components. Check elevations against independent control, propagate measurement and scale uncertainty to prototype results and round to defensible precision rather than retaining unsupported decimal places.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「讀值誤差的放大」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Scaling measurement uncertainty\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","縮尺合力只需要跟長度成正比而不必考慮受壓面積。","分開估水位零偏、讀值散布及模型尺寸誤差，說明哪些為共同分量。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Model force scales only linearly with length and does not depend on loaded area.","Estimate level bias, reading scatter and fabrication error separately, identifying shared components."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分開估水位零偏、讀值散布及模型尺寸誤差，說明哪些為共同分量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Estimate level bias, reading scatter and fabrication error separately, identifying shared components. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b257-v15-36","title":"讀值誤差的放大：失效診斷","titleEn":"Scaling measurement uncertainty: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「讀值誤差的放大」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Scaling measurement uncertainty” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"水位零偏在所有測點共同存在時不會靠平均消失，尺度錯誤還可能同時影響水深和流量。只放大平均讀值而不放大誤差，會讓原型推估看起來過度精確。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A shared level offset survives averaging, and incorrect scale can affect both depth and discharge. Scaling the mean reading without its uncertainty makes the inferred prototype result appear more precise than the experiment actually supports. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設模型水位標準不確定度0.0005m、λL=40且比例視為精確，原型相應標準不確定度0.020m；未含尺度本身誤差。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Prototype-equivalent uncertainty is0.020m, excluding uncertainty in the scale itself.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模型讀值誤差很小所以換算回原型後可以完全忽略不計。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small model reading error can be ignored completely after conversion to prototype scale.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"水位零偏在所有測點共同存在時不會靠平均消失，尺度錯誤還可能同時影響水深和流量。只放大平均讀值而不放大誤差，會讓原型推估看起來過度精確。","textEn":"A shared level offset survives averaging, and incorrect scale can affect both depth and discharge. Scaling the mean reading without its uncertainty makes the inferred prototype result appear more precise than the experiment actually supports.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「讀值誤差的放大」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Scaling measurement uncertainty\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["水位零偏在所有測點共同存在時不會靠平均消失，尺度錯誤還可能同時影響水深和流量。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","重複三次結果很接近就代表所有未測工況與系統偏差都已驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A shared level offset survives averaging, and incorrect scale can affect both depth and discharge.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Three closely agreeing repeats validate every untested condition and eliminate systematic bias."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水位零偏在所有測點共同存在時不會靠平均消失，尺度錯誤還可能同時影響水深和流量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A shared level offset survives averaging, and incorrect scale can affect both depth and discharge. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b257-v15-37","title":"重複試驗與代表性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Replicates and representativeness: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「重複試驗與代表性」如何影響水力模型縮尺試驗的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Replicates and representativeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Scale-model testing of hydraulic structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"重複試驗能估計同條件下的散布，但三次重複不能涵蓋未測水位、流量或邊界狀態。平均值標準誤與單次觀測標準差用途不同，獨立性也需要重新建立初始條件；若同一零點偏差持續存在，增加次數只會讓錯誤平均顯得更穩定。 假設獨立流量結果0.098、0.100、0.102m³/s，平均0.100、樣本標準差0.002m³/s，變異係數2%；非全部工況不確定度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「重複試驗與代表性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Replicates estimate scatter under one condition but do not cover untested levels, discharges or boundaries. Standard error of a mean differs from the deviation of individual observations, and independence requires reestablishing initial conditions. A persistent zero bias is not reduced by replication; more runs can merely make the wrong mean appear increasingly stable and convincing. Assume independent discharges0.098,0.100,0.102m³/s. Mean0.100 and sample deviation0.002m³/s give2% coefficient of variation, not uncertainty for all operating conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Replicates and representativeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「重複三次結果很接近就代表所有未測工況與系統偏差都已驗證。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Three closely agreeing repeats validate every untested condition and eliminate systematic bias.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「重複試驗與代表性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Replicates and representativeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-37-k1","title":"重複試驗與代表性","titleEn":"Replicates and representativeness","text":"重複試驗能估計同條件下的散布，但三次重複不能涵蓋未測水位、流量或邊界狀態。平均值標準誤與單次觀測標準差用途不同，獨立性也需要重新建立初始條件；若同一零點偏差持續存在，增加次數只會讓錯誤平均顯得更穩定。","textEn":"Replicates estimate scatter under one condition but do not cover untested levels, discharges or boundaries. Standard error of a mean differs from the deviation of individual observations, and independence requires reestablishing initial conditions.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：重複三次結果很接近就代表所有未測工況與系統偏差都已驗證。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Three closely agreeing repeats validate every untested condition and eliminate systematic bias. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「重複試驗與代表性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Replicates and representativeness\" is correct?","options":["重複三次結果很接近就代表所有未測工況與系統偏差都已驗證。","重複試驗能估計同條件下的散布，但三次重複不能涵蓋未測水位、流量或邊界狀態。","只要模型外觀像原型就可以忽略局部縫隙與尺度方向差異。"],"optionsEn":["Three closely agreeing repeats validate every untested condition and eliminate systematic bias.","Replicates estimate scatter under one condition but do not cover untested levels, discharges or boundaries.","Visual similarity alone permits ignoring gaps and differences between horizontal and vertical scales."],"answer":1,"explanation":"重複試驗能估計同條件下的散布，但三次重複不能涵蓋未測水位、流量或邊界狀態。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Replicates estimate scatter under one condition but do not cover untested levels, discharges or boundaries. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b257-v15-38","title":"重複試驗與代表性：定量估算","titleEn":"Replicates and representativeness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「重複試驗與代表性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Replicates and representativeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設獨立流量結果0.098、0.100、0.102m³/s，平均0.100、樣本標準差0.002m³/s，變異係數2%；非全部工況不確定度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume independent discharges0.098,0.100,0.102m³/s. Mean0.100 and sample deviation0.002m³/s give2% coefficient of variation, not uncertainty for all operating conditions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：事先定義重複方式和回復初始水位程序，保留每次原始紀錄與共同校正資料。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Define repetition and initial-level restoration beforehand, retaining raw runs and shared calibration records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設獨立流量結果0.098、0.100、0.102m³/s，平均0.100、樣本標準差0.002m³/s，變異係數2%；非全部工況不確定度。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume independent discharges0.098,0.100,0.102m³/s. Mean0.100 and sample deviation0.002m³/s give2% coefficient of variation, not uncertainty for all operating conditions.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「重複試驗與代表性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Replicates and representativeness\", which statement holds?","options":["總流量與每米寬度流量在縮尺模型都使用同一比例次方。","重力壓力比例正確就表示空化與封閉氣泡壓縮也完全相似。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Total discharge and discharge per unit width use the same scaling exponent.","Correct gravity-pressure scaling proves that cavitation and trapped-air compression are also fully similar.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b257-v15-39","title":"重複試驗與代表性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Replicates and representativeness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「重複試驗與代表性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Replicates and representativeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"事先定義重複方式和回復初始水位程序，保留每次原始紀錄與共同校正資料。用樣本而非母體分母計標準差，另列未試工況矩陣，避免以少量重複的低散布宣稱整個模型已驗證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Define repetition and initial-level restoration beforehand, retaining raw runs and shared calibration records. Use the sample-deviation denominator and list the untested condition matrix separately, without interpreting low scatter from a few replicates as complete validation of the model domain. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：事先定義重複方式和回復初始水位程序，保留每次原始紀錄與共同校正資料。用樣本而非母體分母計標準差，另列未試工況矩陣，避免以少量重複的低散布宣稱整個模型已驗證。","observationEn":"Site practice: Define repetition and initial-level restoration beforehand, retaining raw runs and shared calibration records. Use the sample-deviation denominator and list the untested condition matrix separately, without interpreting low scatter from a few replicates as complete validation of the model domain.","failure":"注意干擾：三次都受同一流量計偏差時仍可非常一致，卻系統性偏離真值。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Three runs sharing one meter bias can agree closely while all miss the true value. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"事先定義重複方式和回復初始水位程序，保留每次原始紀錄與共同校正資料。用樣本而非母體分母計標準差，另列未試工況矩陣，避免以少量重複的低散布宣稱整個模型已驗證。","textEn":"Define repetition and initial-level restoration beforehand, retaining raw runs and shared calibration records. Use the sample-deviation denominator and list the untested condition matrix separately, without interpreting low scatter from a few replicates as complete validation of the model domain.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"事先定義重複方式和回復初始水位程序，保留每次原始紀錄與共同校正資料。用樣本而非母體分母計標準差，另列未試工況矩陣，避免以少量重複的低散布宣稱整個模型已驗證。","textEn":"Define repetition and initial-level restoration beforehand, retaining raw runs and shared calibration records. Use the sample-deviation denominator and list the untested condition matrix separately, without interpreting low scatter from a few replicates as complete validation of the model domain.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「重複試驗與代表性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Replicates and representativeness\"?","options":["事先定義重複方式和回復初始水位程序，保留每次原始紀錄與共同校正資料。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","模型主流雷諾數高就可以證明每個細縫和近壁區都與原型相似。"],"optionsEn":["Define repetition and initial-level restoration beforehand, retaining raw runs and shared calibration records.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A high main-flow Reynolds number proves similarity in every small gap and near-wall region."],"answer":0,"explanation":"事先定義重複方式和回復初始水位程序，保留每次原始紀錄與共同校正資料。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Define repetition and initial-level restoration beforehand, retaining raw runs and shared calibration records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b257-v15-40","title":"重複試驗與代表性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Replicates and representativeness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"prerequisiteIds":["b257-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「重複試驗與代表性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Replicates and representativeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"三次都受同一流量計偏差時仍可非常一致，卻系統性偏離真值。挑掉不喜歡的試驗又會縮小散布，若沒有預定排除規則，所謂重複性可能只反映選擇性報告。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Three runs sharing one meter bias can agree closely while all miss the true value. Selective deletion shrinks scatter further, and without predefined exclusion criteria apparent repeatability may reflect reporting choices rather than reliable experimental behavior. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設獨立流量結果0.098、0.100、0.102m³/s，平均0.100、樣本標準差0.002m³/s，變異係數2%；非全部工況不確定度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mean0.100 and sample deviation0.002m³/s give2% coefficient of variation, not uncertainty for all operating conditions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「重複三次結果很接近就代表所有未測工況與系統偏差都已驗證。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Three closely agreeing repeats validate every untested condition and eliminate systematic bias.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b257-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"三次都受同一流量計偏差時仍可非常一致，卻系統性偏離真值。挑掉不喜歡的試驗又會縮小散布，若沒有預定排除規則，所謂重複性可能只反映選擇性報告。","textEn":"Three runs sharing one meter bias can agree closely while all miss the true value. Selective deletion shrinks scatter further, and without predefined exclusion criteria apparent repeatability may reflect reporting choices rather than reliable experimental behavior.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]},{"id":"b257-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「重複試驗與代表性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Replicates and representativeness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","三次都受同一流量計偏差時仍可非常一致，卻系統性偏離真值。","只要模型外觀像原型就可以忽略局部縫隙與尺度方向差異。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Three runs sharing one meter bias can agree closely while all miss the true value.","Visual similarity alone permits ignoring gaps and differences between horizontal and vertical scales."],"answer":1,"explanation":"三次都受同一流量計偏差時仍可非常一致，卻系統性偏離真值。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Three runs sharing one meter bias can agree closely while all miss the true value. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-hydraulic-lab","v15s-froude-manual","v15s-lab-projects","v15s-deltares-model"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b258","title":"抽蓄水庫水位調度","titleEn":"Reservoir-level scheduling for pumped storage","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課從上下庫逐時水量守恆開始，將庫容、水位、淨水頭、機組效率與電能連成可追溯帳本。十個單元分別處理抽水與發電方向、往返效率、可用時數、爬坡積分、天氣損失和期末預留，要求學徒在每個時間步查兩庫限制，並把慢速排程與快速水錘模型分開驗證。","summaryEn":"Starting with paired-reservoir conservation, this course connects storage, level, net head, machine efficiency and energy in a traceable ledger. Ten units distinguish pumping and generation, cycle efficiency, duration, ramps, weather exchange and terminal reserves. Apprentices check both reservoirs at every step and verify slow scheduling separately from rapid waterway transients.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-hydraulics","subcategoryTitle":"壩工監測、溢洪與壓力水路","subcategoryTitleEn":"Dam monitoring, spillways and pressure waterways","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-hydraulics","learningTags":["water","water-hydraulics","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-hydraulic","architectureNodes":[["雙庫水量帳本","Paired reservoir water balance"],["毛水頭與淨水頭","Gross and net head"],["抽水輸入與損失","Pumping input and losses"],["爬坡流量積分","Integrating flow ramps"],["期末庫存與預留","Terminal inventory and reservation"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-hydraulic","labels":["雙庫水量帳本","毛水頭與淨水頭","抽水輸入與損失","爬坡流量積分","期末庫存與預留"],"labelsEn":["Paired reservoir water balance","Gross and net head","Pumping input and losses","Integrating flow ramps","Terminal inventory and reservation"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創水頭敏感度：固定流量100m³/s、總發電效率0.90與密度1000kg/m³，淨水頭385m時功率為339.9165MW。如果其他假設維持不變而淨水頭提高10%至423.5m，功率為373.90815MW，正好提高10%。這不表示真實機組可突破額定容量，也不表示水頭提高後效率必然固定。學徒應把新工況放回效率曲線、流量與電氣容量限制，再沿上下庫水位歷時積分電能。若要求固定功率，流量會反向調整，不能仍用原先水量帳本，且需重新檢查管路瞬態與進水條件。","textEn":"Original head sensitivity: with discharge100m³/s, overall generating efficiency0.90 and density1000kg/m³ fixed, net head385m gives339.9165MW. Raising net head by10% to423.5m while holding the other assumptions fixed gives373.90815MW, exactly10% higher. This does not permit exceeding nameplate capacity or establish constant real-machine efficiency at the new head. Place the new condition on the efficiency map and check discharge and electrical limits before integrating energy along the reservoir-level histories. If constant power is required instead, discharge changes inversely; the original water ledger no longer applies and transient and intake conditions must be checked again.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b258-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「雙庫水量帳本」與「水位庫容換算」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Paired reservoir water balance\" and \"Level and storage conversion\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b258-v15-01","title":"雙庫水量帳本：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Paired reservoir water balance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「雙庫水量帳本」如何影響抽蓄水庫水位調度的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Paired reservoir water balance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-level scheduling for pumped storage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"抽蓄把水在上下庫之間搬移，不會因為發電而消耗同等體積的水，但外部入流、蒸發與放流仍要分別列帳。每個時間步都應同時更新兩庫，明確約定流量正方向；只看上庫水位容易掩蓋下庫已滿或總水量不守恆的排程錯誤。 假設無外部交換，發電流量100m³/s持續1800s，上庫減少180000m³、下庫增加同量，兩庫合計不變。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「雙庫水量帳本」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pumped storage transfers water between reservoirs without consuming the transferred volume through generation, although external inflow, evaporation and release remain separate terms. Update both reservoirs at every interval with explicit flow signs. Tracking only the upper level can hide a full lower reservoir or a schedule that violates total water conservation. Assume no external exchange and generation flow100m³/s for1800s. Upper storage falls180000m³ while lower storage rises equally, preserving their combined volume. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Paired reservoir water balance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要日終上庫水位正確就不需要檢查下庫逐時水量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A correct final upper-reservoir level removes any need to check lower-reservoir storage through time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「雙庫水量帳本」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Paired reservoir water balance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-01-k1","title":"雙庫水量帳本","titleEn":"Paired reservoir water balance","text":"抽蓄把水在上下庫之間搬移，不會因為發電而消耗同等體積的水，但外部入流、蒸發與放流仍要分別列帳。每個時間步都應同時更新兩庫，明確約定流量正方向；只看上庫水位容易掩蓋下庫已滿或總水量不守恆的排程錯誤。","textEn":"Pumped storage transfers water between reservoirs without consuming the transferred volume through generation, although external inflow, evaporation and release remain separate terms. Update both reservoirs at every interval with explicit flow signs.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要日終上庫水位正確就不需要檢查下庫逐時水量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A correct final upper-reservoir level removes any need to check lower-reservoir storage through time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「雙庫水量帳本」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Paired reservoir water balance\" is correct?","options":["只要日終上庫水位正確就不需要檢查下庫逐時水量。","抽蓄把水在上下庫之間搬移，不會因為發電而消耗同等體積的水，但外部入流、蒸發與放流仍要分別列帳。","同樣的移水量在上下庫必定造成完全相同的水位變化。"],"optionsEn":["A correct final upper-reservoir level removes any need to check lower-reservoir storage through time.","Pumped storage transfers water between reservoirs without consuming the transferred volume through generation, although external inflow, evaporation and release remain separate terms.","The same transferred volume must produce identical level changes in both reservoirs."],"answer":1,"explanation":"抽蓄把水在上下庫之間搬移，不會因為發電而消耗同等體積的水，但外部入流、蒸發與放流仍要分別列帳。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pumped storage transfers water between reservoirs without consuming the transferred volume through generation, although external inflow, evaporation and release remain separate terms. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b258-v15-02","title":"雙庫水量帳本：定量估算","titleEn":"Paired reservoir water balance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雙庫水量帳本」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Paired reservoir water balance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設無外部交換，發電流量100m³/s持續1800s，上庫減少180000m³、下庫增加同量，兩庫合計不變。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume no external exchange and generation flow100m³/s for1800s. Upper storage falls180000m³ while lower storage rises equally, preserving their combined volume. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立上庫與下庫兩欄逐時帳本，逐一核對抽水及發電符號並把外部交換獨立列出。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build separate time-step ledgers, checking pumping and generating signs and listing external exchanges explicitly.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設無外部交換，發電流量100m³/s持續1800s，上庫減少180000m³、下庫增加同量，兩庫合計不變。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume no external exchange and generation flow100m³/s for1800s. Upper storage falls180000m³ while lower storage rises equally, preserving their combined volume.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「雙庫水量帳本」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Paired reservoir water balance\", which statement holds?","options":["額定發電容量足夠就保證任意水位都能連續輸出相同功率。","只要輸出電量除以當日抽水電量超過一就證明儲能效率超過百分之百。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate nameplate capacity guarantees identical continuous output at any reservoir level.","Output exceeding the same day’s pumping input proves a storage efficiency above one hundred percent.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b258-v15-03","title":"雙庫水量帳本：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Paired reservoir water balance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「雙庫水量帳本」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Paired reservoir water balance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立上庫與下庫兩欄逐時帳本，逐一核對抽水及發電符號並把外部交換獨立列出。以兩庫總量閉合差找單位或漏項錯誤，再確認每步結果沒有超過個別可用容積邊界。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build separate time-step ledgers, checking pumping and generating signs and listing external exchanges explicitly. Use total-volume closure to locate unit errors or omissions, then confirm each step remains inside both reservoirs’ individual usable-storage bounds. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立上庫與下庫兩欄逐時帳本，逐一核對抽水及發電符號並把外部交換獨立列出。以兩庫總量閉合差找單位或漏項錯誤，再確認每步結果沒有超過個別可用容積邊界。","observationEn":"Site practice: Build separate time-step ledgers, checking pumping and generating signs and listing external exchanges explicitly. Use total-volume closure to locate unit errors or omissions, then confirm each step remains inside both reservoirs’ individual usable-storage bounds.","failure":"注意干擾：將同一流量在兩庫都列成流出會製造虛假耗水，反過來都列入流又會創造水量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Entering a transfer as outflow from both reservoirs invents losses, while dual inflow creates water. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立上庫與下庫兩欄逐時帳本，逐一核對抽水及發電符號並把外部交換獨立列出。以兩庫總量閉合差找單位或漏項錯誤，再確認每步結果沒有超過個別可用容積邊界。","textEn":"Build separate time-step ledgers, checking pumping and generating signs and listing external exchanges explicitly. Use total-volume closure to locate unit errors or omissions, then confirm each step remains inside both reservoirs’ individual usable-storage bounds.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立上庫與下庫兩欄逐時帳本，逐一核對抽水及發電符號並把外部交換獨立列出。以兩庫總量閉合差找單位或漏項錯誤，再確認每步結果沒有超過個別可用容積邊界。","textEn":"Build separate time-step ledgers, checking pumping and generating signs and listing external exchanges explicitly. Use total-volume closure to locate unit errors or omissions, then confirm each step remains inside both reservoirs’ individual usable-storage bounds.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「雙庫水量帳本」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Paired reservoir water balance\"?","options":["建立上庫與下庫兩欄逐時帳本，逐一核對抽水及發電符號並把外部交換獨立列出。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","爬坡期間總水量正確就能證明任何閥門動作都不會產生水錘。"],"optionsEn":["Build separate time-step ledgers, checking pumping and generating signs and listing external exchanges explicitly.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A correct total ramp volume proves that every associated valve movement is free of water hammer."],"answer":0,"explanation":"建立上庫與下庫兩欄逐時帳本，逐一核對抽水及發電符號並把外部交換獨立列出。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build separate time-step ledgers, checking pumping and generating signs and listing external exchanges explicitly. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b258-v15-04","title":"雙庫水量帳本：失效診斷","titleEn":"Paired reservoir water balance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雙庫水量帳本」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Paired reservoir water balance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將同一流量在兩庫都列成流出會製造虛假耗水，反過來都列入流又會創造水量。日終總量碰巧正確也不能證明中途下庫未經溢流或超界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Entering a transfer as outflow from both reservoirs invents losses, while dual inflow creates water. A correct daily total does not prove that intermediate lower-reservoir storage avoided overflow or other boundary violations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設無外部交換，發電流量100m³/s持續1800s，上庫減少180000m³、下庫增加同量，兩庫合計不變。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Upper storage falls180000m³ while lower storage rises equally, preserving their combined volume.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要日終上庫水位正確就不需要檢查下庫逐時水量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A correct final upper-reservoir level removes any need to check lower-reservoir storage through time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將同一流量在兩庫都列成流出會製造虛假耗水，反過來都列入流又會創造水量。日終總量碰巧正確也不能證明中途下庫未經溢流或超界。","textEn":"Entering a transfer as outflow from both reservoirs invents losses, while dual inflow creates water. A correct daily total does not prove that intermediate lower-reservoir storage avoided overflow or other boundary violations.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雙庫水量帳本」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Paired reservoir water balance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","將同一流量在兩庫都列成流出會製造虛假耗水，反過來都列入流又會創造水量。","同樣的移水量在上下庫必定造成完全相同的水位變化。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Entering a transfer as outflow from both reservoirs invents losses, while dual inflow creates water.","The same transferred volume must produce identical level changes in both reservoirs."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將同一流量在兩庫都列成流出會製造虛假耗水，反過來都列入流又會創造水量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Entering a transfer as outflow from both reservoirs invents losses, while dual inflow creates water. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b258-v15-05","title":"水位庫容換算：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Level and storage conversion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「水位庫容換算」如何影響抽蓄水庫水位調度的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Level and storage conversion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-level scheduling for pumped storage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水位不是可直接加減的能量刻度，必須透過測得的庫容曲線換成水量。局部面積不變只適合小範圍近似，廣大的淺灘或陡岸會改變同一水量對應的水位變化；上下庫曲線也不能混用，即使它們具有相近的最大面積。 假設局部上庫面積600000m²恆定，抽入180000m³，Δz=ΔV/A=0.300m；大範圍水位需積分實際庫容曲線。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水位庫容換算」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Water level is not an additive energy scale; surveyed storage curves connect level to volume. A constant surface area is a local approximation, and broad shelves or steep banks change the level response to equal transfers. Upper and lower curves are not interchangeable merely because their maximum surface areas appear similar. Assume locally constant upper area600000m² and inflow180000m³. Δz=ΔV/A=0.300m; broader changes require the actual integrated storage curve. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Level and storage conversion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「同樣的移水量在上下庫必定造成完全相同的水位變化。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The same transferred volume must produce identical level changes in both reservoirs.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水位庫容換算」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Level and storage conversion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-05-k1","title":"水位庫容換算","titleEn":"Level and storage conversion","text":"水位不是可直接加減的能量刻度，必須透過測得的庫容曲線換成水量。局部面積不變只適合小範圍近似，廣大的淺灘或陡岸會改變同一水量對應的水位變化；上下庫曲線也不能混用，即使它們具有相近的最大面積。","textEn":"Water level is not an additive energy scale; surveyed storage curves connect level to volume. A constant surface area is a local approximation, and broad shelves or steep banks change the level response to equal transfers.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：同樣的移水量在上下庫必定造成完全相同的水位變化。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The same transferred volume must produce identical level changes in both reservoirs. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水位庫容換算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Level and storage conversion\" is correct?","options":["同樣的移水量在上下庫必定造成完全相同的水位變化。","毛水頭與機組淨水頭在所有流量下都完全相等。","水位不是可直接加減的能量刻度，必須透過測得的庫容曲線換成水量。"],"optionsEn":["The same transferred volume must produce identical level changes in both reservoirs.","Gross reservoir head and machine net head are equal at every discharge.","Water level is not an additive energy scale; surveyed storage curves connect level to volume."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水位不是可直接加減的能量刻度，必須透過測得的庫容曲線換成水量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Water level is not an additive energy scale; surveyed storage curves connect level to volume. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b258-v15-06","title":"水位庫容換算：定量估算","titleEn":"Level and storage conversion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水位庫容換算」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Level and storage conversion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設局部上庫面積600000m²恆定，抽入180000m³，Δz=ΔV/A=0.300m；大範圍水位需積分實際庫容曲線。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume locally constant upper area600000m² and inflow180000m³. Δz=ΔV/A=0.300m; broader changes require the actual integrated storage curve. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將水位、庫容及面積資料用共同高程基準整理，檢查曲線斜率是否等於水面面積。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Put level, storage and area on a common datum and check that storage-curve slope equals surface area.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設局部上庫面積600000m²恆定，抽入180000m³，Δz=ΔV/A=0.300m；大範圍水位需積分實際庫容曲線。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume locally constant upper area600000m² and inflow180000m³. Δz=ΔV/A=0.300m; broader changes require the actual integrated storage curve.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水位庫容換算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Level and storage conversion\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","抽水效率越低時用電需求反而應該越小。","只要上庫尚未排空就可以維持額定功率直到最後一滴水。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Lower pumping efficiency should reduce the electrical input required for the same lift and flow.","Rated power can be maintained until the upper reservoir is completely empty."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b258-v15-07","title":"水位庫容換算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Level and storage conversion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水位庫容換算」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Level and storage conversion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將水位、庫容及面積資料用共同高程基準整理，檢查曲線斜率是否等於水面面積。以已知移水量回算兩庫水位並比較實測殘差，遇到灘地轉折時縮短時間步或直接用曲線求解。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Put level, storage and area on a common datum and check that storage-curve slope equals surface area. Back-calculate levels from known transfers, inspect measured residuals and resolve shoreline breaks with smaller steps or direct curve inversion. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將水位、庫容及面積資料用共同高程基準整理，檢查曲線斜率是否等於水面面積。以已知移水量回算兩庫水位並比較實測殘差，遇到灘地轉折時縮短時間步或直接用曲線求解。","observationEn":"Site practice: Put level, storage and area on a common datum and check that storage-curve slope equals surface area. Back-calculate levels from known transfers, inspect measured residuals and resolve shoreline breaks with smaller steps or direct curve inversion.","failure":"注意干擾：將平方公里當成平方米會使水位變化嚴重失真，沿用過期地形也會錯估可用容積。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing square kilometers with square meters grossly distorts level change, and outdated bathymetry misstates usable storage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將水位、庫容及面積資料用共同高程基準整理，檢查曲線斜率是否等於水面面積。以已知移水量回算兩庫水位並比較實測殘差，遇到灘地轉折時縮短時間步或直接用曲線求解。","textEn":"Put level, storage and area on a common datum and check that storage-curve slope equals surface area. Back-calculate levels from known transfers, inspect measured residuals and resolve shoreline breaks with smaller steps or direct curve inversion.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將水位、庫容及面積資料用共同高程基準整理，檢查曲線斜率是否等於水面面積。以已知移水量回算兩庫水位並比較實測殘差，遇到灘地轉折時縮短時間步或直接用曲線求解。","textEn":"Put level, storage and area on a common datum and check that storage-curve slope equals surface area. Back-calculate levels from known transfers, inspect measured residuals and resolve shoreline breaks with smaller steps or direct curve inversion.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水位庫容換算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Level and storage conversion\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將水位、庫容及面積資料用共同高程基準整理，檢查曲線斜率是否等於水面面積。","封閉循環抽蓄完全不會受到降雨、蒸發或滲漏影響。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Put level, storage and area on a common datum and check that storage-curve slope equals surface area.","Closed-loop pumped storage is completely unaffected by rainfall, evaporation or seepage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將水位、庫容及面積資料用共同高程基準整理，檢查曲線斜率是否等於水面面積。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Put level, storage and area on a common datum and check that storage-curve slope equals surface area. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b258-v15-08","title":"水位庫容換算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Level and storage conversion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水位庫容換算」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Level and storage conversion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將平方公里當成平方米會使水位變化嚴重失真，沿用過期地形也會錯估可用容積。感測器高程基準偏移時，曲線再精細也不能修復錯誤輸入。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing square kilometers with square meters grossly distorts level change, and outdated bathymetry misstates usable storage. A detailed curve cannot correct a sensor referenced to the wrong elevation datum. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設局部上庫面積600000m²恆定，抽入180000m³，Δz=ΔV/A=0.300m；大範圍水位需積分實際庫容曲線。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume locally constant upper area600000m² and inflow180000m³. Δz=ΔV/A=0.300m; broader changes require the actual integrated storage curve.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「同樣的移水量在上下庫必定造成完全相同的水位變化。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The same transferred volume must produce identical level changes in both reservoirs.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將平方公里當成平方米會使水位變化嚴重失真，沿用過期地形也會錯估可用容積。感測器高程基準偏移時，曲線再精細也不能修復錯誤輸入。","textEn":"Confusing square kilometers with square meters grossly distorts level change, and outdated bathymetry misstates usable storage. A detailed curve cannot correct a sensor referenced to the wrong elevation datum.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水位庫容換算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Level and storage conversion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","毛水頭與機組淨水頭在所有流量下都完全相等。","將平方公里當成平方米會使水位變化嚴重失真，沿用過期地形也會錯估可用容積。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Gross reservoir head and machine net head are equal at every discharge.","Confusing square kilometers with square meters grossly distorts level change, and outdated bathymetry misstates usable storage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將平方公里當成平方米會使水位變化嚴重失真，沿用過期地形也會錯估可用容積。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing square kilometers with square meters grossly distorts level change, and outdated bathymetry misstates usable storage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b258-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「毛水頭與淨水頭」與「發電功率與輸出」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Gross and net head\" and \"Generating power and output\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b258-v15-09","title":"毛水頭與淨水頭：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Gross and net head: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「毛水頭與淨水頭」如何影響抽蓄水庫水位調度的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gross and net head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-level scheduling for pumped storage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"上下游水面高差是毛水頭，機組可利用的淨水頭還受沿程與局部損失影響，且損失隨流量及模式改變。把泵送和發電套同一個帶符號的效率可能混淆能量方向；先畫能量線，才能知道損失在哪一側增加需求或減少輸出。 假設上庫600m、下庫200m、發電水頭損失15m，淨水頭H=600−200−15=385m；未代表其他流量的損失。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「毛水頭與淨水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The reservoir-level difference is gross head, while usable turbine head also depends on distributed and local losses that vary with flow and mode. Applying one signed efficiency to both pumping and generation obscures energy direction. An energy-grade sketch identifies where losses increase pumping demand or reduce generating output for the chosen operating point. Assume upper elevation600m, lower200m and generation loss15m. Net headH=600−200−15=385m, without prescribing losses at other discharges. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gross and net head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「毛水頭與機組淨水頭在所有流量下都完全相等。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Gross reservoir head and machine net head are equal at every discharge.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「毛水頭與淨水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gross and net head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-09-k1","title":"毛水頭與淨水頭","titleEn":"Gross and net head","text":"上下游水面高差是毛水頭，機組可利用的淨水頭還受沿程與局部損失影響，且損失隨流量及模式改變。把泵送和發電套同一個帶符號的效率可能混淆能量方向；先畫能量線，才能知道損失在哪一側增加需求或減少輸出。","textEn":"The reservoir-level difference is gross head, while usable turbine head also depends on distributed and local losses that vary with flow and mode. Applying one signed efficiency to both pumping and generation obscures energy direction.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：毛水頭與機組淨水頭在所有流量下都完全相等。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Gross reservoir head and machine net head are equal at every discharge. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「毛水頭與淨水頭」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gross and net head\" is correct?","options":["上下游水面高差是毛水頭，機組可利用的淨水頭還受沿程與局部損失影響，且損失隨流量及模式改變。","毛水頭與機組淨水頭在所有流量下都完全相等。","額定發電容量足夠就保證任意水位都能連續輸出相同功率。"],"optionsEn":["The reservoir-level difference is gross head, while usable turbine head also depends on distributed and local losses that vary with flow and mode.","Gross reservoir head and machine net head are equal at every discharge.","Adequate nameplate capacity guarantees identical continuous output at any reservoir level."],"answer":0,"explanation":"上下游水面高差是毛水頭，機組可利用的淨水頭還受沿程與局部損失影響，且損失隨流量及模式改變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The reservoir-level difference is gross head, while usable turbine head also depends on distributed and local losses that vary with flow and mode. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b258-v15-10","title":"毛水頭與淨水頭：定量估算","titleEn":"Gross and net head: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「毛水頭與淨水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gross and net head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設上庫600m、下庫200m、發電水頭損失15m，淨水頭H=600−200−15=385m；未代表其他流量的損失。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume upper elevation600m, lower200m and generation loss15m. Net headH=600−200−15=385m, without prescribing losses at other discharges. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用同時刻的上下庫水位建立毛水頭，逐項標註流道損失與量測位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Calculate gross head from simultaneous levels and label each loss and measurement location.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設上庫600m、下庫200m、發電水頭損失15m，淨水頭H=600−200−15=385m；未代表其他流量的損失。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume upper elevation600m, lower200m and generation loss15m. Net headH=600−200−15=385m, without prescribing losses at other discharges.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「毛水頭與淨水頭」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gross and net head\", which statement holds?","options":["只要輸出電量除以當日抽水電量超過一就證明儲能效率超過百分之百。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","爬坡期間總水量正確就能證明任何閥門動作都不會產生水錘。"],"optionsEn":["Output exceeding the same day’s pumping input proves a storage efficiency above one hundred percent.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","A correct total ramp volume proves that every associated valve movement is free of water hammer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b258-v15-11","title":"毛水頭與淨水頭：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gross and net head: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「毛水頭與淨水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gross and net head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用同時刻的上下庫水位建立毛水頭，逐項標註流道損失與量測位置。核對泵送時損失應加到所需揚程，發電時則扣除，並以不同流量資料檢查固定損失假設的適用範圍。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Calculate gross head from simultaneous levels and label each loss and measurement location. Verify that pumping adds losses to required lift while generation subtracts them, then use different flow observations to test the limited range of a constant-loss approximation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用同時刻的上下庫水位建立毛水頭，逐項標註流道損失與量測位置。核對泵送時損失應加到所需揚程，發電時則扣除，並以不同流量資料檢查固定損失假設的適用範圍。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate gross head from simultaneous levels and label each loss and measurement location. Verify that pumping adds losses to required lift while generation subtracts them, then use different flow observations to test the limited range of a constant-loss approximation.","failure":"注意干擾：水位資料時間不一致會創造不存在的水頭，將損失重複扣除會低估輸出。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unsynchronized levels create a fictitious head, and double-counted losses understate output. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用同時刻的上下庫水位建立毛水頭，逐項標註流道損失與量測位置。核對泵送時損失應加到所需揚程，發電時則扣除，並以不同流量資料檢查固定損失假設的適用範圍。","textEn":"Calculate gross head from simultaneous levels and label each loss and measurement location. Verify that pumping adds losses to required lift while generation subtracts them, then use different flow observations to test the limited range of a constant-loss approximation.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用同時刻的上下庫水位建立毛水頭，逐項標註流道損失與量測位置。核對泵送時損失應加到所需揚程，發電時則扣除，並以不同流量資料檢查固定損失假設的適用範圍。","textEn":"Calculate gross head from simultaneous levels and label each loss and measurement location. Verify that pumping adds losses to required lift while generation subtracts them, then use different flow observations to test the limited range of a constant-loss approximation.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「毛水頭與淨水頭」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gross and net head\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","同一份預留水量可以同時保證任意多個獨立備援服務。","用同時刻的上下庫水位建立毛水頭，逐項標註流道損失與量測位置。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The same reserved water can simultaneously guarantee any number of independent backup services.","Calculate gross head from simultaneous levels and label each loss and measurement location."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用同時刻的上下庫水位建立毛水頭，逐項標註流道損失與量測位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Calculate gross head from simultaneous levels and label each loss and measurement location. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b258-v15-12","title":"毛水頭與淨水頭：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gross and net head: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「毛水頭與淨水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gross and net head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"水位資料時間不一致會創造不存在的水頭，將損失重複扣除會低估輸出。忽略低水位進水條件與空化限制，也可能讓數學上可行的排程超出機組適用範圍。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unsynchronized levels create a fictitious head, and double-counted losses understate output. Neglecting low-level intake and cavitation constraints can also place an arithmetically feasible schedule outside the machine’s permitted operating envelope. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設上庫600m、下庫200m、發電水頭損失15m，淨水頭H=600−200−15=385m；未代表其他流量的損失。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Net headH=600−200−15=385m, without prescribing losses at other discharges.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「毛水頭與機組淨水頭在所有流量下都完全相等。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Gross reservoir head and machine net head are equal at every discharge.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"水位資料時間不一致會創造不存在的水頭，將損失重複扣除會低估輸出。忽略低水位進水條件與空化限制，也可能讓數學上可行的排程超出機組適用範圍。","textEn":"Unsynchronized levels create a fictitious head, and double-counted losses understate output. Neglecting low-level intake and cavitation constraints can also place an arithmetically feasible schedule outside the machine’s permitted operating envelope.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「毛水頭與淨水頭」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gross and net head\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["水位資料時間不一致會創造不存在的水頭，將損失重複扣除會低估輸出。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","額定發電容量足夠就保證任意水位都能連續輸出相同功率。"],"optionsEn":["Unsynchronized levels create a fictitious head, and double-counted losses understate output.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Adequate nameplate capacity guarantees identical continuous output at any reservoir level."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水位資料時間不一致會創造不存在的水頭，將損失重複扣除會低估輸出。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unsynchronized levels create a fictitious head, and double-counted losses understate output. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b258-v15-13","title":"發電功率與輸出：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Generating power and output: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「發電功率與輸出」如何影響抽蓄水庫水位調度的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Generating power and output” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-level scheduling for pumped storage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水力功率由流量與淨水頭共同決定，電輸出還要乘適用工況的總效率。額定容量只是設備界限而不是每一時刻都能供應的功率；水位下降、效率曲線或流道限制會改變結果，排程應保存每步輸入而非只指定固定兆瓦數。 假設單一工況ρ=1000kg/m³、Q=100m³/s、淨水頭385m、總效率0.90，P=ρgQHη=339.9165MW。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「發電功率與輸出」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Hydraulic power depends jointly on discharge and net head, with electrical output reduced by the efficiency appropriate to that condition. Nameplate capacity is an equipment bound rather than power available at every instant. Changing level, efficiency curves and waterway limits require stored stepwise inputs instead of simply assigning a constant megawatt output. Assume density1000kg/m³, discharge100m³/s, net head385m and overall generating efficiency0.90. P=ρgQHη=339.9165MW at this stated operating point. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Generating power and output” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「額定發電容量足夠就保證任意水位都能連續輸出相同功率。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate nameplate capacity guarantees identical continuous output at any reservoir level.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「發電功率與輸出」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Generating power and output”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-13-k1","title":"發電功率與輸出","titleEn":"Generating power and output","text":"水力功率由流量與淨水頭共同決定，電輸出還要乘適用工況的總效率。額定容量只是設備界限而不是每一時刻都能供應的功率；水位下降、效率曲線或流道限制會改變結果，排程應保存每步輸入而非只指定固定兆瓦數。","textEn":"Hydraulic power depends jointly on discharge and net head, with electrical output reduced by the efficiency appropriate to that condition. Nameplate capacity is an equipment bound rather than power available at every instant.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：額定發電容量足夠就保證任意水位都能連續輸出相同功率。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate nameplate capacity guarantees identical continuous output at any reservoir level. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「發電功率與輸出」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Generating power and output\" is correct?","options":["額定發電容量足夠就保證任意水位都能連續輸出相同功率。","水力功率由流量與淨水頭共同決定，電輸出還要乘適用工況的總效率。","抽水效率越低時用電需求反而應該越小。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate nameplate capacity guarantees identical continuous output at any reservoir level.","Hydraulic power depends jointly on discharge and net head, with electrical output reduced by the efficiency appropriate to that condition.","Lower pumping efficiency should reduce the electrical input required for the same lift and flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水力功率由流量與淨水頭共同決定，電輸出還要乘適用工況的總效率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Hydraulic power depends jointly on discharge and net head, with electrical output reduced by the efficiency appropriate to that condition. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b258-v15-14","title":"發電功率與輸出：定量估算","titleEn":"Generating power and output: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「發電功率與輸出」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Generating power and output” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設單一工況ρ=1000kg/m³、Q=100m³/s、淨水頭385m、總效率0.90，P=ρgQHη=339.9165MW。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume density1000kg/m³, discharge100m³/s, net head385m and overall generating efficiency0.90. P=ρgQHη=339.9165MW at this stated operating point. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分清機械、發電機與總效率的定義，避免把同一損失計算兩遍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Distinguish mechanical, generator and overall efficiency to avoid duplicated losses.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設單一工況ρ=1000kg/m³、Q=100m³/s、淨水頭385m、總效率0.90，P=ρgQHη=339.9165MW。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume density1000kg/m³, discharge100m³/s, net head385m and overall generating efficiency0.90. P=ρgQHη=339.9165MW at this stated operating point.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「發電功率與輸出」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Generating power and output\", which statement holds?","options":["只要上庫尚未排空就可以維持額定功率直到最後一滴水。","封閉循環抽蓄完全不會受到降雨、蒸發或滲漏影響。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Rated power can be maintained until the upper reservoir is completely empty.","Closed-loop pumped storage is completely unaffected by rainfall, evaporation or seepage.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b258-v15-15","title":"發電功率與輸出：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Generating power and output: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「發電功率與輸出」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Generating power and output” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分清機械、發電機與總效率的定義，避免把同一損失計算兩遍。以每步流量和淨水頭算功率，積分成電能後對照電表，同時保留啟停、輔機與不可運轉區域的獨立紀錄。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Distinguish mechanical, generator and overall efficiency to avoid duplicated losses. Compute each step’s power from discharge and net head, integrate to energy and compare with meters while separately retaining starts, auxiliary loads and prohibited operating regions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分清機械、發電機與總效率的定義，避免把同一損失計算兩遍。以每步流量和淨水頭算功率，積分成電能後對照電表，同時保留啟停、輔機與不可運轉區域的獨立紀錄。","observationEn":"Site practice: Distinguish mechanical, generator and overall efficiency to avoid duplicated losses. Compute each step’s power from discharge and net head, integrate to energy and compare with meters while separately retaining starts, auxiliary loads and prohibited operating regions.","failure":"注意干擾：將百分之九十直接代成九十會放大百倍，忽略功率與電能的時間轉換則使排程帳本失衡。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Entering ninety instead of0.90 inflates output a hundredfold, while omitting the time conversion confuses power and energy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分清機械、發電機與總效率的定義，避免把同一損失計算兩遍。以每步流量和淨水頭算功率，積分成電能後對照電表，同時保留啟停、輔機與不可運轉區域的獨立紀錄。","textEn":"Distinguish mechanical, generator and overall efficiency to avoid duplicated losses. Compute each step’s power from discharge and net head, integrate to energy and compare with meters while separately retaining starts, auxiliary loads and prohibited operating regions.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分清機械、發電機與總效率的定義，避免把同一損失計算兩遍。以每步流量和淨水頭算功率，積分成電能後對照電表，同時保留啟停、輔機與不可運轉區域的獨立紀錄。","textEn":"Distinguish mechanical, generator and overall efficiency to avoid duplicated losses. Compute each step’s power from discharge and net head, integrate to energy and compare with meters while separately retaining starts, auxiliary loads and prohibited operating regions.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「發電功率與輸出」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Generating power and output\"?","options":["分清機械、發電機與總效率的定義，避免把同一損失計算兩遍。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要日終上庫水位正確就不需要檢查下庫逐時水量。"],"optionsEn":["Distinguish mechanical, generator and overall efficiency to avoid duplicated losses.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A correct final upper-reservoir level removes any need to check lower-reservoir storage through time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分清機械、發電機與總效率的定義，避免把同一損失計算兩遍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Distinguish mechanical, generator and overall efficiency to avoid duplicated losses. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b258-v15-16","title":"發電功率與輸出：失效診斷","titleEn":"Generating power and output: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「發電功率與輸出」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Generating power and output” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將百分之九十直接代成九十會放大百倍，忽略功率與電能的時間轉換則使排程帳本失衡。用額定效率覆蓋全部負載，也可能系統性高估低負載輸出。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Entering ninety instead of0.90 inflates output a hundredfold, while omitting the time conversion confuses power and energy. Extending rated efficiency to every load can systematically overstate output away from the reference condition. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設單一工況ρ=1000kg/m³、Q=100m³/s、淨水頭385m、總效率0.90，P=ρgQHη=339.9165MW。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: P=ρgQHη=339.9165MW at this stated operating point.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「額定發電容量足夠就保證任意水位都能連續輸出相同功率。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate nameplate capacity guarantees identical continuous output at any reservoir level.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將百分之九十直接代成九十會放大百倍，忽略功率與電能的時間轉換則使排程帳本失衡。用額定效率覆蓋全部負載，也可能系統性高估低負載輸出。","textEn":"Entering ninety instead of0.90 inflates output a hundredfold, while omitting the time conversion confuses power and energy. Extending rated efficiency to every load can systematically overstate output away from the reference condition.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「發電功率與輸出」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Generating power and output\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","將百分之九十直接代成九十會放大百倍，忽略功率與電能的時間轉換則使排程帳本失衡。","抽水效率越低時用電需求反而應該越小。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Entering ninety instead of0.90 inflates output a hundredfold, while omitting the time conversion confuses power and energy.","Lower pumping efficiency should reduce the electrical input required for the same lift and flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將百分之九十直接代成九十會放大百倍，忽略功率與電能的時間轉換則使排程帳本失衡。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Entering ninety instead of0.90 inflates output a hundredfold, while omitting the time conversion confuses power and energy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b258-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「抽水輸入與損失」與「往返效率的邊界」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pumping input and losses\" and \"Round-trip efficiency boundaries\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b258-v15-17","title":"抽水輸入與損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pumping input and losses: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「抽水輸入與損失」如何影響抽蓄水庫水位調度的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pumping input and losses” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-level scheduling for pumped storage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"抽水必須提供提升水體與克服損失所需的能量，因此電輸入除以效率而不是乘以效率。泵的穩定運轉範圍、可變速能力及轉換時間會影響流量是否可調；能源帳本可比較方案，但不能把連續公式直接當成每座固定轉速機組的控制命令。 假設抽水流量100m³/s、總揚程415m、電至水效率0.88，Pin=1000×9.81×100×415/0.88=462.631MW。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「抽水輸入與損失」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pumping input must cover both elevation gain and hydraulic losses, so electrical demand divides by efficiency rather than multiplying it. Stable pump range, speed flexibility and mode-transition time determine whether discharge can actually be varied. An energy ledger can compare options without turning a continuous formula into an operating command for every fixed-speed unit. Assume pumping discharge100m³/s, total lift415m and electricity-to-water efficiency0.88. Pin=1000×9.81×100×415/0.88=462.631MW, excluding any separately modeled auxiliaries. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pumping input and losses” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「抽水效率越低時用電需求反而應該越小。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Lower pumping efficiency should reduce the electrical input required for the same lift and flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「抽水輸入與損失」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pumping input and losses”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-17-k1","title":"抽水輸入與損失","titleEn":"Pumping input and losses","text":"抽水必須提供提升水體與克服損失所需的能量，因此電輸入除以效率而不是乘以效率。泵的穩定運轉範圍、可變速能力及轉換時間會影響流量是否可調；能源帳本可比較方案，但不能把連續公式直接當成每座固定轉速機組的控制命令。","textEn":"Pumping input must cover both elevation gain and hydraulic losses, so electrical demand divides by efficiency rather than multiplying it. Stable pump range, speed flexibility and mode-transition time determine whether discharge can actually be varied.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：抽水效率越低時用電需求反而應該越小。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Lower pumping efficiency should reduce the electrical input required for the same lift and flow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「抽水輸入與損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pumping input and losses\" is correct?","options":["抽水效率越低時用電需求反而應該越小。","只要輸出電量除以當日抽水電量超過一就證明儲能效率超過百分之百。","抽水必須提供提升水體與克服損失所需的能量，因此電輸入除以效率而不是乘以效率。"],"optionsEn":["Lower pumping efficiency should reduce the electrical input required for the same lift and flow.","Output exceeding the same day’s pumping input proves a storage efficiency above one hundred percent.","Pumping input must cover both elevation gain and hydraulic losses, so electrical demand divides by efficiency rather than multiplying it."],"answer":2,"explanation":"抽水必須提供提升水體與克服損失所需的能量，因此電輸入除以效率而不是乘以效率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pumping input must cover both elevation gain and hydraulic losses, so electrical demand divides by efficiency rather than multiplying it. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b258-v15-18","title":"抽水輸入與損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Pumping input and losses: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「抽水輸入與損失」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pumping input and losses” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設抽水流量100m³/s、總揚程415m、電至水效率0.88，Pin=1000×9.81×100×415/0.88=462.631MW。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume pumping discharge100m³/s, total lift415m and electricity-to-water efficiency0.88. Pin=1000×9.81×100×415/0.88=462.631MW, excluding any separately modeled auxiliaries. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在同一能量邊界記錄泵輸入與水體得到的能量，標註效率是否已含馬達及變頻設備。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record pump input and water-energy gain across the same boundary, noting whether motor and converter losses are included.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設抽水流量100m³/s、總揚程415m、電至水效率0.88，Pin=1000×9.81×100×415/0.88=462.631MW。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume pumping discharge100m³/s, total lift415m and electricity-to-water efficiency0.88. Pin=1000×9.81×100×415/0.88=462.631MW, excluding any separately modeled auxiliaries.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「抽水輸入與損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pumping input and losses\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","爬坡期間總水量正確就能證明任何閥門動作都不會產生水錘。","同一份預留水量可以同時保證任意多個獨立備援服務。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","A correct total ramp volume proves that every associated valve movement is free of water hammer.","The same reserved water can simultaneously guarantee any number of independent backup services."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b258-v15-19","title":"抽水輸入與損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pumping input and losses: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「抽水輸入與損失」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pumping input and losses” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在同一能量邊界記錄泵輸入與水體得到的能量，標註效率是否已含馬達及變頻設備。檢查機組曲線與模式切換時段，將不可行的中間流量排除，再用電表積分核對假設效率。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record pump input and water-energy gain across the same boundary, noting whether motor and converter losses are included. Check machine curves and mode transitions, exclude infeasible intermediate flows and compare metered energy with the assumed aggregate efficiency. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在同一能量邊界記錄泵輸入與水體得到的能量，標註效率是否已含馬達及變頻設備。檢查機組曲線與模式切換時段，將不可行的中間流量排除，再用電表積分核對假設效率。","observationEn":"Site practice: Record pump input and water-energy gain across the same boundary, noting whether motor and converter losses are included. Check machine curves and mode transitions, exclude infeasible intermediate flows and compare metered energy with the assumed aggregate efficiency.","failure":"注意干擾：將效率相乘會得到比水力需求還小的電輸入，違反能量守恆。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Multiplying by efficiency produces electrical input below the water-energy requirement and violates conservation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在同一能量邊界記錄泵輸入與水體得到的能量，標註效率是否已含馬達及變頻設備。檢查機組曲線與模式切換時段，將不可行的中間流量排除，再用電表積分核對假設效率。","textEn":"Record pump input and water-energy gain across the same boundary, noting whether motor and converter losses are included. Check machine curves and mode transitions, exclude infeasible intermediate flows and compare metered energy with the assumed aggregate efficiency.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在同一能量邊界記錄泵輸入與水體得到的能量，標註效率是否已含馬達及變頻設備。檢查機組曲線與模式切換時段，將不可行的中間流量排除，再用電表積分核對假設效率。","textEn":"Record pump input and water-energy gain across the same boundary, noting whether motor and converter losses are included. Check machine curves and mode transitions, exclude infeasible intermediate flows and compare metered energy with the assumed aggregate efficiency.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「抽水輸入與損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pumping input and losses\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在同一能量邊界記錄泵輸入與水體得到的能量，標註效率是否已含馬達及變頻設備。","同樣的移水量在上下庫必定造成完全相同的水位變化。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Record pump input and water-energy gain across the same boundary, noting whether motor and converter losses are included.","The same transferred volume must produce identical level changes in both reservoirs."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在同一能量邊界記錄泵輸入與水體得到的能量，標註效率是否已含馬達及變頻設備。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record pump input and water-energy gain across the same boundary, noting whether motor and converter losses are included. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b258-v15-20","title":"抽水輸入與損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pumping input and losses: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「抽水輸入與損失」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pumping input and losses” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將效率相乘會得到比水力需求還小的電輸入，違反能量守恆。若輔機已含在總效率又再扣一次，亦會錯估整個循環的損失與可回收電量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Multiplying by efficiency produces electrical input below the water-energy requirement and violates conservation. Counting auxiliaries both within aggregate efficiency and separately also misstates cycle loss and recoverable electrical output. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設抽水流量100m³/s、總揚程415m、電至水效率0.88，Pin=1000×9.81×100×415/0.88=462.631MW。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Pin=1000×9.81×100×415/0.88=462.631MW, excluding any separately modeled auxiliaries.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「抽水效率越低時用電需求反而應該越小。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Lower pumping efficiency should reduce the electrical input required for the same lift and flow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將效率相乘會得到比水力需求還小的電輸入，違反能量守恆。若輔機已含在總效率又再扣一次，亦會錯估整個循環的損失與可回收電量。","textEn":"Multiplying by efficiency produces electrical input below the water-energy requirement and violates conservation. Counting auxiliaries both within aggregate efficiency and separately also misstates cycle loss and recoverable electrical output.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「抽水輸入與損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pumping input and losses\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","只要輸出電量除以當日抽水電量超過一就證明儲能效率超過百分之百。","將效率相乘會得到比水力需求還小的電輸入，違反能量守恆。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Output exceeding the same day’s pumping input proves a storage efficiency above one hundred percent.","Multiplying by efficiency produces electrical input below the water-energy requirement and violates conservation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將效率相乘會得到比水力需求還小的電輸入，違反能量守恆。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Multiplying by efficiency produces electrical input below the water-energy requirement and violates conservation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b258-v15-21","title":"往返效率的邊界：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Round-trip efficiency boundaries: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「往返效率的邊界」如何影響抽蓄水庫水位調度的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Round-trip efficiency boundaries” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-level scheduling for pumped storage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"往返效率應以完整且一致的週期比較輸入與輸出，起終庫存不同時不能把借用的水能誤當效率提升。定水頭理想化下兩個方向效率相乘很方便，但水頭損失和輔機仍要說明；不同計量邊界的結果不可直接排名優劣。 假設相同定水頭且起終庫存相同，抽水效率0.88、發電效率0.90，往返ηrt=0.88×0.90=0.792即79.2%。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「往返效率的邊界」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Round-trip efficiency compares input and output over a complete cycle with consistent boundaries. Different terminal storage can make borrowed water energy look like improved efficiency. Multiplying directional efficiencies is convenient under equal constant head, but hydraulic loss and auxiliaries must be stated, and values measured across different boundaries should not be ranked as equivalent. Assume equal constant head and identical initial and final storage. Pumping efficiency0.88 and generating efficiency0.90 give round-tripηrt=0.792, or79.2%. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Round-trip efficiency boundaries” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要輸出電量除以當日抽水電量超過一就證明儲能效率超過百分之百。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Output exceeding the same day’s pumping input proves a storage efficiency above one hundred percent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「往返效率的邊界」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Round-trip efficiency boundaries”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-21-k1","title":"往返效率的邊界","titleEn":"Round-trip efficiency boundaries","text":"往返效率應以完整且一致的週期比較輸入與輸出，起終庫存不同時不能把借用的水能誤當效率提升。定水頭理想化下兩個方向效率相乘很方便，但水頭損失和輔機仍要說明；不同計量邊界的結果不可直接排名優劣。","textEn":"Round-trip efficiency compares input and output over a complete cycle with consistent boundaries. Different terminal storage can make borrowed water energy look like improved efficiency.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要輸出電量除以當日抽水電量超過一就證明儲能效率超過百分之百。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Output exceeding the same day’s pumping input proves a storage efficiency above one hundred percent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「往返效率的邊界」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Round-trip efficiency boundaries\" is correct?","options":["往返效率應以完整且一致的週期比較輸入與輸出，起終庫存不同時不能把借用的水能誤當效率提升。","只要輸出電量除以當日抽水電量超過一就證明儲能效率超過百分之百。","只要上庫尚未排空就可以維持額定功率直到最後一滴水。"],"optionsEn":["Round-trip efficiency compares input and output over a complete cycle with consistent boundaries.","Output exceeding the same day’s pumping input proves a storage efficiency above one hundred percent.","Rated power can be maintained until the upper reservoir is completely empty."],"answer":0,"explanation":"往返效率應以完整且一致的週期比較輸入與輸出，起終庫存不同時不能把借用的水能誤當效率提升。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Round-trip efficiency compares input and output over a complete cycle with consistent boundaries. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b258-v15-22","title":"往返效率的邊界：定量估算","titleEn":"Round-trip efficiency boundaries: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「往返效率的邊界」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Round-trip efficiency boundaries” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設相同定水頭且起終庫存相同，抽水效率0.88、發電效率0.90，往返ηrt=0.88×0.90=0.792即79.2%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume equal constant head and identical initial and final storage. Pumping efficiency0.88 and generating efficiency0.90 give round-tripηrt=0.792, or79.2%. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：列出週期起終兩庫水位、輸入電能與輸出電能，校正外來水量造成的能量改變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: List initial and final levels in both reservoirs and metered input and output, correcting for energy introduced by external water.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設相同定水頭且起終庫存相同，抽水效率0.88、發電效率0.90，往返ηrt=0.88×0.90=0.792即79.2%。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume equal constant head and identical initial and final storage. Pumping efficiency0.88 and generating efficiency0.90 give round-tripηrt=0.792, or79.2%.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「往返效率的邊界」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Round-trip efficiency boundaries\", which statement holds?","options":["封閉循環抽蓄完全不會受到降雨、蒸發或滲漏影響。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","只要日終上庫水位正確就不需要檢查下庫逐時水量。"],"optionsEn":["Closed-loop pumped storage is completely unaffected by rainfall, evaporation or seepage.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","A correct final upper-reservoir level removes any need to check lower-reservoir storage through time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b258-v15-23","title":"往返效率的邊界：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Round-trip efficiency boundaries: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「往返效率的邊界」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Round-trip efficiency boundaries” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"列出週期起終兩庫水位、輸入電能與輸出電能，校正外來水量造成的能量改變。註明是否計入待機及變壓器損失，只有邊界相同時才比較往返效率，並保留原始電表時間區間。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"List initial and final levels in both reservoirs and metered input and output, correcting for energy introduced by external water. State treatment of standby and transformer losses and compare round-trip figures only across matching boundaries and time intervals. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：列出週期起終兩庫水位、輸入電能與輸出電能，校正外來水量造成的能量改變。註明是否計入待機及變壓器損失，只有邊界相同時才比較往返效率，並保留原始電表時間區間。","observationEn":"Site practice: List initial and final levels in both reservoirs and metered input and output, correcting for energy introduced by external water. State treatment of standby and transformer losses and compare round-trip figures only across matching boundaries and time intervals.","failure":"注意干擾：若日終上庫比起初低，額外發電可能只是消耗庫存。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ending with a lower upper reservoir can add generation by consuming inventory. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"列出週期起終兩庫水位、輸入電能與輸出電能，校正外來水量造成的能量改變。註明是否計入待機及變壓器損失，只有邊界相同時才比較往返效率，並保留原始電表時間區間。","textEn":"List initial and final levels in both reservoirs and metered input and output, correcting for energy introduced by external water. State treatment of standby and transformer losses and compare round-trip figures only across matching boundaries and time intervals.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"列出週期起終兩庫水位、輸入電能與輸出電能，校正外來水量造成的能量改變。註明是否計入待機及變壓器損失，只有邊界相同時才比較往返效率，並保留原始電表時間區間。","textEn":"List initial and final levels in both reservoirs and metered input and output, correcting for energy introduced by external water. State treatment of standby and transformer losses and compare round-trip figures only across matching boundaries and time intervals.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「往返效率的邊界」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Round-trip efficiency boundaries\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","毛水頭與機組淨水頭在所有流量下都完全相等。","列出週期起終兩庫水位、輸入電能與輸出電能，校正外來水量造成的能量改變。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Gross reservoir head and machine net head are equal at every discharge.","List initial and final levels in both reservoirs and metered input and output, correcting for energy introduced by external water."],"answer":2,"explanation":"列出週期起終兩庫水位、輸入電能與輸出電能，校正外來水量造成的能量改變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"List initial and final levels in both reservoirs and metered input and output, correcting for energy introduced by external water. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b258-v15-24","title":"往返效率的邊界：失效診斷","titleEn":"Round-trip efficiency boundaries: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「往返效率的邊界」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Round-trip efficiency boundaries” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若日終上庫比起初低，額外發電可能只是消耗庫存。把這部分輸出除以當日抽水電量會出現虛高甚至超過百分之百的結果，卻不是無損儲能。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ending with a lower upper reservoir can add generation by consuming inventory. Dividing that output by only the day’s pumping input yields inflated or even above-unity efficiency without demonstrating lossless storage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設相同定水頭且起終庫存相同，抽水效率0.88、發電效率0.90，往返ηrt=0.88×0.90=0.792即79.2%。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Pumping efficiency0.88 and generating efficiency0.90 give round-tripηrt=0.792, or79.2%.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要輸出電量除以當日抽水電量超過一就證明儲能效率超過百分之百。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Output exceeding the same day’s pumping input proves a storage efficiency above one hundred percent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若日終上庫比起初低，額外發電可能只是消耗庫存。把這部分輸出除以當日抽水電量會出現虛高甚至超過百分之百的結果，卻不是無損儲能。","textEn":"Ending with a lower upper reservoir can add generation by consuming inventory. Dividing that output by only the day’s pumping input yields inflated or even above-unity efficiency without demonstrating lossless storage.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「往返效率的邊界」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Round-trip efficiency boundaries\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若日終上庫比起初低，額外發電可能只是消耗庫存。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","只要上庫尚未排空就可以維持額定功率直到最後一滴水。"],"optionsEn":["Ending with a lower upper reservoir can add generation by consuming inventory.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Rated power can be maintained until the upper reservoir is completely empty."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若日終上庫比起初低，額外發電可能只是消耗庫存。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ending with a lower upper reservoir can add generation by consuming inventory. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b258-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「可用水量與時數」與「爬坡流量積分」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Usable volume and duration\" and \"Integrating flow ramps\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b258-v15-25","title":"可用水量與時數：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Usable volume and duration: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「可用水量與時數」如何影響抽蓄水庫水位調度的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Usable volume and duration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-level scheduling for pumped storage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"儲能時數受可移動水量及可接受流量共同限制，不等同於水庫總容積除以任意大流量。死水位、下庫空間、最低淹沒深度和保留需求會縮小可用範圍；長時間輸出還會改變水頭，所以等流量時數只提供第一層水量檢核。 假設已扣保留量的可移水量720000m³、定流量100m³/s，t=720000/100=7200s即2h；不保證定功率兩小時。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「可用水量與時數」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Storage duration is limited by transferable water and feasible discharge, not total reservoir volume divided by any desired flow. Dead storage, lower-reservoir room, intake submergence and reserved water reduce the usable range. Head changes during a long release, so constant-discharge duration provides only the first water-balance check rather than constant-power endurance. Assume transferable volume720000m³ after reservations and constant discharge100m³/s. Duration7200s equals2h, without guaranteeing constant electrical power throughout. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Usable volume and duration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要上庫尚未排空就可以維持額定功率直到最後一滴水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Rated power can be maintained until the upper reservoir is completely empty.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「可用水量與時數」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Usable volume and duration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-25-k1","title":"可用水量與時數","titleEn":"Usable volume and duration","text":"儲能時數受可移動水量及可接受流量共同限制，不等同於水庫總容積除以任意大流量。死水位、下庫空間、最低淹沒深度和保留需求會縮小可用範圍；長時間輸出還會改變水頭，所以等流量時數只提供第一層水量檢核。","textEn":"Storage duration is limited by transferable water and feasible discharge, not total reservoir volume divided by any desired flow. Dead storage, lower-reservoir room, intake submergence and reserved water reduce the usable range.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要上庫尚未排空就可以維持額定功率直到最後一滴水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Rated power can be maintained until the upper reservoir is completely empty. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「可用水量與時數」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Usable volume and duration\" is correct?","options":["只要上庫尚未排空就可以維持額定功率直到最後一滴水。","儲能時數受可移動水量及可接受流量共同限制，不等同於水庫總容積除以任意大流量。","爬坡期間總水量正確就能證明任何閥門動作都不會產生水錘。"],"optionsEn":["Rated power can be maintained until the upper reservoir is completely empty.","Storage duration is limited by transferable water and feasible discharge, not total reservoir volume divided by any desired flow.","A correct total ramp volume proves that every associated valve movement is free of water hammer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"儲能時數受可移動水量及可接受流量共同限制，不等同於水庫總容積除以任意大流量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Storage duration is limited by transferable water and feasible discharge, not total reservoir volume divided by any desired flow. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b258-v15-26","title":"可用水量與時數：定量估算","titleEn":"Usable volume and duration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「可用水量與時數」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Usable volume and duration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設已扣保留量的可移水量720000m³、定流量100m³/s，t=720000/100=7200s即2h；不保證定功率兩小時。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume transferable volume720000m³ after reservations and constant discharge100m³/s. Duration7200s equals2h, without guaranteeing constant electrical power throughout. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從上下庫限制交集求可移水量，逐項列出死庫容與保留用途，避免直接用最大庫容。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Derive transferable volume from the intersection of both reservoirs’ constraints, explicitly subtracting dead storage and reservations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設已扣保留量的可移水量720000m³、定流量100m³/s，t=720000/100=7200s即2h；不保證定功率兩小時。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume transferable volume720000m³ after reservations and constant discharge100m³/s. Duration7200s equals2h, without guaranteeing constant electrical power throughout.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「可用水量與時數」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Usable volume and duration\", which statement holds?","options":["同一份預留水量可以同時保證任意多個獨立備援服務。","同樣的移水量在上下庫必定造成完全相同的水位變化。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["The same reserved water can simultaneously guarantee any number of independent backup services.","The same transferred volume must produce identical level changes in both reservoirs.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b258-v15-27","title":"可用水量與時數：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Usable volume and duration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「可用水量與時數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Usable volume and duration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從上下庫限制交集求可移水量，逐項列出死庫容與保留用途，避免直接用最大庫容。沿兩小時路徑更新水頭和效率，檢查下庫、進水淹沒及機組界限，最後才給出可交付電能。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Derive transferable volume from the intersection of both reservoirs’ constraints, explicitly subtracting dead storage and reservations. Update head and efficiency along the two-hour path, checking lower storage, intake submergence and machine limits before reporting deliverable energy. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：從上下庫限制交集求可移水量，逐項列出死庫容與保留用途，避免直接用最大庫容。沿兩小時路徑更新水頭和效率，檢查下庫、進水淹沒及機組界限，最後才給出可交付電能。","observationEn":"Site practice: Derive transferable volume from the intersection of both reservoirs’ constraints, explicitly subtracting dead storage and reservations. Update head and efficiency along the two-hour path, checking lower storage, intake submergence and machine limits before reporting deliverable energy.","failure":"注意干擾：上庫仍有水不代表下庫還有接收空間，最低進水淹沒也可能先被觸及。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Water remaining upstream does not imply space downstream, and minimum intake submergence may bind first. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從上下庫限制交集求可移水量，逐項列出死庫容與保留用途，避免直接用最大庫容。沿兩小時路徑更新水頭和效率，檢查下庫、進水淹沒及機組界限，最後才給出可交付電能。","textEn":"Derive transferable volume from the intersection of both reservoirs’ constraints, explicitly subtracting dead storage and reservations. Update head and efficiency along the two-hour path, checking lower storage, intake submergence and machine limits before reporting deliverable energy.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"從上下庫限制交集求可移水量，逐項列出死庫容與保留用途，避免直接用最大庫容。沿兩小時路徑更新水頭和效率，檢查下庫、進水淹沒及機組界限，最後才給出可交付電能。","textEn":"Derive transferable volume from the intersection of both reservoirs’ constraints, explicitly subtracting dead storage and reservations. Update head and efficiency along the two-hour path, checking lower storage, intake submergence and machine limits before reporting deliverable energy.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「可用水量與時數」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Usable volume and duration\"?","options":["從上下庫限制交集求可移水量，逐項列出死庫容與保留用途，避免直接用最大庫容。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","額定發電容量足夠就保證任意水位都能連續輸出相同功率。"],"optionsEn":["Derive transferable volume from the intersection of both reservoirs’ constraints, explicitly subtracting dead storage and reservations.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adequate nameplate capacity guarantees identical continuous output at any reservoir level."],"answer":0,"explanation":"從上下庫限制交集求可移水量，逐項列出死庫容與保留用途，避免直接用最大庫容。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Derive transferable volume from the intersection of both reservoirs’ constraints, explicitly subtracting dead storage and reservations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b258-v15-28","title":"可用水量與時數：失效診斷","titleEn":"Usable volume and duration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「可用水量與時數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Usable volume and duration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"上庫仍有水不代表下庫還有接收空間，最低進水淹沒也可能先被觸及。將定流量的時數宣稱為額定功率時數，會忽略逐步減少的水頭及效率變動。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Water remaining upstream does not imply space downstream, and minimum intake submergence may bind first. Reporting constant-flow duration as rated-power endurance ignores falling head and changing efficiency during release. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設已扣保留量的可移水量720000m³、定流量100m³/s，t=720000/100=7200s即2h；不保證定功率兩小時。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Duration7200s equals2h, without guaranteeing constant electrical power throughout.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要上庫尚未排空就可以維持額定功率直到最後一滴水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Rated power can be maintained until the upper reservoir is completely empty.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"上庫仍有水不代表下庫還有接收空間，最低進水淹沒也可能先被觸及。將定流量的時數宣稱為額定功率時數，會忽略逐步減少的水頭及效率變動。","textEn":"Water remaining upstream does not imply space downstream, and minimum intake submergence may bind first. Reporting constant-flow duration as rated-power endurance ignores falling head and changing efficiency during release.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「可用水量與時數」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Usable volume and duration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","上庫仍有水不代表下庫還有接收空間，最低進水淹沒也可能先被觸及。","爬坡期間總水量正確就能證明任何閥門動作都不會產生水錘。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Water remaining upstream does not imply space downstream, and minimum intake submergence may bind first.","A correct total ramp volume proves that every associated valve movement is free of water hammer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"上庫仍有水不代表下庫還有接收空間，最低進水淹沒也可能先被觸及。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Water remaining upstream does not imply space downstream, and minimum intake submergence may bind first. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b258-v15-29","title":"爬坡流量積分：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Integrating flow ramps: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「爬坡流量積分」如何影響抽蓄水庫水位調度的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Integrating flow ramps” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-level scheduling for pumped storage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"排程時間步內的流量若持續變化，採末端值代表整段會錯估移水量。線性爬坡可用梯形積分，但真實閥門和機組反應未必線性；較慢的水量排程也不能取代水錘檢查，因為相同總移水量可能對應完全不同的瞬態壓力。 假設流量在300s內由0線性升至100m³/s，V=(0+100)×300/2=15000m³；此為水量積分而非水錘驗算。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「爬坡流量積分」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A changing discharge should not be represented by its final value over the whole interval. A linear ramp permits trapezoidal integration, although real actuators and machines may respond nonlinearly. Slow scheduling calculations do not replace water-hammer checks because equal transferred volume can arise from very different pressure-transient histories in the waterway. Assume discharge rises linearly from0 to100m³/s in300s. Transferred V=15000m³ by trapezoidal integration, not a water-hammer assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Integrating flow ramps” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「爬坡期間總水量正確就能證明任何閥門動作都不會產生水錘。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A correct total ramp volume proves that every associated valve movement is free of water hammer.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「爬坡流量積分」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Integrating flow ramps”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-29-k1","title":"爬坡流量積分","titleEn":"Integrating flow ramps","text":"排程時間步內的流量若持續變化，採末端值代表整段會錯估移水量。線性爬坡可用梯形積分，但真實閥門和機組反應未必線性；較慢的水量排程也不能取代水錘檢查，因為相同總移水量可能對應完全不同的瞬態壓力。","textEn":"A changing discharge should not be represented by its final value over the whole interval. A linear ramp permits trapezoidal integration, although real actuators and machines may respond nonlinearly.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：爬坡期間總水量正確就能證明任何閥門動作都不會產生水錘。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A correct total ramp volume proves that every associated valve movement is free of water hammer. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「爬坡流量積分」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Integrating flow ramps\" is correct?","options":["爬坡期間總水量正確就能證明任何閥門動作都不會產生水錘。","封閉循環抽蓄完全不會受到降雨、蒸發或滲漏影響。","排程時間步內的流量若持續變化，採末端值代表整段會錯估移水量。"],"optionsEn":["A correct total ramp volume proves that every associated valve movement is free of water hammer.","Closed-loop pumped storage is completely unaffected by rainfall, evaporation or seepage.","A changing discharge should not be represented by its final value over the whole interval."],"answer":2,"explanation":"排程時間步內的流量若持續變化，採末端值代表整段會錯估移水量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A changing discharge should not be represented by its final value over the whole interval. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b258-v15-30","title":"爬坡流量積分：定量估算","titleEn":"Integrating flow ramps: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「爬坡流量積分」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Integrating flow ramps” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設流量在300s內由0線性升至100m³/s，V=(0+100)×300/2=15000m³；此為水量積分而非水錘驗算。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume discharge rises linearly from0 to100m³/s in300s. Transferred V=15000m³ by trapezoidal integration, not a water-hammer assessment. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保留流量歷時並檢查爬坡形狀，將梯形積分與較短時間步積分比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Retain the discharge history, check ramp shape and compare trapezoidal integration with smaller time steps.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設流量在300s內由0線性升至100m³/s，V=(0+100)×300/2=15000m³；此為水量積分而非水錘驗算。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume discharge rises linearly from0 to100m³/s in300s. Transferred V=15000m³ by trapezoidal integration, not a water-hammer assessment.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「爬坡流量積分」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Integrating flow ramps\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","只要日終上庫水位正確就不需要檢查下庫逐時水量。","毛水頭與機組淨水頭在所有流量下都完全相等。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","A correct final upper-reservoir level removes any need to check lower-reservoir storage through time.","Gross reservoir head and machine net head are equal at every discharge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b258-v15-31","title":"爬坡流量積分：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Integrating flow ramps: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「爬坡流量積分」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Integrating flow ramps” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保留流量歷時並檢查爬坡形狀，將梯形積分與較短時間步積分比較。另把閥位、轉速及壓力歷時送到瞬態分析，清楚標註此水量帳本沒有證明閥門速度或壓力變化可被接受。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Retain the discharge history, check ramp shape and compare trapezoidal integration with smaller time steps. Examine valve, speed and pressure histories in a separate transient analysis, explicitly recording that the volume ledger does not approve actuator rates or pressure excursions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保留流量歷時並檢查爬坡形狀，將梯形積分與較短時間步積分比較。另把閥位、轉速及壓力歷時送到瞬態分析，清楚標註此水量帳本沒有證明閥門速度或壓力變化可被接受。","observationEn":"Site practice: Retain the discharge history, check ramp shape and compare trapezoidal integration with smaller time steps. Examine valve, speed and pressure histories in a separate transient analysis, explicitly recording that the volume ledger does not approve actuator rates or pressure excursions.","failure":"注意干擾：以末端一百立方米每秒乘全段會把移水量加倍，造成下一時段庫位預測偏移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using the final discharge over the full interval doubles this transferred volume and biases the next storage estimate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保留流量歷時並檢查爬坡形狀，將梯形積分與較短時間步積分比較。另把閥位、轉速及壓力歷時送到瞬態分析，清楚標註此水量帳本沒有證明閥門速度或壓力變化可被接受。","textEn":"Retain the discharge history, check ramp shape and compare trapezoidal integration with smaller time steps. Examine valve, speed and pressure histories in a separate transient analysis, explicitly recording that the volume ledger does not approve actuator rates or pressure excursions.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保留流量歷時並檢查爬坡形狀，將梯形積分與較短時間步積分比較。另把閥位、轉速及壓力歷時送到瞬態分析，清楚標註此水量帳本沒有證明閥門速度或壓力變化可被接受。","textEn":"Retain the discharge history, check ramp shape and compare trapezoidal integration with smaller time steps. Examine valve, speed and pressure histories in a separate transient analysis, explicitly recording that the volume ledger does not approve actuator rates or pressure excursions.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「爬坡流量積分」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Integrating flow ramps\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","保留流量歷時並檢查爬坡形狀，將梯形積分與較短時間步積分比較。","抽水效率越低時用電需求反而應該越小。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Retain the discharge history, check ramp shape and compare trapezoidal integration with smaller time steps.","Lower pumping efficiency should reduce the electrical input required for the same lift and flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"保留流量歷時並檢查爬坡形狀，將梯形積分與較短時間步積分比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Retain the discharge history, check ramp shape and compare trapezoidal integration with smaller time steps. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b258-v15-32","title":"爬坡流量積分：失效診斷","titleEn":"Integrating flow ramps: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「爬坡流量積分」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Integrating flow ramps” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以末端一百立方米每秒乘全段會把移水量加倍，造成下一時段庫位預測偏移。即使水量積分正確，短暫快速動作仍可能產生排程模型看不到的壓力波。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using the final discharge over the full interval doubles this transferred volume and biases the next storage estimate. Correct integration still cannot reveal short rapid actions that generate pressure waves outside the scheduling model. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設流量在300s內由0線性升至100m³/s，V=(0+100)×300/2=15000m³；此為水量積分而非水錘驗算。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Transferred V=15000m³ by trapezoidal integration, not a water-hammer assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「爬坡期間總水量正確就能證明任何閥門動作都不會產生水錘。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A correct total ramp volume proves that every associated valve movement is free of water hammer.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以末端一百立方米每秒乘全段會把移水量加倍，造成下一時段庫位預測偏移。即使水量積分正確，短暫快速動作仍可能產生排程模型看不到的壓力波。","textEn":"Using the final discharge over the full interval doubles this transferred volume and biases the next storage estimate. Correct integration still cannot reveal short rapid actions that generate pressure waves outside the scheduling model.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「爬坡流量積分」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Integrating flow ramps\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","封閉循環抽蓄完全不會受到降雨、蒸發或滲漏影響。","以末端一百立方米每秒乘全段會把移水量加倍，造成下一時段庫位預測偏移。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Closed-loop pumped storage is completely unaffected by rainfall, evaporation or seepage.","Using the final discharge over the full interval doubles this transferred volume and biases the next storage estimate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以末端一百立方米每秒乘全段會把移水量加倍，造成下一時段庫位預測偏移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using the final discharge over the full interval doubles this transferred volume and biases the next storage estimate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b258-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「外部水量與封閉循環」與「期末庫存與預留」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"External water and closed loops\" and \"Terminal inventory and reservation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b258-v15-33","title":"外部水量與封閉循環：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"External water and closed loops: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「外部水量與封閉循環」如何影響抽蓄水庫水位調度的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “External water and closed loops” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-level scheduling for pumped storage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"封閉循環表示缺乏持續天然水體連通，並不代表沒有降雨、蒸發、滲漏或補水。這些小流量累積後會改變長期可用庫存，兩庫表面積不同又會造成不對稱損失；調度帳本要分清天氣水量與機組搬移，才能找到真實偏差來源。 假設兩庫合計水面1000000m²、日蒸發0.004m，日損失4000m³；未計降雨與滲漏，不可稱封閉循環零耗水。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「外部水量與封閉循環」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A closed loop lacks an ongoing natural-water connection, but rainfall, evaporation, seepage and makeup water still matter. Small persistent fluxes alter long-term inventory, and different reservoir areas produce unequal losses. Separating weather exchange from machine transfers allows the scheduling ledger to diagnose the actual source of a storage discrepancy rather than assign every change to pumping. Assume combined surface area1000000m² and daily evaporation0.004m. Loss is4000m³/day, excluding rain and seepage; closed-loop does not mean zero water use. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “External water and closed loops” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「封閉循環抽蓄完全不會受到降雨、蒸發或滲漏影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Closed-loop pumped storage is completely unaffected by rainfall, evaporation or seepage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「外部水量與封閉循環」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “External water and closed loops”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-33-k1","title":"外部水量與封閉循環","titleEn":"External water and closed loops","text":"封閉循環表示缺乏持續天然水體連通，並不代表沒有降雨、蒸發、滲漏或補水。這些小流量累積後會改變長期可用庫存，兩庫表面積不同又會造成不對稱損失；調度帳本要分清天氣水量與機組搬移，才能找到真實偏差來源。","textEn":"A closed loop lacks an ongoing natural-water connection, but rainfall, evaporation, seepage and makeup water still matter. Small persistent fluxes alter long-term inventory, and different reservoir areas produce unequal losses.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：封閉循環抽蓄完全不會受到降雨、蒸發或滲漏影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Closed-loop pumped storage is completely unaffected by rainfall, evaporation or seepage. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「外部水量與封閉循環」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"External water and closed loops\" is correct?","options":["封閉循環表示缺乏持續天然水體連通，並不代表沒有降雨、蒸發、滲漏或補水。","封閉循環抽蓄完全不會受到降雨、蒸發或滲漏影響。","同一份預留水量可以同時保證任意多個獨立備援服務。"],"optionsEn":["A closed loop lacks an ongoing natural-water connection, but rainfall, evaporation, seepage and makeup water still matter.","Closed-loop pumped storage is completely unaffected by rainfall, evaporation or seepage.","The same reserved water can simultaneously guarantee any number of independent backup services."],"answer":0,"explanation":"封閉循環表示缺乏持續天然水體連通，並不代表沒有降雨、蒸發、滲漏或補水。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A closed loop lacks an ongoing natural-water connection, but rainfall, evaporation, seepage and makeup water still matter. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b258-v15-34","title":"外部水量與封閉循環：定量估算","titleEn":"External water and closed loops: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「外部水量與封閉循環」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “External water and closed loops” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設兩庫合計水面1000000m²、日蒸發0.004m，日損失4000m³；未計降雨與滲漏，不可稱封閉循環零耗水。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume combined surface area1000000m² and daily evaporation0.004m. Loss is4000m³/day, excluding rain and seepage; closed-loop does not mean zero water use. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將降雨蒸發深度乘當日水面積，核對毫米與米及每日與每秒的換算。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Multiply weather depths by contemporaneous surface area and verify millimeter-to-meter and daily-to-second conversions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設兩庫合計水面1000000m²、日蒸發0.004m，日損失4000m³；未計降雨與滲漏，不可稱封閉循環零耗水。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume combined surface area1000000m² and daily evaporation0.004m. Loss is4000m³/day, excluding rain and seepage; closed-loop does not mean zero water use.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「外部水量與封閉循環」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"External water and closed loops\", which statement holds?","options":["同樣的移水量在上下庫必定造成完全相同的水位變化。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","額定發電容量足夠就保證任意水位都能連續輸出相同功率。"],"optionsEn":["The same transferred volume must produce identical level changes in both reservoirs.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Adequate nameplate capacity guarantees identical continuous output at any reservoir level."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b258-v15-35","title":"外部水量與封閉循環：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"External water and closed loops: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「外部水量與封閉循環」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “External water and closed loops” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將降雨蒸發深度乘當日水面積，核對毫米與米及每日與每秒的換算。把滲漏、補水與量測零漂分開追蹤，以多日總量閉合而非單一水位點判斷是否存在持續庫存損失。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Multiply weather depths by contemporaneous surface area and verify millimeter-to-meter and daily-to-second conversions. Track seepage, makeup and sensor drift separately, using multi-day volume closure rather than one level reading to identify persistent inventory loss. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將降雨蒸發深度乘當日水面積，核對毫米與米及每日與每秒的換算。把滲漏、補水與量測零漂分開追蹤，以多日總量閉合而非單一水位點判斷是否存在持續庫存損失。","observationEn":"Site practice: Multiply weather depths by contemporaneous surface area and verify millimeter-to-meter and daily-to-second conversions. Track seepage, makeup and sensor drift separately, using multi-day volume closure rather than one level reading to identify persistent inventory loss.","failure":"注意干擾：將蒸發列成每次抽水循環的固定損失會讓結果隨排程次數虛增，忽略面積變化又會產生季節偏差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating evaporation as a fixed loss per pumping cycle makes it grow artificially with cycling frequency. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將降雨蒸發深度乘當日水面積，核對毫米與米及每日與每秒的換算。把滲漏、補水與量測零漂分開追蹤，以多日總量閉合而非單一水位點判斷是否存在持續庫存損失。","textEn":"Multiply weather depths by contemporaneous surface area and verify millimeter-to-meter and daily-to-second conversions. Track seepage, makeup and sensor drift separately, using multi-day volume closure rather than one level reading to identify persistent inventory loss.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將降雨蒸發深度乘當日水面積，核對毫米與米及每日與每秒的換算。把滲漏、補水與量測零漂分開追蹤，以多日總量閉合而非單一水位點判斷是否存在持續庫存損失。","textEn":"Multiply weather depths by contemporaneous surface area and verify millimeter-to-meter and daily-to-second conversions. Track seepage, makeup and sensor drift separately, using multi-day volume closure rather than one level reading to identify persistent inventory loss.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「外部水量與封閉循環」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"External water and closed loops\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只要輸出電量除以當日抽水電量超過一就證明儲能效率超過百分之百。","將降雨蒸發深度乘當日水面積，核對毫米與米及每日與每秒的換算。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Output exceeding the same day’s pumping input proves a storage efficiency above one hundred percent.","Multiply weather depths by contemporaneous surface area and verify millimeter-to-meter and daily-to-second conversions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將降雨蒸發深度乘當日水面積，核對毫米與米及每日與每秒的換算。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Multiply weather depths by contemporaneous surface area and verify millimeter-to-meter and daily-to-second conversions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b258-v15-36","title":"外部水量與封閉循環：失效診斷","titleEn":"External water and closed loops: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「外部水量與封閉循環」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “External water and closed loops” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將蒸發列成每次抽水循環的固定損失會讓結果隨排程次數虛增，忽略面積變化又會產生季節偏差。漏水與零漂混在一起時，錯誤補水判斷也可能擴大。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating evaporation as a fixed loss per pumping cycle makes it grow artificially with cycling frequency. Ignoring area variation adds seasonal bias, while confusing leakage with sensor drift can lead to inappropriate makeup estimates. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設兩庫合計水面1000000m²、日蒸發0.004m，日損失4000m³；未計降雨與滲漏，不可稱封閉循環零耗水。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Loss is4000m³/day, excluding rain and seepage; closed-loop does not mean zero water use.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「封閉循環抽蓄完全不會受到降雨、蒸發或滲漏影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Closed-loop pumped storage is completely unaffected by rainfall, evaporation or seepage.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將蒸發列成每次抽水循環的固定損失會讓結果隨排程次數虛增，忽略面積變化又會產生季節偏差。漏水與零漂混在一起時，錯誤補水判斷也可能擴大。","textEn":"Treating evaporation as a fixed loss per pumping cycle makes it grow artificially with cycling frequency. Ignoring area variation adds seasonal bias, while confusing leakage with sensor drift can lead to inappropriate makeup estimates.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「外部水量與封閉循環」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"External water and closed loops\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["將蒸發列成每次抽水循環的固定損失會讓結果隨排程次數虛增，忽略面積變化又會產生季節偏差。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","同一份預留水量可以同時保證任意多個獨立備援服務。"],"optionsEn":["Treating evaporation as a fixed loss per pumping cycle makes it grow artificially with cycling frequency.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The same reserved water can simultaneously guarantee any number of independent backup services."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將蒸發列成每次抽水循環的固定損失會讓結果隨排程次數虛增，忽略面積變化又會產生季節偏差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating evaporation as a fixed loss per pumping cycle makes it grow artificially with cycling frequency. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b258-v15-37","title":"期末庫存與預留：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Terminal inventory and reservation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「期末庫存與預留」如何影響抽蓄水庫水位調度的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Terminal inventory and reservation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Reservoir-level scheduling for pumped storage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"有限時域排程若不約束期末庫存，會把最後一刻耗盡上庫當成最佳結果，卻把下一日需求隱藏起來。預留可用水量與電能不能直接互換，必須考慮當時水頭和可用機組；應明列預留目的以及何時可以釋放，避免重複承諾同一份水。 假設上庫可用800000m³，其中預留200000m³，其他條件允許時最多移出600000m³；兩項服務不能重複使用同一預留量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「期末庫存與預留」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A finite-horizon schedule without a terminal-storage constraint can favor emptying the upper reservoir at the last instant while hiding the following day’s need. Reserved water is not automatically reserved electrical energy because head and unit availability matter. State the purpose and release condition of each reservation to avoid committing the same inventory to multiple services. Assume upper usable storage800000m³ with200000m³ reserved. At most600000m³ is transferable if other constraints permit, without double-allocating the reservation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Terminal inventory and reservation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「同一份預留水量可以同時保證任意多個獨立備援服務。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The same reserved water can simultaneously guarantee any number of independent backup services.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「期末庫存與預留」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Terminal inventory and reservation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-37-k1","title":"期末庫存與預留","titleEn":"Terminal inventory and reservation","text":"有限時域排程若不約束期末庫存，會把最後一刻耗盡上庫當成最佳結果，卻把下一日需求隱藏起來。預留可用水量與電能不能直接互換，必須考慮當時水頭和可用機組；應明列預留目的以及何時可以釋放，避免重複承諾同一份水。","textEn":"A finite-horizon schedule without a terminal-storage constraint can favor emptying the upper reservoir at the last instant while hiding the following day’s need. Reserved water is not automatically reserved electrical energy because head and unit availability matter.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：同一份預留水量可以同時保證任意多個獨立備援服務。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The same reserved water can simultaneously guarantee any number of independent backup services. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「期末庫存與預留」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Terminal inventory and reservation\" is correct?","options":["同一份預留水量可以同時保證任意多個獨立備援服務。","有限時域排程若不約束期末庫存，會把最後一刻耗盡上庫當成最佳結果，卻把下一日需求隱藏起來。","只要日終上庫水位正確就不需要檢查下庫逐時水量。"],"optionsEn":["The same reserved water can simultaneously guarantee any number of independent backup services.","A finite-horizon schedule without a terminal-storage constraint can favor emptying the upper reservoir at the last instant while hiding the following day’s need.","A correct final upper-reservoir level removes any need to check lower-reservoir storage through time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"有限時域排程若不約束期末庫存，會把最後一刻耗盡上庫當成最佳結果，卻把下一日需求隱藏起來。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A finite-horizon schedule without a terminal-storage constraint can favor emptying the upper reservoir at the last instant while hiding the following day’s need. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b258-v15-38","title":"期末庫存與預留：定量估算","titleEn":"Terminal inventory and reservation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「期末庫存與預留」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Terminal inventory and reservation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設上庫可用800000m³，其中預留200000m³，其他條件允許時最多移出600000m³；兩項服務不能重複使用同一預留量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume upper usable storage800000m³ with200000m³ reserved. At most600000m³ is transferable if other constraints permit, without double-allocating the reservation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把期末目標、預留用途與可釋放條件寫成獨立約束，逐步檢查同一水量是否被重複計入不同服務。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Express terminal targets, reserved services and release conditions as separate constraints and check inventory is not allocated twice.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設上庫可用800000m³，其中預留200000m³，其他條件允許時最多移出600000m³；兩項服務不能重複使用同一預留量。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume upper usable storage800000m³ with200000m³ reserved. At most600000m³ is transferable if other constraints permit, without double-allocating the reservation.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「期末庫存與預留」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Terminal inventory and reservation\", which statement holds?","options":["毛水頭與機組淨水頭在所有流量下都完全相等。","抽水效率越低時用電需求反而應該越小。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Gross reservoir head and machine net head are equal at every discharge.","Lower pumping efficiency should reduce the electrical input required for the same lift and flow.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b258-v15-39","title":"期末庫存與預留：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Terminal inventory and reservation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「期末庫存與預留」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Terminal inventory and reservation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把期末目標、預留用途與可釋放條件寫成獨立約束，逐步檢查同一水量是否被重複計入不同服務。將預報入流減少的情境再跑一次，報告未滿足需求而非讓計算暗中借用下一日庫存。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Express terminal targets, reserved services and release conditions as separate constraints and check inventory is not allocated twice. Repeat the schedule with reduced forecast inflow and report unmet demand rather than silently borrowing storage intended for the next day. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把期末目標、預留用途與可釋放條件寫成獨立約束，逐步檢查同一水量是否被重複計入不同服務。將預報入流減少的情境再跑一次，報告未滿足需求而非讓計算暗中借用下一日庫存。","observationEn":"Site practice: Express terminal targets, reserved services and release conditions as separate constraints and check inventory is not allocated twice. Repeat the schedule with reduced forecast inflow and report unmet demand rather than silently borrowing storage intended for the next day.","failure":"注意干擾：完美預報假設會讓預留不足的方案看似可行，期末缺水又會被截斷時域隱藏。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Perfect-forecast assumptions can make inadequate reserves seem feasible, while horizon truncation hides terminal shortage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把期末目標、預留用途與可釋放條件寫成獨立約束，逐步檢查同一水量是否被重複計入不同服務。將預報入流減少的情境再跑一次，報告未滿足需求而非讓計算暗中借用下一日庫存。","textEn":"Express terminal targets, reserved services and release conditions as separate constraints and check inventory is not allocated twice. Repeat the schedule with reduced forecast inflow and report unmet demand rather than silently borrowing storage intended for the next day.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把期末目標、預留用途與可釋放條件寫成獨立約束，逐步檢查同一水量是否被重複計入不同服務。將預報入流減少的情境再跑一次，報告未滿足需求而非讓計算暗中借用下一日庫存。","textEn":"Express terminal targets, reserved services and release conditions as separate constraints and check inventory is not allocated twice. Repeat the schedule with reduced forecast inflow and report unmet demand rather than silently borrowing storage intended for the next day.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「期末庫存與預留」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Terminal inventory and reservation\"?","options":["把期末目標、預留用途與可釋放條件寫成獨立約束，逐步檢查同一水量是否被重複計入不同服務。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要上庫尚未排空就可以維持額定功率直到最後一滴水。"],"optionsEn":["Express terminal targets, reserved services and release conditions as separate constraints and check inventory is not allocated twice.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Rated power can be maintained until the upper reservoir is completely empty."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把期末目標、預留用途與可釋放條件寫成獨立約束，逐步檢查同一水量是否被重複計入不同服務。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Express terminal targets, reserved services and release conditions as separate constraints and check inventory is not allocated twice. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b258-v15-40","title":"期末庫存與預留：失效診斷","titleEn":"Terminal inventory and reservation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b258-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「期末庫存與預留」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Terminal inventory and reservation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"完美預報假設會讓預留不足的方案看似可行，期末缺水又會被截斷時域隱藏。若兩個備援服務同時到來，共用一份預留水量的承諾便無法全部履行。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Perfect-forecast assumptions can make inadequate reserves seem feasible, while horizon truncation hides terminal shortage. If two reserve services arrive together, promises backed by the same water inventory cannot both be fulfilled. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設上庫可用800000m³，其中預留200000m³，其他條件允許時最多移出600000m³；兩項服務不能重複使用同一預留量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: At most600000m³ is transferable if other constraints permit, without double-allocating the reservation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「同一份預留水量可以同時保證任意多個獨立備援服務。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The same reserved water can simultaneously guarantee any number of independent backup services.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b258-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"完美預報假設會讓預留不足的方案看似可行，期末缺水又會被截斷時域隱藏。若兩個備援服務同時到來，共用一份預留水量的承諾便無法全部履行。","textEn":"Perfect-forecast assumptions can make inadequate reserves seem feasible, while horizon truncation hides terminal shortage. If two reserve services arrive together, promises backed by the same water inventory cannot both be fulfilled.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b258-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「期末庫存與預留」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Terminal inventory and reservation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","完美預報假設會讓預留不足的方案看似可行，期末缺水又會被截斷時域隱藏。","只要日終上庫水位正確就不需要檢查下庫逐時水量。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Perfect-forecast assumptions can make inadequate reserves seem feasible, while horizon truncation hides terminal shortage.","A correct final upper-reservoir level removes any need to check lower-reservoir storage through time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"完美預報假設會讓預留不足的方案看似可行，期末缺水又會被截斷時域隱藏。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Perfect-forecast assumptions can make inadequate reserves seem feasible, while horizon truncation hides terminal shortage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v4-related-8aae3d2b752a","v15s-psh-guide","v15s-bath-storage","v15s-elbert-storage","v15s-hydro-structures"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b259","title":"壓力鋼管錨定與支承","titleEn":"Penstock anchorage and supports","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課用完整荷載路徑理解壓力鋼管，而不只套一條薄壁應力公式。十個單元依序分辨環向與軸向力、彎管向量、熱伸縮、滿管重量、跨距反力、滑動摩擦、錨塊基底及減薄檢查，要求每個簡化模型先畫自由體與邊界，再說明未包含的局部殼體、基礎與疲勞問題。","summaryEn":"This course follows the complete penstock load path rather than relying on one thin-wall formula. Ten units distinguish hoop and axial action, elbow vectors, thermal movement, full-pipe weight, span reactions, friction, anchor bearing and wall loss. Each simplified model begins with a free body and boundaries and identifies excluded shell, foundation and fatigue behavior.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-hydraulics","subcategoryTitle":"壩工監測、溢洪與壓力水路","subcategoryTitleEn":"Dam monitoring, spillways and pressure waterways","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-hydraulics","learningTags":["water","water-hydraulics","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-hydraulic","architectureNodes":[["環向薄膜應力","Circumferential membrane stress"],["彎管壓力向量","Elbow pressure vectors"],["完全約束熱應力","Fully restrained thermal stress"],["滑動摩擦與固定點","Sliding friction and fixed points"],["減薄與剩餘厚度","Wall loss and remaining thickness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-hydraulic","labels":["環向薄膜應力","彎管壓力向量","完全約束熱應力","滑動摩擦與固定點","減薄與剩餘厚度"],"labelsEn":["Circumferential membrane stress","Elbow pressure vectors","Fully restrained thermal stress","Sliding friction and fixed points","Wall loss and remaining thickness"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創壓力敏感度：薄壁圓管內徑2m、均勻厚度0.020m，表壓2MPa時環向膜應力為100MPa。如果保持幾何及線彈性假設而壓力增加10%至2.2MPa，應力增為110MPa，增加10%。此線性關係不能證明材料、焊縫或支座仍有足夠餘量。學徒應再列端部軸力、彎管壓力向量和錨塊需求如何同時增加，並檢查壓力峰值是否出自水錘。若發生減薄、塑性或外壓屈曲，原先模型邊界已改變，不能以這個單一百分比概括所有失效機制。","textEn":"Original pressure sensitivity: a thin circular pipe with inner diameter2m and uniform thickness0.020m has hoop membrane stress100MPa at gauge pressure2MPa. Holding geometry and linear-elastic assumptions fixed while increasing pressure10% to2.2MPa raises stress to110MPa, also10%. That proportionality does not demonstrate adequate material, weld or support margin. Apprentices should also trace increased end force, elbow pressure vectors and anchor demands and determine whether the peak is a water-hammer transient. Wall loss, plasticity or external-pressure buckling changes the original model boundary, so one percentage cannot summarize every failure mechanism.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b259-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「環向薄膜應力」與「封閉端軸向作用」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Circumferential membrane stress\" and \"Closed-end axial action\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b259-v15-01","title":"環向薄膜應力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Circumferential membrane stress: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「環向薄膜應力」如何影響壓力鋼管錨定與支承的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Circumferential membrane stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Penstock anchorage and supports”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"圓管內壓使管壁承受環向拉力，薄壁公式可先估量級，但只描述遠離支承與接頭的膜應力。焊接缺陷、橢圓化和局部加勁會改變應力分布，外壓失穩又是另一機制；必須先辨明幾何與壓力方向，不能把一個平均值當成整根鋼管安全證明。 假設薄壁圓管表壓p=2MPa、內徑D=2m、均勻壁厚t=0.020m，σh=pD/(2t)=100MPa；未含局部彎曲。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「環向薄膜應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Internal pressure creates circumferential tension, and a thin-wall estimate gives membrane stress away from supports and connections. Weld defects, ovality and local stiffening alter the distribution, while external-pressure buckling is a different mechanism. Establish geometry and pressure direction before treating a mean stress as evidence about the entire penstock’s structural behavior. Assume thin circular pipe gauge pressure2MPa, inner diameter2m and uniform thickness0.020m. Hoopσh=pD/(2t)=100MPa, excluding local bending. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Circumferential membrane stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均環向應力低於某個數字就能證明所有支座與焊縫都安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A low average hoop stress proves every support and weld is structurally acceptable.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「環向薄膜應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Circumferential membrane stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-01-k1","title":"環向薄膜應力","titleEn":"Circumferential membrane stress","text":"圓管內壓使管壁承受環向拉力，薄壁公式可先估量級，但只描述遠離支承與接頭的膜應力。焊接缺陷、橢圓化和局部加勁會改變應力分布，外壓失穩又是另一機制；必須先辨明幾何與壓力方向，不能把一個平均值當成整根鋼管安全證明。","textEn":"Internal pressure creates circumferential tension, and a thin-wall estimate gives membrane stress away from supports and connections. Weld defects, ovality and local stiffening alter the distribution, while external-pressure buckling is a different mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均環向應力低於某個數字就能證明所有支座與焊縫都安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A low average hoop stress proves every support and weld is structurally acceptable. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「環向薄膜應力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Circumferential membrane stress\" is correct?","options":["平均環向應力低於某個數字就能證明所有支座與焊縫都安全。","圓管內壓使管壁承受環向拉力，薄壁公式可先估量級，但只描述遠離支承與接頭的膜應力。","封閉端公式可直接代表任何固定、埋設或帶伸縮接頭管線的軸向應力。"],"optionsEn":["A low average hoop stress proves every support and weld is structurally acceptable.","Internal pressure creates circumferential tension, and a thin-wall estimate gives membrane stress away from supports and connections.","The closed-end formula directly gives axial stress for every fixed, buried or expansion-jointed pipeline."],"answer":1,"explanation":"圓管內壓使管壁承受環向拉力，薄壁公式可先估量級，但只描述遠離支承與接頭的膜應力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Internal pressure creates circumferential tension, and a thin-wall estimate gives membrane stress away from supports and connections. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b259-v15-02","title":"環向薄膜應力：定量估算","titleEn":"Circumferential membrane stress: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「環向薄膜應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Circumferential membrane stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設薄壁圓管表壓p=2MPa、內徑D=2m、均勻壁厚t=0.020m，σh=pD/(2t)=100MPa；未含局部彎曲。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume thin circular pipe gauge pressure2MPa, inner diameter2m and uniform thickness0.020m. Hoopσh=pD/(2t)=100MPa, excluding local bending. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：畫半圓自由體平衡，核對內徑、有效厚度及表壓使用方式，並計算厚徑比。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw a half-cylinder equilibrium diagram, checking inner diameter, effective thickness and gauge pressure and calculating thickness ratio.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設薄壁圓管表壓p=2MPa、內徑D=2m、均勻壁厚t=0.020m，σh=pD/(2t)=100MPa；未含局部彎曲。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume thin circular pipe gauge pressure2MPa, inner diameter2m and uniform thickness0.020m. Hoopσh=pD/(2t)=100MPa, excluding local bending.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「環向薄膜應力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Circumferential membrane stress\", which statement holds?","options":["算出自由伸長後就可假定任何固定錨塊之間都會發生同樣位移。","管線支座只需要承受鋼材自重而不必考慮管內水重。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Calculated free expansion occurs unchanged between any pair of fixed anchor blocks.","Penstock supports carry only the steel’s own weight and need not consider contained water.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b259-v15-03","title":"環向薄膜應力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Circumferential membrane stress: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「環向薄膜應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Circumferential membrane stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"畫半圓自由體平衡，核對內徑、有效厚度及表壓使用方式，並計算厚徑比。將支座、分岔、焊縫與變厚位置另列局部分析範圍，保留材料和厚度量測資料而不只比較單一應力數字。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw a half-cylinder equilibrium diagram, checking inner diameter, effective thickness and gauge pressure and calculating thickness ratio. Flag supports, branches, welds and thickness transitions for local analysis and retain material and measurement evidence rather than comparing only one stress value. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫半圓自由體平衡，核對內徑、有效厚度及表壓使用方式，並計算厚徑比。將支座、分岔、焊縫與變厚位置另列局部分析範圍，保留材料和厚度量測資料而不只比較單一應力數字。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw a half-cylinder equilibrium diagram, checking inner diameter, effective thickness and gauge pressure and calculating thickness ratio. Flag supports, branches, welds and thickness transitions for local analysis and retain material and measurement evidence rather than comparing only one stress value.","failure":"注意干擾：局部腐蝕孔與焊縫缺陷可能控制承載，平均厚度會掩蓋最弱位置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Local pits and weld flaws may govern strength while mean thickness hides the weakest region. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"畫半圓自由體平衡，核對內徑、有效厚度及表壓使用方式，並計算厚徑比。將支座、分岔、焊縫與變厚位置另列局部分析範圍，保留材料和厚度量測資料而不只比較單一應力數字。","textEn":"Draw a half-cylinder equilibrium diagram, checking inner diameter, effective thickness and gauge pressure and calculating thickness ratio. Flag supports, branches, welds and thickness transitions for local analysis and retain material and measurement evidence rather than comparing only one stress value.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫半圓自由體平衡，核對內徑、有效厚度及表壓使用方式，並計算厚徑比。將支座、分岔、焊縫與變厚位置另列局部分析範圍，保留材料和厚度量測資料而不只比較單一應力數字。","textEn":"Draw a half-cylinder equilibrium diagram, checking inner diameter, effective thickness and gauge pressure and calculating thickness ratio. Flag supports, branches, welds and thickness transitions for local analysis and retain material and measurement evidence rather than comparing only one stress value.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「環向薄膜應力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Circumferential membrane stress\"?","options":["畫半圓自由體平衡，核對內徑、有效厚度及表壓使用方式，並計算厚徑比。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","靜止滑動支座的實際摩擦力在任何時刻都必定等於摩擦係數乘法向力。"],"optionsEn":["Draw a half-cylinder equilibrium diagram, checking inner diameter, effective thickness and gauge pressure and calculating thickness ratio.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Actual friction at a stationary sliding support always equals coefficient times normal force."],"answer":0,"explanation":"畫半圓自由體平衡，核對內徑、有效厚度及表壓使用方式，並計算厚徑比。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw a half-cylinder equilibrium diagram, checking inner diameter, effective thickness and gauge pressure and calculating thickness ratio. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b259-v15-04","title":"環向薄膜應力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Circumferential membrane stress: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「環向薄膜應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Circumferential membrane stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"局部腐蝕孔與焊縫缺陷可能控制承載，平均厚度會掩蓋最弱位置。空管外部地下水形成的壓力方向相反，不能把內壓拉力公式直接用來證明抗屈曲能力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Local pits and weld flaws may govern strength while mean thickness hides the weakest region. Groundwater acting on a drained pipe reverses pressure direction, so an internal-tension formula does not establish external-buckling resistance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設薄壁圓管表壓p=2MPa、內徑D=2m、均勻壁厚t=0.020m，σh=pD/(2t)=100MPa；未含局部彎曲。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Hoopσh=pD/(2t)=100MPa, excluding local bending.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均環向應力低於某個數字就能證明所有支座與焊縫都安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A low average hoop stress proves every support and weld is structurally acceptable.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"局部腐蝕孔與焊縫缺陷可能控制承載，平均厚度會掩蓋最弱位置。空管外部地下水形成的壓力方向相反，不能把內壓拉力公式直接用來證明抗屈曲能力。","textEn":"Local pits and weld flaws may govern strength while mean thickness hides the weakest region. Groundwater acting on a drained pipe reverses pressure direction, so an internal-tension formula does not establish external-buckling resistance.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「環向薄膜應力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Circumferential membrane stress\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","局部腐蝕孔與焊縫缺陷可能控制承載，平均厚度會掩蓋最弱位置。","封閉端公式可直接代表任何固定、埋設或帶伸縮接頭管線的軸向應力。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Local pits and weld flaws may govern strength while mean thickness hides the weakest region.","The closed-end formula directly gives axial stress for every fixed, buried or expansion-jointed pipeline."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部腐蝕孔與焊縫缺陷可能控制承載，平均厚度會掩蓋最弱位置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Local pits and weld flaws may govern strength while mean thickness hides the weakest region. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b259-v15-05","title":"封閉端軸向作用：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Closed-end axial action: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「封閉端軸向作用」如何影響壓力鋼管錨定與支承的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Closed-end axial action” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Penstock anchorage and supports”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"封閉端的壓力合力需要由管壁或其他結構路徑平衡，軸向應力取決於端部約束與伸縮接頭。對可自由伸長的封閉薄壁管可以直接用端面平衡，但固定管線、泊松變形和錨塊分擔會改變答案；不能將教學圓筒公式無條件貼到埋設管。 假設封閉端且軸向無外部約束，p=2MPa、D=2m、t=0.020m，σa=pD/(4t)=50MPa；固定管段需另建約束模型。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「封閉端軸向作用」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pressure on a closed end must be balanced through the wall or another structural path. Axial stress depends on end restraint and expansion joints. End equilibrium applies directly to a freely extending closed thin cylinder, but fixed pipelines, Poisson effects and anchor load sharing change that answer and require a consistent boundary model. Assume closed ends and no external axial restraint, withp=2MPa,D=2m,t=0.020m. Axialσa=pD/(4t)=50MPa; restrained segments require another model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Closed-end axial action” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「封閉端公式可直接代表任何固定、埋設或帶伸縮接頭管線的軸向應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The closed-end formula directly gives axial stress for every fixed, buried or expansion-jointed pipeline.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「封閉端軸向作用」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Closed-end axial action”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-05-k1","title":"封閉端軸向作用","titleEn":"Closed-end axial action","text":"封閉端的壓力合力需要由管壁或其他結構路徑平衡，軸向應力取決於端部約束與伸縮接頭。對可自由伸長的封閉薄壁管可以直接用端面平衡，但固定管線、泊松變形和錨塊分擔會改變答案；不能將教學圓筒公式無條件貼到埋設管。","textEn":"Pressure on a closed end must be balanced through the wall or another structural path. Axial stress depends on end restraint and expansion joints.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：封閉端公式可直接代表任何固定、埋設或帶伸縮接頭管線的軸向應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The closed-end formula directly gives axial stress for every fixed, buried or expansion-jointed pipeline. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「封閉端軸向作用」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Closed-end axial action\" is correct?","options":["封閉端公式可直接代表任何固定、埋設或帶伸縮接頭管線的軸向應力。","彎管的錨定合力永遠等於一端壓力乘截面積而與轉角無關。","封閉端的壓力合力需要由管壁或其他結構路徑平衡，軸向應力取決於端部約束與伸縮接頭。"],"optionsEn":["The closed-end formula directly gives axial stress for every fixed, buried or expansion-jointed pipeline.","Elbow anchorage force always equals one end pressure times area, regardless of the turn angle.","Pressure on a closed end must be balanced through the wall or another structural path."],"answer":2,"explanation":"封閉端的壓力合力需要由管壁或其他結構路徑平衡，軸向應力取決於端部約束與伸縮接頭。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pressure on a closed end must be balanced through the wall or another structural path. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b259-v15-06","title":"封閉端軸向作用：定量估算","titleEn":"Closed-end axial action: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「封閉端軸向作用」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Closed-end axial action” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設封閉端且軸向無外部約束，p=2MPa、D=2m、t=0.020m，σa=pD/(4t)=50MPa；固定管段需另建約束模型。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume closed ends and no external axial restraint, withp=2MPa,D=2m,t=0.020m. Axialσa=pD/(4t)=50MPa; restrained segments require another model. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿管線標出固定點、滑動點與伸縮接頭，畫端部壓力進入管壁或錨塊的路徑。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map fixed points, sliding supports and expansion joints and trace end pressure into wall or anchor reactions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設封閉端且軸向無外部約束，p=2MPa、D=2m、t=0.020m，σa=pD/(4t)=50MPa；固定管段需另建約束模型。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume closed ends and no external axial restraint, withp=2MPa,D=2m,t=0.020m. Axialσa=pD/(4t)=50MPa; restrained segments require another model.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「封閉端軸向作用」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Closed-end axial action\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","完全固定熱應力公式能直接描述任何降伏、滑移與殘餘變形。","梁式跨中彎矩通過檢查就等於鞍座周圍殼體應力也已驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","The fully restrained elastic formula directly describes yielding, sliding and all residual deformation.","A satisfactory beam midspan moment automatically verifies shell stresses around every saddle."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b259-v15-07","title":"封閉端軸向作用：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Closed-end axial action: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「封閉端軸向作用」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Closed-end axial action” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿管線標出固定點、滑動點與伸縮接頭，畫端部壓力進入管壁或錨塊的路徑。分開列自由伸長與完全固定的邊界情境，核對管壁軸力與外部反力是否共同滿足整體平衡。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map fixed points, sliding supports and expansion joints and trace end pressure into wall or anchor reactions. Separate free-extension and fixed-boundary cases, checking that wall force and external reactions together satisfy equilibrium of the complete selected pipe segment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：沿管線標出固定點、滑動點與伸縮接頭，畫端部壓力進入管壁或錨塊的路徑。分開列自由伸長與完全固定的邊界情境，核對管壁軸力與外部反力是否共同滿足整體平衡。","observationEn":"Site practice: Map fixed points, sliding supports and expansion joints and trace end pressure into wall or anchor reactions. Separate free-extension and fixed-boundary cases, checking that wall force and external reactions together satisfy equilibrium of the complete selected pipe segment.","failure":"注意干擾：若壓力推力已被錨塊承擔又完整加到管壁，會重複荷載；反之兩邊都忽略則遺失力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assigning full pressure thrust to both wall and anchor double-counts load, while assigning it to neither loses equilibrium. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿管線標出固定點、滑動點與伸縮接頭，畫端部壓力進入管壁或錨塊的路徑。分開列自由伸長與完全固定的邊界情境，核對管壁軸力與外部反力是否共同滿足整體平衡。","textEn":"Map fixed points, sliding supports and expansion joints and trace end pressure into wall or anchor reactions. Separate free-extension and fixed-boundary cases, checking that wall force and external reactions together satisfy equilibrium of the complete selected pipe segment.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"沿管線標出固定點、滑動點與伸縮接頭，畫端部壓力進入管壁或錨塊的路徑。分開列自由伸長與完全固定的邊界情境，核對管壁軸力與外部反力是否共同滿足整體平衡。","textEn":"Map fixed points, sliding supports and expansion joints and trace end pressure into wall or anchor reactions. Separate free-extension and fixed-boundary cases, checking that wall force and external reactions together satisfy equilibrium of the complete selected pipe segment.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「封閉端軸向作用」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Closed-end axial action\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","沿管線標出固定點、滑動點與伸縮接頭，畫端部壓力進入管壁或錨塊的路徑。","基底平均壓力算得出來就代表錨塊抗滑、傾覆與地基承載均已合格。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Map fixed points, sliding supports and expansion joints and trace end pressure into wall or anchor reactions.","Calculating average base pressure proves acceptable sliding, overturning and foundation capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"沿管線標出固定點、滑動點與伸縮接頭，畫端部壓力進入管壁或錨塊的路徑。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map fixed points, sliding supports and expansion joints and trace end pressure into wall or anchor reactions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b259-v15-08","title":"封閉端軸向作用：失效診斷","titleEn":"Closed-end axial action: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「封閉端軸向作用」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Closed-end axial action” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若壓力推力已被錨塊承擔又完整加到管壁，會重複荷載；反之兩邊都忽略則遺失力。約束不清時即使公式算得精準，軸向設計仍可能根本錯位。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assigning full pressure thrust to both wall and anchor double-counts load, while assigning it to neither loses equilibrium. Precise arithmetic cannot repair an axial design based on an undefined or inconsistent restraint condition. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設封閉端且軸向無外部約束，p=2MPa、D=2m、t=0.020m，σa=pD/(4t)=50MPa；固定管段需另建約束模型。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Axialσa=pD/(4t)=50MPa; restrained segments require another model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「封閉端公式可直接代表任何固定、埋設或帶伸縮接頭管線的軸向應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The closed-end formula directly gives axial stress for every fixed, buried or expansion-jointed pipeline.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若壓力推力已被錨塊承擔又完整加到管壁，會重複荷載；反之兩邊都忽略則遺失力。約束不清時即使公式算得精準，軸向設計仍可能根本錯位。","textEn":"Assigning full pressure thrust to both wall and anchor double-counts load, while assigning it to neither loses equilibrium. Precise arithmetic cannot repair an axial design based on an undefined or inconsistent restraint condition.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「封閉端軸向作用」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Closed-end axial action\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","彎管的錨定合力永遠等於一端壓力乘截面積而與轉角無關。","若壓力推力已被錨塊承擔又完整加到管壁，會重複荷載；反之兩邊都忽略則遺失力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Elbow anchorage force always equals one end pressure times area, regardless of the turn angle.","Assigning full pressure thrust to both wall and anchor double-counts load, while assigning it to neither loses equilibrium."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若壓力推力已被錨塊承擔又完整加到管壁，會重複荷載；反之兩邊都忽略則遺失力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assigning full pressure thrust to both wall and anchor double-counts load, while assigning it to neither loses equilibrium. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b259-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「彎管壓力向量」與「自由熱伸長」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Elbow pressure vectors\" and \"Free thermal expansion\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b259-v15-09","title":"彎管壓力向量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Elbow pressure vectors: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「彎管壓力向量」如何影響壓力鋼管錨定與支承的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Elbow pressure vectors” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Penstock anchorage and supports”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"管線轉向時兩端壓力力的向量差形成彎管合力，不能只把壓力乘單一截面就當成所有方向的錨定荷載。動量變化、水重、管重與支承反力還要在完整自由體另列；等壓靜態示例只幫助確認角度與方向，不代表實際組合荷載。 假設等徑2m、兩端表壓2MPa、轉角90°且忽略動量及重量，F=2pA sin45°=8.8858MN，方向沿兩壓力向量合成。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「彎管壓力向量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A change in direction produces a resultant from the pressure-force vectors at an elbow’s ends. Pressure times one area alone does not describe every anchorage component. Momentum flux, water and pipe weight and support reactions belong in the full free body; an equal-pressure static example checks orientation rather than replacing the actual load combination. Assume diameter2m, equal gauge pressure2MPa and90° turn, neglecting momentum and weight. F=2pA sin45°=8.8858MN along the pressure-vector resultant. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Elbow pressure vectors” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「彎管的錨定合力永遠等於一端壓力乘截面積而與轉角無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Elbow anchorage force always equals one end pressure times area, regardless of the turn angle.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「彎管壓力向量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Elbow pressure vectors”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-09-k1","title":"彎管壓力向量","titleEn":"Elbow pressure vectors","text":"管線轉向時兩端壓力力的向量差形成彎管合力，不能只把壓力乘單一截面就當成所有方向的錨定荷載。動量變化、水重、管重與支承反力還要在完整自由體另列；等壓靜態示例只幫助確認角度與方向，不代表實際組合荷載。","textEn":"A change in direction produces a resultant from the pressure-force vectors at an elbow’s ends. Pressure times one area alone does not describe every anchorage component.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：彎管的錨定合力永遠等於一端壓力乘截面積而與轉角無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Elbow anchorage force always equals one end pressure times area, regardless of the turn angle. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「彎管壓力向量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Elbow pressure vectors\" is correct?","options":["管線轉向時兩端壓力力的向量差形成彎管合力，不能只把壓力乘單一截面就當成所有方向的錨定荷載。","彎管的錨定合力永遠等於一端壓力乘截面積而與轉角無關。","算出自由伸長後就可假定任何固定錨塊之間都會發生同樣位移。"],"optionsEn":["A change in direction produces a resultant from the pressure-force vectors at an elbow’s ends.","Elbow anchorage force always equals one end pressure times area, regardless of the turn angle.","Calculated free expansion occurs unchanged between any pair of fixed anchor blocks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"管線轉向時兩端壓力力的向量差形成彎管合力，不能只把壓力乘單一截面就當成所有方向的錨定荷載。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A change in direction produces a resultant from the pressure-force vectors at an elbow’s ends. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b259-v15-10","title":"彎管壓力向量：定量估算","titleEn":"Elbow pressure vectors: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「彎管壓力向量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Elbow pressure vectors” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設等徑2m、兩端表壓2MPa、轉角90°且忽略動量及重量，F=2pA sin45°=8.8858MN，方向沿兩壓力向量合成。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume diameter2m, equal gauge pressure2MPa and90° turn, neglecting momentum and weight. F=2pA sin45°=8.8858MN along the pressure-vector resultant. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在平面圖畫兩端法向及壓力箭頭，用分量法和向量模長各算一次，確認轉角定義。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw end normals and pressure arrows, calculating both components and resultant magnitude with a stated turn angle.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設等徑2m、兩端表壓2MPa、轉角90°且忽略動量及重量，F=2pA sin45°=8.8858MN，方向沿兩壓力向量合成。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume diameter2m, equal gauge pressure2MPa and90° turn, neglecting momentum and weight. F=2pA sin45°=8.8858MN along the pressure-vector resultant.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「彎管壓力向量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Elbow pressure vectors\", which statement holds?","options":["管線支座只需要承受鋼材自重而不必考慮管內水重。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","靜止滑動支座的實際摩擦力在任何時刻都必定等於摩擦係數乘法向力。"],"optionsEn":["Penstock supports carry only the steel’s own weight and need not consider contained water.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Actual friction at a stationary sliding support always equals coefficient times normal force."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b259-v15-11","title":"彎管壓力向量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Elbow pressure vectors: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「彎管壓力向量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Elbow pressure vectors” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在平面圖畫兩端法向及壓力箭頭，用分量法和向量模長各算一次，確認轉角定義。再加入流速動量、重力與管壁傳力，標註哪些項已由相鄰固定點吸收，避免重複或漏列。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw end normals and pressure arrows, calculating both components and resultant magnitude with a stated turn angle. Then add momentum, gravity and wall-force paths, marking loads transferred to adjacent fixed points to prevent omission or double counting. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在平面圖畫兩端法向及壓力箭頭，用分量法和向量模長各算一次，確認轉角定義。再加入流速動量、重力與管壁傳力，標註哪些項已由相鄰固定點吸收，避免重複或漏列。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw end normals and pressure arrows, calculating both components and resultant magnitude with a stated turn angle. Then add momentum, gravity and wall-force paths, marking loads transferred to adjacent fixed points to prevent omission or double counting.","failure":"注意干擾：把九十度誤認為兩箭頭之夾角可能改變符號，錯把單端推力當合力則低估需求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing pipe turn with arrow orientation can reverse signs, and using one end thrust understates the resultant. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在平面圖畫兩端法向及壓力箭頭，用分量法和向量模長各算一次，確認轉角定義。再加入流速動量、重力與管壁傳力，標註哪些項已由相鄰固定點吸收，避免重複或漏列。","textEn":"Draw end normals and pressure arrows, calculating both components and resultant magnitude with a stated turn angle. Then add momentum, gravity and wall-force paths, marking loads transferred to adjacent fixed points to prevent omission or double counting.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在平面圖畫兩端法向及壓力箭頭，用分量法和向量模長各算一次，確認轉角定義。再加入流速動量、重力與管壁傳力，標註哪些項已由相鄰固定點吸收，避免重複或漏列。","textEn":"Draw end normals and pressure arrows, calculating both components and resultant magnitude with a stated turn angle. Then add momentum, gravity and wall-force paths, marking loads transferred to adjacent fixed points to prevent omission or double counting.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「彎管壓力向量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Elbow pressure vectors\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","壁厚減少百分之十時膜應力一定也只增加百分之十且不需檢查局部缺陷。","在平面圖畫兩端法向及壓力箭頭，用分量法和向量模長各算一次，確認轉角定義。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A ten-percent thickness loss raises stress by exactly ten percent and removes any need to check local defects.","Draw end normals and pressure arrows, calculating both components and resultant magnitude with a stated turn angle."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在平面圖畫兩端法向及壓力箭頭，用分量法和向量模長各算一次，確認轉角定義。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw end normals and pressure arrows, calculating both components and resultant magnitude with a stated turn angle. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b259-v15-12","title":"彎管壓力向量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Elbow pressure vectors: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「彎管壓力向量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Elbow pressure vectors” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把九十度誤認為兩箭頭之夾角可能改變符號，錯把單端推力當合力則低估需求。真實彎管若有不同管徑或壓力，等壓等面積捷徑便不再成立。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing pipe turn with arrow orientation can reverse signs, and using one end thrust understates the resultant. Unequal diameters or pressures invalidate the equal-area, equal-pressure shortcut even if the elbow angle is unchanged. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設等徑2m、兩端表壓2MPa、轉角90°且忽略動量及重量，F=2pA sin45°=8.8858MN，方向沿兩壓力向量合成。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: F=2pA sin45°=8.8858MN along the pressure-vector resultant.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「彎管的錨定合力永遠等於一端壓力乘截面積而與轉角無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Elbow anchorage force always equals one end pressure times area, regardless of the turn angle.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把九十度誤認為兩箭頭之夾角可能改變符號，錯把單端推力當合力則低估需求。真實彎管若有不同管徑或壓力，等壓等面積捷徑便不再成立。","textEn":"Confusing pipe turn with arrow orientation can reverse signs, and using one end thrust understates the resultant. Unequal diameters or pressures invalidate the equal-area, equal-pressure shortcut even if the elbow angle is unchanged.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「彎管壓力向量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Elbow pressure vectors\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把九十度誤認為兩箭頭之夾角可能改變符號，錯把單端推力當合力則低估需求。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","算出自由伸長後就可假定任何固定錨塊之間都會發生同樣位移。"],"optionsEn":["Confusing pipe turn with arrow orientation can reverse signs, and using one end thrust understates the resultant.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Calculated free expansion occurs unchanged between any pair of fixed anchor blocks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把九十度誤認為兩箭頭之夾角可能改變符號，錯把單端推力當合力則低估需求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing pipe turn with arrow orientation can reverse signs, and using one end thrust understates the resultant. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b259-v15-13","title":"自由熱伸長：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Free thermal expansion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「自由熱伸長」如何影響壓力鋼管錨定與支承的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Free thermal expansion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Penstock anchorage and supports”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"暴露鋼管溫度改變會產生自由伸縮，支座與接頭必須提供與模型一致的運動空間。水溫、日照及安裝時溫度不必相同，沿線不均勻加熱還會造成彎曲；先算無約束伸長有助於辨認需求，但不能把這個位移視為固定管段也會自由發生。 假設均勻升溫30°C、α=12×10⁻⁶/°C、自由長度100m，ΔL=αLΔT=0.036m；未含溫度梯度與約束。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「自由熱伸長」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Exposed steel changes length with temperature, so supports and joints must permit the motion assumed by the model. Water temperature, solar heating and erection temperature differ, and nonuniform heating can induce bending. Computing unconstrained extension identifies movement demand without implying that a fixed segment can actually undergo the same free displacement. Assume uniform warming30°C, expansion coefficient12×10⁻⁶/°C and free length100m. ΔL=0.036m, excluding temperature gradients and restraint. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Free thermal expansion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「算出自由伸長後就可假定任何固定錨塊之間都會發生同樣位移。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Calculated free expansion occurs unchanged between any pair of fixed anchor blocks.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「自由熱伸長」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Free thermal expansion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-13-k1","title":"自由熱伸長","titleEn":"Free thermal expansion","text":"暴露鋼管溫度改變會產生自由伸縮，支座與接頭必須提供與模型一致的運動空間。水溫、日照及安裝時溫度不必相同，沿線不均勻加熱還會造成彎曲；先算無約束伸長有助於辨認需求，但不能把這個位移視為固定管段也會自由發生。","textEn":"Exposed steel changes length with temperature, so supports and joints must permit the motion assumed by the model. Water temperature, solar heating and erection temperature differ, and nonuniform heating can induce bending.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：算出自由伸長後就可假定任何固定錨塊之間都會發生同樣位移。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Calculated free expansion occurs unchanged between any pair of fixed anchor blocks. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「自由熱伸長」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Free thermal expansion\" is correct?","options":["算出自由伸長後就可假定任何固定錨塊之間都會發生同樣位移。","暴露鋼管溫度改變會產生自由伸縮，支座與接頭必須提供與模型一致的運動空間。","完全固定熱應力公式能直接描述任何降伏、滑移與殘餘變形。"],"optionsEn":["Calculated free expansion occurs unchanged between any pair of fixed anchor blocks.","Exposed steel changes length with temperature, so supports and joints must permit the motion assumed by the model.","The fully restrained elastic formula directly describes yielding, sliding and all residual deformation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"暴露鋼管溫度改變會產生自由伸縮，支座與接頭必須提供與模型一致的運動空間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Exposed steel changes length with temperature, so supports and joints must permit the motion assumed by the model. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b259-v15-14","title":"自由熱伸長：定量估算","titleEn":"Free thermal expansion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「自由熱伸長」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Free thermal expansion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設均勻升溫30°C、α=12×10⁻⁶/°C、自由長度100m，ΔL=αLΔT=0.036m；未含溫度梯度與約束。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume uniform warming30°C, expansion coefficient12×10⁻⁶/°C and free length100m. ΔL=0.036m, excluding temperature gradients and restraint. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以安裝溫度為基準記錄季節溫度範圍，核對自由長度兩端是否真能移動。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reference the seasonal range to erection temperature and verify both ends of the free length can move as assumed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設均勻升溫30°C、α=12×10⁻⁶/°C、自由長度100m，ΔL=αLΔT=0.036m；未含溫度梯度與約束。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume uniform warming30°C, expansion coefficient12×10⁻⁶/°C and free length100m. ΔL=0.036m, excluding temperature gradients and restraint.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「自由熱伸長」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Free thermal expansion\", which statement holds?","options":["梁式跨中彎矩通過檢查就等於鞍座周圍殼體應力也已驗證。","基底平均壓力算得出來就代表錨塊抗滑、傾覆與地基承載均已合格。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["A satisfactory beam midspan moment automatically verifies shell stresses around every saddle.","Calculating average base pressure proves acceptable sliding, overturning and foundation capacity.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b259-v15-15","title":"自由熱伸長：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Free thermal expansion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「自由熱伸長」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Free thermal expansion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以安裝溫度為基準記錄季節溫度範圍，核對自由長度兩端是否真能移動。將預測位移與接頭行程及滑動支座位置對照，並檢查沿管溫差是否需要分段積分而非使用單一平均溫度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reference the seasonal range to erection temperature and verify both ends of the free length can move as assumed. Compare predicted displacement with joint travel and sliding-support position, and assess whether varying temperature requires integration along separate pipe segments. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以安裝溫度為基準記錄季節溫度範圍，核對自由長度兩端是否真能移動。將預測位移與接頭行程及滑動支座位置對照，並檢查沿管溫差是否需要分段積分而非使用單一平均溫度。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reference the seasonal range to erection temperature and verify both ends of the free length can move as assumed. Compare predicted displacement with joint travel and sliding-support position, and assess whether varying temperature requires integration along separate pipe segments.","failure":"注意干擾：接頭卡死會把本來的位移需求轉成內力，支座滑到行程端也會改變邊界。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A seized joint converts movement demand into internal force, and a support reaching its travel stop changes the boundary. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以安裝溫度為基準記錄季節溫度範圍，核對自由長度兩端是否真能移動。將預測位移與接頭行程及滑動支座位置對照，並檢查沿管溫差是否需要分段積分而非使用單一平均溫度。","textEn":"Reference the seasonal range to erection temperature and verify both ends of the free length can move as assumed. Compare predicted displacement with joint travel and sliding-support position, and assess whether varying temperature requires integration along separate pipe segments.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以安裝溫度為基準記錄季節溫度範圍，核對自由長度兩端是否真能移動。將預測位移與接頭行程及滑動支座位置對照，並檢查沿管溫差是否需要分段積分而非使用單一平均溫度。","textEn":"Reference the seasonal range to erection temperature and verify both ends of the free length can move as assumed. Compare predicted displacement with joint travel and sliding-support position, and assess whether varying temperature requires integration along separate pipe segments.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「自由熱伸長」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Free thermal expansion\"?","options":["以安裝溫度為基準記錄季節溫度範圍，核對自由長度兩端是否真能移動。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","平均環向應力低於某個數字就能證明所有支座與焊縫都安全。"],"optionsEn":["Reference the seasonal range to erection temperature and verify both ends of the free length can move as assumed.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A low average hoop stress proves every support and weld is structurally acceptable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以安裝溫度為基準記錄季節溫度範圍，核對自由長度兩端是否真能移動。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reference the seasonal range to erection temperature and verify both ends of the free length can move as assumed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b259-v15-16","title":"自由熱伸長：失效診斷","titleEn":"Free thermal expansion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「自由熱伸長」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Free thermal expansion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"接頭卡死會把本來的位移需求轉成內力，支座滑到行程端也會改變邊界。只用水溫估暴露管線，可能漏掉日照引起的上下壁溫差和彎曲。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A seized joint converts movement demand into internal force, and a support reaching its travel stop changes the boundary. Water temperature alone may miss solar differences between upper and lower pipe walls and associated bending. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設均勻升溫30°C、α=12×10⁻⁶/°C、自由長度100m，ΔL=αLΔT=0.036m；未含溫度梯度與約束。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume uniform warming30°C, expansion coefficient12×10⁻⁶/°C and free length100m. ΔL=0.036m, excluding temperature gradients and restraint.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「算出自由伸長後就可假定任何固定錨塊之間都會發生同樣位移。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Calculated free expansion occurs unchanged between any pair of fixed anchor blocks.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"接頭卡死會把本來的位移需求轉成內力，支座滑到行程端也會改變邊界。只用水溫估暴露管線，可能漏掉日照引起的上下壁溫差和彎曲。","textEn":"A seized joint converts movement demand into internal force, and a support reaching its travel stop changes the boundary. Water temperature alone may miss solar differences between upper and lower pipe walls and associated bending.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「自由熱伸長」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Free thermal expansion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","接頭卡死會把本來的位移需求轉成內力，支座滑到行程端也會改變邊界。","完全固定熱應力公式能直接描述任何降伏、滑移與殘餘變形。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A seized joint converts movement demand into internal force, and a support reaching its travel stop changes the boundary.","The fully restrained elastic formula directly describes yielding, sliding and all residual deformation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"接頭卡死會把本來的位移需求轉成內力，支座滑到行程端也會改變邊界。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A seized joint converts movement demand into internal force, and a support reaching its travel stop changes the boundary. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b259-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「完全約束熱應力」與「管體與充水重量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Fully restrained thermal stress\" and \"Pipe and contained-water weight\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b259-v15-17","title":"完全約束熱應力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fully restrained thermal stress: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「完全約束熱應力」如何影響壓力鋼管錨定與支承的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fully restrained thermal stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Penstock anchorage and supports”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"熱伸縮被阻止時會產生軸向內力，其大小取決於管壁、錨塊與地基共同剛度。完全固定只是一個清楚的極端情境，實際支座滑移或混凝土變形會重新分配力；溫度循環還可能形成疲勞，因此不能僅檢查一次最大升溫的平均應力。 假設軸向完全固定、均勻升溫30°C、E=200GPa、α=12×10⁻⁶/°C，壓應力幅值EαΔT=72MPa，限線彈性。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「完全約束熱應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Prevented thermal movement creates axial force governed by combined pipe, anchor and foundation stiffness. Full restraint is a defined limiting case; sliding and concrete deformation redistribute force in practice. Temperature cycling can also contribute to fatigue, so a single maximum-warming stress does not characterize the complete history or the response of every connection. Assume full axial restraint, uniform warming30°C,E=200GPa andα=12×10⁻⁶/°C. Compressive stress magnitudeEαΔT=72MPa in the linear-elastic idealization. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fully restrained thermal stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「完全固定熱應力公式能直接描述任何降伏、滑移與殘餘變形。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The fully restrained elastic formula directly describes yielding, sliding and all residual deformation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「完全約束熱應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fully restrained thermal stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-17-k1","title":"完全約束熱應力","titleEn":"Fully restrained thermal stress","text":"熱伸縮被阻止時會產生軸向內力，其大小取決於管壁、錨塊與地基共同剛度。完全固定只是一個清楚的極端情境，實際支座滑移或混凝土變形會重新分配力；溫度循環還可能形成疲勞，因此不能僅檢查一次最大升溫的平均應力。","textEn":"Prevented thermal movement creates axial force governed by combined pipe, anchor and foundation stiffness. Full restraint is a defined limiting case; sliding and concrete deformation redistribute force in practice.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：完全固定熱應力公式能直接描述任何降伏、滑移與殘餘變形。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The fully restrained elastic formula directly describes yielding, sliding and all residual deformation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「完全約束熱應力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fully restrained thermal stress\" is correct?","options":["完全固定熱應力公式能直接描述任何降伏、滑移與殘餘變形。","管線支座只需要承受鋼材自重而不必考慮管內水重。","熱伸縮被阻止時會產生軸向內力，其大小取決於管壁、錨塊與地基共同剛度。"],"optionsEn":["The fully restrained elastic formula directly describes yielding, sliding and all residual deformation.","Penstock supports carry only the steel’s own weight and need not consider contained water.","Prevented thermal movement creates axial force governed by combined pipe, anchor and foundation stiffness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱伸縮被阻止時會產生軸向內力，其大小取決於管壁、錨塊與地基共同剛度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Prevented thermal movement creates axial force governed by combined pipe, anchor and foundation stiffness. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b259-v15-18","title":"完全約束熱應力：定量估算","titleEn":"Fully restrained thermal stress: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「完全約束熱應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fully restrained thermal stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設軸向完全固定、均勻升溫30°C、E=200GPa、α=12×10⁻⁶/°C，壓應力幅值EαΔT=72MPa，限線彈性。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume full axial restraint, uniform warming30°C,E=200GPa andα=12×10⁻⁶/°C. Compressive stress magnitudeEαΔT=72MPa in the linear-elastic idealization. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先說明固定是位移約束還是高剛度彈簧，分開計算完全自由與固定兩端情境。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: State whether restraint is a prescribed displacement or a stiff spring and compare free and fixed limiting cases.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設軸向完全固定、均勻升溫30°C、E=200GPa、α=12×10⁻⁶/°C，壓應力幅值EαΔT=72MPa，限線彈性。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume full axial restraint, uniform warming30°C,E=200GPa andα=12×10⁻⁶/°C. Compressive stress magnitudeEαΔT=72MPa in the linear-elastic idealization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「完全約束熱應力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fully restrained thermal stress\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","靜止滑動支座的實際摩擦力在任何時刻都必定等於摩擦係數乘法向力。","壁厚減少百分之十時膜應力一定也只增加百分之十且不需檢查局部缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Actual friction at a stationary sliding support always equals coefficient times normal force.","A ten-percent thickness loss raises stress by exactly ten percent and removes any need to check local defects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b259-v15-19","title":"完全約束熱應力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fully restrained thermal stress: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「完全約束熱應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fully restrained thermal stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先說明固定是位移約束還是高剛度彈簧，分開計算完全自由與固定兩端情境。核對升溫造成壓縮、降溫造成拉伸的符號，再與壓力軸力及支承變形組合，保留各荷載的時間關係。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"State whether restraint is a prescribed displacement or a stiff spring and compare free and fixed limiting cases. Check warming-compression and cooling-tension signs, then combine pressure force and support deformation while retaining the timing of each load contribution. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：先說明固定是位移約束還是高剛度彈簧，分開計算完全自由與固定兩端情境。核對升溫造成壓縮、降溫造成拉伸的符號，再與壓力軸力及支承變形組合，保留各荷載的時間關係。","observationEn":"Site practice: State whether restraint is a prescribed displacement or a stiff spring and compare free and fixed limiting cases. Check warming-compression and cooling-tension signs, then combine pressure force and support deformation while retaining the timing of each load contribution.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略錨塊位移可能高估平均熱力，但忽略局部卡阻又可能低估局部需求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring anchor movement can overstate average thermal force, while missing local seizure understates local demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先說明固定是位移約束還是高剛度彈簧，分開計算完全自由與固定兩端情境。核對升溫造成壓縮、降溫造成拉伸的符號，再與壓力軸力及支承變形組合，保留各荷載的時間關係。","textEn":"State whether restraint is a prescribed displacement or a stiff spring and compare free and fixed limiting cases. Check warming-compression and cooling-tension signs, then combine pressure force and support deformation while retaining the timing of each load contribution.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"先說明固定是位移約束還是高剛度彈簧，分開計算完全自由與固定兩端情境。核對升溫造成壓縮、降溫造成拉伸的符號，再與壓力軸力及支承變形組合，保留各荷載的時間關係。","textEn":"State whether restraint is a prescribed displacement or a stiff spring and compare free and fixed limiting cases. Check warming-compression and cooling-tension signs, then combine pressure force and support deformation while retaining the timing of each load contribution.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「完全約束熱應力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fully restrained thermal stress\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","先說明固定是位移約束還是高剛度彈簧，分開計算完全自由與固定兩端情境。","封閉端公式可直接代表任何固定、埋設或帶伸縮接頭管線的軸向應力。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","State whether restraint is a prescribed displacement or a stiff spring and compare free and fixed limiting cases.","The closed-end formula directly gives axial stress for every fixed, buried or expansion-jointed pipeline."],"answer":1,"explanation":"先說明固定是位移約束還是高剛度彈簧，分開計算完全自由與固定兩端情境。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"State whether restraint is a prescribed displacement or a stiff spring and compare free and fixed limiting cases. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b259-v15-20","title":"完全約束熱應力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fully restrained thermal stress: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「完全約束熱應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fully restrained thermal stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略錨塊位移可能高估平均熱力，但忽略局部卡阻又可能低估局部需求。若進入降伏或接頭滑移，線性完全固定公式便不能描述卸載後的殘餘變形。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring anchor movement can overstate average thermal force, while missing local seizure understates local demand. Yielding or joint slip invalidates the linear fully restrained model for residual deformation after unloading. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設軸向完全固定、均勻升溫30°C、E=200GPa、α=12×10⁻⁶/°C，壓應力幅值EαΔT=72MPa，限線彈性。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compressive stress magnitudeEαΔT=72MPa in the linear-elastic idealization.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「完全固定熱應力公式能直接描述任何降伏、滑移與殘餘變形。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The fully restrained elastic formula directly describes yielding, sliding and all residual deformation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略錨塊位移可能高估平均熱力，但忽略局部卡阻又可能低估局部需求。若進入降伏或接頭滑移，線性完全固定公式便不能描述卸載後的殘餘變形。","textEn":"Ignoring anchor movement can overstate average thermal force, while missing local seizure understates local demand. Yielding or joint slip invalidates the linear fully restrained model for residual deformation after unloading.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「完全約束熱應力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fully restrained thermal stress\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","管線支座只需要承受鋼材自重而不必考慮管內水重。","忽略錨塊位移可能高估平均熱力，但忽略局部卡阻又可能低估局部需求。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Penstock supports carry only the steel’s own weight and need not consider contained water.","Ignoring anchor movement can overstate average thermal force, while missing local seizure understates local demand."],"answer":2,"explanation":"忽略錨塊位移可能高估平均熱力，但忽略局部卡阻又可能低估局部需求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring anchor movement can overstate average thermal force, while missing local seizure understates local demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b259-v15-21","title":"管體與充水重量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pipe and contained-water weight: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「管體與充水重量」如何影響壓力鋼管錨定與支承的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pipe and contained-water weight” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Penstock anchorage and supports”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"支承承受的不只有鋼殼重量，充水狀態通常還有大量水重，空管與滿管因而是不同荷載情境。斜管重量要分解到管軸與法向，包覆混凝土或外部浮力也需要獨立列項；不能把管內水的體積當成鋼材體積或忽略單位長度的定義。 假設水平滿管內徑2m、外徑2.04m、鋼密度7850及水1000kg/m³，w=g[7850π(2.04²−2²)/4+1000π]=40.593kN/m。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「管體與充水重量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Supports carry both steel and contained water, making empty and full conditions distinct load cases. Inclined weight must be resolved axially and normally, while encasement or external buoyancy requires separate terms. Internal water volume is not steel volume, and the reference unit length must remain explicit before reactions are distributed between supports. Assume a horizontal full pipe with inner diameter2m, outer2.04m, steel density7850 and water1000kg/m³. Combined distributed weight is40.593kN/m. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pipe and contained-water weight” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「管線支座只需要承受鋼材自重而不必考慮管內水重。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Penstock supports carry only the steel’s own weight and need not consider contained water.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「管體與充水重量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pipe and contained-water weight”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-21-k1","title":"管體與充水重量","titleEn":"Pipe and contained-water weight","text":"支承承受的不只有鋼殼重量，充水狀態通常還有大量水重，空管與滿管因而是不同荷載情境。斜管重量要分解到管軸與法向，包覆混凝土或外部浮力也需要獨立列項；不能把管內水的體積當成鋼材體積或忽略單位長度的定義。","textEn":"Supports carry both steel and contained water, making empty and full conditions distinct load cases. Inclined weight must be resolved axially and normally, while encasement or external buoyancy requires separate terms.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：管線支座只需要承受鋼材自重而不必考慮管內水重。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Penstock supports carry only the steel’s own weight and need not consider contained water. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「管體與充水重量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pipe and contained-water weight\" is correct?","options":["支承承受的不只有鋼殼重量，充水狀態通常還有大量水重，空管與滿管因而是不同荷載情境。","管線支座只需要承受鋼材自重而不必考慮管內水重。","梁式跨中彎矩通過檢查就等於鞍座周圍殼體應力也已驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Supports carry both steel and contained water, making empty and full conditions distinct load cases.","Penstock supports carry only the steel’s own weight and need not consider contained water.","A satisfactory beam midspan moment automatically verifies shell stresses around every saddle."],"answer":0,"explanation":"支承承受的不只有鋼殼重量，充水狀態通常還有大量水重，空管與滿管因而是不同荷載情境。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Supports carry both steel and contained water, making empty and full conditions distinct load cases. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b259-v15-22","title":"管體與充水重量：定量估算","titleEn":"Pipe and contained-water weight: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「管體與充水重量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pipe and contained-water weight” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設水平滿管內徑2m、外徑2.04m、鋼密度7850及水1000kg/m³，w=g[7850π(2.04²−2²)/4+1000π]=40.593kN/m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume a horizontal full pipe with inner diameter2m, outer2.04m, steel density7850 and water1000kg/m³. Combined distributed weight is40.593kN/m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分別畫鋼環與水圓截面，以密度乘面積再乘重力計單位長度荷載，核對外徑減內徑的平方順序。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw steel annulus and water disk separately, multiplying density by area and gravity for each unit-length load.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設水平滿管內徑2m、外徑2.04m、鋼密度7850及水1000kg/m³，w=g[7850π(2.04²−2²)/4+1000π]=40.593kN/m。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume a horizontal full pipe with inner diameter2m, outer2.04m, steel density7850 and water1000kg/m³. Combined distributed weight is40.593kN/m.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「管體與充水重量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pipe and contained-water weight\", which statement holds?","options":["基底平均壓力算得出來就代表錨塊抗滑、傾覆與地基承載均已合格。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","平均環向應力低於某個數字就能證明所有支座與焊縫都安全。"],"optionsEn":["Calculating average base pressure proves acceptable sliding, overturning and foundation capacity.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","A low average hoop stress proves every support and weld is structurally acceptable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b259-v15-23","title":"管體與充水重量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pipe and contained-water weight: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「管體與充水重量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pipe and contained-water weight” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分別畫鋼環與水圓截面，以密度乘面積再乘重力計單位長度荷載，核對外徑減內徑的平方順序。比較空管和滿管，再按斜率分解重量，將外部水壓或混凝土支承另列清楚。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw steel annulus and water disk separately, multiplying density by area and gravity for each unit-length load. Check squared diameters, compare empty and full cases, resolve inclined weight and separately identify external pressure and any concrete support contribution. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分別畫鋼環與水圓截面，以密度乘面積再乘重力計單位長度荷載，核對外徑減內徑的平方順序。比較空管和滿管，再按斜率分解重量，將外部水壓或混凝土支承另列清楚。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw steel annulus and water disk separately, multiplying density by area and gravity for each unit-length load. Check squared diameters, compare empty and full cases, resolve inclined weight and separately identify external pressure and any concrete support contribution.","failure":"注意干擾：漏算水重會低估反力，將壁厚直接當成截面面積則量綱已錯。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting water understates reactions, while using thickness as area is dimensionally wrong. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分別畫鋼環與水圓截面，以密度乘面積再乘重力計單位長度荷載，核對外徑減內徑的平方順序。比較空管和滿管，再按斜率分解重量，將外部水壓或混凝土支承另列清楚。","textEn":"Draw steel annulus and water disk separately, multiplying density by area and gravity for each unit-length load. Check squared diameters, compare empty and full cases, resolve inclined weight and separately identify external pressure and any concrete support contribution.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分別畫鋼環與水圓截面，以密度乘面積再乘重力計單位長度荷載，核對外徑減內徑的平方順序。比較空管和滿管，再按斜率分解重量，將外部水壓或混凝土支承另列清楚。","textEn":"Draw steel annulus and water disk separately, multiplying density by area and gravity for each unit-length load. Check squared diameters, compare empty and full cases, resolve inclined weight and separately identify external pressure and any concrete support contribution.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「管體與充水重量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pipe and contained-water weight\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","彎管的錨定合力永遠等於一端壓力乘截面積而與轉角無關。","分別畫鋼環與水圓截面，以密度乘面積再乘重力計單位長度荷載，核對外徑減內徑的平方順序。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Elbow anchorage force always equals one end pressure times area, regardless of the turn angle.","Draw steel annulus and water disk separately, multiplying density by area and gravity for each unit-length load."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分別畫鋼環與水圓截面，以密度乘面積再乘重力計單位長度荷載，核對外徑減內徑的平方順序。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw steel annulus and water disk separately, multiplying density by area and gravity for each unit-length load. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b259-v15-24","title":"管體與充水重量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pipe and contained-water weight: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「管體與充水重量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pipe and contained-water weight” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏算水重會低估反力，將壁厚直接當成截面面積則量綱已錯。外部地下水作用於空管時可能有淨上浮，與滿管向下重量情境不能混為同一驗算。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting water understates reactions, while using thickness as area is dimensionally wrong. Groundwater can produce net uplift on an empty conduit, which must not be conflated with the downward weight of the full-pipe case. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設水平滿管內徑2m、外徑2.04m、鋼密度7850及水1000kg/m³，w=g[7850π(2.04²−2²)/4+1000π]=40.593kN/m。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Combined distributed weight is40.593kN/m.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「管線支座只需要承受鋼材自重而不必考慮管內水重。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Penstock supports carry only the steel’s own weight and need not consider contained water.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏算水重會低估反力，將壁厚直接當成截面面積則量綱已錯。外部地下水作用於空管時可能有淨上浮，與滿管向下重量情境不能混為同一驗算。","textEn":"Omitting water understates reactions, while using thickness as area is dimensionally wrong. Groundwater can produce net uplift on an empty conduit, which must not be conflated with the downward weight of the full-pipe case.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「管體與充水重量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pipe and contained-water weight\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["漏算水重會低估反力，將壁厚直接當成截面面積則量綱已錯。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","梁式跨中彎矩通過檢查就等於鞍座周圍殼體應力也已驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Omitting water understates reactions, while using thickness as area is dimensionally wrong.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A satisfactory beam midspan moment automatically verifies shell stresses around every saddle."],"answer":0,"explanation":"漏算水重會低估反力，將壁厚直接當成截面面積則量綱已錯。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting water understates reactions, while using thickness as area is dimensionally wrong. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b259-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「跨距與梁式反力」與「滑動摩擦與固定點」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Span and beam reactions\" and \"Sliding friction and fixed points\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b259-v15-25","title":"跨距與梁式反力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Span and beam reactions: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「跨距與梁式反力」如何影響壓力鋼管錨定與支承的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Span and beam reactions” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Penstock anchorage and supports”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"相鄰支座之間的管段可先用梁模型理解整體彎矩與反力，但鞍座附近的環向彎曲和殼體橢圓化不是梁公式能描述。連續支承、不同沉陷與壓力剛化也可能改變分配，因此必須把全跨分析與局部殼體查核分開，同時保持一致荷載路徑。 假設簡支跨距10m、均布荷載40kN/m，Mmax=wL²/8=500kNm，兩端反力各200kN；未評估鞍座局部殼應力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「跨距與梁式反力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A beam idealization helps interpret span moment and reactions, but it does not resolve circumferential bending and shell ovality near saddles. Continuity, differential settlement and pressure effects can change load distribution. Separate global span response from local shell assessment while keeping a consistent load path between the two analytical representations. Assume a simply supported10m span under uniform40kN/m. Maximum moment500kNm and reactions200kN each exclude local saddle shell stresses. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Span and beam reactions” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「梁式跨中彎矩通過檢查就等於鞍座周圍殼體應力也已驗證。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A satisfactory beam midspan moment automatically verifies shell stresses around every saddle.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「跨距與梁式反力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Span and beam reactions”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-25-k1","title":"跨距與梁式反力","titleEn":"Span and beam reactions","text":"相鄰支座之間的管段可先用梁模型理解整體彎矩與反力，但鞍座附近的環向彎曲和殼體橢圓化不是梁公式能描述。連續支承、不同沉陷與壓力剛化也可能改變分配，因此必須把全跨分析與局部殼體查核分開，同時保持一致荷載路徑。","textEn":"A beam idealization helps interpret span moment and reactions, but it does not resolve circumferential bending and shell ovality near saddles. Continuity, differential settlement and pressure effects can change load distribution.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：梁式跨中彎矩通過檢查就等於鞍座周圍殼體應力也已驗證。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A satisfactory beam midspan moment automatically verifies shell stresses around every saddle. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「跨距與梁式反力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Span and beam reactions\" is correct?","options":["梁式跨中彎矩通過檢查就等於鞍座周圍殼體應力也已驗證。","相鄰支座之間的管段可先用梁模型理解整體彎矩與反力，但鞍座附近的環向彎曲和殼體橢圓化不是梁公式能描述。","靜止滑動支座的實際摩擦力在任何時刻都必定等於摩擦係數乘法向力。"],"optionsEn":["A satisfactory beam midspan moment automatically verifies shell stresses around every saddle.","A beam idealization helps interpret span moment and reactions, but it does not resolve circumferential bending and shell ovality near saddles.","Actual friction at a stationary sliding support always equals coefficient times normal force."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相鄰支座之間的管段可先用梁模型理解整體彎矩與反力，但鞍座附近的環向彎曲和殼體橢圓化不是梁公式能描述。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A beam idealization helps interpret span moment and reactions, but it does not resolve circumferential bending and shell ovality near saddles. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b259-v15-26","title":"跨距與梁式反力：定量估算","titleEn":"Span and beam reactions: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「跨距與梁式反力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Span and beam reactions” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設簡支跨距10m、均布荷載40kN/m，Mmax=wL²/8=500kNm，兩端反力各200kN；未評估鞍座局部殼應力。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume a simply supported10m span under uniform40kN/m. Maximum moment500kNm and reactions200kN each exclude local saddle shell stresses. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：畫清支座轉動及平移自由度，以反力總和檢查荷載平衡，再比較連續梁或支座沉陷情境。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Define support rotational and translational freedoms and check reaction sum against total load, then compare continuity and settlement cases.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設簡支跨距10m、均布荷載40kN/m，Mmax=wL²/8=500kNm，兩端反力各200kN；未評估鞍座局部殼應力。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume a simply supported10m span under uniform40kN/m. Maximum moment500kNm and reactions200kN each exclude local saddle shell stresses.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「跨距與梁式反力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Span and beam reactions\", which statement holds?","options":["壁厚減少百分之十時膜應力一定也只增加百分之十且不需檢查局部缺陷。","封閉端公式可直接代表任何固定、埋設或帶伸縮接頭管線的軸向應力。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["A ten-percent thickness loss raises stress by exactly ten percent and removes any need to check local defects.","The closed-end formula directly gives axial stress for every fixed, buried or expansion-jointed pipeline.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b259-v15-27","title":"跨距與梁式反力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Span and beam reactions: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「跨距與梁式反力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Span and beam reactions” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"畫清支座轉動及平移自由度，以反力總和檢查荷載平衡，再比較連續梁或支座沉陷情境。把全跨彎矩傳入管壁應力分析，並另設鞍座接觸角、加勁環及局部變形檢核項目。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Define support rotational and translational freedoms and check reaction sum against total load, then compare continuity and settlement cases. Carry span moment into wall analysis while separately assessing saddle contact angle, stiffening rings and local shell distortion. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫清支座轉動及平移自由度，以反力總和檢查荷載平衡，再比較連續梁或支座沉陷情境。把全跨彎矩傳入管壁應力分析，並另設鞍座接觸角、加勁環及局部變形檢核項目。","observationEn":"Site practice: Define support rotational and translational freedoms and check reaction sum against total load, then compare continuity and settlement cases. Carry span moment into wall analysis while separately assessing saddle contact angle, stiffening rings and local shell distortion.","failure":"注意干擾：簡支假設若不符合實際固定程度會改變彎矩位置，單看跨中最大值也可能漏掉支座負彎矩。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An incorrect simple-support assumption shifts moment distribution, and focusing on midspan misses support moments. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"畫清支座轉動及平移自由度，以反力總和檢查荷載平衡，再比較連續梁或支座沉陷情境。把全跨彎矩傳入管壁應力分析，並另設鞍座接觸角、加勁環及局部變形檢核項目。","textEn":"Define support rotational and translational freedoms and check reaction sum against total load, then compare continuity and settlement cases. Carry span moment into wall analysis while separately assessing saddle contact angle, stiffening rings and local shell distortion.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫清支座轉動及平移自由度，以反力總和檢查荷載平衡，再比較連續梁或支座沉陷情境。把全跨彎矩傳入管壁應力分析，並另設鞍座接觸角、加勁環及局部變形檢核項目。","textEn":"Define support rotational and translational freedoms and check reaction sum against total load, then compare continuity and settlement cases. Carry span moment into wall analysis while separately assessing saddle contact angle, stiffening rings and local shell distortion.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「跨距與梁式反力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Span and beam reactions\"?","options":["畫清支座轉動及平移自由度，以反力總和檢查荷載平衡，再比較連續梁或支座沉陷情境。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","算出自由伸長後就可假定任何固定錨塊之間都會發生同樣位移。"],"optionsEn":["Define support rotational and translational freedoms and check reaction sum against total load, then compare continuity and settlement cases.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Calculated free expansion occurs unchanged between any pair of fixed anchor blocks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"畫清支座轉動及平移自由度，以反力總和檢查荷載平衡，再比較連續梁或支座沉陷情境。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Define support rotational and translational freedoms and check reaction sum against total load, then compare continuity and settlement cases. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b259-v15-28","title":"跨距與梁式反力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Span and beam reactions: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「跨距與梁式反力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Span and beam reactions” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"簡支假設若不符合實際固定程度會改變彎矩位置，單看跨中最大值也可能漏掉支座負彎矩。管殼局部壓扁即使總體梁應力不高，仍可能控制支承細節。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An incorrect simple-support assumption shifts moment distribution, and focusing on midspan misses support moments. Local flattening of the shell can govern saddle details even when the global beam stress appears modest. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設簡支跨距10m、均布荷載40kN/m，Mmax=wL²/8=500kNm，兩端反力各200kN；未評估鞍座局部殼應力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Maximum moment500kNm and reactions200kN each exclude local saddle shell stresses.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「梁式跨中彎矩通過檢查就等於鞍座周圍殼體應力也已驗證。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A satisfactory beam midspan moment automatically verifies shell stresses around every saddle.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"簡支假設若不符合實際固定程度會改變彎矩位置，單看跨中最大值也可能漏掉支座負彎矩。管殼局部壓扁即使總體梁應力不高，仍可能控制支承細節。","textEn":"An incorrect simple-support assumption shifts moment distribution, and focusing on midspan misses support moments. Local flattening of the shell can govern saddle details even when the global beam stress appears modest.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「跨距與梁式反力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Span and beam reactions\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","簡支假設若不符合實際固定程度會改變彎矩位置，單看跨中最大值也可能漏掉支座負彎矩。","靜止滑動支座的實際摩擦力在任何時刻都必定等於摩擦係數乘法向力。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","An incorrect simple-support assumption shifts moment distribution, and focusing on midspan misses support moments.","Actual friction at a stationary sliding support always equals coefficient times normal force."],"answer":1,"explanation":"簡支假設若不符合實際固定程度會改變彎矩位置，單看跨中最大值也可能漏掉支座負彎矩。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An incorrect simple-support assumption shifts moment distribution, and focusing on midspan misses support moments. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b259-v15-29","title":"滑動摩擦與固定點：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Sliding friction and fixed points: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「滑動摩擦與固定點」如何影響壓力鋼管錨定與支承的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sliding friction and fixed points” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Penstock anchorage and supports”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"滑動支座的目的通常是容許伸縮，但摩擦仍會把部分軸力傳到固定點。靜摩擦上限與實際動摩擦力不同，接觸壓力、鏽蝕及潤滑會改變參數；不能用名義摩擦係數保證永遠能滑動，也不能把所有支座最大摩擦同時同向當成必然情況。 假設接觸法向力400kN、庫侖摩擦係數0.15，摩擦上限μN=60kN；靜止時實際摩擦可小於此值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「滑動摩擦與固定點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Sliding supports permit movement while friction still transfers axial force to fixed points. Limiting static friction differs from actual sliding resistance, and contact pressure, corrosion and lubrication change the parameter. A nominal coefficient does not guarantee motion, nor does it establish that every support simultaneously mobilizes its maximum resistance in the same direction. Assume contact normal force400kN and Coulomb coefficient0.15. Limiting frictionμN=60kN; actual static friction may be smaller than this bound. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sliding friction and fixed points” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「靜止滑動支座的實際摩擦力在任何時刻都必定等於摩擦係數乘法向力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Actual friction at a stationary sliding support always equals coefficient times normal force.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「滑動摩擦與固定點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sliding friction and fixed points”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-29-k1","title":"滑動摩擦與固定點","titleEn":"Sliding friction and fixed points","text":"滑動支座的目的通常是容許伸縮，但摩擦仍會把部分軸力傳到固定點。靜摩擦上限與實際動摩擦力不同，接觸壓力、鏽蝕及潤滑會改變參數；不能用名義摩擦係數保證永遠能滑動，也不能把所有支座最大摩擦同時同向當成必然情況。","textEn":"Sliding supports permit movement while friction still transfers axial force to fixed points. Limiting static friction differs from actual sliding resistance, and contact pressure, corrosion and lubrication change the parameter.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：靜止滑動支座的實際摩擦力在任何時刻都必定等於摩擦係數乘法向力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Actual friction at a stationary sliding support always equals coefficient times normal force. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「滑動摩擦與固定點」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sliding friction and fixed points\" is correct?","options":["靜止滑動支座的實際摩擦力在任何時刻都必定等於摩擦係數乘法向力。","基底平均壓力算得出來就代表錨塊抗滑、傾覆與地基承載均已合格。","滑動支座的目的通常是容許伸縮，但摩擦仍會把部分軸力傳到固定點。"],"optionsEn":["Actual friction at a stationary sliding support always equals coefficient times normal force.","Calculating average base pressure proves acceptable sliding, overturning and foundation capacity.","Sliding supports permit movement while friction still transfers axial force to fixed points."],"answer":2,"explanation":"滑動支座的目的通常是容許伸縮，但摩擦仍會把部分軸力傳到固定點。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Sliding supports permit movement while friction still transfers axial force to fixed points. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b259-v15-30","title":"滑動摩擦與固定點：定量估算","titleEn":"Sliding friction and fixed points: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「滑動摩擦與固定點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sliding friction and fixed points” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設接觸法向力400kN、庫侖摩擦係數0.15，摩擦上限μN=60kN；靜止時實際摩擦可小於此值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume contact normal force400kN and Coulomb coefficient0.15. Limiting frictionμN=60kN; actual static friction may be smaller than this bound. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先判斷支座處於黏著還是滑動狀態，對照位移紀錄、接觸面狀況與法向荷載。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Determine sticking or sliding from movement records, contact condition and normal load.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設接觸法向力400kN、庫侖摩擦係數0.15，摩擦上限μN=60kN；靜止時實際摩擦可小於此值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume contact normal force400kN and Coulomb coefficient0.15. Limiting frictionμN=60kN; actual static friction may be smaller than this bound.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「滑動摩擦與固定點」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sliding friction and fixed points\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","平均環向應力低於某個數字就能證明所有支座與焊縫都安全。","彎管的錨定合力永遠等於一端壓力乘截面積而與轉角無關。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","A low average hoop stress proves every support and weld is structurally acceptable.","Elbow anchorage force always equals one end pressure times area, regardless of the turn angle."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b259-v15-31","title":"滑動摩擦與固定點：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sliding friction and fixed points: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「滑動摩擦與固定點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sliding friction and fixed points” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先判斷支座處於黏著還是滑動狀態，對照位移紀錄、接觸面狀況與法向荷載。用摩擦上下界做反力敏感度，逐段檢查軸向平衡，不把極限值當成每個時刻都存在的固定外力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Determine sticking or sliding from movement records, contact condition and normal load. Explore plausible friction bounds in reaction sensitivity and check axial equilibrium segment by segment rather than treating the limit as a constant force acting at all times. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：先判斷支座處於黏著還是滑動狀態，對照位移紀錄、接觸面狀況與法向荷載。用摩擦上下界做反力敏感度，逐段檢查軸向平衡，不把極限值當成每個時刻都存在的固定外力。","observationEn":"Site practice: Determine sticking or sliding from movement records, contact condition and normal load. Explore plausible friction bounds in reaction sensitivity and check axial equilibrium segment by segment rather than treating the limit as a constant force acting at all times.","failure":"注意干擾：支座鏽死時原先的滑動邊界可能變成固定點，熱力路徑隨之改變。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A corroded seized support may become a fixed point and redirect thermal force. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先判斷支座處於黏著還是滑動狀態，對照位移紀錄、接觸面狀況與法向荷載。用摩擦上下界做反力敏感度，逐段檢查軸向平衡，不把極限值當成每個時刻都存在的固定外力。","textEn":"Determine sticking or sliding from movement records, contact condition and normal load. Explore plausible friction bounds in reaction sensitivity and check axial equilibrium segment by segment rather than treating the limit as a constant force acting at all times.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"先判斷支座處於黏著還是滑動狀態，對照位移紀錄、接觸面狀況與法向荷載。用摩擦上下界做反力敏感度，逐段檢查軸向平衡，不把極限值當成每個時刻都存在的固定外力。","textEn":"Determine sticking or sliding from movement records, contact condition and normal load. Explore plausible friction bounds in reaction sensitivity and check axial equilibrium segment by segment rather than treating the limit as a constant force acting at all times.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「滑動摩擦與固定點」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sliding friction and fixed points\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","先判斷支座處於黏著還是滑動狀態，對照位移紀錄、接觸面狀況與法向荷載。","完全固定熱應力公式能直接描述任何降伏、滑移與殘餘變形。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Determine sticking or sliding from movement records, contact condition and normal load.","The fully restrained elastic formula directly describes yielding, sliding and all residual deformation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"先判斷支座處於黏著還是滑動狀態，對照位移紀錄、接觸面狀況與法向荷載。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Determine sticking or sliding from movement records, contact condition and normal load. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b259-v15-32","title":"滑動摩擦與固定點：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sliding friction and fixed points: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「滑動摩擦與固定點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sliding friction and fixed points” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"支座鏽死時原先的滑動邊界可能變成固定點，熱力路徑隨之改變。摩擦方向也會在升降溫時反轉，忽略歷時便可能錯算錨塊反力及接頭行程。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A corroded seized support may become a fixed point and redirect thermal force. Friction reverses with movement direction, so neglecting the sequence can misstate anchor reaction and expansion-joint travel during temperature cycles. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設接觸法向力400kN、庫侖摩擦係數0.15，摩擦上限μN=60kN；靜止時實際摩擦可小於此值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Limiting frictionμN=60kN; actual static friction may be smaller than this bound.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「靜止滑動支座的實際摩擦力在任何時刻都必定等於摩擦係數乘法向力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Actual friction at a stationary sliding support always equals coefficient times normal force.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"支座鏽死時原先的滑動邊界可能變成固定點，熱力路徑隨之改變。摩擦方向也會在升降溫時反轉，忽略歷時便可能錯算錨塊反力及接頭行程。","textEn":"A corroded seized support may become a fixed point and redirect thermal force. Friction reverses with movement direction, so neglecting the sequence can misstate anchor reaction and expansion-joint travel during temperature cycles.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「滑動摩擦與固定點」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sliding friction and fixed points\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","基底平均壓力算得出來就代表錨塊抗滑、傾覆與地基承載均已合格。","支座鏽死時原先的滑動邊界可能變成固定點，熱力路徑隨之改變。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Calculating average base pressure proves acceptable sliding, overturning and foundation capacity.","A corroded seized support may become a fixed point and redirect thermal force."],"answer":2,"explanation":"支座鏽死時原先的滑動邊界可能變成固定點，熱力路徑隨之改變。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A corroded seized support may become a fixed point and redirect thermal force. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b259-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「錨塊基底平均壓力」與「減薄與剩餘厚度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Anchor base average pressure\" and \"Wall loss and remaining thickness\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b259-v15-33","title":"錨塊基底平均壓力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Anchor base average pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「錨塊基底平均壓力」如何影響壓力鋼管錨定與支承的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Anchor base average pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Penstock anchorage and supports”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"錨塊把管線荷載傳到地基，但平均基底壓力只適用於假設的接觸狀態，不能單獨評估抗滑或抗傾覆。偏心、基底張開及地基不均勻會改變壓力分布；應把力、力矩、排水及基礎剛度放在同一自由體中，再決定簡化均壓是否合理。 假設中心向下合力2MN作用於全接觸基底4m²，q=N/A=500kPa；不是地基允許承壓值且未計偏心。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「錨塊基底平均壓力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An anchor transfers pipeline loads to the foundation, but average base pressure depends on the assumed contact state and does not establish sliding or overturning resistance. Eccentricity, uplifted contact and variable ground stiffness change the distribution. Include force, moment, drainage and foundation stiffness before deciding whether a uniform-pressure idealization is defensible. Assume a centered downward resultant2MN on a fully contacting4m² base. Averageq=500kPa is not allowable bearing pressure and excludes eccentricity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Anchor base average pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「基底平均壓力算得出來就代表錨塊抗滑、傾覆與地基承載均已合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Calculating average base pressure proves acceptable sliding, overturning and foundation capacity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「錨塊基底平均壓力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Anchor base average pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-33-k1","title":"錨塊基底平均壓力","titleEn":"Anchor base average pressure","text":"錨塊把管線荷載傳到地基，但平均基底壓力只適用於假設的接觸狀態，不能單獨評估抗滑或抗傾覆。偏心、基底張開及地基不均勻會改變壓力分布；應把力、力矩、排水及基礎剛度放在同一自由體中，再決定簡化均壓是否合理。","textEn":"An anchor transfers pipeline loads to the foundation, but average base pressure depends on the assumed contact state and does not establish sliding or overturning resistance. Eccentricity, uplifted contact and variable ground stiffness change the distribution.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：基底平均壓力算得出來就代表錨塊抗滑、傾覆與地基承載均已合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Calculating average base pressure proves acceptable sliding, overturning and foundation capacity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「錨塊基底平均壓力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Anchor base average pressure\" is correct?","options":["錨塊把管線荷載傳到地基，但平均基底壓力只適用於假設的接觸狀態，不能單獨評估抗滑或抗傾覆。","基底平均壓力算得出來就代表錨塊抗滑、傾覆與地基承載均已合格。","壁厚減少百分之十時膜應力一定也只增加百分之十且不需檢查局部缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["An anchor transfers pipeline loads to the foundation, but average base pressure depends on the assumed contact state and does not establish sliding or overturning resistance.","Calculating average base pressure proves acceptable sliding, overturning and foundation capacity.","A ten-percent thickness loss raises stress by exactly ten percent and removes any need to check local defects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"錨塊把管線荷載傳到地基，但平均基底壓力只適用於假設的接觸狀態，不能單獨評估抗滑或抗傾覆。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An anchor transfers pipeline loads to the foundation, but average base pressure depends on the assumed contact state and does not establish sliding or overturning resistance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b259-v15-34","title":"錨塊基底平均壓力：定量估算","titleEn":"Anchor base average pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「錨塊基底平均壓力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Anchor base average pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設中心向下合力2MN作用於全接觸基底4m²，q=N/A=500kPa；不是地基允許承壓值且未計偏心。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume a centered downward resultant2MN on a fully contacting4m² base. Averageq=500kPa is not allowable bearing pressure and excludes eccentricity. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對錨塊整體列垂直力與力矩平衡，核對是否有地下水上浮或水平管推力造成偏心。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check vertical-force and moment equilibrium, including groundwater uplift and eccentricity from horizontal pipe thrust.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設中心向下合力2MN作用於全接觸基底4m²，q=N/A=500kPa；不是地基允許承壓值且未計偏心。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume a centered downward resultant2MN on a fully contacting4m² base. Averageq=500kPa is not allowable bearing pressure and excludes eccentricity.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「錨塊基底平均壓力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Anchor base average pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["封閉端公式可直接代表任何固定、埋設或帶伸縮接頭管線的軸向應力。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","算出自由伸長後就可假定任何固定錨塊之間都會發生同樣位移。"],"optionsEn":["The closed-end formula directly gives axial stress for every fixed, buried or expansion-jointed pipeline.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Calculated free expansion occurs unchanged between any pair of fixed anchor blocks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b259-v15-35","title":"錨塊基底平均壓力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Anchor base average pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「錨塊基底平均壓力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Anchor base average pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對錨塊整體列垂直力與力矩平衡，核對是否有地下水上浮或水平管推力造成偏心。用接觸範圍和地基資料判斷均壓假設，再分別查抗滑、傾覆、沉陷與混凝土局部受力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check vertical-force and moment equilibrium, including groundwater uplift and eccentricity from horizontal pipe thrust. Use contact and ground evidence to assess uniform pressure, then examine sliding, overturning, settlement and local concrete actions as separate mechanisms. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對錨塊整體列垂直力與力矩平衡，核對是否有地下水上浮或水平管推力造成偏心。用接觸範圍和地基資料判斷均壓假設，再分別查抗滑、傾覆、沉陷與混凝土局部受力。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check vertical-force and moment equilibrium, including groundwater uplift and eccentricity from horizontal pipe thrust. Use contact and ground evidence to assess uniform pressure, then examine sliding, overturning, settlement and local concrete actions as separate mechanisms.","failure":"注意干擾：將五百千帕誤寫成地基承載能力會倒置需求與抗力，偏心時平均值又會掩蓋最大壓力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Calling500kPa a foundation capacity reverses demand and resistance, while average pressure hides peaks under eccentricity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對錨塊整體列垂直力與力矩平衡，核對是否有地下水上浮或水平管推力造成偏心。用接觸範圍和地基資料判斷均壓假設，再分別查抗滑、傾覆、沉陷與混凝土局部受力。","textEn":"Check vertical-force and moment equilibrium, including groundwater uplift and eccentricity from horizontal pipe thrust. Use contact and ground evidence to assess uniform pressure, then examine sliding, overturning, settlement and local concrete actions as separate mechanisms.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對錨塊整體列垂直力與力矩平衡，核對是否有地下水上浮或水平管推力造成偏心。用接觸範圍和地基資料判斷均壓假設，再分別查抗滑、傾覆、沉陷與混凝土局部受力。","textEn":"Check vertical-force and moment equilibrium, including groundwater uplift and eccentricity from horizontal pipe thrust. Use contact and ground evidence to assess uniform pressure, then examine sliding, overturning, settlement and local concrete actions as separate mechanisms.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「錨塊基底平均壓力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Anchor base average pressure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","管線支座只需要承受鋼材自重而不必考慮管內水重。","對錨塊整體列垂直力與力矩平衡，核對是否有地下水上浮或水平管推力造成偏心。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Penstock supports carry only the steel’s own weight and need not consider contained water.","Check vertical-force and moment equilibrium, including groundwater uplift and eccentricity from horizontal pipe thrust."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對錨塊整體列垂直力與力矩平衡，核對是否有地下水上浮或水平管推力造成偏心。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check vertical-force and moment equilibrium, including groundwater uplift and eccentricity from horizontal pipe thrust. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b259-v15-36","title":"錨塊基底平均壓力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Anchor base average pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「錨塊基底平均壓力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Anchor base average pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將五百千帕誤寫成地基承載能力會倒置需求與抗力，偏心時平均值又會掩蓋最大壓力。基底部分脫離後，仍以原面積均分會低估剩餘接觸區需求。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Calling500kPa a foundation capacity reverses demand and resistance, while average pressure hides peaks under eccentricity. After partial loss of contact, dividing by the original area understates demand on the remaining bearing region. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設中心向下合力2MN作用於全接觸基底4m²，q=N/A=500kPa；不是地基允許承壓值且未計偏心。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Averageq=500kPa is not allowable bearing pressure and excludes eccentricity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「基底平均壓力算得出來就代表錨塊抗滑、傾覆與地基承載均已合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Calculating average base pressure proves acceptable sliding, overturning and foundation capacity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將五百千帕誤寫成地基承載能力會倒置需求與抗力，偏心時平均值又會掩蓋最大壓力。基底部分脫離後，仍以原面積均分會低估剩餘接觸區需求。","textEn":"Calling500kPa a foundation capacity reverses demand and resistance, while average pressure hides peaks under eccentricity. After partial loss of contact, dividing by the original area understates demand on the remaining bearing region.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「錨塊基底平均壓力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Anchor base average pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["將五百千帕誤寫成地基承載能力會倒置需求與抗力，偏心時平均值又會掩蓋最大壓力。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","壁厚減少百分之十時膜應力一定也只增加百分之十且不需檢查局部缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Calling500kPa a foundation capacity reverses demand and resistance, while average pressure hides peaks under eccentricity.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A ten-percent thickness loss raises stress by exactly ten percent and removes any need to check local defects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將五百千帕誤寫成地基承載能力會倒置需求與抗力，偏心時平均值又會掩蓋最大壓力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Calling500kPa a foundation capacity reverses demand and resistance, while average pressure hides peaks under eccentricity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b259-v15-37","title":"減薄與剩餘厚度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Wall loss and remaining thickness: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「減薄與剩餘厚度」如何影響壓力鋼管錨定與支承的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wall loss and remaining thickness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Penstock anchorage and supports”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"腐蝕造成的壁厚減少會提高相同內壓下的膜應力，但均勻減薄只是一種理想情境，局部坑蝕與裂縫需要不同評估。厚度量測的網格與位置應可追溯，不能用最容易量到的一點代表整段；塗層良好也不等於內外壁都沒有缺陷。 假設壓力及直徑不變、均勻厚度20mm降至18mm，環向應力100×20/18=111.11MPa，增加11.11%；未評局部坑蝕。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「減薄與剩餘厚度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Wall loss raises membrane stress at the same internal pressure, but uniform thinning is only one idealization and pits or cracks require different assessment. Measurement grids and locations must be traceable; an easily accessible point cannot represent the whole segment. A sound coating also does not prove the absence of defects on either surface. Assume unchanged pressure and diameter with uniform thickness falling20 to18mm. Hoop stress rises100×20/18=111.11MPa, an11.11% increase, excluding pitting assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wall loss and remaining thickness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「壁厚減少百分之十時膜應力一定也只增加百分之十且不需檢查局部缺陷。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A ten-percent thickness loss raises stress by exactly ten percent and removes any need to check local defects.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「減薄與剩餘厚度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wall loss and remaining thickness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-37-k1","title":"減薄與剩餘厚度","titleEn":"Wall loss and remaining thickness","text":"腐蝕造成的壁厚減少會提高相同內壓下的膜應力，但均勻減薄只是一種理想情境，局部坑蝕與裂縫需要不同評估。厚度量測的網格與位置應可追溯，不能用最容易量到的一點代表整段；塗層良好也不等於內外壁都沒有缺陷。","textEn":"Wall loss raises membrane stress at the same internal pressure, but uniform thinning is only one idealization and pits or cracks require different assessment. Measurement grids and locations must be traceable; an easily accessible point cannot represent the whole segment.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：壁厚減少百分之十時膜應力一定也只增加百分之十且不需檢查局部缺陷。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A ten-percent thickness loss raises stress by exactly ten percent and removes any need to check local defects. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「減薄與剩餘厚度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wall loss and remaining thickness\" is correct?","options":["壁厚減少百分之十時膜應力一定也只增加百分之十且不需檢查局部缺陷。","腐蝕造成的壁厚減少會提高相同內壓下的膜應力，但均勻減薄只是一種理想情境，局部坑蝕與裂縫需要不同評估。","平均環向應力低於某個數字就能證明所有支座與焊縫都安全。"],"optionsEn":["A ten-percent thickness loss raises stress by exactly ten percent and removes any need to check local defects.","Wall loss raises membrane stress at the same internal pressure, but uniform thinning is only one idealization and pits or cracks require different assessment.","A low average hoop stress proves every support and weld is structurally acceptable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"腐蝕造成的壁厚減少會提高相同內壓下的膜應力，但均勻減薄只是一種理想情境，局部坑蝕與裂縫需要不同評估。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Wall loss raises membrane stress at the same internal pressure, but uniform thinning is only one idealization and pits or cracks require different assessment. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b259-v15-38","title":"減薄與剩餘厚度：定量估算","titleEn":"Wall loss and remaining thickness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「減薄與剩餘厚度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wall loss and remaining thickness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設壓力及直徑不變、均勻厚度20mm降至18mm，環向應力100×20/18=111.11MPa，增加11.11%；未評局部坑蝕。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume unchanged pressure and diameter with uniform thickness falling20 to18mm. Hoop stress rises100×20/18=111.11MPa, an11.11% increase, excluding pitting assessment. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將厚度圖與原始製造、焊縫和歷次量測對位，確認儀器校正與塗層修正。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Register thickness maps with fabrication, weld and prior inspection records, checking calibration and coating corrections.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設壓力及直徑不變、均勻厚度20mm降至18mm，環向應力100×20/18=111.11MPa，增加11.11%；未評局部坑蝕。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume unchanged pressure and diameter with uniform thickness falling20 to18mm. Hoop stress rises100×20/18=111.11MPa, an11.11% increase, excluding pitting assessment.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「減薄與剩餘厚度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wall loss and remaining thickness\", which statement holds?","options":["彎管的錨定合力永遠等於一端壓力乘截面積而與轉角無關。","完全固定熱應力公式能直接描述任何降伏、滑移與殘餘變形。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Elbow anchorage force always equals one end pressure times area, regardless of the turn angle.","The fully restrained elastic formula directly describes yielding, sliding and all residual deformation.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b259-v15-39","title":"減薄與剩餘厚度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wall loss and remaining thickness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「減薄與剩餘厚度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wall loss and remaining thickness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將厚度圖與原始製造、焊縫和歷次量測對位，確認儀器校正與塗層修正。分辨均勻減薄、局部坑蝕和裂紋，再用相應方法評估，不以平均厚度或外觀照片取代最弱區域的證據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Register thickness maps with fabrication, weld and prior inspection records, checking calibration and coating corrections. Distinguish uniform loss, pits and cracks and apply appropriate assessment methods rather than substituting average thickness or appearance for evidence at the weakest region. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將厚度圖與原始製造、焊縫和歷次量測對位，確認儀器校正與塗層修正。分辨均勻減薄、局部坑蝕和裂紋，再用相應方法評估，不以平均厚度或外觀照片取代最弱區域的證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Register thickness maps with fabrication, weld and prior inspection records, checking calibration and coating corrections. Distinguish uniform loss, pits and cracks and apply appropriate assessment methods rather than substituting average thickness or appearance for evidence at the weakest region.","failure":"注意干擾：量測點偏離最薄區會得到假安心，腐蝕速率也未必長期固定。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Measurements missing the thinnest area give false reassurance, and corrosion rate need not remain constant. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將厚度圖與原始製造、焊縫和歷次量測對位，確認儀器校正與塗層修正。分辨均勻減薄、局部坑蝕和裂紋，再用相應方法評估，不以平均厚度或外觀照片取代最弱區域的證據。","textEn":"Register thickness maps with fabrication, weld and prior inspection records, checking calibration and coating corrections. Distinguish uniform loss, pits and cracks and apply appropriate assessment methods rather than substituting average thickness or appearance for evidence at the weakest region.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將厚度圖與原始製造、焊縫和歷次量測對位，確認儀器校正與塗層修正。分辨均勻減薄、局部坑蝕和裂紋，再用相應方法評估，不以平均厚度或外觀照片取代最弱區域的證據。","textEn":"Register thickness maps with fabrication, weld and prior inspection records, checking calibration and coating corrections. Distinguish uniform loss, pits and cracks and apply appropriate assessment methods rather than substituting average thickness or appearance for evidence at the weakest region.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「減薄與剩餘厚度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wall loss and remaining thickness\"?","options":["將厚度圖與原始製造、焊縫和歷次量測對位，確認儀器校正與塗層修正。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","梁式跨中彎矩通過檢查就等於鞍座周圍殼體應力也已驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Register thickness maps with fabrication, weld and prior inspection records, checking calibration and coating corrections.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A satisfactory beam midspan moment automatically verifies shell stresses around every saddle."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將厚度圖與原始製造、焊縫和歷次量測對位，確認儀器校正與塗層修正。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Register thickness maps with fabrication, weld and prior inspection records, checking calibration and coating corrections. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b259-v15-40","title":"減薄與剩餘厚度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wall loss and remaining thickness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"prerequisiteIds":["b259-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「減薄與剩餘厚度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wall loss and remaining thickness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"量測點偏離最薄區會得到假安心，腐蝕速率也未必長期固定。單靠線性外推厚度可能漏掉局部加速或裂紋擴展，應保留測值不確定度與機制分類。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Measurements missing the thinnest area give false reassurance, and corrosion rate need not remain constant. Linear thickness extrapolation can miss local acceleration or crack growth, requiring retained uncertainty and a clear classification of damage mechanisms. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設壓力及直徑不變、均勻厚度20mm降至18mm，環向應力100×20/18=111.11MPa，增加11.11%；未評局部坑蝕。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Hoop stress rises100×20/18=111.11MPa, an11.11% increase, excluding pitting assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「壁厚減少百分之十時膜應力一定也只增加百分之十且不需檢查局部缺陷。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A ten-percent thickness loss raises stress by exactly ten percent and removes any need to check local defects.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b259-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"量測點偏離最薄區會得到假安心，腐蝕速率也未必長期固定。單靠線性外推厚度可能漏掉局部加速或裂紋擴展，應保留測值不確定度與機制分類。","textEn":"Measurements missing the thinnest area give false reassurance, and corrosion rate need not remain constant. Linear thickness extrapolation can miss local acceleration or crack growth, requiring retained uncertainty and a clear classification of damage mechanisms.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]},{"id":"b259-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「減薄與剩餘厚度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wall loss and remaining thickness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","量測點偏離最薄區會得到假安心，腐蝕速率也未必長期固定。","平均環向應力低於某個數字就能證明所有支座與焊縫都安全。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Measurements missing the thinnest area give false reassurance, and corrosion rate need not remain constant.","A low average hoop stress proves every support and weld is structurally acceptable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"量測點偏離最薄區會得到假安心，腐蝕速率也未必長期固定。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Measurements missing the thinnest area give false reassurance, and corrosion rate need not remain constant. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-penstock-inspection","v6-hoover-history","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-hydro-structures"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b260","title":"調壓井水錘控制","titleEn":"Surge-shaft control of water hammer","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課將快速彈性壓力波與較慢的調壓井自由水面振盪分開建模，再用共同邊界把兩者連起來。十個單元涵蓋波速、往返時間、首波增量、井內連續方程、剛性水柱週期、無損湧升、摩擦節流、汽化及數值收斂，所有算例都明定原創假設，不提供可直接套用的閥門動作規程。","summaryEn":"This course models rapid elastic pressure waves separately from slower free-surface surge oscillations, then reconnects them through shared boundaries. Ten units cover celerity, travel time, first-wave increment, continuity, rigid-column period, ideal upsurge, friction, throttling, vapor formation and numerical convergence. All examples state original assumptions rather than prescribing transferable valve-operating procedures.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-hydraulics","subcategoryTitle":"壩工監測、溢洪與壓力水路","subcategoryTitleEn":"Dam monitoring, spillways and pressure waterways","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-hydraulics","learningTags":["water","water-hydraulics","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-hydraulic","architectureNodes":[["彈性波速與管壁","Elastic wave speed and pipe wall"],["快速變速壓力增量","Rapid velocity-change pressure"],["剛性水柱振盪週期","Rigid-column oscillation period"],["節流孔與局部損失","Throttle opening and local loss"],["特徵網格與收斂","Characteristic grid and convergence"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-hydraulic","labels":["彈性波速與管壁","快速變速壓力增量","剛性水柱振盪週期","節流孔與局部損失","特徵網格與收斂"],"labelsEn":["Elastic wave speed and pipe wall","Rapid velocity-change pressure","Rigid-column oscillation period","Throttle opening and local loss","Characteristic grid and convergence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創井面積敏感度：定水位上庫、無損剛性水柱、初始井位與庫位相同，L=1000m、Ap=10m²、V0=2m/s且瞬停下游時，As=100m²得到zmax=6.3855m。將井面積增加10%至110m²而其他假設不變，湧升變為6.3855/√1.1≈6.0883m，降低約4.65%，並非10%。同時理想週期會乘√1.1而變長。學徒應比較較低湧升與較長振盪的不同效果，再加入摩擦、井水慣性、通氣及彈性管路，不把理想幅值減少誤稱所有壓力風險均以相同比例降低。","textEn":"Original shaft-area sensitivity: assume a fixed reservoir, lossless rigid column, equal initial shaft and reservoir levels,L=1000m,Ap=10m²,V0=2m/s and instantaneous downstream demand stop. Shaft area100m² gives maximum rise6.3855m. Increasing area10% to110m² with all other assumptions fixed gives6.3855/√1.1≈6.0883m, about4.65% lower rather than10%. The ideal period simultaneously increases by√1.1. Apprentices compare lower rise with longer oscillation before adding friction, shaft inertia, ventilation and elastic waterways. A reduced ideal amplitude does not imply that every pressure risk declines by the same percentage across the full connected system.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b260-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「彈性波速與管壁」與「往返時間與邊界」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall\" and \"Round-trip time and boundaries\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b260-v15-01","title":"彈性波速與管壁：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「彈性波速與管壁」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Elastic wave speed and pipe wall” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水錘傳播速度同時受水可壓縮性與管壁變形影響，不是把水視為完全剛性就能描述。管壁約束、材料模數與含氣量會改變波速，薄壁圓管公式需要明列修正係數；用一個假設波速計算的壓力峰值，必須隨參數不確定度重新檢查。 假設K=2.2GPa、ρ=1000kg/m³、E=200GPa、D=2m、t=0.02m，管壁修正係數取1，a=√[K/ρ/(1+KD/Et)]=1023.53m/s。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「彈性波速與管壁」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Water-hammer propagation depends on both fluid compressibility and pipe-wall deformation, so a rigid-water assumption cannot describe the wave. Restraint, material modulus and gas content affect celerity, and the thin circular-pipe expression requires an explicit restraint factor. Pressure estimates made with one assumed speed must be reconsidered when that parameter is uncertain. AssumeK=2.2GPa,ρ=1000kg/m³,E=200GPa,D=2m,t=0.02m and wall-restraint factor1. Wave speeda=√[K/ρ/(1+KD/Et)]=1023.53m/s for this idealization. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Elastic wave speed and pipe wall” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「彈性波速與管壁」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Elastic wave speed and pipe wall”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-01-k1","title":"彈性波速與管壁","titleEn":"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall","text":"水錘傳播速度同時受水可壓縮性與管壁變形影響，不是把水視為完全剛性就能描述。管壁約束、材料模數與含氣量會改變波速，薄壁圓管公式需要明列修正係數；用一個假設波速計算的壓力峰值，必須隨參數不確定度重新檢查。","textEn":"Water-hammer propagation depends on both fluid compressibility and pipe-wall deformation, so a rigid-water assumption cannot describe the wave. Restraint, material modulus and gas content affect celerity, and the thin circular-pipe expression requires an explicit restraint factor.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「彈性波速與管壁」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall\" is correct?","options":["水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。","水錘傳播速度同時受水可壓縮性與管壁變形影響，不是把水視為完全剛性就能描述。","閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas.","Water-hammer propagation depends on both fluid compressibility and pipe-wall deformation, so a rigid-water assumption cannot describe the wave.","An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水錘傳播速度同時受水可壓縮性與管壁變形影響，不是把水視為完全剛性就能描述。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Water-hammer propagation depends on both fluid compressibility and pipe-wall deformation, so a rigid-water assumption cannot describe the wave. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b260-v15-02","title":"彈性波速與管壁：定量估算","titleEn":"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「彈性波速與管壁」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Elastic wave speed and pipe wall” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設K=2.2GPa、ρ=1000kg/m³、E=200GPa、D=2m、t=0.02m，管壁修正係數取1，a=√[K/ρ/(1+KD/Et)]=1023.53m/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. AssumeK=2.2GPa,ρ=1000kg/m³,E=200GPa,D=2m,t=0.02m and wall-restraint factor1. Wave speeda=√[K/ρ/(1+KD/Et)]=1023.53m/s for this idealization. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：記錄流體與管材模數、厚度和軸向約束來源，確認管壁修正係數是否適用。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Document fluid and wall moduli, thickness and axial-restraint evidence and check the chosen correction factor.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設K=2.2GPa、ρ=1000kg/m³、E=200GPa、D=2m、t=0.02m，管壁修正係數取1，a=√[K/ρ/(1+KD/Et)]=1023.53m/s。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. AssumeK=2.2GPa,ρ=1000kg/m³,E=200GPa,D=2m,t=0.02m and wall-restraint factor1. Wave speeda=√[K/ρ/(1+KD/Et)]=1023.53m/s for this idealization.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「彈性波速與管壁」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall\", which statement holds?","options":["瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。","理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow.","The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b260-v15-03","title":"彈性波速與管壁：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「彈性波速與管壁」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Elastic wave speed and pipe wall” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"記錄流體與管材模數、厚度和軸向約束來源，確認管壁修正係數是否適用。用量測波到達時間比較估計波速，再測試含氣或厚度變動的敏感度，不藉調整波速掩蓋錯誤邊界。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Document fluid and wall moduli, thickness and axial-restraint evidence and check the chosen correction factor. Compare predicted speed with measured wave arrival, then test gas-content and wall variations rather than tuning celerity to conceal an incorrect boundary condition. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：記錄流體與管材模數、厚度和軸向約束來源，確認管壁修正係數是否適用。用量測波到達時間比較估計波速，再測試含氣或厚度變動的敏感度，不藉調整波速掩蓋錯誤邊界。","observationEn":"Site practice: Document fluid and wall moduli, thickness and axial-restraint evidence and check the chosen correction factor. Compare predicted speed with measured wave arrival, then test gas-content and wall variations rather than tuning celerity to conceal an incorrect boundary condition.","failure":"注意干擾：少量夾氣可能顯著改變可壓縮性，複合管或厚壁管也不符合簡式。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Entrained gas changes compressibility, and composite or thick walls fall outside this simple expression. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"記錄流體與管材模數、厚度和軸向約束來源，確認管壁修正係數是否適用。用量測波到達時間比較估計波速，再測試含氣或厚度變動的敏感度，不藉調整波速掩蓋錯誤邊界。","textEn":"Document fluid and wall moduli, thickness and axial-restraint evidence and check the chosen correction factor. Compare predicted speed with measured wave arrival, then test gas-content and wall variations rather than tuning celerity to conceal an incorrect boundary condition.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"記錄流體與管材模數、厚度和軸向約束來源，確認管壁修正係數是否適用。用量測波到達時間比較估計波速，再測試含氣或厚度變動的敏感度，不藉調整波速掩蓋錯誤邊界。","textEn":"Document fluid and wall moduli, thickness and axial-restraint evidence and check the chosen correction factor. Compare predicted speed with measured wave arrival, then test gas-content and wall variations rather than tuning celerity to conceal an incorrect boundary condition.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「彈性波速與管壁」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall\"?","options":["記錄流體與管材模數、厚度和軸向約束來源，確認管壁修正係數是否適用。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。"],"optionsEn":["Document fluid and wall moduli, thickness and axial-restraint evidence and check the chosen correction factor.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system."],"answer":0,"explanation":"記錄流體與管材模數、厚度和軸向約束來源，確認管壁修正係數是否適用。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Document fluid and wall moduli, thickness and axial-restraint evidence and check the chosen correction factor. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b260-v15-04","title":"彈性波速與管壁：失效診斷","titleEn":"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「彈性波速與管壁」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Elastic wave speed and pipe wall” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"少量夾氣可能顯著改變可壓縮性，複合管或厚壁管也不符合簡式。把鋼材彈性模數當水體積模數，或漏掉帕與吉帕換算，會使壓力與時間尺度同時失真。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Entrained gas changes compressibility, and composite or thick walls fall outside this simple expression. Substituting steel modulus for water bulk modulus or confusing pascals and gigapascals distorts both pressure magnitude and wave timing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設K=2.2GPa、ρ=1000kg/m³、E=200GPa、D=2m、t=0.02m，管壁修正係數取1，a=√[K/ρ/(1+KD/Et)]=1023.53m/s。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Wave speeda=√[K/ρ/(1+KD/Et)]=1023.53m/s for this idealization.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"少量夾氣可能顯著改變可壓縮性，複合管或厚壁管也不符合簡式。把鋼材彈性模數當水體積模數，或漏掉帕與吉帕換算，會使壓力與時間尺度同時失真。","textEn":"Entrained gas changes compressibility, and composite or thick walls fall outside this simple expression. Substituting steel modulus for water bulk modulus or confusing pascals and gigapascals distorts both pressure magnitude and wave timing.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「彈性波速與管壁」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Elastic wave speed and pipe wall\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","少量夾氣可能顯著改變可壓縮性，複合管或厚壁管也不符合簡式。","閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Entrained gas changes compressibility, and composite or thick walls fall outside this simple expression.","An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"少量夾氣可能顯著改變可壓縮性，複合管或厚壁管也不符合簡式。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Entrained gas changes compressibility, and composite or thick walls fall outside this simple expression. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b260-v15-05","title":"往返時間與邊界：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Round-trip time and boundaries: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「往返時間與邊界」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Round-trip time and boundaries” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"閥門動作與壓力波往返時間的比較，決定反射是否已在動作期間返回控制點。最簡水庫管閥系統只有一條明確路徑，但分岔、調壓井與不同波速管段會產生多重反射；時間尺度只是辨識模型的入口，不能據此直接宣布某個關閉時間安全。 假設均勻管長L=1000m、波速a=1000m/s，往返時間2L/a=2s；只代表此單一路徑，不是允許關閉時間。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「往返時間與邊界」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Comparing actuator duration with wave round-trip time shows whether a reflection returns during the action. A reservoir-pipe-valve system has one simple path, whereas branches, shafts and segments with different celerity create multiple reflections. This time scale helps select the analysis and does not by itself approve a particular valve-closing duration. Assume uniform pipe length1000m and celerity1000m/s. Round-trip2L/a=2s describes only this path, not an allowable closing time. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Round-trip time and boundaries” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「往返時間與邊界」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Round-trip time and boundaries”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-05-k1","title":"往返時間與邊界","titleEn":"Round-trip time and boundaries","text":"閥門動作與壓力波往返時間的比較，決定反射是否已在動作期間返回控制點。最簡水庫管閥系統只有一條明確路徑，但分岔、調壓井與不同波速管段會產生多重反射；時間尺度只是辨識模型的入口，不能據此直接宣布某個關閉時間安全。","textEn":"Comparing actuator duration with wave round-trip time shows whether a reflection returns during the action. A reservoir-pipe-valve system has one simple path, whereas branches, shafts and segments with different celerity create multiple reflections.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「往返時間與邊界」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Round-trip time and boundaries\" is correct?","options":["閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。","焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。","閥門動作與壓力波往返時間的比較，決定反射是否已在動作期間返回控制點。"],"optionsEn":["An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure.","The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario.","Comparing actuator duration with wave round-trip time shows whether a reflection returns during the action."],"answer":2,"explanation":"閥門動作與壓力波往返時間的比較，決定反射是否已在動作期間返回控制點。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Comparing actuator duration with wave round-trip time shows whether a reflection returns during the action. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b260-v15-06","title":"往返時間與邊界：定量估算","titleEn":"Round-trip time and boundaries: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「往返時間與邊界」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Round-trip time and boundaries” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設均勻管長L=1000m、波速a=1000m/s，往返時間2L/a=2s；只代表此單一路徑，不是允許關閉時間。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume uniform pipe length1000m and celerity1000m/s. Round-trip2L/a=2s describes only this path, not an allowable closing time. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在系統圖標出反射邊界及每段長度波速，逐段累加單程時間，再與閥門實際流量變化歷時比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark reflecting boundaries and each segment’s length and celerity, sum one-way travel times and compare with actual discharge-change histories.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設均勻管長L=1000m、波速a=1000m/s，往返時間2L/a=2s；只代表此單一路徑，不是允許關閉時間。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume uniform pipe length1000m and celerity1000m/s. Round-trip2L/a=2s describes only this path, not an allowable closing time.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「往返時間與邊界」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Round-trip time and boundaries\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。","管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time.","During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b260-v15-07","title":"往返時間與邊界：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Round-trip time and boundaries: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「往返時間與邊界」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Round-trip time and boundaries” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在系統圖標出反射邊界及每段長度波速，逐段累加單程時間，再與閥門實際流量變化歷時比較。遇到分岔或調壓接點就建立多路徑時間表，不能只取地圖上兩點直線距離。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark reflecting boundaries and each segment’s length and celerity, sum one-way travel times and compare with actual discharge-change histories. For branches and shaft junctions construct a multiple-path timing table instead of using the straight-line distance between map locations. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在系統圖標出反射邊界及每段長度波速，逐段累加單程時間，再與閥門實際流量變化歷時比較。遇到分岔或調壓接點就建立多路徑時間表，不能只取地圖上兩點直線距離。","observationEn":"Site practice: Mark reflecting boundaries and each segment’s length and celerity, sum one-way travel times and compare with actual discharge-change histories. For branches and shaft junctions construct a multiple-path timing table instead of using the straight-line distance between map locations.","failure":"注意干擾：將單程時間當往返時間會改變快速與慢速的分類，忽略分岔反射則可能漏掉疊加峰值。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing one-way with round-trip time changes the rapid-action classification, while omitted branch reflections can hide superposed peaks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在系統圖標出反射邊界及每段長度波速，逐段累加單程時間，再與閥門實際流量變化歷時比較。遇到分岔或調壓接點就建立多路徑時間表，不能只取地圖上兩點直線距離。","textEn":"Mark reflecting boundaries and each segment’s length and celerity, sum one-way travel times and compare with actual discharge-change histories. For branches and shaft junctions construct a multiple-path timing table instead of using the straight-line distance between map locations.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在系統圖標出反射邊界及每段長度波速，逐段累加單程時間，再與閥門實際流量變化歷時比較。遇到分岔或調壓接點就建立多路徑時間表，不能只取地圖上兩點直線距離。","textEn":"Mark reflecting boundaries and each segment’s length and celerity, sum one-way travel times and compare with actual discharge-change histories. For branches and shaft junctions construct a multiple-path timing table instead of using the straight-line distance between map locations.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「往返時間與邊界」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Round-trip time and boundaries\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在系統圖標出反射邊界及每段長度波速，逐段累加單程時間，再與閥門實際流量變化歷時比較。","任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Mark reflecting boundaries and each segment’s length and celerity, sum one-way travel times and compare with actual discharge-change histories.","Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在系統圖標出反射邊界及每段長度波速，逐段累加單程時間，再與閥門實際流量變化歷時比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark reflecting boundaries and each segment’s length and celerity, sum one-way travel times and compare with actual discharge-change histories. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b260-v15-08","title":"往返時間與邊界：失效診斷","titleEn":"Round-trip time and boundaries: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「往返時間與邊界」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Round-trip time and boundaries” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將單程時間當往返時間會改變快速與慢速的分類，忽略分岔反射則可能漏掉疊加峰值。即使動作很慢，長時間水位振盪或控制不穩定仍可能存在。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing one-way with round-trip time changes the rapid-action classification, while omitted branch reflections can hide superposed peaks. Slow actuation can still produce long-period level oscillations or unstable control interactions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設均勻管長L=1000m、波速a=1000m/s，往返時間2L/a=2s；只代表此單一路徑，不是允許關閉時間。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Round-trip2L/a=2s describes only this path, not an allowable closing time.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將單程時間當往返時間會改變快速與慢速的分類，忽略分岔反射則可能漏掉疊加峰值。即使動作很慢，長時間水位振盪或控制不穩定仍可能存在。","textEn":"Confusing one-way with round-trip time changes the rapid-action classification, while omitted branch reflections can hide superposed peaks. Slow actuation can still produce long-period level oscillations or unstable control interactions.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「往返時間與邊界」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Round-trip time and boundaries\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。","將單程時間當往返時間會改變快速與慢速的分類，忽略分岔反射則可能漏掉疊加峰值。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario.","Confusing one-way with round-trip time changes the rapid-action classification, while omitted branch reflections can hide superposed peaks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將單程時間當往返時間會改變快速與慢速的分類，忽略分岔反射則可能漏掉疊加峰值。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing one-way with round-trip time changes the rapid-action classification, while omitted branch reflections can hide superposed peaks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b260-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「快速變速壓力增量」與「井內連續方程」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rapid velocity-change pressure\" and \"Continuity within the shaft\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b260-v15-09","title":"快速變速壓力增量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rapid velocity-change pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「快速變速壓力增量」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rapid velocity-change pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"單相彈性管中的突然流速變化會形成壓力波，焦科夫斯基關係估第一個波前的壓力增量。它不是整段歷時的通用最大值，反射疊加、氣穴與控制器仍可能改變結果；應先區分增量和原有靜壓，再檢查是否仍滿足單相及快速動作假設。 假設ρ=1000kg/m³、a=1000m/s，0.5s內減速1m/s且小於2s往返，Δp=ρaΔV=1MPa，ΔH=101.94m。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「快速變速壓力增量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A rapid velocity change in a single-phase elastic conduit generates a pressure wave, with the Joukowsky relation estimating the first-front increment. It is not a universal maximum for the entire history: reflections, cavities and control behavior can alter the result. Distinguish this increment from initial pressure and verify both the rapid-action and single-phase assumptions. Assumeρ=1000kg/m³,a=1000m/s and velocity reduction1m/s in0.5s, shorter than2s round-trip. Initial pressure increment1MPa corresponds to101.94m head. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rapid velocity-change pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「快速變速壓力增量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rapid velocity-change pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-09-k1","title":"快速變速壓力增量","titleEn":"Rapid velocity-change pressure","text":"單相彈性管中的突然流速變化會形成壓力波，焦科夫斯基關係估第一個波前的壓力增量。它不是整段歷時的通用最大值，反射疊加、氣穴與控制器仍可能改變結果；應先區分增量和原有靜壓，再檢查是否仍滿足單相及快速動作假設。","textEn":"A rapid velocity change in a single-phase elastic conduit generates a pressure wave, with the Joukowsky relation estimating the first-front increment. It is not a universal maximum for the entire history: reflections, cavities and control behavior can alter the result.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「快速變速壓力增量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rapid velocity-change pressure\" is correct?","options":["單相彈性管中的突然流速變化會形成壓力波，焦科夫斯基關係估第一個波前的壓力增量。","焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。","瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。"],"optionsEn":["A rapid velocity change in a single-phase elastic conduit generates a pressure wave, with the Joukowsky relation estimating the first-front increment.","The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario.","An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"單相彈性管中的突然流速變化會形成壓力波，焦科夫斯基關係估第一個波前的壓力增量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A rapid velocity change in a single-phase elastic conduit generates a pressure wave, with the Joukowsky relation estimating the first-front increment. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b260-v15-10","title":"快速變速壓力增量：定量估算","titleEn":"Rapid velocity-change pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「快速變速壓力增量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rapid velocity-change pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設ρ=1000kg/m³、a=1000m/s，0.5s內減速1m/s且小於2s往返，Δp=ρaΔV=1MPa，ΔH=101.94m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assumeρ=1000kg/m³,a=1000m/s and velocity reduction1m/s in0.5s, shorter than2s round-trip. Initial pressure increment1MPa corresponds to101.94m head. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：明列初始壓力與增量的符號，核對減速與壓力上升的傳播方向。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: State initial pressure and increment signs and verify the propagation direction associated with deceleration.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設ρ=1000kg/m³、a=1000m/s，0.5s內減速1m/s且小於2s往返，Δp=ρaΔV=1MPa，ΔH=101.94m。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assumeρ=1000kg/m³,a=1000m/s and velocity reduction1m/s in0.5s, shorter than2s round-trip. Initial pressure increment1MPa corresponds to101.94m head.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「快速變速壓力增量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rapid velocity-change pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。"],"optionsEn":["The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b260-v15-11","title":"快速變速壓力增量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rapid velocity-change pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「快速變速壓力增量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rapid velocity-change pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"明列初始壓力與增量的符號，核對減速與壓力上升的傳播方向。將第一波預估和完整瞬態歷時比較，另查後續反射最低壓力、局部空化及機組反應，不把首波算式視為完整包絡。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"State initial pressure and increment signs and verify the propagation direction associated with deceleration. Compare the first-wave estimate with a full transient history and separately examine reflected minima, local cavitation and machine response rather than treating the first front as the complete envelope. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：明列初始壓力與增量的符號，核對減速與壓力上升的傳播方向。將第一波預估和完整瞬態歷時比較，另查後續反射最低壓力、局部空化及機組反應，不把首波算式視為完整包絡。","observationEn":"Site practice: State initial pressure and increment signs and verify the propagation direction associated with deceleration. Compare the first-wave estimate with a full transient history and separately examine reflected minima, local cavitation and machine response rather than treating the first front as the complete envelope.","failure":"注意干擾：把壓力增量當成總壓力會漏掉原有水頭，慢關閉時套完整瞬降公式又可能錯估反應。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating the increment as total pressure omits the initial head, while applying instantaneous reduction to slow closure misrepresents the response. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"明列初始壓力與增量的符號，核對減速與壓力上升的傳播方向。將第一波預估和完整瞬態歷時比較，另查後續反射最低壓力、局部空化及機組反應，不把首波算式視為完整包絡。","textEn":"State initial pressure and increment signs and verify the propagation direction associated with deceleration. Compare the first-wave estimate with a full transient history and separately examine reflected minima, local cavitation and machine response rather than treating the first front as the complete envelope.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"明列初始壓力與增量的符號，核對減速與壓力上升的傳播方向。將第一波預估和完整瞬態歷時比較，另查後續反射最低壓力、局部空化及機組反應，不把首波算式視為完整包絡。","textEn":"State initial pressure and increment signs and verify the propagation direction associated with deceleration. Compare the first-wave estimate with a full transient history and separately examine reflected minima, local cavitation and machine response rather than treating the first front as the complete envelope.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「快速變速壓力增量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rapid velocity-change pressure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。","明列初始壓力與增量的符號，核對減速與壓力上升的傳播方向。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct.","State initial pressure and increment signs and verify the propagation direction associated with deceleration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"明列初始壓力與增量的符號，核對減速與壓力上升的傳播方向。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"State initial pressure and increment signs and verify the propagation direction associated with deceleration. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b260-v15-12","title":"快速變速壓力增量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rapid velocity-change pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「快速變速壓力增量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rapid velocity-change pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把壓力增量當成總壓力會漏掉原有水頭，慢關閉時套完整瞬降公式又可能錯估反應。若發生水柱分離，重新閉合壓力不能靠原單相首波關係完整描述。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating the increment as total pressure omits the initial head, while applying instantaneous reduction to slow closure misrepresents the response. Column separation and rejoining cannot be fully described by the original single-phase first-wave relation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設ρ=1000kg/m³、a=1000m/s，0.5s內減速1m/s且小於2s往返，Δp=ρaΔV=1MPa，ΔH=101.94m。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Initial pressure increment1MPa corresponds to101.94m head.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把壓力增量當成總壓力會漏掉原有水頭，慢關閉時套完整瞬降公式又可能錯估反應。若發生水柱分離，重新閉合壓力不能靠原單相首波關係完整描述。","textEn":"Treating the increment as total pressure omits the initial head, while applying instantaneous reduction to slow closure misrepresents the response. Column separation and rejoining cannot be fully described by the original single-phase first-wave relation.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「快速變速壓力增量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rapid velocity-change pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把壓力增量當成總壓力會漏掉原有水頭，慢關閉時套完整瞬降公式又可能錯估反應。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。"],"optionsEn":["Treating the increment as total pressure omits the initial head, while applying instantaneous reduction to slow closure misrepresents the response.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把壓力增量當成總壓力會漏掉原有水頭，慢關閉時套完整瞬降公式又可能錯估反應。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating the increment as total pressure omits the initial head, while applying instantaneous reduction to slow closure misrepresents the response. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b260-v15-13","title":"井內連續方程：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Continuity within the shaft: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「井內連續方程」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Continuity within the shaft” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"調壓井提供暫時儲水空間，管內來水與下游取水不相等時便改變井內水位。這個體積平衡不需要先求水錘峰值，但流量差本身會隨水位與管內慣性變化；固定面積只能用在井身相應區段，不能把瞬時上升速率無限制外推。 假設井面積100m²、瞬時流入20及流出5m³/s，dz/dt=(20−5)/100=0.15m/s；流量差不假定長期固定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「井內連續方程」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A surge shaft temporarily stores the difference between conduit inflow and downstream demand. Volume continuity can be written before solving the pressure-wave peak, but that flow difference evolves with level and conduit inertia. Constant area applies only within the relevant shaft segment, and an instantaneous rise rate cannot be extrapolated indefinitely through the entire transient. Assume shaft area100m² with instantaneous inflow20 and outflow5m³/s. Rise ratedz/dt=0.15m/s does not assume that imbalance persists. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Continuity within the shaft” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「井內連續方程」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Continuity within the shaft”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-13-k1","title":"井內連續方程","titleEn":"Continuity within the shaft","text":"調壓井提供暫時儲水空間，管內來水與下游取水不相等時便改變井內水位。這個體積平衡不需要先求水錘峰值，但流量差本身會隨水位與管內慣性變化；固定面積只能用在井身相應區段，不能把瞬時上升速率無限制外推。","textEn":"A surge shaft temporarily stores the difference between conduit inflow and downstream demand. Volume continuity can be written before solving the pressure-wave peak, but that flow difference evolves with level and conduit inertia.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「井內連續方程」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Continuity within the shaft\" is correct?","options":["瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。","調壓井提供暫時儲水空間，管內來水與下游取水不相等時便改變井內水位。","調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow.","A surge shaft temporarily stores the difference between conduit inflow and downstream demand.","The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"調壓井提供暫時儲水空間，管內來水與下游取水不相等時便改變井內水位。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A surge shaft temporarily stores the difference between conduit inflow and downstream demand. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b260-v15-14","title":"井內連續方程：定量估算","titleEn":"Continuity within the shaft: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「井內連續方程」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Continuity within the shaft” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設井面積100m²、瞬時流入20及流出5m³/s，dz/dt=(20−5)/100=0.15m/s；流量差不假定長期固定。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume shaft area100m² with instantaneous inflow20 and outflow5m³/s. Rise ratedz/dt=0.15m/s does not assume that imbalance persists. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將流入流出正方向畫在接點，核對井面積是否隨高程變化，並用短時間積分檢查水位增量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw flow signs at the junction, check whether shaft area changes with elevation and verify level increments by short-step integration.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設井面積100m²、瞬時流入20及流出5m³/s，dz/dt=(20−5)/100=0.15m/s；流量差不假定長期固定。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume shaft area100m² with instantaneous inflow20 and outflow5m³/s. Rise ratedz/dt=0.15m/s does not assume that imbalance persists.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「井內連續方程」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Continuity within the shaft\", which statement holds?","options":["管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。","任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water.","Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b260-v15-15","title":"井內連續方程：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Continuity within the shaft: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「井內連續方程」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Continuity within the shaft” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將流入流出正方向畫在接點，核對井面積是否隨高程變化，並用短時間積分檢查水位增量。將算出的水位回饋到管路動量方程，不把指定流量差當成與井水位完全無關的邊界。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw flow signs at the junction, check whether shaft area changes with elevation and verify level increments by short-step integration. Feed the updated level back into conduit momentum rather than treating the imposed imbalance as independent of shaft water level. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將流入流出正方向畫在接點，核對井面積是否隨高程變化，並用短時間積分檢查水位增量。將算出的水位回饋到管路動量方程，不把指定流量差當成與井水位完全無關的邊界。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw flow signs at the junction, check whether shaft area changes with elevation and verify level increments by short-step integration. Feed the updated level back into conduit momentum rather than treating the imposed imbalance as independent of shaft water level.","failure":"注意干擾：面積使用直徑代替會破壞量綱，井身變截面時固定面積又會誤估上升速度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Substituting diameter for area breaks dimensional consistency, while changing shaft sections invalidate a fixed-area rate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將流入流出正方向畫在接點，核對井面積是否隨高程變化，並用短時間積分檢查水位增量。將算出的水位回饋到管路動量方程，不把指定流量差當成與井水位完全無關的邊界。","textEn":"Draw flow signs at the junction, check whether shaft area changes with elevation and verify level increments by short-step integration. Feed the updated level back into conduit momentum rather than treating the imposed imbalance as independent of shaft water level.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將流入流出正方向畫在接點，核對井面積是否隨高程變化，並用短時間積分檢查水位增量。將算出的水位回饋到管路動量方程，不把指定流量差當成與井水位完全無關的邊界。","textEn":"Draw flow signs at the junction, check whether shaft area changes with elevation and verify level increments by short-step integration. Feed the updated level back into conduit momentum rather than treating the imposed imbalance as independent of shaft water level.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「井內連續方程」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Continuity within the shaft\"?","options":["將流入流出正方向畫在接點，核對井面積是否隨高程變化，並用短時間積分檢查水位增量。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。"],"optionsEn":["Draw flow signs at the junction, check whether shaft area changes with elevation and verify level increments by short-step integration.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將流入流出正方向畫在接點，核對井面積是否隨高程變化，並用短時間積分檢查水位增量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw flow signs at the junction, check whether shaft area changes with elevation and verify level increments by short-step integration. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b260-v15-16","title":"井內連續方程：失效診斷","titleEn":"Continuity within the shaft: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「井內連續方程」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Continuity within the shaft” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"面積使用直徑代替會破壞量綱，井身變截面時固定面積又會誤估上升速度。只積分入流不扣下游流量，會虛增儲水並製造不存在的溢井預測。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Substituting diameter for area breaks dimensional consistency, while changing shaft sections invalidate a fixed-area rate. Integrating inflow without subtracting downstream flow invents storage and can predict a shaft overflow that the stated balance does not support. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設井面積100m²、瞬時流入20及流出5m³/s，dz/dt=(20−5)/100=0.15m/s；流量差不假定長期固定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Rise ratedz/dt=0.15m/s does not assume that imbalance persists.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"面積使用直徑代替會破壞量綱，井身變截面時固定面積又會誤估上升速度。只積分入流不扣下游流量，會虛增儲水並製造不存在的溢井預測。","textEn":"Substituting diameter for area breaks dimensional consistency, while changing shaft sections invalidate a fixed-area rate. Integrating inflow without subtracting downstream flow invents storage and can predict a shaft overflow that the stated balance does not support.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「井內連續方程」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Continuity within the shaft\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","面積使用直徑代替會破壞量綱，井身變截面時固定面積又會誤估上升速度。","調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Substituting diameter for area breaks dimensional consistency, while changing shaft sections invalidate a fixed-area rate.","The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"面積使用直徑代替會破壞量綱，井身變截面時固定面積又會誤估上升速度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Substituting diameter for area breaks dimensional consistency, while changing shaft sections invalidate a fixed-area rate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b260-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「剛性水柱振盪週期」與「理想湧升能量界限」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rigid-column oscillation period\" and \"Ideal upsurge energy estimate\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b260-v15-17","title":"剛性水柱振盪週期：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rigid-column oscillation period: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「剛性水柱振盪週期」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rigid-column oscillation period” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"較慢的井水位振盪可在特定條件下用剛性水柱近似，水柱慣性與自由水面重力形成回復系統。這與快速彈性波不同，忽略摩擦與壓縮性只為得到可核對的基準週期；實際控制器、節流口及變截面會改變衰減與穩定性。 假設定水位上庫、均勻管L=1000m及Ap=10m²、井As=100m²，無摩擦小振幅且忽略井水慣性，T=2π√(LAs/gAp)=200.607s。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「剛性水柱振盪週期」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Slower shaft-level oscillation can be approximated by a rigid water column under defined conditions, with column inertia and free-surface gravity forming a restoring system. This differs from the fast elastic wave. Neglecting friction and compressibility gives a checkable reference period, while controls, throttles and variable geometry change damping and stability in the actual installation. Assume fixed reservoir level, uniform conduitL=1000m,Ap=10m² and shaftAs=100m². Frictionless small oscillations neglecting shaft inertia haveT=200.607s. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rigid-column oscillation period” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「剛性水柱振盪週期」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rigid-column oscillation period”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-17-k1","title":"剛性水柱振盪週期","titleEn":"Rigid-column oscillation period","text":"較慢的井水位振盪可在特定條件下用剛性水柱近似，水柱慣性與自由水面重力形成回復系統。這與快速彈性波不同，忽略摩擦與壓縮性只為得到可核對的基準週期；實際控制器、節流口及變截面會改變衰減與穩定性。","textEn":"Slower shaft-level oscillation can be approximated by a rigid water column under defined conditions, with column inertia and free-surface gravity forming a restoring system. This differs from the fast elastic wave.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「剛性水柱振盪週期」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rigid-column oscillation period\" is correct?","options":["調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。","理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。","較慢的井水位振盪可在特定條件下用剛性水柱近似，水柱慣性與自由水面重力形成回復系統。"],"optionsEn":["The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time.","The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft.","Slower shaft-level oscillation can be approximated by a rigid water column under defined conditions, with column inertia and free-surface gravity forming a restoring system."],"answer":2,"explanation":"較慢的井水位振盪可在特定條件下用剛性水柱近似，水柱慣性與自由水面重力形成回復系統。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Slower shaft-level oscillation can be approximated by a rigid water column under defined conditions, with column inertia and free-surface gravity forming a restoring system. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b260-v15-18","title":"剛性水柱振盪週期：定量估算","titleEn":"Rigid-column oscillation period: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剛性水柱振盪週期」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rigid-column oscillation period” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設定水位上庫、均勻管L=1000m及Ap=10m²、井As=100m²，無摩擦小振幅且忽略井水慣性，T=2π√(LAs/gAp)=200.607s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume fixed reservoir level, uniform conduitL=1000m,Ap=10m² and shaftAs=100m². Frictionless small oscillations neglecting shaft inertia haveT=200.607s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將管內剛性水柱動量與井內連續方程聯立，核對係數量綱為時間平方。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Couple rigid-column momentum with shaft continuity and check that the period coefficient has time-squared units.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設定水位上庫、均勻管L=1000m及Ap=10m²、井As=100m²，無摩擦小振幅且忽略井水慣性，T=2π√(LAs/gAp)=200.607s。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume fixed reservoir level, uniform conduitL=1000m,Ap=10m² and shaftAs=100m². Frictionless small oscillations neglecting shaft inertia haveT=200.607s.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「剛性水柱振盪週期」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rigid-column oscillation period\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。","Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system.","A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b260-v15-19","title":"剛性水柱振盪週期：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rigid-column oscillation period: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剛性水柱振盪週期」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rigid-column oscillation period” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將管內剛性水柱動量與井內連續方程聯立，核對係數量綱為時間平方。以小擾動數值解比較解析週期，再逐步加入摩擦、井水慣性與控制器，標註每次加入機制後的週期及衰減差異。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Couple rigid-column momentum with shaft continuity and check that the period coefficient has time-squared units. Compare an analytical period with a small-disturbance numerical solution, then add friction, shaft inertia and controls separately, recording changes in period and damping. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將管內剛性水柱動量與井內連續方程聯立，核對係數量綱為時間平方。以小擾動數值解比較解析週期，再逐步加入摩擦、井水慣性與控制器，標註每次加入機制後的週期及衰減差異。","observationEn":"Site practice: Couple rigid-column momentum with shaft continuity and check that the period coefficient has time-squared units. Compare an analytical period with a small-disturbance numerical solution, then add friction, shaft inertia and controls separately, recording changes in period and damping.","failure":"注意干擾：用此長週期代替壓力波往返時間會漏掉早期水錘，忽略機組控制又可能看不到自激振盪。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using this long period in place of wave travel time misses early water hammer, and omitted machine control can hide self-excitation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將管內剛性水柱動量與井內連續方程聯立，核對係數量綱為時間平方。以小擾動數值解比較解析週期，再逐步加入摩擦、井水慣性與控制器，標註每次加入機制後的週期及衰減差異。","textEn":"Couple rigid-column momentum with shaft continuity and check that the period coefficient has time-squared units. Compare an analytical period with a small-disturbance numerical solution, then add friction, shaft inertia and controls separately, recording changes in period and damping.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將管內剛性水柱動量與井內連續方程聯立，核對係數量綱為時間平方。以小擾動數值解比較解析週期，再逐步加入摩擦、井水慣性與控制器，標註每次加入機制後的週期及衰減差異。","textEn":"Couple rigid-column momentum with shaft continuity and check that the period coefficient has time-squared units. Compare an analytical period with a small-disturbance numerical solution, then add friction, shaft inertia and controls separately, recording changes in period and damping.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「剛性水柱振盪週期」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rigid-column oscillation period\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","將管內剛性水柱動量與井內連續方程聯立，核對係數量綱為時間平方。","閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Couple rigid-column momentum with shaft continuity and check that the period coefficient has time-squared units.","An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將管內剛性水柱動量與井內連續方程聯立，核對係數量綱為時間平方。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Couple rigid-column momentum with shaft continuity and check that the period coefficient has time-squared units. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b260-v15-20","title":"剛性水柱振盪週期：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rigid-column oscillation period: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剛性水柱振盪週期」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rigid-column oscillation period” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用此長週期代替壓力波往返時間會漏掉早期水錘，忽略機組控制又可能看不到自激振盪。模型沒有耗散時持續振動是其假設結果，不能當成實際阻尼證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using this long period in place of wave travel time misses early water hammer, and omitted machine control can hide self-excitation. Persistent motion in a lossless model follows its assumptions and does not measure real-system damping. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設定水位上庫、均勻管L=1000m及Ap=10m²、井As=100m²，無摩擦小振幅且忽略井水慣性，T=2π√(LAs/gAp)=200.607s。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Frictionless small oscillations neglecting shaft inertia haveT=200.607s.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用此長週期代替壓力波往返時間會漏掉早期水錘，忽略機組控制又可能看不到自激振盪。模型沒有耗散時持續振動是其假設結果，不能當成實際阻尼證據。","textEn":"Using this long period in place of wave travel time misses early water hammer, and omitted machine control can hide self-excitation. Persistent motion in a lossless model follows its assumptions and does not measure real-system damping.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「剛性水柱振盪週期」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rigid-column oscillation period\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。","用此長週期代替壓力波往返時間會漏掉早期水錘，忽略機組控制又可能看不到自激振盪。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft.","Using this long period in place of wave travel time misses early water hammer, and omitted machine control can hide self-excitation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用此長週期代替壓力波往返時間會漏掉早期水錘，忽略機組控制又可能看不到自激振盪。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using this long period in place of wave travel time misses early water hammer, and omitted machine control can hide self-excitation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b260-v15-21","title":"理想湧升能量界限：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ideal upsurge energy estimate: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「理想湧升能量界限」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ideal upsurge energy estimate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"突然停止下游取水後，管內水柱動能可轉為井中水位上升的位能，提供無損理想基準。必須把井位移相對於固定水庫水面定義，並說明初始水位偏差；忽略摩擦、井水慣性與壓力彈性能量時，結果不能視為實際溢流高度的完整設計包絡。 假設初始井位等於固定庫位、L=1000m、Ap=10m²、As=100m²、V0=2m/s，瞬停下游且無損，zmax=V0√(LAp/gAs)=6.3855m。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「理想湧升能量界限」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After downstream demand stops, conduit kinetic energy can become potential energy in a rising shaft, giving a lossless reference. Define displacement relative to the fixed reservoir surface and specify the initial level offset. When friction, shaft inertia and elastic-wave energy are omitted, the estimate cannot serve as a complete design envelope for actual overflow height. Assume initial shaft level equals fixed reservoir level,L=1000m,Ap=10m²,As=100m²,V0=2m/s and instantaneous demand stop. Lossless rigid-columnzmax=6.3855m. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ideal upsurge energy estimate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「理想湧升能量界限」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ideal upsurge energy estimate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-21-k1","title":"理想湧升能量界限","titleEn":"Ideal upsurge energy estimate","text":"突然停止下游取水後，管內水柱動能可轉為井中水位上升的位能，提供無損理想基準。必須把井位移相對於固定水庫水面定義，並說明初始水位偏差；忽略摩擦、井水慣性與壓力彈性能量時，結果不能視為實際溢流高度的完整設計包絡。","textEn":"After downstream demand stops, conduit kinetic energy can become potential energy in a rising shaft, giving a lossless reference. Define displacement relative to the fixed reservoir surface and specify the initial level offset.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「理想湧升能量界限」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ideal upsurge energy estimate\" is correct?","options":["突然停止下游取水後，管內水柱動能可轉為井中水位上升的位能，提供無損理想基準。","理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。","管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。"],"optionsEn":["After downstream demand stops, conduit kinetic energy can become potential energy in a rising shaft, giving a lossless reference.","The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft.","During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water."],"answer":0,"explanation":"突然停止下游取水後，管內水柱動能可轉為井中水位上升的位能，提供無損理想基準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After downstream demand stops, conduit kinetic energy can become potential energy in a rising shaft, giving a lossless reference. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b260-v15-22","title":"理想湧升能量界限：定量估算","titleEn":"Ideal upsurge energy estimate: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「理想湧升能量界限」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ideal upsurge energy estimate” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設初始井位等於固定庫位、L=1000m、Ap=10m²、As=100m²、V0=2m/s，瞬停下游且無損，zmax=V0√(LAp/gAs)=6.3855m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume initial shaft level equals fixed reservoir level,L=1000m,Ap=10m²,As=100m²,V0=2m/s and instantaneous demand stop. Lossless rigid-columnzmax=6.3855m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：寫出初始水柱動能與井水位能的等式，確認上庫可視為定水位且初始井位偏差為零。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Write initial column kinetic energy and shaft potential energy, checking fixed reservoir level and zero initial shaft offset.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設初始井位等於固定庫位、L=1000m、Ap=10m²、As=100m²、V0=2m/s，瞬停下游且無損，zmax=V0√(LAp/gAs)=6.3855m。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume initial shaft level equals fixed reservoir level,L=1000m,Ap=10m²,As=100m²,V0=2m/s and instantaneous demand stop. Lossless rigid-columnzmax=6.3855m.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「理想湧升能量界限」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ideal upsurge energy estimate\", which statement holds?","options":["任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。"],"optionsEn":["Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b260-v15-23","title":"理想湧升能量界限：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ideal upsurge energy estimate: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「理想湧升能量界限」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ideal upsurge energy estimate” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"寫出初始水柱動能與井水位能的等式，確認上庫可視為定水位且初始井位偏差為零。再用動量連續方程數值解對照，另測非零初始偏差、損失和彈性波對最高及最低水位的影響。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Write initial column kinetic energy and shaft potential energy, checking fixed reservoir level and zero initial shaft offset. Compare with coupled momentum-continuity integration, then separately test nonzero initial offset, loss and elastic-wave effects on both maximum and minimum levels. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：寫出初始水柱動能與井水位能的等式，確認上庫可視為定水位且初始井位偏差為零。再用動量連續方程數值解對照，另測非零初始偏差、損失和彈性波對最高及最低水位的影響。","observationEn":"Site practice: Write initial column kinetic energy and shaft potential energy, checking fixed reservoir level and zero initial shaft offset. Compare with coupled momentum-continuity integration, then separately test nonzero initial offset, loss and elastic-wave effects on both maximum and minimum levels.","failure":"注意干擾：初始井水位若已因摩擦低於庫位，直接套零偏差公式會遺漏能量項。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An initial shaft level depressed by friction requires an additional energy term. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"寫出初始水柱動能與井水位能的等式，確認上庫可視為定水位且初始井位偏差為零。再用動量連續方程數值解對照，另測非零初始偏差、損失和彈性波對最高及最低水位的影響。","textEn":"Write initial column kinetic energy and shaft potential energy, checking fixed reservoir level and zero initial shaft offset. Compare with coupled momentum-continuity integration, then separately test nonzero initial offset, loss and elastic-wave effects on both maximum and minimum levels.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"寫出初始水柱動能與井水位能的等式，確認上庫可視為定水位且初始井位偏差為零。再用動量連續方程數值解對照，另測非零初始偏差、損失和彈性波對最高及最低水位的影響。","textEn":"Write initial column kinetic energy and shaft potential energy, checking fixed reservoir level and zero initial shaft offset. Compare with coupled momentum-continuity integration, then separately test nonzero initial offset, loss and elastic-wave effects on both maximum and minimum levels.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「理想湧升能量界限」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ideal upsurge energy estimate\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。","寫出初始水柱動能與井水位能的等式，確認上庫可視為定水位且初始井位偏差為零。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario.","Write initial column kinetic energy and shaft potential energy, checking fixed reservoir level and zero initial shaft offset."],"answer":2,"explanation":"寫出初始水柱動能與井水位能的等式，確認上庫可視為定水位且初始井位偏差為零。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Write initial column kinetic energy and shaft potential energy, checking fixed reservoir level and zero initial shaft offset. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b260-v15-24","title":"理想湧升能量界限：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ideal upsurge energy estimate: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「理想湧升能量界限」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ideal upsurge energy estimate” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"初始井水位若已因摩擦低於庫位，直接套零偏差公式會遺漏能量項。把無損湧升直接當允許井高也會忽略自由高、通氣與更複雜邊界造成的變化。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An initial shaft level depressed by friction requires an additional energy term. Treating the lossless rise as an allowable shaft height also omits freeboard, ventilation and changes caused by more complex boundaries. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設初始井位等於固定庫位、L=1000m、Ap=10m²、As=100m²、V0=2m/s，瞬停下游且無損，zmax=V0√(LAp/gAs)=6.3855m。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Lossless rigid-columnzmax=6.3855m.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"初始井水位若已因摩擦低於庫位，直接套零偏差公式會遺漏能量項。把無損湧升直接當允許井高也會忽略自由高、通氣與更複雜邊界造成的變化。","textEn":"An initial shaft level depressed by friction requires an additional energy term. Treating the lossless rise as an allowable shaft height also omits freeboard, ventilation and changes caused by more complex boundaries.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「理想湧升能量界限」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ideal upsurge energy estimate\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["初始井水位若已因摩擦低於庫位，直接套零偏差公式會遺漏能量項。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。"],"optionsEn":["An initial shaft level depressed by friction requires an additional energy term.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water."],"answer":0,"explanation":"初始井水位若已因摩擦低於庫位，直接套零偏差公式會遺漏能量項。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An initial shaft level depressed by friction requires an additional energy term. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b260-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「沿程摩擦與耗散」與「節流孔與局部損失」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Distributed friction and dissipation\" and \"Throttle opening and local loss\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b260-v15-25","title":"沿程摩擦與耗散：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Distributed friction and dissipation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「沿程摩擦與耗散」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Distributed friction and dissipation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"管壁摩擦耗散能量並影響井水振盪衰減，穩態摩擦式可作第一層準穩態近似。反向流動時損失應反向抵抗速度，不能永遠沿固定坐標扣水頭；快速瞬態的非穩態摩擦則可能需要額外模型，不能只靠增大摩擦係數修正錯誤結果。 假設Darcy摩擦係數0.02、管長1000m、直徑2m、速率2m/s，hf=f(L/D)V²/(2g)=2.0387m，僅為此工況準穩態損失。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沿程摩擦與耗散」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Wall friction dissipates energy and influences surge decay, with a steady relation serving as a first quasi-steady approximation. During flow reversal the loss must oppose velocity rather than remain fixed in one coordinate direction. Rapid transients may require unsteady friction, which should not be replaced by arbitrarily increasing a coefficient to compensate for an incorrect model. Assume Darcy factor0.02,length1000m,diameter2m and speed2m/s. Quasi-steady loss hf=f(L/D)V²/(2g)=2.0387m at this condition. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Distributed friction and dissipation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沿程摩擦與耗散」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Distributed friction and dissipation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-25-k1","title":"沿程摩擦與耗散","titleEn":"Distributed friction and dissipation","text":"管壁摩擦耗散能量並影響井水振盪衰減，穩態摩擦式可作第一層準穩態近似。反向流動時損失應反向抵抗速度，不能永遠沿固定坐標扣水頭；快速瞬態的非穩態摩擦則可能需要額外模型，不能只靠增大摩擦係數修正錯誤結果。","textEn":"Wall friction dissipates energy and influences surge decay, with a steady relation serving as a first quasi-steady approximation. During flow reversal the loss must oppose velocity rather than remain fixed in one coordinate direction.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沿程摩擦與耗散」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Distributed friction and dissipation\" is correct?","options":["管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。","管壁摩擦耗散能量並影響井水振盪衰減，穩態摩擦式可作第一層準穩態近似。","節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。"],"optionsEn":["During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water.","Wall friction dissipates energy and influences surge decay, with a steady relation serving as a first quasi-steady approximation.","A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system."],"answer":1,"explanation":"管壁摩擦耗散能量並影響井水振盪衰減，穩態摩擦式可作第一層準穩態近似。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Wall friction dissipates energy and influences surge decay, with a steady relation serving as a first quasi-steady approximation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b260-v15-26","title":"沿程摩擦與耗散：定量估算","titleEn":"Distributed friction and dissipation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沿程摩擦與耗散」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Distributed friction and dissipation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設Darcy摩擦係數0.02、管長1000m、直徑2m、速率2m/s，hf=f(L/D)V²/(2g)=2.0387m，僅為此工況準穩態損失。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume Darcy factor0.02,length1000m,diameter2m and speed2m/s. Quasi-steady loss hf=f(L/D)V²/(2g)=2.0387m at this condition. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：註明使用Darcy而非Fanning係數，從粗糙度與雷諾數核對假設範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Identify the Darcy rather than Fanning convention and check roughness and Reynolds assumptions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設Darcy摩擦係數0.02、管長1000m、直徑2m、速率2m/s，hf=f(L/D)V²/(2g)=2.0387m，僅為此工況準穩態損失。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume Darcy factor0.02,length1000m,diameter2m and speed2m/s. Quasi-steady loss hf=f(L/D)V²/(2g)=2.0387m at this condition.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沿程摩擦與耗散」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Distributed friction and dissipation\", which statement holds?","options":["Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。","閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct.","An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b260-v15-27","title":"沿程摩擦與耗散：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Distributed friction and dissipation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沿程摩擦與耗散」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Distributed friction and dissipation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"註明使用Darcy而非Fanning係數，從粗糙度與雷諾數核對假設範圍。將摩擦寫成抵抗流向的V乘絕對V形式，檢查流向反轉時仍耗能，再比較不同摩擦模型對衰減歷時的影響。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Identify the Darcy rather than Fanning convention and check roughness and Reynolds assumptions. Express directional friction using velocity times its magnitude, verify dissipation during reversal and compare how alternative friction representations change the decay history. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：註明使用Darcy而非Fanning係數，從粗糙度與雷諾數核對假設範圍。將摩擦寫成抵抗流向的V乘絕對V形式，檢查流向反轉時仍耗能，再比較不同摩擦模型對衰減歷時的影響。","observationEn":"Site practice: Identify the Darcy rather than Fanning convention and check roughness and Reynolds assumptions. Express directional friction using velocity times its magnitude, verify dissipation during reversal and compare how alternative friction representations change the decay history.","failure":"注意干擾：混淆兩種摩擦係數可造成四倍差異，流向反轉後符號不改更可能讓摩擦虛假供能。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing friction conventions introduces a factor-of-four error, and the wrong reversal sign can make friction supply energy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"註明使用Darcy而非Fanning係數，從粗糙度與雷諾數核對假設範圍。將摩擦寫成抵抗流向的V乘絕對V形式，檢查流向反轉時仍耗能，再比較不同摩擦模型對衰減歷時的影響。","textEn":"Identify the Darcy rather than Fanning convention and check roughness and Reynolds assumptions. Express directional friction using velocity times its magnitude, verify dissipation during reversal and compare how alternative friction representations change the decay history.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"註明使用Darcy而非Fanning係數，從粗糙度與雷諾數核對假設範圍。將摩擦寫成抵抗流向的V乘絕對V形式，檢查流向反轉時仍耗能，再比較不同摩擦模型對衰減歷時的影響。","textEn":"Identify the Darcy rather than Fanning convention and check roughness and Reynolds assumptions. Express directional friction using velocity times its magnitude, verify dissipation during reversal and compare how alternative friction representations change the decay history.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沿程摩擦與耗散」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Distributed friction and dissipation\"?","options":["註明使用Darcy而非Fanning係數，從粗糙度與雷諾數核對假設範圍。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。"],"optionsEn":["Identify the Darcy rather than Fanning convention and check roughness and Reynolds assumptions.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"註明使用Darcy而非Fanning係數，從粗糙度與雷諾數核對假設範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Identify the Darcy rather than Fanning convention and check roughness and Reynolds assumptions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b260-v15-28","title":"沿程摩擦與耗散：失效診斷","titleEn":"Distributed friction and dissipation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沿程摩擦與耗散」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Distributed friction and dissipation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"混淆兩種摩擦係數可造成四倍差異，流向反轉後符號不改更可能讓摩擦虛假供能。以強阻尼掩蓋時間步誤差，會讓看似平順的曲線失去物理可信度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing friction conventions introduces a factor-of-four error, and the wrong reversal sign can make friction supply energy. Artificial damping that hides time-step errors yields smooth-looking curves without reliable physical meaning. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設Darcy摩擦係數0.02、管長1000m、直徑2m、速率2m/s，hf=f(L/D)V²/(2g)=2.0387m，僅為此工況準穩態損失。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Quasi-steady loss hf=f(L/D)V²/(2g)=2.0387m at this condition.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"混淆兩種摩擦係數可造成四倍差異，流向反轉後符號不改更可能讓摩擦虛假供能。以強阻尼掩蓋時間步誤差，會讓看似平順的曲線失去物理可信度。","textEn":"Confusing friction conventions introduces a factor-of-four error, and the wrong reversal sign can make friction supply energy. Artificial damping that hides time-step errors yields smooth-looking curves without reliable physical meaning.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沿程摩擦與耗散」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Distributed friction and dissipation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","混淆兩種摩擦係數可造成四倍差異，流向反轉後符號不改更可能讓摩擦虛假供能。","節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Confusing friction conventions introduces a factor-of-four error, and the wrong reversal sign can make friction supply energy.","A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system."],"answer":1,"explanation":"混淆兩種摩擦係數可造成四倍差異，流向反轉後符號不改更可能讓摩擦虛假供能。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing friction conventions introduces a factor-of-four error, and the wrong reversal sign can make friction supply energy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b260-v15-29","title":"節流孔與局部損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Throttle opening and local loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「節流孔與局部損失」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Throttle opening and local loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"節流可改變井與主管之間的交換及耗散，但更大阻力不保證所有壓力峰值都下降。孔口附近的局部低壓、流向切換和收縮係數需要另外檢查；準穩態孔流關係只描述指定瞬間的流量水頭差，不能直接取代完整調壓設施的瞬態模型。 假設孔口Q=10m³/s、Cd=0.65、有效面積2m²，水頭差h=(Q/CdA)²/(2g)=3.0159m；未驗局部空化。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「節流孔與局部損失」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A throttle changes exchange and dissipation between shaft and conduit, but increased resistance does not guarantee lower pressure peaks everywhere. Local suction, reversal and contraction behavior require separate checks. A quasi-steady orifice relation describes one flow-head condition and cannot replace a transient model of the complete surge arrangement and its connected waterway. Assume orifice flow10m³/s, coefficient0.65 and effective area2m². Head differenceh=(Q/CdA)²/(2g)=3.0159m, without evaluating local cavitation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Throttle opening and local loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「節流孔與局部損失」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Throttle opening and local loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-29-k1","title":"節流孔與局部損失","titleEn":"Throttle opening and local loss","text":"節流可改變井與主管之間的交換及耗散，但更大阻力不保證所有壓力峰值都下降。孔口附近的局部低壓、流向切換和收縮係數需要另外檢查；準穩態孔流關係只描述指定瞬間的流量水頭差，不能直接取代完整調壓設施的瞬態模型。","textEn":"A throttle changes exchange and dissipation between shaft and conduit, but increased resistance does not guarantee lower pressure peaks everywhere. Local suction, reversal and contraction behavior require separate checks.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「節流孔與局部損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Throttle opening and local loss\" is correct?","options":["節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。","任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。","節流可改變井與主管之間的交換及耗散，但更大阻力不保證所有壓力峰值都下降。"],"optionsEn":["A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system.","Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere.","A throttle changes exchange and dissipation between shaft and conduit, but increased resistance does not guarantee lower pressure peaks everywhere."],"answer":2,"explanation":"節流可改變井與主管之間的交換及耗散，但更大阻力不保證所有壓力峰值都下降。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A throttle changes exchange and dissipation between shaft and conduit, but increased resistance does not guarantee lower pressure peaks everywhere. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b260-v15-30","title":"節流孔與局部損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Throttle opening and local loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「節流孔與局部損失」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Throttle opening and local loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設孔口Q=10m³/s、Cd=0.65、有效面積2m²，水頭差h=(Q/CdA)²/(2g)=3.0159m；未驗局部空化。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume orifice flow10m³/s, coefficient0.65 and effective area2m². Head differenceh=(Q/CdA)²/(2g)=3.0159m, without evaluating local cavitation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對係數對應的幾何與流向，標明有效孔面積而非整個井面積。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check the coefficient’s geometry and direction and use opening area rather than full shaft area.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設孔口Q=10m³/s、Cd=0.65、有效面積2m²，水頭差h=(Q/CdA)²/(2g)=3.0159m；未驗局部空化。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume orifice flow10m³/s, coefficient0.65 and effective area2m². Head differenceh=(Q/CdA)²/(2g)=3.0159m, without evaluating local cavitation.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「節流孔與局部損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Throttle opening and local loss\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設，非操作設定。","水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。","焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas.","The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b260-v15-31","title":"節流孔與局部損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Throttle opening and local loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「節流孔與局部損失」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Throttle opening and local loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對係數對應的幾何與流向，標明有效孔面積而非整個井面積。比較入井與出井的壓差資料，將孔口關係接入動量及連續方程，再檢查最低絕對壓力與反向流條件而非只看耗能增加。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check the coefficient’s geometry and direction and use opening area rather than full shaft area. Compare inward and outward pressure differences, couple the opening relation to momentum and continuity and inspect minimum absolute pressure and reversal rather than only increased dissipation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：核對係數對應的幾何與流向，標明有效孔面積而非整個井面積。比較入井與出井的壓差資料，將孔口關係接入動量及連續方程，再檢查最低絕對壓力與反向流條件而非只看耗能增加。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check the coefficient’s geometry and direction and use opening area rather than full shaft area. Compare inward and outward pressure differences, couple the opening relation to momentum and continuity and inspect minimum absolute pressure and reversal rather than only increased dissipation.","failure":"注意干擾：孔口太小可能限制快速交換而提高主管壓力，收縮區低壓也可能造成空化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An overly restrictive opening can hinder rapid exchange and raise conduit pressure, while a contracted jet can cavitate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對係數對應的幾何與流向，標明有效孔面積而非整個井面積。比較入井與出井的壓差資料，將孔口關係接入動量及連續方程，再檢查最低絕對壓力與反向流條件而非只看耗能增加。","textEn":"Check the coefficient’s geometry and direction and use opening area rather than full shaft area. Compare inward and outward pressure differences, couple the opening relation to momentum and continuity and inspect minimum absolute pressure and reversal rather than only increased dissipation.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"核對係數對應的幾何與流向，標明有效孔面積而非整個井面積。比較入井與出井的壓差資料，將孔口關係接入動量及連續方程，再檢查最低絕對壓力與反向流條件而非只看耗能增加。","textEn":"Check the coefficient’s geometry and direction and use opening area rather than full shaft area. Compare inward and outward pressure differences, couple the opening relation to momentum and continuity and inspect minimum absolute pressure and reversal rather than only increased dissipation.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「節流孔與局部損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Throttle opening and local loss\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對係數對應的幾何與流向，標明有效孔面積而非整個井面積。","調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check the coefficient’s geometry and direction and use opening area rather than full shaft area.","The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對係數對應的幾何與流向，標明有效孔面積而非整個井面積。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check the coefficient’s geometry and direction and use opening area rather than full shaft area. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b260-v15-32","title":"節流孔與局部損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Throttle opening and local loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「節流孔與局部損失」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Throttle opening and local loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"孔口太小可能限制快速交換而提高主管壓力，收縮區低壓也可能造成空化。直接用同一係數描述兩個方向，會漏掉非對稱構造引起的不同水頭損失。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An overly restrictive opening can hinder rapid exchange and raise conduit pressure, while a contracted jet can cavitate. Applying one coefficient to both directions misses asymmetric losses caused by the actual opening arrangement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設孔口Q=10m³/s、Cd=0.65、有效面積2m²，水頭差h=(Q/CdA)²/(2g)=3.0159m；未驗局部空化。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Head differenceh=(Q/CdA)²/(2g)=3.0159m, without evaluating local cavitation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「節流孔越小就必定同時降低所有位置的最大與最小壓力風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A smaller throttle opening necessarily reduces every maximum- and minimum-pressure risk throughout the system.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"孔口太小可能限制快速交換而提高主管壓力，收縮區低壓也可能造成空化。直接用同一係數描述兩個方向，會漏掉非對稱構造引起的不同水頭損失。","textEn":"An overly restrictive opening can hinder rapid exchange and raise conduit pressure, while a contracted jet can cavitate. Applying one coefficient to both directions misses asymmetric losses caused by the actual opening arrangement.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「節流孔與局部損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Throttle opening and local loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。","孔口太小可能限制快速交換而提高主管壓力，收縮區低壓也可能造成空化。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere.","An overly restrictive opening can hinder rapid exchange and raise conduit pressure, while a contracted jet can cavitate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"孔口太小可能限制快速交換而提高主管壓力，收縮區低壓也可能造成空化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An overly restrictive opening can hinder rapid exchange and raise conduit pressure, while a contracted jet can cavitate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b260-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「絕對壓力與汽化」與「特徵網格與收斂」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Absolute pressure and vapor formation\" and \"Characteristic grid and convergence\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b260-v15-33","title":"絕對壓力與汽化：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Absolute pressure and vapor formation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「絕對壓力與汽化」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Absolute pressure and vapor formation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"負表壓不等於汽化，必須加上當地大氣壓後與相應溫度的蒸氣壓比較。即使某測點高於蒸氣壓，附近收縮區或未量到的瞬態仍可能更低；水柱分離涉及兩相或氣穴模型，不能把單相計算得到的不合理低壓照單全收。 假設大氣壓100kPa、表壓−80kPa、蒸氣壓2.34kPa，絕對壓20kPa，比蒸氣壓高17.66kPa；只代表該點該時刻。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「絕對壓力與汽化」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Negative gauge pressure is not itself vapor formation; add local atmospheric pressure and compare against vapor pressure at the relevant temperature. A measured point above vapor pressure does not exclude lower local or unresolved transient values. Column separation requires appropriate cavity or multiphase treatment rather than accepting physically impossible pressures from a single-phase computation. Assume atmospheric100kPa,gauge−80kPa and vapor pressure2.34kPa. Absolute pressure20kPa exceeds vapor by17.66kPa only at that location and instant. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Absolute pressure and vapor formation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「絕對壓力與汽化」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Absolute pressure and vapor formation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-33-k1","title":"絕對壓力與汽化","titleEn":"Absolute pressure and vapor formation","text":"負表壓不等於汽化，必須加上當地大氣壓後與相應溫度的蒸氣壓比較。即使某測點高於蒸氣壓，附近收縮區或未量到的瞬態仍可能更低；水柱分離涉及兩相或氣穴模型，不能把單相計算得到的不合理低壓照單全收。","textEn":"Negative gauge pressure is not itself vapor formation; add local atmospheric pressure and compare against vapor pressure at the relevant temperature. A measured point above vapor pressure does not exclude lower local or unresolved transient values.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「絕對壓力與汽化」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Absolute pressure and vapor formation\" is correct?","options":["負表壓不等於汽化，必須加上當地大氣壓後與相應溫度的蒸氣壓比較。","任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。","Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。"],"optionsEn":["Negative gauge pressure is not itself vapor formation; add local atmospheric pressure and compare against vapor pressure at the relevant temperature.","Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere.","A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct."],"answer":0,"explanation":"負表壓不等於汽化，必須加上當地大氣壓後與相應溫度的蒸氣壓比較。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Negative gauge pressure is not itself vapor formation; add local atmospheric pressure and compare against vapor pressure at the relevant temperature. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b260-v15-34","title":"絕對壓力與汽化：定量估算","titleEn":"Absolute pressure and vapor formation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「絕對壓力與汽化」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Absolute pressure and vapor formation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設大氣壓100kPa、表壓−80kPa、蒸氣壓2.34kPa，絕對壓20kPa，比蒸氣壓高17.66kPa；只代表該點該時刻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume atmospheric100kPa,gauge−80kPa and vapor pressure2.34kPa. Absolute pressure20kPa exceeds vapor by17.66kPa only at that location and instant. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：確認壓力感測器為表壓或絕對型，記錄大氣壓與水溫並統一基準。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify gauge versus absolute instrumentation, record atmospheric pressure and temperature and align references.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設大氣壓100kPa、表壓−80kPa、蒸氣壓2.34kPa，絕對壓20kPa，比蒸氣壓高17.66kPa；只代表該點該時刻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assume atmospheric100kPa,gauge−80kPa and vapor pressure2.34kPa. Absolute pressure20kPa exceeds vapor by17.66kPa only at that location and instant.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「絕對壓力與汽化」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Absolute pressure and vapor formation\", which statement holds?","options":["閥門動作時間大於單一往返時間就一定不會出現任何危險壓力。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。","瞬時水位上升速度可直接乘任意長時間而不必更新管內流量。"],"optionsEn":["An actuator duration longer than one round-trip time guarantees the absence of dangerous pressure.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","An instantaneous shaft rise rate can be multiplied by any duration without updating conduit flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b260-v15-35","title":"絕對壓力與汽化：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Absolute pressure and vapor formation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「絕對壓力與汽化」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Absolute pressure and vapor formation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"確認壓力感測器為表壓或絕對型，記錄大氣壓與水溫並統一基準。沿整條管線檢查最低壓力歷時及高點，對低於蒸氣壓的單相結果改用適當模型，並保留未解析局部區域的限制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify gauge versus absolute instrumentation, record atmospheric pressure and temperature and align references. Inspect minimum histories and high points along the full conduit, replace invalid single-phase predictions with suitable models and retain limitations for unresolved local regions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：確認壓力感測器為表壓或絕對型，記錄大氣壓與水溫並統一基準。沿整條管線檢查最低壓力歷時及高點，對低於蒸氣壓的單相結果改用適當模型，並保留未解析局部區域的限制。","observationEn":"Site practice: Verify gauge versus absolute instrumentation, record atmospheric pressure and temperature and align references. Inspect minimum histories and high points along the full conduit, replace invalid single-phase predictions with suitable models and retain limitations for unresolved local regions.","failure":"注意干擾：用海平面標準大氣壓代替高海拔實值會錯估餘量，稀疏取樣則可能漏掉短低壓。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using standard sea-level atmosphere at altitude misstates the margin, and sparse sampling can miss brief minima. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"確認壓力感測器為表壓或絕對型，記錄大氣壓與水溫並統一基準。沿整條管線檢查最低壓力歷時及高點，對低於蒸氣壓的單相結果改用適當模型，並保留未解析局部區域的限制。","textEn":"Verify gauge versus absolute instrumentation, record atmospheric pressure and temperature and align references. Inspect minimum histories and high points along the full conduit, replace invalid single-phase predictions with suitable models and retain limitations for unresolved local regions.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"確認壓力感測器為表壓或絕對型，記錄大氣壓與水溫並統一基準。沿整條管線檢查最低壓力歷時及高點，對低於蒸氣壓的單相結果改用適當模型，並保留未解析局部區域的限制。","textEn":"Verify gauge versus absolute instrumentation, record atmospheric pressure and temperature and align references. Inspect minimum histories and high points along the full conduit, replace invalid single-phase predictions with suitable models and retain limitations for unresolved local regions.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「絕對壓力與汽化」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Absolute pressure and vapor formation\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","理想無損湧升數值就是任何真實調壓井所需的完整井高。","確認壓力感測器為表壓或絕對型，記錄大氣壓與水溫並統一基準。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The ideal lossless rise directly gives the complete required height for every real surge shaft.","Verify gauge versus absolute instrumentation, record atmospheric pressure and temperature and align references."],"answer":2,"explanation":"確認壓力感測器為表壓或絕對型，記錄大氣壓與水溫並統一基準。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify gauge versus absolute instrumentation, record atmospheric pressure and temperature and align references. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b260-v15-36","title":"絕對壓力與汽化：失效診斷","titleEn":"Absolute pressure and vapor formation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「絕對壓力與汽化」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Absolute pressure and vapor formation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用海平面標準大氣壓代替高海拔實值會錯估餘量，稀疏取樣則可能漏掉短低壓。氣穴再閉合形成的壓力峰值也不會在只檢查原始高壓的流程中出現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using standard sea-level atmosphere at altitude misstates the margin, and sparse sampling can miss brief minima. Cavity rejoining can produce pressure peaks absent from a procedure that checks only the original high-pressure state. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設大氣壓100kPa、表壓−80kPa、蒸氣壓2.34kPa，絕對壓20kPa，比蒸氣壓高17.66kPa；只代表該點該時刻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Absolute pressure20kPa exceeds vapor by17.66kPa only at that location and instant.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任何負表壓都立即代表汽化而正表壓則保證整條管線沒有空化。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every negative gauge pressure means vaporization, while positive gauge pressure guarantees no cavitation anywhere.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用海平面標準大氣壓代替高海拔實值會錯估餘量，稀疏取樣則可能漏掉短低壓。氣穴再閉合形成的壓力峰值也不會在只檢查原始高壓的流程中出現。","textEn":"Using standard sea-level atmosphere at altitude misstates the margin, and sparse sampling can miss brief minima. Cavity rejoining can produce pressure peaks absent from a procedure that checks only the original high-pressure state.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「絕對壓力與汽化」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Absolute pressure and vapor formation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用海平面標準大氣壓代替高海拔實值會錯估餘量，稀疏取樣則可能漏掉短低壓。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。"],"optionsEn":["Using standard sea-level atmosphere at altitude misstates the margin, and sparse sampling can miss brief minima.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用海平面標準大氣壓代替高海拔實值會錯估餘量，稀疏取樣則可能漏掉短低壓。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using standard sea-level atmosphere at altitude misstates the margin, and sparse sampling can miss brief minima. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b260-v15-37","title":"特徵網格與收斂：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Characteristic grid and convergence: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「特徵網格與收斂」如何影響調壓井水錘控制的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Characteristic grid and convergence” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surge-shaft control of water hammer”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"瞬態數值解需要把傳播速度、空間網格與時間步配合，否則波前可能被過度擴散或錯置。特徵線恰好落在網格點是便利條件，並不是邊界、摩擦或兩相處理都正確的證明；必須用可解析基準及細化比較檢查壓力峰值、到時和守恆。 假設a=1000m/s、Δx=100m、Δt=0.10s，Courant數aΔt/Δx=1；只對此均勻網格特徵到點，不是完整精度證明。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「特徵網格與收斂」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Transient calculations coordinate wave speed, spatial grid and time step to avoid misplaced or excessively diffused fronts. Characteristics landing on grid points is convenient, not proof that boundaries, friction and cavities are handled correctly. Analytical benchmarks and refinement comparisons must check peak pressure, arrival time and conservation as separate aspects of numerical credibility. Assumea=1000m/s,spacing100m and step0.10s. Courant number1 aligns characteristics on this uniform grid but does not prove full accuracy. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Characteristic grid and convergence” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設，非操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「特徵網格與收斂」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Characteristic grid and convergence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-37-k1","title":"特徵網格與收斂","titleEn":"Characteristic grid and convergence","text":"瞬態數值解需要把傳播速度、空間網格與時間步配合，否則波前可能被過度擴散或錯置。特徵線恰好落在網格點是便利條件，並不是邊界、摩擦或兩相處理都正確的證明；必須用可解析基準及細化比較檢查壓力峰值、到時和守恆。","textEn":"Transient calculations coordinate wave speed, spatial grid and time step to avoid misplaced or excessively diffused fronts. Characteristics landing on grid points is convenient, not proof that boundaries, friction and cavities are handled correctly.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「特徵網格與收斂」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Characteristic grid and convergence\" is correct?","options":["Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。","瞬態數值解需要把傳播速度、空間網格與時間步配合，否則波前可能被過度擴散或錯置。","水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。"],"optionsEn":["A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct.","Transient calculations coordinate wave speed, spatial grid and time step to avoid misplaced or excessively diffused fronts.","Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas."],"answer":1,"explanation":"瞬態數值解需要把傳播速度、空間網格與時間步配合，否則波前可能被過度擴散或錯置。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Transient calculations coordinate wave speed, spatial grid and time step to avoid misplaced or excessively diffused fronts. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b260-v15-38","title":"特徵網格與收斂：定量估算","titleEn":"Characteristic grid and convergence: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「特徵網格與收斂」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Characteristic grid and convergence” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設a=1000m/s、Δx=100m、Δt=0.10s，Courant數aΔt/Δx=1；只對此均勻網格特徵到點，不是完整精度證明。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assumea=1000m/s,spacing100m and step0.10s. Courant number1 aligns characteristics on this uniform grid but does not prove full accuracy. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先用單管首波及已知反射時序作基準，將空間與時間步一起細化並比較峰值和到達時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Benchmark first-wave amplitude and known reflection timing, refine space and time together and compare peaks and arrival.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。假設a=1000m/s、Δx=100m、Δt=0.10s，Courant數aΔt/Δx=1；只對此均勻網格特徵到點，不是完整精度證明。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Assumea=1000m/s,spacing100m and step0.10s. Courant number1 aligns characteristics on this uniform grid but does not prove full accuracy.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「特徵網格與收斂」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Characteristic grid and convergence\", which statement holds?","options":["焦科夫斯基首波增量就是所有反射與氣穴情境下的完整最大總壓力。","調壓井剛性水柱週期與管路彈性壓力波往返時間必定完全相同。","原創教學假設，非操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["The Joukowsky first-wave increment is the complete maximum total pressure for every reflection and cavitation scenario.","The rigid-column surge period must equal the conduit’s elastic-wave round-trip time.","Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設，非操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions, not operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b260-v15-39","title":"特徵網格與收斂：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Characteristic grid and convergence: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「特徵網格與收斂」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Characteristic grid and convergence” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先用單管首波及已知反射時序作基準，將空間與時間步一起細化並比較峰值和到達時間。對各支管核對波速與網格，檢查質量殘差及邊界更新順序，記錄收斂而非只呈現平滑曲線。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Benchmark first-wave amplitude and known reflection timing, refine space and time together and compare peaks and arrival. Check every branch’s celerity and grid, mass residual and boundary-update sequence, documenting convergence rather than merely presenting smooth plots. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：先用單管首波及已知反射時序作基準，將空間與時間步一起細化並比較峰值和到達時間。對各支管核對波速與網格，檢查質量殘差及邊界更新順序，記錄收斂而非只呈現平滑曲線。","observationEn":"Site practice: Benchmark first-wave amplitude and known reflection timing, refine space and time together and compare peaks and arrival. Check every branch’s celerity and grid, mass residual and boundary-update sequence, documenting convergence rather than merely presenting smooth plots.","failure":"注意干擾：光滑曲線可能只是數值耗散抹掉了尖峰，Courant數正確也不能修復錯誤閥門邊界。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A smooth curve may reflect numerical damping that erased a peak, and correct Courant number cannot repair an incorrect valve boundary. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先用單管首波及已知反射時序作基準，將空間與時間步一起細化並比較峰值和到達時間。對各支管核對波速與網格，檢查質量殘差及邊界更新順序，記錄收斂而非只呈現平滑曲線。","textEn":"Benchmark first-wave amplitude and known reflection timing, refine space and time together and compare peaks and arrival. Check every branch’s celerity and grid, mass residual and boundary-update sequence, documenting convergence rather than merely presenting smooth plots.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"先用單管首波及已知反射時序作基準，將空間與時間步一起細化並比較峰值和到達時間。對各支管核對波速與網格，檢查質量殘差及邊界更新順序，記錄收斂而非只呈現平滑曲線。","textEn":"Benchmark first-wave amplitude and known reflection timing, refine space and time together and compare peaks and arrival. Check every branch’s celerity and grid, mass residual and boundary-update sequence, documenting convergence rather than merely presenting smooth plots.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「特徵網格與收斂」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Characteristic grid and convergence\"?","options":["先用單管首波及已知反射時序作基準，將空間與時間步一起細化並比較峰值和到達時間。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","管路反向流動時摩擦仍應保持原方向並向水流提供能量。"],"optionsEn":["Benchmark first-wave amplitude and known reflection timing, refine space and time together and compare peaks and arrival.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","During reversed flow friction keeps its original direction and supplies energy to the water."],"answer":0,"explanation":"先用單管首波及已知反射時序作基準，將空間與時間步一起細化並比較峰值和到達時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Benchmark first-wave amplitude and known reflection timing, refine space and time together and compare peaks and arrival. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b260-v15-40","title":"特徵網格與收斂：失效診斷","titleEn":"Characteristic grid and convergence: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"prerequisiteIds":["b260-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「特徵網格與收斂」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Characteristic grid and convergence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"光滑曲線可能只是數值耗散抹掉了尖峰，Courant數正確也不能修復錯誤閥門邊界。若網格改變就讓峰值大幅移動，未收斂結果不應被包裝成確定的壓力包絡。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A smooth curve may reflect numerical damping that erased a peak, and correct Courant number cannot repair an incorrect valve boundary. Peaks that move materially under refinement indicate an unconverged result rather than a definitive pressure envelope. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設a=1000m/s、Δx=100m、Δt=0.10s，Courant數aΔt/Δx=1；只對此均勻網格特徵到點，不是完整精度證明。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Courant number1 aligns characteristics on this uniform grid but does not prove full accuracy.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「Courant數等於一就能保證任何邊界、空化與摩擦模型都完全正確。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A Courant number of one guarantees that every boundary, cavitation and friction model is correct.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b260-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"光滑曲線可能只是數值耗散抹掉了尖峰，Courant數正確也不能修復錯誤閥門邊界。若網格改變就讓峰值大幅移動，未收斂結果不應被包裝成確定的壓力包絡。","textEn":"A smooth curve may reflect numerical damping that erased a peak, and correct Courant number cannot repair an incorrect valve boundary. Peaks that move materially under refinement indicate an unconverged result rather than a definitive pressure envelope.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]},{"id":"b260-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「特徵網格與收斂」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Characteristic grid and convergence\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","光滑曲線可能只是數值耗散抹掉了尖峰，Courant數正確也不能修復錯誤閥門邊界。","水錘波速只由水決定而完全不受管壁、約束或夾氣影響。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A smooth curve may reflect numerical damping that erased a peak, and correct Courant number cannot repair an incorrect valve boundary.","Water-hammer wave speed depends only on water and never on pipe walls, restraint or entrained gas."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光滑曲線可能只是數值耗散抹掉了尖峰，Courant數正確也不能修復錯誤閥門邊界。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A smooth curve may reflect numerical damping that erased a peak, and correct Courant number cannot repair an incorrect valve boundary. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-hydro-structures","b-src-water-manuals","v15s-eklutna-history","v15s-coachella-project"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b265","title":"配水管網壓力管理","titleEn":"Pressure management of water-distribution networks","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課從高程與服務壓力出發，分析壓力相依需求、漏失指數及閥門耗能，再進入閥權度、遠端延遲、回授方向和備援供水。最後把快速水錘與低流量水質納入同一管理問題，讓節水效益與服務可靠度各有證據，不把降低平均壓力當成唯一成功指標。","summaryEn":"Beginning with elevation and service pressure, this course examines pressure-dependent demand, leakage exponents and valve dissipation, then addresses authority, remote delay, feedback direction and backup supply. Rapid transients and low-flow water quality complete the management problem, giving savings and service reliability separate evidence instead of treating lower average pressure as the only success metric.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-pipe","architectureNodes":[["服務與地形","Service and terrain"],["管網與漏口","Network and leaks"],["減壓閥與回授","Reducing valve and feedback"],["備援及瞬變","Backup and transients"],["成效與水質","Performance and quality"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]],"diagram":{"type":"water-pipe","labels":["服務與地形","管網與漏口","減壓閥與回授","備援及瞬變","成效與水質"],"labelsEn":["Service and terrain","Network and leaks","Reducing valve and feedback","Backup and transients","Performance and quality"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創敏感度例設定同一漏口群的初始漏失10 L/s、代表壓力水頭40 m，降至30 m後若採固定孔口指數N=0.5，漏失為8.660 L/s；若改用假設校準指數N=1.2，則為7.081 L/s。兩個模型分別預測13.4%與29.2%的減少，差異來自模型而非新的現場量測。應用獨立資料校準指數，同時檢查高處服務壓力、閥動作水錘及低更新支線水質。不得選擇看起來節水較多的指數來替代驗證，也不能將本例壓力寫成真實控制設定。","textEn":"An original sensitivity example uses the same leak population with initial leakage 10 L/s at representative head 40 m. Reducing head to 30 m gives 8.660 L/s with fixed-orifice exponent N=0.5, or 7.081 L/s with hypothetical calibrated exponent N=1.2. The predicted reductions are 13.4% and 29.2%; the difference comes from the model rather than new field observations. Calibrate the exponent independently while checking elevated-customer pressure, valve-induced transients and quality in low-renewal branches. Choosing the exponent that promises greater savings cannot replace validation, and the assumed heads are not real control settings.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b265-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證」與「壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification\" and \"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b265-v15-01","title":"高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「高程水頭與服務壓力」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Elevation head and service pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"壓力管理要控制的是用戶與關鍵設施可取得的壓力，不能只追求減壓閥出口的一個數字。節點水頭包含高程與壓力，沿途摩阻又隨需求變動，因此低處壓力過高時，高處仍可能接近供水不足；管理分區需同時考慮高程帶、管路阻力與代表性服務點。下式分開能量水頭、高程及流動損失，忽略速度水頭差；所得壓力水頭只適用指定需求工況，不代表全天最小值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「高程水頭與服務壓力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pressure management concerns pressure available to customers and critical facilities, not merely one number at a reducing-valve outlet. Nodal head includes elevation and pressure, while friction changes with demand. A low-lying area can have excessive pressure while an elevated area approaches insufficient supply, so zoning must consider elevation bands, resistance and representative service points together. The relation separates energy head, elevation and losses while neglecting velocity-head differences. The resulting pressure head applies to one demand condition, not the daily minimum. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Elevation head and service pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設供水水頭H=100 m、節點高程z=60 m、路徑損失hf=15 m，壓力水頭h=H−z−hf=25 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume supply head H=100 m, node elevation z=60 m and path loss hf=15 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「高程水頭與服務壓力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Elevation head and service pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-01-k1","title":"高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證","titleEn":"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification","text":"壓力管理要控制的是用戶與關鍵設施可取得的壓力，不能只追求減壓閥出口的一個數字。節點水頭包含高程與壓力，沿途摩阻又隨需求變動，因此低處壓力過高時，高處仍可能接近供水不足；管理分區需同時考慮高程帶、管路阻力與代表性服務點。","textEn":"Pressure management concerns pressure available to customers and critical facilities, not merely one number at a reducing-valve outlet. Nodal head includes elevation and pressure, while friction changes with demand.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。","壓力管理要控制的是用戶與關鍵設施可取得的壓力，不能只追求減壓閥出口的一個數字。","管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer.","Pressure management concerns pressure available to customers and critical facilities, not merely one number at a reducing-valve outlet.","A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"壓力管理要控制的是用戶與關鍵設施可取得的壓力，不能只追求減壓閥出口的一個數字。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pressure management concerns pressure available to customers and critical facilities, not merely one number at a reducing-valve outlet. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b265-v15-02","title":"高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「高程水頭與服務壓力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Elevation head and service pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設供水水頭H=100 m、節點高程z=60 m、路徑損失hf=15 m，壓力水頭h=H−z−hf=25 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume supply head H=100 m, node elevation z=60 m and path loss hf=15 m. Pressure head h=H−z−hf=25 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將關鍵服務點的高程、壓力與需求時間對齊，核對感測器讀值是表壓或水頭。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align elevations, pressure and demand times at critical service points, checking whether sensors report gauge pressure or head.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設供水水頭H=100 m、節點高程z=60 m、路徑損失hf=15 m，壓力水頭h=H−z−hf=25 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume supply head H=100 m, node elevation z=60 m and path loss hf=15 m. Pressure head h=H−z−hf=25 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。","通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設供水水頭H=100 m、節點高程z=60 m、路徑損失hf=15 m，壓力水頭h=H−z−hf=25 m。"],"optionsEn":["All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity.","A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume supply head H=100 m, node elevation z=60 m and path loss hf=15 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設供水水頭H=100 m、節點高程z=60 m、路徑損失hf=15 m，壓力水頭h=H−z−hf=25 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume supply head H=100 m, node elevation z=60 m and path loss hf=15 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b265-v15-03","title":"高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「高程水頭與服務壓力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Elevation head and service pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將關鍵服務點的高程、壓力與需求時間對齊，核對感測器讀值是表壓或水頭。比較尖峰與低需求兩個時段的水頭線，檢查閥後量測是否能代表最不利用戶而非只代表附近低點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align elevations, pressure and demand times at critical service points, checking whether sensors report gauge pressure or head. Compare hydraulic grades at peak and low demand and test whether the downstream sensor represents the limiting customer rather than a nearby low point. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：繪出高低兩個服務點在相同閥後水頭下的壓力差，加入需求增加造成的摩阻。列出應監測的最不利位置，避免只以平均區壓決定管理策略。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw pressures at high and low service points under one valve-outlet head and add demand-dependent friction. Identify limiting monitoring locations instead of selecting management strategy from average district pressure alone.","failure":"注意干擾：只在減壓閥附近量到足夠壓力，可能漏掉遠端或高處缺壓；若把地面高程錯當管線量測基準，模型又會把壓力不足誤判成儀器偏差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adequate pressure near a reducing valve can conceal shortages at remote or elevated users. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將關鍵服務點的高程、壓力與需求時間對齊，核對感測器讀值是表壓或水頭。比較尖峰與低需求兩個時段的水頭線，檢查閥後量測是否能代表最不利用戶而非只代表附近低點。","textEn":"Align elevations, pressure and demand times at critical service points, checking whether sensors report gauge pressure or head. Compare hydraulic grades at peak and low demand and test whether the downstream sensor represents the limiting customer rather than a nearby low point.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"繪出高低兩個服務點在相同閥後水頭下的壓力差，加入需求增加造成的摩阻。列出應監測的最不利位置，避免只以平均區壓決定管理策略。","textEn":"Draw pressures at high and low service points under one valve-outlet head and add demand-dependent friction. Identify limiting monitoring locations instead of selecting management strategy from average district pressure alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification\"?","options":["將關鍵服務點的高程、壓力與需求時間對齊，核對感測器讀值是表壓或水頭。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。"],"optionsEn":["Align elevations, pressure and demand times at critical service points, checking whether sensors report gauge pressure or head.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將關鍵服務點的高程、壓力與需求時間對齊，核對感測器讀值是表壓或水頭。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align elevations, pressure and demand times at critical service points, checking whether sensors report gauge pressure or head. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b265-v15-04","title":"高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「高程水頭與服務壓力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Elevation head and service pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只在減壓閥附近量到足夠壓力，可能漏掉遠端或高處缺壓；若把地面高程錯當管線量測基準，模型又會把壓力不足誤判成儀器偏差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adequate pressure near a reducing valve can conceal shortages at remote or elevated users. Confusing ground elevation with the pressure-measurement datum can then misclassify a genuine pressure deficit as instrument error. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：下式分開能量水頭、高程及流動損失，忽略速度水頭差；所得壓力水頭只適用指定需求工況，不代表全天最小值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The resulting pressure head applies to one demand condition, not the daily minimum.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只在減壓閥附近量到足夠壓力，可能漏掉遠端或高處缺壓；若把地面高程錯當管線量測基準，模型又會把壓力不足誤判成儀器偏差。","textEn":"Adequate pressure near a reducing valve can conceal shortages at remote or elevated users. Confusing ground elevation with the pressure-measurement datum can then misclassify a genuine pressure deficit as instrument error.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高程水頭與服務壓力機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Elevation head and service pressure mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只在減壓閥附近量到足夠壓力，可能漏掉遠端或高處缺壓；若把地面高程錯當管線量測基準，模型又會把壓力不足誤判成儀器偏差。","管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Adequate pressure near a reducing valve can conceal shortages at remote or elevated users.","A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只在減壓閥附近量到足夠壓力，可能漏掉遠端或高處缺壓；若把地面高程錯當管線量測基準，模型又會把壓力不足誤判成儀器偏差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adequate pressure near a reducing valve can conceal shortages at remote or elevated users. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b265-v15-05","title":"壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「壓力相依需求與缺水量」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pressure-dependent demand and deficit” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"傳統固定需求模型可能在壓力不足時仍要求節點供出全部流量，造成不合理的負壓結果。壓力相依需求把可供流量連到可用壓力區間，使缺水成為可量化輸出；但需求曲線仍是模型假設，不能將所有用戶、儲水設備與消防用途視為相同的孔口行為。此例採分段模型：低於最低水頭供量為零，達要求水頭供滿量，中間以平方根插值；參數不是任何地方服務標準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壓力相依需求與缺水量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A fixed-demand model can require full delivery even when pressure is insufficient, producing unrealistic negative pressures. Pressure-dependent demand relates available flow to a pressure range and makes supply deficit an explicit output. The demand curve remains an assumption, however, and customers, storage installations and fire-service functions cannot all be treated as identical orifices. The example sets zero delivery below minimum head, full delivery at required head and square-root interpolation between them. Its parameters are not jurisdictional service standards. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pressure-dependent demand and deficit” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設需求qreq=20 L/s、hmin=10 m、hreq=30 m、實際h=20 m，q=20√[(20−10)/(30−10)]=14.14 L/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume required demand qreq=20 L/s, hmin=10 m, hreq=30 m and actual h=20 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「壓力相依需求與缺水量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pressure-dependent demand and deficit”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-05-k1","title":"壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證","titleEn":"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification","text":"傳統固定需求模型可能在壓力不足時仍要求節點供出全部流量，造成不合理的負壓結果。壓力相依需求把可供流量連到可用壓力區間，使缺水成為可量化輸出；但需求曲線仍是模型假設，不能將所有用戶、儲水設備與消防用途視為相同的孔口行為。","textEn":"A fixed-demand model can require full delivery even when pressure is insufficient, producing unrealistic negative pressures. Pressure-dependent demand relates available flow to a pressure range and makes supply deficit an explicit output.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。","漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。","傳統固定需求模型可能在壓力不足時仍要求節點供出全部流量，造成不合理的負壓結果。"],"optionsEn":["A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow.","The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break.","A fixed-demand model can require full delivery even when pressure is insufficient, producing unrealistic negative pressures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"傳統固定需求模型可能在壓力不足時仍要求節點供出全部流量，造成不合理的負壓結果。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A fixed-demand model can require full delivery even when pressure is insufficient, producing unrealistic negative pressures. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b265-v15-06","title":"壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「壓力相依需求與缺水量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pressure-dependent demand and deficit” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設需求qreq=20 L/s、hmin=10 m、hreq=30 m、實際h=20 m，q=20√[(20−10)/(30−10)]=14.14 L/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume required demand qreq=20 L/s, hmin=10 m, hreq=30 m and actual h=20 m. Delivered q=20√[(20−10)/(30−10)]=14.14 L/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較固定需求與壓力相依模型在相同邊界下的供量與低壓分布，查核用戶類別與儲水設備是否需不同描述。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare fixed and pressure-dependent demand models under identical boundaries, examining delivery and low-pressure distribution.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設需求qreq=20 L/s、hmin=10 m、hreq=30 m、實際h=20 m，q=20√[(20−10)/(30−10)]=14.14 L/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume required demand qreq=20 L/s, hmin=10 m, hreq=30 m and actual h=20 m. Delivered q=20√[(20−10)/(30−10)]=14.14 L/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設需求qreq=20 L/s、hmin=10 m、hreq=30 m、實際h=20 m，q=20√[(20−10)/(30−10)]=14.14 L/s。","控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。","比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume required demand qreq=20 L/s, hmin=10 m, hreq=30 m and actual h=20 m.","A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow.","Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設需求qreq=20 L/s、hmin=10 m、hreq=30 m、實際h=20 m，q=20√[(20−10)/(30−10)]=14.14 L/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume required demand qreq=20 L/s, hmin=10 m, hreq=30 m and actual h=20 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b265-v15-07","title":"壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「壓力相依需求與缺水量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pressure-dependent demand and deficit” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較固定需求與壓力相依模型在相同邊界下的供量與低壓分布，查核用戶類別與儲水設備是否需不同描述。用可取得的壓力及服務資料驗證缺水量，不只要求數值迭代收斂。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare fixed and pressure-dependent demand models under identical boundaries, examining delivery and low-pressure distribution. Check whether customer categories and storage installations need different representations, and validate deficits using available pressure and service data rather than accepting numerical convergence alone. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以三個水頭值跨越最低與要求界線，檢查分段需求是否連續且不超過滿額需求。再說明哪些用戶資料可支持參數，而哪些仍應保留敏感度範圍。","observationEn":"Site practice: Evaluate three heads spanning minimum and required limits, checking continuity and the full-demand cap. Explain which customer observations support the parameters and which uncertainties should remain as sensitivity ranges.","failure":"注意干擾：以固定需求強迫缺壓節點繼續滿額供水會低估服務中斷，反之把假設需求曲線當精確行為也會製造過度確定的缺水預測；兩者都可能錯排優先改善區。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Forcing full demand at a pressure-deficient node understates service disruption, while treating an assumed demand curve as exact behavior creates false certainty in deficit estimates. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較固定需求與壓力相依模型在相同邊界下的供量與低壓分布，查核用戶類別與儲水設備是否需不同描述。用可取得的壓力及服務資料驗證缺水量，不只要求數值迭代收斂。","textEn":"Compare fixed and pressure-dependent demand models under identical boundaries, examining delivery and low-pressure distribution. Check whether customer categories and storage installations need different representations, and validate deficits using available pressure and service data rather than accepting numerical convergence alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以三個水頭值跨越最低與要求界線，檢查分段需求是否連續且不超過滿額需求。再說明哪些用戶資料可支持參數，而哪些仍應保留敏感度範圍。","textEn":"Evaluate three heads spanning minimum and required limits, checking continuity and the full-demand cap. Explain which customer observations support the parameters and which uncertainties should remain as sensitivity ranges.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較固定需求與壓力相依模型在相同邊界下的供量與低壓分布，查核用戶類別與儲水設備是否需不同描述。","平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare fixed and pressure-dependent demand models under identical boundaries, examining delivery and low-pressure distribution.","Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較固定需求與壓力相依模型在相同邊界下的供量與低壓分布，查核用戶類別與儲水設備是否需不同描述。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare fixed and pressure-dependent demand models under identical boundaries, examining delivery and low-pressure distribution. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b265-v15-08","title":"壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「壓力相依需求與缺水量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pressure-dependent demand and deficit” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以固定需求強迫缺壓節點繼續滿額供水會低估服務中斷，反之把假設需求曲線當精確行為也會製造過度確定的缺水預測；兩者都可能錯排優先改善區。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Forcing full demand at a pressure-deficient node understates service disruption, while treating an assumed demand curve as exact behavior creates false certainty in deficit estimates. Both can misdirect improvement priorities. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：此例採分段模型：低於最低水頭供量為零，達要求水頭供滿量，中間以平方根插值；參數不是任何地方服務標準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Its parameters are not jurisdictional service standards.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以固定需求強迫缺壓節點繼續滿額供水會低估服務中斷，反之把假設需求曲線當精確行為也會製造過度確定的缺水預測；兩者都可能錯排優先改善區。","textEn":"Forcing full demand at a pressure-deficient node understates service disruption, while treating an assumed demand curve as exact behavior creates false certainty in deficit estimates. Both can misdirect improvement priorities.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「壓力相依需求與缺水量機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pressure-dependent demand and deficit mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。","以固定需求強迫缺壓節點繼續滿額供水會低估服務中斷，反之把假設需求曲線當精確行為也會製造過度確定的缺水預測；兩者都可能錯排優先改善區。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break.","Forcing full demand at a pressure-deficient node understates service disruption, while treating an assumed demand curve as exact behavior creates false certainty in deficit estimates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以固定需求強迫缺壓節點繼續滿額供水會低估服務中斷，反之把假設需求曲線當精確行為也會製造過度確定的缺水預測；兩者都可能錯排優先改善區。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Forcing full demand at a pressure-deficient node understates service disruption, while treating an assumed demand curve as exact behavior creates false certainty in deficit estimates. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b265-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證」與「減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification\" and \"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b265-v15-09","title":"漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「漏口變形與壓力指數」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Leak deformation and pressure exponent” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"降低壓力通常能降低既有漏口流量，但效果取決於漏口是否隨壓力張開、材料拘束及不同漏點的組合。固定孔口平方根關係不一定代表整區漏失，經驗指數也不是材料常數；若合法用水、閥位或漏點數同時改變，觀測到的曲線便不能單獨歸因於壓力。本式比較相同漏口群、代表壓力定義不變的兩個狀態，不預測新破口發生率；指數須在適用範圍內校準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「漏口變形與壓力指數」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Reducing pressure generally reduces flow through existing leaks, but the effect depends on opening deformation, restraint and the mix of leaks. A fixed-orifice square-root relation need not represent district leakage, and an empirical exponent is not a material constant. Simultaneous changes in authorized use, valve state or leak count prevent attributing an observed curve to pressure alone. The relation compares the same leak population under a consistent representative-pressure definition. It does not predict new-break frequency, and its exponent requires calibration within the applicable range. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Leak deformation and pressure exponent” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭由40 m降至30 m、漏失指數N=1.2，Q2/Q1=(30/40)^1.2=0.7081；假設原漏失10 L/s，則為7.081 L/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head falls from 40 m to 30 m and leakage exponent N=1.2.","failure":"常見誤解：「漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「漏口變形與壓力指數」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Leak deformation and pressure exponent”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-09-k1","title":"漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證","titleEn":"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification","text":"降低壓力通常能降低既有漏口流量，但效果取決於漏口是否隨壓力張開、材料拘束及不同漏點的組合。固定孔口平方根關係不一定代表整區漏失，經驗指數也不是材料常數；若合法用水、閥位或漏點數同時改變，觀測到的曲線便不能單獨歸因於壓力。","textEn":"Reducing pressure generally reduces flow through existing leaks, but the effect depends on opening deformation, restraint and the mix of leaks. A fixed-orifice square-root relation need not represent district leakage, and an empirical exponent is not a material constant.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["降低壓力通常能降低既有漏口流量，但效果取決於漏口是否隨壓力張開、材料拘束及不同漏點的組合。","漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。","減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。"],"optionsEn":["Reducing pressure generally reduces flow through existing leaks, but the effect depends on opening deformation, restraint and the mix of leaks.","The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break.","All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"降低壓力通常能降低既有漏口流量，但效果取決於漏口是否隨壓力張開、材料拘束及不同漏點的組合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Reducing pressure generally reduces flow through existing leaks, but the effect depends on opening deformation, restraint and the mix of leaks. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b265-v15-10","title":"漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「漏口變形與壓力指數」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Leak deformation and pressure exponent” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭由40 m降至30 m、漏失指數N=1.2，Q2/Q1=(30/40)^1.2=0.7081；假設原漏失10 L/s，則為7.081 L/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head falls from 40 m to 30 m and leakage exponent N=1.2. Q2/Q1=(30/40)^1.2=0.7081; assumed initial leakage 10 L/s becomes 7.081 L/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在需求及邊界可比的觀測時段配對壓力與漏失估計，將修復或新爆管事件另外標記。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pair pressure and leakage estimates over comparable demand and boundary conditions, marking repairs and new bursts separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭由40 m降至30 m、漏失指數N=1.2，Q2/Q1=(30/40)^1.2=0.7081；假設原漏失10 L/s，則為7.081 L/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head falls from 40 m to 30 m and leakage exponent N=1.2. Q2/Q1=(30/40)^1.2=0.7081; assumed initial leakage 10 L/s becomes 7.081 L/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭由40 m降至30 m、漏失指數N=1.2，Q2/Q1=(30/40)^1.2=0.7081。","現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。"],"optionsEn":["A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head falls from 40 m to 30 m and leakage exponent N=1.2.","Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭由40 m降至30 m、漏失指數N=1.2，Q2/Q1=(30/40)^1.2=0.7081；假設原漏失10 L/s，則為7.081 L/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head falls from 40 m to 30 m and leakage exponent N=1.2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b265-v15-11","title":"漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「漏口變形與壓力指數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Leak deformation and pressure exponent” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在需求及邊界可比的觀測時段配對壓力與漏失估計，將修復或新爆管事件另外標記。用多個壓力點檢查代表區壓是否合理，並把指數擬合殘差與預測範圍共同呈現。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pair pressure and leakage estimates over comparable demand and boundary conditions, marking repairs and new bursts separately. Use several pressure locations to test the representative district pressure and present exponent-fit residuals together with the prediction range. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用固定孔口指數與另一個假設經驗指數比較同一壓力變化，列出結果差異。把減少既有漏流與降低新破管風險分成兩個需不同證據的問題。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare one pressure change using a fixed-orifice exponent and another hypothetical fitted exponent. Separate reduction of existing leakage from prevention of new breaks, identifying the different evidence needed for each.","failure":"注意干擾：若把修復後漏點減少的效果算進壓力指數，會高估下一次減壓效益；相反，合法夜用水增加也可能掩蓋真實漏失下降，讓管理措施被誤判無效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Including leak removal from repairs in a pressure exponent overstates the benefit of a later pressure reduction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在需求及邊界可比的觀測時段配對壓力與漏失估計，將修復或新爆管事件另外標記。用多個壓力點檢查代表區壓是否合理，並把指數擬合殘差與預測範圍共同呈現。","textEn":"Pair pressure and leakage estimates over comparable demand and boundary conditions, marking repairs and new bursts separately. Use several pressure locations to test the representative district pressure and present exponent-fit residuals together with the prediction range.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用固定孔口指數與另一個假設經驗指數比較同一壓力變化，列出結果差異。把減少既有漏流與降低新破管風險分成兩個需不同證據的問題。","textEn":"Compare one pressure change using a fixed-orifice exponent and another hypothetical fitted exponent. Separate reduction of existing leakage from prevention of new breaks, identifying the different evidence needed for each.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。","在需求及邊界可比的觀測時段配對壓力與漏失估計，將修復或新爆管事件另外標記。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality.","Pair pressure and leakage estimates over comparable demand and boundary conditions, marking repairs and new bursts separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在需求及邊界可比的觀測時段配對壓力與漏失估計，將修復或新爆管事件另外標記。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pair pressure and leakage estimates over comparable demand and boundary conditions, marking repairs and new bursts separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b265-v15-12","title":"漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「漏口變形與壓力指數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Leak deformation and pressure exponent” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若把修復後漏點減少的效果算進壓力指數，會高估下一次減壓效益；相反，合法夜用水增加也可能掩蓋真實漏失下降，讓管理措施被誤判無效。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Including leak removal from repairs in a pressure exponent overstates the benefit of a later pressure reduction. Conversely, increased legitimate night use can hide real leakage reduction and make the measure appear ineffective. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本式比較相同漏口群、代表壓力定義不變的兩個狀態，不預測新破口發生率；指數須在適用範圍內校準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It does not predict new-break frequency, and its exponent requires calibration within the applicable range.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把修復後漏點減少的效果算進壓力指數，會高估下一次減壓效益；相反，合法夜用水增加也可能掩蓋真實漏失下降，讓管理措施被誤判無效。","textEn":"Including leak removal from repairs in a pressure exponent overstates the benefit of a later pressure reduction. Conversely, increased legitimate night use can hide real leakage reduction and make the measure appear ineffective.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「漏口變形與壓力指數機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Leak deformation and pressure exponent mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若把修復後漏點減少的效果算進壓力指數，會高估下一次減壓效益；相反，合法夜用水增加也可能掩蓋真實漏失下降，讓管理措施被誤判無效。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。"],"optionsEn":["Including leak removal from repairs in a pressure exponent overstates the benefit of a later pressure reduction.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若把修復後漏點減少的效果算進壓力指數，會高估下一次減壓效益；相反，合法夜用水增加也可能掩蓋真實漏失下降，讓管理措施被誤判無效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Including leak removal from repairs in a pressure exponent overstates the benefit of a later pressure reduction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b265-v15-13","title":"減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「減壓閥能量耗散」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Energy dissipation in reducing valves” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"減壓閥藉節流將一部分水力能轉成湍流、熱及振動，閥後壓力降低不代表能量被回收。壓差與通量共同決定耗散功率，而局部高速區可能涉及空化與噪音；設計需對照閥型、上下游絕對壓力及運轉範圍，不能只從平均壓差選擇設備。壓差乘流量是流體功率差，未乘任何發電效率；只有另設能量回收裝置並證實效率時，才能估可利用電力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「減壓閥能量耗散」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A pressure-reducing valve converts hydraulic energy into turbulence, heat and vibration through throttling; lower downstream pressure does not mean energy recovery. Pressure difference and flow determine dissipated power, while local high-speed zones may involve cavitation and noise. Equipment assessment needs valve type, absolute boundary pressures and operating range rather than average pressure drop alone. Pressure difference times flow is a fluid-power difference with no generation efficiency applied. Useful electric power requires a separate recovery device and substantiated efficiency. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Energy dissipation in reducing valves” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓差Δp=200 kPa、Q=0.020 m³/s，耗散水力功率P=ΔpQ=4000 W=4.0 kW，不是發電量。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve drop Δp=200 kPa and Q=0.020 m³/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「減壓閥能量耗散」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Energy dissipation in reducing valves”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-13-k1","title":"減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證","titleEn":"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification","text":"減壓閥藉節流將一部分水力能轉成湍流、熱及振動，閥後壓力降低不代表能量被回收。壓差與通量共同決定耗散功率，而局部高速區可能涉及空化與噪音；設計需對照閥型、上下游絕對壓力及運轉範圍，不能只從平均壓差選擇設備。","textEn":"A pressure-reducing valve converts hydraulic energy into turbulence, heat and vibration through throttling; lower downstream pressure does not mean energy recovery. Pressure difference and flow determine dissipated power, while local high-speed zones may involve cavitation and noise.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。","減壓閥藉節流將一部分水力能轉成湍流、熱及振動，閥後壓力降低不代表能量被回收。","控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。"],"optionsEn":["All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity.","A pressure-reducing valve converts hydraulic energy into turbulence, heat and vibration through throttling.","A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"減壓閥藉節流將一部分水力能轉成湍流、熱及振動，閥後壓力降低不代表能量被回收。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A pressure-reducing valve converts hydraulic energy into turbulence, heat and vibration through throttling; lower downstream pressure does not mean energy recovery. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b265-v15-14","title":"減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「減壓閥能量耗散」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Energy dissipation in reducing valves” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓差Δp=200 kPa、Q=0.020 m³/s，耗散水力功率P=ΔpQ=4000 W=4.0 kW，不是發電量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve drop Δp=200 kPa and Q=0.020 m³/s. Dissipated hydraulic power P=ΔpQ=4000 W=4.0 kW, not generated power. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測閥前後壓力與流量，核對壓力取樣點是否避開不適當的局部擾動。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure upstream and downstream pressure with flow simultaneously, checking whether pressure taps are affected by unsuitable local disturbances.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓差Δp=200 kPa、Q=0.020 m³/s，耗散水力功率P=ΔpQ=4000 W=4.0 kW，不是發電量。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve drop Δp=200 kPa and Q=0.020 m³/s. Dissipated hydraulic power P=ΔpQ=4000 W=4.0 kW, not generated power.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。","平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓差Δp=200 kPa、Q=0.020 m³/s，耗散水力功率P=ΔpQ=4000 W=4.0 kW，不是發電量。"],"optionsEn":["Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation.","Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve drop Δp=200 kPa and Q=0.020 m³/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓差Δp=200 kPa、Q=0.020 m³/s，耗散水力功率P=ΔpQ=4000 W=4.0 kW，不是發電量。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve drop Δp=200 kPa and Q=0.020 m³/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b265-v15-15","title":"減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「減壓閥能量耗散」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Energy dissipation in reducing valves” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測閥前後壓力與流量，核對壓力取樣點是否避開不適當的局部擾動。比較設備核定的壓差及流量範圍，並追蹤噪音、振動和內部損傷，避免只以能量帳判定設備適用性。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure upstream and downstream pressure with flow simultaneously, checking whether pressure taps are affected by unsuitable local disturbances. Compare the approved pressure-drop and flow range and track noise, vibration and internal damage instead of judging suitability from the energy ledger alone. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將同一壓差下兩個流量的耗散功率比較，另畫出有能量回收裝置時的效率鏈。明確區分功率與一段時間的能量，再列出設備適用性仍需的資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare dissipated power at two flows under one pressure drop and draw a separate efficiency chain for a recovery device. Distinguish power from time-integrated energy and list remaining equipment-suitability data.","failure":"注意干擾：把耗散功率寫成可回收發電功率會誇大效益，忽略局部低壓又可能漏掉空化損傷；閥後平均壓力正常並不能保證閥內最低壓力也正常。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reporting dissipated power as recoverable generation exaggerates benefits, while ignoring local low pressure misses possible cavitation damage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測閥前後壓力與流量，核對壓力取樣點是否避開不適當的局部擾動。比較設備核定的壓差及流量範圍，並追蹤噪音、振動和內部損傷，避免只以能量帳判定設備適用性。","textEn":"Measure upstream and downstream pressure with flow simultaneously, checking whether pressure taps are affected by unsuitable local disturbances. Compare the approved pressure-drop and flow range and track noise, vibration and internal damage instead of judging suitability from the energy ledger alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將同一壓差下兩個流量的耗散功率比較，另畫出有能量回收裝置時的效率鏈。明確區分功率與一段時間的能量，再列出設備適用性仍需的資料。","textEn":"Compare dissipated power at two flows under one pressure drop and draw a separate efficiency chain for a recovery device. Distinguish power from time-integrated energy and list remaining equipment-suitability data.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification\"?","options":["同步量測閥前後壓力與流量，核對壓力取樣點是否避開不適當的局部擾動。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Measure upstream and downstream pressure with flow simultaneously, checking whether pressure taps are affected by unsuitable local disturbances.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步量測閥前後壓力與流量，核對壓力取樣點是否避開不適當的局部擾動。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure upstream and downstream pressure with flow simultaneously, checking whether pressure taps are affected by unsuitable local disturbances. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b265-v15-16","title":"減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「減壓閥能量耗散」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Energy dissipation in reducing valves” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把耗散功率寫成可回收發電功率會誇大效益，忽略局部低壓又可能漏掉空化損傷；閥後平均壓力正常並不能保證閥內最低壓力也正常。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reporting dissipated power as recoverable generation exaggerates benefits, while ignoring local low pressure misses possible cavitation damage. Normal downstream mean pressure does not ensure an acceptable internal minimum pressure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：壓差乘流量是流體功率差，未乘任何發電效率；只有另設能量回收裝置並證實效率時，才能估可利用電力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Useful electric power requires a separate recovery device and substantiated efficiency.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把耗散功率寫成可回收發電功率會誇大效益，忽略局部低壓又可能漏掉空化損傷；閥後平均壓力正常並不能保證閥內最低壓力也正常。","textEn":"Reporting dissipated power as recoverable generation exaggerates benefits, while ignoring local low pressure misses possible cavitation damage. Normal downstream mean pressure does not ensure an acceptable internal minimum pressure.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「減壓閥能量耗散機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Energy dissipation in reducing valves mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把耗散功率寫成可回收發電功率會誇大效益，忽略局部低壓又可能漏掉空化損傷；閥後平均壓力正常並不能保證閥內最低壓力也正常。","控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Reporting dissipated power as recoverable generation exaggerates benefits, while ignoring local low pressure misses possible cavitation damage.","A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把耗散功率寫成可回收發電功率會誇大效益，忽略局部低壓又可能漏掉空化損傷；閥後平均壓力正常並不能保證閥內最低壓力也正常。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reporting dissipated power as recoverable generation exaggerates benefits, while ignoring local low pressure misses possible cavitation damage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b265-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證」與「遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification\" and \"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b265-v15-17","title":"閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「閥權度與穩定調節」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Valve authority and stable regulation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"控制閥的作用取決於自身壓降相對整個受控支路壓降的比例，閥位改變不一定帶來同樣比例的流量變化。閥過大時可能長期在很小開度工作，機械間隙與摩擦會放大調節困難；閥權度提供一種局部比較，但不能單獨描述導閥、控制器與管網的動態穩定性。此比值在同一工況下分開閥門與其餘支路損失，沒有給出通用合格門檻；實際控制增益還取決於閥特性與邊界。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「閥權度與穩定調節」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A control valve’s influence depends on its pressure drop relative to the controlled branch, so a position change does not necessarily produce a proportional flow change. An oversized valve may operate near closure where backlash and friction complicate regulation. Valve authority offers a local comparison but cannot by itself describe pilot, controller and network dynamic stability. The ratio separates valve loss from the rest of the branch at one condition and supplies no universal acceptance threshold. Actual control gain also depends on valve characteristic and boundaries. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Valve authority and stable regulation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓降hv=20 m、其餘受控支路損失hr=30 m，權度Av=hv/(hv+hr)=0.40，為指定工況比較。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve loss hv=20 m and remaining controlled-branch loss hr=30 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「閥權度與穩定調節」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Valve authority and stable regulation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-17-k1","title":"閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證","titleEn":"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification","text":"控制閥的作用取決於自身壓降相對整個受控支路壓降的比例，閥位改變不一定帶來同樣比例的流量變化。閥過大時可能長期在很小開度工作，機械間隙與摩擦會放大調節困難；閥權度提供一種局部比較，但不能單獨描述導閥、控制器與管網的動態穩定性。","textEn":"A control valve’s influence depends on its pressure drop relative to the controlled branch, so a position change does not necessarily produce a proportional flow change. An oversized valve may operate near closure where backlash and friction complicate regulation.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。","通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。","控制閥的作用取決於自身壓降相對整個受控支路壓降的比例，閥位改變不一定帶來同樣比例的流量變化。"],"optionsEn":["A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow.","A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure.","A control valve’s influence depends on its pressure drop relative to the controlled branch, so a position change does not necessarily produce a proportional flow change."],"answer":2,"explanation":"控制閥的作用取決於自身壓降相對整個受控支路壓降的比例，閥位改變不一定帶來同樣比例的流量變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A control valve’s influence depends on its pressure drop relative to the controlled branch, so a position change does not necessarily produce a proportional flow change. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b265-v15-18","title":"閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「閥權度與穩定調節」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Valve authority and stable regulation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓降hv=20 m、其餘受控支路損失hr=30 m，權度Av=hv/(hv+hr)=0.40，為指定工況比較。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve loss hv=20 m and remaining controlled-branch loss hr=30 m. Authority Av=hv/(hv+hr)=0.40 for the specified operating condition. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：取得閥位、流量係數與實測壓差關係，檢查低流量及高流量時是否仍具可調範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Obtain valve-position, flow-coefficient and measured-drop relationships, checking controllable range at low and high flow.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓降hv=20 m、其餘受控支路損失hr=30 m，權度Av=hv/(hv+hr)=0.40，為指定工況比較。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve loss hv=20 m and remaining controlled-branch loss hr=30 m. Authority Av=hv/(hv+hr)=0.40 for the specified operating condition.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓降hv=20 m、其餘受控支路損失hr=30 m，權度Av=hv/(hv+hr)=0.40，為指定工況比較。","現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。","壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve loss hv=20 m and remaining controlled-branch loss hr=30 m.","Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario.","Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設閥壓降hv=20 m、其餘受控支路損失hr=30 m，權度Av=hv/(hv+hr)=0.40，為指定工況比較。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume valve loss hv=20 m and remaining controlled-branch loss hr=30 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b265-v15-19","title":"閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「閥權度與穩定調節」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Valve authority and stable regulation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"取得閥位、流量係數與實測壓差關係，檢查低流量及高流量時是否仍具可調範圍。將導閥、摩擦遲滯與控制器時間尺度納入離線模型，以實際穩態和小擾動資料交叉驗證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Obtain valve-position, flow-coefficient and measured-drop relationships, checking controllable range at low and high flow. Include pilot dynamics, frictional hysteresis and controller time scales in offline modeling, cross-checking against observed steady states and small disturbances. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在相同邊界下比較兩種假設閥特性，標出日常工況落在哪個開度區間。使用權度解釋局部敏感性，同時列出它無法判斷的動態與機械問題。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare two hypothetical valve characteristics under identical boundaries, marking their normal operating openings. Use authority to explain local sensitivity while listing dynamic and mechanical issues it cannot resolve.","failure":"注意干擾：只按最大流量選擇很大閥徑，可能讓日常操作落在難以控制的小開度；反覆小幅動作會增加磨耗與壓力波動，即使最大供量仍能達到。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sizing a valve only for maximum flow can place ordinary operation in a poorly controllable near-closed range. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"取得閥位、流量係數與實測壓差關係，檢查低流量及高流量時是否仍具可調範圍。將導閥、摩擦遲滯與控制器時間尺度納入離線模型，以實際穩態和小擾動資料交叉驗證。","textEn":"Obtain valve-position, flow-coefficient and measured-drop relationships, checking controllable range at low and high flow. Include pilot dynamics, frictional hysteresis and controller time scales in offline modeling, cross-checking against observed steady states and small disturbances.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在相同邊界下比較兩種假設閥特性，標出日常工況落在哪個開度區間。使用權度解釋局部敏感性，同時列出它無法判斷的動態與機械問題。","textEn":"Compare two hypothetical valve characteristics under identical boundaries, marking their normal operating openings. Use authority to explain local sensitivity while listing dynamic and mechanical issues it cannot resolve.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","取得閥位、流量係數與實測壓差關係，檢查低流量及高流量時是否仍具可調範圍。","管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Obtain valve-position, flow-coefficient and measured-drop relationships, checking controllable range at low and high flow.","A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"取得閥位、流量係數與實測壓差關係，檢查低流量及高流量時是否仍具可調範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Obtain valve-position, flow-coefficient and measured-drop relationships, checking controllable range at low and high flow. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b265-v15-20","title":"閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「閥權度與穩定調節」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Valve authority and stable regulation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只按最大流量選擇很大閥徑，可能讓日常操作落在難以控制的小開度；反覆小幅動作會增加磨耗與壓力波動，即使最大供量仍能達到。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sizing a valve only for maximum flow can place ordinary operation in a poorly controllable near-closed range. Repeated small movements increase wear and pressure fluctuation even when maximum delivery remains adequate. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：此比值在同一工況下分開閥門與其餘支路損失，沒有給出通用合格門檻；實際控制增益還取決於閥特性與邊界。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Actual control gain also depends on valve characteristic and boundaries.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只按最大流量選擇很大閥徑，可能讓日常操作落在難以控制的小開度；反覆小幅動作會增加磨耗與壓力波動，即使最大供量仍能達到。","textEn":"Sizing a valve only for maximum flow can place ordinary operation in a poorly controllable near-closed range. Repeated small movements increase wear and pressure fluctuation even when maximum delivery remains adequate.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「閥權度與穩定調節機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Valve authority and stable regulation mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。","只按最大流量選擇很大閥徑，可能讓日常操作落在難以控制的小開度；反覆小幅動作會增加磨耗與壓力波動，即使最大供量仍能達到。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure.","Sizing a valve only for maximum flow can place ordinary operation in a poorly controllable near-closed range."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只按最大流量選擇很大閥徑，可能讓日常操作落在難以控制的小開度；反覆小幅動作會增加磨耗與壓力波動，即使最大供量仍能達到。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sizing a valve only for maximum flow can place ordinary operation in a poorly controllable near-closed range. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b265-v15-21","title":"遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「遠端壓力與通訊延遲」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Remote pressure and communication delay” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"以遠端服務點回授可改善代表性，但通訊延遲使控制器看到的是過去狀態而非當前壓力。需求快速增加時，延遲期間的壓降可能已消耗原有裕度；資料時間戳、封包重送與感測器濾波都會增加有效滯後，不能只把無線傳輸的名目速度當整體延遲。線性變化率乘延遲只估未觀測的水頭改變，並非實際控制響應；需求突變與非線性管網仍需另外模擬。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「遠端壓力與通訊延遲」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Remote service-point feedback can improve representation, but communication delay means the controller sees a past state rather than current pressure. During rising demand, pressure can consume its available margin before the update arrives. Timestamps, retransmission and sensor filtering all add effective lag, so nominal wireless transmission speed does not equal total feedback delay. A linear rate times delay estimates unobserved head change, not actual closed-loop response. Demand steps and nonlinear network behavior still require separate modeling. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Remote pressure and communication delay” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭變化率dh/dt=−0.020 m/s、總延遲τ=180 s，未觀測變化Δh≈τdh/dt=−3.60 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head-change rate dh/dt=−0.020 m/s and total delay τ=180 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「遠端壓力與通訊延遲」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Remote pressure and communication delay”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-21-k1","title":"遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證","titleEn":"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification","text":"以遠端服務點回授可改善代表性，但通訊延遲使控制器看到的是過去狀態而非當前壓力。需求快速增加時，延遲期間的壓降可能已消耗原有裕度；資料時間戳、封包重送與感測器濾波都會增加有效滯後，不能只把無線傳輸的名目速度當整體延遲。","textEn":"Remote service-point feedback can improve representation, but communication delay means the controller sees a past state rather than current pressure. During rising demand, pressure can consume its available margin before the update arrives.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["以遠端服務點回授可改善代表性，但通訊延遲使控制器看到的是過去狀態而非當前壓力。","通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。","比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。"],"optionsEn":["Remote service-point feedback can improve representation, but communication delay means the controller sees a past state rather than current pressure.","A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure.","Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以遠端服務點回授可改善代表性，但通訊延遲使控制器看到的是過去狀態而非當前壓力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Remote service-point feedback can improve representation, but communication delay means the controller sees a past state rather than current pressure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b265-v15-22","title":"遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「遠端壓力與通訊延遲」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Remote pressure and communication delay” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭變化率dh/dt=−0.020 m/s、總延遲τ=180 s，未觀測變化Δh≈τdh/dt=−3.60 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head-change rate dh/dt=−0.020 m/s and total delay τ=180 s. Unobserved change Δh≈τdh/dt=−3.60 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從感測器採樣到控制器使用資料的整條路徑量測延遲，保留來源時間與接收時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure delay from sensor sampling to actual controller use, retaining source and receipt timestamps.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭變化率dh/dt=−0.020 m/s、總延遲τ=180 s，未觀測變化Δh≈τdh/dt=−3.60 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head-change rate dh/dt=−0.020 m/s and total delay τ=180 s. Unobserved change Δh≈τdh/dt=−3.60 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭變化率dh/dt=−0.020 m/s、總延遲τ=180 s，未觀測變化Δh≈τdh/dt=−3.60 m。","減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head-change rate dh/dt=−0.020 m/s and total delay τ=180 s.","Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設壓力水頭變化率dh/dt=−0.020 m/s、總延遲τ=180 s，未觀測變化Δh≈τdh/dt=−3.60 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume head-change rate dh/dt=−0.020 m/s and total delay τ=180 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b265-v15-23","title":"遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「遠端壓力與通訊延遲」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Remote pressure and communication delay” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從感測器採樣到控制器使用資料的整條路徑量測延遲，保留來源時間與接收時間。對缺值、重送及過期資料建立可辨識標記，在離線情境中檢查失去遠端訊號時的核定備援行為。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure delay from sensor sampling to actual controller use, retaining source and receipt timestamps. Flag missing, retransmitted and stale records explicitly and examine the approved fallback behavior during loss of remote signals in offline scenarios. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出採樣、傳送、重送與使用四個時間點，分開資料新鮮度與連線狀態。用假設壓力斜率估延遲影響，再說明核定控制設計應如何驗證過期資料處理。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw sampling, transmission, retransmission and use timestamps, separating data freshness from link status. Estimate delay effect with a hypothetical pressure slope and explain how approved control design should verify stale-data handling.","failure":"注意干擾：控制器若將重送的舊壓力當成新資料，可能反向修正已經恢復的壓力，造成反覆追逐與振盪；通訊恢復也不等於所有歷史封包都可立即參與控制。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If a controller treats retransmitted old pressure as current, it can counteract a pressure condition that has already recovered and create repeated chasing or oscillation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從感測器採樣到控制器使用資料的整條路徑量測延遲，保留來源時間與接收時間。對缺值、重送及過期資料建立可辨識標記，在離線情境中檢查失去遠端訊號時的核定備援行為。","textEn":"Measure delay from sensor sampling to actual controller use, retaining source and receipt timestamps. Flag missing, retransmitted and stale records explicitly and examine the approved fallback behavior during loss of remote signals in offline scenarios.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出採樣、傳送、重送與使用四個時間點，分開資料新鮮度與連線狀態。用假設壓力斜率估延遲影響，再說明核定控制設計應如何驗證過期資料處理。","textEn":"Draw sampling, transmission, retransmission and use timestamps, separating data freshness from link status. Estimate delay effect with a hypothetical pressure slope and explain how approved control design should verify stale-data handling.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。","從感測器採樣到控制器使用資料的整條路徑量測延遲，保留來源時間與接收時間。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break.","Measure delay from sensor sampling to actual controller use, retaining source and receipt timestamps."],"answer":2,"explanation":"從感測器採樣到控制器使用資料的整條路徑量測延遲，保留來源時間與接收時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure delay from sensor sampling to actual controller use, retaining source and receipt timestamps. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b265-v15-24","title":"遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「遠端壓力與通訊延遲」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Remote pressure and communication delay” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"控制器若將重送的舊壓力當成新資料，可能反向修正已經恢復的壓力，造成反覆追逐與振盪；通訊恢復也不等於所有歷史封包都可立即參與控制。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If a controller treats retransmitted old pressure as current, it can counteract a pressure condition that has already recovered and create repeated chasing or oscillation. Restored communication does not make every historical packet suitable for immediate control. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：線性變化率乘延遲只估未觀測的水頭改變，並非實際控制響應；需求突變與非線性管網仍需另外模擬。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Demand steps and nonlinear network behavior still require separate modeling.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"控制器若將重送的舊壓力當成新資料，可能反向修正已經恢復的壓力，造成反覆追逐與振盪；通訊恢復也不等於所有歷史封包都可立即參與控制。","textEn":"If a controller treats retransmitted old pressure as current, it can counteract a pressure condition that has already recovered and create repeated chasing or oscillation. Restored communication does not make every historical packet suitable for immediate control.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「遠端壓力與通訊延遲機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Remote pressure and communication delay mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["控制器若將重送的舊壓力當成新資料，可能反向修正已經恢復的壓力，造成反覆追逐與振盪；通訊恢復也不等於所有歷史封包都可立即參與控制。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。"],"optionsEn":["If a controller treats retransmitted old pressure as current, it can counteract a pressure condition that has already recovered and create repeated chasing or oscillation.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"控制器若將重送的舊壓力當成新資料，可能反向修正已經恢復的壓力，造成反覆追逐與振盪；通訊恢復也不等於所有歷史封包都可立即參與控制。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If a controller treats retransmitted old pressure as current, it can counteract a pressure condition that has already recovered and create repeated chasing or oscillation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b265-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證」與「備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification\" and \"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b265-v15-25","title":"回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「回授增益與控制方向」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Feedback gain and control direction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"壓力回授必須先確認誤差符號與閥門作用方向，否則負回授可能被接成正回授。比例增益把壓力誤差轉成控制量，但實際壓力還受閥特性、管網儲能及延遲影響；提高增益未必改善速度，積分飽和與機械死區可能讓系統反而反覆超越目標。本式只是指定符號的控制量算術，不是可直接投入現場的增益；正百分點方向必須由設備作用定義，不假設等於開閥。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「回授增益與控制方向」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pressure feedback first needs consistent error sign and valve action, or intended negative feedback becomes positive feedback. Proportional gain converts pressure error into a command, while actual pressure also depends on valve characteristics, network storage and delay. Higher gain need not improve response; integral saturation and mechanical deadband can instead create repeated overshoot. This is command arithmetic under a declared sign convention, not a field-ready gain. The positive percentage-point direction must be defined by equipment action and is not presumed to mean opening. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Feedback gain and control direction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設誤差e=目標−量測=5 m、比較增益Kp=0.40百分點/m，比例命令Δu=Kp e=2.0百分點；未計動態。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume error e=target−measured=5 m and comparison gain Kp=0.40 percentage points/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「回授增益與控制方向」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Feedback gain and control direction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-25-k1","title":"回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證","titleEn":"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification","text":"壓力回授必須先確認誤差符號與閥門作用方向，否則負回授可能被接成正回授。比例增益把壓力誤差轉成控制量，但實際壓力還受閥特性、管網儲能及延遲影響；提高增益未必改善速度，積分飽和與機械死區可能讓系統反而反覆超越目標。","textEn":"Pressure feedback first needs consistent error sign and valve action, or intended negative feedback becomes positive feedback. Proportional gain converts pressure error into a command, while actual pressure also depends on valve characteristics, network storage and delay.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。","壓力回授必須先確認誤差符號與閥門作用方向，否則負回授可能被接成正回授。","現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。"],"optionsEn":["Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation.","Pressure feedback first needs consistent error sign and valve action, or intended negative feedback becomes positive feedback.","Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario."],"answer":1,"explanation":"壓力回授必須先確認誤差符號與閥門作用方向，否則負回授可能被接成正回授。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pressure feedback first needs consistent error sign and valve action, or intended negative feedback becomes positive feedback. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b265-v15-26","title":"回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「回授增益與控制方向」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Feedback gain and control direction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設誤差e=目標−量測=5 m、比較增益Kp=0.40百分點/m，比例命令Δu=Kp e=2.0百分點；未計動態。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume error e=target−measured=5 m and comparison gain Kp=0.40 percentage points/m. Proportional command Δu=Kp e=2.0 percentage points, excluding dynamics. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在離線模型確認誤差與設備方向，再檢查命令限制、死區及回授延遲。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Confirm error and device direction in an offline model, then inspect command limits, deadband and feedback delay.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設誤差e=目標−量測=5 m、比較增益Kp=0.40百分點/m，比例命令Δu=Kp e=2.0百分點；未計動態。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume error e=target−measured=5 m and comparison gain Kp=0.40 percentage points/m. Proportional command Δu=Kp e=2.0 percentage points, excluding dynamics.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。","管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設誤差e=目標−量測=5 m、比較增益Kp=0.40百分點/m，比例命令Δu=Kp e=2.0百分點；未計動態。"],"optionsEn":["Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality.","A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume error e=target−measured=5 m and comparison gain Kp=0.40 percentage points/m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設誤差e=目標−量測=5 m、比較增益Kp=0.40百分點/m，比例命令Δu=Kp e=2.0百分點；未計動態。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume error e=target−measured=5 m and comparison gain Kp=0.40 percentage points/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b265-v15-27","title":"回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「回授增益與控制方向」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Feedback gain and control direction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在離線模型確認誤差與設備方向，再檢查命令限制、死區及回授延遲。以核准測試資料比較目標、量測、閥位與控制命令，確認任何飽和或失訊時均使用已設計的行為。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Confirm error and device direction in an offline model, then inspect command limits, deadband and feedback delay. Compare target, measurement, position and command using approved test records, verifying designed behavior during saturation or signal loss. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用兩種相反的設備方向畫出回授符號圖，判斷哪一種形成負回授。把簡單命令計算與完整動態驗證分開，列出延遲及飽和需要的額外情境。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw feedback-sign diagrams for two opposite device actions and identify negative feedback. Separate command arithmetic from dynamic validation, listing additional delay and saturation scenarios needed.","failure":"注意干擾：符號設定錯誤會讓低壓時的動作進一步降低壓力，形成正回授；增益過高還可能使閥位頻繁反轉，增加磨耗並把控制波動傳到用戶端。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An incorrect sign can make the response to low pressure reduce pressure further, creating positive feedback. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在離線模型確認誤差與設備方向，再檢查命令限制、死區及回授延遲。以核准測試資料比較目標、量測、閥位與控制命令，確認任何飽和或失訊時均使用已設計的行為。","textEn":"Confirm error and device direction in an offline model, then inspect command limits, deadband and feedback delay. Compare target, measurement, position and command using approved test records, verifying designed behavior during saturation or signal loss.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用兩種相反的設備方向畫出回授符號圖，判斷哪一種形成負回授。把簡單命令計算與完整動態驗證分開，列出延遲及飽和需要的額外情境。","textEn":"Draw feedback-sign diagrams for two opposite device actions and identify negative feedback. Separate command arithmetic from dynamic validation, listing additional delay and saturation scenarios needed.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification\"?","options":["在離線模型確認誤差與設備方向，再檢查命令限制、死區及回授延遲。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。"],"optionsEn":["Confirm error and device direction in an offline model, then inspect command limits, deadband and feedback delay.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在離線模型確認誤差與設備方向，再檢查命令限制、死區及回授延遲。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Confirm error and device direction in an offline model, then inspect command limits, deadband and feedback delay. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b265-v15-28","title":"回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「回授增益與控制方向」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Feedback gain and control direction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"符號設定錯誤會讓低壓時的動作進一步降低壓力，形成正回授；增益過高還可能使閥位頻繁反轉，增加磨耗並把控制波動傳到用戶端。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An incorrect sign can make the response to low pressure reduce pressure further, creating positive feedback. Excessive gain can also reverse valve motion repeatedly, increasing wear and transmitting control oscillations to customers. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本式只是指定符號的控制量算術，不是可直接投入現場的增益；正百分點方向必須由設備作用定義，不假設等於開閥。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The positive percentage-point direction must be defined by equipment action and is not presumed to mean opening.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"符號設定錯誤會讓低壓時的動作進一步降低壓力，形成正回授；增益過高還可能使閥位頻繁反轉，增加磨耗並把控制波動傳到用戶端。","textEn":"An incorrect sign can make the response to low pressure reduce pressure further, creating positive feedback. Excessive gain can also reverse valve motion repeatedly, increasing wear and transmitting control oscillations to customers.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「回授增益與控制方向機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Feedback gain and control direction mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","符號設定錯誤會讓低壓時的動作進一步降低壓力，形成正回授；增益過高還可能使閥位頻繁反轉，增加磨耗並把控制波動傳到用戶端。","現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","An incorrect sign can make the response to low pressure reduce pressure further, creating positive feedback.","Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario."],"answer":1,"explanation":"符號設定錯誤會讓低壓時的動作進一步降低壓力，形成正回授；增益過高還可能使閥位頻繁反轉，增加磨耗並把控制波動傳到用戶端。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An incorrect sign can make the response to low pressure reduce pressure further, creating positive feedback. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b265-v15-29","title":"備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「備援供水與非常態邊界」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Backup supply and abnormal boundaries” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"壓力管理設備檢修或失效時，替代供水路徑的水頭損失可能不同於正常路徑。備援管路存在不代表備援服務能力足夠，較小管徑、較長距離或不同水源高程都會降低遠端壓力；評估需按實際可用的水源與閥位重建網路，而不是把名目容量直接相加。此例只檢查一個指定備援工況的水頭餘量，不包含水源可用性、消防需求與瞬變；負餘量表示假設條件未滿足比較需求。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「備援供水與非常態邊界」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"During maintenance or failure of pressure-management equipment, an alternative supply path can have different head losses from the normal route. A bypass does not guarantee adequate backup service: smaller diameter, longer length or another source elevation can reduce remote pressure. Assessment must reconstruct actual available sources and valve states instead of simply adding nominal capacities. The example checks head margin for one backup condition, excluding source availability, fire demand and transients. A negative margin means the assumed case does not meet the comparison requirement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Backup supply and abnormal boundaries” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設備援水頭45 m、節點高程20 m、損失18 m，h=7 m；比較需求15 m，餘量h−hreq=−8 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume backup head 45 m, node elevation 20 m and loss 18 m, giving h=7 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「備援供水與非常態邊界」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Backup supply and abnormal boundaries”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-29-k1","title":"備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證","titleEn":"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification","text":"壓力管理設備檢修或失效時，替代供水路徑的水頭損失可能不同於正常路徑。備援管路存在不代表備援服務能力足夠，較小管徑、較長距離或不同水源高程都會降低遠端壓力；評估需按實際可用的水源與閥位重建網路，而不是把名目容量直接相加。","textEn":"During maintenance or failure of pressure-management equipment, an alternative supply path can have different head losses from the normal route. A bypass does not guarantee adequate backup service: smaller diameter, longer length or another source elevation can reduce remote pressure.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。","平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。","壓力管理設備檢修或失效時，替代供水路徑的水頭損失可能不同於正常路徑。"],"optionsEn":["Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario.","Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients.","During maintenance or failure of pressure-management equipment, an alternative supply path can have different head losses from the normal route."],"answer":2,"explanation":"壓力管理設備檢修或失效時，替代供水路徑的水頭損失可能不同於正常路徑。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"During maintenance or failure of pressure-management equipment, an alternative supply path can have different head losses from the normal route. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b265-v15-30","title":"備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「備援供水與非常態邊界」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Backup supply and abnormal boundaries” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設備援水頭45 m、節點高程20 m、損失18 m，h=7 m；比較需求15 m，餘量h−hreq=−8 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume backup head 45 m, node elevation 20 m and loss 18 m, giving h=7 m. Against comparison requirement 15 m, margin h−hreq=−8 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對備援水源、旁通閥及相鄰分區可承受的供量，對正常和失效狀態各保存一份拓樸。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify backup sources, bypass valves and neighboring-district supply availability, retaining separate normal and failed-state topologies.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設備援水頭45 m、節點高程20 m、損失18 m，h=7 m；比較需求15 m，餘量h−hreq=−8 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume backup head 45 m, node elevation 20 m and loss 18 m, giving h=7 m. Against comparison requirement 15 m, margin h−hreq=−8 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設備援水頭45 m、節點高程20 m、損失18 m，h=7 m；比較需求15 m，餘量h−hreq=−8 m。","減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。","漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume backup head 45 m, node elevation 20 m and loss 18 m, giving h=7 m.","Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer.","The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設備援水頭45 m、節點高程20 m、損失18 m，h=7 m；比較需求15 m，餘量h−hreq=−8 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume backup head 45 m, node elevation 20 m and loss 18 m, giving h=7 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b265-v15-31","title":"備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「備援供水與非常態邊界」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Backup supply and abnormal boundaries” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對備援水源、旁通閥及相鄰分區可承受的供量，對正常和失效狀態各保存一份拓樸。以代表需求組合重算遠端壓力，檢查備援切換是否把缺壓轉移到其他服務區。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify backup sources, bypass valves and neighboring-district supply availability, retaining separate normal and failed-state topologies. Recompute remote pressure for representative demand combinations and check whether backup switching transfers a pressure deficit to another service area. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對同一需求分別畫出正常與備援水頭線，標出哪段損失增加。列出可能共同失效的水源、電力及通訊依賴，避免把名義上兩條路徑當成完全獨立備援。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw normal and backup hydraulic grades for one demand, identifying increased losses. List shared source, power and communications dependencies so two nominal paths are not mistaken for fully independent backup.","failure":"注意干擾：只確認旁通閥能開啟而未檢查路徑損失，可能在真正需要備援時才發現供壓不足；借用相鄰區水頭又可能使另一區同時失去服務裕度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Checking only that a bypass valve can open can leave inadequate pressure undiscovered until backup is needed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對備援水源、旁通閥及相鄰分區可承受的供量，對正常和失效狀態各保存一份拓樸。以代表需求組合重算遠端壓力，檢查備援切換是否把缺壓轉移到其他服務區。","textEn":"Verify backup sources, bypass valves and neighboring-district supply availability, retaining separate normal and failed-state topologies. Recompute remote pressure for representative demand combinations and check whether backup switching transfers a pressure deficit to another service area.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對同一需求分別畫出正常與備援水頭線，標出哪段損失增加。列出可能共同失效的水源、電力及通訊依賴，避免把名義上兩條路徑當成完全獨立備援。","textEn":"Draw normal and backup hydraulic grades for one demand, identifying increased losses. List shared source, power and communications dependencies so two nominal paths are not mistaken for fully independent backup.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對備援水源、旁通閥及相鄰分區可承受的供量，對正常和失效狀態各保存一份拓樸。","控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Verify backup sources, bypass valves and neighboring-district supply availability, retaining separate normal and failed-state topologies.","A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對備援水源、旁通閥及相鄰分區可承受的供量，對正常和失效狀態各保存一份拓樸。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify backup sources, bypass valves and neighboring-district supply availability, retaining separate normal and failed-state topologies. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b265-v15-32","title":"備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「備援供水與非常態邊界」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Backup supply and abnormal boundaries” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只確認旁通閥能開啟而未檢查路徑損失，可能在真正需要備援時才發現供壓不足；借用相鄰區水頭又可能使另一區同時失去服務裕度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Checking only that a bypass valve can open can leave inadequate pressure undiscovered until backup is needed. Drawing on a neighboring district’s head may also remove its service margin at the same time. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：此例只檢查一個指定備援工況的水頭餘量，不包含水源可用性、消防需求與瞬變；負餘量表示假設條件未滿足比較需求。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A negative margin means the assumed case does not meet the comparison requirement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「現場有旁通管就代表任何失效情境都能維持原有供水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Having a bypass guarantees unchanged supply in every failure scenario.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只確認旁通閥能開啟而未檢查路徑損失，可能在真正需要備援時才發現供壓不足；借用相鄰區水頭又可能使另一區同時失去服務裕度。","textEn":"Checking only that a bypass valve can open can leave inadequate pressure undiscovered until backup is needed. Drawing on a neighboring district’s head may also remove its service margin at the same time.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「備援供水與非常態邊界機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Backup supply and abnormal boundaries mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。","只確認旁通閥能開啟而未檢查路徑損失，可能在真正需要備援時才發現供壓不足；借用相鄰區水頭又可能使另一區同時失去服務裕度。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients.","Checking only that a bypass valve can open can leave inadequate pressure undiscovered until backup is needed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只確認旁通閥能開啟而未檢查路徑損失，可能在真正需要備援時才發現供壓不足；借用相鄰區水頭又可能使另一區同時失去服務裕度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Checking only that a bypass valve can open can leave inadequate pressure undiscovered until backup is needed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b265-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證」與「低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification\" and \"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b265-v15-33","title":"調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「調壓動作與快速瞬變」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pressure adjustments and rapid transients” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"降低長期平均壓力不代表每一次調節都降低瞬間峰值，過快閥動作會改變流速並激發壓力波。控制器時間尺度與管線波傳時間可能相差很大，延時管網模型無法解析快速水錘；因此壓力管理方案需把服務水頭、控制動態及瞬變包絡分開而又一致地驗證。焦可夫斯基算例只估單一快速波前的壓力增量，不是閥動作建議，也不包含反射、低壓空穴及其他設備邊界。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「調壓動作與快速瞬變」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Lower long-term mean pressure does not guarantee lower instantaneous peaks during every adjustment. Rapid valve motion changes velocity and launches pressure waves. Controller and wave-travel time scales can differ greatly, and an extended-period network model cannot resolve fast water hammer. Service head, control dynamics and transient envelopes therefore need separate but consistent verification. The Joukowsky example estimates one rapid wavefront’s increment only. It is not a valve-action recommendation and excludes reflections, low-pressure cavities and other equipment boundaries. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pressure adjustments and rapid transients” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、a=800 m/s、快速速度變化幅度Δv=0.20 m/s，Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa，須另加初始壓力。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, a=800 m/s and rapid velocity-change magnitude Δv=0.20 m/s. Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa, separate from initial pressure.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「調壓動作與快速瞬變」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pressure adjustments and rapid transients”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-33-k1","title":"調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證","titleEn":"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification","text":"降低長期平均壓力不代表每一次調節都降低瞬間峰值，過快閥動作會改變流速並激發壓力波。控制器時間尺度與管線波傳時間可能相差很大，延時管網模型無法解析快速水錘；因此壓力管理方案需把服務水頭、控制動態及瞬變包絡分開而又一致地驗證。","textEn":"Lower long-term mean pressure does not guarantee lower instantaneous peaks during every adjustment. Rapid valve motion changes velocity and launches pressure waves.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["降低長期平均壓力不代表每一次調節都降低瞬間峰值，過快閥動作會改變流速並激發壓力波。","平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。","壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。"],"optionsEn":["Lower long-term mean pressure does not guarantee lower instantaneous peaks during every adjustment.","Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients.","Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"降低長期平均壓力不代表每一次調節都降低瞬間峰值，過快閥動作會改變流速並激發壓力波。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Lower long-term mean pressure does not guarantee lower instantaneous peaks during every adjustment. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b265-v15-34","title":"調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「調壓動作與快速瞬變」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pressure adjustments and rapid transients” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、a=800 m/s、快速速度變化幅度Δv=0.20 m/s，Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa，須另加初始壓力。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, a=800 m/s and rapid velocity-change magnitude Δv=0.20 m/s. Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa, separate from initial pressure. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將閥位時間歷程與高速壓力紀錄同步，確認一般遙測是否足以看見短時尖峰。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronize valve-position history with high-rate pressure records and check whether ordinary telemetry can resolve short peaks.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、a=800 m/s、快速速度變化幅度Δv=0.20 m/s，Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa，須另加初始壓力。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, a=800 m/s and rapid velocity-change magnitude Δv=0.20 m/s. Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa, separate from initial pressure.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["管網模型能收斂就表示每一節點都實際得到要求水量。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、a=800 m/s、快速速度變化幅度Δv=0.20 m/s，Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa，須另加初始壓力。","減壓閥降低的水力功率都已自動轉換成可使用電力。"],"optionsEn":["A converged network model means every node actually receives its required flow.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, a=800 m/s and rapid velocity-change magnitude Δv=0.20 m/s. Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa, separate from initial pressure.","All hydraulic power removed by a reducing valve automatically becomes usable electricity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、a=800 m/s、快速速度變化幅度Δv=0.20 m/s，Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa，須另加初始壓力。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, a=800 m/s and rapid velocity-change magnitude Δv=0.20 m/s. Δp=ρaΔv=160 kPa, separate from initial pressure. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b265-v15-35","title":"調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「調壓動作與快速瞬變」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pressure adjustments and rapid transients” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將閥位時間歷程與高速壓力紀錄同步，確認一般遙測是否足以看見短時尖峰。使用相容的瞬變模型檢查正常調節、停電及失訊情境，再與延時模型的初始水頭及需求保持一致。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronize valve-position history with high-rate pressure records and check whether ordinary telemetry can resolve short peaks. Use a compatible transient model for regulation, power loss and signal loss, keeping initial heads and demands consistent with the extended-period model. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將一段含短時尖峰的假設壓力歷程做低頻平均，觀察哪些資訊消失。列出應用延時與瞬變模型的不同問題，並指出兩者需要共同保留的邊界資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Average a hypothetical pressure history containing a short peak and identify the information lost. List questions for extended-period and transient models and the boundary data that both must share.","failure":"注意干擾：只看每十五分鐘平均壓力可能完全漏掉秒級壓峰，讓減壓措施被誤判為同時解決所有水錘；快速回授反覆動作也可能增加管殼循環應力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Fifteen-minute mean pressure can completely miss second-scale peaks and falsely suggest that pressure reduction solved every transient. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將閥位時間歷程與高速壓力紀錄同步，確認一般遙測是否足以看見短時尖峰。使用相容的瞬變模型檢查正常調節、停電及失訊情境，再與延時模型的初始水頭及需求保持一致。","textEn":"Synchronize valve-position history with high-rate pressure records and check whether ordinary telemetry can resolve short peaks. Use a compatible transient model for regulation, power loss and signal loss, keeping initial heads and demands consistent with the extended-period model.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將一段含短時尖峰的假設壓力歷程做低頻平均，觀察哪些資訊消失。列出應用延時與瞬變模型的不同問題，並指出兩者需要共同保留的邊界資料。","textEn":"Average a hypothetical pressure history containing a short peak and identify the information lost. List questions for extended-period and transient models and the boundary data that both must share.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","通訊連線正常就表示控制器讀到的壓力一定是即時值。","將閥位時間歷程與高速壓力紀錄同步，確認一般遙測是否足以看見短時尖峰。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A working communication link guarantees the controller sees current pressure.","Synchronize valve-position history with high-rate pressure records and check whether ordinary telemetry can resolve short peaks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將閥位時間歷程與高速壓力紀錄同步，確認一般遙測是否足以看見短時尖峰。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronize valve-position history with high-rate pressure records and check whether ordinary telemetry can resolve short peaks. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b265-v15-36","title":"調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「調壓動作與快速瞬變」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pressure adjustments and rapid transients” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只看每十五分鐘平均壓力可能完全漏掉秒級壓峰，讓減壓措施被誤判為同時解決所有水錘；快速回授反覆動作也可能增加管殼循環應力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Fifteen-minute mean pressure can completely miss second-scale peaks and falsely suggest that pressure reduction solved every transient. Repeated rapid feedback actions can also increase cyclic shell stress. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：焦可夫斯基算例只估單一快速波前的壓力增量，不是閥動作建議，也不包含反射、低壓空穴及其他設備邊界。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It is not a valve-action recommendation and excludes reflections, low-pressure cavities and other equipment boundaries.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均壓力降低後就不需要再檢查任何快速水錘事件。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Lower average pressure removes the need to examine rapid transients.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只看每十五分鐘平均壓力可能完全漏掉秒級壓峰，讓減壓措施被誤判為同時解決所有水錘；快速回授反覆動作也可能增加管殼循環應力。","textEn":"Fifteen-minute mean pressure can completely miss second-scale peaks and falsely suggest that pressure reduction solved every transient. Repeated rapid feedback actions can also increase cyclic shell stress.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「調壓動作與快速瞬變機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pressure adjustments and rapid transients mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只看每十五分鐘平均壓力可能完全漏掉秒級壓峰，讓減壓措施被誤判為同時解決所有水錘；快速回授反覆動作也可能增加管殼循環應力。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。"],"optionsEn":["Fifteen-minute mean pressure can completely miss second-scale peaks and falsely suggest that pressure reduction solved every transient.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只看每十五分鐘平均壓力可能完全漏掉秒級壓峰，讓減壓措施被誤判為同時解決所有水錘；快速回授反覆動作也可能增加管殼循環應力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fifteen-minute mean pressure can completely miss second-scale peaks and falsely suggest that pressure reduction solved every transient. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b265-v15-37","title":"低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「低流量水齡與水質介面」如何影響配水管網壓力管理的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Low-flow residence and water-quality interface” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pressure management of water-distribution networks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"壓力管理改變漏流與部分壓力相依需求後，某些支線的更新水量可能下降，水齡和消毒劑衰減便需要重新評估。幾何容積除以通量只給理想平均停留尺度，實際管網有混合、短路及死端分布；不能以較少水量損失直接推定所有水質指標都會改善。本例假設固定容積與穩定通量，只計平均尺度；它不是所有水粒子的年齡，也沒有提供任何水質合格判準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「低流量水齡與水質介面」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After pressure management changes leakage and some pressure-dependent demand, renewal flow in certain branches can decrease, requiring reassessment of water age and disinfectant decay. Volume divided by flow gives an ideal mean residence scale, while actual networks contain mixing, short circuits and dead ends. Reduced physical loss therefore does not directly establish improvement in every water-quality indicator. The example assumes fixed volume and steady throughput to calculate a mean scale only. It is not the age of every water parcel and supplies no water-quality acceptance criterion. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Low-flow residence and water-quality interface” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設支路有效水量V=500 m³、更新通量Q=10 m³/h，平均停留尺度τ=V/Q=50 h；若Q降至8 m³/h，τ=62.5 h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective branch volume V=500 m³ and renewal flow Q=10 m³/h.","failure":"常見誤解：「壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「低流量水齡與水質介面」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Low-flow residence and water-quality interface”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-37-k1","title":"低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證","titleEn":"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification","text":"壓力管理改變漏流與部分壓力相依需求後，某些支線的更新水量可能下降，水齡和消毒劑衰減便需要重新評估。幾何容積除以通量只給理想平均停留尺度，實際管網有混合、短路及死端分布；不能以較少水量損失直接推定所有水質指標都會改善。","textEn":"After pressure management changes leakage and some pressure-dependent demand, renewal flow in certain branches can decrease, requiring reassessment of water age and disinfectant decay. Volume divided by flow gives an ideal mean residence scale, while actual networks contain mixing, short circuits and dead ends.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。","壓力管理改變漏流與部分壓力相依需求後，某些支線的更新水量可能下降，水齡和消毒劑衰減便需要重新評估。","減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality.","After pressure management changes leakage and some pressure-dependent demand, renewal flow in certain branches can decrease, requiring reassessment of water age and disinfectant decay.","Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"壓力管理改變漏流與部分壓力相依需求後，某些支線的更新水量可能下降，水齡和消毒劑衰減便需要重新評估。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After pressure management changes leakage and some pressure-dependent demand, renewal flow in certain branches can decrease, requiring reassessment of water age and disinfectant decay. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b265-v15-38","title":"低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「低流量水齡與水質介面」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Low-flow residence and water-quality interface” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設支路有效水量V=500 m³、更新通量Q=10 m³/h，平均停留尺度τ=V/Q=50 h；若Q降至8 m³/h，τ=62.5 h。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective branch volume V=500 m³ and renewal flow Q=10 m³/h. Mean residence scale τ=V/Q=50 h; at Q=8 m³/h, τ=62.5 h. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將壓力管理前後的流量、溫度及水質採樣位置對齊，使用適當管網水質模型檢查死端與水池混合。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align pre- and post-management flow, temperature and water-quality sampling locations, using an appropriate network-quality model to examine dead ends and tank mixing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設支路有效水量V=500 m³、更新通量Q=10 m³/h，平均停留尺度τ=V/Q=50 h；若Q降至8 m³/h，τ=62.5 h。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective branch volume V=500 m³ and renewal flow Q=10 m³/h. Mean residence scale τ=V/Q=50 h; at Q=8 m³/h, τ=62.5 h.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["漏失壓力指數固定不變且能直接預測未來所有爆管。","控制閥只要能通過最大流量就一定能穩定調節所有流量。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設支路有效水量V=500 m³、更新通量Q=10 m³/h，平均停留尺度τ=V/Q=50 h。"],"optionsEn":["The leakage exponent is fixed and directly predicts every future pipe break.","A valve that passes maximum flow can stably regulate every lower flow.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective branch volume V=500 m³ and renewal flow Q=10 m³/h."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設支路有效水量V=500 m³、更新通量Q=10 m³/h，平均停留尺度τ=V/Q=50 h；若Q降至8 m³/h，τ=62.5 h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective branch volume V=500 m³ and renewal flow Q=10 m³/h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b265-v15-39","title":"低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「低流量水齡與水質介面」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Low-flow residence and water-quality interface” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將壓力管理前後的流量、溫度及水質採樣位置對齊，使用適當管網水質模型檢查死端與水池混合。保留代表性時段及實測殘留資料，避免只用平均停留時間代替水質驗證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align pre- and post-management flow, temperature and water-quality sampling locations, using an appropriate network-quality model to examine dead ends and tank mixing. Retain representative periods and measured residuals rather than substituting mean residence time for water-quality verification. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以相同支路容積比較兩個更新通量的停留尺度，再說明死端與混合會如何改變年齡分布。把節水、供壓與水質列成三個需要共同驗證的成果。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare residence scales at two renewal flows for one branch volume, then explain how dead ends and mixing change the age distribution. Treat water savings, service pressure and quality as three outcomes requiring joint verification.","failure":"注意干擾：漏流減少後若忽略低更新支線，可能讓水齡增加而未被平均區壓監測發現；把理想停留尺度當成每個用戶的實際水齡，又會錯估局部水質風險。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring low-renewal branches after leakage reduction can allow water age to rise without appearing in average-pressure monitoring. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將壓力管理前後的流量、溫度及水質採樣位置對齊，使用適當管網水質模型檢查死端與水池混合。保留代表性時段及實測殘留資料，避免只用平均停留時間代替水質驗證。","textEn":"Align pre- and post-management flow, temperature and water-quality sampling locations, using an appropriate network-quality model to examine dead ends and tank mixing. Retain representative periods and measured residuals rather than substituting mean residence time for water-quality verification.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以相同支路容積比較兩個更新通量的停留尺度，再說明死端與混合會如何改變年齡分布。把節水、供壓與水質列成三個需要共同驗證的成果。","textEn":"Compare residence scales at two renewal flows for one branch volume, then explain how dead ends and mixing change the age distribution. Treat water savings, service pressure and quality as three outcomes requiring joint verification.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification\"?","options":["將壓力管理前後的流量、溫度及水質採樣位置對齊，使用適當管網水質模型檢查死端與水池混合。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","比例增益越大就一定越快達標且不會增加振盪。"],"optionsEn":["Align pre- and post-management flow, temperature and water-quality sampling locations, using an appropriate network-quality model to examine dead ends and tank mixing.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Larger proportional gain always reaches the target faster without increasing oscillation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將壓力管理前後的流量、溫度及水質採樣位置對齊，使用適當管網水質模型檢查死端與水池混合。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align pre- and post-management flow, temperature and water-quality sampling locations, using an appropriate network-quality model to examine dead ends and tank mixing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b265-v15-40","title":"低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"prerequisiteIds":["b265-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「低流量水齡與水質介面」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Low-flow residence and water-quality interface” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏流減少後若忽略低更新支線，可能讓水齡增加而未被平均區壓監測發現；把理想停留尺度當成每個用戶的實際水齡，又會錯估局部水質風險。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring low-renewal branches after leakage reduction can allow water age to rise without appearing in average-pressure monitoring. Treating ideal residence scale as every customer’s actual water age also misrepresents localized quality concerns. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例假設固定容積與穩定通量，只計平均尺度；它不是所有水粒子的年齡，也沒有提供任何水質合格判準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It is not the age of every water parcel and supplies no water-quality acceptance criterion.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「壓力管理只會影響漏水量而完全不會改變水齡或水質。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Pressure management affects leakage only and cannot change water age or quality.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b265-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏流減少後若忽略低更新支線，可能讓水齡增加而未被平均區壓監測發現；把理想停留尺度當成每個用戶的實際水齡，又會錯估局部水質風險。","textEn":"Ignoring low-renewal branches after leakage reduction can allow water age to rise without appearing in average-pressure monitoring. Treating ideal residence scale as every customer’s actual water age also misrepresents localized quality concerns.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]},{"id":"b265-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「低流量水齡與水質介面機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Low-flow residence and water-quality interface mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","漏流減少後若忽略低更新支線，可能讓水齡增加而未被平均區壓監測發現；把理想停留尺度當成每個用戶的實際水齡，又會錯估局部水質風險。","減壓閥出口壓力足夠就能保證所有用戶壓力都足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Ignoring low-renewal branches after leakage reduction can allow water age to rise without appearing in average-pressure monitoring.","Adequate reducing-valve outlet pressure guarantees adequate pressure for every customer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"漏流減少後若忽略低更新支線，可能讓水齡增加而未被平均區壓監測發現；把理想停留尺度當成每個用戶的實際水齡，又會錯估局部水質風險。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring low-renewal branches after leakage reduction can allow water age to rise without appearing in average-pressure monitoring. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-loss-guide","v15s-epa-epanet","v15s-wsd-win","v15s-pub-smart"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b266","title":"海水淡化取水工程","titleEn":"Seawater-desalination intake works","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課由淡化回收率推導取水需求，依序分析篩網法向流速、有效面積、管路損失及潮位吸入裕度，再比較地下取水、堵塞、海管浮力與生物暴露。最後將排放回流接回進水水質，要求每個算例保留控制體、單位及適用邊界，不將平均值直接當成生態或設備允收結論。","summaryEn":"Starting from desalination recovery, this course develops intake demand through screen-normal velocity, effective area, losses and tidal suction margin, then examines subsurface collection, clogging, pipe buoyancy and biological exposure. Outfall recirculation closes the feed-quality loop. Every example retains its control volume, units and limits rather than converting an average into ecological or equipment acceptance.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-pipe","architectureNodes":[["海域與生物","Coast and organisms"],["取水頭與篩面","Intake head and screens"],["海管與抽水","Marine pipe and pumping"],["預處理介面","Pretreatment interface"],["監測及回流","Monitoring and recirculation"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]],"diagram":{"type":"water-pipe","labels":["海域與生物","取水頭與篩面","海管與抽水","預處理介面","監測及回流"],"labelsEn":["Coast and organisms","Intake head and screens","Marine pipe and pumping","Pretreatment interface","Monitoring and recirculation"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創敏感度例設定產品水0.50 m³/s，膜段回收率45%時需進水1.111 m³/s；只把回收率降至40%，進水增為1.250 m³/s，增加12.5%。若有效篩面維持10 m²，平均法向速度隨之由0.1111增至0.1250 m/s。這只是膜段與理想均勻篩面的聯動，尚未加入反洗、堵塞與物種條件。接著應以全廠水量帳及局部流場檢查結果，再比較地下取水的水文地質可行性。數值不是兩座西澳案例的操作參數，也不是推薦取水或生態門檻。","textEn":"An original sensitivity example supplies product water at 0.50 m³/s. Membrane recovery of 45% requires feed 1.111 m³/s; lowering only recovery to 40% increases feed to 1.250 m³/s, a 12.5% rise. With effective screen area fixed at 10 m², mean normal velocity rises from 0.1111 to 0.1250 m/s. This couples only the membrane balance and an ideally uniform screen, omitting backwash, blockage and species conditions. Check the result against the complete plant balance and local flow field, then compare hydrogeological feasibility of subsurface alternatives. These values are neither operating parameters from the Western Australian cases nor recommended intake or ecological limits.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b266-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「產水需求與取水總量機理與驗證」與「接近流速與篩網面積機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Product demand and intake volume mechanism and verification\" and \"Approach velocity and screen area mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b266-v15-01","title":"產水需求與取水總量機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Product demand and intake volume mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「產水需求與取水總量」如何影響海水淡化取水工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Product demand and intake volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seawater-desalination intake works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"淡化廠取水量大於產品水量，回收率把膜系統產水與進水連結，預處理排泥、反洗及其他支流還會增加總取水需求。若只用產品容量選擇取水口，可能低估海管、篩網與抽水負荷；不同流程的回收率定義須明確標示是膜段或全廠，避免重複或漏算支流。本例只對膜段作水量守恆，忽略密度差及其他支流；不能把得到的進水流量直接當成全廠海水取水設計值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「產水需求與取水總量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A desalination plant takes in more seawater than its product output. Recovery links membrane product and feed, while pretreatment sludge, backwash and other streams can increase total intake. Sizing an intake from product capacity alone can understate pipeline, screen and pumping loads. Recovery definitions must distinguish the membrane stage from the entire plant to avoid omitting or double-counting side streams. The example applies volume balance to the membrane stage only, neglecting density differences and side streams. Its feed flow is not automatically the complete plant intake design flow. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Product demand and intake volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設產品Qp=0.50 m³/s、膜段回收率R=0.45，Qf=Qp/R=1.111 m³/s，濃水Qb=Qf−Qp=0.611 m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume product Qp=0.50 m³/s and membrane recovery R=0.45.","failure":"常見誤解：「淡化廠標示的產品水容量就等於需要的海水取水流量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A plant’s stated product capacity equals the required seawater intake flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「產水需求與取水總量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Product demand and intake volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-01-k1","title":"產水需求與取水總量機理與驗證","titleEn":"Product demand and intake volume mechanism and verification","text":"淡化廠取水量大於產品水量，回收率把膜系統產水與進水連結，預處理排泥、反洗及其他支流還會增加總取水需求。若只用產品容量選擇取水口，可能低估海管、篩網與抽水負荷；不同流程的回收率定義須明確標示是膜段或全廠，避免重複或漏算支流。","textEn":"A desalination plant takes in more seawater than its product output. Recovery links membrane product and feed, while pretreatment sludge, backwash and other streams can increase total intake.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：淡化廠標示的產品水容量就等於需要的海水取水流量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A plant’s stated product capacity equals the required seawater intake flow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「產水需求與取水總量機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Product demand and intake volume mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["淡化廠標示的產品水容量就等於需要的海水取水流量。","淡化廠取水量大於產品水量，回收率把膜系統產水與進水連結，預處理排泥、反洗及其他支流還會增加總取水需求。","篩網平均流速低就能直接證明所有海洋生物都不受影響。"],"optionsEn":["A plant’s stated product capacity equals the required seawater intake flow.","A desalination plant takes in more seawater than its product output.","Low average screen velocity proves that no marine organisms are affected."],"answer":1,"explanation":"淡化廠取水量大於產品水量，回收率把膜系統產水與進水連結，預處理排泥、反洗及其他支流還會增加總取水需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A desalination plant takes in more seawater than its product output. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b266-v15-02","title":"產水需求與取水總量機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Product demand and intake volume mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「產水需求與取水總量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Product demand and intake volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設產品Qp=0.50 m³/s、膜段回收率R=0.45，Qf=Qp/R=1.111 m³/s，濃水Qb=Qf−Qp=0.611 m³/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume product Qp=0.50 m³/s and membrane recovery R=0.45. Feed Qf=Qp/R=1.111 m³/s and concentrate Qb=Qf−Qp=0.611 m³/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以流程圖列出產品、濃水、反洗與排泥等支流，為每支流標明連續或間歇性及計量時間窗。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map product, concentrate, backwash and sludge streams, identifying continuous or intermittent operation and measurement windows.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設產品Qp=0.50 m³/s、膜段回收率R=0.45，Qf=Qp/R=1.111 m³/s，濃水Qb=Qf−Qp=0.611 m³/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume product Qp=0.50 m³/s and membrane recovery R=0.45. Feed Qf=Qp/R=1.111 m³/s and concentrate Qb=Qf−Qp=0.611 m³/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「產水需求與取水總量機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Product demand and intake volume mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["所有局部損失係數都可直接相加而不必核對速度基準。","地下取水只要量到一處高滲透層就能保證全廠長期供水。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設產品Qp=0.50 m³/s、膜段回收率R=0.45，Qf=Qp/R=1.111 m³/s，濃水Qb=Qf−Qp=0.611 m³/s。"],"optionsEn":["All local-loss coefficients can be added without checking their velocity basis.","One highly permeable layer guarantees long-term supply for the whole plant.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume product Qp=0.50 m³/s and membrane recovery R=0.45."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設產品Qp=0.50 m³/s、膜段回收率R=0.45，Qf=Qp/R=1.111 m³/s，濃水Qb=Qf−Qp=0.611 m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume product Qp=0.50 m³/s and membrane recovery R=0.45. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b266-v15-03","title":"產水需求與取水總量機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Product demand and intake volume mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「產水需求與取水總量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Product demand and intake volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以流程圖列出產品、濃水、反洗與排泥等支流，為每支流標明連續或間歇性及計量時間窗。核對回收率的實際控制體，將膜段水量帳與全廠取水帳分開驗證後再合併。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map product, concentrate, backwash and sludge streams, identifying continuous or intermittent operation and measurement windows. Verify the recovery control volume and validate membrane and whole-plant balances separately against synchronized flow-meter records before combining them. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出膜段與全廠兩個控制體，分別填入相同產品需求和假設回收率。逐一指出尚未計量的支流，並說明哪些額外資料會改變海管容量估計。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw membrane and whole-plant control volumes using the same product demand and assumed recovery. Identify unmetered side streams and explain which additional information would alter the intake-pipeline estimate.","failure":"注意干擾：把膜回收率當成全廠回收率會漏掉預處理耗水，使取水泵與海管容量估計偏小；高回收率情境也可能增加濃水鹽度，不能只把它視為減少取水的單向好處。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using membrane recovery as whole-plant recovery omits pretreatment water and understates intake pump and pipeline demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以流程圖列出產品、濃水、反洗與排泥等支流，為每支流標明連續或間歇性及計量時間窗。核對回收率的實際控制體，將膜段水量帳與全廠取水帳分開驗證後再合併。","textEn":"Map product, concentrate, backwash and sludge streams, identifying continuous or intermittent operation and measurement windows. Verify the recovery control volume and validate membrane and whole-plant balances separately against synchronized flow-meter records before combining them.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出膜段與全廠兩個控制體，分別填入相同產品需求和假設回收率。逐一指出尚未計量的支流，並說明哪些額外資料會改變海管容量估計。","textEn":"Draw membrane and whole-plant control volumes using the same product demand and assumed recovery. Identify unmetered side streams and explain which additional information would alter the intake-pipeline estimate.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「產水需求與取水總量機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Product demand and intake volume mechanism and verification\"?","options":["以流程圖列出產品、濃水、反洗與排泥等支流，為每支流標明連續或間歇性及計量時間窗。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","海管永久狀態穩定就代表空管施工或排空維修時也一定穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Map product, concentrate, backwash and sludge streams, identifying continuous or intermittent operation and measurement windows.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Permanent stability guarantees stability during empty-pipe construction or drained maintenance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以流程圖列出產品、濃水、反洗與排泥等支流，為每支流標明連續或間歇性及計量時間窗。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map product, concentrate, backwash and sludge streams, identifying continuous or intermittent operation and measurement windows. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b266-v15-04","title":"產水需求與取水總量機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Product demand and intake volume mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「產水需求與取水總量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Product demand and intake volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把膜回收率當成全廠回收率會漏掉預處理耗水，使取水泵與海管容量估計偏小；高回收率情境也可能增加濃水鹽度，不能只把它視為減少取水的單向好處。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using membrane recovery as whole-plant recovery omits pretreatment water and understates intake pump and pipeline demand. Higher recovery can also increase concentrate salinity, so it is not simply a one-directional intake benefit. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例只對膜段作水量守恆，忽略密度差及其他支流；不能把得到的進水流量直接當成全廠海水取水設計值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Its feed flow is not automatically the complete plant intake design flow.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「淡化廠標示的產品水容量就等於需要的海水取水流量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A plant’s stated product capacity equals the required seawater intake flow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把膜回收率當成全廠回收率會漏掉預處理耗水，使取水泵與海管容量估計偏小；高回收率情境也可能增加濃水鹽度，不能只把它視為減少取水的單向好處。","textEn":"Using membrane recovery as whole-plant recovery omits pretreatment water and understates intake pump and pipeline demand. Higher recovery can also increase concentrate salinity, so it is not simply a one-directional intake benefit.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「產水需求與取水總量機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Product demand and intake volume mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把膜回收率當成全廠回收率會漏掉預處理耗水，使取水泵與海管容量估計偏小；高回收率情境也可能增加濃水鹽度，不能只把它視為減少取水的單向好處。","篩網平均流速低就能直接證明所有海洋生物都不受影響。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using membrane recovery as whole-plant recovery omits pretreatment water and understates intake pump and pipeline demand.","Low average screen velocity proves that no marine organisms are affected."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把膜回收率當成全廠回收率會漏掉預處理耗水，使取水泵與海管容量估計偏小；高回收率情境也可能增加濃水鹽度，不能只把它視為減少取水的單向好處。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using membrane recovery as whole-plant recovery omits pretreatment water and understates intake pump and pipeline demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b266-v15-05","title":"接近流速與篩網面積機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Approach velocity and screen area mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「接近流速與篩網面積」如何影響海水淡化取水工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Approach velocity and screen area” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seawater-desalination intake works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"取水口附近流場包含垂直篩面的接近分量及沿篩面的掃流分量，兩者對生物暴露的意義不同。增加有效過水面積可降低平均法向流速，但局部堵塞、潮流與幾何不均仍會產生較高速度；生物保護還取決於物種、生命階段與孔隙尺寸，不能只用平均流速保證無影響。以下面積為有效法向過水面積，尚未換算成外框尺寸或考慮局部不均；假設流速只供計算，不代表任何物種或許可標準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「接近流速與篩網面積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Flow near an intake includes approach velocity normal to the screen and sweeping velocity parallel to it, with different implications for biological exposure. More effective area lowers mean normal velocity, but blockage, currents and uneven geometry can produce local peaks. Protection also depends on species, life stage and opening size, so mean velocity alone cannot prove absence of impact. The area is effective normal flow area, not gross frame dimensions, and local nonuniformity is omitted. The assumed velocity is a calculation input, not a species or permit criterion. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Approach velocity and screen area” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設取水Q=1.20 m³/s、平均法向速度vn=0.12 m/s，所需有效面積Aeff=Q/vn=10.0 m²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume intake Q=1.20 m³/s and mean normal velocity vn=0.12 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「篩網平均流速低就能直接證明所有海洋生物都不受影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Low average screen velocity proves that no marine organisms are affected.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「接近流速與篩網面積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Approach velocity and screen area”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-05-k1","title":"接近流速與篩網面積機理與驗證","titleEn":"Approach velocity and screen area mechanism and verification","text":"取水口附近流場包含垂直篩面的接近分量及沿篩面的掃流分量，兩者對生物暴露的意義不同。增加有效過水面積可降低平均法向流速，但局部堵塞、潮流與幾何不均仍會產生較高速度；生物保護還取決於物種、生命階段與孔隙尺寸，不能只用平均流速保證無影響。","textEn":"Flow near an intake includes approach velocity normal to the screen and sweeping velocity parallel to it, with different implications for biological exposure. More effective area lowers mean normal velocity, but blockage, currents and uneven geometry can produce local peaks.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：篩網平均流速低就能直接證明所有海洋生物都不受影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Low average screen velocity proves that no marine organisms are affected. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接近流速與篩網面積機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Approach velocity and screen area mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["篩網平均流速低就能直接證明所有海洋生物都不受影響。","篩網標示面積可以直接當成任何運轉狀態的有效過水面積。","取水口附近流場包含垂直篩面的接近分量及沿篩面的掃流分量，兩者對生物暴露的意義不同。"],"optionsEn":["Low average screen velocity proves that no marine organisms are affected.","A screen’s labeled area equals effective flow area under every operating condition.","Flow near an intake includes approach velocity normal to the screen and sweeping velocity parallel to it, with different implications for biological exposure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"取水口附近流場包含垂直篩面的接近分量及沿篩面的掃流分量，兩者對生物暴露的意義不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Flow near an intake includes approach velocity normal to the screen and sweeping velocity parallel to it, with different implications for biological exposure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b266-v15-06","title":"接近流速與篩網面積機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Approach velocity and screen area mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「接近流速與篩網面積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Approach velocity and screen area” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設取水Q=1.20 m³/s、平均法向速度vn=0.12 m/s，所需有效面積Aeff=Q/vn=10.0 m²。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume intake Q=1.20 m³/s and mean normal velocity vn=0.12 m/s. Required effective area Aeff=Q/vn=10.0 m². Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以流場量測或核定模型分開法向與沿篩速度，覆蓋不同潮位、海流與部分堵塞情境。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Separate normal and sweeping velocities using field measurements or an approved model across tides, currents and partial blockage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設取水Q=1.20 m³/s、平均法向速度vn=0.12 m/s，所需有效面積Aeff=Q/vn=10.0 m²。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume intake Q=1.20 m³/s and mean normal velocity vn=0.12 m/s. Required effective area Aeff=Q/vn=10.0 m².","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接近流速與篩網面積機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Approach velocity and screen area mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設取水Q=1.20 m³/s、平均法向速度vn=0.12 m/s，所需有效面積Aeff=Q/vn=10.0 m²。","淨正吸入水頭有正餘量就代表入口渦流與捲氣都不存在。","只要提高抽吸就能無限制補償濾床或地下取水層的堵塞。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume intake Q=1.20 m³/s and mean normal velocity vn=0.12 m/s.","A positive NPSH margin proves that intake vortices and entrained air are absent.","Increasing suction can compensate indefinitely for filter or subsurface-intake clogging."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設取水Q=1.20 m³/s、平均法向速度vn=0.12 m/s，所需有效面積Aeff=Q/vn=10.0 m²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume intake Q=1.20 m³/s and mean normal velocity vn=0.12 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b266-v15-07","title":"接近流速與篩網面積機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Approach velocity and screen area mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「接近流速與篩網面積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Approach velocity and screen area” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以流場量測或核定模型分開法向與沿篩速度，覆蓋不同潮位、海流與部分堵塞情境。將有效面積、孔隙及物種調查一起核對，驗證局部峰值而不只比較全篩平均。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Separate normal and sweeping velocities using field measurements or an approved model across tides, currents and partial blockage. Check effective area, openings and biological surveys together, evaluating local peaks rather than only the screen-wide average. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：為同一取水量畫出均勻與局部堵塞兩種速度分布，指出平均值掩蓋的區域。將水理結果與特定物種證據分開列出，再說明兩者如何共同支持設計比較。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw uniform and locally blocked velocity distributions for one flow, identifying regions hidden by the average. Present hydraulic results separately from species evidence and explain how they jointly support design comparison.","failure":"注意干擾：篩網平均速度符合假設時，局部窄縫仍可能形成高速吸入或生物附著區；若把掃流速度誤當接近速度，生物暴露評估會失去正確方向。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Local constrictions can create high-speed entry or impingement even when average velocity matches the assumption. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以流場量測或核定模型分開法向與沿篩速度，覆蓋不同潮位、海流與部分堵塞情境。將有效面積、孔隙及物種調查一起核對，驗證局部峰值而不只比較全篩平均。","textEn":"Separate normal and sweeping velocities using field measurements or an approved model across tides, currents and partial blockage. Check effective area, openings and biological surveys together, evaluating local peaks rather than only the screen-wide average.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"為同一取水量畫出均勻與局部堵塞兩種速度分布，指出平均值掩蓋的區域。將水理結果與特定物種證據分開列出，再說明兩者如何共同支持設計比較。","textEn":"Draw uniform and locally blocked velocity distributions for one flow, identifying regions hidden by the average. Present hydraulic results separately from species evidence and explain how they jointly support design comparison.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接近流速與篩網面積機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Approach velocity and screen area mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以流場量測或核定模型分開法向與沿篩速度，覆蓋不同潮位、海流與部分堵塞情境。","濃度乘取水量算出的生物數就等於已證明的死亡數。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Separate normal and sweeping velocities using field measurements or an approved model across tides, currents and partial blockage.","Concentration times intake volume equals proven biological mortality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以流場量測或核定模型分開法向與沿篩速度，覆蓋不同潮位、海流與部分堵塞情境。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Separate normal and sweeping velocities using field measurements or an approved model across tides, currents and partial blockage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b266-v15-08","title":"接近流速與篩網面積機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Approach velocity and screen area mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「接近流速與篩網面積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Approach velocity and screen area” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"篩網平均速度符合假設時，局部窄縫仍可能形成高速吸入或生物附著區；若把掃流速度誤當接近速度，生物暴露評估會失去正確方向。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Local constrictions can create high-speed entry or impingement even when average velocity matches the assumption. Confusing sweeping with approach velocity removes the directional basis needed for biological-exposure assessment. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以下面積為有效法向過水面積，尚未換算成外框尺寸或考慮局部不均；假設流速只供計算，不代表任何物種或許可標準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The assumed velocity is a calculation input, not a species or permit criterion.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「篩網平均流速低就能直接證明所有海洋生物都不受影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Low average screen velocity proves that no marine organisms are affected.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"篩網平均速度符合假設時，局部窄縫仍可能形成高速吸入或生物附著區；若把掃流速度誤當接近速度，生物暴露評估會失去正確方向。","textEn":"Local constrictions can create high-speed entry or impingement even when average velocity matches the assumption. Confusing sweeping with approach velocity removes the directional basis needed for biological-exposure assessment.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接近流速與篩網面積機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Approach velocity and screen area mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","篩網標示面積可以直接當成任何運轉狀態的有效過水面積。","篩網平均速度符合假設時，局部窄縫仍可能形成高速吸入或生物附著區；若把掃流速度誤當接近速度，生物暴露評估會失去正確方向。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A screen’s labeled area equals effective flow area under every operating condition.","Local constrictions can create high-speed entry or impingement even when average velocity matches the assumption."],"answer":2,"explanation":"篩網平均速度符合假設時，局部窄縫仍可能形成高速吸入或生物附著區；若把掃流速度誤當接近速度，生物暴露評估會失去正確方向。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Local constrictions can create high-speed entry or impingement even when average velocity matches the assumption. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b266-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「孔隙率與堵塞餘量機理與驗證」與「取水損失與局部構件機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Open area and blockage allowance mechanism and verification\" and \"Intake losses and local components mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b266-v15-09","title":"孔隙率與堵塞餘量機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Open area and blockage allowance mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「孔隙率與堵塞餘量」如何影響海水淡化取水工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Open area and blockage allowance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seawater-desalination intake works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"篩網外框面積不等於真正可供水流穿過的面積，構件遮蔽、孔隙率與生物污損會逐層減少開口。清潔時的水力條件只能作起點，運轉後局部沉積可能改變流量分配和清理需求；若所有堵塞都假設均勻，仍可能漏掉小區域的高流速與高壓差。本例將孔隙率與剩餘通暢比例相乘，假設兩者定義不重複；若廠商有效面積已含遮蔽，不可再扣同一項。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「孔隙率與堵塞餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Gross screen area differs from the area actually available to flow. Structural blockage, open-area ratio and biological fouling progressively reduce openings. Clean-screen hydraulics provide only a starting point, since deposits change flow distribution and cleaning demand. Treating all blockage as uniform can still miss localized high velocities and pressure differences. The example multiplies open-area ratio by remaining unblocked fraction, assuming nonoverlapping definitions. If a manufacturer’s effective area already includes an obstruction, it must not be deducted again. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Open area and blockage allowance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設外框A=20 m²、孔隙率φ=0.60、通暢比例β=0.75，Aeff=Aφβ=9.0 m²；Q=1.20 m³/s時vn=0.1333 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gross A=20 m², open-area ratio φ=0.60 and unblocked fraction β=0.75.","failure":"常見誤解：「篩網標示面積可以直接當成任何運轉狀態的有效過水面積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A screen’s labeled area equals effective flow area under every operating condition.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「孔隙率與堵塞餘量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Open area and blockage allowance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-09-k1","title":"孔隙率與堵塞餘量機理與驗證","titleEn":"Open area and blockage allowance mechanism and verification","text":"篩網外框面積不等於真正可供水流穿過的面積，構件遮蔽、孔隙率與生物污損會逐層減少開口。清潔時的水力條件只能作起點，運轉後局部沉積可能改變流量分配和清理需求；若所有堵塞都假設均勻，仍可能漏掉小區域的高流速與高壓差。","textEn":"Gross screen area differs from the area actually available to flow. Structural blockage, open-area ratio and biological fouling progressively reduce openings.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：篩網標示面積可以直接當成任何運轉狀態的有效過水面積。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A screen’s labeled area equals effective flow area under every operating condition. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「孔隙率與堵塞餘量機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Open area and blockage allowance mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["篩網外框面積不等於真正可供水流穿過的面積，構件遮蔽、孔隙率與生物污損會逐層減少開口。","篩網標示面積可以直接當成任何運轉狀態的有效過水面積。","所有局部損失係數都可直接相加而不必核對速度基準。"],"optionsEn":["Gross screen area differs from the area actually available to flow.","A screen’s labeled area equals effective flow area under every operating condition.","All local-loss coefficients can be added without checking their velocity basis."],"answer":0,"explanation":"篩網外框面積不等於真正可供水流穿過的面積，構件遮蔽、孔隙率與生物污損會逐層減少開口。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Gross screen area differs from the area actually available to flow. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b266-v15-10","title":"孔隙率與堵塞餘量機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Open area and blockage allowance mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「孔隙率與堵塞餘量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Open area and blockage allowance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設外框A=20 m²、孔隙率φ=0.60、通暢比例β=0.75，Aeff=Aφβ=9.0 m²；Q=1.20 m³/s時vn=0.1333 m/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gross A=20 m², open-area ratio φ=0.60 and unblocked fraction β=0.75. Aeff=Aφβ=9.0 m²; at Q=1.20 m³/s, vn=0.1333 m/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保存清潔與運轉後的篩面影像、壓差及流量，按位置記錄污損而非只報整體比例。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Retain clean and operating screen images with pressure difference and flow, recording fouling by location rather than only an overall fraction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設外框A=20 m²、孔隙率φ=0.60、通暢比例β=0.75，Aeff=Aφβ=9.0 m²；Q=1.20 m³/s時vn=0.1333 m/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gross A=20 m², open-area ratio φ=0.60 and unblocked fraction β=0.75. Aeff=Aφβ=9.0 m²; at Q=1.20 m³/s, vn=0.1333 m/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「孔隙率與堵塞餘量機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Open area and blockage allowance mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["地下取水只要量到一處高滲透層就能保證全廠長期供水。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設外框A=20 m²、孔隙率φ=0.60、通暢比例β=0.75，Aeff=Aφβ=9.0 m²。","海管永久狀態穩定就代表空管施工或排空維修時也一定穩定。"],"optionsEn":["One highly permeable layer guarantees long-term supply for the whole plant.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gross A=20 m², open-area ratio φ=0.60 and unblocked fraction β=0.75.","Permanent stability guarantees stability during empty-pipe construction or drained maintenance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設外框A=20 m²、孔隙率φ=0.60、通暢比例β=0.75，Aeff=Aφβ=9.0 m²；Q=1.20 m³/s時vn=0.1333 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gross A=20 m², open-area ratio φ=0.60 and unblocked fraction β=0.75. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b266-v15-11","title":"孔隙率與堵塞餘量機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Open area and blockage allowance mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「孔隙率與堵塞餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Open area and blockage allowance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保存清潔與運轉後的篩面影像、壓差及流量，按位置記錄污損而非只報整體比例。檢查有效面積定義是否包含支架與邊框，再用相同定義比較不同設備及清理狀態。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Retain clean and operating screen images with pressure difference and flow, recording fouling by location rather than only an overall fraction. Check whether effective area includes frames and supports, then compare devices and cleaning states using consistent definitions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立由外框到有效開口的面積帳，逐項標示遮蔽與污損。比較相同總堵塞量集中於一角或均勻分布時的驗證需求，避免只用單一剩餘比例代表全部流場。","observationEn":"Site practice: Build an area ledger from gross frame to effective openings, identifying structural and fouling reductions. Compare verification needs for concentrated and uniform blockage with the same total loss, avoiding one fraction as a complete flow-field description.","failure":"注意干擾：重複扣除孔隙或完全忽略框架遮蔽都會算錯流速，均勻堵塞假設則可能高估局部可用面積；堵塞造成的壓差升高還會增加構件受力與泵吸入損失。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Double-counting porosity or ignoring frame obstruction miscalculates velocity, while uniform blockage can overstate local available area. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保存清潔與運轉後的篩面影像、壓差及流量，按位置記錄污損而非只報整體比例。檢查有效面積定義是否包含支架與邊框，再用相同定義比較不同設備及清理狀態。","textEn":"Retain clean and operating screen images with pressure difference and flow, recording fouling by location rather than only an overall fraction. Check whether effective area includes frames and supports, then compare devices and cleaning states using consistent definitions.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立由外框到有效開口的面積帳，逐項標示遮蔽與污損。比較相同總堵塞量集中於一角或均勻分布時的驗證需求，避免只用單一剩餘比例代表全部流場。","textEn":"Build an area ledger from gross frame to effective openings, identifying structural and fouling reductions. Compare verification needs for concentrated and uniform blockage with the same total loss, avoiding one fraction as a complete flow-field description.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「孔隙率與堵塞餘量機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Open area and blockage allowance mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只要取水口與排放口有一定水平距離就絕對不會回流。","保存清潔與運轉後的篩面影像、壓差及流量，按位置記錄污損而非只報整體比例。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A horizontal separation between intake and outfall guarantees no recirculation.","Retain clean and operating screen images with pressure difference and flow, recording fouling by location rather than only an overall fraction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"保存清潔與運轉後的篩面影像、壓差及流量，按位置記錄污損而非只報整體比例。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Retain clean and operating screen images with pressure difference and flow, recording fouling by location rather than only an overall fraction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b266-v15-12","title":"孔隙率與堵塞餘量機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Open area and blockage allowance mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「孔隙率與堵塞餘量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Open area and blockage allowance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"重複扣除孔隙或完全忽略框架遮蔽都會算錯流速，均勻堵塞假設則可能高估局部可用面積；堵塞造成的壓差升高還會增加構件受力與泵吸入損失。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Double-counting porosity or ignoring frame obstruction miscalculates velocity, while uniform blockage can overstate local available area. Increased blockage pressure difference also raises structural loading and suction losses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例將孔隙率與剩餘通暢比例相乘，假設兩者定義不重複；若廠商有效面積已含遮蔽，不可再扣同一項。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If a manufacturer’s effective area already includes an obstruction, it must not be deducted again.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「篩網標示面積可以直接當成任何運轉狀態的有效過水面積。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A screen’s labeled area equals effective flow area under every operating condition.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"重複扣除孔隙或完全忽略框架遮蔽都會算錯流速，均勻堵塞假設則可能高估局部可用面積；堵塞造成的壓差升高還會增加構件受力與泵吸入損失。","textEn":"Double-counting porosity or ignoring frame obstruction miscalculates velocity, while uniform blockage can overstate local available area. Increased blockage pressure difference also raises structural loading and suction losses.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔隙率與堵塞餘量機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Open area and blockage allowance mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["重複扣除孔隙或完全忽略框架遮蔽都會算錯流速，均勻堵塞假設則可能高估局部可用面積；堵塞造成的壓差升高還會增加構件受力與泵吸入損失。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","所有局部損失係數都可直接相加而不必核對速度基準。"],"optionsEn":["Double-counting porosity or ignoring frame obstruction miscalculates velocity, while uniform blockage can overstate local available area.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","All local-loss coefficients can be added without checking their velocity basis."],"answer":0,"explanation":"重複扣除孔隙或完全忽略框架遮蔽都會算錯流速，均勻堵塞假設則可能高估局部可用面積；堵塞造成的壓差升高還會增加構件受力與泵吸入損失。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Double-counting porosity or ignoring frame obstruction miscalculates velocity, while uniform blockage can overstate local available area. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b266-v15-13","title":"取水損失與局部構件機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Intake losses and local components mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「取水損失與局部構件」如何影響海水淡化取水工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Intake losses and local components” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seawater-desalination intake works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"取水頭、彎管、格柵與管徑轉換都會消耗能量，局部損失係數必須對應指定速度截面與幾何。將不同來源的係數直接相加而不核對基準速度，可能造成錯誤揚程；污損與潮流還會改變入流方向，使清潔均勻來流下的係數不再代表長期運轉。本式對單一等效構件使用既定速度，未含沿程摩阻或所有篩網堵塞；損失水頭與靜水深度不可混為同一項。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「取水損失與局部構件」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Intake heads, bends, screens and transitions dissipate energy, and each local-loss coefficient refers to a particular velocity section and geometry. Adding coefficients from different references without checking velocity basis can miscalculate required head. Fouling and currents also change approach direction, so coefficients for clean uniform inflow need not represent long-term operation. The expression uses a specified velocity for one equivalent component, excluding distributed friction and complete screen fouling. Loss head and static submergence are distinct terms. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Intake losses and local components” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設K=2.0、基準速度v=1.5 m/s、g=9.81 m/s²，局部損失hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume K=2.0, reference velocity v=1.5 m/s and g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「所有局部損失係數都可直接相加而不必核對速度基準。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All local-loss coefficients can be added without checking their velocity basis.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「取水損失與局部構件」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Intake losses and local components”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-13-k1","title":"取水損失與局部構件機理與驗證","titleEn":"Intake losses and local components mechanism and verification","text":"取水頭、彎管、格柵與管徑轉換都會消耗能量，局部損失係數必須對應指定速度截面與幾何。將不同來源的係數直接相加而不核對基準速度，可能造成錯誤揚程；污損與潮流還會改變入流方向，使清潔均勻來流下的係數不再代表長期運轉。","textEn":"Intake heads, bends, screens and transitions dissipate energy, and each local-loss coefficient refers to a particular velocity section and geometry. Adding coefficients from different references without checking velocity basis can miscalculate required head.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有局部損失係數都可直接相加而不必核對速度基準。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All local-loss coefficients can be added without checking their velocity basis. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「取水損失與局部構件機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Intake losses and local components mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["所有局部損失係數都可直接相加而不必核對速度基準。","取水頭、彎管、格柵與管徑轉換都會消耗能量，局部損失係數必須對應指定速度截面與幾何。","淨正吸入水頭有正餘量就代表入口渦流與捲氣都不存在。"],"optionsEn":["All local-loss coefficients can be added without checking their velocity basis.","Intake heads, bends, screens and transitions dissipate energy, and each local-loss coefficient refers to a particular velocity section and geometry.","A positive NPSH margin proves that intake vortices and entrained air are absent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"取水頭、彎管、格柵與管徑轉換都會消耗能量，局部損失係數必須對應指定速度截面與幾何。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Intake heads, bends, screens and transitions dissipate energy, and each local-loss coefficient refers to a particular velocity section and geometry. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b266-v15-14","title":"取水損失與局部構件機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Intake losses and local components mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「取水損失與局部構件」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Intake losses and local components” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設K=2.0、基準速度v=1.5 m/s、g=9.81 m/s²，局部損失hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume K=2.0, reference velocity v=1.5 m/s and g=9.81 m/s². Local loss hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把每個損失係數的來源、速度基準與清潔狀態註記在水力帳，核對壓力取樣點的高程差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Annotate coefficient source, velocity basis and cleanliness in the hydraulic ledger and check elevation differences between pressure taps.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設K=2.0、基準速度v=1.5 m/s、g=9.81 m/s²，局部損失hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume K=2.0, reference velocity v=1.5 m/s and g=9.81 m/s². Local loss hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「取水損失與局部構件機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Intake losses and local components mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["只要提高抽吸就能無限制補償濾床或地下取水層的堵塞。","濃度乘取水量算出的生物數就等於已證明的死亡數。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設K=2.0、基準速度v=1.5 m/s、g=9.81 m/s²，局部損失hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing suction can compensate indefinitely for filter or subsurface-intake clogging.","Concentration times intake volume equals proven biological mortality.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume K=2.0, reference velocity v=1.5 m/s and g=9.81 m/s²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設K=2.0、基準速度v=1.5 m/s、g=9.81 m/s²，局部損失hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume K=2.0, reference velocity v=1.5 m/s and g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b266-v15-15","title":"取水損失與局部構件機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Intake losses and local components mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「取水損失與局部構件」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Intake losses and local components” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把每個損失係數的來源、速度基準與清潔狀態註記在水力帳，核對壓力取樣點的高程差。使用可比潮位和流量的量測驗證總損失，再區分局部構件與長管摩阻的貢獻。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Annotate coefficient source, velocity basis and cleanliness in the hydraulic ledger and check elevation differences between pressure taps. Validate total loss at comparable tide and flow, then separate contributions from local components and long-pipe friction. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：為兩個不同管徑構件分別計算速度與損失，再換成同一能量帳比較。增加假設污損後重新檢查吸入端壓力，說明為何損失變化會連到設備性能。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate velocity and loss for two components with different diameters before combining their energy contributions. Add hypothetical fouling and reassess suction pressure, explaining the connection between losses and machine performance.","failure":"注意干擾：使用錯誤截面速度會因平方關係放大壓損偏差，漏計污損則會高估泵吸入裕度；把水深當作可用揚程而不扣損失，也會錯判最低潮工況。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A wrong reference velocity amplifies loss error through its square, while omitted fouling overstates pump suction margin. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把每個損失係數的來源、速度基準與清潔狀態註記在水力帳，核對壓力取樣點的高程差。使用可比潮位和流量的量測驗證總損失，再區分局部構件與長管摩阻的貢獻。","textEn":"Annotate coefficient source, velocity basis and cleanliness in the hydraulic ledger and check elevation differences between pressure taps. Validate total loss at comparable tide and flow, then separate contributions from local components and long-pipe friction.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"為兩個不同管徑構件分別計算速度與損失，再換成同一能量帳比較。增加假設污損後重新檢查吸入端壓力，說明為何損失變化會連到設備性能。","textEn":"Calculate velocity and loss for two components with different diameters before combining their energy contributions. Add hypothetical fouling and reassess suction pressure, explaining the connection between losses and machine performance.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「取水損失與局部構件機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Intake losses and local components mechanism and verification\"?","options":["把每個損失係數的來源、速度基準與清潔狀態註記在水力帳，核對壓力取樣點的高程差。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","淡化廠標示的產品水容量就等於需要的海水取水流量。"],"optionsEn":["Annotate coefficient source, velocity basis and cleanliness in the hydraulic ledger and check elevation differences between pressure taps.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A plant’s stated product capacity equals the required seawater intake flow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把每個損失係數的來源、速度基準與清潔狀態註記在水力帳，核對壓力取樣點的高程差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Annotate coefficient source, velocity basis and cleanliness in the hydraulic ledger and check elevation differences between pressure taps. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b266-v15-16","title":"取水損失與局部構件機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Intake losses and local components mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「取水損失與局部構件」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Intake losses and local components” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"使用錯誤截面速度會因平方關係放大壓損偏差，漏計污損則會高估泵吸入裕度；把水深當作可用揚程而不扣損失，也會錯判最低潮工況。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A wrong reference velocity amplifies loss error through its square, while omitted fouling overstates pump suction margin. Treating water depth as available head without subtracting losses also misrepresents the low-tide condition. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本式對單一等效構件使用既定速度，未含沿程摩阻或所有篩網堵塞；損失水頭與靜水深度不可混為同一項。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Loss head and static submergence are distinct terms.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有局部損失係數都可直接相加而不必核對速度基準。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All local-loss coefficients can be added without checking their velocity basis.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"使用錯誤截面速度會因平方關係放大壓損偏差，漏計污損則會高估泵吸入裕度；把水深當作可用揚程而不扣損失，也會錯判最低潮工況。","textEn":"A wrong reference velocity amplifies loss error through its square, while omitted fouling overstates pump suction margin. Treating water depth as available head without subtracting losses also misrepresents the low-tide condition.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「取水損失與局部構件機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Intake losses and local components mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","使用錯誤截面速度會因平方關係放大壓損偏差，漏計污損則會高估泵吸入裕度；把水深當作可用揚程而不扣損失，也會錯判最低潮工況。","淨正吸入水頭有正餘量就代表入口渦流與捲氣都不存在。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A wrong reference velocity amplifies loss error through its square, while omitted fouling overstates pump suction margin.","A positive NPSH margin proves that intake vortices and entrained air are absent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"使用錯誤截面速度會因平方關係放大壓損偏差，漏計污損則會高估泵吸入裕度；把水深當作可用揚程而不扣損失，也會錯判最低潮工況。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A wrong reference velocity amplifies loss error through its square, while omitted fouling overstates pump suction margin. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b266-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「潮位與泵吸入裕度機理與驗證」與「地下取水與滲透能力機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Tide and pump suction margin mechanism and verification\" and \"Subsurface intake and permeability mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b266-v15-17","title":"潮位與泵吸入裕度機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tide and pump suction margin mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「潮位與泵吸入裕度」如何影響海水淡化取水工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tide and pump suction margin” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seawater-desalination intake works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海潮改變泵入口可用的靜水頭，而吸入管損失、海水溫度與大氣壓共同影響汽蝕裕度。淹水深度足夠也不必然消除入口渦流或不均勻速度，淨正吸入水頭與流場品質應分開驗證；設備要求值還需對應實際流量、轉速及試驗定義，不能只拿一個型錄數字比較。以下各項都已換算為同一海水密度下的水頭，吸入水面高於泵基準取正；比較餘量不是通用汽蝕允收標準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「潮位與泵吸入裕度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Tides change static head available at a pump, while suction losses, seawater temperature and atmospheric pressure affect cavitation margin. Adequate submergence does not necessarily eliminate vortices or uneven velocity, so net positive suction head and intake flow quality require separate checks. Required values must match flow, speed and test definition rather than one catalog number. All terms are expressed as head using the same seawater density, with water surface above the pump datum positive. The calculated margin is not a universal cavitation acceptance criterion. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tide and pump suction margin” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設大氣水頭10.0 m、靜淹水3.0 m、蒸氣壓水頭0.3 m、吸入損失1.5 m，NPSHa=11.2 m；若NPSHr=8.0 m，差3.2 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume atmospheric head 10.0 m, static submergence 3.0 m, vapor head 0.3 m and suction loss 1.5 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「淨正吸入水頭有正餘量就代表入口渦流與捲氣都不存在。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A positive NPSH margin proves that intake vortices and entrained air are absent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「潮位與泵吸入裕度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tide and pump suction margin”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-17-k1","title":"潮位與泵吸入裕度機理與驗證","titleEn":"Tide and pump suction margin mechanism and verification","text":"海潮改變泵入口可用的靜水頭，而吸入管損失、海水溫度與大氣壓共同影響汽蝕裕度。淹水深度足夠也不必然消除入口渦流或不均勻速度，淨正吸入水頭與流場品質應分開驗證；設備要求值還需對應實際流量、轉速及試驗定義，不能只拿一個型錄數字比較。","textEn":"Tides change static head available at a pump, while suction losses, seawater temperature and atmospheric pressure affect cavitation margin. Adequate submergence does not necessarily eliminate vortices or uneven velocity, so net positive suction head and intake flow quality require separate checks.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：淨正吸入水頭有正餘量就代表入口渦流與捲氣都不存在。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A positive NPSH margin proves that intake vortices and entrained air are absent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「潮位與泵吸入裕度機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tide and pump suction margin mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["淨正吸入水頭有正餘量就代表入口渦流與捲氣都不存在。","地下取水只要量到一處高滲透層就能保證全廠長期供水。","海潮改變泵入口可用的靜水頭，而吸入管損失、海水溫度與大氣壓共同影響汽蝕裕度。"],"optionsEn":["A positive NPSH margin proves that intake vortices and entrained air are absent.","One highly permeable layer guarantees long-term supply for the whole plant.","Tides change static head available at a pump, while suction losses, seawater temperature and atmospheric pressure affect cavitation margin."],"answer":2,"explanation":"海潮改變泵入口可用的靜水頭，而吸入管損失、海水溫度與大氣壓共同影響汽蝕裕度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Tides change static head available at a pump, while suction losses, seawater temperature and atmospheric pressure affect cavitation margin. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b266-v15-18","title":"潮位與泵吸入裕度機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Tide and pump suction margin mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「潮位與泵吸入裕度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tide and pump suction margin” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設大氣水頭10.0 m、靜淹水3.0 m、蒸氣壓水頭0.3 m、吸入損失1.5 m，NPSHa=11.2 m；若NPSHr=8.0 m，差3.2 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume atmospheric head 10.0 m, static submergence 3.0 m, vapor head 0.3 m and suction loss 1.5 m. NPSHa=11.2 m; compared with NPSHr=8.0 m, the difference is 3.2 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以低潮、高溫及代表流量組合核對吸入水頭，將泵基準、壓力取樣與密度換算記錄完整。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check suction head for low tide, high temperature and representative flows, documenting pump datum, pressure taps and density conversion.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設大氣水頭10.0 m、靜淹水3.0 m、蒸氣壓水頭0.3 m、吸入損失1.5 m，NPSHa=11.2 m；若NPSHr=8.0 m，差3.2 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume atmospheric head 10.0 m, static submergence 3.0 m, vapor head 0.3 m and suction loss 1.5 m. NPSHa=11.2 m; compared with NPSHr=8.0 m, the difference is 3.2 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「潮位與泵吸入裕度機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tide and pump suction margin mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設大氣水頭10.0 m、靜淹水3.0 m、蒸氣壓水頭0.3 m、吸入損失1.5 m，NPSHa=11.2 m。","海管永久狀態穩定就代表空管施工或排空維修時也一定穩定。","只要取水口與排放口有一定水平距離就絕對不會回流。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume atmospheric head 10.0 m, static submergence 3.0 m, vapor head 0.3 m and suction loss 1.5 m.","Permanent stability guarantees stability during empty-pipe construction or drained maintenance.","A horizontal separation between intake and outfall guarantees no recirculation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設大氣水頭10.0 m、靜淹水3.0 m、蒸氣壓水頭0.3 m、吸入損失1.5 m，NPSHa=11.2 m；若NPSHr=8.0 m，差3.2 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume atmospheric head 10.0 m, static submergence 3.0 m, vapor head 0.3 m and suction loss 1.5 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b266-v15-19","title":"潮位與泵吸入裕度機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tide and pump suction margin mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「潮位與泵吸入裕度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tide and pump suction margin” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以低潮、高溫及代表流量組合核對吸入水頭，將泵基準、壓力取樣與密度換算記錄完整。另用流場量測或模型查渦流和速度不均，避免把單一NPSH差值當成整體入口品質。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check suction head for low tide, high temperature and representative flows, documenting pump datum, pressure taps and density conversion. Independently assess vortices and velocity distortion through measurements or modeling instead of treating one NPSH difference as complete intake quality. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把高潮與低潮兩個情境畫在同一泵基準上，分別扣除損失及蒸氣壓。將汽蝕水頭與渦流證據分列，說明需要哪種量測才能判斷各自問題。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw high- and low-tide cases against one pump datum and subtract losses and vapor head separately. Keep cavitation-head and vortex evidence distinct, identifying measurements capable of addressing each issue.","failure":"注意干擾：將海水水頭與淡水水頭混用會帶入換算偏差，未考慮最低潮則可能高估可用裕度；入口渦流捲氣也可能在名目NPSH尚足夠時損害性能。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mixing seawater and freshwater head introduces conversion bias, and omitting low tide can overstate available margin. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以低潮、高溫及代表流量組合核對吸入水頭，將泵基準、壓力取樣與密度換算記錄完整。另用流場量測或模型查渦流和速度不均，避免把單一NPSH差值當成整體入口品質。","textEn":"Check suction head for low tide, high temperature and representative flows, documenting pump datum, pressure taps and density conversion. Independently assess vortices and velocity distortion through measurements or modeling instead of treating one NPSH difference as complete intake quality.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把高潮與低潮兩個情境畫在同一泵基準上，分別扣除損失及蒸氣壓。將汽蝕水頭與渦流證據分列，說明需要哪種量測才能判斷各自問題。","textEn":"Draw high- and low-tide cases against one pump datum and subtract losses and vapor head separately. Keep cavitation-head and vortex evidence distinct, identifying measurements capable of addressing each issue.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「潮位與泵吸入裕度機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tide and pump suction margin mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以低潮、高溫及代表流量組合核對吸入水頭，將泵基準、壓力取樣與密度換算記錄完整。","篩網平均流速低就能直接證明所有海洋生物都不受影響。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check suction head for low tide, high temperature and representative flows, documenting pump datum, pressure taps and density conversion.","Low average screen velocity proves that no marine organisms are affected."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以低潮、高溫及代表流量組合核對吸入水頭，將泵基準、壓力取樣與密度換算記錄完整。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check suction head for low tide, high temperature and representative flows, documenting pump datum, pressure taps and density conversion. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b266-v15-20","title":"潮位與泵吸入裕度機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tide and pump suction margin mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「潮位與泵吸入裕度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tide and pump suction margin” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將海水水頭與淡水水頭混用會帶入換算偏差，未考慮最低潮則可能高估可用裕度；入口渦流捲氣也可能在名目NPSH尚足夠時損害性能。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mixing seawater and freshwater head introduces conversion bias, and omitting low tide can overstate available margin. Air entrainment from intake vortices can also impair performance while nominal NPSH appears adequate. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以下各項都已換算為同一海水密度下的水頭，吸入水面高於泵基準取正；比較餘量不是通用汽蝕允收標準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The calculated margin is not a universal cavitation acceptance criterion.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「淨正吸入水頭有正餘量就代表入口渦流與捲氣都不存在。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A positive NPSH margin proves that intake vortices and entrained air are absent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將海水水頭與淡水水頭混用會帶入換算偏差，未考慮最低潮則可能高估可用裕度；入口渦流捲氣也可能在名目NPSH尚足夠時損害性能。","textEn":"Mixing seawater and freshwater head introduces conversion bias, and omitting low tide can overstate available margin. Air entrainment from intake vortices can also impair performance while nominal NPSH appears adequate.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「潮位與泵吸入裕度機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tide and pump suction margin mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","地下取水只要量到一處高滲透層就能保證全廠長期供水。","將海水水頭與淡水水頭混用會帶入換算偏差，未考慮最低潮則可能高估可用裕度；入口渦流捲氣也可能在名目NPSH尚足夠時損害性能。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","One highly permeable layer guarantees long-term supply for the whole plant.","Mixing seawater and freshwater head introduces conversion bias, and omitting low tide can overstate available margin."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將海水水頭與淡水水頭混用會帶入換算偏差，未考慮最低潮則可能高估可用裕度；入口渦流捲氣也可能在名目NPSH尚足夠時損害性能。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mixing seawater and freshwater head introduces conversion bias, and omitting low tide can overstate available margin. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b266-v15-21","title":"地下取水與滲透能力機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Subsurface intake and permeability mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「地下取水與滲透能力」如何影響海水淡化取水工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Subsurface intake and permeability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seawater-desalination intake works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海床或岸邊地下取水藉地層傳輸海水，可能改變懸浮物及生物進入方式，但可用流量受滲透性、厚度、補注邊界與水質反應控制。單一鑽孔的高滲透層不能代表整個集水範圍，長期抽水還可能造成堵塞或改變混合水源；可行性必須由現地試驗與水文地質模型共同建立。達西算例假設均質飽和介質與一維穩定流，不表示任何海岸都可提供相同產能，也沒有估計水質或生態效益。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「地下取水與滲透能力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Subsurface intakes transmit seawater through sediment and can change suspended-solid and organism entry, but yield depends on permeability, thickness, recharge boundaries and geochemical reactions. One permeable borehole interval cannot represent the entire collection area. Long-term pumping can cause clogging or alter source mixing, so feasibility needs field testing together with a hydrogeological model. The Darcy example assumes homogeneous saturated material and steady one-dimensional flow. It does not imply equal yield at every coast or quantify quality and ecological benefits. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Subsurface intake and permeability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設k=5×10⁻⁴ m/s、截面A=300 m²、水力坡降i=0.10，Q=kAi=0.0150 m³/s，為理想介質比較。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume k=5×10⁻⁴ m/s, section A=300 m² and hydraulic gradient i=0.10.","failure":"常見誤解：「地下取水只要量到一處高滲透層就能保證全廠長期供水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One highly permeable layer guarantees long-term supply for the whole plant.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「地下取水與滲透能力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Subsurface intake and permeability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-21-k1","title":"地下取水與滲透能力機理與驗證","titleEn":"Subsurface intake and permeability mechanism and verification","text":"海床或岸邊地下取水藉地層傳輸海水，可能改變懸浮物及生物進入方式，但可用流量受滲透性、厚度、補注邊界與水質反應控制。單一鑽孔的高滲透層不能代表整個集水範圍，長期抽水還可能造成堵塞或改變混合水源；可行性必須由現地試驗與水文地質模型共同建立。","textEn":"Subsurface intakes transmit seawater through sediment and can change suspended-solid and organism entry, but yield depends on permeability, thickness, recharge boundaries and geochemical reactions. One permeable borehole interval cannot represent the entire collection area.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：地下取水只要量到一處高滲透層就能保證全廠長期供水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One highly permeable layer guarantees long-term supply for the whole plant. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地下取水與滲透能力機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Subsurface intake and permeability mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["海床或岸邊地下取水藉地層傳輸海水，可能改變懸浮物及生物進入方式，但可用流量受滲透性、厚度、補注邊界與水質反應控制。","地下取水只要量到一處高滲透層就能保證全廠長期供水。","只要提高抽吸就能無限制補償濾床或地下取水層的堵塞。"],"optionsEn":["Subsurface intakes transmit seawater through sediment and can change suspended-solid and organism entry, but yield depends on permeability, thickness, recharge boundaries and geochemical reactions.","One highly permeable layer guarantees long-term supply for the whole plant.","Increasing suction can compensate indefinitely for filter or subsurface-intake clogging."],"answer":0,"explanation":"海床或岸邊地下取水藉地層傳輸海水，可能改變懸浮物及生物進入方式，但可用流量受滲透性、厚度、補注邊界與水質反應控制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Subsurface intakes transmit seawater through sediment and can change suspended-solid and organism entry, but yield depends on permeability, thickness, recharge boundaries and geochemical reactions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b266-v15-22","title":"地下取水與滲透能力機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Subsurface intake and permeability mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「地下取水與滲透能力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Subsurface intake and permeability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設k=5×10⁻⁴ m/s、截面A=300 m²、水力坡降i=0.10，Q=kAi=0.0150 m³/s，為理想介質比較。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume k=5×10⁻⁴ m/s, section A=300 m² and hydraulic gradient i=0.10. Q=kAi=0.0150 m³/s for an idealized medium. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以分層調查、抽水試驗及潮位反應建立滲透與邊界範圍，將進水水質和長期流量衰減一起觀察。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Establish permeability and boundary ranges from stratified investigation, pumping tests and tidal response, observing water quality with long-term yield decline.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設k=5×10⁻⁴ m/s、截面A=300 m²、水力坡降i=0.10，Q=kAi=0.0150 m³/s，為理想介質比較。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume k=5×10⁻⁴ m/s, section A=300 m² and hydraulic gradient i=0.10. Q=kAi=0.0150 m³/s for an idealized medium.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地下取水與滲透能力機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Subsurface intake and permeability mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["濃度乘取水量算出的生物數就等於已證明的死亡數。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設k=5×10⁻⁴ m/s、截面A=300 m²、水力坡降i=0.10，Q=kAi=0.0150 m³/s，為理想介質比較。","淡化廠標示的產品水容量就等於需要的海水取水流量。"],"optionsEn":["Concentration times intake volume equals proven biological mortality.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume k=5×10⁻⁴ m/s, section A=300 m² and hydraulic gradient i=0.10.","A plant’s stated product capacity equals the required seawater intake flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設k=5×10⁻⁴ m/s、截面A=300 m²、水力坡降i=0.10，Q=kAi=0.0150 m³/s，為理想介質比較。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume k=5×10⁻⁴ m/s, section A=300 m² and hydraulic gradient i=0.10. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b266-v15-23","title":"地下取水與滲透能力機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Subsurface intake and permeability mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「地下取水與滲透能力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Subsurface intake and permeability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以分層調查、抽水試驗及潮位反應建立滲透與邊界範圍，將進水水質和長期流量衰減一起觀察。比較多種地下取水配置，並連同主管機關對研究限制的說明閱讀可行性資料。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Establish permeability and boundary ranges from stratified investigation, pumping tests and tidal response, observing water quality with long-term yield decline. Compare several subsurface configurations and read feasibility material together with agency statements about study limitations. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出均質地層與夾細層地層兩種概念模型，指出達西截面和流徑可能如何改變。為每個模型列出可推翻它的抽水或潮位觀察，再討論調查優先順序。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw homogeneous and fine-layered conceptual models, showing changes in Darcy area and flow path. Identify pumping or tidal observations that could falsify each model and use them to prioritize investigation.","failure":"注意干擾：只以短期高流量試驗外推長期產能可能忽略堵塞或補注不足，遇到細層連續阻隔時更會高估集水範圍；把技術比較報告當唯一許可依據也會混淆研究與審查。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Extrapolating short high-yield tests can miss clogging or limited recharge, and continuous fine layers can further shrink the collection area. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以分層調查、抽水試驗及潮位反應建立滲透與邊界範圍，將進水水質和長期流量衰減一起觀察。比較多種地下取水配置，並連同主管機關對研究限制的說明閱讀可行性資料。","textEn":"Establish permeability and boundary ranges from stratified investigation, pumping tests and tidal response, observing water quality with long-term yield decline. Compare several subsurface configurations and read feasibility material together with agency statements about study limitations.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出均質地層與夾細層地層兩種概念模型，指出達西截面和流徑可能如何改變。為每個模型列出可推翻它的抽水或潮位觀察，再討論調查優先順序。","textEn":"Draw homogeneous and fine-layered conceptual models, showing changes in Darcy area and flow path. Identify pumping or tidal observations that could falsify each model and use them to prioritize investigation.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地下取水與滲透能力機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Subsurface intake and permeability mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","篩網標示面積可以直接當成任何運轉狀態的有效過水面積。","以分層調查、抽水試驗及潮位反應建立滲透與邊界範圍，將進水水質和長期流量衰減一起觀察。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A screen’s labeled area equals effective flow area under every operating condition.","Establish permeability and boundary ranges from stratified investigation, pumping tests and tidal response, observing water quality with long-term yield decline."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以分層調查、抽水試驗及潮位反應建立滲透與邊界範圍，將進水水質和長期流量衰減一起觀察。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Establish permeability and boundary ranges from stratified investigation, pumping tests and tidal response, observing water quality with long-term yield decline. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b266-v15-24","title":"地下取水與滲透能力機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Subsurface intake and permeability mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「地下取水與滲透能力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Subsurface intake and permeability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只以短期高流量試驗外推長期產能可能忽略堵塞或補注不足，遇到細層連續阻隔時更會高估集水範圍；把技術比較報告當唯一許可依據也會混淆研究與審查。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Extrapolating short high-yield tests can miss clogging or limited recharge, and continuous fine layers can further shrink the collection area. Treating a comparison report as the sole permitting basis also confuses research with regulatory evaluation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：達西算例假設均質飽和介質與一維穩定流，不表示任何海岸都可提供相同產能，也沒有估計水質或生態效益。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It does not imply equal yield at every coast or quantify quality and ecological benefits.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「地下取水只要量到一處高滲透層就能保證全廠長期供水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One highly permeable layer guarantees long-term supply for the whole plant.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只以短期高流量試驗外推長期產能可能忽略堵塞或補注不足，遇到細層連續阻隔時更會高估集水範圍；把技術比較報告當唯一許可依據也會混淆研究與審查。","textEn":"Extrapolating short high-yield tests can miss clogging or limited recharge, and continuous fine layers can further shrink the collection area. Treating a comparison report as the sole permitting basis also confuses research with regulatory evaluation.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地下取水與滲透能力機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Subsurface intake and permeability mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只以短期高流量試驗外推長期產能可能忽略堵塞或補注不足，遇到細層連續阻隔時更會高估集水範圍；把技術比較報告當唯一許可依據也會混淆研究與審查。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","只要提高抽吸就能無限制補償濾床或地下取水層的堵塞。"],"optionsEn":["Extrapolating short high-yield tests can miss clogging or limited recharge, and continuous fine layers can further shrink the collection area.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Increasing suction can compensate indefinitely for filter or subsurface-intake clogging."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只以短期高流量試驗外推長期產能可能忽略堵塞或補注不足，遇到細層連續阻隔時更會高估集水範圍；把技術比較報告當唯一許可依據也會混淆研究與審查。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Extrapolating short high-yield tests can miss clogging or limited recharge, and continuous fine layers can further shrink the collection area. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b266-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「堵塞演變與水頭損失機理與驗證」與「海管浮力與施工狀態機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Clogging evolution and head loss mechanism and verification\" and \"Marine-pipe buoyancy and construction state mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b266-v15-25","title":"堵塞演變與水頭損失機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Clogging evolution and head loss mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「堵塞演變與水頭損失」如何影響海水淡化取水工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Clogging evolution and head loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seawater-desalination intake works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"地下集水層或濾床的堵塞會改變有效滲透性，維持相同流量時可能需要更大水頭差。沉積、微生物與化學沉澱不一定以相同位置或速率發生，因此整體流量下降無法唯一辨認堵塞機制；應把水頭分布、顆粒與水化學共同追蹤，避免只增加抽吸來補償性能衰退。本式包含實際假設流徑長度，計算的是水頭差而不是無量綱坡降；介質均質且流量固定的條件不可省略。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「堵塞演變與水頭損失」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Clogging in collection sediments or filters changes effective permeability, requiring greater head difference to maintain flow. Deposition, biological growth and precipitation need not occur at the same location or rate, so declining yield cannot uniquely identify the mechanism. Track head distribution, particles and chemistry together rather than compensating for deterioration only by increasing suction. The expression includes the assumed flow-path length and calculates head difference rather than dimensionless gradient. Homogeneous material and fixed-flow assumptions are essential. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Clogging evolution and head loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=0.020 m³/s、L=2 m、k=1×10⁻⁴ m/s、A=100 m²，Δh=QL/(kA)=4.0 m；k減半時需8.0 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=0.020 m³/s, L=2 m, k=1×10⁻⁴ m/s and A=100 m². Δh=QL/(kA)=4.0 m; halving k requires 8.0 m at the same flow.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要提高抽吸就能無限制補償濾床或地下取水層的堵塞。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Increasing suction can compensate indefinitely for filter or subsurface-intake clogging.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「堵塞演變與水頭損失」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Clogging evolution and head loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-25-k1","title":"堵塞演變與水頭損失機理與驗證","titleEn":"Clogging evolution and head loss mechanism and verification","text":"地下集水層或濾床的堵塞會改變有效滲透性，維持相同流量時可能需要更大水頭差。沉積、微生物與化學沉澱不一定以相同位置或速率發生，因此整體流量下降無法唯一辨認堵塞機制；應把水頭分布、顆粒與水化學共同追蹤，避免只增加抽吸來補償性能衰退。","textEn":"Clogging in collection sediments or filters changes effective permeability, requiring greater head difference to maintain flow. Deposition, biological growth and precipitation need not occur at the same location or rate, so declining yield cannot uniquely identify the mechanism.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要提高抽吸就能無限制補償濾床或地下取水層的堵塞。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Increasing suction can compensate indefinitely for filter or subsurface-intake clogging. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「堵塞演變與水頭損失機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Clogging evolution and head loss mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["只要提高抽吸就能無限制補償濾床或地下取水層的堵塞。","地下集水層或濾床的堵塞會改變有效滲透性，維持相同流量時可能需要更大水頭差。","海管永久狀態穩定就代表空管施工或排空維修時也一定穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing suction can compensate indefinitely for filter or subsurface-intake clogging.","Clogging in collection sediments or filters changes effective permeability, requiring greater head difference to maintain flow.","Permanent stability guarantees stability during empty-pipe construction or drained maintenance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"地下集水層或濾床的堵塞會改變有效滲透性，維持相同流量時可能需要更大水頭差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Clogging in collection sediments or filters changes effective permeability, requiring greater head difference to maintain flow. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b266-v15-26","title":"堵塞演變與水頭損失機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Clogging evolution and head loss mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「堵塞演變與水頭損失」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Clogging evolution and head loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=0.020 m³/s、L=2 m、k=1×10⁻⁴ m/s、A=100 m²，Δh=QL/(kA)=4.0 m；k減半時需8.0 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=0.020 m³/s, L=2 m, k=1×10⁻⁴ m/s and A=100 m². Δh=QL/(kA)=4.0 m; halving k requires 8.0 m at the same flow. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿集水路徑量測水頭與流量，定期比較顆粒、化學及生物指標，將清理事件與恢復效果對時。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure head and flow along the collection path and periodically compare particle, chemical and biological indicators, aligning cleaning events with recovery.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=0.020 m³/s、L=2 m、k=1×10⁻⁴ m/s、A=100 m²，Δh=QL/(kA)=4.0 m；k減半時需8.0 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=0.020 m³/s, L=2 m, k=1×10⁻⁴ m/s and A=100 m². Δh=QL/(kA)=4.0 m; halving k requires 8.0 m at the same flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「堵塞演變與水頭損失機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Clogging evolution and head loss mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["只要取水口與排放口有一定水平距離就絕對不會回流。","篩網平均流速低就能直接證明所有海洋生物都不受影響。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=0.020 m³/s、L=2 m、k=1×10⁻⁴ m/s、A=100 m²，Δh=QL/(kA)=4.0 m。"],"optionsEn":["A horizontal separation between intake and outfall guarantees no recirculation.","Low average screen velocity proves that no marine organisms are affected.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=0.020 m³/s, L=2 m, k=1×10⁻⁴ m/s and A=100 m². Δh=QL/(kA)=4.0 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=0.020 m³/s、L=2 m、k=1×10⁻⁴ m/s、A=100 m²，Δh=QL/(kA)=4.0 m；k減半時需8.0 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=0.020 m³/s, L=2 m, k=1×10⁻⁴ m/s and A=100 m². Δh=QL/(kA)=4.0 m; halving k requires 8.0 m at the same flow. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b266-v15-27","title":"堵塞演變與水頭損失機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Clogging evolution and head loss mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「堵塞演變與水頭損失」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Clogging evolution and head loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿集水路徑量測水頭與流量，定期比較顆粒、化學及生物指標，將清理事件與恢復效果對時。用局部水頭變化辨認堵塞區，避免只由總壓差推斷全層均勻劣化。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure head and flow along the collection path and periodically compare particle, chemical and biological indicators, aligning cleaning events with recovery. Use local head changes to identify clogged zones rather than inferring uniform deterioration from the total pressure difference. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在固定流量下比較原始與減半滲透性的水頭需求，再畫出集中堵塞與均勻堵塞的可能水頭線。選擇可區分兩者的中間量測點，避免只追蹤出口流量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare head demand at original and halved permeability under fixed flow, then draw possible profiles for concentrated and uniform clogging. Select intermediate sensors that distinguish them instead of monitoring outlet flow alone.","failure":"注意干擾：提高抽吸維持流量可能讓局部梯度和細粒移動增加，卻掩蓋滲透性持續下降；若壓力測點只設在兩端，集中堵塞的位置也可能一直無法辨識。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Increasing suction to hold flow can raise local gradients and fines movement while concealing continuing permeability loss. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿集水路徑量測水頭與流量，定期比較顆粒、化學及生物指標，將清理事件與恢復效果對時。用局部水頭變化辨認堵塞區，避免只由總壓差推斷全層均勻劣化。","textEn":"Measure head and flow along the collection path and periodically compare particle, chemical and biological indicators, aligning cleaning events with recovery. Use local head changes to identify clogged zones rather than inferring uniform deterioration from the total pressure difference.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在固定流量下比較原始與減半滲透性的水頭需求，再畫出集中堵塞與均勻堵塞的可能水頭線。選擇可區分兩者的中間量測點，避免只追蹤出口流量。","textEn":"Compare head demand at original and halved permeability under fixed flow, then draw possible profiles for concentrated and uniform clogging. Select intermediate sensors that distinguish them instead of monitoring outlet flow alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「堵塞演變與水頭損失機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Clogging evolution and head loss mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿集水路徑量測水頭與流量，定期比較顆粒、化學及生物指標，將清理事件與恢復效果對時。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","所有局部損失係數都可直接相加而不必核對速度基準。"],"optionsEn":["Measure head and flow along the collection path and periodically compare particle, chemical and biological indicators, aligning cleaning events with recovery.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","All local-loss coefficients can be added without checking their velocity basis."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沿集水路徑量測水頭與流量，定期比較顆粒、化學及生物指標，將清理事件與恢復效果對時。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure head and flow along the collection path and periodically compare particle, chemical and biological indicators, aligning cleaning events with recovery. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b266-v15-28","title":"堵塞演變與水頭損失機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Clogging evolution and head loss mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「堵塞演變與水頭損失」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Clogging evolution and head loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"提高抽吸維持流量可能讓局部梯度和細粒移動增加，卻掩蓋滲透性持續下降；若壓力測點只設在兩端，集中堵塞的位置也可能一直無法辨識。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Increasing suction to hold flow can raise local gradients and fines movement while concealing continuing permeability loss. With pressure measurements only at both ends, the location of concentrated clogging may remain unidentified. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本式包含實際假設流徑長度，計算的是水頭差而不是無量綱坡降；介質均質且流量固定的條件不可省略。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Homogeneous material and fixed-flow assumptions are essential.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要提高抽吸就能無限制補償濾床或地下取水層的堵塞。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Increasing suction can compensate indefinitely for filter or subsurface-intake clogging.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"提高抽吸維持流量可能讓局部梯度和細粒移動增加，卻掩蓋滲透性持續下降；若壓力測點只設在兩端，集中堵塞的位置也可能一直無法辨識。","textEn":"Increasing suction to hold flow can raise local gradients and fines movement while concealing continuing permeability loss. With pressure measurements only at both ends, the location of concentrated clogging may remain unidentified.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「堵塞演變與水頭損失機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Clogging evolution and head loss mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","提高抽吸維持流量可能讓局部梯度和細粒移動增加，卻掩蓋滲透性持續下降；若壓力測點只設在兩端，集中堵塞的位置也可能一直無法辨識。","海管永久狀態穩定就代表空管施工或排空維修時也一定穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Increasing suction to hold flow can raise local gradients and fines movement while concealing continuing permeability loss.","Permanent stability guarantees stability during empty-pipe construction or drained maintenance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"提高抽吸維持流量可能讓局部梯度和細粒移動增加，卻掩蓋滲透性持續下降；若壓力測點只設在兩端，集中堵塞的位置也可能一直無法辨識。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Increasing suction to hold flow can raise local gradients and fines movement while concealing continuing permeability loss. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b266-v15-29","title":"海管浮力與施工狀態機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Marine-pipe buoyancy and construction state mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「海管浮力與施工狀態」如何影響海水淡化取水工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Marine-pipe buoyancy and construction state” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seawater-desalination intake works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海底管線在空管、充水與覆土後具有不同的淨重，浮力按排開海水體積計算而不是只看管材重量。施工階段尚未完成壓重或回填時可能最不利，波流作用又會同時增加滑動與抬升需求；因此永久穩定模型不能直接替代安裝、試驗或排空維護的階段模型。本例為一米長、外徑圓管的靜水浮力，假設空管且未計壓重；不含波流動力、土體吸附或海床接觸抗力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「海管浮力與施工狀態」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A submarine pipe has different net weight when empty, flooded and buried. Buoyancy follows displaced seawater volume rather than pipe-material weight alone. Installation before ballast or cover may govern, while waves and currents add sliding and uplift demands. Permanent stability therefore cannot replace separate installation, testing or drained-maintenance models. This is static buoyancy for a one-metre circular outside diameter, assuming an empty unballasted pipe. Wave/current forces, soil suction and seabed resistance are excluded. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Marine-pipe buoyancy and construction state” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設外徑D=1.20 m、海水單位重γ=10.055 kN/m³、空管重w=6.0 kN/m，淨上浮u=γπD²/4−w=5.372 kN/m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume outside D=1.20 m, seawater unit weight γ=10.055 kN/m³ and empty-pipe weight w=6.0 kN/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「海管永久狀態穩定就代表空管施工或排空維修時也一定穩定。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Permanent stability guarantees stability during empty-pipe construction or drained maintenance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「海管浮力與施工狀態」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Marine-pipe buoyancy and construction state”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-29-k1","title":"海管浮力與施工狀態機理與驗證","titleEn":"Marine-pipe buoyancy and construction state mechanism and verification","text":"海底管線在空管、充水與覆土後具有不同的淨重，浮力按排開海水體積計算而不是只看管材重量。施工階段尚未完成壓重或回填時可能最不利，波流作用又會同時增加滑動與抬升需求；因此永久穩定模型不能直接替代安裝、試驗或排空維護的階段模型。","textEn":"A submarine pipe has different net weight when empty, flooded and buried. Buoyancy follows displaced seawater volume rather than pipe-material weight alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：海管永久狀態穩定就代表空管施工或排空維修時也一定穩定。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Permanent stability guarantees stability during empty-pipe construction or drained maintenance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「海管浮力與施工狀態機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Marine-pipe buoyancy and construction state mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["海管永久狀態穩定就代表空管施工或排空維修時也一定穩定。","濃度乘取水量算出的生物數就等於已證明的死亡數。","海底管線在空管、充水與覆土後具有不同的淨重，浮力按排開海水體積計算而不是只看管材重量。"],"optionsEn":["Permanent stability guarantees stability during empty-pipe construction or drained maintenance.","Concentration times intake volume equals proven biological mortality.","A submarine pipe has different net weight when empty, flooded and buried."],"answer":2,"explanation":"海底管線在空管、充水與覆土後具有不同的淨重，浮力按排開海水體積計算而不是只看管材重量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A submarine pipe has different net weight when empty, flooded and buried. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b266-v15-30","title":"海管浮力與施工狀態機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Marine-pipe buoyancy and construction state mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「海管浮力與施工狀態」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Marine-pipe buoyancy and construction state” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設外徑D=1.20 m、海水單位重γ=10.055 kN/m³、空管重w=6.0 kN/m，淨上浮u=γπD²/4−w=5.372 kN/m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume outside D=1.20 m, seawater unit weight γ=10.055 kN/m³ and empty-pipe weight w=6.0 kN/m. Net uplift u=γπD²/4−w=5.372 kN/m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：為各施工階段核對充水狀態、壓重配置與外徑，將單位長度重量和海床接觸範圍列入同一帳。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify flooding state, ballast and outside diameter for every construction stage, recording unit weight with seabed contact.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設外徑D=1.20 m、海水單位重γ=10.055 kN/m³、空管重w=6.0 kN/m，淨上浮u=γπD²/4−w=5.372 kN/m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume outside D=1.20 m, seawater unit weight γ=10.055 kN/m³ and empty-pipe weight w=6.0 kN/m. Net uplift u=γπD²/4−w=5.372 kN/m.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「海管浮力與施工狀態機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Marine-pipe buoyancy and construction state mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設外徑D=1.20 m、海水單位重γ=10.055 kN/m³、空管重w=6.0 kN/m，淨上浮u=γπD²/4−w=5.372 kN/m。","淡化廠標示的產品水容量就等於需要的海水取水流量。","篩網標示面積可以直接當成任何運轉狀態的有效過水面積。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume outside D=1.20 m, seawater unit weight γ=10.055 kN/m³ and empty-pipe weight w=6.0 kN/m.","A plant’s stated product capacity equals the required seawater intake flow.","A screen’s labeled area equals effective flow area under every operating condition."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設外徑D=1.20 m、海水單位重γ=10.055 kN/m³、空管重w=6.0 kN/m，淨上浮u=γπD²/4−w=5.372 kN/m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume outside D=1.20 m, seawater unit weight γ=10.055 kN/m³ and empty-pipe weight w=6.0 kN/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b266-v15-31","title":"海管浮力與施工狀態機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Marine-pipe buoyancy and construction state mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「海管浮力與施工狀態」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Marine-pipe buoyancy and construction state” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"為各施工階段核對充水狀態、壓重配置與外徑，將單位長度重量和海床接觸範圍列入同一帳。另依核定海事條件檢查波流作用與支承，避免靜態重量比通過就跳過階段穩定。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify flooding state, ballast and outside diameter for every construction stage, recording unit weight with seabed contact. Independently assess wave/current actions and support under approved marine conditions rather than skipping staged stability after a static weight-ratio check. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將空管、充水與覆土三個狀態的重量和浮力逐項列出，指出哪些項目會變。把淨垂向力與抗滑、接頭及動態問題分開，建立分階段驗證表。","observationEn":"Site practice: List weight and buoyancy for empty, flooded and buried states, identifying changing terms. Separate net vertical force from sliding, joint and dynamic issues in a staged verification table.","failure":"注意干擾：把永久覆土重量提早計入尚未回填的管段會低估上浮，排空維修時若忘記扣除內水重也可能使既有穩定判斷失效；局部浮起還會改變接頭彎曲。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Crediting permanent cover before placement understates uplift, and forgetting the loss of internal water weight during draining invalidates stability assumptions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"為各施工階段核對充水狀態、壓重配置與外徑，將單位長度重量和海床接觸範圍列入同一帳。另依核定海事條件檢查波流作用與支承，避免靜態重量比通過就跳過階段穩定。","textEn":"Verify flooding state, ballast and outside diameter for every construction stage, recording unit weight with seabed contact. Independently assess wave/current actions and support under approved marine conditions rather than skipping staged stability after a static weight-ratio check.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將空管、充水與覆土三個狀態的重量和浮力逐項列出，指出哪些項目會變。把淨垂向力與抗滑、接頭及動態問題分開，建立分階段驗證表。","textEn":"List weight and buoyancy for empty, flooded and buried states, identifying changing terms. Separate net vertical force from sliding, joint and dynamic issues in a staged verification table.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「海管浮力與施工狀態機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Marine-pipe buoyancy and construction state mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","為各施工階段核對充水狀態、壓重配置與外徑，將單位長度重量和海床接觸範圍列入同一帳。","淨正吸入水頭有正餘量就代表入口渦流與捲氣都不存在。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Verify flooding state, ballast and outside diameter for every construction stage, recording unit weight with seabed contact.","A positive NPSH margin proves that intake vortices and entrained air are absent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"為各施工階段核對充水狀態、壓重配置與外徑，將單位長度重量和海床接觸範圍列入同一帳。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify flooding state, ballast and outside diameter for every construction stage, recording unit weight with seabed contact. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b266-v15-32","title":"海管浮力與施工狀態機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Marine-pipe buoyancy and construction state mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「海管浮力與施工狀態」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Marine-pipe buoyancy and construction state” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把永久覆土重量提早計入尚未回填的管段會低估上浮，排空維修時若忘記扣除內水重也可能使既有穩定判斷失效；局部浮起還會改變接頭彎曲。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Crediting permanent cover before placement understates uplift, and forgetting the loss of internal water weight during draining invalidates stability assumptions. Local lift-off also changes joint bending demands. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例為一米長、外徑圓管的靜水浮力，假設空管且未計壓重；不含波流動力、土體吸附或海床接觸抗力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Wave/current forces, soil suction and seabed resistance are excluded.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「海管永久狀態穩定就代表空管施工或排空維修時也一定穩定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Permanent stability guarantees stability during empty-pipe construction or drained maintenance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把永久覆土重量提早計入尚未回填的管段會低估上浮，排空維修時若忘記扣除內水重也可能使既有穩定判斷失效；局部浮起還會改變接頭彎曲。","textEn":"Crediting permanent cover before placement understates uplift, and forgetting the loss of internal water weight during draining invalidates stability assumptions. Local lift-off also changes joint bending demands.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「海管浮力與施工狀態機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Marine-pipe buoyancy and construction state mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","濃度乘取水量算出的生物數就等於已證明的死亡數。","把永久覆土重量提早計入尚未回填的管段會低估上浮，排空維修時若忘記扣除內水重也可能使既有穩定判斷失效；局部浮起還會改變接頭彎曲。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Concentration times intake volume equals proven biological mortality.","Crediting permanent cover before placement understates uplift, and forgetting the loss of internal water weight during draining invalidates stability assumptions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把永久覆土重量提早計入尚未回填的管段會低估上浮，排空維修時若忘記扣除內水重也可能使既有穩定判斷失效；局部浮起還會改變接頭彎曲。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Crediting permanent cover before placement understates uplift, and forgetting the loss of internal water weight during draining invalidates stability assumptions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b266-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「生物暴露與取樣代表性機理與驗證」與「排放回流與取水水質機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Biological exposure and sampling representation mechanism and verification\" and \"Outfall recirculation and intake quality mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b266-v15-33","title":"生物暴露與取樣代表性機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Biological exposure and sampling representation mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「生物暴露與取樣代表性」如何影響海水淡化取水工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Biological exposure and sampling representation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seawater-desalination intake works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"取水可能使生物撞擊篩面或隨水進入系統，兩種途徑的體型、生命階段與評估方法不同。濃度乘取水量可估接觸或輸送數量，但死亡率、避讓與季節分布須另有證據；短期平均樣本若漏掉繁殖季或潮汐高峰，可能低估真正暴露，不能用單次低濃度宣稱影響微小。此算例假設濃度及流量在時段內均勻，得到的是潛在通過數量而非死亡數；實際需考慮空間分布與取樣效率。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「生物暴露與取樣代表性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Organisms may be impinged on screens or entrained into the system, with different sizes, life stages and assessment methods. Concentration times intake volume estimates encounter or transport count, while mortality, avoidance and seasonal distribution need separate evidence. Short mean samples can miss spawning or tidal peaks, so one low concentration cannot establish negligible impact. The example assumes uniform concentration and flow over the interval and gives potential passage count rather than mortality. Spatial distribution and sampling efficiency remain separate. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Biological exposure and sampling representation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設生物濃度C=2 individuals/m³、Q=1.0 m³/s、Δt=600 s，潛在通過數N=CQΔt=1200 individuals，未乘死亡比例。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume organism concentration C=2 individuals/m³, Q=1.0 m³/s and Δt=600 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「濃度乘取水量算出的生物數就等於已證明的死亡數。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Concentration times intake volume equals proven biological mortality.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「生物暴露與取樣代表性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Biological exposure and sampling representation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-33-k1","title":"生物暴露與取樣代表性機理與驗證","titleEn":"Biological exposure and sampling representation mechanism and verification","text":"取水可能使生物撞擊篩面或隨水進入系統，兩種途徑的體型、生命階段與評估方法不同。濃度乘取水量可估接觸或輸送數量，但死亡率、避讓與季節分布須另有證據；短期平均樣本若漏掉繁殖季或潮汐高峰，可能低估真正暴露，不能用單次低濃度宣稱影響微小。","textEn":"Organisms may be impinged on screens or entrained into the system, with different sizes, life stages and assessment methods. Concentration times intake volume estimates encounter or transport count, while mortality, avoidance and seasonal distribution need separate evidence.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：濃度乘取水量算出的生物數就等於已證明的死亡數。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Concentration times intake volume equals proven biological mortality. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「生物暴露與取樣代表性機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Biological exposure and sampling representation mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["取水可能使生物撞擊篩面或隨水進入系統，兩種途徑的體型、生命階段與評估方法不同。","濃度乘取水量算出的生物數就等於已證明的死亡數。","只要取水口與排放口有一定水平距離就絕對不會回流。"],"optionsEn":["Organisms may be impinged on screens or entrained into the system, with different sizes, life stages and assessment methods.","Concentration times intake volume equals proven biological mortality.","A horizontal separation between intake and outfall guarantees no recirculation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"取水可能使生物撞擊篩面或隨水進入系統，兩種途徑的體型、生命階段與評估方法不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Organisms may be impinged on screens or entrained into the system, with different sizes, life stages and assessment methods. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b266-v15-34","title":"生物暴露與取樣代表性機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Biological exposure and sampling representation mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「生物暴露與取樣代表性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Biological exposure and sampling representation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設生物濃度C=2 individuals/m³、Q=1.0 m³/s、Δt=600 s，潛在通過數N=CQΔt=1200 individuals，未乘死亡比例。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume organism concentration C=2 individuals/m³, Q=1.0 m³/s and Δt=600 s. Potential count N=CQΔt=1200 individuals, with no mortality fraction applied. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按物種與生命階段規劃季節、潮汐及深度取樣，核對網具或感測方法的捕獲效率。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plan sampling by species and life stage across seasons, tides and depths, checking capture efficiency of nets or sensors.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設生物濃度C=2 individuals/m³、Q=1.0 m³/s、Δt=600 s，潛在通過數N=CQΔt=1200 individuals，未乘死亡比例。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume organism concentration C=2 individuals/m³, Q=1.0 m³/s and Δt=600 s. Potential count N=CQΔt=1200 individuals, with no mortality fraction applied.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「生物暴露與取樣代表性機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Biological exposure and sampling representation mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["篩網平均流速低就能直接證明所有海洋生物都不受影響。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設生物濃度C=2 individuals/m³、Q=1.0 m³/s、Δt=600 s，潛在通過數N=CQΔt=1200 individuals，未乘死亡比例。","所有局部損失係數都可直接相加而不必核對速度基準。"],"optionsEn":["Low average screen velocity proves that no marine organisms are affected.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume organism concentration C=2 individuals/m³, Q=1.0 m³/s and Δt=600 s.","All local-loss coefficients can be added without checking their velocity basis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設生物濃度C=2 individuals/m³、Q=1.0 m³/s、Δt=600 s，潛在通過數N=CQΔt=1200 individuals，未乘死亡比例。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume organism concentration C=2 individuals/m³, Q=1.0 m³/s and Δt=600 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b266-v15-35","title":"生物暴露與取樣代表性機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Biological exposure and sampling representation mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「生物暴露與取樣代表性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Biological exposure and sampling representation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按物種與生命階段規劃季節、潮汐及深度取樣，核對網具或感測方法的捕獲效率。將暴露估計、存活資料與背景變動分開報告，對未觀測季節保留不確定性而非補成零。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plan sampling by species and life stage across seasons, tides and depths, checking capture efficiency of nets or sensors. Report exposure, survival evidence and background variability separately, retaining uncertainty for unobserved periods instead of replacing them with zero. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把暴露量、受傷率與存活率畫成不同資料欄位，說明何時可以及不可以相乘。以兩個季節的假設濃度比較結果，指出長期評估需要的代表性樣本。","observationEn":"Site practice: Separate exposure, injury and survival into distinct data fields, explaining when multiplication is justified. Compare hypothetical concentrations in two seasons and identify representative sampling needed for long-term assessment.","failure":"注意干擾：把潛在通過數直接稱為死亡數會混淆機制，反之以篩網擋住大魚便推定幼生也受保護則會漏掉不同尺度風險；不完整取樣可讓兩種錯誤同時存在。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Calling potential passage count mortality confuses mechanisms, while protection of large fish does not demonstrate protection of larvae. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按物種與生命階段規劃季節、潮汐及深度取樣，核對網具或感測方法的捕獲效率。將暴露估計、存活資料與背景變動分開報告，對未觀測季節保留不確定性而非補成零。","textEn":"Plan sampling by species and life stage across seasons, tides and depths, checking capture efficiency of nets or sensors. Report exposure, survival evidence and background variability separately, retaining uncertainty for unobserved periods instead of replacing them with zero.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把暴露量、受傷率與存活率畫成不同資料欄位，說明何時可以及不可以相乘。以兩個季節的假設濃度比較結果，指出長期評估需要的代表性樣本。","textEn":"Separate exposure, injury and survival into distinct data fields, explaining when multiplication is justified. Compare hypothetical concentrations in two seasons and identify representative sampling needed for long-term assessment.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「生物暴露與取樣代表性機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Biological exposure and sampling representation mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","地下取水只要量到一處高滲透層就能保證全廠長期供水。","按物種與生命階段規劃季節、潮汐及深度取樣，核對網具或感測方法的捕獲效率。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","One highly permeable layer guarantees long-term supply for the whole plant.","Plan sampling by species and life stage across seasons, tides and depths, checking capture efficiency of nets or sensors."],"answer":2,"explanation":"按物種與生命階段規劃季節、潮汐及深度取樣，核對網具或感測方法的捕獲效率。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plan sampling by species and life stage across seasons, tides and depths, checking capture efficiency of nets or sensors. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b266-v15-36","title":"生物暴露與取樣代表性機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Biological exposure and sampling representation mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「生物暴露與取樣代表性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Biological exposure and sampling representation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把潛在通過數直接稱為死亡數會混淆機制，反之以篩網擋住大魚便推定幼生也受保護則會漏掉不同尺度風險；不完整取樣可讓兩種錯誤同時存在。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Calling potential passage count mortality confuses mechanisms, while protection of large fish does not demonstrate protection of larvae. Incomplete sampling can allow both errors to persist simultaneously. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：此算例假設濃度及流量在時段內均勻，得到的是潛在通過數量而非死亡數；實際需考慮空間分布與取樣效率。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Spatial distribution and sampling efficiency remain separate.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「濃度乘取水量算出的生物數就等於已證明的死亡數。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Concentration times intake volume equals proven biological mortality.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把潛在通過數直接稱為死亡數會混淆機制，反之以篩網擋住大魚便推定幼生也受保護則會漏掉不同尺度風險；不完整取樣可讓兩種錯誤同時存在。","textEn":"Calling potential passage count mortality confuses mechanisms, while protection of large fish does not demonstrate protection of larvae. Incomplete sampling can allow both errors to persist simultaneously.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「生物暴露與取樣代表性機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Biological exposure and sampling representation mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把潛在通過數直接稱為死亡數會混淆機制，反之以篩網擋住大魚便推定幼生也受保護則會漏掉不同尺度風險；不完整取樣可讓兩種錯誤同時存在。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要取水口與排放口有一定水平距離就絕對不會回流。"],"optionsEn":["Calling potential passage count mortality confuses mechanisms, while protection of large fish does not demonstrate protection of larvae.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A horizontal separation between intake and outfall guarantees no recirculation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把潛在通過數直接稱為死亡數會混淆機制，反之以篩網擋住大魚便推定幼生也受保護則會漏掉不同尺度風險；不完整取樣可讓兩種錯誤同時存在。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Calling potential passage count mortality confuses mechanisms, while protection of large fish does not demonstrate protection of larvae. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b266-v15-37","title":"排放回流與取水水質機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Outfall recirculation and intake quality mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「排放回流與取水水質」如何影響海水淡化取水工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Outfall recirculation and intake quality” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seawater-desalination intake works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"取水與排放位置不能各自孤立設計，濃鹽水在潮流轉向、弱流或密度流條件下可能重新進入取水區。回流會提高進水鹽度並改變膜系統能耗及濃水條件，形成系統回饋；只看兩管水平距離不足以判定獨立，需把三維水深、分層及季節水動力一起分析。此例以質量分率混合兩股海水，鹽度用g/kg，沒有混用體積分率；它不預測實際回流比例，該比例需由水動力及現場資料決定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「排放回流與取水水質」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Intake and outfall cannot be designed independently: brine can return toward the intake during current reversal, weak flow or density-driven transport. Recirculation raises feed salinity and changes membrane energy and concentrate conditions, creating feedback. Horizontal separation alone cannot prove independence; three-dimensional bathymetry, stratification and seasonal hydrodynamics must be assessed together. The example mixes two streams by mass fraction with salinity in g/kg, not volume fraction. It does not predict actual recirculation, which requires hydrodynamic and field evidence. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Outfall recirculation and intake quality” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設背景鹽度S0=35 g/kg、回流水Sr=45 g/kg、回流質量分率f=0.10，Sint=(1−f)S0+fSr=36.0 g/kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume background S0=35 g/kg, returning water Sr=45 g/kg and returning mass fraction f=0.10.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要取水口與排放口有一定水平距離就絕對不會回流。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A horizontal separation between intake and outfall guarantees no recirculation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「排放回流與取水水質」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Outfall recirculation and intake quality”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-37-k1","title":"排放回流與取水水質機理與驗證","titleEn":"Outfall recirculation and intake quality mechanism and verification","text":"取水與排放位置不能各自孤立設計，濃鹽水在潮流轉向、弱流或密度流條件下可能重新進入取水區。回流會提高進水鹽度並改變膜系統能耗及濃水條件，形成系統回饋；只看兩管水平距離不足以判定獨立，需把三維水深、分層及季節水動力一起分析。","textEn":"Intake and outfall cannot be designed independently: brine can return toward the intake during current reversal, weak flow or density-driven transport. Recirculation raises feed salinity and changes membrane energy and concentrate conditions, creating feedback.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要取水口與排放口有一定水平距離就絕對不會回流。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A horizontal separation between intake and outfall guarantees no recirculation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「排放回流與取水水質機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Outfall recirculation and intake quality mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["只要取水口與排放口有一定水平距離就絕對不會回流。","取水與排放位置不能各自孤立設計，濃鹽水在潮流轉向、弱流或密度流條件下可能重新進入取水區。","淡化廠標示的產品水容量就等於需要的海水取水流量。"],"optionsEn":["A horizontal separation between intake and outfall guarantees no recirculation.","Intake and outfall cannot be designed independently: brine can return toward the intake during current reversal, weak flow or density-driven transport.","A plant’s stated product capacity equals the required seawater intake flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"取水與排放位置不能各自孤立設計，濃鹽水在潮流轉向、弱流或密度流條件下可能重新進入取水區。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Intake and outfall cannot be designed independently: brine can return toward the intake during current reversal, weak flow or density-driven transport. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b266-v15-38","title":"排放回流與取水水質機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Outfall recirculation and intake quality mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「排放回流與取水水質」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Outfall recirculation and intake quality” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設背景鹽度S0=35 g/kg、回流水Sr=45 g/kg、回流質量分率f=0.10，Sint=(1−f)S0+fSr=36.0 g/kg。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume background S0=35 g/kg, returning water Sr=45 g/kg and returning mass fraction f=0.10. Sint=(1−f)S0+fSr=36.0 g/kg. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將取排水鹽度、溫度與海流剖面同步量測，涵蓋潮流反轉及低交換時段。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronize intake/outfall salinity and temperature with current profiles, covering reversals and weak exchange.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設背景鹽度S0=35 g/kg、回流水Sr=45 g/kg、回流質量分率f=0.10，Sint=(1−f)S0+fSr=36.0 g/kg。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume background S0=35 g/kg, returning water Sr=45 g/kg and returning mass fraction f=0.10. Sint=(1−f)S0+fSr=36.0 g/kg.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「排放回流與取水水質機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Outfall recirculation and intake quality mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["篩網標示面積可以直接當成任何運轉狀態的有效過水面積。","淨正吸入水頭有正餘量就代表入口渦流與捲氣都不存在。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設背景鹽度S0=35 g/kg、回流水Sr=45 g/kg、回流質量分率f=0.10，Sint=(1−f)S0+fSr=36.0 g/kg。"],"optionsEn":["A screen’s labeled area equals effective flow area under every operating condition.","A positive NPSH margin proves that intake vortices and entrained air are absent.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume background S0=35 g/kg, returning water Sr=45 g/kg and returning mass fraction f=0.10."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設背景鹽度S0=35 g/kg、回流水Sr=45 g/kg、回流質量分率f=0.10，Sint=(1−f)S0+fSr=36.0 g/kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume background S0=35 g/kg, returning water Sr=45 g/kg and returning mass fraction f=0.10. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b266-v15-39","title":"排放回流與取水水質機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Outfall recirculation and intake quality mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「排放回流與取水水質」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Outfall recirculation and intake quality” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將取排水鹽度、溫度與海流剖面同步量測，涵蓋潮流反轉及低交換時段。比較適用的近場與遠場模型，保留背景鹽度變化，避免把所有進水升鹽都歸因於本廠排放。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronize intake/outfall salinity and temperature with current profiles, covering reversals and weak exchange. Compare suitable near- and far-field models while retaining natural background variation rather than attributing every feed-salinity increase to the plant’s discharge. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用兩個假設回流質量分率比較進水鹽度，再指出為何需另解潮流與密度輸送。設計上游背景與取水點的同步比較，避免以受影響水體充當未受影響基線。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare feed salinity at two assumed returning mass fractions and explain why tidal and density transport still need separate solution. Design synchronized background and intake observations without using affected water as an unaffected baseline.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略回流可能低估膜進水負荷與排放濃度，若又以升高後的取水鹽度當自然背景，會把排放造成的長期增加藏進基線，形成自我合理化的比較。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring recirculation can understate feed loading and discharge salinity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將取排水鹽度、溫度與海流剖面同步量測，涵蓋潮流反轉及低交換時段。比較適用的近場與遠場模型，保留背景鹽度變化，避免把所有進水升鹽都歸因於本廠排放。","textEn":"Synchronize intake/outfall salinity and temperature with current profiles, covering reversals and weak exchange. Compare suitable near- and far-field models while retaining natural background variation rather than attributing every feed-salinity increase to the plant’s discharge.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用兩個假設回流質量分率比較進水鹽度，再指出為何需另解潮流與密度輸送。設計上游背景與取水點的同步比較，避免以受影響水體充當未受影響基線。","textEn":"Compare feed salinity at two assumed returning mass fractions and explain why tidal and density transport still need separate solution. Design synchronized background and intake observations without using affected water as an unaffected baseline.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「排放回流與取水水質機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Outfall recirculation and intake quality mechanism and verification\"?","options":["將取排水鹽度、溫度與海流剖面同步量測，涵蓋潮流反轉及低交換時段。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要提高抽吸就能無限制補償濾床或地下取水層的堵塞。"],"optionsEn":["Synchronize intake/outfall salinity and temperature with current profiles, covering reversals and weak exchange.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Increasing suction can compensate indefinitely for filter or subsurface-intake clogging."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將取排水鹽度、溫度與海流剖面同步量測，涵蓋潮流反轉及低交換時段。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronize intake/outfall salinity and temperature with current profiles, covering reversals and weak exchange. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b266-v15-40","title":"排放回流與取水水質機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Outfall recirculation and intake quality mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b266-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「排放回流與取水水質」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Outfall recirculation and intake quality” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略回流可能低估膜進水負荷與排放濃度，若又以升高後的取水鹽度當自然背景，會把排放造成的長期增加藏進基線，形成自我合理化的比較。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring recirculation can understate feed loading and discharge salinity. If the elevated intake salinity is then treated as natural background, long-term discharge effects are hidden inside the baseline and appear self-justifying. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：此例以質量分率混合兩股海水，鹽度用g/kg，沒有混用體積分率；它不預測實際回流比例，該比例需由水動力及現場資料決定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It does not predict actual recirculation, which requires hydrodynamic and field evidence.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要取水口與排放口有一定水平距離就絕對不會回流。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A horizontal separation between intake and outfall guarantees no recirculation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b266-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略回流可能低估膜進水負荷與排放濃度，若又以升高後的取水鹽度當自然背景，會把排放造成的長期增加藏進基線，形成自我合理化的比較。","textEn":"Ignoring recirculation can understate feed loading and discharge salinity. If the elevated intake salinity is then treated as natural background, long-term discharge effects are hidden inside the baseline and appear self-justifying.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b266-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「排放回流與取水水質機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Outfall recirculation and intake quality mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","忽略回流可能低估膜進水負荷與排放濃度，若又以升高後的取水鹽度當自然背景，會把排放造成的長期增加藏進基線，形成自我合理化的比較。","淡化廠標示的產品水容量就等於需要的海水取水流量。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Ignoring recirculation can understate feed loading and discharge salinity.","A plant’s stated product capacity equals the required seawater intake flow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"忽略回流可能低估膜進水負荷與排放濃度，若又以升高後的取水鹽度當自然背景，會把排放造成的長期增加藏進基線，形成自我合理化的比較。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring recirculation can understate feed loading and discharge salinity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-cal-desal","v15s-cal-ssi-memo","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b267","title":"海水淡化鹵水擴散排放","titleEn":"Brine diffuser outfalls for desalination","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課逐步拆解膜段鹽量、背景稀釋、孔口流速、密度差、噴流動量與海域交換，建立可檢核的鹵水擴散分析鏈。近場、遠場和長期箱體各有控制體與適用邊界，必須分別驗證後才銜接；全部算例為原創假設，並非實廠排放或許可限值。","summaryEn":"This course develops a checkable brine-analysis chain through membrane salt balance, background dilution, port velocity, density contrast, jet momentum and receiving-basin exchange. Near-field, far-field and long-term box models have distinct control volumes and validity limits that require separate verification before coupling. All calculations use original assumptions, not plant discharge measurements or permit limits.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-pipe","architectureNodes":[["鹽量帳","Salt balance"],["孔口動量","Port momentum"],["負浮力近場","Dense near field"],["海域交換","Basin exchange"],["監測驗證","Monitoring verification"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]],"diagram":{"type":"water-pipe","labels":["鹽量帳","孔口動量","負浮力近場","海域交換","監測驗證"],"labelsEn":["Salt balance","Port momentum","Dense near field","Basin exchange","Monitoring verification"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"敏感度算例固定單孔流量q=0.050 m³/s及縮減重力g′=0.15 m/s²，只將孔徑由0.20 m增加至0.22 m。面平均噴速由1.5915降至1.3153 m/s，降低17.36%；密度福祿數由9.1888降至7.2407，降低21.20%，因固定流量時速度隨孔徑平方反比而變，福祿數隨孔徑的二點五次方反比。這只比較初始尺度，沒有把福祿數當成稀釋倍數，也沒有預測海床接觸點。實際比較還需幹管壓力、角度、潮流和多孔交互作用，不能只依孔徑變大就宣稱環境改善。","textEn":"For sensitivity, hold one-port flow q=0.050 m³/s and reduced gravity g′=0.15 m/s² fixed while increasing diameter from 0.20 to 0.22 m. Mean exit velocity falls from 1.5915 to 1.3153 m/s, a 17.36% reduction. Densimetric Froude number falls from 9.1888 to 7.2407, a 21.20% reduction: velocity varies as diameter to the power −2 and Froude number as diameter to the power −2.5 at fixed flow. These are initial-scale comparisons, not dilution predictions or seabed-contact locations. Header pressure, discharge angle, tidal currents, seabed clearance and multiport interaction remain necessary before judging environmental performance. The calculation does not establish an ecological threshold or discharge approval.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b267-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「濃縮鹽量守恆機理與驗證」與「背景鹽度與稀釋定義機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Concentrate salt conservation mechanism and verification\" and \"Background salinity and dilution mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b267-v15-01","title":"濃縮鹽量守恆機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Concentrate salt conservation mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「濃縮鹽量守恆」如何影響海水淡化鹵水擴散排放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Concentrate salt conservation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brine diffuser outfalls for desalination”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"淡化膜將進流水分配成產品與濃水，鹽分不會因水量減少而消失。若用質量鹽度表示濃度，必須同時使用質量流率，並保留產品水殘餘鹽分；以體積流量近似時則須明說密度差的處理。濃水濃度不只決定排口鹽負荷，也會改變密度、浮力與混合路徑，不能把產水效率與海域影響分開看待。本例固定進水質量流率並假設產品完全不含鹽，只作理想守恆；真實產品鹽分、藥劑與其他支流需要另外計入。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「濃縮鹽量守恆」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A membrane separates feed into product and concentrate without making dissolved salt disappear. Mass-based salinity requires mass flow rates and retention of residual product salt. A volume-flow approximation must state how density differences are treated. Concentrate salinity affects salt loading, density, buoyancy and mixing trajectory, linking recovery decisions to the receiving environment. This ideal balance fixes feed mass flow and assumes salt-free product. Actual product salt, chemical additions and side streams require separate accounting. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Concentrate salt conservation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設進水mf=1000 kg/s、產品mp=400 kg/s、進水鹽度Sf=35 g/kg且Sp=0，mb=600 kg/s，Sb=mfSf/mb=58.33 g/kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume feed mf=1000 kg/s, product mp=400 kg/s, feed Sf=35 g/kg and product Sp=0.","failure":"常見誤解：「提高產水回收率會讓剩下濃水中的總鹽量自行消失。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Higher water recovery makes the remaining concentrate salt disappear.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「濃縮鹽量守恆」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Concentrate salt conservation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-01-k1","title":"濃縮鹽量守恆機理與驗證","titleEn":"Concentrate salt conservation mechanism and verification","text":"淡化膜將進流水分配成產品與濃水，鹽分不會因水量減少而消失。若用質量鹽度表示濃度，必須同時使用質量流率，並保留產品水殘餘鹽分；以體積流量近似時則須明說密度差的處理。","textEn":"A membrane separates feed into product and concentrate without making dissolved salt disappear. Mass-based salinity requires mass flow rates and retention of residual product salt.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：提高產水回收率會讓剩下濃水中的總鹽量自行消失。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Higher water recovery makes the remaining concentrate salt disappear. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「濃縮鹽量守恆機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Concentrate salt conservation mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["提高產水回收率會讓剩下濃水中的總鹽量自行消失。","淡化膜將進流水分配成產品與濃水，鹽分不會因水量減少而消失。","海水鹵水稀釋十倍就是把原始總鹽度直接除以十。"],"optionsEn":["Higher water recovery makes the remaining concentrate salt disappear.","A membrane separates feed into product and concentrate without making dissolved salt disappear.","Tenfold seawater-brine dilution means dividing total original salinity by ten."],"answer":1,"explanation":"淡化膜將進流水分配成產品與濃水，鹽分不會因水量減少而消失。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A membrane separates feed into product and concentrate without making dissolved salt disappear. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b267-v15-02","title":"濃縮鹽量守恆機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Concentrate salt conservation mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「濃縮鹽量守恆」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Concentrate salt conservation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設進水mf=1000 kg/s、產品mp=400 kg/s、進水鹽度Sf=35 g/kg且Sp=0，mb=600 kg/s，Sb=mfSf/mb=58.33 g/kg。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume feed mf=1000 kg/s, product mp=400 kg/s, feed Sf=35 g/kg and product Sp=0. Concentrate mb=600 kg/s and Sb=mfSf/mb=58.33 g/kg. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將各股流的流率、密度與鹽度同步量測，統一為質量鹽通量後檢查收支。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure stream flow, density and salinity synchronously, convert them to salt mass flux and check closure.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設進水mf=1000 kg/s、產品mp=400 kg/s、進水鹽度Sf=35 g/kg且Sp=0，mb=600 kg/s，Sb=mfSf/mb=58.33 g/kg。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume feed mf=1000 kg/s, product mp=400 kg/s, feed Sf=35 g/kg and product Sp=0. Concentrate mb=600 kg/s and Sb=mfSf/mb=58.33 g/kg.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「濃縮鹽量守恆機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Concentrate salt conservation mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["只要鹽度較高，就可忽略溫度並沿用所有上浮羽流公式。","流量乘速度已經是牛頓力，而且所有噴口反力只須加大小。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設進水mf=1000 kg/s、產品mp=400 kg/s、進水鹽度Sf=35 g/kg且Sp=0，mb=600 kg/s，Sb=mfSf/mb=58.33 g/kg。"],"optionsEn":["Higher salinity allows temperature to be ignored and all rising-plume formulas reused.","Flow times velocity is already force in newtons and port reactions require only scalar addition.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume feed mf=1000 kg/s, product mp=400 kg/s, feed Sf=35 g/kg and product Sp=0."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設進水mf=1000 kg/s、產品mp=400 kg/s、進水鹽度Sf=35 g/kg且Sp=0，mb=600 kg/s，Sb=mfSf/mb=58.33 g/kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume feed mf=1000 kg/s, product mp=400 kg/s, feed Sf=35 g/kg and product Sp=0. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b267-v15-03","title":"濃縮鹽量守恆機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Concentrate salt conservation mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「濃縮鹽量守恆」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Concentrate salt conservation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將各股流的流率、密度與鹽度同步量測，統一為質量鹽通量後檢查收支。保留儀表校正與預處理支流資料，確認未把不同時間的最大流量與最高鹽度拼成不存在的工況。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure stream flow, density and salinity synchronously, convert them to salt mass flux and check closure. Retain calibration and pretreatment-stream records, ensuring that maxima from different times are not combined into a physically nonexistent operating state. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出三股質量流及鹽通量，先用理想零產品鹽度求解，再加入假設殘餘鹽分。說明哪些流量計資料必須搭配密度才能維持相同守恆基準。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw the three mass and salt flows, solve first with salt-free product, then introduce residual product salinity. Explain which flow-meter data require density to maintain a consistent conservation basis.","failure":"注意干擾：用質量鹽度直接乘不一致的體積流率會引入密度誤差，忽略產品與排泥鹽分則使收支失真；錯誤的濃度輸入還會傳到負浮力羽流模型。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Multiplying mass salinity by inconsistent volume flow introduces density error, while omitted product or sludge salt distorts closure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將各股流的流率、密度與鹽度同步量測，統一為質量鹽通量後檢查收支。保留儀表校正與預處理支流資料，確認未把不同時間的最大流量與最高鹽度拼成不存在的工況。","textEn":"Measure stream flow, density and salinity synchronously, convert them to salt mass flux and check closure. Retain calibration and pretreatment-stream records, ensuring that maxima from different times are not combined into a physically nonexistent operating state.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出三股質量流及鹽通量，先用理想零產品鹽度求解，再加入假設殘餘鹽分。說明哪些流量計資料必須搭配密度才能維持相同守恆基準。","textEn":"Draw the three mass and salt flows, solve first with salt-free product, then introduce residual product salinity. Explain which flow-meter data require density to maintain a consistent conservation basis.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「濃縮鹽量守恆機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Concentrate salt conservation mechanism and verification\"?","options":["將各股流的流率、密度與鹽度同步量測，統一為質量鹽通量後檢查收支。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","海流速度乘一小時得到的距離，就是鹵水必然被稀釋完的位置。"],"optionsEn":["Measure stream flow, density and salinity synchronously, convert them to salt mass flux and check closure.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Current speed times one hour gives the distance at which brine is necessarily fully diluted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將各股流的流率、密度與鹽度同步量測，統一為質量鹽通量後檢查收支。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure stream flow, density and salinity synchronously, convert them to salt mass flux and check closure. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b267-v15-04","title":"濃縮鹽量守恆機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Concentrate salt conservation mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「濃縮鹽量守恆」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Concentrate salt conservation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用質量鹽度直接乘不一致的體積流率會引入密度誤差，忽略產品與排泥鹽分則使收支失真；錯誤的濃度輸入還會傳到負浮力羽流模型。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Multiplying mass salinity by inconsistent volume flow introduces density error, while omitted product or sludge salt distorts closure. Incorrect concentrate inputs then propagate into the negatively buoyant plume model. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例固定進水質量流率並假設產品完全不含鹽，只作理想守恆；真實產品鹽分、藥劑與其他支流需要另外計入。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Actual product salt, chemical additions and side streams require separate accounting.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「提高產水回收率會讓剩下濃水中的總鹽量自行消失。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher water recovery makes the remaining concentrate salt disappear.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用質量鹽度直接乘不一致的體積流率會引入密度誤差，忽略產品與排泥鹽分則使收支失真；錯誤的濃度輸入還會傳到負浮力羽流模型。","textEn":"Multiplying mass salinity by inconsistent volume flow introduces density error, while omitted product or sludge salt distorts closure. Incorrect concentrate inputs then propagate into the negatively buoyant plume model.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「濃縮鹽量守恆機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Concentrate salt conservation mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","用質量鹽度直接乘不一致的體積流率會引入密度誤差，忽略產品與排泥鹽分則使收支失真；錯誤的濃度輸入還會傳到負浮力羽流模型。","海水鹵水稀釋十倍就是把原始總鹽度直接除以十。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Multiplying mass salinity by inconsistent volume flow introduces density error, while omitted product or sludge salt distorts closure.","Tenfold seawater-brine dilution means dividing total original salinity by ten."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用質量鹽度直接乘不一致的體積流率會引入密度誤差，忽略產品與排泥鹽分則使收支失真；錯誤的濃度輸入還會傳到負浮力羽流模型。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Multiplying mass salinity by inconsistent volume flow introduces density error, while omitted product or sludge salt distorts closure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b267-v15-05","title":"背景鹽度與稀釋定義機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Background salinity and dilution mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「背景鹽度與稀釋定義」如何影響海水淡化鹵水擴散排放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Background salinity and dilution” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brine diffuser outfalls for desalination”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海水本身含鹽，因此稀釋應追蹤相對於背景的鹽度增量，而不是把環境當成無鹽水。以質量流率定義的混合倍數等於混合後總質量流率除以原排放質量流率，對應超額濃度的衰減；中心線、截面平均與通量平均值可能不同，報告中必須明確指明所比較的量。本例為完全混合的質量鹽度守恆，不預測達到該混合倍數的位置，也不把它當作許可或生態允收值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「背景鹽度與稀釋定義」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Seawater already contains salt, so dilution tracks salinity excess above background rather than treating the environment as freshwater. A mass-flow dilution factor divides mixed total mass flow by discharged mass flow and corresponds to excess-concentration reduction. Centerline, section-averaged and flux-averaged values can differ, making the stated comparison quantity essential. The example is a fully mixed mass-salinity balance. It predicts neither where this dilution occurs nor whether it satisfies a permit or ecological criterion. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Background salinity and dilution” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排放Sb=60 g/kg、背景Sa=35 g/kg、質量稀釋D=10，混合Sm=Sa+(Sb−Sa)/D=37.5 g/kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume discharge Sb=60 g/kg, ambient Sa=35 g/kg and mass dilution D=10.","failure":"常見誤解：「海水鹵水稀釋十倍就是把原始總鹽度直接除以十。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Tenfold seawater-brine dilution means dividing total original salinity by ten.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「背景鹽度與稀釋定義」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Background salinity and dilution”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-05-k1","title":"背景鹽度與稀釋定義機理與驗證","titleEn":"Background salinity and dilution mechanism and verification","text":"海水本身含鹽，因此稀釋應追蹤相對於背景的鹽度增量，而不是把環境當成無鹽水。以質量流率定義的混合倍數等於混合後總質量流率除以原排放質量流率，對應超額濃度的衰減；中心線、截面平均與通量平均值可能不同，報告中必須明確指明所比較的量。","textEn":"Seawater already contains salt, so dilution tracks salinity excess above background rather than treating the environment as freshwater. A mass-flow dilution factor divides mixed total mass flow by discharged mass flow and corresponds to excess-concentration reduction.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：海水鹵水稀釋十倍就是把原始總鹽度直接除以十。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Tenfold seawater-brine dilution means dividing total original salinity by ten. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「背景鹽度與稀釋定義機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Background salinity and dilution mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["海水鹵水稀釋十倍就是把原始總鹽度直接除以十。","多孔擴散器的每個孔在所有流量和堵塞狀態下必定等量。","海水本身含鹽，因此稀釋應追蹤相對於背景的鹽度增量，而不是把環境當成無鹽水。"],"optionsEn":["Tenfold seawater-brine dilution means dividing total original salinity by ten.","Every diffuser port carries equal flow at all discharges and blockage states.","Seawater already contains salt, so dilution tracks salinity excess above background rather than treating the environment as freshwater."],"answer":2,"explanation":"海水本身含鹽，因此稀釋應追蹤相對於背景的鹽度增量，而不是把環境當成無鹽水。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Seawater already contains salt, so dilution tracks salinity excess above background rather than treating the environment as freshwater. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b267-v15-06","title":"背景鹽度與稀釋定義機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Background salinity and dilution mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「背景鹽度與稀釋定義」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Background salinity and dilution” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排放Sb=60 g/kg、背景Sa=35 g/kg、質量稀釋D=10，混合Sm=Sa+(Sb−Sa)/D=37.5 g/kg。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume discharge Sb=60 g/kg, ambient Sa=35 g/kg and mass dilution D=10. Mixed Sm=Sa+(Sb−Sa)/D=37.5 g/kg. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在排口影響範圍外量測背景剖面，將潮位、深度與取樣時刻和羽流資料配對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure ambient profiles beyond the discharge influence and pair tide, depth and sampling time with plume observations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排放Sb=60 g/kg、背景Sa=35 g/kg、質量稀釋D=10，混合Sm=Sa+(Sb−Sa)/D=37.5 g/kg。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume discharge Sb=60 g/kg, ambient Sa=35 g/kg and mass dilution D=10. Mixed Sm=Sa+(Sb−Sa)/D=37.5 g/kg.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「背景鹽度與稀釋定義機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Background salinity and dilution mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排放Sb=60 g/kg、背景Sa=35 g/kg、質量稀釋D=10，混合Sm=Sa+(Sb−Sa)/D=37.5 g/kg。","密度福祿數等於最後稀釋倍數，而且越大就一定越環保。","只要孔距是孔徑十倍，就能保證任何海況下噴流不互相影響。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume discharge Sb=60 g/kg, ambient Sa=35 g/kg and mass dilution D=10.","Densimetric Froude number equals final dilution and a larger value always means less impact.","Spacing of ten diameters guarantees no jet interaction under any marine condition."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排放Sb=60 g/kg、背景Sa=35 g/kg、質量稀釋D=10，混合Sm=Sa+(Sb−Sa)/D=37.5 g/kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume discharge Sb=60 g/kg, ambient Sa=35 g/kg and mass dilution D=10. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b267-v15-07","title":"背景鹽度與稀釋定義機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Background salinity and dilution mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「背景鹽度與稀釋定義」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Background salinity and dilution” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在排口影響範圍外量測背景剖面，將潮位、深度與取樣時刻和羽流資料配對。檢查模型輸出是中心線或平均濃度，再以一致的質量或體積定義換算稀釋倍數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure ambient profiles beyond the discharge influence and pair tide, depth and sampling time with plume observations. Determine whether model outputs are centerline or averaged concentrations, then convert dilution using a consistent mass or volume definition throughout the comparison. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用相同排放鹽度比較有鹽與無鹽背景，計算兩種混合結果並指出物理差異。為中心線與通量平均輸出各寫一句精確圖說，避免讀者以為兩者相同。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare saline and salt-free backgrounds for the same discharge, calculating both mixtures and explaining the physical difference. Write precise captions for centerline and flux-averaged outputs so readers do not mistake them for identical quantities.","failure":"注意干擾：用排放鹽度直接除以稀釋倍數會得到低於背景的不合理結果，混用中心線與平均濃度則可能低估局部暴露；背景採樣受排口污染時也會掩蓋真實增量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Dividing discharge salinity directly by dilution can produce an impossible value below ambient. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在排口影響範圍外量測背景剖面，將潮位、深度與取樣時刻和羽流資料配對。檢查模型輸出是中心線或平均濃度，再以一致的質量或體積定義換算稀釋倍數。","textEn":"Measure ambient profiles beyond the discharge influence and pair tide, depth and sampling time with plume observations. Determine whether model outputs are centerline or averaged concentrations, then convert dilution using a consistent mass or volume definition throughout the comparison.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用相同排放鹽度比較有鹽與無鹽背景，計算兩種混合結果並指出物理差異。為中心線與通量平均輸出各寫一句精確圖說，避免讀者以為兩者相同。","textEn":"Compare saline and salt-free backgrounds for the same discharge, calculating both mixtures and explaining the physical difference. Write precise captions for centerline and flux-averaged outputs so readers do not mistake them for identical quantities.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「背景鹽度與稀釋定義機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Background salinity and dilution mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在排口影響範圍外量測背景剖面，將潮位、深度與取樣時刻和羽流資料配對。","排口附近混合很快，所以半封閉海灣的長期鹽量帳不必計算。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Measure ambient profiles beyond the discharge influence and pair tide, depth and sampling time with plume observations.","Rapid mixing near the outlet makes a long-term salt budget unnecessary in a semi-enclosed bay."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在排口影響範圍外量測背景剖面，將潮位、深度與取樣時刻和羽流資料配對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure ambient profiles beyond the discharge influence and pair tide, depth and sampling time with plume observations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b267-v15-08","title":"背景鹽度與稀釋定義機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Background salinity and dilution mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「背景鹽度與稀釋定義」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Background salinity and dilution” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用排放鹽度直接除以稀釋倍數會得到低於背景的不合理結果，混用中心線與平均濃度則可能低估局部暴露；背景採樣受排口污染時也會掩蓋真實增量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Dividing discharge salinity directly by dilution can produce an impossible value below ambient. Mixing centerline and average concentration may understate local exposure, and contaminated background sampling can conceal the actual increment. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例為完全混合的質量鹽度守恆，不預測達到該混合倍數的位置，也不把它當作許可或生態允收值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It predicts neither where this dilution occurs nor whether it satisfies a permit or ecological criterion.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「海水鹵水稀釋十倍就是把原始總鹽度直接除以十。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Tenfold seawater-brine dilution means dividing total original salinity by ten.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用排放鹽度直接除以稀釋倍數會得到低於背景的不合理結果，混用中心線與平均濃度則可能低估局部暴露；背景採樣受排口污染時也會掩蓋真實增量。","textEn":"Dividing discharge salinity directly by dilution can produce an impossible value below ambient. Mixing centerline and average concentration may understate local exposure, and contaminated background sampling can conceal the actual increment.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「背景鹽度與稀釋定義機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Background salinity and dilution mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","多孔擴散器的每個孔在所有流量和堵塞狀態下必定等量。","用排放鹽度直接除以稀釋倍數會得到低於背景的不合理結果，混用中心線與平均濃度則可能低估局部暴露；背景採樣受排口污染時也會掩蓋真實增量。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Every diffuser port carries equal flow at all discharges and blockage states.","Dividing discharge salinity directly by dilution can produce an impossible value below ambient."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用排放鹽度直接除以稀釋倍數會得到低於背景的不合理結果，混用中心線與平均濃度則可能低估局部暴露；背景採樣受排口污染時也會掩蓋真實增量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Dividing discharge salinity directly by dilution can produce an impossible value below ambient. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b267-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「多孔流量分配機理與驗證」與「密度差與縮減重力機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Multiport flow distribution mechanism and verification\" and \"Density contrast and reduced gravity mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b267-v15-09","title":"多孔流量分配機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Multiport flow distribution mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「多孔流量分配」如何影響海水淡化鹵水擴散排放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Multiport flow distribution” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brine diffuser outfalls for desalination”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"擴散器將總排放分配到多個噴口以改變初始動量與接觸環境水的方式，但各孔未必等量。幹管沿程損失、孔口高程、局部背壓與堵塞會使流量偏向部分噴口；因此總流量除以孔數只是一個起始假設，不能取代幹管壓力與孔口出流的聯立分析。以下圓孔速度使用相同孔徑與等量流分配，未包含收縮係數；實際縮流速度與幾何面平均速度需要區分。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「多孔流量分配」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A diffuser divides discharge among ports to modify initial momentum and contact with ambient water, but equal port flow is not guaranteed. Header friction, elevation, local backpressure and blockage redistribute discharge. Dividing total flow by port count is therefore an initial assumption, not a substitute for coupled header-pressure and orifice-flow analysis. The circular-port calculation assumes identical diameters and equal flow, without a contraction coefficient. Actual contracted-jet velocity and geometric-area mean velocity must be distinguished. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Multiport flow distribution” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總Q=0.40 m³/s、孔數n=8、直徑d=0.15 m，單孔q=0.050 m³/s，v=q/(πd²/4)=2.829 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume total Q=0.40 m³/s, n=8 ports and diameter d=0.15 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「多孔擴散器的每個孔在所有流量和堵塞狀態下必定等量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every diffuser port carries equal flow at all discharges and blockage states.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「多孔流量分配」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Multiport flow distribution”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-09-k1","title":"多孔流量分配機理與驗證","titleEn":"Multiport flow distribution mechanism and verification","text":"擴散器將總排放分配到多個噴口以改變初始動量與接觸環境水的方式，但各孔未必等量。幹管沿程損失、孔口高程、局部背壓與堵塞會使流量偏向部分噴口；因此總流量除以孔數只是一個起始假設，不能取代幹管壓力與孔口出流的聯立分析。","textEn":"A diffuser divides discharge among ports to modify initial momentum and contact with ambient water, but equal port flow is not guaranteed. Header friction, elevation, local backpressure and blockage redistribute discharge.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：多孔擴散器的每個孔在所有流量和堵塞狀態下必定等量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every diffuser port carries equal flow at all discharges and blockage states. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「多孔流量分配機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Multiport flow distribution mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["擴散器將總排放分配到多個噴口以改變初始動量與接觸環境水的方式，但各孔未必等量。","多孔擴散器的每個孔在所有流量和堵塞狀態下必定等量。","只要鹽度較高，就可忽略溫度並沿用所有上浮羽流公式。"],"optionsEn":["A diffuser divides discharge among ports to modify initial momentum and contact with ambient water, but equal port flow is not guaranteed.","Every diffuser port carries equal flow at all discharges and blockage states.","Higher salinity allows temperature to be ignored and all rising-plume formulas reused."],"answer":0,"explanation":"擴散器將總排放分配到多個噴口以改變初始動量與接觸環境水的方式，但各孔未必等量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A diffuser divides discharge among ports to modify initial momentum and contact with ambient water, but equal port flow is not guaranteed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b267-v15-10","title":"多孔流量分配機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Multiport flow distribution mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「多孔流量分配」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Multiport flow distribution” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總Q=0.40 m³/s、孔數n=8、直徑d=0.15 m，單孔q=0.050 m³/s，v=q/(πd²/4)=2.829 m/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume total Q=0.40 m³/s, n=8 ports and diameter d=0.15 m. Each q=0.050 m³/s and v=q/(πd²/4)=2.829 m/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對每孔幾何、標高與壓力，將可量測的分流量和總流量對帳。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check each port geometry, elevation and pressure, reconciling measured branch flows with the total.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總Q=0.40 m³/s、孔數n=8、直徑d=0.15 m，單孔q=0.050 m³/s，v=q/(πd²/4)=2.829 m/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume total Q=0.40 m³/s, n=8 ports and diameter d=0.15 m. Each q=0.050 m³/s and v=q/(πd²/4)=2.829 m/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「多孔流量分配機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Multiport flow distribution mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["流量乘速度已經是牛頓力，而且所有噴口反力只須加大小。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總Q=0.40 m³/s、孔數n=8、直徑d=0.15 m，單孔q=0.050 m³/s，v=q/(πd²/4)=2.829 m/s。","海流速度乘一小時得到的距離，就是鹵水必然被稀釋完的位置。"],"optionsEn":["Flow times velocity is already force in newtons and port reactions require only scalar addition.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume total Q=0.40 m³/s, n=8 ports and diameter d=0.15 m.","Current speed times one hour gives the distance at which brine is necessarily fully diluted."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總Q=0.40 m³/s、孔數n=8、直徑d=0.15 m，單孔q=0.050 m³/s，v=q/(πd²/4)=2.829 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume total Q=0.40 m³/s, n=8 ports and diameter d=0.15 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b267-v15-11","title":"多孔流量分配機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Multiport flow distribution mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「多孔流量分配」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Multiport flow distribution” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對每孔幾何、標高與壓力，將可量測的分流量和總流量對帳。以部分堵塞及低流量情境測試均勻分配假設，並區分孔面速度、縮流速度及後續羽流平均速度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check each port geometry, elevation and pressure, reconciling measured branch flows with the total. Test equal-flow assumptions under partial blockage and low discharge, distinguishing geometric port velocity, contracted-jet velocity and subsequent plume-average velocity in all records. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：先建立等量八孔基準，再假設一孔完全堵塞且總流量不變，重算其餘孔速度。指出維持總流量所需的新壓力尚未由這個面積計算求得。","observationEn":"Site practice: Build an equal-flow eight-port baseline, then block one port while holding total flow fixed and recalculate the remaining velocities. Explain that the new pressure needed to maintain total flow is not provided by this area calculation.","failure":"注意干擾：只以孔數平均會忽略堵孔造成的局部高速及動量增大，低流量時部分孔也可能受到逆流影響；用錯有效孔徑會透過平方關係放大速度誤差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A port-count average misses local acceleration and momentum increases caused by blockage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對每孔幾何、標高與壓力，將可量測的分流量和總流量對帳。以部分堵塞及低流量情境測試均勻分配假設，並區分孔面速度、縮流速度及後續羽流平均速度。","textEn":"Check each port geometry, elevation and pressure, reconciling measured branch flows with the total. Test equal-flow assumptions under partial blockage and low discharge, distinguishing geometric port velocity, contracted-jet velocity and subsequent plume-average velocity in all records.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"先建立等量八孔基準，再假設一孔完全堵塞且總流量不變，重算其餘孔速度。指出維持總流量所需的新壓力尚未由這個面積計算求得。","textEn":"Build an equal-flow eight-port baseline, then block one port while holding total flow fixed and recalculate the remaining velocities. Explain that the new pressure needed to maintain total flow is not provided by this area calculation.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「多孔流量分配機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Multiport flow distribution mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","感測器讀值差很小，就能直接證明長期海域生態完全安全。","核對每孔幾何、標高與壓力，將可量測的分流量和總流量對帳。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A small sensor difference directly proves complete long-term ecological safety.","Check each port geometry, elevation and pressure, reconciling measured branch flows with the total."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對每孔幾何、標高與壓力，將可量測的分流量和總流量對帳。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check each port geometry, elevation and pressure, reconciling measured branch flows with the total. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b267-v15-12","title":"多孔流量分配機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Multiport flow distribution mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「多孔流量分配」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Multiport flow distribution” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只以孔數平均會忽略堵孔造成的局部高速及動量增大，低流量時部分孔也可能受到逆流影響；用錯有效孔徑會透過平方關係放大速度誤差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A port-count average misses local acceleration and momentum increases caused by blockage. Some ports can experience reverse flow at low discharge, while incorrect effective diameter amplifies velocity error through the squared-area relationship. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以下圓孔速度使用相同孔徑與等量流分配，未包含收縮係數；實際縮流速度與幾何面平均速度需要區分。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Actual contracted-jet velocity and geometric-area mean velocity must be distinguished.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「多孔擴散器的每個孔在所有流量和堵塞狀態下必定等量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every diffuser port carries equal flow at all discharges and blockage states.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只以孔數平均會忽略堵孔造成的局部高速及動量增大，低流量時部分孔也可能受到逆流影響；用錯有效孔徑會透過平方關係放大速度誤差。","textEn":"A port-count average misses local acceleration and momentum increases caused by blockage. Some ports can experience reverse flow at low discharge, while incorrect effective diameter amplifies velocity error through the squared-area relationship.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「多孔流量分配機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Multiport flow distribution mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只以孔數平均會忽略堵孔造成的局部高速及動量增大，低流量時部分孔也可能受到逆流影響；用錯有效孔徑會透過平方關係放大速度誤差。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要鹽度較高，就可忽略溫度並沿用所有上浮羽流公式。"],"optionsEn":["A port-count average misses local acceleration and momentum increases caused by blockage.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Higher salinity allows temperature to be ignored and all rising-plume formulas reused."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只以孔數平均會忽略堵孔造成的局部高速及動量增大，低流量時部分孔也可能受到逆流影響；用錯有效孔徑會透過平方關係放大速度誤差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A port-count average misses local acceleration and momentum increases caused by blockage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b267-v15-13","title":"密度差與縮減重力機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Density contrast and reduced gravity mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「密度差與縮減重力」如何影響海水淡化鹵水擴散排放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Density contrast and reduced gravity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brine diffuser outfalls for desalination”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"鹵水通常比受納海水密度大，其浮力方向與較淡的污水羽流不同。密度差受鹽度和溫度共同影響，應在相同壓力基準下比較；縮減重力把密度差轉為浮力尺度，但並不單獨決定上升高度、落點或海床濃度，這些仍取決於噴射動量與環境流場。本例採環境密度作分母，計算負浮力的大小；若座標向上為正，對較重排放的有號浮力加速度應另記為負值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「密度差與縮減重力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Brine is commonly denser than receiving seawater, giving it the opposite buoyancy direction to a fresher wastewater plume. Salinity and temperature jointly affect density and must be compared at a consistent pressure basis. Reduced gravity expresses the density contrast as a buoyancy scale, but jet momentum and ambient flow are still needed to predict rise, return or seabed concentration. Ambient density is the reference denominator and the calculation gives negative-buoyancy magnitude. With upward positive, the signed buoyancy acceleration for denser discharge is negative. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Density contrast and reduced gravity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排放ρb=1040 kg/m³、環境ρa=1025 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²，g′=g(ρb−ρa)/ρa=0.1436 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume discharge ρb=1040 kg/m³, ambient ρa=1025 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「只要鹽度較高，就可忽略溫度並沿用所有上浮羽流公式。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Higher salinity allows temperature to be ignored and all rising-plume formulas reused.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「密度差與縮減重力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Density contrast and reduced gravity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-13-k1","title":"密度差與縮減重力機理與驗證","titleEn":"Density contrast and reduced gravity mechanism and verification","text":"鹵水通常比受納海水密度大，其浮力方向與較淡的污水羽流不同。密度差受鹽度和溫度共同影響，應在相同壓力基準下比較；縮減重力把密度差轉為浮力尺度，但並不單獨決定上升高度、落點或海床濃度，這些仍取決於噴射動量與環境流場。","textEn":"Brine is commonly denser than receiving seawater, giving it the opposite buoyancy direction to a fresher wastewater plume. Salinity and temperature jointly affect density and must be compared at a consistent pressure basis.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要鹽度較高，就可忽略溫度並沿用所有上浮羽流公式。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Higher salinity allows temperature to be ignored and all rising-plume formulas reused. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「密度差與縮減重力機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Density contrast and reduced gravity mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["只要鹽度較高，就可忽略溫度並沿用所有上浮羽流公式。","鹵水通常比受納海水密度大，其浮力方向與較淡的污水羽流不同。","密度福祿數等於最後稀釋倍數，而且越大就一定越環保。"],"optionsEn":["Higher salinity allows temperature to be ignored and all rising-plume formulas reused.","Brine is commonly denser than receiving seawater, giving it the opposite buoyancy direction to a fresher wastewater plume.","Densimetric Froude number equals final dilution and a larger value always means less impact."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鹵水通常比受納海水密度大，其浮力方向與較淡的污水羽流不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Brine is commonly denser than receiving seawater, giving it the opposite buoyancy direction to a fresher wastewater plume. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b267-v15-14","title":"密度差與縮減重力機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Density contrast and reduced gravity mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「密度差與縮減重力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Density contrast and reduced gravity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排放ρb=1040 kg/m³、環境ρa=1025 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²，g′=g(ρb−ρa)/ρa=0.1436 m/s²。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume discharge ρb=1040 kg/m³, ambient ρa=1025 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Reduced-gravity magnitude g′=g(ρb−ρa)/ρa=0.1436 m/s². Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將排放與環境溫鹽資料轉成一致密度基準，保留垂向分層而非只取表層樣本。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Convert discharge and ambient temperature-salinity data to consistent density estimates, retaining vertical stratification rather than only surface samples.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排放ρb=1040 kg/m³、環境ρa=1025 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²，g′=g(ρb−ρa)/ρa=0.1436 m/s²。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume discharge ρb=1040 kg/m³, ambient ρa=1025 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Reduced-gravity magnitude g′=g(ρb−ρa)/ρa=0.1436 m/s².","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「密度差與縮減重力機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Density contrast and reduced gravity mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["只要孔距是孔徑十倍，就能保證任何海況下噴流不互相影響。","排口附近混合很快，所以半封閉海灣的長期鹽量帳不必計算。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排放ρb=1040 kg/m³、環境ρa=1025 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²，g′=g(ρb−ρa)/ρa=0.1436 m/s²。"],"optionsEn":["Spacing of ten diameters guarantees no jet interaction under any marine condition.","Rapid mixing near the outlet makes a long-term salt budget unnecessary in a semi-enclosed bay.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume discharge ρb=1040 kg/m³, ambient ρa=1025 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排放ρb=1040 kg/m³、環境ρa=1025 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²，g′=g(ρb−ρa)/ρa=0.1436 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume discharge ρb=1040 kg/m³, ambient ρa=1025 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b267-v15-15","title":"密度差與縮減重力機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Density contrast and reduced gravity mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「密度差與縮減重力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Density contrast and reduced gravity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將排放與環境溫鹽資料轉成一致密度基準，保留垂向分層而非只取表層樣本。核對模型正負號及參考密度，並用零密度差極限確認浮力項會消失。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Convert discharge and ambient temperature-salinity data to consistent density estimates, retaining vertical stratification rather than only surface samples. Check model sign conventions and reference density, and test the zero-density-difference limit to confirm that the buoyancy term vanishes. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：為相同鹽度差建立兩種溫度情境，說明密度資料如何改變浮力輸入。畫出向上為正的座標，標記重鹵水的浮力方向及需要額外求解的軌跡。","observationEn":"Site practice: Create two temperature scenarios for the same salinity contrast and explain how density data change buoyancy input. Draw an upward-positive coordinate system, marking dense-brine buoyancy and the trajectory that still requires solution.","failure":"注意干擾：把負浮力套入只適合上浮羽流的終止或遠場假設，可能漏掉海床接觸與沿底擴散；忽略溫度差也可能誤估密度差大小甚至方向。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying rising-plume termination or far-field assumptions to negative buoyancy can omit seabed contact and bottom spreading. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將排放與環境溫鹽資料轉成一致密度基準，保留垂向分層而非只取表層樣本。核對模型正負號及參考密度，並用零密度差極限確認浮力項會消失。","textEn":"Convert discharge and ambient temperature-salinity data to consistent density estimates, retaining vertical stratification rather than only surface samples. Check model sign conventions and reference density, and test the zero-density-difference limit to confirm that the buoyancy term vanishes.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"為相同鹽度差建立兩種溫度情境，說明密度資料如何改變浮力輸入。畫出向上為正的座標，標記重鹵水的浮力方向及需要額外求解的軌跡。","textEn":"Create two temperature scenarios for the same salinity contrast and explain how density data change buoyancy input. Draw an upward-positive coordinate system, marking dense-brine buoyancy and the trajectory that still requires solution.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「密度差與縮減重力機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Density contrast and reduced gravity mechanism and verification\"?","options":["將排放與環境溫鹽資料轉成一致密度基準，保留垂向分層而非只取表層樣本。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","提高產水回收率會讓剩下濃水中的總鹽量自行消失。"],"optionsEn":["Convert discharge and ambient temperature-salinity data to consistent density estimates, retaining vertical stratification rather than only surface samples.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Higher water recovery makes the remaining concentrate salt disappear."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將排放與環境溫鹽資料轉成一致密度基準，保留垂向分層而非只取表層樣本。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Convert discharge and ambient temperature-salinity data to consistent density estimates, retaining vertical stratification rather than only surface samples. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b267-v15-16","title":"密度差與縮減重力機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Density contrast and reduced gravity mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「密度差與縮減重力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Density contrast and reduced gravity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把負浮力套入只適合上浮羽流的終止或遠場假設，可能漏掉海床接觸與沿底擴散；忽略溫度差也可能誤估密度差大小甚至方向。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying rising-plume termination or far-field assumptions to negative buoyancy can omit seabed contact and bottom spreading. Ignoring temperature differences can also misestimate the magnitude or even direction of the density contrast. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例採環境密度作分母，計算負浮力的大小；若座標向上為正，對較重排放的有號浮力加速度應另記為負值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: With upward positive, the signed buoyancy acceleration for denser discharge is negative.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要鹽度較高，就可忽略溫度並沿用所有上浮羽流公式。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher salinity allows temperature to be ignored and all rising-plume formulas reused.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把負浮力套入只適合上浮羽流的終止或遠場假設，可能漏掉海床接觸與沿底擴散；忽略溫度差也可能誤估密度差大小甚至方向。","textEn":"Applying rising-plume termination or far-field assumptions to negative buoyancy can omit seabed contact and bottom spreading. Ignoring temperature differences can also misestimate the magnitude or even direction of the density contrast.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「密度差與縮減重力機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Density contrast and reduced gravity mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把負浮力套入只適合上浮羽流的終止或遠場假設，可能漏掉海床接觸與沿底擴散；忽略溫度差也可能誤估密度差大小甚至方向。","密度福祿數等於最後稀釋倍數，而且越大就一定越環保。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Applying rising-plume termination or far-field assumptions to negative buoyancy can omit seabed contact and bottom spreading.","Densimetric Froude number equals final dilution and a larger value always means less impact."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把負浮力套入只適合上浮羽流的終止或遠場假設，可能漏掉海床接觸與沿底擴散；忽略溫度差也可能誤估密度差大小甚至方向。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying rising-plume termination or far-field assumptions to negative buoyancy can omit seabed contact and bottom spreading. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b267-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「密度福祿數機理與驗證」與「動量通量與反力機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Densimetric Froude number mechanism and verification\" and \"Momentum flux and reaction mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b267-v15-17","title":"密度福祿數機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Densimetric Froude number mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「密度福祿數」如何影響海水淡化鹵水擴散排放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Densimetric Froude number” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brine diffuser outfalls for desalination”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"密度福祿數比較噴口慣性與密度差浮力，以孔徑、噴射速度及縮減重力構成無量綱比例。較大的比例代表初始動量相對較強，卻不保證所有位置的稀釋更好；出口角度、海床距離、相鄰噴流與環境流向都會改變後續軌跡，必須在相似條件下比較。本例使用單孔圓射流的尺度定義，沒有套入未驗證的經驗稀釋係數；無量綱值不能直接當成稀釋倍數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「密度福祿數」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The densimetric Froude number compares port inertia with density-driven buoyancy using diameter, velocity and reduced gravity. A larger ratio indicates stronger initial momentum relative to buoyancy but does not guarantee better dilution everywhere. Discharge angle, bed clearance, neighboring jets and ambient-current direction alter the subsequent trajectory, so comparisons require compatible conditions. The example uses the scale definition for one circular jet without an unverified empirical dilution coefficient. This dimensionless value is not itself a dilution factor. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Densimetric Froude number” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設噴速v=3.0 m/s、g′=0.15 m/s²、孔徑d=0.20 m，Fd=v/√(g′d)=17.32。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume jet speed v=3.0 m/s, g′=0.15 m/s² and diameter d=0.20 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「密度福祿數等於最後稀釋倍數，而且越大就一定越環保。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Densimetric Froude number equals final dilution and a larger value always means less impact.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「密度福祿數」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Densimetric Froude number”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-17-k1","title":"密度福祿數機理與驗證","titleEn":"Densimetric Froude number mechanism and verification","text":"密度福祿數比較噴口慣性與密度差浮力，以孔徑、噴射速度及縮減重力構成無量綱比例。較大的比例代表初始動量相對較強，卻不保證所有位置的稀釋更好；出口角度、海床距離、相鄰噴流與環境流向都會改變後續軌跡，必須在相似條件下比較。","textEn":"The densimetric Froude number compares port inertia with density-driven buoyancy using diameter, velocity and reduced gravity. A larger ratio indicates stronger initial momentum relative to buoyancy but does not guarantee better dilution everywhere.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：密度福祿數等於最後稀釋倍數，而且越大就一定越環保。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Densimetric Froude number equals final dilution and a larger value always means less impact. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「密度福祿數機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Densimetric Froude number mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["密度福祿數等於最後稀釋倍數，而且越大就一定越環保。","流量乘速度已經是牛頓力，而且所有噴口反力只須加大小。","密度福祿數比較噴口慣性與密度差浮力，以孔徑、噴射速度及縮減重力構成無量綱比例。"],"optionsEn":["Densimetric Froude number equals final dilution and a larger value always means less impact.","Flow times velocity is already force in newtons and port reactions require only scalar addition.","The densimetric Froude number compares port inertia with density-driven buoyancy using diameter, velocity and reduced gravity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"密度福祿數比較噴口慣性與密度差浮力，以孔徑、噴射速度及縮減重力構成無量綱比例。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The densimetric Froude number compares port inertia with density-driven buoyancy using diameter, velocity and reduced gravity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b267-v15-18","title":"密度福祿數機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Densimetric Froude number mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「密度福祿數」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Densimetric Froude number” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設噴速v=3.0 m/s、g′=0.15 m/s²、孔徑d=0.20 m，Fd=v/√(g′d)=17.32。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume jet speed v=3.0 m/s, g′=0.15 m/s² and diameter d=0.20 m. Densimetric Froude number Fd=v/√(g′d)=17.32. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐項核對孔徑、速度截面及密度差的定義，確認比較試驗使用相同角度和邊界條件。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check diameter, velocity section and density-contrast definitions, ensuring comparison experiments use matching angles and boundaries.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設噴速v=3.0 m/s、g′=0.15 m/s²、孔徑d=0.20 m，Fd=v/√(g′d)=17.32。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume jet speed v=3.0 m/s, g′=0.15 m/s² and diameter d=0.20 m. Densimetric Froude number Fd=v/√(g′d)=17.32.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「密度福祿數機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Densimetric Froude number mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設噴速v=3.0 m/s、g′=0.15 m/s²、孔徑d=0.20 m，Fd=v/√(g′d)=17.32。","海流速度乘一小時得到的距離，就是鹵水必然被稀釋完的位置。","感測器讀值差很小，就能直接證明長期海域生態完全安全。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume jet speed v=3.0 m/s, g′=0.15 m/s² and diameter d=0.20 m.","Current speed times one hour gives the distance at which brine is necessarily fully diluted.","A small sensor difference directly proves complete long-term ecological safety."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設噴速v=3.0 m/s、g′=0.15 m/s²、孔徑d=0.20 m，Fd=v/√(g′d)=17.32。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume jet speed v=3.0 m/s, g′=0.15 m/s² and diameter d=0.20 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b267-v15-19","title":"密度福祿數機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Densimetric Froude number mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「密度福祿數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Densimetric Froude number” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐項核對孔徑、速度截面及密度差的定義，確認比較試驗使用相同角度和邊界條件。對照實驗或適用模型的參數範圍，並另行驗證海床接觸位置與峰值濃度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check diameter, velocity section and density-contrast definitions, ensuring comparison experiments use matching angles and boundaries. Compare inputs with the validated parameter range of the experiment or model, and independently verify seabed contact location and peak concentration before interpreting performance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在固定流量下將孔徑增加一成，分別更新面積、噴速與福祿數。說明為何不能只把孔徑代入分母而保持速度不變，並列出仍未求解的環境結果。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase diameter by ten percent at fixed flow and update area, velocity and Froude number separately. Explain why velocity cannot remain fixed while only the denominator changes, and identify environmental outcomes still unresolved.","failure":"注意干擾：把福祿數當稀釋倍數會省略真正的混合過程，增加噴速也可能把高濃度水送到敏感區；超出經驗式試驗範圍時，漂亮的無量綱圖不代表預測可靠。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating Froude number as dilution bypasses the mixing process, and increased velocity can carry concentrated water toward sensitive locations. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐項核對孔徑、速度截面及密度差的定義，確認比較試驗使用相同角度和邊界條件。對照實驗或適用模型的參數範圍，並另行驗證海床接觸位置與峰值濃度。","textEn":"Check diameter, velocity section and density-contrast definitions, ensuring comparison experiments use matching angles and boundaries. Compare inputs with the validated parameter range of the experiment or model, and independently verify seabed contact location and peak concentration before interpreting performance.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在固定流量下將孔徑增加一成，分別更新面積、噴速與福祿數。說明為何不能只把孔徑代入分母而保持速度不變，並列出仍未求解的環境結果。","textEn":"Increase diameter by ten percent at fixed flow and update area, velocity and Froude number separately. Explain why velocity cannot remain fixed while only the denominator changes, and identify environmental outcomes still unresolved.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「密度福祿數機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Densimetric Froude number mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","逐項核對孔徑、速度截面及密度差的定義，確認比較試驗使用相同角度和邊界條件。","海水鹵水稀釋十倍就是把原始總鹽度直接除以十。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check diameter, velocity section and density-contrast definitions, ensuring comparison experiments use matching angles and boundaries.","Tenfold seawater-brine dilution means dividing total original salinity by ten."],"answer":1,"explanation":"逐項核對孔徑、速度截面及密度差的定義，確認比較試驗使用相同角度和邊界條件。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check diameter, velocity section and density-contrast definitions, ensuring comparison experiments use matching angles and boundaries. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b267-v15-20","title":"密度福祿數機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Densimetric Froude number mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「密度福祿數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Densimetric Froude number” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把福祿數當稀釋倍數會省略真正的混合過程，增加噴速也可能把高濃度水送到敏感區；超出經驗式試驗範圍時，漂亮的無量綱圖不代表預測可靠。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating Froude number as dilution bypasses the mixing process, and increased velocity can carry concentrated water toward sensitive locations. Outside an empirical correlation’s test range, a neat dimensionless plot does not establish predictive reliability. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例使用單孔圓射流的尺度定義，沒有套入未驗證的經驗稀釋係數；無量綱值不能直接當成稀釋倍數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This dimensionless value is not itself a dilution factor.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「密度福祿數等於最後稀釋倍數，而且越大就一定越環保。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Densimetric Froude number equals final dilution and a larger value always means less impact.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把福祿數當稀釋倍數會省略真正的混合過程，增加噴速也可能把高濃度水送到敏感區；超出經驗式試驗範圍時，漂亮的無量綱圖不代表預測可靠。","textEn":"Treating Froude number as dilution bypasses the mixing process, and increased velocity can carry concentrated water toward sensitive locations. Outside an empirical correlation’s test range, a neat dimensionless plot does not establish predictive reliability.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「密度福祿數機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Densimetric Froude number mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","流量乘速度已經是牛頓力，而且所有噴口反力只須加大小。","把福祿數當稀釋倍數會省略真正的混合過程，增加噴速也可能把高濃度水送到敏感區；超出經驗式試驗範圍時，漂亮的無量綱圖不代表預測可靠。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Flow times velocity is already force in newtons and port reactions require only scalar addition.","Treating Froude number as dilution bypasses the mixing process, and increased velocity can carry concentrated water toward sensitive locations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把福祿數當稀釋倍數會省略真正的混合過程，增加噴速也可能把高濃度水送到敏感區；超出經驗式試驗範圍時，漂亮的無量綱圖不代表預測可靠。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating Froude number as dilution bypasses the mixing process, and increased velocity can carry concentrated water toward sensitive locations. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b267-v15-21","title":"動量通量與反力機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Momentum flux and reaction mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「動量通量與反力」如何影響海水淡化鹵水擴散排放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Momentum flux and reaction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brine diffuser outfalls for desalination”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"噴口把壓力能轉為射流動量，單孔的運動學動量通量與真正的力具有不同單位。若需估算構件反力，必須包含密度並考慮方向與控制體上的壓力作用；只加上所有速度大小不會得到合力，對向噴口的水平分量可能抵消而垂直分量仍保留。以下只算均勻自由射流的動量力大小，未含幹管壓力、彎頭及支承作用；不能直接拿此數值設計整支擴散管錨定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「動量通量與反力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A port converts pressure energy into jet momentum, but kinematic momentum flux and force have different units. Estimating structural reaction requires density, direction and pressure forces on the control volume. Adding speed magnitudes does not produce a resultant: opposing horizontal components may cancel while vertical components remain. This calculates momentum-force magnitude for a uniform free jet only, excluding header pressure, bends and supports. It is not a complete anchorage load for the diffuser. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Momentum flux and reaction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設單孔ρ=1040 kg/m³、q=0.050 m³/s、v=3.0 m/s，動量力F=ρqv=156 N；運動學通量qv=0.150 m⁴/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume one port ρ=1040 kg/m³, q=0.050 m³/s and v=3.0 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「流量乘速度已經是牛頓力，而且所有噴口反力只須加大小。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Flow times velocity is already force in newtons and port reactions require only scalar addition.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「動量通量與反力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Momentum flux and reaction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-21-k1","title":"動量通量與反力機理與驗證","titleEn":"Momentum flux and reaction mechanism and verification","text":"噴口把壓力能轉為射流動量，單孔的運動學動量通量與真正的力具有不同單位。若需估算構件反力，必須包含密度並考慮方向與控制體上的壓力作用；只加上所有速度大小不會得到合力，對向噴口的水平分量可能抵消而垂直分量仍保留。","textEn":"A port converts pressure energy into jet momentum, but kinematic momentum flux and force have different units. Estimating structural reaction requires density, direction and pressure forces on the control volume.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：流量乘速度已經是牛頓力，而且所有噴口反力只須加大小。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Flow times velocity is already force in newtons and port reactions require only scalar addition. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「動量通量與反力機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Momentum flux and reaction mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["噴口把壓力能轉為射流動量，單孔的運動學動量通量與真正的力具有不同單位。","流量乘速度已經是牛頓力，而且所有噴口反力只須加大小。","只要孔距是孔徑十倍，就能保證任何海況下噴流不互相影響。"],"optionsEn":["A port converts pressure energy into jet momentum, but kinematic momentum flux and force have different units.","Flow times velocity is already force in newtons and port reactions require only scalar addition.","Spacing of ten diameters guarantees no jet interaction under any marine condition."],"answer":0,"explanation":"噴口把壓力能轉為射流動量，單孔的運動學動量通量與真正的力具有不同單位。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A port converts pressure energy into jet momentum, but kinematic momentum flux and force have different units. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b267-v15-22","title":"動量通量與反力機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Momentum flux and reaction mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「動量通量與反力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Momentum flux and reaction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設單孔ρ=1040 kg/m³、q=0.050 m³/s、v=3.0 m/s，動量力F=ρqv=156 N；運動學通量qv=0.150 m⁴/s²。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume one port ρ=1040 kg/m³, q=0.050 m³/s and v=3.0 m/s. Momentum force F=ρqv=156 N; kinematic flux qv=0.150 m⁴/s². Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在控制體圖上標明每孔流向、流量及壓力邊界，將動量力分解為座標分量後才求和。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark port directions, flows and pressure boundaries on a control-volume diagram, resolving momentum forces into components before summation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設單孔ρ=1040 kg/m³、q=0.050 m³/s、v=3.0 m/s，動量力F=ρqv=156 N；運動學通量qv=0.150 m⁴/s²。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume one port ρ=1040 kg/m³, q=0.050 m³/s and v=3.0 m/s. Momentum force F=ρqv=156 N; kinematic flux qv=0.150 m⁴/s².","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「動量通量與反力機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Momentum flux and reaction mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["排口附近混合很快，所以半封閉海灣的長期鹽量帳不必計算。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設單孔ρ=1040 kg/m³、q=0.050 m³/s、v=3.0 m/s，動量力F=ρqv=156 N。","提高產水回收率會讓剩下濃水中的總鹽量自行消失。"],"optionsEn":["Rapid mixing near the outlet makes a long-term salt budget unnecessary in a semi-enclosed bay.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume one port ρ=1040 kg/m³, q=0.050 m³/s and v=3.0 m/s.","Higher water recovery makes the remaining concentrate salt disappear."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設單孔ρ=1040 kg/m³、q=0.050 m³/s、v=3.0 m/s，動量力F=ρqv=156 N；運動學通量qv=0.150 m⁴/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume one port ρ=1040 kg/m³, q=0.050 m³/s and v=3.0 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b267-v15-23","title":"動量通量與反力機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Momentum flux and reaction mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「動量通量與反力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Momentum flux and reaction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在控制體圖上標明每孔流向、流量及壓力邊界，將動量力分解為座標分量後才求和。與支承及幹管內力模型核對載荷傳遞，避免把單孔自由射流值當完整結構反力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark port directions, flows and pressure boundaries on a control-volume diagram, resolving momentum forces into components before summation. Check load transfer against support and header-force models, avoiding use of a single free-jet result as the complete structural reaction. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以兩個對稱斜噴口畫出動量向量，分別求水平與垂直分量。將自由射流反力和幹管壓力端力分開列帳，指出支承模型還需要哪些幾何資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw momentum vectors for two symmetric inclined ports and resolve horizontal and vertical components. List free-jet reaction separately from header pressure end force, identifying the geometry still required by the support model.","failure":"注意干擾：漏乘密度會把運動學通量誤認成力，忽略方向則可能錯估總反力與扭矩；若再漏掉壓力端力，錨定分析即使數字整齊也缺少必要載荷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting density mistakes kinematic flux for force, while ignoring direction misstates resultant force and torque. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在控制體圖上標明每孔流向、流量及壓力邊界，將動量力分解為座標分量後才求和。與支承及幹管內力模型核對載荷傳遞，避免把單孔自由射流值當完整結構反力。","textEn":"Mark port directions, flows and pressure boundaries on a control-volume diagram, resolving momentum forces into components before summation. Check load transfer against support and header-force models, avoiding use of a single free-jet result as the complete structural reaction.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以兩個對稱斜噴口畫出動量向量，分別求水平與垂直分量。將自由射流反力和幹管壓力端力分開列帳，指出支承模型還需要哪些幾何資料。","textEn":"Draw momentum vectors for two symmetric inclined ports and resolve horizontal and vertical components. List free-jet reaction separately from header pressure end force, identifying the geometry still required by the support model.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「動量通量與反力機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Momentum flux and reaction mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","多孔擴散器的每個孔在所有流量和堵塞狀態下必定等量。","在控制體圖上標明每孔流向、流量及壓力邊界，將動量力分解為座標分量後才求和。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Every diffuser port carries equal flow at all discharges and blockage states.","Mark port directions, flows and pressure boundaries on a control-volume diagram, resolving momentum forces into components before summation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在控制體圖上標明每孔流向、流量及壓力邊界，將動量力分解為座標分量後才求和。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark port directions, flows and pressure boundaries on a control-volume diagram, resolving momentum forces into components before summation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b267-v15-24","title":"動量通量與反力機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Momentum flux and reaction mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「動量通量與反力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Momentum flux and reaction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏乘密度會把運動學通量誤認成力，忽略方向則可能錯估總反力與扭矩；若再漏掉壓力端力，錨定分析即使數字整齊也缺少必要載荷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting density mistakes kinematic flux for force, while ignoring direction misstates resultant force and torque. Missing pressure end forces then leaves anchorage analysis incomplete even when its arithmetic appears orderly. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以下只算均勻自由射流的動量力大小，未含幹管壓力、彎頭及支承作用；不能直接拿此數值設計整支擴散管錨定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It is not a complete anchorage load for the diffuser.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「流量乘速度已經是牛頓力，而且所有噴口反力只須加大小。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Flow times velocity is already force in newtons and port reactions require only scalar addition.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏乘密度會把運動學通量誤認成力，忽略方向則可能錯估總反力與扭矩；若再漏掉壓力端力，錨定分析即使數字整齊也缺少必要載荷。","textEn":"Omitting density mistakes kinematic flux for force, while ignoring direction misstates resultant force and torque. Missing pressure end forces then leaves anchorage analysis incomplete even when its arithmetic appears orderly.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「動量通量與反力機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Momentum flux and reaction mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["漏乘密度會把運動學通量誤認成力，忽略方向則可能錯估總反力與扭矩；若再漏掉壓力端力，錨定分析即使數字整齊也缺少必要載荷。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","只要孔距是孔徑十倍，就能保證任何海況下噴流不互相影響。"],"optionsEn":["Omitting density mistakes kinematic flux for force, while ignoring direction misstates resultant force and torque.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Spacing of ten diameters guarantees no jet interaction under any marine condition."],"answer":0,"explanation":"漏乘密度會把運動學通量誤認成力，忽略方向則可能錯估總反力與扭矩；若再漏掉壓力端力，錨定分析即使數字整齊也缺少必要載荷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting density mistakes kinematic flux for force, while ignoring direction misstates resultant force and torque. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b267-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「孔距與噴流合併機理與驗證」與「環境流與停留尺度機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Port spacing and jet merging mechanism and verification\" and \"Ambient currents and residence scales mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b267-v15-25","title":"孔距與噴流合併機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Port spacing and jet merging mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「孔距與噴流合併」如何影響海水淡化鹵水擴散排放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Port spacing and jet merging” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brine diffuser outfalls for desalination”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"相鄰射流會在擴展過程中互相影響，過早合併可能減少各自可捲吸的環境水，但是否有利不能只由孔距大小判斷。角度、交錯排列、海流與密度差會改變交會位置；單孔模型的稀釋結果也不能直接乘以孔數當成多孔系統的表現。孔距除以孔徑只是幾何比較，不是通用的無干擾門檻；本例沒有預測合併高度或環境可接受性。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「孔距與噴流合併」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Neighboring jets interact as they widen, and early merging can reduce ambient water available to each jet. Whether a layout is beneficial cannot be judged from spacing alone. Angle, staggering, current and density contrast shift the interaction location, and single-port dilution cannot simply be multiplied by port count to represent the whole diffuser. Spacing divided by diameter is a geometric comparison, not a universal noninteraction threshold. The example predicts neither merging height nor environmental acceptability. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Port spacing and jet merging” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設中心孔距s=2.0 m、孔徑d=0.20 m，幾何比例s/d=10；若d增至0.22 m且s不變，比例為9.09。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume center spacing s=2.0 m and diameter d=0.20 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要孔距是孔徑十倍，就能保證任何海況下噴流不互相影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Spacing of ten diameters guarantees no jet interaction under any marine condition.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「孔距與噴流合併」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Port spacing and jet merging”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-25-k1","title":"孔距與噴流合併機理與驗證","titleEn":"Port spacing and jet merging mechanism and verification","text":"相鄰射流會在擴展過程中互相影響，過早合併可能減少各自可捲吸的環境水，但是否有利不能只由孔距大小判斷。角度、交錯排列、海流與密度差會改變交會位置；單孔模型的稀釋結果也不能直接乘以孔數當成多孔系統的表現。","textEn":"Neighboring jets interact as they widen, and early merging can reduce ambient water available to each jet. Whether a layout is beneficial cannot be judged from spacing alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要孔距是孔徑十倍，就能保證任何海況下噴流不互相影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Spacing of ten diameters guarantees no jet interaction under any marine condition. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「孔距與噴流合併機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Port spacing and jet merging mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["只要孔距是孔徑十倍，就能保證任何海況下噴流不互相影響。","相鄰射流會在擴展過程中互相影響，過早合併可能減少各自可捲吸的環境水，但是否有利不能只由孔距大小判斷。","海流速度乘一小時得到的距離，就是鹵水必然被稀釋完的位置。"],"optionsEn":["Spacing of ten diameters guarantees no jet interaction under any marine condition.","Neighboring jets interact as they widen, and early merging can reduce ambient water available to each jet.","Current speed times one hour gives the distance at which brine is necessarily fully diluted."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相鄰射流會在擴展過程中互相影響，過早合併可能減少各自可捲吸的環境水，但是否有利不能只由孔距大小判斷。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Neighboring jets interact as they widen, and early merging can reduce ambient water available to each jet. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b267-v15-26","title":"孔距與噴流合併機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Port spacing and jet merging mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「孔距與噴流合併」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Port spacing and jet merging” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設中心孔距s=2.0 m、孔徑d=0.20 m，幾何比例s/d=10；若d增至0.22 m且s不變，比例為9.09。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume center spacing s=2.0 m and diameter d=0.20 m. Geometric s/d=10; increasing d to 0.22 m at fixed spacing gives 9.09. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以平面及剖面圖核對孔位和方向，使用適合多孔合併的模型或物理試驗觀察交互作用。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify port positions and directions in plan and section, using a model or physical experiment suited to multiport merging.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設中心孔距s=2.0 m、孔徑d=0.20 m，幾何比例s/d=10；若d增至0.22 m且s不變，比例為9.09。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume center spacing s=2.0 m and diameter d=0.20 m. Geometric s/d=10; increasing d to 0.22 m at fixed spacing gives 9.09.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「孔距與噴流合併機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Port spacing and jet merging mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["感測器讀值差很小，就能直接證明長期海域生態完全安全。","海水鹵水稀釋十倍就是把原始總鹽度直接除以十。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設中心孔距s=2.0 m、孔徑d=0.20 m，幾何比例s/d=10。"],"optionsEn":["A small sensor difference directly proves complete long-term ecological safety.","Tenfold seawater-brine dilution means dividing total original salinity by ten.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume center spacing s=2.0 m and diameter d=0.20 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設中心孔距s=2.0 m、孔徑d=0.20 m，幾何比例s/d=10；若d增至0.22 m且s不變，比例為9.09。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume center spacing s=2.0 m and diameter d=0.20 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b267-v15-27","title":"孔距與噴流合併機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Port spacing and jet merging mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「孔距與噴流合併」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Port spacing and jet merging” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以平面及剖面圖核對孔位和方向，使用適合多孔合併的模型或物理試驗觀察交互作用。檢查低潮、弱流及不同流向，並追蹤環境水可進入噴流間隙的路徑。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify port positions and directions in plan and section, using a model or physical experiment suited to multiport merging. Examine low tide, weak currents and changing current direction, tracking pathways through which ambient water can enter between adjacent jets. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出相同總長度的直列與交錯擴散器，指出可能的合併與捲吸區域。列出區分兩種布局所需的試驗觀察，而不是只用孔數或總長度選優。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw aligned and staggered diffusers of equal total length, marking possible merging and entrainment regions. Identify experimental observations that distinguish their behavior instead of selecting a layout solely by port count or overall length.","failure":"注意干擾：把某個孔距比例當通用保證可能漏掉回流與合併，部分孔停用後有效排列也會改變；沿用正常全開工況的稀釋率會掩蓋維護或低負荷的不利情境。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating one spacing ratio as a universal guarantee can miss recirculation and merging. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以平面及剖面圖核對孔位和方向，使用適合多孔合併的模型或物理試驗觀察交互作用。檢查低潮、弱流及不同流向，並追蹤環境水可進入噴流間隙的路徑。","textEn":"Verify port positions and directions in plan and section, using a model or physical experiment suited to multiport merging. Examine low tide, weak currents and changing current direction, tracking pathways through which ambient water can enter between adjacent jets.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出相同總長度的直列與交錯擴散器，指出可能的合併與捲吸區域。列出區分兩種布局所需的試驗觀察，而不是只用孔數或總長度選優。","textEn":"Draw aligned and staggered diffusers of equal total length, marking possible merging and entrainment regions. Identify experimental observations that distinguish their behavior instead of selecting a layout solely by port count or overall length.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「孔距與噴流合併機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Port spacing and jet merging mechanism and verification\"?","options":["以平面及剖面圖核對孔位和方向，使用適合多孔合併的模型或物理試驗觀察交互作用。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要鹽度較高，就可忽略溫度並沿用所有上浮羽流公式。"],"optionsEn":["Verify port positions and directions in plan and section, using a model or physical experiment suited to multiport merging.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Higher salinity allows temperature to be ignored and all rising-plume formulas reused."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以平面及剖面圖核對孔位和方向，使用適合多孔合併的模型或物理試驗觀察交互作用。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify port positions and directions in plan and section, using a model or physical experiment suited to multiport merging. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b267-v15-28","title":"孔距與噴流合併機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Port spacing and jet merging mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「孔距與噴流合併」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Port spacing and jet merging” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把某個孔距比例當通用保證可能漏掉回流與合併，部分孔停用後有效排列也會改變；沿用正常全開工況的稀釋率會掩蓋維護或低負荷的不利情境。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating one spacing ratio as a universal guarantee can miss recirculation and merging. Port shutdown changes the effective arrangement, so normal all-open dilution may conceal unfavorable maintenance or low-load conditions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：孔距除以孔徑只是幾何比較，不是通用的無干擾門檻；本例沒有預測合併高度或環境可接受性。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The example predicts neither merging height nor environmental acceptability.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要孔距是孔徑十倍，就能保證任何海況下噴流不互相影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Spacing of ten diameters guarantees no jet interaction under any marine condition.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把某個孔距比例當通用保證可能漏掉回流與合併，部分孔停用後有效排列也會改變；沿用正常全開工況的稀釋率會掩蓋維護或低負荷的不利情境。","textEn":"Treating one spacing ratio as a universal guarantee can miss recirculation and merging. Port shutdown changes the effective arrangement, so normal all-open dilution may conceal unfavorable maintenance or low-load conditions.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔距與噴流合併機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Port spacing and jet merging mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把某個孔距比例當通用保證可能漏掉回流與合併，部分孔停用後有效排列也會改變；沿用正常全開工況的稀釋率會掩蓋維護或低負荷的不利情境。","海流速度乘一小時得到的距離，就是鹵水必然被稀釋完的位置。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating one spacing ratio as a universal guarantee can miss recirculation and merging.","Current speed times one hour gives the distance at which brine is necessarily fully diluted."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把某個孔距比例當通用保證可能漏掉回流與合併，部分孔停用後有效排列也會改變；沿用正常全開工況的稀釋率會掩蓋維護或低負荷的不利情境。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating one spacing ratio as a universal guarantee can miss recirculation and merging. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b267-v15-29","title":"環境流與停留尺度機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ambient currents and residence scales mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「環境流與停留尺度」如何影響海水淡化鹵水擴散排放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ambient currents and residence scales” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brine diffuser outfalls for desalination”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"離開初始動量主導區後，羽流會受到海流、潮汐反轉及紊動輸送影響。以流速乘時間只能估計被動水團的平移尺度，不能描述密度流沿底滑動或回流累積；弱流時平均流向也可能不穩定，單一順流斷面可能漏掉往返經過的高鹽水。本例假設速度均勻且方向不變，忽略擴散、剪切及重力流；平移距離不是混合區邊界或鹽度達標距離。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「環境流與停留尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Beyond the initial momentum-dominated region, currents, tidal reversal and turbulence influence transport. Velocity times time estimates passive water-parcel translation but does not describe bottom density currents or recirculating accumulation. Under weak flow the mean direction may be unstable, and one downstream transect can miss concentrated water returning with the tide. The example assumes uniform constant-direction velocity, excluding dispersion, shear and gravity currents. Translation distance is neither a mixing-zone boundary nor a distance to a salinity target. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ambient currents and residence scales” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設均勻海流U=0.10 m/s、時間t=1800 s，被動平移尺度x=Ut=180 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume uniform current U=0.10 m/s and time t=1800 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「海流速度乘一小時得到的距離，就是鹵水必然被稀釋完的位置。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Current speed times one hour gives the distance at which brine is necessarily fully diluted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「環境流與停留尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ambient currents and residence scales”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-29-k1","title":"環境流與停留尺度機理與驗證","titleEn":"Ambient currents and residence scales mechanism and verification","text":"離開初始動量主導區後，羽流會受到海流、潮汐反轉及紊動輸送影響。以流速乘時間只能估計被動水團的平移尺度，不能描述密度流沿底滑動或回流累積；弱流時平均流向也可能不穩定，單一順流斷面可能漏掉往返經過的高鹽水。","textEn":"Beyond the initial momentum-dominated region, currents, tidal reversal and turbulence influence transport. Velocity times time estimates passive water-parcel translation but does not describe bottom density currents or recirculating accumulation.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：海流速度乘一小時得到的距離，就是鹵水必然被稀釋完的位置。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Current speed times one hour gives the distance at which brine is necessarily fully diluted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「環境流與停留尺度機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ambient currents and residence scales mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["海流速度乘一小時得到的距離，就是鹵水必然被稀釋完的位置。","排口附近混合很快，所以半封閉海灣的長期鹽量帳不必計算。","離開初始動量主導區後，羽流會受到海流、潮汐反轉及紊動輸送影響。"],"optionsEn":["Current speed times one hour gives the distance at which brine is necessarily fully diluted.","Rapid mixing near the outlet makes a long-term salt budget unnecessary in a semi-enclosed bay.","Beyond the initial momentum-dominated region, currents, tidal reversal and turbulence influence transport."],"answer":2,"explanation":"離開初始動量主導區後，羽流會受到海流、潮汐反轉及紊動輸送影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Beyond the initial momentum-dominated region, currents, tidal reversal and turbulence influence transport. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b267-v15-30","title":"環境流與停留尺度機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Ambient currents and residence scales mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「環境流與停留尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ambient currents and residence scales” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設均勻海流U=0.10 m/s、時間t=1800 s，被動平移尺度x=Ut=180 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume uniform current U=0.10 m/s and time t=1800 s. Passive translation scale x=Ut=180 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：使用涵蓋潮週期的流速剖面和溫鹽量測，區分平均流、剪切與短時反轉。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use velocity profiles and temperature-salinity measurements spanning tidal cycles to distinguish mean transport, shear and short reversals.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設均勻海流U=0.10 m/s、時間t=1800 s，被動平移尺度x=Ut=180 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume uniform current U=0.10 m/s and time t=1800 s. Passive translation scale x=Ut=180 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「環境流與停留尺度機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ambient currents and residence scales mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設均勻海流U=0.10 m/s、時間t=1800 s，被動平移尺度x=Ut=180 m。","提高產水回收率會讓剩下濃水中的總鹽量自行消失。","多孔擴散器的每個孔在所有流量和堵塞狀態下必定等量。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume uniform current U=0.10 m/s and time t=1800 s.","Higher water recovery makes the remaining concentrate salt disappear.","Every diffuser port carries equal flow at all discharges and blockage states."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設均勻海流U=0.10 m/s、時間t=1800 s，被動平移尺度x=Ut=180 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume uniform current U=0.10 m/s and time t=1800 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b267-v15-31","title":"環境流與停留尺度機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ambient currents and residence scales mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「環境流與停留尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ambient currents and residence scales” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"使用涵蓋潮週期的流速剖面和溫鹽量測，區分平均流、剪切與短時反轉。檢查近場與遠場銜接時的濃度、位置及通量連續性，另確認負浮力接觸海床後的模型適用性。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use velocity profiles and temperature-salinity measurements spanning tidal cycles to distinguish mean transport, shear and short reversals. Check concentration, position and flux continuity between near and far fields, separately confirming model validity after negatively buoyant flow contacts the seabed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較單向流與半小時後反轉的平移示意，說明相同速率不代表相同淨位移或暴露歷史。列出需要三維水動力與密度耦合分析的情境。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare one-way transport with a current reversing after half an hour, explaining why equal speed does not imply equal displacement or exposure history. Identify cases requiring three-dimensional hydrodynamics coupled to density.","failure":"注意干擾：只用最大順流速度會低估弱流期停留與累積，直接把上浮羽流的被動遠場模組接到沿底重流也可能違反模型假設，造成系統性低估暴露。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using only maximum favorable current understates residence and accumulation during weak flow. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"使用涵蓋潮週期的流速剖面和溫鹽量測，區分平均流、剪切與短時反轉。檢查近場與遠場銜接時的濃度、位置及通量連續性，另確認負浮力接觸海床後的模型適用性。","textEn":"Use velocity profiles and temperature-salinity measurements spanning tidal cycles to distinguish mean transport, shear and short reversals. Check concentration, position and flux continuity between near and far fields, separately confirming model validity after negatively buoyant flow contacts the seabed.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較單向流與半小時後反轉的平移示意，說明相同速率不代表相同淨位移或暴露歷史。列出需要三維水動力與密度耦合分析的情境。","textEn":"Compare one-way transport with a current reversing after half an hour, explaining why equal speed does not imply equal displacement or exposure history. Identify cases requiring three-dimensional hydrodynamics coupled to density.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「環境流與停留尺度機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ambient currents and residence scales mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","使用涵蓋潮週期的流速剖面和溫鹽量測，區分平均流、剪切與短時反轉。","密度福祿數等於最後稀釋倍數，而且越大就一定越環保。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Use velocity profiles and temperature-salinity measurements spanning tidal cycles to distinguish mean transport, shear and short reversals.","Densimetric Froude number equals final dilution and a larger value always means less impact."],"answer":1,"explanation":"使用涵蓋潮週期的流速剖面和溫鹽量測，區分平均流、剪切與短時反轉。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use velocity profiles and temperature-salinity measurements spanning tidal cycles to distinguish mean transport, shear and short reversals. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b267-v15-32","title":"環境流與停留尺度機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ambient currents and residence scales mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「環境流與停留尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ambient currents and residence scales” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只用最大順流速度會低估弱流期停留與累積，直接把上浮羽流的被動遠場模組接到沿底重流也可能違反模型假設，造成系統性低估暴露。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using only maximum favorable current understates residence and accumulation during weak flow. Connecting a passive far-field module for rising plumes directly to bottom gravity flow can violate assumptions and systematically understate exposure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例假設速度均勻且方向不變，忽略擴散、剪切及重力流；平移距離不是混合區邊界或鹽度達標距離。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Translation distance is neither a mixing-zone boundary nor a distance to a salinity target.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「海流速度乘一小時得到的距離，就是鹵水必然被稀釋完的位置。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Current speed times one hour gives the distance at which brine is necessarily fully diluted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只用最大順流速度會低估弱流期停留與累積，直接把上浮羽流的被動遠場模組接到沿底重流也可能違反模型假設，造成系統性低估暴露。","textEn":"Using only maximum favorable current understates residence and accumulation during weak flow. Connecting a passive far-field module for rising plumes directly to bottom gravity flow can violate assumptions and systematically understate exposure.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「環境流與停留尺度機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ambient currents and residence scales mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","排口附近混合很快，所以半封閉海灣的長期鹽量帳不必計算。","只用最大順流速度會低估弱流期停留與累積，直接把上浮羽流的被動遠場模組接到沿底重流也可能違反模型假設，造成系統性低估暴露。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Rapid mixing near the outlet makes a long-term salt budget unnecessary in a semi-enclosed bay.","Using only maximum favorable current understates residence and accumulation during weak flow."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只用最大順流速度會低估弱流期停留與累積，直接把上浮羽流的被動遠場模組接到沿底重流也可能違反模型假設，造成系統性低估暴露。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using only maximum favorable current understates residence and accumulation during weak flow. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b267-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「海域箱體鹽度收支機理與驗證」與「監測誤差與暴露判讀機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Receiving-basin salinity budget mechanism and verification\" and \"Monitoring uncertainty and exposure mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b267-v15-33","title":"海域箱體鹽度收支機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Receiving-basin salinity budget mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「海域箱體鹽度收支」如何影響海水淡化鹵水擴散排放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Receiving-basin salinity budget” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brine diffuser outfalls for desalination”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"近場高稀釋不代表半封閉水域不會長期累積鹽分，外海交換、潮汐回流與排放持續時間共同控制背景變化。簡化箱體可以檢查鹽量與交換流的尺度，卻把空間分層和局部高濃度平均掉；因此它適合守恆檢查，不適合取代底棲暴露或敏感區域的空間預測。本例以質量流率表示交換，箱體均勻且穩態，出流等於環境入流加排放；這不是忽略排放增量的近似交換式。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「海域箱體鹽度收支」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Strong near-field dilution does not prevent long-term salt accumulation in a semi-enclosed basin. Exchange with offshore water, tidal return and discharge duration control background change. A simple box checks salt and exchange scales but averages away stratification and local peaks, making it useful for conservation checks rather than spatial prediction of benthic exposure. The example uses mass flow, a uniform steady box, and outflow equal to ambient inflow plus discharge. It does not omit the additional discharged mass from the outlet balance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Receiving-basin salinity budget” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設外海入流Ma=9000 kg/s、Sa=35 g/kg，排放Mb=1000 kg/s、Sb=60 g/kg，穩態S=(MaSa+MbSb)/(Ma+Mb)=37.5 g/kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ambient inflow Ma=9000 kg/s, Sa=35 g/kg, discharge Mb=1000 kg/s and Sb=60 g/kg.","failure":"常見誤解：「排口附近混合很快，所以半封閉海灣的長期鹽量帳不必計算。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Rapid mixing near the outlet makes a long-term salt budget unnecessary in a semi-enclosed bay.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「海域箱體鹽度收支」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Receiving-basin salinity budget”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-33-k1","title":"海域箱體鹽度收支機理與驗證","titleEn":"Receiving-basin salinity budget mechanism and verification","text":"近場高稀釋不代表半封閉水域不會長期累積鹽分，外海交換、潮汐回流與排放持續時間共同控制背景變化。簡化箱體可以檢查鹽量與交換流的尺度，卻把空間分層和局部高濃度平均掉；因此它適合守恆檢查，不適合取代底棲暴露或敏感區域的空間預測。","textEn":"Strong near-field dilution does not prevent long-term salt accumulation in a semi-enclosed basin. Exchange with offshore water, tidal return and discharge duration control background change.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：排口附近混合很快，所以半封閉海灣的長期鹽量帳不必計算。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Rapid mixing near the outlet makes a long-term salt budget unnecessary in a semi-enclosed bay. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「海域箱體鹽度收支機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Receiving-basin salinity budget mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["近場高稀釋不代表半封閉水域不會長期累積鹽分，外海交換、潮汐回流與排放持續時間共同控制背景變化。","排口附近混合很快，所以半封閉海灣的長期鹽量帳不必計算。","感測器讀值差很小，就能直接證明長期海域生態完全安全。"],"optionsEn":["Strong near-field dilution does not prevent long-term salt accumulation in a semi-enclosed basin.","Rapid mixing near the outlet makes a long-term salt budget unnecessary in a semi-enclosed bay.","A small sensor difference directly proves complete long-term ecological safety."],"answer":0,"explanation":"近場高稀釋不代表半封閉水域不會長期累積鹽分，外海交換、潮汐回流與排放持續時間共同控制背景變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Strong near-field dilution does not prevent long-term salt accumulation in a semi-enclosed basin. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b267-v15-34","title":"海域箱體鹽度收支機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Receiving-basin salinity budget mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「海域箱體鹽度收支」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Receiving-basin salinity budget” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設外海入流Ma=9000 kg/s、Sa=35 g/kg，排放Mb=1000 kg/s、Sb=60 g/kg，穩態S=(MaSa+MbSb)/(Ma+Mb)=37.5 g/kg。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ambient inflow Ma=9000 kg/s, Sa=35 g/kg, discharge Mb=1000 kg/s and Sb=60 g/kg. Steady box S=(MaSa+MbSb)/(Ma+Mb)=37.5 g/kg. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先核對箱體水量與鹽量收支，確認外海交換不是重複計入同一來回潮水。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check both water and salt balances, ensuring that offshore exchange does not count the same returning tidal water twice.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設外海入流Ma=9000 kg/s、Sa=35 g/kg，排放Mb=1000 kg/s、Sb=60 g/kg，穩態S=(MaSa+MbSb)/(Ma+Mb)=37.5 g/kg。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ambient inflow Ma=9000 kg/s, Sa=35 g/kg, discharge Mb=1000 kg/s and Sb=60 g/kg. Steady box S=(MaSa+MbSb)/(Ma+Mb)=37.5 g/kg.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「海域箱體鹽度收支機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Receiving-basin salinity budget mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["海水鹵水稀釋十倍就是把原始總鹽度直接除以十。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設外海入流Ma=9000 kg/s、Sa=35 g/kg，排放Mb=1000 kg/s、Sb=60 g/kg，穩態S=(MaSa+MbSb)/(Ma+Mb)=37.5 g/kg。","只要鹽度較高，就可忽略溫度並沿用所有上浮羽流公式。"],"optionsEn":["Tenfold seawater-brine dilution means dividing total original salinity by ten.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ambient inflow Ma=9000 kg/s, Sa=35 g/kg, discharge Mb=1000 kg/s and Sb=60 g/kg.","Higher salinity allows temperature to be ignored and all rising-plume formulas reused."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設外海入流Ma=9000 kg/s、Sa=35 g/kg，排放Mb=1000 kg/s、Sb=60 g/kg，穩態S=(MaSa+MbSb)/(Ma+Mb)=37.5 g/kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ambient inflow Ma=9000 kg/s, Sa=35 g/kg, discharge Mb=1000 kg/s and Sb=60 g/kg. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b267-v15-35","title":"海域箱體鹽度收支機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Receiving-basin salinity budget mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「海域箱體鹽度收支」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Receiving-basin salinity budget” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先核對箱體水量與鹽量收支，確認外海交換不是重複計入同一來回潮水。用多深度長時間觀測測試均勻穩態假設，並對交換減弱及初始鹽度做敏感度比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check both water and salt balances, ensuring that offshore exchange does not count the same returning tidal water twice. Test uniform steady conditions against long-duration measurements at several depths, and compare sensitivity to weaker exchange and different initial salinity. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以固定排放分別計算強弱交換情境，畫出完整入出流而非只列超額鹽量。指出箱體平均無法回答哪些底棲問題，並提出可觀察分層的測點配置。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate strong and weak exchange cases at fixed discharge, drawing all inflows and outflows rather than only excess salt. Identify benthic questions that a box average cannot answer and propose measurements capable of detecting stratification.","failure":"注意干擾：把潮汐往返總流量全當新鮮外海交換會高估沖淡能力，均勻箱體也會掩蓋沿底鹽層；近場校正良好仍不能證明長期區域背景不會改變。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating all back-and-forth tidal flow as fresh offshore exchange overstates flushing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先核對箱體水量與鹽量收支，確認外海交換不是重複計入同一來回潮水。用多深度長時間觀測測試均勻穩態假設，並對交換減弱及初始鹽度做敏感度比較。","textEn":"Check both water and salt balances, ensuring that offshore exchange does not count the same returning tidal water twice. Test uniform steady conditions against long-duration measurements at several depths, and compare sensitivity to weaker exchange and different initial salinity.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以固定排放分別計算強弱交換情境，畫出完整入出流而非只列超額鹽量。指出箱體平均無法回答哪些底棲問題，並提出可觀察分層的測點配置。","textEn":"Calculate strong and weak exchange cases at fixed discharge, drawing all inflows and outflows rather than only excess salt. Identify benthic questions that a box average cannot answer and propose measurements capable of detecting stratification.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「海域箱體鹽度收支機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Receiving-basin salinity budget mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","流量乘速度已經是牛頓力，而且所有噴口反力只須加大小。","先核對箱體水量與鹽量收支，確認外海交換不是重複計入同一來回潮水。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Flow times velocity is already force in newtons and port reactions require only scalar addition.","Check both water and salt balances, ensuring that offshore exchange does not count the same returning tidal water twice."],"answer":2,"explanation":"先核對箱體水量與鹽量收支，確認外海交換不是重複計入同一來回潮水。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check both water and salt balances, ensuring that offshore exchange does not count the same returning tidal water twice. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b267-v15-36","title":"海域箱體鹽度收支機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Receiving-basin salinity budget mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「海域箱體鹽度收支」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Receiving-basin salinity budget” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把潮汐往返總流量全當新鮮外海交換會高估沖淡能力，均勻箱體也會掩蓋沿底鹽層；近場校正良好仍不能證明長期區域背景不會改變。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating all back-and-forth tidal flow as fresh offshore exchange overstates flushing. A uniform box also hides bottom salinity layers, and successful near-field calibration does not prove that regional background remains unchanged over time. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例以質量流率表示交換，箱體均勻且穩態，出流等於環境入流加排放；這不是忽略排放增量的近似交換式。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It does not omit the additional discharged mass from the outlet balance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「排口附近混合很快，所以半封閉海灣的長期鹽量帳不必計算。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Rapid mixing near the outlet makes a long-term salt budget unnecessary in a semi-enclosed bay.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把潮汐往返總流量全當新鮮外海交換會高估沖淡能力，均勻箱體也會掩蓋沿底鹽層；近場校正良好仍不能證明長期區域背景不會改變。","textEn":"Treating all back-and-forth tidal flow as fresh offshore exchange overstates flushing. A uniform box also hides bottom salinity layers, and successful near-field calibration does not prove that regional background remains unchanged over time.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「海域箱體鹽度收支機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Receiving-basin salinity budget mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把潮汐往返總流量全當新鮮外海交換會高估沖淡能力，均勻箱體也會掩蓋沿底鹽層；近場校正良好仍不能證明長期區域背景不會改變。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","感測器讀值差很小，就能直接證明長期海域生態完全安全。"],"optionsEn":["Treating all back-and-forth tidal flow as fresh offshore exchange overstates flushing.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A small sensor difference directly proves complete long-term ecological safety."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把潮汐往返總流量全當新鮮外海交換會高估沖淡能力，均勻箱體也會掩蓋沿底鹽層；近場校正良好仍不能證明長期區域背景不會改變。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating all back-and-forth tidal flow as fresh offshore exchange overstates flushing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b267-v15-37","title":"監測誤差與暴露判讀機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Monitoring uncertainty and exposure mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「監測誤差與暴露判讀」如何影響海水淡化鹵水擴散排放的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Monitoring uncertainty and exposure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Brine diffuser outfalls for desalination”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"鹽度監測需要同時控制感測器校正、溫度補償、深度定位與時間對齊，否則小幅鹽度增量可能與量測偏差混淆。單點超額鹽度不能直接代表整個生態系的暴露，還必須關注持續時間、空間範圍與背景變化；不確定度的合成也取決於誤差是否獨立。下式只合成兩個獨立標準不確定度，未加涵蓋因子或系統漂移；它不是法定容許誤差，也不是生態效應門檻。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「監測誤差與暴露判讀」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Salinity monitoring requires calibration, temperature compensation, depth control and synchronized timing, because a small salinity increment can be confused with measurement bias. One-point excess salinity does not represent exposure of the entire ecosystem; duration, spatial extent and background variation also matter. Combining uncertainty requires attention to whether errors are independent. The expression combines two independent standard uncertainties only, without a coverage factor or systematic drift. It is neither a legal tolerance nor an ecological-effect threshold. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Monitoring uncertainty and exposure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排口樣本與背景標準不確定度各u1=u2=0.10 g/kg且獨立，差值uΔ=√(u1²+u2²)=0.1414 g/kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent sample and background standard uncertainties u1=u2=0.10 g/kg.","failure":"常見誤解：「感測器讀值差很小，就能直接證明長期海域生態完全安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small sensor difference directly proves complete long-term ecological safety.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「監測誤差與暴露判讀」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Monitoring uncertainty and exposure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-37-k1","title":"監測誤差與暴露判讀機理與驗證","titleEn":"Monitoring uncertainty and exposure mechanism and verification","text":"鹽度監測需要同時控制感測器校正、溫度補償、深度定位與時間對齊，否則小幅鹽度增量可能與量測偏差混淆。單點超額鹽度不能直接代表整個生態系的暴露，還必須關注持續時間、空間範圍與背景變化；不確定度的合成也取決於誤差是否獨立。","textEn":"Salinity monitoring requires calibration, temperature compensation, depth control and synchronized timing, because a small salinity increment can be confused with measurement bias. One-point excess salinity does not represent exposure of the entire ecosystem; duration, spatial extent and background variation also matter.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：感測器讀值差很小，就能直接證明長期海域生態完全安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small sensor difference directly proves complete long-term ecological safety. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「監測誤差與暴露判讀機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Monitoring uncertainty and exposure mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["感測器讀值差很小，就能直接證明長期海域生態完全安全。","鹽度監測需要同時控制感測器校正、溫度補償、深度定位與時間對齊，否則小幅鹽度增量可能與量測偏差混淆。","提高產水回收率會讓剩下濃水中的總鹽量自行消失。"],"optionsEn":["A small sensor difference directly proves complete long-term ecological safety.","Salinity monitoring requires calibration, temperature compensation, depth control and synchronized timing, because a small salinity increment can be confused with measurement bias.","Higher water recovery makes the remaining concentrate salt disappear."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鹽度監測需要同時控制感測器校正、溫度補償、深度定位與時間對齊，否則小幅鹽度增量可能與量測偏差混淆。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Salinity monitoring requires calibration, temperature compensation, depth control and synchronized timing, because a small salinity increment can be confused with measurement bias. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b267-v15-38","title":"監測誤差與暴露判讀機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Monitoring uncertainty and exposure mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「監測誤差與暴露判讀」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Monitoring uncertainty and exposure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排口樣本與背景標準不確定度各u1=u2=0.10 g/kg且獨立，差值uΔ=√(u1²+u2²)=0.1414 g/kg。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent sample and background standard uncertainties u1=u2=0.10 g/kg. Difference uncertainty uΔ=√(u1²+u2²)=0.1414 g/kg. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將校正前後結果、重複樣本與定位資料保留，核對兩儀器是否共享偏差來源。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Retain before-and-after calibration, duplicate samples and positioning records, checking whether instruments share bias sources.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排口樣本與背景標準不確定度各u1=u2=0.10 g/kg且獨立，差值uΔ=√(u1²+u2²)=0.1414 g/kg。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent sample and background standard uncertainties u1=u2=0.10 g/kg. Difference uncertainty uΔ=√(u1²+u2²)=0.1414 g/kg.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「監測誤差與暴露判讀機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Monitoring uncertainty and exposure mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["多孔擴散器的每個孔在所有流量和堵塞狀態下必定等量。","密度福祿數等於最後稀釋倍數，而且越大就一定越環保。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排口樣本與背景標準不確定度各u1=u2=0.10 g/kg且獨立，差值uΔ=√(u1²+u2²)=0.1414 g/kg。"],"optionsEn":["Every diffuser port carries equal flow at all discharges and blockage states.","Densimetric Froude number equals final dilution and a larger value always means less impact.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent sample and background standard uncertainties u1=u2=0.10 g/kg."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排口樣本與背景標準不確定度各u1=u2=0.10 g/kg且獨立，差值uΔ=√(u1²+u2²)=0.1414 g/kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent sample and background standard uncertainties u1=u2=0.10 g/kg. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b267-v15-39","title":"監測誤差與暴露判讀機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Monitoring uncertainty and exposure mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「監測誤差與暴露判讀」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Monitoring uncertainty and exposure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將校正前後結果、重複樣本與定位資料保留，核對兩儀器是否共享偏差來源。以相同潮相和深度比較背景及影響區，並把量測不確定度、暴露持續時間與生態證據分開報告。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Retain before-and-after calibration, duplicate samples and positioning records, checking whether instruments share bias sources. Compare background and affected locations at matched tidal phase and depth, reporting measurement uncertainty, exposure duration and ecological evidence as distinct components of the assessment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：為兩支感測器列出獨立與共同誤差來源，說明哪些可以平方和合成。設計跨潮位、深度與時間的對照採樣表，將濃度證據和生態解釋清楚分欄。","observationEn":"Site practice: List independent and shared error sources for two sensors and identify which support root-sum-square combination. Design paired sampling across tide, depth and time, keeping concentration evidence separate from ecological interpretation.","failure":"注意干擾：共同校正偏差不一定符合獨立平方和假設，漂移也不會靠增加樣本自動消失；將短時單點差異直接描述成長期生態安全或危害，會超出資料支持範圍。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Shared calibration bias may violate the independent root-sum-square assumption, and drift does not vanish automatically with more samples. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將校正前後結果、重複樣本與定位資料保留，核對兩儀器是否共享偏差來源。以相同潮相和深度比較背景及影響區，並把量測不確定度、暴露持續時間與生態證據分開報告。","textEn":"Retain before-and-after calibration, duplicate samples and positioning records, checking whether instruments share bias sources. Compare background and affected locations at matched tidal phase and depth, reporting measurement uncertainty, exposure duration and ecological evidence as distinct components of the assessment.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"為兩支感測器列出獨立與共同誤差來源，說明哪些可以平方和合成。設計跨潮位、深度與時間的對照採樣表，將濃度證據和生態解釋清楚分欄。","textEn":"List independent and shared error sources for two sensors and identify which support root-sum-square combination. Design paired sampling across tide, depth and time, keeping concentration evidence separate from ecological interpretation.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「監測誤差與暴露判讀機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Monitoring uncertainty and exposure mechanism and verification\"?","options":["將校正前後結果、重複樣本與定位資料保留，核對兩儀器是否共享偏差來源。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要孔距是孔徑十倍，就能保證任何海況下噴流不互相影響。"],"optionsEn":["Retain before-and-after calibration, duplicate samples and positioning records, checking whether instruments share bias sources.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Spacing of ten diameters guarantees no jet interaction under any marine condition."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將校正前後結果、重複樣本與定位資料保留，核對兩儀器是否共享偏差來源。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Retain before-and-after calibration, duplicate samples and positioning records, checking whether instruments share bias sources. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b267-v15-40","title":"監測誤差與暴露判讀機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Monitoring uncertainty and exposure mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"prerequisiteIds":["b267-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「監測誤差與暴露判讀」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Monitoring uncertainty and exposure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"共同校正偏差不一定符合獨立平方和假設，漂移也不會靠增加樣本自動消失；將短時單點差異直接描述成長期生態安全或危害，會超出資料支持範圍。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Shared calibration bias may violate the independent root-sum-square assumption, and drift does not vanish automatically with more samples. Calling a brief point difference evidence of long-term ecological safety or harm exceeds the observations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：下式只合成兩個獨立標準不確定度，未加涵蓋因子或系統漂移；它不是法定容許誤差，也不是生態效應門檻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It is neither a legal tolerance nor an ecological-effect threshold.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「感測器讀值差很小，就能直接證明長期海域生態完全安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small sensor difference directly proves complete long-term ecological safety.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b267-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共同校正偏差不一定符合獨立平方和假設，漂移也不會靠增加樣本自動消失；將短時單點差異直接描述成長期生態安全或危害，會超出資料支持範圍。","textEn":"Shared calibration bias may violate the independent root-sum-square assumption, and drift does not vanish automatically with more samples. Calling a brief point difference evidence of long-term ecological safety or harm exceeds the observations.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]},{"id":"b267-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「監測誤差與暴露判讀機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Monitoring uncertainty and exposure mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","共同校正偏差不一定符合獨立平方和假設，漂移也不會靠增加樣本自動消失；將短時單點差異直接描述成長期生態安全或危害，會超出資料支持範圍。","提高產水回收率會讓剩下濃水中的總鹽量自行消失。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Shared calibration bias may violate the independent root-sum-square assumption, and drift does not vanish automatically with more samples.","Higher water recovery makes the remaining concentrate salt disappear."],"answer":1,"explanation":"共同校正偏差不一定符合獨立平方和假設，漂移也不會靠增加樣本自動消失；將短時單點差異直接描述成長期生態安全或危害，會超出資料支持範圍。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Shared calibration bias may violate the independent root-sum-square assumption, and drift does not vanish automatically with more samples. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-plumes","v15s-cal-desal","v15s-wc-perth","v15s-wc-southern"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b268","title":"河岸取水口防淤設計","titleEn":"Sediment-resistant river intake design","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"課程由季節分流和泥砂輸入開始，逐步分析沉降、沉砂面積、起動剪應力、篩網方向與沖砂水量，再以庫容和縮尺試驗建立可驗證的維護策略。紅崖與弗里波特提供真實取水工程背景，所有量值為獨立教學假設，不把水理比較當成魚類保護、許可或現場操作判定。","summaryEn":"Starting with seasonal diversion and sediment input, the course develops settling, basin area, incipient-motion stress, screen orientation and flushing-volume analyses, then connects storage and scale experiments to verifiable maintenance planning. Red Bluff and Freeport provide real intake context. Numerical values are independent assumptions, and hydraulic comparisons do not establish fish protection, permission or field operating decisions.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-pipe","architectureNodes":[["河川工況","River states"],["泥砂輸入","Sediment input"],["取水篩網","Intake screen"],["沖砂與庫容","Flushing and storage"],["現地驗證","Field verification"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]],"diagram":{"type":"water-pipe","labels":["河川工況","泥砂輸入","取水篩網","沖砂與庫容","現地驗證"],"labelsEn":["River states","Sediment input","Intake screen","Flushing and storage","Field verification"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"敏感度以稀薄、不絮凝球形顆粒的斯托克斯模型為基準，水黏度0.001 Pa·s、顆粒及水密度2650與1000 kg/m³。粒徑由20 μm增至22 μm，只增加10%，沉降速度卻由0.0003597增至0.0004352 m/s，增加21%；顆粒雷諾數由0.00719增至0.00958，仍符合此理想低雷諾數比較。這不能代表絮凝泥或實際沉砂率，因為粒徑分布、短路和再懸浮未納入。若改變粒徑到粗砂，必須重新檢查阻力流態，而不是繼續使用平方比例。","textEn":"Use the Stokes model for dilute, nonflocculating spheres with viscosity 0.001 Pa·s and particle/water densities 2650 and 1000 kg/m³. Increasing diameter from 20 to 22 μm is only a ten-percent change, but settling speed increases from 0.0003597 to 0.0004352 m/s, or 21%. Particle Reynolds number rises from 0.00719 to 0.00958, remaining small for this ideal comparison. This is not a prediction of flocculating mud or actual basin removal, because size distributions, short-circuiting and resuspension are excluded. Moving to coarse sand requires a fresh drag-regime check rather than continued use of the squared-diameter scaling.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b268-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證」與「懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification\" and \"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b268-v15-01","title":"引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「引水比例與季節工況」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diversion fraction and seasonal states” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"河岸取水會改變局部分流與近岸流線，防淤設計必須同時考慮供水、河川剩餘流量與魚類通行。洪水期高含砂不一定和最大取水量同時發生，枯水期則可能暴露取水門檻或降低掃流。單一設計流量會掩蓋季節差異，應用成組水位、流量和泥砂資料描述實際可能的工況。本例只是整體水量分配，沒有推導局部流線或可容許取水比例；下游需求與許可條件須另由實際資料確認。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「引水比例與季節工況」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A river intake alters local flow division and near-bank streamlines, linking sediment management to supply, remaining river flow and fish passage. High flood sediment does not necessarily coincide with maximum diversion, while low water may expose the sill or weaken sweeping flow. One design discharge hides seasonal differences; paired stage, flow and sediment records should define physically plausible operating states. The example is a bulk flow allocation, not a prediction of local streamlines or an allowable diversion fraction. Downstream requirements and permission conditions need separate evidence. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diversion fraction and seasonal states” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設河流Qr=80 m³/s、取水Qd=8 m³/s，引水比r=Qd/Qr=0.10，忽略其他支流後剩餘72 m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume river Qr=80 m³/s and diversion Qd=8 m³/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「引水比例與季節工況」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diversion fraction and seasonal states”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-01-k1","title":"引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證","titleEn":"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification","text":"河岸取水會改變局部分流與近岸流線，防淤設計必須同時考慮供水、河川剩餘流量與魚類通行。洪水期高含砂不一定和最大取水量同時發生，枯水期則可能暴露取水門檻或降低掃流。","textEn":"A river intake alters local flow division and near-bank streamlines, linking sediment management to supply, remaining river flow and fish passage. High flood sediment does not necessarily coincide with maximum diversion, while low water may expose the sill or weaken sweeping flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。","河岸取水會改變局部分流與近岸流線，防淤設計必須同時考慮供水、河川剩餘流量與魚類通行。","取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。"],"optionsEn":["Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary.","A river intake alters local flow division and near-bank streamlines, linking sediment management to supply, remaining river flow and fish passage.","With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input."],"answer":1,"explanation":"河岸取水會改變局部分流與近岸流線，防淤設計必須同時考慮供水、河川剩餘流量與魚類通行。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A river intake alters local flow division and near-bank streamlines, linking sediment management to supply, remaining river flow and fish passage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b268-v15-02","title":"引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「引水比例與季節工況」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diversion fraction and seasonal states” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設河流Qr=80 m³/s、取水Qd=8 m³/s，引水比r=Qd/Qr=0.10，忽略其他支流後剩餘72 m³/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume river Qr=80 m³/s and diversion Qd=8 m³/s. Fraction r=Qd/Qr=0.10, leaving 72 m³/s when other streams are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將取水紀錄與同時河川流量配對，分別整理枯水、常水及洪水事件。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pair diversion records with simultaneous river flow and separate low, ordinary and flood events.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設河流Qr=80 m³/s、取水Qd=8 m³/s，引水比r=Qd/Qr=0.10，忽略其他支流後剩餘72 m³/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume river Qr=80 m³/s and diversion Qd=8 m³/s. Fraction r=Qd/Qr=0.10, leaving 72 m³/s when other streams are excluded.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。","均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設河流Qr=80 m³/s、取水Qd=8 m³/s，引水比r=Qd/Qr=0.10，忽略其他支流後剩餘72 m³/s。"],"optionsEn":["A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size.","Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume river Qr=80 m³/s and diversion Qd=8 m³/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設河流Qr=80 m³/s、取水Qd=8 m³/s，引水比r=Qd/Qr=0.10，忽略其他支流後剩餘72 m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume river Qr=80 m³/s and diversion Qd=8 m³/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b268-v15-03","title":"引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「引水比例與季節工況」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Diversion fraction and seasonal states” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將取水紀錄與同時河川流量配對，分別整理枯水、常水及洪水事件。核對上游支流與下游量測的控制體，避免用不同時刻的流量計算分流比，再驗證門檻高程是否仍淹沒。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pair diversion records with simultaneous river flow and separate low, ordinary and flood events. Check tributaries and downstream measurement control volumes, avoiding ratios formed from different times, then verify whether the intake sill remains submerged in each selected state. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：製作三種季節工況表，為每列填入同時水位、流量與濃度。將資料缺口列出，說明哪種缺測會妨礙判斷淹沒、泥砂或魚類掃流條件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Create three seasonal scenarios with simultaneous stage, discharge and concentration. Identify missing observations and explain which gaps prevent assessment of submergence, sediment behavior or fish-guiding sweeping flow.","failure":"注意干擾：用年平均流量判斷取水比例會掩蓋枯水壓力，將洪水流量和低水位拼接則可能形成不可能工況；未檢查剩餘流量也會把防淤效率與河川功能割裂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An annual mean conceals low-flow pressure, while combining flood discharge with unrelated low stage may create an impossible scenario. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將取水紀錄與同時河川流量配對，分別整理枯水、常水及洪水事件。核對上游支流與下游量測的控制體，避免用不同時刻的流量計算分流比，再驗證門檻高程是否仍淹沒。","textEn":"Pair diversion records with simultaneous river flow and separate low, ordinary and flood events. Check tributaries and downstream measurement control volumes, avoiding ratios formed from different times, then verify whether the intake sill remains submerged in each selected state.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"製作三種季節工況表，為每列填入同時水位、流量與濃度。將資料缺口列出，說明哪種缺測會妨礙判斷淹沒、泥砂或魚類掃流條件。","textEn":"Create three seasonal scenarios with simultaneous stage, discharge and concentration. Identify missing observations and explain which gaps prevent assessment of submergence, sediment behavior or fish-guiding sweeping flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification\"?","options":["將取水紀錄與同時河川流量配對，分別整理枯水、常水及洪水事件。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。"],"optionsEn":["Pair diversion records with simultaneous river flow and separate low, ordinary and flood events.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將取水紀錄與同時河川流量配對，分別整理枯水、常水及洪水事件。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pair diversion records with simultaneous river flow and separate low, ordinary and flood events. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b268-v15-04","title":"引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「引水比例與季節工況」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Diversion fraction and seasonal states” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用年平均流量判斷取水比例會掩蓋枯水壓力，將洪水流量和低水位拼接則可能形成不可能工況；未檢查剩餘流量也會把防淤效率與河川功能割裂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An annual mean conceals low-flow pressure, while combining flood discharge with unrelated low stage may create an impossible scenario. Omitting remaining flow also separates sediment performance from the river functions affected by diversion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例只是整體水量分配，沒有推導局部流線或可容許取水比例；下游需求與許可條件須另由實際資料確認。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Downstream requirements and permission conditions need separate evidence.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用年平均流量判斷取水比例會掩蓋枯水壓力，將洪水流量和低水位拼接則可能形成不可能工況；未檢查剩餘流量也會把防淤效率與河川功能割裂。","textEn":"An annual mean conceals low-flow pressure, while combining flood discharge with unrelated low stage may create an impossible scenario. Omitting remaining flow also separates sediment performance from the river functions affected by diversion.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","用年平均流量判斷取水比例會掩蓋枯水壓力，將洪水流量和低水位拼接則可能形成不可能工況；未檢查剩餘流量也會把防淤效率與河川功能割裂。","取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","An annual mean conceals low-flow pressure, while combining flood discharge with unrelated low stage may create an impossible scenario.","With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用年平均流量判斷取水比例會掩蓋枯水壓力，將洪水流量和低水位拼接則可能形成不可能工況；未檢查剩餘流量也會把防淤效率與河川功能割裂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An annual mean conceals low-flow pressure, while combining flood discharge with unrelated low stage may create an impossible scenario. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b268-v15-05","title":"懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「懸移質輸入帳」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Suspended-sediment input budget” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"進入取水口的懸移質負荷由濃度和流量共同決定，短時高濃度事件可能主導全年清淤量。濁度只有在與現地懸浮固體校正後才能作代理量，粒徑和顏色改變會破壞單一關係；底床推移質另有運移途徑，不能把懸移質帳當成完整泥砂預算。本例假設濃度在事件內固定並代表截面流量加權平均，未含推移質或取水選擇性；事件質量不等於全部沉積量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「懸移質輸入帳」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Suspended load entering an intake depends on both concentration and discharge, and brief sediment pulses may dominate maintenance demand. Turbidity becomes a proxy only after local calibration against suspended solids; changing size or color can alter that relation. Bed material has a separate transport pathway, so a suspended-load ledger is not a complete sediment budget. The example assumes constant event concentration representative of a flow-weighted section mean, excluding bed load and selective withdrawal. Event mass is not the mass necessarily deposited. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Suspended-sediment input budget” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=2.0 m³/s、C=0.30 kg/m³、事件t=3600 s，輸入泥砂M=QCt=2160 kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=2.0 m³/s, concentration C=0.30 kg/m³ and duration t=3600 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「懸移質輸入帳」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Suspended-sediment input budget”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-05-k1","title":"懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證","titleEn":"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification","text":"進入取水口的懸移質負荷由濃度和流量共同決定，短時高濃度事件可能主導全年清淤量。濁度只有在與現地懸浮固體校正後才能作代理量，粒徑和顏色改變會破壞單一關係；底床推移質另有運移途徑，不能把懸移質帳當成完整泥砂預算。","textEn":"Suspended load entering an intake depends on both concentration and discharge, and brief sediment pulses may dominate maintenance demand. Turbidity becomes a proxy only after local calibration against suspended solids; changing size or color can alter that relation.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。","斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。","進入取水口的懸移質負荷由濃度和流量共同決定，短時高濃度事件可能主導全年清淤量。"],"optionsEn":["With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input.","Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration.","Suspended load entering an intake depends on both concentration and discharge, and brief sediment pulses may dominate maintenance demand."],"answer":2,"explanation":"進入取水口的懸移質負荷由濃度和流量共同決定，短時高濃度事件可能主導全年清淤量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Suspended load entering an intake depends on both concentration and discharge, and brief sediment pulses may dominate maintenance demand. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b268-v15-06","title":"懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「懸移質輸入帳」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Suspended-sediment input budget” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=2.0 m³/s、C=0.30 kg/m³、事件t=3600 s，輸入泥砂M=QCt=2160 kg。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=2.0 m³/s, concentration C=0.30 kg/m³ and duration t=3600 s. Incoming sediment M=QCt=2160 kg. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：於上升和退水段採樣並與流量同步，檢查濁度關係是否隨事件或粒徑改變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample rising and falling limbs with synchronized discharge, checking whether turbidity calibration changes by event or grain size.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=2.0 m³/s、C=0.30 kg/m³、事件t=3600 s，輸入泥砂M=QCt=2160 kg。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=2.0 m³/s, concentration C=0.30 kg/m³ and duration t=3600 s. Incoming sediment M=QCt=2160 kg.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=2.0 m³/s、C=0.30 kg/m³、事件t=3600 s，輸入泥砂M=QCt=2160 kg。","床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。","沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=2.0 m³/s, concentration C=0.30 kg/m³ and duration t=3600 s.","Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition.","Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=2.0 m³/s、C=0.30 kg/m³、事件t=3600 s，輸入泥砂M=QCt=2160 kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=2.0 m³/s, concentration C=0.30 kg/m³ and duration t=3600 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b268-v15-07","title":"懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「懸移質輸入帳」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Suspended-sediment input budget” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"於上升和退水段採樣並與流量同步，檢查濁度關係是否隨事件或粒徑改變。對截面不均勻性與取樣代表性作紀錄，再以進出質量和清淤紀錄核對累積結果。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample rising and falling limbs with synchronized discharge, checking whether turbidity calibration changes by event or grain size. Document section nonuniformity and sampling representation, then compare cumulative inputs and outputs with recovered sediment records to evaluate the budget. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用分段濃度序列計算事件質量，與平均濃度乘總體積比較。指出哪個平均必須按流量加權，並將未計入的推移質列為獨立資料需求。","observationEn":"Site practice: Integrate a segmented concentration series and compare it with mean concentration times total volume. Identify the average requiring flow weighting and list excluded bed load as an independent data requirement.","failure":"注意干擾：以單次低濁度樣本外推整場洪水會漏掉峰值負荷，直接把輸入質量全當沉積又會忽略穿越出流；兩種誤差可能相反但不能假設互相抵消。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Extrapolating one low-turbidity sample misses event peaks, while treating all incoming mass as deposited ignores sediment passing through. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"於上升和退水段採樣並與流量同步，檢查濁度關係是否隨事件或粒徑改變。對截面不均勻性與取樣代表性作紀錄，再以進出質量和清淤紀錄核對累積結果。","textEn":"Sample rising and falling limbs with synchronized discharge, checking whether turbidity calibration changes by event or grain size. Document section nonuniformity and sampling representation, then compare cumulative inputs and outputs with recovered sediment records to evaluate the budget.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用分段濃度序列計算事件質量，與平均濃度乘總體積比較。指出哪個平均必須按流量加權，並將未計入的推移質列為獨立資料需求。","textEn":"Integrate a segmented concentration series and compare it with mean concentration times total volume. Identify the average requiring flow weighting and list excluded bed load as an independent data requirement.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","於上升和退水段採樣並與流量同步，檢查濁度關係是否隨事件或粒徑改變。","清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Sample rising and falling limbs with synchronized discharge, checking whether turbidity calibration changes by event or grain size.","Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys."],"answer":1,"explanation":"於上升和退水段採樣並與流量同步，檢查濁度關係是否隨事件或粒徑改變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample rising and falling limbs with synchronized discharge, checking whether turbidity calibration changes by event or grain size. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b268-v15-08","title":"懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「懸移質輸入帳」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Suspended-sediment input budget” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以單次低濁度樣本外推整場洪水會漏掉峰值負荷，直接把輸入質量全當沉積又會忽略穿越出流；兩種誤差可能相反但不能假設互相抵消。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Extrapolating one low-turbidity sample misses event peaks, while treating all incoming mass as deposited ignores sediment passing through. These errors can oppose each other but cannot be assumed to cancel. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例假設濃度在事件內固定並代表截面流量加權平均，未含推移質或取水選擇性；事件質量不等於全部沉積量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Event mass is not the mass necessarily deposited.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以單次低濁度樣本外推整場洪水會漏掉峰值負荷，直接把輸入質量全當沉積又會忽略穿越出流；兩種誤差可能相反但不能假設互相抵消。","textEn":"Extrapolating one low-turbidity sample misses event peaks, while treating all incoming mass as deposited ignores sediment passing through. These errors can oppose each other but cannot be assumed to cancel.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。","以單次低濁度樣本外推整場洪水會漏掉峰值負荷，直接把輸入質量全當沉積又會忽略穿越出流；兩種誤差可能相反但不能假設互相抵消。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration.","Extrapolating one low-turbidity sample misses event peaks, while treating all incoming mass as deposited ignores sediment passing through."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以單次低濁度樣本外推整場洪水會漏掉峰值負荷，直接把輸入質量全當沉積又會忽略穿越出流；兩種誤差可能相反但不能假設互相抵消。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Extrapolating one low-turbidity sample misses event peaks, while treating all incoming mass as deposited ignores sediment passing through. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b268-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證」與「沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification\" and \"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b268-v15-09","title":"細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「細粒沉降尺度」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fine-particle settling scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"顆粒沉降速度影響取水渠與沉砂區內的分離，但粒徑不是唯一因素，密度、形狀、黏度和絮凝都會改變結果。斯托克斯關係適用低顆粒雷諾數的孤立球形顆粒，不能套用到所有砂粒或高濃度團聚；計算後應回查流態，避免公式假設與所得速度互相矛盾。以下粒徑為二十微米並假設不絮凝、稀薄懸浮；若顆粒雷諾數不小或具黏聚性，需換用適當實測或模型。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「細粒沉降尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Settling speed influences separation in intake channels and basins, but size alone is insufficient: density, shape, viscosity and flocculation also matter. Stokes settling describes isolated spherical particles at low particle Reynolds number, not all sand or concentrated aggregates. The calculated speed must be used to recheck flow regime so that the result does not contradict its assumptions. The example uses twenty-micrometer particles in dilute nonflocculating suspension. Larger particle Reynolds number or cohesive behavior requires suitable measurements or another model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fine-particle settling scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=20 μm、μ=0.001 Pa·s，ws=(ρs−ρw)gd²/(18μ)=0.0003597 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³, d=20 μm and μ=0.001 Pa·s.","failure":"常見誤解：「斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「細粒沉降尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fine-particle settling scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-09-k1","title":"細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證","titleEn":"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification","text":"顆粒沉降速度影響取水渠與沉砂區內的分離，但粒徑不是唯一因素，密度、形狀、黏度和絮凝都會改變結果。斯托克斯關係適用低顆粒雷諾數的孤立球形顆粒，不能套用到所有砂粒或高濃度團聚；計算後應回查流態，避免公式假設與所得速度互相矛盾。","textEn":"Settling speed influences separation in intake channels and basins, but size alone is insufficient: density, shape, viscosity and flocculation also matter. Stokes settling describes isolated spherical particles at low particle Reynolds number, not all sand or concentrated aggregates.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["顆粒沉降速度影響取水渠與沉砂區內的分離，但粒徑不是唯一因素，密度、形狀、黏度和絮凝都會改變結果。","斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。","沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。"],"optionsEn":["Settling speed influences separation in intake channels and basins, but size alone is insufficient: density, shape, viscosity and flocculation also matter.","Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration.","A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size."],"answer":0,"explanation":"顆粒沉降速度影響取水渠與沉砂區內的分離，但粒徑不是唯一因素，密度、形狀、黏度和絮凝都會改變結果。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Settling speed influences separation in intake channels and basins, but size alone is insufficient: density, shape, viscosity and flocculation also matter. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b268-v15-10","title":"細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「細粒沉降尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fine-particle settling scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=20 μm、μ=0.001 Pa·s，ws=(ρs−ρw)gd²/(18μ)=0.0003597 m/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³, d=20 μm and μ=0.001 Pa·s. Stokes ws=(ρs−ρw)gd²/(18μ)=0.0003597 m/s with g=9.81 m/s². Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將微米轉為公尺後重算速度，利用所得值檢查顆粒雷諾數約為零點〇〇七二。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Convert micrometers to meters and recompute speed, then use that result to check a particle Reynolds number of approximately 0.0072.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=20 μm、μ=0.001 Pa·s，ws=(ρs−ρw)gd²/(18μ)=0.0003597 m/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³, d=20 μm and μ=0.001 Pa·s. Stokes ws=(ρs−ρw)gd²/(18μ)=0.0003597 m/s with g=9.81 m/s².","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=20 μm、μ=0.001 Pa·s，ws=(ρs−ρw)gd²/(18μ)=0.0003597 m/s。","排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。"],"optionsEn":["Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³, d=20 μm and μ=0.001 Pa·s.","More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=20 μm、μ=0.001 Pa·s，ws=(ρs−ρw)gd²/(18μ)=0.0003597 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³, d=20 μm and μ=0.001 Pa·s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b268-v15-11","title":"細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「細粒沉降尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fine-particle settling scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將微米轉為公尺後重算速度，利用所得值檢查顆粒雷諾數約為零點〇〇七二。用沉降柱或代表水樣觀察絮凝及濃度效應，區分理想單粒速度與實際群體沉降。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Convert micrometers to meters and recompute speed, then use that result to check a particle Reynolds number of approximately 0.0072. Examine flocculation and concentration effects with settling-column observations or representative samples, distinguishing ideal single-particle from bulk settling behavior. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將粒徑增加一倍並計算理想速度與雷諾數變化，說明何時需要停止沿用低雷諾數公式。比較單粒礦砂和絮體試驗需要控制的不同條件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double diameter and calculate the ideal changes in speed and Reynolds number, explaining when the low-Reynolds formula should no longer be retained. Compare experimental controls required for mineral particles and flocs.","failure":"注意干擾：把微米直接當公尺會造成巨大的平方誤差，將斯托克斯式用於粗砂則會忽略阻力流態改變；有機絮體的有效密度和形狀也不等於礦物球粒。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using micrometers as meters creates a huge squared-unit error, while applying Stokes law to coarse sand ignores changing drag regime. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將微米轉為公尺後重算速度，利用所得值檢查顆粒雷諾數約為零點〇〇七二。用沉降柱或代表水樣觀察絮凝及濃度效應，區分理想單粒速度與實際群體沉降。","textEn":"Convert micrometers to meters and recompute speed, then use that result to check a particle Reynolds number of approximately 0.0072. Examine flocculation and concentration effects with settling-column observations or representative samples, distinguishing ideal single-particle from bulk settling behavior.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將粒徑增加一倍並計算理想速度與雷諾數變化，說明何時需要停止沿用低雷諾數公式。比較單粒礦砂和絮體試驗需要控制的不同條件。","textEn":"Double diameter and calculate the ideal changes in speed and Reynolds number, explaining when the low-Reynolds formula should no longer be retained. Compare experimental controls required for mineral particles and flocs.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。","將微米轉為公尺後重算速度，利用所得值檢查顆粒雷諾數約為零點〇〇七二。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior.","Convert micrometers to meters and recompute speed, then use that result to check a particle Reynolds number of approximately 0.0072."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將微米轉為公尺後重算速度，利用所得值檢查顆粒雷諾數約為零點〇〇七二。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Convert micrometers to meters and recompute speed, then use that result to check a particle Reynolds number of approximately 0.0072. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b268-v15-12","title":"細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「細粒沉降尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fine-particle settling scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把微米直接當公尺會造成巨大的平方誤差，將斯托克斯式用於粗砂則會忽略阻力流態改變；有機絮體的有效密度和形狀也不等於礦物球粒。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using micrometers as meters creates a huge squared-unit error, while applying Stokes law to coarse sand ignores changing drag regime. Organic flocs also have effective density and shape unlike mineral spheres. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以下粒徑為二十微米並假設不絮凝、稀薄懸浮；若顆粒雷諾數不小或具黏聚性，需換用適當實測或模型。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Larger particle Reynolds number or cohesive behavior requires suitable measurements or another model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把微米直接當公尺會造成巨大的平方誤差，將斯托克斯式用於粗砂則會忽略阻力流態改變；有機絮體的有效密度和形狀也不等於礦物球粒。","textEn":"Using micrometers as meters creates a huge squared-unit error, while applying Stokes law to coarse sand ignores changing drag regime. Organic flocs also have effective density and shape unlike mineral spheres.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把微米直接當公尺會造成巨大的平方誤差，將斯托克斯式用於粗砂則會忽略阻力流態改變；有機絮體的有效密度和形狀也不等於礦物球粒。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。"],"optionsEn":["Using micrometers as meters creates a huge squared-unit error, while applying Stokes law to coarse sand ignores changing drag regime.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把微米直接當公尺會造成巨大的平方誤差，將斯托克斯式用於粗砂則會忽略阻力流態改變；有機絮體的有效密度和形狀也不等於礦物球粒。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using micrometers as meters creates a huge squared-unit error, while applying Stokes law to coarse sand ignores changing drag regime. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b268-v15-13","title":"沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「沉砂池表面負荷」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Settling-basin surface loading” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"理想水平流沉砂池中，顆粒能否落到底部取決於沉降速度與表面溢流負荷的比較，而不只是池深。增加深度同時增加沉降距離與停留時間，不能在其他條件不變時保證理想去除率提高；短路流、入口紊動與再懸浮會使實際表現偏離理想粒子軌跡。本例只求表面負荷並與指定單粒速度比較，假設均勻穩定流；不將理論臨界值當成全粒徑的實際去除率。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沉砂池表面負荷」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In an ideal horizontal-flow basin, settling depends on the comparison of particle settling speed with surface overflow loading, not depth alone. Greater depth increases both settling distance and residence time and therefore does not automatically improve ideal removal at unchanged plan area and flow. Short-circuiting, inlet turbulence and resuspension cause departures from ideal particle trajectories. The example calculates surface loading against a specified settling speed under uniform steady flow. It does not turn a theoretical cutoff into actual removal for every grain class. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Settling-basin surface loading” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=0.20 m³/s、平面面積A=100 m²，表面負荷vo=Q/A=0.0020 m/s；指定ws=0.003 m/s大於vo。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=0.20 m³/s and plan area A=100 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沉砂池表面負荷」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Settling-basin surface loading”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-13-k1","title":"沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證","titleEn":"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification","text":"理想水平流沉砂池中，顆粒能否落到底部取決於沉降速度與表面溢流負荷的比較，而不只是池深。增加深度同時增加沉降距離與停留時間，不能在其他條件不變時保證理想去除率提高；短路流、入口紊動與再懸浮會使實際表現偏離理想粒子軌跡。","textEn":"In an ideal horizontal-flow basin, settling depends on the comparison of particle settling speed with surface overflow loading, not depth alone. Greater depth increases both settling distance and residence time and therefore does not automatically improve ideal removal at unchanged plan area and flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。","理想水平流沉砂池中，顆粒能否落到底部取決於沉降速度與表面溢流負荷的比較，而不只是池深。","床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。"],"optionsEn":["A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size.","In an ideal horizontal-flow basin, settling depends on the comparison of particle settling speed with surface overflow loading, not depth alone.","Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"理想水平流沉砂池中，顆粒能否落到底部取決於沉降速度與表面溢流負荷的比較，而不只是池深。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In an ideal horizontal-flow basin, settling depends on the comparison of particle settling speed with surface overflow loading, not depth alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b268-v15-14","title":"沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沉砂池表面負荷」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Settling-basin surface loading” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=0.20 m³/s、平面面積A=100 m²，表面負荷vo=Q/A=0.0020 m/s；指定ws=0.003 m/s大於vo。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=0.20 m³/s and plan area A=100 m². Surface loading vo=Q/A=0.0020 m/s; specified ws=0.003 m/s exceeds vo. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對有效平面面積及進出口流量，利用示蹤或速度分布檢查短路與死區。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check effective plan area and inlet/outlet flow, using tracer or velocity measurements to detect short circuits and dead zones.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=0.20 m³/s、平面面積A=100 m²，表面負荷vo=Q/A=0.0020 m/s；指定ws=0.003 m/s大於vo。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=0.20 m³/s and plan area A=100 m². Surface loading vo=Q/A=0.0020 m/s; specified ws=0.003 m/s exceeds vo.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。","清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=0.20 m³/s、平面面積A=100 m²，表面負荷vo=Q/A=0.0020 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged.","Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=0.20 m³/s and plan area A=100 m²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=0.20 m³/s、平面面積A=100 m²，表面負荷vo=Q/A=0.0020 m/s；指定ws=0.003 m/s大於vo。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=0.20 m³/s and plan area A=100 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b268-v15-15","title":"沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沉砂池表面負荷」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Settling-basin surface loading” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對有效平面面積及進出口流量，利用示蹤或速度分布檢查短路與死區。依粒徑分組比較進出濃度，再觀察清淤前後是否因床面抬高造成再懸浮或入口擾動。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check effective plan area and inlet/outlet flow, using tracer or velocity measurements to detect short circuits and dead zones. Compare incoming and outgoing concentration by size class, then inspect whether deposited material alters resuspension or inlet disturbance before and after cleaning. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：固定流量比較增加面積與增加深度兩種方案，分別計算表面負荷和停留時間。指出理想模型無法描述的入口短路，並規劃一個可檢查它的示蹤觀察。","observationEn":"Site practice: At fixed flow compare added area with added depth, calculating surface loading and residence time separately. Identify inlet short-circuiting absent from the ideal model and plan a tracer observation capable of detecting it.","failure":"注意干擾：只加深沉砂池而不處理短路流可能幾乎沒有改善，堆積泥砂還會縮小有效空間；把單粒理想條件直接報成整體去除百分率會掩蓋粒徑分布。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Deepening a basin without addressing short-circuiting may offer little benefit, while sediment deposits shrink its effective space. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對有效平面面積及進出口流量，利用示蹤或速度分布檢查短路與死區。依粒徑分組比較進出濃度，再觀察清淤前後是否因床面抬高造成再懸浮或入口擾動。","textEn":"Check effective plan area and inlet/outlet flow, using tracer or velocity measurements to detect short circuits and dead zones. Compare incoming and outgoing concentration by size class, then inspect whether deposited material alters resuspension or inlet disturbance before and after cleaning.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"固定流量比較增加面積與增加深度兩種方案，分別計算表面負荷和停留時間。指出理想模型無法描述的入口短路，並規劃一個可檢查它的示蹤觀察。","textEn":"At fixed flow compare added area with added depth, calculating surface loading and residence time separately. Identify inlet short-circuiting absent from the ideal model and plan a tracer observation capable of detecting it.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification\"?","options":["核對有效平面面積及進出口流量，利用示蹤或速度分布檢查短路與死區。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。"],"optionsEn":["Check effective plan area and inlet/outlet flow, using tracer or velocity measurements to detect short circuits and dead zones.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對有效平面面積及進出口流量，利用示蹤或速度分布檢查短路與死區。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check effective plan area and inlet/outlet flow, using tracer or velocity measurements to detect short circuits and dead zones. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b268-v15-16","title":"沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沉砂池表面負荷」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Settling-basin surface loading” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只加深沉砂池而不處理短路流可能幾乎沒有改善，堆積泥砂還會縮小有效空間；把單粒理想條件直接報成整體去除百分率會掩蓋粒徑分布。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Deepening a basin without addressing short-circuiting may offer little benefit, while sediment deposits shrink its effective space. Reporting a single-particle ideal condition as overall removal percentage conceals the incoming grain-size distribution. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例只求表面負荷並與指定單粒速度比較，假設均勻穩定流；不將理論臨界值當成全粒徑的實際去除率。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It does not turn a theoretical cutoff into actual removal for every grain class.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只加深沉砂池而不處理短路流可能幾乎沒有改善，堆積泥砂還會縮小有效空間；把單粒理想條件直接報成整體去除百分率會掩蓋粒徑分布。","textEn":"Deepening a basin without addressing short-circuiting may offer little benefit, while sediment deposits shrink its effective space. Reporting a single-particle ideal condition as overall removal percentage conceals the incoming grain-size distribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只加深沉砂池而不處理短路流可能幾乎沒有改善，堆積泥砂還會縮小有效空間；把單粒理想條件直接報成整體去除百分率會掩蓋粒徑分布。","床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Deepening a basin without addressing short-circuiting may offer little benefit, while sediment deposits shrink its effective space.","Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只加深沉砂池而不處理短路流可能幾乎沒有改善，堆積泥砂還會縮小有效空間；把單粒理想條件直接報成整體去除百分率會掩蓋粒徑分布。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Deepening a basin without addressing short-circuiting may offer little benefit, while sediment deposits shrink its effective space. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b268-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證」與「沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification\" and \"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b268-v15-17","title":"非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「非黏性顆粒起動」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Noncohesive incipient motion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"沖砂能力可先由床面剪應力與顆粒抗移尺度比較，但起動不是固定流速一到就所有顆粒一起移動。無量綱希爾茲參數受粒徑、黏度、床面坡度與顆粒遮蔽影響，混合粒床還會有護甲效應；黏土的侵蝕則涉及黏聚與固結，不能沿用相同單粒非黏性判準。本例的臨界希爾茲數是指定假設，只用於水平、均勻非黏性床比較；未由此預測輸砂率或沖砂完成時間。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「非黏性顆粒起動」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Flushing potential can first be compared through bed shear and particle-resistance scales, but motion does not begin simultaneously for every grain at one fixed velocity. Shields behavior depends on size, viscosity, bed slope and hiding, while mixed beds can armor. Cohesive erosion also depends on bonding and consolidation and cannot reuse the same noncohesive single-grain criterion. The critical Shields value is an assumed input for a horizontal uniform noncohesive bed. It predicts neither sediment transport rate nor time to complete flushing. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Noncohesive incipient motion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設θc=0.05、ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=0.001 m，τc=θc(ρs−ρw)gd=0.8093 Pa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume θc=0.05, ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³ and d=0.001 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「非黏性顆粒起動」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Noncohesive incipient motion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-17-k1","title":"非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證","titleEn":"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification","text":"沖砂能力可先由床面剪應力與顆粒抗移尺度比較，但起動不是固定流速一到就所有顆粒一起移動。無量綱希爾茲參數受粒徑、黏度、床面坡度與顆粒遮蔽影響，混合粒床還會有護甲效應；黏土的侵蝕則涉及黏聚與固結，不能沿用相同單粒非黏性判準。","textEn":"Flushing potential can first be compared through bed shear and particle-resistance scales, but motion does not begin simultaneously for every grain at one fixed velocity. Shields behavior depends on size, viscosity, bed slope and hiding, while mixed beds can armor.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。","均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。","沖砂能力可先由床面剪應力與顆粒抗移尺度比較，但起動不是固定流速一到就所有顆粒一起移動。"],"optionsEn":["Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition.","Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate.","Flushing potential can first be compared through bed shear and particle-resistance scales, but motion does not begin simultaneously for every grain at one fixed velocity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沖砂能力可先由床面剪應力與顆粒抗移尺度比較，但起動不是固定流速一到就所有顆粒一起移動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Flushing potential can first be compared through bed shear and particle-resistance scales, but motion does not begin simultaneously for every grain at one fixed velocity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b268-v15-18","title":"非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「非黏性顆粒起動」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Noncohesive incipient motion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設θc=0.05、ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=0.001 m，τc=θc(ρs−ρw)gd=0.8093 Pa。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume θc=0.05, ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³ and d=0.001 m. Critical τc=θc(ρs−ρw)gd=0.8093 Pa at g=9.81 m/s². Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：調查床砂粒徑與黏性成分，核對臨界參數來源的粒徑及流態範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey grain distribution and cohesive content, checking the source parameter’s grain and flow-regime range.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設θc=0.05、ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=0.001 m，τc=θc(ρs−ρw)gd=0.8093 Pa。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume θc=0.05, ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³ and d=0.001 m. Critical τc=θc(ρs−ρw)gd=0.8093 Pa at g=9.81 m/s².","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設θc=0.05、ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=0.001 m，τc=θc(ρs−ρw)gd=0.8093 Pa。","排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。","水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume θc=0.05, ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³ and d=0.001 m.","More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked.","Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設θc=0.05、ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=0.001 m，τc=θc(ρs−ρw)gd=0.8093 Pa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume θc=0.05, ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³ and d=0.001 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b268-v15-19","title":"非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「非黏性顆粒起動」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Noncohesive incipient motion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"調查床砂粒徑與黏性成分，核對臨界參數來源的粒徑及流態範圍。將模型床面應力與起動觀察比較，保留護甲和局部坡度證據，再判斷是否需要多粒徑或黏性侵蝕模型。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey grain distribution and cohesive content, checking the source parameter’s grain and flow-regime range. Compare modeled bed stress with observed onset, retain evidence of armoring and local slope, then decide whether multiple-size or cohesive-erosion modeling is required. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用兩種假設粒徑比較臨界應力，再將含黏土的第三種材料標為公式範圍外。畫出由起動到輸送出口的路徑，列出每段仍需驗證的條件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare critical stress for two assumed grain sizes and mark a third clay-bearing material outside the formula’s scope. Draw the path from initial motion to outlet transport, identifying conditions still requiring verification along each reach.","failure":"注意干擾：把非黏性常數套用固結淤泥會錯估沖砂需求，將平均應力當所有位置應力也會漏掉低速堆積區；達到起動條件仍不保證泥砂能通過下游出口。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying a noncohesive constant to consolidated mud misstates flushing demand, and treating mean stress as universal misses low-velocity deposits. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"調查床砂粒徑與黏性成分，核對臨界參數來源的粒徑及流態範圍。將模型床面應力與起動觀察比較，保留護甲和局部坡度證據，再判斷是否需要多粒徑或黏性侵蝕模型。","textEn":"Survey grain distribution and cohesive content, checking the source parameter’s grain and flow-regime range. Compare modeled bed stress with observed onset, retain evidence of armoring and local slope, then decide whether multiple-size or cohesive-erosion modeling is required.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用兩種假設粒徑比較臨界應力，再將含黏土的第三種材料標為公式範圍外。畫出由起動到輸送出口的路徑，列出每段仍需驗證的條件。","textEn":"Compare critical stress for two assumed grain sizes and mark a third clay-bearing material outside the formula’s scope. Draw the path from initial motion to outlet transport, identifying conditions still requiring verification along each reach.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","調查床砂粒徑與黏性成分，核對臨界參數來源的粒徑及流態範圍。","取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Survey grain distribution and cohesive content, checking the source parameter’s grain and flow-regime range.","With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input."],"answer":1,"explanation":"調查床砂粒徑與黏性成分，核對臨界參數來源的粒徑及流態範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey grain distribution and cohesive content, checking the source parameter’s grain and flow-regime range. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b268-v15-20","title":"非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「非黏性顆粒起動」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Noncohesive incipient motion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把非黏性常數套用固結淤泥會錯估沖砂需求，將平均應力當所有位置應力也會漏掉低速堆積區；達到起動條件仍不保證泥砂能通過下游出口。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying a noncohesive constant to consolidated mud misstates flushing demand, and treating mean stress as universal misses low-velocity deposits. Reaching incipient motion does not guarantee that sediment can travel through the downstream outlet. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例的臨界希爾茲數是指定假設，只用於水平、均勻非黏性床比較；未由此預測輸砂率或沖砂完成時間。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It predicts neither sediment transport rate nor time to complete flushing.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把非黏性常數套用固結淤泥會錯估沖砂需求，將平均應力當所有位置應力也會漏掉低速堆積區；達到起動條件仍不保證泥砂能通過下游出口。","textEn":"Applying a noncohesive constant to consolidated mud misstates flushing demand, and treating mean stress as universal misses low-velocity deposits. Reaching incipient motion does not guarantee that sediment can travel through the downstream outlet.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。","把非黏性常數套用固結淤泥會錯估沖砂需求，將平均應力當所有位置應力也會漏掉低速堆積區；達到起動條件仍不保證泥砂能通過下游出口。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate.","Applying a noncohesive constant to consolidated mud misstates flushing demand, and treating mean stress as universal misses low-velocity deposits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把非黏性常數套用固結淤泥會錯估沖砂需求，將平均應力當所有位置應力也會漏掉低速堆積區；達到起動條件仍不保證泥砂能通過下游出口。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying a noncohesive constant to consolidated mud misstates flushing demand, and treating mean stress as universal misses low-velocity deposits. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b268-v15-21","title":"沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「沖砂渠床面應力」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Flushing-channel bed stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"均勻明渠流的平均邊界應力可用水力半徑和能量坡降估算，適合作為沖砂能力的初步尺度。取水口附近的彎流、收縮和閘下射流通常不均勻，局部床面剪應力可能與周界平均值差很大；若用水面坡度代替能量坡度，還必須先確認沿程加速度與損失分布。本例假設穩定均勻流，所得為平均邊界應力；不能把它直接指定給取水口角落、彎道外岸或閘下局部沖刷。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沖砂渠床面應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Uniform open-channel flow permits a mean boundary-stress estimate from hydraulic radius and energy slope, providing an initial flushing scale. Bends, contractions and gate jets near intakes are nonuniform, so local bed stress can differ substantially from the wetted-perimeter mean. Substituting water-surface slope for energy slope additionally requires checking acceleration and the distribution of losses. The example assumes steady uniform flow and yields mean boundary stress. It cannot directly prescribe stress at intake corners, outer bends or local scour beneath a gate. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Flushing-channel bed stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²、水力半徑R=0.50 m、能坡Sf=0.001，τ=ρgRSf=4.905 Pa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s², hydraulic radius R=0.50 m and energy slope Sf=0.001.","failure":"常見誤解：「均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沖砂渠床面應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Flushing-channel bed stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-21-k1","title":"沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證","titleEn":"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification","text":"均勻明渠流的平均邊界應力可用水力半徑和能量坡降估算，適合作為沖砂能力的初步尺度。取水口附近的彎流、收縮和閘下射流通常不均勻，局部床面剪應力可能與周界平均值差很大；若用水面坡度代替能量坡度，還必須先確認沿程加速度與損失分布。","textEn":"Uniform open-channel flow permits a mean boundary-stress estimate from hydraulic radius and energy slope, providing an initial flushing scale. Bends, contractions and gate jets near intakes are nonuniform, so local bed stress can differ substantially from the wetted-perimeter mean.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["均勻明渠流的平均邊界應力可用水力半徑和能量坡降估算，適合作為沖砂能力的初步尺度。","均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。","沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。"],"optionsEn":["Uniform open-channel flow permits a mean boundary-stress estimate from hydraulic radius and energy slope, providing an initial flushing scale.","Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate.","Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged."],"answer":0,"explanation":"均勻明渠流的平均邊界應力可用水力半徑和能量坡降估算，適合作為沖砂能力的初步尺度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Uniform open-channel flow permits a mean boundary-stress estimate from hydraulic radius and energy slope, providing an initial flushing scale. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b268-v15-22","title":"沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沖砂渠床面應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Flushing-channel bed stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²、水力半徑R=0.50 m、能坡Sf=0.001，τ=ρgRSf=4.905 Pa。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s², hydraulic radius R=0.50 m and energy slope Sf=0.001. Mean stress τ=ρgRSf=4.905 Pa. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測渠段斷面與水面高程，核對流況是否接近均勻並估計能量項。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure channel sections and water-surface elevations, assess proximity to uniform flow and account for energy terms.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²、水力半徑R=0.50 m、能坡Sf=0.001，τ=ρgRSf=4.905 Pa。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s², hydraulic radius R=0.50 m and energy slope Sf=0.001. Mean stress τ=ρgRSf=4.905 Pa.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²、水力半徑R=0.50 m、能坡Sf=0.001，τ=ρgRSf=4.905 Pa。","只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。"],"optionsEn":["Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s², hydraulic radius R=0.50 m and energy slope Sf=0.001.","Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²、水力半徑R=0.50 m、能坡Sf=0.001，τ=ρgRSf=4.905 Pa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s², hydraulic radius R=0.50 m and energy slope Sf=0.001. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b268-v15-23","title":"沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沖砂渠床面應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Flushing-channel bed stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測渠段斷面與水面高程，核對流況是否接近均勻並估計能量項。對轉彎、死角及閘下區另用局部速度或模型檢查應力，不能只以全渠平均值驗證清淤效果。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure channel sections and water-surface elevations, assess proximity to uniform flow and account for energy terms. Examine bends, dead zones and gate-jet regions with local velocities or modeling instead of using one channel-average value to verify sediment-clearing performance everywhere. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：計算平均應力後，在平面圖標示可能較低或較高的局部區域。為每個區域選擇可驗證的速度或床形觀察，說明為何它不能被平均值取代。","observationEn":"Site practice: After calculating mean stress, mark potentially lower and higher local zones on a plan. Select velocity or bed-form observations for each zone and explain why the mean cannot replace these local measurements.","failure":"注意干擾：以平均應力高於臨界值就宣稱全渠無淤積，會漏掉死區及分流口；提高沖砂水量也可能把沖刷風險轉移到結構基礎或下游河岸。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Declaring the whole channel sediment-free because average stress exceeds a threshold overlooks dead zones and branching entrances. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測渠段斷面與水面高程，核對流況是否接近均勻並估計能量項。對轉彎、死角及閘下區另用局部速度或模型檢查應力，不能只以全渠平均值驗證清淤效果。","textEn":"Measure channel sections and water-surface elevations, assess proximity to uniform flow and account for energy terms. Examine bends, dead zones and gate-jet regions with local velocities or modeling instead of using one channel-average value to verify sediment-clearing performance everywhere.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"計算平均應力後，在平面圖標示可能較低或較高的局部區域。為每個區域選擇可驗證的速度或床形觀察，說明為何它不能被平均值取代。","textEn":"After calculating mean stress, mark potentially lower and higher local zones on a plan. Select velocity or bed-form observations for each zone and explain why the mean cannot replace these local measurements.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。","量測渠段斷面與水面高程，核對流況是否接近均勻並估計能量項。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration.","Measure channel sections and water-surface elevations, assess proximity to uniform flow and account for energy terms."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測渠段斷面與水面高程，核對流況是否接近均勻並估計能量項。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure channel sections and water-surface elevations, assess proximity to uniform flow and account for energy terms. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b268-v15-24","title":"沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沖砂渠床面應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Flushing-channel bed stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以平均應力高於臨界值就宣稱全渠無淤積，會漏掉死區及分流口；提高沖砂水量也可能把沖刷風險轉移到結構基礎或下游河岸。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Declaring the whole channel sediment-free because average stress exceeds a threshold overlooks dead zones and branching entrances. Increasing flushing discharge can also transfer erosion risk to structural foundations or downstream riverbanks. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例假設穩定均勻流，所得為平均邊界應力；不能把它直接指定給取水口角落、彎道外岸或閘下局部沖刷。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It cannot directly prescribe stress at intake corners, outer bends or local scour beneath a gate.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以平均應力高於臨界值就宣稱全渠無淤積，會漏掉死區及分流口；提高沖砂水量也可能把沖刷風險轉移到結構基礎或下游河岸。","textEn":"Declaring the whole channel sediment-free because average stress exceeds a threshold overlooks dead zones and branching entrances. Increasing flushing discharge can also transfer erosion risk to structural foundations or downstream riverbanks.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["以平均應力高於臨界值就宣稱全渠無淤積，會漏掉死區及分流口；提高沖砂水量也可能把沖刷風險轉移到結構基礎或下游河岸。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。"],"optionsEn":["Declaring the whole channel sediment-free because average stress exceeds a threshold overlooks dead zones and branching entrances.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以平均應力高於臨界值就宣稱全渠無淤積，會漏掉死區及分流口；提高沖砂水量也可能把沖刷風險轉移到結構基礎或下游河岸。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Declaring the whole channel sediment-free because average stress exceeds a threshold overlooks dead zones and branching entrances. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b268-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證」與「沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification\" and \"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b268-v15-25","title":"篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「篩網方向與掃流」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Screen orientation and sweeping flow” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"河岸篩網的防淤與魚類導引都受到來流方向影響，總速度應分成垂直篩面的接近分量和沿面的掃流分量。改變角度可能減少法向吸入但增加設施長度，且實際河流有垂向和橫向不均；簡單向量分解只能描述指定位置，不能替代整片篩面的速度普查。本例角度明確定義為流向相對篩面切線的夾角，未把假設速度當魚種標準；接近速度的量測位置須依評估方法指定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「篩網方向與掃流」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Screen sediment behavior and fish guidance depend on approach direction, requiring separation of normal approach velocity from tangential sweeping velocity. Reorientation may reduce normal entry while increasing structure length, and real rivers have vertical and lateral variation. A vector decomposition describes one location only and cannot replace a spatial velocity survey across the screen. The angle is measured from the screen tangent to the flow direction, and the assumed speed is not a species criterion. Measurement offset must follow the selected evaluation method. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Screen orientation and sweeping flow” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設來流V=0.50 m/s、與篩面切線夾角α=20°，法向Vn=Vsinα=0.1710 m/s，沿面Vs=Vcosα=0.4698 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flow V=0.50 m/s at α=20° from the screen tangent.","failure":"常見誤解：「沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「篩網方向與掃流」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Screen orientation and sweeping flow”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-25-k1","title":"篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證","titleEn":"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification","text":"河岸篩網的防淤與魚類導引都受到來流方向影響，總速度應分成垂直篩面的接近分量和沿面的掃流分量。改變角度可能減少法向吸入但增加設施長度，且實際河流有垂向和橫向不均；簡單向量分解只能描述指定位置，不能替代整片篩面的速度普查。","textEn":"Screen sediment behavior and fish guidance depend on approach direction, requiring separation of normal approach velocity from tangential sweeping velocity. Reorientation may reduce normal entry while increasing structure length, and real rivers have vertical and lateral variation.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。","河岸篩網的防淤與魚類導引都受到來流方向影響，總速度應分成垂直篩面的接近分量和沿面的掃流分量。","排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。"],"optionsEn":["Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged.","Screen sediment behavior and fish guidance depend on approach direction, requiring separation of normal approach velocity from tangential sweeping velocity.","More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked."],"answer":1,"explanation":"河岸篩網的防淤與魚類導引都受到來流方向影響，總速度應分成垂直篩面的接近分量和沿面的掃流分量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Screen sediment behavior and fish guidance depend on approach direction, requiring separation of normal approach velocity from tangential sweeping velocity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b268-v15-26","title":"篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「篩網方向與掃流」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Screen orientation and sweeping flow” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設來流V=0.50 m/s、與篩面切線夾角α=20°，法向Vn=Vsinα=0.1710 m/s，沿面Vs=Vcosα=0.4698 m/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flow V=0.50 m/s at α=20° from the screen tangent. Normal Vn=Vsinα=0.1710 m/s and sweeping Vs=Vcosα=0.4698 m/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在測點圖標明篩面切線、法線及感測器方向，依相同離面距離量測速度分量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark screen tangent, normal and sensor orientation on the survey map, measuring components at consistent offsets.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設來流V=0.50 m/s、與篩面切線夾角α=20°，法向Vn=Vsinα=0.1710 m/s，沿面Vs=Vcosα=0.4698 m/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flow V=0.50 m/s at α=20° from the screen tangent. Normal Vn=Vsinα=0.1710 m/s and sweeping Vs=Vcosα=0.4698 m/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。","取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設來流V=0.50 m/s、與篩面切線夾角α=20°，法向Vn=Vsinα=0.1710 m/s，沿面Vs=Vcosα=0.4698 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior.","With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flow V=0.50 m/s at α=20° from the screen tangent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設來流V=0.50 m/s、與篩面切線夾角α=20°，法向Vn=Vsinα=0.1710 m/s，沿面Vs=Vcosα=0.4698 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flow V=0.50 m/s at α=20° from the screen tangent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b268-v15-27","title":"篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「篩網方向與掃流」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Screen orientation and sweeping flow” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在測點圖標明篩面切線、法線及感測器方向，依相同離面距離量測速度分量。將面積積分流量與取水計量核對，並在堵塞、低水位與不同機組運轉下重查熱點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark screen tangent, normal and sensor orientation on the survey map, measuring components at consistent offsets. Reconcile area-integrated flow with intake metering and revisit hotspots under blockage, low water and different pump combinations to check spatial representation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：為同一來流畫出兩個篩面角度並分解速度，清楚標記角度起算方向。指出幾何比較之外仍需驗證的旁通入口、局部堵塞與物種條件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw two screen angles for the same incoming flow and resolve velocities, explicitly marking the angle reference. Identify bypass-entry, local-blockage and species conditions that still need checking beyond the geometric comparison.","failure":"注意干擾：把角度從法線量卻套切線公式會交換兩個分量，局部高速區可能因此被低估；只報平均掃流也無法證明魚類可順利到達旁通出口。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Measuring angle from the normal but using tangent-based formulas swaps components and can understate hotspots. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在測點圖標明篩面切線、法線及感測器方向，依相同離面距離量測速度分量。將面積積分流量與取水計量核對，並在堵塞、低水位與不同機組運轉下重查熱點。","textEn":"Mark screen tangent, normal and sensor orientation on the survey map, measuring components at consistent offsets. Reconcile area-integrated flow with intake metering and revisit hotspots under blockage, low water and different pump combinations to check spatial representation.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"為同一來流畫出兩個篩面角度並分解速度，清楚標記角度起算方向。指出幾何比較之外仍需驗證的旁通入口、局部堵塞與物種條件。","textEn":"Draw two screen angles for the same incoming flow and resolve velocities, explicitly marking the angle reference. Identify bypass-entry, local-blockage and species conditions that still need checking beyond the geometric comparison.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification\"?","options":["在測點圖標明篩面切線、法線及感測器方向，依相同離面距離量測速度分量。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。"],"optionsEn":["Mark screen tangent, normal and sensor orientation on the survey map, measuring components at consistent offsets.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在測點圖標明篩面切線、法線及感測器方向，依相同離面距離量測速度分量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark screen tangent, normal and sensor orientation on the survey map, measuring components at consistent offsets. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b268-v15-28","title":"篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「篩網方向與掃流」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Screen orientation and sweeping flow” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把角度從法線量卻套切線公式會交換兩個分量，局部高速區可能因此被低估；只報平均掃流也無法證明魚類可順利到達旁通出口。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Measuring angle from the normal but using tangent-based formulas swaps components and can understate hotspots. Reporting mean sweeping velocity alone also does not establish successful movement to the bypass outlet. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例角度明確定義為流向相對篩面切線的夾角，未把假設速度當魚種標準；接近速度的量測位置須依評估方法指定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Measurement offset must follow the selected evaluation method.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把角度從法線量卻套切線公式會交換兩個分量，局部高速區可能因此被低估；只報平均掃流也無法證明魚類可順利到達旁通出口。","textEn":"Measuring angle from the normal but using tangent-based formulas swaps components and can understate hotspots. Reporting mean sweeping velocity alone also does not establish successful movement to the bypass outlet.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把角度從法線量卻套切線公式會交換兩個分量，局部高速區可能因此被低估；只報平均掃流也無法證明魚類可順利到達旁通出口。","排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Measuring angle from the normal but using tangent-based formulas swaps components and can understate hotspots.","More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把角度從法線量卻套切線公式會交換兩個分量，局部高速區可能因此被低估；只報平均掃流也無法證明魚類可順利到達旁通出口。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Measuring angle from the normal but using tangent-based formulas swaps components and can understate hotspots. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b268-v15-29","title":"沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「沖砂水量與事件管理」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Flushing volume and event management” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"沖砂不是只要閘門開啟就完成，水量、持續時間和下游輸送能力共同決定效果。短時大流量可能啟動床砂卻在出口形成新沉積，長時低流量則可能不足以維持運移；用水帳還須與供水和河川需求協調，不能把排砂水當作沒有代價的額外資源。本例只求指定穩定排砂流量的總水體積，不預測泥砂去除率，也不建議任何現場開閘順序或時間設定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沖砂水量與事件管理」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Opening a gate does not by itself complete sediment flushing. Flow, duration and downstream transport capacity determine performance. A brief large release may mobilize material that redeposits at the outlet, while prolonged low flow may not sustain movement. The water budget must also account for supply and river needs rather than treating flushing water as a free additional resource. The example calculates water volume for a specified constant flushing flow, not sediment removal efficiency. It gives no field gate-opening sequence or operating-time recommendation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Flushing volume and event management” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排砂流量Qf=3.0 m³/s、持續t=600 s，使用水量V=Qft=1800 m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flushing flow Qf=3.0 m³/s for t=600 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沖砂水量與事件管理」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Flushing volume and event management”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-29-k1","title":"沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證","titleEn":"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification","text":"沖砂不是只要閘門開啟就完成，水量、持續時間和下游輸送能力共同決定效果。短時大流量可能啟動床砂卻在出口形成新沉積，長時低流量則可能不足以維持運移；用水帳還須與供水和河川需求協調，不能把排砂水當作沒有代價的額外資源。","textEn":"Opening a gate does not by itself complete sediment flushing. Flow, duration and downstream transport capacity determine performance.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。","清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。","沖砂不是只要閘門開啟就完成，水量、持續時間和下游輸送能力共同決定效果。"],"optionsEn":["More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked.","Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys.","Opening a gate does not by itself complete sediment flushing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沖砂不是只要閘門開啟就完成，水量、持續時間和下游輸送能力共同決定效果。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Opening a gate does not by itself complete sediment flushing. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b268-v15-30","title":"沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沖砂水量與事件管理」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Flushing volume and event management” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排砂流量Qf=3.0 m³/s、持續t=600 s，使用水量V=Qft=1800 m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flushing flow Qf=3.0 m³/s for t=600 s. Water volume V=Qft=1800 m³. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將排砂前後地形和出流泥砂濃度對時，核對實際水量與輸出質量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align before-and-after bathymetry with outgoing sediment concentration, checking actual water volume and exported mass.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排砂流量Qf=3.0 m³/s、持續t=600 s，使用水量V=Qft=1800 m³。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flushing flow Qf=3.0 m³/s for t=600 s. Water volume V=Qft=1800 m³.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排砂流量Qf=3.0 m³/s、持續t=600 s，使用水量V=Qft=1800 m³。","只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。","斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flushing flow Qf=3.0 m³/s for t=600 s.","Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary.","Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排砂流量Qf=3.0 m³/s、持續t=600 s，使用水量V=Qft=1800 m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flushing flow Qf=3.0 m³/s for t=600 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b268-v15-31","title":"沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沖砂水量與事件管理」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Flushing volume and event management” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將排砂前後地形和出流泥砂濃度對時，核對實際水量與輸出質量。另觀察下游沉積、濁度及供水變化，確認移走的泥砂沒有只轉移到另一個敏感或阻塞位置。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align before-and-after bathymetry with outgoing sediment concentration, checking actual water volume and exported mass. Observe downstream deposits, turbidity and supply changes to establish whether removed sediment has merely shifted to another sensitive location or potential blockage rather than leaving the system. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立一次假設排砂的水量、泥砂輸出與床形變化三本帳。說明三者不一致時可能是取樣、密度換算或泥砂轉移問題，並提出可區分原因的觀察。","observationEn":"Site practice: Create separate ledgers for flushing water, exported sediment and bed-volume change. Explain how disagreement can reflect sampling, density conversion or relocation, and propose observations that distinguish those possible causes.","failure":"注意干擾：以耗水量大就推定沖砂有效會忽略低速死區，未檢查下游則可能把取水口的問題搬到河道；沖砂後供水恢復也不能證明所有沉積已清除。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: High water use does not prove effective flushing in low-velocity dead zones. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將排砂前後地形和出流泥砂濃度對時，核對實際水量與輸出質量。另觀察下游沉積、濁度及供水變化，確認移走的泥砂沒有只轉移到另一個敏感或阻塞位置。","textEn":"Align before-and-after bathymetry with outgoing sediment concentration, checking actual water volume and exported mass. Observe downstream deposits, turbidity and supply changes to establish whether removed sediment has merely shifted to another sensitive location or potential blockage rather than leaving the system.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立一次假設排砂的水量、泥砂輸出與床形變化三本帳。說明三者不一致時可能是取樣、密度換算或泥砂轉移問題，並提出可區分原因的觀察。","textEn":"Create separate ledgers for flushing water, exported sediment and bed-volume change. Explain how disagreement can reflect sampling, density conversion or relocation, and propose observations that distinguish those possible causes.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將排砂前後地形和出流泥砂濃度對時，核對實際水量與輸出質量。","床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Align before-and-after bathymetry with outgoing sediment concentration, checking actual water volume and exported mass.","Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將排砂前後地形和出流泥砂濃度對時，核對實際水量與輸出質量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align before-and-after bathymetry with outgoing sediment concentration, checking actual water volume and exported mass. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b268-v15-32","title":"沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沖砂水量與事件管理」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Flushing volume and event management” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以耗水量大就推定沖砂有效會忽略低速死區，未檢查下游則可能把取水口的問題搬到河道；沖砂後供水恢復也不能證明所有沉積已清除。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"High water use does not prove effective flushing in low-velocity dead zones. Without downstream checks the intake problem may simply move into the river, and restored supply does not demonstrate complete sediment removal. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例只求指定穩定排砂流量的總水體積，不預測泥砂去除率，也不建議任何現場開閘順序或時間設定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It gives no field gate-opening sequence or operating-time recommendation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以耗水量大就推定沖砂有效會忽略低速死區，未檢查下游則可能把取水口的問題搬到河道；沖砂後供水恢復也不能證明所有沉積已清除。","textEn":"High water use does not prove effective flushing in low-velocity dead zones. Without downstream checks the intake problem may simply move into the river, and restored supply does not demonstrate complete sediment removal.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。","以耗水量大就推定沖砂有效會忽略低速死區，未檢查下游則可能把取水口的問題搬到河道；沖砂後供水恢復也不能證明所有沉積已清除。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys.","High water use does not prove effective flushing in low-velocity dead zones."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以耗水量大就推定沖砂有效會忽略低速死區，未檢查下游則可能把取水口的問題搬到河道；沖砂後供水恢復也不能證明所有沉積已清除。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"High water use does not prove effective flushing in low-velocity dead zones. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b268-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證」與「實體模型相似限制機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification\" and \"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b268-v15-33","title":"沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「沉積庫容與清淤頻率」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Deposit storage and maintenance interval” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"沉砂設施需要把固體質量換成含孔隙的沉積體積，才可估計可用庫容與清理需求。顆粒密度不是沉積乾容重，孔隙、含水與固結會改變體積；平均沉積率只提供規劃尺度，洪水脈衝和空間不均可能使局部高程先達限制，不能只等總庫容耗盡。本例採乾固體質量和指定乾容重，忽略固結與事件變動；算得間隔是線性庫容比較，並非實際維護排程。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沉積庫容與清淤頻率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Sediment storage planning converts solid mass into deposit volume including pores. Grain density is not dry bulk density, and porosity, water content and consolidation alter volume. A mean deposition rate gives a planning scale only: flood pulses and uneven deposits can reach local elevation constraints before total nominal storage is exhausted. The example uses dry solid mass and specified dry bulk density, excluding consolidation and event variability. The interval is a linear storage comparison, not an actual maintenance schedule. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Deposit storage and maintenance interval” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設日沉積乾質量Md=1200 kg/day、乾容重ρd=1500 kg/m³，日體積0.80 m³/day；可用容積40 m³對應50 day。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume deposited dry mass Md=1200 kg/day and dry bulk density ρd=1500 kg/m³.","failure":"常見誤解：「清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沉積庫容與清淤頻率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Deposit storage and maintenance interval”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-33-k1","title":"沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證","titleEn":"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification","text":"沉砂設施需要把固體質量換成含孔隙的沉積體積，才可估計可用庫容與清理需求。顆粒密度不是沉積乾容重，孔隙、含水與固結會改變體積；平均沉積率只提供規劃尺度，洪水脈衝和空間不均可能使局部高程先達限制，不能只等總庫容耗盡。","textEn":"Sediment storage planning converts solid mass into deposit volume including pores. Grain density is not dry bulk density, and porosity, water content and consolidation alter volume.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["沉砂設施需要把固體質量換成含孔隙的沉積體積，才可估計可用庫容與清理需求。","清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。","水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。"],"optionsEn":["Sediment storage planning converts solid mass into deposit volume including pores.","Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys.","Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沉砂設施需要把固體質量換成含孔隙的沉積體積，才可估計可用庫容與清理需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Sediment storage planning converts solid mass into deposit volume including pores. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b268-v15-34","title":"沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沉積庫容與清淤頻率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Deposit storage and maintenance interval” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設日沉積乾質量Md=1200 kg/day、乾容重ρd=1500 kg/m³，日體積0.80 m³/day；可用容積40 m³對應50 day。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume deposited dry mass Md=1200 kg/day and dry bulk density ρd=1500 kg/m³. Volume is 0.80 m³/day; 40 m³ usable storage corresponds to 50 days. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以代表樣本量測乾容重並以測深確認沉積分布，將清理量、事件負荷與剩餘庫容交叉比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure representative dry bulk density and map deposit distribution, comparing removed volume, event loads and remaining storage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設日沉積乾質量Md=1200 kg/day、乾容重ρd=1500 kg/m³，日體積0.80 m³/day；可用容積40 m³對應50 day。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume deposited dry mass Md=1200 kg/day and dry bulk density ρd=1500 kg/m³. Volume is 0.80 m³/day; 40 m³ usable storage corresponds to 50 days.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設日沉積乾質量Md=1200 kg/day、乾容重ρd=1500 kg/m³，日體積0.80 m³/day。","沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。"],"optionsEn":["With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume deposited dry mass Md=1200 kg/day and dry bulk density ρd=1500 kg/m³.","A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設日沉積乾質量Md=1200 kg/day、乾容重ρd=1500 kg/m³，日體積0.80 m³/day；可用容積40 m³對應50 day。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume deposited dry mass Md=1200 kg/day and dry bulk density ρd=1500 kg/m³. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b268-v15-35","title":"沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沉積庫容與清淤頻率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Deposit storage and maintenance interval” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以代表樣本量測乾容重並以測深確認沉積分布，將清理量、事件負荷與剩餘庫容交叉比對。對門檻與取水附近設局部高程檢查，避免用總體積掩蓋關鍵區域先被填滿。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure representative dry bulk density and map deposit distribution, comparing removed volume, event loads and remaining storage. Check local elevations near sills and intake openings so that a total-volume ledger does not conceal critical areas filling before the nominal capacity is reached. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較相同固體質量在兩種乾容重下的體積，再加入一次假設洪水脈衝。指出庫容帳和局部床形檢查各回答什麼問題，設計可更新間隔的資料表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare deposit volumes at two dry bulk densities, then add a hypothetical flood pulse. Explain the distinct questions answered by storage accounting and local bathymetry, and create a record that supports updating the interval.","failure":"注意干擾：用礦物密度代替乾容重會低估堆積體積，以平均日量推算固定清淤日可能漏掉一次大洪水；局部堆積抬高即使總庫容仍足夠也能妨礙取水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using grain density instead of dry bulk density understates deposit volume, and a fixed date based on mean daily load can miss a major flood pulse. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以代表樣本量測乾容重並以測深確認沉積分布，將清理量、事件負荷與剩餘庫容交叉比對。對門檻與取水附近設局部高程檢查，避免用總體積掩蓋關鍵區域先被填滿。","textEn":"Measure representative dry bulk density and map deposit distribution, comparing removed volume, event loads and remaining storage. Check local elevations near sills and intake openings so that a total-volume ledger does not conceal critical areas filling before the nominal capacity is reached.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較相同固體質量在兩種乾容重下的體積，再加入一次假設洪水脈衝。指出庫容帳和局部床形檢查各回答什麼問題，設計可更新間隔的資料表。","textEn":"Compare deposit volumes at two dry bulk densities, then add a hypothetical flood pulse. Explain the distinct questions answered by storage accounting and local bathymetry, and create a record that supports updating the interval.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。","以代表樣本量測乾容重並以測深確認沉積分布，將清理量、事件負荷與剩餘庫容交叉比對。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate.","Measure representative dry bulk density and map deposit distribution, comparing removed volume, event loads and remaining storage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以代表樣本量測乾容重並以測深確認沉積分布，將清理量、事件負荷與剩餘庫容交叉比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure representative dry bulk density and map deposit distribution, comparing removed volume, event loads and remaining storage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b268-v15-36","title":"沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沉積庫容與清淤頻率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Deposit storage and maintenance interval” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用礦物密度代替乾容重會低估堆積體積，以平均日量推算固定清淤日可能漏掉一次大洪水；局部堆積抬高即使總庫容仍足夠也能妨礙取水。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using grain density instead of dry bulk density understates deposit volume, and a fixed date based on mean daily load can miss a major flood pulse. Local buildup may obstruct diversion while overall storage remains available. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例採乾固體質量和指定乾容重，忽略固結與事件變動；算得間隔是線性庫容比較，並非實際維護排程。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The interval is a linear storage comparison, not an actual maintenance schedule.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用礦物密度代替乾容重會低估堆積體積，以平均日量推算固定清淤日可能漏掉一次大洪水；局部堆積抬高即使總庫容仍足夠也能妨礙取水。","textEn":"Using grain density instead of dry bulk density understates deposit volume, and a fixed date based on mean daily load can miss a major flood pulse. Local buildup may obstruct diversion while overall storage remains available.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用礦物密度代替乾容重會低估堆積體積，以平均日量推算固定清淤日可能漏掉一次大洪水；局部堆積抬高即使總庫容仍足夠也能妨礙取水。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。"],"optionsEn":["Using grain density instead of dry bulk density understates deposit volume, and a fixed date based on mean daily load can miss a major flood pulse.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用礦物密度代替乾容重會低估堆積體積，以平均日量推算固定清淤日可能漏掉一次大洪水；局部堆積抬高即使總庫容仍足夠也能妨礙取水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using grain density instead of dry bulk density understates deposit volume, and a fixed date based on mean daily load can miss a major flood pulse. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b268-v15-37","title":"實體模型相似限制機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「實體模型相似限制」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Physical-model similarity limits” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"縮尺水工模型常優先保持重力與慣性相似，以觀察水面、分流和旋渦，但泥砂運移還受黏性、粒徑與密度控制。幾何縮小不代表原型砂粒能按相同比例直接替換，否則沉降與起動可能失真；清水流場試驗可以驗證水力部分，不能自動宣稱防淤與生態功能都已驗證。本例定義長度比為模型除以原型，採福祿相似求速度與流量比；未宣稱雷諾相似或可動床相似同時成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「實體模型相似限制」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Hydraulic scale models often preserve gravity-inertia similarity to examine water levels, flow division and vortices, while sediment transport also depends on viscosity, grain size and density. Geometric reduction does not guarantee proportionally scaled grains reproduce settling and motion. A clear-water experiment can verify hydraulic behavior without automatically validating sediment exclusion or ecological performance. Length ratio is model divided by prototype. Froude similarity supplies velocity and discharge ratios without claiming simultaneous Reynolds or mobile-bed similarity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Physical-model similarity limits” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設長度比λL=1/25，福祿相似λV=√λL=1/5，流量比λQ=λL^(5/2)=1/3125。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume length ratio λL=1/25.","failure":"常見誤解：「水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「實體模型相似限制」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Physical-model similarity limits”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-37-k1","title":"實體模型相似限制機理與驗證","titleEn":"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification","text":"縮尺水工模型常優先保持重力與慣性相似，以觀察水面、分流和旋渦，但泥砂運移還受黏性、粒徑與密度控制。幾何縮小不代表原型砂粒能按相同比例直接替換，否則沉降與起動可能失真；清水流場試驗可以驗證水力部分，不能自動宣稱防淤與生態功能都已驗證。","textEn":"Hydraulic scale models often preserve gravity-inertia similarity to examine water levels, flow division and vortices, while sediment transport also depends on viscosity, grain size and density. Geometric reduction does not guarantee proportionally scaled grains reproduce settling and motion.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「實體模型相似限制機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。","縮尺水工模型常優先保持重力與慣性相似，以觀察水面、分流和旋渦，但泥砂運移還受黏性、粒徑與密度控制。","只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。"],"optionsEn":["Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior.","Hydraulic scale models often preserve gravity-inertia similarity to examine water levels, flow division and vortices, while sediment transport also depends on viscosity, grain size and density.","Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"縮尺水工模型常優先保持重力與慣性相似，以觀察水面、分流和旋渦，但泥砂運移還受黏性、粒徑與密度控制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Hydraulic scale models often preserve gravity-inertia similarity to examine water levels, flow division and vortices, while sediment transport also depends on viscosity, grain size and density. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b268-v15-38","title":"實體模型相似限制機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「實體模型相似限制」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Physical-model similarity limits” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設長度比λL=1/25，福祿相似λV=√λL=1/5，流量比λQ=λL^(5/2)=1/3125。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume length ratio λL=1/25. Under Froude similarity λV=√λL=1/5 and discharge ratio λQ=λL^(5/2)=1/3125. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在試驗計畫分開列出已保持與失真的無量綱群，核對模型流量、粗糙度和量測解析度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: List preserved and distorted dimensionless groups separately, checking model flow, roughness and measurement resolution.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設長度比λL=1/25，福祿相似λV=√λL=1/5，流量比λQ=λL^(5/2)=1/3125。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume length ratio λL=1/25. Under Froude similarity λV=√λL=1/5 and discharge ratio λQ=λL^(5/2)=1/3125.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「實體模型相似限制機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。","床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設長度比λL=1/25，福祿相似λV=√λL=1/5，流量比λQ=λL^(5/2)=1/3125。"],"optionsEn":["Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration.","Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume length ratio λL=1/25."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設長度比λL=1/25，福祿相似λV=√λL=1/5，流量比λQ=λL^(5/2)=1/3125。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume length ratio λL=1/25. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b268-v15-39","title":"實體模型相似限制機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「實體模型相似限制」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Physical-model similarity limits” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在試驗計畫分開列出已保持與失真的無量綱群，核對模型流量、粗糙度和量測解析度。若加入可動床，另驗證起動與沉降尺度，並用原型觀測檢查放大後的預測。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"List preserved and distorted dimensionless groups separately, checking model flow, roughness and measurement resolution. If a mobile bed is added, verify motion and settling scales independently, and compare scaled predictions with prototype observations rather than assuming geometric similarity guarantees sediment similarity. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：為指定縮尺計算速度與流量比，再列出雷諾數和沉降尺度需要的額外資料。把水力、可動床與魚類觀察分成三個驗證問題，避免以同一試驗全數代替。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate velocity and discharge ratios for the selected scale, then list additional information needed for Reynolds and settling scales. Separate hydraulic, mobile-bed and fish observations into three verification questions instead of claiming one experiment answers all.","failure":"注意干擾：只按幾何比縮砂會讓黏性與黏聚效應變得相對重要，過小模型也可能落入不同流態；忽略這些失真會把清水試驗的漂亮流線誤當成可靠排砂證據。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Scaling grains geometrically can make viscosity and cohesion disproportionately important, and a small model may enter a different flow regime. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在試驗計畫分開列出已保持與失真的無量綱群，核對模型流量、粗糙度和量測解析度。若加入可動床，另驗證起動與沉降尺度，並用原型觀測檢查放大後的預測。","textEn":"List preserved and distorted dimensionless groups separately, checking model flow, roughness and measurement resolution. If a mobile bed is added, verify motion and settling scales independently, and compare scaled predictions with prototype observations rather than assuming geometric similarity guarantees sediment similarity.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"為指定縮尺計算速度與流量比，再列出雷諾數和沉降尺度需要的額外資料。把水力、可動床與魚類觀察分成三個驗證問題，避免以同一試驗全數代替。","textEn":"Calculate velocity and discharge ratios for the selected scale, then list additional information needed for Reynolds and settling scales. Separate hydraulic, mobile-bed and fish observations into three verification questions instead of claiming one experiment answers all.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「實體模型相似限制機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification\"?","options":["在試驗計畫分開列出已保持與失真的無量綱群，核對模型流量、粗糙度和量測解析度。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。"],"optionsEn":["List preserved and distorted dimensionless groups separately, checking model flow, roughness and measurement resolution.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在試驗計畫分開列出已保持與失真的無量綱群，核對模型流量、粗糙度和量測解析度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"List preserved and distorted dimensionless groups separately, checking model flow, roughness and measurement resolution. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b268-v15-40","title":"實體模型相似限制機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「實體模型相似限制」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Physical-model similarity limits” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只按幾何比縮砂會讓黏性與黏聚效應變得相對重要，過小模型也可能落入不同流態；忽略這些失真會把清水試驗的漂亮流線誤當成可靠排砂證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Scaling grains geometrically can make viscosity and cohesion disproportionately important, and a small model may enter a different flow regime. Ignoring these distortions turns attractive clear-water streamlines into unjustified evidence of sediment-removal performance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例定義長度比為模型除以原型，採福祿相似求速度與流量比；未宣稱雷諾相似或可動床相似同時成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Froude similarity supplies velocity and discharge ratios without claiming simultaneous Reynolds or mobile-bed similarity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只按幾何比縮砂會讓黏性與黏聚效應變得相對重要，過小模型也可能落入不同流態；忽略這些失真會把清水試驗的漂亮流線誤當成可靠排砂證據。","textEn":"Scaling grains geometrically can make viscosity and cohesion disproportionately important, and a small model may enter a different flow regime. Ignoring these distortions turns attractive clear-water streamlines into unjustified evidence of sediment-removal performance.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「實體模型相似限制機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只按幾何比縮砂會讓黏性與黏聚效應變得相對重要，過小模型也可能落入不同流態；忽略這些失真會把清水試驗的漂亮流線誤當成可靠排砂證據。","只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Scaling grains geometrically can make viscosity and cohesion disproportionately important, and a small model may enter a different flow regime.","Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只按幾何比縮砂會讓黏性與黏聚效應變得相對重要，過小模型也可能落入不同流態；忽略這些失真會把清水試驗的漂亮流線誤當成可靠排砂證據。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Scaling grains geometrically can make viscosity and cohesion disproportionately important, and a small model may enter a different flow regime. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b269","title":"河川水位自動遙測","titleEn":"Automatic river-level telemetry","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課將自動水位站拆為基準、感測、取樣、傳輸、率定與電源備援，逐一區分準確度、資料時效及可用性。以李斯渡口和維克斯堡真實站點為背景，所有算例是合成資料；觀測水位、推估流量和警戒決策屬不同層次，必須保留各自假設及品質旗標。","summaryEn":"This course separates automated gaging into datum, sensing, sampling, transmission, rating and power redundancy, distinguishing accuracy, data age and availability. Lees Ferry and Vicksburg provide real station context, while every calculation uses synthetic observations. Measured stage, estimated discharge and warning decisions occupy different layers and require their own assumptions and quality flags.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["高程基準","Elevation datum"],["感測取樣","Sensing and sampling"],["現地記錄","Local logging"],["遙測發布","Telemetry publication"],["品質追溯","Quality traceability"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["高程基準","感測取樣","現地記錄","遙測發布","品質追溯"],"labelsEn":["Elevation datum","Sensing and sampling","Local logging","Telemetry publication","Quality traceability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"敏感度固定率定係數a=20 m^1.4/s與指數b=1.6，原水位h=2.0 m、零流量參數h0=0.5 m，流量為38.26 m³/s。若水位有正偏差0.10 m而其他參數不變，有效水頭由1.5增至1.6 m，推估流量變成42.43 m³/s，增加約10.88%。這不是把水位增加5%就讓流量增加5%，因率定依有效水頭的非線性冪次變化。實際站點還可能有回水、控制改變及率定參數不確定度；本例只隔離水位偏差，不能據此宣稱流量總誤差或設置警戒值。","textEn":"Hold rating coefficient a=20 m^1.4/s and exponent b=1.6 fixed, with h=2.0 m and zero-flow parameter h0=0.5 m. The baseline estimate is 38.26 m³/s. A positive stage bias of 0.10 m raises effective head from 1.5 to 1.6 m and gives 42.43 m³/s, approximately 10.88% higher. A five-percent increase in the displayed stage therefore does not produce a five-percent discharge change, because the relation is nonlinear in effective head. Real stations additionally face backwater, control changes and uncertain rating parameters. This isolates stage bias only and establishes neither total discharge error nor a warning setting. Datum checks and independent discharge measurements remain separate evidence needed to evaluate the resulting record.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b269-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「測站基準與水面高程機理與驗證」與「壓力式量測與氣壓補償機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Gage datum and water elevation mechanism and verification\" and \"Pressure sensing and barometric compensation mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b269-v15-01","title":"測站基準與水面高程機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Gage datum and water elevation mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「測站基準與水面高程」如何影響河川水位自動遙測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gage datum and water elevation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic river-level telemetry”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水位計讀值通常相對測站自訂零點，不等於海拔或工程共用高程。基準點沉陷、支架位移與換儀器可能使整段資料產生偏移，即使曲線仍然平滑；跨站或與堤頂比較前必須連接相同垂直基準，並保存基準更動日期，避免把儀器零點變化誤認為河川水位突變。本例基準與讀值已用同一垂直系統及公尺表示；沒有處理不同國家高程系統、橢球高或潮位基準間的轉換。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測站基準與水面高程」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A gage reading is generally relative to a station datum rather than sea level or a shared project elevation. Benchmark settlement, support movement and instrument replacement can shift an entire record while leaving a smooth curve. Comparing stations or levee crests requires a common vertical datum and documented changes so that instrument offsets are not mistaken for river-level changes. The example uses meters and one vertical system for datum and reading. It does not convert national height systems, ellipsoidal heights or tidal datums. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gage datum and water elevation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設測站零點高程z0=100.00 m、水尺讀值h=2.35 m，水面高程Z=z0+h=102.35 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gage-datum elevation z0=100.00 m and reading h=2.35 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有水位計顯示的公尺數都已是同一海拔基準下的高程。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every water-level reading in meters already uses the same sea-level datum.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測站基準與水面高程」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gage datum and water elevation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-01-k1","title":"測站基準與水面高程機理與驗證","titleEn":"Gage datum and water elevation mechanism and verification","text":"水位計讀值通常相對測站自訂零點，不等於海拔或工程共用高程。基準點沉陷、支架位移與換儀器可能使整段資料產生偏移，即使曲線仍然平滑；跨站或與堤頂比較前必須連接相同垂直基準，並保存基準更動日期，避免把儀器零點變化誤認為河川水位突變。","textEn":"A gage reading is generally relative to a station datum rather than sea level or a shared project elevation. Benchmark settlement, support movement and instrument replacement can shift an entire record while leaving a smooth curve.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有水位計顯示的公尺數都已是同一海拔基準下的高程。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every water-level reading in meters already uses the same sea-level datum. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測站基準與水面高程機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gage datum and water elevation mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["所有水位計顯示的公尺數都已是同一海拔基準下的高程。","水位計讀值通常相對測站自訂零點，不等於海拔或工程共用高程。","任何壓力感測器輸出除以水重度就一定得到真實河川水深。"],"optionsEn":["Every water-level reading in meters already uses the same sea-level datum.","A gage reading is generally relative to a station datum rather than sea level or a shared project elevation.","Any pressure output divided by water unit weight gives true river depth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水位計讀值通常相對測站自訂零點，不等於海拔或工程共用高程。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A gage reading is generally relative to a station datum rather than sea level or a shared project elevation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b269-v15-02","title":"測站基準與水面高程機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Gage datum and water elevation mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測站基準與水面高程」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gage datum and water elevation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設測站零點高程z0=100.00 m、水尺讀值h=2.35 m，水面高程Z=z0+h=102.35 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gage-datum elevation z0=100.00 m and reading h=2.35 m. Water-surface elevation Z=z0+h=102.35 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：由獨立穩定基準點檢查水尺及感測器標高，保留水準閉合與前後儀器高度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check staff-gage and sensor elevations from independent stable marks, retaining leveling closure and instrument-height records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設測站零點高程z0=100.00 m、水尺讀值h=2.35 m，水面高程Z=z0+h=102.35 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gage-datum elevation z0=100.00 m and reading h=2.35 m. Water-surface elevation Z=z0+h=102.35 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測站基準與水面高程機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gage datum and water elevation mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["只要圖表每秒重畫，就代表河川每秒都有一筆新量測。","裝好水位計後，任何洪水流量都能無誤差地自動換算。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設測站零點高程z0=100.00 m、水尺讀值h=2.35 m，水面高程Z=z0+h=102.35 m。"],"optionsEn":["A graph refreshed every second means the river has a new measurement every second.","Once a stage sensor is installed, every flood discharge converts automatically without error.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gage-datum elevation z0=100.00 m and reading h=2.35 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設測站零點高程z0=100.00 m、水尺讀值h=2.35 m，水面高程Z=z0+h=102.35 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gage-datum elevation z0=100.00 m and reading h=2.35 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b269-v15-03","title":"測站基準與水面高程機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gage datum and water elevation mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測站基準與水面高程」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gage datum and water elevation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"由獨立穩定基準點檢查水尺及感測器標高，保留水準閉合與前後儀器高度。對任何零點改正加上生效日期和版本，並用同時人工讀值確認自動資料沒有未標記跳變。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check staff-gage and sensor elevations from independent stable marks, retaining leveling closure and instrument-height records. Date and version every datum correction, and compare simultaneous manual observations to ensure that automated data contain no unmarked discontinuity after installation or adjustment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：為兩站建立零點、讀值和水面高程表，讓一站零點改變但實際水面不變。說明資料庫應如何保留原值、改正值及版本，以免形成假洪峰。","observationEn":"Site practice: Build datum, reading and elevation tables for two stations, changing one datum without changing the physical surface. Explain how original values, corrections and versions should be retained to prevent an artificial flood peak.","failure":"注意干擾：把局部水尺數字直接和海拔堤頂比較會產生錯誤餘高，支架沉陷又可能讓整季記錄偏移；若改正覆蓋原資料，事後便無法追溯當時顯示的警戒情境。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Comparing a local gage number directly with a levee elevation gives false freeboard, and support settlement can bias a season of data. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"由獨立穩定基準點檢查水尺及感測器標高，保留水準閉合與前後儀器高度。對任何零點改正加上生效日期和版本，並用同時人工讀值確認自動資料沒有未標記跳變。","textEn":"Check staff-gage and sensor elevations from independent stable marks, retaining leveling closure and instrument-height records. Date and version every datum correction, and compare simultaneous manual observations to ensure that automated data contain no unmarked discontinuity after installation or adjustment.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"為兩站建立零點、讀值和水面高程表，讓一站零點改變但實際水面不變。說明資料庫應如何保留原值、改正值及版本，以免形成假洪峰。","textEn":"Build datum, reading and elevation tables for two stations, changing one datum without changing the physical surface. Explain how original values, corrections and versions should be retained to prevent an artificial flood peak.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測站基準與水面高程機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gage datum and water elevation mechanism and verification\"?","options":["由獨立穩定基準點檢查水尺及感測器標高，保留水準閉合與前後儀器高度。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","感測器顯示到毫米，就代表水面絕對高程也準確到毫米。"],"optionsEn":["Check staff-gage and sensor elevations from independent stable marks, retaining leveling closure and instrument-height records.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Millimeter display resolution means absolute water elevation is accurate to a millimeter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"由獨立穩定基準點檢查水尺及感測器標高，保留水準閉合與前後儀器高度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check staff-gage and sensor elevations from independent stable marks, retaining leveling closure and instrument-height records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b269-v15-04","title":"測站基準與水面高程機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gage datum and water elevation mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測站基準與水面高程」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gage datum and water elevation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把局部水尺數字直接和海拔堤頂比較會產生錯誤餘高，支架沉陷又可能讓整季記錄偏移；若改正覆蓋原資料，事後便無法追溯當時顯示的警戒情境。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Comparing a local gage number directly with a levee elevation gives false freeboard, and support settlement can bias a season of data. Overwriting originals with corrections prevents reconstruction of the warning information displayed at the time. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例基準與讀值已用同一垂直系統及公尺表示；沒有處理不同國家高程系統、橢球高或潮位基準間的轉換。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It does not convert national height systems, ellipsoidal heights or tidal datums.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有水位計顯示的公尺數都已是同一海拔基準下的高程。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every water-level reading in meters already uses the same sea-level datum.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把局部水尺數字直接和海拔堤頂比較會產生錯誤餘高，支架沉陷又可能讓整季記錄偏移；若改正覆蓋原資料，事後便無法追溯當時顯示的警戒情境。","textEn":"Comparing a local gage number directly with a levee elevation gives false freeboard, and support settlement can bias a season of data. Overwriting originals with corrections prevents reconstruction of the warning information displayed at the time.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測站基準與水面高程機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gage datum and water elevation mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把局部水尺數字直接和海拔堤頂比較會產生錯誤餘高，支架沉陷又可能讓整季記錄偏移；若改正覆蓋原資料，事後便無法追溯當時顯示的警戒情境。","任何壓力感測器輸出除以水重度就一定得到真實河川水深。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Comparing a local gage number directly with a levee elevation gives false freeboard, and support settlement can bias a season of data.","Any pressure output divided by water unit weight gives true river depth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把局部水尺數字直接和海拔堤頂比較會產生錯誤餘高，支架沉陷又可能讓整季記錄偏移；若改正覆蓋原資料，事後便無法追溯當時顯示的警戒情境。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Comparing a local gage number directly with a levee elevation gives false freeboard, and support settlement can bias a season of data. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b269-v15-05","title":"壓力式量測與氣壓補償機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pressure sensing and barometric compensation mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「壓力式量測與氣壓補償」如何影響河川水位自動遙測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pressure sensing and barometric compensation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic river-level telemetry”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"浸水式壓力計依水柱壓力換算深度，絕對壓力感測器需扣除同步大氣壓，通氣式則依通氣管維持參考。水密度受溫鹽影響，感測器位置也可能被淤埋或漂移；因此壓力變化不一定全是水位變化，氣壓補償和安裝高程必須與原始壓力一起保存。本例使用已扣氣壓的表壓並假設靜水、淡水定密度；在高速流或堵塞導壓管附近，動壓與延遲需要另行評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壓力式量測與氣壓補償」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A submerged pressure sensor converts water-column pressure to depth. Absolute sensors require synchronized atmospheric subtraction, while vented sensors rely on a reference vent. Density varies with temperature and salinity, and the sensor can be buried or displaced. Pressure changes therefore need not all represent stage changes; barometric compensation and installation elevation must accompany the raw pressure record. The example uses gauge pressure after atmospheric subtraction and assumes hydrostatic freshwater of fixed density. Dynamic pressure and lag require separate assessment near fast flow or blocked pressure tubing. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pressure sensing and barometric compensation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設表壓p=19620 Pa、ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²，水柱h=p/(ρg)=2.00 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gauge pressure p=19620 Pa, density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「任何壓力感測器輸出除以水重度就一定得到真實河川水深。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any pressure output divided by water unit weight gives true river depth.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「壓力式量測與氣壓補償」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pressure sensing and barometric compensation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-05-k1","title":"壓力式量測與氣壓補償機理與驗證","titleEn":"Pressure sensing and barometric compensation mechanism and verification","text":"浸水式壓力計依水柱壓力換算深度，絕對壓力感測器需扣除同步大氣壓，通氣式則依通氣管維持參考。水密度受溫鹽影響，感測器位置也可能被淤埋或漂移；因此壓力變化不一定全是水位變化，氣壓補償和安裝高程必須與原始壓力一起保存。","textEn":"A submerged pressure sensor converts water-column pressure to depth. Absolute sensors require synchronized atmospheric subtraction, while vented sensors rely on a reference vent.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任何壓力感測器輸出除以水重度就一定得到真實河川水深。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any pressure output divided by water unit weight gives true river depth. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壓力式量測與氣壓補償機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pressure sensing and barometric compensation mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["任何壓力感測器輸出除以水重度就一定得到真實河川水深。","雷達不接觸水，所以不需要高程測量或現地水尺交叉驗證。","浸水式壓力計依水柱壓力換算深度，絕對壓力感測器需扣除同步大氣壓，通氣式則依通氣管維持參考。"],"optionsEn":["Any pressure output divided by water unit weight gives true river depth.","Noncontact radar needs neither elevation surveying nor field staff-gage checks.","A submerged pressure sensor converts water-column pressure to depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"浸水式壓力計依水柱壓力換算深度，絕對壓力感測器需扣除同步大氣壓，通氣式則依通氣管維持參考。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A submerged pressure sensor converts water-column pressure to depth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b269-v15-06","title":"壓力式量測與氣壓補償機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Pressure sensing and barometric compensation mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「壓力式量測與氣壓補償」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pressure sensing and barometric compensation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設表壓p=19620 Pa、ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²，水柱h=p/(ρg)=2.00 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gauge pressure p=19620 Pa, density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Water-column height h=p/(ρg)=2.00 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步記錄水壓與氣壓，核對壓力種類、單位與感測器標高，並以人工水尺交叉比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record water and atmospheric pressure synchronously, checking pressure type, units and sensor elevation against a manual staff gage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設表壓p=19620 Pa、ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²，水柱h=p/(ρg)=2.00 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gauge pressure p=19620 Pa, density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Water-column height h=p/(ρg)=2.00 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「壓力式量測與氣壓補償機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pressure sensing and barometric compensation mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設表壓p=19620 Pa、ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²，水柱h=p/(ρg)=2.00 m。","封包剛收到就一定代表此刻水位，無需再看量測時間。","取樣越密，任何相鄰兩點差分得到的水位速率就一定越可靠。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gauge pressure p=19620 Pa, density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s².","A newly received packet necessarily represents current stage without checking observation time.","Denser sampling always makes a two-point stage derivative more reliable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設表壓p=19620 Pa、ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²，水柱h=p/(ρg)=2.00 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gauge pressure p=19620 Pa, density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b269-v15-07","title":"壓力式量測與氣壓補償機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pressure sensing and barometric compensation mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「壓力式量測與氣壓補償」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pressure sensing and barometric compensation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步記錄水壓與氣壓，核對壓力種類、單位與感測器標高，並以人工水尺交叉比較。檢查通氣管結露、導壓管堵塞與漂移，避免用軟體校正常數掩蓋實際安裝故障。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record water and atmospheric pressure synchronously, checking pressure type, units and sensor elevation against a manual staff gage. Inspect vent condensation, pressure-line blockage and displacement so that software correction constants do not conceal physical installation faults or delayed response. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較相同水位下兩種大氣壓的絕對壓力讀值，完成扣除後確認水深不變。再加入氣壓資料延遲情境，說明時間同步和精確感測同樣必要。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare absolute readings at two atmospheric pressures with unchanged water level and confirm invariant depth after subtraction. Then introduce delayed barometric data and explain why synchronization matters alongside sensor precision.","failure":"注意干擾：將絕對壓力直接換成水深會把大氣壓算入水柱，通氣管受潮則可能形成緩慢偏差；淤埋造成的遲滯也可能讓洪峰看起來較低且較晚。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Converting absolute pressure directly includes atmospheric pressure as water depth. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步記錄水壓與氣壓，核對壓力種類、單位與感測器標高，並以人工水尺交叉比較。檢查通氣管結露、導壓管堵塞與漂移，避免用軟體校正常數掩蓋實際安裝故障。","textEn":"Record water and atmospheric pressure synchronously, checking pressure type, units and sensor elevation against a manual staff gage. Inspect vent condensation, pressure-line blockage and displacement so that software correction constants do not conceal physical installation faults or delayed response.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較相同水位下兩種大氣壓的絕對壓力讀值，完成扣除後確認水深不變。再加入氣壓資料延遲情境，說明時間同步和精確感測同樣必要。","textEn":"Compare absolute readings at two atmospheric pressures with unchanged water level and confirm invariant depth after subtraction. Then introduce delayed barometric data and explain why synchronization matters alongside sensor precision.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「壓力式量測與氣壓補償機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pressure sensing and barometric compensation mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","同步記錄水壓與氣壓，核對壓力種類、單位與感測器標高，並以人工水尺交叉比較。","電池安培小時越大就可直接比較續航，不需要知道電壓或負載。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Record water and atmospheric pressure synchronously, checking pressure type, units and sensor elevation against a manual staff gage.","Battery ampere-hours alone compare endurance without voltage or load information."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同步記錄水壓與氣壓，核對壓力種類、單位與感測器標高，並以人工水尺交叉比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record water and atmospheric pressure synchronously, checking pressure type, units and sensor elevation against a manual staff gage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b269-v15-08","title":"壓力式量測與氣壓補償機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pressure sensing and barometric compensation mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「壓力式量測與氣壓補償」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pressure sensing and barometric compensation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將絕對壓力直接換成水深會把大氣壓算入水柱，通氣管受潮則可能形成緩慢偏差；淤埋造成的遲滯也可能讓洪峰看起來較低且較晚。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Converting absolute pressure directly includes atmospheric pressure as water depth. A wet vent can produce gradual bias, while sediment burial may delay response and make a flood crest appear lower and later. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例使用已扣氣壓的表壓並假設靜水、淡水定密度；在高速流或堵塞導壓管附近，動壓與延遲需要另行評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Dynamic pressure and lag require separate assessment near fast flow or blocked pressure tubing.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任何壓力感測器輸出除以水重度就一定得到真實河川水深。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any pressure output divided by water unit weight gives true river depth.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將絕對壓力直接換成水深會把大氣壓算入水柱，通氣管受潮則可能形成緩慢偏差；淤埋造成的遲滯也可能讓洪峰看起來較低且較晚。","textEn":"Converting absolute pressure directly includes atmospheric pressure as water depth. A wet vent can produce gradual bias, while sediment burial may delay response and make a flood crest appear lower and later.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「壓力式量測與氣壓補償機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pressure sensing and barometric compensation mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","雷達不接觸水，所以不需要高程測量或現地水尺交叉驗證。","將絕對壓力直接換成水深會把大氣壓算入水柱，通氣管受潮則可能形成緩慢偏差；淤埋造成的遲滯也可能讓洪峰看起來較低且較晚。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Noncontact radar needs neither elevation surveying nor field staff-gage checks.","Converting absolute pressure directly includes atmospheric pressure as water depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將絕對壓力直接換成水深會把大氣壓算入水柱，通氣管受潮則可能形成緩慢偏差；淤埋造成的遲滯也可能讓洪峰看起來較低且較晚。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Converting absolute pressure directly includes atmospheric pressure as water depth. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b269-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「雷達距離與安裝幾何機理與驗證」與「取樣間隔與漏失洪峰機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Radar range and installation geometry mechanism and verification\" and \"Sampling interval and missed crests mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b269-v15-09","title":"雷達距離與安裝幾何機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Radar range and installation geometry mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「雷達距離與安裝幾何」如何影響河川水位自動遙測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Radar range and installation geometry” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic river-level telemetry”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"非接觸雷達由天線到水面的傳播訊號求距離，再與天線高程組合成水面高程。量到的是距離而不是直接水位，斜裝、波浪、橋構件與漂浮物可能改變有效回波；儀器內部常使用調頻等處理，但基礎往返傳播關係仍可用來核對量綱與幾何方向。本例為理想垂直往返飛行時間示意，近似空氣中光速；不是描述特定雷達的電子取樣解析度或實際量測準確度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「雷達距離與安裝幾何」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Noncontact radar derives antenna-to-surface range from the propagation signal and combines it with antenna elevation. It measures distance rather than stage directly; tilt, waves, bridge members and floating debris can change the effective return. Practical instruments often use frequency-modulated processing, but the basic round-trip relation remains useful for checking dimensions and geometric direction. The example illustrates ideal vertical round-trip travel time using approximate light speed in air. It does not describe a particular radar’s sampling resolution or field accuracy. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Radar range and installation geometry” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設c=3.0×10⁸ m/s、往返t=40 ns，距離d=ct/2=6.00 m；天線Zs=110 m時水面Z=104 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume c=3.0×10⁸ m/s and round-trip t=40 ns.","failure":"常見誤解：「雷達不接觸水，所以不需要高程測量或現地水尺交叉驗證。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Noncontact radar needs neither elevation surveying nor field staff-gage checks.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「雷達距離與安裝幾何」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Radar range and installation geometry”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-09-k1","title":"雷達距離與安裝幾何機理與驗證","titleEn":"Radar range and installation geometry mechanism and verification","text":"非接觸雷達由天線到水面的傳播訊號求距離，再與天線高程組合成水面高程。量到的是距離而不是直接水位，斜裝、波浪、橋構件與漂浮物可能改變有效回波；儀器內部常使用調頻等處理，但基礎往返傳播關係仍可用來核對量綱與幾何方向。","textEn":"Noncontact radar derives antenna-to-surface range from the propagation signal and combines it with antenna elevation. It measures distance rather than stage directly; tilt, waves, bridge members and floating debris can change the effective return.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：雷達不接觸水，所以不需要高程測量或現地水尺交叉驗證。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Noncontact radar needs neither elevation surveying nor field staff-gage checks. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「雷達距離與安裝幾何機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Radar range and installation geometry mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["非接觸雷達由天線到水面的傳播訊號求距離，再與天線高程組合成水面高程。","雷達不接觸水，所以不需要高程測量或現地水尺交叉驗證。","只要圖表每秒重畫，就代表河川每秒都有一筆新量測。"],"optionsEn":["Noncontact radar derives antenna-to-surface range from the propagation signal and combines it with antenna elevation.","Noncontact radar needs neither elevation surveying nor field staff-gage checks.","A graph refreshed every second means the river has a new measurement every second."],"answer":0,"explanation":"非接觸雷達由天線到水面的傳播訊號求距離，再與天線高程組合成水面高程。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Noncontact radar derives antenna-to-surface range from the propagation signal and combines it with antenna elevation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b269-v15-10","title":"雷達距離與安裝幾何機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Radar range and installation geometry mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雷達距離與安裝幾何」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Radar range and installation geometry” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設c=3.0×10⁸ m/s、往返t=40 ns，距離d=ct/2=6.00 m；天線Zs=110 m時水面Z=104 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume c=3.0×10⁸ m/s and round-trip t=40 ns. Range d=ct/2=6.00 m; antenna elevation Zs=110 m gives water elevation Z=104 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測天線標高與傾角並檢查波束覆蓋，將回波品質和水尺讀值同步保存。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey antenna elevation and tilt, inspect beam coverage and retain echo-quality indicators with simultaneous staff-gage readings.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設c=3.0×10⁸ m/s、往返t=40 ns，距離d=ct/2=6.00 m；天線Zs=110 m時水面Z=104 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume c=3.0×10⁸ m/s and round-trip t=40 ns. Range d=ct/2=6.00 m; antenna elevation Zs=110 m gives water elevation Z=104 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「雷達距離與安裝幾何機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Radar range and installation geometry mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["裝好水位計後，任何洪水流量都能無誤差地自動換算。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設c=3.0×10⁸ m/s、往返t=40 ns，距離d=ct/2=6.00 m。","感測器顯示到毫米，就代表水面絕對高程也準確到毫米。"],"optionsEn":["Once a stage sensor is installed, every flood discharge converts automatically without error.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume c=3.0×10⁸ m/s and round-trip t=40 ns.","Millimeter display resolution means absolute water elevation is accurate to a millimeter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設c=3.0×10⁸ m/s、往返t=40 ns，距離d=ct/2=6.00 m；天線Zs=110 m時水面Z=104 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume c=3.0×10⁸ m/s and round-trip t=40 ns. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b269-v15-11","title":"雷達距離與安裝幾何機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Radar range and installation geometry mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「雷達距離與安裝幾何」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Radar range and installation geometry” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測天線標高與傾角並檢查波束覆蓋，將回波品質和水尺讀值同步保存。針對橋面反射、漂浮物及暴雨測試異常旗標，確認失去有效水面回波時不會輸出看似正常的舊值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey antenna elevation and tilt, inspect beam coverage and retain echo-quality indicators with simultaneous staff-gage readings. Test anomaly flags for bridge reflections, floating objects and intense rain, ensuring that lost water-surface returns do not silently appear as normal stale measurements. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出天線、橋構件及水面三個回波路徑，指出哪條距離可用於水面高程。改變天線標高並保持水面不變，說明資料系統必須同步更新哪些參數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw antenna, bridge-member and water-surface return paths, identifying the range usable for elevation. Change antenna height without moving the water and explain which data-system parameters must be updated together.","failure":"注意干擾：漏除往返因子二會把距離加倍，天線支架位移則使所有高程產生偏移；挑錯回波可能讀到橋梁或漂流物，曲線平滑也不能保證目標正確。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting the round-trip factor doubles range, and support movement shifts all elevations. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測天線標高與傾角並檢查波束覆蓋，將回波品質和水尺讀值同步保存。針對橋面反射、漂浮物及暴雨測試異常旗標，確認失去有效水面回波時不會輸出看似正常的舊值。","textEn":"Survey antenna elevation and tilt, inspect beam coverage and retain echo-quality indicators with simultaneous staff-gage readings. Test anomaly flags for bridge reflections, floating objects and intense rain, ensuring that lost water-surface returns do not silently appear as normal stale measurements.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出天線、橋構件及水面三個回波路徑，指出哪條距離可用於水面高程。改變天線標高並保持水面不變，說明資料系統必須同步更新哪些參數。","textEn":"Draw antenna, bridge-member and water-surface return paths, identifying the range usable for elevation. Change antenna height without moving the water and explain which data-system parameters must be updated together.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「雷達距離與安裝幾何機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Radar range and installation geometry mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只要現場裝兩支感測器，就一定可以把全部失效機率相乘。","量測天線標高與傾角並檢查波束覆蓋，將回波品質和水尺讀值同步保存。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Installing two field sensors always permits multiplication of all failure probabilities.","Survey antenna elevation and tilt, inspect beam coverage and retain echo-quality indicators with simultaneous staff-gage readings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測天線標高與傾角並檢查波束覆蓋，將回波品質和水尺讀值同步保存。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey antenna elevation and tilt, inspect beam coverage and retain echo-quality indicators with simultaneous staff-gage readings. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b269-v15-12","title":"雷達距離與安裝幾何機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Radar range and installation geometry mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雷達距離與安裝幾何」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Radar range and installation geometry” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏除往返因子二會把距離加倍，天線支架位移則使所有高程產生偏移；挑錯回波可能讀到橋梁或漂流物，曲線平滑也不能保證目標正確。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting the round-trip factor doubles range, and support movement shifts all elevations. Selecting the wrong return may track a bridge or floating debris; a smooth time series does not guarantee the correct target. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例為理想垂直往返飛行時間示意，近似空氣中光速；不是描述特定雷達的電子取樣解析度或實際量測準確度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It does not describe a particular radar’s sampling resolution or field accuracy.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「雷達不接觸水，所以不需要高程測量或現地水尺交叉驗證。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Noncontact radar needs neither elevation surveying nor field staff-gage checks.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏除往返因子二會把距離加倍，天線支架位移則使所有高程產生偏移；挑錯回波可能讀到橋梁或漂流物，曲線平滑也不能保證目標正確。","textEn":"Omitting the round-trip factor doubles range, and support movement shifts all elevations. Selecting the wrong return may track a bridge or floating debris; a smooth time series does not guarantee the correct target.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雷達距離與安裝幾何機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Radar range and installation geometry mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["漏除往返因子二會把距離加倍，天線支架位移則使所有高程產生偏移；挑錯回波可能讀到橋梁或漂流物，曲線平滑也不能保證目標正確。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要圖表每秒重畫，就代表河川每秒都有一筆新量測。"],"optionsEn":["Omitting the round-trip factor doubles range, and support movement shifts all elevations.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A graph refreshed every second means the river has a new measurement every second."],"answer":0,"explanation":"漏除往返因子二會把距離加倍，天線支架位移則使所有高程產生偏移；挑錯回波可能讀到橋梁或漂流物，曲線平滑也不能保證目標正確。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting the round-trip factor doubles range, and support movement shifts all elevations. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b269-v15-13","title":"取樣間隔與漏失洪峰機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Sampling interval and missed crests mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「取樣間隔與漏失洪峰」如何影響河川水位自動遙測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sampling interval and missed crests” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic river-level telemetry”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"離散水位資料只能觀察取樣時刻，洪峰若發生在兩筆之間就可能被低估。提高取樣頻率可縮小這類誤差，但儲存、傳輸頻率與畫面更新不一定相同；平均濾波又可能壓低短時尖峰，因此應保存原始取樣時間，並區分缺測與真正平穩水位。下式假設內部洪峰附近水位變化速率有已知上限且兩側取樣完整；只界定時間離散誤差，未含儀器誤差或資料中斷。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「取樣間隔與漏失洪峰」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Discrete records observe stage only at sample times, so a crest between samples can be underestimated. Faster sampling reduces this error, but storage, transmission and display frequencies need not match. Averaging can additionally suppress short peaks, making original timestamps and a clear distinction between missing data and genuinely stable stage essential. The bound assumes a known maximum rate around an interior crest and complete samples on both sides. It concerns temporal discretization only, excluding sensor error and missing records. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sampling interval and missed crests” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設|dh/dt|≤r=0.004 m/s、等距取樣Δt=60 s，洪峰到最近取樣最多30 s，漏峰界限rΔt/2=0.12 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume |dh/dt|≤r=0.004 m/s and sample interval Δt=60 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要圖表每秒重畫，就代表河川每秒都有一筆新量測。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A graph refreshed every second means the river has a new measurement every second.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「取樣間隔與漏失洪峰」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sampling interval and missed crests”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-13-k1","title":"取樣間隔與漏失洪峰機理與驗證","titleEn":"Sampling interval and missed crests mechanism and verification","text":"離散水位資料只能觀察取樣時刻，洪峰若發生在兩筆之間就可能被低估。提高取樣頻率可縮小這類誤差，但儲存、傳輸頻率與畫面更新不一定相同；平均濾波又可能壓低短時尖峰，因此應保存原始取樣時間，並區分缺測與真正平穩水位。","textEn":"Discrete records observe stage only at sample times, so a crest between samples can be underestimated. Faster sampling reduces this error, but storage, transmission and display frequencies need not match.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要圖表每秒重畫，就代表河川每秒都有一筆新量測。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A graph refreshed every second means the river has a new measurement every second. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「取樣間隔與漏失洪峰機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sampling interval and missed crests mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["只要圖表每秒重畫，就代表河川每秒都有一筆新量測。","離散水位資料只能觀察取樣時刻，洪峰若發生在兩筆之間就可能被低估。","封包剛收到就一定代表此刻水位，無需再看量測時間。"],"optionsEn":["A graph refreshed every second means the river has a new measurement every second.","Discrete records observe stage only at sample times, so a crest between samples can be underestimated.","A newly received packet necessarily represents current stage without checking observation time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"離散水位資料只能觀察取樣時刻，洪峰若發生在兩筆之間就可能被低估。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Discrete records observe stage only at sample times, so a crest between samples can be underestimated. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b269-v15-14","title":"取樣間隔與漏失洪峰機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Sampling interval and missed crests mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「取樣間隔與漏失洪峰」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sampling interval and missed crests” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設|dh/dt|≤r=0.004 m/s、等距取樣Δt=60 s，洪峰到最近取樣最多30 s，漏峰界限rΔt/2=0.12 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume |dh/dt|≤r=0.004 m/s and sample interval Δt=60 s. The nearest sample is at most 30 s away, giving missed-crest bound rΔt/2=0.12 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從原始時間戳檢查實際取樣間距及遺漏，將平均後曲線與高頻原資料比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check actual intervals and omissions from original timestamps, comparing averaged curves with high-frequency records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設|dh/dt|≤r=0.004 m/s、等距取樣Δt=60 s，洪峰到最近取樣最多30 s，漏峰界限rΔt/2=0.12 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume |dh/dt|≤r=0.004 m/s and sample interval Δt=60 s. The nearest sample is at most 30 s away, giving missed-crest bound rΔt/2=0.12 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「取樣間隔與漏失洪峰機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sampling interval and missed crests mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["取樣越密，任何相鄰兩點差分得到的水位速率就一定越可靠。","電池安培小時越大就可直接比較續航，不需要知道電壓或負載。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設|dh/dt|≤r=0.004 m/s、等距取樣Δt=60 s，洪峰到最近取樣最多30 s，漏峰界限rΔt/2=0.12 m。"],"optionsEn":["Denser sampling always makes a two-point stage derivative more reliable.","Battery ampere-hours alone compare endurance without voltage or load information.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume |dh/dt|≤r=0.004 m/s and sample interval Δt=60 s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設|dh/dt|≤r=0.004 m/s、等距取樣Δt=60 s，洪峰到最近取樣最多30 s，漏峰界限rΔt/2=0.12 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume |dh/dt|≤r=0.004 m/s and sample interval Δt=60 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b269-v15-15","title":"取樣間隔與漏失洪峰機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sampling interval and missed crests mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「取樣間隔與漏失洪峰」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sampling interval and missed crests” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從原始時間戳檢查實際取樣間距及遺漏，將平均後曲線與高頻原資料比較。以獨立事件驗證速率上限的合理性；若有缺筆或未觀測尖峰，需撤回此完整取樣誤差界限。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check actual intervals and omissions from original timestamps, comparing averaged curves with high-frequency records. Assess the assumed rate bound against independent events; if samples are missing or sharper behavior is unobserved, withdraw this complete-sampling error bound instead of treating it as guaranteed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立一個落在兩取樣點中間的三角洪峰，分別以六十秒和三十秒取樣比較峰值。將顯示更新頻率保持相同，說明它為何不會補回漏掉的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Create a triangular crest between samples and compare sixty- and thirty-second sampling. Keep display refresh unchanged and explain why faster redraws do not recover observations that were never collected.","failure":"注意干擾：把傳輸每小時一次誤當成現地每分鐘取樣會低估資訊延遲，平均值也可能掩蓋警戒尖峰；無資料時延用最後值會產生看似平穩的假象。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing hourly transmission with minute-by-minute local sampling understates information delay, and averaging can conceal a warning crest. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從原始時間戳檢查實際取樣間距及遺漏，將平均後曲線與高頻原資料比較。以獨立事件驗證速率上限的合理性；若有缺筆或未觀測尖峰，需撤回此完整取樣誤差界限。","textEn":"Check actual intervals and omissions from original timestamps, comparing averaged curves with high-frequency records. Assess the assumed rate bound against independent events; if samples are missing or sharper behavior is unobserved, withdraw this complete-sampling error bound instead of treating it as guaranteed.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立一個落在兩取樣點中間的三角洪峰，分別以六十秒和三十秒取樣比較峰值。將顯示更新頻率保持相同，說明它為何不會補回漏掉的觀測。","textEn":"Create a triangular crest between samples and compare sixty- and thirty-second sampling. Keep display refresh unchanged and explain why faster redraws do not recover observations that were never collected.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「取樣間隔與漏失洪峰機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sampling interval and missed crests mechanism and verification\"?","options":["從原始時間戳檢查實際取樣間距及遺漏，將平均後曲線與高頻原資料比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","所有水位計顯示的公尺數都已是同一海拔基準下的高程。"],"optionsEn":["Check actual intervals and omissions from original timestamps, comparing averaged curves with high-frequency records.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Every water-level reading in meters already uses the same sea-level datum."],"answer":0,"explanation":"從原始時間戳檢查實際取樣間距及遺漏，將平均後曲線與高頻原資料比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check actual intervals and omissions from original timestamps, comparing averaged curves with high-frequency records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b269-v15-16","title":"取樣間隔與漏失洪峰機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sampling interval and missed crests mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「取樣間隔與漏失洪峰」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sampling interval and missed crests” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把傳輸每小時一次誤當成現地每分鐘取樣會低估資訊延遲，平均值也可能掩蓋警戒尖峰；無資料時延用最後值會產生看似平穩的假象。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing hourly transmission with minute-by-minute local sampling understates information delay, and averaging can conceal a warning crest. Repeating the last value during an outage creates the false appearance of stable water level. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：下式假設內部洪峰附近水位變化速率有已知上限且兩側取樣完整；只界定時間離散誤差，未含儀器誤差或資料中斷。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It concerns temporal discretization only, excluding sensor error and missing records.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要圖表每秒重畫，就代表河川每秒都有一筆新量測。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A graph refreshed every second means the river has a new measurement every second.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把傳輸每小時一次誤當成現地每分鐘取樣會低估資訊延遲，平均值也可能掩蓋警戒尖峰；無資料時延用最後值會產生看似平穩的假象。","textEn":"Confusing hourly transmission with minute-by-minute local sampling understates information delay, and averaging can conceal a warning crest. Repeating the last value during an outage creates the false appearance of stable water level.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「取樣間隔與漏失洪峰機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sampling interval and missed crests mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把傳輸每小時一次誤當成現地每分鐘取樣會低估資訊延遲，平均值也可能掩蓋警戒尖峰；無資料時延用最後值會產生看似平穩的假象。","封包剛收到就一定代表此刻水位，無需再看量測時間。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Confusing hourly transmission with minute-by-minute local sampling understates information delay, and averaging can conceal a warning crest.","A newly received packet necessarily represents current stage without checking observation time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把傳輸每小時一次誤當成現地每分鐘取樣會低估資訊延遲，平均值也可能掩蓋警戒尖峰；無資料時延用最後值會產生看似平穩的假象。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing hourly transmission with minute-by-minute local sampling understates information delay, and averaging can conceal a warning crest. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b269-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「傳輸延遲與資料時效機理與驗證」與「水位流量關係與外推機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Transmission latency and data age mechanism and verification\" and \"Stage-discharge relation and extrapolation mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b269-v15-17","title":"傳輸延遲與資料時效機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Transmission latency and data age mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「傳輸延遲與資料時效」如何影響河川水位自動遙測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Transmission latency and data age” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic river-level telemetry”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"自動遙測鏈包含感測、記錄、通訊、接收與發布，各段延遲相加才形成使用者看到的資料年齡。接收時間不等於量測時間，補傳舊封包更可能讓新到資料看似最新水位；洪水快速上升時，即使數值本身準確，過時資料仍可能造成錯誤情境判讀。本例在固定上升速率下比較量測時與現在的差異，不是預報模型；真實加速度、回落及通訊中斷會破壞線性外推。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「傳輸延遲與資料時效」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An automated chain includes sensing, logging, communication, reception and publication; their delays determine the age of displayed information. Receipt time is not observation time, and retransmitted old packets can look deceptively current. During a rapid rise, an accurate but stale reading can still produce a misleading picture of the river. The example compares observation time with the present under a constant rise rate. It is not a forecast model; acceleration, recession and communication outages invalidate simple linear extrapolation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Transmission latency and data age” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設水位上升率r=0.003 m/s、總資料延遲L=120 s，線性時效差Δh=rL=0.36 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume rise rate r=0.003 m/s and total data latency L=120 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「封包剛收到就一定代表此刻水位，無需再看量測時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A newly received packet necessarily represents current stage without checking observation time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「傳輸延遲與資料時效」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Transmission latency and data age”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-17-k1","title":"傳輸延遲與資料時效機理與驗證","titleEn":"Transmission latency and data age mechanism and verification","text":"自動遙測鏈包含感測、記錄、通訊、接收與發布，各段延遲相加才形成使用者看到的資料年齡。接收時間不等於量測時間，補傳舊封包更可能讓新到資料看似最新水位；洪水快速上升時，即使數值本身準確，過時資料仍可能造成錯誤情境判讀。","textEn":"An automated chain includes sensing, logging, communication, reception and publication; their delays determine the age of displayed information. Receipt time is not observation time, and retransmitted old packets can look deceptively current.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：封包剛收到就一定代表此刻水位，無需再看量測時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A newly received packet necessarily represents current stage without checking observation time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「傳輸延遲與資料時效機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Transmission latency and data age mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["封包剛收到就一定代表此刻水位，無需再看量測時間。","裝好水位計後，任何洪水流量都能無誤差地自動換算。","自動遙測鏈包含感測、記錄、通訊、接收與發布，各段延遲相加才形成使用者看到的資料年齡。"],"optionsEn":["A newly received packet necessarily represents current stage without checking observation time.","Once a stage sensor is installed, every flood discharge converts automatically without error.","An automated chain includes sensing, logging, communication, reception and publication; their delays determine the age of displayed information."],"answer":2,"explanation":"自動遙測鏈包含感測、記錄、通訊、接收與發布，各段延遲相加才形成使用者看到的資料年齡。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An automated chain includes sensing, logging, communication, reception and publication; their delays determine the age of displayed information. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b269-v15-18","title":"傳輸延遲與資料時效機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Transmission latency and data age mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「傳輸延遲與資料時效」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Transmission latency and data age” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設水位上升率r=0.003 m/s、總資料延遲L=120 s，線性時效差Δh=rL=0.36 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume rise rate r=0.003 m/s and total data latency L=120 s. Linear age-related difference Δh=rL=0.36 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保存量測、封包發送、接收與發布四種時間，使用一致時區和校時紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Retain observation, transmission, receipt and publication times with consistent timezone and clock records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設水位上升率r=0.003 m/s、總資料延遲L=120 s，線性時效差Δh=rL=0.36 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume rise rate r=0.003 m/s and total data latency L=120 s. Linear age-related difference Δh=rL=0.36 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「傳輸延遲與資料時效機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Transmission latency and data age mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設水位上升率r=0.003 m/s、總資料延遲L=120 s，線性時效差Δh=rL=0.36 m。","感測器顯示到毫米，就代表水面絕對高程也準確到毫米。","只要現場裝兩支感測器，就一定可以把全部失效機率相乘。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume rise rate r=0.003 m/s and total data latency L=120 s.","Millimeter display resolution means absolute water elevation is accurate to a millimeter.","Installing two field sensors always permits multiplication of all failure probabilities."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設水位上升率r=0.003 m/s、總資料延遲L=120 s，線性時效差Δh=rL=0.36 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume rise rate r=0.003 m/s and total data latency L=120 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b269-v15-19","title":"傳輸延遲與資料時效機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Transmission latency and data age mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「傳輸延遲與資料時效」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Transmission latency and data age” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保存量測、封包發送、接收與發布四種時間，使用一致時區和校時紀錄。透過測試封包量測端到端延遲分布，對補傳和過期資料加註旗標，避免只報平均延遲而漏掉長尾。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Retain observation, transmission, receipt and publication times with consistent timezone and clock records. Measure end-to-end latency distributions using test packets, flag backfilled and stale data, and inspect long delays rather than reporting only an average that hides the tail. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出含一次補傳的時間線，分開標記觀測與發布順序。計算每筆資料年齡並制定畫面標示規則，說明哪些值只能補歷史而不能覆蓋最新狀態。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw a timeline containing a retransmission, separating observation order from publication order. Calculate each record’s age and define display labels, explaining which records may fill history but must not replace the latest state.","failure":"注意干擾：用收到封包的時間覆蓋量測時間會把歷史水位當現況，時區錯置也可能產生假負延遲；只用平均通訊速度無法描述暴雨時的最長資料空窗。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Replacing observation time with receipt time presents historical stage as current, while timezone mistakes can create impossible negative latency. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保存量測、封包發送、接收與發布四種時間，使用一致時區和校時紀錄。透過測試封包量測端到端延遲分布，對補傳和過期資料加註旗標，避免只報平均延遲而漏掉長尾。","textEn":"Retain observation, transmission, receipt and publication times with consistent timezone and clock records. Measure end-to-end latency distributions using test packets, flag backfilled and stale data, and inspect long delays rather than reporting only an average that hides the tail.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出含一次補傳的時間線，分開標記觀測與發布順序。計算每筆資料年齡並制定畫面標示規則，說明哪些值只能補歷史而不能覆蓋最新狀態。","textEn":"Draw a timeline containing a retransmission, separating observation order from publication order. Calculate each record’s age and define display labels, explaining which records may fill history but must not replace the latest state.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「傳輸延遲與資料時效機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Transmission latency and data age mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","保存量測、封包發送、接收與發布四種時間，使用一致時區和校時紀錄。","任何壓力感測器輸出除以水重度就一定得到真實河川水深。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Retain observation, transmission, receipt and publication times with consistent timezone and clock records.","Any pressure output divided by water unit weight gives true river depth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"保存量測、封包發送、接收與發布四種時間，使用一致時區和校時紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Retain observation, transmission, receipt and publication times with consistent timezone and clock records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b269-v15-20","title":"傳輸延遲與資料時效機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Transmission latency and data age mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「傳輸延遲與資料時效」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Transmission latency and data age” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用收到封包的時間覆蓋量測時間會把歷史水位當現況，時區錯置也可能產生假負延遲；只用平均通訊速度無法描述暴雨時的最長資料空窗。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Replacing observation time with receipt time presents historical stage as current, while timezone mistakes can create impossible negative latency. Average communication speed does not describe the longest information gaps during a storm. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例在固定上升速率下比較量測時與現在的差異，不是預報模型；真實加速度、回落及通訊中斷會破壞線性外推。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It is not a forecast model; acceleration, recession and communication outages invalidate simple linear extrapolation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「封包剛收到就一定代表此刻水位，無需再看量測時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A newly received packet necessarily represents current stage without checking observation time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用收到封包的時間覆蓋量測時間會把歷史水位當現況，時區錯置也可能產生假負延遲；只用平均通訊速度無法描述暴雨時的最長資料空窗。","textEn":"Replacing observation time with receipt time presents historical stage as current, while timezone mistakes can create impossible negative latency. Average communication speed does not describe the longest information gaps during a storm.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「傳輸延遲與資料時效機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Transmission latency and data age mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","裝好水位計後，任何洪水流量都能無誤差地自動換算。","用收到封包的時間覆蓋量測時間會把歷史水位當現況，時區錯置也可能產生假負延遲；只用平均通訊速度無法描述暴雨時的最長資料空窗。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Once a stage sensor is installed, every flood discharge converts automatically without error.","Replacing observation time with receipt time presents historical stage as current, while timezone mistakes can create impossible negative latency."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用收到封包的時間覆蓋量測時間會把歷史水位當現況，時區錯置也可能產生假負延遲；只用平均通訊速度無法描述暴雨時的最長資料空窗。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Replacing observation time with receipt time presents historical stage as current, while timezone mistakes can create impossible negative latency. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b269-v15-21","title":"水位流量關係與外推機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Stage-discharge relation and extrapolation mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「水位流量關係與外推」如何影響河川水位自動遙測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Stage-discharge relation and extrapolation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic river-level telemetry”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"河川水位轉成流量通常依現地率定關係，控制斷面、糙率及回水變化會讓同一水位對應不同流量。漲退水遲滯與下游潮位可能使單值曲線失效；因此水位遙測完成不代表流量已直接量到，率定版本、有效範圍與量測支撐必須隨資料一起提供。本例採指定單值冪次曲線並明列係數單位，限定有效水頭為正；不是實站率定，也不應外推到回水或河床劇變情境。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水位流量關係與外推」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Converting stage to discharge normally uses a site-calibrated relation whose behavior depends on channel control, roughness and backwater. Rising/falling hysteresis and downstream tide can give different flows at the same stage. Automated stage measurement therefore does not mean discharge was directly measured; rating version, valid range and supporting observations must accompany derived flow. The example specifies a single-valued power rating with coefficient units and positive effective head. It is not a real station rating and should not be extrapolated into backwater or major bed change. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Stage-discharge relation and extrapolation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=a(h−h0)^b，a=20 m^1.4/s、b=1.6、h=2.0 m、h0=0.5 m，Q=38.26 m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=a(h−h0)^b, a=20 m^1.4/s, b=1.6, h=2.0 m and h0=0.5 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「裝好水位計後，任何洪水流量都能無誤差地自動換算。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once a stage sensor is installed, every flood discharge converts automatically without error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水位流量關係與外推」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Stage-discharge relation and extrapolation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-21-k1","title":"水位流量關係與外推機理與驗證","titleEn":"Stage-discharge relation and extrapolation mechanism and verification","text":"河川水位轉成流量通常依現地率定關係，控制斷面、糙率及回水變化會讓同一水位對應不同流量。漲退水遲滯與下游潮位可能使單值曲線失效；因此水位遙測完成不代表流量已直接量到，率定版本、有效範圍與量測支撐必須隨資料一起提供。","textEn":"Converting stage to discharge normally uses a site-calibrated relation whose behavior depends on channel control, roughness and backwater. Rising/falling hysteresis and downstream tide can give different flows at the same stage.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：裝好水位計後，任何洪水流量都能無誤差地自動換算。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once a stage sensor is installed, every flood discharge converts automatically without error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水位流量關係與外推機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stage-discharge relation and extrapolation mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["河川水位轉成流量通常依現地率定關係，控制斷面、糙率及回水變化會讓同一水位對應不同流量。","裝好水位計後，任何洪水流量都能無誤差地自動換算。","取樣越密，任何相鄰兩點差分得到的水位速率就一定越可靠。"],"optionsEn":["Converting stage to discharge normally uses a site-calibrated relation whose behavior depends on channel control, roughness and backwater.","Once a stage sensor is installed, every flood discharge converts automatically without error.","Denser sampling always makes a two-point stage derivative more reliable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"河川水位轉成流量通常依現地率定關係，控制斷面、糙率及回水變化會讓同一水位對應不同流量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Converting stage to discharge normally uses a site-calibrated relation whose behavior depends on channel control, roughness and backwater. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b269-v15-22","title":"水位流量關係與外推機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Stage-discharge relation and extrapolation mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水位流量關係與外推」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Stage-discharge relation and extrapolation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=a(h−h0)^b，a=20 m^1.4/s、b=1.6、h=2.0 m、h0=0.5 m，Q=38.26 m³/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=a(h−h0)^b, a=20 m^1.4/s, b=1.6, h=2.0 m and h0=0.5 m. Discharge Q=38.26 m³/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以獨立流量量測覆蓋漲退水及不同水位，檢查殘差是否與下游水位或時間有系統關係。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use independent discharge measurements across stages and both hydrograph limbs, checking whether residuals depend systematically on downstream level or time.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=a(h−h0)^b，a=20 m^1.4/s、b=1.6、h=2.0 m、h0=0.5 m，Q=38.26 m³/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=a(h−h0)^b, a=20 m^1.4/s, b=1.6, h=2.0 m and h0=0.5 m. Discharge Q=38.26 m³/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水位流量關係與外推機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stage-discharge relation and extrapolation mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["電池安培小時越大就可直接比較續航，不需要知道電壓或負載。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=a(h−h0)^b，a=20 m^1.4/s、b=1.6、h=2.0 m、h0=0.5 m，Q=38.26 m³/s。","所有水位計顯示的公尺數都已是同一海拔基準下的高程。"],"optionsEn":["Battery ampere-hours alone compare endurance without voltage or load information.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=a(h−h0)^b, a=20 m^1.4/s, b=1.6, h=2.0 m and h0=0.5 m.","Every water-level reading in meters already uses the same sea-level datum."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=a(h−h0)^b，a=20 m^1.4/s、b=1.6、h=2.0 m、h0=0.5 m，Q=38.26 m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=a(h−h0)^b, a=20 m^1.4/s, b=1.6, h=2.0 m and h0=0.5 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b269-v15-23","title":"水位流量關係與外推機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Stage-discharge relation and extrapolation mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水位流量關係與外推」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Stage-discharge relation and extrapolation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以獨立流量量測覆蓋漲退水及不同水位，檢查殘差是否與下游水位或時間有系統關係。保存率定版本和外推旗標，洪水後重新查控制斷面，而不是只調係數追求漂亮擬合。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use independent discharge measurements across stages and both hydrograph limbs, checking whether residuals depend systematically on downstream level or time. Retain rating versions and extrapolation flags, and resurvey channel control after floods instead of merely adjusting coefficients for an attractive fit. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用指定曲線計算兩個水位，標出有效水頭與係數單位。再畫出相同水位有兩個流量的遲滯示意，說明需要增加哪種觀測才能區分兩支曲線。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate two discharges from the specified rating, labeling effective head and coefficient units. Draw a hysteresis example with two flows at one stage and explain what additional observation could distinguish the two branches.","failure":"注意干擾：把超出量測範圍的曲線延伸當實測會低估高水位不確定度，河床沖淤後沿用舊率定也可能產生系統偏差；單點水位無法唯一解決強回水流量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Calling an extrapolated curve measured flow understates high-stage uncertainty, and using an old rating after bed change introduces bias. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以獨立流量量測覆蓋漲退水及不同水位，檢查殘差是否與下游水位或時間有系統關係。保存率定版本和外推旗標，洪水後重新查控制斷面，而不是只調係數追求漂亮擬合。","textEn":"Use independent discharge measurements across stages and both hydrograph limbs, checking whether residuals depend systematically on downstream level or time. Retain rating versions and extrapolation flags, and resurvey channel control after floods instead of merely adjusting coefficients for an attractive fit.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用指定曲線計算兩個水位，標出有效水頭與係數單位。再畫出相同水位有兩個流量的遲滯示意，說明需要增加哪種觀測才能區分兩支曲線。","textEn":"Calculate two discharges from the specified rating, labeling effective head and coefficient units. Draw a hysteresis example with two flows at one stage and explain what additional observation could distinguish the two branches.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水位流量關係與外推機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stage-discharge relation and extrapolation mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","雷達不接觸水，所以不需要高程測量或現地水尺交叉驗證。","以獨立流量量測覆蓋漲退水及不同水位，檢查殘差是否與下游水位或時間有系統關係。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Noncontact radar needs neither elevation surveying nor field staff-gage checks.","Use independent discharge measurements across stages and both hydrograph limbs, checking whether residuals depend systematically on downstream level or time."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以獨立流量量測覆蓋漲退水及不同水位，檢查殘差是否與下游水位或時間有系統關係。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use independent discharge measurements across stages and both hydrograph limbs, checking whether residuals depend systematically on downstream level or time. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b269-v15-24","title":"水位流量關係與外推機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stage-discharge relation and extrapolation mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水位流量關係與外推」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Stage-discharge relation and extrapolation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把超出量測範圍的曲線延伸當實測會低估高水位不確定度，河床沖淤後沿用舊率定也可能產生系統偏差；單點水位無法唯一解決強回水流量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Calling an extrapolated curve measured flow understates high-stage uncertainty, and using an old rating after bed change introduces bias. One stage observation cannot uniquely resolve discharge under strong backwater. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例採指定單值冪次曲線並明列係數單位，限定有效水頭為正；不是實站率定，也不應外推到回水或河床劇變情境。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It is not a real station rating and should not be extrapolated into backwater or major bed change.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「裝好水位計後，任何洪水流量都能無誤差地自動換算。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once a stage sensor is installed, every flood discharge converts automatically without error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把超出量測範圍的曲線延伸當實測會低估高水位不確定度，河床沖淤後沿用舊率定也可能產生系統偏差；單點水位無法唯一解決強回水流量。","textEn":"Calling an extrapolated curve measured flow understates high-stage uncertainty, and using an old rating after bed change introduces bias. One stage observation cannot uniquely resolve discharge under strong backwater.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水位流量關係與外推機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stage-discharge relation and extrapolation mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把超出量測範圍的曲線延伸當實測會低估高水位不確定度，河床沖淤後沿用舊率定也可能產生系統偏差；單點水位無法唯一解決強回水流量。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","取樣越密，任何相鄰兩點差分得到的水位速率就一定越可靠。"],"optionsEn":["Calling an extrapolated curve measured flow understates high-stage uncertainty, and using an old rating after bed change introduces bias.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Denser sampling always makes a two-point stage derivative more reliable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把超出量測範圍的曲線延伸當實測會低估高水位不確定度，河床沖淤後沿用舊率定也可能產生系統偏差；單點水位無法唯一解決強回水流量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Calling an extrapolated curve measured flow understates high-stage uncertainty, and using an old rating after bed change introduces bias. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b269-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「上升速率與雜訊機理與驗證」與「高程不確定度合成機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rise-rate estimation and noise mechanism and verification\" and \"Elevation uncertainty combination mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b269-v15-25","title":"上升速率與雜訊機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rise-rate estimation and noise mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「上升速率與雜訊」如何影響河川水位自動遙測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rise-rate estimation and noise” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic river-level telemetry”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水位上升速率能補充絕對水位資訊，但差分運算會放大量測雜訊和時間誤差。取樣間隔越短，並不保證速率越準確；過度平滑雖降低雜訊卻延遲急升訊號，因此應將原始資料、濾波方式和速率計算窗分開保存，避免用單一尖峰差分觸發無法解釋的判斷。本例計算兩筆有效讀值間的平均變化率，不代表區間內瞬時最大值；警戒規則與多源確認需另按實際防洪系統制定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「上升速率與雜訊」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Rise rate supplements absolute stage, but differencing amplifies measurement noise and timing errors. A shorter interval does not guarantee a more accurate derivative. Heavy smoothing reduces noise while delaying rapid-rise signals, so raw data, filtering method and derivative window should remain separately documented rather than relying on an unexplained single-sample spike. The example is the mean rate between two valid readings, not the maximum instantaneous rate within the interval. Warning rules and multisource confirmation require a separate operational framework. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rise-rate estimation and noise” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設水位由2.10升至2.22 m、間隔Δt=600 s，平均r=0.12/600=0.00020 m/s=0.72 m/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume stage rises from 2.10 to 2.22 m over Δt=600 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「取樣越密，任何相鄰兩點差分得到的水位速率就一定越可靠。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Denser sampling always makes a two-point stage derivative more reliable.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「上升速率與雜訊」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rise-rate estimation and noise”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-25-k1","title":"上升速率與雜訊機理與驗證","titleEn":"Rise-rate estimation and noise mechanism and verification","text":"水位上升速率能補充絕對水位資訊，但差分運算會放大量測雜訊和時間誤差。取樣間隔越短，並不保證速率越準確；過度平滑雖降低雜訊卻延遲急升訊號，因此應將原始資料、濾波方式和速率計算窗分開保存，避免用單一尖峰差分觸發無法解釋的判斷。","textEn":"Rise rate supplements absolute stage, but differencing amplifies measurement noise and timing errors. A shorter interval does not guarantee a more accurate derivative.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：取樣越密，任何相鄰兩點差分得到的水位速率就一定越可靠。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Denser sampling always makes a two-point stage derivative more reliable. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「上升速率與雜訊機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rise-rate estimation and noise mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["取樣越密，任何相鄰兩點差分得到的水位速率就一定越可靠。","水位上升速率能補充絕對水位資訊，但差分運算會放大量測雜訊和時間誤差。","感測器顯示到毫米，就代表水面絕對高程也準確到毫米。"],"optionsEn":["Denser sampling always makes a two-point stage derivative more reliable.","Rise rate supplements absolute stage, but differencing amplifies measurement noise and timing errors.","Millimeter display resolution means absolute water elevation is accurate to a millimeter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水位上升速率能補充絕對水位資訊，但差分運算會放大量測雜訊和時間誤差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Rise rate supplements absolute stage, but differencing amplifies measurement noise and timing errors. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b269-v15-26","title":"上升速率與雜訊機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Rise-rate estimation and noise mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「上升速率與雜訊」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rise-rate estimation and noise” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設水位由2.10升至2.22 m、間隔Δt=600 s，平均r=0.12/600=0.00020 m/s=0.72 m/h。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume stage rises from 2.10 to 2.22 m over Δt=600 s. Mean r=0.12/600=0.00020 m/s=0.72 m/h. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：檢查兩筆資料的品質旗標、實際時間差及是否跨越零點改正，再比較不同窗長的速率。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check quality flags, actual time separation and any intervening datum correction, then compare rates from different windows.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設水位由2.10升至2.22 m、間隔Δt=600 s，平均r=0.12/600=0.00020 m/s=0.72 m/h。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume stage rises from 2.10 to 2.22 m over Δt=600 s. Mean r=0.12/600=0.00020 m/s=0.72 m/h.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「上升速率與雜訊機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rise-rate estimation and noise mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["只要現場裝兩支感測器，就一定可以把全部失效機率相乘。","任何壓力感測器輸出除以水重度就一定得到真實河川水深。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設水位由2.10升至2.22 m、間隔Δt=600 s，平均r=0.12/600=0.00020 m/s=0.72 m/h。"],"optionsEn":["Installing two field sensors always permits multiplication of all failure probabilities.","Any pressure output divided by water unit weight gives true river depth.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume stage rises from 2.10 to 2.22 m over Δt=600 s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設水位由2.10升至2.22 m、間隔Δt=600 s，平均r=0.12/600=0.00020 m/s=0.72 m/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume stage rises from 2.10 to 2.22 m over Δt=600 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b269-v15-27","title":"上升速率與雜訊機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rise-rate estimation and noise mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「上升速率與雜訊」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rise-rate estimation and noise” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"檢查兩筆資料的品質旗標、實際時間差及是否跨越零點改正，再比較不同窗長的速率。用已知事件或合成訊號量測濾波延遲，將可接受雜訊與漏失急升的取捨明確記錄。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check quality flags, actual time separation and any intervening datum correction, then compare rates from different windows. Measure filter delay with known events or synthetic signals, explicitly recording the tradeoff between tolerated noise and missed or delayed rapid rises. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：給兩筆水位加入正負一公分誤差，比較短窗和長窗的速率偏差。另以快速上升訊號測試移動平均，說明減噪與延遲不能只用同一個指標評分。","observationEn":"Site practice: Add opposite one-centimeter errors to two readings and compare rate bias over short and long windows. Test a moving average on a rapid rise and explain why noise reduction and delay need separate evaluation metrics.","failure":"注意干擾：兩個相鄰讀值的小誤差經短時間差相除可變成巨大速率，跨越零點調整也會形成假急升；過度濾波則可能把真實快速上漲延後呈現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Small adjacent-reading errors divided by a short interval can create a large apparent rate, and a datum adjustment can mimic a surge. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"檢查兩筆資料的品質旗標、實際時間差及是否跨越零點改正，再比較不同窗長的速率。用已知事件或合成訊號量測濾波延遲，將可接受雜訊與漏失急升的取捨明確記錄。","textEn":"Check quality flags, actual time separation and any intervening datum correction, then compare rates from different windows. Measure filter delay with known events or synthetic signals, explicitly recording the tradeoff between tolerated noise and missed or delayed rapid rises.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"給兩筆水位加入正負一公分誤差，比較短窗和長窗的速率偏差。另以快速上升訊號測試移動平均，說明減噪與延遲不能只用同一個指標評分。","textEn":"Add opposite one-centimeter errors to two readings and compare rate bias over short and long windows. Test a moving average on a rapid rise and explain why noise reduction and delay need separate evaluation metrics.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「上升速率與雜訊機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rise-rate estimation and noise mechanism and verification\"?","options":["檢查兩筆資料的品質旗標、實際時間差及是否跨越零點改正，再比較不同窗長的速率。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要圖表每秒重畫，就代表河川每秒都有一筆新量測。"],"optionsEn":["Check quality flags, actual time separation and any intervening datum correction, then compare rates from different windows.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A graph refreshed every second means the river has a new measurement every second."],"answer":0,"explanation":"檢查兩筆資料的品質旗標、實際時間差及是否跨越零點改正，再比較不同窗長的速率。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check quality flags, actual time separation and any intervening datum correction, then compare rates from different windows. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b269-v15-28","title":"上升速率與雜訊機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rise-rate estimation and noise mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「上升速率與雜訊」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rise-rate estimation and noise” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩個相鄰讀值的小誤差經短時間差相除可變成巨大速率，跨越零點調整也會形成假急升；過度濾波則可能把真實快速上漲延後呈現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Small adjacent-reading errors divided by a short interval can create a large apparent rate, and a datum adjustment can mimic a surge. Excessive filtering can instead display a genuine rapid rise too late. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例計算兩筆有效讀值間的平均變化率，不代表區間內瞬時最大值；警戒規則與多源確認需另按實際防洪系統制定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Warning rules and multisource confirmation require a separate operational framework.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「取樣越密，任何相鄰兩點差分得到的水位速率就一定越可靠。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Denser sampling always makes a two-point stage derivative more reliable.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩個相鄰讀值的小誤差經短時間差相除可變成巨大速率，跨越零點調整也會形成假急升；過度濾波則可能把真實快速上漲延後呈現。","textEn":"Small adjacent-reading errors divided by a short interval can create a large apparent rate, and a datum adjustment can mimic a surge. Excessive filtering can instead display a genuine rapid rise too late.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「上升速率與雜訊機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rise-rate estimation and noise mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","兩個相鄰讀值的小誤差經短時間差相除可變成巨大速率，跨越零點調整也會形成假急升；過度濾波則可能把真實快速上漲延後呈現。","感測器顯示到毫米，就代表水面絕對高程也準確到毫米。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Small adjacent-reading errors divided by a short interval can create a large apparent rate, and a datum adjustment can mimic a surge.","Millimeter display resolution means absolute water elevation is accurate to a millimeter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩個相鄰讀值的小誤差經短時間差相除可變成巨大速率，跨越零點調整也會形成假急升；過度濾波則可能把真實快速上漲延後呈現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Small adjacent-reading errors divided by a short interval can create a large apparent rate, and a datum adjustment can mimic a surge. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b269-v15-29","title":"高程不確定度合成機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Elevation uncertainty combination mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「高程不確定度合成」如何影響河川水位自動遙測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Elevation uncertainty combination” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic river-level telemetry”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"自動水位高程包含感測、基準連接和安裝幾何等不確定度，顯示小數位數不代表同樣程度的可信度。獨立隨機項可用平方和合成，但共同基準偏差、漂移及未修正系統誤差不能隨意當成獨立量；報告需區分標準不確定度、擴展區間與誤差來源，而不是只給一個精度標籤。下式只合成兩個指定獨立標準不確定度，沒有乘涵蓋因子；不能把結果直接稱為百分之九十五信賴區間或量測閉合差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「高程不確定度合成」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Automated elevation combines sensor, datum-transfer and installation-geometry uncertainty, and display decimals do not imply equal confidence. Independent random contributions can be combined by root-sum-square, but shared datum bias, drift and uncorrected systematic error cannot simply be treated as independent. Reports should distinguish standard uncertainty, expanded intervals and contributing sources rather than provide one vague accuracy label. The expression combines two specified independent standard uncertainties without a coverage factor. It is neither automatically a 95-percent interval nor a measured leveling closure error. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Elevation uncertainty combination” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設感測標準不確定度us=0.010 m、基準連接ud=0.020 m且獨立，uc=√(us²+ud²)=0.02236 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent sensor uncertainty us=0.010 m and datum-transfer uncertainty ud=0.020 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「感測器顯示到毫米，就代表水面絕對高程也準確到毫米。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Millimeter display resolution means absolute water elevation is accurate to a millimeter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「高程不確定度合成」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Elevation uncertainty combination”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-29-k1","title":"高程不確定度合成機理與驗證","titleEn":"Elevation uncertainty combination mechanism and verification","text":"自動水位高程包含感測、基準連接和安裝幾何等不確定度，顯示小數位數不代表同樣程度的可信度。獨立隨機項可用平方和合成，但共同基準偏差、漂移及未修正系統誤差不能隨意當成獨立量；報告需區分標準不確定度、擴展區間與誤差來源，而不是只給一個精度標籤。","textEn":"Automated elevation combines sensor, datum-transfer and installation-geometry uncertainty, and display decimals do not imply equal confidence. Independent random contributions can be combined by root-sum-square, but shared datum bias, drift and uncorrected systematic error cannot simply be treated as independent.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：感測器顯示到毫米，就代表水面絕對高程也準確到毫米。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Millimeter display resolution means absolute water elevation is accurate to a millimeter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高程不確定度合成機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Elevation uncertainty combination mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["感測器顯示到毫米，就代表水面絕對高程也準確到毫米。","電池安培小時越大就可直接比較續航，不需要知道電壓或負載。","自動水位高程包含感測、基準連接和安裝幾何等不確定度，顯示小數位數不代表同樣程度的可信度。"],"optionsEn":["Millimeter display resolution means absolute water elevation is accurate to a millimeter.","Battery ampere-hours alone compare endurance without voltage or load information.","Automated elevation combines sensor, datum-transfer and installation-geometry uncertainty, and display decimals do not imply equal confidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"自動水位高程包含感測、基準連接和安裝幾何等不確定度，顯示小數位數不代表同樣程度的可信度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Automated elevation combines sensor, datum-transfer and installation-geometry uncertainty, and display decimals do not imply equal confidence. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b269-v15-30","title":"高程不確定度合成機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Elevation uncertainty combination mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「高程不確定度合成」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Elevation uncertainty combination” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設感測標準不確定度us=0.010 m、基準連接ud=0.020 m且獨立，uc=√(us²+ud²)=0.02236 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent sensor uncertainty us=0.010 m and datum-transfer uncertainty ud=0.020 m. Combined standard uc=√(us²+ud²)=0.02236 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立誤差來源表，列明每項來自校正、重複量測或幾何估計，以及是否共享參考。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build a source table identifying calibration, repeat measurement or geometric estimation and shared references.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設感測標準不確定度us=0.010 m、基準連接ud=0.020 m且獨立，uc=√(us²+ud²)=0.02236 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent sensor uncertainty us=0.010 m and datum-transfer uncertainty ud=0.020 m. Combined standard uc=√(us²+ud²)=0.02236 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高程不確定度合成機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Elevation uncertainty combination mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設感測標準不確定度us=0.010 m、基準連接ud=0.020 m且獨立，uc=√(us²+ud²)=0.02236 m。","所有水位計顯示的公尺數都已是同一海拔基準下的高程。","雷達不接觸水，所以不需要高程測量或現地水尺交叉驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent sensor uncertainty us=0.010 m and datum-transfer uncertainty ud=0.020 m.","Every water-level reading in meters already uses the same sea-level datum.","Noncontact radar needs neither elevation surveying nor field staff-gage checks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設感測標準不確定度us=0.010 m、基準連接ud=0.020 m且獨立，uc=√(us²+ud²)=0.02236 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent sensor uncertainty us=0.010 m and datum-transfer uncertainty ud=0.020 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b269-v15-31","title":"高程不確定度合成機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Elevation uncertainty combination mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「高程不確定度合成」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Elevation uncertainty combination” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立誤差來源表，列明每項來自校正、重複量測或幾何估計，以及是否共享參考。檢查偏差是否已改正，將標準不確定度和實際水準閉合值分開，必要時保留相關係數再合成。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build a source table identifying calibration, repeat measurement or geometric estimation and shared references. Check whether bias has been corrected, keep standard uncertainty distinct from actual leveling closure, and retain covariance terms where dependence prevents a simple independent combination. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將一份誤差表分成獨立與共用來源，先合成可獨立的項，再討論共用基準如何影響兩站高差。寫出包含單位和涵蓋說明的完整結果句。","observationEn":"Site practice: Separate independent and shared sources, combine only eligible terms, then discuss how a shared datum affects a two-station elevation difference. Write a complete result sentence with units and an explicit statement about coverage.","failure":"注意干擾：把共同基準誤差當兩個獨立項可能錯估比較結果，增加取樣也無法消除固定偏差；將平方和結果直接標為最大誤差則又混淆機率尺度與保證界限。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating shared datum error as independent can misstate a comparison, and more samples do not remove fixed bias. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立誤差來源表，列明每項來自校正、重複量測或幾何估計，以及是否共享參考。檢查偏差是否已改正，將標準不確定度和實際水準閉合值分開，必要時保留相關係數再合成。","textEn":"Build a source table identifying calibration, repeat measurement or geometric estimation and shared references. Check whether bias has been corrected, keep standard uncertainty distinct from actual leveling closure, and retain covariance terms where dependence prevents a simple independent combination.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將一份誤差表分成獨立與共用來源，先合成可獨立的項，再討論共用基準如何影響兩站高差。寫出包含單位和涵蓋說明的完整結果句。","textEn":"Separate independent and shared sources, combine only eligible terms, then discuss how a shared datum affects a two-station elevation difference. Write a complete result sentence with units and an explicit statement about coverage.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高程不確定度合成機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Elevation uncertainty combination mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","建立誤差來源表，列明每項來自校正、重複量測或幾何估計，以及是否共享參考。","封包剛收到就一定代表此刻水位，無需再看量測時間。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Build a source table identifying calibration, repeat measurement or geometric estimation and shared references.","A newly received packet necessarily represents current stage without checking observation time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"建立誤差來源表，列明每項來自校正、重複量測或幾何估計，以及是否共享參考。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build a source table identifying calibration, repeat measurement or geometric estimation and shared references. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b269-v15-32","title":"高程不確定度合成機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Elevation uncertainty combination mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「高程不確定度合成」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Elevation uncertainty combination” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把共同基準誤差當兩個獨立項可能錯估比較結果，增加取樣也無法消除固定偏差；將平方和結果直接標為最大誤差則又混淆機率尺度與保證界限。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating shared datum error as independent can misstate a comparison, and more samples do not remove fixed bias. Labeling a root-sum-square result as maximum error further confuses a probabilistic scale with a guaranteed bound. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：下式只合成兩個指定獨立標準不確定度，沒有乘涵蓋因子；不能把結果直接稱為百分之九十五信賴區間或量測閉合差。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It is neither automatically a 95-percent interval nor a measured leveling closure error.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「感測器顯示到毫米，就代表水面絕對高程也準確到毫米。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Millimeter display resolution means absolute water elevation is accurate to a millimeter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把共同基準誤差當兩個獨立項可能錯估比較結果，增加取樣也無法消除固定偏差；將平方和結果直接標為最大誤差則又混淆機率尺度與保證界限。","textEn":"Treating shared datum error as independent can misstate a comparison, and more samples do not remove fixed bias. Labeling a root-sum-square result as maximum error further confuses a probabilistic scale with a guaranteed bound.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高程不確定度合成機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Elevation uncertainty combination mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","電池安培小時越大就可直接比較續航，不需要知道電壓或負載。","把共同基準誤差當兩個獨立項可能錯估比較結果，增加取樣也無法消除固定偏差；將平方和結果直接標為最大誤差則又混淆機率尺度與保證界限。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Battery ampere-hours alone compare endurance without voltage or load information.","Treating shared datum error as independent can misstate a comparison, and more samples do not remove fixed bias."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把共同基準誤差當兩個獨立項可能錯估比較結果，增加取樣也無法消除固定偏差；將平方和結果直接標為最大誤差則又混淆機率尺度與保證界限。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating shared datum error as independent can misstate a comparison, and more samples do not remove fixed bias. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b269-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「備援電源與能量帳機理與驗證」與「獨立備援與共因失效機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Backup power and energy budget mechanism and verification\" and \"Independent redundancy and common causes mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b269-v15-33","title":"備援電源與能量帳機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Backup power and energy budget mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「備援電源與能量帳」如何影響河川水位自動遙測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Backup power and energy budget” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic river-level telemetry”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"偏遠測站的可用時間取決於平均負載、通訊脈衝、電池可用容量及環境條件，不能只看安培小時數。電壓換算、允許放電深度和電源轉換損失都影響可用能量，低溫與老化又可能降低容量；太陽能日均供電也無法單獨保證連續陰雨期間仍有資料。本例以固定平均負載與指定可用係數作能量比較，忽略自放電、老化和低溫；計算時數不是實站續航保證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「備援電源與能量帳」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Remote-station endurance depends on average load, transmission pulses, usable battery capacity and environment rather than ampere-hours alone. Voltage, allowed depth of discharge and conversion losses determine useful energy, while cold and aging may reduce capacity. Mean solar input likewise cannot guarantee observations throughout an extended cloudy period. The example uses fixed mean load and specified usable factors, excluding self-discharge, aging and cold. Calculated hours are an energy comparison, not a station-endurance guarantee. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Backup power and energy budget” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設電池12 V、40 Ah、可用放電比例0.50、轉換效率0.85、平均負載2 W，續航t=12×40×0.50×0.85/2=102 h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume battery 12 V, 40 Ah, usable discharge fraction 0.50, conversion efficiency 0.85 and mean load 2 W.","failure":"常見誤解：「電池安培小時越大就可直接比較續航，不需要知道電壓或負載。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Battery ampere-hours alone compare endurance without voltage or load information.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「備援電源與能量帳」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Backup power and energy budget”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-33-k1","title":"備援電源與能量帳機理與驗證","titleEn":"Backup power and energy budget mechanism and verification","text":"偏遠測站的可用時間取決於平均負載、通訊脈衝、電池可用容量及環境條件，不能只看安培小時數。電壓換算、允許放電深度和電源轉換損失都影響可用能量，低溫與老化又可能降低容量；太陽能日均供電也無法單獨保證連續陰雨期間仍有資料。","textEn":"Remote-station endurance depends on average load, transmission pulses, usable battery capacity and environment rather than ampere-hours alone. Voltage, allowed depth of discharge and conversion losses determine useful energy, while cold and aging may reduce capacity.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：電池安培小時越大就可直接比較續航，不需要知道電壓或負載。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Battery ampere-hours alone compare endurance without voltage or load information. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「備援電源與能量帳機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Backup power and energy budget mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["偏遠測站的可用時間取決於平均負載、通訊脈衝、電池可用容量及環境條件，不能只看安培小時數。","電池安培小時越大就可直接比較續航，不需要知道電壓或負載。","只要現場裝兩支感測器，就一定可以把全部失效機率相乘。"],"optionsEn":["Remote-station endurance depends on average load, transmission pulses, usable battery capacity and environment rather than ampere-hours alone.","Battery ampere-hours alone compare endurance without voltage or load information.","Installing two field sensors always permits multiplication of all failure probabilities."],"answer":0,"explanation":"偏遠測站的可用時間取決於平均負載、通訊脈衝、電池可用容量及環境條件，不能只看安培小時數。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Remote-station endurance depends on average load, transmission pulses, usable battery capacity and environment rather than ampere-hours alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b269-v15-34","title":"備援電源與能量帳機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Backup power and energy budget mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「備援電源與能量帳」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Backup power and energy budget” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設電池12 V、40 Ah、可用放電比例0.50、轉換效率0.85、平均負載2 W，續航t=12×40×0.50×0.85/2=102 h。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume battery 12 V, 40 Ah, usable discharge fraction 0.50, conversion efficiency 0.85 and mean load 2 W. Endurance t=12×40×0.50×0.85/2=102 h. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測感測、待機和傳輸各狀態功率及占空比，將短時峰值和平均能量分開核對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure sensing, standby and transmission power with duty cycles, checking peak demand separately from average energy.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設電池12 V、40 Ah、可用放電比例0.50、轉換效率0.85、平均負載2 W，續航t=12×40×0.50×0.85/2=102 h。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume battery 12 V, 40 Ah, usable discharge fraction 0.50, conversion efficiency 0.85 and mean load 2 W. Endurance t=12×40×0.50×0.85/2=102 h.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「備援電源與能量帳機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Backup power and energy budget mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["任何壓力感測器輸出除以水重度就一定得到真實河川水深。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設電池12 V、40 Ah、可用放電比例0.50、轉換效率0.85、平均負載2 W，續航t=12×40×0.50×0.85/2=102 h。","只要圖表每秒重畫，就代表河川每秒都有一筆新量測。"],"optionsEn":["Any pressure output divided by water unit weight gives true river depth.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume battery 12 V, 40 Ah, usable discharge fraction 0.50, conversion efficiency 0.85 and mean load 2 W.","A graph refreshed every second means the river has a new measurement every second."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設電池12 V、40 Ah、可用放電比例0.50、轉換效率0.85、平均負載2 W，續航t=12×40×0.50×0.85/2=102 h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume battery 12 V, 40 Ah, usable discharge fraction 0.50, conversion efficiency 0.85 and mean load 2 W. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b269-v15-35","title":"備援電源與能量帳機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Backup power and energy budget mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「備援電源與能量帳」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Backup power and energy budget” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測感測、待機和傳輸各狀態功率及占空比，將短時峰值和平均能量分開核對。以老化與低溫容量資料更新可用量，並用中斷充電的測試確認低電量標示及資料保存行為。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure sensing, standby and transmission power with duty cycles, checking peak demand separately from average energy. Update usable capacity with aging and temperature evidence, and test interrupted charging to confirm low-battery indication and preservation of observations before power is exhausted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將通訊占空比增加一倍後重算平均負載，再比較低溫容量下降情境。為能量耗盡前後設計資料旗標，區分感測中斷、通訊中斷和仍可本地記錄的狀態。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double communication duty cycle and recalculate mean load, then compare reduced cold-weather capacity. Define data flags around energy exhaustion that distinguish sensing failure, communication loss and continued local recording.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略傳輸峰值可能使電池尚有能量卻因瞬時壓降重啟，使用新電池容量估計老站又會高估續航；斷電後無明確旗標可能被誤解為河水停止變化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring transmission peaks can cause reset from voltage sag despite remaining energy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測感測、待機和傳輸各狀態功率及占空比，將短時峰值和平均能量分開核對。以老化與低溫容量資料更新可用量，並用中斷充電的測試確認低電量標示及資料保存行為。","textEn":"Measure sensing, standby and transmission power with duty cycles, checking peak demand separately from average energy. Update usable capacity with aging and temperature evidence, and test interrupted charging to confirm low-battery indication and preservation of observations before power is exhausted.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將通訊占空比增加一倍後重算平均負載，再比較低溫容量下降情境。為能量耗盡前後設計資料旗標，區分感測中斷、通訊中斷和仍可本地記錄的狀態。","textEn":"Double communication duty cycle and recalculate mean load, then compare reduced cold-weather capacity. Define data flags around energy exhaustion that distinguish sensing failure, communication loss and continued local recording.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「備援電源與能量帳機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Backup power and energy budget mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","裝好水位計後，任何洪水流量都能無誤差地自動換算。","量測感測、待機和傳輸各狀態功率及占空比，將短時峰值和平均能量分開核對。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Once a stage sensor is installed, every flood discharge converts automatically without error.","Measure sensing, standby and transmission power with duty cycles, checking peak demand separately from average energy."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測感測、待機和傳輸各狀態功率及占空比，將短時峰值和平均能量分開核對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure sensing, standby and transmission power with duty cycles, checking peak demand separately from average energy. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b269-v15-36","title":"備援電源與能量帳機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Backup power and energy budget mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「備援電源與能量帳」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Backup power and energy budget” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略傳輸峰值可能使電池尚有能量卻因瞬時壓降重啟，使用新電池容量估計老站又會高估續航；斷電後無明確旗標可能被誤解為河水停止變化。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring transmission peaks can cause reset from voltage sag despite remaining energy. Using new-battery capacity for an aged station overstates endurance, and missing outage flags can make power failure look like unchanging river stage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例以固定平均負載與指定可用係數作能量比較，忽略自放電、老化和低溫；計算時數不是實站續航保證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Calculated hours are an energy comparison, not a station-endurance guarantee.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「電池安培小時越大就可直接比較續航，不需要知道電壓或負載。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Battery ampere-hours alone compare endurance without voltage or load information.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略傳輸峰值可能使電池尚有能量卻因瞬時壓降重啟，使用新電池容量估計老站又會高估續航；斷電後無明確旗標可能被誤解為河水停止變化。","textEn":"Ignoring transmission peaks can cause reset from voltage sag despite remaining energy. Using new-battery capacity for an aged station overstates endurance, and missing outage flags can make power failure look like unchanging river stage.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「備援電源與能量帳機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Backup power and energy budget mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["忽略傳輸峰值可能使電池尚有能量卻因瞬時壓降重啟，使用新電池容量估計老站又會高估續航；斷電後無明確旗標可能被誤解為河水停止變化。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要現場裝兩支感測器，就一定可以把全部失效機率相乘。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring transmission peaks can cause reset from voltage sag despite remaining energy.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Installing two field sensors always permits multiplication of all failure probabilities."],"answer":0,"explanation":"忽略傳輸峰值可能使電池尚有能量卻因瞬時壓降重啟，使用新電池容量估計老站又會高估續航；斷電後無明確旗標可能被誤解為河水停止變化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring transmission peaks can cause reset from voltage sag despite remaining energy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b269-v15-37","title":"獨立備援與共因失效機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Independent redundancy and common causes mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「獨立備援與共因失效」如何影響河川水位自動遙測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Independent redundancy and common causes” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Automatic river-level telemetry”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"兩套感測或通訊可提高資料可用性，但只有真正獨立的失效才可直接相乘。若共用電源、支架、基準點或被同一洪水淹沒，備援仍可能同時失效；不同技術也可能共享資料伺服器，應沿整條量測到發布路徑辨認共因，而不是只數現場儀器數量。本例定義相同觀察期間兩通道失效機率且假設獨立，只示範理想備援；未加入修復、共因及不同失效模式。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「獨立備援與共因失效」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Two sensors or links can improve availability, but failure probabilities multiply only for independent events. Shared power, support, datum or flood exposure can disable both. Different sensing technologies may still share a publication server, so common causes must be traced through the complete observation-to-display chain rather than inferred from device count. The example defines channel-failure probabilities over the same observation period and assumes independence. It illustrates ideal redundancy without repair, common causes or multiple failure modes. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Independent redundancy and common causes” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩通道期間失效機率p1=p2=0.02且獨立，同時失效p=p1p2=0.0004，即0.04%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent channel-failure probabilities p1=p2=0.02 over the same period.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要現場裝兩支感測器，就一定可以把全部失效機率相乘。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Installing two field sensors always permits multiplication of all failure probabilities.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「獨立備援與共因失效」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Independent redundancy and common causes”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-37-k1","title":"獨立備援與共因失效機理與驗證","titleEn":"Independent redundancy and common causes mechanism and verification","text":"兩套感測或通訊可提高資料可用性，但只有真正獨立的失效才可直接相乘。若共用電源、支架、基準點或被同一洪水淹沒，備援仍可能同時失效；不同技術也可能共享資料伺服器，應沿整條量測到發布路徑辨認共因，而不是只數現場儀器數量。","textEn":"Two sensors or links can improve availability, but failure probabilities multiply only for independent events. Shared power, support, datum or flood exposure can disable both.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要現場裝兩支感測器，就一定可以把全部失效機率相乘。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Installing two field sensors always permits multiplication of all failure probabilities. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「獨立備援與共因失效機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Independent redundancy and common causes mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["只要現場裝兩支感測器，就一定可以把全部失效機率相乘。","兩套感測或通訊可提高資料可用性，但只有真正獨立的失效才可直接相乘。","所有水位計顯示的公尺數都已是同一海拔基準下的高程。"],"optionsEn":["Installing two field sensors always permits multiplication of all failure probabilities.","Two sensors or links can improve availability, but failure probabilities multiply only for independent events.","Every water-level reading in meters already uses the same sea-level datum."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩套感測或通訊可提高資料可用性，但只有真正獨立的失效才可直接相乘。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Two sensors or links can improve availability, but failure probabilities multiply only for independent events. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b269-v15-38","title":"獨立備援與共因失效機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Independent redundancy and common causes mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「獨立備援與共因失效」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Independent redundancy and common causes” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩通道期間失效機率p1=p2=0.02且獨立，同時失效p=p1p2=0.0004，即0.04%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent channel-failure probabilities p1=p2=0.02 over the same period. Joint failure p=p1p2=0.0004, or 0.04%. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：畫出感測、電源、通訊與發布的依賴圖，逐項尋找共用構件和洪水暴露。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map dependencies among sensing, power, communication and publication, identifying shared components and flood exposure.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩通道期間失效機率p1=p2=0.02且獨立，同時失效p=p1p2=0.0004，即0.04%。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent channel-failure probabilities p1=p2=0.02 over the same period. Joint failure p=p1p2=0.0004, or 0.04%.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「獨立備援與共因失效機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Independent redundancy and common causes mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["雷達不接觸水，所以不需要高程測量或現地水尺交叉驗證。","封包剛收到就一定代表此刻水位，無需再看量測時間。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩通道期間失效機率p1=p2=0.02且獨立，同時失效p=p1p2=0.0004，即0.04%。"],"optionsEn":["Noncontact radar needs neither elevation surveying nor field staff-gage checks.","A newly received packet necessarily represents current stage without checking observation time.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent channel-failure probabilities p1=p2=0.02 over the same period."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩通道期間失效機率p1=p2=0.02且獨立，同時失效p=p1p2=0.0004，即0.04%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent channel-failure probabilities p1=p2=0.02 over the same period. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b269-v15-39","title":"獨立備援與共因失效機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Independent redundancy and common causes mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「獨立備援與共因失效」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Independent redundancy and common causes” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"畫出感測、電源、通訊與發布的依賴圖，逐項尋找共用構件和洪水暴露。以受控故障測試確認切換、補傳與資料旗標，並用實際事件記錄評估獨立假設是否成立。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map dependencies among sensing, power, communication and publication, identifying shared components and flood exposure. Use controlled failure tests to check switching, backfill and quality flags, then examine event records to assess whether the assumed independence is supported rather than merely convenient. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：為雙感測器畫出共用與獨立電源兩個架構，指出哪些故障可由另一通道保留觀測。加入共同淹水事件後重新描述模型限制，避免把理想數字當保證。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw shared- and independent-power versions of a dual-sensor system, identifying failures that leave observations available. Add a common inundation event and restate the model limits rather than presenting the ideal probability as a guarantee.","failure":"注意干擾：共用電源的雙感測器可能一次斷電全部停擺，雙通訊也可能同時依賴同一伺服器；直接乘機率會給出過度樂觀的可用性，卻沒有增加真正的失效隔離。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Two sensors on one supply can fail in a single outage, and two links may depend on the same server. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"畫出感測、電源、通訊與發布的依賴圖，逐項尋找共用構件和洪水暴露。以受控故障測試確認切換、補傳與資料旗標，並用實際事件記錄評估獨立假設是否成立。","textEn":"Map dependencies among sensing, power, communication and publication, identifying shared components and flood exposure. Use controlled failure tests to check switching, backfill and quality flags, then examine event records to assess whether the assumed independence is supported rather than merely convenient.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"為雙感測器畫出共用與獨立電源兩個架構，指出哪些故障可由另一通道保留觀測。加入共同淹水事件後重新描述模型限制，避免把理想數字當保證。","textEn":"Draw shared- and independent-power versions of a dual-sensor system, identifying failures that leave observations available. Add a common inundation event and restate the model limits rather than presenting the ideal probability as a guarantee.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「獨立備援與共因失效機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Independent redundancy and common causes mechanism and verification\"?","options":["畫出感測、電源、通訊與發布的依賴圖，逐項尋找共用構件和洪水暴露。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","取樣越密，任何相鄰兩點差分得到的水位速率就一定越可靠。"],"optionsEn":["Map dependencies among sensing, power, communication and publication, identifying shared components and flood exposure.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Denser sampling always makes a two-point stage derivative more reliable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"畫出感測、電源、通訊與發布的依賴圖，逐項尋找共用構件和洪水暴露。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map dependencies among sensing, power, communication and publication, identifying shared components and flood exposure. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b269-v15-40","title":"獨立備援與共因失效機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Independent redundancy and common causes mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"prerequisiteIds":["b269-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「獨立備援與共因失效」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Independent redundancy and common causes” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"共用電源的雙感測器可能一次斷電全部停擺，雙通訊也可能同時依賴同一伺服器；直接乘機率會給出過度樂觀的可用性，卻沒有增加真正的失效隔離。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Two sensors on one supply can fail in a single outage, and two links may depend on the same server. Multiplying probabilities then gives optimistic availability without genuine isolation of the failure mechanisms. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例定義相同觀察期間兩通道失效機率且假設獨立，只示範理想備援；未加入修復、共因及不同失效模式。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It illustrates ideal redundancy without repair, common causes or multiple failure modes.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要現場裝兩支感測器，就一定可以把全部失效機率相乘。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Installing two field sensors always permits multiplication of all failure probabilities.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b269-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共用電源的雙感測器可能一次斷電全部停擺，雙通訊也可能同時依賴同一伺服器；直接乘機率會給出過度樂觀的可用性，卻沒有增加真正的失效隔離。","textEn":"Two sensors on one supply can fail in a single outage, and two links may depend on the same server. Multiplying probabilities then gives optimistic availability without genuine isolation of the failure mechanisms.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]},{"id":"b269-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「獨立備援與共因失效機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Independent redundancy and common causes mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","共用電源的雙感測器可能一次斷電全部停擺，雙通訊也可能同時依賴同一伺服器；直接乘機率會給出過度樂觀的可用性，卻沒有增加真正的失效隔離。","所有水位計顯示的公尺數都已是同一海拔基準下的高程。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Two sensors on one supply can fail in a single outage, and two links may depend on the same server.","Every water-level reading in meters already uses the same sea-level datum."],"answer":1,"explanation":"共用電源的雙感測器可能一次斷電全部停擺，雙通訊也可能同時依賴同一伺服器；直接乘機率會給出過度樂觀的可用性，卻沒有增加真正的失效隔離。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Two sensors on one supply can fail in a single outage, and two links may depend on the same server. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-usgs-stage","v15s-usgs-levels","v15s-usgs-lees","v15s-usgs-vicksburg","v15s-noaa-dcs"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b270","title":"防洪抽水站機組整合","titleEn":"Flood-pumping-station integration","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課由內水收支與系統揚程進入並聯泵、效率、變速、啟停及吸入條件，再串接電源、閘門與備援能力。上環與西部封閉綜合工程提供不同尺度的實例，所有算例為原創簡化條件；課程要求可追溯驗證與失效界面分析，不將教學數字當現場操作設定。","summaryEn":"The course moves from interior-water balance and system head to parallel units, efficiency, speed, cycling and suction conditions, then integrates power, gates and retained capacity. Sheung Wan and the West Closure Complex provide examples at different scales. Every calculation is an original simplification, requiring traceable verification and interface analysis rather than treating lesson values as field operating settings.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["雨洪與儲水","Runoff and storage"],["機組與管路","Pumps and pipes"],["閘門防倒灌","Backflow gates"],["供電與控制","Power and control"],["故障驗證","Failure verification"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["雨洪與儲水","機組與管路","閘門防倒灌","供電與控制","故障驗證"],"labelsEn":["Runoff and storage","Pumps and pipes","Backflow gates","Power and control","Failure verification"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"敏感度沿用兩台相同泵的Hp=10−0.25q²與系統H=Hs+0.20Q²，流量以m³/s、揚程以m表示且Q=2q。靜揚程Hs由3.0增至3.3 m，增加10%，兩台總流量由5.164降至5.052 m³/s，約減少2.17%。此例不是說所有外水位上升都只減少少量排水，而是展示實際變化由泵與系統曲線共同決定；若新交點超出允許工況，簡化曲線就不能繼續外推。效率、電功率、汽蝕及儲水演算需在新工作點重新檢查。","textEn":"Use two identical pumps with Hp=10−0.25q² and system H=Hs+0.20Q², flows in m³/s, heads in meters and Q=2q. Increasing static head Hs from 3.0 to 3.3 m, or ten percent, reduces combined flow from 5.164 to 5.052 m³/s, approximately 2.17%. This does not imply that rising receiving water always causes only a small drainage loss. It demonstrates that the response follows both pump and system curves. A new intersection outside allowable operation invalidates extrapolation of the simplified curve. Efficiency, electrical power, cavitation and storage routing all need reassessment at the new operating point.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b270-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「內水蓄積與抽排收支機理與驗證」與「系統揚程與外水位機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Interior storage and pumping balance mechanism and verification\" and \"System head and receiving stage mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b270-v15-01","title":"內水蓄積與抽排收支機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Interior storage and pumping balance mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「內水蓄積與抽排收支」如何影響防洪抽水站機組整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Interior storage and pumping balance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood-pumping-station integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"防洪抽水站處理的是隨時間進入低窪區的水量，而不是單一固定流量。外河高水位關閉重力出口時，集水池與上游管網共同儲存未排出的水，水位上升速度取決於淨入流和有效面積；抽水能力需要與降雨逕流、儲水曲線和外水位成組分析，不能只比較泵銘牌與最大入流。本例在短時間內固定面積和進出流量，假設沒有其他溢流或滲流；不是整場洪水演算，也未描述管網局部積水。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「內水蓄積與抽排收支」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A flood station handles a time-varying inflow rather than one fixed discharge. When high receiving water closes a gravity outlet, the sump and upstream network store unremoved water; rise rate depends on net inflow and effective surface area. Pumping must be evaluated with runoff, storage curves and receiving stage rather than merely comparing nameplate capacity with peak inflow. The short-step example fixes area and flows and excludes other overflow or seepage. It is neither full-event routing nor a description of local network flooding. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Interior storage and pumping balance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設入流Qi=6、抽排Qp=4 m³/s、時間Δt=300 s、有效面積A=600 m²，水位升幅Δh=(Qi−Qp)Δt/A=1.00 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume inflow Qi=6, pumping Qp=4 m³/s, Δt=300 s and effective area A=600 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「泵的標示總流量大於平均雨水流量，就能保證任何洪水不積水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Total labeled pump flow above mean runoff guarantees no flooding in any event.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「內水蓄積與抽排收支」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Interior storage and pumping balance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-01-k1","title":"內水蓄積與抽排收支機理與驗證","titleEn":"Interior storage and pumping balance mechanism and verification","text":"防洪抽水站處理的是隨時間進入低窪區的水量，而不是單一固定流量。外河高水位關閉重力出口時，集水池與上游管網共同儲存未排出的水，水位上升速度取決於淨入流和有效面積；抽水能力需要與降雨逕流、儲水曲線和外水位成組分析，不能只比較泵銘牌與最大入流。","textEn":"A flood station handles a time-varying inflow rather than one fixed discharge. When high receiving water closes a gravity outlet, the sump and upstream network store unremoved water; rise rate depends on net inflow and effective surface area.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：泵的標示總流量大於平均雨水流量，就能保證任何洪水不積水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Total labeled pump flow above mean runoff guarantees no flooding in any event. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「內水蓄積與抽排收支機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Interior storage and pumping balance mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["泵的標示總流量大於平均雨水流量，就能保證任何洪水不積水。","防洪抽水站處理的是隨時間進入低窪區的水量，而不是單一固定流量。","防洪泵在所有外河水位下都會維持同一銘牌流量。"],"optionsEn":["Total labeled pump flow above mean runoff guarantees no flooding in any event.","A flood station handles a time-varying inflow rather than one fixed discharge.","A flood pump maintains the same nameplate flow at every receiving-river level."],"answer":1,"explanation":"防洪抽水站處理的是隨時間進入低窪區的水量，而不是單一固定流量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A flood station handles a time-varying inflow rather than one fixed discharge. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b270-v15-02","title":"內水蓄積與抽排收支機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Interior storage and pumping balance mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「內水蓄積與抽排收支」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Interior storage and pumping balance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設入流Qi=6、抽排Qp=4 m³/s、時間Δt=300 s、有效面積A=600 m²，水位升幅Δh=(Qi−Qp)Δt/A=1.00 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume inflow Qi=6, pumping Qp=4 m³/s, Δt=300 s and effective area A=600 m². Rise Δh=(Qi−Qp)Δt/A=1.00 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同步雨量、入流、泵流量和池水位核對每個時間步的體積收支，確認有效面積是否隨水位改變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile stepwise volumes with synchronized rainfall, inflow, pumping and sump level, checking whether effective area changes with stage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設入流Qi=6、抽排Qp=4 m³/s、時間Δt=300 s、有效面積A=600 m²，水位升幅Δh=(Qi−Qp)Δt/A=1.00 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume inflow Qi=6, pumping Qp=4 m³/s, Δt=300 s and effective area A=600 m². Rise Δh=(Qi−Qp)Δt/A=1.00 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「內水蓄積與抽排收支機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Interior storage and pumping balance mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["水力功率就是抽水站電表功率，不必計入馬達和泵的損失。","啟停週期等於調節容積除以泵流量，入流大小完全無關。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設入流Qi=6、抽排Qp=4 m³/s、時間Δt=300 s、有效面積A=600 m²，水位升幅Δh=(Qi−Qp)Δt/A=1.00 m。"],"optionsEn":["Hydraulic power equals metered station power without pump or motor losses.","The start-stop cycle equals regulating volume divided by pump flow and is independent of inflow.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume inflow Qi=6, pumping Qp=4 m³/s, Δt=300 s and effective area A=600 m²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設入流Qi=6、抽排Qp=4 m³/s、時間Δt=300 s、有效面積A=600 m²，水位升幅Δh=(Qi−Qp)Δt/A=1.00 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume inflow Qi=6, pumping Qp=4 m³/s, Δt=300 s and effective area A=600 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b270-v15-03","title":"內水蓄積與抽排收支機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Interior storage and pumping balance mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「內水蓄積與抽排收支」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Interior storage and pumping balance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同步雨量、入流、泵流量和池水位核對每個時間步的體積收支，確認有效面積是否隨水位改變。將溢流、重力排水與閘門狀態分開記錄，避免把未知出口造成的差額歸因感測誤差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile stepwise volumes with synchronized rainfall, inflow, pumping and sump level, checking whether effective area changes with stage. Record overflow, gravity discharge and gate state separately so that an unrecognized outlet is not incorrectly absorbed into a sensor-error correction. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立五分鐘體積帳並逐步更新池水位，讓其中一段抽排量降低。指出峰值入流比較與全事件體積演算各會發現什麼問題，並標記需要水位面積曲線的區段。","observationEn":"Site practice: Build a five-minute volume ledger with sequential stage updates and reduce pumping during one interval. Explain the different problems revealed by peak-flow comparison and full-event volume routing, marking where a stage-area curve becomes necessary.","failure":"注意干擾：只用最大泵量而忽略高外水位的實際工況會高估抽排，漏掉上游管網蓄水則可能錯估池水位變化；淨入流長時間為正時，有限儲量終究會耗盡。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using maximum pump flow without the high-tailwater operating point overstates drainage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同步雨量、入流、泵流量和池水位核對每個時間步的體積收支，確認有效面積是否隨水位改變。將溢流、重力排水與閘門狀態分開記錄，避免把未知出口造成的差額歸因感測誤差。","textEn":"Reconcile stepwise volumes with synchronized rainfall, inflow, pumping and sump level, checking whether effective area changes with stage. Record overflow, gravity discharge and gate state separately so that an unrecognized outlet is not incorrectly absorbed into a sensor-error correction.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立五分鐘體積帳並逐步更新池水位，讓其中一段抽排量降低。指出峰值入流比較與全事件體積演算各會發現什麼問題，並標記需要水位面積曲線的區段。","textEn":"Build a five-minute volume ledger with sequential stage updates and reduce pumping during one interval. Explain the different problems revealed by peak-flow comparison and full-event volume routing, marking where a stage-area curve becomes necessary.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「內水蓄積與抽排收支機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Interior storage and pumping balance mechanism and verification\"?","options":["以同步雨量、入流、泵流量和池水位核對每個時間步的體積收支，確認有效面積是否隨水位改變。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","備援電源連續千瓦足夠，就代表所有泵可以同時順利啟動。"],"optionsEn":["Reconcile stepwise volumes with synchronized rainfall, inflow, pumping and sump level, checking whether effective area changes with stage.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adequate continuous backup kilowatts guarantee that all pumps can start simultaneously."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以同步雨量、入流、泵流量和池水位核對每個時間步的體積收支，確認有效面積是否隨水位改變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile stepwise volumes with synchronized rainfall, inflow, pumping and sump level, checking whether effective area changes with stage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b270-v15-04","title":"內水蓄積與抽排收支機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Interior storage and pumping balance mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「內水蓄積與抽排收支」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Interior storage and pumping balance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只用最大泵量而忽略高外水位的實際工況會高估抽排，漏掉上游管網蓄水則可能錯估池水位變化；淨入流長時間為正時，有限儲量終究會耗盡。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using maximum pump flow without the high-tailwater operating point overstates drainage. Omitting upstream network storage distorts sump response, and persistently positive net inflow eventually exhausts finite available storage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例在短時間內固定面積和進出流量，假設沒有其他溢流或滲流；不是整場洪水演算，也未描述管網局部積水。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It is neither full-event routing nor a description of local network flooding.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「泵的標示總流量大於平均雨水流量，就能保證任何洪水不積水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Total labeled pump flow above mean runoff guarantees no flooding in any event.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只用最大泵量而忽略高外水位的實際工況會高估抽排，漏掉上游管網蓄水則可能錯估池水位變化；淨入流長時間為正時，有限儲量終究會耗盡。","textEn":"Using maximum pump flow without the high-tailwater operating point overstates drainage. Omitting upstream network storage distorts sump response, and persistently positive net inflow eventually exhausts finite available storage.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「內水蓄積與抽排收支機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Interior storage and pumping balance mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只用最大泵量而忽略高外水位的實際工況會高估抽排，漏掉上游管網蓄水則可能錯估池水位變化；淨入流長時間為正時，有限儲量終究會耗盡。","防洪泵在所有外河水位下都會維持同一銘牌流量。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using maximum pump flow without the high-tailwater operating point overstates drainage.","A flood pump maintains the same nameplate flow at every receiving-river level."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只用最大泵量而忽略高外水位的實際工況會高估抽排，漏掉上游管網蓄水則可能錯估池水位變化；淨入流長時間為正時，有限儲量終究會耗盡。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using maximum pump flow without the high-tailwater operating point overstates drainage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b270-v15-05","title":"系統揚程與外水位機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"System head and receiving stage mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「系統揚程與外水位」如何影響防洪抽水站機組整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “System head and receiving stage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood-pumping-station integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"泵需要克服內外水面差與管路損失，外河或海潮升高會改變系統曲線並移動工作點。靜揚程可隨內水位上升而降低，但摩阻通常隨流量增加，兩者不能混成固定總揚程；不同閘門與出口狀態也會改變損失，需為代表工況建立一致的能量帳。本例用二次損失近似固定配置的系統曲線，係數帶有單位；不涵蓋氣塞、虹吸建立或瞬變逆流。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「系統揚程與外水位」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A pump overcomes the difference between interior and receiving surfaces plus hydraulic losses. Rising river or tide shifts the system curve and operating point. Static head can decrease as the sump rises, while friction generally increases with flow; they cannot be collapsed into one fixed total head. Gate and outlet states also require separate, consistent energy balances. The example uses a quadratic loss approximation for a fixed configuration, with a dimensional coefficient. It excludes trapped air, siphon establishment and transient reverse flow. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “System head and receiving stage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設靜揚程Hs=3.0 m、損失係數K=0.20 s²/m⁵、流量Q=4.0 m³/s，Hsys=Hs+KQ²=6.20 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume static head Hs=3.0 m, loss coefficient K=0.20 s²/m⁵ and flow Q=4.0 m³/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「防洪泵在所有外河水位下都會維持同一銘牌流量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A flood pump maintains the same nameplate flow at every receiving-river level.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「系統揚程與外水位」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “System head and receiving stage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-05-k1","title":"系統揚程與外水位機理與驗證","titleEn":"System head and receiving stage mechanism and verification","text":"泵需要克服內外水面差與管路損失，外河或海潮升高會改變系統曲線並移動工作點。靜揚程可隨內水位上升而降低，但摩阻通常隨流量增加，兩者不能混成固定總揚程；不同閘門與出口狀態也會改變損失，需為代表工況建立一致的能量帳。","textEn":"A pump overcomes the difference between interior and receiving surfaces plus hydraulic losses. Rising river or tide shifts the system curve and operating point.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：防洪泵在所有外河水位下都會維持同一銘牌流量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A flood pump maintains the same nameplate flow at every receiving-river level. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「系統揚程與外水位機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"System head and receiving stage mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["防洪泵在所有外河水位下都會維持同一銘牌流量。","兩台並聯泵的實際排水量必定是單台接原管路時的兩倍。","泵需要克服內外水面差與管路損失，外河或海潮升高會改變系統曲線並移動工作點。"],"optionsEn":["A flood pump maintains the same nameplate flow at every receiving-river level.","Two parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow through the original system.","A pump overcomes the difference between interior and receiving surfaces plus hydraulic losses."],"answer":2,"explanation":"泵需要克服內外水面差與管路損失，外河或海潮升高會改變系統曲線並移動工作點。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A pump overcomes the difference between interior and receiving surfaces plus hydraulic losses. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b270-v15-06","title":"系統揚程與外水位機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"System head and receiving stage mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「系統揚程與外水位」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “System head and receiving stage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設靜揚程Hs=3.0 m、損失係數K=0.20 s²/m⁵、流量Q=4.0 m³/s，Hsys=Hs+KQ²=6.20 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume static head Hs=3.0 m, loss coefficient K=0.20 s²/m⁵ and flow Q=4.0 m³/s. System head Hsys=Hs+KQ²=6.20 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測內外水位並核對同一高程基準，將流量、閥位及壓差配對以辨認系統損失。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure interior and receiving stages on one datum, pairing flow, valve position and pressure difference to identify system losses.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設靜揚程Hs=3.0 m、損失係數K=0.20 s²/m⁵、流量Q=4.0 m³/s，Hsys=Hs+KQ²=6.20 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume static head Hs=3.0 m, loss coefficient K=0.20 s²/m⁵ and flow Q=4.0 m³/s. System head Hsys=Hs+KQ²=6.20 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「系統揚程與外水位機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"System head and receiving stage mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設靜揚程Hs=3.0 m、損失係數K=0.20 s²/m⁵、流量Q=4.0 m³/s，Hsys=Hs+KQ²=6.20 m。","泵降速一成，整站一定同時少抽一成水且省下固定立方比例電力。","池水位只要夠高，任何機組組合都不可能出現渦流或汽蝕。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume static head Hs=3.0 m, loss coefficient K=0.20 s²/m⁵ and flow Q=4.0 m³/s.","Reducing speed ten percent guarantees ten percent less station flow and fixed cube-law energy savings.","Sufficient sump level makes vortices or cavitation impossible for every pump combination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設靜揚程Hs=3.0 m、損失係數K=0.20 s²/m⁵、流量Q=4.0 m³/s，Hsys=Hs+KQ²=6.20 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume static head Hs=3.0 m, loss coefficient K=0.20 s²/m⁵ and flow Q=4.0 m³/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b270-v15-07","title":"系統揚程與外水位機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"System head and receiving stage mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「系統揚程與外水位」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “System head and receiving stage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測內外水位並核對同一高程基準，將流量、閥位及壓差配對以辨認系統損失。分別檢查高外水位、低內水位及部分堵塞工況，不把單次測試曲線直接套用全部事件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure interior and receiving stages on one datum, pairing flow, valve position and pressure difference to identify system losses. Examine high tailwater, low sump level and partial blockage separately rather than applying one test curve unchanged to every storm condition. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出兩種外水位的系統曲線，保持管路損失係數不變。說明曲線移動如何影響與泵曲線的交點，再列出哪些構件改變會使係數也必須更新。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw system curves for two receiving stages while holding the loss coefficient fixed. Explain their changed intersections with the pump curve, then identify component changes that would also require updating the coefficient.","failure":"注意干擾：把外水位忽略會在最需要抽排時高估流量，將靜揚程當成全部揚程又會低估摩阻；出口堵塞或閥位改變可使原有工作點預測失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting tailwater overstates flow when drainage is most needed, while treating static head as total head understates friction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測內外水位並核對同一高程基準，將流量、閥位及壓差配對以辨認系統損失。分別檢查高外水位、低內水位及部分堵塞工況，不把單次測試曲線直接套用全部事件。","textEn":"Measure interior and receiving stages on one datum, pairing flow, valve position and pressure difference to identify system losses. Examine high tailwater, low sump level and partial blockage separately rather than applying one test curve unchanged to every storm condition.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出兩種外水位的系統曲線，保持管路損失係數不變。說明曲線移動如何影響與泵曲線的交點，再列出哪些構件改變會使係數也必須更新。","textEn":"Draw system curves for two receiving stages while holding the loss coefficient fixed. Explain their changed intersections with the pump curve, then identify component changes that would also require updating the coefficient.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「系統揚程與外水位機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"System head and receiving stage mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","量測內外水位並核對同一高程基準，將流量、閥位及壓差配對以辨認系統損失。","閘門兩側淨水壓只需把水位差平方，與各側實際水深無關。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Measure interior and receiving stages on one datum, pairing flow, valve position and pressure difference to identify system losses.","Net gate pressure depends only on squared level difference, not the individual water depths."],"answer":1,"explanation":"量測內外水位並核對同一高程基準，將流量、閥位及壓差配對以辨認系統損失。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure interior and receiving stages on one datum, pairing flow, valve position and pressure difference to identify system losses. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b270-v15-08","title":"系統揚程與外水位機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"System head and receiving stage mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「系統揚程與外水位」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “System head and receiving stage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把外水位忽略會在最需要抽排時高估流量，將靜揚程當成全部揚程又會低估摩阻；出口堵塞或閥位改變可使原有工作點預測失效。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting tailwater overstates flow when drainage is most needed, while treating static head as total head understates friction. Outlet blockage or changed valve position can invalidate the originally predicted operating point. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例用二次損失近似固定配置的系統曲線，係數帶有單位；不涵蓋氣塞、虹吸建立或瞬變逆流。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It excludes trapped air, siphon establishment and transient reverse flow.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「防洪泵在所有外河水位下都會維持同一銘牌流量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A flood pump maintains the same nameplate flow at every receiving-river level.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把外水位忽略會在最需要抽排時高估流量，將靜揚程當成全部揚程又會低估摩阻；出口堵塞或閥位改變可使原有工作點預測失效。","textEn":"Omitting tailwater overstates flow when drainage is most needed, while treating static head as total head understates friction. Outlet blockage or changed valve position can invalidate the originally predicted operating point.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「系統揚程與外水位機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"System head and receiving stage mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","兩台並聯泵的實際排水量必定是單台接原管路時的兩倍。","把外水位忽略會在最需要抽排時高估流量，將靜揚程當成全部揚程又會低估摩阻；出口堵塞或閥位改變可使原有工作點預測失效。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Two parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow through the original system.","Omitting tailwater overstates flow when drainage is most needed, while treating static head as total head understates friction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把外水位忽略會在最需要抽排時高估流量，將靜揚程當成全部揚程又會低估摩阻；出口堵塞或閥位改變可使原有工作點預測失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting tailwater overstates flow when drainage is most needed, while treating static head as total head understates friction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b270-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「並聯機組與共同管路機理與驗證」與「電功率與效率鏈機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Parallel pumps and common pipework mechanism and verification\" and \"Electrical power and efficiency chain mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b270-v15-09","title":"並聯機組與共同管路機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Parallel pumps and common pipework mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「並聯機組與共同管路」如何影響防洪抽水站機組整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Parallel pumps and common pipework” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood-pumping-station integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"並聯泵在相同揚程下疊加流量，但共同管路的摩阻會隨總流量增加，因此加開第二台通常不會使站流量正好加倍。不同機組曲線、止回閥及局部損失還可能造成不均分流，甚至讓一台落在不利區域；整合時須同時解機組與系統曲線，而不是把型錄數字相加。以下兩台完全相同且均分流量，泵曲線與系統曲線均為教學二次式；沒有替代實機穩定區、效率及汽蝕檢查。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「並聯機組與共同管路」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Parallel pumps add flow at a common head, but shared-pipe friction grows with total flow, so a second pump generally does not double station discharge. Different unit curves, check valves and local losses can create uneven sharing or an unfavorable operating region. Integration therefore solves pump and system curves together rather than adding catalog values. The two units are identical and share flow equally, with hypothetical quadratic pump and system curves. This does not replace real-machine stability, efficiency or cavitation checks. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Parallel pumps and common pipework” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設單泵Hp=10−0.25q² m、系統Hs=3+0.20Q² m，q、Q以m³/s計；兩泵Q=2q得Q=2√(7/1.05)=5.164 m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume pump Hp=10−0.25q² m and system Hs=3+0.20Q² m, with q,Q in m³/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩台並聯泵的實際排水量必定是單台接原管路時的兩倍。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow through the original system.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「並聯機組與共同管路」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Parallel pumps and common pipework”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-09-k1","title":"並聯機組與共同管路機理與驗證","titleEn":"Parallel pumps and common pipework mechanism and verification","text":"並聯泵在相同揚程下疊加流量，但共同管路的摩阻會隨總流量增加，因此加開第二台通常不會使站流量正好加倍。不同機組曲線、止回閥及局部損失還可能造成不均分流，甚至讓一台落在不利區域；整合時須同時解機組與系統曲線，而不是把型錄數字相加。","textEn":"Parallel pumps add flow at a common head, but shared-pipe friction grows with total flow, so a second pump generally does not double station discharge. Different unit curves, check valves and local losses can create uneven sharing or an unfavorable operating region.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩台並聯泵的實際排水量必定是單台接原管路時的兩倍。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow through the original system. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「並聯機組與共同管路機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Parallel pumps and common pipework mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["並聯泵在相同揚程下疊加流量，但共同管路的摩阻會隨總流量增加，因此加開第二台通常不會使站流量正好加倍。","兩台並聯泵的實際排水量必定是單台接原管路時的兩倍。","水力功率就是抽水站電表功率，不必計入馬達和泵的損失。"],"optionsEn":["Parallel pumps add flow at a common head, but shared-pipe friction grows with total flow, so a second pump generally does not double station discharge.","Two parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow through the original system.","Hydraulic power equals metered station power without pump or motor losses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"並聯泵在相同揚程下疊加流量，但共同管路的摩阻會隨總流量增加，因此加開第二台通常不會使站流量正好加倍。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Parallel pumps add flow at a common head, but shared-pipe friction grows with total flow, so a second pump generally does not double station discharge. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b270-v15-10","title":"並聯機組與共同管路機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Parallel pumps and common pipework mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「並聯機組與共同管路」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Parallel pumps and common pipework” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設單泵Hp=10−0.25q² m、系統Hs=3+0.20Q² m，q、Q以m³/s計；兩泵Q=2q得Q=2√(7/1.05)=5.164 m³/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume pump Hp=10−0.25q² m and system Hs=3+0.20Q² m, with q,Q in m³/s. Two pumps give Q=2q=2√(7/1.05)=5.164 m³/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以每台支路流量、共同揚程及轉速驗證分流，核對曲線使用的流量單位與機組組合。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify sharing from individual branch flows, common head and speed, checking curve units and pump combinations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設單泵Hp=10−0.25q² m、系統Hs=3+0.20Q² m，q、Q以m³/s計；兩泵Q=2q得Q=2√(7/1.05)=5.164 m³/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume pump Hp=10−0.25q² m and system Hs=3+0.20Q² m, with q,Q in m³/s. Two pumps give Q=2q=2√(7/1.05)=5.164 m³/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「並聯機組與共同管路機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Parallel pumps and common pipework mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["啟停週期等於調節容積除以泵流量，入流大小完全無關。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設單泵Hp=10−0.25q² m、系統Hs=3+0.20Q² m，q、Q以m³/s計。","備援電源連續千瓦足夠，就代表所有泵可以同時順利啟動。"],"optionsEn":["The start-stop cycle equals regulating volume divided by pump flow and is independent of inflow.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume pump Hp=10−0.25q² m and system Hs=3+0.20Q² m, with q,Q in m³/s.","Adequate continuous backup kilowatts guarantee that all pumps can start simultaneously."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設單泵Hp=10−0.25q² m、系統Hs=3+0.20Q² m，q、Q以m³/s計；兩泵Q=2q得Q=2√(7/1.05)=5.164 m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume pump Hp=10−0.25q² m and system Hs=3+0.20Q² m, with q,Q in m³/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b270-v15-11","title":"並聯機組與共同管路機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Parallel pumps and common pipework mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「並聯機組與共同管路」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Parallel pumps and common pipework” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以每台支路流量、共同揚程及轉速驗證分流，核對曲線使用的流量單位與機組組合。比較單台及多台實測交點，檢查止回閥開啟與低流量穩定性，再評估剩餘備援能力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify sharing from individual branch flows, common head and speed, checking curve units and pump combinations. Compare measured single- and multiple-unit intersections, inspect check-valve opening and low-flow stability, and only then assess the drainage capability retained under backup arrangements. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：先解單台交點，再解兩台交點並比較增加比例。將一台泵曲線稍微下移，說明均分流量假設為何不再成立，以及需要補量測哪個支路。","observationEn":"Site practice: Solve single- and two-pump intersections and compare the increase. Shift one pump curve downward slightly, explaining why equal sharing then fails and which branch measurements would be needed to determine the new distribution.","failure":"注意干擾：直接把單台工況流量乘台數會忽略共同摩阻，異型泵也可能出現分流失衡；名義總容量足夠時，某台仍可能偏離允許運轉區而增加振動或過熱。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Multiplying a single-unit operating flow by unit count ignores shared friction, and dissimilar pumps may share unevenly. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以每台支路流量、共同揚程及轉速驗證分流，核對曲線使用的流量單位與機組組合。比較單台及多台實測交點，檢查止回閥開啟與低流量穩定性，再評估剩餘備援能力。","textEn":"Verify sharing from individual branch flows, common head and speed, checking curve units and pump combinations. Compare measured single- and multiple-unit intersections, inspect check-valve opening and low-flow stability, and only then assess the drainage capability retained under backup arrangements.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"先解單台交點，再解兩台交點並比較增加比例。將一台泵曲線稍微下移，說明均分流量假設為何不再成立，以及需要補量測哪個支路。","textEn":"Solve single- and two-pump intersections and compare the increase. Shift one pump curve downward slightly, explaining why equal sharing then fails and which branch measurements would be needed to determine the new distribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「並聯機組與共同管路機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Parallel pumps and common pipework mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","設有一台備用泵就能保證抽水站任何單一故障都不減排水量。","以每台支路流量、共同揚程及轉速驗證分流，核對曲線使用的流量單位與機組組合。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","One spare pump guarantees unchanged station discharge under every single failure.","Verify sharing from individual branch flows, common head and speed, checking curve units and pump combinations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以每台支路流量、共同揚程及轉速驗證分流，核對曲線使用的流量單位與機組組合。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify sharing from individual branch flows, common head and speed, checking curve units and pump combinations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b270-v15-12","title":"並聯機組與共同管路機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Parallel pumps and common pipework mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「並聯機組與共同管路」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Parallel pumps and common pipework” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"直接把單台工況流量乘台數會忽略共同摩阻，異型泵也可能出現分流失衡；名義總容量足夠時，某台仍可能偏離允許運轉區而增加振動或過熱。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Multiplying a single-unit operating flow by unit count ignores shared friction, and dissimilar pumps may share unevenly. Even with adequate nominal total capacity, an individual unit can leave its acceptable range and experience vibration or overheating. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以下兩台完全相同且均分流量，泵曲線與系統曲線均為教學二次式；沒有替代實機穩定區、效率及汽蝕檢查。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This does not replace real-machine stability, efficiency or cavitation checks.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩台並聯泵的實際排水量必定是單台接原管路時的兩倍。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow through the original system.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"直接把單台工況流量乘台數會忽略共同摩阻，異型泵也可能出現分流失衡；名義總容量足夠時，某台仍可能偏離允許運轉區而增加振動或過熱。","textEn":"Multiplying a single-unit operating flow by unit count ignores shared friction, and dissimilar pumps may share unevenly. Even with adequate nominal total capacity, an individual unit can leave its acceptable range and experience vibration or overheating.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「並聯機組與共同管路機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Parallel pumps and common pipework mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["直接把單台工況流量乘台數會忽略共同摩阻，異型泵也可能出現分流失衡；名義總容量足夠時，某台仍可能偏離允許運轉區而增加振動或過熱。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","水力功率就是抽水站電表功率，不必計入馬達和泵的損失。"],"optionsEn":["Multiplying a single-unit operating flow by unit count ignores shared friction, and dissimilar pumps may share unevenly.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Hydraulic power equals metered station power without pump or motor losses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"直接把單台工況流量乘台數會忽略共同摩阻，異型泵也可能出現分流失衡；名義總容量足夠時，某台仍可能偏離允許運轉區而增加振動或過熱。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Multiplying a single-unit operating flow by unit count ignores shared friction, and dissimilar pumps may share unevenly. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b270-v15-13","title":"電功率與效率鏈機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Electrical power and efficiency chain mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「電功率與效率鏈」如何影響防洪抽水站機組整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Electrical power and efficiency chain” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood-pumping-station integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"抽水的水力功率由流量和總揚程決定，馬達輸入還須考慮泵、傳動與電機效率。不同效率應對應各自能量邊界，不能重複扣同一損失；峰值功率、啟動需求與整場耗電又是不同問題，平均節能指標不足以代表防洪事件中的供電能力。本例泵與馬達效率分開且忽略其他輔機，計算穩態實功率；不包含啟動電流、功率因數或發電機瞬態容量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「電功率與效率鏈」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Hydraulic power follows flow and total head, while motor input includes pump, transmission and electrical efficiencies. Each efficiency must correspond to a distinct energy boundary so losses are not counted twice. Peak power, starting demand and event energy are separate questions; a mean energy metric does not establish electrical adequacy during a flood. Pump and motor efficiencies are separate and auxiliary loads are excluded. The result is steady real power, not starting current, power factor or generator transient capacity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Electrical power and efficiency chain” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、Q=4 m³/s、H=6 m、ηp=0.75、ηm=0.95，P=ρgQH/(ηpηm)=330.44 kW，g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, Q=4 m³/s, H=6 m, ηp=0.75, ηm=0.95 and g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「水力功率就是抽水站電表功率，不必計入馬達和泵的損失。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Hydraulic power equals metered station power without pump or motor losses.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「電功率與效率鏈」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Electrical power and efficiency chain”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-13-k1","title":"電功率與效率鏈機理與驗證","titleEn":"Electrical power and efficiency chain mechanism and verification","text":"抽水的水力功率由流量和總揚程決定，馬達輸入還須考慮泵、傳動與電機效率。不同效率應對應各自能量邊界，不能重複扣同一損失；峰值功率、啟動需求與整場耗電又是不同問題，平均節能指標不足以代表防洪事件中的供電能力。","textEn":"Hydraulic power follows flow and total head, while motor input includes pump, transmission and electrical efficiencies. Each efficiency must correspond to a distinct energy boundary so losses are not counted twice.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水力功率就是抽水站電表功率，不必計入馬達和泵的損失。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Hydraulic power equals metered station power without pump or motor losses. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電功率與效率鏈機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Electrical power and efficiency chain mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["水力功率就是抽水站電表功率，不必計入馬達和泵的損失。","抽水的水力功率由流量和總揚程決定，馬達輸入還須考慮泵、傳動與電機效率。","泵降速一成，整站一定同時少抽一成水且省下固定立方比例電力。"],"optionsEn":["Hydraulic power equals metered station power without pump or motor losses.","Hydraulic power follows flow and total head, while motor input includes pump, transmission and electrical efficiencies.","Reducing speed ten percent guarantees ten percent less station flow and fixed cube-law energy savings."],"answer":1,"explanation":"抽水的水力功率由流量和總揚程決定，馬達輸入還須考慮泵、傳動與電機效率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Hydraulic power follows flow and total head, while motor input includes pump, transmission and electrical efficiencies. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b270-v15-14","title":"電功率與效率鏈機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Electrical power and efficiency chain mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「電功率與效率鏈」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Electrical power and efficiency chain” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、Q=4 m³/s、H=6 m、ηp=0.75、ηm=0.95，P=ρgQH/(ηpηm)=330.44 kW，g=9.81 m/s²。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, Q=4 m³/s, H=6 m, ηp=0.75, ηm=0.95 and g=9.81 m/s². Input P=ρgQH/(ηpηm)=330.44 kW. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測流量、揚程與電表實功率，核對效率曲線是否對應當時轉速和負載。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure flow, head and real electrical power synchronously, checking efficiency curves against actual speed and load.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、Q=4 m³/s、H=6 m、ηp=0.75、ηm=0.95，P=ρgQH/(ηpηm)=330.44 kW，g=9.81 m/s²。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, Q=4 m³/s, H=6 m, ηp=0.75, ηm=0.95 and g=9.81 m/s². Input P=ρgQH/(ηpηm)=330.44 kW.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「電功率與效率鏈機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Electrical power and efficiency chain mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["池水位只要夠高，任何機組組合都不可能出現渦流或汽蝕。","閘門兩側淨水壓只需把水位差平方，與各側實際水深無關。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、Q=4 m³/s、H=6 m、ηp=0.75、ηm=0.95，P=ρgQH/(ηpηm)=330.44 kW，g=9.81 m/s²。"],"optionsEn":["Sufficient sump level makes vortices or cavitation impossible for every pump combination.","Net gate pressure depends only on squared level difference, not the individual water depths.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, Q=4 m³/s, H=6 m, ηp=0.75, ηm=0.95 and g=9.81 m/s²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、Q=4 m³/s、H=6 m、ηp=0.75、ηm=0.95，P=ρgQH/(ηpηm)=330.44 kW，g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, Q=4 m³/s, H=6 m, ηp=0.75, ηm=0.95 and g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b270-v15-15","title":"電功率與效率鏈機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Electrical power and efficiency chain mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「電功率與效率鏈」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Electrical power and efficiency chain” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測流量、揚程與電表實功率，核對效率曲線是否對應當時轉速和負載。將輔機與馬達邊界分開，另記錄啟動電壓和電流，避免以穩態功率測試代替啟動能力驗證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure flow, head and real electrical power synchronously, checking efficiency curves against actual speed and load. Separate auxiliaries from motor boundaries and record starting voltage and current independently so that a steady-power test is not mistaken for validation of starting capability. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出電表、馬達軸與水流三個能量邊界，將效率放在正確位置。比較泵效率下降而其他條件固定時的輸入功率，再指出啟動分析尚缺的電氣資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw meter, motor-shaft and water-flow energy boundaries with efficiencies at the correct interfaces. Compare input power after reduced pump efficiency at fixed conditions, then identify electrical information still missing for a starting analysis.","failure":"注意干擾：把泵效率當成整體效率會低估供電需求，使用額定高效率代替偏離工況的效率也會造成偏差；只看平均千瓦可能忽略啟動壓降使其他機組掉電。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using pump efficiency as overall efficiency understates electrical demand, and rated efficiency can misrepresent off-design operation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測流量、揚程與電表實功率，核對效率曲線是否對應當時轉速和負載。將輔機與馬達邊界分開，另記錄啟動電壓和電流，避免以穩態功率測試代替啟動能力驗證。","textEn":"Measure flow, head and real electrical power synchronously, checking efficiency curves against actual speed and load. Separate auxiliaries from motor boundaries and record starting voltage and current independently so that a steady-power test is not mistaken for validation of starting capability.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出電表、馬達軸與水流三個能量邊界，將效率放在正確位置。比較泵效率下降而其他條件固定時的輸入功率，再指出啟動分析尚缺的電氣資料。","textEn":"Draw meter, motor-shaft and water-flow energy boundaries with efficiencies at the correct interfaces. Compare input power after reduced pump efficiency at fixed conditions, then identify electrical information still missing for a starting analysis.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「電功率與效率鏈機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Electrical power and efficiency chain mechanism and verification\"?","options":["同步量測流量、揚程與電表實功率，核對效率曲線是否對應當時轉速和負載。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","泵的標示總流量大於平均雨水流量，就能保證任何洪水不積水。"],"optionsEn":["Measure flow, head and real electrical power synchronously, checking efficiency curves against actual speed and load.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Total labeled pump flow above mean runoff guarantees no flooding in any event."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步量測流量、揚程與電表實功率，核對效率曲線是否對應當時轉速和負載。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure flow, head and real electrical power synchronously, checking efficiency curves against actual speed and load. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b270-v15-16","title":"電功率與效率鏈機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Electrical power and efficiency chain mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「電功率與效率鏈」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Electrical power and efficiency chain” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把泵效率當成整體效率會低估供電需求，使用額定高效率代替偏離工況的效率也會造成偏差；只看平均千瓦可能忽略啟動壓降使其他機組掉電。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using pump efficiency as overall efficiency understates electrical demand, and rated efficiency can misrepresent off-design operation. Average kilowatts can also conceal a starting voltage dip that disconnects other operating units. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例泵與馬達效率分開且忽略其他輔機，計算穩態實功率；不包含啟動電流、功率因數或發電機瞬態容量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The result is steady real power, not starting current, power factor or generator transient capacity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水力功率就是抽水站電表功率，不必計入馬達和泵的損失。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Hydraulic power equals metered station power without pump or motor losses.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把泵效率當成整體效率會低估供電需求，使用額定高效率代替偏離工況的效率也會造成偏差；只看平均千瓦可能忽略啟動壓降使其他機組掉電。","textEn":"Using pump efficiency as overall efficiency understates electrical demand, and rated efficiency can misrepresent off-design operation. Average kilowatts can also conceal a starting voltage dip that disconnects other operating units.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電功率與效率鏈機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Electrical power and efficiency chain mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把泵效率當成整體效率會低估供電需求，使用額定高效率代替偏離工況的效率也會造成偏差；只看平均千瓦可能忽略啟動壓降使其他機組掉電。","泵降速一成，整站一定同時少抽一成水且省下固定立方比例電力。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using pump efficiency as overall efficiency understates electrical demand, and rated efficiency can misrepresent off-design operation.","Reducing speed ten percent guarantees ten percent less station flow and fixed cube-law energy savings."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把泵效率當成整體效率會低估供電需求，使用額定高效率代替偏離工況的效率也會造成偏差；只看平均千瓦可能忽略啟動壓降使其他機組掉電。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using pump efficiency as overall efficiency understates electrical demand, and rated efficiency can misrepresent off-design operation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b270-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「變速相似與實際工況機理與驗證」與「啟停水位差與循環機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Speed affinity and operating conditions mechanism and verification\" and \"Level hysteresis and cycling mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b270-v15-17","title":"變速相似與實際工況機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Speed affinity and operating conditions mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「變速相似與實際工況」如何影響防洪抽水站機組整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Speed affinity and operating conditions” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood-pumping-station integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"幾何相同的泵在相似工況下，流量、揚程和軸功率可依轉速比例建立近似關係，適合檢查性能曲線變化。實際站的靜揚程不隨轉速縮放，因此新工作點未必位於相似點；效率、汽蝕與低速穩定區也可能改變，不能把轉速平方或立方律直接當成整站保證。本例假設同一葉輪與近似相同效率，僅比較相似點；實際抽排量必須再與未同比縮放的系統曲線求交。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「變速相似與實際工況」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For a geometrically unchanged pump at homologous conditions, flow, head and shaft power approximately scale with speed, supporting a curve-shift check. Station static head does not scale with speed, so the new operating point need not be homologous. Efficiency, cavitation and low-speed stability may change, preventing direct use of square or cube laws as station-wide guarantees. The example assumes one impeller and approximately unchanged efficiency and compares homologous points only. Actual discharge requires intersecting the shifted pump curve with the system curve. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Speed affinity and operating conditions” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設轉速比N2/N1=0.90，相似點Q2/Q1=0.90、H2/H1=0.81、P2/P1=0.729。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume speed ratio N2/N1=0.90.","failure":"常見誤解：「泵降速一成，整站一定同時少抽一成水且省下固定立方比例電力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reducing speed ten percent guarantees ten percent less station flow and fixed cube-law energy savings.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「變速相似與實際工況」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Speed affinity and operating conditions”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-17-k1","title":"變速相似與實際工況機理與驗證","titleEn":"Speed affinity and operating conditions mechanism and verification","text":"幾何相同的泵在相似工況下，流量、揚程和軸功率可依轉速比例建立近似關係，適合檢查性能曲線變化。實際站的靜揚程不隨轉速縮放，因此新工作點未必位於相似點；效率、汽蝕與低速穩定區也可能改變，不能把轉速平方或立方律直接當成整站保證。","textEn":"For a geometrically unchanged pump at homologous conditions, flow, head and shaft power approximately scale with speed, supporting a curve-shift check. Station static head does not scale with speed, so the new operating point need not be homologous.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：泵降速一成，整站一定同時少抽一成水且省下固定立方比例電力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reducing speed ten percent guarantees ten percent less station flow and fixed cube-law energy savings. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「變速相似與實際工況機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Speed affinity and operating conditions mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["泵降速一成，整站一定同時少抽一成水且省下固定立方比例電力。","啟停週期等於調節容積除以泵流量，入流大小完全無關。","幾何相同的泵在相似工況下，流量、揚程和軸功率可依轉速比例建立近似關係，適合檢查性能曲線變化。"],"optionsEn":["Reducing speed ten percent guarantees ten percent less station flow and fixed cube-law energy savings.","The start-stop cycle equals regulating volume divided by pump flow and is independent of inflow.","For a geometrically unchanged pump at homologous conditions, flow, head and shaft power approximately scale with speed, supporting a curve-shift check."],"answer":2,"explanation":"幾何相同的泵在相似工況下，流量、揚程和軸功率可依轉速比例建立近似關係，適合檢查性能曲線變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For a geometrically unchanged pump at homologous conditions, flow, head and shaft power approximately scale with speed, supporting a curve-shift check. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b270-v15-18","title":"變速相似與實際工況機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Speed affinity and operating conditions mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「變速相似與實際工況」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Speed affinity and operating conditions” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設轉速比N2/N1=0.90，相似點Q2/Q1=0.90、H2/H1=0.81、P2/P1=0.729。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume speed ratio N2/N1=0.90. At homologous points Q2/Q1=0.90, H2/H1=0.81 and P2/P1=0.729. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將原泵曲線按相似律移動後與實際系統曲線重求交點，核對效率、允許轉速和汽蝕資料。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Shift the pump curve using affinity laws and solve its intersection with the actual system curve, checking efficiency, allowed speed and cavitation data.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設轉速比N2/N1=0.90，相似點Q2/Q1=0.90、H2/H1=0.81、P2/P1=0.729。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume speed ratio N2/N1=0.90. At homologous points Q2/Q1=0.90, H2/H1=0.81 and P2/P1=0.729.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「變速相似與實際工況機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Speed affinity and operating conditions mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設轉速比N2/N1=0.90，相似點Q2/Q1=0.90、H2/H1=0.81、P2/P1=0.729。","備援電源連續千瓦足夠，就代表所有泵可以同時順利啟動。","設有一台備用泵就能保證抽水站任何單一故障都不減排水量。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume speed ratio N2/N1=0.90.","Adequate continuous backup kilowatts guarantee that all pumps can start simultaneously.","One spare pump guarantees unchanged station discharge under every single failure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設轉速比N2/N1=0.90，相似點Q2/Q1=0.90、H2/H1=0.81、P2/P1=0.729。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume speed ratio N2/N1=0.90. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b270-v15-19","title":"變速相似與實際工況機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Speed affinity and operating conditions mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「變速相似與實際工況」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Speed affinity and operating conditions” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將原泵曲線按相似律移動後與實際系統曲線重求交點，核對效率、允許轉速和汽蝕資料。用現地量測驗證結果，尤其檢查靜揚程占比高時是否仍能維持有效出流。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Shift the pump curve using affinity laws and solve its intersection with the actual system curve, checking efficiency, allowed speed and cavitation data. Validate with field observations, especially whether useful discharge remains when static head forms a large share of total head. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出含靜揚程與不含靜揚程兩條系統曲線，比較同一降速泵曲線的交點。指出相似點與實際工作點的差別，避免把兩種比例放在同一張效益表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw system curves with and without static head and compare intersections with one reduced-speed pump curve. Distinguish homologous points from operating points so their ratios are not mixed in a performance table.","failure":"注意干擾：直接宣稱降速一成必節電百分之二十七點一，會忽略新工作點和效率改變；靜揚程較大時，低速泵可能無法克服外水位而幾乎沒有抽排。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Claiming a guaranteed 27.1-percent saving from a ten-percent speed reduction ignores the changed operating point and efficiency. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將原泵曲線按相似律移動後與實際系統曲線重求交點，核對效率、允許轉速和汽蝕資料。用現地量測驗證結果，尤其檢查靜揚程占比高時是否仍能維持有效出流。","textEn":"Shift the pump curve using affinity laws and solve its intersection with the actual system curve, checking efficiency, allowed speed and cavitation data. Validate with field observations, especially whether useful discharge remains when static head forms a large share of total head.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出含靜揚程與不含靜揚程兩條系統曲線，比較同一降速泵曲線的交點。指出相似點與實際工作點的差別，避免把兩種比例放在同一張效益表。","textEn":"Draw system curves with and without static head and compare intersections with one reduced-speed pump curve. Distinguish homologous points from operating points so their ratios are not mixed in a performance table.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「變速相似與實際工況機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Speed affinity and operating conditions mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","將原泵曲線按相似律移動後與實際系統曲線重求交點，核對效率、允許轉速和汽蝕資料。","防洪泵在所有外河水位下都會維持同一銘牌流量。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Shift the pump curve using affinity laws and solve its intersection with the actual system curve, checking efficiency, allowed speed and cavitation data.","A flood pump maintains the same nameplate flow at every receiving-river level."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將原泵曲線按相似律移動後與實際系統曲線重求交點，核對效率、允許轉速和汽蝕資料。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Shift the pump curve using affinity laws and solve its intersection with the actual system curve, checking efficiency, allowed speed and cavitation data. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b270-v15-20","title":"變速相似與實際工況機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Speed affinity and operating conditions mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「變速相似與實際工況」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Speed affinity and operating conditions” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"直接宣稱降速一成必節電百分之二十七點一，會忽略新工作點和效率改變；靜揚程較大時，低速泵可能無法克服外水位而幾乎沒有抽排。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Claiming a guaranteed 27.1-percent saving from a ten-percent speed reduction ignores the changed operating point and efficiency. With substantial static head, a slower pump may barely overcome receiving water and provide little drainage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例假設同一葉輪與近似相同效率，僅比較相似點；實際抽排量必須再與未同比縮放的系統曲線求交。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Actual discharge requires intersecting the shifted pump curve with the system curve.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「泵降速一成，整站一定同時少抽一成水且省下固定立方比例電力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reducing speed ten percent guarantees ten percent less station flow and fixed cube-law energy savings.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"直接宣稱降速一成必節電百分之二十七點一，會忽略新工作點和效率改變；靜揚程較大時，低速泵可能無法克服外水位而幾乎沒有抽排。","textEn":"Claiming a guaranteed 27.1-percent saving from a ten-percent speed reduction ignores the changed operating point and efficiency. With substantial static head, a slower pump may barely overcome receiving water and provide little drainage.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「變速相似與實際工況機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Speed affinity and operating conditions mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","啟停週期等於調節容積除以泵流量，入流大小完全無關。","直接宣稱降速一成必節電百分之二十七點一，會忽略新工作點和效率改變；靜揚程較大時，低速泵可能無法克服外水位而幾乎沒有抽排。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","The start-stop cycle equals regulating volume divided by pump flow and is independent of inflow.","Claiming a guaranteed 27.1-percent saving from a ten-percent speed reduction ignores the changed operating point and efficiency."],"answer":2,"explanation":"直接宣稱降速一成必節電百分之二十七點一，會忽略新工作點和效率改變；靜揚程較大時，低速泵可能無法克服外水位而幾乎沒有抽排。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Claiming a guaranteed 27.1-percent saving from a ten-percent speed reduction ignores the changed operating point and efficiency. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b270-v15-21","title":"啟停水位差與循環機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Level hysteresis and cycling mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「啟停水位差與循環」如何影響防洪抽水站機組整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Level hysteresis and cycling” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood-pumping-station integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"單台泵的啟停水位差形成可用調節容積，能減少頻繁啟動，但過大水位帶可能占用防洪儲量或降低淹沒裕度。填充與抽降時間分別受入流及淨抽出量控制，不可只用池容積除以泵流量；多台輪替、變入流與感測遲延會讓實際循環更複雜。本例為一台泵、固定池面積與固定入流，且抽排大於入流；算得啟動頻率只是比較，不是設備允許值或現場設定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「啟停水位差與循環」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The start-stop level band creates regulating volume that can reduce repeated starts, but an excessive band may consume flood storage or reduce submergence margin. Filling and drawdown depend on inflow and net pumping respectively, not simply volume divided by pump flow. Multiple-unit rotation, variable inflow and sensing delay further complicate actual cycling. The example uses one pump, constant area and inflow, with pumping exceeding inflow. Its start frequency is a comparison, not an equipment limit or field setting. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Level hysteresis and cycling” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設A=100 m²、啟停差Δh=0.60 m、Qi=0.50、Qp=2.0 m³/s；循環T=60/0.50+60/(2−0.50)=160 s，即22.5次/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume A=100 m², level band Δh=0.60 m, Qi=0.50 and Qp=2.0 m³/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「啟停週期等於調節容積除以泵流量，入流大小完全無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The start-stop cycle equals regulating volume divided by pump flow and is independent of inflow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「啟停水位差與循環」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Level hysteresis and cycling”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-21-k1","title":"啟停水位差與循環機理與驗證","titleEn":"Level hysteresis and cycling mechanism and verification","text":"單台泵的啟停水位差形成可用調節容積，能減少頻繁啟動，但過大水位帶可能占用防洪儲量或降低淹沒裕度。填充與抽降時間分別受入流及淨抽出量控制，不可只用池容積除以泵流量；多台輪替、變入流與感測遲延會讓實際循環更複雜。","textEn":"The start-stop level band creates regulating volume that can reduce repeated starts, but an excessive band may consume flood storage or reduce submergence margin. Filling and drawdown depend on inflow and net pumping respectively, not simply volume divided by pump flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：啟停週期等於調節容積除以泵流量，入流大小完全無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The start-stop cycle equals regulating volume divided by pump flow and is independent of inflow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「啟停水位差與循環機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Level hysteresis and cycling mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["單台泵的啟停水位差形成可用調節容積，能減少頻繁啟動，但過大水位帶可能占用防洪儲量或降低淹沒裕度。","啟停週期等於調節容積除以泵流量，入流大小完全無關。","池水位只要夠高，任何機組組合都不可能出現渦流或汽蝕。"],"optionsEn":["The start-stop level band creates regulating volume that can reduce repeated starts, but an excessive band may consume flood storage or reduce submergence margin.","The start-stop cycle equals regulating volume divided by pump flow and is independent of inflow.","Sufficient sump level makes vortices or cavitation impossible for every pump combination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"單台泵的啟停水位差形成可用調節容積，能減少頻繁啟動，但過大水位帶可能占用防洪儲量或降低淹沒裕度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The start-stop level band creates regulating volume that can reduce repeated starts, but an excessive band may consume flood storage or reduce submergence margin. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b270-v15-22","title":"啟停水位差與循環機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Level hysteresis and cycling mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「啟停水位差與循環」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Level hysteresis and cycling” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設A=100 m²、啟停差Δh=0.60 m、Qi=0.50、Qp=2.0 m³/s；循環T=60/0.50+60/(2−0.50)=160 s，即22.5次/h。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume A=100 m², level band Δh=0.60 m, Qi=0.50 and Qp=2.0 m³/s. Cycle T=60/0.50+60/(2−0.50)=160 s, or 22.5 starts/h. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用事件紀錄核對啟動、停止、入流及池水位，檢查每次實際抽降時間與計算差異。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check starts, stops, inflow and sump level against event logs, comparing actual and calculated drawdown time.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設A=100 m²、啟停差Δh=0.60 m、Qi=0.50、Qp=2.0 m³/s；循環T=60/0.50+60/(2−0.50)=160 s，即22.5次/h。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume A=100 m², level band Δh=0.60 m, Qi=0.50 and Qp=2.0 m³/s. Cycle T=60/0.50+60/(2−0.50)=160 s, or 22.5 starts/h.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「啟停水位差與循環機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Level hysteresis and cycling mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["閘門兩側淨水壓只需把水位差平方，與各側實際水深無關。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設A=100 m²、啟停差Δh=0.60 m、Qi=0.50、Qp=2.0 m³/s。","泵的標示總流量大於平均雨水流量，就能保證任何洪水不積水。"],"optionsEn":["Net gate pressure depends only on squared level difference, not the individual water depths.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume A=100 m², level band Δh=0.60 m, Qi=0.50 and Qp=2.0 m³/s.","Total labeled pump flow above mean runoff guarantees no flooding in any event."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設A=100 m²、啟停差Δh=0.60 m、Qi=0.50、Qp=2.0 m³/s；循環T=60/0.50+60/(2−0.50)=160 s，即22.5次/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume A=100 m², level band Δh=0.60 m, Qi=0.50 and Qp=2.0 m³/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b270-v15-23","title":"啟停水位差與循環機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Level hysteresis and cycling mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「啟停水位差與循環」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Level hysteresis and cycling” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用事件紀錄核對啟動、停止、入流及池水位，檢查每次實際抽降時間與計算差異。將設備可允許啟動次數、最小運轉時間及池體淹沒條件一起核對，避免只靠一條水位帶決策。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check starts, stops, inflow and sump level against event logs, comparing actual and calculated drawdown time. Review permitted starts, minimum run time and submergence together rather than deciding from the level band alone, and record any delayed switching behavior. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分開計算填充與抽降時間，再把入流改成原值兩倍觀察循環變化。將水位帶、可用防洪儲量和最低淹沒畫在同一剖面，說明三者的限制關係。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate fill and drawdown times separately, then double inflow and examine the cycle change. Show the level band, available flood storage and minimum submergence on one section, explaining how their constraints interact.","failure":"注意干擾：漏掉持續入流會低估抽降時間，水位噪訊可能使接點反覆切換；為減少啟動而任意擴大水位帶，則可能犧牲暴雨時原本可用的儲水空間。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring continuing inflow understates drawdown time, and level noise can chatter the switching signal. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用事件紀錄核對啟動、停止、入流及池水位，檢查每次實際抽降時間與計算差異。將設備可允許啟動次數、最小運轉時間及池體淹沒條件一起核對，避免只靠一條水位帶決策。","textEn":"Check starts, stops, inflow and sump level against event logs, comparing actual and calculated drawdown time. Review permitted starts, minimum run time and submergence together rather than deciding from the level band alone, and record any delayed switching behavior.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分開計算填充與抽降時間，再把入流改成原值兩倍觀察循環變化。將水位帶、可用防洪儲量和最低淹沒畫在同一剖面，說明三者的限制關係。","textEn":"Calculate fill and drawdown times separately, then double inflow and examine the cycle change. Show the level band, available flood storage and minimum submergence on one section, explaining how their constraints interact.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「啟停水位差與循環機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Level hysteresis and cycling mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","兩台並聯泵的實際排水量必定是單台接原管路時的兩倍。","用事件紀錄核對啟動、停止、入流及池水位，檢查每次實際抽降時間與計算差異。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Two parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow through the original system.","Check starts, stops, inflow and sump level against event logs, comparing actual and calculated drawdown time."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用事件紀錄核對啟動、停止、入流及池水位，檢查每次實際抽降時間與計算差異。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check starts, stops, inflow and sump level against event logs, comparing actual and calculated drawdown time. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b270-v15-24","title":"啟停水位差與循環機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Level hysteresis and cycling mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「啟停水位差與循環」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Level hysteresis and cycling” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏掉持續入流會低估抽降時間，水位噪訊可能使接點反覆切換；為減少啟動而任意擴大水位帶，則可能犧牲暴雨時原本可用的儲水空間。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring continuing inflow understates drawdown time, and level noise can chatter the switching signal. Enlarging the band solely to reduce starts may consume storage that would otherwise be available during heavy rainfall. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例為一台泵、固定池面積與固定入流，且抽排大於入流；算得啟動頻率只是比較，不是設備允許值或現場設定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Its start frequency is a comparison, not an equipment limit or field setting.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「啟停週期等於調節容積除以泵流量，入流大小完全無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The start-stop cycle equals regulating volume divided by pump flow and is independent of inflow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏掉持續入流會低估抽降時間，水位噪訊可能使接點反覆切換；為減少啟動而任意擴大水位帶，則可能犧牲暴雨時原本可用的儲水空間。","textEn":"Ignoring continuing inflow understates drawdown time, and level noise can chatter the switching signal. Enlarging the band solely to reduce starts may consume storage that would otherwise be available during heavy rainfall.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「啟停水位差與循環機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Level hysteresis and cycling mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["漏掉持續入流會低估抽降時間，水位噪訊可能使接點反覆切換；為減少啟動而任意擴大水位帶，則可能犧牲暴雨時原本可用的儲水空間。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","池水位只要夠高，任何機組組合都不可能出現渦流或汽蝕。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring continuing inflow understates drawdown time, and level noise can chatter the switching signal.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Sufficient sump level makes vortices or cavitation impossible for every pump combination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"漏掉持續入流會低估抽降時間，水位噪訊可能使接點反覆切換；為減少啟動而任意擴大水位帶，則可能犧牲暴雨時原本可用的儲水空間。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring continuing inflow understates drawdown time, and level noise can chatter the switching signal. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b270-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「吸入工況與流場品質機理與驗證」與「實功率視在功率與備援機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Suction conditions and flow quality mechanism and verification\" and \"Real apparent and backup power mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b270-v15-25","title":"吸入工況與流場品質機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Suction conditions and flow quality mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「吸入工況與流場品質」如何影響防洪抽水站機組整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Suction conditions and flow quality” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood-pumping-station integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"抽水站入口須同時滿足壓力裕度與均勻流場，池水位足夠也可能因不對稱入流而產生渦流與捲氣。淨正吸入水頭取決於大氣壓、吸入水位、蒸氣壓及損失，設備需求又隨流量和轉速變動；整合多台機組時應檢查不同組合造成的流場，不能只驗證全開狀態。下式各項均以同一淡水密度的水頭表示，水面高於泵參考取正；正差值不保證沒有渦流、捲氣或其他吸入問題。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「吸入工況與流場品質」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pump inlets need both pressure margin and acceptable flow quality; adequate depth can still coexist with vortices from asymmetric inflow. Available NPSH depends on atmospheric pressure, sump level, vapor pressure and losses, while required NPSH varies with flow and speed. Integrating several units requires checking different combinations rather than testing only all-units-on operation. All terms are freshwater heads on one density basis, with surface above the pump reference positive. A positive margin does not guarantee absence of vortices, air entrainment or other inlet problems. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Suction conditions and flow quality” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設大氣水頭10.3 m、靜淹水1.5 m、蒸氣壓水頭0.25 m、吸入損失1.2 m，NPSHa=10.35 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume atmospheric head 10.3 m, static submergence 1.5 m, vapor head 0.25 m and suction loss 1.2 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「池水位只要夠高，任何機組組合都不可能出現渦流或汽蝕。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Sufficient sump level makes vortices or cavitation impossible for every pump combination.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「吸入工況與流場品質」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Suction conditions and flow quality”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-25-k1","title":"吸入工況與流場品質機理與驗證","titleEn":"Suction conditions and flow quality mechanism and verification","text":"抽水站入口須同時滿足壓力裕度與均勻流場，池水位足夠也可能因不對稱入流而產生渦流與捲氣。淨正吸入水頭取決於大氣壓、吸入水位、蒸氣壓及損失，設備需求又隨流量和轉速變動；整合多台機組時應檢查不同組合造成的流場，不能只驗證全開狀態。","textEn":"Pump inlets need both pressure margin and acceptable flow quality; adequate depth can still coexist with vortices from asymmetric inflow. Available NPSH depends on atmospheric pressure, sump level, vapor pressure and losses, while required NPSH varies with flow and speed.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：池水位只要夠高，任何機組組合都不可能出現渦流或汽蝕。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Sufficient sump level makes vortices or cavitation impossible for every pump combination. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「吸入工況與流場品質機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Suction conditions and flow quality mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["池水位只要夠高，任何機組組合都不可能出現渦流或汽蝕。","抽水站入口須同時滿足壓力裕度與均勻流場，池水位足夠也可能因不對稱入流而產生渦流與捲氣。","備援電源連續千瓦足夠，就代表所有泵可以同時順利啟動。"],"optionsEn":["Sufficient sump level makes vortices or cavitation impossible for every pump combination.","Pump inlets need both pressure margin and acceptable flow quality; adequate depth can still coexist with vortices from asymmetric inflow.","Adequate continuous backup kilowatts guarantee that all pumps can start simultaneously."],"answer":1,"explanation":"抽水站入口須同時滿足壓力裕度與均勻流場，池水位足夠也可能因不對稱入流而產生渦流與捲氣。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pump inlets need both pressure margin and acceptable flow quality; adequate depth can still coexist with vortices from asymmetric inflow. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b270-v15-26","title":"吸入工況與流場品質機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Suction conditions and flow quality mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「吸入工況與流場品質」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Suction conditions and flow quality” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設大氣水頭10.3 m、靜淹水1.5 m、蒸氣壓水頭0.25 m、吸入損失1.2 m，NPSHa=10.35 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume atmospheric head 10.3 m, static submergence 1.5 m, vapor head 0.25 m and suction loss 1.2 m. Available NPSH is 10.35 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以低池水位、高水溫及代表機組組合檢查吸入壓力，核對泵參考高程與需求曲線。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check suction pressure at low sump level, high water temperature and representative unit combinations, verifying pump datum and required curves.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設大氣水頭10.3 m、靜淹水1.5 m、蒸氣壓水頭0.25 m、吸入損失1.2 m，NPSHa=10.35 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume atmospheric head 10.3 m, static submergence 1.5 m, vapor head 0.25 m and suction loss 1.2 m. Available NPSH is 10.35 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「吸入工況與流場品質機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Suction conditions and flow quality mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["設有一台備用泵就能保證抽水站任何單一故障都不減排水量。","防洪泵在所有外河水位下都會維持同一銘牌流量。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設大氣水頭10.3 m、靜淹水1.5 m、蒸氣壓水頭0.25 m、吸入損失1.2 m，NPSHa=10.35 m。"],"optionsEn":["One spare pump guarantees unchanged station discharge under every single failure.","A flood pump maintains the same nameplate flow at every receiving-river level.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume atmospheric head 10.3 m, static submergence 1.5 m, vapor head 0.25 m and suction loss 1.2 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設大氣水頭10.3 m、靜淹水1.5 m、蒸氣壓水頭0.25 m、吸入損失1.2 m，NPSHa=10.35 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume atmospheric head 10.3 m, static submergence 1.5 m, vapor head 0.25 m and suction loss 1.2 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b270-v15-27","title":"吸入工況與流場品質機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Suction conditions and flow quality mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「吸入工況與流場品質」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Suction conditions and flow quality” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以低池水位、高水溫及代表機組組合檢查吸入壓力，核對泵參考高程與需求曲線。另用速度分布、渦流觀察或適用模型驗證入口品質，將汽蝕壓力與捲氣問題分開判讀。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check suction pressure at low sump level, high water temperature and representative unit combinations, verifying pump datum and required curves. Independently examine velocity distribution and vortices through observations or suitable models, keeping cavitation-pressure and air-entrainment assessments distinct in the evidence. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：列出全開、單台與相鄰一台停用三種流場檢查，分別指出壓力與速度證據。計算一個增加入口損失的情境，說明同樣水位也會改變吸入裕度。","observationEn":"Site practice: List all-on, single-unit and adjacent-unit-out checks, distinguishing pressure from velocity evidence. Calculate a case with greater entrance loss and explain why identical sump level can still produce a different suction margin.","failure":"注意干擾：只以池水深推定無汽蝕會忽略入口損失與溫度，某些機組停用後也可能產生偏流；入口整流改善一種組合時，未必同時改善其他組合。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Inferring cavitation freedom from depth alone ignores entrance losses and temperature. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以低池水位、高水溫及代表機組組合檢查吸入壓力，核對泵參考高程與需求曲線。另用速度分布、渦流觀察或適用模型驗證入口品質，將汽蝕壓力與捲氣問題分開判讀。","textEn":"Check suction pressure at low sump level, high water temperature and representative unit combinations, verifying pump datum and required curves. Independently examine velocity distribution and vortices through observations or suitable models, keeping cavitation-pressure and air-entrainment assessments distinct in the evidence.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"列出全開、單台與相鄰一台停用三種流場檢查，分別指出壓力與速度證據。計算一個增加入口損失的情境，說明同樣水位也會改變吸入裕度。","textEn":"List all-on, single-unit and adjacent-unit-out checks, distinguishing pressure from velocity evidence. Calculate a case with greater entrance loss and explain why identical sump level can still produce a different suction margin.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「吸入工況與流場品質機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Suction conditions and flow quality mechanism and verification\"?","options":["以低池水位、高水溫及代表機組組合檢查吸入壓力，核對泵參考高程與需求曲線。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","水力功率就是抽水站電表功率，不必計入馬達和泵的損失。"],"optionsEn":["Check suction pressure at low sump level, high water temperature and representative unit combinations, verifying pump datum and required curves.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Hydraulic power equals metered station power without pump or motor losses."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以低池水位、高水溫及代表機組組合檢查吸入壓力，核對泵參考高程與需求曲線。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check suction pressure at low sump level, high water temperature and representative unit combinations, verifying pump datum and required curves. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b270-v15-28","title":"吸入工況與流場品質機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Suction conditions and flow quality mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「吸入工況與流場品質」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Suction conditions and flow quality” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只以池水深推定無汽蝕會忽略入口損失與溫度，某些機組停用後也可能產生偏流；入口整流改善一種組合時，未必同時改善其他組合。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Inferring cavitation freedom from depth alone ignores entrance losses and temperature. Idle units can change approach symmetry, and an intake modification improving one combination may not improve all other operating combinations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：下式各項均以同一淡水密度的水頭表示，水面高於泵參考取正；正差值不保證沒有渦流、捲氣或其他吸入問題。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A positive margin does not guarantee absence of vortices, air entrainment or other inlet problems.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「池水位只要夠高，任何機組組合都不可能出現渦流或汽蝕。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Sufficient sump level makes vortices or cavitation impossible for every pump combination.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只以池水深推定無汽蝕會忽略入口損失與溫度，某些機組停用後也可能產生偏流；入口整流改善一種組合時，未必同時改善其他組合。","textEn":"Inferring cavitation freedom from depth alone ignores entrance losses and temperature. Idle units can change approach symmetry, and an intake modification improving one combination may not improve all other operating combinations.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「吸入工況與流場品質機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Suction conditions and flow quality mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只以池水深推定無汽蝕會忽略入口損失與溫度，某些機組停用後也可能產生偏流；入口整流改善一種組合時，未必同時改善其他組合。","備援電源連續千瓦足夠，就代表所有泵可以同時順利啟動。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Inferring cavitation freedom from depth alone ignores entrance losses and temperature.","Adequate continuous backup kilowatts guarantee that all pumps can start simultaneously."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只以池水深推定無汽蝕會忽略入口損失與溫度，某些機組停用後也可能產生偏流；入口整流改善一種組合時，未必同時改善其他組合。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Inferring cavitation freedom from depth alone ignores entrance losses and temperature. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b270-v15-29","title":"實功率視在功率與備援機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Real apparent and backup power mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「實功率視在功率與備援」如何影響防洪抽水站機組整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Real apparent and backup power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood-pumping-station integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"備援電源須供應泵、控制和輔機，實功率與視在功率是不同容量約束，功率因數不能被效率取代。機組啟動時的電流與電壓暫降可能決定可行組合，即使連續千瓦需求足夠也不代表能順利啟動；燃料、冷卻及淹水隔離另影響可維持的事件時間。本例只換算平衡穩態負載的視在功率，不提供發電機選型容量；啟動、諧波及備援輔機需求尚未加入。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「實功率視在功率與備援」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Backup supply serves pumps, controls and auxiliaries. Real and apparent power impose different constraints, and power factor is not efficiency. Starting current and voltage dip can determine feasible combinations even when continuous kilowatts appear adequate. Fuel, cooling and flood isolation separately influence how long the station can continue through an event. The example converts a balanced steady load to apparent power only, not generator selection capacity. Starting, harmonics and backup auxiliary demand remain excluded. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Real apparent and backup power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設穩態實功率P=500 kW、功率因數pf=0.80，視在功率S=P/pf=625 kVA。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume steady real power P=500 kW and power factor pf=0.80.","failure":"常見誤解：「備援電源連續千瓦足夠，就代表所有泵可以同時順利啟動。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate continuous backup kilowatts guarantee that all pumps can start simultaneously.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「實功率視在功率與備援」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Real apparent and backup power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-29-k1","title":"實功率視在功率與備援機理與驗證","titleEn":"Real apparent and backup power mechanism and verification","text":"備援電源須供應泵、控制和輔機，實功率與視在功率是不同容量約束，功率因數不能被效率取代。機組啟動時的電流與電壓暫降可能決定可行組合，即使連續千瓦需求足夠也不代表能順利啟動；燃料、冷卻及淹水隔離另影響可維持的事件時間。","textEn":"Backup supply serves pumps, controls and auxiliaries. Real and apparent power impose different constraints, and power factor is not efficiency.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：備援電源連續千瓦足夠，就代表所有泵可以同時順利啟動。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate continuous backup kilowatts guarantee that all pumps can start simultaneously. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「實功率視在功率與備援機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Real apparent and backup power mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["備援電源連續千瓦足夠，就代表所有泵可以同時順利啟動。","閘門兩側淨水壓只需把水位差平方，與各側實際水深無關。","備援電源須供應泵、控制和輔機，實功率與視在功率是不同容量約束，功率因數不能被效率取代。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate continuous backup kilowatts guarantee that all pumps can start simultaneously.","Net gate pressure depends only on squared level difference, not the individual water depths.","Backup supply serves pumps, controls and auxiliaries."],"answer":2,"explanation":"備援電源須供應泵、控制和輔機，實功率與視在功率是不同容量約束，功率因數不能被效率取代。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Backup supply serves pumps, controls and auxiliaries. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b270-v15-30","title":"實功率視在功率與備援機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Real apparent and backup power mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「實功率視在功率與備援」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Real apparent and backup power” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設穩態實功率P=500 kW、功率因數pf=0.80，視在功率S=P/pf=625 kVA。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume steady real power P=500 kW and power factor pf=0.80. Apparent power S=P/pf=625 kVA. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立機組與輔機負載表，分開持續千瓦、千伏安及啟動事件，核對供電邊界和保護配合。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build a pump-and-auxiliary load list separating continuous kilowatts, kilovolt-amperes and starts, checking supply boundaries and protection coordination.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設穩態實功率P=500 kW、功率因數pf=0.80，視在功率S=P/pf=625 kVA。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume steady real power P=500 kW and power factor pf=0.80. Apparent power S=P/pf=625 kVA.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「實功率視在功率與備援機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Real apparent and backup power mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設穩態實功率P=500 kW、功率因數pf=0.80，視在功率S=P/pf=625 kVA。","泵的標示總流量大於平均雨水流量，就能保證任何洪水不積水。","兩台並聯泵的實際排水量必定是單台接原管路時的兩倍。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume steady real power P=500 kW and power factor pf=0.80.","Total labeled pump flow above mean runoff guarantees no flooding in any event.","Two parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow through the original system."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設穩態實功率P=500 kW、功率因數pf=0.80，視在功率S=P/pf=625 kVA。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume steady real power P=500 kW and power factor pf=0.80. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b270-v15-31","title":"實功率視在功率與備援機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Real apparent and backup power mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「實功率視在功率與備援」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Real apparent and backup power” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立機組與輔機負載表，分開持續千瓦、千伏安及啟動事件，核對供電邊界和保護配合。以受控測試記錄電壓、頻率和恢復時間，另檢查燃料及冷卻不會受同一洪水中斷。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build a pump-and-auxiliary load list separating continuous kilowatts, kilovolt-amperes and starts, checking supply boundaries and protection coordination. Record voltage, frequency and recovery in controlled tests, and independently verify that fuel and cooling are not interrupted by the same flood exposure. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把三個假設負載分成持續與啟動兩張表，再計算同一實功率在不同功率因數下的視在功率。指出仍需電源動態資料才能判斷的啟動問題。","observationEn":"Site practice: Separate three hypothetical loads into continuous and starting tables, then compare apparent power at different power factors for the same real load. Identify starting questions that still require dynamic supply information rather than steady arithmetic.","failure":"注意干擾：把千瓦直接當千伏安會低估電氣容量，忽略啟動可能造成連鎖跳脫；備援發電機若與主配電共處易淹位置，也可能在需要時一起失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Equating kilowatts with kilovolt-amperes understates electrical capacity, and omitted starting demand can trigger cascading trips. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立機組與輔機負載表，分開持續千瓦、千伏安及啟動事件，核對供電邊界和保護配合。以受控測試記錄電壓、頻率和恢復時間，另檢查燃料及冷卻不會受同一洪水中斷。","textEn":"Build a pump-and-auxiliary load list separating continuous kilowatts, kilovolt-amperes and starts, checking supply boundaries and protection coordination. Record voltage, frequency and recovery in controlled tests, and independently verify that fuel and cooling are not interrupted by the same flood exposure.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把三個假設負載分成持續與啟動兩張表，再計算同一實功率在不同功率因數下的視在功率。指出仍需電源動態資料才能判斷的啟動問題。","textEn":"Separate three hypothetical loads into continuous and starting tables, then compare apparent power at different power factors for the same real load. Identify starting questions that still require dynamic supply information rather than steady arithmetic.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「實功率視在功率與備援機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Real apparent and backup power mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","建立機組與輔機負載表，分開持續千瓦、千伏安及啟動事件，核對供電邊界和保護配合。","泵降速一成，整站一定同時少抽一成水且省下固定立方比例電力。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Build a pump-and-auxiliary load list separating continuous kilowatts, kilovolt-amperes and starts, checking supply boundaries and protection coordination.","Reducing speed ten percent guarantees ten percent less station flow and fixed cube-law energy savings."],"answer":1,"explanation":"建立機組與輔機負載表，分開持續千瓦、千伏安及啟動事件，核對供電邊界和保護配合。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build a pump-and-auxiliary load list separating continuous kilowatts, kilovolt-amperes and starts, checking supply boundaries and protection coordination. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b270-v15-32","title":"實功率視在功率與備援機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Real apparent and backup power mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「實功率視在功率與備援」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Real apparent and backup power” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把千瓦直接當千伏安會低估電氣容量，忽略啟動可能造成連鎖跳脫；備援發電機若與主配電共處易淹位置，也可能在需要時一起失效。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Equating kilowatts with kilovolt-amperes understates electrical capacity, and omitted starting demand can trigger cascading trips. A backup generator sharing a flood-prone location with main distribution can fail at the same time it is needed. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例只換算平衡穩態負載的視在功率，不提供發電機選型容量；啟動、諧波及備援輔機需求尚未加入。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Starting, harmonics and backup auxiliary demand remain excluded.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「備援電源連續千瓦足夠，就代表所有泵可以同時順利啟動。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate continuous backup kilowatts guarantee that all pumps can start simultaneously.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把千瓦直接當千伏安會低估電氣容量，忽略啟動可能造成連鎖跳脫；備援發電機若與主配電共處易淹位置，也可能在需要時一起失效。","textEn":"Equating kilowatts with kilovolt-amperes understates electrical capacity, and omitted starting demand can trigger cascading trips. A backup generator sharing a flood-prone location with main distribution can fail at the same time it is needed.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「實功率視在功率與備援機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Real apparent and backup power mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","閘門兩側淨水壓只需把水位差平方，與各側實際水深無關。","把千瓦直接當千伏安會低估電氣容量，忽略啟動可能造成連鎖跳脫；備援發電機若與主配電共處易淹位置，也可能在需要時一起失效。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Net gate pressure depends only on squared level difference, not the individual water depths.","Equating kilowatts with kilovolt-amperes understates electrical capacity, and omitted starting demand can trigger cascading trips."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把千瓦直接當千伏安會低估電氣容量，忽略啟動可能造成連鎖跳脫；備援發電機若與主配電共處易淹位置，也可能在需要時一起失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Equating kilowatts with kilovolt-amperes understates electrical capacity, and omitted starting demand can trigger cascading trips. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b270-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「外水倒灌與閘門界面機理與驗證」與「單機停用與整站能力機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Backflow and gate interfaces mechanism and verification\" and \"Unit outage and station capability mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b270-v15-33","title":"外水倒灌與閘門界面機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Backflow and gate interfaces mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「外水倒灌與閘門界面」如何影響防洪抽水站機組整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Backflow and gate interfaces” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood-pumping-station integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"外水高於內水時，重力出口可能成為倒灌通道，閘門和止回構件的作用必須與抽排路徑協調。兩側水壓的差額決定部分靜水載荷，但實際關閉還涉及摩擦、浮物、動水與機構力；把閘門關閉訊號當成水密保證，會掩蓋漏水或位置感測錯誤。本例為同底高程直立矩形門兩側靜水合力差，不含動水與摩擦，也不直接給出致動器推力或關閉時機。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「外水倒灌與閘門界面」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When receiving water exceeds interior stage, a gravity outlet can become a backflow path, requiring coordination of gates and check devices with pumping routes. Differential hydrostatic pressure supplies part of the static load, but closure also involves friction, debris, moving water and actuator forces. A closed indication is not proof of watertightness or correct position sensing. The example is the difference in hydrostatic resultants on a vertical rectangular gate with a common bottom datum. It excludes flow and friction and does not specify actuator force or closure timing. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Backflow and gate interfaces” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設水重度γ=9.81 kN/m³、門寬b=2 m、外水深ho=3 m、內水深hi=1 m，淨力F=γb(ho²−hi²)/2=78.48 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume γ=9.81 kN/m³, gate width b=2 m, outside depth ho=3 m and inside hi=1 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「閘門兩側淨水壓只需把水位差平方，與各側實際水深無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Net gate pressure depends only on squared level difference, not the individual water depths.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「外水倒灌與閘門界面」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Backflow and gate interfaces”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-33-k1","title":"外水倒灌與閘門界面機理與驗證","titleEn":"Backflow and gate interfaces mechanism and verification","text":"外水高於內水時，重力出口可能成為倒灌通道，閘門和止回構件的作用必須與抽排路徑協調。兩側水壓的差額決定部分靜水載荷，但實際關閉還涉及摩擦、浮物、動水與機構力；把閘門關閉訊號當成水密保證，會掩蓋漏水或位置感測錯誤。","textEn":"When receiving water exceeds interior stage, a gravity outlet can become a backflow path, requiring coordination of gates and check devices with pumping routes. Differential hydrostatic pressure supplies part of the static load, but closure also involves friction, debris, moving water and actuator forces.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：閘門兩側淨水壓只需把水位差平方，與各側實際水深無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Net gate pressure depends only on squared level difference, not the individual water depths. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「外水倒灌與閘門界面機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Backflow and gate interfaces mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["外水高於內水時，重力出口可能成為倒灌通道，閘門和止回構件的作用必須與抽排路徑協調。","閘門兩側淨水壓只需把水位差平方，與各側實際水深無關。","設有一台備用泵就能保證抽水站任何單一故障都不減排水量。"],"optionsEn":["When receiving water exceeds interior stage, a gravity outlet can become a backflow path, requiring coordination of gates and check devices with pumping routes.","Net gate pressure depends only on squared level difference, not the individual water depths.","One spare pump guarantees unchanged station discharge under every single failure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"外水高於內水時，重力出口可能成為倒灌通道，閘門和止回構件的作用必須與抽排路徑協調。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When receiving water exceeds interior stage, a gravity outlet can become a backflow path, requiring coordination of gates and check devices with pumping routes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b270-v15-34","title":"外水倒灌與閘門界面機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Backflow and gate interfaces mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「外水倒灌與閘門界面」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Backflow and gate interfaces” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設水重度γ=9.81 kN/m³、門寬b=2 m、外水深ho=3 m、內水深hi=1 m，淨力F=γb(ho²−hi²)/2=78.48 kN。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume γ=9.81 kN/m³, gate width b=2 m, outside depth ho=3 m and inside hi=1 m. Net force F=γb(ho²−hi²)/2=78.48 kN. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對門底和兩側水位基準，將位置回饋、實際行程及漏流量交叉檢查。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check gate-bottom and water-level datums, comparing position feedback with physical travel and leakage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設水重度γ=9.81 kN/m³、門寬b=2 m、外水深ho=3 m、內水深hi=1 m，淨力F=γb(ho²−hi²)/2=78.48 kN。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume γ=9.81 kN/m³, gate width b=2 m, outside depth ho=3 m and inside hi=1 m. Net force F=γb(ho²−hi²)/2=78.48 kN.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「外水倒灌與閘門界面機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Backflow and gate interfaces mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["防洪泵在所有外河水位下都會維持同一銘牌流量。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設水重度γ=9.81 kN/m³、門寬b=2 m、外水深ho=3 m、內水深hi=1 m，淨力F=γb(ho²−hi²)/2=78.48 kN。","水力功率就是抽水站電表功率，不必計入馬達和泵的損失。"],"optionsEn":["A flood pump maintains the same nameplate flow at every receiving-river level.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume γ=9.81 kN/m³, gate width b=2 m, outside depth ho=3 m and inside hi=1 m.","Hydraulic power equals metered station power without pump or motor losses."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設水重度γ=9.81 kN/m³、門寬b=2 m、外水深ho=3 m、內水深hi=1 m，淨力F=γb(ho²−hi²)/2=78.48 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume γ=9.81 kN/m³, gate width b=2 m, outside depth ho=3 m and inside hi=1 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b270-v15-35","title":"外水倒灌與閘門界面機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Backflow and gate interfaces mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「外水倒灌與閘門界面」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Backflow and gate interfaces” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對門底和兩側水位基準，將位置回饋、實際行程及漏流量交叉檢查。測試狀態介面時保留閘門與泵的時間紀錄，並依核准操作文件確認不會形成封閉抽排或倒灌路徑。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check gate-bottom and water-level datums, comparing position feedback with physical travel and leakage. Retain gate and pump timestamps during interface tests, and use approved operating documentation to verify that transitions do not create a blocked discharge or backflow path. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出兩側三角壓力圖並相減，和只用水位差平方的錯誤結果比較。另列位置訊號與實際漏水兩種驗證，說明它們為何不能互相代替。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw and subtract the two triangular pressure diagrams, comparing the result with the incorrect squared-level-difference method. Separately list position-signal and leakage checks, explaining why neither substitutes for the other.","failure":"注意干擾：只算外側三角水壓會漏掉內側抵銷，誤用水位差平方則不能代替兩水深平方差；關閉回饋失真或漂流物夾住時，抽水站仍可能持續承受倒灌。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using only outside pressure omits interior opposition, while squaring the level difference cannot replace the difference of squared depths. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對門底和兩側水位基準，將位置回饋、實際行程及漏流量交叉檢查。測試狀態介面時保留閘門與泵的時間紀錄，並依核准操作文件確認不會形成封閉抽排或倒灌路徑。","textEn":"Check gate-bottom and water-level datums, comparing position feedback with physical travel and leakage. Retain gate and pump timestamps during interface tests, and use approved operating documentation to verify that transitions do not create a blocked discharge or backflow path.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出兩側三角壓力圖並相減，和只用水位差平方的錯誤結果比較。另列位置訊號與實際漏水兩種驗證，說明它們為何不能互相代替。","textEn":"Draw and subtract the two triangular pressure diagrams, comparing the result with the incorrect squared-level-difference method. Separately list position-signal and leakage checks, explaining why neither substitutes for the other.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「外水倒灌與閘門界面機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Backflow and gate interfaces mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","啟停週期等於調節容積除以泵流量，入流大小完全無關。","核對門底和兩側水位基準，將位置回饋、實際行程及漏流量交叉檢查。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The start-stop cycle equals regulating volume divided by pump flow and is independent of inflow.","Check gate-bottom and water-level datums, comparing position feedback with physical travel and leakage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對門底和兩側水位基準，將位置回饋、實際行程及漏流量交叉檢查。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check gate-bottom and water-level datums, comparing position feedback with physical travel and leakage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b270-v15-36","title":"外水倒灌與閘門界面機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Backflow and gate interfaces mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「外水倒灌與閘門界面」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Backflow and gate interfaces” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只算外側三角水壓會漏掉內側抵銷，誤用水位差平方則不能代替兩水深平方差；關閉回饋失真或漂流物夾住時，抽水站仍可能持續承受倒灌。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using only outside pressure omits interior opposition, while squaring the level difference cannot replace the difference of squared depths. False closed feedback or trapped debris can leave a backflow path despite the station’s indicated state. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例為同底高程直立矩形門兩側靜水合力差，不含動水與摩擦，也不直接給出致動器推力或關閉時機。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It excludes flow and friction and does not specify actuator force or closure timing.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「閘門兩側淨水壓只需把水位差平方，與各側實際水深無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Net gate pressure depends only on squared level difference, not the individual water depths.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只算外側三角水壓會漏掉內側抵銷，誤用水位差平方則不能代替兩水深平方差；關閉回饋失真或漂流物夾住時，抽水站仍可能持續承受倒灌。","textEn":"Using only outside pressure omits interior opposition, while squaring the level difference cannot replace the difference of squared depths. False closed feedback or trapped debris can leave a backflow path despite the station’s indicated state.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「外水倒灌與閘門界面機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Backflow and gate interfaces mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只算外側三角水壓會漏掉內側抵銷，誤用水位差平方則不能代替兩水深平方差；關閉回饋失真或漂流物夾住時，抽水站仍可能持續承受倒灌。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","設有一台備用泵就能保證抽水站任何單一故障都不減排水量。"],"optionsEn":["Using only outside pressure omits interior opposition, while squaring the level difference cannot replace the difference of squared depths.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","One spare pump guarantees unchanged station discharge under every single failure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只算外側三角水壓會漏掉內側抵銷，誤用水位差平方則不能代替兩水深平方差；關閉回饋失真或漂流物夾住時，抽水站仍可能持續承受倒灌。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using only outside pressure omits interior opposition, while squaring the level difference cannot replace the difference of squared depths. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b270-v15-37","title":"單機停用與整站能力機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Unit outage and station capability mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「單機停用與整站能力」如何影響防洪抽水站機組整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Unit outage and station capability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood-pumping-station integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"備援台數只有在實際揚程、電源和管路條件下才有意義，保留一台泵不代表任何故障都能維持完整排水。多台可能共用變壓器、閘門、攔污設備或控制，因此機械可用性不等於整站可用性；故障情境應把剩餘排量與儲水時間一起評估，並辨認共因失效。本例每台排量已指定為相同實際揚程下的可用量，假設停機不改變其他台工作點；真實並聯工況須重新求解。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「單機停用與整站能力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Spare-unit counts matter only at actual head, electrical and pipe conditions. One spare does not preserve full drainage for every fault. Units can share a transformer, gate, screen or controller, so mechanical availability is not station availability. Failure scenarios should compare retained flow with storage time and identify common causes across the complete system. Each unit’s stated flow is available at the same actual head, and an outage is assumed not to shift other operating points. Real parallel-system performance must be solved again. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Unit outage and station capability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設三台各可排2.0 m³/s、需求5.0 m³/s；一台停用後可用4.0 m³/s，瞬時缺口為1.0 m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume three units each available at 2.0 m³/s and demand 5.0 m³/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「設有一台備用泵就能保證抽水站任何單一故障都不減排水量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One spare pump guarantees unchanged station discharge under every single failure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「單機停用與整站能力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Unit outage and station capability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-37-k1","title":"單機停用與整站能力機理與驗證","titleEn":"Unit outage and station capability mechanism and verification","text":"備援台數只有在實際揚程、電源和管路條件下才有意義，保留一台泵不代表任何故障都能維持完整排水。多台可能共用變壓器、閘門、攔污設備或控制，因此機械可用性不等於整站可用性；故障情境應把剩餘排量與儲水時間一起評估，並辨認共因失效。","textEn":"Spare-unit counts matter only at actual head, electrical and pipe conditions. One spare does not preserve full drainage for every fault.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：設有一台備用泵就能保證抽水站任何單一故障都不減排水量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One spare pump guarantees unchanged station discharge under every single failure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「單機停用與整站能力機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Unit outage and station capability mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["設有一台備用泵就能保證抽水站任何單一故障都不減排水量。","備援台數只有在實際揚程、電源和管路條件下才有意義，保留一台泵不代表任何故障都能維持完整排水。","泵的標示總流量大於平均雨水流量，就能保證任何洪水不積水。"],"optionsEn":["One spare pump guarantees unchanged station discharge under every single failure.","Spare-unit counts matter only at actual head, electrical and pipe conditions.","Total labeled pump flow above mean runoff guarantees no flooding in any event."],"answer":1,"explanation":"備援台數只有在實際揚程、電源和管路條件下才有意義，保留一台泵不代表任何故障都能維持完整排水。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Spare-unit counts matter only at actual head, electrical and pipe conditions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b270-v15-38","title":"單機停用與整站能力機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Unit outage and station capability mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「單機停用與整站能力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Unit outage and station capability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設三台各可排2.0 m³/s、需求5.0 m³/s；一台停用後可用4.0 m³/s，瞬時缺口為1.0 m³/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume three units each available at 2.0 m³/s and demand 5.0 m³/s. One outage leaves 4.0 m³/s, an instantaneous shortfall of 1.0 m³/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐一列出單泵、電源、攔污與共同管路故障，確認剩餘流量不是直接沿用正常工況。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: List pump, supply, screen and common-pipe failures, checking that retained flow is not simply copied from normal operation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設三台各可排2.0 m³/s、需求5.0 m³/s；一台停用後可用4.0 m³/s，瞬時缺口為1.0 m³/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume three units each available at 2.0 m³/s and demand 5.0 m³/s. One outage leaves 4.0 m³/s, an instantaneous shortfall of 1.0 m³/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「單機停用與整站能力機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Unit outage and station capability mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["兩台並聯泵的實際排水量必定是單台接原管路時的兩倍。","泵降速一成，整站一定同時少抽一成水且省下固定立方比例電力。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設三台各可排2.0 m³/s、需求5.0 m³/s；一台停用後可用4.0 m³/s，瞬時缺口為1.0 m³/s。"],"optionsEn":["Two parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow through the original system.","Reducing speed ten percent guarantees ten percent less station flow and fixed cube-law energy savings.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume three units each available at 2.0 m³/s and demand 5.0 m³/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設三台各可排2.0 m³/s、需求5.0 m³/s；一台停用後可用4.0 m³/s，瞬時缺口為1.0 m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume three units each available at 2.0 m³/s and demand 5.0 m³/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b270-v15-39","title":"單機停用與整站能力機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Unit outage and station capability mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「單機停用與整站能力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Unit outage and station capability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐一列出單泵、電源、攔污與共同管路故障，確認剩餘流量不是直接沿用正常工況。以可用儲量演算缺口持續時間，並測試故障旗標和人工接管介面，保存實際限制而非只報備援台數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"List pump, supply, screen and common-pipe failures, checking that retained flow is not simply copied from normal operation. Route shortfalls through available storage, test fault indication and manual takeover interfaces, and document real limitations rather than reporting only the number of spare units. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立至少三種故障的剩餘能力表，將共同電源故障與單泵故障分開。把一個排量缺口轉成池水位變化，說明儲水只能提供有限緩衝而非永久替代抽排。","observationEn":"Site practice: Build retained-capacity cases for at least three failures, separating shared-power loss from a single-pump outage. Convert one flow shortfall into sump rise and explain why storage provides a finite buffer rather than a permanent substitute for pumping.","failure":"注意干擾：三台泵共用一個失效配電盤時，名義備援無法保留排量；以正常單台能力乘剩餘台數也可能忽略新揚程，導致可支撐的洪水時間被高估。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If three pumps share one failed switchboard, nominal redundancy preserves no flow. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐一列出單泵、電源、攔污與共同管路故障，確認剩餘流量不是直接沿用正常工況。以可用儲量演算缺口持續時間，並測試故障旗標和人工接管介面，保存實際限制而非只報備援台數。","textEn":"List pump, supply, screen and common-pipe failures, checking that retained flow is not simply copied from normal operation. Route shortfalls through available storage, test fault indication and manual takeover interfaces, and document real limitations rather than reporting only the number of spare units.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立至少三種故障的剩餘能力表，將共同電源故障與單泵故障分開。把一個排量缺口轉成池水位變化，說明儲水只能提供有限緩衝而非永久替代抽排。","textEn":"Build retained-capacity cases for at least three failures, separating shared-power loss from a single-pump outage. Convert one flow shortfall into sump rise and explain why storage provides a finite buffer rather than a permanent substitute for pumping.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「單機停用與整站能力機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Unit outage and station capability mechanism and verification\"?","options":["逐一列出單泵、電源、攔污與共同管路故障，確認剩餘流量不是直接沿用正常工況。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","池水位只要夠高，任何機組組合都不可能出現渦流或汽蝕。"],"optionsEn":["List pump, supply, screen and common-pipe failures, checking that retained flow is not simply copied from normal operation.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Sufficient sump level makes vortices or cavitation impossible for every pump combination."],"answer":0,"explanation":"逐一列出單泵、電源、攔污與共同管路故障，確認剩餘流量不是直接沿用正常工況。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"List pump, supply, screen and common-pipe failures, checking that retained flow is not simply copied from normal operation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b270-v15-40","title":"單機停用與整站能力機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Unit outage and station capability mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"prerequisiteIds":["b270-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「單機停用與整站能力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Unit outage and station capability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"三台泵共用一個失效配電盤時，名義備援無法保留排量；以正常單台能力乘剩餘台數也可能忽略新揚程，導致可支撐的洪水時間被高估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If three pumps share one failed switchboard, nominal redundancy preserves no flow. Multiplying normal unit capacity by remaining count may also miss changed head and overstate the duration for which storage can bridge the flood. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例每台排量已指定為相同實際揚程下的可用量，假設停機不改變其他台工作點；真實並聯工況須重新求解。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Real parallel-system performance must be solved again.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「設有一台備用泵就能保證抽水站任何單一故障都不減排水量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One spare pump guarantees unchanged station discharge under every single failure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b270-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"三台泵共用一個失效配電盤時，名義備援無法保留排量；以正常單台能力乘剩餘台數也可能忽略新揚程，導致可支撐的洪水時間被高估。","textEn":"If three pumps share one failed switchboard, nominal redundancy preserves no flow. Multiplying normal unit capacity by remaining count may also miss changed head and overstate the duration for which storage can bridge the flood.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]},{"id":"b270-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「單機停用與整站能力機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Unit outage and station capability mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","三台泵共用一個失效配電盤時，名義備援無法保留排量；以正常單台能力乘剩餘台數也可能忽略新揚程，導致可支撐的洪水時間被高估。","泵的標示總流量大於平均雨水流量，就能保證任何洪水不積水。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","If three pumps share one failed switchboard, nominal redundancy preserves no flow.","Total labeled pump flow above mean runoff guarantees no flooding in any event."],"answer":1,"explanation":"三台泵共用一個失效配電盤時，名義備援無法保留排量；以正常單台能力乘剩餘台數也可能忽略新揚程，導致可支撐的洪水時間被高估。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If three pumps share one failed switchboard, nominal redundancy preserves no flow. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-pumps2020","v15s-usace-westclosure","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-sheungwan"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b271","title":"都市滯洪池配置","titleEn":"Urban detention-basin planning","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"課程從連通集水區和事件體積進入儲量演算，逐項建立池容、孔口、溢流、滲透與排空模型，最後檢查下游峰時、沉積和數值閉合。大坑東與跑馬地提供地下蓄洪實例，全部數值為合成假設；規劃的核心是保存水量與確認去向，不把單一削峰百分比當完整防洪成效。","summaryEn":"The course moves from connected catchment and event volume into storage routing, geometry, orifices, overflow, infiltration and drawdown, then checks downstream timing, sediment and numerical closure. Tai Hang Tung and Happy Valley provide underground-storage examples. All numbers are synthetic assumptions; planning centers on conservation and destination rather than treating one peak-reduction percentage as complete flood performance.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["連通集水區","Connected catchment"],["入流歷線","Inflow hydrograph"],["儲量與出口","Storage and outlet"],["下游匯流","Downstream combination"],["維護與驗證","Maintenance and verification"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["連通集水區","入流歷線","儲量與出口","下游匯流","維護與驗證"],"labelsEn":["Connected catchment","Inflow hydrograph","Storage and outlet","Downstream combination","Maintenance and verification"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"敏感度固定孔口係數Cd=0.62與兩側水頭差1.0 m，只把圓孔直徑增加10%。面積和瞬時流量都增加21%，若原開口0.10 m²的流量為0.2746 m³/s，新面積0.121 m²對應0.3323 m³/s。這可能較快恢復池容，但也可能增加下游負荷；在同一固定池面積及自由排水積分模型下，排空時間因面積增加而降為原值的82.64%。實際事件的水位會隨出流改變，尾水和部分淹沒也可能變動，因此不能直接用固定水頭比例取代全歷線重算。","textEn":"For sensitivity, hold Cd=0.62 and differential head at 1.0 m while increasing circular-orifice diameter by ten percent. Area and instantaneous discharge both rise by 21%. An original 0.10 m² opening releases 0.2746 m³/s; the new 0.121 m² opening releases 0.3323 m³/s. This can restore storage sooner but also increases downstream loading. Under the same constant-area, free-drawdown integral model, time falls to 82.64% of its original value. Real event stage responds to release, while tailwater and submergence may change. The fixed-head ratio therefore cannot replace rerouting the complete hydrograph.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b271-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證」與「歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification\" and \"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b271-v15-01","title":"集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「集水區與逕流體積」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Catchment and runoff volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"滯洪池的第一個問題是哪些地表真正連到入口，而不是行政邊界內有多少面積。屋頂、道路和透水地的產流不同，前期含水與管網分流又會改變有效貢獻；事件總量可用簡化係數作初估，但它沒有提供洪峰出現時間或歷線形狀，不能單靠總雨量完成池容設計。本例係數為指定事件的體積比例，假設雨量均勻且無跨區來水；它不是用於求瞬時洪峰的完整理性式分析。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「集水區與逕流體積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The first detention question is which surfaces actually connect to the inlet, not how much area lies inside an administrative boundary. Roofs, roads and permeable land generate different runoff, while antecedent wetness and network diversion change effective contribution. An event coefficient provides an initial volume estimate but not crest timing or hydrograph shape, so rainfall total alone cannot size the basin. The coefficient is a specified event-volume fraction under uniform rainfall and no imported flow. This is not a complete rational-method peak-flow analysis. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Catchment and runoff volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件雨量P=0.050 m、連通面積A=200000 m²、體積逕流係數C=0.70，V=CPA=7000 m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event rainfall P=0.050 m, connected area A=200000 m² and volume runoff coefficient C=0.70.","failure":"常見誤解：「知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「集水區與逕流體積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Catchment and runoff volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-01-k1","title":"集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證","titleEn":"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification","text":"滯洪池的第一個問題是哪些地表真正連到入口，而不是行政邊界內有多少面積。屋頂、道路和透水地的產流不同，前期含水與管網分流又會改變有效貢獻；事件總量可用簡化係數作初估，但它沒有提供洪峰出現時間或歷線形狀，不能單靠總雨量完成池容設計。","textEn":"The first detention question is which surfaces actually connect to the inlet, not how much area lies inside an administrative boundary. Roofs, roads and permeable land generate different runoff, while antecedent wetness and network diversion change effective contribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。","滯洪池的第一個問題是哪些地表真正連到入口，而不是行政邊界內有多少面積。","所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。"],"optionsEn":["Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity.","The first detention question is which surfaces actually connect to the inlet, not how much area lies inside an administrative boundary.","Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"滯洪池的第一個問題是哪些地表真正連到入口，而不是行政邊界內有多少面積。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The first detention question is which surfaces actually connect to the inlet, not how much area lies inside an administrative boundary. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b271-v15-02","title":"集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「集水區與逕流體積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Catchment and runoff volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件雨量P=0.050 m、連通面積A=200000 m²、體積逕流係數C=0.70，V=CPA=7000 m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event rainfall P=0.050 m, connected area A=200000 m² and volume runoff coefficient C=0.70. Runoff V=CPA=7000 m³. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以排水連通調查核對有效面積，將雨量與入口事件體積比較，分開記錄跨區分流和前期含水。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify connected area through drainage mapping and compare rainfall with measured inlet event volume, recording imported flow and antecedent wetness separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件雨量P=0.050 m、連通面積A=200000 m²、體積逕流係數C=0.70，V=CPA=7000 m³。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event rainfall P=0.050 m, connected area A=200000 m² and volume runoff coefficient C=0.70. Runoff V=CPA=7000 m³.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。","透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件雨量P=0.050 m、連通面積A=200000 m²、體積逕流係數C=0.70，V=CPA=7000 m³。"],"optionsEn":["Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level.","A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event rainfall P=0.050 m, connected area A=200000 m² and volume runoff coefficient C=0.70."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件雨量P=0.050 m、連通面積A=200000 m²、體積逕流係數C=0.70，V=CPA=7000 m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event rainfall P=0.050 m, connected area A=200000 m² and volume runoff coefficient C=0.70. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b271-v15-03","title":"集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「集水區與逕流體積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Catchment and runoff volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以排水連通調查核對有效面積，將雨量與入口事件體積比較，分開記錄跨區分流和前期含水。檢查係數是否隨事件改變，並補上時間分布資料才能進行真正的滯洪演算。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify connected area through drainage mapping and compare rainfall with measured inlet event volume, recording imported flow and antecedent wetness separately. Check event-to-event coefficient changes and obtain temporal distribution before using the volume estimate in actual detention routing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出行政界和實際排水界，辨認一條跨界管線對體積帳的影響。為相同事件雨量安排兩種時間分布，說明為何後續必須比較完整入流歷線。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw administrative and drainage boundaries and identify the effect of one cross-boundary pipe on the volume ledger. Arrange two temporal patterns for equal rainfall and explain why complete inflow hydrographs must subsequently be compared.","failure":"注意干擾：把整個集水區都當不透水會高估部分情境，漏掉管網跨區來水則可能低估；即使事件總量正確，不同雨型仍可能產生完全不同的峰值與需要庫容。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating the whole catchment as impervious overestimates some cases, while omitted network imports underestimate others. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以排水連通調查核對有效面積，將雨量與入口事件體積比較，分開記錄跨區分流和前期含水。檢查係數是否隨事件改變，並補上時間分布資料才能進行真正的滯洪演算。","textEn":"Verify connected area through drainage mapping and compare rainfall with measured inlet event volume, recording imported flow and antecedent wetness separately. Check event-to-event coefficient changes and obtain temporal distribution before using the volume estimate in actual detention routing.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出行政界和實際排水界，辨認一條跨界管線對體積帳的影響。為相同事件雨量安排兩種時間分布，說明為何後續必須比較完整入流歷線。","textEn":"Draw administrative and drainage boundaries and identify the effect of one cross-boundary pipe on the volume ledger. Arrange two temporal patterns for equal rainfall and explain why complete inflow hydrographs must subsequently be compared.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification\"?","options":["以排水連通調查核對有效面積，將雨量與入口事件體積比較，分開記錄跨區分流和前期含水。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。"],"optionsEn":["Verify connected area through drainage mapping and compare rainfall with measured inlet event volume, recording imported flow and antecedent wetness separately.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以排水連通調查核對有效面積，將雨量與入口事件體積比較，分開記錄跨區分流和前期含水。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify connected area through drainage mapping and compare rainfall with measured inlet event volume, recording imported flow and antecedent wetness separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b271-v15-04","title":"集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「集水區與逕流體積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Catchment and runoff volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把整個集水區都當不透水會高估部分情境，漏掉管網跨區來水則可能低估；即使事件總量正確，不同雨型仍可能產生完全不同的峰值與需要庫容。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating the whole catchment as impervious overestimates some cases, while omitted network imports underestimate others. Even a correct event volume can produce very different peaks and storage requirements under different rainfall timing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例係數為指定事件的體積比例，假設雨量均勻且無跨區來水；它不是用於求瞬時洪峰的完整理性式分析。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This is not a complete rational-method peak-flow analysis.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把整個集水區都當不透水會高估部分情境，漏掉管網跨區來水則可能低估；即使事件總量正確，不同雨型仍可能產生完全不同的峰值與需要庫容。","textEn":"Treating the whole catchment as impervious overestimates some cases, while omitted network imports underestimate others. Even a correct event volume can produce very different peaks and storage requirements under different rainfall timing.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把整個集水區都當不透水會高估部分情境，漏掉管網跨區來水則可能低估；即使事件總量正確，不同雨型仍可能產生完全不同的峰值與需要庫容。","所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating the whole catchment as impervious overestimates some cases, while omitted network imports underestimate others.","Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把整個集水區都當不透水會高估部分情境，漏掉管網跨區來水則可能低估；即使事件總量正確，不同雨型仍可能產生完全不同的峰值與需要庫容。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating the whole catchment as impervious overestimates some cases, while omitted network imports underestimate others. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b271-v15-05","title":"歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「歷線演算與儲量變化」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Hydrograph routing and storage change” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"滯洪利用進出流量的時間差暫存水量，所需最大庫容來自累積差額而不是洪峰流量相減。出口流量又依池水位與下游水位變化，使儲量和出流彼此耦合；若只固定一個出流上限而不限制可用水量，演算可能在池空時仍排水，產生不可能的負儲量。本例以一個時間步的已知端點流量作梯形積分，假設步內線性變化且儲量足夠；未求完整水位依存出口。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「歷線演算與儲量變化」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Detention stores the time-integrated difference between inflow and outflow, not the difference of peak discharges alone. Outlet flow depends on basin and downstream stages, coupling storage and release. A fixed outflow cap without water-availability constraints can continue releasing from an empty basin and create physically impossible negative storage. The example trapezoidally integrates known endpoint flows over one step, assuming linear variation and sufficient water. It does not solve a complete stage-dependent outlet. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Hydrograph routing and storage change” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δt=300 s、入流I1=4、I2=6及出流O1=2、O2=3 m³/s，ΔS=[(I1+I2)−(O1+O2)]Δt/2=750 m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δt=300 s, inflows I1=4, I2=6 and outflows O1=2, O2=3 m³/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「歷線演算與儲量變化」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Hydrograph routing and storage change”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-05-k1","title":"歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證","titleEn":"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification","text":"滯洪利用進出流量的時間差暫存水量，所需最大庫容來自累積差額而不是洪峰流量相減。出口流量又依池水位與下游水位變化，使儲量和出流彼此耦合；若只固定一個出流上限而不限制可用水量，演算可能在池空時仍排水，產生不可能的負儲量。","textEn":"Detention stores the time-integrated difference between inflow and outflow, not the difference of peak discharges alone. Outlet flow depends on basin and downstream stages, coupling storage and release.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。","池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。","滯洪利用進出流量的時間差暫存水量，所需最大庫容來自累積差額而不是洪峰流量相減。"],"optionsEn":["Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration.","Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage.","Detention stores the time-integrated difference between inflow and outflow, not the difference of peak discharges alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"滯洪利用進出流量的時間差暫存水量，所需最大庫容來自累積差額而不是洪峰流量相減。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Detention stores the time-integrated difference between inflow and outflow, not the difference of peak discharges alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b271-v15-06","title":"歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「歷線演算與儲量變化」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Hydrograph routing and storage change” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δt=300 s、入流I1=4、I2=6及出流O1=2、O2=3 m³/s，ΔS=[(I1+I2)−(O1+O2)]Δt/2=750 m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δt=300 s, inflows I1=4, I2=6 and outflows O1=2, O2=3 m³/s. Storage change ΔS=[(I1+I2)−(O1+O2)]Δt/2=750 m³. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐步核對入流、出流、初始和最終儲量，確認流量時間戳與積分區間一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile inflow, outflow and initial/final storage step by step, aligning timestamps with integration intervals.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δt=300 s、入流I1=4、I2=6及出流O1=2、O2=3 m³/s，ΔS=[(I1+I2)−(O1+O2)]Δt/2=750 m³。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δt=300 s, inflows I1=4, I2=6 and outflows O1=2, O2=3 m³/s. Storage change ΔS=[(I1+I2)−(O1+O2)]Δt/2=750 m³.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δt=300 s、入流I1=4、I2=6及出流O1=2、O2=3 m³/s，ΔS=[(I1+I2)−(O1+O2)]Δt/2=750 m³。","只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。","孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δt=300 s, inflows I1=4, I2=6 and outflows O1=2, O2=3 m³/s.","An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis.","Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δt=300 s、入流I1=4、I2=6及出流O1=2、O2=3 m³/s，ΔS=[(I1+I2)−(O1+O2)]Δt/2=750 m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δt=300 s, inflows I1=4, I2=6 and outflows O1=2, O2=3 m³/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b271-v15-07","title":"歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「歷線演算與儲量變化」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hydrograph routing and storage change” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐步核對入流、出流、初始和最終儲量，確認流量時間戳與積分區間一致。縮小時間步比較最大水位及峰值時刻，並檢查池空、滿溢與逆流時的邊界切換是否守恆。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile inflow, outflow and initial/final storage step by step, aligning timestamps with integration intervals. Reduce the time step to compare maximum stage and crest timing, and check conservation when boundaries switch at empty storage, overflow or reverse flow. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用四個時間步建立累積儲量，讓最後一步可能排空並修正不可能出流。將修正前後的總水量比較，指出負儲量不是可接受的數值小誤差。","observationEn":"Site practice: Build cumulative storage over four steps, allowing the last to empty the basin and correcting impossible outflow. Compare total water before and after correction and explain why negative storage is not an acceptable small numerical error.","failure":"注意干擾：將立方公尺每秒差額直接當池容積會漏掉時間量綱，過大時間步又可能跨過短時峰值；未處理池空邊界會製造不存在的排水量和虛假削峰效益。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using a discharge difference as storage omits time dimensions, and overly large steps can skip a brief peak. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐步核對入流、出流、初始和最終儲量，確認流量時間戳與積分區間一致。縮小時間步比較最大水位及峰值時刻，並檢查池空、滿溢與逆流時的邊界切換是否守恆。","textEn":"Reconcile inflow, outflow and initial/final storage step by step, aligning timestamps with integration intervals. Reduce the time step to compare maximum stage and crest timing, and check conservation when boundaries switch at empty storage, overflow or reverse flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用四個時間步建立累積儲量，讓最後一步可能排空並修正不可能出流。將修正前後的總水量比較，指出負儲量不是可接受的數值小誤差。","textEn":"Build cumulative storage over four steps, allowing the last to empty the basin and correcting impossible outflow. Compare total water before and after correction and explain why negative storage is not an acceptable small numerical error.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","逐步核對入流、出流、初始和最終儲量，確認流量時間戳與積分區間一致。","只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Reconcile inflow, outflow and initial/final storage step by step, aligning timestamps with integration intervals.","A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"逐步核對入流、出流、初始和最終儲量，確認流量時間戳與積分區間一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile inflow, outflow and initial/final storage step by step, aligning timestamps with integration intervals. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b271-v15-08","title":"歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「歷線演算與儲量變化」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hydrograph routing and storage change” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將立方公尺每秒差額直接當池容積會漏掉時間量綱，過大時間步又可能跨過短時峰值；未處理池空邊界會製造不存在的排水量和虛假削峰效益。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using a discharge difference as storage omits time dimensions, and overly large steps can skip a brief peak. Missing the empty-basin boundary invents discharge and produces a false attenuation benefit. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例以一個時間步的已知端點流量作梯形積分，假設步內線性變化且儲量足夠；未求完整水位依存出口。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It does not solve a complete stage-dependent outlet.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將立方公尺每秒差額直接當池容積會漏掉時間量綱，過大時間步又可能跨過短時峰值；未處理池空邊界會製造不存在的排水量和虛假削峰效益。","textEn":"Using a discharge difference as storage omits time dimensions, and overly large steps can skip a brief peak. Missing the empty-basin boundary invents discharge and produces a false attenuation benefit.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。","將立方公尺每秒差額直接當池容積會漏掉時間量綱，過大時間步又可能跨過短時峰值；未處理池空邊界會製造不存在的排水量和虛假削峰效益。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage.","Using a discharge difference as storage omits time dimensions, and overly large steps can skip a brief peak."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將立方公尺每秒差額直接當池容積會漏掉時間量綱，過大時間步又可能跨過短時峰值；未處理池空邊界會製造不存在的排水量和虛假削峰效益。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using a discharge difference as storage omits time dimensions, and overly large steps can skip a brief peak. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b271-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證」與「孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification\" and \"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b271-v15-09","title":"水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「水位面積與有效池容」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Stage area and usable storage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"滯洪池的平面面積可隨水位增加，邊坡、柱體及設備又會改變有效蓄水空間。面積曲線積分才得到庫容，不能用最高水位面積乘水深代替所有幾何；永久水池、沉砂區與不可抽空部分也應從可用調洪容積分開，避免以總挖方體積宣稱防洪能力。本例採線性水位面積關係且從指定空池基準積分，未含柱體或死水容積；實際幾何需由測量和竣工資料建立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水位面積與有效池容」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Basin surface area may grow with stage, while slopes, columns and equipment alter usable space. Integrating the area curve yields storage; maximum surface area times depth does not represent all geometries. Permanent pools, sediment reserves and undrainable zones must also be separated from available flood storage instead of equating excavation volume with flood capacity. The example integrates a linear stage-area relation from a specified empty datum, excluding columns and dead storage. Actual geometry needs survey and as-built records. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Stage area and usable storage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設A(h)=1000+200h m²，其中h以m計；到h=2 m的庫容S=1000h+100h²=2400 m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume A(h)=1000+200h m² with h in meters.","failure":"常見誤解：「池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水位面積與有效池容」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Stage area and usable storage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-09-k1","title":"水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證","titleEn":"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification","text":"滯洪池的平面面積可隨水位增加，邊坡、柱體及設備又會改變有效蓄水空間。面積曲線積分才得到庫容，不能用最高水位面積乘水深代替所有幾何；永久水池、沉砂區與不可抽空部分也應從可用調洪容積分開，避免以總挖方體積宣稱防洪能力。","textEn":"Basin surface area may grow with stage, while slopes, columns and equipment alter usable space. Integrating the area curve yields storage; maximum surface area times depth does not represent all geometries.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["滯洪池的平面面積可隨水位增加，邊坡、柱體及設備又會改變有效蓄水空間。","池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。","孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。"],"optionsEn":["Basin surface area may grow with stage, while slopes, columns and equipment alter usable space.","Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage.","Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level."],"answer":0,"explanation":"滯洪池的平面面積可隨水位增加，邊坡、柱體及設備又會改變有效蓄水空間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Basin surface area may grow with stage, while slopes, columns and equipment alter usable space. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b271-v15-10","title":"水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水位面積與有效池容」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Stage area and usable storage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設A(h)=1000+200h m²，其中h以m計；到h=2 m的庫容S=1000h+100h²=2400 m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume A(h)=1000+200h m² with h in meters. Storage at h=2 m is S=1000h+100h²=2400 m³. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對面積曲線的標高基準與插值方式，將分層積分容積和三維幾何模型比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check elevation datum and interpolation of the area curve, comparing layered integration with three-dimensional geometry.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設A(h)=1000+200h m²，其中h以m計；到h=2 m的庫容S=1000h+100h²=2400 m³。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume A(h)=1000+200h m² with h in meters. Storage at h=2 m is S=1000h+100h²=2400 m³.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設A(h)=1000+200h m²，其中h以m計；到h=2 m的庫容S=1000h+100h²=2400 m³。","每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。"],"optionsEn":["A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume A(h)=1000+200h m² with h in meters.","Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設A(h)=1000+200h m²，其中h以m計；到h=2 m的庫容S=1000h+100h²=2400 m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume A(h)=1000+200h m² with h in meters. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b271-v15-11","title":"水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水位面積與有效池容」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Stage area and usable storage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對面積曲線的標高基準與插值方式，將分層積分容積和三維幾何模型比較。另列永久水位、沉積及構件占用，確認演算使用可動用的庫容，而不是圖面標示的總空間。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check elevation datum and interpolation of the area curve, comparing layered integration with three-dimensional geometry. List permanent water, deposits and structural displacement separately, confirming that routing uses accessible storage rather than the gross space labeled on a drawing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對線性面積曲線做分層與解析兩種積分，再扣除一個假設永久水位以下體積。說明最高水位不變時，初始積水如何減少可用調洪容量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Integrate the linear area curve numerically and analytically, then subtract volume below a hypothetical permanent level. Explain how initial water reduces available flood storage even when the maximum permitted stage is unchanged.","failure":"注意干擾：用頂面積乘深度會對向上擴張池體高估容積，漏掉柱體或既有積水也會虛增可用量；基準不一致時甚至可能把同一段水深重複計入。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Multiplying top area by depth overstates storage in an expanding basin. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對面積曲線的標高基準與插值方式，將分層積分容積和三維幾何模型比較。另列永久水位、沉積及構件占用，確認演算使用可動用的庫容，而不是圖面標示的總空間。","textEn":"Check elevation datum and interpolation of the area curve, comparing layered integration with three-dimensional geometry. List permanent water, deposits and structural displacement separately, confirming that routing uses accessible storage rather than the gross space labeled on a drawing.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對線性面積曲線做分層與解析兩種積分，再扣除一個假設永久水位以下體積。說明最高水位不變時，初始積水如何減少可用調洪容量。","textEn":"Integrate the linear area curve numerically and analytically, then subtract volume below a hypothetical permanent level. Explain how initial water reduces available flood storage even when the maximum permitted stage is unchanged.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。","核對面積曲線的標高基準與插值方式，將分層積分容積和三維幾何模型比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision.","Check elevation datum and interpolation of the area curve, comparing layered integration with three-dimensional geometry."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對面積曲線的標高基準與插值方式，將分層積分容積和三維幾何模型比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check elevation datum and interpolation of the area curve, comparing layered integration with three-dimensional geometry. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b271-v15-12","title":"水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水位面積與有效池容」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Stage area and usable storage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用頂面積乘深度會對向上擴張池體高估容積，漏掉柱體或既有積水也會虛增可用量；基準不一致時甚至可能把同一段水深重複計入。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Multiplying top area by depth overstates storage in an expanding basin. Omitted columns or initial water also inflate available capacity, and inconsistent datums can cause the same depth interval to be counted twice. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例採線性水位面積關係且從指定空池基準積分，未含柱體或死水容積；實際幾何需由測量和竣工資料建立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Actual geometry needs survey and as-built records.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用頂面積乘深度會對向上擴張池體高估容積，漏掉柱體或既有積水也會虛增可用量；基準不一致時甚至可能把同一段水深重複計入。","textEn":"Multiplying top area by depth overstates storage in an expanding basin. Omitted columns or initial water also inflate available capacity, and inconsistent datums can cause the same depth interval to be counted twice.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用頂面積乘深度會對向上擴張池體高估容積，漏掉柱體或既有積水也會虛增可用量；基準不一致時甚至可能把同一段水深重複計入。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。"],"optionsEn":["Multiplying top area by depth overstates storage in an expanding basin.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用頂面積乘深度會對向上擴張池體高估容積，漏掉柱體或既有積水也會虛增可用量；基準不一致時甚至可能把同一段水深重複計入。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Multiplying top area by depth overstates storage in an expanding basin. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b271-v15-13","title":"孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「孔口出流與尾水」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orifice release and tailwater” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"池底孔口把水頭轉為出流速度，流量取決於有效開口、流量係數及兩側能量差。自由出流時可由孔心到池水面估水頭，但下游淹沒後必須改用兩側水頭差；入口垃圾和沉積也會改變有效面積，不能把設計孔徑永久視為可用開口。本例是淹沒薄孔的簡化定常流，指定係數與兩側水頭差，忽略接管沿程損失；不推定任何產品或許可排量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「孔口出流與尾水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A low-level orifice converts head to outlet velocity according to effective opening, discharge coefficient and energy difference. For free discharge the basin surface-to-orifice-center head may be used, but submerged discharge requires the difference between both sides. Debris and deposits alter effective area, so nominal diameter cannot be treated as permanently available opening. The example is simplified steady flow through a submerged thin orifice with specified coefficient and differential head, excluding downstream pipe friction and any product or permit rating. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orifice release and tailwater” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Cd=0.62、開口A=0.10 m²、兩側水頭差ΔH=1.0 m、g=9.81 m/s²，Q=CdA√(2gΔH)=0.2746 m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Cd=0.62, opening A=0.10 m², differential head ΔH=1.0 m and g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「孔口出流與尾水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orifice release and tailwater”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-13-k1","title":"孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證","titleEn":"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification","text":"池底孔口把水頭轉為出流速度，流量取決於有效開口、流量係數及兩側能量差。自由出流時可由孔心到池水面估水頭，但下游淹沒後必須改用兩側水頭差；入口垃圾和沉積也會改變有效面積，不能把設計孔徑永久視為可用開口。","textEn":"A low-level orifice converts head to outlet velocity according to effective opening, discharge coefficient and energy difference. For free discharge the basin surface-to-orifice-center head may be used, but submerged discharge requires the difference between both sides.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。","池底孔口把水頭轉為出流速度，流量取決於有效開口、流量係數及兩側能量差。","只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。"],"optionsEn":["Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level.","A low-level orifice converts head to outlet velocity according to effective opening, discharge coefficient and energy difference.","An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"池底孔口把水頭轉為出流速度，流量取決於有效開口、流量係數及兩側能量差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A low-level orifice converts head to outlet velocity according to effective opening, discharge coefficient and energy difference. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b271-v15-14","title":"孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「孔口出流與尾水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orifice release and tailwater” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Cd=0.62、開口A=0.10 m²、兩側水頭差ΔH=1.0 m、g=9.81 m/s²，Q=CdA√(2gΔH)=0.2746 m³/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Cd=0.62, opening A=0.10 m², differential head ΔH=1.0 m and g=9.81 m/s². Flow Q=CdA√(2gΔH)=0.2746 m³/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同時量測池內與下游水位，核對孔心高程、開口和係數來源。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure basin and downstream stages together, checking orifice elevation, opening and coefficient source.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Cd=0.62、開口A=0.10 m²、兩側水頭差ΔH=1.0 m、g=9.81 m/s²，Q=CdA√(2gΔH)=0.2746 m³/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Cd=0.62, opening A=0.10 m², differential head ΔH=1.0 m and g=9.81 m/s². Flow Q=CdA√(2gΔH)=0.2746 m³/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。","只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Cd=0.62、開口A=0.10 m²、兩側水頭差ΔH=1.0 m、g=9.81 m/s²，Q=CdA√(2gΔH)=0.2746 m³/s。"],"optionsEn":["Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release.","A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Cd=0.62, opening A=0.10 m², differential head ΔH=1.0 m and g=9.81 m/s²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Cd=0.62、開口A=0.10 m²、兩側水頭差ΔH=1.0 m、g=9.81 m/s²，Q=CdA√(2gΔH)=0.2746 m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Cd=0.62, opening A=0.10 m², differential head ΔH=1.0 m and g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b271-v15-15","title":"孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「孔口出流與尾水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orifice release and tailwater” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同時量測池內與下游水位，核對孔心高程、開口和係數來源。比較清潔、部分堵塞與尾水上升的出流資料，確認模型在自由與淹沒狀態切換時不會突然創造或消失流量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure basin and downstream stages together, checking orifice elevation, opening and coefficient source. Compare clean, partially blocked and rising-tailwater observations, ensuring that switching between free and submerged representations does not abruptly create or remove flow in the model. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持池水位不變而提高尾水，計算兩個水頭差的出流量。再將有效面積減半，區分堵塞和尾水兩種原因如何在量測上辨認。","observationEn":"Site practice: Hold basin stage fixed while raising tailwater and calculate releases at two differential heads. Then halve effective area, distinguishing the observations needed to separate blockage from a tailwater-driven reduction.","failure":"注意干擾：尾水升高仍用池深當水頭會高估出流而低估池水位，忽略堵塞則讓維護不足被掩蓋；水頭差反向時，未設防倒流的開口可能反而進水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using basin depth despite high tailwater overstates release and understates basin stage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同時量測池內與下游水位，核對孔心高程、開口和係數來源。比較清潔、部分堵塞與尾水上升的出流資料，確認模型在自由與淹沒狀態切換時不會突然創造或消失流量。","textEn":"Measure basin and downstream stages together, checking orifice elevation, opening and coefficient source. Compare clean, partially blocked and rising-tailwater observations, ensuring that switching between free and submerged representations does not abruptly create or remove flow in the model.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持池水位不變而提高尾水，計算兩個水頭差的出流量。再將有效面積減半，區分堵塞和尾水兩種原因如何在量測上辨認。","textEn":"Hold basin stage fixed while raising tailwater and calculate releases at two differential heads. Then halve effective area, distinguishing the observations needed to separate blockage from a tailwater-driven reduction.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification\"?","options":["同時量測池內與下游水位，核對孔心高程、開口和係數來源。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。"],"optionsEn":["Measure basin and downstream stages together, checking orifice elevation, opening and coefficient source.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同時量測池內與下游水位，核對孔心高程、開口和係數來源。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure basin and downstream stages together, checking orifice elevation, opening and coefficient source. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b271-v15-16","title":"孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「孔口出流與尾水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orifice release and tailwater” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"尾水升高仍用池深當水頭會高估出流而低估池水位，忽略堵塞則讓維護不足被掩蓋；水頭差反向時，未設防倒流的開口可能反而進水。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using basin depth despite high tailwater overstates release and understates basin stage. Ignored blockage conceals maintenance loss, and reversed differential head can admit water through an opening without backflow protection. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例是淹沒薄孔的簡化定常流，指定係數與兩側水頭差，忽略接管沿程損失；不推定任何產品或許可排量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The example is simplified steady flow through a submerged thin orifice with specified coefficient and differential head, excluding downstream pipe friction and any product or permit rating.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"尾水升高仍用池深當水頭會高估出流而低估池水位，忽略堵塞則讓維護不足被掩蓋；水頭差反向時，未設防倒流的開口可能反而進水。","textEn":"Using basin depth despite high tailwater overstates release and understates basin stage. Ignored blockage conceals maintenance loss, and reversed differential head can admit water through an opening without backflow protection.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","尾水升高仍用池深當水頭會高估出流而低估池水位，忽略堵塞則讓維護不足被掩蓋；水頭差反向時，未設防倒流的開口可能反而進水。","只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using basin depth despite high tailwater overstates release and understates basin stage.","An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"尾水升高仍用池深當水頭會高估出流而低估池水位，忽略堵塞則讓維護不足被掩蓋；水頭差反向時，未設防倒流的開口可能反而進水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using basin depth despite high tailwater overstates release and understates basin stage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b271-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證」與「滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification\" and \"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b271-v15-17","title":"超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「超量溢流與越頂路徑」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Exceedance overflow and routes” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"滯洪池遇到超過控制出口能力的事件時，需要辨認水會流向何處，正常出流設計不能代表超量情境。溢流堰流量與堰頂以上水頭呈非線性，來流速度、淹沒與側向幾何會改變係數；更重要的是溢出後的路徑和受影響空間，不能只證明池內水位降低而忽略下游風險。本例用指定係數的自由矩形堰比較，係數已包含單位；未模擬側堰、淹沒或街道二維流動。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「超量溢流與越頂路徑」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When an event exceeds the controlled outlet, the overflow destination matters; normal-release design does not represent exceedance behavior. Weir flow is nonlinear in head above crest, and approach velocity, submergence and lateral geometry alter the coefficient. The route and exposed spaces downstream must be assessed rather than claiming success merely because basin level is reduced. The example uses a free rectangular weir with a specified dimensional coefficient, excluding side-weir behavior, submergence and two-dimensional street flow. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Exceedance overflow and routes” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=Cw bH^1.5，Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s、堰寬b=2.0 m、水頭H=0.30 m，Q=0.5587 m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=Cw bH^1.5, Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s, width b=2.0 m and head H=0.30 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「超量溢流與越頂路徑」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Exceedance overflow and routes”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-17-k1","title":"超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證","titleEn":"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification","text":"滯洪池遇到超過控制出口能力的事件時，需要辨認水會流向何處，正常出流設計不能代表超量情境。溢流堰流量與堰頂以上水頭呈非線性，來流速度、淹沒與側向幾何會改變係數；更重要的是溢出後的路徑和受影響空間，不能只證明池內水位降低而忽略下游風險。","textEn":"When an event exceeds the controlled outlet, the overflow destination matters; normal-release design does not represent exceedance behavior. Weir flow is nonlinear in head above crest, and approach velocity, submergence and lateral geometry alter the coefficient.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。","透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。","滯洪池遇到超過控制出口能力的事件時，需要辨認水會流向何處，正常出流設計不能代表超量情境。"],"optionsEn":["An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis.","A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage.","When an event exceeds the controlled outlet, the overflow destination matters; normal-release design does not represent exceedance behavior."],"answer":2,"explanation":"滯洪池遇到超過控制出口能力的事件時，需要辨認水會流向何處，正常出流設計不能代表超量情境。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When an event exceeds the controlled outlet, the overflow destination matters; normal-release design does not represent exceedance behavior. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b271-v15-18","title":"超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「超量溢流與越頂路徑」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Exceedance overflow and routes” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=Cw bH^1.5，Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s、堰寬b=2.0 m、水頭H=0.30 m，Q=0.5587 m³/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=Cw bH^1.5, Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s, width b=2.0 m and head H=0.30 m. Overflow Q=0.5587 m³/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：測量堰頂、相鄰低點和下游路徑，核對流量係數及淹沒範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey crest, adjacent low points and downstream routes, checking coefficient basis and submergence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=Cw bH^1.5，Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s、堰寬b=2.0 m、水頭H=0.30 m，Q=0.5587 m³/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=Cw bH^1.5, Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s, width b=2.0 m and head H=0.30 m. Overflow Q=0.5587 m³/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=Cw bH^1.5，Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s、堰寬b=2.0 m、水頭H=0.30 m，Q=0.5587 m³/s。","每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。","模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=Cw bH^1.5, Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s, width b=2.0 m and head H=0.30 m.","Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus.","A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=Cw bH^1.5，Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s、堰寬b=2.0 m、水頭H=0.30 m，Q=0.5587 m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=Cw bH^1.5, Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s, width b=2.0 m and head H=0.30 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b271-v15-19","title":"超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「超量溢流與越頂路徑」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Exceedance overflow and routes” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"測量堰頂、相鄰低點和下游路徑，核對流量係數及淹沒範圍。以超量事件追蹤地面流向和深度，確認出口不導向脆弱空間，並保留正常出口堵塞時的獨立情境。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey crest, adjacent low points and downstream routes, checking coefficient basis and submergence. Track surface direction and depth during exceedance, verifying that overflow does not lead toward vulnerable spaces, and retain a separate scenario for blockage of the normal outlet. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在地形圖標出設計溢流口和其他低點，為同一水位比較可能先出流的位置。用簡化堰式計算後，列出仍需地表流模型回答的深度與速度問題。","observationEn":"Site practice: Mark the designed overflow and other low points on a terrain map and compare which can spill first at one stage. After a weir calculation, identify depth and velocity questions still requiring surface-flow analysis.","failure":"注意干擾：把溢流量視為無害排出會漏掉街道或地下室的暴露，忽略鄰近較低缺口則可能使實際溢流繞過設計堰；下游回水還能降低溢流能力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating overflow as harmless removal overlooks street or basement exposure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"測量堰頂、相鄰低點和下游路徑，核對流量係數及淹沒範圍。以超量事件追蹤地面流向和深度，確認出口不導向脆弱空間，並保留正常出口堵塞時的獨立情境。","textEn":"Survey crest, adjacent low points and downstream routes, checking coefficient basis and submergence. Track surface direction and depth during exceedance, verifying that overflow does not lead toward vulnerable spaces, and retain a separate scenario for blockage of the normal outlet.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在地形圖標出設計溢流口和其他低點，為同一水位比較可能先出流的位置。用簡化堰式計算後，列出仍需地表流模型回答的深度與速度問題。","textEn":"Mark the designed overflow and other low points on a terrain map and compare which can spill first at one stage. After a weir calculation, identify depth and velocity questions still requiring surface-flow analysis.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","測量堰頂、相鄰低點和下游路徑，核對流量係數及淹沒範圍。","所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Survey crest, adjacent low points and downstream routes, checking coefficient basis and submergence.","Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"測量堰頂、相鄰低點和下游路徑，核對流量係數及淹沒範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey crest, adjacent low points and downstream routes, checking coefficient basis and submergence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b271-v15-20","title":"超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「超量溢流與越頂路徑」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Exceedance overflow and routes” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把溢流量視為無害排出會漏掉街道或地下室的暴露，忽略鄰近較低缺口則可能使實際溢流繞過設計堰；下游回水還能降低溢流能力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating overflow as harmless removal overlooks street or basement exposure. A nearby lower gap may bypass the intended weir, and downstream backwater can further reduce the available overflow capacity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例用指定係數的自由矩形堰比較，係數已包含單位；未模擬側堰、淹沒或街道二維流動。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The example uses a free rectangular weir with a specified dimensional coefficient, excluding side-weir behavior, submergence and two-dimensional street flow.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把溢流量視為無害排出會漏掉街道或地下室的暴露，忽略鄰近較低缺口則可能使實際溢流繞過設計堰；下游回水還能降低溢流能力。","textEn":"Treating overflow as harmless removal overlooks street or basement exposure. A nearby lower gap may bypass the intended weir, and downstream backwater can further reduce the available overflow capacity.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。","把溢流量視為無害排出會漏掉街道或地下室的暴露，忽略鄰近較低缺口則可能使實際溢流繞過設計堰；下游回水還能降低溢流能力。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage.","Treating overflow as harmless removal overlooks street or basement exposure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把溢流量視為無害排出會漏掉街道或地下室的暴露，忽略鄰近較低缺口則可能使實際溢流繞過設計堰；下游回水還能降低溢流能力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating overflow as harmless removal overlooks street or basement exposure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b271-v15-21","title":"滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「滲透折減與前期飽和」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"透水滯洪池可讓部分水進入地層，但滲透能力會受到前期含水、地下水位、細粒堵塞與土層連續性控制。短時間現地試驗不能直接代表長期暴雨條件，尤其地下水接近池底時，向下水力梯度可能減小；將滲透當作永遠固定的額外出口，可能低估連續降雨所需庫容。本例使用指定均勻入滲速率作體積尺度，沒有採用實測保證值；飽和、污染控制或襯底條件可能使可計入滲透為零。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「滲透折減與前期飽和」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A permeable basin can infiltrate some water, but antecedent wetness, groundwater, fine-particle clogging and stratigraphy control that capacity. A short field test does not necessarily represent prolonged rainfall, particularly when groundwater approaches the floor and downward gradient weakens. Treating infiltration as a permanently fixed extra outlet can understate storage needed during successive storms. The example uses a specified uniform infiltration rate as a volume scale, not a guaranteed field value. Saturation, contamination controls or lining may reduce creditable infiltration to zero. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設有效池底A=1000 m²、入滲率f=5 mm/h、時間t=2 h，滲透體積Vi=Aft=10.0 m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective floor A=1000 m², infiltration f=5 mm/h and duration t=2 h.","failure":"常見誤解：「透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「滲透折減與前期飽和」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-21-k1","title":"滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證","titleEn":"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification","text":"透水滯洪池可讓部分水進入地層，但滲透能力會受到前期含水、地下水位、細粒堵塞與土層連續性控制。短時間現地試驗不能直接代表長期暴雨條件，尤其地下水接近池底時，向下水力梯度可能減小；將滲透當作永遠固定的額外出口，可能低估連續降雨所需庫容。","textEn":"A permeable basin can infiltrate some water, but antecedent wetness, groundwater, fine-particle clogging and stratigraphy control that capacity. A short field test does not necessarily represent prolonged rainfall, particularly when groundwater approaches the floor and downward gradient weakens.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["透水滯洪池可讓部分水進入地層，但滲透能力會受到前期含水、地下水位、細粒堵塞與土層連續性控制。","透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。","孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。"],"optionsEn":["A permeable basin can infiltrate some water, but antecedent wetness, groundwater, fine-particle clogging and stratigraphy control that capacity.","A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage.","Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release."],"answer":0,"explanation":"透水滯洪池可讓部分水進入地層，但滲透能力會受到前期含水、地下水位、細粒堵塞與土層連續性控制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A permeable basin can infiltrate some water, but antecedent wetness, groundwater, fine-particle clogging and stratigraphy control that capacity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b271-v15-22","title":"滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「滲透折減與前期飽和」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設有效池底A=1000 m²、入滲率f=5 mm/h、時間t=2 h，滲透體積Vi=Aft=10.0 m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective floor A=1000 m², infiltration f=5 mm/h and duration t=2 h. Infiltrated volume Vi=Aft=10.0 m³. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在代表土層與季節進行入滲和地下水觀測，將試驗持續時間、前期含水與堵塞狀態記錄完整。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Observe infiltration and groundwater in representative strata and seasons, documenting test duration, antecedent wetness and clogging state.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設有效池底A=1000 m²、入滲率f=5 mm/h、時間t=2 h，滲透體積Vi=Aft=10.0 m³。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective floor A=1000 m², infiltration f=5 mm/h and duration t=2 h. Infiltrated volume Vi=Aft=10.0 m³.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設有效池底A=1000 m²、入滲率f=5 mm/h、時間t=2 h，滲透體積Vi=Aft=10.0 m³。","知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。"],"optionsEn":["A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective floor A=1000 m², infiltration f=5 mm/h and duration t=2 h.","Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設有效池底A=1000 m²、入滲率f=5 mm/h、時間t=2 h，滲透體積Vi=Aft=10.0 m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective floor A=1000 m², infiltration f=5 mm/h and duration t=2 h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b271-v15-23","title":"滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「滲透折減與前期飽和」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在代表土層與季節進行入滲和地下水觀測，將試驗持續時間、前期含水與堵塞狀態記錄完整。比較可計入與零滲透兩個情境，並確認水質或襯底需求不與假設滲透功能衝突。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Observe infiltration and groundwater in representative strata and seasons, documenting test duration, antecedent wetness and clogging state. Compare credited-infiltration and zero-infiltration cases, checking that water-quality or lining requirements do not contradict the infiltration function assumed by the storage model. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把指定滲透體積與事件逕流體積比較，判斷它在此假設下的相對影響。將入滲設為零重新演算，說明哪些場地證據才能支持恢復部分折減。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare the specified infiltration volume with event runoff to assess its relative influence under these assumptions. Rerun with zero infiltration and identify site evidence needed before restoring any infiltration credit.","failure":"注意干擾：以乾季初始入滲率外推連續暴雨會高估損失，孔隙堵塞又可能逐年降低能力；只計入滲優點而未檢查地下水與水質，會形成不完整的工程比較。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Extrapolating dry-season initial infiltration through prolonged storms overstates losses, while clogging can reduce performance over years. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在代表土層與季節進行入滲和地下水觀測，將試驗持續時間、前期含水與堵塞狀態記錄完整。比較可計入與零滲透兩個情境，並確認水質或襯底需求不與假設滲透功能衝突。","textEn":"Observe infiltration and groundwater in representative strata and seasons, documenting test duration, antecedent wetness and clogging state. Compare credited-infiltration and zero-infiltration cases, checking that water-quality or lining requirements do not contradict the infiltration function assumed by the storage model.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把指定滲透體積與事件逕流體積比較，判斷它在此假設下的相對影響。將入滲設為零重新演算，說明哪些場地證據才能支持恢復部分折減。","textEn":"Compare the specified infiltration volume with event runoff to assess its relative influence under these assumptions. Rerun with zero infiltration and identify site evidence needed before restoring any infiltration credit.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。","在代表土層與季節進行入滲和地下水觀測，將試驗持續時間、前期含水與堵塞狀態記錄完整。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage.","Observe infiltration and groundwater in representative strata and seasons, documenting test duration, antecedent wetness and clogging state."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在代表土層與季節進行入滲和地下水觀測，將試驗持續時間、前期含水與堵塞狀態記錄完整。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Observe infiltration and groundwater in representative strata and seasons, documenting test duration, antecedent wetness and clogging state. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b271-v15-24","title":"滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「滲透折減與前期飽和」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以乾季初始入滲率外推連續暴雨會高估損失，孔隙堵塞又可能逐年降低能力；只計入滲優點而未檢查地下水與水質，會形成不完整的工程比較。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Extrapolating dry-season initial infiltration through prolonged storms overstates losses, while clogging can reduce performance over years. Counting infiltration benefits without groundwater and water-quality checks produces an incomplete engineering comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例使用指定均勻入滲速率作體積尺度，沒有採用實測保證值；飽和、污染控制或襯底條件可能使可計入滲透為零。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Saturation, contamination controls or lining may reduce creditable infiltration to zero.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以乾季初始入滲率外推連續暴雨會高估損失，孔隙堵塞又可能逐年降低能力；只計入滲優點而未檢查地下水與水質，會形成不完整的工程比較。","textEn":"Extrapolating dry-season initial infiltration through prolonged storms overstates losses, while clogging can reduce performance over years. Counting infiltration benefits without groundwater and water-quality checks produces an incomplete engineering comparison.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["以乾季初始入滲率外推連續暴雨會高估損失，孔隙堵塞又可能逐年降低能力；只計入滲優點而未檢查地下水與水質，會形成不完整的工程比較。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。"],"optionsEn":["Extrapolating dry-season initial infiltration through prolonged storms overstates losses, while clogging can reduce performance over years.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以乾季初始入滲率外推連續暴雨會高估損失，孔隙堵塞又可能逐年降低能力；只計入滲優點而未檢查地下水與水質，會形成不完整的工程比較。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Extrapolating dry-season initial infiltration through prolonged storms overstates losses, while clogging can reduce performance over years. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b271-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「變水頭排空時間機理與驗證」與「下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification\" and \"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b271-v15-25","title":"變水頭排空時間機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「變水頭排空時間」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drawdown under changing head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"孔口排水會隨水位下降而減慢，因此以初始最大出流除池容會低估排空時間。若後續降雨在池尚未恢復容量時到達，前一場殘留水會改變下一場峰值；排空策略需同時考慮下游容許出流和連續事件，而非只追求單場暴雨結束後最快放空。本例池面積固定、無入流與滲透、自由孔口小到可用孔心水頭近似，積分到仍為正的水頭；不外推到孔口部分露出階段。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「變水頭排空時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Orifice release slows as stage falls, so dividing storage by the initial maximum discharge understates drawdown time. A second storm arriving before recovery encounters less available storage. Drawdown planning must therefore consider downstream release constraints and successive events rather than simply emptying as quickly as possible after one storm. The example assumes constant basin area, no inflow or infiltration and a small free orifice described by center head, integrating only to a positive head before partial uncovering. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drawdown under changing head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池面積Ab=1000 m²、Cd=0.62、孔面a=0.10 m²、h1=2.0、h2=0.20 m，t=2Ab(√h1−√h2)/(Cd a√(2g))=7042 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume basin Ab=1000 m², Cd=0.62, orifice a=0.10 m², h1=2.0, h2=0.20 m and g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「變水頭排空時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drawdown under changing head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-25-k1","title":"變水頭排空時間機理與驗證","titleEn":"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification","text":"孔口排水會隨水位下降而減慢，因此以初始最大出流除池容會低估排空時間。若後續降雨在池尚未恢復容量時到達，前一場殘留水會改變下一場峰值；排空策略需同時考慮下游容許出流和連續事件，而非只追求單場暴雨結束後最快放空。","textEn":"Orifice release slows as stage falls, so dividing storage by the initial maximum discharge understates drawdown time. A second storm arriving before recovery encounters less available storage.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「變水頭排空時間機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。","孔口排水會隨水位下降而減慢，因此以初始最大出流除池容會低估排空時間。","每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。"],"optionsEn":["Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release.","Orifice release slows as stage falls, so dividing storage by the initial maximum discharge understates drawdown time.","Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus."],"answer":1,"explanation":"孔口排水會隨水位下降而減慢，因此以初始最大出流除池容會低估排空時間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Orifice release slows as stage falls, so dividing storage by the initial maximum discharge understates drawdown time. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b271-v15-26","title":"變水頭排空時間機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「變水頭排空時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drawdown under changing head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池面積Ab=1000 m²、Cd=0.62、孔面a=0.10 m²、h1=2.0、h2=0.20 m，t=2Ab(√h1−√h2)/(Cd a√(2g))=7042 s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume basin Ab=1000 m², Cd=0.62, orifice a=0.10 m², h1=2.0, h2=0.20 m and g=9.81 m/s². Drawdown t=7042 s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用不同水位下實測出流檢查孔口關係，核對排空期間是否仍有管網入流或尾水抬升。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check the outlet relation using measured releases at several stages and identify continuing network inflow or rising tailwater during drawdown.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池面積Ab=1000 m²、Cd=0.62、孔面a=0.10 m²、h1=2.0、h2=0.20 m，t=2Ab(√h1−√h2)/(Cd a√(2g))=7042 s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume basin Ab=1000 m², Cd=0.62, orifice a=0.10 m², h1=2.0, h2=0.20 m and g=9.81 m/s². Drawdown t=7042 s.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「變水頭排空時間機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。","所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池面積Ab=1000 m²、Cd=0.62、孔面a=0.10 m²、h1=2.0、h2=0.20 m，t=2Ab(√h1−√h2)/(Cd a√(2g))=7042 s。"],"optionsEn":["A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision.","Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume basin Ab=1000 m², Cd=0.62, orifice a=0.10 m², h1=2.0, h2=0.20 m and g=9.81 m/s²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池面積Ab=1000 m²、Cd=0.62、孔面a=0.10 m²、h1=2.0、h2=0.20 m，t=2Ab(√h1−√h2)/(Cd a√(2g))=7042 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume basin Ab=1000 m², Cd=0.62, orifice a=0.10 m², h1=2.0, h2=0.20 m and g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b271-v15-27","title":"變水頭排空時間機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「變水頭排空時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drawdown under changing head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用不同水位下實測出流檢查孔口關係，核對排空期間是否仍有管網入流或尾水抬升。比較積分解與逐步演算，並確認終止水頭仍符合孔口完整淹沒的幾何假設。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check the outlet relation using measured releases at several stages and identify continuing network inflow or rising tailwater during drawdown. Compare the integrated solution with stepwise routing, verifying that the final head still satisfies the assumed geometry of a fully covered opening. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較固定初始流量估計與變水頭積分結果，畫出排水逐漸減慢的曲線。讓第二場雨在恢復前到達，指出演算必須保留的初始儲量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare a fixed-initial-flow estimate with changing-head integration and plot the slowing release. Introduce a second storm before recovery and identify the initial storage that must carry into the new routing calculation.","failure":"注意干擾：以初始流量當全程固定會低估恢復容量所需時間，忽略尾水或再降雨更會過度樂觀；積分到孔口露出後仍沿用同式，則超出原有流況。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Holding the initial discharge constant understates recovery time, and omitted tailwater or renewed rainfall makes it more optimistic. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用不同水位下實測出流檢查孔口關係，核對排空期間是否仍有管網入流或尾水抬升。比較積分解與逐步演算，並確認終止水頭仍符合孔口完整淹沒的幾何假設。","textEn":"Check the outlet relation using measured releases at several stages and identify continuing network inflow or rising tailwater during drawdown. Compare the integrated solution with stepwise routing, verifying that the final head still satisfies the assumed geometry of a fully covered opening.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較固定初始流量估計與變水頭積分結果，畫出排水逐漸減慢的曲線。讓第二場雨在恢復前到達，指出演算必須保留的初始儲量。","textEn":"Compare a fixed-initial-flow estimate with changing-head integration and plot the slowing release. Introduce a second storm before recovery and identify the initial storage that must carry into the new routing calculation.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「變水頭排空時間機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification\"?","options":["用不同水位下實測出流檢查孔口關係，核對排空期間是否仍有管網入流或尾水抬升。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。"],"optionsEn":["Check the outlet relation using measured releases at several stages and identify continuing network inflow or rising tailwater during drawdown.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用不同水位下實測出流檢查孔口關係，核對排空期間是否仍有管網入流或尾水抬升。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check the outlet relation using measured releases at several stages and identify continuing network inflow or rising tailwater during drawdown. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b271-v15-28","title":"變水頭排空時間機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「變水頭排空時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drawdown under changing head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以初始流量當全程固定會低估恢復容量所需時間，忽略尾水或再降雨更會過度樂觀；積分到孔口露出後仍沿用同式，則超出原有流況。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Holding the initial discharge constant understates recovery time, and omitted tailwater or renewed rainfall makes it more optimistic. Continuing the same equation after the opening becomes exposed extends it beyond the assumed flow regime. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例池面積固定、無入流與滲透、自由孔口小到可用孔心水頭近似，積分到仍為正的水頭；不外推到孔口部分露出階段。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The example assumes constant basin area, no inflow or infiltration and a small free orifice described by center head, integrating only to a positive head before partial uncovering.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以初始流量當全程固定會低估恢復容量所需時間，忽略尾水或再降雨更會過度樂觀；積分到孔口露出後仍沿用同式，則超出原有流況。","textEn":"Holding the initial discharge constant understates recovery time, and omitted tailwater or renewed rainfall makes it more optimistic. Continuing the same equation after the opening becomes exposed extends it beyond the assumed flow regime.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「變水頭排空時間機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","以初始流量當全程固定會低估恢復容量所需時間，忽略尾水或再降雨更會過度樂觀；積分到孔口露出後仍沿用同式，則超出原有流況。","每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Holding the initial discharge constant understates recovery time, and omitted tailwater or renewed rainfall makes it more optimistic.","Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以初始流量當全程固定會低估恢復容量所需時間，忽略尾水或再降雨更會過度樂觀；積分到孔口露出後仍沿用同式，則超出原有流況。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Holding the initial discharge constant understates recovery time, and omitted tailwater or renewed rainfall makes it more optimistic. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b271-v15-29","title":"下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「下游匯流與峰值錯時」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Downstream combination and peak timing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"單一池出口削峰不一定降低流域最下游峰值，因延後的出流可能剛好與另一支流洪峰重疊。配置池址和出流歷線時應在共同時間軸上做河網演算，不能把各支流最大值不加區分地相加；也不能只比較工程前後同一個時刻而忽略新峰值出現時間。本例在匯流點忽略傳播延遲與局部儲水，只示範同時流量相加；完整流域需先把各歷線演算至同一位置。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「下游匯流與峰值錯時」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Attenuation at one basin outlet does not necessarily reduce the furthest downstream peak: delayed release may coincide with another tributary crest. Basin siting and release hydrographs require routing on a shared time axis. Adding separate maxima ignores timing, while comparing only one preselected instant can miss a new peak occurring later. The example neglects travel time and local storage at a junction and demonstrates only simultaneous addition. Full-basin work must route each hydrograph to the same location first. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Downstream combination and peak timing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩支流在時刻t1為8與2 m³/s、t2為3與7 m³/s，兩時刻合流皆10 m³/s；各自峰值相加15 m³/s並非同時峰值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume tributaries are 8 and 2 m³/s at t1, then 3 and 7 m³/s at t2.","failure":"常見誤解：「每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「下游匯流與峰值錯時」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Downstream combination and peak timing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-29-k1","title":"下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證","titleEn":"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification","text":"單一池出口削峰不一定降低流域最下游峰值，因延後的出流可能剛好與另一支流洪峰重疊。配置池址和出流歷線時應在共同時間軸上做河網演算，不能把各支流最大值不加區分地相加；也不能只比較工程前後同一個時刻而忽略新峰值出現時間。","textEn":"Attenuation at one basin outlet does not necessarily reduce the furthest downstream peak: delayed release may coincide with another tributary crest. Basin siting and release hydrographs require routing on a shared time axis.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。","只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。","單一池出口削峰不一定降低流域最下游峰值，因延後的出流可能剛好與另一支流洪峰重疊。"],"optionsEn":["Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus.","A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance.","Attenuation at one basin outlet does not necessarily reduce the furthest downstream peak: delayed release may coincide with another tributary crest."],"answer":2,"explanation":"單一池出口削峰不一定降低流域最下游峰值，因延後的出流可能剛好與另一支流洪峰重疊。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Attenuation at one basin outlet does not necessarily reduce the furthest downstream peak: delayed release may coincide with another tributary crest. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b271-v15-30","title":"下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「下游匯流與峰值錯時」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Downstream combination and peak timing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩支流在時刻t1為8與2 m³/s、t2為3與7 m³/s，兩時刻合流皆10 m³/s；各自峰值相加15 m³/s並非同時峰值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume tributaries are 8 and 2 m³/s at t1, then 3 and 7 m³/s at t2. Both totals are 10 m³/s; adding separate peaks gives 15 m³/s without concurrence. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將各支流與池出口時間戳統一並校核傳播時間，在匯流點比較完整工程前後歷線。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align tributary and basin-outlet timestamps and verify travel times before comparing complete pre- and post-project hydrographs at the junction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩支流在時刻t1為8與2 m³/s、t2為3與7 m³/s，兩時刻合流皆10 m³/s；各自峰值相加15 m³/s並非同時峰值。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume tributaries are 8 and 2 m³/s at t1, then 3 and 7 m³/s at t2. Both totals are 10 m³/s; adding separate peaks gives 15 m³/s without concurrence.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩支流在時刻t1為8與2 m³/s、t2為3與7 m³/s，兩時刻合流皆10 m³/s。","知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。","池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume tributaries are 8 and 2 m³/s at t1, then 3 and 7 m³/s at t2.","Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity.","Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩支流在時刻t1為8與2 m³/s、t2為3與7 m³/s，兩時刻合流皆10 m³/s；各自峰值相加15 m³/s並非同時峰值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume tributaries are 8 and 2 m³/s at t1, then 3 and 7 m³/s at t2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b271-v15-31","title":"下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「下游匯流與峰值錯時」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Downstream combination and peak timing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將各支流與池出口時間戳統一並校核傳播時間，在匯流點比較完整工程前後歷線。檢查峰值時刻、持續時間及受納水位，而不是只記錄池出口的單一削峰百分比。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align tributary and basin-outlet timestamps and verify travel times before comparing complete pre- and post-project hydrographs at the junction. Examine crest timing, duration and receiving stage instead of reporting only one attenuation percentage measured at the basin outlet. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把一支出流歷線平移一個時間步，重新計算匯流而不改總體積。比較局部峰值和下游峰值，說明時間配置為何是池址規劃的一部分。","observationEn":"Site practice: Shift one release hydrograph by one step without changing volume and recompute junction flow. Compare local and downstream peaks, explaining why temporal alignment is part of basin planning rather than a secondary plotting detail.","failure":"注意干擾：延遲出流若與另一支流同時達峰，可能把局部改善轉成下游負擔；直接加各峰值會高估某些情境，但忽略時間變化也可能漏掉真正最不利組合。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Delayed release can coincide with another tributary crest and transfer a local improvement downstream. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將各支流與池出口時間戳統一並校核傳播時間，在匯流點比較完整工程前後歷線。檢查峰值時刻、持續時間及受納水位，而不是只記錄池出口的單一削峰百分比。","textEn":"Align tributary and basin-outlet timestamps and verify travel times before comparing complete pre- and post-project hydrographs at the junction. Examine crest timing, duration and receiving stage instead of reporting only one attenuation percentage measured at the basin outlet.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把一支出流歷線平移一個時間步，重新計算匯流而不改總體積。比較局部峰值和下游峰值，說明時間配置為何是池址規劃的一部分。","textEn":"Shift one release hydrograph by one step without changing volume and recompute junction flow. Compare local and downstream peaks, explaining why temporal alignment is part of basin planning rather than a secondary plotting detail.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將各支流與池出口時間戳統一並校核傳播時間，在匯流點比較完整工程前後歷線。","只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Align tributary and basin-outlet timestamps and verify travel times before comparing complete pre- and post-project hydrographs at the junction.","An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將各支流與池出口時間戳統一並校核傳播時間，在匯流點比較完整工程前後歷線。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align tributary and basin-outlet timestamps and verify travel times before comparing complete pre- and post-project hydrographs at the junction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b271-v15-32","title":"下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「下游匯流與峰值錯時」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Downstream combination and peak timing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"延遲出流若與另一支流同時達峰，可能把局部改善轉成下游負擔；直接加各峰值會高估某些情境，但忽略時間變化也可能漏掉真正最不利組合。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Delayed release can coincide with another tributary crest and transfer a local improvement downstream. Adding separate maxima overstates some scenarios, but ignoring changing timing can also miss the truly unfavorable combination. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例在匯流點忽略傳播延遲與局部儲水，只示範同時流量相加；完整流域需先把各歷線演算至同一位置。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Full-basin work must route each hydrograph to the same location first.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"延遲出流若與另一支流同時達峰，可能把局部改善轉成下游負擔；直接加各峰值會高估某些情境，但忽略時間變化也可能漏掉真正最不利組合。","textEn":"Delayed release can coincide with another tributary crest and transfer a local improvement downstream. Adding separate maxima overstates some scenarios, but ignoring changing timing can also miss the truly unfavorable combination.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。","延遲出流若與另一支流同時達峰，可能把局部改善轉成下游負擔；直接加各峰值會高估某些情境，但忽略時間變化也可能漏掉真正最不利組合。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance.","Delayed release can coincide with another tributary crest and transfer a local improvement downstream."],"answer":2,"explanation":"延遲出流若與另一支流同時達峰，可能把局部改善轉成下游負擔；直接加各峰值會高估某些情境，但忽略時間變化也可能漏掉真正最不利組合。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Delayed release can coincide with another tributary crest and transfer a local improvement downstream. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b271-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證」與「數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification\" and \"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b271-v15-33","title":"沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「沉積與可用容量維持」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sediment and retained capacity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"滯洪池會接收顆粒與垃圾，沉積不僅占去容積，也可能堵塞出口或改變入流分配。總容量衰減與局部水力失效是不同路徑，平均薄層估算不能代表出口附近的堆積；維護應以測量、出流能力和可清理性共同評估，而不是等到池完全填滿才處理。本例沉積層厚度均勻且直接扣除有效容積，未模擬固結或出流堵塞；真實局部影響可能比體積比例更早主導。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沉積與可用容量維持」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Detention basins receive particles and debris that occupy volume, obstruct outlets and redistribute incoming flow. Bulk storage loss and localized hydraulic failure are different mechanisms, and a mean thin-layer estimate does not represent deposits near an outlet. Maintenance should combine survey, outlet performance and cleaning access rather than wait until the entire basin fills. The example subtracts a uniform deposit layer from usable storage without consolidation or outlet blockage. Local hydraulic effects may govern before the bulk volume fraction becomes large. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sediment and retained capacity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池底A=1000 m²、平均沉積厚度d=0.15 m，損失Vd=Ad=150 m³；原可用2400 m³剩2250 m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume floor A=1000 m² and mean deposit thickness d=0.15 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沉積與可用容量維持」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sediment and retained capacity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-33-k1","title":"沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證","titleEn":"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification","text":"滯洪池會接收顆粒與垃圾，沉積不僅占去容積，也可能堵塞出口或改變入流分配。總容量衰減與局部水力失效是不同路徑，平均薄層估算不能代表出口附近的堆積；維護應以測量、出流能力和可清理性共同評估，而不是等到池完全填滿才處理。","textEn":"Detention basins receive particles and debris that occupy volume, obstruct outlets and redistribute incoming flow. Bulk storage loss and localized hydraulic failure are different mechanisms, and a mean thin-layer estimate does not represent deposits near an outlet.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["滯洪池會接收顆粒與垃圾，沉積不僅占去容積，也可能堵塞出口或改變入流分配。","只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。","模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。"],"optionsEn":["Detention basins receive particles and debris that occupy volume, obstruct outlets and redistribute incoming flow.","A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance.","A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision."],"answer":0,"explanation":"滯洪池會接收顆粒與垃圾，沉積不僅占去容積，也可能堵塞出口或改變入流分配。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Detention basins receive particles and debris that occupy volume, obstruct outlets and redistribute incoming flow. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b271-v15-34","title":"沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沉積與可用容量維持」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sediment and retained capacity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池底A=1000 m²、平均沉積厚度d=0.15 m，損失Vd=Ad=150 m³；原可用2400 m³剩2250 m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume floor A=1000 m² and mean deposit thickness d=0.15 m. Lost Vd=Ad=150 m³; initial usable 2400 m³ becomes 2250 m³. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以固定基準測深並標出出口附近的局部堆積，將清淤量與容積曲線更新對帳。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey deposits on a fixed datum and map local buildup near the outlet, reconciling removed volume with the updated storage curve.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池底A=1000 m²、平均沉積厚度d=0.15 m，損失Vd=Ad=150 m³；原可用2400 m³剩2250 m³。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume floor A=1000 m² and mean deposit thickness d=0.15 m. Lost Vd=Ad=150 m³; initial usable 2400 m³ becomes 2250 m³.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池底A=1000 m²、平均沉積厚度d=0.15 m，損失Vd=Ad=150 m³。","孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。"],"optionsEn":["Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume floor A=1000 m² and mean deposit thickness d=0.15 m.","Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池底A=1000 m²、平均沉積厚度d=0.15 m，損失Vd=Ad=150 m³；原可用2400 m³剩2250 m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume floor A=1000 m² and mean deposit thickness d=0.15 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b271-v15-35","title":"沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沉積與可用容量維持」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sediment and retained capacity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以固定基準測深並標出出口附近的局部堆積，將清淤量與容積曲線更新對帳。另測正常出口能力及垃圾攔截狀態，確認容量恢復和水力通暢都已驗證而非只完成清理作業。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey deposits on a fixed datum and map local buildup near the outlet, reconciling removed volume with the updated storage curve. Independently check normal-release capacity and debris control so that both recovered storage and hydraulic openness are verified, not merely the completion of cleaning work. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較均勻沉積和集中堵住孔口兩種同體積情境，分別更新池容與出流關係。說明為何維護績效需要容量和水力兩個指標，而不是只報清出重量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare uniform deposition with the same volume concentrated at the orifice, updating storage and release relations separately. Explain why maintenance performance needs both capacity and hydraulic indicators rather than only removed mass.","failure":"注意干擾：只扣平均沉積容積會漏掉孔口先被堵塞的情況，未更新模型則持續高估可用池容；清淤若只移動泥砂到另一區，也不代表總有效容量已恢復。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Subtracting mean deposit volume misses an outlet blocked first, while an unchanged model continues to overstate storage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以固定基準測深並標出出口附近的局部堆積，將清淤量與容積曲線更新對帳。另測正常出口能力及垃圾攔截狀態，確認容量恢復和水力通暢都已驗證而非只完成清理作業。","textEn":"Survey deposits on a fixed datum and map local buildup near the outlet, reconciling removed volume with the updated storage curve. Independently check normal-release capacity and debris control so that both recovered storage and hydraulic openness are verified, not merely the completion of cleaning work.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較均勻沉積和集中堵住孔口兩種同體積情境，分別更新池容與出流關係。說明為何維護績效需要容量和水力兩個指標，而不是只報清出重量。","textEn":"Compare uniform deposition with the same volume concentrated at the orifice, updating storage and release relations separately. Explain why maintenance performance needs both capacity and hydraulic indicators rather than only removed mass.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。","以固定基準測深並標出出口附近的局部堆積，將清淤量與容積曲線更新對帳。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage.","Survey deposits on a fixed datum and map local buildup near the outlet, reconciling removed volume with the updated storage curve."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以固定基準測深並標出出口附近的局部堆積，將清淤量與容積曲線更新對帳。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey deposits on a fixed datum and map local buildup near the outlet, reconciling removed volume with the updated storage curve. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b271-v15-36","title":"沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沉積與可用容量維持」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sediment and retained capacity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只扣平均沉積容積會漏掉孔口先被堵塞的情況，未更新模型則持續高估可用池容；清淤若只移動泥砂到另一區，也不代表總有效容量已恢復。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Subtracting mean deposit volume misses an outlet blocked first, while an unchanged model continues to overstate storage. Moving sediment to another part of the basin does not necessarily restore total usable capacity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例沉積層厚度均勻且直接扣除有效容積，未模擬固結或出流堵塞；真實局部影響可能比體積比例更早主導。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Local hydraulic effects may govern before the bulk volume fraction becomes large.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只扣平均沉積容積會漏掉孔口先被堵塞的情況，未更新模型則持續高估可用池容；清淤若只移動泥砂到另一區，也不代表總有效容量已恢復。","textEn":"Subtracting mean deposit volume misses an outlet blocked first, while an unchanged model continues to overstate storage. Moving sediment to another part of the basin does not necessarily restore total usable capacity.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只扣平均沉積容積會漏掉孔口先被堵塞的情況，未更新模型則持續高估可用池容；清淤若只移動泥砂到另一區，也不代表總有效容量已恢復。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。"],"optionsEn":["Subtracting mean deposit volume misses an outlet blocked first, while an unchanged model continues to overstate storage.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只扣平均沉積容積會漏掉孔口先被堵塞的情況，未更新模型則持續高估可用池容；清淤若只移動泥砂到另一區，也不代表總有效容量已恢復。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Subtracting mean deposit volume misses an outlet blocked first, while an unchanged model continues to overstate storage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b271-v15-37","title":"數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「數值水量閉合與收斂」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Numerical closure and convergence” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雨洪模型的水量閉合檢查能發現漏列出流、時間積分或邊界處理問題，但閉合良好不代表洪峰位置或水位一定正確。粗網格和粗時間步可能保住總體積卻錯過短時高水位，錯誤糙率也能得到漂亮收支；因此守恆、時間收斂與獨立事件驗證應分開進行。本例殘差定義為入流減出流再減儲量增加，百分比以總入流作分母；正殘差只表示未解釋水量，並不直接指出物理漏水位置。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「數值水量閉合與收斂」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A water-balance check can reveal missing outlets, integration problems or boundary errors, but good closure does not prove correct peak timing or stage. Coarse grids and time steps can preserve volume while missing brief high water, and wrong roughness may still yield a neat balance. Conservation, temporal convergence and independent-event validation therefore require separate checks. Residual is inflow minus outflow minus storage increase, normalized by total inflow. A positive residual is unexplained water and does not locate a physical leak. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Numerical closure and convergence” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件入流Vi=10000 m³、出流Vo=7600 m³、儲量增ΔS=2350 m³，殘差R=50 m³，即入流的0.50%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event inflow Vi=10000 m³, outflow Vo=7600 m³ and storage increase ΔS=2350 m³.","failure":"常見誤解：「模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「數值水量閉合與收斂」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Numerical closure and convergence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-37-k1","title":"數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證","titleEn":"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification","text":"雨洪模型的水量閉合檢查能發現漏列出流、時間積分或邊界處理問題，但閉合良好不代表洪峰位置或水位一定正確。粗網格和粗時間步可能保住總體積卻錯過短時高水位，錯誤糙率也能得到漂亮收支；因此守恆、時間收斂與獨立事件驗證應分開進行。","textEn":"A water-balance check can reveal missing outlets, integration problems or boundary errors, but good closure does not prove correct peak timing or stage. Coarse grids and time steps can preserve volume while missing brief high water, and wrong roughness may still yield a neat balance.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。","雨洪模型的水量閉合檢查能發現漏列出流、時間積分或邊界處理問題，但閉合良好不代表洪峰位置或水位一定正確。","知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。"],"optionsEn":["A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision.","A water-balance check can reveal missing outlets, integration problems or boundary errors, but good closure does not prove correct peak timing or stage.","Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"雨洪模型的水量閉合檢查能發現漏列出流、時間積分或邊界處理問題，但閉合良好不代表洪峰位置或水位一定正確。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A water-balance check can reveal missing outlets, integration problems or boundary errors, but good closure does not prove correct peak timing or stage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b271-v15-38","title":"數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「數值水量閉合與收斂」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Numerical closure and convergence” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件入流Vi=10000 m³、出流Vo=7600 m³、儲量增ΔS=2350 m³，殘差R=50 m³，即入流的0.50%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event inflow Vi=10000 m³, outflow Vo=7600 m³ and storage increase ΔS=2350 m³. Residual R=50 m³, or 0.50% of inflow. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：列出所有水量項與正負號，核對初始儲量、溢流、滲透和反向流是否都有計入。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: List all terms with signs, checking initial storage, overflow, infiltration and reversed flow.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件入流Vi=10000 m³、出流Vo=7600 m³、儲量增ΔS=2350 m³，殘差R=50 m³，即入流的0.50%。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event inflow Vi=10000 m³, outflow Vo=7600 m³ and storage increase ΔS=2350 m³. Residual R=50 m³, or 0.50% of inflow.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。","只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件入流Vi=10000 m³、出流Vo=7600 m³、儲量增ΔS=2350 m³，殘差R=50 m³，即入流的0.50%。"],"optionsEn":["Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage.","An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event inflow Vi=10000 m³, outflow Vo=7600 m³ and storage increase ΔS=2350 m³."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件入流Vi=10000 m³、出流Vo=7600 m³、儲量增ΔS=2350 m³，殘差R=50 m³，即入流的0.50%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event inflow Vi=10000 m³, outflow Vo=7600 m³ and storage increase ΔS=2350 m³. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b271-v15-39","title":"數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「數值水量閉合與收斂」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Numerical closure and convergence” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"列出所有水量項與正負號，核對初始儲量、溢流、滲透和反向流是否都有計入。逐次縮小時間步比較最大水位和峰時，再以獨立事件檢查參數，避免只以殘差達標宣告模型有效。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"List all terms with signs, checking initial storage, overflow, infiltration and reversed flow. Progressively reduce time steps to compare maximum stage and peak time, then assess parameters against an independent event rather than declaring validity solely from a small residual. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：製作三種時間步的水量殘差與最大水位比較表，讓其中一種總量相近但漏掉尖峰。說明要保留哪幾項證據，才能同時支持守恆和峰值解析度。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare water residual and maximum stage at three time steps, including one that preserves volume but misses a sharp peak. Identify the evidence needed to support both conservation and adequate resolution of the maximum.","failure":"注意干擾：將未列溢流當數值誤差會掩蓋真實外排，反之把數值殘差當漏水又會誤導維護；只校正總體積而不查水位歷線，可能得到錯誤的池容配置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Calling omitted overflow numerical error hides actual discharge, while interpreting numerical residual as leakage misdirects maintenance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"列出所有水量項與正負號，核對初始儲量、溢流、滲透和反向流是否都有計入。逐次縮小時間步比較最大水位和峰時，再以獨立事件檢查參數，避免只以殘差達標宣告模型有效。","textEn":"List all terms with signs, checking initial storage, overflow, infiltration and reversed flow. Progressively reduce time steps to compare maximum stage and peak time, then assess parameters against an independent event rather than declaring validity solely from a small residual.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"製作三種時間步的水量殘差與最大水位比較表，讓其中一種總量相近但漏掉尖峰。說明要保留哪幾項證據，才能同時支持守恆和峰值解析度。","textEn":"Compare water residual and maximum stage at three time steps, including one that preserves volume but misses a sharp peak. Identify the evidence needed to support both conservation and adequate resolution of the maximum.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification\"?","options":["列出所有水量項與正負號，核對初始儲量、溢流、滲透和反向流是否都有計入。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。"],"optionsEn":["List all terms with signs, checking initial storage, overflow, infiltration and reversed flow.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release."],"answer":0,"explanation":"列出所有水量項與正負號，核對初始儲量、溢流、滲透和反向流是否都有計入。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"List all terms with signs, checking initial storage, overflow, infiltration and reversed flow. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b271-v15-40","title":"數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「數值水量閉合與收斂」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Numerical closure and convergence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將未列溢流當數值誤差會掩蓋真實外排，反之把數值殘差當漏水又會誤導維護；只校正總體積而不查水位歷線，可能得到錯誤的池容配置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Calling omitted overflow numerical error hides actual discharge, while interpreting numerical residual as leakage misdirects maintenance. Calibrating total volume without examining stage trajectories can produce the wrong basin configuration. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例殘差定義為入流減出流再減儲量增加，百分比以總入流作分母；正殘差只表示未解釋水量，並不直接指出物理漏水位置。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A positive residual is unexplained water and does not locate a physical leak.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將未列溢流當數值誤差會掩蓋真實外排，反之把數值殘差當漏水又會誤導維護；只校正總體積而不查水位歷線，可能得到錯誤的池容配置。","textEn":"Calling omitted overflow numerical error hides actual discharge, while interpreting numerical residual as leakage misdirects maintenance. Calibrating total volume without examining stage trajectories can produce the wrong basin configuration.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","將未列溢流當數值誤差會掩蓋真實外排，反之把數值殘差當漏水又會誤導維護；只校正總體積而不查水位歷線，可能得到錯誤的池容配置。","知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Calling omitted overflow numerical error hides actual discharge, while interpreting numerical residual as leakage misdirects maintenance.","Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將未列溢流當數值誤差會掩蓋真實外排，反之把數值殘差當漏水又會誤導維護；只校正總體積而不查水位歷線，可能得到錯誤的池容配置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Calling omitted overflow numerical error hides actual discharge, while interpreting numerical residual as leakage misdirects maintenance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b272","title":"河道分洪工程","titleEn":"River flood-diversion works","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"課程把分洪入口、渠段、收縮、尾水及重匯流視為同一系統，逐步計算流量、比能、臨界水深、波速與泥砂收支，再檢查高程餘量及數值解析度。紅河與元朗是已核對的實際工程背景，所有算例均為原創假設，並非這兩處的操作門檻或斷面設計。","summaryEn":"The course treats inlet, channel, contraction, tailwater and rejoining reach as one system, calculating discharge, specific energy, critical depth, wave speed and sediment budgets before checking elevation margins and numerical resolution. Red River and Yuen Long are verified project contexts. All numerical examples are original assumptions rather than their operating thresholds or section designs.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["分流入口","Diversion inlet"],["主河與繞道","Main river and bypass"],["局部控制","Local controls"],["出口回水","Outlet backwater"],["影響與驗證","Effects and verification"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["分流入口","主河與繞道","局部控制","出口回水","影響與驗證"],"labelsEn":["Diversion inlet","Main river and bypass","Local controls","Outlet backwater","Effects and verification"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"敏感度固定矩形渠寬20 m、水深2 m及能坡0.0004，只把曼寧糙率由0.030增至0.036 s/m^(1/3)。在這個固定幾何與能坡比較下，流量由37.49降至31.24 m³/s，減少16.67%。這不是說洪水流量固定時水位會同樣減少；若入流必須通過，水深與回水曲線會重新調整。植被、沉積與橋孔還可能同時改變有效幾何，所以實務敏感度應逐項隔離再合併情境，並檢查下游邊界是否仍適用。","textEn":"Hold rectangular width at 20 m, depth at 2 m and energy slope at 0.0004 while increasing Manning roughness from 0.030 to 0.036 s/m^(1/3). Under this fixed-geometry and fixed-slope comparison, flow falls from 37.49 to 31.24 m³/s, a 16.67% reduction. This does not mean stage falls proportionally when a fixed flood inflow must pass; depth and backwater must then adjust. Vegetation, deposits and bridge openings may also change effective geometry. Practical sensitivity work should isolate those effects before combining scenarios and recheck the receiving boundary throughout. Field observations should distinguish vegetation resistance from an actual reduction of channel area.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b272-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「分流控制體與受益範圍機理與驗證」與「入口門檻與自由溢流機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Diversion control volume and effects mechanism and verification\" and \"Inlet threshold and free overflow mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b272-v15-01","title":"分流控制體與受益範圍機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Diversion control volume and effects mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「分流控制體與受益範圍」如何影響河道分洪工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diversion control volume and effects” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River flood-diversion works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分洪道把部分洪水移至另一條路徑，並沒有消除水量，因此必須同時描述主河道、分洪道和重新匯流的受益與負擔。局部水位降低可能伴隨上游回水或出口負荷增加，跨區影響不能藏在模型邊界外；分流比例是水位、構造物和支路阻力共同求得的結果，而不是永遠固定的設計百分比。本例只作瞬時水量連續，假設分流節點沒有蓄水或其他支路；不由此推定任何河段水位或可接受的影響分配。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分流控制體與受益範圍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A floodway transfers water to another route rather than eliminating it, requiring assessment of the main channel, bypass and rejoining reach. Local stage reduction may accompany upstream backwater or greater outlet loading, and transferred effects must not be hidden outside model boundaries. Diversion fraction emerges from levels, structures and branch resistance rather than remaining a fixed design percentage. The example applies instantaneous continuity without junction storage or other branches. It determines neither reach stages nor an acceptable distribution of impacts. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diversion control volume and effects” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設上游Qin=400 m³/s、分洪Qb=120 m³/s，主河道Qm=Qin−Qb=280 m³/s，分流比30%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume upstream Qin=400 m³/s and bypass Qb=120 m³/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「分洪道把洪水帶離城市後，這部分水就不需要再納入下游分析。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once a floodway removes water from a city, that water no longer needs downstream analysis.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「分流控制體與受益範圍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diversion control volume and effects”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-01-k1","title":"分流控制體與受益範圍機理與驗證","titleEn":"Diversion control volume and effects mechanism and verification","text":"分洪道把部分洪水移至另一條路徑，並沒有消除水量，因此必須同時描述主河道、分洪道和重新匯流的受益與負擔。局部水位降低可能伴隨上游回水或出口負荷增加，跨區影響不能藏在模型邊界外；分流比例是水位、構造物和支路阻力共同求得的結果，而不是永遠固定的設計百分比。","textEn":"A floodway transfers water to another route rather than eliminating it, requiring assessment of the main channel, bypass and rejoining reach. Local stage reduction may accompany upstream backwater or greater outlet loading, and transferred effects must not be hidden outside model boundaries.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：分洪道把洪水帶離城市後，這部分水就不需要再納入下游分析。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once a floodway removes water from a city, that water no longer needs downstream analysis. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分流控制體與受益範圍機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Diversion control volume and effects mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["分洪道把洪水帶離城市後，這部分水就不需要再納入下游分析。","分洪道把部分洪水移至另一條路徑，並沒有消除水量，因此必須同時描述主河道、分洪道和重新匯流的受益與負擔。","所有分洪入口只需一個自由堰公式，不受入口方向與尾水影響。"],"optionsEn":["Once a floodway removes water from a city, that water no longer needs downstream analysis.","A floodway transfers water to another route rather than eliminating it, requiring assessment of the main channel, bypass and rejoining reach.","Every floodway inlet needs only one free-weir formula regardless of orientation or tailwater."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分洪道把部分洪水移至另一條路徑，並沒有消除水量，因此必須同時描述主河道、分洪道和重新匯流的受益與負擔。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A floodway transfers water to another route rather than eliminating it, requiring assessment of the main channel, bypass and rejoining reach. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b272-v15-02","title":"分流控制體與受益範圍機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Diversion control volume and effects mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「分流控制體與受益範圍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diversion control volume and effects” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設上游Qin=400 m³/s、分洪Qb=120 m³/s，主河道Qm=Qin−Qb=280 m³/s，分流比30%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume upstream Qin=400 m³/s and bypass Qb=120 m³/s. Main-channel Qm=Qin−Qb=280 m³/s, with a 30% diversion fraction. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將上下游與分洪入口流量同步對帳，確認量測區間內是否有河段蓄水或支流。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile upstream, downstream and bypass flows synchronously, identifying reach storage and tributaries within the measurement interval.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設上游Qin=400 m³/s、分洪Qb=120 m³/s，主河道Qm=Qin−Qb=280 m³/s，分流比30%。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume upstream Qin=400 m³/s and bypass Qb=120 m³/s. Main-channel Qm=Qin−Qb=280 m³/s, with a 30% diversion fraction.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「分流控制體與受益範圍機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Diversion control volume and effects mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["算出臨界水深後，就已經得到分洪道所有位置的正常水深。","分洪道只要向下游傾斜，下游漲水就不可能影響上游水位。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設上游Qin=400 m³/s、分洪Qb=120 m³/s，主河道Qm=Qin−Qb=280 m³/s，分流比30%。"],"optionsEn":["Calculating critical depth gives normal depth at every location in the floodway.","A floodway sloping downstream cannot experience upstream effects from rising tailwater.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume upstream Qin=400 m³/s and bypass Qb=120 m³/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設上游Qin=400 m³/s、分洪Qb=120 m³/s，主河道Qm=Qin−Qb=280 m³/s，分流比30%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume upstream Qin=400 m³/s and bypass Qb=120 m³/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b272-v15-03","title":"分流控制體與受益範圍機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Diversion control volume and effects mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「分流控制體與受益範圍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Diversion control volume and effects” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將上下游與分洪入口流量同步對帳，確認量測區間內是否有河段蓄水或支流。把主河、繞道與重匯流區列在同一評估邊界，分別比較水位、流量及受影響土地。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile upstream, downstream and bypass flows synchronously, identifying reach storage and tributaries within the measurement interval. Include the main river, bypass and rejoining area in one assessment boundary, comparing stage, discharge and affected land separately rather than reporting one local benefit. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出含重新匯流點的完整控制體，標記每股流量和可能儲水區。說明缺少哪個邊界會讓局部效益被誤認為全流域效益，再檢查合成水量帳。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw a complete control volume including the rejoining point, labeling flows and possible storage. Identify a missing boundary that could turn a local benefit into a misleading basin-wide claim, then reconcile the synthetic ledger.","failure":"注意干擾：只展示城市段降水位會漏掉其他地區的負擔，將分流比例固定則可能忽略尾水和入口控制；水量帳不閉合時，模型可能把外排錯當成消失的洪水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Showing only reduced city stage omits burdens elsewhere, while a fixed split can ignore tailwater and inlet control. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將上下游與分洪入口流量同步對帳，確認量測區間內是否有河段蓄水或支流。把主河、繞道與重匯流區列在同一評估邊界，分別比較水位、流量及受影響土地。","textEn":"Reconcile upstream, downstream and bypass flows synchronously, identifying reach storage and tributaries within the measurement interval. Include the main river, bypass and rejoining area in one assessment boundary, comparing stage, discharge and affected land separately rather than reporting one local benefit.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出含重新匯流點的完整控制體，標記每股流量和可能儲水區。說明缺少哪個邊界會讓局部效益被誤認為全流域效益，再檢查合成水量帳。","textEn":"Draw a complete control volume including the rejoining point, labeling flows and possible storage. Identify a missing boundary that could turn a local benefit into a misleading basin-wide claim, then reconcile the synthetic ledger.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「分流控制體與受益範圍機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Diversion control volume and effects mechanism and verification\"?","options":["將上下游與分洪入口流量同步對帳，確認量測區間內是否有河段蓄水或支流。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要水面沒有碰到堤頂，分洪道及兩側堤防就不存在失效可能。"],"optionsEn":["Reconcile upstream, downstream and bypass flows synchronously, identifying reach storage and tributaries within the measurement interval.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","If water remains below the crest, the floodway and its embankments cannot fail."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將上下游與分洪入口流量同步對帳，確認量測區間內是否有河段蓄水或支流。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile upstream, downstream and bypass flows synchronously, identifying reach storage and tributaries within the measurement interval. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b272-v15-04","title":"分流控制體與受益範圍機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Diversion control volume and effects mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「分流控制體與受益範圍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Diversion control volume and effects” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只展示城市段降水位會漏掉其他地區的負擔，將分流比例固定則可能忽略尾水和入口控制；水量帳不閉合時，模型可能把外排錯當成消失的洪水。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Showing only reduced city stage omits burdens elsewhere, while a fixed split can ignore tailwater and inlet control. An unclosed ledger may treat transferred water as flood volume that has disappeared. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例只作瞬時水量連續，假設分流節點沒有蓄水或其他支路；不由此推定任何河段水位或可接受的影響分配。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It determines neither reach stages nor an acceptable distribution of impacts.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「分洪道把洪水帶離城市後，這部分水就不需要再納入下游分析。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once a floodway removes water from a city, that water no longer needs downstream analysis.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只展示城市段降水位會漏掉其他地區的負擔，將分流比例固定則可能忽略尾水和入口控制；水量帳不閉合時，模型可能把外排錯當成消失的洪水。","textEn":"Showing only reduced city stage omits burdens elsewhere, while a fixed split can ignore tailwater and inlet control. An unclosed ledger may treat transferred water as flood volume that has disappeared.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分流控制體與受益範圍機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Diversion control volume and effects mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只展示城市段降水位會漏掉其他地區的負擔，將分流比例固定則可能忽略尾水和入口控制；水量帳不閉合時，模型可能把外排錯當成消失的洪水。","所有分洪入口只需一個自由堰公式，不受入口方向與尾水影響。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Showing only reduced city stage omits burdens elsewhere, while a fixed split can ignore tailwater and inlet control.","Every floodway inlet needs only one free-weir formula regardless of orientation or tailwater."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只展示城市段降水位會漏掉其他地區的負擔，將分流比例固定則可能忽略尾水和入口控制；水量帳不閉合時，模型可能把外排錯當成消失的洪水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Showing only reduced city stage omits burdens elsewhere, while a fixed split can ignore tailwater and inlet control. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b272-v15-05","title":"入口門檻與自由溢流機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Inlet threshold and free overflow mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「入口門檻與自由溢流」如何影響河道分洪工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Inlet threshold and free overflow” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River flood-diversion works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分洪入口門檻使低水位時流量留在主河，水位超過門檻後才逐漸啟動支路。堰頂以上水頭的非線性關係，使小幅高程誤差可能明顯改變開始分流的時間與比例；實際側向入口、閘門和回水會偏離簡單正面堰，因此計算式應與入口構型一致。本例為理想正面自由矩形堰並指定係數，不描述紅河或元朗實際入口；不將此算式用作現場閘門操作規則。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「入口門檻與自由溢流」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An inlet sill retains low flows in the main river and progressively activates the bypass as stage rises. Nonlinear dependence on head above crest means small elevation errors can alter diversion timing and share. Real lateral entrances, gates and backwater differ from a simple frontal weir, so the chosen relation must match the actual inlet configuration. The example is an ideal frontal free rectangular weir with a specified coefficient, not the actual Red River or Yuen Long inlet and not a field gate rule. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Inlet threshold and free overflow” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設堰式Q=C bH^1.5，C=1.70 m^0.5/s、寬b=10 m、堰上水頭H=1.0 m，分流Q=17.0 m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume weir Q=C bH^1.5, C=1.70 m^0.5/s, width b=10 m and crest head H=1.0 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有分洪入口只需一個自由堰公式，不受入口方向與尾水影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every floodway inlet needs only one free-weir formula regardless of orientation or tailwater.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「入口門檻與自由溢流」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Inlet threshold and free overflow”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-05-k1","title":"入口門檻與自由溢流機理與驗證","titleEn":"Inlet threshold and free overflow mechanism and verification","text":"分洪入口門檻使低水位時流量留在主河，水位超過門檻後才逐漸啟動支路。堰頂以上水頭的非線性關係，使小幅高程誤差可能明顯改變開始分流的時間與比例；實際側向入口、閘門和回水會偏離簡單正面堰，因此計算式應與入口構型一致。","textEn":"An inlet sill retains low flows in the main river and progressively activates the bypass as stage rises. Nonlinear dependence on head above crest means small elevation errors can alter diversion timing and share.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有分洪入口只需一個自由堰公式，不受入口方向與尾水影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every floodway inlet needs only one free-weir formula regardless of orientation or tailwater. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「入口門檻與自由溢流機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Inlet threshold and free overflow mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["所有分洪入口只需一個自由堰公式，不受入口方向與尾水影響。","分洪道某一斷面用曼寧式算得的流量，就是全系統任何洪水下的容量。","分洪入口門檻使低水位時流量留在主河，水位超過門檻後才逐漸啟動支路。"],"optionsEn":["Every floodway inlet needs only one free-weir formula regardless of orientation or tailwater.","Manning flow at one section is the entire system capacity under every flood condition.","An inlet sill retains low flows in the main river and progressively activates the bypass as stage rises."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分洪入口門檻使低水位時流量留在主河，水位超過門檻後才逐漸啟動支路。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An inlet sill retains low flows in the main river and progressively activates the bypass as stage rises. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b272-v15-06","title":"入口門檻與自由溢流機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Inlet threshold and free overflow mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「入口門檻與自由溢流」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Inlet threshold and free overflow” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設堰式Q=C bH^1.5，C=1.70 m^0.5/s、寬b=10 m、堰上水頭H=1.0 m，分流Q=17.0 m³/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume weir Q=C bH^1.5, C=1.70 m^0.5/s, width b=10 m and crest head H=1.0 m. Diversion Q=17.0 m³/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對堰頂和上游量測的共同基準，觀察分流開始與尾水淹沒的時刻。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check crest and upstream-stage datums and observe the onset of diversion and tailwater submergence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設堰式Q=C bH^1.5，C=1.70 m^0.5/s、寬b=10 m、堰上水頭H=1.0 m，分流Q=17.0 m³/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume weir Q=C bH^1.5, C=1.70 m^0.5/s, width b=10 m and crest head H=1.0 m. Diversion Q=17.0 m³/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「入口門檻與自由溢流機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Inlet threshold and free overflow mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設堰式Q=C bH^1.5，C=1.70 m^0.5/s、寬b=10 m、堰上水頭H=1.0 m，分流Q=17.0 m³/s。","速度水頭增加就是全部局部損失，兩者可以視為同一個項目。","洪峰永遠和平均水流等速，所以距離除流速就是精確到達時間。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume weir Q=C bH^1.5, C=1.70 m^0.5/s, width b=10 m and crest head H=1.0 m.","An increase in velocity head is the entire local loss and the two terms are identical.","A flood crest always moves at mean flow velocity, giving exact arrival from distance divided by velocity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設堰式Q=C bH^1.5，C=1.70 m^0.5/s、寬b=10 m、堰上水頭H=1.0 m，分流Q=17.0 m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume weir Q=C bH^1.5, C=1.70 m^0.5/s, width b=10 m and crest head H=1.0 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b272-v15-07","title":"入口門檻與自由溢流機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Inlet threshold and free overflow mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「入口門檻與自由溢流」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Inlet threshold and free overflow” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對堰頂和上游量測的共同基準，觀察分流開始與尾水淹沒的時刻。將模型入口類型、係數及有效長度記錄完整，必要時以實體或三維流場試驗驗證側向進流。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check crest and upstream-stage datums and observe the onset of diversion and tailwater submergence. Document inlet type, coefficient and effective length, using physical or three-dimensional flow testing where lateral approach invalidates a simple frontal-weir representation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出正面與側向入口的差異，為同一指定水頭先做理想計算。再列出側向流、淹沒與閘門會新增的資料需求，避免把手算結果當實際分流量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw frontal and lateral inlet differences and perform the ideal calculation at one specified head. List additional information for lateral approach, submergence and gates so that the hand result is not mistaken for actual diversion.","failure":"注意干擾：把側堰直接當正面堰會忽略沿程水頭變化，門檻高程錯誤也可能造成過早或過晚分流；下游淹沒時沿用自由堰式則通常高估能力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating a side weir as frontal ignores head variation along its length. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對堰頂和上游量測的共同基準，觀察分流開始與尾水淹沒的時刻。將模型入口類型、係數及有效長度記錄完整，必要時以實體或三維流場試驗驗證側向進流。","textEn":"Check crest and upstream-stage datums and observe the onset of diversion and tailwater submergence. Document inlet type, coefficient and effective length, using physical or three-dimensional flow testing where lateral approach invalidates a simple frontal-weir representation.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出正面與側向入口的差異，為同一指定水頭先做理想計算。再列出側向流、淹沒與閘門會新增的資料需求，避免把手算結果當實際分流量。","textEn":"Draw frontal and lateral inlet differences and perform the ideal calculation at one specified head. List additional information for lateral approach, submergence and gates so that the hand result is not mistaken for actual diversion.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「入口門檻與自由溢流機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Inlet threshold and free overflow mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對堰頂和上游量測的共同基準，觀察分流開始與尾水淹沒的時刻。","分走三成水就必定分走三成泥砂，而且河床可以永遠固定。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check crest and upstream-stage datums and observe the onset of diversion and tailwater submergence.","Diverting thirty percent of water necessarily diverts thirty percent of sediment with an unchanged bed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對堰頂和上游量測的共同基準，觀察分流開始與尾水淹沒的時刻。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check crest and upstream-stage datums and observe the onset of diversion and tailwater submergence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b272-v15-08","title":"入口門檻與自由溢流機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Inlet threshold and free overflow mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「入口門檻與自由溢流」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Inlet threshold and free overflow” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把側堰直接當正面堰會忽略沿程水頭變化，門檻高程錯誤也可能造成過早或過晚分流；下游淹沒時沿用自由堰式則通常高估能力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating a side weir as frontal ignores head variation along its length. Incorrect sill elevation can activate diversion too early or late, and retaining a free-weir relation under submergence generally overstates capacity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例為理想正面自由矩形堰並指定係數，不描述紅河或元朗實際入口；不將此算式用作現場閘門操作規則。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The example is an ideal frontal free rectangular weir with a specified coefficient, not the actual Red River or Yuen Long inlet and not a field gate rule.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有分洪入口只需一個自由堰公式，不受入口方向與尾水影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every floodway inlet needs only one free-weir formula regardless of orientation or tailwater.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把側堰直接當正面堰會忽略沿程水頭變化，門檻高程錯誤也可能造成過早或過晚分流；下游淹沒時沿用自由堰式則通常高估能力。","textEn":"Treating a side weir as frontal ignores head variation along its length. Incorrect sill elevation can activate diversion too early or late, and retaining a free-weir relation under submergence generally overstates capacity.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「入口門檻與自由溢流機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Inlet threshold and free overflow mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","分洪道某一斷面用曼寧式算得的流量，就是全系統任何洪水下的容量。","把側堰直接當正面堰會忽略沿程水頭變化，門檻高程錯誤也可能造成過早或過晚分流；下游淹沒時沿用自由堰式則通常高估能力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Manning flow at one section is the entire system capacity under every flood condition.","Treating a side weir as frontal ignores head variation along its length."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把側堰直接當正面堰會忽略沿程水頭變化，門檻高程錯誤也可能造成過早或過晚分流；下游淹沒時沿用自由堰式則通常高估能力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating a side weir as frontal ignores head variation along its length. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b272-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「分洪渠輸水能力機理與驗證」與「臨界水深與控制斷面機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Floodway conveyance capacity mechanism and verification\" and \"Critical depth and control sections mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b272-v15-09","title":"分洪渠輸水能力機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Floodway conveyance capacity mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「分洪渠輸水能力」如何影響河道分洪工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Floodway conveyance capacity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River flood-diversion works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分洪道的能力不只取決於寬度，水深、濕周、糙率和能量坡降都會改變輸水量。曼寧式適合穩定均勻流的初步尺度，但入口、橋梁、出口與潮汐回水通常需要非均勻流分析；將地形坡度不加檢查地當成能坡，可能高估平緩河段可提供的驅動水頭。本例為矩形固定斷面且採國際單位的曼寧式，所得不是整條分洪道的保證容量；最窄控制段與回水仍須另算。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分洪渠輸水能力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Floodway capacity depends on depth, wetted perimeter, roughness and energy slope as well as width. Manning’s equation gives a steady-uniform preliminary scale, while entrances, bridges, outlets and tidal backwater generally need nonuniform analysis. Substituting bed slope for energy slope without checking can overstate the driving head available in a flat reach. The example uses a fixed rectangular section and SI Manning form. It is not guaranteed capacity of the whole floodway; constrictions and backwater require separate analysis. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Floodway conveyance capacity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設b=20 m、y=2 m、n=0.030 s/m^(1/3)、Sf=0.0004；A=40 m²、R=40/24 m，Q=AR^(2/3)√Sf/n=37.49 m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume b=20 m, y=2 m, n=0.030 s/m^(1/3), Sf=0.0004, A=40 m² and R=40/24 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「分洪道某一斷面用曼寧式算得的流量，就是全系統任何洪水下的容量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Manning flow at one section is the entire system capacity under every flood condition.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「分洪渠輸水能力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Floodway conveyance capacity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-09-k1","title":"分洪渠輸水能力機理與驗證","titleEn":"Floodway conveyance capacity mechanism and verification","text":"分洪道的能力不只取決於寬度，水深、濕周、糙率和能量坡降都會改變輸水量。曼寧式適合穩定均勻流的初步尺度，但入口、橋梁、出口與潮汐回水通常需要非均勻流分析；將地形坡度不加檢查地當成能坡，可能高估平緩河段可提供的驅動水頭。","textEn":"Floodway capacity depends on depth, wetted perimeter, roughness and energy slope as well as width. Manning’s equation gives a steady-uniform preliminary scale, while entrances, bridges, outlets and tidal backwater generally need nonuniform analysis.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：分洪道某一斷面用曼寧式算得的流量，就是全系統任何洪水下的容量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Manning flow at one section is the entire system capacity under every flood condition. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分洪渠輸水能力機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Floodway conveyance capacity mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["分洪道的能力不只取決於寬度，水深、濕周、糙率和能量坡降都會改變輸水量。","分洪道某一斷面用曼寧式算得的流量，就是全系統任何洪水下的容量。","算出臨界水深後，就已經得到分洪道所有位置的正常水深。"],"optionsEn":["Floodway capacity depends on depth, wetted perimeter, roughness and energy slope as well as width.","Manning flow at one section is the entire system capacity under every flood condition.","Calculating critical depth gives normal depth at every location in the floodway."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分洪道的能力不只取決於寬度，水深、濕周、糙率和能量坡降都會改變輸水量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Floodway capacity depends on depth, wetted perimeter, roughness and energy slope as well as width. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b272-v15-10","title":"分洪渠輸水能力機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Floodway conveyance capacity mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「分洪渠輸水能力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Floodway conveyance capacity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設b=20 m、y=2 m、n=0.030 s/m^(1/3)、Sf=0.0004；A=40 m²、R=40/24 m，Q=AR^(2/3)√Sf/n=37.49 m³/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume b=20 m, y=2 m, n=0.030 s/m^(1/3), Sf=0.0004, A=40 m² and R=40/24 m. Manning Q=37.49 m³/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：測量實際斷面、植被與障礙物，核對能坡來自哪個水位區間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey actual sections, vegetation and obstructions, identifying the stage interval used to estimate energy slope.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設b=20 m、y=2 m、n=0.030 s/m^(1/3)、Sf=0.0004；A=40 m²、R=40/24 m，Q=AR^(2/3)√Sf/n=37.49 m³/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume b=20 m, y=2 m, n=0.030 s/m^(1/3), Sf=0.0004, A=40 m² and R=40/24 m. Manning Q=37.49 m³/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「分洪渠輸水能力機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Floodway conveyance capacity mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["分洪道只要向下游傾斜，下游漲水就不可能影響上游水位。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設b=20 m、y=2 m、n=0.030 s/m^(1/3)、Sf=0.0004。","只要水面沒有碰到堤頂，分洪道及兩側堤防就不存在失效可能。"],"optionsEn":["A floodway sloping downstream cannot experience upstream effects from rising tailwater.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume b=20 m, y=2 m, n=0.030 s/m^(1/3), Sf=0.0004, A=40 m² and R=40/24 m.","If water remains below the crest, the floodway and its embankments cannot fail."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設b=20 m、y=2 m、n=0.030 s/m^(1/3)、Sf=0.0004；A=40 m²、R=40/24 m，Q=AR^(2/3)√Sf/n=37.49 m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume b=20 m, y=2 m, n=0.030 s/m^(1/3), Sf=0.0004, A=40 m² and R=40/24 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b272-v15-11","title":"分洪渠輸水能力機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Floodway conveyance capacity mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「分洪渠輸水能力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Floodway conveyance capacity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"測量實際斷面、植被與障礙物，核對能坡來自哪個水位區間。用多個流況校驗糙率，並把橋孔及出口控制接入整體模型，避免單段均勻流計算掩蓋系統瓶頸。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey actual sections, vegetation and obstructions, identifying the stage interval used to estimate energy slope. Calibrate roughness across several flows and connect bridge and outlet controls to the full model so that one uniform reach does not conceal a system bottleneck. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：固定水深和坡降，把糙率提高兩成重算流量，再指出這不是定流量時的水位變化。將入口、橋梁和出口畫成控制鏈，辨認可能先限制能力的位置。","observationEn":"Site practice: At fixed depth and slope increase roughness by twenty percent and recompute flow, noting that this is not the stage response at fixed discharge. Map inlet, bridge and outlet controls to identify possible governing restrictions.","failure":"注意干擾：只加寬一段而不處理下游控制可能幾乎不增加整體能力，季節植被也會改變有效糙率；若模型仍用清潔新渠值，長期排洪能力會被高估。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Widening one reach without addressing downstream control may barely improve overall capacity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"測量實際斷面、植被與障礙物，核對能坡來自哪個水位區間。用多個流況校驗糙率，並把橋孔及出口控制接入整體模型，避免單段均勻流計算掩蓋系統瓶頸。","textEn":"Survey actual sections, vegetation and obstructions, identifying the stage interval used to estimate energy slope. Calibrate roughness across several flows and connect bridge and outlet controls to the full model so that one uniform reach does not conceal a system bottleneck.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"固定水深和坡降，把糙率提高兩成重算流量，再指出這不是定流量時的水位變化。將入口、橋梁和出口畫成控制鏈，辨認可能先限制能力的位置。","textEn":"At fixed depth and slope increase roughness by twenty percent and recompute flow, noting that this is not the stage response at fixed discharge. Map inlet, bridge and outlet controls to identify possible governing restrictions.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「分洪渠輸水能力機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Floodway conveyance capacity mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","模型沒有發散且水量閉合，就足以證明分洪水位預測完全可靠。","測量實際斷面、植被與障礙物，核對能坡來自哪個水位區間。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A nondiverging model with volume closure proves fully reliable floodway stage predictions.","Survey actual sections, vegetation and obstructions, identifying the stage interval used to estimate energy slope."],"answer":2,"explanation":"測量實際斷面、植被與障礙物，核對能坡來自哪個水位區間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey actual sections, vegetation and obstructions, identifying the stage interval used to estimate energy slope. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b272-v15-12","title":"分洪渠輸水能力機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Floodway conveyance capacity mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「分洪渠輸水能力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Floodway conveyance capacity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只加寬一段而不處理下游控制可能幾乎不增加整體能力，季節植被也會改變有效糙率；若模型仍用清潔新渠值，長期排洪能力會被高估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Widening one reach without addressing downstream control may barely improve overall capacity. Seasonal vegetation changes effective roughness, and continued use of a clean new-channel value can overstate long-term conveyance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例為矩形固定斷面且採國際單位的曼寧式，所得不是整條分洪道的保證容量；最窄控制段與回水仍須另算。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It is not guaranteed capacity of the whole floodway; constrictions and backwater require separate analysis.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「分洪道某一斷面用曼寧式算得的流量，就是全系統任何洪水下的容量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Manning flow at one section is the entire system capacity under every flood condition.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只加寬一段而不處理下游控制可能幾乎不增加整體能力，季節植被也會改變有效糙率；若模型仍用清潔新渠值，長期排洪能力會被高估。","textEn":"Widening one reach without addressing downstream control may barely improve overall capacity. Seasonal vegetation changes effective roughness, and continued use of a clean new-channel value can overstate long-term conveyance.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分洪渠輸水能力機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Floodway conveyance capacity mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只加寬一段而不處理下游控制可能幾乎不增加整體能力，季節植被也會改變有效糙率；若模型仍用清潔新渠值，長期排洪能力會被高估。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","算出臨界水深後，就已經得到分洪道所有位置的正常水深。"],"optionsEn":["Widening one reach without addressing downstream control may barely improve overall capacity.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Calculating critical depth gives normal depth at every location in the floodway."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只加寬一段而不處理下游控制可能幾乎不增加整體能力，季節植被也會改變有效糙率；若模型仍用清潔新渠值，長期排洪能力會被高估。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Widening one reach without addressing downstream control may barely improve overall capacity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b272-v15-13","title":"臨界水深與控制斷面機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Critical depth and control sections mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「臨界水深與控制斷面」如何影響河道分洪工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Critical depth and control sections” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River flood-diversion works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"明渠比能在指定單寬流量下存在最小值，對應臨界水深，縮窄或抬高底床可能把流況推向控制。臨界條件不等於正常水深，也不直接指出上游水面高程；判斷入口或橋孔是否壅水時，還須比較可用能量、局部損失與兩側邊界，不能只靠水深大小分類。本例為寬度固定的矩形渠、靜水壓分布且動能修正係數取一；複合斷面或強三維入口需其他求解。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「臨界水深與控制斷面」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For a specified unit discharge, open-channel specific energy has a minimum at critical depth. Contraction or bed raising can drive a section toward control. Critical depth differs from normal depth and does not directly give upstream elevation; assessing choking also requires available energy, local losses and both boundaries rather than classifying flow from depth alone. The example assumes a fixed-width rectangular channel, hydrostatic pressure and unit energy coefficient. Compound sections or strongly three-dimensional entrances require another solution. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Critical depth and control sections” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設單寬流量q=5.0 m²/s、g=9.81 m/s²，臨界水深yc=(q²/g)^(1/3)=1.366 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume unit discharge q=5.0 m²/s and g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「算出臨界水深後，就已經得到分洪道所有位置的正常水深。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Calculating critical depth gives normal depth at every location in the floodway.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「臨界水深與控制斷面」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Critical depth and control sections”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-13-k1","title":"臨界水深與控制斷面機理與驗證","titleEn":"Critical depth and control sections mechanism and verification","text":"明渠比能在指定單寬流量下存在最小值，對應臨界水深，縮窄或抬高底床可能把流況推向控制。臨界條件不等於正常水深，也不直接指出上游水面高程；判斷入口或橋孔是否壅水時，還須比較可用能量、局部損失與兩側邊界，不能只靠水深大小分類。","textEn":"For a specified unit discharge, open-channel specific energy has a minimum at critical depth. Contraction or bed raising can drive a section toward control.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：算出臨界水深後，就已經得到分洪道所有位置的正常水深。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Calculating critical depth gives normal depth at every location in the floodway. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「臨界水深與控制斷面機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Critical depth and control sections mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["算出臨界水深後，就已經得到分洪道所有位置的正常水深。","明渠比能在指定單寬流量下存在最小值，對應臨界水深，縮窄或抬高底床可能把流況推向控制。","速度水頭增加就是全部局部損失，兩者可以視為同一個項目。"],"optionsEn":["Calculating critical depth gives normal depth at every location in the floodway.","For a specified unit discharge, open-channel specific energy has a minimum at critical depth.","An increase in velocity head is the entire local loss and the two terms are identical."],"answer":1,"explanation":"明渠比能在指定單寬流量下存在最小值，對應臨界水深，縮窄或抬高底床可能把流況推向控制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For a specified unit discharge, open-channel specific energy has a minimum at critical depth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b272-v15-14","title":"臨界水深與控制斷面機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Critical depth and control sections mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「臨界水深與控制斷面」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Critical depth and control sections” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設單寬流量q=5.0 m²/s、g=9.81 m/s²，臨界水深yc=(q²/g)^(1/3)=1.366 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume unit discharge q=5.0 m²/s and g=9.81 m/s². Critical depth yc=(q²/g)^(1/3)=1.366 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對單寬流量使用的有效寬度，計算比能曲線並標出最小值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify the effective width used for unit discharge and plot the specific-energy minimum.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設單寬流量q=5.0 m²/s、g=9.81 m/s²，臨界水深yc=(q²/g)^(1/3)=1.366 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume unit discharge q=5.0 m²/s and g=9.81 m/s². Critical depth yc=(q²/g)^(1/3)=1.366 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「臨界水深與控制斷面機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Critical depth and control sections mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["洪峰永遠和平均水流等速，所以距離除流速就是精確到達時間。","分走三成水就必定分走三成泥砂，而且河床可以永遠固定。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設單寬流量q=5.0 m²/s、g=9.81 m/s²，臨界水深yc=(q²/g)^(1/3)=1.366 m。"],"optionsEn":["A flood crest always moves at mean flow velocity, giving exact arrival from distance divided by velocity.","Diverting thirty percent of water necessarily diverts thirty percent of sediment with an unchanged bed.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume unit discharge q=5.0 m²/s and g=9.81 m/s²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設單寬流量q=5.0 m²/s、g=9.81 m/s²，臨界水深yc=(q²/g)^(1/3)=1.366 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume unit discharge q=5.0 m²/s and g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b272-v15-15","title":"臨界水深與控制斷面機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Critical depth and control sections mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「臨界水深與控制斷面」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Critical depth and control sections” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對單寬流量使用的有效寬度，計算比能曲線並標出最小值。以量測流況、下游控制和局部損失檢查可能的水面分支，避免直接把臨界水深填成全河段水位。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify the effective width used for unit discharge and plot the specific-energy minimum. Check possible water-surface branches against observed regime, downstream control and local losses instead of assigning critical depth as the water level throughout the floodway. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出指定單寬流量的比能曲線，標示可能的兩個水深分支。加入一個底床抬升情境，說明還需要哪些能量資料才能判斷是否發生控制。","observationEn":"Site practice: Plot specific energy for the given unit discharge and mark the two possible depth branches. Introduce a bed rise and identify the energy information still needed to decide whether choking occurs.","failure":"注意干擾：把正常水深與臨界水深混同會選錯水面分支，忽略縮窄損失則可能漏掉入口壅水；只看到渠深大於臨界值，也不能證明整個系統都不會出現急流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing normal and critical depth selects the wrong branch, and omitted contraction losses can miss inlet backwater. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對單寬流量使用的有效寬度，計算比能曲線並標出最小值。以量測流況、下游控制和局部損失檢查可能的水面分支，避免直接把臨界水深填成全河段水位。","textEn":"Verify the effective width used for unit discharge and plot the specific-energy minimum. Check possible water-surface branches against observed regime, downstream control and local losses instead of assigning critical depth as the water level throughout the floodway.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出指定單寬流量的比能曲線，標示可能的兩個水深分支。加入一個底床抬升情境，說明還需要哪些能量資料才能判斷是否發生控制。","textEn":"Plot specific energy for the given unit discharge and mark the two possible depth branches. Introduce a bed rise and identify the energy information still needed to decide whether choking occurs.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「臨界水深與控制斷面機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Critical depth and control sections mechanism and verification\"?","options":["核對單寬流量使用的有效寬度，計算比能曲線並標出最小值。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","分洪道把洪水帶離城市後，這部分水就不需要再納入下游分析。"],"optionsEn":["Verify the effective width used for unit discharge and plot the specific-energy minimum.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Once a floodway removes water from a city, that water no longer needs downstream analysis."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對單寬流量使用的有效寬度，計算比能曲線並標出最小值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify the effective width used for unit discharge and plot the specific-energy minimum. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b272-v15-16","title":"臨界水深與控制斷面機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Critical depth and control sections mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「臨界水深與控制斷面」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Critical depth and control sections” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把正常水深與臨界水深混同會選錯水面分支，忽略縮窄損失則可能漏掉入口壅水；只看到渠深大於臨界值，也不能證明整個系統都不會出現急流。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing normal and critical depth selects the wrong branch, and omitted contraction losses can miss inlet backwater. Depth above critical at one section does not prove that the entire system remains subcritical. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例為寬度固定的矩形渠、靜水壓分布且動能修正係數取一；複合斷面或強三維入口需其他求解。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compound sections or strongly three-dimensional entrances require another solution.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「算出臨界水深後，就已經得到分洪道所有位置的正常水深。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Calculating critical depth gives normal depth at every location in the floodway.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把正常水深與臨界水深混同會選錯水面分支，忽略縮窄損失則可能漏掉入口壅水；只看到渠深大於臨界值，也不能證明整個系統都不會出現急流。","textEn":"Confusing normal and critical depth selects the wrong branch, and omitted contraction losses can miss inlet backwater. Depth above critical at one section does not prove that the entire system remains subcritical.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「臨界水深與控制斷面機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Critical depth and control sections mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把正常水深與臨界水深混同會選錯水面分支，忽略縮窄損失則可能漏掉入口壅水；只看到渠深大於臨界值，也不能證明整個系統都不會出現急流。","速度水頭增加就是全部局部損失，兩者可以視為同一個項目。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Confusing normal and critical depth selects the wrong branch, and omitted contraction losses can miss inlet backwater.","An increase in velocity head is the entire local loss and the two terms are identical."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把正常水深與臨界水深混同會選錯水面分支，忽略縮窄損失則可能漏掉入口壅水；只看到渠深大於臨界值，也不能證明整個系統都不會出現急流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing normal and critical depth selects the wrong branch, and omitted contraction losses can miss inlet backwater. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b272-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「收縮速度與能量轉換機理與驗證」與「回水曲線與下游控制機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Contraction velocity and energy change mechanism and verification\" and \"Backwater profiles and downstream control mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b272-v15-17","title":"收縮速度與能量轉換機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Contraction velocity and energy change mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「收縮速度與能量轉換」如何影響河道分洪工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Contraction velocity and energy change” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River flood-diversion works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分洪入口或橋孔縮窄會提高速度，部分水面位能轉為動能，另外還有不可回復的局部損失。速度水頭增加本身不是摩阻損失，把兩者重複扣除會錯算水面；反之若完全忽略損失，則可能高估可通流量，需要用一致能量線分開表達可逆轉換與耗散。本例只比較動能水頭、兩截面動能修正係數均取一；沒有假定相同底床或已求得水面差，也未包含局部損失。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「收縮速度與能量轉換」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A contracted inlet or bridge opening accelerates flow, converting some surface potential into kinetic energy while also causing irreversible local losses. Increased velocity head is not itself friction loss, and deducting it twice miscalculates the surface. Ignoring actual loss has the opposite problem, so one energy line must distinguish reversible conversion from dissipation. The example compares kinetic heads with unit energy coefficients only. It does not assume equal bed elevations or determine surface difference, and it excludes local loss. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Contraction velocity and energy change” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設上游v1=1.0 m/s、縮口v2=3.0 m/s、g=9.81 m/s²，動能水頭增量Δhv=(v2²−v1²)/(2g)=0.4077 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume upstream v1=1.0 m/s, contracted v2=3.0 m/s and g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「速度水頭增加就是全部局部損失，兩者可以視為同一個項目。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An increase in velocity head is the entire local loss and the two terms are identical.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「收縮速度與能量轉換」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Contraction velocity and energy change”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-17-k1","title":"收縮速度與能量轉換機理與驗證","titleEn":"Contraction velocity and energy change mechanism and verification","text":"分洪入口或橋孔縮窄會提高速度，部分水面位能轉為動能，另外還有不可回復的局部損失。速度水頭增加本身不是摩阻損失，把兩者重複扣除會錯算水面；反之若完全忽略損失，則可能高估可通流量，需要用一致能量線分開表達可逆轉換與耗散。","textEn":"A contracted inlet or bridge opening accelerates flow, converting some surface potential into kinetic energy while also causing irreversible local losses. Increased velocity head is not itself friction loss, and deducting it twice miscalculates the surface.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：速度水頭增加就是全部局部損失，兩者可以視為同一個項目。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An increase in velocity head is the entire local loss and the two terms are identical. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「收縮速度與能量轉換機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Contraction velocity and energy change mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["速度水頭增加就是全部局部損失，兩者可以視為同一個項目。","分洪道只要向下游傾斜，下游漲水就不可能影響上游水位。","分洪入口或橋孔縮窄會提高速度，部分水面位能轉為動能，另外還有不可回復的局部損失。"],"optionsEn":["An increase in velocity head is the entire local loss and the two terms are identical.","A floodway sloping downstream cannot experience upstream effects from rising tailwater.","A contracted inlet or bridge opening accelerates flow, converting some surface potential into kinetic energy while also causing irreversible local losses."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分洪入口或橋孔縮窄會提高速度，部分水面位能轉為動能，另外還有不可回復的局部損失。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A contracted inlet or bridge opening accelerates flow, converting some surface potential into kinetic energy while also causing irreversible local losses. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b272-v15-18","title":"收縮速度與能量轉換機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Contraction velocity and energy change mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「收縮速度與能量轉換」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Contraction velocity and energy change” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設上游v1=1.0 m/s、縮口v2=3.0 m/s、g=9.81 m/s²，動能水頭增量Δhv=(v2²−v1²)/(2g)=0.4077 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume upstream v1=1.0 m/s, contracted v2=3.0 m/s and g=9.81 m/s². Kinetic-head increase Δhv=(v2²−v1²)/(2g)=0.4077 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把底床、水面和能量線畫在同一剖面，核對速度截面與修正係數。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot bed, water surface and energy line on one section, checking velocity sections and correction factors.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設上游v1=1.0 m/s、縮口v2=3.0 m/s、g=9.81 m/s²，動能水頭增量Δhv=(v2²−v1²)/(2g)=0.4077 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume upstream v1=1.0 m/s, contracted v2=3.0 m/s and g=9.81 m/s². Kinetic-head increase Δhv=(v2²−v1²)/(2g)=0.4077 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「收縮速度與能量轉換機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Contraction velocity and energy change mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設上游v1=1.0 m/s、縮口v2=3.0 m/s、g=9.81 m/s²，動能水頭增量Δhv=(v2²−v1²)/(2g)=0.4077 m。","只要水面沒有碰到堤頂，分洪道及兩側堤防就不存在失效可能。","模型沒有發散且水量閉合，就足以證明分洪水位預測完全可靠。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume upstream v1=1.0 m/s, contracted v2=3.0 m/s and g=9.81 m/s².","If water remains below the crest, the floodway and its embankments cannot fail.","A nondiverging model with volume closure proves fully reliable floodway stage predictions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設上游v1=1.0 m/s、縮口v2=3.0 m/s、g=9.81 m/s²，動能水頭增量Δhv=(v2²−v1²)/(2g)=0.4077 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume upstream v1=1.0 m/s, contracted v2=3.0 m/s and g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b272-v15-19","title":"收縮速度與能量轉換機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Contraction velocity and energy change mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「收縮速度與能量轉換」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Contraction velocity and energy change” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把底床、水面和能量線畫在同一剖面，核對速度截面與修正係數。以量測總能量差辨認真正損失，再檢查是否把速度水頭變化同時放入損失項和能量項造成重複扣除。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot bed, water surface and energy line on one section, checking velocity sections and correction factors. Identify genuine losses from measured total-energy change, then inspect whether velocity-head conversion has been counted both as an energy term and as a separate loss. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立含底高、水深、速度水頭與損失的能量帳，將已知和未知項分開。用兩種假設損失係數比較可用能量，說明速度變化無法單獨決定水面差。","observationEn":"Site practice: Build an energy ledger with bed elevation, depth, kinetic head and loss, separating knowns from unknowns. Compare available energy under two assumed loss coefficients and explain why velocity change alone cannot determine surface difference.","failure":"注意干擾：把所有水面下降當成能量耗散會混淆加速與損失，模型校正可能因此選錯係數；漏掉局部損失又會使收縮控制過於樂觀，兩者都會影響上游壅水預測。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Calling every surface drop dissipation confuses acceleration with loss and can lead calibration to the wrong coefficient. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把底床、水面和能量線畫在同一剖面，核對速度截面與修正係數。以量測總能量差辨認真正損失，再檢查是否把速度水頭變化同時放入損失項和能量項造成重複扣除。","textEn":"Plot bed, water surface and energy line on one section, checking velocity sections and correction factors. Identify genuine losses from measured total-energy change, then inspect whether velocity-head conversion has been counted both as an energy term and as a separate loss.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立含底高、水深、速度水頭與損失的能量帳，將已知和未知項分開。用兩種假設損失係數比較可用能量，說明速度變化無法單獨決定水面差。","textEn":"Build an energy ledger with bed elevation, depth, kinetic head and loss, separating knowns from unknowns. Compare available energy under two assumed loss coefficients and explain why velocity change alone cannot determine surface difference.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「收縮速度與能量轉換機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Contraction velocity and energy change mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","把底床、水面和能量線畫在同一剖面，核對速度截面與修正係數。","所有分洪入口只需一個自由堰公式，不受入口方向與尾水影響。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Plot bed, water surface and energy line on one section, checking velocity sections and correction factors.","Every floodway inlet needs only one free-weir formula regardless of orientation or tailwater."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把底床、水面和能量線畫在同一剖面，核對速度截面與修正係數。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot bed, water surface and energy line on one section, checking velocity sections and correction factors. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b272-v15-20","title":"收縮速度與能量轉換機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Contraction velocity and energy change mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「收縮速度與能量轉換」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Contraction velocity and energy change” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把所有水面下降當成能量耗散會混淆加速與損失，模型校正可能因此選錯係數；漏掉局部損失又會使收縮控制過於樂觀，兩者都會影響上游壅水預測。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Calling every surface drop dissipation confuses acceleration with loss and can lead calibration to the wrong coefficient. Omitting local losses makes contraction control optimistic; both errors affect predicted upstream backwater. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例只比較動能水頭、兩截面動能修正係數均取一；沒有假定相同底床或已求得水面差，也未包含局部損失。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It does not assume equal bed elevations or determine surface difference, and it excludes local loss.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「速度水頭增加就是全部局部損失，兩者可以視為同一個項目。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An increase in velocity head is the entire local loss and the two terms are identical.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把所有水面下降當成能量耗散會混淆加速與損失，模型校正可能因此選錯係數；漏掉局部損失又會使收縮控制過於樂觀，兩者都會影響上游壅水預測。","textEn":"Calling every surface drop dissipation confuses acceleration with loss and can lead calibration to the wrong coefficient. Omitting local losses makes contraction control optimistic; both errors affect predicted upstream backwater.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「收縮速度與能量轉換機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Contraction velocity and energy change mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","分洪道只要向下游傾斜，下游漲水就不可能影響上游水位。","把所有水面下降當成能量耗散會混淆加速與損失，模型校正可能因此選錯係數；漏掉局部損失又會使收縮控制過於樂觀，兩者都會影響上游壅水預測。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A floodway sloping downstream cannot experience upstream effects from rising tailwater.","Calling every surface drop dissipation confuses acceleration with loss and can lead calibration to the wrong coefficient."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把所有水面下降當成能量耗散會混淆加速與損失，模型校正可能因此選錯係數；漏掉局部損失又會使收縮控制過於樂觀，兩者都會影響上游壅水預測。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Calling every surface drop dissipation confuses acceleration with loss and can lead calibration to the wrong coefficient. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b272-v15-21","title":"回水曲線與下游控制機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Backwater profiles and downstream control mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「回水曲線與下游控制」如何影響河道分洪工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Backwater profiles and downstream control” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River flood-diversion works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"緩流分洪道的下游水位可向上游影響水深，因此出口河川漲水可能降低分洪效益。漸變流方程把底坡、摩阻坡與福祿數連到局部水深梯度，但接近臨界時分母變小，局部線性外推會不可靠；閘門、跌水和水躍還需另處理，不能跨越不連續流況套同一坡度。本例為稜柱渠的局部漸變流導數，正座標沿下游，水深變化不等於絕對水面高程變化；不作長距離定坡外推。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「回水曲線與下游控制」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Downstream stage influences upstream depth in subcritical flow, so rising receiving water can reduce diversion benefit. The gradually varied equation relates bed slope, friction slope and Froude number to local depth gradient. Near critical conditions its denominator becomes small and linear extrapolation becomes unreliable; gates, drops and jumps also need separate treatment rather than one continuous slope. The example is a local gradually varied derivative in a prismatic channel with downstream-positive coordinate. Depth change is not absolute water-surface elevation change, and the slope is not extrapolated over a long reach. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Backwater profiles and downstream control” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設S0=0.001、Sf=0.0005、Fr=0.60，dy/dx=(S0−Sf)/(1−Fr²)=0.00078125 m/m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume S0=0.001, Sf=0.0005 and Fr=0.60.","failure":"常見誤解：「分洪道只要向下游傾斜，下游漲水就不可能影響上游水位。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A floodway sloping downstream cannot experience upstream effects from rising tailwater.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「回水曲線與下游控制」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Backwater profiles and downstream control”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-21-k1","title":"回水曲線與下游控制機理與驗證","titleEn":"Backwater profiles and downstream control mechanism and verification","text":"緩流分洪道的下游水位可向上游影響水深，因此出口河川漲水可能降低分洪效益。漸變流方程把底坡、摩阻坡與福祿數連到局部水深梯度，但接近臨界時分母變小，局部線性外推會不可靠；閘門、跌水和水躍還需另處理，不能跨越不連續流況套同一坡度。","textEn":"Downstream stage influences upstream depth in subcritical flow, so rising receiving water can reduce diversion benefit. The gradually varied equation relates bed slope, friction slope and Froude number to local depth gradient.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：分洪道只要向下游傾斜，下游漲水就不可能影響上游水位。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A floodway sloping downstream cannot experience upstream effects from rising tailwater. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「回水曲線與下游控制機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Backwater profiles and downstream control mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["緩流分洪道的下游水位可向上游影響水深，因此出口河川漲水可能降低分洪效益。","分洪道只要向下游傾斜，下游漲水就不可能影響上游水位。","洪峰永遠和平均水流等速，所以距離除流速就是精確到達時間。"],"optionsEn":["Downstream stage influences upstream depth in subcritical flow, so rising receiving water can reduce diversion benefit.","A floodway sloping downstream cannot experience upstream effects from rising tailwater.","A flood crest always moves at mean flow velocity, giving exact arrival from distance divided by velocity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"緩流分洪道的下游水位可向上游影響水深，因此出口河川漲水可能降低分洪效益。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Downstream stage influences upstream depth in subcritical flow, so rising receiving water can reduce diversion benefit. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b272-v15-22","title":"回水曲線與下游控制機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Backwater profiles and downstream control mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「回水曲線與下游控制」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Backwater profiles and downstream control” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設S0=0.001、Sf=0.0005、Fr=0.60，dy/dx=(S0−Sf)/(1−Fr²)=0.00078125 m/m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume S0=0.001, Sf=0.0005 and Fr=0.60. Local depth gradient dy/dx=(S0−Sf)/(1−Fr²)=0.00078125 m/m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：確認座標、底坡與水深定義，從適當邊界逐段求解並隨水深更新摩阻和福祿數。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Confirm coordinates, bed slope and depth definitions, solve reachwise from an appropriate boundary and update friction and Froude number with depth.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設S0=0.001、Sf=0.0005、Fr=0.60，dy/dx=(S0−Sf)/(1−Fr²)=0.00078125 m/m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume S0=0.001, Sf=0.0005 and Fr=0.60. Local depth gradient dy/dx=(S0−Sf)/(1−Fr²)=0.00078125 m/m.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「回水曲線與下游控制機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Backwater profiles and downstream control mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["分走三成水就必定分走三成泥砂，而且河床可以永遠固定。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設S0=0.001、Sf=0.0005、Fr=0.60，dy/dx=(S0−Sf)/(1−Fr²)=0.00078125 m/m。","分洪道把洪水帶離城市後，這部分水就不需要再納入下游分析。"],"optionsEn":["Diverting thirty percent of water necessarily diverts thirty percent of sediment with an unchanged bed.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume S0=0.001, Sf=0.0005 and Fr=0.60.","Once a floodway removes water from a city, that water no longer needs downstream analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設S0=0.001、Sf=0.0005、Fr=0.60，dy/dx=(S0−Sf)/(1−Fr²)=0.00078125 m/m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume S0=0.001, Sf=0.0005 and Fr=0.60. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b272-v15-23","title":"回水曲線與下游控制機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Backwater profiles and downstream control mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「回水曲線與下游控制」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Backwater profiles and downstream control” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"確認座標、底坡與水深定義，從適當邊界逐段求解並隨水深更新摩阻和福祿數。用沿程水位資料檢查曲線，接近臨界或存在水躍時改用可處理轉換的分析而非延長局部直線。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Confirm coordinates, bed slope and depth definitions, solve reachwise from an appropriate boundary and update friction and Froude number with depth. Compare the profile with longitudinal observations and use transition-capable analysis near critical flow or jumps instead of extending a local straight line. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將局部水深坡度與底坡合成絕對水面坡度，再比較不同福祿數下的分母。說明為何需要逐段更新而不能將一點導數乘整條河長。","observationEn":"Site practice: Combine local depth gradient with bed slope to obtain the absolute surface slope, then compare denominators at different Froude numbers. Explain why reachwise updating is needed instead of multiplying one derivative by the entire channel length.","failure":"注意干擾：把水深坡度當成水面坡度會漏掉底床高程，從錯誤端指定緩流邊界也可能得到錯誤曲線；接近臨界仍用粗步長則會放大數值不穩定。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mistaking depth slope for surface slope omits bed elevation, and imposing subcritical control from the wrong end can give the wrong profile. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"確認座標、底坡與水深定義，從適當邊界逐段求解並隨水深更新摩阻和福祿數。用沿程水位資料檢查曲線，接近臨界或存在水躍時改用可處理轉換的分析而非延長局部直線。","textEn":"Confirm coordinates, bed slope and depth definitions, solve reachwise from an appropriate boundary and update friction and Froude number with depth. Compare the profile with longitudinal observations and use transition-capable analysis near critical flow or jumps instead of extending a local straight line.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將局部水深坡度與底坡合成絕對水面坡度，再比較不同福祿數下的分母。說明為何需要逐段更新而不能將一點導數乘整條河長。","textEn":"Combine local depth gradient with bed slope to obtain the absolute surface slope, then compare denominators at different Froude numbers. Explain why reachwise updating is needed instead of multiplying one derivative by the entire channel length.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「回水曲線與下游控制機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Backwater profiles and downstream control mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","分洪道某一斷面用曼寧式算得的流量，就是全系統任何洪水下的容量。","確認座標、底坡與水深定義，從適當邊界逐段求解並隨水深更新摩阻和福祿數。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Manning flow at one section is the entire system capacity under every flood condition.","Confirm coordinates, bed slope and depth definitions, solve reachwise from an appropriate boundary and update friction and Froude number with depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"確認座標、底坡與水深定義，從適當邊界逐段求解並隨水深更新摩阻和福祿數。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Confirm coordinates, bed slope and depth definitions, solve reachwise from an appropriate boundary and update friction and Froude number with depth. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b272-v15-24","title":"回水曲線與下游控制機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Backwater profiles and downstream control mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「回水曲線與下游控制」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Backwater profiles and downstream control” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把水深坡度當成水面坡度會漏掉底床高程，從錯誤端指定緩流邊界也可能得到錯誤曲線；接近臨界仍用粗步長則會放大數值不穩定。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mistaking depth slope for surface slope omits bed elevation, and imposing subcritical control from the wrong end can give the wrong profile. Coarse steps near critical flow can further magnify numerical instability. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例為稜柱渠的局部漸變流導數，正座標沿下游，水深變化不等於絕對水面高程變化；不作長距離定坡外推。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Depth change is not absolute water-surface elevation change, and the slope is not extrapolated over a long reach.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「分洪道只要向下游傾斜，下游漲水就不可能影響上游水位。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A floodway sloping downstream cannot experience upstream effects from rising tailwater.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把水深坡度當成水面坡度會漏掉底床高程，從錯誤端指定緩流邊界也可能得到錯誤曲線；接近臨界仍用粗步長則會放大數值不穩定。","textEn":"Mistaking depth slope for surface slope omits bed elevation, and imposing subcritical control from the wrong end can give the wrong profile. Coarse steps near critical flow can further magnify numerical instability.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「回水曲線與下游控制機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Backwater profiles and downstream control mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把水深坡度當成水面坡度會漏掉底床高程，從錯誤端指定緩流邊界也可能得到錯誤曲線；接近臨界仍用粗步長則會放大數值不穩定。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","洪峰永遠和平均水流等速，所以距離除流速就是精確到達時間。"],"optionsEn":["Mistaking depth slope for surface slope omits bed elevation, and imposing subcritical control from the wrong end can give the wrong profile.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A flood crest always moves at mean flow velocity, giving exact arrival from distance divided by velocity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把水深坡度當成水面坡度會漏掉底床高程，從錯誤端指定緩流邊界也可能得到錯誤曲線；接近臨界仍用粗步長則會放大數值不穩定。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mistaking depth slope for surface slope omits bed elevation, and imposing subcritical control from the wrong end can give the wrong profile. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b272-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「洪波傳遞與水團速度機理與驗證」與「堤頂餘高與高程預留機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Flood-wave travel and parcel speed mechanism and verification\" and \"Crest margin and elevation allowances mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b272-v15-25","title":"洪波傳遞與水團速度機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Flood-wave travel and parcel speed mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「洪波傳遞與水團速度」如何影響河道分洪工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Flood-wave travel and parcel speed” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River flood-diversion works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"洪峰訊號的傳遞速度不等於某一水團的移動速度，波速取決於流量隨儲水或水深的變化。對寬矩形均勻曼寧流的運動波近似，可得到流速的特定倍數，但回水、擴散與洪泛區儲存會破壞這個簡化；以距離除平均流速直接估警戒時間可能混淆兩種傳遞。本例採寬矩形、固定坡降與糙率的運動波關係c=5V/3，不用於強回水、閘控或急變洪水；不是實際預警提前量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「洪波傳遞與水團速度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A flood signal does not travel at the same speed as a water parcel; wave celerity depends on how discharge changes with storage or depth. A wide rectangular uniform Manning channel yields a particular velocity multiple under a kinematic approximation, but backwater, diffusion and floodplain storage break that simplification. Distance divided by mean velocity can therefore confuse parcel and warning travel times. The example uses c=5V/3 for a wide rectangular kinematic Manning channel with fixed slope and roughness, excluding strong backwater, gate control and abrupt flood transitions. It is not an operational warning lead time. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Flood-wave travel and parcel speed” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設平均流速V=1.5 m/s、長度L=5000 m，運動波c=2.5 m/s，傳遞尺度t=L/c=2000 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume mean velocity V=1.5 m/s and length L=5000 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「洪峰永遠和平均水流等速，所以距離除流速就是精確到達時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A flood crest always moves at mean flow velocity, giving exact arrival from distance divided by velocity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「洪波傳遞與水團速度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Flood-wave travel and parcel speed”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-25-k1","title":"洪波傳遞與水團速度機理與驗證","titleEn":"Flood-wave travel and parcel speed mechanism and verification","text":"洪峰訊號的傳遞速度不等於某一水團的移動速度，波速取決於流量隨儲水或水深的變化。對寬矩形均勻曼寧流的運動波近似，可得到流速的特定倍數，但回水、擴散與洪泛區儲存會破壞這個簡化；以距離除平均流速直接估警戒時間可能混淆兩種傳遞。","textEn":"A flood signal does not travel at the same speed as a water parcel; wave celerity depends on how discharge changes with storage or depth. A wide rectangular uniform Manning channel yields a particular velocity multiple under a kinematic approximation, but backwater, diffusion and floodplain storage break that simplification.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：洪峰永遠和平均水流等速，所以距離除流速就是精確到達時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A flood crest always moves at mean flow velocity, giving exact arrival from distance divided by velocity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「洪波傳遞與水團速度機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Flood-wave travel and parcel speed mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["洪峰永遠和平均水流等速，所以距離除流速就是精確到達時間。","洪峰訊號的傳遞速度不等於某一水團的移動速度，波速取決於流量隨儲水或水深的變化。","只要水面沒有碰到堤頂，分洪道及兩側堤防就不存在失效可能。"],"optionsEn":["A flood crest always moves at mean flow velocity, giving exact arrival from distance divided by velocity.","A flood signal does not travel at the same speed as a water parcel; wave celerity depends on how discharge changes with storage or depth.","If water remains below the crest, the floodway and its embankments cannot fail."],"answer":1,"explanation":"洪峰訊號的傳遞速度不等於某一水團的移動速度，波速取決於流量隨儲水或水深的變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A flood signal does not travel at the same speed as a water parcel; wave celerity depends on how discharge changes with storage or depth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b272-v15-26","title":"洪波傳遞與水團速度機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Flood-wave travel and parcel speed mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「洪波傳遞與水團速度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Flood-wave travel and parcel speed” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設平均流速V=1.5 m/s、長度L=5000 m，運動波c=2.5 m/s，傳遞尺度t=L/c=2000 s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume mean velocity V=1.5 m/s and length L=5000 m. Kinematic celerity c=2.5 m/s gives travel scale t=L/c=2000 s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以多次洪水的上下游歷線估計傳遞與展寬，檢查是否受到尾水或漫地儲存控制。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Estimate travel and broadening from upstream/downstream hydrographs across several floods, checking tailwater and overbank storage influence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設平均流速V=1.5 m/s、長度L=5000 m，運動波c=2.5 m/s，傳遞尺度t=L/c=2000 s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume mean velocity V=1.5 m/s and length L=5000 m. Kinematic celerity c=2.5 m/s gives travel scale t=L/c=2000 s.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「洪波傳遞與水團速度機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Flood-wave travel and parcel speed mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["模型沒有發散且水量閉合，就足以證明分洪水位預測完全可靠。","所有分洪入口只需一個自由堰公式，不受入口方向與尾水影響。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設平均流速V=1.5 m/s、長度L=5000 m，運動波c=2.5 m/s，傳遞尺度t=L/c=2000 s。"],"optionsEn":["A nondiverging model with volume closure proves fully reliable floodway stage predictions.","Every floodway inlet needs only one free-weir formula regardless of orientation or tailwater.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume mean velocity V=1.5 m/s and length L=5000 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設平均流速V=1.5 m/s、長度L=5000 m，運動波c=2.5 m/s，傳遞尺度t=L/c=2000 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume mean velocity V=1.5 m/s and length L=5000 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b272-v15-27","title":"洪波傳遞與水團速度機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Flood-wave travel and parcel speed mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「洪波傳遞與水團速度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Flood-wave travel and parcel speed” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以多次洪水的上下游歷線估計傳遞與展寬，檢查是否受到尾水或漫地儲存控制。分別標示流速、波速及資料延遲，並比較簡化尺度與完整非恆定演算的適用差異。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Estimate travel and broadening from upstream/downstream hydrographs across several floods, checking tailwater and overbank storage influence. Label flow velocity, wave celerity and data latency separately, and compare the simplified scale with the conditions represented by full unsteady routing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用同一河長分別算水團和運動波行程，清楚標出兩者差異。加入假設通訊延遲後，將物理傳遞與資訊到達分開列帳，避免混成一個校正係數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate parcel and kinematic-wave travel for one reach and label their difference. Add a hypothetical communication delay, keeping physical travel and information arrival in separate ledgers instead of combining them into one calibration factor.","failure":"注意干擾：把水團行程當洪峰行程可能錯估訊號到達時間，忽略洪泛區儲存則可能漏掉展寬；若再把遙測延遲算進物理波速，模型參數會失去明確意義。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using parcel travel for crest travel misstates arrival, while omitting floodplain storage misses broadening. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以多次洪水的上下游歷線估計傳遞與展寬，檢查是否受到尾水或漫地儲存控制。分別標示流速、波速及資料延遲，並比較簡化尺度與完整非恆定演算的適用差異。","textEn":"Estimate travel and broadening from upstream/downstream hydrographs across several floods, checking tailwater and overbank storage influence. Label flow velocity, wave celerity and data latency separately, and compare the simplified scale with the conditions represented by full unsteady routing.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用同一河長分別算水團和運動波行程，清楚標出兩者差異。加入假設通訊延遲後，將物理傳遞與資訊到達分開列帳，避免混成一個校正係數。","textEn":"Calculate parcel and kinematic-wave travel for one reach and label their difference. Add a hypothetical communication delay, keeping physical travel and information arrival in separate ledgers instead of combining them into one calibration factor.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「洪波傳遞與水團速度機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Flood-wave travel and parcel speed mechanism and verification\"?","options":["以多次洪水的上下游歷線估計傳遞與展寬，檢查是否受到尾水或漫地儲存控制。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","算出臨界水深後，就已經得到分洪道所有位置的正常水深。"],"optionsEn":["Estimate travel and broadening from upstream/downstream hydrographs across several floods, checking tailwater and overbank storage influence.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Calculating critical depth gives normal depth at every location in the floodway."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以多次洪水的上下游歷線估計傳遞與展寬，檢查是否受到尾水或漫地儲存控制。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Estimate travel and broadening from upstream/downstream hydrographs across several floods, checking tailwater and overbank storage influence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b272-v15-28","title":"洪波傳遞與水團速度機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Flood-wave travel and parcel speed mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「洪波傳遞與水團速度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Flood-wave travel and parcel speed” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把水團行程當洪峰行程可能錯估訊號到達時間，忽略洪泛區儲存則可能漏掉展寬；若再把遙測延遲算進物理波速，模型參數會失去明確意義。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using parcel travel for crest travel misstates arrival, while omitting floodplain storage misses broadening. Folding telemetry delay into physical celerity additionally gives model parameters an ambiguous and misleading meaning. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例採寬矩形、固定坡降與糙率的運動波關係c=5V/3，不用於強回水、閘控或急變洪水；不是實際預警提前量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It is not an operational warning lead time.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「洪峰永遠和平均水流等速，所以距離除流速就是精確到達時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A flood crest always moves at mean flow velocity, giving exact arrival from distance divided by velocity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把水團行程當洪峰行程可能錯估訊號到達時間，忽略洪泛區儲存則可能漏掉展寬；若再把遙測延遲算進物理波速，模型參數會失去明確意義。","textEn":"Using parcel travel for crest travel misstates arrival, while omitting floodplain storage misses broadening. Folding telemetry delay into physical celerity additionally gives model parameters an ambiguous and misleading meaning.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「洪波傳遞與水團速度機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Flood-wave travel and parcel speed mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把水團行程當洪峰行程可能錯估訊號到達時間，忽略洪泛區儲存則可能漏掉展寬；若再把遙測延遲算進物理波速，模型參數會失去明確意義。","只要水面沒有碰到堤頂，分洪道及兩側堤防就不存在失效可能。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using parcel travel for crest travel misstates arrival, while omitting floodplain storage misses broadening.","If water remains below the crest, the floodway and its embankments cannot fail."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把水團行程當洪峰行程可能錯估訊號到達時間，忽略洪泛區儲存則可能漏掉展寬；若再把遙測延遲算進物理波速，模型參數會失去明確意義。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using parcel travel for crest travel misstates arrival, while omitting floodplain storage misses broadening. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b272-v15-29","title":"堤頂餘高與高程預留機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Crest margin and elevation allowances mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「堤頂餘高與高程預留」如何影響河道分洪工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Crest margin and elevation allowances” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River flood-diversion works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分洪道兩側堤頂到水面的幾何差只是起點，沉陷、波浪、模型不確定度與局部水位抬升都會消耗可用餘量。各項預留需要一致定義，不能重複扣已包含在設計水位中的因素；同一標準餘高也不能代替滲流、邊坡和出口安全分析，因為未越頂仍可能發生其他失效。本例只扣指定沉陷量，未加入波浪或其他必要項，也不是任何規範的所需餘高；輸入皆採相同高程基準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「堤頂餘高與高程預留」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The geometric difference between crest and water surface is only a starting point. Settlement, waves, model uncertainty and local setup consume available margin. Allowances need consistent definitions to avoid deducting factors already included in design stage. A crest margin also does not replace seepage, slope or outlet analysis, because failure can occur without overtopping. The example deducts specified settlement only, omitting waves and other necessary terms. It is not a code-required freeboard, and all elevations use one datum. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Crest margin and elevation allowances” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設堤頂Zc=102.5 m、計算水面Zw=101.7 m、預留沉陷s=0.20 m，剩餘幾何餘量F=Zc−Zw−s=0.60 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume crest Zc=102.5 m, computed surface Zw=101.7 m and settlement allowance s=0.20 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要水面沒有碰到堤頂，分洪道及兩側堤防就不存在失效可能。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If water remains below the crest, the floodway and its embankments cannot fail.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「堤頂餘高與高程預留」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Crest margin and elevation allowances”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-29-k1","title":"堤頂餘高與高程預留機理與驗證","titleEn":"Crest margin and elevation allowances mechanism and verification","text":"分洪道兩側堤頂到水面的幾何差只是起點，沉陷、波浪、模型不確定度與局部水位抬升都會消耗可用餘量。各項預留需要一致定義，不能重複扣已包含在設計水位中的因素；同一標準餘高也不能代替滲流、邊坡和出口安全分析，因為未越頂仍可能發生其他失效。","textEn":"The geometric difference between crest and water surface is only a starting point. Settlement, waves, model uncertainty and local setup consume available margin.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要水面沒有碰到堤頂，分洪道及兩側堤防就不存在失效可能。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If water remains below the crest, the floodway and its embankments cannot fail. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「堤頂餘高與高程預留機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Crest margin and elevation allowances mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["只要水面沒有碰到堤頂，分洪道及兩側堤防就不存在失效可能。","分走三成水就必定分走三成泥砂，而且河床可以永遠固定。","分洪道兩側堤頂到水面的幾何差只是起點，沉陷、波浪、模型不確定度與局部水位抬升都會消耗可用餘量。"],"optionsEn":["If water remains below the crest, the floodway and its embankments cannot fail.","Diverting thirty percent of water necessarily diverts thirty percent of sediment with an unchanged bed.","The geometric difference between crest and water surface is only a starting point."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分洪道兩側堤頂到水面的幾何差只是起點，沉陷、波浪、模型不確定度與局部水位抬升都會消耗可用餘量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The geometric difference between crest and water surface is only a starting point. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b272-v15-30","title":"堤頂餘高與高程預留機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Crest margin and elevation allowances mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「堤頂餘高與高程預留」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Crest margin and elevation allowances” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設堤頂Zc=102.5 m、計算水面Zw=101.7 m、預留沉陷s=0.20 m，剩餘幾何餘量F=Zc−Zw−s=0.60 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume crest Zc=102.5 m, computed surface Zw=101.7 m and settlement allowance s=0.20 m. Remaining geometric margin F=Zc−Zw−s=0.60 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿線測量最低堤頂與接合點，確認水位和沉陷使用同一基準及時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey minimum crest and transitions along the route, aligning water level and settlement by datum and time.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設堤頂Zc=102.5 m、計算水面Zw=101.7 m、預留沉陷s=0.20 m，剩餘幾何餘量F=Zc−Zw−s=0.60 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume crest Zc=102.5 m, computed surface Zw=101.7 m and settlement allowance s=0.20 m. Remaining geometric margin F=Zc−Zw−s=0.60 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「堤頂餘高與高程預留機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Crest margin and elevation allowances mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設堤頂Zc=102.5 m、計算水面Zw=101.7 m、預留沉陷s=0.20 m，剩餘幾何餘量F=Zc−Zw−s=0.60 m。","分洪道把洪水帶離城市後，這部分水就不需要再納入下游分析。","分洪道某一斷面用曼寧式算得的流量，就是全系統任何洪水下的容量。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume crest Zc=102.5 m, computed surface Zw=101.7 m and settlement allowance s=0.20 m.","Once a floodway removes water from a city, that water no longer needs downstream analysis.","Manning flow at one section is the entire system capacity under every flood condition."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設堤頂Zc=102.5 m、計算水面Zw=101.7 m、預留沉陷s=0.20 m，剩餘幾何餘量F=Zc−Zw−s=0.60 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume crest Zc=102.5 m, computed surface Zw=101.7 m and settlement allowance s=0.20 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b272-v15-31","title":"堤頂餘高與高程預留機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Crest margin and elevation allowances mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「堤頂餘高與高程預留」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Crest margin and elevation allowances” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿線測量最低堤頂與接合點，確認水位和沉陷使用同一基準及時間。把波浪、模型誤差與沉陷來源逐項列出，檢查哪些已含在設計水位，並另外評估未越頂的失效模式。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey minimum crest and transitions along the route, aligning water level and settlement by datum and time. List wave, model-error and settlement sources, check which are already included in stage, and independently assess failure mechanisms that do not require overtopping. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用三個沿線堤頂與水面資料找最小餘量，加入局部沉陷後重新排序。將越頂和非越頂失效列成平行檢查，說明高程表無法回答的土工問題。","observationEn":"Site practice: Find the minimum margin from three crest/surface pairs and reorder them after local settlement. List overtopping and non-overtopping checks in parallel, explaining geotechnical questions that an elevation table cannot answer.","failure":"注意干擾：只用平均堤頂會漏掉低點，將預留沉陷重複扣除又可能扭曲比較；宣稱仍有幾何餘量就完全安全，則忽略內部侵蝕、邊坡或基礎問題。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An average crest hides low points, while double-counted settlement distorts comparisons. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿線測量最低堤頂與接合點，確認水位和沉陷使用同一基準及時間。把波浪、模型誤差與沉陷來源逐項列出，檢查哪些已含在設計水位，並另外評估未越頂的失效模式。","textEn":"Survey minimum crest and transitions along the route, aligning water level and settlement by datum and time. List wave, model-error and settlement sources, check which are already included in stage, and independently assess failure mechanisms that do not require overtopping.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用三個沿線堤頂與水面資料找最小餘量，加入局部沉陷後重新排序。將越頂和非越頂失效列成平行檢查，說明高程表無法回答的土工問題。","textEn":"Find the minimum margin from three crest/surface pairs and reorder them after local settlement. List overtopping and non-overtopping checks in parallel, explaining geotechnical questions that an elevation table cannot answer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「堤頂餘高與高程預留機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Crest margin and elevation allowances mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","沿線測量最低堤頂與接合點，確認水位和沉陷使用同一基準及時間。","速度水頭增加就是全部局部損失，兩者可以視為同一個項目。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Survey minimum crest and transitions along the route, aligning water level and settlement by datum and time.","An increase in velocity head is the entire local loss and the two terms are identical."],"answer":1,"explanation":"沿線測量最低堤頂與接合點，確認水位和沉陷使用同一基準及時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey minimum crest and transitions along the route, aligning water level and settlement by datum and time. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b272-v15-32","title":"堤頂餘高與高程預留機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Crest margin and elevation allowances mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「堤頂餘高與高程預留」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Crest margin and elevation allowances” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只用平均堤頂會漏掉低點，將預留沉陷重複扣除又可能扭曲比較；宣稱仍有幾何餘量就完全安全，則忽略內部侵蝕、邊坡或基礎問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An average crest hides low points, while double-counted settlement distorts comparisons. Declaring complete safety from positive geometric margin overlooks internal erosion, slope instability and foundation problems below overtopping conditions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例只扣指定沉陷量，未加入波浪或其他必要項，也不是任何規範的所需餘高；輸入皆採相同高程基準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It is not a code-required freeboard, and all elevations use one datum.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要水面沒有碰到堤頂，分洪道及兩側堤防就不存在失效可能。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If water remains below the crest, the floodway and its embankments cannot fail.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只用平均堤頂會漏掉低點，將預留沉陷重複扣除又可能扭曲比較；宣稱仍有幾何餘量就完全安全，則忽略內部侵蝕、邊坡或基礎問題。","textEn":"An average crest hides low points, while double-counted settlement distorts comparisons. Declaring complete safety from positive geometric margin overlooks internal erosion, slope instability and foundation problems below overtopping conditions.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「堤頂餘高與高程預留機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Crest margin and elevation allowances mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","分走三成水就必定分走三成泥砂，而且河床可以永遠固定。","只用平均堤頂會漏掉低點，將預留沉陷重複扣除又可能扭曲比較；宣稱仍有幾何餘量就完全安全，則忽略內部侵蝕、邊坡或基礎問題。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Diverting thirty percent of water necessarily diverts thirty percent of sediment with an unchanged bed.","An average crest hides low points, while double-counted settlement distorts comparisons."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只用平均堤頂會漏掉低點，將預留沉陷重複扣除又可能扭曲比較；宣稱仍有幾何餘量就完全安全，則忽略內部侵蝕、邊坡或基礎問題。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An average crest hides low points, while double-counted settlement distorts comparisons. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b272-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「分洪泥砂與河床演變機理與驗證」與「非恆定時間步與驗證機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Diversion sediment and bed evolution mechanism and verification\" and \"Unsteady time step and verification mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b272-v15-33","title":"分洪泥砂與河床演變機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Diversion sediment and bed evolution mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「分洪泥砂與河床演變」如何影響河道分洪工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diversion sediment and bed evolution” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River flood-diversion works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分洪改變水量分配也會改變輸砂，進入支路的粒徑與濃度不一定和主河平均相同。長期淤積可能抬高入口或減少渠容，沖刷則可能威脅基礎；泥砂體積帳需要區分固體體積與含孔隙床體積，不能把水量分流比例直接當成泥砂分流比例。本例採均勻床面變化、固定孔隙率與固體體積輸砂率，只表示區段平均沉積；未預測局部沖刷或粒徑分選。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分洪泥砂與河床演變」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Diverting water also redistributes sediment, whose size and concentration entering a branch may differ from the main-river average. Aggradation can raise the inlet or reduce channel space, while scour threatens foundations. A sediment-volume ledger distinguishes solids from porous bed volume and must not equate water diversion fraction with sediment diversion fraction. The example assumes uniform bed change, fixed porosity and solid-volume transport rates. It gives reach-average deposition only, excluding local scour and size sorting. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diversion sediment and bed evolution” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設固體輸入Qs,in=0.020、輸出Qs,out=0.015 m³/s，t=3600 s、孔隙率p=0.40、寬B=20 m、長L=1000 m，Δz=0.0015 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume solid inflow 0.020 and outflow 0.015 m³/s, t=3600 s, porosity p=0.40, B=20 m and L=1000 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「分走三成水就必定分走三成泥砂，而且河床可以永遠固定。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Diverting thirty percent of water necessarily diverts thirty percent of sediment with an unchanged bed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「分洪泥砂與河床演變」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diversion sediment and bed evolution”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-33-k1","title":"分洪泥砂與河床演變機理與驗證","titleEn":"Diversion sediment and bed evolution mechanism and verification","text":"分洪改變水量分配也會改變輸砂，進入支路的粒徑與濃度不一定和主河平均相同。長期淤積可能抬高入口或減少渠容，沖刷則可能威脅基礎；泥砂體積帳需要區分固體體積與含孔隙床體積，不能把水量分流比例直接當成泥砂分流比例。","textEn":"Diverting water also redistributes sediment, whose size and concentration entering a branch may differ from the main-river average. Aggradation can raise the inlet or reduce channel space, while scour threatens foundations.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：分走三成水就必定分走三成泥砂，而且河床可以永遠固定。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Diverting thirty percent of water necessarily diverts thirty percent of sediment with an unchanged bed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分洪泥砂與河床演變機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Diversion sediment and bed evolution mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["分洪改變水量分配也會改變輸砂，進入支路的粒徑與濃度不一定和主河平均相同。","分走三成水就必定分走三成泥砂，而且河床可以永遠固定。","模型沒有發散且水量閉合，就足以證明分洪水位預測完全可靠。"],"optionsEn":["Diverting water also redistributes sediment, whose size and concentration entering a branch may differ from the main-river average.","Diverting thirty percent of water necessarily diverts thirty percent of sediment with an unchanged bed.","A nondiverging model with volume closure proves fully reliable floodway stage predictions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分洪改變水量分配也會改變輸砂，進入支路的粒徑與濃度不一定和主河平均相同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Diverting water also redistributes sediment, whose size and concentration entering a branch may differ from the main-river average. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b272-v15-34","title":"分洪泥砂與河床演變機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Diversion sediment and bed evolution mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「分洪泥砂與河床演變」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diversion sediment and bed evolution” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設固體輸入Qs,in=0.020、輸出Qs,out=0.015 m³/s，t=3600 s、孔隙率p=0.40、寬B=20 m、長L=1000 m，Δz=0.0015 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume solid inflow 0.020 and outflow 0.015 m³/s, t=3600 s, porosity p=0.40, B=20 m and L=1000 m. Mean Δz=(Qsin−Qsout)t/[(1−p)BL]=0.0015 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將上下游分粒徑輸砂量與重複地形測量比較，統一固體與床體積定義。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare size-resolved upstream/downstream transport with repeat surveys using consistent solid and bulk-volume definitions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設固體輸入Qs,in=0.020、輸出Qs,out=0.015 m³/s，t=3600 s、孔隙率p=0.40、寬B=20 m、長L=1000 m，Δz=0.0015 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume solid inflow 0.020 and outflow 0.015 m³/s, t=3600 s, porosity p=0.40, B=20 m and L=1000 m. Mean Δz=(Qsin−Qsout)t/[(1−p)BL]=0.0015 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「分洪泥砂與河床演變機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Diversion sediment and bed evolution mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["所有分洪入口只需一個自由堰公式，不受入口方向與尾水影響。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設固體輸入Qs,in=0.020、輸出Qs,out=0.015 m³/s，t=3600 s、孔隙率p=0.40、寬B=20 m、長L=1000 m，Δz=0.0015 m。","算出臨界水深後，就已經得到分洪道所有位置的正常水深。"],"optionsEn":["Every floodway inlet needs only one free-weir formula regardless of orientation or tailwater.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume solid inflow 0.020 and outflow 0.015 m³/s, t=3600 s, porosity p=0.40, B=20 m and L=1000 m.","Calculating critical depth gives normal depth at every location in the floodway."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設固體輸入Qs,in=0.020、輸出Qs,out=0.015 m³/s，t=3600 s、孔隙率p=0.40、寬B=20 m、長L=1000 m，Δz=0.0015 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume solid inflow 0.020 and outflow 0.015 m³/s, t=3600 s, porosity p=0.40, B=20 m and L=1000 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b272-v15-35","title":"分洪泥砂與河床演變機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Diversion sediment and bed evolution mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「分洪泥砂與河床演變」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Diversion sediment and bed evolution” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將上下游分粒徑輸砂量與重複地形測量比較，統一固體與床體積定義。檢查入口附近和彎道的局部變化，並讓更新後河床回饋到水理模型，而不是永久固定初始斷面。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare size-resolved upstream/downstream transport with repeat surveys using consistent solid and bulk-volume definitions. Inspect localized changes near the inlet and bends, and feed the updated bed back into hydraulics instead of retaining the initial channel geometry indefinitely despite sediment evolution. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用相同固體量比較兩種孔隙率的床面升幅，再把沉積集中於入口短段。說明平均高程與局部高程對水理模型有何不同影響，規劃重複測量位置。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare bed rise at two porosities for the same solid volume, then concentrate deposition in a short inlet reach. Explain how mean and local elevations affect hydraulics differently and choose repeat-survey locations accordingly.","failure":"注意干擾：漏掉孔隙率會低估沉積床體積，區段平均很小也可能掩蓋入口沙洲；固定河床模型若用於多年規劃，可能高估未來分洪能力或漏掉局部基礎沖刷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting porosity understates deposited bed volume, and a small reach average can conceal an inlet bar. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將上下游分粒徑輸砂量與重複地形測量比較，統一固體與床體積定義。檢查入口附近和彎道的局部變化，並讓更新後河床回饋到水理模型，而不是永久固定初始斷面。","textEn":"Compare size-resolved upstream/downstream transport with repeat surveys using consistent solid and bulk-volume definitions. Inspect localized changes near the inlet and bends, and feed the updated bed back into hydraulics instead of retaining the initial channel geometry indefinitely despite sediment evolution.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用相同固體量比較兩種孔隙率的床面升幅，再把沉積集中於入口短段。說明平均高程與局部高程對水理模型有何不同影響，規劃重複測量位置。","textEn":"Compare bed rise at two porosities for the same solid volume, then concentrate deposition in a short inlet reach. Explain how mean and local elevations affect hydraulics differently and choose repeat-survey locations accordingly.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「分洪泥砂與河床演變機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Diversion sediment and bed evolution mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","分洪道只要向下游傾斜，下游漲水就不可能影響上游水位。","將上下游分粒徑輸砂量與重複地形測量比較，統一固體與床體積定義。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A floodway sloping downstream cannot experience upstream effects from rising tailwater.","Compare size-resolved upstream/downstream transport with repeat surveys using consistent solid and bulk-volume definitions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將上下游分粒徑輸砂量與重複地形測量比較，統一固體與床體積定義。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare size-resolved upstream/downstream transport with repeat surveys using consistent solid and bulk-volume definitions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b272-v15-36","title":"分洪泥砂與河床演變機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Diversion sediment and bed evolution mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「分洪泥砂與河床演變」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Diversion sediment and bed evolution” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏掉孔隙率會低估沉積床體積，區段平均很小也可能掩蓋入口沙洲；固定河床模型若用於多年規劃，可能高估未來分洪能力或漏掉局部基礎沖刷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting porosity understates deposited bed volume, and a small reach average can conceal an inlet bar. A fixed-bed model used for long-term planning may overstate future diversion or miss local foundation scour. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例採均勻床面變化、固定孔隙率與固體體積輸砂率，只表示區段平均沉積；未預測局部沖刷或粒徑分選。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It gives reach-average deposition only, excluding local scour and size sorting.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「分走三成水就必定分走三成泥砂，而且河床可以永遠固定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Diverting thirty percent of water necessarily diverts thirty percent of sediment with an unchanged bed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏掉孔隙率會低估沉積床體積，區段平均很小也可能掩蓋入口沙洲；固定河床模型若用於多年規劃，可能高估未來分洪能力或漏掉局部基礎沖刷。","textEn":"Omitting porosity understates deposited bed volume, and a small reach average can conceal an inlet bar. A fixed-bed model used for long-term planning may overstate future diversion or miss local foundation scour.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分洪泥砂與河床演變機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Diversion sediment and bed evolution mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["漏掉孔隙率會低估沉積床體積，區段平均很小也可能掩蓋入口沙洲；固定河床模型若用於多年規劃，可能高估未來分洪能力或漏掉局部基礎沖刷。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","模型沒有發散且水量閉合，就足以證明分洪水位預測完全可靠。"],"optionsEn":["Omitting porosity understates deposited bed volume, and a small reach average can conceal an inlet bar.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A nondiverging model with volume closure proves fully reliable floodway stage predictions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"漏掉孔隙率會低估沉積床體積，區段平均很小也可能掩蓋入口沙洲；固定河床模型若用於多年規劃，可能高估未來分洪能力或漏掉局部基礎沖刷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting porosity understates deposited bed volume, and a small reach average can conceal an inlet bar. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b272-v15-37","title":"非恆定時間步與驗證機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Unsteady time step and verification mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「非恆定時間步與驗證」如何影響河道分洪工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Unsteady time step and verification” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River flood-diversion works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"洪水演算需解析波在網格間的傳遞，時間步過大可能造成振盪、數值擴散或漏失短時控制。庫朗數可作顯式淺水波離散的尺度檢查，但不同求解器的穩定與準確條件不同，不能把一個數值當所有軟體保證；網格、時間步和邊界敏感度應與量測驗證一同檢查。本例使用矩形水深的重力波速與順流速度相加，指定目標庫朗數只為示範；隱式求解器或其他格式需依自身文件判斷。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「非恆定時間步與驗證」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Flood routing must resolve propagation between cells; a large time step can cause oscillation, numerical diffusion or missed brief control. Courant number offers a scale check for explicit shallow-water discretization, but stability and accuracy differ among solvers. One number is not a universal software guarantee; grid, time-step and boundary sensitivity require checking alongside observations. The example adds rectangular-channel gravity-wave speed to downstream velocity for an illustrative target Courant number. Implicit solvers and other schemes require their own documented criteria. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Unsteady time step and verification” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δx=50 m、V=2 m/s、h=2 m、g=9.81 m/s²、C=0.80，Δt=CΔx/(V+√gh)=6.221 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δx=50 m, V=2 m/s, h=2 m, g=9.81 m/s² and C=0.80.","failure":"常見誤解：「模型沒有發散且水量閉合，就足以證明分洪水位預測完全可靠。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A nondiverging model with volume closure proves fully reliable floodway stage predictions.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「非恆定時間步與驗證」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Unsteady time step and verification”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-37-k1","title":"非恆定時間步與驗證機理與驗證","titleEn":"Unsteady time step and verification mechanism and verification","text":"洪水演算需解析波在網格間的傳遞，時間步過大可能造成振盪、數值擴散或漏失短時控制。庫朗數可作顯式淺水波離散的尺度檢查，但不同求解器的穩定與準確條件不同，不能把一個數值當所有軟體保證；網格、時間步和邊界敏感度應與量測驗證一同檢查。","textEn":"Flood routing must resolve propagation between cells; a large time step can cause oscillation, numerical diffusion or missed brief control. Courant number offers a scale check for explicit shallow-water discretization, but stability and accuracy differ among solvers.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模型沒有發散且水量閉合，就足以證明分洪水位預測完全可靠。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A nondiverging model with volume closure proves fully reliable floodway stage predictions. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「非恆定時間步與驗證機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Unsteady time step and verification mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["模型沒有發散且水量閉合，就足以證明分洪水位預測完全可靠。","洪水演算需解析波在網格間的傳遞，時間步過大可能造成振盪、數值擴散或漏失短時控制。","分洪道把洪水帶離城市後，這部分水就不需要再納入下游分析。"],"optionsEn":["A nondiverging model with volume closure proves fully reliable floodway stage predictions.","Flood routing must resolve propagation between cells; a large time step can cause oscillation, numerical diffusion or missed brief control.","Once a floodway removes water from a city, that water no longer needs downstream analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"洪水演算需解析波在網格間的傳遞，時間步過大可能造成振盪、數值擴散或漏失短時控制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Flood routing must resolve propagation between cells; a large time step can cause oscillation, numerical diffusion or missed brief control. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b272-v15-38","title":"非恆定時間步與驗證機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Unsteady time step and verification mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「非恆定時間步與驗證」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Unsteady time step and verification” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δx=50 m、V=2 m/s、h=2 m、g=9.81 m/s²、C=0.80，Δt=CΔx/(V+√gh)=6.221 s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δx=50 m, V=2 m/s, h=2 m, g=9.81 m/s² and C=0.80. Time step Δt=CΔx/(V+√gh)=6.221 s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：確認求解器格式和庫朗數定義，縮小網格與時間步比較水位、分流比例和峰時。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Confirm solver formulation and Courant definition, refine grid and time step and compare stage, diversion share and peak time.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δx=50 m、V=2 m/s、h=2 m、g=9.81 m/s²、C=0.80，Δt=CΔx/(V+√gh)=6.221 s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δx=50 m, V=2 m/s, h=2 m, g=9.81 m/s² and C=0.80. Time step Δt=CΔx/(V+√gh)=6.221 s.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「非恆定時間步與驗證機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Unsteady time step and verification mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["分洪道某一斷面用曼寧式算得的流量，就是全系統任何洪水下的容量。","速度水頭增加就是全部局部損失，兩者可以視為同一個項目。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δx=50 m、V=2 m/s、h=2 m、g=9.81 m/s²、C=0.80，Δt=CΔx/(V+√gh)=6.221 s。"],"optionsEn":["Manning flow at one section is the entire system capacity under every flood condition.","An increase in velocity head is the entire local loss and the two terms are identical.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δx=50 m, V=2 m/s, h=2 m, g=9.81 m/s² and C=0.80."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δx=50 m、V=2 m/s、h=2 m、g=9.81 m/s²、C=0.80，Δt=CΔx/(V+√gh)=6.221 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δx=50 m, V=2 m/s, h=2 m, g=9.81 m/s² and C=0.80. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b272-v15-39","title":"非恆定時間步與驗證機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Unsteady time step and verification mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「非恆定時間步與驗證」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Unsteady time step and verification” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"確認求解器格式和庫朗數定義，縮小網格與時間步比較水位、分流比例和峰時。保留水量殘差及局部振盪位置，再用未參與校正的事件驗證，不能只以計算成功結束當作通過。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Confirm solver formulation and Courant definition, refine grid and time step and compare stage, diversion share and peak time. Retain balance residuals and locations of oscillation, then validate against an event excluded from calibration rather than treating successful program completion as proof. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：製作粗細兩組網格與時間步的比較表，分開列穩定性、守恆與峰值差異。指出哪種差異需要改善數值解析度，哪種可能需要重新調查實際邊界。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare coarse and fine grids and steps, listing stability, conservation and peak differences separately. Identify differences requiring numerical refinement versus those suggesting renewed investigation of the physical boundary conditions.","failure":"注意干擾：穩定但過度擴散的解仍可能壓低洪峰，粗網格也會抹平入口或堤頂低點；只為通過數值穩定而修改物理糙率，會讓參數失去真實意義。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A stable but diffusive solution can suppress the crest, and coarse cells can smooth an inlet or low crest point. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"確認求解器格式和庫朗數定義，縮小網格與時間步比較水位、分流比例和峰時。保留水量殘差及局部振盪位置，再用未參與校正的事件驗證，不能只以計算成功結束當作通過。","textEn":"Confirm solver formulation and Courant definition, refine grid and time step and compare stage, diversion share and peak time. Retain balance residuals and locations of oscillation, then validate against an event excluded from calibration rather than treating successful program completion as proof.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"製作粗細兩組網格與時間步的比較表，分開列穩定性、守恆與峰值差異。指出哪種差異需要改善數值解析度，哪種可能需要重新調查實際邊界。","textEn":"Compare coarse and fine grids and steps, listing stability, conservation and peak differences separately. Identify differences requiring numerical refinement versus those suggesting renewed investigation of the physical boundary conditions.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「非恆定時間步與驗證機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Unsteady time step and verification mechanism and verification\"?","options":["確認求解器格式和庫朗數定義，縮小網格與時間步比較水位、分流比例和峰時。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","洪峰永遠和平均水流等速，所以距離除流速就是精確到達時間。"],"optionsEn":["Confirm solver formulation and Courant definition, refine grid and time step and compare stage, diversion share and peak time.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A flood crest always moves at mean flow velocity, giving exact arrival from distance divided by velocity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"確認求解器格式和庫朗數定義，縮小網格與時間步比較水位、分流比例和峰時。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Confirm solver formulation and Courant definition, refine grid and time step and compare stage, diversion share and peak time. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b272-v15-40","title":"非恆定時間步與驗證機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Unsteady time step and verification mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"prerequisiteIds":["b272-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「非恆定時間步與驗證」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Unsteady time step and verification” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"穩定但過度擴散的解仍可能壓低洪峰，粗網格也會抹平入口或堤頂低點；只為通過數值穩定而修改物理糙率，會讓參數失去真實意義。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A stable but diffusive solution can suppress the crest, and coarse cells can smooth an inlet or low crest point. Changing physical roughness merely to achieve numerical stability gives that parameter a false physical interpretation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例使用矩形水深的重力波速與順流速度相加，指定目標庫朗數只為示範；隱式求解器或其他格式需依自身文件判斷。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Implicit solvers and other schemes require their own documented criteria.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模型沒有發散且水量閉合，就足以證明分洪水位預測完全可靠。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A nondiverging model with volume closure proves fully reliable floodway stage predictions.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b272-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"穩定但過度擴散的解仍可能壓低洪峰，粗網格也會抹平入口或堤頂低點；只為通過數值穩定而修改物理糙率，會讓參數失去真實意義。","textEn":"A stable but diffusive solution can suppress the crest, and coarse cells can smooth an inlet or low crest point. Changing physical roughness merely to achieve numerical stability gives that parameter a false physical interpretation.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]},{"id":"b272-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「非恆定時間步與驗證機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Unsteady time step and verification mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","穩定但過度擴散的解仍可能壓低洪峰，粗網格也會抹平入口或堤頂低點；只為通過數值穩定而修改物理糙率，會讓參數失去真實意義。","分洪道把洪水帶離城市後，這部分水就不需要再納入下游分析。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A stable but diffusive solution can suppress the crest, and coarse cells can smooth an inlet or low crest point.","Once a floodway removes water from a city, that water no longer needs downstream analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"穩定但過度擴散的解仍可能壓低洪峰，粗網格也會抹平入口或堤頂低點；只為通過數值穩定而修改物理糙率，會讓參數失去真實意義。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A stable but diffusive solution can suppress the crest, and coarse cells can smooth an inlet or low crest point. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-manitoba-floodway","v15s-dsd-yuenlong"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b273","title":"土堤壓密與防滲","titleEn":"Levee compaction and seepage control","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"由土料三相、調濕與乾密度出發，課程連結地基壓密時間、達西流徑、防滲牆阻抗、濾層及孔壓監測。每一步區分材料試驗與整體構造行為，特別避免把抗隆起比值當所有管湧的安全證明。西沙加緬度及紅河提供已核對背景，數學量值全部是獨立教學假設。","summaryEn":"Starting from soil phases, conditioning and dry density, the course connects consolidation timing, Darcy paths, cutoff resistance, filters and pore-pressure monitoring. Each step distinguishes material tests from whole-structure behavior, especially avoiding claims that a heave ratio proves safety against all piping. West Sacramento and Red River provide verified context; every numerical value is an independent teaching assumption.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["土料與調濕","Soil and conditioning"],["層間與密度","Lifts and density"],["地基壓密","Foundation consolidation"],["濾層防滲","Filters and cutoff"],["監測反饋","Monitoring feedback"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["土料與調濕","層間與密度","地基壓密","濾層防滲","監測反饋"],"labelsEn":["Soil and conditioning","Lifts and density","Foundation consolidation","Filters and cutoff","Monitoring feedback"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"敏感度固定一維均質層的排水長2 m及百分之九十時間因子0.848，只把壓密係數由1.0×10⁻⁷提高到1.1×10⁻⁷ m²/s。時間由392.59降至356.90日，減少9.09%，並非減少百分之十；壓密係數在分母，所以必須用倒數比例。此比較假設排水邊界、荷載與土性模型均不變，不能代表打設排水板或改變填築速度後的現場工期。這些變更還會影響排水路徑、塗抹區、井阻與荷載歷程，應另建立模型並以多深度孔壓及沉陷歷線檢核。","textEn":"Hold drainage length at 2 m and the ninety-percent time factor at 0.848 for a uniform one-dimensional layer, increasing consolidation coefficient from 1.0×10⁻⁷ to 1.1×10⁻⁷ m²/s. Time decreases from 392.59 to 356.90 days, a 9.09% reduction rather than ten percent because the coefficient enters the denominator. This comparison holds drainage boundaries, loading and the material model fixed. It does not predict construction time after adding vertical drains or changing fill rate. Such changes can alter drainage distance, smear, well resistance and loading history, requiring a different model checked against multi-depth pore-pressure and settlement histories. The uncertainty in the coefficient should therefore remain visible alongside the computed time.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b273-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「含水量與乾密度機理與驗證」與「土料調濕與拌合機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Moisture and dry density mechanism and verification\" and \"Moisture conditioning and blending mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b273-v15-01","title":"含水量與乾密度機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Moisture and dry density mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「含水量與乾密度」如何影響土堤壓密與防滲的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Moisture and dry density” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Levee compaction and seepage control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"夯實以機械能改變土粒排列並排出部分空氣，現場濕密度同時含固體與水，必須配合含水量換算乾密度。相對夯實度還需對應相同土料及試驗能量的室內最大乾密度；不同級配、超粒徑修正或取樣位置會改變可比性，不能只追求單一百分比而忽略土層接合與滲透性。本例含水量以水重除乾土重定義，密度均為質量密度。數值只做換算，不把假設室內峰值或百分比當任何現場驗收標準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「含水量與乾密度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compaction rearranges particles mechanically and removes some air. Field wet density includes solids and water and must be converted using moisture content. Relative compaction additionally requires a laboratory maximum for compatible material and test energy. Gradation changes, oversize corrections and sampling location affect comparability, so one percentage cannot replace attention to lift bonding and permeability. Moisture is water mass divided by dry-solid mass, and densities are mass densities. This conversion does not make the assumed laboratory peak or resulting percentage a field acceptance criterion. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Moisture and dry density” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設濕密度ρ=2.00 Mg/m³、w=0.15，乾密度ρd=ρ/(1+w)=1.739 Mg/m³；室內峰值1.85 Mg/m³，相對夯實度94.01%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume wet density 2.00 Mg/m³ and moisture w=0.15.","failure":"常見誤解：「現場濕密度較高就必定表示乾密度與防滲能力都較好。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Higher field wet density necessarily means better dry density and seepage resistance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「含水量與乾密度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Moisture and dry density”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-01-k1","title":"含水量與乾密度機理與驗證","titleEn":"Moisture and dry density mechanism and verification","text":"夯實以機械能改變土粒排列並排出部分空氣，現場濕密度同時含固體與水，必須配合含水量換算乾密度。相對夯實度還需對應相同土料及試驗能量的室內最大乾密度；不同級配、超粒徑修正或取樣位置會改變可比性，不能只追求單一百分比而忽略土層接合與滲透性。","textEn":"Compaction rearranges particles mechanically and removes some air. Field wet density includes solids and water and must be converted using moisture content.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：現場濕密度較高就必定表示乾密度與防滲能力都較好。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Higher field wet density necessarily means better dry density and seepage resistance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「含水量與乾密度機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Moisture and dry density mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["現場濕密度較高就必定表示乾密度與防滲能力都較好。","夯實以機械能改變土粒排列並排出部分空氣，現場濕密度同時含固體與水，必須配合含水量換算乾密度。","只要加水總量正確，每個土團就會立即具有相同含水量。"],"optionsEn":["Higher field wet density necessarily means better dry density and seepage resistance.","Compaction rearranges particles mechanically and removes some air.","A correct total water dose immediately gives every soil clod identical moisture."],"answer":1,"explanation":"夯實以機械能改變土粒排列並排出部分空氣，現場濕密度同時含固體與水，必須配合含水量換算乾密度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compaction rearranges particles mechanically and removes some air. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b273-v15-02","title":"含水量與乾密度機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Moisture and dry density mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「含水量與乾密度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Moisture and dry density” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設濕密度ρ=2.00 Mg/m³、w=0.15，乾密度ρd=ρ/(1+w)=1.739 Mg/m³；室內峰值1.85 Mg/m³，相對夯實度94.01%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume wet density 2.00 Mg/m³ and moisture w=0.15. Dry density is 1.739 Mg/m³; relative to a laboratory maximum of 1.85 Mg/m³, compaction is 94.01%. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將密度與含水量取自可對應的土樣和位置，核對室內試驗能量、級配及超粒徑處理。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pair density and moisture from corresponding material and locations, checking laboratory energy, gradation and oversize treatment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設濕密度ρ=2.00 Mg/m³、w=0.15，乾密度ρd=ρ/(1+w)=1.739 Mg/m³；室內峰值1.85 Mg/m³，相對夯實度94.01%。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume wet density 2.00 Mg/m³ and moisture w=0.15. Dry density is 1.739 Mg/m³; relative to a laboratory maximum of 1.85 Mg/m³, compaction is 94.01%.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「含水量與乾密度機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Moisture and dry density mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["填土達到指定夯實度，就能證明下方軟弱地基不再壓密。","達西公式中的水位差本身就是水力坡降，不需要流徑長度。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設濕密度ρ=2.00 Mg/m³、w=0.15，乾密度ρd=ρ/(1+w)=1.739 Mg/m³。"],"optionsEn":["Specified fill compaction proves that the underlying soft foundation will no longer consolidate.","Head difference alone is the Darcy hydraulic gradient and needs no flow-path length.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume wet density 2.00 Mg/m³ and moisture w=0.15."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設濕密度ρ=2.00 Mg/m³、w=0.15，乾密度ρd=ρ/(1+w)=1.739 Mg/m³；室內峰值1.85 Mg/m³，相對夯實度94.01%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume wet density 2.00 Mg/m³ and moisture w=0.15. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b273-v15-03","title":"含水量與乾密度機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Moisture and dry density mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「含水量與乾密度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Moisture and dry density” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將密度與含水量取自可對應的土樣和位置，核對室內試驗能量、級配及超粒徑處理。沿每層厚度與接合帶安排檢查，異常時先追查土料和儀器校核，不能用另一處含水量替代。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pair density and moisture from corresponding material and locations, checking laboratory energy, gradation and oversize treatment. Inspect lift thickness and transitions as well as point density; investigate material changes and instrument calibration before substituting moisture measurements from another location. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以兩組相同濕密度但不同含水量重算乾密度，再列出室內與現場必須一致的條件。說明為何密度比較仍不能代替滲透試驗和層間連續性檢查。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate dry density for equal wet densities at two moisture contents, then list laboratory and field comparability conditions. Explain why density comparison still cannot replace permeability testing and inspection of continuity between lifts.","failure":"注意干擾：濕土可能有較高濕密度卻較低乾密度，誤用不同材料的室內峰值會造成錯誤合格判斷；局部表面測得密實也可能掩蓋厚層底部未壓實。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Wet soil may show high bulk density but low dry density. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將密度與含水量取自可對應的土樣和位置，核對室內試驗能量、級配及超粒徑處理。沿每層厚度與接合帶安排檢查，異常時先追查土料和儀器校核，不能用另一處含水量替代。","textEn":"Pair density and moisture from corresponding material and locations, checking laboratory energy, gradation and oversize treatment. Inspect lift thickness and transitions as well as point density; investigate material changes and instrument calibration before substituting moisture measurements from another location.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以兩組相同濕密度但不同含水量重算乾密度，再列出室內與現場必須一致的條件。說明為何密度比較仍不能代替滲透試驗和層間連續性檢查。","textEn":"Recalculate dry density for equal wet densities at two moisture contents, then list laboratory and field comparability conditions. Explain why density comparison still cannot replace permeability testing and inspection of continuity between lifts.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「含水量與乾密度機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Moisture and dry density mechanism and verification\"?","options":["將密度與含水量取自可對應的土樣和位置，核對室內試驗能量、級配及超粒徑處理。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","牆材滲透係數很低，就能忽略所有牆尖繞流與施工接頭。"],"optionsEn":["Pair density and moisture from corresponding material and locations, checking laboratory energy, gradation and oversize treatment.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Very low wall-material conductivity makes all tip bypass and construction joints irrelevant."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將密度與含水量取自可對應的土樣和位置，核對室內試驗能量、級配及超粒徑處理。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pair density and moisture from corresponding material and locations, checking laboratory energy, gradation and oversize treatment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b273-v15-04","title":"含水量與乾密度機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Moisture and dry density mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「含水量與乾密度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Moisture and dry density” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"濕土可能有較高濕密度卻較低乾密度，誤用不同材料的室內峰值會造成錯誤合格判斷；局部表面測得密實也可能掩蓋厚層底部未壓實。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Wet soil may show high bulk density but low dry density. A laboratory peak from different material misclassifies acceptance, while a dense surface can conceal an inadequately compacted lower part of a thick lift. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：數值只做換算，不把假設室內峰值或百分比當任何現場驗收標準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This conversion does not make the assumed laboratory peak or resulting percentage a field acceptance criterion.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「現場濕密度較高就必定表示乾密度與防滲能力都較好。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher field wet density necessarily means better dry density and seepage resistance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"濕土可能有較高濕密度卻較低乾密度，誤用不同材料的室內峰值會造成錯誤合格判斷；局部表面測得密實也可能掩蓋厚層底部未壓實。","textEn":"Wet soil may show high bulk density but low dry density. A laboratory peak from different material misclassifies acceptance, while a dense surface can conceal an inadequately compacted lower part of a thick lift.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「含水量與乾密度機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Moisture and dry density mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","濕土可能有較高濕密度卻較低乾密度，誤用不同材料的室內峰值會造成錯誤合格判斷；局部表面測得密實也可能掩蓋厚層底部未壓實。","只要加水總量正確，每個土團就會立即具有相同含水量。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Wet soil may show high bulk density but low dry density.","A correct total water dose immediately gives every soil clod identical moisture."],"answer":1,"explanation":"濕土可能有較高濕密度卻較低乾密度，誤用不同材料的室內峰值會造成錯誤合格判斷；局部表面測得密實也可能掩蓋厚層底部未壓實。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Wet soil may show high bulk density but low dry density. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b273-v15-05","title":"土料調濕與拌合機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Moisture conditioning and blending mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「土料調濕與拌合」如何影響土堤壓密與防滲的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Moisture conditioning and blending” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Levee compaction and seepage control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"土料調濕改變施工時的可壓實性，但最佳含水量隨土性與夯實能量而異。加水計畫需以乾土質量建立水量帳，再考慮拌合均勻度、蒸發與雨水；平均含水量符合目標不代表每一團塊都符合，過濕或乾硬團塊仍可能留下不同變形與滲流通道。本例封閉水量帳假設乾土質量不變、加入的水全部保留，目標只是指定教學值，不宣稱位於最佳含水量或可立即施工。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「土料調濕與拌合」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Moisture conditioning changes compactability, but optimum moisture depends on material and compaction energy. Added water is calculated from dry-solid mass before accounting for mixing, evaporation and rainfall. Meeting an average moisture target does not mean every clod meets it; wet pockets and hard dry clods can produce contrasting deformation and seepage paths. The closed water balance holds dry mass fixed and retains all added water. The target is an assigned teaching value, not a demonstrated optimum or authorization to place the soil. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Moisture conditioning and blending” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設乾土Md=1000 kg，初始w1=0.12、目標w2=0.15，需加水ΔMw=Md(w2−w1)=30 kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume dry soil Md=1000 kg, initial moisture w1=0.12 and target w2=0.15.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要加水總量正確，每個土團就會立即具有相同含水量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A correct total water dose immediately gives every soil clod identical moisture.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「土料調濕與拌合」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Moisture conditioning and blending”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-05-k1","title":"土料調濕與拌合機理與驗證","titleEn":"Moisture conditioning and blending mechanism and verification","text":"土料調濕改變施工時的可壓實性，但最佳含水量隨土性與夯實能量而異。加水計畫需以乾土質量建立水量帳，再考慮拌合均勻度、蒸發與雨水；平均含水量符合目標不代表每一團塊都符合，過濕或乾硬團塊仍可能留下不同變形與滲流通道。","textEn":"Moisture conditioning changes compactability, but optimum moisture depends on material and compaction energy. Added water is calculated from dry-solid mass before accounting for mixing, evaporation and rainfall.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要加水總量正確，每個土團就會立即具有相同含水量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A correct total water dose immediately gives every soil clod identical moisture. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「土料調濕與拌合機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Moisture conditioning and blending mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["只要加水總量正確，每個土團就會立即具有相同含水量。","相同乾密度的兩份土一定具有相同飽和度與滲透係數。","土料調濕改變施工時的可壓實性，但最佳含水量隨土性與夯實能量而異。"],"optionsEn":["A correct total water dose immediately gives every soil clod identical moisture.","Two soils with equal dry density necessarily have equal saturation and hydraulic conductivity.","Moisture conditioning changes compactability, but optimum moisture depends on material and compaction energy."],"answer":2,"explanation":"土料調濕改變施工時的可壓實性，但最佳含水量隨土性與夯實能量而異。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Moisture conditioning changes compactability, but optimum moisture depends on material and compaction energy. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b273-v15-06","title":"土料調濕與拌合機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Moisture conditioning and blending mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「土料調濕與拌合」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Moisture conditioning and blending” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設乾土Md=1000 kg，初始w1=0.12、目標w2=0.15，需加水ΔMw=Md(w2−w1)=30 kg。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume dry soil Md=1000 kg, initial moisture w1=0.12 and target w2=0.15. Required retained water ΔMw=Md(w2−w1)=30 kg. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先核對含水量分母為乾土質量，追蹤加水計量、天候及拌合後各點試樣。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Confirm the dry-mass moisture denominator and track metered water, weather and samples after blending.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設乾土Md=1000 kg，初始w1=0.12、目標w2=0.15，需加水ΔMw=Md(w2−w1)=30 kg。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume dry soil Md=1000 kg, initial moisture w1=0.12 and target w2=0.15. Required retained water ΔMw=Md(w2−w1)=30 kg.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「土料調濕與拌合機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Moisture conditioning and blending mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設乾土Md=1000 kg，初始w1=0.12、目標w2=0.15，需加水ΔMw=Md(w2−w1)=30 kg。","土層厚度減半時，所有情況的壓密時間都只會減半。","抗隆起比值大於一，就能排除所有逆向侵蝕與管湧機制。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume dry soil Md=1000 kg, initial moisture w1=0.12 and target w2=0.15.","Halving soil thickness always halves consolidation time under every drainage condition.","A heave ratio above one eliminates every backward-erosion and piping mechanism."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設乾土Md=1000 kg，初始w1=0.12、目標w2=0.15，需加水ΔMw=Md(w2−w1)=30 kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume dry soil Md=1000 kg, initial moisture w1=0.12 and target w2=0.15. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b273-v15-07","title":"土料調濕與拌合機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Moisture conditioning and blending mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「土料調濕與拌合」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Moisture conditioning and blending” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先核對含水量分母為乾土質量，追蹤加水計量、天候及拌合後各點試樣。利用試驗填築確認鬆鋪厚度、機具與遍數，並比較表層和內部含水量以辨識混合不均。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Confirm the dry-mass moisture denominator and track metered water, weather and samples after blending. Use trial placement to establish loose-lift thickness, equipment and passes, comparing surface and interior moisture to detect uneven mixing rather than relying solely on a delivered water total. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把乾土質量、水量與可能蒸發分開列帳，另設幾個混合後取樣點。比較平均合格但離散很大的情況，提出能辨識土團內外差異的驗證方式。","observationEn":"Site practice: Separate dry mass, water dose and possible evaporation in a ledger, with several post-mixing sample locations. Compare a compliant mean with high scatter and propose verification that distinguishes clod interiors from their surfaces.","failure":"注意干擾：以濕土總重乘含水量差會算錯加水量，短時間表面灑水也可能只弄濕外皮；直接增加機具遍數未必能補救內部含水量不適或團塊未打散。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Multiplying moisture change by wet total mass gives the wrong dose. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先核對含水量分母為乾土質量，追蹤加水計量、天候及拌合後各點試樣。利用試驗填築確認鬆鋪厚度、機具與遍數，並比較表層和內部含水量以辨識混合不均。","textEn":"Confirm the dry-mass moisture denominator and track metered water, weather and samples after blending. Use trial placement to establish loose-lift thickness, equipment and passes, comparing surface and interior moisture to detect uneven mixing rather than relying solely on a delivered water total.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把乾土質量、水量與可能蒸發分開列帳，另設幾個混合後取樣點。比較平均合格但離散很大的情況，提出能辨識土團內外差異的驗證方式。","textEn":"Separate dry mass, water dose and possible evaporation in a ledger, with several post-mixing sample locations. Compare a compliant mean with high scatter and propose verification that distinguishes clod interiors from their surfaces.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「土料調濕與拌合機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Moisture conditioning and blending mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","先核對含水量分母為乾土質量，追蹤加水計量、天候及拌合後各點試樣。","兩個粒徑比看起來合理，就能證明任何土類的濾層完整合格。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Confirm the dry-mass moisture denominator and track metered water, weather and samples after blending.","Plausible values of two particle ratios prove complete filter acceptance for every soil type."],"answer":1,"explanation":"先核對含水量分母為乾土質量，追蹤加水計量、天候及拌合後各點試樣。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Confirm the dry-mass moisture denominator and track metered water, weather and samples after blending. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b273-v15-08","title":"土料調濕與拌合機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Moisture conditioning and blending mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「土料調濕與拌合」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Moisture conditioning and blending” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以濕土總重乘含水量差會算錯加水量，短時間表面灑水也可能只弄濕外皮；直接增加機具遍數未必能補救內部含水量不適或團塊未打散。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Multiplying moisture change by wet total mass gives the wrong dose. Brief surface spraying can wet only the exterior, and additional passes may not correct unsuitable interior moisture or clods that remain intact. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例封閉水量帳假設乾土質量不變、加入的水全部保留，目標只是指定教學值，不宣稱位於最佳含水量或可立即施工。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The target is an assigned teaching value, not a demonstrated optimum or authorization to place the soil.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要加水總量正確，每個土團就會立即具有相同含水量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A correct total water dose immediately gives every soil clod identical moisture.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以濕土總重乘含水量差會算錯加水量，短時間表面灑水也可能只弄濕外皮；直接增加機具遍數未必能補救內部含水量不適或團塊未打散。","textEn":"Multiplying moisture change by wet total mass gives the wrong dose. Brief surface spraying can wet only the exterior, and additional passes may not correct unsuitable interior moisture or clods that remain intact.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「土料調濕與拌合機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Moisture conditioning and blending mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","相同乾密度的兩份土一定具有相同飽和度與滲透係數。","以濕土總重乘含水量差會算錯加水量，短時間表面灑水也可能只弄濕外皮；直接增加機具遍數未必能補救內部含水量不適或團塊未打散。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Two soils with equal dry density necessarily have equal saturation and hydraulic conductivity.","Multiplying moisture change by wet total mass gives the wrong dose."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以濕土總重乘含水量差會算錯加水量，短時間表面灑水也可能只弄濕外皮；直接增加機具遍數未必能補救內部含水量不適或團塊未打散。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Multiplying moisture change by wet total mass gives the wrong dose. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b273-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「孔隙比與飽和度機理與驗證」與「地基一次壓密沉陷機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Void ratio and saturation mechanism and verification\" and \"Primary consolidation settlement mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b273-v15-09","title":"孔隙比與飽和度機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Void ratio and saturation mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「孔隙比與飽和度」如何影響土堤壓密與防滲的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Void ratio and saturation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Levee compaction and seepage control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"乾密度只描述單位總體積中的固體質量，配合土粒比重才能求孔隙比，再由含水量判斷孔隙中水與空氣的比例。相同乾密度可能對應不同飽和度與吸力，浸水後的濕陷或膨脹也不能由密度一項排除；三相圖是檢查量測一致性的工具，不是直接推定滲透係數的公式。本例土粒比重與水密度已指定，忽略溶解鹽及體積量測誤差。飽和度應介於零與一，超界值要追查輸入而非截斷後繼續計算。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「孔隙比與飽和度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Dry density describes solid mass per bulk volume. Particle specific gravity enables void ratio, and moisture then divides void space into water and air. Equal dry density can coexist with different saturation and suction; density alone does not exclude collapse or swelling on wetting. A phase diagram checks measurement consistency rather than directly predicting hydraulic conductivity. Specific gravity and water density are specified, with dissolved salts and volume error neglected. Saturation must lie between zero and one; an impossible value triggers input investigation rather than silent clipping. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Void ratio and saturation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Gs=2.70、ρw=1.00、ρd=1.80 Mg/m³、w=0.15，e=Gsρw/ρd−1=0.50，Sr=wGs/e=0.81。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Gs=2.70, water density 1.00 and dry density 1.80 Mg/m³, with moisture w=0.15.","failure":"常見誤解：「相同乾密度的兩份土一定具有相同飽和度與滲透係數。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two soils with equal dry density necessarily have equal saturation and hydraulic conductivity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「孔隙比與飽和度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Void ratio and saturation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-09-k1","title":"孔隙比與飽和度機理與驗證","titleEn":"Void ratio and saturation mechanism and verification","text":"乾密度只描述單位總體積中的固體質量，配合土粒比重才能求孔隙比，再由含水量判斷孔隙中水與空氣的比例。相同乾密度可能對應不同飽和度與吸力，浸水後的濕陷或膨脹也不能由密度一項排除；三相圖是檢查量測一致性的工具，不是直接推定滲透係數的公式。","textEn":"Dry density describes solid mass per bulk volume. Particle specific gravity enables void ratio, and moisture then divides void space into water and air.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：相同乾密度的兩份土一定具有相同飽和度與滲透係數。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two soils with equal dry density necessarily have equal saturation and hydraulic conductivity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「孔隙比與飽和度機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Void ratio and saturation mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["乾密度只描述單位總體積中的固體質量，配合土粒比重才能求孔隙比，再由含水量判斷孔隙中水與空氣的比例。","相同乾密度的兩份土一定具有相同飽和度與滲透係數。","填土達到指定夯實度，就能證明下方軟弱地基不再壓密。"],"optionsEn":["Dry density describes solid mass per bulk volume.","Two soils with equal dry density necessarily have equal saturation and hydraulic conductivity.","Specified fill compaction proves that the underlying soft foundation will no longer consolidate."],"answer":0,"explanation":"乾密度只描述單位總體積中的固體質量，配合土粒比重才能求孔隙比，再由含水量判斷孔隙中水與空氣的比例。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Dry density describes solid mass per bulk volume. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b273-v15-10","title":"孔隙比與飽和度機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Void ratio and saturation mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「孔隙比與飽和度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Void ratio and saturation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Gs=2.70、ρw=1.00、ρd=1.80 Mg/m³、w=0.15，e=Gsρw/ρd−1=0.50，Sr=wGs/e=0.81。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Gs=2.70, water density 1.00 and dry density 1.80 Mg/m³, with moisture w=0.15. Void ratio e=0.50 and saturation Sr=0.81. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用三相圖核對質量與體積守恆，將飽和度與含水量、密度的不確定度一同呈現。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check phase mass and volume closure and report saturation alongside uncertainty in moisture and density.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Gs=2.70、ρw=1.00、ρd=1.80 Mg/m³、w=0.15，e=Gsρw/ρd−1=0.50，Sr=wGs/e=0.81。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Gs=2.70, water density 1.00 and dry density 1.80 Mg/m³, with moisture w=0.15. Void ratio e=0.50 and saturation Sr=0.81.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「孔隙比與飽和度機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Void ratio and saturation mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["達西公式中的水位差本身就是水力坡降，不需要流徑長度。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Gs=2.70、ρw=1.00、ρd=1.80 Mg/m³、w=0.15，e=Gsρw/ρd−1=0.50，Sr=wGs/e=0.81。","牆材滲透係數很低，就能忽略所有牆尖繞流與施工接頭。"],"optionsEn":["Head difference alone is the Darcy hydraulic gradient and needs no flow-path length.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Gs=2.70, water density 1.00 and dry density 1.80 Mg/m³, with moisture w=0.15.","Very low wall-material conductivity makes all tip bypass and construction joints irrelevant."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Gs=2.70、ρw=1.00、ρd=1.80 Mg/m³、w=0.15，e=Gsρw/ρd−1=0.50，Sr=wGs/e=0.81。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Gs=2.70, water density 1.00 and dry density 1.80 Mg/m³, with moisture w=0.15. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b273-v15-11","title":"孔隙比與飽和度機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Void ratio and saturation mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「孔隙比與飽和度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Void ratio and saturation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用三相圖核對質量與體積守恆，將飽和度與含水量、密度的不確定度一同呈現。若需要預估浸水行為，另做代表性應力下的濕陷、膨脹和滲透試驗，不能由單次相圖外推。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check phase mass and volume closure and report saturation alongside uncertainty in moisture and density. When wetting behavior matters, conduct collapse, swelling and permeability tests under representative stresses instead of extrapolating those responses from one phase-diagram calculation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：固定乾密度並改變含水量，繪出孔隙中水與空氣的比例，再試算一組不可能的超飽和輸入。說明應回查哪些量測，而不是直接把結果改成百分之百。","observationEn":"Site practice: Hold dry density fixed while varying moisture and draw the water/air shares of voids. Try an impossible supersaturated input and explain which measurements should be checked instead of forcing the result to one hundred percent.","failure":"注意干擾：錯把含水量當水體積比例會造成飽和度誤差，不同土粒比重也使同密度材料具有不同孔隙比；推定密實土必定不透水則可能忽略裂縫和連通大孔隙。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing gravimetric moisture with a water-volume fraction distorts saturation, while different particle gravity changes void ratio at equal density. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用三相圖核對質量與體積守恆，將飽和度與含水量、密度的不確定度一同呈現。若需要預估浸水行為，另做代表性應力下的濕陷、膨脹和滲透試驗，不能由單次相圖外推。","textEn":"Check phase mass and volume closure and report saturation alongside uncertainty in moisture and density. When wetting behavior matters, conduct collapse, swelling and permeability tests under representative stresses instead of extrapolating those responses from one phase-diagram calculation.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"固定乾密度並改變含水量，繪出孔隙中水與空氣的比例，再試算一組不可能的超飽和輸入。說明應回查哪些量測，而不是直接把結果改成百分之百。","textEn":"Hold dry density fixed while varying moisture and draw the water/air shares of voids. Try an impossible supersaturated input and explain which measurements should be checked instead of forcing the result to one hundred percent.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「孔隙比與飽和度機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Void ratio and saturation mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","兩支孔壓計讀值較大的那支，無論安裝高度如何都位於上游。","用三相圖核對質量與體積守恆，將飽和度與含水量、密度的不確定度一同呈現。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The higher pressure reading always identifies the upstream sensor regardless of installation elevation.","Check phase mass and volume closure and report saturation alongside uncertainty in moisture and density."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用三相圖核對質量與體積守恆，將飽和度與含水量、密度的不確定度一同呈現。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check phase mass and volume closure and report saturation alongside uncertainty in moisture and density. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b273-v15-12","title":"孔隙比與飽和度機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Void ratio and saturation mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「孔隙比與飽和度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Void ratio and saturation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"錯把含水量當水體積比例會造成飽和度誤差，不同土粒比重也使同密度材料具有不同孔隙比；推定密實土必定不透水則可能忽略裂縫和連通大孔隙。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing gravimetric moisture with a water-volume fraction distorts saturation, while different particle gravity changes void ratio at equal density. Declaring dense soil impermeable additionally ignores cracks and connected macropores through the fill. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：飽和度應介於零與一，超界值要追查輸入而非截斷後繼續計算。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Saturation must lie between zero and one; an impossible value triggers input investigation rather than silent clipping.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「相同乾密度的兩份土一定具有相同飽和度與滲透係數。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two soils with equal dry density necessarily have equal saturation and hydraulic conductivity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"錯把含水量當水體積比例會造成飽和度誤差，不同土粒比重也使同密度材料具有不同孔隙比；推定密實土必定不透水則可能忽略裂縫和連通大孔隙。","textEn":"Confusing gravimetric moisture with a water-volume fraction distorts saturation, while different particle gravity changes void ratio at equal density. Declaring dense soil impermeable additionally ignores cracks and connected macropores through the fill.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔隙比與飽和度機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Void ratio and saturation mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["錯把含水量當水體積比例會造成飽和度誤差，不同土粒比重也使同密度材料具有不同孔隙比；推定密實土必定不透水則可能忽略裂縫和連通大孔隙。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","填土達到指定夯實度，就能證明下方軟弱地基不再壓密。"],"optionsEn":["Confusing gravimetric moisture with a water-volume fraction distorts saturation, while different particle gravity changes void ratio at equal density.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Specified fill compaction proves that the underlying soft foundation will no longer consolidate."],"answer":0,"explanation":"錯把含水量當水體積比例會造成飽和度誤差，不同土粒比重也使同密度材料具有不同孔隙比；推定密實土必定不透水則可能忽略裂縫和連通大孔隙。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing gravimetric moisture with a water-volume fraction distorts saturation, while different particle gravity changes void ratio at equal density. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b273-v15-13","title":"地基一次壓密沉陷機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Primary consolidation settlement mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「地基一次壓密沉陷」如何影響土堤壓密與防滲的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Primary consolidation settlement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Levee compaction and seepage control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"堤身機械夯實與軟弱地基的壓密是不同過程：新增填土荷載可先引起孔壓，之後排水使有效應力增加與孔隙減少。正常固結土在指定應力範圍可用壓縮指數估算一次壓密量，但超固結、分層、次壓縮或側向變形需要另處理，不能把現場夯實百分比當作地基沉陷保證。本例為均質正常固結層的一維平均應力近似，使用常用十進對數。忽略側移與次壓縮，並不代表實際堤頂最終總沉陷。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「地基一次壓密沉陷」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mechanical compaction of fill differs from consolidation of soft foundation soil. New loading initially creates pore pressure; drainage then increases effective stress and reduces void space. A compression index estimates primary settlement for normally consolidated soil within its tested stress range. Overconsolidation, layering, secondary compression and lateral deformation require additional treatment beyond fill-density acceptance. This is a one-dimensional mean-stress estimate for a uniform normally consolidated layer using base-ten logarithms. Lateral movement and secondary compression are omitted, so the result is not total final crest settlement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Primary consolidation settlement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設H=4 m、Cc=0.25、e0=0.80、初始σ′0=100 kPa、增量Δσ′=50 kPa，S=CcH log10(150/100)/(1+e0)=0.09783 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume H=4 m, Cc=0.25, e0=0.80, initial effective stress 100 kPa and increase 50 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「填土達到指定夯實度，就能證明下方軟弱地基不再壓密。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Specified fill compaction proves that the underlying soft foundation will no longer consolidate.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「地基一次壓密沉陷」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Primary consolidation settlement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-13-k1","title":"地基一次壓密沉陷機理與驗證","titleEn":"Primary consolidation settlement mechanism and verification","text":"堤身機械夯實與軟弱地基的壓密是不同過程：新增填土荷載可先引起孔壓，之後排水使有效應力增加與孔隙減少。正常固結土在指定應力範圍可用壓縮指數估算一次壓密量，但超固結、分層、次壓縮或側向變形需要另處理，不能把現場夯實百分比當作地基沉陷保證。","textEn":"Mechanical compaction of fill differs from consolidation of soft foundation soil. New loading initially creates pore pressure; drainage then increases effective stress and reduces void space.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：填土達到指定夯實度，就能證明下方軟弱地基不再壓密。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Specified fill compaction proves that the underlying soft foundation will no longer consolidate. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地基一次壓密沉陷機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Primary consolidation settlement mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["填土達到指定夯實度，就能證明下方軟弱地基不再壓密。","堤身機械夯實與軟弱地基的壓密是不同過程：新增填土荷載可先引起孔壓，之後排水使有效應力增加與孔隙減少。","土層厚度減半時，所有情況的壓密時間都只會減半。"],"optionsEn":["Specified fill compaction proves that the underlying soft foundation will no longer consolidate.","Mechanical compaction of fill differs from consolidation of soft foundation soil.","Halving soil thickness always halves consolidation time under every drainage condition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"堤身機械夯實與軟弱地基的壓密是不同過程：新增填土荷載可先引起孔壓，之後排水使有效應力增加與孔隙減少。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mechanical compaction of fill differs from consolidation of soft foundation soil. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b273-v15-14","title":"地基一次壓密沉陷機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Primary consolidation settlement mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「地基一次壓密沉陷」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Primary consolidation settlement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設H=4 m、Cc=0.25、e0=0.80、初始σ′0=100 kPa、增量Δσ′=50 kPa，S=CcH log10(150/100)/(1+e0)=0.09783 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume H=4 m, Cc=0.25, e0=0.80, initial effective stress 100 kPa and increase 50 kPa. Primary settlement S=CcH log10(150/100)/(1+e0)=0.09783 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對原狀取樣品質、先期固結壓力與實際新增應力分布，將地層細分後比較結果。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check sample quality, preconsolidation stress and the distribution of added stress, comparing a layered calculation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設H=4 m、Cc=0.25、e0=0.80、初始σ′0=100 kPa、增量Δσ′=50 kPa，S=CcH log10(150/100)/(1+e0)=0.09783 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume H=4 m, Cc=0.25, e0=0.80, initial effective stress 100 kPa and increase 50 kPa. Primary settlement S=CcH log10(150/100)/(1+e0)=0.09783 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地基一次壓密沉陷機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Primary consolidation settlement mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["抗隆起比值大於一，就能排除所有逆向侵蝕與管湧機制。","兩個粒徑比看起來合理，就能證明任何土類的濾層完整合格。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設H=4 m、Cc=0.25、e0=0.80、初始σ′0=100 kPa、增量Δσ′=50 kPa，S=CcH log10(150/100)/(1+e0)=0.09783 m。"],"optionsEn":["A heave ratio above one eliminates every backward-erosion and piping mechanism.","Plausible values of two particle ratios prove complete filter acceptance for every soil type.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume H=4 m, Cc=0.25, e0=0.80, initial effective stress 100 kPa and increase 50 kPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設H=4 m、Cc=0.25、e0=0.80、初始σ′0=100 kPa、增量Δσ′=50 kPa，S=CcH log10(150/100)/(1+e0)=0.09783 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume H=4 m, Cc=0.25, e0=0.80, initial effective stress 100 kPa and increase 50 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b273-v15-15","title":"地基一次壓密沉陷機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Primary consolidation settlement mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「地基一次壓密沉陷」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Primary consolidation settlement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對原狀取樣品質、先期固結壓力與實際新增應力分布，將地層細分後比較結果。利用沉陷板與孔壓同步觀測區別排水壓密與側移，並保留填築階段及水位變動紀錄。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check sample quality, preconsolidation stress and the distribution of added stress, comparing a layered calculation. Observe settlement plates and pore pressures together to distinguish drainage-driven consolidation from lateral movement, retaining fill-stage and groundwater records when interpreting displacement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將一層地基分成兩個應力不同的子層並比較總沉陷，列出先期固結壓力不足時的資料缺口。規劃沉陷與孔壓配對觀測，避免只從單一沉陷值推斷原因。","observationEn":"Site practice: Divide the foundation into two layers with different stress changes and compare total settlement. List missing preconsolidation information and plan paired settlement/pore-pressure observations instead of inferring the mechanism from one displacement value.","failure":"注意干擾：把超固結層全用正常固結斜率可能失真，用總應力代替有效應力也會錯估壓縮；只測堤頂而不分地基和填土，則難以辨識沉陷機制與後續變形。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using a virgin-compression slope throughout overconsolidated soil distorts settlement, as does substituting total for effective stress. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對原狀取樣品質、先期固結壓力與實際新增應力分布，將地層細分後比較結果。利用沉陷板與孔壓同步觀測區別排水壓密與側移，並保留填築階段及水位變動紀錄。","textEn":"Check sample quality, preconsolidation stress and the distribution of added stress, comparing a layered calculation. Observe settlement plates and pore pressures together to distinguish drainage-driven consolidation from lateral movement, retaining fill-stage and groundwater records when interpreting displacement.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將一層地基分成兩個應力不同的子層並比較總沉陷，列出先期固結壓力不足時的資料缺口。規劃沉陷與孔壓配對觀測，避免只從單一沉陷值推斷原因。","textEn":"Divide the foundation into two layers with different stress changes and compare total settlement. List missing preconsolidation information and plan paired settlement/pore-pressure observations instead of inferring the mechanism from one displacement value.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地基一次壓密沉陷機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Primary consolidation settlement mechanism and verification\"?","options":["核對原狀取樣品質、先期固結壓力與實際新增應力分布，將地層細分後比較結果。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","現場濕密度較高就必定表示乾密度與防滲能力都較好。"],"optionsEn":["Check sample quality, preconsolidation stress and the distribution of added stress, comparing a layered calculation.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Higher field wet density necessarily means better dry density and seepage resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對原狀取樣品質、先期固結壓力與實際新增應力分布，將地層細分後比較結果。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check sample quality, preconsolidation stress and the distribution of added stress, comparing a layered calculation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b273-v15-16","title":"地基一次壓密沉陷機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Primary consolidation settlement mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「地基一次壓密沉陷」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Primary consolidation settlement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把超固結層全用正常固結斜率可能失真，用總應力代替有效應力也會錯估壓縮；只測堤頂而不分地基和填土，則難以辨識沉陷機制與後續變形。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using a virgin-compression slope throughout overconsolidated soil distorts settlement, as does substituting total for effective stress. Crest observations alone cannot separate foundation and fill contributions or identify the mechanism of continuing movement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：忽略側移與次壓縮，並不代表實際堤頂最終總沉陷。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Lateral movement and secondary compression are omitted, so the result is not total final crest settlement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「填土達到指定夯實度，就能證明下方軟弱地基不再壓密。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Specified fill compaction proves that the underlying soft foundation will no longer consolidate.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把超固結層全用正常固結斜率可能失真，用總應力代替有效應力也會錯估壓縮；只測堤頂而不分地基和填土，則難以辨識沉陷機制與後續變形。","textEn":"Using a virgin-compression slope throughout overconsolidated soil distorts settlement, as does substituting total for effective stress. Crest observations alone cannot separate foundation and fill contributions or identify the mechanism of continuing movement.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地基一次壓密沉陷機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Primary consolidation settlement mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把超固結層全用正常固結斜率可能失真，用總應力代替有效應力也會錯估壓縮；只測堤頂而不分地基和填土，則難以辨識沉陷機制與後續變形。","土層厚度減半時，所有情況的壓密時間都只會減半。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using a virgin-compression slope throughout overconsolidated soil distorts settlement, as does substituting total for effective stress.","Halving soil thickness always halves consolidation time under every drainage condition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把超固結層全用正常固結斜率可能失真，用總應力代替有效應力也會錯估壓縮；只測堤頂而不分地基和填土，則難以辨識沉陷機制與後續變形。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using a virgin-compression slope throughout overconsolidated soil distorts settlement, as does substituting total for effective stress. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b273-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「排水路徑與壓密時間機理與驗證」與「滲流量與流徑長度機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Drainage path and consolidation time mechanism and verification\" and \"Seepage discharge and path length mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b273-v15-17","title":"排水路徑與壓密時間機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Drainage path and consolidation time mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「排水路徑與壓密時間」如何影響土堤壓密與防滲的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drainage path and consolidation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Levee compaction and seepage control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"一次壓密時間由排水距離平方和壓密係數控制；雙向排水時的最長路徑不同於整層厚度。壓密係數會隨應力與土層而變，排水邊界也可能因低透水覆層或堵塞而改變，因此施工階段的孔壓消散不能只由一個實驗值和日曆時間決定，需與沉陷歷線一起判讀。本例使用均質一維壓密的平均百分之九十時間因子，瞬時均布荷載且排水邊界固定。係數明列為平方公尺每秒，換算日數另除秒數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「排水路徑與壓密時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Primary consolidation time scales with the square of drainage distance and inversely with the coefficient of consolidation. Double drainage changes the longest path relative to full layer thickness. Stress-dependent properties, low-permeability covers and clogged drains can alter the response, so elapsed time and one laboratory coefficient cannot alone establish field pore-pressure dissipation. The example uses the average ninety-percent time factor for uniform one-dimensional consolidation under instantaneous uniform loading and fixed drainage boundaries. The coefficient is in square metres per second, with a separate seconds-to-days conversion. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drainage path and consolidation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Tv,90=0.848、排水長Hdr=2 m、cv=1×10⁻⁷ m²/s，t90=TvHdr²/cv=33,920,000 s=392.59日。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Tv,90=0.848, drainage length Hdr=2 m and cv=1×10⁻⁷ m²/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「土層厚度減半時，所有情況的壓密時間都只會減半。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Halving soil thickness always halves consolidation time under every drainage condition.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「排水路徑與壓密時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drainage path and consolidation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-17-k1","title":"排水路徑與壓密時間機理與驗證","titleEn":"Drainage path and consolidation time mechanism and verification","text":"一次壓密時間由排水距離平方和壓密係數控制；雙向排水時的最長路徑不同於整層厚度。壓密係數會隨應力與土層而變，排水邊界也可能因低透水覆層或堵塞而改變，因此施工階段的孔壓消散不能只由一個實驗值和日曆時間決定，需與沉陷歷線一起判讀。","textEn":"Primary consolidation time scales with the square of drainage distance and inversely with the coefficient of consolidation. Double drainage changes the longest path relative to full layer thickness.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：土層厚度減半時，所有情況的壓密時間都只會減半。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Halving soil thickness always halves consolidation time under every drainage condition. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「排水路徑與壓密時間機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drainage path and consolidation time mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["土層厚度減半時，所有情況的壓密時間都只會減半。","達西公式中的水位差本身就是水力坡降，不需要流徑長度。","一次壓密時間由排水距離平方和壓密係數控制；雙向排水時的最長路徑不同於整層厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Halving soil thickness always halves consolidation time under every drainage condition.","Head difference alone is the Darcy hydraulic gradient and needs no flow-path length.","Primary consolidation time scales with the square of drainage distance and inversely with the coefficient of consolidation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"一次壓密時間由排水距離平方和壓密係數控制；雙向排水時的最長路徑不同於整層厚度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Primary consolidation time scales with the square of drainage distance and inversely with the coefficient of consolidation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b273-v15-18","title":"排水路徑與壓密時間機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Drainage path and consolidation time mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「排水路徑與壓密時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drainage path and consolidation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Tv,90=0.848、排水長Hdr=2 m、cv=1×10⁻⁷ m²/s，t90=TvHdr²/cv=33,920,000 s=392.59日。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Tv,90=0.848, drainage length Hdr=2 m and cv=1×10⁻⁷ m²/s. Time t90=TvHdr²/cv=33,920,000 s=392.59 days. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在地質剖面標出可排水與不透水邊界，辨識實際最長路徑及分階段荷載。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark draining and impermeable boundaries on the ground profile and identify the longest path and staged loading.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Tv,90=0.848、排水長Hdr=2 m、cv=1×10⁻⁷ m²/s，t90=TvHdr²/cv=33,920,000 s=392.59日。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Tv,90=0.848, drainage length Hdr=2 m and cv=1×10⁻⁷ m²/s. Time t90=TvHdr²/cv=33,920,000 s=392.59 days.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「排水路徑與壓密時間機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drainage path and consolidation time mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Tv,90=0.848、排水長Hdr=2 m、cv=1×10⁻⁷ m²/s，t90=TvHdr²/cv=33,920,000 s=392.59日。","牆材滲透係數很低，就能忽略所有牆尖繞流與施工接頭。","兩支孔壓計讀值較大的那支，無論安裝高度如何都位於上游。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Tv,90=0.848, drainage length Hdr=2 m and cv=1×10⁻⁷ m²/s.","Very low wall-material conductivity makes all tip bypass and construction joints irrelevant.","The higher pressure reading always identifies the upstream sensor regardless of installation elevation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Tv,90=0.848、排水長Hdr=2 m、cv=1×10⁻⁷ m²/s，t90=TvHdr²/cv=33,920,000 s=392.59日。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Tv,90=0.848, drainage length Hdr=2 m and cv=1×10⁻⁷ m²/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b273-v15-19","title":"排水路徑與壓密時間機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drainage path and consolidation time mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「排水路徑與壓密時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drainage path and consolidation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在地質剖面標出可排水與不透水邊界，辨識實際最長路徑及分階段荷載。以多深度孔壓和沉陷反算時間尺度，再檢查相同係數能否描述不同階段而不是只擬合單一點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark draining and impermeable boundaries on the ground profile and identify the longest path and staged loading. Compare multi-depth pore pressure and settlement against the time scale, testing whether one coefficient explains several stages rather than fitting a single observation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較同一層單向與雙向排水的路徑平方，再將秒與日逐項換算。提出可辨識排水邊界失效的孔壓觀測配置，並說明分段填築為何改變時間起點。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare squared drainage distances for single and double drainage and convert seconds to days explicitly. Design pore-pressure observations to identify a failed drainage boundary and explain why staged filling changes the loading time origin.","failure":"注意干擾：把全層厚度誤當雙向排水路徑會放大時間估算，反向錯用則可能提早判定壓密完成；若忽略低透水夾層，名義上雙向排水也未必等於真實邊界。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using full thickness for double drainage overstates time, while the opposite mistake can suggest premature completion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在地質剖面標出可排水與不透水邊界，辨識實際最長路徑及分階段荷載。以多深度孔壓和沉陷反算時間尺度，再檢查相同係數能否描述不同階段而不是只擬合單一點。","textEn":"Mark draining and impermeable boundaries on the ground profile and identify the longest path and staged loading. Compare multi-depth pore pressure and settlement against the time scale, testing whether one coefficient explains several stages rather than fitting a single observation.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較同一層單向與雙向排水的路徑平方，再將秒與日逐項換算。提出可辨識排水邊界失效的孔壓觀測配置，並說明分段填築為何改變時間起點。","textEn":"Compare squared drainage distances for single and double drainage and convert seconds to days explicitly. Design pore-pressure observations to identify a failed drainage boundary and explain why staged filling changes the loading time origin.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「排水路徑與壓密時間機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drainage path and consolidation time mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在地質剖面標出可排水與不透水邊界，辨識實際最長路徑及分階段荷載。","只要加水總量正確，每個土團就會立即具有相同含水量。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Mark draining and impermeable boundaries on the ground profile and identify the longest path and staged loading.","A correct total water dose immediately gives every soil clod identical moisture."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在地質剖面標出可排水與不透水邊界，辨識實際最長路徑及分階段荷載。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark draining and impermeable boundaries on the ground profile and identify the longest path and staged loading. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b273-v15-20","title":"排水路徑與壓密時間機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drainage path and consolidation time mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「排水路徑與壓密時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drainage path and consolidation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把全層厚度誤當雙向排水路徑會放大時間估算，反向錯用則可能提早判定壓密完成；若忽略低透水夾層，名義上雙向排水也未必等於真實邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using full thickness for double drainage overstates time, while the opposite mistake can suggest premature completion. Low-permeability interlayers can also prevent nominal double drainage from representing the actual hydraulic boundary conditions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：係數明列為平方公尺每秒，換算日數另除秒數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The coefficient is in square metres per second, with a separate seconds-to-days conversion.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「土層厚度減半時，所有情況的壓密時間都只會減半。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Halving soil thickness always halves consolidation time under every drainage condition.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把全層厚度誤當雙向排水路徑會放大時間估算，反向錯用則可能提早判定壓密完成；若忽略低透水夾層，名義上雙向排水也未必等於真實邊界。","textEn":"Using full thickness for double drainage overstates time, while the opposite mistake can suggest premature completion. Low-permeability interlayers can also prevent nominal double drainage from representing the actual hydraulic boundary conditions.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「排水路徑與壓密時間機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drainage path and consolidation time mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","達西公式中的水位差本身就是水力坡降，不需要流徑長度。","把全層厚度誤當雙向排水路徑會放大時間估算，反向錯用則可能提早判定壓密完成；若忽略低透水夾層，名義上雙向排水也未必等於真實邊界。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Head difference alone is the Darcy hydraulic gradient and needs no flow-path length.","Using full thickness for double drainage overstates time, while the opposite mistake can suggest premature completion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把全層厚度誤當雙向排水路徑會放大時間估算，反向錯用則可能提早判定壓密完成；若忽略低透水夾層，名義上雙向排水也未必等於真實邊界。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using full thickness for double drainage overstates time, while the opposite mistake can suggest premature completion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b273-v15-21","title":"滲流量與流徑長度機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Seepage discharge and path length mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「滲流量與流徑長度」如何影響土堤壓密與防滲的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Seepage discharge and path length” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Levee compaction and seepage control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"達西流量由滲透係數、過水面積及水力坡降共同決定，坡降是總水頭差除流徑長度，並非只有水位差。堤身和地基通常具有分層與異向性，簡化一維流線只能建立尺度；總漏水量偏小也可能伴隨局部集中的危險出口，故流量與局部梯度需要分開檢查。本例採飽和、均質、固定截面的恆定一維流，面積垂直於流向。未模擬自由水面、接縫或繞過防滲構造的流線。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「滲流量與流徑長度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Darcy discharge combines hydraulic conductivity, flow area and hydraulic gradient, which is total-head difference divided by path length rather than head difference alone. Embankments and foundations are commonly layered and anisotropic, so a one-dimensional path supplies only a scale. A small total discharge may still accompany a concentrated adverse exit gradient. The example assumes steady saturated one-dimensional flow through a uniform constant section, with area normal to flow. It omits the phreatic surface, joints and paths around seepage-control structures. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Seepage discharge and path length” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設k=1×10⁻⁶ m/s、厚5 m、寬100 m、Δh=3 m、L=30 m，Q=kAΔh/L=5×10⁻⁵ m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume k=1×10⁻⁶ m/s, thickness 5 m, width 100 m, head difference 3 m and length 30 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「達西公式中的水位差本身就是水力坡降，不需要流徑長度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Head difference alone is the Darcy hydraulic gradient and needs no flow-path length.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「滲流量與流徑長度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Seepage discharge and path length”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-21-k1","title":"滲流量與流徑長度機理與驗證","titleEn":"Seepage discharge and path length mechanism and verification","text":"達西流量由滲透係數、過水面積及水力坡降共同決定，坡降是總水頭差除流徑長度，並非只有水位差。堤身和地基通常具有分層與異向性，簡化一維流線只能建立尺度；總漏水量偏小也可能伴隨局部集中的危險出口，故流量與局部梯度需要分開檢查。","textEn":"Darcy discharge combines hydraulic conductivity, flow area and hydraulic gradient, which is total-head difference divided by path length rather than head difference alone. Embankments and foundations are commonly layered and anisotropic, so a one-dimensional path supplies only a scale.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：達西公式中的水位差本身就是水力坡降，不需要流徑長度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Head difference alone is the Darcy hydraulic gradient and needs no flow-path length. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「滲流量與流徑長度機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Seepage discharge and path length mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["達西流量由滲透係數、過水面積及水力坡降共同決定，坡降是總水頭差除流徑長度，並非只有水位差。","達西公式中的水位差本身就是水力坡降，不需要流徑長度。","抗隆起比值大於一，就能排除所有逆向侵蝕與管湧機制。"],"optionsEn":["Darcy discharge combines hydraulic conductivity, flow area and hydraulic gradient, which is total-head difference divided by path length rather than head difference alone.","Head difference alone is the Darcy hydraulic gradient and needs no flow-path length.","A heave ratio above one eliminates every backward-erosion and piping mechanism."],"answer":0,"explanation":"達西流量由滲透係數、過水面積及水力坡降共同決定，坡降是總水頭差除流徑長度，並非只有水位差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Darcy discharge combines hydraulic conductivity, flow area and hydraulic gradient, which is total-head difference divided by path length rather than head difference alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b273-v15-22","title":"滲流量與流徑長度機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Seepage discharge and path length mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「滲流量與流徑長度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Seepage discharge and path length” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設k=1×10⁻⁶ m/s、厚5 m、寬100 m、Δh=3 m、L=30 m，Q=kAΔh/L=5×10⁻⁵ m³/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume k=1×10⁻⁶ m/s, thickness 5 m, width 100 m, head difference 3 m and length 30 m. Darcy discharge Q=kAΔh/L=5×10⁻⁵ m³/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：標出總水頭測點、流向、面積和路徑長度，核對滲透試驗方向與現場分層。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Label total-head points, flow direction, area and path length, checking test orientation against layering.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設k=1×10⁻⁶ m/s、厚5 m、寬100 m、Δh=3 m、L=30 m，Q=kAΔh/L=5×10⁻⁵ m³/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume k=1×10⁻⁶ m/s, thickness 5 m, width 100 m, head difference 3 m and length 30 m. Darcy discharge Q=kAΔh/L=5×10⁻⁵ m³/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「滲流量與流徑長度機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Seepage discharge and path length mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["兩個粒徑比看起來合理，就能證明任何土類的濾層完整合格。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設k=1×10⁻⁶ m/s、厚5 m、寬100 m、Δh=3 m、L=30 m，Q=kAΔh/L=5×10⁻⁵ m³/s。","現場濕密度較高就必定表示乾密度與防滲能力都較好。"],"optionsEn":["Plausible values of two particle ratios prove complete filter acceptance for every soil type.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume k=1×10⁻⁶ m/s, thickness 5 m, width 100 m, head difference 3 m and length 30 m.","Higher field wet density necessarily means better dry density and seepage resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設k=1×10⁻⁶ m/s、厚5 m、寬100 m、Δh=3 m、L=30 m，Q=kAΔh/L=5×10⁻⁵ m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume k=1×10⁻⁶ m/s, thickness 5 m, width 100 m, head difference 3 m and length 30 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b273-v15-23","title":"滲流量與流徑長度機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Seepage discharge and path length mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「滲流量與流徑長度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Seepage discharge and path length” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"標出總水頭測點、流向、面積和路徑長度，核對滲透試驗方向與現場分層。用實測孔壓和排水流量一起校核；如有異向性、裂縫或明顯自由面，改採能表示該幾何的模型。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Label total-head points, flow direction, area and path length, checking test orientation against layering. Calibrate with both pore pressures and drain discharge; where anisotropy, cracks or a moving free surface matter, use a model that represents that geometry explicitly. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把水頭差和流長各改一倍，分別比較坡降與流量，再畫出測點高程。說明總水頭含壓力水頭與位置水頭，避免把不同高度的壓力表直接相減。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double head difference and path length separately and compare gradient and discharge. Draw measurement elevations and explain total head as pressure plus elevation head, avoiding direct subtraction of pressure readings at different heights.","failure":"注意干擾：漏掉流徑長度會造成量綱錯誤，誤用沿流向面積也會使流量失真；只以總流量穩定判定安全，則可能看不到局部裂縫流逐漸集中與顆粒流失。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting path length creates a dimensional error, and using area parallel to flow distorts discharge. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"標出總水頭測點、流向、面積和路徑長度，核對滲透試驗方向與現場分層。用實測孔壓和排水流量一起校核；如有異向性、裂縫或明顯自由面，改採能表示該幾何的模型。","textEn":"Label total-head points, flow direction, area and path length, checking test orientation against layering. Calibrate with both pore pressures and drain discharge; where anisotropy, cracks or a moving free surface matter, use a model that represents that geometry explicitly.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把水頭差和流長各改一倍，分別比較坡降與流量，再畫出測點高程。說明總水頭含壓力水頭與位置水頭，避免把不同高度的壓力表直接相減。","textEn":"Double head difference and path length separately and compare gradient and discharge. Draw measurement elevations and explain total head as pressure plus elevation head, avoiding direct subtraction of pressure readings at different heights.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「滲流量與流徑長度機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Seepage discharge and path length mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","相同乾密度的兩份土一定具有相同飽和度與滲透係數。","標出總水頭測點、流向、面積和路徑長度，核對滲透試驗方向與現場分層。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Two soils with equal dry density necessarily have equal saturation and hydraulic conductivity.","Label total-head points, flow direction, area and path length, checking test orientation against layering."],"answer":2,"explanation":"標出總水頭測點、流向、面積和路徑長度，核對滲透試驗方向與現場分層。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Label total-head points, flow direction, area and path length, checking test orientation against layering. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b273-v15-24","title":"滲流量與流徑長度機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Seepage discharge and path length mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「滲流量與流徑長度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Seepage discharge and path length” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏掉流徑長度會造成量綱錯誤，誤用沿流向面積也會使流量失真；只以總流量穩定判定安全，則可能看不到局部裂縫流逐漸集中與顆粒流失。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting path length creates a dimensional error, and using area parallel to flow distorts discharge. Stable total leakage alone can conceal progressively concentrated crack flow and soil loss within a small part of the system. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：未模擬自由水面、接縫或繞過防滲構造的流線。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It omits the phreatic surface, joints and paths around seepage-control structures.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「達西公式中的水位差本身就是水力坡降，不需要流徑長度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Head difference alone is the Darcy hydraulic gradient and needs no flow-path length.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏掉流徑長度會造成量綱錯誤，誤用沿流向面積也會使流量失真；只以總流量穩定判定安全，則可能看不到局部裂縫流逐漸集中與顆粒流失。","textEn":"Omitting path length creates a dimensional error, and using area parallel to flow distorts discharge. Stable total leakage alone can conceal progressively concentrated crack flow and soil loss within a small part of the system.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「滲流量與流徑長度機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Seepage discharge and path length mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["漏掉流徑長度會造成量綱錯誤，誤用沿流向面積也會使流量失真；只以總流量穩定判定安全，則可能看不到局部裂縫流逐漸集中與顆粒流失。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","抗隆起比值大於一，就能排除所有逆向侵蝕與管湧機制。"],"optionsEn":["Omitting path length creates a dimensional error, and using area parallel to flow distorts discharge.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A heave ratio above one eliminates every backward-erosion and piping mechanism."],"answer":0,"explanation":"漏掉流徑長度會造成量綱錯誤，誤用沿流向面積也會使流量失真；只以總流量穩定判定安全，則可能看不到局部裂縫流逐漸集中與顆粒流失。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting path length creates a dimensional error, and using area parallel to flow distorts discharge. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b273-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「出口隆起與內部侵蝕區別機理與驗證」與「防滲牆與串聯水力阻抗機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Exit heave versus internal erosion mechanism and verification\" and \"Cutoff walls and series resistance mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b273-v15-25","title":"出口隆起與內部侵蝕區別機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Exit heave versus internal erosion mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「出口隆起與內部侵蝕區別」如何影響土堤壓密與防滲的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Exit heave versus internal erosion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Levee compaction and seepage control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"向上滲流的滲透力可抵消顆粒的浮重，在理想非黏性土柱中有效應力趨近零時可能隆起。這種垂直臨界梯度分析不等於水平逆向侵蝕或裂縫集中沖蝕的門檻；內部侵蝕還受級配、濾層、幾何與缺陷控制，不能把抗隆起比值命名為涵蓋一切管湧的安全係數。本例無覆載、均質非黏性土且出口垂直向上，僅比較理想臨界梯度與指定局部梯度；不能據此核准堤防或濾層配置。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出口隆起與內部侵蝕區別」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Upward seepage force can counter submerged particle weight, approaching zero effective stress in an ideal cohesionless column and allowing heave. This vertical critical-gradient calculation is not the onset criterion for horizontal backward erosion or concentrated crack erosion. Internal erosion also depends on gradation, filters, geometry and defects, so a heave ratio cannot represent every piping mechanism. The example has no surcharge and uses uniform cohesionless soil with vertical upward exit flow. It compares ideal critical and assigned local gradients only, not approval of an embankment or filter arrangement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Exit heave versus internal erosion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Gs=2.65、e=0.65、垂直出口梯度ie=0.40，icr=(Gs−1)/(1+e)=1.00，理想抗隆起比icr/ie=2.50。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Gs=2.65, e=0.65 and vertical exit gradient ie=0.40.","failure":"常見誤解：「抗隆起比值大於一，就能排除所有逆向侵蝕與管湧機制。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A heave ratio above one eliminates every backward-erosion and piping mechanism.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「出口隆起與內部侵蝕區別」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Exit heave versus internal erosion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-25-k1","title":"出口隆起與內部侵蝕區別機理與驗證","titleEn":"Exit heave versus internal erosion mechanism and verification","text":"向上滲流的滲透力可抵消顆粒的浮重，在理想非黏性土柱中有效應力趨近零時可能隆起。這種垂直臨界梯度分析不等於水平逆向侵蝕或裂縫集中沖蝕的門檻；內部侵蝕還受級配、濾層、幾何與缺陷控制，不能把抗隆起比值命名為涵蓋一切管湧的安全係數。","textEn":"Upward seepage force can counter submerged particle weight, approaching zero effective stress in an ideal cohesionless column and allowing heave. This vertical critical-gradient calculation is not the onset criterion for horizontal backward erosion or concentrated crack erosion.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：抗隆起比值大於一，就能排除所有逆向侵蝕與管湧機制。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A heave ratio above one eliminates every backward-erosion and piping mechanism. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「出口隆起與內部侵蝕區別機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Exit heave versus internal erosion mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["抗隆起比值大於一，就能排除所有逆向侵蝕與管湧機制。","向上滲流的滲透力可抵消顆粒的浮重，在理想非黏性土柱中有效應力趨近零時可能隆起。","牆材滲透係數很低，就能忽略所有牆尖繞流與施工接頭。"],"optionsEn":["A heave ratio above one eliminates every backward-erosion and piping mechanism.","Upward seepage force can counter submerged particle weight, approaching zero effective stress in an ideal cohesionless column and allowing heave.","Very low wall-material conductivity makes all tip bypass and construction joints irrelevant."],"answer":1,"explanation":"向上滲流的滲透力可抵消顆粒的浮重，在理想非黏性土柱中有效應力趨近零時可能隆起。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Upward seepage force can counter submerged particle weight, approaching zero effective stress in an ideal cohesionless column and allowing heave. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b273-v15-26","title":"出口隆起與內部侵蝕區別機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Exit heave versus internal erosion mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出口隆起與內部侵蝕區別」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Exit heave versus internal erosion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Gs=2.65、e=0.65、垂直出口梯度ie=0.40，icr=(Gs−1)/(1+e)=1.00，理想抗隆起比icr/ie=2.50。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Gs=2.65, e=0.65 and vertical exit gradient ie=0.40. Ideal critical gradient icr=(Gs−1)/(1+e)=1.00; heave ratio icr/ie=2.50. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：確認出口梯度的方向與取樣距離，檢查覆載、土性和排水層接觸。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Confirm gradient direction and sampling distance and check surcharge, material and drain contacts.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Gs=2.65、e=0.65、垂直出口梯度ie=0.40，icr=(Gs−1)/(1+e)=1.00，理想抗隆起比icr/ie=2.50。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Gs=2.65, e=0.65 and vertical exit gradient ie=0.40. Ideal critical gradient icr=(Gs−1)/(1+e)=1.00; heave ratio icr/ie=2.50.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「出口隆起與內部侵蝕區別機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Exit heave versus internal erosion mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["兩支孔壓計讀值較大的那支，無論安裝高度如何都位於上游。","只要加水總量正確，每個土團就會立即具有相同含水量。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Gs=2.65、e=0.65、垂直出口梯度ie=0.40，icr=(Gs−1)/(1+e)=1.00，理想抗隆起比icr/ie=2.50。"],"optionsEn":["The higher pressure reading always identifies the upstream sensor regardless of installation elevation.","A correct total water dose immediately gives every soil clod identical moisture.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Gs=2.65, e=0.65 and vertical exit gradient ie=0.40."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Gs=2.65、e=0.65、垂直出口梯度ie=0.40，icr=(Gs−1)/(1+e)=1.00，理想抗隆起比icr/ie=2.50。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Gs=2.65, e=0.65 and vertical exit gradient ie=0.40. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b273-v15-27","title":"出口隆起與內部侵蝕區別機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Exit heave versus internal erosion mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出口隆起與內部侵蝕區別」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Exit heave versus internal erosion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"確認出口梯度的方向與取樣距離，檢查覆載、土性和排水層接觸。另行建立逆向侵蝕、集中漏水與濾層失效情境，配對觀測排水量、濁度及地表隆起，不能只看單一梯度比。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Confirm gradient direction and sampling distance and check surcharge, material and drain contacts. Separately assess backward erosion, concentrated leaks and filter failure, observing discharge, turbidity and heave together instead of treating a single gradient ratio as the entire seepage assessment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將垂直隆起與沿弱層逆向侵蝕各畫一張機理圖，列出它們需要的不同資料。比較縮短梯度取樣距離的影響，說明為何必須同時觀測帶砂出水。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw separate mechanisms for vertical heave and backward erosion along a weak layer, listing their different data needs. Compare shorter gradient measurement distances and explain why sediment-bearing seepage must also be observed.","failure":"注意干擾：粗網格平均梯度可能掩蓋局部出口峰值，黏性土裂縫也不符合無黏土柱假設；把大於一的比值當全面安全會漏掉可在不同條件下發展的侵蝕通道。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A coarse averaged gradient can hide an exit peak, and cracks in cohesive soil violate the ideal granular-column assumption. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"確認出口梯度的方向與取樣距離，檢查覆載、土性和排水層接觸。另行建立逆向侵蝕、集中漏水與濾層失效情境，配對觀測排水量、濁度及地表隆起，不能只看單一梯度比。","textEn":"Confirm gradient direction and sampling distance and check surcharge, material and drain contacts. Separately assess backward erosion, concentrated leaks and filter failure, observing discharge, turbidity and heave together instead of treating a single gradient ratio as the entire seepage assessment.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將垂直隆起與沿弱層逆向侵蝕各畫一張機理圖，列出它們需要的不同資料。比較縮短梯度取樣距離的影響，說明為何必須同時觀測帶砂出水。","textEn":"Draw separate mechanisms for vertical heave and backward erosion along a weak layer, listing their different data needs. Compare shorter gradient measurement distances and explain why sediment-bearing seepage must also be observed.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「出口隆起與內部侵蝕區別機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Exit heave versus internal erosion mechanism and verification\"?","options":["確認出口梯度的方向與取樣距離，檢查覆載、土性和排水層接觸。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","填土達到指定夯實度，就能證明下方軟弱地基不再壓密。"],"optionsEn":["Confirm gradient direction and sampling distance and check surcharge, material and drain contacts.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Specified fill compaction proves that the underlying soft foundation will no longer consolidate."],"answer":0,"explanation":"確認出口梯度的方向與取樣距離，檢查覆載、土性和排水層接觸。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Confirm gradient direction and sampling distance and check surcharge, material and drain contacts. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b273-v15-28","title":"出口隆起與內部侵蝕區別機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Exit heave versus internal erosion mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出口隆起與內部侵蝕區別」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Exit heave versus internal erosion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"粗網格平均梯度可能掩蓋局部出口峰值，黏性土裂縫也不符合無黏土柱假設；把大於一的比值當全面安全會漏掉可在不同條件下發展的侵蝕通道。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A coarse averaged gradient can hide an exit peak, and cracks in cohesive soil violate the ideal granular-column assumption. A ratio above unity does not exclude erosion paths developing under distinctly different conditions elsewhere in the foundation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例無覆載、均質非黏性土且出口垂直向上，僅比較理想臨界梯度與指定局部梯度；不能據此核准堤防或濾層配置。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It compares ideal critical and assigned local gradients only, not approval of an embankment or filter arrangement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「抗隆起比值大於一，就能排除所有逆向侵蝕與管湧機制。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A heave ratio above one eliminates every backward-erosion and piping mechanism.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"粗網格平均梯度可能掩蓋局部出口峰值，黏性土裂縫也不符合無黏土柱假設；把大於一的比值當全面安全會漏掉可在不同條件下發展的侵蝕通道。","textEn":"A coarse averaged gradient can hide an exit peak, and cracks in cohesive soil violate the ideal granular-column assumption. A ratio above unity does not exclude erosion paths developing under distinctly different conditions elsewhere in the foundation.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「出口隆起與內部侵蝕區別機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Exit heave versus internal erosion mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","粗網格平均梯度可能掩蓋局部出口峰值，黏性土裂縫也不符合無黏土柱假設；把大於一的比值當全面安全會漏掉可在不同條件下發展的侵蝕通道。","牆材滲透係數很低，就能忽略所有牆尖繞流與施工接頭。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A coarse averaged gradient can hide an exit peak, and cracks in cohesive soil violate the ideal granular-column assumption.","Very low wall-material conductivity makes all tip bypass and construction joints irrelevant."],"answer":1,"explanation":"粗網格平均梯度可能掩蓋局部出口峰值，黏性土裂縫也不符合無黏土柱假設；把大於一的比值當全面安全會漏掉可在不同條件下發展的侵蝕通道。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A coarse averaged gradient can hide an exit peak, and cracks in cohesive soil violate the ideal granular-column assumption. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b273-v15-29","title":"防滲牆與串聯水力阻抗機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cutoff walls and series resistance mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「防滲牆與串聯水力阻抗」如何影響土堤壓密與防滲的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cutoff walls and series resistance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Levee compaction and seepage control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"低透水防滲牆可以增加理想流路的水力阻抗，但效果取決於接頭、嵌入深度和周邊地層連續性。串聯阻抗把每段長度除滲透係數與面積後相加，適合展示低透水薄層的重要性；真實水流會繞過牆尖、側緣或施工缺陷，所以一維小流量不代表牆後壓力和局部出口都已降低。本例所有水量必須依序通過兩段相同截面，牆無缺陷且不存在繞流；僅為阻抗比較，不能當二維防滲牆設計成果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「防滲牆與串聯水力阻抗」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A low-conductivity cutoff increases resistance along an ideal path, but effectiveness depends on joints, penetration and surrounding strata. Series resistance sums each length divided by conductivity and area, illustrating a thin low-permeability layer. Actual flow may bypass tips, edges or defects, so a small one-dimensional discharge does not prove favorable downstream pressures and exit gradients. All flow in this example crosses two equal-area sections in series through a defect-free wall without bypass. It is a resistance comparison rather than a two-dimensional cutoff-wall design result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cutoff walls and series resistance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δh=3 m、A=10 m²，牆厚0.6 m、kw=10⁻⁹ m/s，土長29.4 m、ks=10⁻⁵ m/s，Q=Δh/[Lw/(kwA)+Ls/(ksA)]=4.976×10⁻⁸ m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δh=3 m and A=10 m²: wall Lw=0.6 m, kw=10⁻⁹ m/s; soil Ls=29.4 m, ks=10⁻⁵ m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「牆材滲透係數很低，就能忽略所有牆尖繞流與施工接頭。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Very low wall-material conductivity makes all tip bypass and construction joints irrelevant.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「防滲牆與串聯水力阻抗」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cutoff walls and series resistance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-29-k1","title":"防滲牆與串聯水力阻抗機理與驗證","titleEn":"Cutoff walls and series resistance mechanism and verification","text":"低透水防滲牆可以增加理想流路的水力阻抗，但效果取決於接頭、嵌入深度和周邊地層連續性。串聯阻抗把每段長度除滲透係數與面積後相加，適合展示低透水薄層的重要性；真實水流會繞過牆尖、側緣或施工缺陷，所以一維小流量不代表牆後壓力和局部出口都已降低。","textEn":"A low-conductivity cutoff increases resistance along an ideal path, but effectiveness depends on joints, penetration and surrounding strata. Series resistance sums each length divided by conductivity and area, illustrating a thin low-permeability layer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：牆材滲透係數很低，就能忽略所有牆尖繞流與施工接頭。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Very low wall-material conductivity makes all tip bypass and construction joints irrelevant. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「防滲牆與串聯水力阻抗機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cutoff walls and series resistance mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["牆材滲透係數很低，就能忽略所有牆尖繞流與施工接頭。","兩個粒徑比看起來合理，就能證明任何土類的濾層完整合格。","低透水防滲牆可以增加理想流路的水力阻抗，但效果取決於接頭、嵌入深度和周邊地層連續性。"],"optionsEn":["Very low wall-material conductivity makes all tip bypass and construction joints irrelevant.","Plausible values of two particle ratios prove complete filter acceptance for every soil type.","A low-conductivity cutoff increases resistance along an ideal path, but effectiveness depends on joints, penetration and surrounding strata."],"answer":2,"explanation":"低透水防滲牆可以增加理想流路的水力阻抗，但效果取決於接頭、嵌入深度和周邊地層連續性。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A low-conductivity cutoff increases resistance along an ideal path, but effectiveness depends on joints, penetration and surrounding strata. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b273-v15-30","title":"防滲牆與串聯水力阻抗機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Cutoff walls and series resistance mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「防滲牆與串聯水力阻抗」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cutoff walls and series resistance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δh=3 m、A=10 m²，牆厚0.6 m、kw=10⁻⁹ m/s，土長29.4 m、ks=10⁻⁵ m/s，Q=Δh/[Lw/(kwA)+Ls/(ksA)]=4.976×10⁻⁸ m³/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δh=3 m and A=10 m²: wall Lw=0.6 m, kw=10⁻⁹ m/s; soil Ls=29.4 m, ks=10⁻⁵ m/s. Series discharge is 4.976×10⁻⁸ m³/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對牆體連續性、施工接頭和嵌入地層，將穿牆與繞牆路徑分開建模。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify wall continuity, joints and the penetrated stratum, modeling through-wall and bypass paths separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δh=3 m、A=10 m²，牆厚0.6 m、kw=10⁻⁹ m/s，土長29.4 m、ks=10⁻⁵ m/s，Q=Δh/[Lw/(kwA)+Ls/(ksA)]=4.976×10⁻⁸ m³/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δh=3 m and A=10 m²: wall Lw=0.6 m, kw=10⁻⁹ m/s; soil Ls=29.4 m, ks=10⁻⁵ m/s. Series discharge is 4.976×10⁻⁸ m³/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「防滲牆與串聯水力阻抗機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cutoff walls and series resistance mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δh=3 m、A=10 m²，牆厚0.6 m、kw=10⁻⁹ m/s，土長29.4 m、ks=10⁻⁵ m/s，Q=Δh/[Lw/(kwA)+Ls/(ksA)]=4.976×10⁻⁸ m³/s。","現場濕密度較高就必定表示乾密度與防滲能力都較好。","相同乾密度的兩份土一定具有相同飽和度與滲透係數。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δh=3 m and A=10 m²: wall Lw=0.6 m, kw=10⁻⁹ m/s.","Higher field wet density necessarily means better dry density and seepage resistance.","Two soils with equal dry density necessarily have equal saturation and hydraulic conductivity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δh=3 m、A=10 m²，牆厚0.6 m、kw=10⁻⁹ m/s，土長29.4 m、ks=10⁻⁵ m/s，Q=Δh/[Lw/(kwA)+Ls/(ksA)]=4.976×10⁻⁸ m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δh=3 m and A=10 m²: wall Lw=0.6 m, kw=10⁻⁹ m/s; soil Ls=29.4 m, ks=10⁻⁵ m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b273-v15-31","title":"防滲牆與串聯水力阻抗機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cutoff walls and series resistance mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「防滲牆與串聯水力阻抗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cutoff walls and series resistance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對牆體連續性、施工接頭和嵌入地層，將穿牆與繞牆路徑分開建模。用牆前後孔壓及排水量辨識壓降位置，必要時檢查不連續缺陷，避免只比較材料試體的滲透係數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify wall continuity, joints and the penetrated stratum, modeling through-wall and bypass paths separately. Use upstream/downstream pressures and discharge to locate head loss, investigating discontinuities where necessary instead of comparing laboratory wall-material conductivity alone as evidence of overall performance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在串聯模型旁增設一條假設平行缺陷，分別列各路的壓差和阻抗。比較總流量及壓降分配，指出現場哪些量測能區分材料不良與繞流問題。","observationEn":"Site practice: Add a hypothetical parallel defect beside the series path and list head differences and resistances separately. Compare total discharge and head-loss distribution, identifying measurements that distinguish poor wall material from hydraulic bypass.","failure":"注意干擾：低透水試體不能保證接縫同樣密實，一條高透水缺陷可成平行流路而破壞串聯假設；僅延長牆深而不檢查出口，也可能把壓降集中到不利位置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A low-conductivity specimen does not prove joint continuity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對牆體連續性、施工接頭和嵌入地層，將穿牆與繞牆路徑分開建模。用牆前後孔壓及排水量辨識壓降位置，必要時檢查不連續缺陷，避免只比較材料試體的滲透係數。","textEn":"Verify wall continuity, joints and the penetrated stratum, modeling through-wall and bypass paths separately. Use upstream/downstream pressures and discharge to locate head loss, investigating discontinuities where necessary instead of comparing laboratory wall-material conductivity alone as evidence of overall performance.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在串聯模型旁增設一條假設平行缺陷，分別列各路的壓差和阻抗。比較總流量及壓降分配，指出現場哪些量測能區分材料不良與繞流問題。","textEn":"Add a hypothetical parallel defect beside the series path and list head differences and resistances separately. Compare total discharge and head-loss distribution, identifying measurements that distinguish poor wall material from hydraulic bypass.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「防滲牆與串聯水力阻抗機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cutoff walls and series resistance mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對牆體連續性、施工接頭和嵌入地層，將穿牆與繞牆路徑分開建模。","土層厚度減半時，所有情況的壓密時間都只會減半。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Verify wall continuity, joints and the penetrated stratum, modeling through-wall and bypass paths separately.","Halving soil thickness always halves consolidation time under every drainage condition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對牆體連續性、施工接頭和嵌入地層，將穿牆與繞牆路徑分開建模。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify wall continuity, joints and the penetrated stratum, modeling through-wall and bypass paths separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b273-v15-32","title":"防滲牆與串聯水力阻抗機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cutoff walls and series resistance mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「防滲牆與串聯水力阻抗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cutoff walls and series resistance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"低透水試體不能保證接縫同樣密實，一條高透水缺陷可成平行流路而破壞串聯假設；僅延長牆深而不檢查出口，也可能把壓降集中到不利位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A low-conductivity specimen does not prove joint continuity. One permeable defect creates a parallel path that invalidates the series model, while deeper penetration without checking exits may concentrate head loss in an unfavorable location. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例所有水量必須依序通過兩段相同截面，牆無缺陷且不存在繞流；僅為阻抗比較，不能當二維防滲牆設計成果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It is a resistance comparison rather than a two-dimensional cutoff-wall design result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「牆材滲透係數很低，就能忽略所有牆尖繞流與施工接頭。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Very low wall-material conductivity makes all tip bypass and construction joints irrelevant.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"低透水試體不能保證接縫同樣密實，一條高透水缺陷可成平行流路而破壞串聯假設；僅延長牆深而不檢查出口，也可能把壓降集中到不利位置。","textEn":"A low-conductivity specimen does not prove joint continuity. One permeable defect creates a parallel path that invalidates the series model, while deeper penetration without checking exits may concentrate head loss in an unfavorable location.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「防滲牆與串聯水力阻抗機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cutoff walls and series resistance mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","兩個粒徑比看起來合理，就能證明任何土類的濾層完整合格。","低透水試體不能保證接縫同樣密實，一條高透水缺陷可成平行流路而破壞串聯假設；僅延長牆深而不檢查出口，也可能把壓降集中到不利位置。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Plausible values of two particle ratios prove complete filter acceptance for every soil type.","A low-conductivity specimen does not prove joint continuity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"低透水試體不能保證接縫同樣密實，一條高透水缺陷可成平行流路而破壞串聯假設；僅延長牆深而不檢查出口，也可能把壓降集中到不利位置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A low-conductivity specimen does not prove joint continuity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b273-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「濾層保土與通水機理與驗證」與「孔壓監測與總水頭機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Filter retention and drainage mechanism and verification\" and \"Pore-pressure monitoring and total head mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b273-v15-33","title":"濾層保土與通水機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Filter retention and drainage mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「濾層保土與通水」如何影響土堤壓密與防滲的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Filter retention and drainage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Levee compaction and seepage control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"濾層需在土料流失前形成可靠的顆粒截留，同時讓水排出而不累積不利孔壓。粒徑比是篩選工具，適用界線取決於基土類別、細料比例、分散性和採用的設計程序；施工離析、污染或濾層中斷會使合格室內級配失去意義，因此保土、通水與連續性都需驗證。本例只算兩個粒徑比，未指定土類或完整設計準則，因此不能標示濾層合格。粒徑均取各自累積通過曲線對應百分位。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「濾層保土與通水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Filters must retain migrating base particles while passing water without adverse pressure buildup. Particle-size ratios are screening tools whose limits depend on base-soil category, fines, dispersivity and the selected procedure. Segregation, contamination or interrupted placement can defeat a compliant laboratory gradation, so retention, drainage and continuity all require verification in the completed work. The example computes two grain-size ratios without specifying soil class or a complete design procedure, so it cannot declare acceptance. Diameters refer to the appropriate percent-finer points on their respective curves. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Filter retention and drainage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設濾料D15=0.60 mm，基土d85=0.20 mm、d15=0.05 mm，保土指標比D15/d85=3，通水指標比D15/d15=12。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume filter D15=0.60 mm, base d85=0.20 mm and base d15=0.05 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩個粒徑比看起來合理，就能證明任何土類的濾層完整合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Plausible values of two particle ratios prove complete filter acceptance for every soil type.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「濾層保土與通水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Filter retention and drainage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-33-k1","title":"濾層保土與通水機理與驗證","titleEn":"Filter retention and drainage mechanism and verification","text":"濾層需在土料流失前形成可靠的顆粒截留，同時讓水排出而不累積不利孔壓。粒徑比是篩選工具，適用界線取決於基土類別、細料比例、分散性和採用的設計程序；施工離析、污染或濾層中斷會使合格室內級配失去意義，因此保土、通水與連續性都需驗證。","textEn":"Filters must retain migrating base particles while passing water without adverse pressure buildup. Particle-size ratios are screening tools whose limits depend on base-soil category, fines, dispersivity and the selected procedure.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩個粒徑比看起來合理，就能證明任何土類的濾層完整合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Plausible values of two particle ratios prove complete filter acceptance for every soil type. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「濾層保土與通水機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Filter retention and drainage mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["濾層需在土料流失前形成可靠的顆粒截留，同時讓水排出而不累積不利孔壓。","兩個粒徑比看起來合理，就能證明任何土類的濾層完整合格。","兩支孔壓計讀值較大的那支，無論安裝高度如何都位於上游。"],"optionsEn":["Filters must retain migrating base particles while passing water without adverse pressure buildup.","Plausible values of two particle ratios prove complete filter acceptance for every soil type.","The higher pressure reading always identifies the upstream sensor regardless of installation elevation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"濾層需在土料流失前形成可靠的顆粒截留，同時讓水排出而不累積不利孔壓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Filters must retain migrating base particles while passing water without adverse pressure buildup. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b273-v15-34","title":"濾層保土與通水機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Filter retention and drainage mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「濾層保土與通水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Filter retention and drainage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設濾料D15=0.60 mm，基土d85=0.20 mm、d15=0.05 mm，保土指標比D15/d85=3，通水指標比D15/d15=12。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume filter D15=0.60 mm, base d85=0.20 mm and base d15=0.05 mm. Screening ratios are D15/d85=3 and D15/d15=12, without an acceptance claim. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對代表性基土完整級配與分散性，按選定手冊土類步驟設計並檢查濾料生產範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check representative full base gradations and dispersivity, follow the chosen manual’s soil-category procedure and review production limits.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設濾料D15=0.60 mm，基土d85=0.20 mm、d15=0.05 mm，保土指標比D15/d85=3，通水指標比D15/d15=12。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume filter D15=0.60 mm, base d85=0.20 mm and base d15=0.05 mm. Screening ratios are D15/d85=3 and D15/d15=12, without an acceptance claim.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「濾層保土與通水機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Filter retention and drainage mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["只要加水總量正確，每個土團就會立即具有相同含水量。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設濾料D15=0.60 mm，基土d85=0.20 mm、d15=0.05 mm，保土指標比D15/d85=3，通水指標比D15/d15=12。","填土達到指定夯實度，就能證明下方軟弱地基不再壓密。"],"optionsEn":["A correct total water dose immediately gives every soil clod identical moisture.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume filter D15=0.60 mm, base d85=0.20 mm and base d15=0.05 mm.","Specified fill compaction proves that the underlying soft foundation will no longer consolidate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設濾料D15=0.60 mm，基土d85=0.20 mm、d15=0.05 mm，保土指標比D15/d85=3，通水指標比D15/d15=12。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume filter D15=0.60 mm, base d85=0.20 mm and base d15=0.05 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b273-v15-35","title":"濾層保土與通水機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Filter retention and drainage mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「濾層保土與通水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Filter retention and drainage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對代表性基土完整級配與分散性，按選定手冊土類步驟設計並檢查濾料生產範圍。施工時追蹤離析、厚度、污染和接縫，必要時用相容性試驗驗證，而不是只留兩個比值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check representative full base gradations and dispersivity, follow the chosen manual’s soil-category procedure and review production limits. Inspect segregation, thickness, contamination and transitions during placement, using compatibility testing when needed instead of retaining only two screening ratios in the acceptance record. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用同一濾料對兩種基土重算比值，列出尚缺的土類和分散性資料。畫出轉角與穿堤構造旁的濾層接續，說明級配計算無法替代施工連續性檢查。","observationEn":"Site practice: Apply one filter to two base soils and recalculate ratios, listing missing classification and dispersivity data. Draw filter continuity at corners and conduits, explaining why grading arithmetic cannot replace inspection of physical continuity.","failure":"注意干擾：用平均基土掩蓋最不利細粒層會漏掉保土需求，運輸離析又可能形成局部粗料窗；即使顆粒比合理，濾層中斷仍讓集中滲流直接侵蝕未保護基土。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An averaged base soil can hide a critical finer layer, and transport segregation can create coarse windows. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對代表性基土完整級配與分散性，按選定手冊土類步驟設計並檢查濾料生產範圍。施工時追蹤離析、厚度、污染和接縫，必要時用相容性試驗驗證，而不是只留兩個比值。","textEn":"Check representative full base gradations and dispersivity, follow the chosen manual’s soil-category procedure and review production limits. Inspect segregation, thickness, contamination and transitions during placement, using compatibility testing when needed instead of retaining only two screening ratios in the acceptance record.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用同一濾料對兩種基土重算比值，列出尚缺的土類和分散性資料。畫出轉角與穿堤構造旁的濾層接續，說明級配計算無法替代施工連續性檢查。","textEn":"Apply one filter to two base soils and recalculate ratios, listing missing classification and dispersivity data. Draw filter continuity at corners and conduits, explaining why grading arithmetic cannot replace inspection of physical continuity.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「濾層保土與通水機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Filter retention and drainage mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","達西公式中的水位差本身就是水力坡降，不需要流徑長度。","核對代表性基土完整級配與分散性，按選定手冊土類步驟設計並檢查濾料生產範圍。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Head difference alone is the Darcy hydraulic gradient and needs no flow-path length.","Check representative full base gradations and dispersivity, follow the chosen manual’s soil-category procedure and review production limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對代表性基土完整級配與分散性，按選定手冊土類步驟設計並檢查濾料生產範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check representative full base gradations and dispersivity, follow the chosen manual’s soil-category procedure and review production limits. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b273-v15-36","title":"濾層保土與通水機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Filter retention and drainage mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「濾層保土與通水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Filter retention and drainage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用平均基土掩蓋最不利細粒層會漏掉保土需求，運輸離析又可能形成局部粗料窗；即使顆粒比合理，濾層中斷仍讓集中滲流直接侵蝕未保護基土。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An averaged base soil can hide a critical finer layer, and transport segregation can create coarse windows. Even plausible particle ratios cannot protect base soil where an interrupted filter exposes it directly to concentrated seepage flow. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：粒徑均取各自累積通過曲線對應百分位。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Diameters refer to the appropriate percent-finer points on their respective curves.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩個粒徑比看起來合理，就能證明任何土類的濾層完整合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Plausible values of two particle ratios prove complete filter acceptance for every soil type.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用平均基土掩蓋最不利細粒層會漏掉保土需求，運輸離析又可能形成局部粗料窗；即使顆粒比合理，濾層中斷仍讓集中滲流直接侵蝕未保護基土。","textEn":"An averaged base soil can hide a critical finer layer, and transport segregation can create coarse windows. Even plausible particle ratios cannot protect base soil where an interrupted filter exposes it directly to concentrated seepage flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「濾層保土與通水機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Filter retention and drainage mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用平均基土掩蓋最不利細粒層會漏掉保土需求，運輸離析又可能形成局部粗料窗；即使顆粒比合理，濾層中斷仍讓集中滲流直接侵蝕未保護基土。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","兩支孔壓計讀值較大的那支，無論安裝高度如何都位於上游。"],"optionsEn":["An averaged base soil can hide a critical finer layer, and transport segregation can create coarse windows.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The higher pressure reading always identifies the upstream sensor regardless of installation elevation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用平均基土掩蓋最不利細粒層會漏掉保土需求，運輸離析又可能形成局部粗料窗；即使顆粒比合理，濾層中斷仍讓集中滲流直接侵蝕未保護基土。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An averaged base soil can hide a critical finer layer, and transport segregation can create coarse windows. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b273-v15-37","title":"孔壓監測與總水頭機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pore-pressure monitoring and total head mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「孔壓監測與總水頭」如何影響土堤壓密與防滲的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pore-pressure monitoring and total head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Levee compaction and seepage control”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"孔壓計量到的是感測點附近壓力，解讀滲流需要把壓力水頭加到感測器高程，並統一氣壓補償與時間基準。若不分感測器高度而直接比較壓力數值，可能誤判流向；水頭變化還應結合排水流量、濁度和填築歷史，才能區別洪水邊界變動、儀器漂移與局部異常。本例使用已扣氣壓的表壓與同一高程基準，忽略速度水頭。總水頭是該點水力勢，不自動等於另一處自由地下水面位置。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「孔壓監測與總水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A piezometer measures pressure near its sensor; seepage interpretation adds pressure head to sensor elevation and aligns atmospheric compensation and timestamps. Comparing pressure alone at different heights can reverse an inferred flow direction. Head changes should also be assessed with discharge, turbidity and construction history to distinguish changing flood boundaries, instrument drift and local anomalies. The example uses gauge pressure after atmospheric correction and one elevation datum, neglecting velocity head. Point total head represents hydraulic potential, not automatically the free groundwater surface at another location. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pore-pressure monitoring and total head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設感測器高程z=12 m、表孔壓u=29.43 kPa、水單位重γw=9.81 kN/m³，總水頭h=z+u/γw=15 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume sensor elevation z=12 m, gauge pore pressure u=29.43 kPa and water unit weight γw=9.81 kN/m³.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩支孔壓計讀值較大的那支，無論安裝高度如何都位於上游。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The higher pressure reading always identifies the upstream sensor regardless of installation elevation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「孔壓監測與總水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pore-pressure monitoring and total head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-37-k1","title":"孔壓監測與總水頭機理與驗證","titleEn":"Pore-pressure monitoring and total head mechanism and verification","text":"孔壓計量到的是感測點附近壓力，解讀滲流需要把壓力水頭加到感測器高程，並統一氣壓補償與時間基準。若不分感測器高度而直接比較壓力數值，可能誤判流向；水頭變化還應結合排水流量、濁度和填築歷史，才能區別洪水邊界變動、儀器漂移與局部異常。","textEn":"A piezometer measures pressure near its sensor; seepage interpretation adds pressure head to sensor elevation and aligns atmospheric compensation and timestamps. Comparing pressure alone at different heights can reverse an inferred flow direction.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩支孔壓計讀值較大的那支，無論安裝高度如何都位於上游。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The higher pressure reading always identifies the upstream sensor regardless of installation elevation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「孔壓監測與總水頭機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pore-pressure monitoring and total head mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["兩支孔壓計讀值較大的那支，無論安裝高度如何都位於上游。","孔壓計量到的是感測點附近壓力，解讀滲流需要把壓力水頭加到感測器高程，並統一氣壓補償與時間基準。","現場濕密度較高就必定表示乾密度與防滲能力都較好。"],"optionsEn":["The higher pressure reading always identifies the upstream sensor regardless of installation elevation.","A piezometer measures pressure near its sensor.","Higher field wet density necessarily means better dry density and seepage resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"孔壓計量到的是感測點附近壓力，解讀滲流需要把壓力水頭加到感測器高程，並統一氣壓補償與時間基準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A piezometer measures pressure near its sensor; seepage interpretation adds pressure head to sensor elevation and aligns atmospheric compensation and timestamps. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b273-v15-38","title":"孔壓監測與總水頭機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Pore-pressure monitoring and total head mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「孔壓監測與總水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pore-pressure monitoring and total head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設感測器高程z=12 m、表孔壓u=29.43 kPa、水單位重γw=9.81 kN/m³，總水頭h=z+u/γw=15 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume sensor elevation z=12 m, gauge pore pressure u=29.43 kPa and water unit weight γw=9.81 kN/m³. Total head h=z+u/γw=15 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保留安裝高程、零點、氣壓與校正紀錄，確認量程及觀測頻率適合洪水變化。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Retain installation elevation, zero, atmospheric and calibration records and match range and frequency to flood changes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設感測器高程z=12 m、表孔壓u=29.43 kPa、水單位重γw=9.81 kN/m³，總水頭h=z+u/γw=15 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume sensor elevation z=12 m, gauge pore pressure u=29.43 kPa and water unit weight γw=9.81 kN/m³. Total head h=z+u/γw=15 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「孔壓監測與總水頭機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pore-pressure monitoring and total head mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["相同乾密度的兩份土一定具有相同飽和度與滲透係數。","土層厚度減半時，所有情況的壓密時間都只會減半。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設感測器高程z=12 m、表孔壓u=29.43 kPa、水單位重γw=9.81 kN/m³，總水頭h=z+u/γw=15 m。"],"optionsEn":["Two soils with equal dry density necessarily have equal saturation and hydraulic conductivity.","Halving soil thickness always halves consolidation time under every drainage condition.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume sensor elevation z=12 m, gauge pore pressure u=29.43 kPa and water unit weight γw=9.81 kN/m³."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設感測器高程z=12 m、表孔壓u=29.43 kPa、水單位重γw=9.81 kN/m³，總水頭h=z+u/γw=15 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume sensor elevation z=12 m, gauge pore pressure u=29.43 kPa and water unit weight γw=9.81 kN/m³. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b273-v15-39","title":"孔壓監測與總水頭機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pore-pressure monitoring and total head mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「孔壓監測與總水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pore-pressure monitoring and total head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保留安裝高程、零點、氣壓與校正紀錄，確認量程及觀測頻率適合洪水變化。比較多測點總水頭和出水量濁度，異常先交叉檢核儀器及邊界，不用單支感測器代表整段堤防。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Retain installation elevation, zero, atmospheric and calibration records and match range and frequency to flood changes. Compare total head across instruments with discharge and turbidity, cross-checking equipment and boundaries before allowing one sensor to represent an entire embankment reach. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：給兩支不同高度感測器相同表壓，計算總水頭並判斷可能流向。再加入儀器零點偏移，列出需要哪些獨立量測才能區分真實滲流改變與感測錯誤。","observationEn":"Site practice: Give two sensors at different elevations equal gauge pressures, compute total heads and infer possible flow direction. Add a zero offset and list independent observations needed to distinguish an actual seepage change from measurement error.","failure":"注意干擾：基準高程錯誤會使所有水頭判讀系統性偏移，堵塞或失聯也可能假裝平穩；如果只設水位警戒而不追蹤出砂，即使孔壓變化不大仍可能漏掉侵蝕發展。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An elevation-datum error systematically shifts inferred heads, while blockage or lost communication may mimic stability. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保留安裝高程、零點、氣壓與校正紀錄，確認量程及觀測頻率適合洪水變化。比較多測點總水頭和出水量濁度，異常先交叉檢核儀器及邊界，不用單支感測器代表整段堤防。","textEn":"Retain installation elevation, zero, atmospheric and calibration records and match range and frequency to flood changes. Compare total head across instruments with discharge and turbidity, cross-checking equipment and boundaries before allowing one sensor to represent an entire embankment reach.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"給兩支不同高度感測器相同表壓，計算總水頭並判斷可能流向。再加入儀器零點偏移，列出需要哪些獨立量測才能區分真實滲流改變與感測錯誤。","textEn":"Give two sensors at different elevations equal gauge pressures, compute total heads and infer possible flow direction. Add a zero offset and list independent observations needed to distinguish an actual seepage change from measurement error.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「孔壓監測與總水頭機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pore-pressure monitoring and total head mechanism and verification\"?","options":["保留安裝高程、零點、氣壓與校正紀錄，確認量程及觀測頻率適合洪水變化。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","抗隆起比值大於一，就能排除所有逆向侵蝕與管湧機制。"],"optionsEn":["Retain installation elevation, zero, atmospheric and calibration records and match range and frequency to flood changes.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A heave ratio above one eliminates every backward-erosion and piping mechanism."],"answer":0,"explanation":"保留安裝高程、零點、氣壓與校正紀錄，確認量程及觀測頻率適合洪水變化。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Retain installation elevation, zero, atmospheric and calibration records and match range and frequency to flood changes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b273-v15-40","title":"孔壓監測與總水頭機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pore-pressure monitoring and total head mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"prerequisiteIds":["b273-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「孔壓監測與總水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pore-pressure monitoring and total head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"基準高程錯誤會使所有水頭判讀系統性偏移，堵塞或失聯也可能假裝平穩；如果只設水位警戒而不追蹤出砂，即使孔壓變化不大仍可能漏掉侵蝕發展。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An elevation-datum error systematically shifts inferred heads, while blockage or lost communication may mimic stability. A stage-only alarm without sediment observations can miss erosion developing even when measured pore-pressure changes remain modest. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：總水頭是該點水力勢，不自動等於另一處自由地下水面位置。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Point total head represents hydraulic potential, not automatically the free groundwater surface at another location.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩支孔壓計讀值較大的那支，無論安裝高度如何都位於上游。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The higher pressure reading always identifies the upstream sensor regardless of installation elevation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b273-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"基準高程錯誤會使所有水頭判讀系統性偏移，堵塞或失聯也可能假裝平穩；如果只設水位警戒而不追蹤出砂，即使孔壓變化不大仍可能漏掉侵蝕發展。","textEn":"An elevation-datum error systematically shifts inferred heads, while blockage or lost communication may mimic stability. A stage-only alarm without sediment observations can miss erosion developing even when measured pore-pressure changes remain modest.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]},{"id":"b273-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔壓監測與總水頭機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pore-pressure monitoring and total head mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","基準高程錯誤會使所有水頭判讀系統性偏移，堵塞或失聯也可能假裝平穩；如果只設水位警戒而不追蹤出砂，即使孔壓變化不大仍可能漏掉侵蝕發展。","現場濕密度較高就必定表示乾密度與防滲能力都較好。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","An elevation-datum error systematically shifts inferred heads, while blockage or lost communication may mimic stability.","Higher field wet density necessarily means better dry density and seepage resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"基準高程錯誤會使所有水頭判讀系統性偏移，堵塞或失聯也可能假裝平穩；如果只設水位警戒而不追蹤出砂，即使孔壓變化不大仍可能漏掉侵蝕發展。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An elevation-datum error systematically shifts inferred heads, while blockage or lost communication may mimic stability. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-embank","v15s-usbr-filters","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-usace-westlevee","v15s-manitoba-floodway"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b274","title":"防洪牆基礎設計","titleEn":"Floodwall foundation design","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"課程串聯靜水合力、揚壓、抗滑、偏心接觸、承載與沉陷，再檢查被動土阻、防滲、接頭及退水反向作用。每個模型明示假設與量綱，區分荷載計算、強度和使用性。比尤德利與波士頓提供工程背景，但本課不把假設尺寸、強度或安全比值當成實際設計或地方核准。","summaryEn":"The course connects hydrostatic force, uplift, sliding, eccentric contact, bearing and settlement before examining passive resistance, cutoffs, joints and recession loads. Each model identifies assumptions and dimensions while distinguishing loading, strength and serviceability. Bewdley and Boston provide engineering context, but assumed dimensions, strengths and resistance ratios are not project designs or local approvals.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["水位與作用","Water levels and actions"],["底版與揚壓","Footing and uplift"],["接觸與抗力","Contact and resistance"],["沉陷與接頭","Settlement and joints"],["情境與維護","Cases and maintenance"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["水位與作用","底版與揚壓","接觸與抗力","沉陷與接頭","情境與維護"],"labelsEn":["Water levels and actions","Footing and uplift","Contact and resistance","Settlement and joints","Cases and maintenance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"敏感度固定單側靜水、每公尺牆長和水單位重9.81 kN/m³，只把水深從3.0增至3.3 m。合力由44.145增至53.41545 kN/m，增加21%；底部力矩由44.145增至58.7570 kN·m/m，增加33.1%。兩者分別按水深平方和立方變化，不能使用相同百分比。這並不直接給出基礎偏心的新值，因為底版揚壓、垂直水重及其他荷載可能也變動；完整比較必須重新組合相同時刻的各項作用，確認接觸模型仍適用，並獨立檢查承載、滑動與變形。","textEn":"Hold one-sided still water, unit wall length and water unit weight at 9.81 kN/m³ while raising depth from 3.0 to 3.3 m. Force rises from 44.145 to 53.41545 kN/m, an increase of 21%; base moment rises from 44.145 to 58.7570 kN·m/m, an increase of 33.1%. Force and moment scale with depth squared and cubed respectively. This does not directly give a new foundation eccentricity, because uplift, vertical water weight and other loads may also change. A complete comparison recombines all actions at compatible times, confirms the contact model remains applicable and independently checks bearing, sliding and deformation. No acceptance criterion is inferred from the scaling exercise alone.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b274-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「靜水荷載與作用點機理與驗證」與「底版揚壓與合力位置機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Hydrostatic load and lever arm mechanism and verification\" and \"Footing uplift and resultant location mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b274-v15-01","title":"靜水荷載與作用點機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Hydrostatic load and lever arm mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「靜水荷載與作用點」如何影響防洪牆基礎設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Hydrostatic load and lever arm” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floodwall foundation design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"防洪牆承受的靜水壓隨水深增加，沿垂直面形成三角形分布，合力與水深平方成正比而底部力矩隨立方改變。荷載必須連到牆身、底版與地基的傳力路徑，不能只以牆頂高度選構件；波浪、漂流物與兩側水位差還需另外建立情境，避免把單側靜水圖當完整設計。本例每公尺牆長、單側淡水、背側乾燥，基底與水深起點相同。忽略動水、土壓和結構自重，結果只是一項外荷載。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「靜水荷載與作用點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Hydrostatic pressure increases with depth, giving a triangular distribution on a vertical face. Force varies with depth squared and base moment with depth cubed. The load must follow a path through stem, footing and soil, rather than sizing from wall height alone. Waves, debris and differing water levels require separate cases beyond one-sided still water. The example is per metre of wall with freshwater on one side and a dry rear face, measured from the same base. Dynamic water, earth pressure and self-weight are excluded. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Hydrostatic load and lever arm” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設γw=9.81 kN/m³、水深h=3 m，合力F=γwh²/2=44.145 kN/m，作用點高h/3=1 m，底矩M=44.145 kN·m/m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume water unit weight 9.81 kN/m³ and depth h=3 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「水深增加一成時，防洪牆的底部水壓力矩也只增加一成。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A ten-percent increase in depth increases hydrostatic base moment by only ten percent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「靜水荷載與作用點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Hydrostatic load and lever arm”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-01-k1","title":"靜水荷載與作用點機理與驗證","titleEn":"Hydrostatic load and lever arm mechanism and verification","text":"防洪牆承受的靜水壓隨水深增加，沿垂直面形成三角形分布，合力與水深平方成正比而底部力矩隨立方改變。荷載必須連到牆身、底版與地基的傳力路徑，不能只以牆頂高度選構件；波浪、漂流物與兩側水位差還需另外建立情境，避免把單側靜水圖當完整設計。","textEn":"Hydrostatic pressure increases with depth, giving a triangular distribution on a vertical face. Force varies with depth squared and base moment with depth cubed.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水深增加一成時，防洪牆的底部水壓力矩也只增加一成。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A ten-percent increase in depth increases hydrostatic base moment by only ten percent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「靜水荷載與作用點機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Hydrostatic load and lever arm mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["水深增加一成時，防洪牆的底部水壓力矩也只增加一成。","防洪牆承受的靜水壓隨水深增加，沿垂直面形成三角形分布，合力與水深平方成正比而底部力矩隨立方改變。","只要揚壓總力算對，它作用在底版何處就完全不影響穩定。"],"optionsEn":["A ten-percent increase in depth increases hydrostatic base moment by only ten percent.","Hydrostatic pressure increases with depth, giving a triangular distribution on a vertical face.","Correct total uplift makes its position beneath the footing irrelevant to stability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"防洪牆承受的靜水壓隨水深增加，沿垂直面形成三角形分布，合力與水深平方成正比而底部力矩隨立方改變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Hydrostatic pressure increases with depth, giving a triangular distribution on a vertical face. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b274-v15-02","title":"靜水荷載與作用點機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Hydrostatic load and lever arm mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「靜水荷載與作用點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Hydrostatic load and lever arm” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設γw=9.81 kN/m³、水深h=3 m，合力F=γwh²/2=44.145 kN/m，作用點高h/3=1 m，底矩M=44.145 kN·m/m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume water unit weight 9.81 kN/m³ and depth h=3 m. Force F=44.145 kN/m acts 1 m above the base, producing moment 44.145 kN·m/m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將兩側水位與基底高程放入同一剖面，逐項積分壓力並檢查合力作用點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Place both water levels and the base on one section, integrate pressure and check its resultant location.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設γw=9.81 kN/m³、水深h=3 m，合力F=γwh²/2=44.145 kN/m，作用點高h/3=1 m，底矩M=44.145 kN·m/m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume water unit weight 9.81 kN/m³ and depth h=3 m. Force F=44.145 kN/m acts 1 m above the base, producing moment 44.145 kN·m/m.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「靜水荷載與作用點機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Hydrostatic load and lever arm mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["底面最小壓力大於零，就足以證明承載、沉陷與牆身強度全都合格。","計算得到小的瞬時彈性沉陷，就能排除所有長期接頭變形。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設γw=9.81 kN/m³、水深h=3 m，合力F=γwh²/2=44.145 kN/m，作用點高h/3=1 m，底矩M=44.145 kN·m/m。"],"optionsEn":["Positive minimum footing pressure proves bearing, settlement and wall strength all acceptable.","Small calculated instantaneous elastic settlement excludes every long-term joint movement problem.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume water unit weight 9.81 kN/m³ and depth h=3 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設γw=9.81 kN/m³、水深h=3 m，合力F=γwh²/2=44.145 kN/m，作用點高h/3=1 m，底矩M=44.145 kN·m/m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume water unit weight 9.81 kN/m³ and depth h=3 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b274-v15-03","title":"靜水荷載與作用點機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Hydrostatic load and lever arm mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「靜水荷載與作用點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hydrostatic load and lever arm” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將兩側水位與基底高程放入同一剖面，逐項積分壓力並檢查合力作用點。列出土壓、波浪及漂流物是否另計，沿牆身到底版追蹤剪力與彎矩，不能只驗算水平力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Place both water levels and the base on one section, integrate pressure and check its resultant location. List separate earth, wave and debris contributions and trace shear and bending into the footing instead of checking horizontal force alone as the complete load path. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出不同水深的三角壓力分布並積分合力與力矩，分開列平方和立方比例。再加入背側水位，說明何時應扣除另一個三角形而不是只用水深差平方。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw triangular pressure diagrams for two depths and integrate force and moment, listing square and cube scaling separately. Add rear water and explain why subtracting two triangles differs from squaring only the depth difference.","failure":"注意干擾：把平均壓力作用在半水深會算錯力矩，漏掉背側水位又會誤判方向；使用水深平方比例估力矩會低估水位升高後的彎曲需求及地基偏心。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying average pressure at half depth gives the wrong moment, while omitted rear water can reverse the assumed direction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將兩側水位與基底高程放入同一剖面，逐項積分壓力並檢查合力作用點。列出土壓、波浪及漂流物是否另計，沿牆身到底版追蹤剪力與彎矩，不能只驗算水平力。","textEn":"Place both water levels and the base on one section, integrate pressure and check its resultant location. List separate earth, wave and debris contributions and trace shear and bending into the footing instead of checking horizontal force alone as the complete load path.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出不同水深的三角壓力分布並積分合力與力矩，分開列平方和立方比例。再加入背側水位，說明何時應扣除另一個三角形而不是只用水深差平方。","textEn":"Draw triangular pressure diagrams for two depths and integrate force and moment, listing square and cube scaling separately. Add rear water and explain why subtracting two triangles differs from squaring only the depth difference.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「靜水荷載與作用點機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Hydrostatic load and lever arm mechanism and verification\"?","options":["將兩側水位與基底高程放入同一剖面，逐項積分壓力並檢查合力作用點。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","防滲牆越深時，所有位置的孔壓與出口梯度必定同時降低。"],"optionsEn":["Place both water levels and the base on one section, integrate pressure and check its resultant location.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A deeper cutoff necessarily lowers pore pressure and exit gradient at every location."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將兩側水位與基底高程放入同一剖面，逐項積分壓力並檢查合力作用點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Place both water levels and the base on one section, integrate pressure and check its resultant location. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b274-v15-04","title":"靜水荷載與作用點機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Hydrostatic load and lever arm mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「靜水荷載與作用點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hydrostatic load and lever arm” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把平均壓力作用在半水深會算錯力矩，漏掉背側水位又會誤判方向；使用水深平方比例估力矩會低估水位升高後的彎曲需求及地基偏心。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying average pressure at half depth gives the wrong moment, while omitted rear water can reverse the assumed direction. Scaling moment with depth squared understates bending and foundation eccentricity as water rises above the original level. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：忽略動水、土壓和結構自重，結果只是一項外荷載。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Dynamic water, earth pressure and self-weight are excluded.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水深增加一成時，防洪牆的底部水壓力矩也只增加一成。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A ten-percent increase in depth increases hydrostatic base moment by only ten percent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把平均壓力作用在半水深會算錯力矩，漏掉背側水位又會誤判方向；使用水深平方比例估力矩會低估水位升高後的彎曲需求及地基偏心。","textEn":"Applying average pressure at half depth gives the wrong moment, while omitted rear water can reverse the assumed direction. Scaling moment with depth squared understates bending and foundation eccentricity as water rises above the original level.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「靜水荷載與作用點機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Hydrostatic load and lever arm mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把平均壓力作用在半水深會算錯力矩，漏掉背側水位又會誤判方向；使用水深平方比例估力矩會低估水位升高後的彎曲需求及地基偏心。","只要揚壓總力算對，它作用在底版何處就完全不影響穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Applying average pressure at half depth gives the wrong moment, while omitted rear water can reverse the assumed direction.","Correct total uplift makes its position beneath the footing irrelevant to stability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把平均壓力作用在半水深會算錯力矩，漏掉背側水位又會誤判方向；使用水深平方比例估力矩會低估水位升高後的彎曲需求及地基偏心。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying average pressure at half depth gives the wrong moment, while omitted rear water can reverse the assumed direction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b274-v15-05","title":"底版揚壓與合力位置機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Footing uplift and resultant location mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「底版揚壓與合力位置」如何影響防洪牆基礎設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Footing uplift and resultant location” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floodwall foundation design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"底版下的孔壓可減少有效向下作用並產生額外力矩，其分布取決於排水、地層及防滲構造，不一定只由兩端水位決定。線性揚壓圖可作教學積分，但排水孔堵塞或局部缺陷可能改變形狀，因此基礎穩定需要同時保留揚壓合力和位置，不能只從自重減一個沒有作用點的總數。本例為每公尺牆長的水平底版，假設揚壓沿寬度線性由高端降到低端；不是由兩個端點自動證明的現場壓力分布。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「底版揚壓與合力位置」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pore pressure beneath a footing reduces effective downward load and contributes moment. Its distribution depends on drainage, strata and cutoffs rather than endpoint stages alone. A linear diagram is useful for integration, but blocked drains and defects can alter its shape. Stability therefore needs both uplift magnitude and location, not merely a scalar deduction from weight. This is a horizontal footing per metre of wall with assumed linear uplift from high to low edge. Two endpoint observations do not automatically prove that distribution in the field. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Footing uplift and resultant location” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設底寬B=4 m，高低端揚壓p1=30、p2=10 kPa，U=(p1+p2)B/2=80 kN/m，合力距高壓端1.667 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume width B=4 m and edge uplifts p1=30, p2=10 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要揚壓總力算對，它作用在底版何處就完全不影響穩定。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Correct total uplift makes its position beneath the footing irrelevant to stability.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「底版揚壓與合力位置」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Footing uplift and resultant location”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-05-k1","title":"底版揚壓與合力位置機理與驗證","titleEn":"Footing uplift and resultant location mechanism and verification","text":"底版下的孔壓可減少有效向下作用並產生額外力矩，其分布取決於排水、地層及防滲構造，不一定只由兩端水位決定。線性揚壓圖可作教學積分，但排水孔堵塞或局部缺陷可能改變形狀，因此基礎穩定需要同時保留揚壓合力和位置，不能只從自重減一個沒有作用點的總數。","textEn":"Pore pressure beneath a footing reduces effective downward load and contributes moment. Its distribution depends on drainage, strata and cutoffs rather than endpoint stages alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要揚壓總力算對，它作用在底版何處就完全不影響穩定。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Correct total uplift makes its position beneath the footing irrelevant to stability. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「底版揚壓與合力位置機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Footing uplift and resultant location mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["只要揚壓總力算對，它作用在底版何處就完全不影響穩定。","底版摩擦永遠由全部自重決定，地下水揚壓不會改變抗滑力。","底版下的孔壓可減少有效向下作用並產生額外力矩，其分布取決於排水、地層及防滲構造，不一定只由兩端水位決定。"],"optionsEn":["Correct total uplift makes its position beneath the footing irrelevant to stability.","Base friction always uses full self-weight and is unaffected by groundwater uplift.","Pore pressure beneath a footing reduces effective downward load and contributes moment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"底版下的孔壓可減少有效向下作用並產生額外力矩，其分布取決於排水、地層及防滲構造，不一定只由兩端水位決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pore pressure beneath a footing reduces effective downward load and contributes moment. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b274-v15-06","title":"底版揚壓與合力位置機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Footing uplift and resultant location mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「底版揚壓與合力位置」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Footing uplift and resultant location” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設底寬B=4 m，高低端揚壓p1=30、p2=10 kPa，U=(p1+p2)B/2=80 kN/m，合力距高壓端1.667 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume width B=4 m and edge uplifts p1=30, p2=10 kPa. U=(p1+p2)B/2=80 kN/m; its resultant is 1.667 m from the high-pressure edge. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把揚壓圖拆成矩形與三角形分別求合力和力矩，核對端點方向與座標。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Split the uplift diagram into rectangular and triangular parts, checking force, moment and coordinate orientation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設底寬B=4 m，高低端揚壓p1=30、p2=10 kPa，U=(p1+p2)B/2=80 kN/m，合力距高壓端1.667 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume width B=4 m and edge uplifts p1=30, p2=10 kPa. U=(p1+p2)B/2=80 kN/m; its resultant is 1.667 m from the high-pressure edge.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「底版揚壓與合力位置機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Footing uplift and resultant location mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設底寬B=4 m，高低端揚壓p1=30、p2=10 kPa，U=(p1+p2)B/2=80 kN/m，合力距高壓端1.667 m。","極限承載力就是工程可長期使用的容許壓力，不需檢查沉陷。","朗肯被動係數算出後，任何微小位移都能立即動員全部被動抗力。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume width B=4 m and edge uplifts p1=30, p2=10 kPa.","Ultimate bearing capacity is the permissible long-term service pressure without settlement checks.","Once the Rankine coefficient is calculated, any tiny displacement immediately mobilizes full passive resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設底寬B=4 m，高低端揚壓p1=30、p2=10 kPa，U=(p1+p2)B/2=80 kN/m，合力距高壓端1.667 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume width B=4 m and edge uplifts p1=30, p2=10 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b274-v15-07","title":"底版揚壓與合力位置機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Footing uplift and resultant location mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「底版揚壓與合力位置」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Footing uplift and resultant location” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把揚壓圖拆成矩形與三角形分別求合力和力矩，核對端點方向與座標。用底版下多點孔壓檢查形狀，另外分析排水失效及洪水快速變化，避免只用正常排水圖。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Split the uplift diagram into rectangular and triangular parts, checking force, moment and coordinate orientation. Compare its shape with several under-footing pressures and analyze drainage failure and rapid stage changes separately instead of carrying only the normal-drainage assumption into stability calculations. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用相同揚壓總力配置兩個不同壓力圖，計算各自對底邊力矩。列出新增中間孔壓測點能排除的假設，說明為何只量兩端仍有未解不確定性。","observationEn":"Site practice: Construct two uplift diagrams with equal force and calculate their moments about one edge. List assumptions that an intermediate pressure measurement can test and explain uncertainty remaining when only endpoint pressures are known.","failure":"注意干擾：錯置合力位置會讓抗傾覆帳失真，直接以背水側低壓套全底版則可能低估揚壓；若排水管堵塞仍沿用原圖，滑動及接觸壓力的有效載重都會過於樂觀。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A misplaced uplift resultant distorts overturning balance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把揚壓圖拆成矩形與三角形分別求合力和力矩，核對端點方向與座標。用底版下多點孔壓檢查形狀，另外分析排水失效及洪水快速變化，避免只用正常排水圖。","textEn":"Split the uplift diagram into rectangular and triangular parts, checking force, moment and coordinate orientation. Compare its shape with several under-footing pressures and analyze drainage failure and rapid stage changes separately instead of carrying only the normal-drainage assumption into stability calculations.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用相同揚壓總力配置兩個不同壓力圖，計算各自對底邊力矩。列出新增中間孔壓測點能排除的假設，說明為何只量兩端仍有未解不確定性。","textEn":"Construct two uplift diagrams with equal force and calculate their moments about one edge. List assumptions that an intermediate pressure measurement can test and explain uncertainty remaining when only endpoint pressures are known.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「底版揚壓與合力位置機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Footing uplift and resultant location mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","把揚壓圖拆成矩形與三角形分別求合力和力矩，核對端點方向與座標。","兩個高程點的沉陷斜率可直接換算止水接頭接觸壓力與水密保證。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Split the uplift diagram into rectangular and triangular parts, checking force, moment and coordinate orientation.","Settlement slope from two elevations directly gives waterstop contact pressure and guaranteed watertightness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把揚壓圖拆成矩形與三角形分別求合力和力矩，核對端點方向與座標。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Split the uplift diagram into rectangular and triangular parts, checking force, moment and coordinate orientation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b274-v15-08","title":"底版揚壓與合力位置機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Footing uplift and resultant location mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「底版揚壓與合力位置」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Footing uplift and resultant location” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"錯置合力位置會讓抗傾覆帳失真，直接以背水側低壓套全底版則可能低估揚壓；若排水管堵塞仍沿用原圖，滑動及接觸壓力的有效載重都會過於樂觀。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A misplaced uplift resultant distorts overturning balance. Applying only the low rear pressure across the base understates uplift, and retaining a drained diagram after blockage overstates the effective loads available for sliding resistance and bearing contact. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例為每公尺牆長的水平底版，假設揚壓沿寬度線性由高端降到低端；不是由兩個端點自動證明的現場壓力分布。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Two endpoint observations do not automatically prove that distribution in the field.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要揚壓總力算對，它作用在底版何處就完全不影響穩定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Correct total uplift makes its position beneath the footing irrelevant to stability.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"錯置合力位置會讓抗傾覆帳失真，直接以背水側低壓套全底版則可能低估揚壓；若排水管堵塞仍沿用原圖，滑動及接觸壓力的有效載重都會過於樂觀。","textEn":"A misplaced uplift resultant distorts overturning balance. Applying only the low rear pressure across the base understates uplift, and retaining a drained diagram after blockage overstates the effective loads available for sliding resistance and bearing contact.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「底版揚壓與合力位置機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Footing uplift and resultant location mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","底版摩擦永遠由全部自重決定，地下水揚壓不會改變抗滑力。","錯置合力位置會讓抗傾覆帳失真，直接以背水側低壓套全底版則可能低估揚壓；若排水管堵塞仍沿用原圖，滑動及接觸壓力的有效載重都會過於樂觀。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Base friction always uses full self-weight and is unaffected by groundwater uplift.","A misplaced uplift resultant distorts overturning balance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"錯置合力位置會讓抗傾覆帳失真，直接以背水側低壓套全底版則可能低估揚壓；若排水管堵塞仍沿用原圖，滑動及接觸壓力的有效載重都會過於樂觀。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A misplaced uplift resultant distorts overturning balance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b274-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「有效法向力與滑動機理與驗證」與「偏心與底面接觸機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Effective normal load and sliding mechanism and verification\" and \"Eccentricity and footing contact mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b274-v15-09","title":"有效法向力與滑動機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Effective normal load and sliding mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「有效法向力與滑動」如何影響防洪牆基礎設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective normal load and sliding” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floodwall foundation design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"底版摩擦取決於接觸面的有效法向作用，揚壓會減少可用摩擦力，不能一面以浮重計自重又重複扣除全部揚壓。界面強度、黏著與前方被動土阻力需有相應證據及可動員變形；受沖刷或未來開挖影響的土體也不能無條件當永久抗力。本例自重採未扣揚壓的總向下力，只考慮無黏著庫侖摩擦，未計土被動阻力或錨定；所得為指定機理的比值，非規範驗收。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「有效法向力與滑動」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Base friction depends on effective normal action, which uplift reduces. Weight and buoyancy conventions must avoid deducting the same water effect twice. Interface strength, adhesion and passive soil resistance require evidence and compatible mobilization movements. Soil exposed to scour or future excavation cannot automatically be credited as permanent resistance in a sliding assessment. The example starts with gross downward weight and includes cohesionless Coulomb interface friction only, excluding passive resistance and anchorage. The resulting mechanism ratio is not a code acceptance decision. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective normal load and sliding” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總向下力W=200 kN/m、揚壓U=80 kN/m、μ=0.50、水平H=40 kN/m，R=μ(W−U)=60 kN/m，R/H=1.50。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gross W=200 kN/m, uplift U=80 kN/m, friction μ=0.50 and horizontal H=40 kN/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「底版摩擦永遠由全部自重決定，地下水揚壓不會改變抗滑力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Base friction always uses full self-weight and is unaffected by groundwater uplift.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「有效法向力與滑動」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective normal load and sliding”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-09-k1","title":"有效法向力與滑動機理與驗證","titleEn":"Effective normal load and sliding mechanism and verification","text":"底版摩擦取決於接觸面的有效法向作用，揚壓會減少可用摩擦力，不能一面以浮重計自重又重複扣除全部揚壓。界面強度、黏著與前方被動土阻力需有相應證據及可動員變形；受沖刷或未來開挖影響的土體也不能無條件當永久抗力。","textEn":"Base friction depends on effective normal action, which uplift reduces. Weight and buoyancy conventions must avoid deducting the same water effect twice.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：底版摩擦永遠由全部自重決定，地下水揚壓不會改變抗滑力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Base friction always uses full self-weight and is unaffected by groundwater uplift. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「有效法向力與滑動機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Effective normal load and sliding mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["底版摩擦取決於接觸面的有效法向作用，揚壓會減少可用摩擦力，不能一面以浮重計自重又重複扣除全部揚壓。","底版摩擦永遠由全部自重決定，地下水揚壓不會改變抗滑力。","底面最小壓力大於零，就足以證明承載、沉陷與牆身強度全都合格。"],"optionsEn":["Base friction depends on effective normal action, which uplift reduces.","Base friction always uses full self-weight and is unaffected by groundwater uplift.","Positive minimum footing pressure proves bearing, settlement and wall strength all acceptable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"底版摩擦取決於接觸面的有效法向作用，揚壓會減少可用摩擦力，不能一面以浮重計自重又重複扣除全部揚壓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Base friction depends on effective normal action, which uplift reduces. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b274-v15-10","title":"有效法向力與滑動機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Effective normal load and sliding mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「有效法向力與滑動」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective normal load and sliding” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總向下力W=200 kN/m、揚壓U=80 kN/m、μ=0.50、水平H=40 kN/m，R=μ(W−U)=60 kN/m，R/H=1.50。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gross W=200 kN/m, uplift U=80 kN/m, friction μ=0.50 and horizontal H=40 kN/m. Resistance R=60 kN/m and ratio R/H=1.50. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對重量與揚壓是否採相容定義，檢查界面試驗、粗糙度與施工接觸條件。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check consistent weight/uplift definitions and evidence for interface behavior, roughness and construction contact.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總向下力W=200 kN/m、揚壓U=80 kN/m、μ=0.50、水平H=40 kN/m，R=μ(W−U)=60 kN/m，R/H=1.50。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gross W=200 kN/m, uplift U=80 kN/m, friction μ=0.50 and horizontal H=40 kN/m. Resistance R=60 kN/m and ratio R/H=1.50.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「有效法向力與滑動機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Effective normal load and sliding mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["計算得到小的瞬時彈性沉陷，就能排除所有長期接頭變形。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總向下力W=200 kN/m、揚壓U=80 kN/m、μ=0.50、水平H=40 kN/m，R=μ(W−U)=60 kN/m，R/H=1.50。","防滲牆越深時，所有位置的孔壓與出口梯度必定同時降低。"],"optionsEn":["Small calculated instantaneous elastic settlement excludes every long-term joint movement problem.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gross W=200 kN/m, uplift U=80 kN/m, friction μ=0.50 and horizontal H=40 kN/m.","A deeper cutoff necessarily lowers pore pressure and exit gradient at every location."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總向下力W=200 kN/m、揚壓U=80 kN/m、μ=0.50、水平H=40 kN/m，R=μ(W−U)=60 kN/m，R/H=1.50。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gross W=200 kN/m, uplift U=80 kN/m, friction μ=0.50 and horizontal H=40 kN/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b274-v15-11","title":"有效法向力與滑動機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Effective normal load and sliding mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「有效法向力與滑動」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective normal load and sliding” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對重量與揚壓是否採相容定義，檢查界面試驗、粗糙度與施工接觸條件。列明未採用的黏著和被動抗力，另考慮沖刷、排水失效及反向荷載，不把計算比值直接標示合格。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check consistent weight/uplift definitions and evidence for interface behavior, roughness and construction contact. Identify excluded adhesion and passive resistance, and assess scour, failed drainage and reversed loading separately rather than treating a computed resistance ratio as an automatic compliance result. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用同一牆重比較兩種揚壓的抗滑比，清楚列出未採用的抗力。再移除前方可能沖刷的土體，說明為何抗力必須符合相同荷載情境與變形條件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare sliding ratios at two uplifts for the same wall weight, identifying excluded resistances. Remove potentially scoured front soil and explain why resistance must correspond to the same load case and compatible movement conditions.","failure":"注意干擾：用總自重計摩擦而忽略揚壓會高估抗力，將浮重再減全揚壓則可能重複扣水效應；把會被沖走的土算成永久被動抗力，也會隱藏失去支承後的滑動風險。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using gross weight for friction ignores uplift, while subtracting full uplift from an already buoyant weight can double-count water. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對重量與揚壓是否採相容定義，檢查界面試驗、粗糙度與施工接觸條件。列明未採用的黏著和被動抗力，另考慮沖刷、排水失效及反向荷載，不把計算比值直接標示合格。","textEn":"Check consistent weight/uplift definitions and evidence for interface behavior, roughness and construction contact. Identify excluded adhesion and passive resistance, and assess scour, failed drainage and reversed loading separately rather than treating a computed resistance ratio as an automatic compliance result.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用同一牆重比較兩種揚壓的抗滑比，清楚列出未採用的抗力。再移除前方可能沖刷的土體，說明為何抗力必須符合相同荷載情境與變形條件。","textEn":"Compare sliding ratios at two uplifts for the same wall weight, identifying excluded resistances. Remove potentially scoured front soil and explain why resistance must correspond to the same load case and compatible movement conditions.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「有效法向力與滑動機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Effective normal load and sliding mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","外河水位一旦下降，防洪牆受到的所有荷載與風險就必定同步減少。","核對重量與揚壓是否採相容定義，檢查界面試驗、粗糙度與施工接觸條件。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Once river stage falls, every floodwall load and failure risk necessarily decreases together.","Check consistent weight/uplift definitions and evidence for interface behavior, roughness and construction contact."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對重量與揚壓是否採相容定義，檢查界面試驗、粗糙度與施工接觸條件。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check consistent weight/uplift definitions and evidence for interface behavior, roughness and construction contact. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b274-v15-12","title":"有效法向力與滑動機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Effective normal load and sliding mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「有效法向力與滑動」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective normal load and sliding” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用總自重計摩擦而忽略揚壓會高估抗力，將浮重再減全揚壓則可能重複扣水效應；把會被沖走的土算成永久被動抗力，也會隱藏失去支承後的滑動風險。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using gross weight for friction ignores uplift, while subtracting full uplift from an already buoyant weight can double-count water. Crediting scour-prone soil as permanent passive resistance hides the change in sliding response after support is lost. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例自重採未扣揚壓的總向下力，只考慮無黏著庫侖摩擦，未計土被動阻力或錨定；所得為指定機理的比值，非規範驗收。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The resulting mechanism ratio is not a code acceptance decision.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「底版摩擦永遠由全部自重決定，地下水揚壓不會改變抗滑力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Base friction always uses full self-weight and is unaffected by groundwater uplift.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用總自重計摩擦而忽略揚壓會高估抗力，將浮重再減全揚壓則可能重複扣水效應；把會被沖走的土算成永久被動抗力，也會隱藏失去支承後的滑動風險。","textEn":"Using gross weight for friction ignores uplift, while subtracting full uplift from an already buoyant weight can double-count water. Crediting scour-prone soil as permanent passive resistance hides the change in sliding response after support is lost.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「有效法向力與滑動機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Effective normal load and sliding mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用總自重計摩擦而忽略揚壓會高估抗力，將浮重再減全揚壓則可能重複扣水效應；把會被沖走的土算成永久被動抗力，也會隱藏失去支承後的滑動風險。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","底面最小壓力大於零，就足以證明承載、沉陷與牆身強度全都合格。"],"optionsEn":["Using gross weight for friction ignores uplift, while subtracting full uplift from an already buoyant weight can double-count water.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Positive minimum footing pressure proves bearing, settlement and wall strength all acceptable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用總自重計摩擦而忽略揚壓會高估抗力，將浮重再減全揚壓則可能重複扣水效應；把會被沖走的土算成永久被動抗力，也會隱藏失去支承後的滑動風險。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using gross weight for friction ignores uplift, while subtracting full uplift from an already buoyant weight can double-count water. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b274-v15-13","title":"偏心與底面接觸機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Eccentricity and footing contact mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「偏心與底面接觸」如何影響防洪牆基礎設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Eccentricity and footing contact” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floodwall foundation design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"合力偏離底版中心會使接觸壓力一側升高另一側降低，在剛性底版與線彈性全接觸近似下可由軸力和力矩估算邊緣壓力。當計算出拉應力時，土通常不能提供所假設的拉力，須改用部分接觸模型；全接觸公式的負值不是可忽略的小數，而是模型邊界已改變的訊號。本例所有載重已含水力效應，N為有效淨向下力、M為對中心的淨力矩，每公尺牆長計。只檢查全接觸線性壓力，不評定承載強度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「偏心與底面接觸」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An eccentric resultant raises contact stress at one edge and lowers it at the other. A rigid footing with linear full contact permits edge stresses from axial force and moment. Calculated tension usually cannot be sustained by soil, requiring a partial-contact model. A negative full-contact stress signals a changed boundary rather than a harmless numerical artifact. All hydraulic effects are included: N is net effective downward action and M its net moment about the center, per metre of wall. This checks linear full contact only, not bearing strength. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Eccentricity and footing contact” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設B=4 m、N=120 kN/m、M=60 kN·m/m，e=M/N=0.50 m；qmax,min=N/B(1±6e/B)=52.5、7.5 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume B=4 m, N=120 kN/m and M=60 kN·m/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「底面最小壓力大於零，就足以證明承載、沉陷與牆身強度全都合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Positive minimum footing pressure proves bearing, settlement and wall strength all acceptable.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「偏心與底面接觸」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Eccentricity and footing contact”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-13-k1","title":"偏心與底面接觸機理與驗證","titleEn":"Eccentricity and footing contact mechanism and verification","text":"合力偏離底版中心會使接觸壓力一側升高另一側降低，在剛性底版與線彈性全接觸近似下可由軸力和力矩估算邊緣壓力。當計算出拉應力時，土通常不能提供所假設的拉力，須改用部分接觸模型；全接觸公式的負值不是可忽略的小數，而是模型邊界已改變的訊號。","textEn":"An eccentric resultant raises contact stress at one edge and lowers it at the other. A rigid footing with linear full contact permits edge stresses from axial force and moment.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：底面最小壓力大於零，就足以證明承載、沉陷與牆身強度全都合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Positive minimum footing pressure proves bearing, settlement and wall strength all acceptable. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「偏心與底面接觸機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Eccentricity and footing contact mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["底面最小壓力大於零，就足以證明承載、沉陷與牆身強度全都合格。","合力偏離底版中心會使接觸壓力一側升高另一側降低，在剛性底版與線彈性全接觸近似下可由軸力和力矩估算邊緣壓力。","極限承載力就是工程可長期使用的容許壓力，不需檢查沉陷。"],"optionsEn":["Positive minimum footing pressure proves bearing, settlement and wall strength all acceptable.","An eccentric resultant raises contact stress at one edge and lowers it at the other.","Ultimate bearing capacity is the permissible long-term service pressure without settlement checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"合力偏離底版中心會使接觸壓力一側升高另一側降低，在剛性底版與線彈性全接觸近似下可由軸力和力矩估算邊緣壓力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An eccentric resultant raises contact stress at one edge and lowers it at the other. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b274-v15-14","title":"偏心與底面接觸機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Eccentricity and footing contact mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「偏心與底面接觸」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Eccentricity and footing contact” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設B=4 m、N=120 kN/m、M=60 kN·m/m，e=M/N=0.50 m；qmax,min=N/B(1±6e/B)=52.5、7.5 kPa。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume B=4 m, N=120 kN/m and M=60 kN·m/m. Eccentricity e=0.50 m; full-contact edge pressures are qmax=52.5 and qmin=7.5 kPa. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以一致中心座標加總所有力矩，核對偏心距與B/6的全壓接觸界限。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sum moments about a consistent center and compare eccentricity with the B/6 full-compression limit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設B=4 m、N=120 kN/m、M=60 kN·m/m，e=M/N=0.50 m；qmax,min=N/B(1±6e/B)=52.5、7.5 kPa。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume B=4 m, N=120 kN/m and M=60 kN·m/m. Eccentricity e=0.50 m; full-contact edge pressures are qmax=52.5 and qmin=7.5 kPa.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「偏心與底面接觸機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Eccentricity and footing contact mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["朗肯被動係數算出後，任何微小位移都能立即動員全部被動抗力。","兩個高程點的沉陷斜率可直接換算止水接頭接觸壓力與水密保證。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設B=4 m、N=120 kN/m、M=60 kN·m/m，e=M/N=0.50 m。"],"optionsEn":["Once the Rankine coefficient is calculated, any tiny displacement immediately mobilizes full passive resistance.","Settlement slope from two elevations directly gives waterstop contact pressure and guaranteed watertightness.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume B=4 m, N=120 kN/m and M=60 kN·m/m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設B=4 m、N=120 kN/m、M=60 kN·m/m，e=M/N=0.50 m；qmax,min=N/B(1±6e/B)=52.5、7.5 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume B=4 m, N=120 kN/m and M=60 kN·m/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b274-v15-15","title":"偏心與底面接觸機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Eccentricity and footing contact mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「偏心與底面接觸」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Eccentricity and footing contact” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以一致中心座標加總所有力矩，核對偏心距與B/6的全壓接觸界限。檢查底版剛度、地層均勻性和壓力分布假設，再另做承載、沉陷及結構驗算，避免把正壓力當全面安全。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sum moments about a consistent center and compare eccentricity with the B/6 full-compression limit. Check footing rigidity, soil uniformity and the assumed pressure distribution, then assess bearing, settlement and structural response separately instead of interpreting positive contact stress as comprehensive safety. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：逐步增加中心力矩，找出最小接觸壓力變成零的點並停止全接觸外推。列出此後需要的接觸幾何與地基資訊，區分壓力分布和承載強度問題。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase center moment until minimum contact stress reaches zero and stop full-contact extrapolation. List the contact geometry and soil information needed afterward, distinguishing stress-distribution questions from soil bearing-strength questions.","failure":"注意干擾：把外水水平力矩與揚壓力矩漏算或重算會改變偏心，使用部分接觸時仍保留全寬線性壓力則可能低估峰值；正的最小壓力也不能證明地基承載或沉陷足夠。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitted or duplicated water moments alter eccentricity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以一致中心座標加總所有力矩，核對偏心距與B/6的全壓接觸界限。檢查底版剛度、地層均勻性和壓力分布假設，再另做承載、沉陷及結構驗算，避免把正壓力當全面安全。","textEn":"Sum moments about a consistent center and compare eccentricity with the B/6 full-compression limit. Check footing rigidity, soil uniformity and the assumed pressure distribution, then assess bearing, settlement and structural response separately instead of interpreting positive contact stress as comprehensive safety.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"逐步增加中心力矩，找出最小接觸壓力變成零的點並停止全接觸外推。列出此後需要的接觸幾何與地基資訊，區分壓力分布和承載強度問題。","textEn":"Increase center moment until minimum contact stress reaches zero and stop full-contact extrapolation. List the contact geometry and soil information needed afterward, distinguishing stress-distribution questions from soil bearing-strength questions.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「偏心與底面接觸機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Eccentricity and footing contact mechanism and verification\"?","options":["以一致中心座標加總所有力矩，核對偏心距與B/6的全壓接觸界限。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","水深增加一成時，防洪牆的底部水壓力矩也只增加一成。"],"optionsEn":["Sum moments about a consistent center and compare eccentricity with the B/6 full-compression limit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A ten-percent increase in depth increases hydrostatic base moment by only ten percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以一致中心座標加總所有力矩，核對偏心距與B/6的全壓接觸界限。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sum moments about a consistent center and compare eccentricity with the B/6 full-compression limit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b274-v15-16","title":"偏心與底面接觸機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Eccentricity and footing contact mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「偏心與底面接觸」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Eccentricity and footing contact” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把外水水平力矩與揚壓力矩漏算或重算會改變偏心，使用部分接觸時仍保留全寬線性壓力則可能低估峰值；正的最小壓力也不能證明地基承載或沉陷足夠。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitted or duplicated water moments alter eccentricity. Retaining a full-width pressure model after contact is lost can understate peak stress, while a positive minimum stress says nothing by itself about bearing capacity or acceptable settlement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只檢查全接觸線性壓力，不評定承載強度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This checks linear full contact only, not bearing strength.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「底面最小壓力大於零，就足以證明承載、沉陷與牆身強度全都合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Positive minimum footing pressure proves bearing, settlement and wall strength all acceptable.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把外水水平力矩與揚壓力矩漏算或重算會改變偏心，使用部分接觸時仍保留全寬線性壓力則可能低估峰值；正的最小壓力也不能證明地基承載或沉陷足夠。","textEn":"Omitted or duplicated water moments alter eccentricity. Retaining a full-width pressure model after contact is lost can understate peak stress, while a positive minimum stress says nothing by itself about bearing capacity or acceptable settlement.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「偏心與底面接觸機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Eccentricity and footing contact mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把外水水平力矩與揚壓力矩漏算或重算會改變偏心，使用部分接觸時仍保留全寬線性壓力則可能低估峰值；正的最小壓力也不能證明地基承載或沉陷足夠。","極限承載力就是工程可長期使用的容許壓力，不需檢查沉陷。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Omitted or duplicated water moments alter eccentricity.","Ultimate bearing capacity is the permissible long-term service pressure without settlement checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把外水水平力矩與揚壓力矩漏算或重算會改變偏心，使用部分接觸時仍保留全寬線性壓力則可能低估峰值；正的最小壓力也不能證明地基承載或沉陷足夠。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitted or duplicated water moments alter eccentricity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b274-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「黏土承載模式篩選機理與驗證」與「基礎彈性變形尺度機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Undrained clay bearing screening mechanism and verification\" and \"Elastic foundation deformation scale mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b274-v15-17","title":"黏土承載模式篩選機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Undrained clay bearing screening mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「黏土承載模式篩選」如何影響防洪牆基礎設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Undrained clay bearing screening” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floodwall foundation design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"地基承載破壞與正常使用沉陷不同，短期飽和黏土可在特定幾何下以不排水強度建立承載尺度。承載係數會隨形狀、埋深、荷載傾斜、地面坡度與土層變化，不能將無埋深條形基礎的簡式套所有防洪牆；偏心和揚壓還必須先以相容方式納入作用。本例水平地面、地表無限長條形基礎、均質不排水黏土及垂直置中荷載，取理想Nc=5.14；是淨極限承載力，不是容許壓力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「黏土承載模式篩選」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Bearing failure differs from service settlement. Short-term saturated clay can provide an undrained bearing scale under specific geometry. Coefficients vary with shape, embedment, load inclination, ground slope and layering, so a surface strip-footing expression is not universal for floodwalls. Eccentricity and uplift also require compatible treatment in the applied actions. The example assumes level ground, a surface strip footing, uniform undrained clay and centered vertical loading with ideal Nc=5.14. It gives net ultimate bearing capacity, not allowable pressure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Undrained clay bearing screening” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設不排水強度su=40 kPa、Nc=5.14，淨極限承載力qnet,ult=Ncsu=205.6 kPa；未施安全係數或折減。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume undrained strength su=40 kPa and Nc=5.14.","failure":"常見誤解：「極限承載力就是工程可長期使用的容許壓力，不需檢查沉陷。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Ultimate bearing capacity is the permissible long-term service pressure without settlement checks.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「黏土承載模式篩選」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Undrained clay bearing screening”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-17-k1","title":"黏土承載模式篩選機理與驗證","titleEn":"Undrained clay bearing screening mechanism and verification","text":"地基承載破壞與正常使用沉陷不同，短期飽和黏土可在特定幾何下以不排水強度建立承載尺度。承載係數會隨形狀、埋深、荷載傾斜、地面坡度與土層變化，不能將無埋深條形基礎的簡式套所有防洪牆；偏心和揚壓還必須先以相容方式納入作用。","textEn":"Bearing failure differs from service settlement. Short-term saturated clay can provide an undrained bearing scale under specific geometry.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：極限承載力就是工程可長期使用的容許壓力，不需檢查沉陷。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Ultimate bearing capacity is the permissible long-term service pressure without settlement checks. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「黏土承載模式篩選機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Undrained clay bearing screening mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["極限承載力就是工程可長期使用的容許壓力，不需檢查沉陷。","計算得到小的瞬時彈性沉陷，就能排除所有長期接頭變形。","地基承載破壞與正常使用沉陷不同，短期飽和黏土可在特定幾何下以不排水強度建立承載尺度。"],"optionsEn":["Ultimate bearing capacity is the permissible long-term service pressure without settlement checks.","Small calculated instantaneous elastic settlement excludes every long-term joint movement problem.","Bearing failure differs from service settlement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"地基承載破壞與正常使用沉陷不同，短期飽和黏土可在特定幾何下以不排水強度建立承載尺度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Bearing failure differs from service settlement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b274-v15-18","title":"黏土承載模式篩選機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Undrained clay bearing screening mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「黏土承載模式篩選」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Undrained clay bearing screening” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設不排水強度su=40 kPa、Nc=5.14，淨極限承載力qnet,ult=Ncsu=205.6 kPa；未施安全係數或折減。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume undrained strength su=40 kPa and Nc=5.14. Ideal net ultimate bearing qnet,ult=Ncsu=205.6 kPa, before any safety factor or reduction. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：檢查強度測試的應力路徑、取樣擾動及地層代表性，辨識短期與長期排水狀態。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check the strength-test stress path, sample disturbance and representativeness and distinguish short-term from long-term drainage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設不排水強度su=40 kPa、Nc=5.14，淨極限承載力qnet,ult=Ncsu=205.6 kPa；未施安全係數或折減。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume undrained strength su=40 kPa and Nc=5.14. Ideal net ultimate bearing qnet,ult=Ncsu=205.6 kPa, before any safety factor or reduction.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「黏土承載模式篩選機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Undrained clay bearing screening mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設不排水強度su=40 kPa、Nc=5.14，淨極限承載力qnet,ult=Ncsu=205.6 kPa。","防滲牆越深時，所有位置的孔壓與出口梯度必定同時降低。","外河水位一旦下降，防洪牆受到的所有荷載與風險就必定同步減少。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume undrained strength su=40 kPa and Nc=5.14.","A deeper cutoff necessarily lowers pore pressure and exit gradient at every location.","Once river stage falls, every floodwall load and failure risk necessarily decreases together."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設不排水強度su=40 kPa、Nc=5.14，淨極限承載力qnet,ult=Ncsu=205.6 kPa；未施安全係數或折減。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume undrained strength su=40 kPa and Nc=5.14. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b274-v15-19","title":"黏土承載模式篩選機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Undrained clay bearing screening mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「黏土承載模式篩選」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Undrained clay bearing screening” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"檢查強度測試的應力路徑、取樣擾動及地層代表性，辨識短期與長期排水狀態。若偏心、傾斜或分層不符簡式，改用相應模型；再獨立驗算沉陷，不能把極限承載值當使用壓力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check the strength-test stress path, sample disturbance and representativeness and distinguish short-term from long-term drainage. Replace the simple expression where eccentricity, inclination or layering violate assumptions, and independently assess settlement rather than using ultimate capacity as a service-pressure recommendation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立淨壓力與總壓力的對照，再列出條形基礎簡式缺少的幾何修正。提出能辨識軟弱下層的調查配置，並說明強度資料為何不能獨自決定使用性。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare net and gross pressure definitions and list geometric corrections missing from the strip-footing expression. Propose investigation capable of finding a weak lower layer and explain why strength data cannot alone establish serviceability.","failure":"注意干擾：把淨極限承載力直接與未整理的總壓力相比會混淆定義，軟弱下臥層也可能控制破壞；即使承載強度有餘量，長期壓密仍可能使接縫和止水失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Comparing net ultimate capacity with an inconsistent gross stress confuses definitions, and a weak underlying layer may control failure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"檢查強度測試的應力路徑、取樣擾動及地層代表性，辨識短期與長期排水狀態。若偏心、傾斜或分層不符簡式，改用相應模型；再獨立驗算沉陷，不能把極限承載值當使用壓力。","textEn":"Check the strength-test stress path, sample disturbance and representativeness and distinguish short-term from long-term drainage. Replace the simple expression where eccentricity, inclination or layering violate assumptions, and independently assess settlement rather than using ultimate capacity as a service-pressure recommendation.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立淨壓力與總壓力的對照，再列出條形基礎簡式缺少的幾何修正。提出能辨識軟弱下層的調查配置，並說明強度資料為何不能獨自決定使用性。","textEn":"Compare net and gross pressure definitions and list geometric corrections missing from the strip-footing expression. Propose investigation capable of finding a weak lower layer and explain why strength data cannot alone establish serviceability.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「黏土承載模式篩選機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Undrained clay bearing screening mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","檢查強度測試的應力路徑、取樣擾動及地層代表性，辨識短期與長期排水狀態。","只要揚壓總力算對，它作用在底版何處就完全不影響穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check the strength-test stress path, sample disturbance and representativeness and distinguish short-term from long-term drainage.","Correct total uplift makes its position beneath the footing irrelevant to stability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"檢查強度測試的應力路徑、取樣擾動及地層代表性，辨識短期與長期排水狀態。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check the strength-test stress path, sample disturbance and representativeness and distinguish short-term from long-term drainage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b274-v15-20","title":"黏土承載模式篩選機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Undrained clay bearing screening mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「黏土承載模式篩選」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Undrained clay bearing screening” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把淨極限承載力直接與未整理的總壓力相比會混淆定義，軟弱下臥層也可能控制破壞；即使承載強度有餘量，長期壓密仍可能使接縫和止水失效。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Comparing net ultimate capacity with an inconsistent gross stress confuses definitions, and a weak underlying layer may control failure. Even with bearing-strength reserve, long-term consolidation can impair wall joints and waterstops through differential movement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例水平地面、地表無限長條形基礎、均質不排水黏土及垂直置中荷載，取理想Nc=5.14；是淨極限承載力，不是容許壓力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It gives net ultimate bearing capacity, not allowable pressure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「極限承載力就是工程可長期使用的容許壓力，不需檢查沉陷。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Ultimate bearing capacity is the permissible long-term service pressure without settlement checks.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把淨極限承載力直接與未整理的總壓力相比會混淆定義，軟弱下臥層也可能控制破壞；即使承載強度有餘量，長期壓密仍可能使接縫和止水失效。","textEn":"Comparing net ultimate capacity with an inconsistent gross stress confuses definitions, and a weak underlying layer may control failure. Even with bearing-strength reserve, long-term consolidation can impair wall joints and waterstops through differential movement.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「黏土承載模式篩選機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Undrained clay bearing screening mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","計算得到小的瞬時彈性沉陷，就能排除所有長期接頭變形。","把淨極限承載力直接與未整理的總壓力相比會混淆定義，軟弱下臥層也可能控制破壞；即使承載強度有餘量，長期壓密仍可能使接縫和止水失效。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Small calculated instantaneous elastic settlement excludes every long-term joint movement problem.","Comparing net ultimate capacity with an inconsistent gross stress confuses definitions, and a weak underlying layer may control failure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把淨極限承載力直接與未整理的總壓力相比會混淆定義，軟弱下臥層也可能控制破壞；即使承載強度有餘量，長期壓密仍可能使接縫和止水失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Comparing net ultimate capacity with an inconsistent gross stress confuses definitions, and a weak underlying layer may control failure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b274-v15-21","title":"基礎彈性變形尺度機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Elastic foundation deformation scale mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「基礎彈性變形尺度」如何影響防洪牆基礎設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Elastic foundation deformation scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floodwall foundation design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"牆基即使未達承載破壞也會變形，沉陷差可能使板段接頭張開或頂高失去餘量。彈性半空間公式可展示壓力、寬度與剛度的比例關係，但土模數與應力水準、排水時間及應變大小有關；形狀係數亦取決於基礎與取點，因此估算尺度不能冒充完整分層沉陷分析。本例明定理想彈性均質半空間及指定影響係數，不含一次壓密與次壓縮。模數以千帕一致代入，結果僅是此理想模型的位移尺度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「基礎彈性變形尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A foundation deforms before bearing failure, and differential settlement can open joints or reduce crest margin. Elastic half-space relations show scaling with pressure, width and stiffness, but soil modulus depends on stress level, drainage time and strain. Shape factors also depend on footing geometry and evaluation point, so a scale estimate cannot substitute for layered settlement analysis. The example specifies a uniform elastic half-space and assigned influence factor, excluding primary and secondary consolidation. Modulus is converted consistently to kilopascals; displacement belongs only to this idealized model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Elastic foundation deformation scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設q=50 kPa、B=4 m、ν=0.30、E=20,000 kPa、影響係數I=1.0，s=qB(1−ν²)I/E=0.00910 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume q=50 kPa, B=4 m, Poisson ratio ν=0.30, E=20,000 kPa and influence I=1.0.","failure":"常見誤解：「計算得到小的瞬時彈性沉陷，就能排除所有長期接頭變形。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Small calculated instantaneous elastic settlement excludes every long-term joint movement problem.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「基礎彈性變形尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Elastic foundation deformation scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-21-k1","title":"基礎彈性變形尺度機理與驗證","titleEn":"Elastic foundation deformation scale mechanism and verification","text":"牆基即使未達承載破壞也會變形，沉陷差可能使板段接頭張開或頂高失去餘量。彈性半空間公式可展示壓力、寬度與剛度的比例關係，但土模數與應力水準、排水時間及應變大小有關；形狀係數亦取決於基礎與取點，因此估算尺度不能冒充完整分層沉陷分析。","textEn":"A foundation deforms before bearing failure, and differential settlement can open joints or reduce crest margin. Elastic half-space relations show scaling with pressure, width and stiffness, but soil modulus depends on stress level, drainage time and strain.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：計算得到小的瞬時彈性沉陷，就能排除所有長期接頭變形。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Small calculated instantaneous elastic settlement excludes every long-term joint movement problem. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基礎彈性變形尺度機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Elastic foundation deformation scale mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["牆基即使未達承載破壞也會變形，沉陷差可能使板段接頭張開或頂高失去餘量。","計算得到小的瞬時彈性沉陷，就能排除所有長期接頭變形。","朗肯被動係數算出後，任何微小位移都能立即動員全部被動抗力。"],"optionsEn":["A foundation deforms before bearing failure, and differential settlement can open joints or reduce crest margin.","Small calculated instantaneous elastic settlement excludes every long-term joint movement problem.","Once the Rankine coefficient is calculated, any tiny displacement immediately mobilizes full passive resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"牆基即使未達承載破壞也會變形，沉陷差可能使板段接頭張開或頂高失去餘量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A foundation deforms before bearing failure, and differential settlement can open joints or reduce crest margin. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b274-v15-22","title":"基礎彈性變形尺度機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Elastic foundation deformation scale mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「基礎彈性變形尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Elastic foundation deformation scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設q=50 kPa、B=4 m、ν=0.30、E=20,000 kPa、影響係數I=1.0，s=qB(1−ν²)I/E=0.00910 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume q=50 kPa, B=4 m, Poisson ratio ν=0.30, E=20,000 kPa and influence I=1.0. Elastic displacement scale s=0.00910 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：確認所用模數和影響係數對應相同排水、應變及基礎條件，另查軟弱層厚度與時間效應。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Confirm modulus and influence factor match drainage, strain and footing conditions, then investigate weak-layer thickness and time effects separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設q=50 kPa、B=4 m、ν=0.30、E=20,000 kPa、影響係數I=1.0，s=qB(1−ν²)I/E=0.00910 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume q=50 kPa, B=4 m, Poisson ratio ν=0.30, E=20,000 kPa and influence I=1.0. Elastic displacement scale s=0.00910 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基礎彈性變形尺度機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Elastic foundation deformation scale mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["兩個高程點的沉陷斜率可直接換算止水接頭接觸壓力與水密保證。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設q=50 kPa、B=4 m、ν=0.30、E=20,000 kPa、影響係數I=1.0，s=qB(1−ν²)I/E=0.00910 m。","水深增加一成時，防洪牆的底部水壓力矩也只增加一成。"],"optionsEn":["Settlement slope from two elevations directly gives waterstop contact pressure and guaranteed watertightness.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume q=50 kPa, B=4 m, Poisson ratio ν=0.30, E=20,000 kPa and influence I=1.0.","A ten-percent increase in depth increases hydrostatic base moment by only ten percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設q=50 kPa、B=4 m、ν=0.30、E=20,000 kPa、影響係數I=1.0，s=qB(1−ν²)I/E=0.00910 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume q=50 kPa, B=4 m, Poisson ratio ν=0.30, E=20,000 kPa and influence I=1.0. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b274-v15-23","title":"基礎彈性變形尺度機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Elastic foundation deformation scale mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「基礎彈性變形尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Elastic foundation deformation scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"確認所用模數和影響係數對應相同排水、應變及基礎條件，另查軟弱層厚度與時間效應。以分段高程觀測比較相對沉陷，核對是否有剛體傾斜，再評估接頭可容許變位。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Confirm modulus and influence factor match drainage, strain and footing conditions, then investigate weak-layer thickness and time effects separately. Compare relative settlements from segment elevations, distinguish rigid-body tilt and assess joint movement capacity rather than relying only on one predicted absolute displacement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將模數減半而保持其餘條件不變，重算理想位移並列出未包含的時間效應。用相鄰牆段高程分開計算平均下沉和差異位移，避免混淆兩種使用性問題。","observationEn":"Site practice: Halve modulus with other assumptions fixed and recalculate elastic displacement, listing omitted time effects. Use adjacent segment elevations to separate average settlement from relative movement rather than confusing the two serviceability concerns.","failure":"注意干擾：把兆帕未換單位就與千帕荷載相除會產生千倍誤差，任選形狀係數也會使精度虛假；以瞬時彈性結果代表多年沉陷，則漏掉可能控制止水接頭的壓密差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Dividing kilopascal loading by an unconverted megapascal modulus creates a thousand-fold error. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"確認所用模數和影響係數對應相同排水、應變及基礎條件，另查軟弱層厚度與時間效應。以分段高程觀測比較相對沉陷，核對是否有剛體傾斜，再評估接頭可容許變位。","textEn":"Confirm modulus and influence factor match drainage, strain and footing conditions, then investigate weak-layer thickness and time effects separately. Compare relative settlements from segment elevations, distinguish rigid-body tilt and assess joint movement capacity rather than relying only on one predicted absolute displacement.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將模數減半而保持其餘條件不變，重算理想位移並列出未包含的時間效應。用相鄰牆段高程分開計算平均下沉和差異位移，避免混淆兩種使用性問題。","textEn":"Halve modulus with other assumptions fixed and recalculate elastic displacement, listing omitted time effects. Use adjacent segment elevations to separate average settlement from relative movement rather than confusing the two serviceability concerns.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基礎彈性變形尺度機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Elastic foundation deformation scale mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","底版摩擦永遠由全部自重決定，地下水揚壓不會改變抗滑力。","確認所用模數和影響係數對應相同排水、應變及基礎條件，另查軟弱層厚度與時間效應。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Base friction always uses full self-weight and is unaffected by groundwater uplift.","Confirm modulus and influence factor match drainage, strain and footing conditions, then investigate weak-layer thickness and time effects separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"確認所用模數和影響係數對應相同排水、應變及基礎條件，另查軟弱層厚度與時間效應。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Confirm modulus and influence factor match drainage, strain and footing conditions, then investigate weak-layer thickness and time effects separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b274-v15-24","title":"基礎彈性變形尺度機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Elastic foundation deformation scale mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「基礎彈性變形尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Elastic foundation deformation scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把兆帕未換單位就與千帕荷載相除會產生千倍誤差，任選形狀係數也會使精度虛假；以瞬時彈性結果代表多年沉陷，則漏掉可能控制止水接頭的壓密差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Dividing kilopascal loading by an unconverted megapascal modulus creates a thousand-fold error. An arbitrary shape factor implies false precision, and treating instantaneous elasticity as years of settlement omits consolidation differences that can control waterstop performance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：模數以千帕一致代入，結果僅是此理想模型的位移尺度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Modulus is converted consistently to kilopascals; displacement belongs only to this idealized model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「計算得到小的瞬時彈性沉陷，就能排除所有長期接頭變形。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Small calculated instantaneous elastic settlement excludes every long-term joint movement problem.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把兆帕未換單位就與千帕荷載相除會產生千倍誤差，任選形狀係數也會使精度虛假；以瞬時彈性結果代表多年沉陷，則漏掉可能控制止水接頭的壓密差。","textEn":"Dividing kilopascal loading by an unconverted megapascal modulus creates a thousand-fold error. An arbitrary shape factor implies false precision, and treating instantaneous elasticity as years of settlement omits consolidation differences that can control waterstop performance.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基礎彈性變形尺度機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Elastic foundation deformation scale mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把兆帕未換單位就與千帕荷載相除會產生千倍誤差，任選形狀係數也會使精度虛假；以瞬時彈性結果代表多年沉陷，則漏掉可能控制止水接頭的壓密差。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","朗肯被動係數算出後，任何微小位移都能立即動員全部被動抗力。"],"optionsEn":["Dividing kilopascal loading by an unconverted megapascal modulus creates a thousand-fold error.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Once the Rankine coefficient is calculated, any tiny displacement immediately mobilizes full passive resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把兆帕未換單位就與千帕荷載相除會產生千倍誤差，任選形狀係數也會使精度虛假；以瞬時彈性結果代表多年沉陷，則漏掉可能控制止水接頭的壓密差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Dividing kilopascal loading by an unconverted megapascal modulus creates a thousand-fold error. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b274-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「被動土壓與可動員變形機理與驗證」與「截水深度與滲透方向機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Passive pressure and mobilization mechanism and verification\" and \"Cutoff depth and seepage direction mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b274-v15-25","title":"被動土壓與可動員變形機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Passive pressure and mobilization mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「被動土壓與可動員變形」如何影響防洪牆基礎設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Passive pressure and mobilization” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floodwall foundation design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"基礎前方土體可提供被動阻力，但充分動員通常需要位移，並受土面坡度、牆土摩擦和應力歷史影響。理想朗肯係數只適用特定無摩擦垂直面與水平地面，並非所有鋼板樁或剪力榫的抗力；前方沖刷與開挖還可能移除可用土體，需和牆的容許變形共同判斷。本例只算無黏乾砂、水平面、光滑直牆的理想係數，未算總抗力，也未宣稱已達被動狀態；飽和土需一致有效應力處理。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「被動土壓與可動員變形」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Soil ahead of a foundation can provide passive resistance, but full mobilization requires movement and depends on ground slope, interface friction and stress history. The ideal Rankine coefficient applies to a smooth vertical interface and level ground, not every sheet pile or shear key. Scour and excavation can remove the resisting soil, linking resistance to allowable wall movement. The example computes only an ideal coefficient for cohesionless dry sand, level ground and a smooth vertical wall. It neither gives total resistance nor establishes mobilization; saturated soil needs consistent effective-stress treatment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Passive pressure and mobilization” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設有效摩擦角φ′=30°，理想朗肯被動係數Kp=tan²(45°+φ′/2)=3.00，無單位。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective friction angle φ′=30°.","failure":"常見誤解：「朗肯被動係數算出後，任何微小位移都能立即動員全部被動抗力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once the Rankine coefficient is calculated, any tiny displacement immediately mobilizes full passive resistance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「被動土壓與可動員變形」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Passive pressure and mobilization”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-25-k1","title":"被動土壓與可動員變形機理與驗證","titleEn":"Passive pressure and mobilization mechanism and verification","text":"基礎前方土體可提供被動阻力，但充分動員通常需要位移，並受土面坡度、牆土摩擦和應力歷史影響。理想朗肯係數只適用特定無摩擦垂直面與水平地面，並非所有鋼板樁或剪力榫的抗力；前方沖刷與開挖還可能移除可用土體，需和牆的容許變形共同判斷。","textEn":"Soil ahead of a foundation can provide passive resistance, but full mobilization requires movement and depends on ground slope, interface friction and stress history. The ideal Rankine coefficient applies to a smooth vertical interface and level ground, not every sheet pile or shear key.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：朗肯被動係數算出後，任何微小位移都能立即動員全部被動抗力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once the Rankine coefficient is calculated, any tiny displacement immediately mobilizes full passive resistance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「被動土壓與可動員變形機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Passive pressure and mobilization mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["朗肯被動係數算出後，任何微小位移都能立即動員全部被動抗力。","基礎前方土體可提供被動阻力，但充分動員通常需要位移，並受土面坡度、牆土摩擦和應力歷史影響。","防滲牆越深時，所有位置的孔壓與出口梯度必定同時降低。"],"optionsEn":["Once the Rankine coefficient is calculated, any tiny displacement immediately mobilizes full passive resistance.","Soil ahead of a foundation can provide passive resistance, but full mobilization requires movement and depends on ground slope, interface friction and stress history.","A deeper cutoff necessarily lowers pore pressure and exit gradient at every location."],"answer":1,"explanation":"基礎前方土體可提供被動阻力，但充分動員通常需要位移，並受土面坡度、牆土摩擦和應力歷史影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Soil ahead of a foundation can provide passive resistance, but full mobilization requires movement and depends on ground slope, interface friction and stress history. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b274-v15-26","title":"被動土壓與可動員變形機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Passive pressure and mobilization mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「被動土壓與可動員變形」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Passive pressure and mobilization” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設有效摩擦角φ′=30°，理想朗肯被動係數Kp=tan²(45°+φ′/2)=3.00，無單位。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective friction angle φ′=30°. Ideal Rankine passive coefficient Kp=tan²(45°+φ′/2)=3.00, dimensionless, without a total-resistance claim. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對土面幾何、界面與地下水，列出需要動員被動阻力的方向及位移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check ground geometry, interface and groundwater, identifying the movement needed to mobilize passive resistance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設有效摩擦角φ′=30°，理想朗肯被動係數Kp=tan²(45°+φ′/2)=3.00，無單位。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective friction angle φ′=30°. Ideal Rankine passive coefficient Kp=tan²(45°+φ′/2)=3.00, dimensionless, without a total-resistance claim.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「被動土壓與可動員變形機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Passive pressure and mobilization mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["外河水位一旦下降，防洪牆受到的所有荷載與風險就必定同步減少。","只要揚壓總力算對，它作用在底版何處就完全不影響穩定。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設有效摩擦角φ′=30°，理想朗肯被動係數Kp=tan²(45°+φ′/2)=3.00，無單位。"],"optionsEn":["Once river stage falls, every floodwall load and failure risk necessarily decreases together.","Correct total uplift makes its position beneath the footing irrelevant to stability.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective friction angle φ′=30°."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設有效摩擦角φ′=30°，理想朗肯被動係數Kp=tan²(45°+φ′/2)=3.00，無單位。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective friction angle φ′=30°. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b274-v15-27","title":"被動土壓與可動員變形機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Passive pressure and mobilization mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「被動土壓與可動員變形」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Passive pressure and mobilization” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對土面幾何、界面與地下水，列出需要動員被動阻力的方向及位移。檢查前方土是否可能沖走、開挖或受管線擾動，再使用適合邊界的模型並與結構可接受變形比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check ground geometry, interface and groundwater, identifying the movement needed to mobilize passive resistance. Assess whether front soil can be scoured, excavated or disturbed by utilities, then choose a boundary-compatible model and compare its required deformation with structural serviceability limits. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分別畫出未變形、局部動員與被動極限三種狀態，列出同一係數不能回答的問題。移除一層前方土後重新界定埋深，說明調查與維護介面的重要性。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw undeformed, partially mobilized and limiting passive states and list questions that one coefficient cannot answer. Remove a front-soil layer, redefine embedment and explain the investigation and maintenance implications of that changed geometry.","failure":"注意干擾：只要看到土在牆前就全額計入被動阻力，可能在小變形下高估抗力；漏掉未來開挖或沖刷情境，則讓原本依賴該土體的抗滑結果失去實體基礎。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Crediting full passive resistance merely because soil exists ahead of the wall can overstate resistance at small movements. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對土面幾何、界面與地下水，列出需要動員被動阻力的方向及位移。檢查前方土是否可能沖走、開挖或受管線擾動，再使用適合邊界的模型並與結構可接受變形比較。","textEn":"Check ground geometry, interface and groundwater, identifying the movement needed to mobilize passive resistance. Assess whether front soil can be scoured, excavated or disturbed by utilities, then choose a boundary-compatible model and compare its required deformation with structural serviceability limits.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分別畫出未變形、局部動員與被動極限三種狀態，列出同一係數不能回答的問題。移除一層前方土後重新界定埋深，說明調查與維護介面的重要性。","textEn":"Draw undeformed, partially mobilized and limiting passive states and list questions that one coefficient cannot answer. Remove a front-soil layer, redefine embedment and explain the investigation and maintenance implications of that changed geometry.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「被動土壓與可動員變形機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Passive pressure and mobilization mechanism and verification\"?","options":["核對土面幾何、界面與地下水，列出需要動員被動阻力的方向及位移。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","底面最小壓力大於零，就足以證明承載、沉陷與牆身強度全都合格。"],"optionsEn":["Check ground geometry, interface and groundwater, identifying the movement needed to mobilize passive resistance.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Positive minimum footing pressure proves bearing, settlement and wall strength all acceptable."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對土面幾何、界面與地下水，列出需要動員被動阻力的方向及位移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check ground geometry, interface and groundwater, identifying the movement needed to mobilize passive resistance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b274-v15-28","title":"被動土壓與可動員變形機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Passive pressure and mobilization mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「被動土壓與可動員變形」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Passive pressure and mobilization” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只要看到土在牆前就全額計入被動阻力，可能在小變形下高估抗力；漏掉未來開挖或沖刷情境，則讓原本依賴該土體的抗滑結果失去實體基礎。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Crediting full passive resistance merely because soil exists ahead of the wall can overstate resistance at small movements. Omitting future excavation or scour allows a sliding calculation to depend on material that may no longer be present. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例只算無黏乾砂、水平面、光滑直牆的理想係數，未算總抗力，也未宣稱已達被動狀態；飽和土需一致有效應力處理。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It neither gives total resistance nor establishes mobilization; saturated soil needs consistent effective-stress treatment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「朗肯被動係數算出後，任何微小位移都能立即動員全部被動抗力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once the Rankine coefficient is calculated, any tiny displacement immediately mobilizes full passive resistance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只要看到土在牆前就全額計入被動阻力，可能在小變形下高估抗力；漏掉未來開挖或沖刷情境，則讓原本依賴該土體的抗滑結果失去實體基礎。","textEn":"Crediting full passive resistance merely because soil exists ahead of the wall can overstate resistance at small movements. Omitting future excavation or scour allows a sliding calculation to depend on material that may no longer be present.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「被動土壓與可動員變形機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Passive pressure and mobilization mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只要看到土在牆前就全額計入被動阻力，可能在小變形下高估抗力；漏掉未來開挖或沖刷情境，則讓原本依賴該土體的抗滑結果失去實體基礎。","防滲牆越深時，所有位置的孔壓與出口梯度必定同時降低。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Crediting full passive resistance merely because soil exists ahead of the wall can overstate resistance at small movements.","A deeper cutoff necessarily lowers pore pressure and exit gradient at every location."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只要看到土在牆前就全額計入被動阻力，可能在小變形下高估抗力；漏掉未來開挖或沖刷情境，則讓原本依賴該土體的抗滑結果失去實體基礎。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Crediting full passive resistance merely because soil exists ahead of the wall can overstate resistance at small movements. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b274-v15-29","title":"截水深度與滲透方向機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cutoff depth and seepage direction mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「截水深度與滲透方向」如何影響防洪牆基礎設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cutoff depth and seepage direction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floodwall foundation design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"牆基防滲構造不只減漏，也會改變底版揚壓和出口位置，深度增加可能使流路轉移至較深透水層。以均質流徑延長估算只表示水力阻抗尺度，實際需考慮二維或三維流線、層間異向性及牆尖梯度；總漏水下降不一定表示所有局部孔壓同步下降。本例使用指定長度的固定截面飽和一維路徑，水頭差與滲透係數不變。延長流路不是把實際牆深直接代入，也不提供出口侵蝕判定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「截水深度與滲透方向」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Foundation cutoffs reduce leakage but also redistribute uplift and exit locations; greater depth can redirect flow into deeper permeable strata. A lengthened uniform path gives only a resistance scale. Actual analysis needs two- or three-dimensional flow, anisotropic layers and tip gradients, because lower total discharge does not necessarily lower every local pore pressure. This example uses an assigned saturated one-dimensional path of constant area, head difference and conductivity. Path extension is not actual wall depth substituted directly, and it gives no exit-erosion acceptance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cutoff depth and seepage direction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設k=2×10⁻⁶ m/s、A=10 m²、Δh=4 m、L=20 m，Q=kAΔh/L=4×10⁻⁶ m³/s；路徑40 m時為2×10⁻⁶ m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume k=2×10⁻⁶ m/s, A=10 m², Δh=4 m and L=20 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「防滲牆越深時，所有位置的孔壓與出口梯度必定同時降低。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A deeper cutoff necessarily lowers pore pressure and exit gradient at every location.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「截水深度與滲透方向」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cutoff depth and seepage direction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-29-k1","title":"截水深度與滲透方向機理與驗證","titleEn":"Cutoff depth and seepage direction mechanism and verification","text":"牆基防滲構造不只減漏，也會改變底版揚壓和出口位置，深度增加可能使流路轉移至較深透水層。以均質流徑延長估算只表示水力阻抗尺度，實際需考慮二維或三維流線、層間異向性及牆尖梯度；總漏水下降不一定表示所有局部孔壓同步下降。","textEn":"Foundation cutoffs reduce leakage but also redistribute uplift and exit locations; greater depth can redirect flow into deeper permeable strata. A lengthened uniform path gives only a resistance scale.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：防滲牆越深時，所有位置的孔壓與出口梯度必定同時降低。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A deeper cutoff necessarily lowers pore pressure and exit gradient at every location. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「截水深度與滲透方向機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cutoff depth and seepage direction mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["防滲牆越深時，所有位置的孔壓與出口梯度必定同時降低。","兩個高程點的沉陷斜率可直接換算止水接頭接觸壓力與水密保證。","牆基防滲構造不只減漏，也會改變底版揚壓和出口位置，深度增加可能使流路轉移至較深透水層。"],"optionsEn":["A deeper cutoff necessarily lowers pore pressure and exit gradient at every location.","Settlement slope from two elevations directly gives waterstop contact pressure and guaranteed watertightness.","Foundation cutoffs reduce leakage but also redistribute uplift and exit locations; greater depth can redirect flow into deeper permeable strata."],"answer":2,"explanation":"牆基防滲構造不只減漏，也會改變底版揚壓和出口位置，深度增加可能使流路轉移至較深透水層。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Foundation cutoffs reduce leakage but also redistribute uplift and exit locations; greater depth can redirect flow into deeper permeable strata. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b274-v15-30","title":"截水深度與滲透方向機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Cutoff depth and seepage direction mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「截水深度與滲透方向」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cutoff depth and seepage direction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設k=2×10⁻⁶ m/s、A=10 m²、Δh=4 m、L=20 m，Q=kAΔh/L=4×10⁻⁶ m³/s；路徑40 m時為2×10⁻⁶ m³/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume k=2×10⁻⁶ m/s, A=10 m², Δh=4 m and L=20 m. Q=4×10⁻⁶ m³/s; increasing the ideal path to 40 m halves it. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在剖面標出地層、牆尖、排水與總水頭邊界，檢查是否存在繞流或高透水夾層。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map layers, cutoff tip, drains and total-head boundaries and inspect bypass and permeable interlayers.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設k=2×10⁻⁶ m/s、A=10 m²、Δh=4 m、L=20 m，Q=kAΔh/L=4×10⁻⁶ m³/s；路徑40 m時為2×10⁻⁶ m³/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume k=2×10⁻⁶ m/s, A=10 m², Δh=4 m and L=20 m. Q=4×10⁻⁶ m³/s; increasing the ideal path to 40 m halves it.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「截水深度與滲透方向機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cutoff depth and seepage direction mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設k=2×10⁻⁶ m/s、A=10 m²、Δh=4 m、L=20 m，Q=kAΔh/L=4×10⁻⁶ m³/s。","水深增加一成時，防洪牆的底部水壓力矩也只增加一成。","底版摩擦永遠由全部自重決定，地下水揚壓不會改變抗滑力。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume k=2×10⁻⁶ m/s, A=10 m², Δh=4 m and L=20 m.","A ten-percent increase in depth increases hydrostatic base moment by only ten percent.","Base friction always uses full self-weight and is unaffected by groundwater uplift."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設k=2×10⁻⁶ m/s、A=10 m²、Δh=4 m、L=20 m，Q=kAΔh/L=4×10⁻⁶ m³/s；路徑40 m時為2×10⁻⁶ m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume k=2×10⁻⁶ m/s, A=10 m², Δh=4 m and L=20 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b274-v15-31","title":"截水深度與滲透方向機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cutoff depth and seepage direction mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「截水深度與滲透方向」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cutoff depth and seepage direction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在剖面標出地層、牆尖、排水與總水頭邊界，檢查是否存在繞流或高透水夾層。比較有無防滲構造時的揚壓分布及局部出口梯度，用實測孔壓和流量共同驗證而非只看漏水總數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map layers, cutoff tip, drains and total-head boundaries and inspect bypass and permeable interlayers. Compare uplift distributions and local exit gradients with and without the cutoff, validating against both measured pressure and discharge rather than total leakage alone as the performance metric. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對一維模型改變流長，另外畫一條繞牆尖的替代路徑。列出需要二維分析才能比較的孔壓位置，說明流量減半不等於每一處梯度減半。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change path length in the one-dimensional model and draw a separate route around the cutoff tip. Identify pressure locations needing two-dimensional analysis and explain why halved discharge does not imply halved gradient everywhere.","failure":"注意干擾：把牆深誤當全部流徑會扭曲流量，忽略透水夾層可能低估繞流；如果只根據總漏水變小宣稱穩定改善，就可能漏掉牆尖或出口附近集中的不利梯度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating cutoff depth as the entire flow path distorts discharge, and an omitted permeable layer understates bypass. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在剖面標出地層、牆尖、排水與總水頭邊界，檢查是否存在繞流或高透水夾層。比較有無防滲構造時的揚壓分布及局部出口梯度，用實測孔壓和流量共同驗證而非只看漏水總數。","textEn":"Map layers, cutoff tip, drains and total-head boundaries and inspect bypass and permeable interlayers. Compare uplift distributions and local exit gradients with and without the cutoff, validating against both measured pressure and discharge rather than total leakage alone as the performance metric.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對一維模型改變流長，另外畫一條繞牆尖的替代路徑。列出需要二維分析才能比較的孔壓位置，說明流量減半不等於每一處梯度減半。","textEn":"Change path length in the one-dimensional model and draw a separate route around the cutoff tip. Identify pressure locations needing two-dimensional analysis and explain why halved discharge does not imply halved gradient everywhere.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「截水深度與滲透方向機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cutoff depth and seepage direction mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在剖面標出地層、牆尖、排水與總水頭邊界，檢查是否存在繞流或高透水夾層。","極限承載力就是工程可長期使用的容許壓力，不需檢查沉陷。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Map layers, cutoff tip, drains and total-head boundaries and inspect bypass and permeable interlayers.","Ultimate bearing capacity is the permissible long-term service pressure without settlement checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在剖面標出地層、牆尖、排水與總水頭邊界，檢查是否存在繞流或高透水夾層。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map layers, cutoff tip, drains and total-head boundaries and inspect bypass and permeable interlayers. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b274-v15-32","title":"截水深度與滲透方向機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cutoff depth and seepage direction mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「截水深度與滲透方向」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cutoff depth and seepage direction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把牆深誤當全部流徑會扭曲流量，忽略透水夾層可能低估繞流；如果只根據總漏水變小宣稱穩定改善，就可能漏掉牆尖或出口附近集中的不利梯度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating cutoff depth as the entire flow path distorts discharge, and an omitted permeable layer understates bypass. Claiming improved stability solely from reduced leakage can miss adverse gradients concentrated near a cutoff tip or exit. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：延長流路不是把實際牆深直接代入，也不提供出口侵蝕判定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Path extension is not actual wall depth substituted directly, and it gives no exit-erosion acceptance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「防滲牆越深時，所有位置的孔壓與出口梯度必定同時降低。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A deeper cutoff necessarily lowers pore pressure and exit gradient at every location.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把牆深誤當全部流徑會扭曲流量，忽略透水夾層可能低估繞流；如果只根據總漏水變小宣稱穩定改善，就可能漏掉牆尖或出口附近集中的不利梯度。","textEn":"Treating cutoff depth as the entire flow path distorts discharge, and an omitted permeable layer understates bypass. Claiming improved stability solely from reduced leakage can miss adverse gradients concentrated near a cutoff tip or exit.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「截水深度與滲透方向機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cutoff depth and seepage direction mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","兩個高程點的沉陷斜率可直接換算止水接頭接觸壓力與水密保證。","把牆深誤當全部流徑會扭曲流量，忽略透水夾層可能低估繞流；如果只根據總漏水變小宣稱穩定改善，就可能漏掉牆尖或出口附近集中的不利梯度。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Settlement slope from two elevations directly gives waterstop contact pressure and guaranteed watertightness.","Treating cutoff depth as the entire flow path distorts discharge, and an omitted permeable layer understates bypass."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把牆深誤當全部流徑會扭曲流量，忽略透水夾層可能低估繞流；如果只根據總漏水變小宣稱穩定改善，就可能漏掉牆尖或出口附近集中的不利梯度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating cutoff depth as the entire flow path distorts discharge, and an omitted permeable layer understates bypass. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b274-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「差異沉陷與止水接頭機理與驗證」與「退水與反向荷載情境機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Differential movement and waterstops mechanism and verification\" and \"Recession and reversed loading mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b274-v15-33","title":"差異沉陷與止水接頭機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Differential movement and waterstops mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「差異沉陷與止水接頭」如何影響防洪牆基礎設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Differential movement and waterstops” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floodwall foundation design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"相鄰牆段的位移差會改變止水材料與接頭幾何，整段平均沉陷很小仍可能在轉折或地層變化處集中變形。以兩測點高差除距離只能得到平均沉陷斜率，未扣剛體轉動時不能直接叫構件角變形；接頭還可能受到開口、剪移和轉角的組合作用，需要與可驗證的材料容許值比較。本例僅為兩點高差的幾何平均斜率，未分解牆段剛體傾斜或局部曲率；不能單憑這個比值計算止水接觸壓力或證明水密。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「差異沉陷與止水接頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Relative movement between wall segments changes waterstop and joint geometry, and a small average settlement can conceal concentration at bends or layer transitions. Elevation difference divided by spacing gives a mean settlement slope, not automatically component angular distortion before removing rigid-body rotation. Joints also experience combined opening, shear and rotation that require validated material capacities. This is only the geometric mean slope between two points, without separation of rigid-body tilt or local curvature. It cannot calculate waterstop contact pressure or establish watertightness. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Differential movement and waterstops” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩測點沉陷s1=8 mm、s2=20 mm、間距L=6 m，平均沉陷斜率Δs/L=0.012/6=0.002 m/m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume settlements s1=8 mm and s2=20 mm separated by L=6 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩個高程點的沉陷斜率可直接換算止水接頭接觸壓力與水密保證。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Settlement slope from two elevations directly gives waterstop contact pressure and guaranteed watertightness.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「差異沉陷與止水接頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Differential movement and waterstops”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-33-k1","title":"差異沉陷與止水接頭機理與驗證","titleEn":"Differential movement and waterstops mechanism and verification","text":"相鄰牆段的位移差會改變止水材料與接頭幾何，整段平均沉陷很小仍可能在轉折或地層變化處集中變形。以兩測點高差除距離只能得到平均沉陷斜率，未扣剛體轉動時不能直接叫構件角變形；接頭還可能受到開口、剪移和轉角的組合作用，需要與可驗證的材料容許值比較。","textEn":"Relative movement between wall segments changes waterstop and joint geometry, and a small average settlement can conceal concentration at bends or layer transitions. Elevation difference divided by spacing gives a mean settlement slope, not automatically component angular distortion before removing rigid-body rotation.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩個高程點的沉陷斜率可直接換算止水接頭接觸壓力與水密保證。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Settlement slope from two elevations directly gives waterstop contact pressure and guaranteed watertightness. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「差異沉陷與止水接頭機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Differential movement and waterstops mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["相鄰牆段的位移差會改變止水材料與接頭幾何，整段平均沉陷很小仍可能在轉折或地層變化處集中變形。","兩個高程點的沉陷斜率可直接換算止水接頭接觸壓力與水密保證。","外河水位一旦下降，防洪牆受到的所有荷載與風險就必定同步減少。"],"optionsEn":["Relative movement between wall segments changes waterstop and joint geometry, and a small average settlement can conceal concentration at bends or layer transitions.","Settlement slope from two elevations directly gives waterstop contact pressure and guaranteed watertightness.","Once river stage falls, every floodwall load and failure risk necessarily decreases together."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相鄰牆段的位移差會改變止水材料與接頭幾何，整段平均沉陷很小仍可能在轉折或地層變化處集中變形。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Relative movement between wall segments changes waterstop and joint geometry, and a small average settlement can conceal concentration at bends or layer transitions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b274-v15-34","title":"差異沉陷與止水接頭機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Differential movement and waterstops mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「差異沉陷與止水接頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Differential movement and waterstops” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩測點沉陷s1=8 mm、s2=20 mm、間距L=6 m，平均沉陷斜率Δs/L=0.012/6=0.002 m/m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume settlements s1=8 mm and s2=20 mm separated by L=6 m. Mean settlement slope Δs/L=0.012/6=0.002 m/m, without a waterstop-capacity claim. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：統一測點高程基準與時間，增加牆段內測點以區分整體傾斜與彎曲。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align survey datum and time and add points within segments to distinguish tilt from curvature.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩測點沉陷s1=8 mm、s2=20 mm、間距L=6 m，平均沉陷斜率Δs/L=0.012/6=0.002 m/m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume settlements s1=8 mm and s2=20 mm separated by L=6 m. Mean settlement slope Δs/L=0.012/6=0.002 m/m, without a waterstop-capacity claim.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「差異沉陷與止水接頭機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Differential movement and waterstops mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["只要揚壓總力算對，它作用在底版何處就完全不影響穩定。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩測點沉陷s1=8 mm、s2=20 mm、間距L=6 m，平均沉陷斜率Δs/L=0.012/6=0.002 m/m。","底面最小壓力大於零，就足以證明承載、沉陷與牆身強度全都合格。"],"optionsEn":["Correct total uplift makes its position beneath the footing irrelevant to stability.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume settlements s1=8 mm and s2=20 mm separated by L=6 m.","Positive minimum footing pressure proves bearing, settlement and wall strength all acceptable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩測點沉陷s1=8 mm、s2=20 mm、間距L=6 m，平均沉陷斜率Δs/L=0.012/6=0.002 m/m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume settlements s1=8 mm and s2=20 mm separated by L=6 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b274-v15-35","title":"差異沉陷與止水接頭機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Differential movement and waterstops mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「差異沉陷與止水接頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Differential movement and waterstops” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"統一測點高程基準與時間，增加牆段內測點以區分整體傾斜與彎曲。量測接頭開口和剪移，取得止水材料在相應溫度、老化與壓差下的性能資料，並以適當漏水測試核對。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align survey datum and time and add points within segments to distinguish tilt from curvature. Measure opening and shear and obtain waterstop performance at relevant temperature, aging and pressure difference, checking with appropriate leakage tests rather than inferring sealing behavior from two elevations. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用三個以上測點分解一個假設的剛體傾斜與局部相對變形，另列開口與剪移。說明仍須哪些材料曲線與漏水試驗，才能連結幾何量測和止水性能。","observationEn":"Site practice: Use at least three points to separate a hypothetical rigid tilt from local relative movement, listing opening and shear independently. Explain which material curves and leakage tests are still required to connect geometry with sealing performance.","failure":"注意干擾：將平均斜率當全部接頭轉角可能錯配性能試驗，忽略剪移和開口組合也會漏掉止水失效；只用目視無裂縫判斷水密，則無法確認隱藏止水材料或接續完整。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating mean slope as the entire joint rotation misapplies performance tests, while ignoring combined shear and opening misses seal failure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"統一測點高程基準與時間，增加牆段內測點以區分整體傾斜與彎曲。量測接頭開口和剪移，取得止水材料在相應溫度、老化與壓差下的性能資料，並以適當漏水測試核對。","textEn":"Align survey datum and time and add points within segments to distinguish tilt from curvature. Measure opening and shear and obtain waterstop performance at relevant temperature, aging and pressure difference, checking with appropriate leakage tests rather than inferring sealing behavior from two elevations.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用三個以上測點分解一個假設的剛體傾斜與局部相對變形，另列開口與剪移。說明仍須哪些材料曲線與漏水試驗，才能連結幾何量測和止水性能。","textEn":"Use at least three points to separate a hypothetical rigid tilt from local relative movement, listing opening and shear independently. Explain which material curves and leakage tests are still required to connect geometry with sealing performance.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「差異沉陷與止水接頭機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Differential movement and waterstops mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","計算得到小的瞬時彈性沉陷，就能排除所有長期接頭變形。","統一測點高程基準與時間，增加牆段內測點以區分整體傾斜與彎曲。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Small calculated instantaneous elastic settlement excludes every long-term joint movement problem.","Align survey datum and time and add points within segments to distinguish tilt from curvature."],"answer":2,"explanation":"統一測點高程基準與時間，增加牆段內測點以區分整體傾斜與彎曲。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align survey datum and time and add points within segments to distinguish tilt from curvature. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b274-v15-36","title":"差異沉陷與止水接頭機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Differential movement and waterstops mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「差異沉陷與止水接頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Differential movement and waterstops” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將平均斜率當全部接頭轉角可能錯配性能試驗，忽略剪移和開口組合也會漏掉止水失效；只用目視無裂縫判斷水密，則無法確認隱藏止水材料或接續完整。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating mean slope as the entire joint rotation misapplies performance tests, while ignoring combined shear and opening misses seal failure. No visible crack does not confirm the integrity of hidden waterstops, connections or their response under pressure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例僅為兩點高差的幾何平均斜率，未分解牆段剛體傾斜或局部曲率；不能單憑這個比值計算止水接觸壓力或證明水密。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It cannot calculate waterstop contact pressure or establish watertightness.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩個高程點的沉陷斜率可直接換算止水接頭接觸壓力與水密保證。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Settlement slope from two elevations directly gives waterstop contact pressure and guaranteed watertightness.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將平均斜率當全部接頭轉角可能錯配性能試驗，忽略剪移和開口組合也會漏掉止水失效；只用目視無裂縫判斷水密，則無法確認隱藏止水材料或接續完整。","textEn":"Treating mean slope as the entire joint rotation misapplies performance tests, while ignoring combined shear and opening misses seal failure. No visible crack does not confirm the integrity of hidden waterstops, connections or their response under pressure.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「差異沉陷與止水接頭機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Differential movement and waterstops mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["將平均斜率當全部接頭轉角可能錯配性能試驗，忽略剪移和開口組合也會漏掉止水失效；只用目視無裂縫判斷水密，則無法確認隱藏止水材料或接續完整。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","外河水位一旦下降，防洪牆受到的所有荷載與風險就必定同步減少。"],"optionsEn":["Treating mean slope as the entire joint rotation misapplies performance tests, while ignoring combined shear and opening misses seal failure.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Once river stage falls, every floodwall load and failure risk necessarily decreases together."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將平均斜率當全部接頭轉角可能錯配性能試驗，忽略剪移和開口組合也會漏掉止水失效；只用目視無裂縫判斷水密，則無法確認隱藏止水材料或接續完整。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating mean slope as the entire joint rotation misapplies performance tests, while ignoring combined shear and opening misses seal failure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b274-v15-37","title":"退水與反向荷載情境機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Recession and reversed loading mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「退水與反向荷載情境」如何影響防洪牆基礎設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Recession and reversed loading” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Floodwall foundation design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"洪水退去後，背側積水或地基孔壓可能尚未消散，原本抵抗外河水的牆會遇到不同方向或分布的作用。水位變化、抽排和排水堵塞應以時間一致的荷載組合處理，不能把各自最大值任意拼湊也不能只檢查最高河水位；反向荷載還可能動員不同界面及接觸區域。本例兩側直牆水深由同一底面量起，取外河向背側為正，僅相減兩個靜水合力；未包含基底揚壓或土壓。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「退水與反向荷載情境」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After river recession, retained water or foundation pressure may persist, changing the direction and distribution of wall loads. Stage change, pumping and blocked drainage need time-consistent combinations, neither arbitrary combinations of unrelated maxima nor only peak river stage. Reversed loading may also mobilize different interfaces, contacts and structural reinforcement than the original forward case. Depths on both vertical faces share the same base, with river-to-landward force positive. The example subtracts two hydrostatic resultants only, excluding base uplift and earth pressure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Recession and reversed loading” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設γw=9.81 kN/m³，外河水深ho=0.5 m、背側hi=1.5 m，淨力F=γw(ho²−hi²)/2=−9.81 kN/m，方向朝河。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume γw=9.81 kN/m³, river depth ho=0.5 m and rear depth hi=1.5 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「外河水位一旦下降，防洪牆受到的所有荷載與風險就必定同步減少。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once river stage falls, every floodwall load and failure risk necessarily decreases together.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「退水與反向荷載情境」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Recession and reversed loading”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-37-k1","title":"退水與反向荷載情境機理與驗證","titleEn":"Recession and reversed loading mechanism and verification","text":"洪水退去後，背側積水或地基孔壓可能尚未消散，原本抵抗外河水的牆會遇到不同方向或分布的作用。水位變化、抽排和排水堵塞應以時間一致的荷載組合處理，不能把各自最大值任意拼湊也不能只檢查最高河水位；反向荷載還可能動員不同界面及接觸區域。","textEn":"After river recession, retained water or foundation pressure may persist, changing the direction and distribution of wall loads. Stage change, pumping and blocked drainage need time-consistent combinations, neither arbitrary combinations of unrelated maxima nor only peak river stage.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：外河水位一旦下降，防洪牆受到的所有荷載與風險就必定同步減少。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once river stage falls, every floodwall load and failure risk necessarily decreases together. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「退水與反向荷載情境機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Recession and reversed loading mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["外河水位一旦下降，防洪牆受到的所有荷載與風險就必定同步減少。","洪水退去後，背側積水或地基孔壓可能尚未消散，原本抵抗外河水的牆會遇到不同方向或分布的作用。","水深增加一成時，防洪牆的底部水壓力矩也只增加一成。"],"optionsEn":["Once river stage falls, every floodwall load and failure risk necessarily decreases together.","After river recession, retained water or foundation pressure may persist, changing the direction and distribution of wall loads.","A ten-percent increase in depth increases hydrostatic base moment by only ten percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"洪水退去後，背側積水或地基孔壓可能尚未消散，原本抵抗外河水的牆會遇到不同方向或分布的作用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After river recession, retained water or foundation pressure may persist, changing the direction and distribution of wall loads. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b274-v15-38","title":"退水與反向荷載情境機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Recession and reversed loading mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「退水與反向荷載情境」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Recession and reversed loading” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設γw=9.81 kN/m³，外河水深ho=0.5 m、背側hi=1.5 m，淨力F=γw(ho²−hi²)/2=−9.81 kN/m，方向朝河。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume γw=9.81 kN/m³, river depth ho=0.5 m and rear depth hi=1.5 m. Net F=γw(ho²−hi²)/2=−9.81 kN/m, directed riverward. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將兩側水位、孔壓與泵站狀態畫在同一時間軸，檢查洪峰、退水及抽排失效。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot both stages, pore pressure and pump state on one time axis and examine peak, recession and pumping failure.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設γw=9.81 kN/m³，外河水深ho=0.5 m、背側hi=1.5 m，淨力F=γw(ho²−hi²)/2=−9.81 kN/m，方向朝河。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume γw=9.81 kN/m³, river depth ho=0.5 m and rear depth hi=1.5 m. Net F=γw(ho²−hi²)/2=−9.81 kN/m, directed riverward.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「退水與反向荷載情境機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Recession and reversed loading mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["底版摩擦永遠由全部自重決定，地下水揚壓不會改變抗滑力。","極限承載力就是工程可長期使用的容許壓力，不需檢查沉陷。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設γw=9.81 kN/m³，外河水深ho=0.5 m、背側hi=1.5 m，淨力F=γw(ho²−hi²)/2=−9.81 kN/m，方向朝河。"],"optionsEn":["Base friction always uses full self-weight and is unaffected by groundwater uplift.","Ultimate bearing capacity is the permissible long-term service pressure without settlement checks.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume γw=9.81 kN/m³, river depth ho=0.5 m and rear depth hi=1.5 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設γw=9.81 kN/m³，外河水深ho=0.5 m、背側hi=1.5 m，淨力F=γw(ho²−hi²)/2=−9.81 kN/m，方向朝河。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume γw=9.81 kN/m³, river depth ho=0.5 m and rear depth hi=1.5 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b274-v15-39","title":"退水與反向荷載情境機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Recession and reversed loading mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「退水與反向荷載情境」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Recession and reversed loading” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將兩側水位、孔壓與泵站狀態畫在同一時間軸，檢查洪峰、退水及抽排失效。明列正負方向和不同作用點，追蹤反向彎矩與接觸區變化，再檢查止水和排水是否可在兩向壓差下運作。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot both stages, pore pressure and pump state on one time axis and examine peak, recession and pumping failure. State signs and lever arms, trace reversed moments and changing contact regions and check whether seals and drainage can function under pressure differences in both directions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立河水先降而背水暫留的三個時點，逐一計算淨力方向。另畫可能延遲的底版孔壓，說明需要時間相容荷載而不能只挑最高河水位。","observationEn":"Site practice: Create three times with falling river water and temporarily retained rear water, calculating force direction at each. Sketch delayed footing pressures and explain why time-consistent loads are needed instead of choosing only the maximum river stage.","failure":"注意干擾：只以外河最高水位驗算會漏掉退水後背側水壓，直接用水深差平方又抹掉兩側共同底面幾何；忽略孔壓消散較慢也會使基礎有效載重的時程不合理。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Checking only peak river stage misses rear water during recession. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將兩側水位、孔壓與泵站狀態畫在同一時間軸，檢查洪峰、退水及抽排失效。明列正負方向和不同作用點，追蹤反向彎矩與接觸區變化，再檢查止水和排水是否可在兩向壓差下運作。","textEn":"Plot both stages, pore pressure and pump state on one time axis and examine peak, recession and pumping failure. State signs and lever arms, trace reversed moments and changing contact regions and check whether seals and drainage can function under pressure differences in both directions.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立河水先降而背水暫留的三個時點，逐一計算淨力方向。另畫可能延遲的底版孔壓，說明需要時間相容荷載而不能只挑最高河水位。","textEn":"Create three times with falling river water and temporarily retained rear water, calculating force direction at each. Sketch delayed footing pressures and explain why time-consistent loads are needed instead of choosing only the maximum river stage.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「退水與反向荷載情境機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Recession and reversed loading mechanism and verification\"?","options":["將兩側水位、孔壓與泵站狀態畫在同一時間軸，檢查洪峰、退水及抽排失效。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","朗肯被動係數算出後，任何微小位移都能立即動員全部被動抗力。"],"optionsEn":["Plot both stages, pore pressure and pump state on one time axis and examine peak, recession and pumping failure.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Once the Rankine coefficient is calculated, any tiny displacement immediately mobilizes full passive resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將兩側水位、孔壓與泵站狀態畫在同一時間軸，檢查洪峰、退水及抽排失效。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot both stages, pore pressure and pump state on one time axis and examine peak, recession and pumping failure. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b274-v15-40","title":"退水與反向荷載情境機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Recession and reversed loading mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"prerequisiteIds":["b274-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「退水與反向荷載情境」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Recession and reversed loading” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只以外河最高水位驗算會漏掉退水後背側水壓，直接用水深差平方又抹掉兩側共同底面幾何；忽略孔壓消散較慢也會使基礎有效載重的時程不合理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Checking only peak river stage misses rear water during recession. Squaring the depth difference loses the shared-base geometry, and ignoring slower pore-pressure dissipation produces an inconsistent time history of effective foundation loading and resistance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例兩側直牆水深由同一底面量起，取外河向背側為正，僅相減兩個靜水合力；未包含基底揚壓或土壓。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The example subtracts two hydrostatic resultants only, excluding base uplift and earth pressure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「外河水位一旦下降，防洪牆受到的所有荷載與風險就必定同步減少。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once river stage falls, every floodwall load and failure risk necessarily decreases together.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b274-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只以外河最高水位驗算會漏掉退水後背側水壓，直接用水深差平方又抹掉兩側共同底面幾何；忽略孔壓消散較慢也會使基礎有效載重的時程不合理。","textEn":"Checking only peak river stage misses rear water during recession. Squaring the depth difference loses the shared-base geometry, and ignoring slower pore-pressure dissipation produces an inconsistent time history of effective foundation loading and resistance.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]},{"id":"b274-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「退水與反向荷載情境機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Recession and reversed loading mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只以外河最高水位驗算會漏掉退水後背側水壓，直接用水深差平方又抹掉兩側共同底面幾何；忽略孔壓消散較慢也會使基礎有效載重的時程不合理。","水深增加一成時，防洪牆的底部水壓力矩也只增加一成。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Checking only peak river stage misses rear water during recession.","A ten-percent increase in depth increases hydrostatic base moment by only ten percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只以外河最高水位驗算會漏掉退水後背側水壓，直接用水深差平方又抹掉兩側共同底面幾何；忽略孔壓消散較慢也會使基礎有效載重的時程不合理。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Checking only peak river stage misses rear water during recession. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-walls","v4-related-7afab40b0a57","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-boston"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b275","title":"移動式防洪擋板部署","titleEn":"Deployable flood-barrier systems","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"課程把可拆構件視為包含預警、儲存、運輸、組裝、基礎、密封及抽排的完整系統，逐步估算時程、載重與水量，再以共同原因及演練統計檢查可靠度。比尤德利與科隆提供官方工程背景，全部算例為假設，不作實際啟動水位、錨定配置或產品合格證明。","summaryEn":"The course treats removable elements as a system of warning, storage, transport, assembly, foundations, sealing and pumping. It calculates timing, loading and water balance before examining common causes and exercise statistics. Bewdley and Cologne provide official project context. Every example is hypothetical, without prescribing operating triggers, anchorage layouts or product certification.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["預警與決策","Warning and decision"],["庫存與運輸","Inventory and transport"],["組裝及基礎","Assembly and bases"],["閉合與抽排","Closure and pumping"],["演練與反饋","Exercises and feedback"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["預警與決策","庫存與運輸","組裝及基礎","閉合與抽排","演練與反饋"],"labelsEn":["Warning and decision","Inventory and transport","Assembly and bases","Closure and pumping","Exercises and feedback"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"敏感度固定四個必要且互相獨立的操作階段，將每階段成功率由0.98提高到0.99，完整成功率由0.98⁴=0.92236816變成0.99⁴=0.96059601，增加3.822785個百分點。這不是失敗率只減少一個百分點，也不代表現場一定達到相同改善；改善若來自共用同一道路的備援車輛，獨立假設可能根本不成立。應先辨識預報、通知、調度與閉合的共同原因，再用可追溯演練估計條件機率，另外保留洪水超標、密封及結構性能的失效範圍，避免把操作成功當成全面防洪保證。","textEn":"Keep four necessary independent operational stages and improve each success probability from 0.98 to 0.99. Complete success increases from 0.98⁴=0.92236816 to 0.99⁴=0.96059601, a gain of 3.822785 percentage points. This is not a reduction of only one percentage point in system failure, nor a promise of the same field improvement. Backup vehicles sharing one road may invalidate independence entirely. First identify common causes across forecasting, alerting, mobilization and closure, then estimate conditional probabilities from traceable exercises. Retain separate failure scopes for flood exceedance, sealing and structural performance so that operational success is never presented as comprehensive protection. Changes in crew composition and available routes also require renewed evidence rather than automatic transfer of old probabilities.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b275-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「預警提前量與時間餘裕機理與驗證」與「平行班組與資源瓶頸機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Warning lead time and float mechanism and verification\" and \"Parallel crews and bottlenecks mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b275-v15-01","title":"預警提前量與時間餘裕機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Warning lead time and float mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「預警提前量與時間餘裕」如何影響移動式防洪擋板部署的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Warning lead time and float” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Deployable flood-barrier systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"可拆擋板在洪水前必須完成整條防線的閉合，預警提前量應以安全施工的最晚時間為終點，而不是只看洪峰到達。通知、調度、運輸、組裝與檢查皆消耗時間，且降雨可能同時影響道路和人員；正的平均餘裕只能作規劃起點，仍需處理預報誤差與作業時間分布。本例各階段依序不重疊，提前量與工時均是假設值，不是任何城市的動員觸發門檻；未將人員安全截止時間等同於水到板頂。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「預警提前量與時間餘裕」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A demountable system must close the entire defence before flooding, with lead time ending at the latest safe installation time rather than merely the crest arrival. Alerting, mobilization, transport, assembly and checking all consume time, while weather may affect roads and staff together. Positive average float is a planning starting point that still requires forecast and duration uncertainty. The example has sequential nonoverlapping phases and hypothetical timing, not any city’s mobilization trigger. The safe working deadline is not assumed to occur when water reaches the barrier top. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Warning lead time and float” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設可用提前量TL=8 h，通知0.5 h、動員1 h、運輸1.5 h、組裝3 h、查驗0.5 h，所需6.5 h，餘裕1.5 h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume available lead time 8 h: alert 0.5 h, mobilization 1 h, transport 1.5 h, assembly 3 h and inspection 0.5 h.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要擋板組裝時間短於洪峰到達時間，就一定來得及安全部署。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Assembly shorter than time to the flood crest guarantees timely and safe deployment.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「預警提前量與時間餘裕」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Warning lead time and float”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-01-k1","title":"預警提前量與時間餘裕機理與驗證","titleEn":"Warning lead time and float mechanism and verification","text":"可拆擋板在洪水前必須完成整條防線的閉合，預警提前量應以安全施工的最晚時間為終點，而不是只看洪峰到達。通知、調度、運輸、組裝與檢查皆消耗時間，且降雨可能同時影響道路和人員；正的平均餘裕只能作規劃起點，仍需處理預報誤差與作業時間分布。","textEn":"A demountable system must close the entire defence before flooding, with lead time ending at the latest safe installation time rather than merely the crest arrival. Alerting, mobilization, transport, assembly and checking all consume time, while weather may affect roads and staff together.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要擋板組裝時間短於洪峰到達時間，就一定來得及安全部署。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Assembly shorter than time to the flood crest guarantees timely and safe deployment. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「預警提前量與時間餘裕機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Warning lead time and float mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["只要擋板組裝時間短於洪峰到達時間，就一定來得及安全部署。","可拆擋板在洪水前必須完成整條防線的閉合，預警提前量應以安全施工的最晚時間為終點，而不是只看洪峰到達。","任意增加一倍人力，所有部署流程的總時間就必定減半。"],"optionsEn":["Assembly shorter than time to the flood crest guarantees timely and safe deployment.","A demountable system must close the entire defence before flooding, with lead time ending at the latest safe installation time rather than merely the crest arrival.","Doubling staff anywhere necessarily halves the total duration of every deployment process."],"answer":1,"explanation":"可拆擋板在洪水前必須完成整條防線的閉合，預警提前量應以安全施工的最晚時間為終點，而不是只看洪峰到達。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A demountable system must close the entire defence before flooding, with lead time ending at the latest safe installation time rather than merely the crest arrival. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b275-v15-02","title":"預警提前量與時間餘裕機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Warning lead time and float mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「預警提前量與時間餘裕」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Warning lead time and float” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設可用提前量TL=8 h，通知0.5 h、動員1 h、運輸1.5 h、組裝3 h、查驗0.5 h，所需6.5 h，餘裕1.5 h。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume available lead time 8 h: alert 0.5 h, mobilization 1 h, transport 1.5 h, assembly 3 h and inspection 0.5 h. Required time is 6.5 h; float is 1.5 h. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：依真實演練記錄各階段開始與結束，檢查是否有重疊或共享資源，並將路線中斷與較快上升洪水列入情境。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record actual start and finish times during exercises, checking overlap and shared resources.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設可用提前量TL=8 h，通知0.5 h、動員1 h、運輸1.5 h、組裝3 h、查驗0.5 h，所需6.5 h，餘裕1.5 h。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume available lead time 8 h: alert 0.5 h, mobilization 1 h, transport 1.5 h, assembly 3 h and inspection 0.5 h. Required time is 6.5 h; float is 1.5 h.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「預警提前量與時間餘裕機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Warning lead time and float mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["板材能承受水壓，就能自動證明立柱底座與地基也完全足夠。","密封條只要算出正的壓縮量，就已證明接觸壓力足夠且完全不漏水。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設可用提前量TL=8 h，通知0.5 h、動員1 h、運輸1.5 h、組裝3 h、查驗0.5 h，所需6.5 h，餘裕1.5 h。"],"optionsEn":["A panel resisting water pressure automatically proves its post base and foundation adequate.","Any positive calculated seal compression proves adequate contact pressure and zero leakage.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume available lead time 8 h: alert 0.5 h, mobilization 1 h, transport 1.5 h, assembly 3 h and inspection 0.5 h."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設可用提前量TL=8 h，通知0.5 h、動員1 h、運輸1.5 h、組裝3 h、查驗0.5 h，所需6.5 h，餘裕1.5 h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume available lead time 8 h: alert 0.5 h, mobilization 1 h, transport 1.5 h, assembly 3 h and inspection 0.5 h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b275-v15-03","title":"預警提前量與時間餘裕機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Warning lead time and float mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「預警提前量與時間餘裕」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Warning lead time and float” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"依真實演練記錄各階段開始與結束，檢查是否有重疊或共享資源，並將路線中斷與較快上升洪水列入情境。以安全截止時間而非單一洪峰預報比較所需時間，清楚保留不確定度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record actual start and finish times during exercises, checking overlap and shared resources. Include interrupted routes and faster-rising floods in scenarios, comparing required duration against the safe closure deadline rather than one crest forecast while retaining uncertainty in both quantities. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把一場假設部署畫成時間線，列出安全截止與預報誤差，再加入交通延遲。比較是否仍有完整查驗時間，並說明不能為了表面準時而省略閉合檢查。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw a deployment timeline with a safe deadline and forecast uncertainty, then introduce traffic delay. Check whether full inspection time remains and explain why omitting closure verification cannot be used to create apparent on-time completion.","failure":"注意干擾：只看組裝速度會漏掉通知和運輸，重複加總平行工作又可能高估時間；若以洪峰當截止而場地更早進水，即使名義餘裕為正也無法安全完成閉合。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Considering assembly alone misses alert and transport time, while adding parallel tasks twice can overstate duration. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"依真實演練記錄各階段開始與結束，檢查是否有重疊或共享資源，並將路線中斷與較快上升洪水列入情境。以安全截止時間而非單一洪峰預報比較所需時間，清楚保留不確定度。","textEn":"Record actual start and finish times during exercises, checking overlap and shared resources. Include interrupted routes and faster-rising floods in scenarios, comparing required duration against the safe closure deadline rather than one crest forecast while retaining uncertainty in both quantities.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把一場假設部署畫成時間線，列出安全截止與預報誤差，再加入交通延遲。比較是否仍有完整查驗時間，並說明不能為了表面準時而省略閉合檢查。","textEn":"Draw a deployment timeline with a safe deadline and forecast uncertainty, then introduce traffic delay. Check whether full inspection time remains and explain why omitting closure verification cannot be used to create apparent on-time completion.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「預警提前量與時間餘裕機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Warning lead time and float mechanism and verification\"?","options":["依真實演練記錄各階段開始與結束，檢查是否有重疊或共享資源，並將路線中斷與較快上升洪水列入情境。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","每塊擋板的額定高度足夠，就不需要檢查兩端與地下開口的連續性。"],"optionsEn":["Record actual start and finish times during exercises, checking overlap and shared resources.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adequate rated height of every panel removes the need to check ends and buried openings."],"answer":0,"explanation":"依真實演練記錄各階段開始與結束，檢查是否有重疊或共享資源，並將路線中斷與較快上升洪水列入情境。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record actual start and finish times during exercises, checking overlap and shared resources. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b275-v15-04","title":"預警提前量與時間餘裕機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Warning lead time and float mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「預警提前量與時間餘裕」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Warning lead time and float” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只看組裝速度會漏掉通知和運輸，重複加總平行工作又可能高估時間；若以洪峰當截止而場地更早進水，即使名義餘裕為正也無法安全完成閉合。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Considering assembly alone misses alert and transport time, while adding parallel tasks twice can overstate duration. Using crest time as the deadline may falsely show positive float even though access or safe working conditions are lost earlier. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例各階段依序不重疊，提前量與工時均是假設值，不是任何城市的動員觸發門檻；未將人員安全截止時間等同於水到板頂。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The safe working deadline is not assumed to occur when water reaches the barrier top.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要擋板組裝時間短於洪峰到達時間，就一定來得及安全部署。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Assembly shorter than time to the flood crest guarantees timely and safe deployment.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只看組裝速度會漏掉通知和運輸，重複加總平行工作又可能高估時間；若以洪峰當截止而場地更早進水，即使名義餘裕為正也無法安全完成閉合。","textEn":"Considering assembly alone misses alert and transport time, while adding parallel tasks twice can overstate duration. Using crest time as the deadline may falsely show positive float even though access or safe working conditions are lost earlier.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「預警提前量與時間餘裕機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Warning lead time and float mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只看組裝速度會漏掉通知和運輸，重複加總平行工作又可能高估時間；若以洪峰當截止而場地更早進水，即使名義餘裕為正也無法安全完成閉合。","任意增加一倍人力，所有部署流程的總時間就必定減半。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Considering assembly alone misses alert and transport time, while adding parallel tasks twice can overstate duration.","Doubling staff anywhere necessarily halves the total duration of every deployment process."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只看組裝速度會漏掉通知和運輸，重複加總平行工作又可能高估時間；若以洪峰當截止而場地更早進水，即使名義餘裕為正也無法安全完成閉合。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Considering assembly alone misses alert and transport time, while adding parallel tasks twice can overstate duration. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b275-v15-05","title":"平行班組與資源瓶頸機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Parallel crews and bottlenecks mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「平行班組與資源瓶頸」如何影響移動式防洪擋板部署的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Parallel crews and bottlenecks” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Deployable flood-barrier systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"增加班組只會加速可真正平行的工作，卸貨機具、單一道路或依序接續的構件仍可能控制總工期。網路排程需要先列工作相依與共同資源，再找最長路徑；平均每人每小時的產量不能直接乘所有人數，因為相互干擾、交接和查驗會限制現場有效產能。本例兩個區段同時開始且人力完全獨立，完成後才能共同進行最終查驗；不含共用吊具、交通或未列前置作業。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「平行班組與資源瓶頸」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"More crews accelerate only work that can genuinely run in parallel; unloading equipment, a single access road or sequentially connected components may still govern duration. Network scheduling first identifies dependencies and shared resources, then the longest path. Individual output cannot simply be multiplied by headcount because interference, handover and inspection constrain effective production. Two sections start together with fully independent crews, followed by one final inspection only after both finish. Shared lifting equipment, traffic and unlisted preliminary work are excluded. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Parallel crews and bottlenecks” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設區段A需2.0 h、B需3.5 h且可平行，最後共同查驗0.5 h，總時間T=max(2.0,3.5)+0.5=4.0 h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent parallel sections A=2.0 h and B=3.5 h, followed by 0.5 h joint inspection.","failure":"常見誤解：「任意增加一倍人力，所有部署流程的總時間就必定減半。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Doubling staff anywhere necessarily halves the total duration of every deployment process.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「平行班組與資源瓶頸」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Parallel crews and bottlenecks”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-05-k1","title":"平行班組與資源瓶頸機理與驗證","titleEn":"Parallel crews and bottlenecks mechanism and verification","text":"增加班組只會加速可真正平行的工作，卸貨機具、單一道路或依序接續的構件仍可能控制總工期。網路排程需要先列工作相依與共同資源，再找最長路徑；平均每人每小時的產量不能直接乘所有人數，因為相互干擾、交接和查驗會限制現場有效產能。","textEn":"More crews accelerate only work that can genuinely run in parallel; unloading equipment, a single access road or sequentially connected components may still govern duration. Network scheduling first identifies dependencies and shared resources, then the longest path.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任意增加一倍人力，所有部署流程的總時間就必定減半。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Doubling staff anywhere necessarily halves the total duration of every deployment process. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「平行班組與資源瓶頸機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Parallel crews and bottlenecks mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["任意增加一倍人力，所有部署流程的總時間就必定減半。","只要總件數和總重量足夠，就能保證每個區段的構件都相容。","增加班組只會加速可真正平行的工作，卸貨機具、單一道路或依序接續的構件仍可能控制總工期。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling staff anywhere necessarily halves the total duration of every deployment process.","Sufficient total count and mass guarantee compatible components for every barrier section.","More crews accelerate only work that can genuinely run in parallel."],"answer":2,"explanation":"增加班組只會加速可真正平行的工作，卸貨機具、單一道路或依序接續的構件仍可能控制總工期。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"More crews accelerate only work that can genuinely run in parallel; unloading equipment, a single access road or sequentially connected components may still govern duration. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b275-v15-06","title":"平行班組與資源瓶頸機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Parallel crews and bottlenecks mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「平行班組與資源瓶頸」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Parallel crews and bottlenecks” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設區段A需2.0 h、B需3.5 h且可平行，最後共同查驗0.5 h，總時間T=max(2.0,3.5)+0.5=4.0 h。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent parallel sections A=2.0 h and B=3.5 h, followed by 0.5 h joint inspection. Total T=max(2.0,3.5)+0.5=4.0 h. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以演練逐項核對可平行的真實條件，追蹤吊具、車輛、鑰匙和檢查人員的共享時段。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify actual parallelism in exercises and track shared lifting equipment, vehicles, keys and inspectors over time.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設區段A需2.0 h、B需3.5 h且可平行，最後共同查驗0.5 h，總時間T=max(2.0,3.5)+0.5=4.0 h。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent parallel sections A=2.0 h and B=3.5 h, followed by 0.5 h joint inspection. Total T=max(2.0,3.5)+0.5=4.0 h.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「平行班組與資源瓶頸機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Parallel crews and bottlenecks mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設區段A需2.0 h、B需3.5 h且可平行，最後共同查驗0.5 h，總時間T=max(2.0,3.5)+0.5=4.0 h。","增加自重一定能解決所有臨時防洪系統的滑動、滲水與承載問題。","擋板閉合後只要任何一台泵在運轉，內側水位就一定不會上升。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent parallel sections A=2.0 h and B=3.5 h, followed by 0.5 h joint inspection.","Added weight necessarily solves every sliding, seepage and bearing problem of a temporary barrier.","Once barriers close, any running pump guarantees that interior water level cannot rise."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設區段A需2.0 h、B需3.5 h且可平行，最後共同查驗0.5 h，總時間T=max(2.0,3.5)+0.5=4.0 h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume independent parallel sections A=2.0 h and B=3.5 h, followed by 0.5 h joint inspection. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b275-v15-07","title":"平行班組與資源瓶頸機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Parallel crews and bottlenecks mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「平行班組與資源瓶頸」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Parallel crews and bottlenecks” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以演練逐項核對可平行的真實條件，追蹤吊具、車輛、鑰匙和檢查人員的共享時段。檢查短路徑加人是否能改變最長路徑，再用不同班表或設備故障情境重算總時程。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify actual parallelism in exercises and track shared lifting equipment, vehicles, keys and inspectors over time. Test whether adding staff to a shorter branch changes the critical path, then recalculate total duration for altered shifts or equipment outages rather than assuming proportional acceleration. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在兩條平行路徑上加入一台共用吊車，重新安排不能重疊的時段。比較增加班組與增加瓶頸設備的效果，說明需要記錄的現場交接資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: Introduce one shared crane into two parallel paths and reschedule nonoverlapping tasks. Compare adding crews with adding bottleneck equipment and identify the field handover information needed to validate the resulting schedule.","failure":"注意干擾：把兩段都假設獨立但共用唯一吊車會低估工期，將人員加到非關鍵工作也不一定提早閉合；忽略最後整線查驗，可能讓局部完成被誤報為全線可用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assuming independent sections that share one crane understates duration. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以演練逐項核對可平行的真實條件，追蹤吊具、車輛、鑰匙和檢查人員的共享時段。檢查短路徑加人是否能改變最長路徑，再用不同班表或設備故障情境重算總時程。","textEn":"Verify actual parallelism in exercises and track shared lifting equipment, vehicles, keys and inspectors over time. Test whether adding staff to a shorter branch changes the critical path, then recalculate total duration for altered shifts or equipment outages rather than assuming proportional acceleration.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在兩條平行路徑上加入一台共用吊車，重新安排不能重疊的時段。比較增加班組與增加瓶頸設備的效果，說明需要記錄的現場交接資訊。","textEn":"Introduce one shared crane into two parallel paths and reschedule nonoverlapping tasks. Compare adding crews with adding bottleneck equipment and identify the field handover information needed to validate the resulting schedule.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「平行班組與資源瓶頸機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Parallel crews and bottlenecks mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以演練逐項核對可平行的真實條件，追蹤吊具、車輛、鑰匙和檢查人員的共享時段。","四個必要環節各有百分之九十八成功率，整個流程就必定也是百分之九十八。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Verify actual parallelism in exercises and track shared lifting equipment, vehicles, keys and inspectors over time.","Four necessary stages each succeeding ninety-eight percent make the entire process ninety-eight percent reliable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以演練逐項核對可平行的真實條件，追蹤吊具、車輛、鑰匙和檢查人員的共享時段。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify actual parallelism in exercises and track shared lifting equipment, vehicles, keys and inspectors over time. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b275-v15-08","title":"平行班組與資源瓶頸機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Parallel crews and bottlenecks mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「平行班組與資源瓶頸」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Parallel crews and bottlenecks” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把兩段都假設獨立但共用唯一吊車會低估工期，將人員加到非關鍵工作也不一定提早閉合；忽略最後整線查驗，可能讓局部完成被誤報為全線可用。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assuming independent sections that share one crane understates duration. Adding people to a noncritical activity may not advance closure, and omitted final inspection lets local completion be incorrectly reported as a fully functioning defence line. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例兩個區段同時開始且人力完全獨立，完成後才能共同進行最終查驗；不含共用吊具、交通或未列前置作業。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Shared lifting equipment, traffic and unlisted preliminary work are excluded.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任意增加一倍人力，所有部署流程的總時間就必定減半。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Doubling staff anywhere necessarily halves the total duration of every deployment process.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把兩段都假設獨立但共用唯一吊車會低估工期，將人員加到非關鍵工作也不一定提早閉合；忽略最後整線查驗，可能讓局部完成被誤報為全線可用。","textEn":"Assuming independent sections that share one crane understates duration. Adding people to a noncritical activity may not advance closure, and omitted final inspection lets local completion be incorrectly reported as a fully functioning defence line.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「平行班組與資源瓶頸機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Parallel crews and bottlenecks mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要總件數和總重量足夠，就能保證每個區段的構件都相容。","把兩段都假設獨立但共用唯一吊車會低估工期，將人員加到非關鍵工作也不一定提早閉合；忽略最後整線查驗，可能讓局部完成被誤報為全線可用。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Sufficient total count and mass guarantee compatible components for every barrier section.","Assuming independent sections that share one crane understates duration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把兩段都假設獨立但共用唯一吊車會低估工期，將人員加到非關鍵工作也不一定提早閉合；忽略最後整線查驗，可能讓局部完成被誤報為全線可用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assuming independent sections that share one crane understates duration. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b275-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「構件清點與運輸趟次機理與驗證」與「板面水壓與立柱傳力機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Component inventory and transport mechanism and verification\" and \"Panel pressure and post load path mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b275-v15-09","title":"構件清點與運輸趟次機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Component inventory and transport mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「構件清點與運輸趟次」如何影響移動式防洪擋板部署的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Component inventory and transport” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Deployable flood-barrier systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"擋板、立柱、螺栓與密封件形成可追溯的組裝系統，運輸容量既受質量也受體積和固定方式限制。清點不只確認總件數，還需匹配區段、方向與介面；一個關鍵專用件缺少就可能中斷閉合，而備品不能任意替換未經驗證的規格。本例只依載重計算整數趟次，假設各件可分配且體積及裝卸已確認不控制；未計司機班時、路程或多車平行調度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「構件清點與運輸趟次」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Panels, posts, fasteners and seals form a traceable assembly system. Transport is constrained by mass, volume and securing arrangements. Inventory must match sections, orientation and interfaces rather than merely total counts. One missing specialist component can prevent closure, and a spare is not interchangeable without verified compatibility with the intended system. The example counts whole trips by payload only, assuming items can be distributed and volume and handling do not govern. Driver hours, travel time and parallel vehicle scheduling are excluded. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Component inventory and transport” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總構件質量M=12,000 kg、每趟有效載重C=3500 kg，趟次N=ceil(M/C)=4；不是3.43趟。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume component mass M=12,000 kg and effective payload C=3500 kg.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要總件數和總重量足夠，就能保證每個區段的構件都相容。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Sufficient total count and mass guarantee compatible components for every barrier section.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「構件清點與運輸趟次」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Component inventory and transport”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-09-k1","title":"構件清點與運輸趟次機理與驗證","titleEn":"Component inventory and transport mechanism and verification","text":"擋板、立柱、螺栓與密封件形成可追溯的組裝系統，運輸容量既受質量也受體積和固定方式限制。清點不只確認總件數，還需匹配區段、方向與介面；一個關鍵專用件缺少就可能中斷閉合，而備品不能任意替換未經驗證的規格。","textEn":"Panels, posts, fasteners and seals form a traceable assembly system. Transport is constrained by mass, volume and securing arrangements.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要總件數和總重量足夠，就能保證每個區段的構件都相容。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Sufficient total count and mass guarantee compatible components for every barrier section. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「構件清點與運輸趟次機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Component inventory and transport mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["擋板、立柱、螺栓與密封件形成可追溯的組裝系統，運輸容量既受質量也受體積和固定方式限制。","只要總件數和總重量足夠，就能保證每個區段的構件都相容。","板材能承受水壓，就能自動證明立柱底座與地基也完全足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Panels, posts, fasteners and seals form a traceable assembly system.","Sufficient total count and mass guarantee compatible components for every barrier section.","A panel resisting water pressure automatically proves its post base and foundation adequate."],"answer":0,"explanation":"擋板、立柱、螺栓與密封件形成可追溯的組裝系統，運輸容量既受質量也受體積和固定方式限制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Panels, posts, fasteners and seals form a traceable assembly system. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b275-v15-10","title":"構件清點與運輸趟次機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Component inventory and transport mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「構件清點與運輸趟次」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Component inventory and transport” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總構件質量M=12,000 kg、每趟有效載重C=3500 kg，趟次N=ceil(M/C)=4；不是3.43趟。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume component mass M=12,000 kg and effective payload C=3500 kg. Required whole trips N=ceil(M/C)=4, not 3.43 trips. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把構件清單連到區段標識與裝車順序，核對尺寸、載重、固定和現場卸貨空間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Link inventory to section identifiers and loading order, checking dimensions, payload, securing and unloading space.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總構件質量M=12,000 kg、每趟有效載重C=3500 kg，趟次N=ceil(M/C)=4；不是3.43趟。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume component mass M=12,000 kg and effective payload C=3500 kg. Required whole trips N=ceil(M/C)=4, not 3.43 trips.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「構件清點與運輸趟次機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Component inventory and transport mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["密封條只要算出正的壓縮量，就已證明接觸壓力足夠且完全不漏水。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總構件質量M=12,000 kg、每趟有效載重C=3500 kg，趟次N=ceil(M/C)=4。","每塊擋板的額定高度足夠，就不需要檢查兩端與地下開口的連續性。"],"optionsEn":["Any positive calculated seal compression proves adequate contact pressure and zero leakage.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume component mass M=12,000 kg and effective payload C=3500 kg.","Adequate rated height of every panel removes the need to check ends and buried openings."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總構件質量M=12,000 kg、每趟有效載重C=3500 kg，趟次N=ceil(M/C)=4；不是3.43趟。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume component mass M=12,000 kg and effective payload C=3500 kg. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b275-v15-11","title":"構件清點與運輸趟次機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Component inventory and transport mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「構件清點與運輸趟次」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Component inventory and transport” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把構件清單連到區段標識與裝車順序，核對尺寸、載重、固定和現場卸貨空間。用實際庫存及備品相容紀錄驗證，演練中記錄最後關鍵件到達時間而非僅平均車趟。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Link inventory to section identifiers and loading order, checking dimensions, payload, securing and unloading space. Verify actual stock and spare compatibility and record arrival of the last critical component during exercises rather than relying only on average truck-trip duration. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：按區段與組裝順序設計一張裝車清單，再加入一件專用件缺貨情境。說明哪項清點可以在出庫前發現問題，以及整數趟次和現場完成時間的差別。","observationEn":"Site practice: Create a loading manifest by section and assembly order, then remove one specialized item. Identify the dispatch check that detects the shortage and distinguish whole-trip count from the actual time of completed installation.","failure":"注意干擾：小數趟次向下取整會遺漏構件，僅按總重量裝車可能讓先用構件最後才到；混用外觀相似但介面不合的零件，則可能在現場造成無法壓緊或閉合的接頭。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Rounding trips downward leaves components behind. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把構件清單連到區段標識與裝車順序，核對尺寸、載重、固定和現場卸貨空間。用實際庫存及備品相容紀錄驗證，演練中記錄最後關鍵件到達時間而非僅平均車趟。","textEn":"Link inventory to section identifiers and loading order, checking dimensions, payload, securing and unloading space. Verify actual stock and spare compatibility and record arrival of the last critical component during exercises rather than relying only on average truck-trip duration.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"按區段與組裝順序設計一張裝車清單，再加入一件專用件缺貨情境。說明哪項清點可以在出庫前發現問題，以及整數趟次和現場完成時間的差別。","textEn":"Create a loading manifest by section and assembly order, then remove one specialized item. Identify the dispatch check that detects the shortage and distinguish whole-trip count from the actual time of completed installation.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「構件清點與運輸趟次機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Component inventory and transport mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","三十次演練都成功，就能用統計方法證明未來失敗機率恰好為零。","把構件清單連到區段標識與裝車順序，核對尺寸、載重、固定和現場卸貨空間。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Thirty successful exercises statistically prove that future failure probability is exactly zero.","Link inventory to section identifiers and loading order, checking dimensions, payload, securing and unloading space."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把構件清單連到區段標識與裝車順序，核對尺寸、載重、固定和現場卸貨空間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Link inventory to section identifiers and loading order, checking dimensions, payload, securing and unloading space. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b275-v15-12","title":"構件清點與運輸趟次機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Component inventory and transport mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「構件清點與運輸趟次」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Component inventory and transport” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"小數趟次向下取整會遺漏構件，僅按總重量裝車可能讓先用構件最後才到；混用外觀相似但介面不合的零件，則可能在現場造成無法壓緊或閉合的接頭。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Rounding trips downward leaves components behind. Loading only by total weight may deliver early-use items last, while visually similar but incompatible parts can create joints that cannot close or achieve their specified compression during installation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例只依載重計算整數趟次，假設各件可分配且體積及裝卸已確認不控制；未計司機班時、路程或多車平行調度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Driver hours, travel time and parallel vehicle scheduling are excluded.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要總件數和總重量足夠，就能保證每個區段的構件都相容。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Sufficient total count and mass guarantee compatible components for every barrier section.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"小數趟次向下取整會遺漏構件，僅按總重量裝車可能讓先用構件最後才到；混用外觀相似但介面不合的零件，則可能在現場造成無法壓緊或閉合的接頭。","textEn":"Rounding trips downward leaves components behind. Loading only by total weight may deliver early-use items last, while visually similar but incompatible parts can create joints that cannot close or achieve their specified compression during installation.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「構件清點與運輸趟次機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Component inventory and transport mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["小數趟次向下取整會遺漏構件，僅按總重量裝車可能讓先用構件最後才到；混用外觀相似但介面不合的零件，則可能在現場造成無法壓緊或閉合的接頭。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","板材能承受水壓，就能自動證明立柱底座與地基也完全足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Rounding trips downward leaves components behind.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A panel resisting water pressure automatically proves its post base and foundation adequate."],"answer":0,"explanation":"小數趟次向下取整會遺漏構件，僅按總重量裝車可能讓先用構件最後才到；混用外觀相似但介面不合的零件，則可能在現場造成無法壓緊或閉合的接頭。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Rounding trips downward leaves components behind. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b275-v15-13","title":"板面水壓與立柱傳力機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Panel pressure and post load path mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「板面水壓與立柱傳力」如何影響移動式防洪擋板部署的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Panel pressure and post load path” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Deployable flood-barrier systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水壓由板面傳到立柱，再經底座與預設基礎承擔，簡單合力分配只能說明某一傳力假設。每根立柱的分攤寬度取決於跨距和邊界，端柱與轉角不一定相同；水深增加還使作用點和彎矩改變，不能只比較板材厚度或額定高度就跳過錨座與地基。本例為垂直單側靜水、均勻跨距的內柱，分攤寬度等於柱距；合力只是外荷載，並非螺栓拉力或任何現場安裝設計。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「板面水壓與立柱傳力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Water pressure passes from panels through posts and bases into prepared foundations. A simple tributary calculation explains only one load-path assumption. Post width depends on span and boundary conditions, with end and corner posts differing from interior posts. Greater depth also changes lever arm and moment, so panel thickness or rated height cannot replace anchorage and foundation assessment. The example uses one-sided still water and an interior post in equally spaced bays, with tributary width equal to spacing. The resultant is external loading, not bolt tension or a field installation design. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Panel pressure and post load path” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設γw=9.81 kN/m³、水深h=1.2 m、柱距s=2 m，單柱分攤F=γwh²s/2=14.1264 kN，底矩Fh/3=5.65056 kN·m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume γw=9.81 kN/m³, depth h=1.2 m and post spacing s=2 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「板材能承受水壓，就能自動證明立柱底座與地基也完全足夠。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A panel resisting water pressure automatically proves its post base and foundation adequate.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「板面水壓與立柱傳力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Panel pressure and post load path”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-13-k1","title":"板面水壓與立柱傳力機理與驗證","titleEn":"Panel pressure and post load path mechanism and verification","text":"水壓由板面傳到立柱，再經底座與預設基礎承擔，簡單合力分配只能說明某一傳力假設。每根立柱的分攤寬度取決於跨距和邊界，端柱與轉角不一定相同；水深增加還使作用點和彎矩改變，不能只比較板材厚度或額定高度就跳過錨座與地基。","textEn":"Water pressure passes from panels through posts and bases into prepared foundations. A simple tributary calculation explains only one load-path assumption.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：板材能承受水壓，就能自動證明立柱底座與地基也完全足夠。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A panel resisting water pressure automatically proves its post base and foundation adequate. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「板面水壓與立柱傳力機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Panel pressure and post load path mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["板材能承受水壓，就能自動證明立柱底座與地基也完全足夠。","水壓由板面傳到立柱，再經底座與預設基礎承擔，簡單合力分配只能說明某一傳力假設。","增加自重一定能解決所有臨時防洪系統的滑動、滲水與承載問題。"],"optionsEn":["A panel resisting water pressure automatically proves its post base and foundation adequate.","Water pressure passes from panels through posts and bases into prepared foundations.","Added weight necessarily solves every sliding, seepage and bearing problem of a temporary barrier."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水壓由板面傳到立柱，再經底座與預設基礎承擔，簡單合力分配只能說明某一傳力假設。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Water pressure passes from panels through posts and bases into prepared foundations. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b275-v15-14","title":"板面水壓與立柱傳力機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Panel pressure and post load path mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「板面水壓與立柱傳力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Panel pressure and post load path” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設γw=9.81 kN/m³、水深h=1.2 m、柱距s=2 m，單柱分攤F=γwh²s/2=14.1264 kN，底矩Fh/3=5.65056 kN·m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume γw=9.81 kN/m³, depth h=1.2 m and post spacing s=2 m. Tributary force F=14.1264 kN gives base moment 5.65056 kN·m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：畫出板到柱、底座及地基的完整傳力路徑，逐一核對邊跨、轉角和接頭邊界。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw the full path from panels to posts, bases and soil, checking end bays, corners and joint boundaries.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設γw=9.81 kN/m³、水深h=1.2 m、柱距s=2 m，單柱分攤F=γwh²s/2=14.1264 kN，底矩Fh/3=5.65056 kN·m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume γw=9.81 kN/m³, depth h=1.2 m and post spacing s=2 m. Tributary force F=14.1264 kN gives base moment 5.65056 kN·m.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「板面水壓與立柱傳力機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Panel pressure and post load path mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["擋板閉合後只要任何一台泵在運轉，內側水位就一定不會上升。","四個必要環節各有百分之九十八成功率，整個流程就必定也是百分之九十八。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設γw=9.81 kN/m³、水深h=1.2 m、柱距s=2 m，單柱分攤F=γwh²s/2=14.1264 kN，底矩Fh/3=5.65056 kN·m。"],"optionsEn":["Once barriers close, any running pump guarantees that interior water level cannot rise.","Four necessary stages each succeeding ninety-eight percent make the entire process ninety-eight percent reliable.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume γw=9.81 kN/m³, depth h=1.2 m and post spacing s=2 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設γw=9.81 kN/m³、水深h=1.2 m、柱距s=2 m，單柱分攤F=γwh²s/2=14.1264 kN，底矩Fh/3=5.65056 kN·m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume γw=9.81 kN/m³, depth h=1.2 m and post spacing s=2 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b275-v15-15","title":"板面水壓與立柱傳力機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Panel pressure and post load path mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「板面水壓與立柱傳力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Panel pressure and post load path” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"畫出板到柱、底座及地基的完整傳力路徑，逐一核對邊跨、轉角和接頭邊界。確認製造商證明資料對應實際底座及水深，另評估撞擊、波浪和反向作用，不由合力直接推定錨栓合格。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw the full path from panels to posts, bases and soil, checking end bays, corners and joint boundaries. Confirm documented system evidence matches the actual base and head, assessing impact, waves and reversed action separately rather than inferring anchor adequacy directly from total force. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對同一水深改變柱距並比較合力，另外畫出端柱與轉角的分攤區。列出合力之外仍需的底座與材料資料，避免把教學載重直接當施工配置。","observationEn":"Site practice: Vary spacing at one depth and compare forces, drawing tributary areas for end and corner posts separately. List base and material evidence still needed beyond total load, avoiding conversion of the teaching calculation into an installation layout.","failure":"注意干擾：把內柱分攤寬度套到所有邊界可能錯分荷載，忽略底座力矩又會漏掉錨定需求；單獨測試板材不能證明柱、基礎與止水組合在同一荷載下可靠。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying interior-post tributary width everywhere can misallocate force. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"畫出板到柱、底座及地基的完整傳力路徑，逐一核對邊跨、轉角和接頭邊界。確認製造商證明資料對應實際底座及水深，另評估撞擊、波浪和反向作用，不由合力直接推定錨栓合格。","textEn":"Draw the full path from panels to posts, bases and soil, checking end bays, corners and joint boundaries. Confirm documented system evidence matches the actual base and head, assessing impact, waves and reversed action separately rather than inferring anchor adequacy directly from total force.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對同一水深改變柱距並比較合力，另外畫出端柱與轉角的分攤區。列出合力之外仍需的底座與材料資料，避免把教學載重直接當施工配置。","textEn":"Vary spacing at one depth and compare forces, drawing tributary areas for end and corner posts separately. List base and material evidence still needed beyond total load, avoiding conversion of the teaching calculation into an installation layout.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「板面水壓與立柱傳力機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Panel pressure and post load path mechanism and verification\"?","options":["畫出板到柱、底座及地基的完整傳力路徑，逐一核對邊跨、轉角和接頭邊界。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要擋板組裝時間短於洪峰到達時間，就一定來得及安全部署。"],"optionsEn":["Draw the full path from panels to posts, bases and soil, checking end bays, corners and joint boundaries.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Assembly shorter than time to the flood crest guarantees timely and safe deployment."],"answer":0,"explanation":"畫出板到柱、底座及地基的完整傳力路徑，逐一核對邊跨、轉角和接頭邊界。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw the full path from panels to posts, bases and soil, checking end bays, corners and joint boundaries. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b275-v15-16","title":"板面水壓與立柱傳力機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Panel pressure and post load path mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「板面水壓與立柱傳力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Panel pressure and post load path” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把內柱分攤寬度套到所有邊界可能錯分荷載，忽略底座力矩又會漏掉錨定需求；單獨測試板材不能證明柱、基礎與止水組合在同一荷載下可靠。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying interior-post tributary width everywhere can misallocate force. Ignoring base moment misses anchorage demand, and a panel-only test cannot establish reliability of posts, foundations and seals acting together under the same loading conditions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例為垂直單側靜水、均勻跨距的內柱，分攤寬度等於柱距；合力只是外荷載，並非螺栓拉力或任何現場安裝設計。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The resultant is external loading, not bolt tension or a field installation design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「板材能承受水壓，就能自動證明立柱底座與地基也完全足夠。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A panel resisting water pressure automatically proves its post base and foundation adequate.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把內柱分攤寬度套到所有邊界可能錯分荷載，忽略底座力矩又會漏掉錨定需求；單獨測試板材不能證明柱、基礎與止水組合在同一荷載下可靠。","textEn":"Applying interior-post tributary width everywhere can misallocate force. Ignoring base moment misses anchorage demand, and a panel-only test cannot establish reliability of posts, foundations and seals acting together under the same loading conditions.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「板面水壓與立柱傳力機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Panel pressure and post load path mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把內柱分攤寬度套到所有邊界可能錯分荷載，忽略底座力矩又會漏掉錨定需求；單獨測試板材不能證明柱、基礎與止水組合在同一荷載下可靠。","增加自重一定能解決所有臨時防洪系統的滑動、滲水與承載問題。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Applying interior-post tributary width everywhere can misallocate force.","Added weight necessarily solves every sliding, seepage and bearing problem of a temporary barrier."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把內柱分攤寬度套到所有邊界可能錯分荷載，忽略底座力矩又會漏掉錨定需求；單獨測試板材不能證明柱、基礎與止水組合在同一荷載下可靠。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying interior-post tributary width everywhere can misallocate force. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b275-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「重力式底座與滑動尺度機理與驗證」與「密封壓縮與幾何公差機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Gravity-base sliding scale mechanism and verification\" and \"Seal compression and geometric tolerance mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b275-v15-17","title":"重力式底座與滑動尺度機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Gravity-base sliding scale mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「重力式底座與滑動尺度」如何影響移動式防洪擋板部署的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gravity-base sliding scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Deployable flood-barrier systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"臨時重力式防洪系統可能依自重、蓄水重量或支撐形成抗力，但底面滲水會降低有效法向力並改變摩擦。地表材質、坡度、泥砂及鋪面接縫也會影響接觸，不能把乾燥平整試驗地面的摩擦係數直接帶到雨中現場；滑動計算需和傾覆、承載及滲流並列。本例是單一假設底座的庫侖摩擦尺度，向下重量尚未扣揚壓，無錨定與被動土抗力；比值不是任何產品額定值或安裝許可。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「重力式底座與滑動尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Temporary gravity systems may resist through self-weight, contained water or bracing, but under-base seepage reduces effective normal force and friction. Surface material, slope, silt and paving joints affect contact, so a coefficient from a dry level test surface cannot automatically represent a wet site. Sliding belongs alongside overturning, bearing and seepage assessment. This is a Coulomb-friction scale for one hypothetical base. Gross weight excludes uplift deduction and no anchors or passive soil resistance are credited; the ratio is neither a product rating nor installation approval. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gravity-base sliding scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設向下W=30 kN、揚壓U=5 kN、μ=0.40、水平力H=8 kN，摩擦R=μ(W−U)=10 kN，R/H=1.25。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gross downward W=30 kN, uplift U=5 kN, friction μ=0.40 and horizontal H=8 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「增加自重一定能解決所有臨時防洪系統的滑動、滲水與承載問題。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Added weight necessarily solves every sliding, seepage and bearing problem of a temporary barrier.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「重力式底座與滑動尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gravity-base sliding scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-17-k1","title":"重力式底座與滑動尺度機理與驗證","titleEn":"Gravity-base sliding scale mechanism and verification","text":"臨時重力式防洪系統可能依自重、蓄水重量或支撐形成抗力，但底面滲水會降低有效法向力並改變摩擦。地表材質、坡度、泥砂及鋪面接縫也會影響接觸，不能把乾燥平整試驗地面的摩擦係數直接帶到雨中現場；滑動計算需和傾覆、承載及滲流並列。","textEn":"Temporary gravity systems may resist through self-weight, contained water or bracing, but under-base seepage reduces effective normal force and friction. Surface material, slope, silt and paving joints affect contact, so a coefficient from a dry level test surface cannot automatically represent a wet site.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：增加自重一定能解決所有臨時防洪系統的滑動、滲水與承載問題。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Added weight necessarily solves every sliding, seepage and bearing problem of a temporary barrier. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「重力式底座與滑動尺度機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gravity-base sliding scale mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["增加自重一定能解決所有臨時防洪系統的滑動、滲水與承載問題。","密封條只要算出正的壓縮量，就已證明接觸壓力足夠且完全不漏水。","臨時重力式防洪系統可能依自重、蓄水重量或支撐形成抗力，但底面滲水會降低有效法向力並改變摩擦。"],"optionsEn":["Added weight necessarily solves every sliding, seepage and bearing problem of a temporary barrier.","Any positive calculated seal compression proves adequate contact pressure and zero leakage.","Temporary gravity systems may resist through self-weight, contained water or bracing, but under-base seepage reduces effective normal force and friction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"臨時重力式防洪系統可能依自重、蓄水重量或支撐形成抗力，但底面滲水會降低有效法向力並改變摩擦。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Temporary gravity systems may resist through self-weight, contained water or bracing, but under-base seepage reduces effective normal force and friction. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b275-v15-18","title":"重力式底座與滑動尺度機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Gravity-base sliding scale mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「重力式底座與滑動尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gravity-base sliding scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設向下W=30 kN、揚壓U=5 kN、μ=0.40、水平力H=8 kN，摩擦R=μ(W−U)=10 kN，R/H=1.25。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gross downward W=30 kN, uplift U=5 kN, friction μ=0.40 and horizontal H=8 kN. R=μ(W−U)=10 kN; R/H=1.25. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：確認摩擦資料與實際濕潤、污染和表面條件相容，追蹤揚壓是否已在重量定義中扣除。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check friction evidence against actual wetness, contamination and surface condition and track whether uplift has already been deducted in weight.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設向下W=30 kN、揚壓U=5 kN、μ=0.40、水平力H=8 kN，摩擦R=μ(W−U)=10 kN，R/H=1.25。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gross downward W=30 kN, uplift U=5 kN, friction μ=0.40 and horizontal H=8 kN. R=μ(W−U)=10 kN; R/H=1.25.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「重力式底座與滑動尺度機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gravity-base sliding scale mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設向下W=30 kN、揚壓U=5 kN、μ=0.40、水平力H=8 kN，摩擦R=μ(W−U)=10 kN，R/H=1.25。","每塊擋板的額定高度足夠，就不需要檢查兩端與地下開口的連續性。","三十次演練都成功，就能用統計方法證明未來失敗機率恰好為零。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gross downward W=30 kN, uplift U=5 kN, friction μ=0.40 and horizontal H=8 kN.","Adequate rated height of every panel removes the need to check ends and buried openings.","Thirty successful exercises statistically prove that future failure probability is exactly zero."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設向下W=30 kN、揚壓U=5 kN、μ=0.40、水平力H=8 kN，摩擦R=μ(W−U)=10 kN，R/H=1.25。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume gross downward W=30 kN, uplift U=5 kN, friction μ=0.40 and horizontal H=8 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b275-v15-19","title":"重力式底座與滑動尺度機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gravity-base sliding scale mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「重力式底座與滑動尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gravity-base sliding scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"確認摩擦資料與實際濕潤、污染和表面條件相容，追蹤揚壓是否已在重量定義中扣除。對排水堵塞、表面沖刷及不平整重新評估，並核對整個經測試系統而不是僅一個底座比值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check friction evidence against actual wetness, contamination and surface condition and track whether uplift has already been deducted in weight. Reassess blocked drainage, surface erosion and unevenness, checking the tested complete system rather than relying on one isolated base resistance ratio. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用兩種假設揚壓比較有效法向力和滑動比，再列出未檢查的失效模式。說明為何改變底座重量或表面配置，需要重新核對完整系統的證明資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare effective normal load and sliding ratio at two hypothetical uplifts, listing unchecked failure modes. Explain why changing base weight or surface preparation requires renewed review of evidence for the complete system configuration.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略泥砂潤滑可能高估摩擦，將乾地試驗係數當成固定材料常數也會失真；只為增加自重而疊放未經核對的重物，還可能改變基礎承載和構件受力方式。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting lubricating silt can overstate friction, and treating a dry-test coefficient as a universal material constant is misleading. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"確認摩擦資料與實際濕潤、污染和表面條件相容，追蹤揚壓是否已在重量定義中扣除。對排水堵塞、表面沖刷及不平整重新評估，並核對整個經測試系統而不是僅一個底座比值。","textEn":"Check friction evidence against actual wetness, contamination and surface condition and track whether uplift has already been deducted in weight. Reassess blocked drainage, surface erosion and unevenness, checking the tested complete system rather than relying on one isolated base resistance ratio.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用兩種假設揚壓比較有效法向力和滑動比，再列出未檢查的失效模式。說明為何改變底座重量或表面配置，需要重新核對完整系統的證明資料。","textEn":"Compare effective normal load and sliding ratio at two hypothetical uplifts, listing unchecked failure modes. Explain why changing base weight or surface preparation requires renewed review of evidence for the complete system configuration.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「重力式底座與滑動尺度機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gravity-base sliding scale mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","確認摩擦資料與實際濕潤、污染和表面條件相容，追蹤揚壓是否已在重量定義中扣除。","任意增加一倍人力，所有部署流程的總時間就必定減半。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check friction evidence against actual wetness, contamination and surface condition and track whether uplift has already been deducted in weight.","Doubling staff anywhere necessarily halves the total duration of every deployment process."],"answer":1,"explanation":"確認摩擦資料與實際濕潤、污染和表面條件相容，追蹤揚壓是否已在重量定義中扣除。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check friction evidence against actual wetness, contamination and surface condition and track whether uplift has already been deducted in weight. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b275-v15-20","title":"重力式底座與滑動尺度機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gravity-base sliding scale mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「重力式底座與滑動尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gravity-base sliding scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略泥砂潤滑可能高估摩擦，將乾地試驗係數當成固定材料常數也會失真；只為增加自重而疊放未經核對的重物，還可能改變基礎承載和構件受力方式。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting lubricating silt can overstate friction, and treating a dry-test coefficient as a universal material constant is misleading. Adding unverified ballast solely for weight can also change bearing demands and the intended loading of individual components. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例是單一假設底座的庫侖摩擦尺度，向下重量尚未扣揚壓，無錨定與被動土抗力；比值不是任何產品額定值或安裝許可。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Gross weight excludes uplift deduction and no anchors or passive soil resistance are credited; the ratio is neither a product rating nor installation approval.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「增加自重一定能解決所有臨時防洪系統的滑動、滲水與承載問題。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Added weight necessarily solves every sliding, seepage and bearing problem of a temporary barrier.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略泥砂潤滑可能高估摩擦，將乾地試驗係數當成固定材料常數也會失真；只為增加自重而疊放未經核對的重物，還可能改變基礎承載和構件受力方式。","textEn":"Omitting lubricating silt can overstate friction, and treating a dry-test coefficient as a universal material constant is misleading. Adding unverified ballast solely for weight can also change bearing demands and the intended loading of individual components.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「重力式底座與滑動尺度機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gravity-base sliding scale mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","密封條只要算出正的壓縮量，就已證明接觸壓力足夠且完全不漏水。","忽略泥砂潤滑可能高估摩擦，將乾地試驗係數當成固定材料常數也會失真；只為增加自重而疊放未經核對的重物，還可能改變基礎承載和構件受力方式。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Any positive calculated seal compression proves adequate contact pressure and zero leakage.","Omitting lubricating silt can overstate friction, and treating a dry-test coefficient as a universal material constant is misleading."],"answer":2,"explanation":"忽略泥砂潤滑可能高估摩擦，將乾地試驗係數當成固定材料常數也會失真；只為增加自重而疊放未經核對的重物，還可能改變基礎承載和構件受力方式。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting lubricating silt can overstate friction, and treating a dry-test coefficient as a universal material constant is misleading. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b275-v15-21","title":"密封壓縮與幾何公差機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Seal compression and geometric tolerance mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「密封壓縮與幾何公差」如何影響移動式防洪擋板部署的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Seal compression and geometric tolerance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Deployable flood-barrier systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"接頭密封需要適當壓縮和連續接觸，板面變形、地面不平與裝配誤差會消耗幾何餘量。壓縮量可以從厚度和間隙求得，但接觸壓力取決於材料曲線、溫度、老化與壓縮歷程；只看到正壓縮不能保證水密，也不能任意增加鎖緊量而忽略構件和密封件的限制。本例僅計算均勻密封條的幾何壓縮率，未指定材料本構或可用範圍；不得由此推定接觸壓力、鎖緊力或水密等級。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「密封壓縮與幾何公差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Seals require suitable compression and continuous contact. Panel movement, uneven ground and assembly errors consume geometric allowance. Thickness and gap give compression, but contact pressure depends on material curves, temperature, aging and loading history. Positive compression does not prove watertightness, and additional tightening cannot ignore component or seal limits and verified installation procedures. The example computes geometric compression of a uniform seal only, without constitutive behavior or an acceptable range. It cannot establish contact pressure, tightening force or a watertightness rating. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Seal compression and geometric tolerance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設自由厚度t0=12 mm、安裝間隙g=9 mm，壓縮量c=t0−g=3 mm，壓縮率c/t0=25%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume free seal thickness t0=12 mm and installed gap g=9 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「密封條只要算出正的壓縮量，就已證明接觸壓力足夠且完全不漏水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any positive calculated seal compression proves adequate contact pressure and zero leakage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「密封壓縮與幾何公差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Seal compression and geometric tolerance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-21-k1","title":"密封壓縮與幾何公差機理與驗證","titleEn":"Seal compression and geometric tolerance mechanism and verification","text":"接頭密封需要適當壓縮和連續接觸，板面變形、地面不平與裝配誤差會消耗幾何餘量。壓縮量可以從厚度和間隙求得，但接觸壓力取決於材料曲線、溫度、老化與壓縮歷程；只看到正壓縮不能保證水密，也不能任意增加鎖緊量而忽略構件和密封件的限制。","textEn":"Seals require suitable compression and continuous contact. Panel movement, uneven ground and assembly errors consume geometric allowance.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：密封條只要算出正的壓縮量，就已證明接觸壓力足夠且完全不漏水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any positive calculated seal compression proves adequate contact pressure and zero leakage. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「密封壓縮與幾何公差機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Seal compression and geometric tolerance mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["接頭密封需要適當壓縮和連續接觸，板面變形、地面不平與裝配誤差會消耗幾何餘量。","密封條只要算出正的壓縮量，就已證明接觸壓力足夠且完全不漏水。","擋板閉合後只要任何一台泵在運轉，內側水位就一定不會上升。"],"optionsEn":["Seals require suitable compression and continuous contact.","Any positive calculated seal compression proves adequate contact pressure and zero leakage.","Once barriers close, any running pump guarantees that interior water level cannot rise."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接頭密封需要適當壓縮和連續接觸，板面變形、地面不平與裝配誤差會消耗幾何餘量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Seals require suitable compression and continuous contact. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b275-v15-22","title":"密封壓縮與幾何公差機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Seal compression and geometric tolerance mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「密封壓縮與幾何公差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Seal compression and geometric tolerance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設自由厚度t0=12 mm、安裝間隙g=9 mm，壓縮量c=t0−g=3 mm，壓縮率c/t0=25%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume free seal thickness t0=12 mm and installed gap g=9 mm. Geometric compression c=3 mm and compression fraction c/t0=25%. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測密封條與槽口狀態、連續性及實際間隙，核對指定材料在相應溫度和老化下的性能曲線。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure seal and groove condition, continuity and actual gap and check specified material curves at relevant temperature and aging.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設自由厚度t0=12 mm、安裝間隙g=9 mm，壓縮量c=t0−g=3 mm，壓縮率c/t0=25%。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume free seal thickness t0=12 mm and installed gap g=9 mm. Geometric compression c=3 mm and compression fraction c/t0=25%.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「密封壓縮與幾何公差機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Seal compression and geometric tolerance mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["四個必要環節各有百分之九十八成功率，整個流程就必定也是百分之九十八。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設自由厚度t0=12 mm、安裝間隙g=9 mm，壓縮量c=t0−g=3 mm，壓縮率c/t0=25%。","只要擋板組裝時間短於洪峰到達時間，就一定來得及安全部署。"],"optionsEn":["Four necessary stages each succeeding ninety-eight percent make the entire process ninety-eight percent reliable.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume free seal thickness t0=12 mm and installed gap g=9 mm.","Assembly shorter than time to the flood crest guarantees timely and safe deployment."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設自由厚度t0=12 mm、安裝間隙g=9 mm，壓縮量c=t0−g=3 mm，壓縮率c/t0=25%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume free seal thickness t0=12 mm and installed gap g=9 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b275-v15-23","title":"密封壓縮與幾何公差機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Seal compression and geometric tolerance mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「密封壓縮與幾何公差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Seal compression and geometric tolerance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測密封條與槽口狀態、連續性及實際間隙，核對指定材料在相應溫度和老化下的性能曲線。用完整接頭壓差試驗及受控檢查驗證漏水，不將單一幾何比值替代製造商程序。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure seal and groove condition, continuity and actual gap and check specified material curves at relevant temperature and aging. Verify leakage through complete-joint differential-pressure tests and controlled inspection rather than substituting a geometric percentage for the documented system installation procedure. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：給三處不同間隙計算壓縮率並找出最不利位置，另列所缺材料曲線。說明為何需要全接頭測試，以及幾何量測和水密驗證是兩種不同證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate compression at three different gaps and identify the limiting location, listing missing material curves. Explain the need for complete-joint testing and distinguish geometric measurements from evidence of sealing performance under pressure.","failure":"注意干擾：地面顆粒可能形成局部未接觸通道，過度壓縮也可能損傷密封或讓板柱受力異常；把名義厚度當每處實際厚度，則會漏掉老化、永久變形和接頭轉角的影響。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Particles under a seal can create local noncontact paths, while excessive compression may damage it or alter panel/post loading. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測密封條與槽口狀態、連續性及實際間隙，核對指定材料在相應溫度和老化下的性能曲線。用完整接頭壓差試驗及受控檢查驗證漏水，不將單一幾何比值替代製造商程序。","textEn":"Measure seal and groove condition, continuity and actual gap and check specified material curves at relevant temperature and aging. Verify leakage through complete-joint differential-pressure tests and controlled inspection rather than substituting a geometric percentage for the documented system installation procedure.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"給三處不同間隙計算壓縮率並找出最不利位置，另列所缺材料曲線。說明為何需要全接頭測試，以及幾何量測和水密驗證是兩種不同證據。","textEn":"Calculate compression at three different gaps and identify the limiting location, listing missing material curves. Explain the need for complete-joint testing and distinguish geometric measurements from evidence of sealing performance under pressure.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「密封壓縮與幾何公差機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Seal compression and geometric tolerance mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","只要總件數和總重量足夠，就能保證每個區段的構件都相容。","量測密封條與槽口狀態、連續性及實際間隙，核對指定材料在相應溫度和老化下的性能曲線。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Sufficient total count and mass guarantee compatible components for every barrier section.","Measure seal and groove condition, continuity and actual gap and check specified material curves at relevant temperature and aging."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測密封條與槽口狀態、連續性及實際間隙，核對指定材料在相應溫度和老化下的性能曲線。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure seal and groove condition, continuity and actual gap and check specified material curves at relevant temperature and aging. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b275-v15-24","title":"密封壓縮與幾何公差機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Seal compression and geometric tolerance mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「密封壓縮與幾何公差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Seal compression and geometric tolerance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"地面顆粒可能形成局部未接觸通道，過度壓縮也可能損傷密封或讓板柱受力異常；把名義厚度當每處實際厚度，則會漏掉老化、永久變形和接頭轉角的影響。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Particles under a seal can create local noncontact paths, while excessive compression may damage it or alter panel/post loading. Assuming nominal thickness everywhere misses aging, permanent set and joint rotation that affect the actual contact geometry. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例僅計算均勻密封條的幾何壓縮率，未指定材料本構或可用範圍；不得由此推定接觸壓力、鎖緊力或水密等級。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It cannot establish contact pressure, tightening force or a watertightness rating.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「密封條只要算出正的壓縮量，就已證明接觸壓力足夠且完全不漏水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any positive calculated seal compression proves adequate contact pressure and zero leakage.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"地面顆粒可能形成局部未接觸通道，過度壓縮也可能損傷密封或讓板柱受力異常；把名義厚度當每處實際厚度，則會漏掉老化、永久變形和接頭轉角的影響。","textEn":"Particles under a seal can create local noncontact paths, while excessive compression may damage it or alter panel/post loading. Assuming nominal thickness everywhere misses aging, permanent set and joint rotation that affect the actual contact geometry.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「密封壓縮與幾何公差機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Seal compression and geometric tolerance mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["地面顆粒可能形成局部未接觸通道，過度壓縮也可能損傷密封或讓板柱受力異常；把名義厚度當每處實際厚度，則會漏掉老化、永久變形和接頭轉角的影響。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","擋板閉合後只要任何一台泵在運轉，內側水位就一定不會上升。"],"optionsEn":["Particles under a seal can create local noncontact paths, while excessive compression may damage it or alter panel/post loading.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Once barriers close, any running pump guarantees that interior water level cannot rise."],"answer":0,"explanation":"地面顆粒可能形成局部未接觸通道，過度壓縮也可能損傷密封或讓板柱受力異常；把名義厚度當每處實際厚度，則會漏掉老化、永久變形和接頭轉角的影響。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Particles under a seal can create local noncontact paths, while excessive compression may damage it or alter panel/post loading. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b275-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「殘餘滲漏與抽排緩衝機理與驗證」與「端部接續與最低高程機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Residual leakage and pumping buffer mechanism and verification\" and \"End tie-ins and minimum elevation mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b275-v15-25","title":"殘餘滲漏與抽排緩衝機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Residual leakage and pumping buffer mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「殘餘滲漏與抽排緩衝」如何影響移動式防洪擋板部署的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Residual leakage and pumping buffer” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Deployable flood-barrier systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"已閉合的擋板仍可能由密封、地層或地下管線滲水，防線後方降雨也會增加積水，因此抽排與暫存是系統的一部分。水量平衡要納入所有進出路徑及泵的實際揚程工作點，不能以名牌流量保證內側不積水；停電或排出口被外河淹沒時還可能改變有效能力。本例入流和抽排量均為固定的假設實際流率，暫存池面積固定，未含背側降雨或外河變化；只算短時水位變化尺度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「殘餘滲漏與抽排緩衝」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A closed barrier may leak through seals, soil or buried services, and rainfall behind it adds water. Pumping and storage therefore belong to the system. Balance all paths using the pump’s actual head-dependent operating point rather than nameplate flow; power loss or a submerged outfall can further alter effective removal during a flood event. Inflows and pumping are hypothetical constant actual rates with fixed storage area, excluding rainfall and changing river stage. This is a short-duration water-level scale only. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Residual leakage and pumping buffer” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總滲入Qi=0.012 m³/s、抽排Qp=0.008 m³/s、t=1800 s、池面積A=40 m²，Δh=(Qi−Qp)t/A=0.18 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume leakage Qi=0.012 m³/s, pumping Qp=0.008 m³/s, time t=1800 s and storage area A=40 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「擋板閉合後只要任何一台泵在運轉，內側水位就一定不會上升。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once barriers close, any running pump guarantees that interior water level cannot rise.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「殘餘滲漏與抽排緩衝」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Residual leakage and pumping buffer”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-25-k1","title":"殘餘滲漏與抽排緩衝機理與驗證","titleEn":"Residual leakage and pumping buffer mechanism and verification","text":"已閉合的擋板仍可能由密封、地層或地下管線滲水，防線後方降雨也會增加積水，因此抽排與暫存是系統的一部分。水量平衡要納入所有進出路徑及泵的實際揚程工作點，不能以名牌流量保證內側不積水；停電或排出口被外河淹沒時還可能改變有效能力。","textEn":"A closed barrier may leak through seals, soil or buried services, and rainfall behind it adds water. Pumping and storage therefore belong to the system.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：擋板閉合後只要任何一台泵在運轉，內側水位就一定不會上升。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once barriers close, any running pump guarantees that interior water level cannot rise. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「殘餘滲漏與抽排緩衝機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Residual leakage and pumping buffer mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["擋板閉合後只要任何一台泵在運轉，內側水位就一定不會上升。","已閉合的擋板仍可能由密封、地層或地下管線滲水，防線後方降雨也會增加積水，因此抽排與暫存是系統的一部分。","每塊擋板的額定高度足夠，就不需要檢查兩端與地下開口的連續性。"],"optionsEn":["Once barriers close, any running pump guarantees that interior water level cannot rise.","A closed barrier may leak through seals, soil or buried services, and rainfall behind it adds water.","Adequate rated height of every panel removes the need to check ends and buried openings."],"answer":1,"explanation":"已閉合的擋板仍可能由密封、地層或地下管線滲水，防線後方降雨也會增加積水，因此抽排與暫存是系統的一部分。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A closed barrier may leak through seals, soil or buried services, and rainfall behind it adds water. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b275-v15-26","title":"殘餘滲漏與抽排緩衝機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Residual leakage and pumping buffer mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「殘餘滲漏與抽排緩衝」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Residual leakage and pumping buffer” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總滲入Qi=0.012 m³/s、抽排Qp=0.008 m³/s、t=1800 s、池面積A=40 m²，Δh=(Qi−Qp)t/A=0.18 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume leakage Qi=0.012 m³/s, pumping Qp=0.008 m³/s, time t=1800 s and storage area A=40 m². Rise Δh=(Qi−Qp)t/A=0.18 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：盤點密封、地下管線和地表降雨的入流路徑，量測實際泵流量及內外水位。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Inventory inflow through seals, services and rainfall and measure actual pumping and both water levels.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總滲入Qi=0.012 m³/s、抽排Qp=0.008 m³/s、t=1800 s、池面積A=40 m²，Δh=(Qi−Qp)t/A=0.18 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume leakage Qi=0.012 m³/s, pumping Qp=0.008 m³/s, time t=1800 s and storage area A=40 m². Rise Δh=(Qi−Qp)t/A=0.18 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「殘餘滲漏與抽排緩衝機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Residual leakage and pumping buffer mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["三十次演練都成功，就能用統計方法證明未來失敗機率恰好為零。","任意增加一倍人力，所有部署流程的總時間就必定減半。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總滲入Qi=0.012 m³/s、抽排Qp=0.008 m³/s、t=1800 s、池面積A=40 m²，Δh=(Qi−Qp)t/A=0.18 m。"],"optionsEn":["Thirty successful exercises statistically prove that future failure probability is exactly zero.","Doubling staff anywhere necessarily halves the total duration of every deployment process.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume leakage Qi=0.012 m³/s, pumping Qp=0.008 m³/s, time t=1800 s and storage area A=40 m²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設總滲入Qi=0.012 m³/s、抽排Qp=0.008 m³/s、t=1800 s、池面積A=40 m²，Δh=(Qi−Qp)t/A=0.18 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume leakage Qi=0.012 m³/s, pumping Qp=0.008 m³/s, time t=1800 s and storage area A=40 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b275-v15-27","title":"殘餘滲漏與抽排緩衝機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Residual leakage and pumping buffer mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「殘餘滲漏與抽排緩衝」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Residual leakage and pumping buffer” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"盤點密封、地下管線和地表降雨的入流路徑，量測實際泵流量及內外水位。檢查電源、出水管和逆止配置，再以停泵或外水抬升情境比較可用儲水時間，而不是只記錄泵已啟動。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Inventory inflow through seals, services and rainfall and measure actual pumping and both water levels. Check power, discharge piping and backflow control, comparing storage time under pump failure or raised tailwater instead of recording only whether the pump motor is running. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將滲水、降雨和抽排分列水量帳，計算固定面積池的短時水位變化。再設定一台泵失效，指出何時需要重新計算實際揚程和可用通行時間。","observationEn":"Site practice: Separate leakage, rainfall and pumping in a water ledger and calculate short-term rise in fixed-area storage. Add a pump outage and identify when actual head and remaining access time must be recalculated.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略地下排水管回流會低估入流，泵啟動但不在預期工作點也可能抽不出名牌流量；如果儲水區還承擔通行，水量雖小仍可能先破壞人員和設備的可用路線。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitted drain backflow understates inflow, and an operating pump may deliver less than its rated flow at the actual head. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"盤點密封、地下管線和地表降雨的入流路徑，量測實際泵流量及內外水位。檢查電源、出水管和逆止配置，再以停泵或外水抬升情境比較可用儲水時間，而不是只記錄泵已啟動。","textEn":"Inventory inflow through seals, services and rainfall and measure actual pumping and both water levels. Check power, discharge piping and backflow control, comparing storage time under pump failure or raised tailwater instead of recording only whether the pump motor is running.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將滲水、降雨和抽排分列水量帳，計算固定面積池的短時水位變化。再設定一台泵失效，指出何時需要重新計算實際揚程和可用通行時間。","textEn":"Separate leakage, rainfall and pumping in a water ledger and calculate short-term rise in fixed-area storage. Add a pump outage and identify when actual head and remaining access time must be recalculated.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「殘餘滲漏與抽排緩衝機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Residual leakage and pumping buffer mechanism and verification\"?","options":["盤點密封、地下管線和地表降雨的入流路徑，量測實際泵流量及內外水位。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","板材能承受水壓，就能自動證明立柱底座與地基也完全足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Inventory inflow through seals, services and rainfall and measure actual pumping and both water levels.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A panel resisting water pressure automatically proves its post base and foundation adequate."],"answer":0,"explanation":"盤點密封、地下管線和地表降雨的入流路徑，量測實際泵流量及內外水位。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Inventory inflow through seals, services and rainfall and measure actual pumping and both water levels. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b275-v15-28","title":"殘餘滲漏與抽排緩衝機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Residual leakage and pumping buffer mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「殘餘滲漏與抽排緩衝」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Residual leakage and pumping buffer” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略地下排水管回流會低估入流，泵啟動但不在預期工作點也可能抽不出名牌流量；如果儲水區還承擔通行，水量雖小仍可能先破壞人員和設備的可用路線。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitted drain backflow understates inflow, and an operating pump may deliver less than its rated flow at the actual head. Storage occupying an access route can also disrupt personnel and equipment before the accumulated volume appears large. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例入流和抽排量均為固定的假設實際流率，暫存池面積固定，未含背側降雨或外河變化；只算短時水位變化尺度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This is a short-duration water-level scale only.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「擋板閉合後只要任何一台泵在運轉，內側水位就一定不會上升。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once barriers close, any running pump guarantees that interior water level cannot rise.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略地下排水管回流會低估入流，泵啟動但不在預期工作點也可能抽不出名牌流量；如果儲水區還承擔通行，水量雖小仍可能先破壞人員和設備的可用路線。","textEn":"Omitted drain backflow understates inflow, and an operating pump may deliver less than its rated flow at the actual head. Storage occupying an access route can also disrupt personnel and equipment before the accumulated volume appears large.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「殘餘滲漏與抽排緩衝機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Residual leakage and pumping buffer mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","忽略地下排水管回流會低估入流，泵啟動但不在預期工作點也可能抽不出名牌流量；如果儲水區還承擔通行，水量雖小仍可能先破壞人員和設備的可用路線。","每塊擋板的額定高度足夠，就不需要檢查兩端與地下開口的連續性。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Omitted drain backflow understates inflow, and an operating pump may deliver less than its rated flow at the actual head.","Adequate rated height of every panel removes the need to check ends and buried openings."],"answer":1,"explanation":"忽略地下排水管回流會低估入流，泵啟動但不在預期工作點也可能抽不出名牌流量；如果儲水區還承擔通行，水量雖小仍可能先破壞人員和設備的可用路線。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitted drain backflow understates inflow, and an operating pump may deliver less than its rated flow at the actual head. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b275-v15-29","title":"端部接續與最低高程機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"End tie-ins and minimum elevation mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「端部接續與最低高程」如何影響移動式防洪擋板部署的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “End tie-ins and minimum elevation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Deployable flood-barrier systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水可以繞過防線端部或從低點進入，即使每塊板本身都達到高度與強度要求，整體仍可能未形成封閉邊界。測量應追蹤連續路線、建築介面、路口和地下開口，將共同高程基準上的最低有效防護點與水位比較；平均高度或最高構件不能代表系統的限制位置。本例只比較三個已確認連續接合點的幾何高程，不含波浪、沉陷或模型誤差預留；正餘量不代表結構、滲流和營運全部通過。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「端部接續與最低高程」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Water can outflank the ends or enter at a low point even when every panel meets its individual height and strength requirements. Survey the continuous route, building interfaces, road openings and buried penetrations. Compare stage with the lowest effective defence point on one datum; average elevation or the tallest component does not define the system’s limiting location. The example compares three assumed continuous tie-in elevations only, without wave, settlement or uncertainty allowances. Positive margin does not establish structural, seepage and operational acceptance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “End tie-ins and minimum elevation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設三處有效頂高102.0、101.7、101.9 m，水面101.5 m，最小幾何餘量F=min(Z)−Zw=0.20 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective crest elevations 102.0, 101.7 and 101.9 m with water level 101.5 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「每塊擋板的額定高度足夠，就不需要檢查兩端與地下開口的連續性。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate rated height of every panel removes the need to check ends and buried openings.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「端部接續與最低高程」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “End tie-ins and minimum elevation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-29-k1","title":"端部接續與最低高程機理與驗證","titleEn":"End tie-ins and minimum elevation mechanism and verification","text":"水可以繞過防線端部或從低點進入，即使每塊板本身都達到高度與強度要求，整體仍可能未形成封閉邊界。測量應追蹤連續路線、建築介面、路口和地下開口，將共同高程基準上的最低有效防護點與水位比較；平均高度或最高構件不能代表系統的限制位置。","textEn":"Water can outflank the ends or enter at a low point even when every panel meets its individual height and strength requirements. Survey the continuous route, building interfaces, road openings and buried penetrations.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每塊擋板的額定高度足夠，就不需要檢查兩端與地下開口的連續性。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate rated height of every panel removes the need to check ends and buried openings. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「端部接續與最低高程機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"End tie-ins and minimum elevation mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["每塊擋板的額定高度足夠，就不需要檢查兩端與地下開口的連續性。","四個必要環節各有百分之九十八成功率，整個流程就必定也是百分之九十八。","水可以繞過防線端部或從低點進入，即使每塊板本身都達到高度與強度要求，整體仍可能未形成封閉邊界。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate rated height of every panel removes the need to check ends and buried openings.","Four necessary stages each succeeding ninety-eight percent make the entire process ninety-eight percent reliable.","Water can outflank the ends or enter at a low point even when every panel meets its individual height and strength requirements."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水可以繞過防線端部或從低點進入，即使每塊板本身都達到高度與強度要求，整體仍可能未形成封閉邊界。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Water can outflank the ends or enter at a low point even when every panel meets its individual height and strength requirements. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b275-v15-30","title":"端部接續與最低高程機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"End tie-ins and minimum elevation mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「端部接續與最低高程」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “End tie-ins and minimum elevation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設三處有效頂高102.0、101.7、101.9 m，水面101.5 m，最小幾何餘量F=min(Z)−Zw=0.20 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective crest elevations 102.0, 101.7 and 101.9 m with water level 101.5 m. Minimum geometric margin F=min(Z)−Zw=0.20 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿整條防線實測端點、門洞與局部低點，確認與水位使用同一基準。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey ends, openings and local lows along the complete line using the same datum as water stage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設三處有效頂高102.0、101.7、101.9 m，水面101.5 m，最小幾何餘量F=min(Z)−Zw=0.20 m。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective crest elevations 102.0, 101.7 and 101.9 m with water level 101.5 m. Minimum geometric margin F=min(Z)−Zw=0.20 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「端部接續與最低高程機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"End tie-ins and minimum elevation mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設三處有效頂高102.0、101.7、101.9 m，水面101.5 m，最小幾何餘量F=min(Z)−Zw=0.20 m。","只要擋板組裝時間短於洪峰到達時間，就一定來得及安全部署。","只要總件數和總重量足夠，就能保證每個區段的構件都相容。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective crest elevations 102.0, 101.7 and 101.9 m with water level 101.5 m.","Assembly shorter than time to the flood crest guarantees timely and safe deployment.","Sufficient total count and mass guarantee compatible components for every barrier section."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設三處有效頂高102.0、101.7、101.9 m，水面101.5 m，最小幾何餘量F=min(Z)−Zw=0.20 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective crest elevations 102.0, 101.7 and 101.9 m with water level 101.5 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b275-v15-31","title":"端部接續與最低高程機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"End tie-ins and minimum elevation mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「端部接續與最低高程」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “End tie-ins and minimum elevation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿整條防線實測端點、門洞與局部低點，確認與水位使用同一基準。逐段查驗接續和地下穿越，將幾何餘量、波浪預留及其他失效模式分列，不以一張平均高度表代替現場閉合確認。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey ends, openings and local lows along the complete line using the same datum as water stage. Verify transitions and buried crossings segment by segment, separating geometric margin, wave allowance and other failure modes instead of substituting an average-height table for physical closure confirmation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出一條包含路口、建築和端部高地的防線，找最低有效高程並加上未封閉管線。分別說明越頂、繞流和地下回流，為每一種安排不同的閉合證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw a line crossing roads, buildings and high ground, identify the lowest effective elevation and add an open service pipe. Distinguish overtopping, outflanking and underground backflow and assign different closure evidence to each pathway.","failure":"注意干擾：只看最高擋板會漏掉端部低地，跨越道路或建築接點未密合也可能形成繞流；基準混用則讓表面上正的餘量消失，與板材本身的強度高低無關。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Checking the tallest panel misses low ground at an end. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿整條防線實測端點、門洞與局部低點，確認與水位使用同一基準。逐段查驗接續和地下穿越，將幾何餘量、波浪預留及其他失效模式分列，不以一張平均高度表代替現場閉合確認。","textEn":"Survey ends, openings and local lows along the complete line using the same datum as water stage. Verify transitions and buried crossings segment by segment, separating geometric margin, wave allowance and other failure modes instead of substituting an average-height table for physical closure confirmation.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出一條包含路口、建築和端部高地的防線，找最低有效高程並加上未封閉管線。分別說明越頂、繞流和地下回流，為每一種安排不同的閉合證據。","textEn":"Draw a line crossing roads, buildings and high ground, identify the lowest effective elevation and add an open service pipe. Distinguish overtopping, outflanking and underground backflow and assign different closure evidence to each pathway.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「端部接續與最低高程機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"End tie-ins and minimum elevation mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","沿整條防線實測端點、門洞與局部低點，確認與水位使用同一基準。","增加自重一定能解決所有臨時防洪系統的滑動、滲水與承載問題。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Survey ends, openings and local lows along the complete line using the same datum as water stage.","Added weight necessarily solves every sliding, seepage and bearing problem of a temporary barrier."],"answer":1,"explanation":"沿整條防線實測端點、門洞與局部低點，確認與水位使用同一基準。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey ends, openings and local lows along the complete line using the same datum as water stage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b275-v15-32","title":"端部接續與最低高程機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"End tie-ins and minimum elevation mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「端部接續與最低高程」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “End tie-ins and minimum elevation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只看最高擋板會漏掉端部低地，跨越道路或建築接點未密合也可能形成繞流；基準混用則讓表面上正的餘量消失，與板材本身的強度高低無關。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Checking the tallest panel misses low ground at an end. Unsealed road or building transitions create bypass paths, and mixed elevation datums can erase an apparently positive margin regardless of the structural strength of the panels themselves. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例只比較三個已確認連續接合點的幾何高程，不含波浪、沉陷或模型誤差預留；正餘量不代表結構、滲流和營運全部通過。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Positive margin does not establish structural, seepage and operational acceptance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每塊擋板的額定高度足夠，就不需要檢查兩端與地下開口的連續性。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate rated height of every panel removes the need to check ends and buried openings.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只看最高擋板會漏掉端部低地，跨越道路或建築接點未密合也可能形成繞流；基準混用則讓表面上正的餘量消失，與板材本身的強度高低無關。","textEn":"Checking the tallest panel misses low ground at an end. Unsealed road or building transitions create bypass paths, and mixed elevation datums can erase an apparently positive margin regardless of the structural strength of the panels themselves.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「端部接續與最低高程機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"End tie-ins and minimum elevation mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","四個必要環節各有百分之九十八成功率，整個流程就必定也是百分之九十八。","只看最高擋板會漏掉端部低地，跨越道路或建築接點未密合也可能形成繞流；基準混用則讓表面上正的餘量消失，與板材本身的強度高低無關。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Four necessary stages each succeeding ninety-eight percent make the entire process ninety-eight percent reliable.","Checking the tallest panel misses low ground at an end."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只看最高擋板會漏掉端部低地，跨越道路或建築接點未密合也可能形成繞流；基準混用則讓表面上正的餘量消失，與板材本身的強度高低無關。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Checking the tallest panel misses low ground at an end. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b275-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「閉合流程可靠度機理與驗證」與「演練證據與失敗率界限機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Closure-process reliability mechanism and verification\" and \"Exercise evidence and failure-rate bounds mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b275-v15-33","title":"閉合流程可靠度機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Closure-process reliability mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「閉合流程可靠度」如何影響移動式防洪擋板部署的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Closure-process reliability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Deployable flood-barrier systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"完整部署依賴預報、通知、到場、組裝與查驗等多個必要環節，一個環節失敗就可能無法及時閉合。獨立串聯系統的成功率是各階段成功率相乘，但真實洪水可能同時影響電力、道路和人員，產生共同原因失效；乘積只能在獨立假設下使用，且成功部署還不等於洪水期間結構永不失效。本例只設四個必要且相互獨立的操作環節，各成功率為指定假設；未包含共同原因或洪水荷載超標，不是任何城市的實測可靠度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「閉合流程可靠度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Timely closure depends on several necessary stages such as forecast, alert, arrival, assembly and inspection. Failure of one can prevent completion. Independent series success is the product of stage probabilities, but a flood can jointly affect power, roads and staff. Multiplication therefore requires independence, and successful deployment remains distinct from structural survival throughout the event. The example specifies four necessary independent operational stages with assumed success rates. Common causes and load exceedance are excluded; this is not measured reliability for any city. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Closure-process reliability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設四個獨立必要環節成功率皆p=0.98，完整操作成功率P=p⁴=0.92236816，即92.2368%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume four independent necessary stages, each with success probability p=0.98.","failure":"常見誤解：「四個必要環節各有百分之九十八成功率，整個流程就必定也是百分之九十八。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Four necessary stages each succeeding ninety-eight percent make the entire process ninety-eight percent reliable.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「閉合流程可靠度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Closure-process reliability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-33-k1","title":"閉合流程可靠度機理與驗證","titleEn":"Closure-process reliability mechanism and verification","text":"完整部署依賴預報、通知、到場、組裝與查驗等多個必要環節，一個環節失敗就可能無法及時閉合。獨立串聯系統的成功率是各階段成功率相乘，但真實洪水可能同時影響電力、道路和人員，產生共同原因失效；乘積只能在獨立假設下使用，且成功部署還不等於洪水期間結構永不失效。","textEn":"Timely closure depends on several necessary stages such as forecast, alert, arrival, assembly and inspection. Failure of one can prevent completion.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：四個必要環節各有百分之九十八成功率，整個流程就必定也是百分之九十八。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Four necessary stages each succeeding ninety-eight percent make the entire process ninety-eight percent reliable. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「閉合流程可靠度機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Closure-process reliability mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["完整部署依賴預報、通知、到場、組裝與查驗等多個必要環節，一個環節失敗就可能無法及時閉合。","四個必要環節各有百分之九十八成功率，整個流程就必定也是百分之九十八。","三十次演練都成功，就能用統計方法證明未來失敗機率恰好為零。"],"optionsEn":["Timely closure depends on several necessary stages such as forecast, alert, arrival, assembly and inspection.","Four necessary stages each succeeding ninety-eight percent make the entire process ninety-eight percent reliable.","Thirty successful exercises statistically prove that future failure probability is exactly zero."],"answer":0,"explanation":"完整部署依賴預報、通知、到場、組裝與查驗等多個必要環節，一個環節失敗就可能無法及時閉合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Timely closure depends on several necessary stages such as forecast, alert, arrival, assembly and inspection. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b275-v15-34","title":"閉合流程可靠度機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Closure-process reliability mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「閉合流程可靠度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Closure-process reliability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設四個獨立必要環節成功率皆p=0.98，完整操作成功率P=p⁴=0.92236816，即92.2368%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume four independent necessary stages, each with success probability p=0.98. Complete operational success P=p⁴=0.92236816, or 92.2368%. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：明列成功事件與條件機率的定義，檢查是否由同一電源、道路或人員造成相關性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Define success events and conditional probabilities and inspect shared power, routes and staff for dependence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設四個獨立必要環節成功率皆p=0.98，完整操作成功率P=p⁴=0.92236816，即92.2368%。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume four independent necessary stages, each with success probability p=0.98. Complete operational success P=p⁴=0.92236816, or 92.2368%.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「閉合流程可靠度機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Closure-process reliability mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["任意增加一倍人力，所有部署流程的總時間就必定減半。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設四個獨立必要環節成功率皆p=0.98，完整操作成功率P=p⁴=0.92236816，即92.2368%。","板材能承受水壓，就能自動證明立柱底座與地基也完全足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling staff anywhere necessarily halves the total duration of every deployment process.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume four independent necessary stages, each with success probability p=0.98.","A panel resisting water pressure automatically proves its post base and foundation adequate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設四個獨立必要環節成功率皆p=0.98，完整操作成功率P=p⁴=0.92236816，即92.2368%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume four independent necessary stages, each with success probability p=0.98. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b275-v15-35","title":"閉合流程可靠度機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Closure-process reliability mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「閉合流程可靠度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Closure-process reliability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"明列成功事件與條件機率的定義，檢查是否由同一電源、道路或人員造成相關性。用演練及事件資料估計各階段而非任意填值，另列荷載超標和部署後失效，避免把不同可靠度範圍混合。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Define success events and conditional probabilities and inspect shared power, routes and staff for dependence. Estimate stages from exercises and events rather than arbitrary values, separating load exceedance and post-deployment failure instead of merging distinct reliability scopes into one misleading percentage. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：先以獨立模型計算完整成功率，再加入一個同時阻斷所有車輛的共同道路事件。畫出失效樹並指出哪些備援真正獨立，哪些只增加數量而沒有增加路徑多樣性。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate independent success, then add one shared road event that blocks every vehicle. Draw a failure tree and identify genuinely independent backups versus resources that add quantity without diversity of access routes.","failure":"注意干擾：取各階段成功率平均值會高估全部必要事件同時成功，直接相乘相關機率也可能失真；重複備援若共用同一路線，仍會在道路中斷時一起失去作用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Averaging stage success overstates the probability that all necessary events occur. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"明列成功事件與條件機率的定義，檢查是否由同一電源、道路或人員造成相關性。用演練及事件資料估計各階段而非任意填值，另列荷載超標和部署後失效，避免把不同可靠度範圍混合。","textEn":"Define success events and conditional probabilities and inspect shared power, routes and staff for dependence. Estimate stages from exercises and events rather than arbitrary values, separating load exceedance and post-deployment failure instead of merging distinct reliability scopes into one misleading percentage.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"先以獨立模型計算完整成功率，再加入一個同時阻斷所有車輛的共同道路事件。畫出失效樹並指出哪些備援真正獨立，哪些只增加數量而沒有增加路徑多樣性。","textEn":"Calculate independent success, then add one shared road event that blocks every vehicle. Draw a failure tree and identify genuinely independent backups versus resources that add quantity without diversity of access routes.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「閉合流程可靠度機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Closure-process reliability mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","密封條只要算出正的壓縮量，就已證明接觸壓力足夠且完全不漏水。","明列成功事件與條件機率的定義，檢查是否由同一電源、道路或人員造成相關性。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Any positive calculated seal compression proves adequate contact pressure and zero leakage.","Define success events and conditional probabilities and inspect shared power, routes and staff for dependence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"明列成功事件與條件機率的定義，檢查是否由同一電源、道路或人員造成相關性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Define success events and conditional probabilities and inspect shared power, routes and staff for dependence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b275-v15-36","title":"閉合流程可靠度機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Closure-process reliability mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「閉合流程可靠度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Closure-process reliability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"取各階段成功率平均值會高估全部必要事件同時成功，直接相乘相關機率也可能失真；重複備援若共用同一路線，仍會在道路中斷時一起失去作用。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Averaging stage success overstates the probability that all necessary events occur. Multiplying dependent probabilities is also misleading, and duplicate resources sharing one route can fail together when that route becomes inaccessible during flooding. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例只設四個必要且相互獨立的操作環節，各成功率為指定假設；未包含共同原因或洪水荷載超標，不是任何城市的實測可靠度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Common causes and load exceedance are excluded; this is not measured reliability for any city.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「四個必要環節各有百分之九十八成功率，整個流程就必定也是百分之九十八。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Four necessary stages each succeeding ninety-eight percent make the entire process ninety-eight percent reliable.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"取各階段成功率平均值會高估全部必要事件同時成功，直接相乘相關機率也可能失真；重複備援若共用同一路線，仍會在道路中斷時一起失去作用。","textEn":"Averaging stage success overstates the probability that all necessary events occur. Multiplying dependent probabilities is also misleading, and duplicate resources sharing one route can fail together when that route becomes inaccessible during flooding.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「閉合流程可靠度機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Closure-process reliability mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["取各階段成功率平均值會高估全部必要事件同時成功，直接相乘相關機率也可能失真；重複備援若共用同一路線，仍會在道路中斷時一起失去作用。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","三十次演練都成功，就能用統計方法證明未來失敗機率恰好為零。"],"optionsEn":["Averaging stage success overstates the probability that all necessary events occur.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Thirty successful exercises statistically prove that future failure probability is exactly zero."],"answer":0,"explanation":"取各階段成功率平均值會高估全部必要事件同時成功，直接相乘相關機率也可能失真；重複備援若共用同一路線，仍會在道路中斷時一起失去作用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Averaging stage success overstates the probability that all necessary events occur. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b275-v15-37","title":"演練證據與失敗率界限機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Exercise evidence and failure-rate bounds mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「演練證據與失敗率界限」如何影響移動式防洪擋板部署的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Exercise evidence and failure-rate bounds” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Deployable flood-barrier systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"多次成功演練能提供流程證據，但有限樣本中未見失敗不等於失敗機率為零。若每次條件獨立且代表同一分布，可由二項模型估算單側信賴上界；晴天日間演練與夜間暴雨現場可能不具代表性，因此統計界限必須連同演練範圍、改版和共因情境一起解讀。本例假設固定未知失敗率、獨立同分布演練，使用零失敗的精確單側百分之九十五上界；不是貝氏後驗也不保證下一次成功。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「演練證據與失敗率界限」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Repeated successful exercises provide evidence but zero observed failures in a finite sample does not mean zero failure probability. Independent representative trials support a binomial one-sided upper bound. Daylight fair-weather drills may not represent night storms, however, so statistical limits must be read alongside exercise scope, system changes and common-cause scenarios rather than as unconditional field guarantees. The example assumes a fixed unknown failure probability and independent identically distributed trials. It uses the exact zero-failure one-sided ninety-five-percent upper confidence bound, not a Bayesian posterior or a promise about the next event. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Exercise evidence and failure-rate bounds” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設n=30次獨立演練均成功，失敗率單側95%上界pf=1−0.05^(1/n)=0.09503，約9.503%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume n=30 independent successful trials with zero failures.","failure":"常見誤解：「三十次演練都成功，就能用統計方法證明未來失敗機率恰好為零。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Thirty successful exercises statistically prove that future failure probability is exactly zero.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「演練證據與失敗率界限」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Exercise evidence and failure-rate bounds”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-37-k1","title":"演練證據與失敗率界限機理與驗證","titleEn":"Exercise evidence and failure-rate bounds mechanism and verification","text":"多次成功演練能提供流程證據，但有限樣本中未見失敗不等於失敗機率為零。若每次條件獨立且代表同一分布，可由二項模型估算單側信賴上界；晴天日間演練與夜間暴雨現場可能不具代表性，因此統計界限必須連同演練範圍、改版和共因情境一起解讀。","textEn":"Repeated successful exercises provide evidence but zero observed failures in a finite sample does not mean zero failure probability. Independent representative trials support a binomial one-sided upper bound.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：三十次演練都成功，就能用統計方法證明未來失敗機率恰好為零。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Thirty successful exercises statistically prove that future failure probability is exactly zero. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「演練證據與失敗率界限機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Exercise evidence and failure-rate bounds mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["三十次演練都成功，就能用統計方法證明未來失敗機率恰好為零。","多次成功演練能提供流程證據，但有限樣本中未見失敗不等於失敗機率為零。","只要擋板組裝時間短於洪峰到達時間，就一定來得及安全部署。"],"optionsEn":["Thirty successful exercises statistically prove that future failure probability is exactly zero.","Repeated successful exercises provide evidence but zero observed failures in a finite sample does not mean zero failure probability.","Assembly shorter than time to the flood crest guarantees timely and safe deployment."],"answer":1,"explanation":"多次成功演練能提供流程證據，但有限樣本中未見失敗不等於失敗機率為零。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Repeated successful exercises provide evidence but zero observed failures in a finite sample does not mean zero failure probability. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b275-v15-38","title":"演練證據與失敗率界限機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Exercise evidence and failure-rate bounds mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「演練證據與失敗率界限」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Exercise evidence and failure-rate bounds” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設n=30次獨立演練均成功，失敗率單側95%上界pf=1−0.05^(1/n)=0.09503，約9.503%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume n=30 independent successful trials with zero failures. The one-sided 95% upper failure bound is pf=1−0.05^(1/n)=0.09503, approximately 9.503%. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對每次演練是否完整涵蓋通知到查驗，保留延遲、近失敗和條件差異，而不只記成功次數。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check that each trial covers alert through inspection and retain delays, near failures and differing conditions rather than only success counts.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設n=30次獨立演練均成功，失敗率單側95%上界pf=1−0.05^(1/n)=0.09503，約9.503%。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume n=30 independent successful trials with zero failures. The one-sided 95% upper failure bound is pf=1−0.05^(1/n)=0.09503, approximately 9.503%.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「演練證據與失敗率界限機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Exercise evidence and failure-rate bounds mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["只要總件數和總重量足夠，就能保證每個區段的構件都相容。","增加自重一定能解決所有臨時防洪系統的滑動、滲水與承載問題。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設n=30次獨立演練均成功，失敗率單側95%上界pf=1−0.05^(1/n)=0.09503，約9.503%。"],"optionsEn":["Sufficient total count and mass guarantee compatible components for every barrier section.","Added weight necessarily solves every sliding, seepage and bearing problem of a temporary barrier.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume n=30 independent successful trials with zero failures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設n=30次獨立演練均成功，失敗率單側95%上界pf=1−0.05^(1/n)=0.09503，約9.503%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume n=30 independent successful trials with zero failures. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b275-v15-39","title":"演練證據與失敗率界限機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Exercise evidence and failure-rate bounds mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「演練證據與失敗率界限」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Exercise evidence and failure-rate bounds” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對每次演練是否完整涵蓋通知到查驗，保留延遲、近失敗和條件差異，而不只記成功次數。系統、班組或路線改版後重新評估可合併樣本，將代表性限制與統計上界一起發布。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check that each trial covers alert through inspection and retain delays, near failures and differing conditions rather than only success counts. Reassess sample comparability after system, crew or route changes and report representativeness limitations beside the statistical bound to avoid overclaiming operational evidence. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較不同成功樣本數的單側上界，保持信賴水準不變。再列出未曾演練的夜間、道路中斷或人員缺席條件，區分增加樣本量與增加情境代表性的效果。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare one-sided bounds at different zero-failure sample sizes while holding confidence fixed. List untested night, blocked-route and absent-staff conditions, distinguishing the effect of more trials from broader representation of relevant operating circumstances.","failure":"注意干擾：只挑順利演練會產生選擇偏差，把相同班組重複練習當完全獨立也可能誇大資訊量；將零失敗寫成百分之百可靠，則掩蓋未測情境與有限樣本的不確定性。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Selecting only smooth exercises creates bias, and treating repeated practice by the same crew as fully independent can exaggerate information. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對每次演練是否完整涵蓋通知到查驗，保留延遲、近失敗和條件差異，而不只記成功次數。系統、班組或路線改版後重新評估可合併樣本，將代表性限制與統計上界一起發布。","textEn":"Check that each trial covers alert through inspection and retain delays, near failures and differing conditions rather than only success counts. Reassess sample comparability after system, crew or route changes and report representativeness limitations beside the statistical bound to avoid overclaiming operational evidence.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較不同成功樣本數的單側上界，保持信賴水準不變。再列出未曾演練的夜間、道路中斷或人員缺席條件，區分增加樣本量與增加情境代表性的效果。","textEn":"Compare one-sided bounds at different zero-failure sample sizes while holding confidence fixed. List untested night, blocked-route and absent-staff conditions, distinguishing the effect of more trials from broader representation of relevant operating circumstances.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「演練證據與失敗率界限機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Exercise evidence and failure-rate bounds mechanism and verification\"?","options":["核對每次演練是否完整涵蓋通知到查驗，保留延遲、近失敗和條件差異，而不只記成功次數。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","擋板閉合後只要任何一台泵在運轉，內側水位就一定不會上升。"],"optionsEn":["Check that each trial covers alert through inspection and retain delays, near failures and differing conditions rather than only success counts.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Once barriers close, any running pump guarantees that interior water level cannot rise."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對每次演練是否完整涵蓋通知到查驗，保留延遲、近失敗和條件差異，而不只記成功次數。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check that each trial covers alert through inspection and retain delays, near failures and differing conditions rather than only success counts. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b275-v15-40","title":"演練證據與失敗率界限機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Exercise evidence and failure-rate bounds mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"prerequisiteIds":["b275-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「演練證據與失敗率界限」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Exercise evidence and failure-rate bounds” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只挑順利演練會產生選擇偏差，把相同班組重複練習當完全獨立也可能誇大資訊量；將零失敗寫成百分之百可靠，則掩蓋未測情境與有限樣本的不確定性。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Selecting only smooth exercises creates bias, and treating repeated practice by the same crew as fully independent can exaggerate information. Reporting zero failures as perfect reliability hides untested conditions and the uncertainty inherent in a limited sample. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例假設固定未知失敗率、獨立同分布演練，使用零失敗的精確單側百分之九十五上界；不是貝氏後驗也不保證下一次成功。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It uses the exact zero-failure one-sided ninety-five-percent upper confidence bound, not a Bayesian posterior or a promise about the next event.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「三十次演練都成功，就能用統計方法證明未來失敗機率恰好為零。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Thirty successful exercises statistically prove that future failure probability is exactly zero.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b275-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只挑順利演練會產生選擇偏差，把相同班組重複練習當完全獨立也可能誇大資訊量；將零失敗寫成百分之百可靠，則掩蓋未測情境與有限樣本的不確定性。","textEn":"Selecting only smooth exercises creates bias, and treating repeated practice by the same crew as fully independent can exaggerate information. Reporting zero failures as perfect reliability hides untested conditions and the uncertainty inherent in a limited sample.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]},{"id":"b275-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「演練證據與失敗率界限機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Exercise evidence and failure-rate bounds mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只挑順利演練會產生選擇偏差，把相同班組重複練習當完全獨立也可能誇大資訊量；將零失敗寫成百分之百可靠，則掩蓋未測情境與有限樣本的不確定性。","只要擋板組裝時間短於洪峰到達時間，就一定來得及安全部署。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Selecting only smooth exercises creates bias, and treating repeated practice by the same crew as fully independent can exaggerate information.","Assembly shorter than time to the flood crest guarantees timely and safe deployment."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只挑順利演練會產生選擇偏差，把相同班組重複練習當完全獨立也可能誇大資訊量；將零失敗寫成百分之百可靠，則掩蓋未測情境與有限樣本的不確定性。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Selecting only smooth exercises creates bias, and treating repeated practice by the same crew as fully independent can exaggerate information. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-ea-demountable","v15s-ea-bewdley","v15s-ea-beales","v15s-steb-mobile"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b276","title":"河岸生態護岸","titleEn":"Bioengineered riverbank protection","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"由趾部沖刷、木構浮力到根系補強與季節存活，逐一拆開生態護岸的承載機制。課程要求先辨認河道變遷與植物適生條件，再安排材料、施工窗口與後續監測，以對照組觀察功能是否形成，而不把綠色外觀當成安全證明。","summaryEn":"Separate the load paths of toe protection, buoyant wood, root reinforcement and seasonal plant establishment. Identify channel adjustment and vegetation suitability before selecting materials, construction windows and monitoring. Use comparison sites to examine whether the intended functions actually develop instead of treating a green bank as evidence of structural performance.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["河岸剪力的尺度","Scales of bank shear"],["根系補強的有效面積","Effective area in root reinforcement"],["岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量","Toe embedment and erosion allowance"],["纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋","Mat overlap and effective coverage"],["對照監測的生態成效","Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["河岸剪力的尺度","根系補強的有效面積","岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量","纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋","對照監測的生態成效"],"labelsEn":["Scales of bank shear","Effective area in root reinforcement","Toe embedment and erosion allowance","Mat overlap and effective coverage","Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課先用「河岸剪力的尺度」建立原創假想基準，再以「植生莖叢的阻力」檢查另一個控制機制。第一組輸入及結果為 rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa；第二組為 rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N。學員需在同一張工作表分列量綱、時間、位置與適用範圍，先核對守恆，再解釋為何兩個得數不能互相代替。最後以第三單元提出的量測設計驗證假設，並將超出模型能力的水理、生態或治理問題列為待研究項目；這些示例並非所列案例的現場實測。敏感度重算：固定 rho=1000 kg/m3、g=9.81 m/s2 與 S=0.003 無因次，只將 R 從 0.8 m 增至 0.88 m，tau=25.8984 Pa，相較 23.544 Pa 增加一成。這仍是河段平均，不能當外彎局部最大值。","textEn":"Begin with an original hypothetical baseline for Scales of bank shear and examine another controlling mechanism through Drag on vegetation stems. The first inputs and result are rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa; the second are rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N. Keep dimensions, time, location and validity conditions in separate columns of the same working sheet. Check conservation before explaining why the two numerical results cannot substitute for one another. Use the third unit measurement design to test assumptions and identify hydraulic, ecological or governance questions that exceed the model. These examples are not field observations from the named reference cases. Sensitivity recalculation: Keep rho=1000 kg/m3, g=9.81 m/s2 and dimensionless S=0.003 fixed, changing only R from 0.8 m to 0.88 m. The stress becomes 25.8984 Pa, ten percent above 23.544 Pa. It remains a reach average rather than the outer-bank local maximum.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b276-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「河岸剪力的尺度」與「植生莖叢的阻力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Scales of bank shear\" and \"Drag on vegetation stems\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b276-v15-01","title":"河岸剪力的尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Scales of bank shear: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「河岸剪力的尺度」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Scales of bank shear” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"河岸植生先面對水流造成的剪力與局部紊流，再由莖葉、根系及土體共同承受。斷面平均水力半徑乘以能坡只能估算河段平均床面剪力，彎道外岸、橋墩附近與淹沒植物間可能有完全不同的局部荷載。選工法前應把深槽、主流線和沖刷痕跡畫在同一張圖，辨認保護對象是表土、岸趾或整個滑動體，才決定平均量是否足以篩選材料。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「河岸剪力的尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Vegetation encounters flow shear and turbulence before stems, roots and soil share the resulting loads. Hydraulic radius and energy slope give a reach averaged boundary stress, while bends, obstructions and submerged plants can produce very different local loads. Map the thalweg, main current and erosion traces together. Identify whether protection targets surface soil, the toe or an entire sliding mass before deciding whether an average stress can screen a treatment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Scales of bank shear” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「河岸剪力的尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Scales of bank shear”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-01-k1","title":"河岸剪力的尺度","titleEn":"Scales of bank shear","text":"河岸植生先面對水流造成的剪力與局部紊流，再由莖葉、根系及土體共同承受。斷面平均水力半徑乘以能坡只能估算河段平均床面剪力，彎道外岸、橋墩附近與淹沒植物間可能有完全不同的局部荷載。","textEn":"Vegetation encounters flow shear and turbulence before stems, roots and soil share the resulting loads. Hydraulic radius and energy slope give a reach averaged boundary stress, while bends, obstructions and submerged plants can produce very different local loads.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「河岸剪力的尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Scales of bank shear\" is correct?","options":["河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力","河岸植生先面對水流造成的剪力與局部紊流，再由莖葉、根系及土體共同承受。","種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積"],"optionsEn":["Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location","Vegetation encounters flow shear and turbulence before stems, roots and soil share the resulting loads.","Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems"],"answer":1,"explanation":"河岸植生先面對水流造成的剪力與局部紊流，再由莖葉、根系及土體共同承受。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Vegetation encounters flow shear and turbulence before stems, roots and soil share the resulting loads. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b276-v15-02","title":"河岸剪力的尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Scales of bank shear: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「河岸剪力的尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Scales of bank shear” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa。適用邊界：假設定常近均勻流，結果是平均邊界剪力，不是外彎岸坡最大剪力或植物耐受值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa. Applicable boundary: Assumes steady approximately uniform flow; the result is average boundary stress, not maximum outer-bank stress or plant resistance. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在同一水位下量測斷面與水面坡度，並以多點流速確認主流位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey cross sections and water surface slope at the same stage, and locate the current with multiple velocity measurements.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa。適用邊界：假設定常近均勻流，結果是平均邊界剪力，不是外彎岸坡最大剪力或植物耐受值。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa. Applicable boundary: Assumes steady approximately uniform flow; the result is average boundary stress, not maximum outer-bank stress or plant resistance.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「河岸剪力的尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Scales of bank shear\", which statement holds?","options":["木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載","原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa。"],"optionsEn":["Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor","The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; R=0.8 m; S=0.003 dimensionless; tau=rho*g*R*S=23.544 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b276-v15-03","title":"河岸剪力的尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Scales of bank shear: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「河岸剪力的尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Scales of bank shear” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在同一水位下量測斷面與水面坡度，並以多點流速確認主流位置。分別記錄裸岸、草叢與岸趾附近的沖刷，若局部集中而平均剪力不高，應增加局部水理分析，不能只提高一個平均係數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey cross sections and water surface slope at the same stage, and locate the current with multiple velocity measurements. Record erosion near bare soil, vegetation and the toe separately. Concentrated erosion despite modest average stress requires local hydraulic investigation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：改以能坡增加一半重算平均剪力，再繪製兩個具有相同平均值但主流位置不同的斷面，說明哪一種情況需要增加岸趾量測，並列出判讀依據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase energy slope by half and recompute average shear. Sketch two sections with equal averages but different current positions, then explain which requires additional toe measurements and what observations would justify that decision.","failure":"注意干擾：彎道近岸高速帶可能掏空根區，使表面完整的植生毯失去支承。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A near-bank jet can undermine roots while the surface mat still appears intact. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在同一水位下量測斷面與水面坡度，並以多點流速確認主流位置。分別記錄裸岸、草叢與岸趾附近的沖刷，若局部集中而平均剪力不高，應增加局部水理分析，不能只提高一個平均係數。","textEn":"Survey cross sections and water surface slope at the same stage, and locate the current with multiple velocity measurements. Record erosion near bare soil, vegetation and the toe separately. Concentrated erosion despite modest average stress requires local hydraulic investigation.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"改以能坡增加一半重算平均剪力，再繪製兩個具有相同平均值但主流位置不同的斷面，說明哪一種情況需要增加岸趾量測，並列出判讀依據。","textEn":"Increase energy slope by half and recompute average shear. Sketch two sections with equal averages but different current positions, then explain which requires additional toe measurements and what observations would justify that decision.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「河岸剪力的尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Scales of bank shear\"?","options":["在同一水位下量測斷面與水面坡度，並以多點流速確認主流位置。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散"],"optionsEn":["Survey cross sections and water surface slope at the same stage, and locate the current with multiple velocity measurements.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated"],"answer":0,"explanation":"在同一水位下量測斷面與水面坡度，並以多點流速確認主流位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey cross sections and water surface slope at the same stage, and locate the current with multiple velocity measurements. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b276-v15-04","title":"河岸剪力的尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Scales of bank shear: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「河岸剪力的尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Scales of bank shear” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"彎道近岸高速帶可能掏空根區，使表面完整的植生毯失去支承。診斷須追查水下岸趾與局部流向，而非先把植株死亡判成養護不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A near-bank jet can undermine roots while the surface mat still appears intact. Investigate the submerged toe and current direction before attributing plant loss to poor maintenance alone. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：選工法前應把深槽、主流線和沖刷痕跡畫在同一張圖，辨認保護對象是表土、岸趾或整個滑動體，才決定平均量是否足以篩選材料。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Identify whether protection targets surface soil, the toe or an entire sliding mass before deciding whether an average stress can screen a treatment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"彎道近岸高速帶可能掏空根區，使表面完整的植生毯失去支承。診斷須追查水下岸趾與局部流向，而非先把植株死亡判成養護不足。","textEn":"A near-bank jet can undermine roots while the surface mat still appears intact. Investigate the submerged toe and current direction before attributing plant loss to poor maintenance alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「河岸剪力的尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Scales of bank shear\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","彎道近岸高速帶可能掏空根區，使表面完整的植生毯失去支承。","種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A near-bank jet can undermine roots while the surface mat still appears intact.","Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems"],"answer":1,"explanation":"彎道近岸高速帶可能掏空根區，使表面完整的植生毯失去支承。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A near-bank jet can undermine roots while the surface mat still appears intact. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b276-v15-05","title":"植生莖叢的阻力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Drag on vegetation stems: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「植生莖叢的阻力」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drag on vegetation stems” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"植物在水中既增加粗糙度，也把水流動量轉成莖幹與根盤的荷載。迎流面積不是種植面積，而是投影在垂直流向平面的有效面積；柔軟植株彎伏後，面積與阻力係數會隨流速改變。群生植物還會彼此遮蔽或集中水流，因此單株試驗不能簡單乘株數。設計時應區分柔性變形、折斷和連根拔起三條失效路徑，並保留季節葉量不同的工況。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「植生莖叢的阻力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Vegetation adds roughness while transferring flow momentum into stems and roots. Frontal area is projected perpendicular to the current, not planted ground area. Flexible plants reconfigure, changing both area and drag coefficient as velocity increases. Neighbouring stems can shelter one another or concentrate flow, so multiplying an isolated plant test by stem count is unreliable. Distinguish bending, stem breakage and root pullout, and retain seasonal changes in foliage as separate loading conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drag on vegetation stems” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N.","failure":"常見誤解：「種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「植生莖叢的阻力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drag on vegetation stems”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-05-k1","title":"植生莖叢的阻力","titleEn":"Drag on vegetation stems","text":"植物在水中既增加粗糙度，也把水流動量轉成莖幹與根盤的荷載。迎流面積不是種植面積，而是投影在垂直流向平面的有效面積；柔軟植株彎伏後，面積與阻力係數會隨流速改變。","textEn":"Vegetation adds roughness while transferring flow momentum into stems and roots. Frontal area is projected perpendicular to the current, not planted ground area.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「植生莖叢的阻力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drag on vegetation stems\" is correct?","options":["種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積","表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力","植物在水中既增加粗糙度，也把水流動量轉成莖幹與根盤的荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems","Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth","Vegetation adds roughness while transferring flow momentum into stems and roots."],"answer":2,"explanation":"植物在水中既增加粗糙度，也把水流動量轉成莖幹與根盤的荷載。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Vegetation adds roughness while transferring flow momentum into stems and roots. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b276-v15-06","title":"植生莖叢的阻力：定量估算","titleEn":"Drag on vegetation stems: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「植生莖叢的阻力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drag on vegetation stems” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N。適用邊界：固定投影面積與阻力係數的準定常示例，未模擬彎伏、波動或群生效應。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N. Applicable boundary: A quasi-steady example with fixed projected area and drag coefficient, excluding reconfiguration, fluctuations and group effects. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以可量測拉力的小型枝條模型比較直立與彎伏狀態，逐級提高流速並拍攝迎流面積。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure force on a small branch model in upright and bent states while increasing velocity gradually.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N。適用邊界：固定投影面積與阻力係數的準定常示例，未模擬彎伏、波動或群生效應。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N. Applicable boundary: A quasi-steady example with fixed projected area and drag coefficient, excluding reconfiguration, fluctuations and group effects.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「植生莖叢的阻力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drag on vegetation stems\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N。","剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定","採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3.","Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood","Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Cd=1.1 dimensionless; A=1.2 m2; v=2 m/s; F=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=2640 N. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b276-v15-07","title":"植生莖叢的阻力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drag on vegetation stems: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「植生莖叢的阻力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drag on vegetation stems” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以可量測拉力的小型枝條模型比較直立與彎伏狀態，逐級提高流速並拍攝迎流面積。把力除以速度平方後查看是否仍接近常數，若偏離便追查形狀改變，勿先當成儀器漂移。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure force on a small branch model in upright and bent states while increasing velocity gradually. Photograph the projected area. Examine force divided by velocity squared; changes may indicate reconfiguration rather than unexplained electronic sensor drift. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將流速增加百分之二十五並保持面積不變重算，再提出一個彎伏後面積縮小的對照案例，說明為何兩者的阻力增幅不同，以及所需影像資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase velocity by twenty five percent at fixed area, then construct a comparison with reduced area after bending. Explain the different force changes and identify the imagery needed to distinguish these cases.","failure":"注意干擾：洪水夾帶雜物會擴大有效迎流面積，使原先按清潔枝條估算的根部荷載偏低。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Debris can enlarge frontal area and make clean-stem calculations underestimate root loading. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以可量測拉力的小型枝條模型比較直立與彎伏狀態，逐級提高流速並拍攝迎流面積。把力除以速度平方後查看是否仍接近常數，若偏離便追查形狀改變，勿先當成儀器漂移。","textEn":"Measure force on a small branch model in upright and bent states while increasing velocity gradually. Photograph the projected area. Examine force divided by velocity squared; changes may indicate reconfiguration rather than unexplained electronic sensor drift.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將流速增加百分之二十五並保持面積不變重算，再提出一個彎伏後面積縮小的對照案例，說明為何兩者的阻力增幅不同，以及所需影像資料。","textEn":"Increase velocity by twenty five percent at fixed area, then construct a comparison with reduced area after bending. Explain the different force changes and identify the imagery needed to distinguish these cases.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「植生莖叢的阻力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drag on vegetation stems\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以可量測拉力的小型枝條模型比較直立與彎伏狀態，逐級提高流速並拍攝迎流面積。","下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Measure force on a small branch model in upright and bent states while increasing velocity gradually.","Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以可量測拉力的小型枝條模型比較直立與彎伏狀態，逐級提高流速並拍攝迎流面積。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure force on a small branch model in upright and bent states while increasing velocity gradually. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b276-v15-08","title":"植生莖叢的阻力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drag on vegetation stems: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「植生莖叢的阻力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drag on vegetation stems” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"洪水夾帶雜物會擴大有效迎流面積，使原先按清潔枝條估算的根部荷載偏低。若只清點折枝而未查根盤位移，會漏掉尚未倒伏的損傷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Debris can enlarge frontal area and make clean-stem calculations underestimate root loading. Counting broken branches without checking root plate movement can miss damage in plants that remain standing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計時應區分柔性變形、折斷和連根拔起三條失效路徑，並保留季節葉量不同的工況。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Distinguish bending, stem breakage and root pullout, and retain seasonal changes in foliage as separate loading conditions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"洪水夾帶雜物會擴大有效迎流面積，使原先按清潔枝條估算的根部荷載偏低。若只清點折枝而未查根盤位移，會漏掉尚未倒伏的損傷。","textEn":"Debris can enlarge frontal area and make clean-stem calculations underestimate root loading. Counting broken branches without checking root plate movement can miss damage in plants that remain standing.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「植生莖叢的阻力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drag on vegetation stems\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力","洪水夾帶雜物會擴大有效迎流面積，使原先按清潔枝條估算的根部荷載偏低。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth","Debris can enlarge frontal area and make clean-stem calculations underestimate root loading."],"answer":2,"explanation":"洪水夾帶雜物會擴大有效迎流面積，使原先按清潔枝條估算的根部荷載偏低。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Debris can enlarge frontal area and make clean-stem calculations underestimate root loading. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b276-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「根系補強的有效面積」與「木構護岸的浮力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Effective area in root reinforcement\" and \"Buoyancy of wood revetments\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b276-v15-09","title":"根系補強的有效面積：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Effective area in root reinforcement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「根系補強的有效面積」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective area in root reinforcement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"根系穿越潛在剪動面時可提供拉力，但這個貢獻取決於根徑、方向、錨定長度與含水狀態。把根拉力除以土體剪動面積只能得到等效的附加抗剪應力，不能當成整體土壤永久增加的黏聚力。部分根會先滑出或腐朽，另一些根尚未受力，因此同步動員的有效拉力必須由試驗支持。模型應清楚標示剪動面位置，避免把表層密根區的數據套到較深的滑動面。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「根系補強的有效面積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Roots crossing a potential shear surface can mobilize tension, depending on diameter, orientation, anchorage and moisture. Dividing effective root force by soil shear area gives an equivalent stress contribution, not a permanent increase in intrinsic soil cohesion. Some roots pull out or decay before others engage, so simultaneous mobilization requires evidence. Locate the assumed shear surface explicitly, rather than transferring measurements from a shallow dense root layer to a deeper failure plane. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective area in root reinforcement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「根系補強的有效面積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective area in root reinforcement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-09-k1","title":"根系補強的有效面積","titleEn":"Effective area in root reinforcement","text":"根系穿越潛在剪動面時可提供拉力，但這個貢獻取決於根徑、方向、錨定長度與含水狀態。把根拉力除以土體剪動面積只能得到等效的附加抗剪應力，不能當成整體土壤永久增加的黏聚力。","textEn":"Roots crossing a potential shear surface can mobilize tension, depending on diameter, orientation, anchorage and moisture. Dividing effective root force by soil shear area gives an equivalent stress contribution, not a permanent increase in intrinsic soil cohesion.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「根系補強的有效面積」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Effective area in root reinforcement\" is correct?","options":["根系穿越潛在剪動面時可提供拉力，但這個貢獻取決於根徑、方向、錨定長度與含水狀態。","表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力","木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載"],"optionsEn":["Roots crossing a potential shear surface can mobilize tension, depending on diameter, orientation, anchorage and moisture.","Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth","Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor"],"answer":0,"explanation":"根系穿越潛在剪動面時可提供拉力，但這個貢獻取決於根徑、方向、錨定長度與含水狀態。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Roots crossing a potential shear surface can mobilize tension, depending on diameter, orientation, anchorage and moisture. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b276-v15-10","title":"根系補強的有效面積：定量估算","titleEn":"Effective area in root reinforcement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「根系補強的有效面積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective area in root reinforcement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa。適用邊界：有效拉力已假設包含方向與動員折減，僅代表指定剪面之附加應力。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa. Applicable boundary: Effective tension already includes assumed orientation and mobilization reductions; the result applies only to the specified shear surface. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對不同根徑做拉拔試驗，同時記錄斷裂或滑出模式，再量測剪動面上的根截面分布。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Test pullout across root diameters and record breakage versus slippage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa。適用邊界：有效拉力已假設包含方向與動員折減，僅代表指定剪面之附加應力。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa. Applicable boundary: Effective tension already includes assumed orientation and mobilization reductions; the result applies only to the specified shear surface.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「根系補強的有效面積」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Effective area in root reinforcement\", which statement holds?","options":["原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa。","岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散"],"optionsEn":["The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa.","A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Tr=1600 N; As=0.2 m2; dc=Tr/As/1000=8 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b276-v15-11","title":"根系補強的有效面積：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Effective area in root reinforcement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「根系補強的有效面積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective area in root reinforcement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對不同根徑做拉拔試驗，同時記錄斷裂或滑出模式，再量測剪動面上的根截面分布。將單根強度與整體土樣剪切結果交叉比較，確認是否真的能同時動員，並保存含水率與植物生長期。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Test pullout across root diameters and record breakage versus slippage. Map roots across the proposed shear plane. Compare individual strength with rooted soil shear tests to assess simultaneous mobilization, retaining measured soil moisture and seasonal growth stage records. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將有效拉力降低四分之一重算，並畫出穿根與不穿根的兩個滑面。為每個滑面列出必須取得的試驗資料，說明等效應力何時應取零。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce effective tension by one quarter and recalculate. Draw failure planes crossing and bypassing roots, list the necessary evidence for each, and explain when the equivalent root contribution must be set to zero.","failure":"注意干擾：若實際滑動面位於根層下方，即使表層根系茂密也可能整塊滑落。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A slide beneath the root zone can remove a densely vegetated surface as one block. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對不同根徑做拉拔試驗，同時記錄斷裂或滑出模式，再量測剪動面上的根截面分布。將單根強度與整體土樣剪切結果交叉比較，確認是否真的能同時動員，並保存含水率與植物生長期。","textEn":"Test pullout across root diameters and record breakage versus slippage. Map roots across the proposed shear plane. Compare individual strength with rooted soil shear tests to assess simultaneous mobilization, retaining measured soil moisture and seasonal growth stage records.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將有效拉力降低四分之一重算，並畫出穿根與不穿根的兩個滑面。為每個滑面列出必須取得的試驗資料，說明等效應力何時應取零。","textEn":"Reduce effective tension by one quarter and recalculate. Draw failure planes crossing and bypassing roots, list the necessary evidence for each, and explain when the equivalent root contribution must be set to zero.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「根系補強的有效面積」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Effective area in root reinforcement\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成","對不同根徑做拉拔試驗，同時記錄斷裂或滑出模式，再量測剪動面上的根截面分布。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works","Test pullout across root diameters and record breakage versus slippage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對不同根徑做拉拔試驗，同時記錄斷裂或滑出模式，再量測剪動面上的根截面分布。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Test pullout across root diameters and record breakage versus slippage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b276-v15-12","title":"根系補強的有效面積：失效診斷","titleEn":"Effective area in root reinforcement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「根系補強的有效面積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective area in root reinforcement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若實際滑動面位於根層下方，即使表層根系茂密也可能整塊滑落。應先查滑面深度與排水條件，而不是繼續增加表層播種密度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A slide beneath the root zone can remove a densely vegetated surface as one block. Investigate slip depth and drainage before prescribing more seed or greater surface planting density. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：模型應清楚標示剪動面位置，避免把表層密根區的數據套到較深的滑動面。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Locate the assumed shear surface explicitly, rather than transferring measurements from a shallow dense root layer to a deeper failure plane.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若實際滑動面位於根層下方，即使表層根系茂密也可能整塊滑落。應先查滑面深度與排水條件，而不是繼續增加表層播種密度。","textEn":"A slide beneath the root zone can remove a densely vegetated surface as one block. Investigate slip depth and drainage before prescribing more seed or greater surface planting density.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「根系補強的有效面積」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Effective area in root reinforcement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若實際滑動面位於根層下方，即使表層根系茂密也可能整塊滑落。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載"],"optionsEn":["A slide beneath the root zone can remove a densely vegetated surface as one block.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor"],"answer":0,"explanation":"若實際滑動面位於根層下方，即使表層根系茂密也可能整塊滑落。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A slide beneath the root zone can remove a densely vegetated surface as one block. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b276-v15-13","title":"木構護岸的浮力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Buoyancy of wood revetments: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「木構護岸的浮力」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Buoyancy of wood revetments” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"河岸枯木或根盤可提供粗糙棲地，也可能在洪水中浮起。木材自重與排水體積必須用同一含水狀態比較，部分浸水時不能使用完整體積計算浮力。淨上浮力只是錨定設計的一個分量，水流拖曳、撞擊與繞支點轉動可能控制接頭。木構隨浸泡吸水與腐朽改變密度，因此檢查不能只依新材出廠重量，還需辨認失去土體包覆後的受力路徑。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「木構護岸的浮力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Wood and rootwads create rough habitat but may lift during floods. Compare weight and displaced volume at a consistent moisture state, and use submerged volume for partial immersion. Net uplift is only one anchorage load; drag, impact and rotation about supports may govern connections. Density changes through saturation and decay. Inspection therefore needs the evolving load path after surrounding soil erodes, rather than relying solely on the weight of freshly supplied timber. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Buoyancy of wood revetments” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N.","failure":"常見誤解：「木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「木構護岸的浮力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Buoyancy of wood revetments”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-13-k1","title":"木構護岸的浮力","titleEn":"Buoyancy of wood revetments","text":"河岸枯木或根盤可提供粗糙棲地，也可能在洪水中浮起。木材自重與排水體積必須用同一含水狀態比較，部分浸水時不能使用完整體積計算浮力。","textEn":"Wood and rootwads create rough habitat but may lift during floods. Compare weight and displaced volume at a consistent moisture state, and use submerged volume for partial immersion.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「木構護岸的浮力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Buoyancy of wood revetments\" is correct?","options":["木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載","河岸枯木或根盤可提供粗糙棲地，也可能在洪水中浮起。","剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定"],"optionsEn":["Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor","Wood and rootwads create rough habitat but may lift during floods.","Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood"],"answer":1,"explanation":"河岸枯木或根盤可提供粗糙棲地，也可能在洪水中浮起。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Wood and rootwads create rough habitat but may lift during floods. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b276-v15-14","title":"木構護岸的浮力：定量估算","titleEn":"Buoyancy of wood revetments: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「木構護岸的浮力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Buoyancy of wood revetments” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N。適用邊界：完全浸沒且密度均勻，僅計靜水淨上浮力，不是錨具額定需求。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N. Applicable boundary: Fully submerged uniform density; calculates net hydrostatic uplift only, not an anchorage rating. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先量木構尺寸與濕重，再以部分浸水試驗檢查排水量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure geometry and wet mass, then check displacement during partial immersion.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N。適用邊界：完全浸沒且密度均勻，僅計靜水淨上浮力，不是錨具額定需求。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N. Applicable boundary: Fully submerged uniform density; calculates net hydrostatic uplift only, not an anchorage rating.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「木構護岸的浮力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Buoyancy of wood revetments\", which statement holds?","options":["採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積","下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N。"],"optionsEn":["Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation","Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhow=1000 kg/m3."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhow=1000 kg/m3; rhol=600 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=0.8 m3; Fu=(rhow-rhol)*g*V=3139.2 N. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b276-v15-15","title":"木構護岸的浮力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Buoyancy of wood revetments: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「木構護岸的浮力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Buoyancy of wood revetments” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先量木構尺寸與濕重，再以部分浸水試驗檢查排水量。洪水後記錄轉角、接頭滑移與岸土流失，將浮力計算和現場受力方向比對，若受力不共線則增加力矩分析與接頭試驗。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure geometry and wet mass, then check displacement during partial immersion. After floods, record rotation, connection movement and soil loss. Compare the buoyancy direction with observed loading and add moment analysis when forces are not aligned. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較木材密度增加到八百公斤每立方公尺後的淨浮力，另畫一個岸趾淘空的偏心支承圖，指出還缺哪些尺寸才能計算錨點受力。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate uplift for timber density of eight hundred kilograms per cubic metre. Draw an eccentric support after toe erosion and identify the additional dimensions needed to resolve anchor forces and moments.","failure":"注意干擾：岸土被淘空後木構可能繞剩餘錨點旋轉，接頭受撬力而非單純拉力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Erosion can leave timber rotating about one anchor, prying connections instead of loading them in simple tension. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先量木構尺寸與濕重，再以部分浸水試驗檢查排水量。洪水後記錄轉角、接頭滑移與岸土流失，將浮力計算和現場受力方向比對，若受力不共線則增加力矩分析與接頭試驗。","textEn":"Measure geometry and wet mass, then check displacement during partial immersion. After floods, record rotation, connection movement and soil loss. Compare the buoyancy direction with observed loading and add moment analysis when forces are not aligned.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較木材密度增加到八百公斤每立方公尺後的淨浮力，另畫一個岸趾淘空的偏心支承圖，指出還缺哪些尺寸才能計算錨點受力。","textEn":"Recalculate uplift for timber density of eight hundred kilograms per cubic metre. Draw an eccentric support after toe erosion and identify the additional dimensions needed to resolve anchor forces and moments.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「木構護岸的浮力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Buoyancy of wood revetments\"?","options":["先量木構尺寸與濕重，再以部分浸水試驗檢查排水量。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力"],"optionsEn":["Measure geometry and wet mass, then check displacement during partial immersion.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location"],"answer":0,"explanation":"先量木構尺寸與濕重，再以部分浸水試驗檢查排水量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure geometry and wet mass, then check displacement during partial immersion. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b276-v15-16","title":"木構護岸的浮力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Buoyancy of wood revetments: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「木構護岸的浮力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Buoyancy of wood revetments” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"岸土被淘空後木構可能繞剩餘錨點旋轉，接頭受撬力而非單純拉力。只用淨浮力除以錨點數，會掩蓋負荷分配不均及漸進破壞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Erosion can leave timber rotating about one anchor, prying connections instead of loading them in simple tension. Dividing uplift equally among anchors hides unequal distribution and progressive connection failure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：木構隨浸泡吸水與腐朽改變密度，因此檢查不能只依新材出廠重量，還需辨認失去土體包覆後的受力路徑。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Inspection therefore needs the evolving load path after surrounding soil erodes, rather than relying solely on the weight of freshly supplied timber.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"岸土被淘空後木構可能繞剩餘錨點旋轉，接頭受撬力而非單純拉力。只用淨浮力除以錨點數，會掩蓋負荷分配不均及漸進破壞。","textEn":"Erosion can leave timber rotating about one anchor, prying connections instead of loading them in simple tension. Dividing uplift equally among anchors hides unequal distribution and progressive connection failure.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「木構護岸的浮力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Buoyancy of wood revetments\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","岸土被淘空後木構可能繞剩餘錨點旋轉，接頭受撬力而非單純拉力。","剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Erosion can leave timber rotating about one anchor, prying connections instead of loading them in simple tension.","Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood"],"answer":1,"explanation":"岸土被淘空後木構可能繞剩餘錨點旋轉，接頭受撬力而非單純拉力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Erosion can leave timber rotating about one anchor, prying connections instead of loading them in simple tension. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b276-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」與「建立期植株存活率」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Toe embedment and erosion allowance\" and \"Plant survival during establishment\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b276-v15-17","title":"岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Toe embedment and erosion allowance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Toe embedment and erosion allowance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"植生護岸常由岸趾流失開始失去支承，因此埋深應相對於可變河床而非單一施工測點。扣除一次量測沖刷深度能得到幾何餘量，但尚未考慮洪水規模、長期下切與橫向深槽遷移。埋得更深也可能增加施工擾動與地下水交換阻力。合理比較需要把施工基準、自然河床高程與預期變化分開記錄，再以重複測線判斷餘量如何消耗。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Vegetated protection often loses support when its toe erodes. Embedment must therefore reference a changing bed rather than one construction survey point. Subtracting observed scour gives geometric reserve but omits larger floods, long term incision and lateral thalweg migration. Greater embedment can also increase disturbance or obstruct groundwater exchange. Separate construction datum, natural bed elevation and expected change, then use repeated cross sections to track how the reserve is consumed over time. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Toe embedment and erosion allowance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Toe embedment and erosion allowance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-17-k1","title":"岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量","titleEn":"Toe embedment and erosion allowance","text":"植生護岸常由岸趾流失開始失去支承，因此埋深應相對於可變河床而非單一施工測點。扣除一次量測沖刷深度能得到幾何餘量，但尚未考慮洪水規模、長期下切與橫向深槽遷移。","textEn":"Vegetated protection often loses support when its toe erodes. Embedment must therefore reference a changing bed rather than one construction survey point.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Toe embedment and erosion allowance\" is correct?","options":["剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定","原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比","植生護岸常由岸趾流失開始失去支承，因此埋深應相對於可變河床而非單一施工測點。"],"optionsEn":["Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood","The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength","Vegetated protection often loses support when its toe erodes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"植生護岸常由岸趾流失開始失去支承，因此埋深應相對於可變河床而非單一施工測點。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Vegetated protection often loses support when its toe erodes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b276-v15-18","title":"岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量：定量估算","titleEn":"Toe embedment and erosion allowance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Toe embedment and erosion allowance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m。適用邊界：同一垂直基準的幾何差值，沒有將剩餘埋深換算成穩定安全係數。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m. Applicable boundary: A geometric difference on one vertical datum, without converting remaining embedment into a stability factor. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在護岸前緣設固定測線並保留基準點，洪水前後用相同方法重測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Establish fixed transects and preserve survey benchmarks.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m。適用邊界：同一垂直基準的幾何差值，沒有將剩餘埋深換算成穩定安全係數。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m. Applicable boundary: A geometric difference on one vertical datum, without converting remaining embedment into a stability factor.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Toe embedment and erosion allowance\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m。","岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散","處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m.","A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated","Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: e=1.2 m; ds=0.5 m; er=e-ds=0.7 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b276-v15-19","title":"岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Toe embedment and erosion allowance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Toe embedment and erosion allowance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在護岸前緣設固定測線並保留基準點，洪水前後用相同方法重測。將最大沖刷與回淤分列，避免以事後填回的河床掩蓋洪峰侵蝕，並檢查岸趾是否出現空洞或局部懸空。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Establish fixed transects and preserve survey benchmarks. Repeat measurements consistently before and after floods. Separate maximum scour from later deposition, because a refilled bed can conceal peak erosion; inspect for submerged voids or locally unsupported toe sections. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：假設第二次事件再降低河床三十公分，更新幾何餘量並說明為何仍無法宣布安全。規劃兩條新增測線以捕捉深槽側移，標出與舊基準的連結。","observationEn":"Site practice: Lower the bed another thirty centimetres and update the reserve without declaring stability. Place two additional transects to detect lateral thalweg migration and show how they connect to the original survey datum.","failure":"注意干擾：若深槽移到護岸外緣，先前測線可能漏掉局部淘空。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A migrating thalweg may create local undermining between previous transects. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在護岸前緣設固定測線並保留基準點，洪水前後用相同方法重測。將最大沖刷與回淤分列，避免以事後填回的河床掩蓋洪峰侵蝕，並檢查岸趾是否出現空洞或局部懸空。","textEn":"Establish fixed transects and preserve survey benchmarks. Repeat measurements consistently before and after floods. Separate maximum scour from later deposition, because a refilled bed can conceal peak erosion; inspect for submerged voids or locally unsupported toe sections.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"假設第二次事件再降低河床三十公分，更新幾何餘量並說明為何仍無法宣布安全。規劃兩條新增測線以捕捉深槽側移，標出與舊基準的連結。","textEn":"Lower the bed another thirty centimetres and update the reserve without declaring stability. Place two additional transects to detect lateral thalweg migration and show how they connect to the original survey datum.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Toe embedment and erosion allowance\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在護岸前緣設固定測線並保留基準點，洪水前後用相同方法重測。","種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Establish fixed transects and preserve survey benchmarks.","Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems"],"answer":1,"explanation":"在護岸前緣設固定測線並保留基準點，洪水前後用相同方法重測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Establish fixed transects and preserve survey benchmarks. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b276-v15-20","title":"岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Toe embedment and erosion allowance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Toe embedment and erosion allowance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若深槽移到護岸外緣，先前測線可能漏掉局部淘空。表面仍貼合的護岸不代表底部有支承，需用水下測量確認邊界是否改變。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A migrating thalweg may create local undermining between previous transects. An apparently flush surface does not prove support underneath; underwater surveys must check whether the erosion boundary has shifted. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：合理比較需要把施工基準、自然河床高程與預期變化分開記錄，再以重複測線判斷餘量如何消耗。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Separate construction datum, natural bed elevation and expected change, then use repeated cross sections to track how the reserve is consumed over time.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若深槽移到護岸外緣，先前測線可能漏掉局部淘空。表面仍貼合的護岸不代表底部有支承，需用水下測量確認邊界是否改變。","textEn":"A migrating thalweg may create local undermining between previous transects. An apparently flush surface does not prove support underneath; underwater surveys must check whether the erosion boundary has shifted.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「岸趾埋深與沖刷餘量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Toe embedment and erosion allowance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比","若深槽移到護岸外緣，先前測線可能漏掉局部淘空。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength","A migrating thalweg may create local undermining between previous transects."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若深槽移到護岸外緣，先前測線可能漏掉局部淘空。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A migrating thalweg may create local undermining between previous transects. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b276-v15-21","title":"建立期植株存活率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Plant survival during establishment: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「建立期植株存活率」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Plant survival during establishment” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"生態護岸的功能會隨植物建立而演變，栽植後存活率只是其中一個可重複觀察的指標。萌芽、根系延伸與土壤覆蓋不同步，存活的插穗也可能尚未穿過潛在沖蝕面。調查應追蹤固定植株群並記錄洪水、乾旱與補植，避免把後來新增的植株混入原始分母。比較坡位與物種可找出適生限制，但不能由存活百分比直接推算抗剪強度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「建立期植株存活率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Bioengineered protection evolves as plants establish, and survival is one repeatable indicator among several. Budding, root extension and soil cover develop at different rates; a living cutting may not yet cross an erosion plane. Track a fixed cohort and record floods, drought and replacements so newly planted individuals do not contaminate the original denominator. Compare species and bank elevations to investigate suitability, without converting survival percentage directly into shear resistance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Plant survival during establishment” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「建立期植株存活率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Plant survival during establishment”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-21-k1","title":"建立期植株存活率","titleEn":"Plant survival during establishment","text":"生態護岸的功能會隨植物建立而演變，栽植後存活率只是其中一個可重複觀察的指標。萌芽、根系延伸與土壤覆蓋不同步，存活的插穗也可能尚未穿過潛在沖蝕面。","textEn":"Bioengineered protection evolves as plants establish, and survival is one repeatable indicator among several. Budding, root extension and soil cover develop at different rates; a living cutting may not yet cross an erosion plane.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「建立期植株存活率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Plant survival during establishment\" is correct?","options":["生態護岸的功能會隨植物建立而演變，栽植後存活率只是其中一個可重複觀察的指標。","原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比","採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積"],"optionsEn":["Bioengineered protection evolves as plants establish, and survival is one repeatable indicator among several.","The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength","Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"生態護岸的功能會隨植物建立而演變，栽植後存活率只是其中一個可重複觀察的指標。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Bioengineered protection evolves as plants establish, and survival is one repeatable indicator among several. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b276-v15-22","title":"建立期植株存活率：定量估算","titleEn":"Plant survival during establishment: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「建立期植株存活率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Plant survival during establishment” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless。適用邊界：固定原始植株群的觀察比例，不含補植且不是抗剪能力比例。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Observed proportion of the fixed original cohort, excluding replacements and not representing a shear strength ratio. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：為原始植株編號，在相同季節重訪並明確定義存活，例如有活體芽或組織。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Tag the original cohort and revisit in the same season with an explicit definition of survival.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless。適用邊界：固定原始植株群的觀察比例，不含補植且不是抗剪能力比例。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Observed proportion of the fixed original cohort, excluding replacements and not representing a shear strength ratio.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「建立期植株存活率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Plant survival during establishment\", which statement holds?","options":["下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless。","河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力"],"optionsEn":["Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless.","Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N0=240 plants; Ns=180 plants; ps=Ns/N0=0.75 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b276-v15-23","title":"建立期植株存活率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Plant survival during establishment: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「建立期植株存活率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Plant survival during establishment” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"為原始植株編號，在相同季節重訪並明確定義存活，例如有活體芽或組織。另記失蹤、確認死亡及無法判定的數量，補植單獨建帳，再依坡位比較，避免淹水區漏查造成偏差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Tag the original cohort and revisit in the same season with an explicit definition of survival. Record missing, confirmed dead and uncertain plants separately. Keep replacements in another register and compare bank elevations to detect incomplete field survey bias. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將失蹤但未確認死亡的二十株分別視為存活及死亡，建立上下界。再設計一個不破壞整片護岸的根區抽樣方案，說明抽樣如何連結功能判讀。","observationEn":"Site practice: Treat twenty missing plants alternately as alive and dead to construct bounds. Design a limited root-zone sampling programme and explain how those observations would connect survival records with the intended protective function.","failure":"注意干擾：補植後若把新株計入存活數而沿用原始分母，會高估建立成功。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Counting replacement plants against the original denominator exaggerates establishment success. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"為原始植株編號，在相同季節重訪並明確定義存活，例如有活體芽或組織。另記失蹤、確認死亡及無法判定的數量，補植單獨建帳，再依坡位比較，避免淹水區漏查造成偏差。","textEn":"Tag the original cohort and revisit in the same season with an explicit definition of survival. Record missing, confirmed dead and uncertain plants separately. Keep replacements in another register and compare bank elevations to detect incomplete field survey bias.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將失蹤但未確認死亡的二十株分別視為存活及死亡，建立上下界。再設計一個不破壞整片護岸的根區抽樣方案，說明抽樣如何連結功能判讀。","textEn":"Treat twenty missing plants alternately as alive and dead to construct bounds. Design a limited root-zone sampling programme and explain how those observations would connect survival records with the intended protective function.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「建立期植株存活率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Plant survival during establishment\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力","為原始植株編號，在相同季節重訪並明確定義存活，例如有活體芽或組織。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth","Tag the original cohort and revisit in the same season with an explicit definition of survival."],"answer":2,"explanation":"為原始植株編號，在相同季節重訪並明確定義存活，例如有活體芽或組織。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Tag the original cohort and revisit in the same season with an explicit definition of survival. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b276-v15-24","title":"建立期植株存活率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Plant survival during establishment: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「建立期植株存活率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Plant survival during establishment” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"補植後若把新株計入存活數而沿用原始分母，會高估建立成功。另一方面，短期綠葉也可能掩蓋根部腐爛，需結合根區與土壤觀察。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Counting replacement plants against the original denominator exaggerates establishment success. Short lived foliage can also conceal root decay, so survival counts need observations of root conditions and surrounding soil. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較坡位與物種可找出適生限制，但不能由存活百分比直接推算抗剪強度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare species and bank elevations to investigate suitability, without converting survival percentage directly into shear resistance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"補植後若把新株計入存活數而沿用原始分母，會高估建立成功。另一方面，短期綠葉也可能掩蓋根部腐爛，需結合根區與土壤觀察。","textEn":"Counting replacement plants against the original denominator exaggerates establishment success. Short lived foliage can also conceal root decay, so survival counts need observations of root conditions and surrounding soil.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「建立期植株存活率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Plant survival during establishment\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補植後若把新株計入存活數而沿用原始分母，會高估建立成功。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積"],"optionsEn":["Counting replacement plants against the original denominator exaggerates establishment success.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"補植後若把新株計入存活數而沿用原始分母，會高估建立成功。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Counting replacement plants against the original denominator exaggerates establishment success. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b276-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」與「退水期孔隙水壓」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Mat overlap and effective coverage\" and \"Pore pressure during drawdown\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b276-v15-25","title":"纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Mat overlap and effective coverage: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mat overlap and effective coverage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"椰纖維毯的採購面積不等於實際覆蓋面積，搭接、端部固定與曲面貼合都會消耗材料。搭接方向要配合水流，避免迎流邊緣掀起後使水在毯下集中。相鄰條帶需保持連續接觸土面，懸空會讓幼根難以穿入，也會形成沖蝕通道。數量估算可以先用平面幾何，但施工驗收還要檢查坡面展長、固定點與排水，不能用足量材料替代安裝品質。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Purchased coir mat area differs from effective cover because seams, end anchorage and surface conformity consume material. Orient overlaps with flow so exposed edges do not lift and channel water underneath. Adjacent strips need continuous soil contact; bridging can obstruct root establishment and create erosion pathways. Begin quantities with planar geometry, then inspect slope length, fixings and drainage. Delivering enough material does not demonstrate that the installation transfers loads or supports vegetation as intended. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Mat overlap and effective coverage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2.","failure":"常見誤解：「採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Mat overlap and effective coverage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-25-k1","title":"纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋","titleEn":"Mat overlap and effective coverage","text":"椰纖維毯的採購面積不等於實際覆蓋面積，搭接、端部固定與曲面貼合都會消耗材料。搭接方向要配合水流，避免迎流邊緣掀起後使水在毯下集中。","textEn":"Purchased coir mat area differs from effective cover because seams, end anchorage and surface conformity consume material. Orient overlaps with flow so exposed edges do not lift and channel water underneath.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mat overlap and effective coverage\" is correct?","options":["採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積","椰纖維毯的採購面積不等於實際覆蓋面積，搭接、端部固定與曲面貼合都會消耗材料。","岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散"],"optionsEn":["Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation","Purchased coir mat area differs from effective cover because seams, end anchorage and surface conformity consume material.","A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"椰纖維毯的採購面積不等於實際覆蓋面積，搭接、端部固定與曲面貼合都會消耗材料。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Purchased coir mat area differs from effective cover because seams, end anchorage and surface conformity consume material. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b276-v15-26","title":"纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋：定量估算","titleEn":"Mat overlap and effective coverage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mat overlap and effective coverage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2。適用邊界：平面平行條帶僅計五道縱向搭接，未扣端部與曲面裁切。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2. Applicable boundary: Parallel planar strips with five longitudinal overlaps only; excludes end anchorage and curved trimming. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在展開圖上逐條標出淨寬與搭接，不把每條兩側都重複扣除。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark net width and seams strip by strip without subtracting every edge twice.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2。適用邊界：平面平行條帶僅計五道縱向搭接，未扣端部與曲面裁切。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2. Applicable boundary: Parallel planar strips with five longitudinal overlaps only; excludes end anchorage and curved trimming.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mat overlap and effective coverage\", which statement holds?","options":["處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成","種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2。"],"optionsEn":["Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works","Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: N=6 strips; w=2 m; o=0.2 m; L=20 m; Ac=(N*w-(N-1)*o)*L=220 m2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b276-v15-27","title":"纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Mat overlap and effective coverage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mat overlap and effective coverage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在展開圖上逐條標出淨寬與搭接，不把每條兩側都重複扣除。現場用卷尺抽驗搭接和坡面貼合，灑少量清水觀察是否沿毯下集中，再另列端部埋設與修剪損耗。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark net width and seams strip by strip without subtracting every edge twice. Check overlap and soil contact in the field. A small controlled water application can reveal underflow; record end anchorage and trimming losses separately. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把搭接改為三十公分重新計算淨覆蓋，並畫出彎曲岸坡需要裁切的位置。將幾何損耗與安裝缺失分成兩項，提出各自的驗收證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase overlap to thirty centimetres and recalculate effective coverage. Draw where a curved bank requires trimming, distinguish geometric waste from installation defects, and specify separate acceptance evidence for those two issues.","failure":"注意干擾：材料總面積足夠但接縫逆流或鬆弛時，水會掀毯並從下方沖走細土。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adequate total material can still fail when loose or upstream-facing seams lift. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在展開圖上逐條標出淨寬與搭接，不把每條兩側都重複扣除。現場用卷尺抽驗搭接和坡面貼合，灑少量清水觀察是否沿毯下集中，再另列端部埋設與修剪損耗。","textEn":"Mark net width and seams strip by strip without subtracting every edge twice. Check overlap and soil contact in the field. A small controlled water application can reveal underflow; record end anchorage and trimming losses separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把搭接改為三十公分重新計算淨覆蓋，並畫出彎曲岸坡需要裁切的位置。將幾何損耗與安裝缺失分成兩項，提出各自的驗收證據。","textEn":"Increase overlap to thirty centimetres and recalculate effective coverage. Draw where a curved bank requires trimming, distinguish geometric waste from installation defects, and specify separate acceptance evidence for those two issues.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mat overlap and effective coverage\"?","options":["在展開圖上逐條標出淨寬與搭接，不把每條兩側都重複扣除。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載"],"optionsEn":["Mark net width and seams strip by strip without subtracting every edge twice.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor"],"answer":0,"explanation":"在展開圖上逐條標出淨寬與搭接，不把每條兩側都重複扣除。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark net width and seams strip by strip without subtracting every edge twice. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b276-v15-28","title":"纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mat overlap and effective coverage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mat overlap and effective coverage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"材料總面積足夠但接縫逆流或鬆弛時，水會掀毯並從下方沖走細土。裸露小縫可能擴大成集中溝，應追查接縫方向及固定點。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adequate total material can still fail when loose or upstream-facing seams lift. Water then removes soil beneath the mat, turning small openings into channels; inspect seam orientation and fixing locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：數量估算可以先用平面幾何，但施工驗收還要檢查坡面展長、固定點與排水，不能用足量材料替代安裝品質。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Delivering enough material does not demonstrate that the installation transfers loads or supports vegetation as intended.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"材料總面積足夠但接縫逆流或鬆弛時，水會掀毯並從下方沖走細土。裸露小縫可能擴大成集中溝，應追查接縫方向及固定點。","textEn":"Adequate total material can still fail when loose or upstream-facing seams lift. Water then removes soil beneath the mat, turning small openings into channels; inspect seam orientation and fixing locations.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「纖維毯搭接與淨覆蓋」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mat overlap and effective coverage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","材料總面積足夠但接縫逆流或鬆弛時，水會掀毯並從下方沖走細土。","岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Adequate total material can still fail when loose or upstream-facing seams lift.","A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料總面積足夠但接縫逆流或鬆弛時，水會掀毯並從下方沖走細土。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adequate total material can still fail when loose or upstream-facing seams lift. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b276-v15-29","title":"退水期孔隙水壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pore pressure during drawdown: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「退水期孔隙水壓」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pore pressure during drawdown” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"洪水退去後，河道側支承水壓可能先降低，而岸土內水位仍高，產生朝河道的滲流與較低有效應力。植物蒸散不能在短時間內保證消除這種壓差，根系補強也不取代排水條件分析。以水頭差估算孔壓只能描述指定位置與假定連通狀態，真實退水過程還受滲透係數、層理與儲水性控制。監測應把河水位與岸內孔壓時間序列同步對齊。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「退水期孔隙水壓」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After a flood, river support pressure may fall before pore pressures inside the bank dissipate, promoting outward seepage and reducing effective stress. Plant transpiration cannot guarantee rapid relief, and roots do not replace drainage analysis. A head difference estimates pressure at a specified point under assumed connectivity, while actual drawdown depends on permeability, layering and storage. Synchronize river stage and internal piezometer records to distinguish transient pressure lag from static groundwater conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pore pressure during drawdown” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「退水期孔隙水壓」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pore pressure during drawdown”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-29-k1","title":"退水期孔隙水壓","titleEn":"Pore pressure during drawdown","text":"洪水退去後，河道側支承水壓可能先降低，而岸土內水位仍高，產生朝河道的滲流與較低有效應力。植物蒸散不能在短時間內保證消除這種壓差，根系補強也不取代排水條件分析。","textEn":"After a flood, river support pressure may fall before pore pressures inside the bank dissipate, promoting outward seepage and reducing effective stress. Plant transpiration cannot guarantee rapid relief, and roots do not replace drainage analysis.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「退水期孔隙水壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pore pressure during drawdown\" is correct?","options":["岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散","下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂","洪水退去後，河道側支承水壓可能先降低，而岸土內水位仍高，產生朝河道的滲流與較低有效應力。"],"optionsEn":["A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated","Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction","After a flood, river support pressure may fall before pore pressures inside the bank dissipate, promoting outward seepage and reducing effective stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"洪水退去後，河道側支承水壓可能先降低，而岸土內水位仍高，產生朝河道的滲流與較低有效應力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After a flood, river support pressure may fall before pore pressures inside the bank dissipate, promoting outward seepage and reducing effective stress. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b276-v15-30","title":"退水期孔隙水壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Pore pressure during drawdown: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「退水期孔隙水壓」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pore pressure during drawdown” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa。適用邊界：同一高程兩點之靜水壓差示例，不求解非定常滲流或整體穩定。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa. Applicable boundary: Illustrates hydrostatic pressure difference at one elevation, without solving transient seepage or overall stability. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在岸內不同深度設孔壓量測點，與河水位使用同一高程及時鐘。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Place piezometers at different depths and use a common datum and clock with river stage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa。適用邊界：同一高程兩點之靜水壓差示例，不求解非定常滲流或整體穩定。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa. Applicable boundary: Illustrates hydrostatic pressure difference at one elevation, without solving transient seepage or overall stability.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「退水期孔隙水壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pore pressure during drawdown\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa。","河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力","表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa.","Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location","Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: gammaw=9.81 kN/m3; dh=2 m; du=gammaw*dh=19.62 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b276-v15-31","title":"退水期孔隙水壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pore pressure during drawdown: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「退水期孔隙水壓」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pore pressure during drawdown” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在岸內不同深度設孔壓量測點，與河水位使用同一高程及時鐘。退水時比較峰值與延遲，並查看排水出口是否阻塞；若土層反應差異大，應分層建模而非平均所有孔壓。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Place piezometers at different depths and use a common datum and clock with river stage. Compare pressure peaks and delays during drawdown, inspect drainage outlets, and model distinct layers separately when their measured pressure responses differ substantially. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：假設河水再降五十公分而岸內水頭未變，重算壓差。畫出兩條可能的消散曲線，指出需要多長的觀測紀錄才能分辨快速與緩慢排水。","observationEn":"Site practice: Lower river stage another fifty centimetres while holding internal head fixed and recalculate the pressure difference. Sketch fast and slow dissipation curves and specify monitoring duration needed to distinguish the two responses.","failure":"注意干擾：不透水夾層可能保留高孔壓，岸面看似乾燥卻仍有深層滑動風險。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A low permeability layer may retain pressure beneath a dry-looking surface. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在岸內不同深度設孔壓量測點，與河水位使用同一高程及時鐘。退水時比較峰值與延遲，並查看排水出口是否阻塞；若土層反應差異大，應分層建模而非平均所有孔壓。","textEn":"Place piezometers at different depths and use a common datum and clock with river stage. Compare pressure peaks and delays during drawdown, inspect drainage outlets, and model distinct layers separately when their measured pressure responses differ substantially.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"假設河水再降五十公分而岸內水頭未變，重算壓差。畫出兩條可能的消散曲線，指出需要多長的觀測紀錄才能分辨快速與緩慢排水。","textEn":"Lower river stage another fifty centimetres while holding internal head fixed and recalculate the pressure difference. Sketch fast and slow dissipation curves and specify monitoring duration needed to distinguish the two responses.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「退水期孔隙水壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pore pressure during drawdown\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在岸內不同深度設孔壓量測點，與河水位使用同一高程及時鐘。","剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Place piezometers at different depths and use a common datum and clock with river stage.","Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood"],"answer":1,"explanation":"在岸內不同深度設孔壓量測點，與河水位使用同一高程及時鐘。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Place piezometers at different depths and use a common datum and clock with river stage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b276-v15-32","title":"退水期孔隙水壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pore pressure during drawdown: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「退水期孔隙水壓」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pore pressure during drawdown” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不透水夾層可能保留高孔壓，岸面看似乾燥卻仍有深層滑動風險。若只量地表含水率，會誤判退水後已恢復承載能力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A low permeability layer may retain pressure beneath a dry-looking surface. Surface moisture alone can therefore suggest recovered resistance while deeper parts of the bank remain vulnerable to sliding. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：監測應把河水位與岸內孔壓時間序列同步對齊。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Synchronize river stage and internal piezometer records to distinguish transient pressure lag from static groundwater conditions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岸面已經乾燥就代表深處孔隙水壓已完全消散」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A dry bank surface proves that deeper pore water pressure has completely dissipated\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不透水夾層可能保留高孔壓，岸面看似乾燥卻仍有深層滑動風險。若只量地表含水率，會誤判退水後已恢復承載能力。","textEn":"A low permeability layer may retain pressure beneath a dry-looking surface. Surface moisture alone can therefore suggest recovered resistance while deeper parts of the bank remain vulnerable to sliding.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「退水期孔隙水壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pore pressure during drawdown\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂","不透水夾層可能保留高孔壓，岸面看似乾燥卻仍有深層滑動風險。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction","A low permeability layer may retain pressure beneath a dry-looking surface."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不透水夾層可能保留高孔壓，岸面看似乾燥卻仍有深層滑動風險。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A low permeability layer may retain pressure beneath a dry-looking surface. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b276-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」與「對照監測的生態成效」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Sediment flux around bank treatments\" and \"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b276-v15-33","title":"泥砂通量的護岸檢核：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Sediment flux around bank treatments: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sediment flux around bank treatments” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"生態護岸可能攔截細砂，也可能在施工或洪水初期釋出土粒，因此應比較質量通量而非只比較濁度讀數。流量與濃度必須在相同控制體邊界及時段取得，清水側向流入會稀釋濃度卻不代表沉積。輸入減輸出得到的是控制體內暫存與未量側向交換的合計，需要另查床面變化才能歸因。濁度轉濃度關係還會隨粒徑與有機質改變，必須用水樣校準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A treatment may trap fines or release soil during construction and early floods. Compare mass flux rather than turbidity alone, matching discharge and concentration at the same boundaries and times. Clear lateral inflow can dilute concentration without depositing sediment. Inflow minus outflow represents storage plus unmeasured exchanges, requiring bed observations before attribution. The turbidity to concentration relation also changes with grain size and organic material, so physical samples are needed for calibration. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sediment flux around bank treatments” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg.","failure":"常見誤解：「下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sediment flux around bank treatments”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-33-k1","title":"泥砂通量的護岸檢核","titleEn":"Sediment flux around bank treatments","text":"生態護岸可能攔截細砂，也可能在施工或洪水初期釋出土粒，因此應比較質量通量而非只比較濁度讀數。流量與濃度必須在相同控制體邊界及時段取得，清水側向流入會稀釋濃度卻不代表沉積。","textEn":"A treatment may trap fines or release soil during construction and early floods. Compare mass flux rather than turbidity alone, matching discharge and concentration at the same boundaries and times.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sediment flux around bank treatments\" is correct?","options":["生態護岸可能攔截細砂，也可能在施工或洪水初期釋出土粒，因此應比較質量通量而非只比較濁度讀數。","下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂","處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成"],"optionsEn":["A treatment may trap fines or release soil during construction and early floods.","Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction","Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works"],"answer":0,"explanation":"生態護岸可能攔截細砂，也可能在施工或洪水初期釋出土粒，因此應比較質量通量而非只比較濁度讀數。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A treatment may trap fines or release soil during construction and early floods. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b276-v15-34","title":"泥砂通量的護岸檢核：定量估算","titleEn":"Sediment flux around bank treatments: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sediment flux around bank treatments” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg。適用邊界：一小時定常且無側向泥砂通量，所得為控制體暫存，不能直接宣稱永久去除。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg. Applicable boundary: Steady one-hour interval without lateral sediment flux; result is control-volume storage, not demonstrated permanent removal. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步採集上下游流量與水樣，以實驗室懸浮固體建立濁度校正，再確認是否有排水溝或岸崩加入泥砂。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Collect synchronized upstream and downstream discharge and samples, calibrate turbidity against suspended solids, and identify drains or bank failures adding sediment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg。適用邊界：一小時定常且無側向泥砂通量，所得為控制體暫存，不能直接宣稱永久去除。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg. Applicable boundary: Steady one-hour interval without lateral sediment flux; result is control-volume storage, not demonstrated permanent removal.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sediment flux around bank treatments\", which statement holds?","options":["種植面積可以直接代替所有莖葉的迎流投影面積","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg。","木構的淨浮力除以錨點數就是每支錨具唯一荷載"],"optionsEn":["Planted ground area directly equals the frontal area of all stems","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qin=0.08 m3/s.","Net buoyancy divided by anchor count is the only load on each anchor"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qin=0.08 m3/s; Cin=0.12 kg/m3; Qout=0.075 m3/s; Cout=0.07 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; dM=(Qin*Cin-Qout*Cout)*dt=15.66 kg. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b276-v15-35","title":"泥砂通量的護岸檢核：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sediment flux around bank treatments: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sediment flux around bank treatments” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步採集上下游流量與水樣，以實驗室懸浮固體建立濁度校正，再確認是否有排水溝或岸崩加入泥砂。用床面標記或沉積盤驗證暫存方向，並在下一次洪水後查是否重新被帶走。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Collect synchronized upstream and downstream discharge and samples, calibrate turbidity against suspended solids, and identify drains or bank failures adding sediment. Check storage direction with bed markers or traps, then inspect whether the next monitored flood event remobilizes that stored material. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：新增一股已知流量與濃度的側向排水後重寫質量平衡，列出新增量測。比較暫存與永久去除需要的追蹤時間，說明下一場洪水可能如何改變結論。","observationEn":"Site practice: Add a lateral drain with specified flow and concentration, rewrite the mass balance and list new measurements. Compare the monitoring needed for temporary storage and permanent removal, including how another flood could reverse the interpretation.","failure":"注意干擾：若下游被清水稀釋，濃度下降可能被誤報成攔砂成功。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Dilution can make lower concentration appear to prove trapping. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步採集上下游流量與水樣，以實驗室懸浮固體建立濁度校正，再確認是否有排水溝或岸崩加入泥砂。用床面標記或沉積盤驗證暫存方向，並在下一次洪水後查是否重新被帶走。","textEn":"Collect synchronized upstream and downstream discharge and samples, calibrate turbidity against suspended solids, and identify drains or bank failures adding sediment. Check storage direction with bed markers or traps, then inspect whether the next monitored flood event remobilizes that stored material.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"新增一股已知流量與濃度的側向排水後重寫質量平衡，列出新增量測。比較暫存與永久去除需要的追蹤時間，說明下一場洪水可能如何改變結論。","textEn":"Add a lateral drain with specified flow and concentration, rewrite the mass balance and list new measurements. Compare the monitoring needed for temporary storage and permanent removal, including how another flood could reverse the interpretation.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sediment flux around bank treatments\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","原始植株存活百分比就是護岸抗剪強度保留百分比","同步採集上下游流量與水樣，以實驗室懸浮固體建立濁度校正，再確認是否有排水溝或岸崩加入泥砂。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The surviving percentage of original plants equals the retained percentage of bank shear strength","Collect synchronized upstream and downstream discharge and samples, calibrate turbidity against suspended solids, and identify drains or bank failures adding sediment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步採集上下游流量與水樣，以實驗室懸浮固體建立濁度校正，再確認是否有排水溝或岸崩加入泥砂。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Collect synchronized upstream and downstream discharge and samples, calibrate turbidity against suspended solids, and identify drains or bank failures adding sediment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b276-v15-36","title":"泥砂通量的護岸檢核：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sediment flux around bank treatments: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sediment flux around bank treatments” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若下游被清水稀釋，濃度下降可能被誤報成攔砂成功。漏算側向流量或採樣時間錯開，也會製造假質量差，應先閉合水量帳。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Dilution can make lower concentration appear to prove trapping. Missing lateral flows or mismatched sampling times also create false mass differences, so close the water balance before interpreting sediment retention. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：濁度轉濃度關係還會隨粒徑與有機質改變，必須用水樣校準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The turbidity to concentration relation also changes with grain size and organic material, so physical samples are needed for calibration.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「下游濃度下降就足以證明護岸永久移除了同等比例泥砂」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Lower downstream concentration alone proves permanent removal of the same sediment fraction\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若下游被清水稀釋，濃度下降可能被誤報成攔砂成功。漏算側向流量或採樣時間錯開，也會製造假質量差，應先閉合水量帳。","textEn":"Dilution can make lower concentration appear to prove trapping. Missing lateral flows or mismatched sampling times also create false mass differences, so close the water balance before interpreting sediment retention.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「泥砂通量的護岸檢核」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sediment flux around bank treatments\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若下游被清水稀釋，濃度下降可能被誤報成攔砂成功。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成"],"optionsEn":["Dilution can make lower concentration appear to prove trapping.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works"],"answer":0,"explanation":"若下游被清水稀釋，濃度下降可能被誤報成攔砂成功。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Dilution can make lower concentration appear to prove trapping. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b276-v15-37","title":"對照監測的生態成效：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「對照監測的生態成效」如何影響河岸生態護岸的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Bioengineered riverbank protection”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"工程後植被增加可能來自較濕的年份、放牧減少或上游治理，而不完全由護岸措施造成。前後加對照的設計，用未處理區的同期間變化扣除共同背景，能提供比單純前後比較更清楚的證據。對照區仍須有相近坡位、土壤與管理，並避免受工程水流改變影響。覆蓋率是面積比例，差中之差應以百分點表示；它不能單獨代表物種多樣性、棲地品質或結構安全。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「對照監測的生態成效」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Vegetation can increase because a year is wetter, grazing declines or upstream management changes. A before-after comparison with an untreated reach subtracts shared background change and offers stronger evidence than a simple before-after count. The comparison reach still needs similar soils, elevation and management, without receiving the treatment's hydraulic effects. Cover is an area proportion, so the difference in differences uses percentage points and does not independently measure biodiversity, habitat quality or structural safety. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points.","failure":"常見誤解：「處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「對照監測的生態成效」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-37-k1","title":"對照監測的生態成效","titleEn":"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring","text":"工程後植被增加可能來自較濕的年份、放牧減少或上游治理，而不完全由護岸措施造成。前後加對照的設計，用未處理區的同期間變化扣除共同背景，能提供比單純前後比較更清楚的證據。","textEn":"Vegetation can increase because a year is wetter, grazing declines or upstream management changes. A before-after comparison with an untreated reach subtracts shared background change and offers stronger evidence than a simple before-after count.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「對照監測的生態成效」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring\" is correct?","options":["處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成","工程後植被增加可能來自較濕的年份、放牧減少或上游治理，而不完全由護岸措施造成。","河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力"],"optionsEn":["Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works","Vegetation can increase because a year is wetter, grazing declines or upstream management changes.","Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location"],"answer":1,"explanation":"工程後植被增加可能來自較濕的年份、放牧減少或上游治理，而不完全由護岸措施造成。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Vegetation can increase because a year is wetter, grazing declines or upstream management changes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b276-v15-38","title":"對照監測的生態成效：定量估算","titleEn":"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「對照監測的生態成效」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points。適用邊界：示範差中之差，因果解釋仍需平行趨勢與不受干擾的對照。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points. Applicable boundary: Illustrates difference in differences; causal interpretation still requires parallel trends and an unaffected comparison. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在工程前至少重複調查不同季節，確認兩區變化方向是否相近，之後用相同樣方與判讀規則追蹤。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Repeat surveys across seasons before treatment to compare trajectories, then retain the same quadrats and interpretation rules.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points。適用邊界：示範差中之差，因果解釋仍需平行趨勢與不受干擾的對照。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points. Applicable boundary: Illustrates difference in differences; causal interpretation still requires parallel trends and an unaffected comparison.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「對照監測的生態成效」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring\", which statement holds?","options":["表層根系密度可直接代表任何深度滑動面的補強能力","剩餘埋深為正就代表護岸在所有洪水下都穩定","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points。"],"optionsEn":["Surface root density directly represents reinforcement on a failure plane at any depth","Any positive remaining embedment proves stability under every flood","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: T0=35 percent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: T0=35 percent; T1=70 percent; C0=40 percent; C1=55 percent; effect=(T1-T0)-(C1-C0)=20 percentage-points. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b276-v15-39","title":"對照監測的生態成效：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「對照監測的生態成效」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在工程前至少重複調查不同季節，確認兩區變化方向是否相近，之後用相同樣方與判讀規則追蹤。另記洪水、放牧與補植，若對照區也受到改流影響，應重新界定對照或限制因果結論。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Repeat surveys across seasons before treatment to compare trajectories, then retain the same quadrats and interpretation rules. Record floods, grazing and replanting. If altered flow affects the comparison reach, redefine it or limit the causal claim. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將對照區的後期覆蓋率改成百分之六十五，重算效果並解釋差異。設計一項獨立棲地指標，使覆蓋率改善不會被誤用為所有生態功能均改善的結論。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change later comparison cover to sixty five percent, recompute the effect and explain the difference. Add an independent habitat indicator so increased cover cannot be mistaken for improvement in every ecological function.","failure":"注意干擾：不同年份用不同樣方位置會把空間差異當成工程效果。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Moving quadrats between years confuses spatial differences with treatment effects. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在工程前至少重複調查不同季節，確認兩區變化方向是否相近，之後用相同樣方與判讀規則追蹤。另記洪水、放牧與補植，若對照區也受到改流影響，應重新界定對照或限制因果結論。","textEn":"Repeat surveys across seasons before treatment to compare trajectories, then retain the same quadrats and interpretation rules. Record floods, grazing and replanting. If altered flow affects the comparison reach, redefine it or limit the causal claim.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將對照區的後期覆蓋率改成百分之六十五，重算效果並解釋差異。設計一項獨立棲地指標，使覆蓋率改善不會被誤用為所有生態功能均改善的結論。","textEn":"Change later comparison cover to sixty five percent, recompute the effect and explain the difference. Add an independent habitat indicator so increased cover cannot be mistaken for improvement in every ecological function.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「對照監測的生態成效」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring\"?","options":["在工程前至少重複調查不同季節，確認兩區變化方向是否相近，之後用相同樣方與判讀規則追蹤。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","採購總面積等於完工後不重疊的有效覆蓋面積"],"optionsEn":["Repeat surveys across seasons before treatment to compare trajectories, then retain the same quadrats and interpretation rules.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Purchased material area equals the effective nonoverlapping area after installation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"在工程前至少重複調查不同季節，確認兩區變化方向是否相近，之後用相同樣方與判讀規則追蹤。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Repeat surveys across seasons before treatment to compare trajectories, then retain the same quadrats and interpretation rules. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b276-v15-40","title":"對照監測的生態成效：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b276-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「對照監測的生態成效」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不同年份用不同樣方位置會把空間差異當成工程效果。若只選長得好的護岸段，平均覆蓋也會偏高，需事先固定抽樣設計。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Moving quadrats between years confuses spatial differences with treatment effects. Selecting only thriving sections further inflates average cover; fix the sampling design before observing which areas appear successful in the field. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：覆蓋率是面積比例，差中之差應以百分點表示；它不能單獨代表物種多樣性、棲地品質或結構安全。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Cover is an area proportion, so the difference in differences uses percentage points and does not independently measure biodiversity, habitat quality or structural safety.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「處理區植被增加的全部百分點都必然由護岸工程造成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every percentage point of vegetation gain in the treated reach must be caused by the works\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b276-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不同年份用不同樣方位置會把空間差異當成工程效果。若只選長得好的護岸段，平均覆蓋也會偏高，需事先固定抽樣設計。","textEn":"Moving quadrats between years confuses spatial differences with treatment effects. Selecting only thriving sections further inflates average cover; fix the sampling design before observing which areas appear successful in the field.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b276-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「對照監測的生態成效」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ecological outcomes with comparison monitoring\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","不同年份用不同樣方位置會把空間差異當成工程效果。","河段平均剪力就是每一處岸坡承受的最大剪力"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Moving quadrats between years confuses spatial differences with treatment effects.","Reach average shear is the maximum stress at every bank location"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同年份用不同樣方位置會把空間差異當成工程效果。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Moving quadrats between years confuses spatial differences with treatment effects. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-nrcs-bank-standard","v15s-eea-regge"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b277","title":"河床固床工設計","titleEn":"Riverbed grade-control structures","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"固床工會改變水面、河床及泥砂通量，並非把河床固定後便完成任務。十個單元連結落差配置、臨界水深、水躍、揚壓、顆粒起動、濾層與上下游地形反應，讓學員分辨幾何可行、結構穩定與河道長期平衡三種不同檢核。","summaryEn":"Grade control changes water levels, bed elevations and sediment fluxes. Ten units connect drop spacing, critical depth, hydraulic jumps, uplift, grain motion, filters and channel response. Learners distinguish geometric feasibility, structural resistance and long term channel adjustment, and examine how protecting one location may transfer erosion or sedimentation to another reach.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["落差配置與縱坡","Drop spacing and longitudinal slope"],["臨界水深與控制斷面","Critical depth and control sections"],["護坦揚壓與排水","Apron uplift and drainage"],["濾層粒徑的相容比較","Filter grading compatibility"],["遷移陡坎的追蹤","Tracking migrating bed steps"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["落差配置與縱坡","臨界水深與控制斷面","護坦揚壓與排水","濾層粒徑的相容比較","遷移陡坎的追蹤"],"labelsEn":["Drop spacing and longitudinal slope","Critical depth and control sections","Apron uplift and drainage","Filter grading compatibility","Tracking migrating bed steps"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課先用「落差配置與縱坡」建立原創假想基準，再以「斷面比能的兩種流態」檢查另一個控制機制。第一組輸入及結果為 dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m；第二組為 y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m。學員需在同一張工作表分列量綱、時間、位置與適用範圍，先核對守恆，再解釋為何兩個得數不能互相代替。最後以第三單元提出的量測設計驗證假設，並將超出模型能力的水理、生態或治理問題列為待研究項目；這些示例並非所列案例的現場實測。敏感度重算：固定兩個無因次坡度 S0=0.012 與 Se=0.004，將單一落差 dz 從 0.6 m 增至 0.66 m，L=82.5 m，相較 75 m 增加一成。此為幾何敏感度，沒有驗證較大落差的消能、通行或結構需求。","textEn":"Begin with an original hypothetical baseline for Drop spacing and longitudinal slope and examine another controlling mechanism through Specific energy and alternate depths. The first inputs and result are dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m; the second are y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m. Keep dimensions, time, location and validity conditions in separate columns of the same working sheet. Check conservation before explaining why the two numerical results cannot substitute for one another. Use the third unit measurement design to test assumptions and identify hydraulic, ecological or governance questions that exceed the model. These examples are not field observations from the named reference cases. Sensitivity recalculation: Hold dimensionless slopes S0=0.012 and Se=0.004 fixed and raise drop dz from 0.6 m to 0.66 m. Spacing becomes 82.5 m, ten percent above 75 m. This is geometric sensitivity and does not validate energy dissipation, passage or structural requirements at the larger drop.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b277-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「落差配置與縱坡」與「斷面比能的兩種流態」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope\" and \"Specific energy and alternate depths\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b277-v15-01","title":"落差配置與縱坡：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「落差配置與縱坡」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drop spacing and longitudinal slope” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"固床工把河段總落差分配到構造物與其間河床，先用幾何關係可以檢查配置是否自洽。原坡與目標坡的差值乘以間距，才是單一落差需要承擔的高程差，並非河段全部天然落差。目標坡還受輸砂、河寬與下游控制影響，不能僅為縮短施工量而任意選定。配置圖須同時標出支流匯入、橋梁與魚類通行位置，因為相同總落差的不同分配會產生不同局部影響。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「落差配置與縱坡」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Grade control distributes total reach fall between structures and intervening bed. A geometric balance checks consistency: the difference between existing and target slope, multiplied by spacing, gives the drop assigned to one structure. Target slope also depends on sediment supply, width and downstream control, so it cannot be chosen solely to reduce construction. Map tributaries, bridges and passage routes because different distributions of identical total fall create different local consequences. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drop spacing and longitudinal slope” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「落差配置與縱坡」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drop spacing and longitudinal slope”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-01-k1","title":"落差配置與縱坡","titleEn":"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope","text":"固床工把河段總落差分配到構造物與其間河床，先用幾何關係可以檢查配置是否自洽。原坡與目標坡的差值乘以間距，才是單一落差需要承擔的高程差，並非河段全部天然落差。","textEn":"Grade control distributes total reach fall between structures and intervening bed. A geometric balance checks consistency: the difference between existing and target slope, multiplied by spacing, gives the drop assigned to one structure.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「落差配置與縱坡」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope\" is correct?","options":["由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距","固床工把河段總落差分配到構造物與其間河床，先用幾何關係可以檢查配置是否自洽。","不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失"],"optionsEn":["Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge","Grade control distributes total reach fall between structures and intervening bed.","Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss"],"answer":1,"explanation":"固床工把河段總落差分配到構造物與其間河床，先用幾何關係可以檢查配置是否自洽。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Grade control distributes total reach fall between structures and intervening bed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b277-v15-02","title":"落差配置與縱坡：定量估算","titleEn":"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「落差配置與縱坡」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drop spacing and longitudinal slope” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m。適用邊界：均一坡度的幾何初估，不是最適間距或平衡坡保證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m. Applicable boundary: Geometric screening with uniform slopes, not an optimal spacing or guarantee of equilibrium. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同一高程基準重測河床縱斷面，分辨局部沙洲頂與深槽底，核對相鄰構造物之間的總落差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Resurvey the bed profile on one datum, distinguishing bar crests from the thalweg, and check total fall between structures.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m。適用邊界：均一坡度的幾何初估，不是最適間距或平衡坡保證。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m. Applicable boundary: Geometric screening with uniform slopes, not an optimal spacing or guarantee of equilibrium.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「落差配置與縱坡」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope\", which statement holds?","options":["共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠","同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m。"],"optionsEn":["A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough","One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: dz=0.6 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: dz=0.6 m; S0=0.012 dimensionless; Se=0.004 dimensionless; L=dz/(S0-Se)=75 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b277-v15-03","title":"落差配置與縱坡：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「落差配置與縱坡」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drop spacing and longitudinal slope” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同一高程基準重測河床縱斷面，分辨局部沙洲頂與深槽底，核對相鄰構造物之間的總落差。將支流出口與洪水水面另畫，若存在回水控制，應進行水面與泥砂分析後再修正幾何配置。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Resurvey the bed profile on one datum, distinguishing bar crests from the thalweg, and check total fall between structures. Plot tributary outlets and flood levels separately; backwater control requires hydraulic and sediment analysis before adopting geometric spacing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將目標坡改成千分之六重算間距，說明為何落差較少分配給河床時構造密度會改變。畫出末端下切時的可能傳遞路徑，列出必要調查點。","observationEn":"Site practice: Set target slope to six per thousand and recompute spacing. Explain the changed distribution of fall, then sketch how terminal incision could propagate and identify the survey points needed to test that sequence.","failure":"注意干擾：間距雖符合幾何式，若下游河床持續下降，末端構造仍可能被淘空並引發逐級失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Geometrically consistent spacing can still fail when downstream incision undermines the terminal structure and progresses upstream. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同一高程基準重測河床縱斷面，分辨局部沙洲頂與深槽底，核對相鄰構造物之間的總落差。將支流出口與洪水水面另畫，若存在回水控制，應進行水面與泥砂分析後再修正幾何配置。","textEn":"Resurvey the bed profile on one datum, distinguishing bar crests from the thalweg, and check total fall between structures. Plot tributary outlets and flood levels separately; backwater control requires hydraulic and sediment analysis before adopting geometric spacing.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將目標坡改成千分之六重算間距，說明為何落差較少分配給河床時構造密度會改變。畫出末端下切時的可能傳遞路徑，列出必要調查點。","textEn":"Set target slope to six per thousand and recompute spacing. Explain the changed distribution of fall, then sketch how terminal incision could propagate and identify the survey points needed to test that sequence.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「落差配置與縱坡」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope\"?","options":["以同一高程基準重測河床縱斷面，分辨局部沙洲頂與深槽底，核對相鄰構造物之間的總落差。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度"],"optionsEn":["Resurvey the bed profile on one datum, distinguishing bar crests from the thalweg, and check total fall between structures.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以同一高程基準重測河床縱斷面，分辨局部沙洲頂與深槽底，核對相鄰構造物之間的總落差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Resurvey the bed profile on one datum, distinguishing bar crests from the thalweg, and check total fall between structures. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b277-v15-04","title":"落差配置與縱坡：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「落差配置與縱坡」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drop spacing and longitudinal slope” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"間距雖符合幾何式，若下游河床持續下降，末端構造仍可能被淘空並引發逐級失效。診斷應從下游控制與供砂變化回查，而非只補高上游堰頂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Geometrically consistent spacing can still fail when downstream incision undermines the terminal structure and progresses upstream. Investigate downstream control and sediment supply before simply raising upstream crests to restore the profile. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：配置圖須同時標出支流匯入、橋梁與魚類通行位置，因為相同總落差的不同分配會產生不同局部影響。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Map tributaries, bridges and passage routes because different distributions of identical total fall create different local consequences.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"間距雖符合幾何式，若下游河床持續下降，末端構造仍可能被淘空並引發逐級失效。診斷應從下游控制與供砂變化回查，而非只補高上游堰頂。","textEn":"Geometrically consistent spacing can still fail when downstream incision undermines the terminal structure and progresses upstream. Investigate downstream control and sediment supply before simply raising upstream crests to restore the profile.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「落差配置與縱坡」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drop spacing and longitudinal slope\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","間距雖符合幾何式，若下游河床持續下降，末端構造仍可能被淘空並引發逐級失效。","不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Geometrically consistent spacing can still fail when downstream incision undermines the terminal structure and progresses upstream.","Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss"],"answer":1,"explanation":"間距雖符合幾何式，若下游河床持續下降，末端構造仍可能被淘空並引發逐級失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Geometrically consistent spacing can still fail when downstream incision undermines the terminal structure and progresses upstream. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b277-v15-05","title":"斷面比能的兩種流態：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Specific energy and alternate depths: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「斷面比能的兩種流態」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Specific energy and alternate depths” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"比能以局部河床為基準，把水深與速度水頭合在一起，適合辨認落差上游是否接近控制斷面。矩形河道的單寬流量固定時，同一比能可能對應深慢與淺快兩種水深解；臨界點則是比能最低位置。這裡所稱兩種解不是可任意互換的現場狀態，還要符合上下游邊界和能量損失。河床高程若改變，總水頭必須另加高程，不能直接比較不同斷面的比能數字。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「斷面比能的兩種流態」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Specific energy combines depth and velocity head relative to the local bed. At fixed unit discharge in a rectangular channel, one energy level can correspond to a deep slow or shallow fast depth, while the minimum defines critical flow. These alternate depths are not freely interchangeable field states; boundary conditions and losses select the actual solution. When bed elevation changes, include elevation in total head rather than comparing specific energy values from different sections directly. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Specific energy and alternate depths” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「斷面比能的兩種流態」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Specific energy and alternate depths”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-05-k1","title":"斷面比能的兩種流態","titleEn":"Specific energy and alternate depths","text":"比能以局部河床為基準，把水深與速度水頭合在一起，適合辨認落差上游是否接近控制斷面。矩形河道的單寬流量固定時，同一比能可能對應深慢與淺快兩種水深解；臨界點則是比能最低位置。","textEn":"Specific energy combines depth and velocity head relative to the local bed. At fixed unit discharge in a rectangular channel, one energy level can correspond to a deep slow or shallow fast depth, while the minimum defines critical flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「斷面比能的兩種流態」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Specific energy and alternate depths\" is correct?","options":["不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失","臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流","比能以局部河床為基準，把水深與速度水頭合在一起，適合辨認落差上游是否接近控制斷面。"],"optionsEn":["Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss","Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge","Specific energy combines depth and velocity head relative to the local bed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"比能以局部河床為基準，把水深與速度水頭合在一起，適合辨認落差上游是否接近控制斷面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Specific energy combines depth and velocity head relative to the local bed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b277-v15-06","title":"斷面比能的兩種流態：定量估算","titleEn":"Specific energy and alternate depths: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「斷面比能的兩種流態」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Specific energy and alternate depths” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m。適用邊界：矩形斷面、速度分布係數取一且近似靜水壓，未包含局部損失。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m. Applicable boundary: Rectangular section with unit velocity correction and approximately hydrostatic pressure, excluding local losses. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量水深與斷面流量後以多點速度確認分布是否均勻，再將實測點放在比能曲線上。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure depth and discharge, check velocity distribution at several points, and place observations on a specific-energy curve.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m。適用邊界：矩形斷面、速度分布係數取一且近似靜水壓，未包含局部損失。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m. Applicable boundary: Rectangular section with unit velocity correction and approximately hydrostatic pressure, excluding local losses.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「斷面比能的兩種流態」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Specific energy and alternate depths\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m。","護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓","任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m.","Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition","Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y=0.8 m; q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; E=y+q^2/(2*g*y^2)=1.258716 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b277-v15-07","title":"斷面比能的兩種流態：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Specific energy and alternate depths: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「斷面比能的兩種流態」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Specific energy and alternate depths” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量水深與斷面流量後以多點速度確認分布是否均勻，再將實測點放在比能曲線上。不同測站需加回各自床高才能比較總水頭，若發現表面落差卻無對應能損，先核對基準與量測位置。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure depth and discharge, check velocity distribution at several points, and place observations on a specific-energy curve. Add bed elevation at each station before comparing total head. Apparent inconsistencies require checks of datum and measurement location before interpreting losses. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持單寬流量不變，另算一個較深水深的比能並畫在曲線上。把兩斷面床高也列入帳表，說明哪些組合需要能量輸入才可能成立。","observationEn":"Site practice: Keep unit discharge fixed and calculate specific energy at a greater depth. Plot both points and add bed elevations in a head ledger, explaining which combinations would require an external energy input.","failure":"注意干擾：在強烈垂直加速度的跌水口直接使用靜水壓比能，可能錯估控制水深。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying a hydrostatic expression within a rapidly curving nappe can misrepresent control depth. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量水深與斷面流量後以多點速度確認分布是否均勻，再將實測點放在比能曲線上。不同測站需加回各自床高才能比較總水頭，若發現表面落差卻無對應能損，先核對基準與量測位置。","textEn":"Measure depth and discharge, check velocity distribution at several points, and place observations on a specific-energy curve. Add bed elevation at each station before comparing total head. Apparent inconsistencies require checks of datum and measurement location before interpreting losses.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持單寬流量不變，另算一個較深水深的比能並畫在曲線上。把兩斷面床高也列入帳表，說明哪些組合需要能量輸入才可能成立。","textEn":"Keep unit discharge fixed and calculate specific energy at a greater depth. Plot both points and add bed elevations in a head ledger, explaining which combinations would require an external energy input.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「斷面比能的兩種流態」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Specific energy and alternate depths\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","量水深與斷面流量後以多點速度確認分布是否均勻，再將實測點放在比能曲線上。","只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Measure depth and discharge, check velocity distribution at several points, and place observations on a specific-energy curve.","Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape"],"answer":1,"explanation":"量水深與斷面流量後以多點速度確認分布是否均勻，再將實測點放在比能曲線上。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure depth and discharge, check velocity distribution at several points, and place observations on a specific-energy curve. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b277-v15-08","title":"斷面比能的兩種流態：失效診斷","titleEn":"Specific energy and alternate depths: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「斷面比能的兩種流態」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Specific energy and alternate depths” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"在強烈垂直加速度的跌水口直接使用靜水壓比能，可能錯估控制水深。應移到壓力分布較合理的斷面，或改用能描述非靜水效應的模型。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying a hydrostatic expression within a rapidly curving nappe can misrepresent control depth. Move the section to a suitable location or use a model resolving nonhydrostatic pressure and vertical acceleration. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：河床高程若改變，總水頭必須另加高程，不能直接比較不同斷面的比能數字。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: When bed elevation changes, include elevation in total head rather than comparing specific energy values from different sections directly.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"在強烈垂直加速度的跌水口直接使用靜水壓比能，可能錯估控制水深。應移到壓力分布較合理的斷面，或改用能描述非靜水效應的模型。","textEn":"Applying a hydrostatic expression within a rapidly curving nappe can misrepresent control depth. Move the section to a suitable location or use a model resolving nonhydrostatic pressure and vertical acceleration.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「斷面比能的兩種流態」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Specific energy and alternate depths\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流","在強烈垂直加速度的跌水口直接使用靜水壓比能，可能錯估控制水深。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge","Applying a hydrostatic expression within a rapidly curving nappe can misrepresent control depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在強烈垂直加速度的跌水口直接使用靜水壓比能，可能錯估控制水深。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying a hydrostatic expression within a rapidly curving nappe can misrepresent control depth. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b277-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「臨界水深與控制斷面」與「水躍共軛水深」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Critical depth and control sections\" and \"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b277-v15-09","title":"臨界水深與控制斷面：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Critical depth and control sections: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「臨界水深與控制斷面」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Critical depth and control sections” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"在矩形斷面中，比能對水深的斜率為零可導出臨界水深，對應水流傳播速度與重力波速的關係。它提供流態分界，但不代表構造物每個位置都會自動達到臨界。寬頂、收縮與下游淹沒情況會決定控制是否存在；若下游水位足夠高，原先假設的自由控制可能被淹沒。解題應先畫水面與床面，再判斷控制位置，最後才帶入單寬流量計算。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「臨界水深與控制斷面」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Critical depth follows from the minimum of specific energy in a rectangular section and relates flow speed to gravity-wave propagation. It marks a regime boundary, not a state that every point near a structure automatically reaches. Crest length, contraction and downstream submergence determine whether a control exists. High tailwater can drown a presumed free control. Draw bed and water surfaces, identify a defensible control location, and only then apply unit discharge. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Critical depth and control sections” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「臨界水深與控制斷面」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Critical depth and control sections”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-09-k1","title":"臨界水深與控制斷面","titleEn":"Critical depth and control sections","text":"在矩形斷面中，比能對水深的斜率為零可導出臨界水深，對應水流傳播速度與重力波速的關係。它提供流態分界，但不代表構造物每個位置都會自動達到臨界。","textEn":"Critical depth follows from the minimum of specific energy in a rectangular section and relates flow speed to gravity-wave propagation. It marks a regime boundary, not a state that every point near a structure automatically reaches.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「臨界水深與控制斷面」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Critical depth and control sections\" is correct?","options":["在矩形斷面中，比能對水深的斜率為零可導出臨界水深，對應水流傳播速度與重力波速的關係。","臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流","共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠"],"optionsEn":["Critical depth follows from the minimum of specific energy in a rectangular section and relates flow speed to gravity-wave propagation.","Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge","A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough"],"answer":0,"explanation":"在矩形斷面中，比能對水深的斜率為零可導出臨界水深，對應水流傳播速度與重力波速的關係。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Critical depth follows from the minimum of specific energy in a rectangular section and relates flow speed to gravity-wave propagation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b277-v15-10","title":"臨界水深與控制斷面：定量估算","titleEn":"Critical depth and control sections: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「臨界水深與控制斷面」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Critical depth and control sections” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m。適用邊界：矩形斷面之臨界水深，不能直接套用梯形斷面或淹沒控制。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m. Applicable boundary: Critical depth for a rectangular section, not directly transferable to trapezoidal sections or drowned controls. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在模型槽逐步調整尾水，觀察堰頂附近水深是否保持近似不變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Raise tailwater progressively in a flume and observe whether crest-region depth remains approximately stable.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m。適用邊界：矩形斷面之臨界水深，不能直接套用梯形斷面或淹沒控制。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m. Applicable boundary: Critical depth for a rectangular section, not directly transferable to trapezoidal sections or drowned controls.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「臨界水深與控制斷面」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Critical depth and control sections\", which statement holds?","options":["同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m。","平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度"],"optionsEn":["One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m.","Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: q=2.4 m2/s; g=9.81 m/s2; yc=(q^2/g)^(1/3)=0.837371 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b277-v15-11","title":"臨界水深與控制斷面：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Critical depth and control sections: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「臨界水深與控制斷面」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Critical depth and control sections” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在模型槽逐步調整尾水，觀察堰頂附近水深是否保持近似不變。同步量測上下游水位與流量，若尾水改變已影響控制區，就應標記淹沒轉換，不再使用單一自由出流假設外推全部工況。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Raise tailwater progressively in a flume and observe whether crest-region depth remains approximately stable. Record both water levels and discharge. Once tailwater influences the control region, identify the submergence transition instead of extrapolating a free-flow assumption. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將單寬流量增加一倍重算臨界水深，與水深也增加一倍的直覺比較。補畫自由與淹沒兩種尾水情境，指出公式仍有效與失去控制意義的位置。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double unit discharge and compare the calculated critical depth with a doubled-depth guess. Sketch free and submerged tailwater conditions and identify where the formula remains valid but no longer defines an actual control.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略尾水淹沒會高估控制能力，並可能誤判上游壅水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring submergence can exaggerate control capacity and misrepresent upstream backwater. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在模型槽逐步調整尾水，觀察堰頂附近水深是否保持近似不變。同步量測上下游水位與流量，若尾水改變已影響控制區，就應標記淹沒轉換，不再使用單一自由出流假設外推全部工況。","textEn":"Raise tailwater progressively in a flume and observe whether crest-region depth remains approximately stable. Record both water levels and discharge. Once tailwater influences the control region, identify the submergence transition instead of extrapolating a free-flow assumption.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將單寬流量增加一倍重算臨界水深，與水深也增加一倍的直覺比較。補畫自由與淹沒兩種尾水情境，指出公式仍有效與失去控制意義的位置。","textEn":"Double unit discharge and compare the calculated critical depth with a doubled-depth guess. Sketch free and submerged tailwater conditions and identify where the formula remains valid but no longer defines an actual control.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「臨界水深與控制斷面」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Critical depth and control sections\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度","在模型槽逐步調整尾水，觀察堰頂附近水深是否保持近似不變。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration","Raise tailwater progressively in a flume and observe whether crest-region depth remains approximately stable."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在模型槽逐步調整尾水，觀察堰頂附近水深是否保持近似不變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Raise tailwater progressively in a flume and observe whether crest-region depth remains approximately stable. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b277-v15-12","title":"臨界水深與控制斷面：失效診斷","titleEn":"Critical depth and control sections: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「臨界水深與控制斷面」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Critical depth and control sections” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略尾水淹沒會高估控制能力，並可能誤判上游壅水。若洪峰時水面連續跨越構造，應檢查淹沒而非只懷疑流量儀器失準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring submergence can exaggerate control capacity and misrepresent upstream backwater. A continuous flood water surface across the structure warrants checking drowning before assuming that discharge instrumentation has failed. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解題應先畫水面與床面，再判斷控制位置，最後才帶入單寬流量計算。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Draw bed and water surfaces, identify a defensible control location, and only then apply unit discharge.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略尾水淹沒會高估控制能力，並可能誤判上游壅水。若洪峰時水面連續跨越構造，應檢查淹沒而非只懷疑流量儀器失準。","textEn":"Ignoring submergence can exaggerate control capacity and misrepresent upstream backwater. A continuous flood water surface across the structure warrants checking drowning before assuming that discharge instrumentation has failed.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「臨界水深與控制斷面」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Critical depth and control sections\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["忽略尾水淹沒會高估控制能力，並可能誤判上游壅水。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring submergence can exaggerate control capacity and misrepresent upstream backwater.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough"],"answer":0,"explanation":"忽略尾水淹沒會高估控制能力，並可能誤判上游壅水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring submergence can exaggerate control capacity and misrepresent upstream backwater. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b277-v15-13","title":"水躍共軛水深：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「水躍共軛水深」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"固床下游的急流可能透過水躍轉成緩流，過程中動量關係可求前後共軛水深，但機械能會耗散。公式假設短距離、矩形斷面與近似水平底床，不能把結果當成消能池長度或護坦厚度。尾水太低時水躍可能向下游移出保護區，太高則呈不同淹沒狀態。設計檢查須同時追蹤流量與尾水組合，並留意脈動壓力對接縫與塊石的反覆作用。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水躍共軛水深」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A hydraulic jump can convert supercritical flow below grade control into subcritical flow. Momentum gives conjugate depths while mechanical energy dissipates. The standard relation assumes a short, horizontal, rectangular reach and does not determine basin length or apron thickness. Low tailwater may sweep the jump beyond protection; higher tailwater changes submergence. Examine combinations of discharge and tailwater, including fluctuating pressures acting repeatedly on joints and loose stones, rather than checking one nominal operating point. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水躍共軛水深」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-13-k1","title":"水躍共軛水深","titleEn":"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump","text":"固床下游的急流可能透過水躍轉成緩流，過程中動量關係可求前後共軛水深，但機械能會耗散。公式假設短距離、矩形斷面與近似水平底床，不能把結果當成消能池長度或護坦厚度。","textEn":"A hydraulic jump can convert supercritical flow below grade control into subcritical flow. Momentum gives conjugate depths while mechanical energy dissipates.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水躍共軛水深」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump\" is correct?","options":["共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠","固床下游的急流可能透過水躍轉成緩流，過程中動量關係可求前後共軛水深，但機械能會耗散。","護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓"],"optionsEn":["A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough","A hydraulic jump can convert supercritical flow below grade control into subcritical flow.","Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"固床下游的急流可能透過水躍轉成緩流，過程中動量關係可求前後共軛水深，但機械能會耗散。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A hydraulic jump can convert supercritical flow below grade control into subcritical flow. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b277-v15-14","title":"水躍共軛水深：定量估算","titleEn":"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水躍共軛水深」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m。適用邊界：水平矩形短水躍，未給消能池長度且忽略外加阻力。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m. Applicable boundary: Short hydraulic jump in a horizontal rectangular reach, without basin length or external resisting forces. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同時量測水躍前深度、速度與尾水，錄影追蹤滾流區前緣的位置及振盪範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure approach depth, velocity and tailwater together, and film the jump front and its oscillation range.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m。適用邊界：水平矩形短水躍，未給消能池長度且忽略外加阻力。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m. Applicable boundary: Short hydraulic jump in a horizontal rectangular reach, without basin length or external resisting forces.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水躍共軛水深」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump\", which statement holds?","options":["任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全","只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m。"],"optionsEn":["Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety","Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y1=0.4 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: y1=0.4 m; v1=5 m/s; g=9.81 m/s2; y2=0.5*y1*(sqrt(1+8*v1^2/(g*y1))-1)=1.241782 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b277-v15-15","title":"水躍共軛水深：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水躍共軛水深」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同時量測水躍前深度、速度與尾水，錄影追蹤滾流區前緣的位置及振盪範圍。以動量計算和實測後水深比較，若偏差大先查坡度、側壁與阻力影響，再決定是否需實體水工模型。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure approach depth, velocity and tailwater together, and film the jump front and its oscillation range. Compare momentum prediction with downstream depth. Large differences require checking bed slope, sidewalls and resistance before considering a physical hydraulic model. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持急流水深不變將速度降低一成重算，並比較兩種尾水高度。畫出水躍可能離開護坦的情況，列出除了水深外還應觀測的三項量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce approach velocity by ten percent at fixed depth and recalculate. Compare two tailwater levels, sketch a jump leaving the apron, and list three observations needed in addition to water depth.","failure":"注意干擾：若尾水不足使水躍跳出護坦，計算得到正確共軛水深仍無法保護裸露河床。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Correct conjugate-depth arithmetic does not protect an exposed bed when inadequate tailwater moves the jump beyond the apron. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同時量測水躍前深度、速度與尾水，錄影追蹤滾流區前緣的位置及振盪範圍。以動量計算和實測後水深比較，若偏差大先查坡度、側壁與阻力影響，再決定是否需實體水工模型。","textEn":"Measure approach depth, velocity and tailwater together, and film the jump front and its oscillation range. Compare momentum prediction with downstream depth. Large differences require checking bed slope, sidewalls and resistance before considering a physical hydraulic model.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持急流水深不變將速度降低一成重算，並比較兩種尾水高度。畫出水躍可能離開護坦的情況，列出除了水深外還應觀測的三項量。","textEn":"Reduce approach velocity by ten percent at fixed depth and recalculate. Compare two tailwater levels, sketch a jump leaving the apron, and list three observations needed in addition to water depth.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水躍共軛水深」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump\"?","options":["同時量測水躍前深度、速度與尾水，錄影追蹤滾流區前緣的位置及振盪範圍。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距"],"optionsEn":["Measure approach depth, velocity and tailwater together, and film the jump front and its oscillation range.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge"],"answer":0,"explanation":"同時量測水躍前深度、速度與尾水，錄影追蹤滾流區前緣的位置及振盪範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure approach depth, velocity and tailwater together, and film the jump front and its oscillation range. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b277-v15-16","title":"水躍共軛水深：失效診斷","titleEn":"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水躍共軛水深」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若尾水不足使水躍跳出護坦，計算得到正確共軛水深仍無法保護裸露河床。下游集中沖坑與水躍前緣移動是比平均水深更直接的警訊。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Correct conjugate-depth arithmetic does not protect an exposed bed when inadequate tailwater moves the jump beyond the apron. A concentrated scour hole and migrating jump front provide more direct warning than mean depth. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計檢查須同時追蹤流量與尾水組合，並留意脈動壓力對接縫與塊石的反覆作用。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Examine combinations of discharge and tailwater, including fluctuating pressures acting repeatedly on joints and loose stones, rather than checking one nominal operating point.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若尾水不足使水躍跳出護坦，計算得到正確共軛水深仍無法保護裸露河床。下游集中沖坑與水躍前緣移動是比平均水深更直接的警訊。","textEn":"Correct conjugate-depth arithmetic does not protect an exposed bed when inadequate tailwater moves the jump beyond the apron. A concentrated scour hole and migrating jump front provide more direct warning than mean depth.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水躍共軛水深」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Conjugate depths of a hydraulic jump\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若尾水不足使水躍跳出護坦，計算得到正確共軛水深仍無法保護裸露河床。","護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Correct conjugate-depth arithmetic does not protect an exposed bed when inadequate tailwater moves the jump beyond the apron.","Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"若尾水不足使水躍跳出護坦，計算得到正確共軛水深仍無法保護裸露河床。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Correct conjugate-depth arithmetic does not protect an exposed bed when inadequate tailwater moves the jump beyond the apron. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b277-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「護坦揚壓與排水」與「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Apron uplift and drainage\" and \"Grain motion and Shields parameter\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b277-v15-17","title":"護坦揚壓與排水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Apron uplift and drainage: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「護坦揚壓與排水」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Apron uplift and drainage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水可能從構造上游滲到護坦下方，形成向上的孔隙水壓；下游水深增加時，上表面也會受到水壓，必須用淨值比較。沿底板線性下降的壓力分布只是可檢核的簡化假設，接縫漏水、排水失效與地層不均會改變形狀。總揚力由壓力積分取得，接著還要檢查偏心力矩與局部裂縫。單純增加重量可能轉移地基問題，因此排水與截水的效果應以孔壓量測驗證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「護坦揚壓與排水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Seepage can press upward beneath an apron, while tailwater also loads its upper surface; resistance must be compared with net pressure. A linear underside pressure distribution is a checkable simplification that joints, blocked drains and heterogeneous strata may invalidate. Integrating pressure gives total uplift, after which moments and local cracking still need evaluation. Adding weight can transfer problems to the foundation, so verify drainage and cutoffs through measured pore pressures rather than assumed effectiveness. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Apron uplift and drainage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「護坦揚壓與排水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Apron uplift and drainage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-17-k1","title":"護坦揚壓與排水","titleEn":"Apron uplift and drainage","text":"水可能從構造上游滲到護坦下方，形成向上的孔隙水壓；下游水深增加時，上表面也會受到水壓，必須用淨值比較。沿底板線性下降的壓力分布只是可檢核的簡化假設，接縫漏水、排水失效與地層不均會改變形狀。","textEn":"Seepage can press upward beneath an apron, while tailwater also loads its upper surface; resistance must be compared with net pressure. A linear underside pressure distribution is a checkable simplification that joints, blocked drains and heterogeneous strata may invalidate.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「護坦揚壓與排水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Apron uplift and drainage\" is correct?","options":["護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓","同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床","水可能從構造上游滲到護坦下方，形成向上的孔隙水壓；下游水深增加時，上表面也會受到水壓，必須用淨值比較。"],"optionsEn":["Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition","One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed","Seepage can press upward beneath an apron, while tailwater also loads its upper surface; resistance must be compared with net pressure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水可能從構造上游滲到護坦下方，形成向上的孔隙水壓；下游水深增加時，上表面也會受到水壓，必須用淨值比較。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Seepage can press upward beneath an apron, while tailwater also loads its upper surface; resistance must be compared with net pressure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b277-v15-18","title":"護坦揚壓與排水：定量估算","titleEn":"Apron uplift and drainage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「護坦揚壓與排水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Apron uplift and drainage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN。適用邊界：給定的是板底淨向上壓力且沿長度線性變化，未檢查板彎曲。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN. Applicable boundary: Specified values are net upward pressures varying linearly along length; slab bending is not checked. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在底板上游、中部與下游設壓力點，與上表面水深同步比較，確認採用的是淨壓力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure pressure beneath the upstream, middle and downstream slab and compare simultaneously with water above it.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN。適用邊界：給定的是板底淨向上壓力且沿長度線性變化，未檢查板彎曲。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN. Applicable boundary: Specified values are net upward pressures varying linearly along length; slab bending is not checked.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「護坦揚壓與排水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Apron uplift and drainage\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN。","平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度","兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN.","Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location","The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: pu=30 kPa; pd=10 kPa; B=4 m; L=6 m; U=0.5*(pu+pd)*B*L=480 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b277-v15-19","title":"護坦揚壓與排水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Apron uplift and drainage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「護坦揚壓與排水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Apron uplift and drainage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在底板上游、中部與下游設壓力點，與上表面水深同步比較，確認採用的是淨壓力。檢查排水出口通暢及流量變化，若中部壓力高於線性假設，應修正積分分布並檢查接縫漏水。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure pressure beneath the upstream, middle and downstream slab and compare simultaneously with water above it. Confirm net pressure and inspect drain flow. A middle pressure exceeding the assumed line requires revising the integrated distribution and checking joints. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：假設下游淨壓力增加一倍而上游不變，重算揚力並比較作用位置。提出至少兩個能區分排水堵塞與河水位上升的量測組合。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double downstream net pressure while keeping upstream pressure fixed. Recalculate uplift and compare its location, then propose at least two measurement combinations that distinguish blocked drainage from a rise in river stage.","failure":"注意干擾：排水堵塞可能使揚壓升高而外觀毫無異常，先出現的接縫張開又會讓更多水進入。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Blocked drainage may raise uplift without visible surface damage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在底板上游、中部與下游設壓力點，與上表面水深同步比較，確認採用的是淨壓力。檢查排水出口通暢及流量變化，若中部壓力高於線性假設，應修正積分分布並檢查接縫漏水。","textEn":"Measure pressure beneath the upstream, middle and downstream slab and compare simultaneously with water above it. Confirm net pressure and inspect drain flow. A middle pressure exceeding the assumed line requires revising the integrated distribution and checking joints.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"假設下游淨壓力增加一倍而上游不變，重算揚力並比較作用位置。提出至少兩個能區分排水堵塞與河水位上升的量測組合。","textEn":"Double downstream net pressure while keeping upstream pressure fixed. Recalculate uplift and compare its location, then propose at least two measurement combinations that distinguish blocked drainage from a rise in river stage.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「護坦揚壓與排水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Apron uplift and drainage\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在底板上游、中部與下游設壓力點，與上表面水深同步比較，確認採用的是淨壓力。","不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure pressure beneath the upstream, middle and downstream slab and compare simultaneously with water above it.","Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss"],"answer":1,"explanation":"在底板上游、中部與下游設壓力點，與上表面水深同步比較，確認採用的是淨壓力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure pressure beneath the upstream, middle and downstream slab and compare simultaneously with water above it. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b277-v15-20","title":"護坦揚壓與排水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Apron uplift and drainage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「護坦揚壓與排水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Apron uplift and drainage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"排水堵塞可能使揚壓升高而外觀毫無異常，先出現的接縫張開又會讓更多水進入。應把孔壓上升與裂縫變化連續比對，防止誤當正常水位波動。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Blocked drainage may raise uplift without visible surface damage. Opening joints can then admit more water, so compare pressure increases with crack changes rather than dismissing them as ordinary stage fluctuations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單純增加重量可能轉移地基問題，因此排水與截水的效果應以孔壓量測驗證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Adding weight can transfer problems to the foundation, so verify drainage and cutoffs through measured pore pressures rather than assumed effectiveness.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"排水堵塞可能使揚壓升高而外觀毫無異常，先出現的接縫張開又會讓更多水進入。應把孔壓上升與裂縫變化連續比對，防止誤當正常水位波動。","textEn":"Blocked drainage may raise uplift without visible surface damage. Opening joints can then admit more water, so compare pressure increases with crack changes rather than dismissing them as ordinary stage fluctuations.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「護坦揚壓與排水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Apron uplift and drainage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床","排水堵塞可能使揚壓升高而外觀毫無異常，先出現的接縫張開又會讓更多水進入。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed","Blocked drainage may raise uplift without visible surface damage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"排水堵塞可能使揚壓升高而外觀毫無異常，先出現的接縫張開又會讓更多水進入。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Blocked drainage may raise uplift without visible surface damage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b277-v15-21","title":"顆粒起動與希爾茲參數：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Grain motion and Shields parameter: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Grain motion and Shields parameter” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"非黏性床料的起動可用水流剪力相對於顆粒浸水重量尺度來表示，形成無因次希爾茲參數。粒徑代表方式、顆粒排列、隱蔽效應與流況會影響臨界判斷，不能把任何單一數字稱為所有材料的法定安全界線。起動也不等同整個河段的輸砂量，少量細粒先動可能改變裝甲層。解題應先說明床料是否非黏性，再選與輸砂關係相容的臨界描述。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For noncohesive sediment, Shields stress compares fluid shear with a submerged grain-weight scale. Grain-size representation, packing, hiding and flow conditions affect the threshold, so no single number is a universal statutory limit for every bed material. Incipient movement also differs from reach sediment transport; early removal of fines may alter armouring. Identify whether the bed is noncohesive and choose a threshold description consistent with the transport relation before interpreting the dimensionless result. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Grain motion and Shields parameter” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Grain motion and Shields parameter”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-21-k1","title":"顆粒起動與希爾茲參數","titleEn":"Grain motion and Shields parameter","text":"非黏性床料的起動可用水流剪力相對於顆粒浸水重量尺度來表示，形成無因次希爾茲參數。粒徑代表方式、顆粒排列、隱蔽效應與流況會影響臨界判斷，不能把任何單一數字稱為所有材料的法定安全界線。","textEn":"For noncohesive sediment, Shields stress compares fluid shear with a submerged grain-weight scale. Grain-size representation, packing, hiding and flow conditions affect the threshold, so no single number is a universal statutory limit for every bed material.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Grain motion and Shields parameter\" is correct?","options":["非黏性床料的起動可用水流剪力相對於顆粒浸水重量尺度來表示，形成無因次希爾茲參數。","同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床","任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全"],"optionsEn":["For noncohesive sediment, Shields stress compares fluid shear with a submerged grain-weight scale.","One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed","Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety"],"answer":0,"explanation":"非黏性床料的起動可用水流剪力相對於顆粒浸水重量尺度來表示，形成無因次希爾茲參數。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For noncohesive sediment, Shields stress compares fluid shear with a submerged grain-weight scale. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b277-v15-22","title":"顆粒起動與希爾茲參數：定量估算","titleEn":"Grain motion and Shields parameter: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Grain motion and Shields parameter” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless。適用邊界：只計非黏性顆粒之無因次應力，沒有指定通用起動門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Calculates dimensionless stress for noncohesive grains without specifying a universal entrainment threshold. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：採集表層與次表層粒徑分布，量測坡度和水深後說明剪力估算方法。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample surface and subsurface grain distributions, then document the stress estimate from slope and depth.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless。適用邊界：只計非黏性顆粒之無因次應力，沒有指定通用起動門檻。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Calculates dimensionless stress for noncohesive grains without specifying a universal entrainment threshold.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Grain motion and Shields parameter\", which statement holds?","options":["只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless。","由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距"],"optionsEn":["Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: tau=40 Pa.","Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: tau=40 Pa; rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.05 m; theta=tau/((rhos-rhow)*g*d)=0.0494239 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b277-v15-23","title":"顆粒起動與希爾茲參數：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Grain motion and Shields parameter: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Grain motion and Shields parameter” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"採集表層與次表層粒徑分布，量測坡度和水深後說明剪力估算方法。用標記顆粒或短時攝影追蹤起動，並記錄先動粒徑；若床料含黏土或根系，須另評估其凝聚與補強效應。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample surface and subsurface grain distributions, then document the stress estimate from slope and depth. Track first movement with marked grains or short video sequences and record moving sizes. Clay or roots require separate cohesion or reinforcement assessment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將粒徑減半而剪力不變重算參數，說明數值變化為何仍不足以求出輸砂量。列出建立輸砂關係前需要補齊的床料與流況資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Halve grain diameter at fixed stress and recalculate. Explain why the changed parameter still does not supply transport rate, and list the sediment and flow information needed before selecting a transport relationship.","failure":"注意干擾：把混合粒徑河床用單一平均粒徑處理，可能漏掉細料淘洗與粗料失去支承。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A single mean size can conceal fine-material removal and loss of support beneath coarse grains. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"採集表層與次表層粒徑分布，量測坡度和水深後說明剪力估算方法。用標記顆粒或短時攝影追蹤起動，並記錄先動粒徑；若床料含黏土或根系，須另評估其凝聚與補強效應。","textEn":"Sample surface and subsurface grain distributions, then document the stress estimate from slope and depth. Track first movement with marked grains or short video sequences and record moving sizes. Clay or roots require separate cohesion or reinforcement assessment.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將粒徑減半而剪力不變重算參數，說明數值變化為何仍不足以求出輸砂量。列出建立輸砂關係前需要補齊的床料與流況資料。","textEn":"Halve grain diameter at fixed stress and recalculate. Explain why the changed parameter still does not supply transport rate, and list the sediment and flow information needed before selecting a transport relationship.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Grain motion and Shields parameter\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流","採集表層與次表層粒徑分布，量測坡度和水深後說明剪力估算方法。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge","Sample surface and subsurface grain distributions, then document the stress estimate from slope and depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"採集表層與次表層粒徑分布，量測坡度和水深後說明剪力估算方法。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample surface and subsurface grain distributions, then document the stress estimate from slope and depth. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b277-v15-24","title":"顆粒起動與希爾茲參數：失效診斷","titleEn":"Grain motion and Shields parameter: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Grain motion and Shields parameter” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把混合粒徑河床用單一平均粒徑處理，可能漏掉細料淘洗與粗料失去支承。若表面粗化卻下方出現空洞，應查分選與內部流失而非只看粗粒未移動。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A single mean size can conceal fine-material removal and loss of support beneath coarse grains. Surface coarsening with subsurface voids calls for checking sorting and internal loss, even if large particles remain stationary. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解題應先說明床料是否非黏性，再選與輸砂關係相容的臨界描述。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Identify whether the bed is noncohesive and choose a threshold description consistent with the transport relation before interpreting the dimensionless result.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把混合粒徑河床用單一平均粒徑處理，可能漏掉細料淘洗與粗料失去支承。若表面粗化卻下方出現空洞，應查分選與內部流失而非只看粗粒未移動。","textEn":"A single mean size can conceal fine-material removal and loss of support beneath coarse grains. Surface coarsening with subsurface voids calls for checking sorting and internal loss, even if large particles remain stationary.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「顆粒起動與希爾茲參數」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Grain motion and Shields parameter\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把混合粒徑河床用單一平均粒徑處理，可能漏掉細料淘洗與粗料失去支承。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全"],"optionsEn":["A single mean size can conceal fine-material removal and loss of support beneath coarse grains.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety"],"answer":0,"explanation":"把混合粒徑河床用單一平均粒徑處理，可能漏掉細料淘洗與粗料失去支承。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A single mean size can conceal fine-material removal and loss of support beneath coarse grains. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b277-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「濾層粒徑的相容比較」與「河床泥砂收支」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Filter grading compatibility\" and \"Bed sediment continuity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b277-v15-25","title":"濾層粒徑的相容比較：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Filter grading compatibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「濾層粒徑的相容比較」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Filter grading compatibility” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"護坦或塊石下的濾層需要讓水通過，同時限制細土被帶出，保土與透水是兩個相互牽制的功能。粒徑分位數比值可以協助比較級配，但選用哪一種準則仍取決於土質、流向、分散性與設施規範。單一比值不能驗證厚度、離析或施工破損。檢查應連結基土和濾料的完整級配曲線，再用代表水力梯度的試驗觀察濁度、流量與壓力是否穩定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「濾層粒徑的相容比較」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A filter beneath stone or concrete must pass water while retaining base soil, creating competing permeability and retention requirements. Ratios of grading percentiles help compare materials, but the applicable criteria depend on soil behaviour, flow direction, dispersivity and project requirements. One ratio does not verify thickness, segregation or construction damage. Compare complete grading curves and use tests at representative hydraulic gradients to observe whether turbidity, discharge and pressure stabilize rather than relying only on sieve labels. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Filter grading compatibility” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「濾層粒徑的相容比較」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Filter grading compatibility”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-25-k1","title":"濾層粒徑的相容比較","titleEn":"Filter grading compatibility","text":"護坦或塊石下的濾層需要讓水通過，同時限制細土被帶出，保土與透水是兩個相互牽制的功能。粒徑分位數比值可以協助比較級配，但選用哪一種準則仍取決於土質、流向、分散性與設施規範。","textEn":"A filter beneath stone or concrete must pass water while retaining base soil, creating competing permeability and retention requirements. Ratios of grading percentiles help compare materials, but the applicable criteria depend on soil behaviour, flow direction, dispersivity and project requirements.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「濾層粒徑的相容比較」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Filter grading compatibility\" is correct?","options":["任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全","護坦或塊石下的濾層需要讓水通過，同時限制細土被帶出，保土與透水是兩個相互牽制的功能。","平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度"],"optionsEn":["Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety","A filter beneath stone or concrete must pass water while retaining base soil, creating competing permeability and retention requirements.","Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location"],"answer":1,"explanation":"護坦或塊石下的濾層需要讓水通過，同時限制細土被帶出，保土與透水是兩個相互牽制的功能。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A filter beneath stone or concrete must pass water while retaining base soil, creating competing permeability and retention requirements. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b277-v15-26","title":"濾層粒徑的相容比較：定量估算","titleEn":"Filter grading compatibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「濾層粒徑的相容比較」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Filter grading compatibility” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless。適用邊界：純級配比值示例，不宣稱四就是任意基土之合格門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: A grading ratio example only; four is not asserted as an acceptance threshold for arbitrary soils. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分別取基土與已鋪濾層樣品做篩分，核對分位數皆用相同長度單位。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sieve base soil and installed filter samples, keeping percentile sizes in identical units.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless。適用邊界：純級配比值示例，不宣稱四就是任意基土之合格門檻。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: A grading ratio example only; four is not asserted as an acceptance threshold for arbitrary soils.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「濾層粒徑的相容比較」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Filter grading compatibility\", which statement holds?","options":["兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度","不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless。"],"optionsEn":["The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration","Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: D15=2 mm; d85=0.5 mm; Rg=D15/d85=4 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b277-v15-27","title":"濾層粒徑的相容比較：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Filter grading compatibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「濾層粒徑的相容比較」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Filter grading compatibility” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分別取基土與已鋪濾層樣品做篩分，核對分位數皆用相同長度單位。另量施工厚度並檢查離析，必要時在試驗柱施加逐級水頭，觀察出水含砂及壓差，將材料相容與施工品質分開驗證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sieve base soil and installed filter samples, keeping percentile sizes in identical units. Check thickness and segregation separately. Where needed, increase head in a test column and monitor discharged sediment and pressure difference to distinguish material compatibility from installation quality. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將濾料分位粒徑改成三毫米重算比值，畫出可能離析的兩個區域。說明還需要哪些透水與保土試驗，才能在指定基土下作選材判斷。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change the filter percentile size to three millimetres and recompute the ratio. Sketch two possible segregation zones and identify permeability and retention tests needed to choose material for the specified base soil.","failure":"注意干擾：合格級配在搬運時離析，可能留下過粗透孔區或過細堵塞區。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A suitable delivered grading can segregate during handling, leaving open coarse zones or clogged fine zones. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分別取基土與已鋪濾層樣品做篩分，核對分位數皆用相同長度單位。另量施工厚度並檢查離析，必要時在試驗柱施加逐級水頭，觀察出水含砂及壓差，將材料相容與施工品質分開驗證。","textEn":"Sieve base soil and installed filter samples, keeping percentile sizes in identical units. Check thickness and segregation separately. Where needed, increase head in a test column and monitor discharged sediment and pressure difference to distinguish material compatibility from installation quality.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將濾料分位粒徑改成三毫米重算比值，畫出可能離析的兩個區域。說明還需要哪些透水與保土試驗，才能在指定基土下作選材判斷。","textEn":"Change the filter percentile size to three millimetres and recompute the ratio. Sketch two possible segregation zones and identify permeability and retention tests needed to choose material for the specified base soil.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「濾層粒徑的相容比較」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Filter grading compatibility\"?","options":["分別取基土與已鋪濾層樣品做篩分，核對分位數皆用相同長度單位。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠"],"optionsEn":["Sieve base soil and installed filter samples, keeping percentile sizes in identical units.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough"],"answer":0,"explanation":"分別取基土與已鋪濾層樣品做篩分，核對分位數皆用相同長度單位。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sieve base soil and installed filter samples, keeping percentile sizes in identical units. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b277-v15-28","title":"濾層粒徑的相容比較：失效診斷","titleEn":"Filter grading compatibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「濾層粒徑的相容比較」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Filter grading compatibility” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"合格級配在搬運時離析，可能留下過粗透孔區或過細堵塞區。若只查出廠報告而不取現場樣品，會錯把材料證書當成完整濾層性能。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A suitable delivered grading can segregate during handling, leaving open coarse zones or clogged fine zones. Factory certificates without installed samples can therefore misrepresent the performance of the completed filter layer. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：檢查應連結基土和濾料的完整級配曲線，再用代表水力梯度的試驗觀察濁度、流量與壓力是否穩定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare complete grading curves and use tests at representative hydraulic gradients to observe whether turbidity, discharge and pressure stabilize rather than relying only on sieve labels.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"合格級配在搬運時離析，可能留下過粗透孔區或過細堵塞區。若只查出廠報告而不取現場樣品，會錯把材料證書當成完整濾層性能。","textEn":"A suitable delivered grading can segregate during handling, leaving open coarse zones or clogged fine zones. Factory certificates without installed samples can therefore misrepresent the performance of the completed filter layer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「濾層粒徑的相容比較」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Filter grading compatibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","合格級配在搬運時離析，可能留下過粗透孔區或過細堵塞區。","平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A suitable delivered grading can segregate during handling, leaving open coarse zones or clogged fine zones.","Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location"],"answer":1,"explanation":"合格級配在搬運時離析，可能留下過粗透孔區或過細堵塞區。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A suitable delivered grading can segregate during handling, leaving open coarse zones or clogged fine zones. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b277-v15-29","title":"河床泥砂收支：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bed sediment continuity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「河床泥砂收支」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bed sediment continuity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"固床工限制高程後仍需允許泥砂進出，否則上游淤積與下游缺砂可能同時發生。固體體積通量的差額除以有效河床面積與固體比例，可估平均床高變化；若輸入數據已含孔隙，再除一次固體比例就會重複放大。這個控制體平均值不表示每個位置均勻升降，實際可能集中於沖坑或沙洲。量測計畫應同時追蹤邊界輸砂和內部地形，才能檢查收支閉合。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「河床泥砂收支」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Grade control must accommodate sediment continuity or upstream deposition and downstream sediment deficit can coexist. Net solid-volume flux divided by bed area and solid fraction estimates mean bed-level change. If input volumes already include pores, another porosity correction double counts the effect. The control-volume average does not imply uniform change at every point; adjustment may concentrate in holes or bars. Monitor both boundary transport and internal topography to test whether the sediment budget closes. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bed sediment continuity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「河床泥砂收支」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bed sediment continuity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-29-k1","title":"河床泥砂收支","titleEn":"Bed sediment continuity","text":"固床工限制高程後仍需允許泥砂進出，否則上游淤積與下游缺砂可能同時發生。固體體積通量的差額除以有效河床面積與固體比例，可估平均床高變化；若輸入數據已含孔隙，再除一次固體比例就會重複放大。","textEn":"Grade control must accommodate sediment continuity or upstream deposition and downstream sediment deficit can coexist. Net solid-volume flux divided by bed area and solid fraction estimates mean bed-level change.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「河床泥砂收支」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bed sediment continuity\" is correct?","options":["平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度","只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力","固床工限制高程後仍需允許泥砂進出，否則上游淤積與下游缺砂可能同時發生。"],"optionsEn":["Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location","Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape","Grade control must accommodate sediment continuity or upstream deposition and downstream sediment deficit can coexist."],"answer":2,"explanation":"固床工限制高程後仍需允許泥砂進出，否則上游淤積與下游缺砂可能同時發生。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Grade control must accommodate sediment continuity or upstream deposition and downstream sediment deficit can coexist. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b277-v15-30","title":"河床泥砂收支：定量估算","titleEn":"Bed sediment continuity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「河床泥砂收支」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bed sediment continuity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m。適用邊界：固體體積通量且無側向輸砂，負值代表控制體平均侵蝕。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m. Applicable boundary: Solid-volume transport without lateral sediment exchange; negative change denotes mean control-volume erosion. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較前後地形時先統一網格與高程基準，再以沉積物密度確認通量是否為固體體積。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use common survey grids and datums, and confirm whether transport represents solid volume using sediment density.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m。適用邊界：固體體積通量且無側向輸砂，負值代表控制體平均侵蝕。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m. Applicable boundary: Solid-volume transport without lateral sediment exchange; negative change denotes mean control-volume erosion.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「河床泥砂收支」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bed sediment continuity\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m。","由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距","臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids.","Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge","Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qsi=0.001 m3/s solids; Qso=0.0015 m3/s solids; dt=86400 s; p=0.35 dimensionless; B=12 m; L=80 m; dz=(Qsi-Qso)*dt/((1-p)*B*L)=-0.0692308 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b277-v15-31","title":"河床泥砂收支：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bed sediment continuity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「河床泥砂收支」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bed sediment continuity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較前後地形時先統一網格與高程基準，再以沉積物密度確認通量是否為固體體積。分列岸崩、支流和清淤量，將地形推算的體積差與邊界通量積分核對，並保留採樣誤差範圍。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use common survey grids and datums, and confirm whether transport represents solid volume using sediment density. Account separately for bank failure, tributaries and excavation. Compare surveyed volume change with integrated boundary fluxes while retaining sampling uncertainty for both estimates. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持總固體虧損不變，假設侵蝕只集中在四分之一面積，計算該區平均下切。說明控制體平均與局部最大值的差別，並安排能辨認集中侵蝕的測線。","observationEn":"Site practice: Keep total solid deficit fixed but concentrate erosion over one quarter of the area. Calculate local mean lowering, distinguish it from the whole-reach mean and local maximum, and place transects to detect concentration.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略岸崩輸入會把實際補砂誤認成量測不準，反之漏算清淤會誇大自然侵蝕。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitted bank input or excavation can respectively conceal supply or exaggerate natural erosion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較前後地形時先統一網格與高程基準，再以沉積物密度確認通量是否為固體體積。分列岸崩、支流和清淤量，將地形推算的體積差與邊界通量積分核對，並保留採樣誤差範圍。","textEn":"Use common survey grids and datums, and confirm whether transport represents solid volume using sediment density. Account separately for bank failure, tributaries and excavation. Compare surveyed volume change with integrated boundary fluxes while retaining sampling uncertainty for both estimates.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持總固體虧損不變，假設侵蝕只集中在四分之一面積，計算該區平均下切。說明控制體平均與局部最大值的差別，並安排能辨認集中侵蝕的測線。","textEn":"Keep total solid deficit fixed but concentrate erosion over one quarter of the area. Calculate local mean lowering, distinguish it from the whole-reach mean and local maximum, and place transects to detect concentration.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「河床泥砂收支」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bed sediment continuity\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較前後地形時先統一網格與高程基準，再以沉積物密度確認通量是否為固體體積。","護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Use common survey grids and datums, and confirm whether transport represents solid volume using sediment density.","Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較前後地形時先統一網格與高程基準，再以沉積物密度確認通量是否為固體體積。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use common survey grids and datums, and confirm whether transport represents solid volume using sediment density. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b277-v15-32","title":"河床泥砂收支：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bed sediment continuity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「河床泥砂收支」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bed sediment continuity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略岸崩輸入會把實際補砂誤認成量測不準，反之漏算清淤會誇大自然侵蝕。收支不閉合時應逐項查來源，不宜直接調孔隙率湊出答案。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitted bank input or excavation can respectively conceal supply or exaggerate natural erosion. When the budget does not close, investigate missing terms rather than adjusting porosity simply to force agreement with surveys. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：量測計畫應同時追蹤邊界輸砂和內部地形，才能檢查收支閉合。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Monitor both boundary transport and internal topography to test whether the sediment budget closes.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均床高下降量必然等於每個位置的實際沖刷深度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Mean bed lowering necessarily equals the actual scour depth at every location\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略岸崩輸入會把實際補砂誤認成量測不準，反之漏算清淤會誇大自然侵蝕。收支不閉合時應逐項查來源，不宜直接調孔隙率湊出答案。","textEn":"Omitted bank input or excavation can respectively conceal supply or exaggerate natural erosion. When the budget does not close, investigate missing terms rather than adjusting porosity simply to force agreement with surveys.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「河床泥砂收支」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bed sediment continuity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力","忽略岸崩輸入會把實際補砂誤認成量測不準，反之漏算清淤會誇大自然侵蝕。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape","Omitted bank input or excavation can respectively conceal supply or exaggerate natural erosion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"忽略岸崩輸入會把實際補砂誤認成量測不準，反之漏算清淤會誇大自然侵蝕。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitted bank input or excavation can respectively conceal supply or exaggerate natural erosion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b277-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「塊石浸水重量」與「遷移陡坎的追蹤」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Submerged weight of loose rock\" and \"Tracking migrating bed steps\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b277-v15-33","title":"塊石浸水重量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Submerged weight of loose rock: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「塊石浸水重量」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Submerged weight of loose rock” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"塊石抗移動的一部分來自浸水重量，水下浮力會減少可提供的法向力，但拖曳、升力與支點位置才共同決定滑動或翻滾。球形假設便於建立體積尺度，真實塊石的角狀、扁平與互鎖不能由同一粒徑完全描述。較重也不保證穩定，因為大尺寸可能同時增加迎流面積。分析應先畫自由體圖，再決定需要摩擦、力矩或群體排列試驗，而不是只比較乾重。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「塊石浸水重量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Submerged weight contributes to rock resistance, but drag, lift and pivot geometry jointly govern sliding or rolling. A sphere provides a transparent volume scale; angularity, flatness and interlocking of real stones are not captured by one diameter. Greater mass does not automatically mean stability because larger stones also expose more frontal area. Draw the free-body diagram before selecting friction, moment or arrangement tests, and distinguish a weight calculation from a complete stability assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Submerged weight of loose rock” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「塊石浸水重量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Submerged weight of loose rock”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-33-k1","title":"塊石浸水重量","titleEn":"Submerged weight of loose rock","text":"塊石抗移動的一部分來自浸水重量，水下浮力會減少可提供的法向力，但拖曳、升力與支點位置才共同決定滑動或翻滾。球形假設便於建立體積尺度，真實塊石的角狀、扁平與互鎖不能由同一粒徑完全描述。","textEn":"Submerged weight contributes to rock resistance, but drag, lift and pivot geometry jointly govern sliding or rolling. A sphere provides a transparent volume scale; angularity, flatness and interlocking of real stones are not captured by one diameter.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「塊石浸水重量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Submerged weight of loose rock\" is correct?","options":["塊石抗移動的一部分來自浸水重量，水下浮力會減少可提供的法向力，但拖曳、升力與支點位置才共同決定滑動或翻滾。","只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力","兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度"],"optionsEn":["Submerged weight contributes to rock resistance, but drag, lift and pivot geometry jointly govern sliding or rolling.","Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape","The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration"],"answer":0,"explanation":"塊石抗移動的一部分來自浸水重量，水下浮力會減少可提供的法向力，但拖曳、升力與支點位置才共同決定滑動或翻滾。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Submerged weight contributes to rock resistance, but drag, lift and pivot geometry jointly govern sliding or rolling. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b277-v15-34","title":"塊石浸水重量：定量估算","titleEn":"Submerged weight of loose rock: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「塊石浸水重量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Submerged weight of loose rock” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N。適用邊界：完全浸沒理想球體的重量尺度，未計升力、拖曳或互鎖。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N. Applicable boundary: Submerged ideal-sphere weight scale, excluding lift, drag and interlocking. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量實際石塊三軸尺寸、乾重與排水體積，檢查等效球假設的偏差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure three axes, dry weight and displaced volume to evaluate the equivalent-sphere approximation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N。適用邊界：完全浸沒理想球體的重量尺度，未計升力、拖曳或互鎖。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N. Applicable boundary: Submerged ideal-sphere weight scale, excluding lift, drag and interlocking.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「塊石浸水重量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Submerged weight of loose rock\", which statement holds?","options":["不同床高斷面的比能可直接相減當作全部水頭損失","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N。","共軛水深算正確就同時證明消能池長度足夠"],"optionsEn":["Specific energies at different bed elevations directly give total head loss","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhos=2650 kg/m3.","A correct conjugate-depth calculation also proves that the stilling basin is long enough"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rhos=2650 kg/m3; rhow=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; d=0.6 m; Ws=(rhos-rhow)*g*pi*d^3/6=1830.650022 N. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b277-v15-35","title":"塊石浸水重量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Submerged weight of loose rock: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「塊石浸水重量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Submerged weight of loose rock” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量實際石塊三軸尺寸、乾重與排水體積，檢查等效球假設的偏差。於代表鋪排方式下觀察最先移動的石塊與支點，並記錄它是滑動或翻滾，避免只以平均重量判定整層材料表現。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure three axes, dry weight and displaced volume to evaluate the equivalent-sphere approximation. Test representative arrangements and identify the first moving stone and pivot. Record sliding versus rolling rather than judging the entire layer from average weight alone. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將等效直徑增加百分之十，計算浸水重量增加比例，再比較迎流面積的增加比例。畫出一塊石的可能支點，指出仍缺哪些荷載才能判斷翻滾。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase equivalent diameter by ten percent and compare the weight increase with frontal-area growth. Draw a possible pivot for one stone and identify the additional loads required before assessing rolling resistance.","failure":"注意干擾：扁平石片迎流後可能受升力而翻起，與同重緻密石塊的行為不同。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A flat stone may lift and overturn differently from a compact stone of equal mass. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量實際石塊三軸尺寸、乾重與排水體積，檢查等效球假設的偏差。於代表鋪排方式下觀察最先移動的石塊與支點，並記錄它是滑動或翻滾，避免只以平均重量判定整層材料表現。","textEn":"Measure three axes, dry weight and displaced volume to evaluate the equivalent-sphere approximation. Test representative arrangements and identify the first moving stone and pivot. Record sliding versus rolling rather than judging the entire layer from average weight alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將等效直徑增加百分之十，計算浸水重量增加比例，再比較迎流面積的增加比例。畫出一塊石的可能支點，指出仍缺哪些荷載才能判斷翻滾。","textEn":"Increase equivalent diameter by ten percent and compare the weight increase with frontal-area growth. Draw a possible pivot for one stone and identify the additional loads required before assessing rolling resistance.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「塊石浸水重量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Submerged weight of loose rock\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","同一個希爾茲臨界值適用所有粒徑混合與黏性河床","量實際石塊三軸尺寸、乾重與排水體積，檢查等效球假設的偏差。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","One critical Shields value applies to every grain mixture and cohesive riverbed","Measure three axes, dry weight and displaced volume to evaluate the equivalent-sphere approximation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量實際石塊三軸尺寸、乾重與排水體積，檢查等效球假設的偏差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure three axes, dry weight and displaced volume to evaluate the equivalent-sphere approximation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b277-v15-36","title":"塊石浸水重量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Submerged weight of loose rock: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「塊石浸水重量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Submerged weight of loose rock” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"扁平石片迎流後可能受升力而翻起，與同重緻密石塊的行為不同。若局部石塊先失去互鎖，後續移動會增加，應檢查鋪排而不只換更重材料。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A flat stone may lift and overturn differently from a compact stone of equal mass. Local loss of interlock can trigger further movement, calling for arrangement checks before simply specifying heavier material. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：分析應先畫自由體圖，再決定需要摩擦、力矩或群體排列試驗，而不是只比較乾重。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Draw the free-body diagram before selecting friction, moment or arrangement tests, and distinguish a weight calculation from a complete stability assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要乾燥重量相同不同形狀石塊就具有相同抗移動能力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Stones with equal dry weight have identical movement resistance regardless of shape\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"扁平石片迎流後可能受升力而翻起，與同重緻密石塊的行為不同。若局部石塊先失去互鎖，後續移動會增加，應檢查鋪排而不只換更重材料。","textEn":"A flat stone may lift and overturn differently from a compact stone of equal mass. Local loss of interlock can trigger further movement, calling for arrangement checks before simply specifying heavier material.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「塊石浸水重量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Submerged weight of loose rock\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["扁平石片迎流後可能受升力而翻起，與同重緻密石塊的行為不同。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度"],"optionsEn":["A flat stone may lift and overturn differently from a compact stone of equal mass.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration"],"answer":0,"explanation":"扁平石片迎流後可能受升力而翻起，與同重緻密石塊的行為不同。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A flat stone may lift and overturn differently from a compact stone of equal mass. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b277-v15-37","title":"遷移陡坎的追蹤：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tracking migrating bed steps: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「遷移陡坎的追蹤」如何影響河床固床工設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tracking migrating bed steps” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Riverbed grade-control structures”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"河床陡坎可能沿河道向上游遷移，把下游擾動傳到支流或基礎附近。重複測量其位置可求期間平均移動速率，但侵蝕通常集中在少數洪水，不能把多年平均當成每日固定速度。里程方向必須先定義，否則正負號容易被解讀相反。調查也需區分同一陡坎移動與新陡坎形成，並配合床質、落差和事件流量辨認過程，避免只把兩個影像點連線外推。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「遷移陡坎的追蹤」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A bed step can migrate upstream and transmit downstream disturbance toward tributaries or foundations. Repeated positions give an interval-average migration rate, but erosion often occurs during a few floods rather than at a constant daily speed. Define chainage direction before interpreting signs. Distinguish movement of the same step from creation of a new one, and combine positions with bed material, drop height and event flows instead of extrapolating a line between two images. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tracking migrating bed steps” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「遷移陡坎的追蹤」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tracking migrating bed steps”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-37-k1","title":"遷移陡坎的追蹤","titleEn":"Tracking migrating bed steps","text":"河床陡坎可能沿河道向上游遷移，把下游擾動傳到支流或基礎附近。重複測量其位置可求期間平均移動速率，但侵蝕通常集中在少數洪水，不能把多年平均當成每日固定速度。","textEn":"A bed step can migrate upstream and transmit downstream disturbance toward tributaries or foundations. Repeated positions give an interval-average migration rate, but erosion often occurs during a few floods rather than at a constant daily speed.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「遷移陡坎的追蹤」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tracking migrating bed steps\" is correct?","options":["兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度","河床陡坎可能沿河道向上游遷移，把下游擾動傳到支流或基礎附近。","由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距"],"optionsEn":["The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration","A bed step can migrate upstream and transmit downstream disturbance toward tributaries or foundations.","Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge"],"answer":1,"explanation":"河床陡坎可能沿河道向上游遷移，把下游擾動傳到支流或基礎附近。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A bed step can migrate upstream and transmit downstream disturbance toward tributaries or foundations. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b277-v15-38","title":"遷移陡坎的追蹤：定量估算","titleEn":"Tracking migrating bed steps: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「遷移陡坎的追蹤」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tracking migrating bed steps” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream。適用邊界：相同陡坎之期間平均向上游速率，不是未來事件預測。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream. Applicable boundary: Interval-average upstream rate for the same bed step, not a forecast of future events. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以固定基準重測陡坎頂與底，並用照片及床料辨認是否為同一特徵。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Resurvey crest and toe from fixed benchmarks and use photographs and bed material to identify the same feature.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream。適用邊界：相同陡坎之期間平均向上游速率，不是未來事件預測。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream. Applicable boundary: Interval-average upstream rate for the same bed step, not a forecast of future events.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「遷移陡坎的追蹤」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tracking migrating bed steps\", which statement holds?","options":["臨界水深只由單寬流量決定所以尾水永遠不影響構造出流","護坦下方有排水孔就可以在所有工況忽略揚壓","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream。"],"optionsEn":["Because critical depth depends on unit discharge, tailwater never affects structure discharge","Drain holes beneath an apron allow uplift to be ignored in every condition","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: x0=350 m downstream-chainage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: x0=350 m downstream-chainage; x1=295 m downstream-chainage; dt=5 year; vu=(x0-x1)/dt=11 m/year upstream. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b277-v15-39","title":"遷移陡坎的追蹤：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tracking migrating bed steps: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「遷移陡坎的追蹤」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tracking migrating bed steps” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以固定基準重測陡坎頂與底，並用照片及床料辨認是否為同一特徵。將每次洪水後的位置加到時間軸，保留位置誤差；如果只有兩期資料，應明確報告平均值而不畫成已知連續速度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Resurvey crest and toe from fixed benchmarks and use photographs and bed material to identify the same feature. Add post-flood positions to a timeline with uncertainty. With only two surveys, report an interval mean rather than a known continuous velocity. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：若兩次位置各有兩公尺可能誤差，估算速率的最保守範圍。提出洪水後加測的時間安排，說明新增資料如何區分事件跳躍與穩定緩慢遷移。","observationEn":"Site practice: Allow two metres of possible error at each position and estimate conservative rate bounds. Plan post-flood surveys and explain how additional observations would distinguish event-driven jumps from steady slow migration.","failure":"注意干擾：不同陡坎被誤配會造成虛假的快速遷移，定位誤差也可能大於真實移動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Matching different steps creates false rapid migration, while positional error can exceed actual movement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以固定基準重測陡坎頂與底，並用照片及床料辨認是否為同一特徵。將每次洪水後的位置加到時間軸，保留位置誤差；如果只有兩期資料，應明確報告平均值而不畫成已知連續速度。","textEn":"Resurvey crest and toe from fixed benchmarks and use photographs and bed material to identify the same feature. Add post-flood positions to a timeline with uncertainty. With only two surveys, report an interval mean rather than a known continuous velocity.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"若兩次位置各有兩公尺可能誤差，估算速率的最保守範圍。提出洪水後加測的時間安排，說明新增資料如何區分事件跳躍與穩定緩慢遷移。","textEn":"Allow two metres of possible error at each position and estimate conservative rate bounds. Plan post-flood surveys and explain how additional observations would distinguish event-driven jumps from steady slow migration.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「遷移陡坎的追蹤」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tracking migrating bed steps\"?","options":["以固定基準重測陡坎頂與底，並用照片及床料辨認是否為同一特徵。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","任一濾料與基土的粒徑比等於四就保證濾層安全"],"optionsEn":["Resurvey crest and toe from fixed benchmarks and use photographs and bed material to identify the same feature.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Any filter to base-soil grading ratio of four guarantees filter safety"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以固定基準重測陡坎頂與底，並用照片及床料辨認是否為同一特徵。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Resurvey crest and toe from fixed benchmarks and use photographs and bed material to identify the same feature. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b277-v15-40","title":"遷移陡坎的追蹤：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tracking migrating bed steps: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"prerequisiteIds":["b277-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「遷移陡坎的追蹤」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tracking migrating bed steps” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不同陡坎被誤配會造成虛假的快速遷移，定位誤差也可能大於真實移動。先核對特徵身分與基準，再討論是否需要額外防護，避免依假速率加碼工程。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Matching different steps creates false rapid migration, while positional error can exceed actual movement. Verify feature identity and survey datum before using the apparent rate to justify additional protective works upstream. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：調查也需區分同一陡坎移動與新陡坎形成，並配合床質、落差和事件流量辨認過程，避免只把兩個影像點連線外推。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Distinguish movement of the same step from creation of a new one, and combine positions with bed material, drop height and event flows instead of extrapolating a line between two images.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次測量算出的平均速率就是未來每日固定的陡坎速度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The average from two surveys is the fixed daily speed of future step migration\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b277-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不同陡坎被誤配會造成虛假的快速遷移，定位誤差也可能大於真實移動。先核對特徵身分與基準，再討論是否需要額外防護，避免依假速率加碼工程。","textEn":"Matching different steps creates false rapid migration, while positional error can exceed actual movement. Verify feature identity and survey datum before using the apparent rate to justify additional protective works upstream.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]},{"id":"b277-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「遷移陡坎的追蹤」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tracking migrating bed steps\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","不同陡坎被誤配會造成虛假的快速遷移，定位誤差也可能大於真實移動。","由坡差算出的間距就是所有流量下的最適構造物間距"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Matching different steps creates false rapid migration, while positional error can exceed actual movement.","Spacing derived from slope difference is optimal at every discharge"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同陡坎被誤配會造成虛假的快速遷移，定位誤差也可能大於真實移動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Matching different steps creates false rapid migration, while positional error can exceed actual movement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-nrcs-grade","v15s-nrcs-grade-standard","v15s-usace-shields"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b278","title":"魚道水理設計","titleEn":"Hydraulic design of fish passages","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從水池落差、孔口流量與能量密度開始，接續游泳能力、入口誘導、休息區與篩網比較。課程不提供通用魚類流速標準，而要求把魚種、體長、季節和水溫寫入設計條件，並透過偵測率及多段通過率分析，區分水理可行性與真正的遷移成果。","summaryEn":"Start with pool drops, opening discharge and energy density, then examine swimming ability, attraction, resting areas and screening. No universal fish velocity limit is supplied. Species, body size, season and temperature belong in the design conditions. Detection efficiency and passage through multiple reaches distinguish a hydraulically plausible facility from demonstrated migration outcomes.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["池間落差與射流","Pool drops and jet velocity"],["池體積與平均能量密度","Pool volume and mean energy density"],["入口誘導流量比例","Attraction flow proportion"],["篩網接近速度比較","Screen approach velocity comparison"],["多段通行的累積效果","Cumulative passage across reaches"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["池間落差與射流","池體積與平均能量密度","入口誘導流量比例","篩網接近速度比較","多段通行的累積效果"],"labelsEn":["Pool drops and jet velocity","Pool volume and mean energy density","Attraction flow proportion","Screen approach velocity comparison","Cumulative passage across reaches"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課先用「池間落差與射流」建立原創假想基準，再以「開口流量與係數」檢查另一個控制機制。第一組輸入及結果為 g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s；第二組為 Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s。學員需在同一張工作表分列量綱、時間、位置與適用範圍，先核對守恆，再解釋為何兩個得數不能互相代替。最後以第三單元提出的量測設計驗證假設，並將超出模型能力的水理、生態或治理問題列為待研究項目；這些示例並非所列案例的現場實測。敏感度重算：固定 g=9.81 m/s2 與理想無損失假設，將 dh 從 0.15 m 增至 0.18 m，速度由 1.715517 m/s 增至 1.879255 m/s，約增加百分之九點五四。落差增加兩成而速度非增加兩成，且仍未判定魚種可通過性。","textEn":"Begin with an original hypothetical baseline for Pool drops and jet velocity and examine another controlling mechanism through Opening discharge and coefficient. The first inputs and result are g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s; the second are Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s. Keep dimensions, time, location and validity conditions in separate columns of the same working sheet. Check conservation before explaining why the two numerical results cannot substitute for one another. Use the third unit measurement design to test assumptions and identify hydraulic, ecological or governance questions that exceed the model. These examples are not field observations from the named reference cases. Sensitivity recalculation: Keep g=9.81 m/s2 and the ideal loss-free assumption fixed while increasing dh from 0.15 m to 0.18 m. Velocity rises from 1.715517 m/s to 1.879255 m/s, approximately 9.54 percent. A twenty percent drop increase does not produce a twenty percent speed increase and still does not determine species passage suitability.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b278-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「池間落差與射流」與「開口流量與係數」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pool drops and jet velocity\" and \"Opening discharge and coefficient\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b278-v15-01","title":"池間落差與射流：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pool drops and jet velocity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「池間落差與射流」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pool drops and jet velocity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"魚道各池之間的水頭差會轉成局部射流動能，分散總落差可以改變每一段的通行負擔。理想能量式只提供速度尺度，真實射流會收縮、耗散並與池內回流互動，不能用它代替魚所選路徑的速度。魚種、體長、水溫與游泳時間共同決定能力，短時爆發速度也不同於可持續速度。設計應先描述目標族群與季節，再把局部水理和可供停留的空間連成一條可走通的路徑。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「池間落差與射流」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Head difference between pools creates local jet energy, so dividing total fall changes the challenge at each passage. An ideal energy equation gives a velocity scale, while real jets contract, dissipate and interact with recirculation. It does not describe every route selected by a fish. Species, length, temperature and duration affect swimming ability, and burst speed differs from sustained speed. Define the target population and season before linking hydraulic conditions with connected resting opportunities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pool drops and jet velocity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「池間落差與射流」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pool drops and jet velocity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-01-k1","title":"池間落差與射流","titleEn":"Pool drops and jet velocity","text":"魚道各池之間的水頭差會轉成局部射流動能，分散總落差可以改變每一段的通行負擔。理想能量式只提供速度尺度，真實射流會收縮、耗散並與池內回流互動，不能用它代替魚所選路徑的速度。","textEn":"Head difference between pools creates local jet energy, so dividing total fall changes the challenge at each passage. An ideal energy equation gives a velocity scale, while real jets contract, dissipate and interact with recirculation.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「池間落差與射流」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pool drops and jet velocity\" is correct?","options":["池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會","魚道各池之間的水頭差會轉成局部射流動能，分散總落差可以改變每一段的通行負擔。","流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變"],"optionsEn":["Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity","Head difference between pools creates local jet energy, so dividing total fall changes the challenge at each passage.","A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater"],"answer":1,"explanation":"魚道各池之間的水頭差會轉成局部射流動能，分散總落差可以改變每一段的通行負擔。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Head difference between pools creates local jet energy, so dividing total fall changes the challenge at each passage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b278-v15-02","title":"池間落差與射流：定量估算","titleEn":"Pool drops and jet velocity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「池間落差與射流」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pool drops and jet velocity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s。適用邊界：忽略損失的局部速度尺度，不是魚種可通過限值或池內平均流速。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s. Applicable boundary: Local ideal velocity scale without losses, not a species passage limit or pool average. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量相鄰池水位，沿開口與魚可能游經區量測速度分布及水深。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure adjoining levels simultaneously and map velocity and depth across the opening and potential routes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s。適用邊界：忽略損失的局部速度尺度，不是魚種可通過限值或池內平均流速。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s. Applicable boundary: Local ideal velocity scale without losses, not a species passage limit or pool average.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「池間落差與射流」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pool drops and jet velocity\", which statement holds?","options":["魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度","名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank","Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; v=sqrt(2*g*dh)=1.715517 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b278-v15-03","title":"池間落差與射流：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pool drops and jet velocity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「池間落差與射流」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pool drops and jet velocity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量相鄰池水位，沿開口與魚可能游經區量測速度分布及水深。將瞬時峰值與時間平均分列，並記錄目標魚體長與水溫，避免把一支流速計的平均值當成完整通行環境。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure adjoining levels simultaneously and map velocity and depth across the opening and potential routes. Separate instantaneous peaks from time averages, recording fish length and water temperature so one meter average is not mistaken for the whole passage environment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將落差增加一倍重算理想速度，與速度也加倍的假設比較。畫出一條包含休息區的通行路徑，標示仍需取得的魚種能力及局部流速資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double the drop and compare ideal velocity with a doubled-speed assumption. Draw a connected route including refuges and identify the species-performance and local velocity observations still needed to assess passage.","failure":"注意干擾：射流正面衝向下一開口可能形成連續高速走廊，讓魚無法休息。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A jet aimed directly at the next opening can create a continuous fast corridor without rest. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量相鄰池水位，沿開口與魚可能游經區量測速度分布及水深。將瞬時峰值與時間平均分列，並記錄目標魚體長與水溫，避免把一支流速計的平均值當成完整通行環境。","textEn":"Measure adjoining levels simultaneously and map velocity and depth across the opening and potential routes. Separate instantaneous peaks from time averages, recording fish length and water temperature so one meter average is not mistaken for the whole passage environment.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將落差增加一倍重算理想速度，與速度也加倍的假設比較。畫出一條包含休息區的通行路徑，標示仍需取得的魚種能力及局部流速資料。","textEn":"Double the drop and compare ideal velocity with a doubled-speed assumption. Draw a connected route including refuges and identify the species-performance and local velocity observations still needed to assess passage.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「池間落差與射流」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pool drops and jet velocity\"?","options":["同步量相鄰池水位，沿開口與魚可能游經區量測速度分布及水深。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流"],"optionsEn":["Measure adjoining levels simultaneously and map velocity and depth across the opening and potential routes.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步量相鄰池水位，沿開口與魚可能游經區量測速度分布及水深。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure adjoining levels simultaneously and map velocity and depth across the opening and potential routes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b278-v15-04","title":"池間落差與射流：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pool drops and jet velocity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「池間落差與射流」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pool drops and jet velocity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"射流正面衝向下一開口可能形成連續高速走廊，讓魚無法休息。即使每池落差相同，也需檢查射流方向及避流區是否彼此連通。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A jet aimed directly at the next opening can create a continuous fast corridor without rest. Equal pool drops therefore still require checking jet orientation and connectivity between lower-velocity refuge areas. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計應先描述目標族群與季節，再把局部水理和可供停留的空間連成一條可走通的路徑。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Define the target population and season before linking hydraulic conditions with connected resting opportunities.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"射流正面衝向下一開口可能形成連續高速走廊，讓魚無法休息。即使每池落差相同，也需檢查射流方向及避流區是否彼此連通。","textEn":"A jet aimed directly at the next opening can create a continuous fast corridor without rest. Equal pool drops therefore still require checking jet orientation and connectivity between lower-velocity refuge areas.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「池間落差與射流」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pool drops and jet velocity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","射流正面衝向下一開口可能形成連續高速走廊，讓魚無法休息。","流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A jet aimed directly at the next opening can create a continuous fast corridor without rest.","A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater"],"answer":1,"explanation":"射流正面衝向下一開口可能形成連續高速走廊，讓魚無法休息。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A jet aimed directly at the next opening can create a continuous fast corridor without rest. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b278-v15-05","title":"開口流量與係數：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Opening discharge and coefficient: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「開口流量與係數」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Opening discharge and coefficient” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"魚道開口把水位差轉為流量，流量係數濃縮了收縮與損失，但它會隨開口形狀、邊緣與淹沒狀態改變。用水深乘寬度建立面積之前，要確認開口是否完全被水淹沒，否則出流型態可能不同。相同流量可以經不同面積形成不同速度與剪切分布，因此滿足供水量並不等於滿足通行條件。控制計算應與入口誘導、下游尾水及池內水位一起閉合。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「開口流量與係數」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An opening converts level difference into discharge. Its coefficient represents contraction and losses but changes with geometry, edges and submergence. Before using width times height, verify that the opening is fully wetted; otherwise a different flow relation may apply. The same discharge through different areas produces different velocities and shear distributions, so supplying enough water does not establish passage suitability. Close the calculation with attraction flow, tailwater and pool levels instead of treating one opening independently. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Opening discharge and coefficient” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「開口流量與係數」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Opening discharge and coefficient”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-05-k1","title":"開口流量與係數","titleEn":"Opening discharge and coefficient","text":"魚道開口把水位差轉為流量，流量係數濃縮了收縮與損失，但它會隨開口形狀、邊緣與淹沒狀態改變。用水深乘寬度建立面積之前，要確認開口是否完全被水淹沒，否則出流型態可能不同。","textEn":"An opening converts level difference into discharge. Its coefficient represents contraction and losses but changes with geometry, edges and submergence.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「開口流量與係數」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Opening discharge and coefficient\" is correct?","options":["流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變","平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同","魚道開口把水位差轉為流量，流量係數濃縮了收縮與損失，但它會隨開口形狀、邊緣與淹沒狀態改變。"],"optionsEn":["A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater","Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool","An opening converts level difference into discharge."],"answer":2,"explanation":"魚道開口把水位差轉為流量，流量係數濃縮了收縮與損失，但它會隨開口形狀、邊緣與淹沒狀態改變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An opening converts level difference into discharge. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b278-v15-06","title":"開口流量與係數：定量估算","titleEn":"Opening discharge and coefficient: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「開口流量與係數」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Opening discharge and coefficient” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s。適用邊界：完全淹沒開口與給定有效係數，未把係數當通用常數。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s. Applicable boundary: Fully submerged opening with an assumed effective coefficient, not a universal coefficient. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在多組水位差下量測流量，反算有效係數並檢查是否隨尾水改變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure discharge over several head differences and infer the effective coefficient, checking tailwater dependence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s。適用邊界：完全淹沒開口與給定有效係數，未把係數當通用常數。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s. Applicable boundary: Fully submerged opening with an assumed effective coefficient, not a universal coefficient.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「開口流量與係數」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Opening discharge and coefficient\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s。","誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比","孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Cd=0.7 dimensionless.","Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance","Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Cd=0.7 dimensionless; b=0.2 m; h=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; dh=0.15 m; Q=Cd*b*h*sqrt(2*g*dh)=0.192138 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b278-v15-07","title":"開口流量與係數：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Opening discharge and coefficient: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「開口流量與係數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Opening discharge and coefficient” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在多組水位差下量測流量，反算有效係數並檢查是否隨尾水改變。量開口實際尺寸及邊緣損傷，將堵塞與未堵塞資料分開；若係數不穩定，應辨認流態轉換而非只取全部平均。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure discharge over several head differences and infer the effective coefficient, checking tailwater dependence. Survey actual dimensions and edge damage. Separate blocked and clear conditions; unstable coefficients call for identifying regime changes rather than averaging every observation together. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：使有效開口寬度縮小四分之一重算流量，再討論水位差可能隨之改變的情況。列出應同步觀測的池水位，說明為何單一開口不能獨立調整。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce effective width by one quarter and recalculate discharge, then discuss possible changes in head difference. Identify pool levels that require simultaneous observation and explain why one opening cannot always be adjusted independently.","failure":"注意干擾：枝葉堵住部分開口會改變流量與局部高速區，可能使其他池水位也偏離預期。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Debris can reduce opening area while changing local jets and levels in adjoining pools. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在多組水位差下量測流量，反算有效係數並檢查是否隨尾水改變。量開口實際尺寸及邊緣損傷，將堵塞與未堵塞資料分開；若係數不穩定，應辨認流態轉換而非只取全部平均。","textEn":"Measure discharge over several head differences and infer the effective coefficient, checking tailwater dependence. Survey actual dimensions and edge damage. Separate blocked and clear conditions; unstable coefficients call for identifying regime changes rather than averaging every observation together.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"使有效開口寬度縮小四分之一重算流量，再討論水位差可能隨之改變的情況。列出應同步觀測的池水位，說明為何單一開口不能獨立調整。","textEn":"Reduce effective width by one quarter and recalculate discharge, then discuss possible changes in head difference. Identify pool levels that require simultaneous observation and explain why one opening cannot always be adjusted independently.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「開口流量與係數」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Opening discharge and coefficient\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在多組水位差下量測流量，反算有效係數並檢查是否隨尾水改變。","上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Measure discharge over several head differences and infer the effective coefficient, checking tailwater dependence.","Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability"],"answer":1,"explanation":"在多組水位差下量測流量，反算有效係數並檢查是否隨尾水改變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure discharge over several head differences and infer the effective coefficient, checking tailwater dependence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b278-v15-08","title":"開口流量與係數：失效診斷","titleEn":"Opening discharge and coefficient: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「開口流量與係數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Opening discharge and coefficient” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"枝葉堵住部分開口會改變流量與局部高速區，可能使其他池水位也偏離預期。只按閘門開度推流量會漏掉堵塞造成的網路連鎖反應。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Debris can reduce opening area while changing local jets and levels in adjoining pools. Inferring discharge solely from gate position misses these blockage effects and their propagation through the connected passage system. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：控制計算應與入口誘導、下游尾水及池內水位一起閉合。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Close the calculation with attraction flow, tailwater and pool levels instead of treating one opening independently.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"枝葉堵住部分開口會改變流量與局部高速區，可能使其他池水位也偏離預期。只按閘門開度推流量會漏掉堵塞造成的網路連鎖反應。","textEn":"Debris can reduce opening area while changing local jets and levels in adjoining pools. Inferring discharge solely from gate position misses these blockage effects and their propagation through the connected passage system.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「開口流量與係數」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Opening discharge and coefficient\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同","枝葉堵住部分開口會改變流量與局部高速區，可能使其他池水位也偏離預期。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool","Debris can reduce opening area while changing local jets and levels in adjoining pools."],"answer":2,"explanation":"枝葉堵住部分開口會改變流量與局部高速區，可能使其他池水位也偏離預期。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Debris can reduce opening area while changing local jets and levels in adjoining pools. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b278-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「池體積與平均能量密度」與「游泳速度與地面進度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pool volume and mean energy density\" and \"Swimming speed and ground progress\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b278-v15-09","title":"池體積與平均能量密度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pool volume and mean energy density: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「池體積與平均能量密度」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pool volume and mean energy density” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"流量跨越水頭差釋出的功率除以池體積，可形成平均體積能量耗散尺度，方便比較不同配置。這個平均數不表示能量在空間均勻分布，入口射流、渦流中心與底部角落可能差異很大。有效參與混合的水體也可能小於幾何池容，死水區增加體積卻未改善通行。魚類反應還受紊流尺度與方向影響，因此平均功率密度須搭配流場和行為觀察，不應單獨作成效判決。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「池體積與平均能量密度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Discharge falling through a head difference releases power; dividing by pool volume gives a mean volumetric dissipation scale for comparing layouts. Dissipation is not spatially uniform: jets, vortex cores and corners differ. The actively mixed volume may be smaller than geometric volume, so dead zones can enlarge a pool without improving passage. Fish also respond to turbulence scale and direction. Pair the average power density with flow mapping and behaviour instead of making it the sole performance criterion. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pool volume and mean energy density” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「池體積與平均能量密度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pool volume and mean energy density”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-09-k1","title":"池體積與平均能量密度","titleEn":"Pool volume and mean energy density","text":"流量跨越水頭差釋出的功率除以池體積，可形成平均體積能量耗散尺度，方便比較不同配置。這個平均數不表示能量在空間均勻分布，入口射流、渦流中心與底部角落可能差異很大。","textEn":"Discharge falling through a head difference releases power; dividing by pool volume gives a mean volumetric dissipation scale for comparing layouts. Dissipation is not spatially uniform: jets, vortex cores and corners differ.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「池體積與平均能量密度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pool volume and mean energy density\" is correct?","options":["流量跨越水頭差釋出的功率除以池體積，可形成平均體積能量耗散尺度，方便比較不同配置。","平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同","魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度"],"optionsEn":["Discharge falling through a head difference releases power; dividing by pool volume gives a mean volumetric dissipation scale for comparing layouts.","Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool","A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank"],"answer":0,"explanation":"流量跨越水頭差釋出的功率除以池體積，可形成平均體積能量耗散尺度，方便比較不同配置。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Discharge falling through a head difference releases power; dividing by pool volume gives a mean volumetric dissipation scale for comparing layouts. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b278-v15-10","title":"池體積與平均能量密度：定量估算","titleEn":"Pool volume and mean energy density: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「池體積與平均能量密度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pool volume and mean energy density” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3。適用邊界：假設該水頭功率全在所列池容內耗散，非魚種允許值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3. Applicable boundary: Assumes the head power dissipates within the stated pool volume; not a species acceptance limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量實際池容並排除淤積占據空間，將水位及流量同步記錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure usable volume after sediment accumulation and synchronize levels with discharge.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3。適用邊界：假設該水頭功率全在所列池容內耗散，非魚種允許值。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3. Applicable boundary: Assumes the head power dissipates within the stated pool volume; not a species acceptance limit.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「池體積與平均能量密度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pool volume and mean energy density\", which statement holds?","options":["名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3。","相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流"],"optionsEn":["Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3.","Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; dh=0.15 m; V=3.5 m3; Pv=rho*g*Q*dh/V=105.107143 W/m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b278-v15-11","title":"池體積與平均能量密度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pool volume and mean energy density: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「池體積與平均能量密度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pool volume and mean energy density” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量實際池容並排除淤積占據空間，將水位及流量同步記錄。以流場測量辨認射流核心與死水區，再觀察魚是否使用預期休息區；平均值降低但局部仍猛烈時，需改配置而非只加池深。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure usable volume after sediment accumulation and synchronize levels with discharge. Map jet cores and dead zones, then observe refuge use. If average power decreases while local turbulence remains intense, revise layout rather than simply deepening the pool. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：假設淤積占去半立方公尺重算功率密度，另畫一個總體積更大但死水區更多的池。提出能區分兩種改善是否有效的流場與魚行為量測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Remove half a cubic metre of usable volume and recalculate power density. Sketch a larger pool with more inactive space and propose hydraulic and behavioural measurements that distinguish genuine improvement from a misleading volume increase.","failure":"注意干擾：池底淤積會減少有效體積，使原計算低估平均耗散；另一方面，大死水區也會掩蓋集中紊流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sediment reduces usable volume and can invalidate the original average dissipation estimate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量實際池容並排除淤積占據空間，將水位及流量同步記錄。以流場測量辨認射流核心與死水區，再觀察魚是否使用預期休息區；平均值降低但局部仍猛烈時，需改配置而非只加池深。","textEn":"Measure usable volume after sediment accumulation and synchronize levels with discharge. Map jet cores and dead zones, then observe refuge use. If average power decreases while local turbulence remains intense, revise layout rather than simply deepening the pool.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"假設淤積占去半立方公尺重算功率密度，另畫一個總體積更大但死水區更多的池。提出能區分兩種改善是否有效的流場與魚行為量測。","textEn":"Remove half a cubic metre of usable volume and recalculate power density. Sketch a larger pool with more inactive space and propose hydraulic and behavioural measurements that distinguish genuine improvement from a misleading volume increase.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「池體積與平均能量密度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pool volume and mean energy density\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成","量實際池容並排除淤積占據空間，將水位及流量同步記錄。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent","Measure usable volume after sediment accumulation and synchronize levels with discharge."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量實際池容並排除淤積占據空間，將水位及流量同步記錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure usable volume after sediment accumulation and synchronize levels with discharge. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b278-v15-12","title":"池體積與平均能量密度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pool volume and mean energy density: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「池體積與平均能量密度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pool volume and mean energy density” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"池底淤積會減少有效體積，使原計算低估平均耗散；另一方面，大死水區也會掩蓋集中紊流。檢查時需同時看淤積地形與主流混合範圍。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sediment reduces usable volume and can invalidate the original average dissipation estimate. Large inactive zones can also conceal concentrated turbulence, requiring inspection of both deposited material and the region actively mixed by the jet. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：魚類反應還受紊流尺度與方向影響，因此平均功率密度須搭配流場和行為觀察，不應單獨作成效判決。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Pair the average power density with flow mapping and behaviour instead of making it the sole performance criterion.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"池底淤積會減少有效體積，使原計算低估平均耗散；另一方面，大死水區也會掩蓋集中紊流。檢查時需同時看淤積地形與主流混合範圍。","textEn":"Sediment reduces usable volume and can invalidate the original average dissipation estimate. Large inactive zones can also conceal concentrated turbulence, requiring inspection of both deposited material and the region actively mixed by the jet.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「池體積與平均能量密度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pool volume and mean energy density\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["池底淤積會減少有效體積，使原計算低估平均耗散；另一方面，大死水區也會掩蓋集中紊流。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度"],"optionsEn":["Sediment reduces usable volume and can invalidate the original average dissipation estimate.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank"],"answer":0,"explanation":"池底淤積會減少有效體積，使原計算低估平均耗散；另一方面，大死水區也會掩蓋集中紊流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sediment reduces usable volume and can invalidate the original average dissipation estimate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b278-v15-13","title":"游泳速度與地面進度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Swimming speed and ground progress: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「游泳速度與地面進度」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Swimming speed and ground progress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"魚相對水的游泳速度與水流相對地面的速度是不同參考系，逆流時兩者相減才是向上游的地面進度。若水流接近可維持游速，通過時間會急遽增加；水流更快時，簡化模型便無正向進度。魚可能利用邊界層或間歇爆發，真實軌跡不能由單一平均速度完整描述。計算應把可維持時間與距離一起列出，並明示水溫及體長條件，避免以最高速度替代耐力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「游泳速度與地面進度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Swimming speed relative to water differs from progress relative to the bank. Against a uniform current, subtract flow speed to obtain upstream ground speed. As current approaches sustainable swimming speed, travel time rises sharply; a faster current gives no positive progress in this simplified model. Fish may use boundary layers or bursts, so an average cannot represent every trajectory. State duration, distance, temperature and body size rather than substituting maximum speed for endurance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Swimming speed and ground progress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「游泳速度與地面進度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Swimming speed and ground progress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-13-k1","title":"游泳速度與地面進度","titleEn":"Swimming speed and ground progress","text":"魚相對水的游泳速度與水流相對地面的速度是不同參考系，逆流時兩者相減才是向上游的地面進度。若水流接近可維持游速，通過時間會急遽增加；水流更快時，簡化模型便無正向進度。","textEn":"Swimming speed relative to water differs from progress relative to the bank. Against a uniform current, subtract flow speed to obtain upstream ground speed.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「游泳速度與地面進度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Swimming speed and ground progress\" is correct?","options":["魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度","魚相對水的游泳速度與水流相對地面的速度是不同參考系，逆流時兩者相減才是向上游的地面進度。","誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比"],"optionsEn":["A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank","Swimming speed relative to water differs from progress relative to the bank.","Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"魚相對水的游泳速度與水流相對地面的速度是不同參考系，逆流時兩者相減才是向上游的地面進度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Swimming speed relative to water differs from progress relative to the bank. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b278-v15-14","title":"游泳速度與地面進度：定量估算","titleEn":"Swimming speed and ground progress: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「游泳速度與地面進度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Swimming speed and ground progress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s。適用邊界：一維定常逆流與固定可維持游速，未包括轉向與疲勞。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s. Applicable boundary: One-dimensional steady counterflow with fixed sustainable swimming speed, excluding turns and fatigue. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先確認游泳能力資料的魚種、體長、水溫及試驗持續時間，再於候選路徑量流速。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check species, size, temperature and test duration behind the swimming input, then measure current along candidate routes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s。適用邊界：一維定常逆流與固定可維持游速，未包括轉向與疲勞。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s. Applicable boundary: One-dimensional steady counterflow with fixed sustainable swimming speed, excluding turns and fatigue.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「游泳速度與地面進度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Swimming speed and ground progress\", which statement holds?","options":["孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同","上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s。"],"optionsEn":["Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical","Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Us=1.2 m/s upstream-relative-water; U=0.8 m/s downstream; L=6 m; t=L/(Us-U)=15 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b278-v15-15","title":"游泳速度與地面進度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Swimming speed and ground progress: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「游泳速度與地面進度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Swimming speed and ground progress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先確認游泳能力資料的魚種、體長、水溫及試驗持續時間，再於候選路徑量流速。以追蹤影像取得地面位移與停留時間，若魚利用邊界低速帶，應沿實際路徑比較而非套斷面平均。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check species, size, temperature and test duration behind the swimming input, then measure current along candidate routes. Use tracking to obtain ground displacement and pauses. Fish using low-velocity boundaries should be assessed along their actual trajectories. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將水流提高到每秒一公尺重算時間，再試每秒一點二公尺並解釋分母為零的物理意義。列出可用來驗證固定游速假設的追蹤資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Raise current to one metre per second and recalculate travel time, then examine current equal to swimming speed. Explain the zero denominator physically and identify tracking data that test the fixed-speed assumption.","failure":"注意干擾：以短時爆發游速估整段長距離通過，會低估疲勞與退回的機會。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using burst speed for a long reach underestimates fatigue and retreat. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先確認游泳能力資料的魚種、體長、水溫及試驗持續時間，再於候選路徑量流速。以追蹤影像取得地面位移與停留時間，若魚利用邊界低速帶，應沿實際路徑比較而非套斷面平均。","textEn":"Check species, size, temperature and test duration behind the swimming input, then measure current along candidate routes. Use tracking to obtain ground displacement and pauses. Fish using low-velocity boundaries should be assessed along their actual trajectories.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將水流提高到每秒一公尺重算時間，再試每秒一點二公尺並解釋分母為零的物理意義。列出可用來驗證固定游速假設的追蹤資料。","textEn":"Raise current to one metre per second and recalculate travel time, then examine current equal to swimming speed. Explain the zero denominator physically and identify tracking data that test the fixed-speed assumption.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「游泳速度與地面進度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Swimming speed and ground progress\"?","options":["先確認游泳能力資料的魚種、體長、水溫及試驗持續時間，再於候選路徑量流速。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會"],"optionsEn":["Check species, size, temperature and test duration behind the swimming input, then measure current along candidate routes.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"先確認游泳能力資料的魚種、體長、水溫及試驗持續時間，再於候選路徑量流速。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check species, size, temperature and test duration behind the swimming input, then measure current along candidate routes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b278-v15-16","title":"游泳速度與地面進度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Swimming speed and ground progress: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「游泳速度與地面進度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Swimming speed and ground progress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以短時爆發游速估整段長距離通過，會低估疲勞與退回的機會。觀察到魚反覆嘗試後下退時，需檢查持續時間而不只檢查最大流速。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using burst speed for a long reach underestimates fatigue and retreat. Repeated attempts followed by downstream movement call for examining endurance and resting opportunities, not merely the maximum local current. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：計算應把可維持時間與距離一起列出，並明示水溫及體長條件，避免以最高速度替代耐力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: State duration, distance, temperature and body size rather than substituting maximum speed for endurance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以短時爆發游速估整段長距離通過，會低估疲勞與退回的機會。觀察到魚反覆嘗試後下退時，需檢查持續時間而不只檢查最大流速。","textEn":"Using burst speed for a long reach underestimates fatigue and retreat. Repeated attempts followed by downstream movement call for examining endurance and resting opportunities, not merely the maximum local current.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「游泳速度與地面進度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Swimming speed and ground progress\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","以短時爆發游速估整段長距離通過，會低估疲勞與退回的機會。","誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using burst speed for a long reach underestimates fatigue and retreat.","Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以短時爆發游速估整段長距離通過，會低估疲勞與退回的機會。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using burst speed for a long reach underestimates fatigue and retreat. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b278-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「入口誘導流量比例」與「水池換水與魚類停留」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Attraction flow proportion\" and \"Water turnover and fish residence\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b278-v15-17","title":"入口誘導流量比例：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Attraction flow proportion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「入口誘導流量比例」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Attraction flow proportion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"魚道入口需讓目標魚在多股水流中辨認可接近的路徑，誘導流量只是其中一個因素。入口位置、尾水深度、射流方向與附近洩流都會改變魚是否找到入口。流量占河川總流量的比例能描述供水分配，卻不直接量化入口可見度或魚的選擇。相同占比在不同洪水與機組運轉條件下可能產生不同流場，因此應把入口尋找與進入後通過分成兩個評估階段。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「入口誘導流量比例」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Attraction flow helps fish locate an accessible entrance among competing currents, but location, tailwater depth, jet direction and nearby releases also matter. Its fraction of river discharge describes water allocation, not entrance detectability or fish choice. Identical fractions can create different flow patterns during floods or generating-unit changes. Evaluate finding the entrance separately from passing through the facility, and examine the operating conditions that alter approach routes rather than assuming a fixed ratio guarantees attraction. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Attraction flow proportion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「入口誘導流量比例」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Attraction flow proportion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-17-k1","title":"入口誘導流量比例","titleEn":"Attraction flow proportion","text":"魚道入口需讓目標魚在多股水流中辨認可接近的路徑，誘導流量只是其中一個因素。入口位置、尾水深度、射流方向與附近洩流都會改變魚是否找到入口。","textEn":"Attraction flow helps fish locate an accessible entrance among competing currents, but location, tailwater depth, jet direction and nearby releases also matter. Its fraction of river discharge describes water allocation, not entrance detectability or fish choice.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「入口誘導流量比例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Attraction flow proportion\" is correct?","options":["誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比","名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間","魚道入口需讓目標魚在多股水流中辨認可接近的路徑，誘導流量只是其中一個因素。"],"optionsEn":["Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance","Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool","Attraction flow helps fish locate an accessible entrance among competing currents, but location, tailwater depth, jet direction and nearby releases also matter."],"answer":2,"explanation":"魚道入口需讓目標魚在多股水流中辨認可接近的路徑，誘導流量只是其中一個因素。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Attraction flow helps fish locate an accessible entrance among competing currents, but location, tailwater depth, jet direction and nearby releases also matter. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b278-v15-18","title":"入口誘導流量比例：定量估算","titleEn":"Attraction flow proportion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「入口誘導流量比例」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Attraction flow proportion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless。適用邊界：僅為指定時刻水量比例，不是普遍建議值或吸引成功率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: A discharge fraction at one specified time, not a universal recommendation or attraction success rate. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：於入口外布設流速測線，記錄河川流量及附近出口操作，同時追蹤魚到達、搜尋與進入時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map approach velocities and record river flow and nearby outlet operation while tracking arrival, search and entry times.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless。適用邊界：僅為指定時刻水量比例，不是普遍建議值或吸引成功率。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: A discharge fraction at one specified time, not a universal recommendation or attraction success rate.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「入口誘導流量比例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Attraction flow proportion\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless。","相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流","每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless.","Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction","If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qa=0.6 m3/s; Qr=40 m3/s; fa=Qa/Qr=0.015 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b278-v15-19","title":"入口誘導流量比例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Attraction flow proportion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「入口誘導流量比例」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Attraction flow proportion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"於入口外布設流速測線，記錄河川流量及附近出口操作，同時追蹤魚到達、搜尋與進入時間。將未找到入口與進入後退出分開統計，並比較不同尾水條件，避免把兩種失敗混成一個通過率。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map approach velocities and record river flow and nearby outlet operation while tracking arrival, search and entry times. Separate failure to find the entrance from retreat after entry, comparing tailwater conditions rather than combining both into one passage statistic. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將河川流量加倍但誘導流量不變，重算比例並說明它不能直接預測成效減半。設計一個同時量水流及搜尋時間的比較試驗，控制魚種與季節。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double river discharge at unchanged attraction flow and recalculate the fraction without assuming success halves. Design a comparison measuring both currents and search time while controlling species and season across observations.","failure":"注意干擾：誘導射流可能被主流偏轉，讓魚聚集在無法進入的位置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: The main current can deflect an attraction jet toward an inaccessible location. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"於入口外布設流速測線，記錄河川流量及附近出口操作，同時追蹤魚到達、搜尋與進入時間。將未找到入口與進入後退出分開統計，並比較不同尾水條件，避免把兩種失敗混成一個通過率。","textEn":"Map approach velocities and record river flow and nearby outlet operation while tracking arrival, search and entry times. Separate failure to find the entrance from retreat after entry, comparing tailwater conditions rather than combining both into one passage statistic.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將河川流量加倍但誘導流量不變，重算比例並說明它不能直接預測成效減半。設計一個同時量水流及搜尋時間的比較試驗，控制魚種與季節。","textEn":"Double river discharge at unchanged attraction flow and recalculate the fraction without assuming success halves. Design a comparison measuring both currents and search time while controlling species and season across observations.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「入口誘導流量比例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Attraction flow proportion\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","於入口外布設流速測線，記錄河川流量及附近出口操作，同時追蹤魚到達、搜尋與進入時間。","流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Map approach velocities and record river flow and nearby outlet operation while tracking arrival, search and entry times.","A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater"],"answer":1,"explanation":"於入口外布設流速測線，記錄河川流量及附近出口操作，同時追蹤魚到達、搜尋與進入時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map approach velocities and record river flow and nearby outlet operation while tracking arrival, search and entry times. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b278-v15-20","title":"入口誘導流量比例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Attraction flow proportion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「入口誘導流量比例」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Attraction flow proportion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"誘導射流可能被主流偏轉，讓魚聚集在無法進入的位置。此時增加同方向流量未必改善，需查入口位置與可達水深，而不是只提高占比。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"The main current can deflect an attraction jet toward an inaccessible location. Increasing discharge in the same direction may not help; investigate entrance placement and accessible depth instead of only increasing the fraction. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：相同占比在不同洪水與機組運轉條件下可能產生不同流場，因此應把入口尋找與進入後通過分成兩個評估階段。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Evaluate finding the entrance separately from passing through the facility, and examine the operating conditions that alter approach routes rather than assuming a fixed ratio guarantees attraction.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"誘導射流可能被主流偏轉，讓魚聚集在無法進入的位置。此時增加同方向流量未必改善，需查入口位置與可達水深，而不是只提高占比。","textEn":"The main current can deflect an attraction jet toward an inaccessible location. Increasing discharge in the same direction may not help; investigate entrance placement and accessible depth instead of only increasing the fraction.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「入口誘導流量比例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Attraction flow proportion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間","誘導射流可能被主流偏轉，讓魚聚集在無法進入的位置。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool","The main current can deflect an attraction jet toward an inaccessible location."],"answer":2,"explanation":"誘導射流可能被主流偏轉，讓魚聚集在無法進入的位置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"The main current can deflect an attraction jet toward an inaccessible location. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b278-v15-21","title":"水池換水與魚類停留：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Water turnover and fish residence: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「水池換水與魚類停留」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Water turnover and fish residence” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"池容除以流量得到名義換水時間，可作水體更新的尺度，但真實水粒子停留時間會因短路與回流形成分布。魚不是被動示蹤物，可能主動停留、避流或反覆進出，所以水的平均換水時間不能代替魚類恢復體力的時間。溶氧與水溫也受外界交換影響，不能只靠較大體積假定適合休息。課程應把幾何池容、有效混合體積與觀測到的行為時間分開記錄。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水池換水與魚類停留」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pool volume divided by discharge gives nominal water turnover time, while short-circuiting and recirculation produce a distribution of particle residence times. Fish are active organisms that can rest, avoid currents or repeatedly enter and leave; hydraulic turnover therefore does not equal recovery time. Oxygen and temperature depend on additional exchanges, so larger volume alone does not establish refuge quality. Keep geometric volume, actively mixed volume and observed behavioural residence as distinct quantities in the assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Water turnover and fish residence” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水池換水與魚類停留」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Water turnover and fish residence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-21-k1","title":"水池換水與魚類停留","titleEn":"Water turnover and fish residence","text":"池容除以流量得到名義換水時間，可作水體更新的尺度，但真實水粒子停留時間會因短路與回流形成分布。魚不是被動示蹤物，可能主動停留、避流或反覆進出，所以水的平均換水時間不能代替魚類恢復體力的時間。","textEn":"Pool volume divided by discharge gives nominal water turnover time, while short-circuiting and recirculation produce a distribution of particle residence times. Fish are active organisms that can rest, avoid currents or repeatedly enter and leave; hydraulic turnover therefore does not equal recovery time.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水池換水與魚類停留」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Water turnover and fish residence\" is correct?","options":["池容除以流量得到名義換水時間，可作水體更新的尺度，但真實水粒子停留時間會因短路與回流形成分布。","名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間","孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同"],"optionsEn":["Pool volume divided by discharge gives nominal water turnover time, while short-circuiting and recirculation produce a distribution of particle residence times.","Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool","Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical"],"answer":0,"explanation":"池容除以流量得到名義換水時間，可作水體更新的尺度，但真實水粒子停留時間會因短路與回流形成分布。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pool volume divided by discharge gives nominal water turnover time, while short-circuiting and recirculation produce a distribution of particle residence times. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b278-v15-22","title":"水池換水與魚類停留：定量估算","titleEn":"Water turnover and fish residence: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水池換水與魚類停留」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Water turnover and fish residence” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s。適用邊界：名義水體換水尺度，未假設每隻魚或每個水粒子停留二十秒。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s. Applicable boundary: Nominal water turnover scale, without assuming every fish or water particle remains twenty seconds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用適合現場且獲准的示蹤方式量入口與出口濃度曲線，檢查早到峰與長尾。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use an appropriate authorized tracer method to measure inlet and outlet concentration histories, looking for early peaks and long tails.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s。適用邊界：名義水體換水尺度，未假設每隻魚或每個水粒子停留二十秒。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s. Applicable boundary: Nominal water turnover scale, without assuming every fish or water particle remains twenty seconds.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水池換水與魚類停留」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Water turnover and fish residence\", which statement holds?","options":["上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s。","池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會"],"optionsEn":["Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s.","Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: V=8 m3; Q=0.4 m3/s; tn=V/Q=20 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b278-v15-23","title":"水池換水與魚類停留：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Water turnover and fish residence: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水池換水與魚類停留」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Water turnover and fish residence” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用適合現場且獲准的示蹤方式量入口與出口濃度曲線，檢查早到峰與長尾。同步追蹤魚停留分布並量水溫、溶氧，將水力短路與魚主動休息區分，不能只用一個平均時間判斷池體功能。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use an appropriate authorized tracer method to measure inlet and outlet concentration histories, looking for early peaks and long tails. Track fish residence alongside temperature and oxygen, distinguishing hydraulic short-circuiting from active resting rather than relying on one mean. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持流量不變將池容增加四分之一重算名義時間，畫兩條平均相近但形狀不同的示蹤曲線。說明哪種附加量測可辨認真正可用的休息空間。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase volume by one quarter at fixed flow and recalculate nominal time. Sketch two tracer curves with similar means but different shapes, then identify additional observations that reveal usable resting space for fish.","failure":"注意干擾：主流直接穿池可能使大部分水快速離開，而角落長時間不更新。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Flow can short-circuit across a pool while corner water renews slowly. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用適合現場且獲准的示蹤方式量入口與出口濃度曲線，檢查早到峰與長尾。同步追蹤魚停留分布並量水溫、溶氧，將水力短路與魚主動休息區分，不能只用一個平均時間判斷池體功能。","textEn":"Use an appropriate authorized tracer method to measure inlet and outlet concentration histories, looking for early peaks and long tails. Track fish residence alongside temperature and oxygen, distinguishing hydraulic short-circuiting from active resting rather than relying on one mean.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持流量不變將池容增加四分之一重算名義時間，畫兩條平均相近但形狀不同的示蹤曲線。說明哪種附加量測可辨認真正可用的休息空間。","textEn":"Increase volume by one quarter at fixed flow and recalculate nominal time. Sketch two tracer curves with similar means but different shapes, then identify additional observations that reveal usable resting space for fish.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水池換水與魚類停留」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Water turnover and fish residence\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同","用適合現場且獲准的示蹤方式量入口與出口濃度曲線，檢查早到峰與長尾。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool","Use an appropriate authorized tracer method to measure inlet and outlet concentration histories, looking for early peaks and long tails."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用適合現場且獲准的示蹤方式量入口與出口濃度曲線，檢查早到峰與長尾。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use an appropriate authorized tracer method to measure inlet and outlet concentration histories, looking for early peaks and long tails. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b278-v15-24","title":"水池換水與魚類停留：失效診斷","titleEn":"Water turnover and fish residence: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水池換水與魚類停留」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Water turnover and fish residence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"主流直接穿池可能使大部分水快速離開，而角落長時間不更新。若只看池容除流量，會同時漏掉高速通道與低氧死水區的問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Flow can short-circuit across a pool while corner water renews slowly. Volume divided by discharge alone then conceals both a fast corridor and stagnant areas that may develop unsuitable oxygen conditions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：課程應把幾何池容、有效混合體積與觀測到的行為時間分開記錄。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Keep geometric volume, actively mixed volume and observed behavioural residence as distinct quantities in the assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"主流直接穿池可能使大部分水快速離開，而角落長時間不更新。若只看池容除流量，會同時漏掉高速通道與低氧死水區的問題。","textEn":"Flow can short-circuit across a pool while corner water renews slowly. Volume divided by discharge alone then conceals both a fast corridor and stagnant areas that may develop unsuitable oxygen conditions.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水池換水與魚類停留」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Water turnover and fish residence\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["主流直接穿池可能使大部分水快速離開，而角落長時間不更新。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同"],"optionsEn":["Flow can short-circuit across a pool while corner water renews slowly.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical"],"answer":0,"explanation":"主流直接穿池可能使大部分水快速離開，而角落長時間不更新。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Flow can short-circuit across a pool while corner water renews slowly. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b278-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「篩網接近速度比較」與「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Screen approach velocity comparison\" and \"Eddy scales and fish size\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b278-v15-25","title":"篩網接近速度比較：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Screen approach velocity comparison: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「篩網接近速度比較」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Screen approach velocity comparison” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"取水篩網與上溯魚道目的不同，前者常需避免魚被吸附或帶入取水口，不能把魚道開口流速直接當成篩網標準。接近速度應相對篩網法向定義，而掃流沿網面方向，兩者對魚的作用不同。以總流量除有效開孔面積得到孔隙平均速度，與按整體網面積計算的表觀速度也不同。教材必須明確標示所用面積和速度定義，才能與指定魚種及生命期的評估方法比較。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「篩網接近速度比較」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Intake screens and upstream fish passages serve different purposes; a passage-opening velocity cannot simply become a screen criterion. Approach velocity is normal to the screen, while sweeping velocity runs along it. Dividing discharge by effective open area gives a mean opening velocity, distinct from superficial velocity based on gross screen area. State both area and velocity definitions explicitly before comparing with an evaluation method for a particular species and life stage or interpreting blockage effects. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Screen approach velocity comparison” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「篩網接近速度比較」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Screen approach velocity comparison”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-25-k1","title":"篩網接近速度比較","titleEn":"Screen approach velocity comparison","text":"取水篩網與上溯魚道目的不同，前者常需避免魚被吸附或帶入取水口，不能把魚道開口流速直接當成篩網標準。接近速度應相對篩網法向定義，而掃流沿網面方向，兩者對魚的作用不同。","textEn":"Intake screens and upstream fish passages serve different purposes; a passage-opening velocity cannot simply become a screen criterion. Approach velocity is normal to the screen, while sweeping velocity runs along it.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「篩網接近速度比較」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Screen approach velocity comparison\" is correct?","options":["孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同","取水篩網與上溯魚道目的不同，前者常需避免魚被吸附或帶入取水口，不能把魚道開口流速直接當成篩網標準。","相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流"],"optionsEn":["Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical","Intake screens and upstream fish passages serve different purposes; a passage-opening velocity cannot simply become a screen criterion.","Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"取水篩網與上溯魚道目的不同，前者常需避免魚被吸附或帶入取水口，不能把魚道開口流速直接當成篩網標準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Intake screens and upstream fish passages serve different purposes; a passage-opening velocity cannot simply become a screen criterion. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b278-v15-26","title":"篩網接近速度比較：定量估算","titleEn":"Screen approach velocity comparison: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「篩網接近速度比較」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Screen approach velocity comparison” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s。適用邊界：均勻法向通流的孔隙平均速度，不與總網面表觀接近速度混稱。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s. Applicable boundary: Mean opening velocity for uniform normal flow, distinct from gross-area superficial approach velocity. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先記錄網面總面積、開孔比例及堵塞分布，再依評估方法在網前規定位置量法向與切向速度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record gross area, open fraction and blockage pattern, then measure normal and tangential velocities at locations specified by the evaluation method.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s。適用邊界：均勻法向通流的孔隙平均速度，不與總網面表觀接近速度混稱。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s. Applicable boundary: Mean opening velocity for uniform normal flow, distinct from gross-area superficial approach velocity.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「篩網接近速度比較」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Screen approach velocity comparison\", which statement holds?","options":["每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成","流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent","A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Q=0.9 m3/s; Ag=3 m2; phi=0.6 dimensionless; vp=Q/(Ag*phi)=0.5 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b278-v15-27","title":"篩網接近速度比較：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Screen approach velocity comparison: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「篩網接近速度比較」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Screen approach velocity comparison” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先記錄網面總面積、開孔比例及堵塞分布，再依評估方法在網前規定位置量法向與切向速度。比較孔隙平均與表觀速度時標出定義，避免把兩種不同面積基準的數字當成儀器不一致。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record gross area, open fraction and blockage pattern, then measure normal and tangential velocities at locations specified by the evaluation method. Label opening and superficial velocities explicitly so different area bases are not mistaken for inconsistent instruments. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將開孔比例降低到零點四重算孔隙速度，另算總網面表觀速度並比較。畫出局部堵塞可能形成的高流速區，說明應如何加密量測而非只取平均。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce open fraction to zero point four and recalculate opening velocity, then compare with gross-area superficial velocity. Sketch a blockage-induced fast region and propose denser measurements instead of relying only on the average.","failure":"注意干擾：局部堵塞會把流量集中到剩餘開孔，平均全網速度可能仍低卻出現高吸附區。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Local blockage concentrates flow through remaining openings even when the gross-area average appears modest. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先記錄網面總面積、開孔比例及堵塞分布，再依評估方法在網前規定位置量法向與切向速度。比較孔隙平均與表觀速度時標出定義，避免把兩種不同面積基準的數字當成儀器不一致。","textEn":"Record gross area, open fraction and blockage pattern, then measure normal and tangential velocities at locations specified by the evaluation method. Label opening and superficial velocities explicitly so different area bases are not mistaken for inconsistent instruments.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將開孔比例降低到零點四重算孔隙速度，另算總網面表觀速度並比較。畫出局部堵塞可能形成的高流速區，說明應如何加密量測而非只取平均。","textEn":"Reduce open fraction to zero point four and recalculate opening velocity, then compare with gross-area superficial velocity. Sketch a blockage-induced fast region and propose denser measurements instead of relying only on the average.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「篩網接近速度比較」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Screen approach velocity comparison\"?","options":["先記錄網面總面積、開孔比例及堵塞分布，再依評估方法在網前規定位置量法向與切向速度。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度"],"optionsEn":["Record gross area, open fraction and blockage pattern, then measure normal and tangential velocities at locations specified by the evaluation method.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank"],"answer":0,"explanation":"先記錄網面總面積、開孔比例及堵塞分布，再依評估方法在網前規定位置量法向與切向速度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record gross area, open fraction and blockage pattern, then measure normal and tangential velocities at locations specified by the evaluation method. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b278-v15-28","title":"篩網接近速度比較：失效診斷","titleEn":"Screen approach velocity comparison: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「篩網接近速度比較」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Screen approach velocity comparison” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"局部堵塞會把流量集中到剩餘開孔，平均全網速度可能仍低卻出現高吸附區。診斷應看空間分布及清污狀態，不能只查總取水量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Local blockage concentrates flow through remaining openings even when the gross-area average appears modest. Investigate spatial velocity patterns and cleaning condition rather than relying solely on total intake discharge or nominal screen area. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：教材必須明確標示所用面積和速度定義，才能與指定魚種及生命期的評估方法比較。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: State both area and velocity definitions explicitly before comparing with an evaluation method for a particular species and life stage or interpreting blockage effects.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"局部堵塞會把流量集中到剩餘開孔，平均全網速度可能仍低卻出現高吸附區。診斷應看空間分布及清污狀態，不能只查總取水量。","textEn":"Local blockage concentrates flow through remaining openings even when the gross-area average appears modest. Investigate spatial velocity patterns and cleaning condition rather than relying solely on total intake discharge or nominal screen area.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「篩網接近速度比較」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Screen approach velocity comparison\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","局部堵塞會把流量集中到剩餘開孔，平均全網速度可能仍低卻出現高吸附區。","相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Local blockage concentrates flow through remaining openings even when the gross-area average appears modest.","Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部堵塞會把流量集中到剩餘開孔，平均全網速度可能仍低卻出現高吸附區。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Local blockage concentrates flow through remaining openings even when the gross-area average appears modest. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b278-v15-29","title":"渦流尺度與魚體尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Eddy scales and fish size: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Eddy scales and fish size” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"紊流不只由速度大小決定，渦流的空間尺度、持續時間及方向都可能影響魚維持姿態的能力。以特徵長度除以速度擾動可建立周轉時間尺度，但這不是魚的疲勞時間，也不是特定物種的允許週期。渦流尺寸相對魚體長度可能改變作用方式，因此測量應保留空間與時間解析度。過度平均會消除瞬時結構，反之短紀錄又可能把偶發渦流當成代表狀態，需要兼顧兩者。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Turbulence affects posture through spatial scale, duration and direction as well as velocity magnitude. Dividing a characteristic length by velocity fluctuation gives an eddy turnover scale, not fish fatigue time or a species acceptance period. Eddy size relative to body length can change the interaction, so measurements need suitable spatial and temporal resolution. Excessive averaging removes transient structures, whereas very short records may mistake a rare event for typical conditions; both sampling limits require attention. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Eddy scales and fish size” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Eddy scales and fish size”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-29-k1","title":"渦流尺度與魚體尺度","titleEn":"Eddy scales and fish size","text":"紊流不只由速度大小決定，渦流的空間尺度、持續時間及方向都可能影響魚維持姿態的能力。以特徵長度除以速度擾動可建立周轉時間尺度，但這不是魚的疲勞時間，也不是特定物種的允許週期。","textEn":"Turbulence affects posture through spatial scale, duration and direction as well as velocity magnitude. Dividing a characteristic length by velocity fluctuation gives an eddy turnover scale, not fish fatigue time or a species acceptance period.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Eddy scales and fish size\" is correct?","options":["相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流","上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率","紊流不只由速度大小決定，渦流的空間尺度、持續時間及方向都可能影響魚維持姿態的能力。"],"optionsEn":["Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction","Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability","Turbulence affects posture through spatial scale, duration and direction as well as velocity magnitude."],"answer":2,"explanation":"紊流不只由速度大小決定，渦流的空間尺度、持續時間及方向都可能影響魚維持姿態的能力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Turbulence affects posture through spatial scale, duration and direction as well as velocity magnitude. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b278-v15-30","title":"渦流尺度與魚體尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Eddy scales and fish size: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Eddy scales and fish size” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s。適用邊界：量綱尺度估算，非完整紊流頻譜或魚類生理反應模型。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s. Applicable boundary: Dimensional scale estimate, not a complete turbulence spectrum or physiological response model. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在魚可能利用的路徑採集足夠長的高速流速序列，說明取樣頻率與探頭空間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Collect sufficiently long high-rate velocity records along likely routes, documenting sampling frequency and probe spacing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s。適用邊界：量綱尺度估算，非完整紊流頻譜或魚類生理反應模型。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s. Applicable boundary: Dimensional scale estimate, not a complete turbulence spectrum or physiological response model.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Eddy scales and fish size\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s。","池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會","平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s.","Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity","Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ell=0.4 m; uprime=0.2 m/s; te=ell/uprime=2 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b278-v15-31","title":"渦流尺度與魚體尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Eddy scales and fish size: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Eddy scales and fish size” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在魚可能利用的路徑採集足夠長的高速流速序列，說明取樣頻率與探頭空間。比較不同位置的變動與相干性，再將影像中的魚體轉向和時間序列對齊，避免只憑均速推論紊流影響。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Collect sufficiently long high-rate velocity records along likely routes, documenting sampling frequency and probe spacing. Compare fluctuations and coherence across locations, then align fish turning observations with the records rather than inferring turbulence effects from mean velocity alone. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將擾動速度增加一倍重算周轉尺度，並比較兩種魚體長度與渦流尺寸的相對大小。提出能檢驗姿態變化與水流擾動時間關係的同步觀測方案。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double fluctuation velocity and recompute turnover scale. Compare eddy size with two fish lengths and propose synchronized observations that test the timing between hydraulic fluctuations and changes in fish posture along the route.","failure":"注意干擾：探頭取樣過慢會漏掉快速擾動，過大的空間平均又會抹平渦流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Slow sampling can miss rapid fluctuations, and broad spatial averaging can erase eddies. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在魚可能利用的路徑採集足夠長的高速流速序列，說明取樣頻率與探頭空間。比較不同位置的變動與相干性，再將影像中的魚體轉向和時間序列對齊，避免只憑均速推論紊流影響。","textEn":"Collect sufficiently long high-rate velocity records along likely routes, documenting sampling frequency and probe spacing. Compare fluctuations and coherence across locations, then align fish turning observations with the records rather than inferring turbulence effects from mean velocity alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將擾動速度增加一倍重算周轉尺度，並比較兩種魚體長度與渦流尺寸的相對大小。提出能檢驗姿態變化與水流擾動時間關係的同步觀測方案。","textEn":"Double fluctuation velocity and recompute turnover scale. Compare eddy size with two fish lengths and propose synchronized observations that test the timing between hydraulic fluctuations and changes in fish posture along the route.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Eddy scales and fish size\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在魚可能利用的路徑採集足夠長的高速流速序列，說明取樣頻率與探頭空間。","誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Collect sufficiently long high-rate velocity records along likely routes, documenting sampling frequency and probe spacing.","Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"在魚可能利用的路徑採集足夠長的高速流速序列，說明取樣頻率與探頭空間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Collect sufficiently long high-rate velocity records along likely routes, documenting sampling frequency and probe spacing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b278-v15-32","title":"渦流尺度與魚體尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Eddy scales and fish size: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Eddy scales and fish size” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"探頭取樣過慢會漏掉快速擾動，過大的空間平均又會抹平渦流。若魚明顯失衡而紀錄平穩，應先查解析度及位置，而非否定行為觀察。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Slow sampling can miss rapid fluctuations, and broad spatial averaging can erase eddies. If fish lose posture while records appear smooth, examine resolution and location before dismissing the behavioural evidence as unreliable. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：過度平均會消除瞬時結構，反之短紀錄又可能把偶發渦流當成代表狀態，需要兼顧兩者。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Excessive averaging removes transient structures, whereas very short records may mistake a rare event for typical conditions; both sampling limits require attention.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「相同平均流速就代表魚會遭遇相同尺度與方向的紊流」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal mean velocity means fish encounter turbulence of identical scale and direction\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"探頭取樣過慢會漏掉快速擾動，過大的空間平均又會抹平渦流。若魚明顯失衡而紀錄平穩，應先查解析度及位置，而非否定行為觀察。","textEn":"Slow sampling can miss rapid fluctuations, and broad spatial averaging can erase eddies. If fish lose posture while records appear smooth, examine resolution and location before dismissing the behavioural evidence as unreliable.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「渦流尺度與魚體尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Eddy scales and fish size\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率","探頭取樣過慢會漏掉快速擾動，過大的空間平均又會抹平渦流。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability","Slow sampling can miss rapid fluctuations, and broad spatial averaging can erase eddies."],"answer":2,"explanation":"探頭取樣過慢會漏掉快速擾動，過大的空間平均又會抹平渦流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Slow sampling can miss rapid fluctuations, and broad spatial averaging can erase eddies. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b278-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「偵測效率與通過比例」與「多段通行的累積效果」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Detection efficiency and passage proportion\" and \"Cumulative passage across reaches\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b278-v15-33","title":"偵測效率與通過比例：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Detection efficiency and passage proportion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「偵測效率與通過比例」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Detection efficiency and passage proportion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"上下游感測站看到的魚數同時受到真實通過及偵測效率影響，直接相除可能把儀器差異誤認為生物損失。用已估偵測機率修正計數，是在同一受追蹤族群、單次計數及相容觀測期間下的簡化估計。重複通過、標記脫落與不同魚種的可偵測性會破壞這些假設。分析需保存個體識別及時間順序，並把尋找入口、進入和完成通過分別定義，才能解釋比例代表什麼。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「偵測效率與通過比例」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Counts at upstream and downstream detectors combine actual passage with detection efficiency, so a raw ratio can mistake instrumentation differences for biological loss. Correcting counts by estimated detection probabilities is a simplified estimator for one tracked cohort, unique counts and compatible observation windows. Repeated passages, tag loss and species-dependent detectability violate those assumptions. Preserve individual identities and event order, and distinguish attraction, entry and completed passage so the estimated proportion has a clear denominator and interpretation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Detection efficiency and passage proportion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「偵測效率與通過比例」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Detection efficiency and passage proportion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-33-k1","title":"偵測效率與通過比例","titleEn":"Detection efficiency and passage proportion","text":"上下游感測站看到的魚數同時受到真實通過及偵測效率影響，直接相除可能把儀器差異誤認為生物損失。用已估偵測機率修正計數，是在同一受追蹤族群、單次計數及相容觀測期間下的簡化估計。","textEn":"Counts at upstream and downstream detectors combine actual passage with detection efficiency, so a raw ratio can mistake instrumentation differences for biological loss. Correcting counts by estimated detection probabilities is a simplified estimator for one tracked cohort, unique counts and compatible observation windows.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「偵測效率與通過比例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Detection efficiency and passage proportion\" is correct?","options":["上下游感測站看到的魚數同時受到真實通過及偵測效率影響，直接相除可能把儀器差異誤認為生物損失。","上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率","每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成"],"optionsEn":["Counts at upstream and downstream detectors combine actual passage with detection efficiency, so a raw ratio can mistake instrumentation differences for biological loss.","Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability","If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent"],"answer":0,"explanation":"上下游感測站看到的魚數同時受到真實通過及偵測效率影響，直接相除可能把儀器差異誤認為生物損失。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Counts at upstream and downstream detectors combine actual passage with detection efficiency, so a raw ratio can mistake instrumentation differences for biological loss. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b278-v15-34","title":"偵測效率與通過比例：定量估算","titleEn":"Detection efficiency and passage proportion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「偵測效率與通過比例」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Detection efficiency and passage proportion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless。適用邊界：同一族群唯一個體計數與已知偵測機率的簡化估計，不含估計不確定性。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Simplified same-cohort unique-count estimator with known detection probabilities, excluding estimation uncertainty. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以重複天線或獨立影像估偵測效率，檢查漏測是否隨流量、魚體大小或標記方向改變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Estimate detection with redundant antennas or independent imagery and test dependence on discharge, size and tag orientation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless。適用邊界：同一族群唯一個體計數與已知偵測機率的簡化估計，不含估計不確定性。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Simplified same-cohort unique-count estimator with known detection probabilities, excluding estimation uncertainty.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「偵測效率與通過比例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Detection efficiency and passage proportion\", which statement holds?","options":["流量係數一旦量到就不會隨開口堵塞或尾水改變","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless。","魚相對水的游速就是它相對岸邊的上游移動速度"],"optionsEn":["A measured discharge coefficient never changes with blockage or tailwater","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nu=80 fish.","A fish's swimming speed relative to water is its upstream speed relative to the bank"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nu=80 fish; pu=0.8 dimensionless; Nd=100 fish; pd=0.9 dimensionless; phat=(Nu/pu)/(Nd/pd)=0.9 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b278-v15-35","title":"偵測效率與通過比例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Detection efficiency and passage proportion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「偵測效率與通過比例」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Detection efficiency and passage proportion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以重複天線或獨立影像估偵測效率，檢查漏測是否隨流量、魚體大小或標記方向改變。清理重複個體並對齊觀測窗，另報修正比例的不確定性，若結果超過一應查假設而非強制截斷掩蓋問題。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Estimate detection with redundant antennas or independent imagery and test dependence on discharge, size and tag orientation. Deduplicate individuals and align observation windows. Report uncertainty; estimates above one require investigating assumptions rather than silently truncating the result. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將上游偵測率改成零點九重算並與原始比例比較。列出需要保留的個體欄位，再設計一項檢查以辨認漏測、重複計數與真正未通過三種情況。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change upstream detection probability to zero point nine and compare the corrected and raw ratios. List required individual records and design a check separating missed detections, repeated counts and genuine failure to complete passage.","failure":"注意干擾：下游偵測效率較低時，分母被低估會誇大通過率。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Poor downstream detection reduces the denominator and inflates apparent passage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以重複天線或獨立影像估偵測效率，檢查漏測是否隨流量、魚體大小或標記方向改變。清理重複個體並對齊觀測窗，另報修正比例的不確定性，若結果超過一應查假設而非強制截斷掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Estimate detection with redundant antennas or independent imagery and test dependence on discharge, size and tag orientation. Deduplicate individuals and align observation windows. Report uncertainty; estimates above one require investigating assumptions rather than silently truncating the result.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將上游偵測率改成零點九重算並與原始比例比較。列出需要保留的個體欄位，再設計一項檢查以辨認漏測、重複計數與真正未通過三種情況。","textEn":"Change upstream detection probability to zero point nine and compare the corrected and raw ratios. List required individual records and design a check separating missed detections, repeated counts and genuine failure to complete passage.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「偵測效率與通過比例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Detection efficiency and passage proportion\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","名義換水時間就是所有魚必須在池中停留的時間","以重複天線或獨立影像估偵測效率，檢查漏測是否隨流量、魚體大小或標記方向改變。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Nominal water turnover time is the time every fish must remain in the pool","Estimate detection with redundant antennas or independent imagery and test dependence on discharge, size and tag orientation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以重複天線或獨立影像估偵測效率，檢查漏測是否隨流量、魚體大小或標記方向改變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Estimate detection with redundant antennas or independent imagery and test dependence on discharge, size and tag orientation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b278-v15-36","title":"偵測效率與通過比例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Detection efficiency and passage proportion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「偵測效率與通過比例」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Detection efficiency and passage proportion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"下游偵測效率較低時，分母被低估會誇大通過率。若把反覆往返同一魚當不同個體，還可能得到表面大於全部進入數的錯誤成果。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Poor downstream detection reduces the denominator and inflates apparent passage. Counting repeated movements of one fish as separate individuals can further produce an implausible number of successes relative to the original cohort. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：分析需保存個體識別及時間順序，並把尋找入口、進入和完成通過分別定義，才能解釋比例代表什麼。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Preserve individual identities and event order, and distinguish attraction, entry and completed passage so the estimated proportion has a clear denominator and interpretation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「上下游原始計數相除必然等於真實通過機率」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Dividing raw upstream by downstream counts necessarily gives the true passage probability\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"下游偵測效率較低時，分母被低估會誇大通過率。若把反覆往返同一魚當不同個體，還可能得到表面大於全部進入數的錯誤成果。","textEn":"Poor downstream detection reduces the denominator and inflates apparent passage. Counting repeated movements of one fish as separate individuals can further produce an implausible number of successes relative to the original cohort.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「偵測效率與通過比例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Detection efficiency and passage proportion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["下游偵測效率較低時，分母被低估會誇大通過率。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成"],"optionsEn":["Poor downstream detection reduces the denominator and inflates apparent passage.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent"],"answer":0,"explanation":"下游偵測效率較低時，分母被低估會誇大通過率。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Poor downstream detection reduces the denominator and inflates apparent passage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b278-v15-37","title":"多段通行的累積效果：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cumulative passage across reaches: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「多段通行的累積效果」如何影響魚道水理設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cumulative passage across reaches” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hydraulic design of fish passages”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"流域中的多個障礙會把單處看似很高的通過率累積成較低的整體成功率，但乘法必須使用相容的條件機率。若每段數值是已到達該段魚群的通過機率，連乘可表示依序完成的比例；若只是不同調查族群的平均值，就未必可直接相乘。等待與繞行也會延長遷移時間，即使最後通過仍可能錯過繁殖窗口。改善排序應同時考慮瓶頸、時序與族群差異，而非只追求單處漂亮數字。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「多段通行的累積效果」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Multiple barriers can turn high local passage into modest basin-wide success, but multiplication requires compatible conditional probabilities. If each value describes fish that actually reach that stage, their product represents sequential completion; averages from unrelated populations need not be compatible. Delays and detours also matter because eventual passage can miss a breeding window. Prioritize improvements using bottlenecks, timing and population differences rather than optimizing one attractive local percentage without considering the connected migration route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cumulative passage across reaches” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「多段通行的累積效果」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cumulative passage across reaches”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-37-k1","title":"多段通行的累積效果","titleEn":"Cumulative passage across reaches","text":"流域中的多個障礙會把單處看似很高的通過率累積成較低的整體成功率，但乘法必須使用相容的條件機率。若每段數值是已到達該段魚群的通過機率，連乘可表示依序完成的比例；若只是不同調查族群的平均值，就未必可直接相乘。","textEn":"Multiple barriers can turn high local passage into modest basin-wide success, but multiplication requires compatible conditional probabilities. If each value describes fish that actually reach that stage, their product represents sequential completion; averages from unrelated populations need not be compatible.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「多段通行的累積效果」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cumulative passage across reaches\" is correct?","options":["每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成","流域中的多個障礙會把單處看似很高的通過率累積成較低的整體成功率，但乘法必須使用相容的條件機率。","池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會"],"optionsEn":["If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent","Multiple barriers can turn high local passage into modest basin-wide success, but multiplication requires compatible conditional probabilities.","Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity"],"answer":1,"explanation":"流域中的多個障礙會把單處看似很高的通過率累積成較低的整體成功率，但乘法必須使用相容的條件機率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Multiple barriers can turn high local passage into modest basin-wide success, but multiplication requires compatible conditional probabilities. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b278-v15-38","title":"多段通行的累積效果：定量估算","titleEn":"Cumulative passage across reaches: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「多段通行的累積效果」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cumulative passage across reaches” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless。適用邊界：五段條件通過率皆給定相同值；若視為邊際率則另需獨立性假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: All five conditional stage probabilities are assumed equal; using marginal rates instead would additionally require independence. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對同一標記族群建立各段到達及通過的時間表，分母使用真正到達該段的個體。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build arrival and completion histories for the same tagged cohort, using actual arrivals as each denominator.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless。適用邊界：五段條件通過率皆給定相同值；若視為邊際率則另需獨立性假設。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: All five conditional stage probabilities are assumed equal; using marginal rates instead would additionally require independence.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「多段通行的累積效果」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cumulative passage across reaches\", which statement holds?","options":["平均功率密度相同就代表池內每個位置紊流程度相同","誘導流量占比就是到達魚道入口的魚類成功百分比","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless。"],"optionsEn":["Equal average power density means identical turbulence at every point in a pool","Attraction discharge fraction equals the percentage of fish that successfully find the entrance","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: p=0.9 dimensionless conditional-stage-probability; N=5 stages; Pall=p^N=0.59049 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b278-v15-39","title":"多段通行的累積效果：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cumulative passage across reaches: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「多段通行的累積效果」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cumulative passage across reaches” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對同一標記族群建立各段到達及通過的時間表，分母使用真正到達該段的個體。檢查魚體狀態與季節是否逐段改變，將累積成功與總延遲分開報告，並追查失聯是否只是偵測不足。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build arrival and completion histories for the same tagged cohort, using actual arrivals as each denominator. Check changing condition and season across stages. Report cumulative completion separately from total delay and investigate whether disappearance reflects inadequate detection rather than loss. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將其中一段條件通過率提高到零點九八重算全程比例，再比較減少等待時間但不改通過率的方案。說明兩種效益需要哪些不同觀測才能評估。","observationEn":"Site practice: Raise one conditional stage probability to zero point nine eight and recompute completion. Compare this with reducing delay at unchanged passage probability, identifying the different observations required to evaluate these two benefits.","failure":"注意干擾：某段延遲可能改變下一段面對的流量或季節，讓從其他年份搬來的局部通過率不適用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Delay at one barrier can change the flow or season encountered next, invalidating local rates borrowed from another year. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對同一標記族群建立各段到達及通過的時間表，分母使用真正到達該段的個體。檢查魚體狀態與季節是否逐段改變，將累積成功與總延遲分開報告，並追查失聯是否只是偵測不足。","textEn":"Build arrival and completion histories for the same tagged cohort, using actual arrivals as each denominator. Check changing condition and season across stages. Report cumulative completion separately from total delay and investigate whether disappearance reflects inadequate detection rather than loss.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將其中一段條件通過率提高到零點九八重算全程比例，再比較減少等待時間但不改通過率的方案。說明兩種效益需要哪些不同觀測才能評估。","textEn":"Raise one conditional stage probability to zero point nine eight and recompute completion. Compare this with reducing delay at unchanged passage probability, identifying the different observations required to evaluate these two benefits.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「多段通行的累積效果」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cumulative passage across reaches\"?","options":["對同一標記族群建立各段到達及通過的時間表，分母使用真正到達該段的個體。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","孔隙平均速度與按總網面積計算的表觀速度永遠相同"],"optionsEn":["Build arrival and completion histories for the same tagged cohort, using actual arrivals as each denominator.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Opening velocity and superficial velocity based on gross screen area are always identical"],"answer":0,"explanation":"對同一標記族群建立各段到達及通過的時間表，分母使用真正到達該段的個體。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build arrival and completion histories for the same tagged cohort, using actual arrivals as each denominator. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b278-v15-40","title":"多段通行的累積效果：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cumulative passage across reaches: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"prerequisiteIds":["b278-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「多段通行的累積效果」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cumulative passage across reaches” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"某段延遲可能改變下一段面對的流量或季節，讓從其他年份搬來的局部通過率不適用。只連乘公布百分比會忽略這種跨段與跨時影響。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Delay at one barrier can change the flow or season encountered next, invalidating local rates borrowed from another year. Multiplying published percentages without cohort and timing checks can therefore misrepresent cumulative migration outcomes. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：改善排序應同時考慮瓶頸、時序與族群差異，而非只追求單處漂亮數字。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Prioritize improvements using bottlenecks, timing and population differences rather than optimizing one attractive local percentage without considering the connected migration route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每一段通過率都是九成所以五段全部通過率仍是九成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If each stage passes ninety percent, passage through all five is still ninety percent\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b278-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"某段延遲可能改變下一段面對的流量或季節，讓從其他年份搬來的局部通過率不適用。只連乘公布百分比會忽略這種跨段與跨時影響。","textEn":"Delay at one barrier can change the flow or season encountered next, invalidating local rates borrowed from another year. Multiplying published percentages without cohort and timing checks can therefore misrepresent cumulative migration outcomes.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]},{"id":"b278-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「多段通行的累積效果」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cumulative passage across reaches\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","某段延遲可能改變下一段面對的流量或季節，讓從其他年份搬來的局部通過率不適用。","池間落差相同就代表所有魚種都具有相同通過機會"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Delay at one barrier can change the flow or season encountered next, invalidating local rates borrowed from another year.","Equal pool drops give every fish species the same passage opportunity"],"answer":1,"explanation":"某段延遲可能改變下一段面對的流量或季節，讓從其他年份搬來的局部通過率不適用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Delay at one barrier can change the flow or season encountered next, invalidating local rates borrowed from another year. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-noaa-passage","v15s-usbr-fish-evaluation","v15s-mcnary-lamprey","v15s-usace-fish-counts"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b279","title":"河川再蜿蜒工程","titleEn":"River remeandering works","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"再蜿蜒不只是把直線河道畫成曲線，而是重新安排河道長度、洪氾空間、地下水交換與泥砂的移動途徑。十個單元由地形量測走向流況及監測設計，並要求比較工程前後及參照區，避免把自然年際變化誤認為復育工程的單一成果。","summaryEn":"Remeandering reorganizes channel length, floodplain space, groundwater exchange and sediment pathways. Ten units move from geometric measurement to flow processes and monitoring design. Comparisons across time and reference reaches help separate restoration signals from natural variation. Learners examine both the intended ecological gains and the hydraulic consequences of reconnecting a river with surrounding land.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["蜿蜒度與量測尺度","Sinuosity and measurement scale"],["粗糙度與通水尺度","Roughness and conveyance scale"],["彎道橫向水面差","Transverse water level in bends"],["側汊連通的交換水量","Exchange volume through a side channel"],["地形差分的量測不確定性","Uncertainty in terrain differences"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["蜿蜒度與量測尺度","粗糙度與通水尺度","彎道橫向水面差","側汊連通的交換水量","地形差分的量測不確定性"],"labelsEn":["Sinuosity and measurement scale","Roughness and conveyance scale","Transverse water level in bends","Exchange volume through a side channel","Uncertainty in terrain differences"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課先用「蜿蜒度與量測尺度」建立原創假想基準，再以「展長後的平均坡度」檢查另一個控制機制。第一組輸入及結果為 Lc=1800 m; Lv=1200 m; P=Lc/Lv=1.5 dimensionless；第二組為 dz=3 m; L=1800 m; S=dz/L=0.001666667 dimensionless。學員需在同一張工作表分列量綱、時間、位置與適用範圍，先核對守恆，再解釋為何兩個得數不能互相代替。最後以第三單元提出的量測設計驗證假設，並將超出模型能力的水理、生態或治理問題列為待研究項目；這些示例並非所列案例的現場實測。敏感度重算：固定谷地參考長 Lv=1200 m，將中心線 Lc 從 1800 m 增至 1980 m，蜿蜒度由 1.5 增至 1.65。河長與指標同增一成，但這個比值不能單獨證明棲地、洪峰或泥砂平衡改善。","textEn":"Begin with an original hypothetical baseline for Sinuosity and measurement scale and examine another controlling mechanism through Mean slope after lengthening. The first inputs and result are Lc=1800 m; Lv=1200 m; P=Lc/Lv=1.5 dimensionless; the second are dz=3 m; L=1800 m; S=dz/L=0.001666667 dimensionless. Keep dimensions, time, location and validity conditions in separate columns of the same working sheet. Check conservation before explaining why the two numerical results cannot substitute for one another. Use the third unit measurement design to test assumptions and identify hydraulic, ecological or governance questions that exceed the model. These examples are not field observations from the named reference cases. Sensitivity recalculation: Keep valley reference length Lv=1200 m fixed and increase centreline Lc from 1800 m to 1980 m. Sinuosity rises from 1.5 to 1.65. Length and index both increase ten percent, but the ratio alone does not establish improvement in habitat, flood peaks or sediment balance.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b279-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「蜿蜒度與量測尺度」與「展長後的平均坡度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Sinuosity and measurement scale\" and \"Mean slope after lengthening\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b279-v15-01","title":"蜿蜒度與量測尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Sinuosity and measurement scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「蜿蜒度與量測尺度」如何影響河川再蜿蜒工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sinuosity and measurement scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River remeandering works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"蜿蜒度比較沿河道中心線與谷地參考路徑的長度，能描述平面幾何，卻不直接代表棲地品質或洪水安全。中心線取自低水槽、滿岸線或影像水面時可能得到不同結果，谷地長度也必須固定相同起訖點。影像解析度太細會把小幅岸線起伏計入長度，太粗則削去彎道。因此工程前後比較應維持相同定義與解析度，先確認幾何變化是真實河道重組而非測圖方式改變。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「蜿蜒度與量測尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Sinuosity compares channel-centreline length with a valley reference route, describing plan geometry rather than habitat quality or flood safety. A centreline based on low flow, bankfull edges or visible water can differ, and valley length must use matching endpoints. Fine imagery may count minor irregularities while coarse mapping removes bends. Keep definitions and resolution consistent before and after works so an apparent change represents channel reorganization rather than a different surveying method or mapping scale. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sinuosity and measurement scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Lc=1800 m; Lv=1200 m; P=Lc/Lv=1.5 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Lc=1800 m; Lv=1200 m; P=Lc/Lv=1.5 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「蜿蜒度較大必然代表所有生態功能與防洪能力較好」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Greater sinuosity necessarily means better ecological function and flood protection in every respect\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「蜿蜒度與量測尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sinuosity and measurement scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-01-k1","title":"蜿蜒度與量測尺度","titleEn":"Sinuosity and measurement scale","text":"蜿蜒度比較沿河道中心線與谷地參考路徑的長度，能描述平面幾何，卻不直接代表棲地品質或洪水安全。中心線取自低水槽、滿岸線或影像水面時可能得到不同結果，谷地長度也必須固定相同起訖點。","textEn":"Sinuosity compares channel-centreline length with a valley reference route, describing plan geometry rather than habitat quality or flood safety. A centreline based on low flow, bankfull edges or visible water can differ, and valley length must use matching endpoints.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：蜿蜒度較大必然代表所有生態功能與防洪能力較好 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Greater sinuosity necessarily means better ecological function and flood protection in every respect Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「蜿蜒度與量測尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sinuosity and measurement scale\" is correct?","options":["蜿蜒度較大必然代表所有生態功能與防洪能力較好","蜿蜒度比較沿河道中心線與谷地參考路徑的長度，能描述平面幾何，卻不直接代表棲地品質或洪水安全。","河道平均床坡就是所有流量下每一斷面的能量坡度"],"optionsEn":["Greater sinuosity necessarily means better ecological function and flood protection in every respect","Sinuosity compares channel-centreline length with a valley reference route, describing plan geometry rather than habitat quality or flood safety.","Mean bed slope equals the energy slope at every section and discharge"],"answer":1,"explanation":"蜿蜒度比較沿河道中心線與谷地參考路徑的長度，能描述平面幾何，卻不直接代表棲地品質或洪水安全。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Sinuosity compares channel-centreline length with a valley reference route, describing plan geometry rather than habitat quality or flood safety. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b279-v15-02","title":"蜿蜒度與量測尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Sinuosity and measurement scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「蜿蜒度與量測尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sinuosity and measurement scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Lc=1800 m; Lv=1200 m; P=Lc/Lv=1.5 dimensionless。適用邊界：相同起訖點與固定中心線定義，只描述平面長度比。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Lc=1800 m; Lv=1200 m; P=Lc/Lv=1.5 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Matching endpoints and a fixed centreline definition; describes plan-length ratio only. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：使用同一底圖投影及解析度數化工程前後中心線，保留起訖點和谷地基準路徑。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Digitize both centrelines using the same projection and resolution, preserving endpoints and valley reference.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Lc=1800 m; Lv=1200 m; P=Lc/Lv=1.5 dimensionless。適用邊界：相同起訖點與固定中心線定義，只描述平面長度比。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Lc=1800 m; Lv=1200 m; P=Lc/Lv=1.5 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Matching endpoints and a fixed centreline definition; describes plan-length ratio only.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「蜿蜒度與量測尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sinuosity and measurement scale\", which statement holds?","options":["幾何蓄水容量直接等於河川洪峰流量減少量","岸坡流失的原位體積必然在同一時刻全部通過下游斷面","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Lc=1800 m; Lv=1200 m; P=Lc/Lv=1.5 dimensionless。"],"optionsEn":["Geometric storage volume directly equals the reduction in river peak discharge","All in-place bank erosion volume necessarily passes the downstream section at the same moment","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Lc=1800 m; Lv=1200 m; P=Lc/Lv=1.5 dimensionless."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Lc=1800 m; Lv=1200 m; P=Lc/Lv=1.5 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Lc=1800 m; Lv=1200 m; P=Lc/Lv=1.5 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b279-v15-03","title":"蜿蜒度與量測尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sinuosity and measurement scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「蜿蜒度與量測尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sinuosity and measurement scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"使用同一底圖投影及解析度數化工程前後中心線，保留起訖點和谷地基準路徑。以第二位判讀者重畫部分彎道估計主觀差異，再將長度改變與實際開挖或自然遷移位置核對，避免把繪圖密度當成果。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Digitize both centrelines using the same projection and resolution, preserving endpoints and valley reference. Have another interpreter redraw selected bends to estimate subjective variation, then compare length changes with actual excavation or migration rather than treating denser digitizing as improvement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在谷地長度固定下將河長增加一成重算蜿蜒度，另畫一個增加長度但缺少洪氾空間的方案。說明還需哪些水理及生態證據才能比較兩者。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase channel length by ten percent at fixed valley length and recalculate sinuosity. Sketch a longer channel without additional floodplain space, then identify hydraulic and ecological evidence needed to compare the alternatives.","failure":"注意干擾：不同年份使用不同解析度影像可能製造虛假蜿蜒度增加，洪水影像還可能把漫流支線誤認主槽。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Different image resolutions can create false sinuosity gains, while flood imagery may confuse overbank branches with the main channel. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"使用同一底圖投影及解析度數化工程前後中心線，保留起訖點和谷地基準路徑。以第二位判讀者重畫部分彎道估計主觀差異，再將長度改變與實際開挖或自然遷移位置核對，避免把繪圖密度當成果。","textEn":"Digitize both centrelines using the same projection and resolution, preserving endpoints and valley reference. Have another interpreter redraw selected bends to estimate subjective variation, then compare length changes with actual excavation or migration rather than treating denser digitizing as improvement.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在谷地長度固定下將河長增加一成重算蜿蜒度，另畫一個增加長度但缺少洪氾空間的方案。說明還需哪些水理及生態證據才能比較兩者。","textEn":"Increase channel length by ten percent at fixed valley length and recalculate sinuosity. Sketch a longer channel without additional floodplain space, then identify hydraulic and ecological evidence needed to compare the alternatives.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「蜿蜒度與量測尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sinuosity and measurement scale\"?","options":["使用同一底圖投影及解析度數化工程前後中心線，保留起訖點和谷地基準路徑。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","達西通量就是孔隙中每個水粒子的實際移動速度"],"optionsEn":["Digitize both centrelines using the same projection and resolution, preserving endpoints and valley reference.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Darcy flux is the actual speed of every water particle inside the pores"],"answer":0,"explanation":"使用同一底圖投影及解析度數化工程前後中心線，保留起訖點和谷地基準路徑。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Digitize both centrelines using the same projection and resolution, preserving endpoints and valley reference. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b279-v15-04","title":"蜿蜒度與量測尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sinuosity and measurement scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「蜿蜒度與量測尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sinuosity and measurement scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不同年份使用不同解析度影像可能製造虛假蜿蜒度增加，洪水影像還可能把漫流支線誤認主槽。診斷應先檢查中心線定義及流量條件。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Different image resolutions can create false sinuosity gains, while flood imagery may confuse overbank branches with the main channel. Check centreline definitions and flow conditions before interpreting apparent geometric improvement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此工程前後比較應維持相同定義與解析度，先確認幾何變化是真實河道重組而非測圖方式改變。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Keep definitions and resolution consistent before and after works so an apparent change represents channel reorganization rather than a different surveying method or mapping scale.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「蜿蜒度較大必然代表所有生態功能與防洪能力較好」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Greater sinuosity necessarily means better ecological function and flood protection in every respect\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不同年份使用不同解析度影像可能製造虛假蜿蜒度增加，洪水影像還可能把漫流支線誤認主槽。診斷應先檢查中心線定義及流量條件。","textEn":"Different image resolutions can create false sinuosity gains, while flood imagery may confuse overbank branches with the main channel. Check centreline definitions and flow conditions before interpreting apparent geometric improvement.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「蜿蜒度與量測尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sinuosity and measurement scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","不同年份使用不同解析度影像可能製造虛假蜿蜒度增加，洪水影像還可能把漫流支線誤認主槽。","河道平均床坡就是所有流量下每一斷面的能量坡度"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Different image resolutions can create false sinuosity gains, while flood imagery may confuse overbank branches with the main channel.","Mean bed slope equals the energy slope at every section and discharge"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同年份使用不同解析度影像可能製造虛假蜿蜒度增加，洪水影像還可能把漫流支線誤認主槽。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Different image resolutions can create false sinuosity gains, while flood imagery may confuse overbank branches with the main channel. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b279-v15-05","title":"展長後的平均坡度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Mean slope after lengthening: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「展長後的平均坡度」如何影響河川再蜿蜒工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mean slope after lengthening” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River remeandering works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"在上游與下游控制高程不變時，河道展長會降低沿程平均坡度，但各彎段的床坡不必均勻。局部深潭、淺瀨與回水可能分配大部分水頭損失，因此不能把平均坡度直接視為每一點能坡。坡度降低也會改變輸砂能力，若上游供砂維持不變，河床可能淤積再調整。設計應把高程控制、幾何長度與預期泥砂交換連在一起，而非只透過平面曲線追求更大的蜿蜒度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「展長後的平均坡度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"With fixed upstream and downstream control elevations, channel lengthening reduces mean longitudinal slope, but individual bends need not share that slope. Pools, riffles and backwater distribute losses unevenly, so mean bed slope is not the energy slope everywhere. Lower slope can alter transport capacity and trigger deposition when upstream sediment supply persists. Connect elevation controls, channel geometry and sediment exchange rather than pursuing a larger sinuosity value through planform geometry alone without checking adjustment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Mean slope after lengthening” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：dz=3 m; L=1800 m; S=dz/L=0.001666667 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: dz=3 m; L=1800 m; S=dz/L=0.001666667 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「河道平均床坡就是所有流量下每一斷面的能量坡度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Mean bed slope equals the energy slope at every section and discharge\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「展長後的平均坡度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Mean slope after lengthening”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-05-k1","title":"展長後的平均坡度","titleEn":"Mean slope after lengthening","text":"在上游與下游控制高程不變時，河道展長會降低沿程平均坡度，但各彎段的床坡不必均勻。局部深潭、淺瀨與回水可能分配大部分水頭損失，因此不能把平均坡度直接視為每一點能坡。","textEn":"With fixed upstream and downstream control elevations, channel lengthening reduces mean longitudinal slope, but individual bends need not share that slope. Pools, riffles and backwater distribute losses unevenly, so mean bed slope is not the energy slope everywhere.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：河道平均床坡就是所有流量下每一斷面的能量坡度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Mean bed slope equals the energy slope at every section and discharge Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「展長後的平均坡度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mean slope after lengthening\" is correct?","options":["河道平均床坡就是所有流量下每一斷面的能量坡度","曼寧粗糙係數只由材料決定且永遠不隨水深改變","在上游與下游控制高程不變時，河道展長會降低沿程平均坡度，但各彎段的床坡不必均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Mean bed slope equals the energy slope at every section and discharge","Manning roughness depends only on material and never changes with water depth","With fixed upstream and downstream control elevations, channel lengthening reduces mean longitudinal slope, but individual bends need not share that slope."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在上游與下游控制高程不變時，河道展長會降低沿程平均坡度，但各彎段的床坡不必均勻。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"With fixed upstream and downstream control elevations, channel lengthening reduces mean longitudinal slope, but individual bends need not share that slope. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b279-v15-06","title":"展長後的平均坡度：定量估算","titleEn":"Mean slope after lengthening: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「展長後的平均坡度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mean slope after lengthening” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：dz=3 m; L=1800 m; S=dz/L=0.001666667 dimensionless。適用邊界：固定兩端床高的平均幾何坡度，不代替局部能坡或輸砂平衡。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: dz=3 m; L=1800 m; S=dz/L=0.001666667 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Mean geometric slope at fixed endpoint bed levels, not local energy slope or sediment equilibrium. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：重測兩端控制高程與沿程縱斷面，將深潭、淺瀨及構造物逐一標示。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey endpoint controls and the full profile, identifying pools, riffles and structures.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：dz=3 m; L=1800 m; S=dz/L=0.001666667 dimensionless。適用邊界：固定兩端床高的平均幾何坡度，不代替局部能坡或輸砂平衡。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: dz=3 m; L=1800 m; S=dz/L=0.001666667 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Mean geometric slope at fixed endpoint bed levels, not local energy slope or sediment equilibrium.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「展長後的平均坡度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mean slope after lengthening\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：dz=3 m; L=1800 m; S=dz/L=0.001666667 dimensionless。","橫向水面差很小就能證明外彎岸坡不會沖刷","側汊總流入體積就是側汊最後增加的淨蓄水體積"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: dz=3 m; L=1800 m; S=dz/L=0.001666667 dimensionless.","A small transverse water-level difference proves that the outer bank will not erode","Total side-channel inflow equals its final increase in net stored volume"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：dz=3 m; L=1800 m; S=dz/L=0.001666667 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: dz=3 m; L=1800 m; S=dz/L=0.001666667 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b279-v15-07","title":"展長後的平均坡度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Mean slope after lengthening: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「展長後的平均坡度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mean slope after lengthening” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"重測兩端控制高程與沿程縱斷面，將深潭、淺瀨及構造物逐一標示。另量代表流量下水面坡度，對照床坡差異；若出現大範圍回水，應調查下游控制而非把所有差異歸因於新彎道。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey endpoint controls and the full profile, identifying pools, riffles and structures. Measure water-surface slope at representative discharge and compare with bed slope. Extensive backwater requires investigating downstream control instead of attributing every difference to the new bends. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將河長縮短三百公尺重算平均坡度，保持兩端高程不變。畫出兩個具有相同平均坡但局部深潭配置不同的縱斷面，說明其水理仍可能不同。","observationEn":"Site practice: Shorten the channel by three hundred metres with endpoint levels fixed and recalculate slope. Draw two profiles with identical mean slope but different pool distributions, explaining why their hydraulic behaviour may still differ.","failure":"注意干擾：若只增加河長卻忽略下游固定水位，上游可能產生預期外壅水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Lengthening while ignoring a fixed downstream level can create unexpected upstream backwater. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"重測兩端控制高程與沿程縱斷面，將深潭、淺瀨及構造物逐一標示。另量代表流量下水面坡度，對照床坡差異；若出現大範圍回水，應調查下游控制而非把所有差異歸因於新彎道。","textEn":"Survey endpoint controls and the full profile, identifying pools, riffles and structures. Measure water-surface slope at representative discharge and compare with bed slope. Extensive backwater requires investigating downstream control instead of attributing every difference to the new bends.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將河長縮短三百公尺重算平均坡度，保持兩端高程不變。畫出兩個具有相同平均坡但局部深潭配置不同的縱斷面，說明其水理仍可能不同。","textEn":"Shorten the channel by three hundred metres with endpoint levels fixed and recalculate slope. Draw two profiles with identical mean slope but different pool distributions, explaining why their hydraulic behaviour may still differ.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「展長後的平均坡度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mean slope after lengthening\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","重測兩端控制高程與沿程縱斷面，將深潭、淺瀨及構造物逐一標示。","水粒子旅行時間一定等於洪水峰值傳到下游的時間"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Survey endpoint controls and the full profile, identifying pools, riffles and structures.","Water-parcel travel time always equals the time for a flood peak to reach downstream"],"answer":1,"explanation":"重測兩端控制高程與沿程縱斷面，將深潭、淺瀨及構造物逐一標示。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey endpoint controls and the full profile, identifying pools, riffles and structures. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b279-v15-08","title":"展長後的平均坡度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mean slope after lengthening: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「展長後的平均坡度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mean slope after lengthening” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只增加河長卻忽略下游固定水位，上游可能產生預期外壅水。床面局部淤積也可能重新縮短有效流路，需追蹤水面與地形的共同演變。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Lengthening while ignoring a fixed downstream level can create unexpected upstream backwater. Local deposition may also shorten the effective flow path, requiring joint monitoring of water levels and evolving channel geometry. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計應把高程控制、幾何長度與預期泥砂交換連在一起，而非只透過平面曲線追求更大的蜿蜒度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Connect elevation controls, channel geometry and sediment exchange rather than pursuing a larger sinuosity value through planform geometry alone without checking adjustment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「河道平均床坡就是所有流量下每一斷面的能量坡度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Mean bed slope equals the energy slope at every section and discharge\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只增加河長卻忽略下游固定水位，上游可能產生預期外壅水。床面局部淤積也可能重新縮短有效流路，需追蹤水面與地形的共同演變。","textEn":"Lengthening while ignoring a fixed downstream level can create unexpected upstream backwater. Local deposition may also shorten the effective flow path, requiring joint monitoring of water levels and evolving channel geometry.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「展長後的平均坡度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mean slope after lengthening\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","曼寧粗糙係數只由材料決定且永遠不隨水深改變","若只增加河長卻忽略下游固定水位，上游可能產生預期外壅水。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Manning roughness depends only on material and never changes with water depth","Lengthening while ignoring a fixed downstream level can create unexpected upstream backwater."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若只增加河長卻忽略下游固定水位，上游可能產生預期外壅水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Lengthening while ignoring a fixed downstream level can create unexpected upstream backwater. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b279-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「粗糙度與通水尺度」與「洪氾地的可用蓄水」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Roughness and conveyance scale\" and \"Available floodplain storage\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b279-v15-09","title":"粗糙度與通水尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Roughness and conveyance scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「粗糙度與通水尺度」如何影響河川再蜿蜒工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Roughness and conveyance scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River remeandering works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"復育後植生、木構與河床形態會改變阻力，用曼寧式可初步比較斷面通水尺度，但必須確認近似均勻流及適用的單位系統。粗糙係數不是純粹材料常數，會隨淹水深度、植生彎伏和季節改變。複式斷面中主槽與洪氾地的交換也難由單一係數描述。計算應保留面積、水力半徑與能坡各自來源，不可用調整係數掩蓋幾何或邊界條件的錯誤。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「粗糙度與通水尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Restored vegetation, wood and bed forms change resistance. Manning's relation offers a preliminary conveyance comparison under approximately uniform flow and a stated unit system. Roughness is not merely a material constant; depth, plant reconfiguration and season affect it. Exchange between the main channel and floodplain also exceeds a single-coefficient description. Keep the origins of area, hydraulic radius and energy slope explicit instead of tuning roughness to conceal errors in geometry or boundary conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Roughness and conveyance scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：n=0.04 s/m^(1/3); A=24 m2; R=1.2 m; S=0.0015 dimensionless; Q=A*R^(2/3)*sqrt(S)/n=26.241241 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: n=0.04 s/m^(1/3); A=24 m2; R=1.2 m; S=0.0015 dimensionless; Q=A*R^(2/3)*sqrt(S)/n=26.241241 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「曼寧粗糙係數只由材料決定且永遠不隨水深改變」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Manning roughness depends only on material and never changes with water depth\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「粗糙度與通水尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Roughness and conveyance scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-09-k1","title":"粗糙度與通水尺度","titleEn":"Roughness and conveyance scale","text":"復育後植生、木構與河床形態會改變阻力，用曼寧式可初步比較斷面通水尺度，但必須確認近似均勻流及適用的單位系統。粗糙係數不是純粹材料常數，會隨淹水深度、植生彎伏和季節改變。","textEn":"Restored vegetation, wood and bed forms change resistance. Manning's relation offers a preliminary conveyance comparison under approximately uniform flow and a stated unit system.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：曼寧粗糙係數只由材料決定且永遠不隨水深改變 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Manning roughness depends only on material and never changes with water depth Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「粗糙度與通水尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Roughness and conveyance scale\" is correct?","options":["復育後植生、木構與河床形態會改變阻力，用曼寧式可初步比較斷面通水尺度，但必須確認近似均勻流及適用的單位系統。","曼寧粗糙係數只由材料決定且永遠不隨水深改變","幾何蓄水容量直接等於河川洪峰流量減少量"],"optionsEn":["Restored vegetation, wood and bed forms change resistance.","Manning roughness depends only on material and never changes with water depth","Geometric storage volume directly equals the reduction in river peak discharge"],"answer":0,"explanation":"復育後植生、木構與河床形態會改變阻力，用曼寧式可初步比較斷面通水尺度，但必須確認近似均勻流及適用的單位系統。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Restored vegetation, wood and bed forms change resistance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b279-v15-10","title":"粗糙度與通水尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Roughness and conveyance scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「粗糙度與通水尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Roughness and conveyance scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：n=0.04 s/m^(1/3); A=24 m2; R=1.2 m; S=0.0015 dimensionless; Q=A*R^(2/3)*sqrt(S)/n=26.241241 m3/s。適用邊界：SI 曼寧形式的近均勻流示例，能坡為獨立假設且非前單元床坡。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: n=0.04 s/m^(1/3); A=24 m2; R=1.2 m; S=0.0015 dimensionless; Q=A*R^(2/3)*sqrt(S)/n=26.241241 m3/s. Applicable boundary: SI Manning approximation for near-uniform flow; energy slope is independently assumed, not the preceding unit's bed slope. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對數個流量實測水位與速度，先驗證斷面幾何，再比較推算係數是否隨水深系統性改變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure levels and velocities at several discharges, verify geometry first, and check systematic depth dependence in inferred roughness.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：n=0.04 s/m^(1/3); A=24 m2; R=1.2 m; S=0.0015 dimensionless; Q=A*R^(2/3)*sqrt(S)/n=26.241241 m3/s。適用邊界：SI 曼寧形式的近均勻流示例，能坡為獨立假設且非前單元床坡。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: n=0.04 s/m^(1/3); A=24 m2; R=1.2 m; S=0.0015 dimensionless; Q=A*R^(2/3)*sqrt(S)/n=26.241241 m3/s. Applicable boundary: SI Manning approximation for near-uniform flow; energy slope is independently assumed, not the preceding unit's bed slope.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「粗糙度與通水尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Roughness and conveyance scale\", which statement holds?","options":["岸坡流失的原位體積必然在同一時刻全部通過下游斷面","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：n=0.04 s/m^(1/3); A=24 m2; R=1.2 m; S=0.0015 dimensionless; Q=A*R^(2/3)*sqrt(S)/n=26.241241 m3/s。","達西通量就是孔隙中每個水粒子的實際移動速度"],"optionsEn":["All in-place bank erosion volume necessarily passes the downstream section at the same moment","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: n=0.04 s/m^(1/3).","Darcy flux is the actual speed of every water particle inside the pores"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：n=0.04 s/m^(1/3); A=24 m2; R=1.2 m; S=0.0015 dimensionless; Q=A*R^(2/3)*sqrt(S)/n=26.241241 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: n=0.04 s/m^(1/3); A=24 m2; R=1.2 m; S=0.0015 dimensionless; Q=A*R^(2/3)*sqrt(S)/n=26.241241 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b279-v15-11","title":"粗糙度與通水尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Roughness and conveyance scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「粗糙度與通水尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Roughness and conveyance scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對數個流量實測水位與速度，先驗證斷面幾何，再比較推算係數是否隨水深系統性改變。分別調查有葉與落葉狀態，若主槽和洪氾地速度差很大，應分區估算並考慮側向交換。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure levels and velocities at several discharges, verify geometry first, and check systematic depth dependence in inferred roughness. Survey leafy and leafless conditions separately. Strong main-channel and floodplain velocity contrasts call for divided treatment and attention to lateral exchange. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將粗糙係數增加四分之一並保持幾何與能坡不變，重算通水量。說明真實河道為何可能改以水位上升回應，並列出判斷所需的邊界條件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase roughness by one quarter at fixed geometry and energy slope and recompute discharge. Explain why a real river may instead respond through rising stage, identifying boundary conditions needed to distinguish these responses.","failure":"注意干擾：用低水位校準的粗糙係數外推洪水，可能誤估植生淹沒後阻力或洪氾通道。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Roughness calibrated at low flow can misrepresent submerged vegetation and floodplain pathways during floods. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對數個流量實測水位與速度，先驗證斷面幾何，再比較推算係數是否隨水深系統性改變。分別調查有葉與落葉狀態，若主槽和洪氾地速度差很大，應分區估算並考慮側向交換。","textEn":"Measure levels and velocities at several discharges, verify geometry first, and check systematic depth dependence in inferred roughness. Survey leafy and leafless conditions separately. Strong main-channel and floodplain velocity contrasts call for divided treatment and attention to lateral exchange.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將粗糙係數增加四分之一並保持幾何與能坡不變，重算通水量。說明真實河道為何可能改以水位上升回應，並列出判斷所需的邊界條件。","textEn":"Increase roughness by one quarter at fixed geometry and energy slope and recompute discharge. Explain why a real river may instead respond through rising stage, identifying boundary conditions needed to distinguish these responses.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「粗糙度與通水尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Roughness and conveyance scale\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","兩期地形圖任何非零差值都代表真實河床變化","對數個流量實測水位與速度，先驗證斷面幾何，再比較推算係數是否隨水深系統性改變。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Every nonzero difference between two terrain surveys represents real bed change","Measure levels and velocities at several discharges, verify geometry first, and check systematic depth dependence in inferred roughness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對數個流量實測水位與速度，先驗證斷面幾何，再比較推算係數是否隨水深系統性改變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure levels and velocities at several discharges, verify geometry first, and check systematic depth dependence in inferred roughness. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b279-v15-12","title":"粗糙度與通水尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Roughness and conveyance scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「粗糙度與通水尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Roughness and conveyance scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用低水位校準的粗糙係數外推洪水，可能誤估植生淹沒後阻力或洪氾通道。若模擬僅在某一水深吻合，應查機制而非宣稱全流量範圍已驗證。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Roughness calibrated at low flow can misrepresent submerged vegetation and floodplain pathways during floods. Agreement at one depth does not validate the full discharge range; investigate the changing resistance mechanism before extrapolation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：計算應保留面積、水力半徑與能坡各自來源，不可用調整係數掩蓋幾何或邊界條件的錯誤。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Keep the origins of area, hydraulic radius and energy slope explicit instead of tuning roughness to conceal errors in geometry or boundary conditions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「曼寧粗糙係數只由材料決定且永遠不隨水深改變」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Manning roughness depends only on material and never changes with water depth\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用低水位校準的粗糙係數外推洪水，可能誤估植生淹沒後阻力或洪氾通道。若模擬僅在某一水深吻合，應查機制而非宣稱全流量範圍已驗證。","textEn":"Roughness calibrated at low flow can misrepresent submerged vegetation and floodplain pathways during floods. Agreement at one depth does not validate the full discharge range; investigate the changing resistance mechanism before extrapolation.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「粗糙度與通水尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Roughness and conveyance scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用低水位校準的粗糙係數外推洪水，可能誤估植生淹沒後阻力或洪氾通道。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","幾何蓄水容量直接等於河川洪峰流量減少量"],"optionsEn":["Roughness calibrated at low flow can misrepresent submerged vegetation and floodplain pathways during floods.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Geometric storage volume directly equals the reduction in river peak discharge"],"answer":0,"explanation":"用低水位校準的粗糙係數外推洪水，可能誤估植生淹沒後阻力或洪氾通道。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Roughness calibrated at low flow can misrepresent submerged vegetation and floodplain pathways during floods. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b279-v15-13","title":"洪氾地的可用蓄水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Available floodplain storage: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「洪氾地的可用蓄水」如何影響河川再蜿蜒工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Available floodplain storage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River remeandering works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"重新連接洪氾地可增加水體暫存空間，但蓄水量取決於地形、水位與進出水時間，而非整片土地面積。以平均淹水深乘面積只是給定水位下的幾何容量，若入口太窄或洪峰太短，空間可能來不及填滿。原本已積水的窪地還需扣除既有水量。削峰效果則取決於容量何時使用與何時退水，必須把容量和流量歷線一起分析，不能把立方公尺直接說成洪峰降低值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「洪氾地的可用蓄水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Reconnecting a floodplain creates potential temporary storage, but usable volume depends on topography, stage and exchange timing rather than land area alone. Area times mean depth gives geometric capacity at a specified stage; a narrow entrance or brief peak may prevent filling. Existing ponded water reduces available capacity. Peak attenuation also depends on filling and drainage timing, so evaluate storage alongside hydrographs instead of treating a volume as if it were a discharge reduction. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Available floodplain storage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：A=60000 m2; d=0.35 m; V=A*d=21000 m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: A=60000 m2; d=0.35 m; V=A*d=21000 m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「幾何蓄水容量直接等於河川洪峰流量減少量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Geometric storage volume directly equals the reduction in river peak discharge\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「洪氾地的可用蓄水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Available floodplain storage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-13-k1","title":"洪氾地的可用蓄水","titleEn":"Available floodplain storage","text":"重新連接洪氾地可增加水體暫存空間，但蓄水量取決於地形、水位與進出水時間，而非整片土地面積。以平均淹水深乘面積只是給定水位下的幾何容量，若入口太窄或洪峰太短，空間可能來不及填滿。","textEn":"Reconnecting a floodplain creates potential temporary storage, but usable volume depends on topography, stage and exchange timing rather than land area alone. Area times mean depth gives geometric capacity at a specified stage; a narrow entrance or brief peak may prevent filling.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：幾何蓄水容量直接等於河川洪峰流量減少量 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Geometric storage volume directly equals the reduction in river peak discharge Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「洪氾地的可用蓄水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Available floodplain storage\" is correct?","options":["幾何蓄水容量直接等於河川洪峰流量減少量","重新連接洪氾地可增加水體暫存空間，但蓄水量取決於地形、水位與進出水時間，而非整片土地面積。","橫向水面差很小就能證明外彎岸坡不會沖刷"],"optionsEn":["Geometric storage volume directly equals the reduction in river peak discharge","Reconnecting a floodplain creates potential temporary storage, but usable volume depends on topography, stage and exchange timing rather than land area alone.","A small transverse water-level difference proves that the outer bank will not erode"],"answer":1,"explanation":"重新連接洪氾地可增加水體暫存空間，但蓄水量取決於地形、水位與進出水時間，而非整片土地面積。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Reconnecting a floodplain creates potential temporary storage, but usable volume depends on topography, stage and exchange timing rather than land area alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b279-v15-14","title":"洪氾地的可用蓄水：定量估算","titleEn":"Available floodplain storage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「洪氾地的可用蓄水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Available floodplain storage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：A=60000 m2; d=0.35 m; V=A*d=21000 m3。適用邊界：指定水位下新增平均水深且無既存積水，不推算洪峰削減。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: A=60000 m2; d=0.35 m; V=A*d=21000 m3. Applicable boundary: Added mean depth at a specified stage with no pre-existing water; peak reduction is not inferred. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以地形模型建立水位容量關係，現場核對低窪與阻水土堤。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Develop a stage-storage relation from terrain and verify depressions and embankments.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：A=60000 m2; d=0.35 m; V=A*d=21000 m3。適用邊界：指定水位下新增平均水深且無既存積水，不推算洪峰削減。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: A=60000 m2; d=0.35 m; V=A*d=21000 m3. Applicable boundary: Added mean depth at a specified stage with no pre-existing water; peak reduction is not inferred.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「洪氾地的可用蓄水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Available floodplain storage\", which statement holds?","options":["側汊總流入體積就是側汊最後增加的淨蓄水體積","水粒子旅行時間一定等於洪水峰值傳到下游的時間","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：A=60000 m2; d=0.35 m; V=A*d=21000 m3。"],"optionsEn":["Total side-channel inflow equals its final increase in net stored volume","Water-parcel travel time always equals the time for a flood peak to reach downstream","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: A=60000 m2; d=0.35 m; V=A*d=21000 m3."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：A=60000 m2; d=0.35 m; V=A*d=21000 m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: A=60000 m2; d=0.35 m; V=A*d=21000 m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b279-v15-15","title":"洪氾地的可用蓄水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Available floodplain storage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「洪氾地的可用蓄水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Available floodplain storage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以地形模型建立水位容量關係，現場核對低窪與阻水土堤。洪水時同步量入口、出口流量及洪氾水位，檢查容量是否真正利用，並比較退水時序，避免只用最高水痕估算整段防洪作用。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Develop a stage-storage relation from terrain and verify depressions and embankments. During events, synchronize inlet and outlet flows with floodplain levels to determine actual use and drainage timing, rather than inferring flood protection solely from the highest water mark. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：假設事件前已有十公分積水，重算剩餘容量。畫出提早及延後填水兩種歷線，說明即使使用相同體積，對下游洪峰仍可能產生不同影響。","observationEn":"Site practice: Assume ten centimetres of water is already present and recalculate remaining capacity. Draw early and late filling hydrographs and explain why equal stored volumes can have different effects on the downstream peak.","failure":"注意干擾：洪氾入口堵塞可能使圖上容量無法使用，出口過快又可能把水送回洪峰。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A blocked entrance can make mapped storage inaccessible, while rapid drainage can return water during the peak. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以地形模型建立水位容量關係，現場核對低窪與阻水土堤。洪水時同步量入口、出口流量及洪氾水位，檢查容量是否真正利用，並比較退水時序，避免只用最高水痕估算整段防洪作用。","textEn":"Develop a stage-storage relation from terrain and verify depressions and embankments. During events, synchronize inlet and outlet flows with floodplain levels to determine actual use and drainage timing, rather than inferring flood protection solely from the highest water mark.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"假設事件前已有十公分積水，重算剩餘容量。畫出提早及延後填水兩種歷線，說明即使使用相同體積，對下游洪峰仍可能產生不同影響。","textEn":"Assume ten centimetres of water is already present and recalculate remaining capacity. Draw early and late filling hydrographs and explain why equal stored volumes can have different effects on the downstream peak.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「洪氾地的可用蓄水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Available floodplain storage\"?","options":["以地形模型建立水位容量關係，現場核對低窪與阻水土堤。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","蜿蜒度較大必然代表所有生態功能與防洪能力較好"],"optionsEn":["Develop a stage-storage relation from terrain and verify depressions and embankments.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Greater sinuosity necessarily means better ecological function and flood protection in every respect"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以地形模型建立水位容量關係，現場核對低窪與阻水土堤。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Develop a stage-storage relation from terrain and verify depressions and embankments. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b279-v15-16","title":"洪氾地的可用蓄水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Available floodplain storage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「洪氾地的可用蓄水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Available floodplain storage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"洪氾入口堵塞可能使圖上容量無法使用，出口過快又可能把水送回洪峰。應檢查連通與時間，而非只增加名義土地面積。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A blocked entrance can make mapped storage inaccessible, while rapid drainage can return water during the peak. Investigate connectivity and timing rather than assuming more nominal floodplain area will necessarily improve attenuation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：削峰效果則取決於容量何時使用與何時退水，必須把容量和流量歷線一起分析，不能把立方公尺直接說成洪峰降低值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Peak attenuation also depends on filling and drainage timing, so evaluate storage alongside hydrographs instead of treating a volume as if it were a discharge reduction.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「幾何蓄水容量直接等於河川洪峰流量減少量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Geometric storage volume directly equals the reduction in river peak discharge\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"洪氾入口堵塞可能使圖上容量無法使用，出口過快又可能把水送回洪峰。應檢查連通與時間，而非只增加名義土地面積。","textEn":"A blocked entrance can make mapped storage inaccessible, while rapid drainage can return water during the peak. Investigate connectivity and timing rather than assuming more nominal floodplain area will necessarily improve attenuation.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「洪氾地的可用蓄水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Available floodplain storage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","洪氾入口堵塞可能使圖上容量無法使用，出口過快又可能把水送回洪峰。","橫向水面差很小就能證明外彎岸坡不會沖刷"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A blocked entrance can make mapped storage inaccessible, while rapid drainage can return water during the peak.","A small transverse water-level difference proves that the outer bank will not erode"],"answer":1,"explanation":"洪氾入口堵塞可能使圖上容量無法使用，出口過快又可能把水送回洪峰。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A blocked entrance can make mapped storage inaccessible, while rapid drainage can return water during the peak. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b279-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「彎道橫向水面差」與「岸線遷移與土方體積」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Transverse water level in bends\" and \"Bank migration and eroded volume\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b279-v15-17","title":"彎道橫向水面差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Transverse water level in bends: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「彎道橫向水面差」如何影響河川再蜿蜒工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Transverse water level in bends” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River remeandering works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水流轉彎需要向心加速度，橫向水面坡度可提供相應壓力差，因此外彎水面可能較高。簡化關係以平均速度、河寬和曲率半徑建立尺度，但真實彎道還有二次流、深槽及垂直速度分布。外彎侵蝕並不只由水面高差決定，近床流向與土體條件同樣重要。再蜿蜒設計應把曲率、岸趾及洪氾邊界一起檢查，避免把平面美觀的急彎當成自然穩定形狀。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「彎道橫向水面差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Turning flow requires centripetal acceleration, which a transverse water-surface gradient can help supply, producing higher levels near the outer bend. A simplified relation uses mean velocity, width and curvature radius, while real bends include secondary circulation, thalweg variation and vertical velocity structure. Outer-bank erosion is not determined by surface difference alone; near-bed currents and soil matter. Examine curvature, toe conditions and floodplain boundaries together rather than assuming an attractive planform is naturally stable. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Transverse water level in bends” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：v=1.5 m/s; B=12 m; g=9.81 m/s2; R=60 m; dh=v^2*B/(g*R)=0.045872 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: v=1.5 m/s; B=12 m; g=9.81 m/s2; R=60 m; dh=v^2*B/(g*R)=0.045872 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「橫向水面差很小就能證明外彎岸坡不會沖刷」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small transverse water-level difference proves that the outer bank will not erode\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「彎道橫向水面差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Transverse water level in bends”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-17-k1","title":"彎道橫向水面差","titleEn":"Transverse water level in bends","text":"水流轉彎需要向心加速度，橫向水面坡度可提供相應壓力差，因此外彎水面可能較高。簡化關係以平均速度、河寬和曲率半徑建立尺度，但真實彎道還有二次流、深槽及垂直速度分布。","textEn":"Turning flow requires centripetal acceleration, which a transverse water-surface gradient can help supply, producing higher levels near the outer bend. A simplified relation uses mean velocity, width and curvature radius, while real bends include secondary circulation, thalweg variation and vertical velocity structure.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：橫向水面差很小就能證明外彎岸坡不會沖刷 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small transverse water-level difference proves that the outer bank will not erode Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「彎道橫向水面差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Transverse water level in bends\" is correct?","options":["橫向水面差很小就能證明外彎岸坡不會沖刷","岸坡流失的原位體積必然在同一時刻全部通過下游斷面","水流轉彎需要向心加速度，橫向水面坡度可提供相應壓力差，因此外彎水面可能較高。"],"optionsEn":["A small transverse water-level difference proves that the outer bank will not erode","All in-place bank erosion volume necessarily passes the downstream section at the same moment","Turning flow requires centripetal acceleration, which a transverse water-surface gradient can help supply, producing higher levels near the outer bend."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水流轉彎需要向心加速度，橫向水面坡度可提供相應壓力差，因此外彎水面可能較高。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Turning flow requires centripetal acceleration, which a transverse water-surface gradient can help supply, producing higher levels near the outer bend. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b279-v15-18","title":"彎道橫向水面差：定量估算","titleEn":"Transverse water level in bends: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「彎道橫向水面差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Transverse water level in bends” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：v=1.5 m/s; B=12 m; g=9.81 m/s2; R=60 m; dh=v^2*B/(g*R)=0.045872 m。適用邊界：小寬徑比與代表平均速度的尺度估算，未解析二次流。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: v=1.5 m/s; B=12 m; g=9.81 m/s2; R=60 m; dh=v^2*B/(g*R)=0.045872 m. Applicable boundary: Scale estimate using modest width-to-radius ratio and representative mean velocity, without resolving secondary circulation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在同一斷面同步量內外彎水位，並取得垂向與橫向流速資料。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure inner and outer levels simultaneously and obtain vertical and transverse velocity data.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：v=1.5 m/s; B=12 m; g=9.81 m/s2; R=60 m; dh=v^2*B/(g*R)=0.045872 m。適用邊界：小寬徑比與代表平均速度的尺度估算，未解析二次流。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: v=1.5 m/s; B=12 m; g=9.81 m/s2; R=60 m; dh=v^2*B/(g*R)=0.045872 m. Applicable boundary: Scale estimate using modest width-to-radius ratio and representative mean velocity, without resolving secondary circulation.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「彎道橫向水面差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Transverse water level in bends\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：v=1.5 m/s; B=12 m; g=9.81 m/s2; R=60 m; dh=v^2*B/(g*R)=0.045872 m。","達西通量就是孔隙中每個水粒子的實際移動速度","兩期地形圖任何非零差值都代表真實河床變化"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: v=1.5 m/s; B=12 m; g=9.81 m/s2; R=60 m; dh=v^2*B/(g*R)=0.045872 m.","Darcy flux is the actual speed of every water particle inside the pores","Every nonzero difference between two terrain surveys represents real bed change"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：v=1.5 m/s; B=12 m; g=9.81 m/s2; R=60 m; dh=v^2*B/(g*R)=0.045872 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: v=1.5 m/s; B=12 m; g=9.81 m/s2; R=60 m; dh=v^2*B/(g*R)=0.045872 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b279-v15-19","title":"彎道橫向水面差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Transverse water level in bends: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「彎道橫向水面差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Transverse water level in bends” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在同一斷面同步量內外彎水位，並取得垂向與橫向流速資料。量測曲率時保持中心線定義一致，若水面差與簡式偏離，先查回水、非均勻速度及幾何急變，不把偏差全歸為測量誤差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure inner and outer levels simultaneously and obtain vertical and transverse velocity data. Use a consistent centreline for curvature. Differences from the simple estimate require checking backwater, nonuniform velocity and abrupt geometry before attributing everything to survey error. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將曲率半徑縮小一半而速度與河寬固定，重算水面差。畫出可能的二次流方向並說明簡式沒有提供哪些近床資訊，安排相應測速位置。","observationEn":"Site practice: Halve curvature radius at fixed speed and width and recalculate level difference. Sketch possible secondary circulation, identify near-bed information missing from the formula, and place velocity measurements to investigate those processes.","failure":"注意干擾：急彎可能把主流壓向尚未穩定的外岸，造成局部淘空和岸塊崩落。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A tight bend can direct the main current toward an unestablished outer bank, causing undermining and block failure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在同一斷面同步量內外彎水位，並取得垂向與橫向流速資料。量測曲率時保持中心線定義一致，若水面差與簡式偏離，先查回水、非均勻速度及幾何急變，不把偏差全歸為測量誤差。","textEn":"Measure inner and outer levels simultaneously and obtain vertical and transverse velocity data. Use a consistent centreline for curvature. Differences from the simple estimate require checking backwater, nonuniform velocity and abrupt geometry before attributing everything to survey error.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將曲率半徑縮小一半而速度與河寬固定，重算水面差。畫出可能的二次流方向並說明簡式沒有提供哪些近床資訊，安排相應測速位置。","textEn":"Halve curvature radius at fixed speed and width and recalculate level difference. Sketch possible secondary circulation, identify near-bed information missing from the formula, and place velocity measurements to investigate those processes.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「彎道橫向水面差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Transverse water level in bends\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在同一斷面同步量內外彎水位，並取得垂向與橫向流速資料。","河道平均床坡就是所有流量下每一斷面的能量坡度"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure inner and outer levels simultaneously and obtain vertical and transverse velocity data.","Mean bed slope equals the energy slope at every section and discharge"],"answer":1,"explanation":"在同一斷面同步量內外彎水位，並取得垂向與橫向流速資料。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure inner and outer levels simultaneously and obtain vertical and transverse velocity data. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b279-v15-20","title":"彎道橫向水面差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Transverse water level in bends: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「彎道橫向水面差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Transverse water level in bends” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"急彎可能把主流壓向尚未穩定的外岸，造成局部淘空和岸塊崩落。即使橫向水面差不大，也不能排除近床高速或土體弱面。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A tight bend can direct the main current toward an unestablished outer bank, causing undermining and block failure. Modest surface difference does not rule out fast near-bed flow or weak soil layers. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：再蜿蜒設計應把曲率、岸趾及洪氾邊界一起檢查，避免把平面美觀的急彎當成自然穩定形狀。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Examine curvature, toe conditions and floodplain boundaries together rather than assuming an attractive planform is naturally stable.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「橫向水面差很小就能證明外彎岸坡不會沖刷」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small transverse water-level difference proves that the outer bank will not erode\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"急彎可能把主流壓向尚未穩定的外岸，造成局部淘空和岸塊崩落。即使橫向水面差不大，也不能排除近床高速或土體弱面。","textEn":"A tight bend can direct the main current toward an unestablished outer bank, causing undermining and block failure. Modest surface difference does not rule out fast near-bed flow or weak soil layers.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「彎道橫向水面差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Transverse water level in bends\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","岸坡流失的原位體積必然在同一時刻全部通過下游斷面","急彎可能把主流壓向尚未穩定的外岸，造成局部淘空和岸塊崩落。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","All in-place bank erosion volume necessarily passes the downstream section at the same moment","A tight bend can direct the main current toward an unestablished outer bank, causing undermining and block failure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"急彎可能把主流壓向尚未穩定的外岸，造成局部淘空和岸塊崩落。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A tight bend can direct the main current toward an unestablished outer bank, causing undermining and block failure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b279-v15-21","title":"岸線遷移與土方體積：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bank migration and eroded volume: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「岸線遷移與土方體積」如何影響河川再蜿蜒工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bank migration and eroded volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River remeandering works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"允許河道在限定走廊內遷移，可以提供沉積物和新生棲地，但也需要清楚界定土地、設施與管理邊界。岸線後退距離乘長度與平均高度，可初估流失土體的原位體積，並非全部會立即成為下游懸浮泥砂。崩落土塊可能暫存岸趾、再被洪水分次帶走，細粗料行為也不同。監測應區分平面遷移、體積侵蝕與輸出通量，避免把三個量互相代替。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「岸線遷移與土方體積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Allowing migration within a defined corridor can create habitat and supply sediment, but land, infrastructure and management boundaries must be explicit. Retreat distance times bank length and mean height estimates in-place eroded volume, not sediment immediately exported downstream. Failed blocks may remain at the toe and be removed during later floods, with fines and coarse material behaving differently. Monitor planform movement, volumetric erosion and exported flux separately rather than substituting one quantity for another. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bank migration and eroded volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L=240 m; r=2.5 m; H=1.8 m; Ve=L*r*H=1080 m3 in-place。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L=240 m; r=2.5 m; H=1.8 m; Ve=L*r*H=1080 m3 in-place.","failure":"常見誤解：「岸坡流失的原位體積必然在同一時刻全部通過下游斷面」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All in-place bank erosion volume necessarily passes the downstream section at the same moment\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「岸線遷移與土方體積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bank migration and eroded volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-21-k1","title":"岸線遷移與土方體積","titleEn":"Bank migration and eroded volume","text":"允許河道在限定走廊內遷移，可以提供沉積物和新生棲地，但也需要清楚界定土地、設施與管理邊界。岸線後退距離乘長度與平均高度，可初估流失土體的原位體積，並非全部會立即成為下游懸浮泥砂。","textEn":"Allowing migration within a defined corridor can create habitat and supply sediment, but land, infrastructure and management boundaries must be explicit. Retreat distance times bank length and mean height estimates in-place eroded volume, not sediment immediately exported downstream.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：岸坡流失的原位體積必然在同一時刻全部通過下游斷面 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All in-place bank erosion volume necessarily passes the downstream section at the same moment Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「岸線遷移與土方體積」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bank migration and eroded volume\" is correct?","options":["允許河道在限定走廊內遷移，可以提供沉積物和新生棲地，但也需要清楚界定土地、設施與管理邊界。","岸坡流失的原位體積必然在同一時刻全部通過下游斷面","側汊總流入體積就是側汊最後增加的淨蓄水體積"],"optionsEn":["Allowing migration within a defined corridor can create habitat and supply sediment, but land, infrastructure and management boundaries must be explicit.","All in-place bank erosion volume necessarily passes the downstream section at the same moment","Total side-channel inflow equals its final increase in net stored volume"],"answer":0,"explanation":"允許河道在限定走廊內遷移，可以提供沉積物和新生棲地，但也需要清楚界定土地、設施與管理邊界。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Allowing migration within a defined corridor can create habitat and supply sediment, but land, infrastructure and management boundaries must be explicit. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b279-v15-22","title":"岸線遷移與土方體積：定量估算","titleEn":"Bank migration and eroded volume: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「岸線遷移與土方體積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bank migration and eroded volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L=240 m; r=2.5 m; H=1.8 m; Ve=L*r*H=1080 m3 in-place。適用邊界：均勻矩形岸塊幾何估算，未轉成固體質量或下游輸砂量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L=240 m; r=2.5 m; H=1.8 m; Ve=L*r*H=1080 m3 in-place. Applicable boundary: Uniform rectangular bank-block estimate, not converted to solid mass or downstream sediment export. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用相同高程與平面基準比較岸頂、岸趾及水下地形，量崩落塊體是否仍留在控制體內。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare bank crest, toe and submerged terrain on common datums and measure failed blocks remaining inside the control volume.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L=240 m; r=2.5 m; H=1.8 m; Ve=L*r*H=1080 m3 in-place。適用邊界：均勻矩形岸塊幾何估算，未轉成固體質量或下游輸砂量。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L=240 m; r=2.5 m; H=1.8 m; Ve=L*r*H=1080 m3 in-place. Applicable boundary: Uniform rectangular bank-block estimate, not converted to solid mass or downstream sediment export.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「岸線遷移與土方體積」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bank migration and eroded volume\", which statement holds?","options":["水粒子旅行時間一定等於洪水峰值傳到下游的時間","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L=240 m; r=2.5 m; H=1.8 m; Ve=L*r*H=1080 m3 in-place。","蜿蜒度較大必然代表所有生態功能與防洪能力較好"],"optionsEn":["Water-parcel travel time always equals the time for a flood peak to reach downstream","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L=240 m; r=2.5 m; H=1.8 m; Ve=L*r*H=1080 m3 in-place.","Greater sinuosity necessarily means better ecological function and flood protection in every respect"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L=240 m; r=2.5 m; H=1.8 m; Ve=L*r*H=1080 m3 in-place。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L=240 m; r=2.5 m; H=1.8 m; Ve=L*r*H=1080 m3 in-place. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b279-v15-23","title":"岸線遷移與土方體積：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bank migration and eroded volume: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「岸線遷移與土方體積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bank migration and eroded volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用相同高程與平面基準比較岸頂、岸趾及水下地形，量崩落塊體是否仍留在控制體內。若需換算質量，另採原位密度與含水資料；再用下游採樣判斷何時輸出，避免把體積直接當通量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare bank crest, toe and submerged terrain on common datums and measure failed blocks remaining inside the control volume. Mass conversion needs density and moisture data; downstream sampling identifies export timing instead of treating volume as a transport rate. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將平均岸高增加三分之一重算體積，再假設一半崩塊暫留岸趾，列出剩餘輸出上限與所需證據。說明為何這仍不是完整輸砂歷線。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase mean bank height by one third and recalculate volume. Assume half remains at the toe, describe the remaining export bound and required evidence, and explain why this still does not provide a transport hydrograph.","failure":"注意干擾：僅用岸頂退縮會漏掉水下掏空，也可能把斜坡整形當成天然侵蝕。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Crest retreat alone can miss underwater undercutting or confuse grading with natural erosion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用相同高程與平面基準比較岸頂、岸趾及水下地形，量崩落塊體是否仍留在控制體內。若需換算質量，另採原位密度與含水資料；再用下游採樣判斷何時輸出，避免把體積直接當通量。","textEn":"Compare bank crest, toe and submerged terrain on common datums and measure failed blocks remaining inside the control volume. Mass conversion needs density and moisture data; downstream sampling identifies export timing instead of treating volume as a transport rate.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將平均岸高增加三分之一重算體積，再假設一半崩塊暫留岸趾，列出剩餘輸出上限與所需證據。說明為何這仍不是完整輸砂歷線。","textEn":"Increase mean bank height by one third and recalculate volume. Assume half remains at the toe, describe the remaining export bound and required evidence, and explain why this still does not provide a transport hydrograph.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「岸線遷移與土方體積」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bank migration and eroded volume\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","曼寧粗糙係數只由材料決定且永遠不隨水深改變","用相同高程與平面基準比較岸頂、岸趾及水下地形，量崩落塊體是否仍留在控制體內。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Manning roughness depends only on material and never changes with water depth","Compare bank crest, toe and submerged terrain on common datums and measure failed blocks remaining inside the control volume."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用相同高程與平面基準比較岸頂、岸趾及水下地形，量崩落塊體是否仍留在控制體內。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare bank crest, toe and submerged terrain on common datums and measure failed blocks remaining inside the control volume. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b279-v15-24","title":"岸線遷移與土方體積：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bank migration and eroded volume: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「岸線遷移與土方體積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bank migration and eroded volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"僅用岸頂退縮會漏掉水下掏空，也可能把斜坡整形當成天然侵蝕。若忽略暫存崩塊，下游輸砂模型會過早加入全部土方而誇大峰值。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Crest retreat alone can miss underwater undercutting or confuse grading with natural erosion. Ignoring stored blocks also injects all eroded material into a transport model too early and exaggerates downstream sediment peaks. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：監測應區分平面遷移、體積侵蝕與輸出通量，避免把三個量互相代替。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Monitor planform movement, volumetric erosion and exported flux separately rather than substituting one quantity for another.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「岸坡流失的原位體積必然在同一時刻全部通過下游斷面」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All in-place bank erosion volume necessarily passes the downstream section at the same moment\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"僅用岸頂退縮會漏掉水下掏空，也可能把斜坡整形當成天然侵蝕。若忽略暫存崩塊，下游輸砂模型會過早加入全部土方而誇大峰值。","textEn":"Crest retreat alone can miss underwater undercutting or confuse grading with natural erosion. Ignoring stored blocks also injects all eroded material into a transport model too early and exaggerates downstream sediment peaks.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「岸線遷移與土方體積」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bank migration and eroded volume\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["僅用岸頂退縮會漏掉水下掏空，也可能把斜坡整形當成天然侵蝕。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","側汊總流入體積就是側汊最後增加的淨蓄水體積"],"optionsEn":["Crest retreat alone can miss underwater undercutting or confuse grading with natural erosion.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Total side-channel inflow equals its final increase in net stored volume"],"answer":0,"explanation":"僅用岸頂退縮會漏掉水下掏空，也可能把斜坡整形當成天然侵蝕。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Crest retreat alone can miss underwater undercutting or confuse grading with natural erosion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b279-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「側汊連通的交換水量」與「河岸地下水交換」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Exchange volume through a side channel\" and \"Groundwater exchange across banks\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b279-v15-25","title":"側汊連通的交換水量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Exchange volume through a side channel: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「側汊連通的交換水量」如何影響河川再蜿蜒工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Exchange volume through a side channel” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River remeandering works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"再連接側汊可改變主槽與洪氾地的水量、泥砂和生物交換，但流向可能隨主河水位升降而反轉。流量乘時間只適用於已知定常流段，變動事件需要逐時積分並保留正負號。流入量不等同淨蓄水，若另一出口同時排出，水體只是通過。設計應把入口、出口與內部水位畫成控制體，並關注過低水位時是否形成孤立水塘或阻斷生物退路。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「側汊連通的交換水量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Reconnecting a side channel changes water, sediment and biological exchange with the main river, but direction can reverse as river stage rises and falls. Discharge times duration applies to a known steady interval; variable events require signed integration. Inflow is not net storage when another outlet simultaneously drains the area. Draw inlet, outlet and internal water levels as a control volume and examine whether low stages isolate pools or interrupt return routes for organisms. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Exchange volume through a side channel” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Q=0.8 m3/s into-side-channel; dt=7200 s; Vin=Q*dt=5760 m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Q=0.8 m3/s into-side-channel; dt=7200 s; Vin=Q*dt=5760 m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「側汊總流入體積就是側汊最後增加的淨蓄水體積」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Total side-channel inflow equals its final increase in net stored volume\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「側汊連通的交換水量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Exchange volume through a side channel”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-25-k1","title":"側汊連通的交換水量","titleEn":"Exchange volume through a side channel","text":"再連接側汊可改變主槽與洪氾地的水量、泥砂和生物交換，但流向可能隨主河水位升降而反轉。流量乘時間只適用於已知定常流段，變動事件需要逐時積分並保留正負號。","textEn":"Reconnecting a side channel changes water, sediment and biological exchange with the main river, but direction can reverse as river stage rises and falls. Discharge times duration applies to a known steady interval; variable events require signed integration.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：側汊總流入體積就是側汊最後增加的淨蓄水體積 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Total side-channel inflow equals its final increase in net stored volume Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「側汊連通的交換水量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Exchange volume through a side channel\" is correct?","options":["側汊總流入體積就是側汊最後增加的淨蓄水體積","再連接側汊可改變主槽與洪氾地的水量、泥砂和生物交換，但流向可能隨主河水位升降而反轉。","達西通量就是孔隙中每個水粒子的實際移動速度"],"optionsEn":["Total side-channel inflow equals its final increase in net stored volume","Reconnecting a side channel changes water, sediment and biological exchange with the main river, but direction can reverse as river stage rises and falls.","Darcy flux is the actual speed of every water particle inside the pores"],"answer":1,"explanation":"再連接側汊可改變主槽與洪氾地的水量、泥砂和生物交換，但流向可能隨主河水位升降而反轉。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Reconnecting a side channel changes water, sediment and biological exchange with the main river, but direction can reverse as river stage rises and falls. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b279-v15-26","title":"側汊連通的交換水量：定量估算","titleEn":"Exchange volume through a side channel: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「側汊連通的交換水量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Exchange volume through a side channel” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Q=0.8 m3/s into-side-channel; dt=7200 s; Vin=Q*dt=5760 m3。適用邊界：定常向內流量之總流入體積，不等於淨蓄水或削峰量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Q=0.8 m3/s into-side-channel; dt=7200 s; Vin=Q*dt=5760 m3. Applicable boundary: Gross inflow volume during steady inward flow, not net storage or peak attenuation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量側汊入口及出口的水位與流量，採可辨方向的儀器並統一正號。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure inlet and outlet levels and signed flows simultaneously.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Q=0.8 m3/s into-side-channel; dt=7200 s; Vin=Q*dt=5760 m3。適用邊界：定常向內流量之總流入體積，不等於淨蓄水或削峰量。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Q=0.8 m3/s into-side-channel; dt=7200 s; Vin=Q*dt=5760 m3. Applicable boundary: Gross inflow volume during steady inward flow, not net storage or peak attenuation.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「側汊連通的交換水量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Exchange volume through a side channel\", which statement holds?","options":["兩期地形圖任何非零差值都代表真實河床變化","河道平均床坡就是所有流量下每一斷面的能量坡度","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Q=0.8 m3/s into-side-channel; dt=7200 s; Vin=Q*dt=5760 m3。"],"optionsEn":["Every nonzero difference between two terrain surveys represents real bed change","Mean bed slope equals the energy slope at every section and discharge","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Q=0.8 m3/s into-side-channel; dt=7200 s; Vin=Q*dt=5760 m3."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Q=0.8 m3/s into-side-channel; dt=7200 s; Vin=Q*dt=5760 m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Q=0.8 m3/s into-side-channel; dt=7200 s; Vin=Q*dt=5760 m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b279-v15-27","title":"側汊連通的交換水量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Exchange volume through a side channel: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「側汊連通的交換水量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Exchange volume through a side channel” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量側汊入口及出口的水位與流量，採可辨方向的儀器並統一正號。將流量積分與水位容量變化比較，檢查地下滲漏或未量支路；退水期另追蹤斷流位置，確認連通性不是只有洪峰時存在。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure inlet and outlet levels and signed flows simultaneously. Compare integrated exchange with stage-storage change and investigate seepage or unmeasured branches. During recession, track where flow disconnects so connectivity is not assessed solely at the flood peak. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：加入每秒零點三立方公尺的同時出流，重算兩小時淨蓄水。再畫流向反轉的退水階段，指出積分正負號與生物退路各需如何檢查。","observationEn":"Site practice: Add simultaneous outflow of zero point three cubic metres per second and compute net storage over two hours. Sketch reversal during recession and explain checks for both integration signs and organism return routes.","failure":"注意干擾：出口未量而只記入口流量，會高估側汊蓄水效益；退水時若形成孤立池，還可能把先前進入的生物困住。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Recording only inlet flow exaggerates storage when an unmeasured outlet is active. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量側汊入口及出口的水位與流量，採可辨方向的儀器並統一正號。將流量積分與水位容量變化比較，檢查地下滲漏或未量支路；退水期另追蹤斷流位置，確認連通性不是只有洪峰時存在。","textEn":"Measure inlet and outlet levels and signed flows simultaneously. Compare integrated exchange with stage-storage change and investigate seepage or unmeasured branches. During recession, track where flow disconnects so connectivity is not assessed solely at the flood peak.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"加入每秒零點三立方公尺的同時出流，重算兩小時淨蓄水。再畫流向反轉的退水階段，指出積分正負號與生物退路各需如何檢查。","textEn":"Add simultaneous outflow of zero point three cubic metres per second and compute net storage over two hours. Sketch reversal during recession and explain checks for both integration signs and organism return routes.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「側汊連通的交換水量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Exchange volume through a side channel\"?","options":["同步量側汊入口及出口的水位與流量，採可辨方向的儀器並統一正號。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","幾何蓄水容量直接等於河川洪峰流量減少量"],"optionsEn":["Measure inlet and outlet levels and signed flows simultaneously.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Geometric storage volume directly equals the reduction in river peak discharge"],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步量側汊入口及出口的水位與流量，採可辨方向的儀器並統一正號。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure inlet and outlet levels and signed flows simultaneously. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b279-v15-28","title":"側汊連通的交換水量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Exchange volume through a side channel: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「側汊連通的交換水量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Exchange volume through a side channel” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"出口未量而只記入口流量，會高估側汊蓄水效益；退水時若形成孤立池，還可能把先前進入的生物困住。需連續追蹤整個水位循環。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Recording only inlet flow exaggerates storage when an unmeasured outlet is active. Disconnected recession pools can also trap organisms that entered earlier, requiring observation across the complete stage cycle rather than only rising water. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計應把入口、出口與內部水位畫成控制體，並關注過低水位時是否形成孤立水塘或阻斷生物退路。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Draw inlet, outlet and internal water levels as a control volume and examine whether low stages isolate pools or interrupt return routes for organisms.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「側汊總流入體積就是側汊最後增加的淨蓄水體積」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Total side-channel inflow equals its final increase in net stored volume\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"出口未量而只記入口流量，會高估側汊蓄水效益；退水時若形成孤立池，還可能把先前進入的生物困住。需連續追蹤整個水位循環。","textEn":"Recording only inlet flow exaggerates storage when an unmeasured outlet is active. Disconnected recession pools can also trap organisms that entered earlier, requiring observation across the complete stage cycle rather than only rising water.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「側汊連通的交換水量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Exchange volume through a side channel\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","出口未量而只記入口流量，會高估側汊蓄水效益；退水時若形成孤立池，還可能把先前進入的生物困住。","達西通量就是孔隙中每個水粒子的實際移動速度"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Recording only inlet flow exaggerates storage when an unmeasured outlet is active.","Darcy flux is the actual speed of every water particle inside the pores"],"answer":1,"explanation":"出口未量而只記入口流量，會高估側汊蓄水效益；退水時若形成孤立池，還可能把先前進入的生物困住。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Recording only inlet flow exaggerates storage when an unmeasured outlet is active. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b279-v15-29","title":"河岸地下水交換：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Groundwater exchange across banks: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「河岸地下水交換」如何影響河川再蜿蜒工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Groundwater exchange across banks” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River remeandering works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"河道復育改變水位與流路後，地下水可能向河道補注，也可能由河道暫時滲入岸土。達西式用水頭梯度與滲透係數估算體積通量，適用於已定義的飽和多孔介質控制面。孔隙中的平均實際流速還需要除有效孔隙率，不能把達西通量直接當成示蹤旅行速度。層狀沉積物可能有方向性，河床堵塞也會改變交換，所以監測須同時掌握水頭、介質與水質。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「河岸地下水交換」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Restoration can shift groundwater discharge to the river or drive temporary bank infiltration. Darcy's relation estimates volume flux from conductivity and head gradient across a defined saturated porous section. Average pore-water velocity additionally depends on effective porosity; Darcy flux is not directly tracer travel speed. Layering can create directional conductivity, and bed clogging can alter exchange. Monitor heads, sediment properties and water quality together to distinguish changes in hydraulic connection from changes in the source water. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Groundwater exchange across banks” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：K=0.00002 m/s; A=300 m2; dh=0.4 m; L=20 m; Q=K*A*dh/L=0.00012 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: K=0.00002 m/s; A=300 m2; dh=0.4 m; L=20 m; Q=K*A*dh/L=0.00012 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「達西通量就是孔隙中每個水粒子的實際移動速度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Darcy flux is the actual speed of every water particle inside the pores\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「河岸地下水交換」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Groundwater exchange across banks”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-29-k1","title":"河岸地下水交換","titleEn":"Groundwater exchange across banks","text":"河道復育改變水位與流路後，地下水可能向河道補注，也可能由河道暫時滲入岸土。達西式用水頭梯度與滲透係數估算體積通量，適用於已定義的飽和多孔介質控制面。","textEn":"Restoration can shift groundwater discharge to the river or drive temporary bank infiltration. Darcy's relation estimates volume flux from conductivity and head gradient across a defined saturated porous section.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：達西通量就是孔隙中每個水粒子的實際移動速度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Darcy flux is the actual speed of every water particle inside the pores Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「河岸地下水交換」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Groundwater exchange across banks\" is correct?","options":["達西通量就是孔隙中每個水粒子的實際移動速度","水粒子旅行時間一定等於洪水峰值傳到下游的時間","河道復育改變水位與流路後，地下水可能向河道補注，也可能由河道暫時滲入岸土。"],"optionsEn":["Darcy flux is the actual speed of every water particle inside the pores","Water-parcel travel time always equals the time for a flood peak to reach downstream","Restoration can shift groundwater discharge to the river or drive temporary bank infiltration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"河道復育改變水位與流路後，地下水可能向河道補注，也可能由河道暫時滲入岸土。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Restoration can shift groundwater discharge to the river or drive temporary bank infiltration. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b279-v15-30","title":"河岸地下水交換：定量估算","titleEn":"Groundwater exchange across banks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「河岸地下水交換」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Groundwater exchange across banks” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：K=0.00002 m/s; A=300 m2; dh=0.4 m; L=20 m; Q=K*A*dh/L=0.00012 m3/s。適用邊界：飽和均質一維定常達西流，水頭差方向已指定。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: K=0.00002 m/s; A=300 m2; dh=0.4 m; L=20 m; Q=K*A*dh/L=0.00012 m3/s. Applicable boundary: Saturated homogeneous one-dimensional steady Darcy flow with a specified head-gradient direction. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在河道與岸內井使用同一高程基準量水頭，透過適合土層的試驗估滲透係數。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure river and well heads on the same datum and estimate conductivity with tests appropriate to the strata.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：K=0.00002 m/s; A=300 m2; dh=0.4 m; L=20 m; Q=K*A*dh/L=0.00012 m3/s。適用邊界：飽和均質一維定常達西流，水頭差方向已指定。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: K=0.00002 m/s; A=300 m2; dh=0.4 m; L=20 m; Q=K*A*dh/L=0.00012 m3/s. Applicable boundary: Saturated homogeneous one-dimensional steady Darcy flow with a specified head-gradient direction.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「河岸地下水交換」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Groundwater exchange across banks\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：K=0.00002 m/s; A=300 m2; dh=0.4 m; L=20 m; Q=K*A*dh/L=0.00012 m3/s。","蜿蜒度較大必然代表所有生態功能與防洪能力較好","曼寧粗糙係數只由材料決定且永遠不隨水深改變"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: K=0.00002 m/s; A=300 m2; dh=0.4 m; L=20 m; Q=K*A*dh/L=0.00012 m3/s.","Greater sinuosity necessarily means better ecological function and flood protection in every respect","Manning roughness depends only on material and never changes with water depth"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：K=0.00002 m/s; A=300 m2; dh=0.4 m; L=20 m; Q=K*A*dh/L=0.00012 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: K=0.00002 m/s; A=300 m2; dh=0.4 m; L=20 m; Q=K*A*dh/L=0.00012 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b279-v15-31","title":"河岸地下水交換：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Groundwater exchange across banks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「河岸地下水交換」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Groundwater exchange across banks” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在河道與岸內井使用同一高程基準量水頭，透過適合土層的試驗估滲透係數。以溫度或保守示蹤資料比對交換方向，若水頭響應有明顯延遲，應加入儲水與非定常效應而非維持定常假設。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure river and well heads on the same datum and estimate conductivity with tests appropriate to the strata. Compare exchange direction using temperature or conservative tracers. Delayed head responses require storage and transient effects instead of retaining a steady-flow assumption. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將水頭差反向而大小不變，計算帶符號流量並畫交換方向。另指定有效孔隙率，說明由通量換算孔隙速度還需要哪個面積定義與流路假設。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reverse the head difference without changing magnitude and calculate signed discharge. Specify an effective porosity and explain the area definition and pathway assumptions needed to convert Darcy flux into average pore velocity.","failure":"注意干擾：以表層砂樣代表深部黏土夾層會高估交換量，堵塞層形成後原係數也可能失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using surface sand to represent a deeper clay layer exaggerates exchange, and new clogging can invalidate earlier conductivity estimates. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在河道與岸內井使用同一高程基準量水頭，透過適合土層的試驗估滲透係數。以溫度或保守示蹤資料比對交換方向，若水頭響應有明顯延遲，應加入儲水與非定常效應而非維持定常假設。","textEn":"Measure river and well heads on the same datum and estimate conductivity with tests appropriate to the strata. Compare exchange direction using temperature or conservative tracers. Delayed head responses require storage and transient effects instead of retaining a steady-flow assumption.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將水頭差反向而大小不變，計算帶符號流量並畫交換方向。另指定有效孔隙率，說明由通量換算孔隙速度還需要哪個面積定義與流路假設。","textEn":"Reverse the head difference without changing magnitude and calculate signed discharge. Specify an effective porosity and explain the area definition and pathway assumptions needed to convert Darcy flux into average pore velocity.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「河岸地下水交換」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Groundwater exchange across banks\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在河道與岸內井使用同一高程基準量水頭，透過適合土層的試驗估滲透係數。","橫向水面差很小就能證明外彎岸坡不會沖刷"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Measure river and well heads on the same datum and estimate conductivity with tests appropriate to the strata.","A small transverse water-level difference proves that the outer bank will not erode"],"answer":1,"explanation":"在河道與岸內井使用同一高程基準量水頭，透過適合土層的試驗估滲透係數。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure river and well heads on the same datum and estimate conductivity with tests appropriate to the strata. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b279-v15-32","title":"河岸地下水交換：失效診斷","titleEn":"Groundwater exchange across banks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「河岸地下水交換」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Groundwater exchange across banks” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以表層砂樣代表深部黏土夾層會高估交換量，堵塞層形成後原係數也可能失效。若模型流量大但示蹤反應弱，應查層理與有效連通面積。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using surface sand to represent a deeper clay layer exaggerates exchange, and new clogging can invalidate earlier conductivity estimates. Large modeled flux with weak tracer response warrants checking layering and the effectively connected area. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：層狀沉積物可能有方向性，河床堵塞也會改變交換，所以監測須同時掌握水頭、介質與水質。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Monitor heads, sediment properties and water quality together to distinguish changes in hydraulic connection from changes in the source water.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「達西通量就是孔隙中每個水粒子的實際移動速度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Darcy flux is the actual speed of every water particle inside the pores\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以表層砂樣代表深部黏土夾層會高估交換量，堵塞層形成後原係數也可能失效。若模型流量大但示蹤反應弱，應查層理與有效連通面積。","textEn":"Using surface sand to represent a deeper clay layer exaggerates exchange, and new clogging can invalidate earlier conductivity estimates. Large modeled flux with weak tracer response warrants checking layering and the effectively connected area.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「河岸地下水交換」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Groundwater exchange across banks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","水粒子旅行時間一定等於洪水峰值傳到下游的時間","以表層砂樣代表深部黏土夾層會高估交換量，堵塞層形成後原係數也可能失效。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Water-parcel travel time always equals the time for a flood peak to reach downstream","Using surface sand to represent a deeper clay layer exaggerates exchange, and new clogging can invalidate earlier conductivity estimates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以表層砂樣代表深部黏土夾層會高估交換量，堵塞層形成後原係數也可能失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using surface sand to represent a deeper clay layer exaggerates exchange, and new clogging can invalidate earlier conductivity estimates. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b279-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「水體平移與洪波傳播」與「地形差分的量測不確定性」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Water advection and flood-wave travel\" and \"Uncertainty in terrain differences\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b279-v15-33","title":"水體平移與洪波傳播：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Water advection and flood-wave travel: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「水體平移與洪波傳播」如何影響河川再蜿蜒工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Water advection and flood-wave travel” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River remeandering works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"河道延長可能增加水體沿流路的平移時間，但洪波傳播速度並不等於水粒子平均流速。以長度除速度得到的是固定速度的平流尺度，未計彌散、死水交換或水位波形變化。示蹤物可能早到也可能留下長尾，洪峰則受蓄水及邊界影響。評估復育的時間效益時，應分別量測示蹤突破、洪水歷線與局部流速，避免用水的旅行時間直接宣稱下游洪峰必然延後同樣秒數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水體平移與洪波傳播」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Lengthening can increase water-parcel advection time, but flood-wave celerity differs from mean parcel velocity. Length divided by velocity gives a constant-speed advection scale without dispersion, inactive-zone exchange or changing wave shape. Tracers can arrive early and leave long tails, while flood peaks depend on storage and boundaries. Evaluate tracer breakthrough, hydrographs and local velocity separately rather than claiming downstream peak delay directly from the calculated travel time of water parcels through the restored reach. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Water advection and flood-wave travel” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L=1800 m; u=0.6 m/s; ta=L/u=3000 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L=1800 m; u=0.6 m/s; ta=L/u=3000 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「水粒子旅行時間一定等於洪水峰值傳到下游的時間」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Water-parcel travel time always equals the time for a flood peak to reach downstream\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水體平移與洪波傳播」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Water advection and flood-wave travel”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-33-k1","title":"水體平移與洪波傳播","titleEn":"Water advection and flood-wave travel","text":"河道延長可能增加水體沿流路的平移時間，但洪波傳播速度並不等於水粒子平均流速。以長度除速度得到的是固定速度的平流尺度，未計彌散、死水交換或水位波形變化。","textEn":"Lengthening can increase water-parcel advection time, but flood-wave celerity differs from mean parcel velocity. Length divided by velocity gives a constant-speed advection scale without dispersion, inactive-zone exchange or changing wave shape.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水粒子旅行時間一定等於洪水峰值傳到下游的時間 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Water-parcel travel time always equals the time for a flood peak to reach downstream Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水體平移與洪波傳播」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Water advection and flood-wave travel\" is correct?","options":["河道延長可能增加水體沿流路的平移時間，但洪波傳播速度並不等於水粒子平均流速。","水粒子旅行時間一定等於洪水峰值傳到下游的時間","兩期地形圖任何非零差值都代表真實河床變化"],"optionsEn":["Lengthening can increase water-parcel advection time, but flood-wave celerity differs from mean parcel velocity.","Water-parcel travel time always equals the time for a flood peak to reach downstream","Every nonzero difference between two terrain surveys represents real bed change"],"answer":0,"explanation":"河道延長可能增加水體沿流路的平移時間，但洪波傳播速度並不等於水粒子平均流速。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Lengthening can increase water-parcel advection time, but flood-wave celerity differs from mean parcel velocity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b279-v15-34","title":"水體平移與洪波傳播：定量估算","titleEn":"Water advection and flood-wave travel: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水體平移與洪波傳播」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Water advection and flood-wave travel” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L=1800 m; u=0.6 m/s; ta=L/u=3000 s。適用邊界：定常均速平流時間尺度，不是洪峰傳播或完整示蹤停留分布。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L=1800 m; u=0.6 m/s; ta=L/u=3000 s. Applicable boundary: Steady uniform advection scale, not flood-peak travel or a full tracer residence distribution. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在合法且適合的示蹤試驗中量測上下游濃度曲線，另用同步水位流量觀測洪波。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use an appropriate authorized tracer test for concentration histories and synchronized level-discharge observations for flood waves.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L=1800 m; u=0.6 m/s; ta=L/u=3000 s。適用邊界：定常均速平流時間尺度，不是洪峰傳播或完整示蹤停留分布。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L=1800 m; u=0.6 m/s; ta=L/u=3000 s. Applicable boundary: Steady uniform advection scale, not flood-peak travel or a full tracer residence distribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水體平移與洪波傳播」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Water advection and flood-wave travel\", which statement holds?","options":["河道平均床坡就是所有流量下每一斷面的能量坡度","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L=1800 m; u=0.6 m/s; ta=L/u=3000 s。","幾何蓄水容量直接等於河川洪峰流量減少量"],"optionsEn":["Mean bed slope equals the energy slope at every section and discharge","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L=1800 m; u=0.6 m/s; ta=L/u=3000 s.","Geometric storage volume directly equals the reduction in river peak discharge"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L=1800 m; u=0.6 m/s; ta=L/u=3000 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L=1800 m; u=0.6 m/s; ta=L/u=3000 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b279-v15-35","title":"水體平移與洪波傳播：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Water advection and flood-wave travel: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水體平移與洪波傳播」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Water advection and flood-wave travel” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在合法且適合的示蹤試驗中量測上下游濃度曲線，另用同步水位流量觀測洪波。比較首達、質心與峰值時間，並說明各自物理意義；若差異大，檢查死水交換及沿程支流，不能任選最有利數字。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use an appropriate authorized tracer test for concentration histories and synchronized level-discharge observations for flood waves. Compare first arrival, centroid and peak times with their distinct meanings. Large differences warrant checking inactive-zone exchange and tributaries rather than selecting a favourable statistic. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將平均流速降低兩成重算平流時間，再畫一條有長尾的示蹤曲線及一條洪水歷線。標出不能直接互換的時間，列出檢驗削峰所需額外資料。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce mean velocity by twenty percent and recalculate advection time. Draw a long-tailed tracer curve and a flood hydrograph, label noninterchangeable times, and identify additional evidence needed to evaluate peak attenuation.","failure":"注意干擾：把示蹤質心時間當洪峰延遲，可能誇大防洪效果；相反地，忽略長尾也會低估污染物停留。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using tracer-centroid travel as flood-peak delay can exaggerate protection, while ignoring long tails understates contaminant persistence. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在合法且適合的示蹤試驗中量測上下游濃度曲線，另用同步水位流量觀測洪波。比較首達、質心與峰值時間，並說明各自物理意義；若差異大，檢查死水交換及沿程支流，不能任選最有利數字。","textEn":"Use an appropriate authorized tracer test for concentration histories and synchronized level-discharge observations for flood waves. Compare first arrival, centroid and peak times with their distinct meanings. Large differences warrant checking inactive-zone exchange and tributaries rather than selecting a favourable statistic.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將平均流速降低兩成重算平流時間，再畫一條有長尾的示蹤曲線及一條洪水歷線。標出不能直接互換的時間，列出檢驗削峰所需額外資料。","textEn":"Reduce mean velocity by twenty percent and recalculate advection time. Draw a long-tailed tracer curve and a flood hydrograph, label noninterchangeable times, and identify additional evidence needed to evaluate peak attenuation.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水體平移與洪波傳播」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Water advection and flood-wave travel\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","岸坡流失的原位體積必然在同一時刻全部通過下游斷面","在合法且適合的示蹤試驗中量測上下游濃度曲線，另用同步水位流量觀測洪波。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","All in-place bank erosion volume necessarily passes the downstream section at the same moment","Use an appropriate authorized tracer test for concentration histories and synchronized level-discharge observations for flood waves."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在合法且適合的示蹤試驗中量測上下游濃度曲線，另用同步水位流量觀測洪波。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use an appropriate authorized tracer test for concentration histories and synchronized level-discharge observations for flood waves. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b279-v15-36","title":"水體平移與洪波傳播：失效診斷","titleEn":"Water advection and flood-wave travel: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水體平移與洪波傳播」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Water advection and flood-wave travel” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把示蹤質心時間當洪峰延遲，可能誇大防洪效果；相反地，忽略長尾也會低估污染物停留。應根據問題選指標，避免混用不同時間尺度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using tracer-centroid travel as flood-peak delay can exaggerate protection, while ignoring long tails understates contaminant persistence. Choose the time metric for the actual question instead of mixing different transport and wave processes. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：評估復育的時間效益時，應分別量測示蹤突破、洪水歷線與局部流速，避免用水的旅行時間直接宣稱下游洪峰必然延後同樣秒數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Evaluate tracer breakthrough, hydrographs and local velocity separately rather than claiming downstream peak delay directly from the calculated travel time of water parcels through the restored reach.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水粒子旅行時間一定等於洪水峰值傳到下游的時間」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Water-parcel travel time always equals the time for a flood peak to reach downstream\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把示蹤質心時間當洪峰延遲，可能誇大防洪效果；相反地，忽略長尾也會低估污染物停留。應根據問題選指標，避免混用不同時間尺度。","textEn":"Using tracer-centroid travel as flood-peak delay can exaggerate protection, while ignoring long tails understates contaminant persistence. Choose the time metric for the actual question instead of mixing different transport and wave processes.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水體平移與洪波傳播」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Water advection and flood-wave travel\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把示蹤質心時間當洪峰延遲，可能誇大防洪效果；相反地，忽略長尾也會低估污染物停留。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","兩期地形圖任何非零差值都代表真實河床變化"],"optionsEn":["Using tracer-centroid travel as flood-peak delay can exaggerate protection, while ignoring long tails understates contaminant persistence.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Every nonzero difference between two terrain surveys represents real bed change"],"answer":0,"explanation":"把示蹤質心時間當洪峰延遲，可能誇大防洪效果；相反地，忽略長尾也會低估污染物停留。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using tracer-centroid travel as flood-peak delay can exaggerate protection, while ignoring long tails understates contaminant persistence. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b279-v15-37","title":"地形差分的量測不確定性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Uncertainty in terrain differences: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「地形差分的量測不確定性」如何影響河川再蜿蜒工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Uncertainty in terrain differences” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River remeandering works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"工程前後地形差分可找出沖淤，但小變化可能只是測量誤差。兩期獨立隨機高程誤差的標準差可用平方和開根號合成，若兩期共享基準偏差或植生遮蔽，獨立假設便不成立。單點標準差也不等於整個土方體積的誤差，空間相關會改變總量不確定性。分析應先分離系統偏差與隨機分散，再清楚報告檢出尺度，而不把所有不同顏色像元當成真實侵蝕或沉積。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「地形差分的量測不確定性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Terrain differencing reveals erosion and deposition, but small changes may be survey noise. Independent random elevation standard deviations combine by root sum of squares; shared datum errors or vegetation bias violate independence. Point uncertainty also differs from volume uncertainty because spatial correlation affects aggregation. Separate systematic bias from random scatter and state the detection scale clearly, rather than interpreting every coloured difference pixel as real morphological change or assigning confidence without an explicit error model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Uncertainty in terrain differences” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：s1=0.03 m; s2=0.04 m; sd=sqrt(s1^2+s2^2)=0.05 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: s1=0.03 m; s2=0.04 m; sd=sqrt(s1^2+s2^2)=0.05 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩期地形圖任何非零差值都代表真實河床變化」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every nonzero difference between two terrain surveys represents real bed change\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「地形差分的量測不確定性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Uncertainty in terrain differences”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-37-k1","title":"地形差分的量測不確定性","titleEn":"Uncertainty in terrain differences","text":"工程前後地形差分可找出沖淤，但小變化可能只是測量誤差。兩期獨立隨機高程誤差的標準差可用平方和開根號合成，若兩期共享基準偏差或植生遮蔽，獨立假設便不成立。","textEn":"Terrain differencing reveals erosion and deposition, but small changes may be survey noise. Independent random elevation standard deviations combine by root sum of squares; shared datum errors or vegetation bias violate independence.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩期地形圖任何非零差值都代表真實河床變化 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every nonzero difference between two terrain surveys represents real bed change Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地形差分的量測不確定性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Uncertainty in terrain differences\" is correct?","options":["兩期地形圖任何非零差值都代表真實河床變化","工程前後地形差分可找出沖淤，但小變化可能只是測量誤差。","蜿蜒度較大必然代表所有生態功能與防洪能力較好"],"optionsEn":["Every nonzero difference between two terrain surveys represents real bed change","Terrain differencing reveals erosion and deposition, but small changes may be survey noise.","Greater sinuosity necessarily means better ecological function and flood protection in every respect"],"answer":1,"explanation":"工程前後地形差分可找出沖淤，但小變化可能只是測量誤差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Terrain differencing reveals erosion and deposition, but small changes may be survey noise. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b279-v15-38","title":"地形差分的量測不確定性：定量估算","titleEn":"Uncertainty in terrain differences: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「地形差分的量測不確定性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Uncertainty in terrain differences” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：s1=0.03 m; s2=0.04 m; sd=sqrt(s1^2+s2^2)=0.05 m。適用邊界：兩期獨立零均值隨機誤差的差分標準差，非自動的可信界限。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: s1=0.03 m; s2=0.04 m; sd=sqrt(s1^2+s2^2)=0.05 m. Applicable boundary: Difference standard deviation for independent zero-mean random errors, not an automatic confidence bound. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在穩定未變區檢查兩期高程偏差，先校正可識別系統差，再分析殘差分布與空間相關。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check differences on stable ground, correct identifiable systematic shifts, and examine residual distributions and spatial correlation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：s1=0.03 m; s2=0.04 m; sd=sqrt(s1^2+s2^2)=0.05 m。適用邊界：兩期獨立零均值隨機誤差的差分標準差，非自動的可信界限。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: s1=0.03 m; s2=0.04 m; sd=sqrt(s1^2+s2^2)=0.05 m. Applicable boundary: Difference standard deviation for independent zero-mean random errors, not an automatic confidence bound.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地形差分的量測不確定性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Uncertainty in terrain differences\", which statement holds?","options":["曼寧粗糙係數只由材料決定且永遠不隨水深改變","橫向水面差很小就能證明外彎岸坡不會沖刷","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：s1=0.03 m; s2=0.04 m; sd=sqrt(s1^2+s2^2)=0.05 m。"],"optionsEn":["Manning roughness depends only on material and never changes with water depth","A small transverse water-level difference proves that the outer bank will not erode","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: s1=0.03 m; s2=0.04 m; sd=sqrt(s1^2+s2^2)=0.05 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：s1=0.03 m; s2=0.04 m; sd=sqrt(s1^2+s2^2)=0.05 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: s1=0.03 m; s2=0.04 m; sd=sqrt(s1^2+s2^2)=0.05 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b279-v15-39","title":"地形差分的量測不確定性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Uncertainty in terrain differences: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「地形差分的量測不確定性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Uncertainty in terrain differences” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在穩定未變區檢查兩期高程偏差，先校正可識別系統差，再分析殘差分布與空間相關。用獨立控制點驗證，並分別報裸地與植生區精度；設定檢出門檻時需交代誤差分布及採用的信心水準。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check differences on stable ground, correct identifiable systematic shifts, and examine residual distributions and spatial correlation. Validate with independent control points and separate bare-ground from vegetated accuracy. Any detection threshold needs a stated error distribution and confidence level. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：假設第二期標準差降到兩公分，重算差分精度並比較改善幅度。再提出兩期誤差相關的情況，說明為何不能繼續使用獨立平方和公式宣稱同樣精度。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce the second survey standard deviation to two centimetres and recompute difference uncertainty. Describe a source of correlated errors and explain why the independent root-sum-square formula would then require modification before claiming equivalent accuracy.","failure":"注意干擾：未校正的共同高程偏移會讓整段河道看似淤積或侵蝕，植生高度也可能被當成地面。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An uncorrected datum shift can make the whole reach appear to deposit or erode, and vegetation may be mistaken for ground. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在穩定未變區檢查兩期高程偏差，先校正可識別系統差，再分析殘差分布與空間相關。用獨立控制點驗證，並分別報裸地與植生區精度；設定檢出門檻時需交代誤差分布及採用的信心水準。","textEn":"Check differences on stable ground, correct identifiable systematic shifts, and examine residual distributions and spatial correlation. Validate with independent control points and separate bare-ground from vegetated accuracy. Any detection threshold needs a stated error distribution and confidence level.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"假設第二期標準差降到兩公分，重算差分精度並比較改善幅度。再提出兩期誤差相關的情況，說明為何不能繼續使用獨立平方和公式宣稱同樣精度。","textEn":"Reduce the second survey standard deviation to two centimetres and recompute difference uncertainty. Describe a source of correlated errors and explain why the independent root-sum-square formula would then require modification before claiming equivalent accuracy.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地形差分的量測不確定性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Uncertainty in terrain differences\"?","options":["在穩定未變區檢查兩期高程偏差，先校正可識別系統差，再分析殘差分布與空間相關。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","側汊總流入體積就是側汊最後增加的淨蓄水體積"],"optionsEn":["Check differences on stable ground, correct identifiable systematic shifts, and examine residual distributions and spatial correlation.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Total side-channel inflow equals its final increase in net stored volume"],"answer":0,"explanation":"在穩定未變區檢查兩期高程偏差，先校正可識別系統差，再分析殘差分布與空間相關。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check differences on stable ground, correct identifiable systematic shifts, and examine residual distributions and spatial correlation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b279-v15-40","title":"地形差分的量測不確定性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Uncertainty in terrain differences: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b279-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「地形差分的量測不確定性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Uncertainty in terrain differences” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未校正的共同高程偏移會讓整段河道看似淤積或侵蝕，植生高度也可能被當成地面。若差分呈現整區同號，應先查基準及分類再解釋地形過程。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An uncorrected datum shift can make the whole reach appear to deposit or erode, and vegetation may be mistaken for ground. Region-wide differences of one sign call for checking datum and classification before interpreting geomorphic processes. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：分析應先分離系統偏差與隨機分散，再清楚報告檢出尺度，而不把所有不同顏色像元當成真實侵蝕或沉積。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Separate systematic bias from random scatter and state the detection scale clearly, rather than interpreting every coloured difference pixel as real morphological change or assigning confidence without an explicit error model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩期地形圖任何非零差值都代表真實河床變化」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every nonzero difference between two terrain surveys represents real bed change\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b279-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未校正的共同高程偏移會讓整段河道看似淤積或侵蝕，植生高度也可能被當成地面。若差分呈現整區同號，應先查基準及分類再解釋地形過程。","textEn":"An uncorrected datum shift can make the whole reach appear to deposit or erode, and vegetation may be mistaken for ground. Region-wide differences of one sign call for checking datum and classification before interpreting geomorphic processes.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]},{"id":"b279-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地形差分的量測不確定性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Uncertainty in terrain differences\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","未校正的共同高程偏移會讓整段河道看似淤積或侵蝕，植生高度也可能被當成地面。","蜿蜒度較大必然代表所有生態功能與防洪能力較好"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","An uncorrected datum shift can make the whole reach appear to deposit or erode, and vegetation may be mistaken for ground.","Greater sinuosity necessarily means better ecological function and flood protection in every respect"],"answer":1,"explanation":"未校正的共同高程偏移會讓整段河道看似淤積或侵蝕，植生高度也可能被當成地面。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An uncorrected datum shift can make the whole reach appear to deposit or erode, and vegetation may be mistaken for ground. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-eea-skjern","v15s-nrcs-bio","v15s-eea-regge"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b280","title":"洪水預報與水庫聯合操作","titleEn":"Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"將預報誤差、河道傳播時間、庫容與下游通洪能力放在同一個運算框架，練習集合機率、校準、預洩與衝突限制辨識。教材以兩座假想水庫展示聯合操作所需的狀態和責任邊界，計算結果只作方法教學，實際操作仍需正式規程與有權機關決策。","summaryEn":"Place forecast uncertainty, routing time, storage and downstream capacity in one calculation framework. Exercises cover ensemble probabilities, calibration, prerelease and conflicting constraints. Two hypothetical reservoirs illustrate the states and responsibilities required for coordinated operation. Results teach methods rather than authorize releases; real decisions require approved operating rules, current observations and the responsible institutions.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["集合超越機率","Ensemble exceedance probability"],["機率預報的布里爾分數","Brier score for probability forecasts"],["匯流點的同步疊加","Aligned flows at a junction"],["預洩所需時間窗","Time window for prerelease"],["預報改善與獨立驗證","Forecast improvement and independent validation"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["集合超越機率","機率預報的布里爾分數","匯流點的同步疊加","預洩所需時間窗","預報改善與獨立驗證"],"labelsEn":["Ensemble exceedance probability","Brier score for probability forecasts","Aligned flows at a junction","Time window for prerelease","Forecast improvement and independent validation"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課先用「集合超越機率」建立原創假想基準，再以「分位數與有限成員」檢查另一個控制機制。第一組輸入及結果為 Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless；第二組為 ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s。學員需在同一張工作表分列量綱、時間、位置與適用範圍，先核對守恆，再解釋為何兩個得數不能互相代替。最後以第三單元提出的量測設計驗證假設，並將超出模型能力的水理、生態或治理問題列為待研究項目；這些示例並非所列案例的現場實測。敏感度重算：保持 N=20 個等權成員及同一流量門檻，把超越成員 Ne 從 8 增至 10，經驗比例由 0.4 增至 0.5，也就是增加十個百分點。這不是證明真實風險上升同樣幅度，仍須用獨立事件檢驗機率校準。","textEn":"Begin with an original hypothetical baseline for Ensemble exceedance probability and examine another controlling mechanism through Quantiles with finite ensembles. The first inputs and result are Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless; the second are ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s. Keep dimensions, time, location and validity conditions in separate columns of the same working sheet. Check conservation before explaining why the two numerical results cannot substitute for one another. Use the third unit measurement design to test assumptions and identify hydraulic, ecological or governance questions that exceed the model. These examples are not field observations from the named reference cases. Sensitivity recalculation: Keep N=20 equally weighted members and the same flow threshold, increasing exceedances Ne from 8 to 10. The empirical fraction rises from 0.4 to 0.5, an increase of ten percentage points. This does not prove an equal change in true risk; probability calibration still requires independent events.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b280-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「集合超越機率」與「分位數與有限成員」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ensemble exceedance probability\" and \"Quantiles with finite ensembles\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b280-v15-01","title":"集合超越機率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ensemble exceedance probability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「集合超越機率」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ensemble exceedance probability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"集合預報用多個可能情境表達不確定性，超過指定流量門檻的成員比例可作經驗超越機率。這些成員不一定相互獨立，也可能共享降雨偏差，因此比例不是自然界真實機率的保證。門檻必須對應同一地點、時段與流量定義，瞬時峰值不能與日平均混用。操作比較應同時看後果與機率，並透過過往未參與校準的事件檢查可靠度，而不是只選最樂觀的成員作決策依據。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「集合超越機率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An ensemble expresses uncertainty through alternative scenarios, and the fraction exceeding a threshold gives an empirical exceedance probability. Members may be dependent or share rainfall bias, so the fraction is not a guarantee of nature's true probability. Match location, lead period and discharge definition; instantaneous peaks differ from daily means. Compare consequences as well as probabilities, and evaluate reliability on events excluded from calibration instead of basing decisions on the most optimistic member. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ensemble exceedance probability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「集合超越機率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ensemble exceedance probability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-01-k1","title":"集合超越機率","titleEn":"Ensemble exceedance probability","text":"集合預報用多個可能情境表達不確定性，超過指定流量門檻的成員比例可作經驗超越機率。這些成員不一定相互獨立，也可能共享降雨偏差，因此比例不是自然界真實機率的保證。","textEn":"An ensemble expresses uncertainty through alternative scenarios, and the fraction exceeding a threshold gives an empirical exceedance probability. Members may be dependent or share rainfall bias, so the fraction is not a guarantee of nature's true probability.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「集合超越機率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ensemble exceedance probability\" is correct?","options":["集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成","集合預報用多個可能情境表達不確定性，超過指定流量門檻的成員比例可作經驗超越機率。","九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限"],"optionsEn":["Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent","An ensemble expresses uncertainty through alternative scenarios, and the fraction exceeding a threshold gives an empirical exceedance probability.","The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey"],"answer":1,"explanation":"集合預報用多個可能情境表達不確定性，超過指定流量門檻的成員比例可作經驗超越機率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An ensemble expresses uncertainty through alternative scenarios, and the fraction exceeding a threshold gives an empirical exceedance probability. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b280-v15-02","title":"集合超越機率：定量估算","titleEn":"Ensemble exceedance probability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「集合超越機率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ensemble exceedance probability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless。適用邊界：等權情境的經驗比例，非已驗證校準之真實洪水機率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Empirical fraction of equally weighted scenarios, not a demonstrated calibrated probability of flooding. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：固定預報發布時刻、有效時段與斷面門檻，逐一檢查成員是否超越。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Fix issue time, valid period and section threshold before counting exceedances.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless。適用邊界：等權情境的經驗比例，非已驗證校準之真實洪水機率。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Empirical fraction of equally weighted scenarios, not a demonstrated calibrated probability of flooding.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「集合超越機率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ensemble exceedance probability\", which statement holds?","options":["水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加","下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless。"],"optionsEn":["A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase","Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Ne=8 members above-threshold."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Ne=8 members above-threshold; N=20 equally-weighted-members; p=Ne/N=0.4 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b280-v15-03","title":"集合超越機率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ensemble exceedance probability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「集合超越機率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ensemble exceedance probability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"固定預報發布時刻、有效時段與斷面門檻，逐一檢查成員是否超越。用獨立歷史預報回放分組比較預報機率和實際發生頻率，保留漏報與誤報紀錄，並確認沒有事後雨量被偷偷加入當時預報。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Fix issue time, valid period and section threshold before counting exceedances. Use independent forecast replays to compare probability groups with observed frequencies, retaining misses and false alarms and ensuring later rainfall observations were not inserted into earlier forecasts. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持二十個等權成員，將超越數增加到十個重算比例。說明需要哪些歷史樣本才能檢查這個機率是否可靠，並列出成員相關可能造成的限制。","observationEn":"Site practice: Keep twenty equally weighted members and increase exceedances to ten. Recalculate the fraction, identify historical samples needed to test reliability, and describe limitations caused by dependence between ensemble members across the forecast set.","failure":"注意干擾：集合全部偏低時，即使成員看似一致也可能漏掉洪水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A consistently low ensemble can miss flooding despite strong member agreement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"固定預報發布時刻、有效時段與斷面門檻，逐一檢查成員是否超越。用獨立歷史預報回放分組比較預報機率和實際發生頻率，保留漏報與誤報紀錄，並確認沒有事後雨量被偷偷加入當時預報。","textEn":"Fix issue time, valid period and section threshold before counting exceedances. Use independent forecast replays to compare probability groups with observed frequencies, retaining misses and false alarms and ensuring later rainfall observations were not inserted into earlier forecasts.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持二十個等權成員，將超越數增加到十個重算比例。說明需要哪些歷史樣本才能檢查這個機率是否可靠，並列出成員相關可能造成的限制。","textEn":"Keep twenty equally weighted members and increase exceedances to ten. Recalculate the fraction, identify historical samples needed to test reliability, and describe limitations caused by dependence between ensemble members across the forecast set.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「集合超越機率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ensemble exceedance probability\"?","options":["固定預報發布時刻、有效時段與斷面門檻，逐一檢查成員是否超越。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足"],"optionsEn":["Fix issue time, valid period and section threshold before counting exceedances.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied"],"answer":0,"explanation":"固定預報發布時刻、有效時段與斷面門檻，逐一檢查成員是否超越。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Fix issue time, valid period and section threshold before counting exceedances. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b280-v15-04","title":"集合超越機率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ensemble exceedance probability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「集合超越機率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ensemble exceedance probability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"集合全部偏低時，即使成員看似一致也可能漏掉洪水。若只用集合範圍當絕對上下界，會掩蓋共同模式誤差，需以獨立事件檢查可靠度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A consistently low ensemble can miss flooding despite strong member agreement. Treating its range as an absolute physical bound conceals shared model error, requiring reliability checks against independent observed events. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：操作比較應同時看後果與機率，並透過過往未參與校準的事件檢查可靠度，而不是只選最樂觀的成員作決策依據。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare consequences as well as probabilities, and evaluate reliability on events excluded from calibration instead of basing decisions on the most optimistic member.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"集合全部偏低時，即使成員看似一致也可能漏掉洪水。若只用集合範圍當絕對上下界，會掩蓋共同模式誤差，需以獨立事件檢查可靠度。","textEn":"A consistently low ensemble can miss flooding despite strong member agreement. Treating its range as an absolute physical bound conceals shared model error, requiring reliability checks against independent observed events.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「集合超越機率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ensemble exceedance probability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","集合全部偏低時，即使成員看似一致也可能漏掉洪水。","九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A consistently low ensemble can miss flooding despite strong member agreement.","The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey"],"answer":1,"explanation":"集合全部偏低時，即使成員看似一致也可能漏掉洪水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A consistently low ensemble can miss flooding despite strong member agreement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b280-v15-05","title":"分位數與有限成員：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Quantiles with finite ensembles: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「分位數與有限成員」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Quantiles with finite ensembles” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"集合分位數把排序後的情境濃縮為可讀摘要，但小集合的高分位數會對插值規則及個別極端成員敏感。分位數描述預報分布的位置，不是平均值的信賴區間，也不是所有可能洪水的上限。比較不同系統時應保留相同分位數定義、權重與有效時段，並報告成員數。操作評估還需檢視完整歷線，因為單一峰值分位數可能無法代表水量和峰值到達時間之間的關係。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分位數與有限成員」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Ensemble quantiles summarize ordered scenarios, but high quantiles in a small set are sensitive to interpolation and individual extremes. A quantile locates a forecast distribution; it is neither a confidence interval for the mean nor a bound on every possible flood. Preserve definitions, weights and valid periods when comparing systems, and report member count. Examine complete hydrographs because a peak quantile alone may miss relationships between flood volume and arrival time that matter for storage decisions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Quantiles with finite ensembles” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「分位數與有限成員」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Quantiles with finite ensembles”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-05-k1","title":"分位數與有限成員","titleEn":"Quantiles with finite ensembles","text":"集合分位數把排序後的情境濃縮為可讀摘要，但小集合的高分位數會對插值規則及個別極端成員敏感。分位數描述預報分布的位置，不是平均值的信賴區間，也不是所有可能洪水的上限。","textEn":"Ensemble quantiles summarize ordered scenarios, but high quantiles in a small set are sensitive to interpolation and individual extremes. A quantile locates a forecast distribution; it is neither a confidence interval for the mean nor a bound on every possible flood.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分位數與有限成員」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Quantiles with finite ensembles\" is correct?","options":["九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限","只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報","集合分位數把排序後的情境濃縮為可讀摘要，但小集合的高分位數會對插值規則及個別極端成員敏感。"],"optionsEn":["The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey","Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system","Ensemble quantiles summarize ordered scenarios, but high quantiles in a small set are sensitive to interpolation and individual extremes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"集合分位數把排序後的情境濃縮為可讀摘要，但小集合的高分位數會對插值規則及個別極端成員敏感。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Ensemble quantiles summarize ordered scenarios, but high quantiles in a small set are sensitive to interpolation and individual extremes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b280-v15-06","title":"分位數與有限成員：定量估算","titleEn":"Quantiles with finite ensembles: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「分位數與有限成員」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Quantiles with finite ensembles” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s。適用邊界：指定線性插值經驗分位數，五個成員不能證明尾部分布校準。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s. Applicable boundary: Specified linearly interpolated empirical quantile; five members do not establish tail calibration. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保存原始排序值與使用的插值規則，手算相鄰兩成員及權重，再與軟體結果比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Preserve sorted values and interpolation rules, manually checking neighbouring members and weights against software output.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s。適用邊界：指定線性插值經驗分位數，五個成員不能證明尾部分布校準。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s. Applicable boundary: Specified linearly interpolated empirical quantile; five members do not establish tail calibration.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「分位數與有限成員」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Quantiles with finite ensembles\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s。","同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達","目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s.","Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together","Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: ordered-flows=[80,100,120,140,160] m3/s; q=0.9 dimensionless; h=(5-1)*q=3.6 zero-based-rank; Qq=140+0.6*(160-140)=152 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b280-v15-07","title":"分位數與有限成員：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Quantiles with finite ensembles: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「分位數與有限成員」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Quantiles with finite ensembles” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保存原始排序值與使用的插值規則，手算相鄰兩成員及權重，再與軟體結果比較。用另一種常見分位數定義做差異檢查，若高分位變動大，應報成員有限造成的不穩定，而不是隱藏選法。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Preserve sorted values and interpolation rules, manually checking neighbouring members and weights against software output. Compare an alternative quantile convention. Large high-quantile differences should be reported as finite-ensemble instability rather than concealed by an undocumented choice of method. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把最高成員改成每秒二百立方公尺重算同一分位數，其他值與定義不變。說明單一成員敏感度如何影響解讀，並保留原始情境供水量分析。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only the largest member to two hundred cubic metres per second and recompute the same quantile. Explain sensitivity to one member and retain complete scenarios for subsequent flood-volume analysis.","failure":"注意干擾：若把不同時刻的各自高分位拼成一條歷線，可能產生不存在於任何成員的水量與峰型組合。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Joining pointwise high quantiles can create a volume and peak shape found in no individual member. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保存原始排序值與使用的插值規則，手算相鄰兩成員及權重，再與軟體結果比較。用另一種常見分位數定義做差異檢查，若高分位變動大，應報成員有限造成的不穩定，而不是隱藏選法。","textEn":"Preserve sorted values and interpolation rules, manually checking neighbouring members and weights against software output. Compare an alternative quantile convention. Large high-quantile differences should be reported as finite-ensemble instability rather than concealed by an undocumented choice of method.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把最高成員改成每秒二百立方公尺重算同一分位數，其他值與定義不變。說明單一成員敏感度如何影響解讀，並保留原始情境供水量分析。","textEn":"Change only the largest member to two hundred cubic metres per second and recompute the same quantile. Explain sensitivity to one member and retain complete scenarios for subsequent flood-volume analysis.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「分位數與有限成員」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Quantiles with finite ensembles\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","保存原始排序值與使用的插值規則，手算相鄰兩成員及權重，再與軟體結果比較。","情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Preserve sorted values and interpolation rules, manually checking neighbouring members and weights against software output.","Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences"],"answer":1,"explanation":"保存原始排序值與使用的插值規則，手算相鄰兩成員及權重，再與軟體結果比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Preserve sorted values and interpolation rules, manually checking neighbouring members and weights against software output. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b280-v15-08","title":"分位數與有限成員：失效診斷","titleEn":"Quantiles with finite ensembles: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「分位數與有限成員」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Quantiles with finite ensembles” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若把不同時刻的各自高分位拼成一條歷線，可能產生不存在於任何成員的水量與峰型組合。應標示此為摘要包絡，不能當成一個一致情境。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Joining pointwise high quantiles can create a volume and peak shape found in no individual member. Label such a curve as a summary envelope rather than treating it as one dynamically consistent forecast scenario. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：操作評估還需檢視完整歷線，因為單一峰值分位數可能無法代表水量和峰值到達時間之間的關係。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Examine complete hydrographs because a peak quantile alone may miss relationships between flood volume and arrival time that matter for storage decisions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把不同時刻的各自高分位拼成一條歷線，可能產生不存在於任何成員的水量與峰型組合。應標示此為摘要包絡，不能當成一個一致情境。","textEn":"Joining pointwise high quantiles can create a volume and peak shape found in no individual member. Label such a curve as a summary envelope rather than treating it as one dynamically consistent forecast scenario.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分位數與有限成員」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Quantiles with finite ensembles\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報","若把不同時刻的各自高分位拼成一條歷線，可能產生不存在於任何成員的水量與峰型組合。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system","Joining pointwise high quantiles can create a volume and peak shape found in no individual member."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若把不同時刻的各自高分位拼成一條歷線，可能產生不存在於任何成員的水量與峰型組合。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Joining pointwise high quantiles can create a volume and peak shape found in no individual member. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b280-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「機率預報的布里爾分數」與「水庫時段水量守恆」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Brier score for probability forecasts\" and \"Reservoir interval water balance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b280-v15-09","title":"機率預報的布里爾分數：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Brier score for probability forecasts: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「機率預報的布里爾分數」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Brier score for probability forecasts” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"布里爾分數以預報機率與二元觀測的平方差衡量機率誤差，數值較小通常表示較好的整體配對，但不直接說明每一次決策的損失。評估事件必須使用相同門檻與預報提前時間，並包含未發生洪水的情況，否則會扭曲分數。不同地區的基準發生率會影響比較，因此還需與適當參考預報對照。可靠度、辨識度及資料不足的問題應分開診斷，避免把一個平均分數當作完整風險認證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「機率預報的布里爾分數」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Brier score averages squared differences between probabilities and binary outcomes. Lower values generally indicate better matching but do not directly measure the loss from each decision. Use consistent thresholds and lead times and include non-events; selecting only floods distorts the score. Different base rates also affect comparisons, requiring an appropriate reference forecast. Diagnose reliability, discrimination and sample limitations separately rather than treating one average score as complete certification of operational risk or forecast quality. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Brier score for probability forecasts” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「機率預報的布里爾分數」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Brier score for probability forecasts”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-09-k1","title":"機率預報的布里爾分數","titleEn":"Brier score for probability forecasts","text":"布里爾分數以預報機率與二元觀測的平方差衡量機率誤差，數值較小通常表示較好的整體配對，但不直接說明每一次決策的損失。評估事件必須使用相同門檻與預報提前時間，並包含未發生洪水的情況，否則會扭曲分數。","textEn":"The Brier score averages squared differences between probabilities and binary outcomes. Lower values generally indicate better matching but do not directly measure the loss from each decision.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「機率預報的布里爾分數」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Brier score for probability forecasts\" is correct?","options":["布里爾分數以預報機率與二元觀測的平方差衡量機率誤差，數值較小通常表示較好的整體配對，但不直接說明每一次決策的損失。","只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報","水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加"],"optionsEn":["The Brier score averages squared differences between probabilities and binary outcomes.","Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system","A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase"],"answer":0,"explanation":"布里爾分數以預報機率與二元觀測的平方差衡量機率誤差，數值較小通常表示較好的整體配對，但不直接說明每一次決策的損失。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Brier score averages squared differences between probabilities and binary outcomes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b280-v15-10","title":"機率預報的布里爾分數：定量估算","titleEn":"Brier score for probability forecasts: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「機率預報的布里爾分數」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Brier score for probability forecasts” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless。適用邊界：四筆獨立保留樣本的示範平均，不代表已完成長期服務驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Illustrative average for four held-out cases, not validation of a long-term forecasting service. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將預報檔案凍結在發布時刻，核對每一筆門檻與後來觀測，再逐項列平方誤差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Freeze forecasts at issue time and match thresholds to subsequent observations before listing each squared error.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless。適用邊界：四筆獨立保留樣本的示範平均，不代表已完成長期服務驗證。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Illustrative average for four held-out cases, not validation of a long-term forecasting service.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「機率預報的布里爾分數」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Brier score for probability forecasts\", which statement holds?","options":["下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless。","求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足"],"optionsEn":["Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless.","Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: probabilities=[0.2,0.7,0.6,0.1] dimensionless; outcomes=[0,1,1,0] binary; BS=(0.2^2+(0.7-1)^2+(0.6-1)^2+0.1^2)/4=0.075 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b280-v15-11","title":"機率預報的布里爾分數：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Brier score for probability forecasts: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「機率預報的布里爾分數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Brier score for probability forecasts” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將預報檔案凍結在發布時刻，核對每一筆門檻與後來觀測，再逐項列平方誤差。另報事件數、非事件數及基準分數，分提前時間比較，避免把較容易的短期預報混入後宣稱長期能力改善。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Freeze forecasts at issue time and match thresholds to subsequent observations before listing each squared error. Report event and non-event counts with reference scores, separating lead times so easier short-range cases do not create a misleading claim of long-range improvement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把第三筆機率從零點六改成零點八，其餘不變重算分數。說明這次改善為何不能保證所有未來事件都較好，並提出需增加的樣本分層方式。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change the third probability from zero point six to zero point eight and recalculate. Explain why improvement on this case does not guarantee future performance, then propose additional strata for evaluating a larger sample.","failure":"注意干擾：只挑曾經發生大洪水的日期會破壞原本機率樣本，使過度警報的系統看似合理。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Selecting only major-flood dates distorts the probability sample and can make frequent over-warning look reasonable. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將預報檔案凍結在發布時刻，核對每一筆門檻與後來觀測，再逐項列平方誤差。另報事件數、非事件數及基準分數，分提前時間比較，避免把較容易的短期預報混入後宣稱長期能力改善。","textEn":"Freeze forecasts at issue time and match thresholds to subsequent observations before listing each squared error. Report event and non-event counts with reference scores, separating lead times so easier short-range cases do not create a misleading claim of long-range improvement.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把第三筆機率從零點六改成零點八，其餘不變重算分數。說明這次改善為何不能保證所有未來事件都較好，並提出需增加的樣本分層方式。","textEn":"Change the third probability from zero point six to zero point eight and recalculate. Explain why improvement on this case does not guarantee future performance, then propose additional strata for evaluating a larger sample.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「機率預報的布里爾分數」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Brier score for probability forecasts\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比","將預報檔案凍結在發布時刻，核對每一筆門檻與後來觀測，再逐項列平方誤差。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction","Freeze forecasts at issue time and match thresholds to subsequent observations before listing each squared error."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將預報檔案凍結在發布時刻，核對每一筆門檻與後來觀測，再逐項列平方誤差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Freeze forecasts at issue time and match thresholds to subsequent observations before listing each squared error. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b280-v15-12","title":"機率預報的布里爾分數：失效診斷","titleEn":"Brier score for probability forecasts: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「機率預報的布里爾分數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Brier score for probability forecasts” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只挑曾經發生大洪水的日期會破壞原本機率樣本，使過度警報的系統看似合理。若評估資料由結果篩選，應重新建立完整發布紀錄。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Selecting only major-flood dates distorts the probability sample and can make frequent over-warning look reasonable. An outcome-selected evaluation needs rebuilding from the complete issue archive, including dates on which the event did not occur. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：可靠度、辨識度及資料不足的問題應分開診斷，避免把一個平均分數當作完整風險認證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Diagnose reliability, discrimination and sample limitations separately rather than treating one average score as complete certification of operational risk or forecast quality.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只挑曾經發生大洪水的日期會破壞原本機率樣本，使過度警報的系統看似合理。若評估資料由結果篩選，應重新建立完整發布紀錄。","textEn":"Selecting only major-flood dates distorts the probability sample and can make frequent over-warning look reasonable. An outcome-selected evaluation needs rebuilding from the complete issue archive, including dates on which the event did not occur.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「機率預報的布里爾分數」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Brier score for probability forecasts\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只挑曾經發生大洪水的日期會破壞原本機率樣本，使過度警報的系統看似合理。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加"],"optionsEn":["Selecting only major-flood dates distorts the probability sample and can make frequent over-warning look reasonable.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase"],"answer":0,"explanation":"只挑曾經發生大洪水的日期會破壞原本機率樣本，使過度警報的系統看似合理。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Selecting only major-flood dates distorts the probability sample and can make frequent over-warning look reasonable. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b280-v15-13","title":"水庫時段水量守恆：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Reservoir interval water balance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「水庫時段水量守恆」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Reservoir interval water balance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"聯合操作必須先確保每座水庫的入流、出流與庫容變化閉合，否則優化可能在不存在的水量上作決策。時段兩端流量線性變化時可用梯形積分，若洪峰在中間突起，端點平均便可能漏算重要水量。蒸發、取水與溢流應依時間尺度決定是否列入，省略時需明示。庫容還必須透過現行水位容量曲線與觀測對照，不能把高程差直接當成體積差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水庫時段水量守恆」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Coordinated operation first requires each reservoir's inflow, outflow and storage to balance; otherwise optimization acts on nonexistent water. Trapezoidal integration is appropriate for linearly changing endpoint flows, but can miss an interior peak. Include or explicitly neglect evaporation, withdrawals and spill according to the time scale. Compare storage with observations through a current stage-storage relation, because elevation change is not itself a volume change and sediment accumulation can alter that relation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Reservoir interval water balance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水庫時段水量守恆」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Reservoir interval water balance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-13-k1","title":"水庫時段水量守恆","titleEn":"Reservoir interval water balance","text":"聯合操作必須先確保每座水庫的入流、出流與庫容變化閉合，否則優化可能在不存在的水量上作決策。時段兩端流量線性變化時可用梯形積分，若洪峰在中間突起，端點平均便可能漏算重要水量。","textEn":"Coordinated operation first requires each reservoir's inflow, outflow and storage to balance; otherwise optimization acts on nonexistent water. Trapezoidal integration is appropriate for linearly changing endpoint flows, but can miss an interior peak.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水庫時段水量守恆」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Reservoir interval water balance\" is correct?","options":["水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加","聯合操作必須先確保每座水庫的入流、出流與庫容變化閉合，否則優化可能在不存在的水量上作決策。","同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達"],"optionsEn":["A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase","Coordinated operation first requires each reservoir's inflow, outflow and storage to balance; otherwise optimization acts on nonexistent water.","Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together"],"answer":1,"explanation":"聯合操作必須先確保每座水庫的入流、出流與庫容變化閉合，否則優化可能在不存在的水量上作決策。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Coordinated operation first requires each reservoir's inflow, outflow and storage to balance; otherwise optimization acts on nonexistent water. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b280-v15-14","title":"水庫時段水量守恆：定量估算","titleEn":"Reservoir interval water balance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水庫時段水量守恆」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Reservoir interval water balance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3。適用邊界：時段流量線性變化且無其他水量項，僅求庫容增量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3. Applicable boundary: Linearly changing flows without other water terms; calculates storage increment only. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：先統一流量時戳及單位，以較細時間資料檢查梯形近似，再用水位容量曲線估觀測增量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align timestamps and units, test the trapezoidal approximation with finer records, and compare storage change inferred from the stage-storage curve.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3。適用邊界：時段流量線性變化且無其他水量項，僅求庫容增量。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3. Applicable boundary: Linearly changing flows without other water terms; calculates storage increment only.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水庫時段水量守恆」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Reservoir interval water balance\", which statement holds?","options":["目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行","情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3。"],"optionsEn":["Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan","Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: I0=100 m3/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: I0=100 m3/s; I1=180 m3/s; O0=80 m3/s; O1=120 m3/s; dt=3600 s; dS=((I0+I1)-(O0+O1))*dt/2=144000 m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b280-v15-15","title":"水庫時段水量守恆：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Reservoir interval water balance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水庫時段水量守恆」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Reservoir interval water balance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"先統一流量時戳及單位，以較細時間資料檢查梯形近似，再用水位容量曲線估觀測增量。分列取水、洩漏及溢流，若殘差集中在洪峰時，應查取樣頻率與測站延遲，不先任意修改入流。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align timestamps and units, test the trapezoidal approximation with finer records, and compare storage change inferred from the stage-storage curve. List withdrawals, leakage and spill. Peak-centred residuals require checking sampling and station delays before arbitrarily adjusting inflow. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將時段縮短一半而保留相同端點流量假設，重算庫容增量並說明線性假設改變了什麼。再加入一個時段中間峰值，提出更適合的積分方式。","observationEn":"Site practice: Halve the interval while retaining the endpoint-flow assumptions and recompute storage change, explaining the altered linear trajectory. Add an interior peak and propose an integration approach that can capture its volume.","failure":"注意干擾：流量資料以小時標記卻被當成秒積分，會造成巨大水量誤差；測站傳輸延遲也可能讓入出流錯配。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating hourly labels as seconds creates major volume errors, while telemetry delays can pair mismatched inflow and outflow. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"先統一流量時戳及單位，以較細時間資料檢查梯形近似，再用水位容量曲線估觀測增量。分列取水、洩漏及溢流，若殘差集中在洪峰時，應查取樣頻率與測站延遲，不先任意修改入流。","textEn":"Align timestamps and units, test the trapezoidal approximation with finer records, and compare storage change inferred from the stage-storage curve. List withdrawals, leakage and spill. Peak-centred residuals require checking sampling and station delays before arbitrarily adjusting inflow.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將時段縮短一半而保留相同端點流量假設，重算庫容增量並說明線性假設改變了什麼。再加入一個時段中間峰值，提出更適合的積分方式。","textEn":"Halve the interval while retaining the endpoint-flow assumptions and recompute storage change, explaining the altered linear trajectory. Add an interior peak and propose an integration approach that can capture its volume.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水庫時段水量守恆」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Reservoir interval water balance\"?","options":["先統一流量時戳及單位，以較細時間資料檢查梯形近似，再用水位容量曲線估觀測增量。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成"],"optionsEn":["Align timestamps and units, test the trapezoidal approximation with finer records, and compare storage change inferred from the stage-storage curve.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent"],"answer":0,"explanation":"先統一流量時戳及單位，以較細時間資料檢查梯形近似，再用水位容量曲線估觀測增量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align timestamps and units, test the trapezoidal approximation with finer records, and compare storage change inferred from the stage-storage curve. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b280-v15-16","title":"水庫時段水量守恆：失效診斷","titleEn":"Reservoir interval water balance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水庫時段水量守恆」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Reservoir interval water balance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"流量資料以小時標記卻被當成秒積分，會造成巨大水量誤差；測站傳輸延遲也可能讓入出流錯配。應先做量綱與時間同步檢查。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating hourly labels as seconds creates major volume errors, while telemetry delays can pair mismatched inflow and outflow. Check dimensions and synchronized timing before interpreting apparent storage residuals as physical leakage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：庫容還必須透過現行水位容量曲線與觀測對照，不能把高程差直接當成體積差。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare storage with observations through a current stage-storage relation, because elevation change is not itself a volume change and sediment accumulation can alter that relation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"流量資料以小時標記卻被當成秒積分，會造成巨大水量誤差；測站傳輸延遲也可能讓入出流錯配。應先做量綱與時間同步檢查。","textEn":"Treating hourly labels as seconds creates major volume errors, while telemetry delays can pair mismatched inflow and outflow. Check dimensions and synchronized timing before interpreting apparent storage residuals as physical leakage.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水庫時段水量守恆」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Reservoir interval water balance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","流量資料以小時標記卻被當成秒積分，會造成巨大水量誤差；測站傳輸延遲也可能讓入出流錯配。","同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Treating hourly labels as seconds creates major volume errors, while telemetry delays can pair mismatched inflow and outflow.","Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together"],"answer":1,"explanation":"流量資料以小時標記卻被當成秒積分，會造成巨大水量誤差；測站傳輸延遲也可能讓入出流錯配。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating hourly labels as seconds creates major volume errors, while telemetry delays can pair mismatched inflow and outflow. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b280-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「匯流點的同步疊加」與「下游剩餘通洪額度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Aligned flows at a junction\" and \"Residual downstream flow allowance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b280-v15-17","title":"匯流點的同步疊加：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Aligned flows at a junction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「匯流點的同步疊加」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Aligned flows at a junction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"多水庫出流在下游匯流點相遇時，必須先經河道演算對齊到達時間，不能把不同水庫同一發布時刻的流量直接相加。支流洪峰可能與水庫洩流錯峰或疊峰，傳播過程也有蓄水與波形變化。本單元只在已演算到同一斷面同一時刻的流量上做守恆相加，明確把路由工作放在前置條件。操作比較應保存每股貢獻歷線，才能追溯下游超限來自哪個時段和來源。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「匯流點的同步疊加」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Reservoir releases must be routed and aligned at the downstream junction before addition; flows issued at the same clock time upstream need not arrive together. Tributary peaks can coincide or separate, while channel storage changes timing and shape. This unit adds contributions already routed to one section and instant, explicitly treating routing as a prerequisite. Preserve each contribution hydrograph so a downstream exceedance can be traced to its source and release period rather than to a misleading simultaneous upstream sum. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Aligned flows at a junction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「匯流點的同步疊加」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Aligned flows at a junction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-17-k1","title":"匯流點的同步疊加","titleEn":"Aligned flows at a junction","text":"多水庫出流在下游匯流點相遇時，必須先經河道演算對齊到達時間，不能把不同水庫同一發布時刻的流量直接相加。支流洪峰可能與水庫洩流錯峰或疊峰，傳播過程也有蓄水與波形變化。","textEn":"Reservoir releases must be routed and aligned at the downstream junction before addition; flows issued at the same clock time upstream need not arrive together. Tributary peaks can coincide or separate, while channel storage changes timing and shape.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「匯流點的同步疊加」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Aligned flows at a junction\" is correct?","options":["同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達","下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令","多水庫出流在下游匯流點相遇時，必須先經河道演算對齊到達時間，不能把不同水庫同一發布時刻的流量直接相加。"],"optionsEn":["Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together","Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing","Reservoir releases must be routed and aligned at the downstream junction before addition; flows issued at the same clock time upstream need not arrive together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多水庫出流在下游匯流點相遇時，必須先經河道演算對齊到達時間，不能把不同水庫同一發布時刻的流量直接相加。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Reservoir releases must be routed and aligned at the downstream junction before addition; flows issued at the same clock time upstream need not arrive together. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b280-v15-18","title":"匯流點的同步疊加：定量估算","titleEn":"Aligned flows at a junction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「匯流點的同步疊加」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Aligned flows at a junction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s。適用邊界：三股流量已演算至同一匯流斷面同一時刻，未在此假設原始洩流同步。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s. Applicable boundary: All contributions are routed to the same junction and instant; upstream releases are not assumed simultaneous here. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以示蹤、事件歷線或校準路由模型檢查傳播時間，將各來源到達歷線放在共同時間軸。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check travel timing with tracers, event hydrographs or calibrated routing, and align arriving contributions on one timeline.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s。適用邊界：三股流量已演算至同一匯流斷面同一時刻，未在此假設原始洩流同步。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s. Applicable boundary: All contributions are routed to the same junction and instant; upstream releases are not assumed simultaneous here.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「匯流點的同步疊加」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Aligned flows at a junction\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s。","求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足","預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: QAarr=120 m3/s.","Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied","The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: QAarr=120 m3/s; QBarr=80 m3/s; Qtarr=60 m3/s; Qj=QAarr+QBarr+Qtarr=260 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b280-v15-19","title":"匯流點的同步疊加：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Aligned flows at a junction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「匯流點的同步疊加」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Aligned flows at a junction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以示蹤、事件歷線或校準路由模型檢查傳播時間，將各來源到達歷線放在共同時間軸。用匯流點實測流量核對合計，並保留河段儲水及側向流入項，避免把差額全歸成某座水庫計量誤差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check travel timing with tracers, event hydrographs or calibrated routing, and align arriving contributions on one timeline. Compare their sum with junction observations, retaining reach storage and lateral inputs instead of assigning every residual to one reservoir's meter error. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將支流到達流量增加二十立方公尺每秒重算合計，再把其峰值提前一小時畫出歷線。說明沒有河道路由資料時，哪些聯合操作結論仍無法成立。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase arriving tributary flow by twenty cubic metres per second and recalculate the sum, then shift its peak one hour earlier on a hydrograph. Identify coordination conclusions that remain unsupported without routing information.","failure":"注意干擾：若忽略支流較早到達，可能在預計空窗內增加洩流卻與真正洪峰重疊。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring earlier tributary arrival can place increased release inside an apparent window that actually overlaps the flood peak. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以示蹤、事件歷線或校準路由模型檢查傳播時間，將各來源到達歷線放在共同時間軸。用匯流點實測流量核對合計，並保留河段儲水及側向流入項，避免把差額全歸成某座水庫計量誤差。","textEn":"Check travel timing with tracers, event hydrographs or calibrated routing, and align arriving contributions on one timeline. Compare their sum with junction observations, retaining reach storage and lateral inputs instead of assigning every residual to one reservoir's meter error.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將支流到達流量增加二十立方公尺每秒重算合計，再把其峰值提前一小時畫出歷線。說明沒有河道路由資料時，哪些聯合操作結論仍無法成立。","textEn":"Increase arriving tributary flow by twenty cubic metres per second and recalculate the sum, then shift its peak one hour earlier on a hydrograph. Identify coordination conclusions that remain unsupported without routing information.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「匯流點的同步疊加」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Aligned flows at a junction\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以示蹤、事件歷線或校準路由模型檢查傳播時間，將各來源到達歷線放在共同時間軸。","九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check travel timing with tracers, event hydrographs or calibrated routing, and align arriving contributions on one timeline.","The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以示蹤、事件歷線或校準路由模型檢查傳播時間，將各來源到達歷線放在共同時間軸。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check travel timing with tracers, event hydrographs or calibrated routing, and align arriving contributions on one timeline. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b280-v15-20","title":"匯流點的同步疊加：失效診斷","titleEn":"Aligned flows at a junction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「匯流點的同步疊加」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Aligned flows at a junction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若忽略支流較早到達，可能在預計空窗內增加洩流卻與真正洪峰重疊。需查到達時間分布與預報誤差，而非只比較各水庫的最大出流值。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring earlier tributary arrival can place increased release inside an apparent window that actually overlaps the flood peak. Examine arrival-time uncertainty rather than comparing only the maximum outflow from each reservoir separately. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：操作比較應保存每股貢獻歷線，才能追溯下游超限來自哪個時段和來源。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Preserve each contribution hydrograph so a downstream exceedance can be traced to its source and release period rather than to a misleading simultaneous upstream sum.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若忽略支流較早到達，可能在預計空窗內增加洩流卻與真正洪峰重疊。需查到達時間分布與預報誤差，而非只比較各水庫的最大出流值。","textEn":"Ignoring earlier tributary arrival can place increased release inside an apparent window that actually overlaps the flood peak. Examine arrival-time uncertainty rather than comparing only the maximum outflow from each reservoir separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「匯流點的同步疊加」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Aligned flows at a junction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令","若忽略支流較早到達，可能在預計空窗內增加洩流卻與真正洪峰重疊。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing","Ignoring earlier tributary arrival can place increased release inside an apparent window that actually overlaps the flood peak."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若忽略支流較早到達，可能在預計空窗內增加洩流卻與真正洪峰重疊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring earlier tributary arrival can place increased release inside an apparent window that actually overlaps the flood peak. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b280-v15-21","title":"下游剩餘通洪額度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Residual downstream flow allowance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「下游剩餘通洪額度」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Residual downstream flow allowance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"下游斷面流量限制扣除已到達的支流與其他來源，可得到某一控制貢獻的剩餘額度，但這仍是斷面到達流量而非立即閘門設定。把它轉成水庫出流需要路由、設備能力與爬升限制，也要面對預報誤差。若其他來源已超過限制，負餘額代表該假設組合無法靠非負洩流解決，不能隨意截成零後宣稱安全。規則來源與權責必須清楚，教材僅比較假想限制的數學含義。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「下游剩餘通洪額度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Subtracting arriving tributary and other flows from a downstream limit gives a residual allowance for one contribution, not an immediate gate setting. Routing, outlet capacity, ramp limits and forecast uncertainty intervene before converting it to release. If other sources already exceed the limit, a negative allowance signals infeasibility under the assumptions; clipping it to zero does not restore safety. Identify rule authority and provenance while treating the numerical limit here only as a hypothetical teaching condition. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Residual downstream flow allowance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「下游剩餘通洪額度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Residual downstream flow allowance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-21-k1","title":"下游剩餘通洪額度","titleEn":"Residual downstream flow allowance","text":"下游斷面流量限制扣除已到達的支流與其他來源，可得到某一控制貢獻的剩餘額度，但這仍是斷面到達流量而非立即閘門設定。把它轉成水庫出流需要路由、設備能力與爬升限制，也要面對預報誤差。","textEn":"Subtracting arriving tributary and other flows from a downstream limit gives a residual allowance for one contribution, not an immediate gate setting. Routing, outlet capacity, ramp limits and forecast uncertainty intervene before converting it to release.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「下游剩餘通洪額度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Residual downstream flow allowance\" is correct?","options":["下游斷面流量限制扣除已到達的支流與其他來源，可得到某一控制貢獻的剩餘額度，但這仍是斷面到達流量而非立即閘門設定。","下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令","目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行"],"optionsEn":["Subtracting arriving tributary and other flows from a downstream limit gives a residual allowance for one contribution, not an immediate gate setting.","Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing","Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan"],"answer":0,"explanation":"下游斷面流量限制扣除已到達的支流與其他來源，可得到某一控制貢獻的剩餘額度，但這仍是斷面到達流量而非立即閘門設定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Subtracting arriving tributary and other flows from a downstream limit gives a residual allowance for one contribution, not an immediate gate setting. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b280-v15-22","title":"下游剩餘通洪額度：定量估算","titleEn":"Residual downstream flow allowance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「下游剩餘通洪額度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Residual downstream flow allowance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s。適用邊界：給定假想斷面限制與同步到達流量，不是實際核准洩流量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s. Applicable boundary: Hypothetical section limit with aligned arriving flows, not an authorized reservoir release. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：查核限制對應的斷面、時段及流量定義，再把其他來源以共同時間軸列入。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify the limit's section, period and flow definition, align other contributions, and test tributary uncertainty.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s。適用邊界：給定假想斷面限制與同步到達流量，不是實際核准洩流量。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s. Applicable boundary: Hypothetical section limit with aligned arriving flows, not an authorized reservoir release.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「下游剩餘通洪額度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Residual downstream flow allowance\", which statement holds?","options":["情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s。","集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成"],"optionsEn":["Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qlim=300 m3/s.","Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Qlim=300 m3/s; Qtrib=90 m3/s; Qother=70 m3/s; Qallow=Qlim-Qtrib-Qother=140 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b280-v15-23","title":"下游剩餘通洪額度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Residual downstream flow allowance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「下游剩餘通洪額度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Residual downstream flow allowance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"查核限制對應的斷面、時段及流量定義，再把其他來源以共同時間軸列入。對預報支流做敏感度範圍，使用路由模型檢查水庫能否形成目標到達流量，並確認設備及正式操作規程是否允許。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify the limit's section, period and flow definition, align other contributions, and test tributary uncertainty. Use routing to examine whether a reservoir can produce the target arriving flow, then check equipment constraints and formally approved operating rules. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將支流到達流量提高到每秒二百五十立方公尺，重算餘額並說明負值意義。列出應回報的限制衝突，而不是自行創造一個看似可行的非負數字。","observationEn":"Site practice: Raise tributary arrival to two hundred fifty cubic metres per second and recompute the allowance. Explain a negative result and list the conflicting conditions to report rather than inventing an apparently feasible nonnegative value.","failure":"注意干擾：若把到達額度直接作成上游即時洩流，可能因傳播延遲在錯誤時段超限。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying an arrival allowance directly as an upstream release can exceed the limit at the wrong time because of routing delay. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"查核限制對應的斷面、時段及流量定義，再把其他來源以共同時間軸列入。對預報支流做敏感度範圍，使用路由模型檢查水庫能否形成目標到達流量，並確認設備及正式操作規程是否允許。","textEn":"Verify the limit's section, period and flow definition, align other contributions, and test tributary uncertainty. Use routing to examine whether a reservoir can produce the target arriving flow, then check equipment constraints and formally approved operating rules.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將支流到達流量提高到每秒二百五十立方公尺，重算餘額並說明負值意義。列出應回報的限制衝突，而不是自行創造一個看似可行的非負數字。","textEn":"Raise tributary arrival to two hundred fifty cubic metres per second and recompute the allowance. Explain a negative result and list the conflicting conditions to report rather than inventing an apparently feasible nonnegative value.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「下游剩餘通洪額度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Residual downstream flow allowance\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報","查核限制對應的斷面、時段及流量定義，再把其他來源以共同時間軸列入。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system","Verify the limit's section, period and flow definition, align other contributions, and test tributary uncertainty."],"answer":2,"explanation":"查核限制對應的斷面、時段及流量定義，再把其他來源以共同時間軸列入。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify the limit's section, period and flow definition, align other contributions, and test tributary uncertainty. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b280-v15-24","title":"下游剩餘通洪額度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Residual downstream flow allowance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「下游剩餘通洪額度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Residual downstream flow allowance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若把到達額度直接作成上游即時洩流，可能因傳播延遲在錯誤時段超限。限制也可能隨堤防或下游施工改變，必須確認版本與有效範圍。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying an arrival allowance directly as an upstream release can exceed the limit at the wrong time because of routing delay. Limits may also depend on current downstream conditions, requiring version and validity checks. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：規則來源與權責必須清楚，教材僅比較假想限制的數學含義。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Identify rule authority and provenance while treating the numerical limit here only as a hypothetical teaching condition.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把到達額度直接作成上游即時洩流，可能因傳播延遲在錯誤時段超限。限制也可能隨堤防或下游施工改變，必須確認版本與有效範圍。","textEn":"Applying an arrival allowance directly as an upstream release can exceed the limit at the wrong time because of routing delay. Limits may also depend on current downstream conditions, requiring version and validity checks.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「下游剩餘通洪額度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Residual downstream flow allowance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若把到達額度直接作成上游即時洩流，可能因傳播延遲在錯誤時段超限。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行"],"optionsEn":["Applying an arrival allowance directly as an upstream release can exceed the limit at the wrong time because of routing delay.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan"],"answer":0,"explanation":"若把到達額度直接作成上游即時洩流，可能因傳播延遲在錯誤時段超限。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying an arrival allowance directly as an upstream release can exceed the limit at the wrong time because of routing delay. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b280-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「預洩所需時間窗」與「不相容操作限制」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Time window for prerelease\" and \"Incompatible operating constraints\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b280-v15-25","title":"預洩所需時間窗：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Time window for prerelease: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「預洩所需時間窗」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Time window for prerelease” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"預洩試算需區分原本既定出流與額外釋放所創造的庫容，否則會把同一股水重複計算。可用時間窗還受下游容量、設備爬升、環境要求與預報可靠度影響，不能只用目標體積除最大閘流量。若入流在窗口內增加，淨庫容形成速度會降低；若將來降雨落空，保留供水也有代價。教材以固定額外淨釋放量建立時間尺度，實際方案必須透過完整情境與授權規則比較。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「預洩所需時間窗」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Prerelease analysis distinguishes baseline outflow from additional net release that creates storage; otherwise the same water is counted twice. The available window depends on downstream capacity, ramping, environmental requirements and forecast reliability, not just maximum gate flow. Increasing inflow reduces net storage creation, while a missed storm creates water-supply tradeoffs. This example uses a fixed additional net release to establish a time scale; real alternatives require full scenarios and authorized rules, not direct execution of the arithmetic. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Time window for prerelease” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h.","failure":"常見誤解：「目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「預洩所需時間窗」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Time window for prerelease”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-25-k1","title":"預洩所需時間窗","titleEn":"Time window for prerelease","text":"預洩試算需區分原本既定出流與額外釋放所創造的庫容，否則會把同一股水重複計算。可用時間窗還受下游容量、設備爬升、環境要求與預報可靠度影響，不能只用目標體積除最大閘流量。","textEn":"Prerelease analysis distinguishes baseline outflow from additional net release that creates storage; otherwise the same water is counted twice. The available window depends on downstream capacity, ramping, environmental requirements and forecast reliability, not just maximum gate flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「預洩所需時間窗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Time window for prerelease\" is correct?","options":["目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行","預洩試算需區分原本既定出流與額外釋放所創造的庫容，否則會把同一股水重複計算。","求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足"],"optionsEn":["Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan","Prerelease analysis distinguishes baseline outflow from additional net release that creates storage; otherwise the same water is counted twice.","Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied"],"answer":1,"explanation":"預洩試算需區分原本既定出流與額外釋放所創造的庫容，否則會把同一股水重複計算。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Prerelease analysis distinguishes baseline outflow from additional net release that creates storage; otherwise the same water is counted twice. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b280-v15-26","title":"預洩所需時間窗：定量估算","titleEn":"Time window for prerelease: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「預洩所需時間窗」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Time window for prerelease” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h。適用邊界：額外淨釋放已扣相對基準入流變化，假設可持續且無爬升時間。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h. Applicable boundary: Additional net release already accounts for inflow change relative to baseline, assuming sustained feasibility and no ramp time. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立基準及預洩兩套水量帳，逐時比較新增庫容，而非只加總全部出流。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build baseline and prerelease water ledgers and compare incremental storage hour by hour rather than summing all outflow.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h。適用邊界：額外淨釋放已扣相對基準入流變化，假設可持續且無爬升時間。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h. Applicable boundary: Additional net release already accounts for inflow change relative to baseline, assuming sustained feasibility and no ramp time.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「預洩所需時間窗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Time window for prerelease\", which statement holds?","options":["預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比","九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h。"],"optionsEn":["The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction","The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Vtarget=1800000 m3; Qnetextra=50 m3/s; t=Vtarget/Qnetextra/3600=10 h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b280-v15-27","title":"預洩所需時間窗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Time window for prerelease: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「預洩所需時間窗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Time window for prerelease” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立基準及預洩兩套水量帳，逐時比較新增庫容，而非只加總全部出流。核對窗口內下游條件與爬升限制，對降雨提前、延後或未發生情境分別演算，並保存決策使用的預報版本。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build baseline and prerelease water ledgers and compare incremental storage hour by hour rather than summing all outflow. Check downstream conditions and ramps, replay early, late and absent rainfall scenarios, and preserve the forecast version used for comparison. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將額外淨釋放降到每秒四十立方公尺重算時間，再加入兩小時逐步爬升。說明為何須積分實際增量歷線，並列出方案比較需要的正式限制。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce additional net release to forty cubic metres per second and recalculate time, then introduce a two-hour ramp. Explain why the actual incremental hydrograph needs integration and list formal constraints required for comparing alternatives.","failure":"注意干擾：如果把最大出口能力當成可全程使用的額外淨釋放，會低估所需時間並漏掉下游限制。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating maximum outlet capacity as sustained additional net release understates required time and ignores downstream constraints. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立基準及預洩兩套水量帳，逐時比較新增庫容，而非只加總全部出流。核對窗口內下游條件與爬升限制，對降雨提前、延後或未發生情境分別演算，並保存決策使用的預報版本。","textEn":"Build baseline and prerelease water ledgers and compare incremental storage hour by hour rather than summing all outflow. Check downstream conditions and ramps, replay early, late and absent rainfall scenarios, and preserve the forecast version used for comparison.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將額外淨釋放降到每秒四十立方公尺重算時間，再加入兩小時逐步爬升。說明為何須積分實際增量歷線，並列出方案比較需要的正式限制。","textEn":"Reduce additional net release to forty cubic metres per second and recalculate time, then introduce a two-hour ramp. Explain why the actual incremental hydrograph needs integration and list formal constraints required for comparing alternatives.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「預洩所需時間窗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Time window for prerelease\"?","options":["建立基準及預洩兩套水量帳，逐時比較新增庫容，而非只加總全部出流。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加"],"optionsEn":["Build baseline and prerelease water ledgers and compare incremental storage hour by hour rather than summing all outflow.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase"],"answer":0,"explanation":"建立基準及預洩兩套水量帳，逐時比較新增庫容，而非只加總全部出流。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build baseline and prerelease water ledgers and compare incremental storage hour by hour rather than summing all outflow. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b280-v15-28","title":"預洩所需時間窗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Time window for prerelease: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「預洩所需時間窗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Time window for prerelease” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"如果把最大出口能力當成可全程使用的額外淨釋放，會低估所需時間並漏掉下游限制。預報延後發布時，原先看似足夠的窗口也可能消失。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating maximum outlet capacity as sustained additional net release understates required time and ignores downstream constraints. A later forecast issue can also remove a previously available window, invalidating the earlier feasibility calculation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：教材以固定額外淨釋放量建立時間尺度，實際方案必須透過完整情境與授權規則比較。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This example uses a fixed additional net release to establish a time scale; real alternatives require full scenarios and authorized rules, not direct execution of the arithmetic.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"如果把最大出口能力當成可全程使用的額外淨釋放，會低估所需時間並漏掉下游限制。預報延後發布時，原先看似足夠的窗口也可能消失。","textEn":"Treating maximum outlet capacity as sustained additional net release understates required time and ignores downstream constraints. A later forecast issue can also remove a previously available window, invalidating the earlier feasibility calculation.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「預洩所需時間窗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Time window for prerelease\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","如果把最大出口能力當成可全程使用的額外淨釋放，會低估所需時間並漏掉下游限制。","求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating maximum outlet capacity as sustained additional net release understates required time and ignores downstream constraints.","Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied"],"answer":1,"explanation":"如果把最大出口能力當成可全程使用的額外淨釋放，會低估所需時間並漏掉下游限制。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating maximum outlet capacity as sustained additional net release understates required time and ignores downstream constraints. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b280-v15-29","title":"不相容操作限制：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Incompatible operating constraints: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「不相容操作限制」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Incompatible operating constraints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"多項規則可以轉成同一時段的出流上下界，最大下界若高於最小上界，數學上便沒有共同可行值。這個結果應揭露限制衝突，不能由程式默默刪除較難滿足的條件。某些規則可能有正式優先序或應變程序，但作者不能自行發明權限。模型需保留各限制的來源、有效時間與物理意義，分辨設備能力不足、下游容量衝突及資料錯誤，讓有權人員能檢查並作成可追溯決策。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「不相容操作限制」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Several rules can become release bounds for one interval. If the largest lower bound exceeds the smallest upper bound, no common feasible value exists. Report that conflict rather than silently discarding a difficult condition. Formal priorities or emergency procedures may apply, but a model author cannot invent authority. Retain each bound's source, valid period and physical meaning to distinguish equipment limits, downstream conflicts and data errors, enabling responsible personnel to make a traceable decision. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Incompatible operating constraints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「不相容操作限制」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Incompatible operating constraints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-29-k1","title":"不相容操作限制","titleEn":"Incompatible operating constraints","text":"多項規則可以轉成同一時段的出流上下界，最大下界若高於最小上界，數學上便沒有共同可行值。這個結果應揭露限制衝突，不能由程式默默刪除較難滿足的條件。","textEn":"Several rules can become release bounds for one interval. If the largest lower bound exceeds the smallest upper bound, no common feasible value exists.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「不相容操作限制」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Incompatible operating constraints\" is correct?","options":["求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足","情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果","多項規則可以轉成同一時段的出流上下界，最大下界若高於最小上界，數學上便沒有共同可行值。"],"optionsEn":["Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied","Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences","Several rules can become release bounds for one interval."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多項規則可以轉成同一時段的出流上下界，最大下界若高於最小上界，數學上便沒有共同可行值。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Several rules can become release bounds for one interval. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b280-v15-30","title":"不相容操作限制：定量估算","titleEn":"Incompatible operating constraints: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「不相容操作限制」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Incompatible operating constraints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s。適用邊界：正缺口表示所給同時限制無交集，未自動放寬任何規則。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s. Applicable boundary: A positive gap means the simultaneous stated bounds have no intersection; no rule is automatically relaxed. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將每條限制附上來源、時段與適用水庫，先統一單位及符號，再計交集。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Attach source, interval and reservoir to every constraint, harmonize units and signs, then compute the intersection.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s。適用邊界：正缺口表示所給同時限制無交集，未自動放寬任何規則。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s. Applicable boundary: A positive gap means the simultaneous stated bounds have no intersection; no rule is automatically relaxed.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「不相容操作限制」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Incompatible operating constraints\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s。","集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成","只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L1=90 m3/s.","Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent","Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: L1=90 m3/s; L2=120 m3/s; U1=140 m3/s; U2=100 m3/s; gap=max(L1,L2)-min(U1,U2)=20 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b280-v15-31","title":"不相容操作限制：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Incompatible operating constraints: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「不相容操作限制」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Incompatible operating constraints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將每條限制附上來源、時段與適用水庫，先統一單位及符號，再計交集。若無解，檢查是否誤把不同時段或不同斷面限制混合，確認後輸出衝突清單及責任窗口，不以數值平滑掩蓋問題。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Attach source, interval and reservoir to every constraint, harmonize units and signs, then compute the intersection. For infeasibility, check mixed periods or sections before producing a conflict list and responsible review route rather than smoothing the numbers to hide it. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把第二下界改成每秒九十五立方公尺，重新求交集並說明可行範圍。再列一個資料時段不一致造成假衝突的例子，設計能攔下它的前置檢查。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change the second lower bound to ninety five cubic metres per second and find the feasible interval. Construct a false conflict caused by mismatched time periods and design a preprocessing check that would catch it.","failure":"注意干擾：優化器若自行移除下游上限，可能回傳漂亮目標值卻已違反原問題。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An optimizer that drops a downstream upper bound can return an attractive objective while violating the original problem. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將每條限制附上來源、時段與適用水庫，先統一單位及符號，再計交集。若無解，檢查是否誤把不同時段或不同斷面限制混合，確認後輸出衝突清單及責任窗口，不以數值平滑掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Attach source, interval and reservoir to every constraint, harmonize units and signs, then compute the intersection. For infeasibility, check mixed periods or sections before producing a conflict list and responsible review route rather than smoothing the numbers to hide it.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把第二下界改成每秒九十五立方公尺，重新求交集並說明可行範圍。再列一個資料時段不一致造成假衝突的例子，設計能攔下它的前置檢查。","textEn":"Change the second lower bound to ninety five cubic metres per second and find the feasible interval. Construct a false conflict caused by mismatched time periods and design a preprocessing check that would catch it.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「不相容操作限制」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Incompatible operating constraints\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將每條限制附上來源、時段與適用水庫，先統一單位及符號，再計交集。","同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Attach source, interval and reservoir to every constraint, harmonize units and signs, then compute the intersection.","Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together"],"answer":1,"explanation":"將每條限制附上來源、時段與適用水庫，先統一單位及符號，再計交集。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Attach source, interval and reservoir to every constraint, harmonize units and signs, then compute the intersection. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b280-v15-32","title":"不相容操作限制：失效診斷","titleEn":"Incompatible operating constraints: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「不相容操作限制」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Incompatible operating constraints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"優化器若自行移除下游上限，可能回傳漂亮目標值卻已違反原問題。必須檢查求解狀態及每條限制殘差，不能只看目標函數有改善。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An optimizer that drops a downstream upper bound can return an attractive objective while violating the original problem. Inspect solver status and every constraint residual rather than judging success solely by an improved objective value. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：模型需保留各限制的來源、有效時間與物理意義，分辨設備能力不足、下游容量衝突及資料錯誤，讓有權人員能檢查並作成可追溯決策。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Retain each bound's source, valid period and physical meaning to distinguish equipment limits, downstream conflicts and data errors, enabling responsible personnel to make a traceable decision.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「求解器有回傳數字就代表原本所有操作限制都已滿足」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any number returned by a solver proves that all original operating constraints are satisfied\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"優化器若自行移除下游上限，可能回傳漂亮目標值卻已違反原問題。必須檢查求解狀態及每條限制殘差，不能只看目標函數有改善。","textEn":"An optimizer that drops a downstream upper bound can return an attractive objective while violating the original problem. Inspect solver status and every constraint residual rather than judging success solely by an improved objective value.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「不相容操作限制」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Incompatible operating constraints\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果","優化器若自行移除下游上限，可能回傳漂亮目標值卻已違反原問題。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences","An optimizer that drops a downstream upper bound can return an attractive objective while violating the original problem."],"answer":2,"explanation":"優化器若自行移除下游上限，可能回傳漂亮目標值卻已違反原問題。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An optimizer that drops a downstream upper bound can return an attractive objective while violating the original problem. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b280-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「情境違反率與風險」與「預報改善與獨立驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Scenario violation rate and risk\" and \"Forecast improvement and independent validation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b280-v15-33","title":"情境違反率與風險：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Scenario violation rate and risk: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「情境違反率與風險」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Scenario violation rate and risk” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"聯合操作方案可對每個預報情境計算是否超過下游或庫容限制，再統計違反比例。此比例取決於情境權重、代表性與相關性，不等於已知真實風險，也未描述超限幅度。少數很嚴重的失敗可能比多次輕微超限更重要，因此應同時報告頻率、最大值、持續時間及涉及對象。增加集合成員只改善抽樣解析度的一部分，若共同模型偏差未修正，風險估計仍會系統性失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「情境違反率與風險」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A coordinated plan can be simulated under each forecast scenario to count downstream or storage violations. The fraction depends on weights, representativeness and dependence; it is not a known true risk and says nothing about severity. A few severe failures may matter more than many slight exceedances, so report frequency, magnitude, duration and affected receptors together. More members refine only part of sampling resolution and cannot by themselves remove shared model bias or an omitted failure mechanism. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Scenario violation rate and risk” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「情境違反率與風險」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Scenario violation rate and risk”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-33-k1","title":"情境違反率與風險","titleEn":"Scenario violation rate and risk","text":"聯合操作方案可對每個預報情境計算是否超過下游或庫容限制，再統計違反比例。此比例取決於情境權重、代表性與相關性，不等於已知真實風險，也未描述超限幅度。","textEn":"A coordinated plan can be simulated under each forecast scenario to count downstream or storage violations. The fraction depends on weights, representativeness and dependence; it is not a known true risk and says nothing about severity.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「情境違反率與風險」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Scenario violation rate and risk\" is correct?","options":["聯合操作方案可對每個預報情境計算是否超過下游或庫容限制，再統計違反比例。","情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果","預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比"],"optionsEn":["A coordinated plan can be simulated under each forecast scenario to count downstream or storage violations.","Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences","The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"聯合操作方案可對每個預報情境計算是否超過下游或庫容限制，再統計違反比例。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A coordinated plan can be simulated under each forecast scenario to count downstream or storage violations. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b280-v15-34","title":"情境違反率與風險：定量估算","titleEn":"Scenario violation rate and risk: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「情境違反率與風險」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Scenario violation rate and risk” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless。適用邊界：等權情境違反比例，沒有將百分之六宣稱成核准風險或真實機率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Equally weighted scenario violation fraction, not an approved risk level or established true probability. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對每個情境保存相同限制定義與完整結果，逐一核對超限時間和幅度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Store identical constraint definitions and full results for every scenario, checking violation timing and magnitude individually.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless。適用邊界：等權情境違反比例，沒有將百分之六宣稱成核准風險或真實機率。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Equally weighted scenario violation fraction, not an approved risk level or established true probability.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「情境違反率與風險」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Scenario violation rate and risk\", which statement holds?","options":["九成分位數就是所有可能洪水永遠不會超越的上限","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless。","水庫水位增加一公尺就代表固定不變的一立方公尺庫容增加"],"optionsEn":["The ninetieth percentile is an upper bound that every possible flood must obey","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nv=3 violating-scenarios.","A one-metre reservoir level rise always means a fixed one-cubic-metre storage increase"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: Nv=3 violating-scenarios; N=50 equally-weighted-scenarios; pv=Nv/N=0.06 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b280-v15-35","title":"情境違反率與風險：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Scenario violation rate and risk: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「情境違反率與風險」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Scenario violation rate and risk” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對每個情境保存相同限制定義與完整結果，逐一核對超限時間和幅度。另檢查高後果但低頻情境是否被抽樣遺漏，以保留事件回放測試共同偏差，並明示若成員有權重時應改用加權比例。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Store identical constraint definitions and full results for every scenario, checking violation timing and magnitude individually. Examine omitted rare but consequential cases and replay held-out events for common bias. If members carry weights, explicitly replace the simple count with weighted probability. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持三個違反情境但將集合增加到六十個重算比例，說明為何不能據此自動宣稱更安全。為三個情境補上不同超限幅度和時間，提出更完整比較表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Keep three violating scenarios but enlarge the ensemble to sixty and recalculate the fraction without automatically claiming greater safety. Assign different magnitudes and durations to the three cases and construct a more informative comparison table.","failure":"注意干擾：把輕微超限與長時間嚴重超限都記成一，可能讓不同方案看似同風險。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Coding slight and prolonged severe exceedances identically can make very different plans appear equally risky. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對每個情境保存相同限制定義與完整結果，逐一核對超限時間和幅度。另檢查高後果但低頻情境是否被抽樣遺漏，以保留事件回放測試共同偏差，並明示若成員有權重時應改用加權比例。","textEn":"Store identical constraint definitions and full results for every scenario, checking violation timing and magnitude individually. Examine omitted rare but consequential cases and replay held-out events for common bias. If members carry weights, explicitly replace the simple count with weighted probability.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持三個違反情境但將集合增加到六十個重算比例，說明為何不能據此自動宣稱更安全。為三個情境補上不同超限幅度和時間，提出更完整比較表。","textEn":"Keep three violating scenarios but enlarge the ensemble to sixty and recalculate the fraction without automatically claiming greater safety. Assign different magnitudes and durations to the three cases and construct a more informative comparison table.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「情境違反率與風險」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Scenario violation rate and risk\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","下游剩餘流量額度可不經路由直接當成上游即時閘門指令","對每個情境保存相同限制定義與完整結果，逐一核對超限時間和幅度。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Residual downstream flow allowance can directly become an immediate upstream gate command without routing","Store identical constraint definitions and full results for every scenario, checking violation timing and magnitude individually."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對每個情境保存相同限制定義與完整結果，逐一核對超限時間和幅度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Store identical constraint definitions and full results for every scenario, checking violation timing and magnitude individually. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b280-v15-36","title":"情境違反率與風險：失效診斷","titleEn":"Scenario violation rate and risk: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「情境違反率與風險」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Scenario violation rate and risk” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把輕微超限與長時間嚴重超限都記成一，可能讓不同方案看似同風險。若只報比例而刪除歷線，決策者便無法辨認真正需要應變的後果。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Coding slight and prolonged severe exceedances identically can make very different plans appear equally risky. Reporting only the fraction while discarding hydrographs prevents reviewers from identifying consequences that require a distinct response. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：增加集合成員只改善抽樣解析度的一部分，若共同模型偏差未修正，風險估計仍會系統性失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: More members refine only part of sampling resolution and cannot by themselves remove shared model bias or an omitted failure mechanism.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「情境違反比例相同就代表兩個方案具有完全相同後果」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal scenario violation fractions mean that two plans have identical consequences\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把輕微超限與長時間嚴重超限都記成一，可能讓不同方案看似同風險。若只報比例而刪除歷線，決策者便無法辨認真正需要應變的後果。","textEn":"Coding slight and prolonged severe exceedances identically can make very different plans appear equally risky. Reporting only the fraction while discarding hydrographs prevents reviewers from identifying consequences that require a distinct response.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「情境違反率與風險」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Scenario violation rate and risk\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把輕微超限與長時間嚴重超限都記成一，可能讓不同方案看似同風險。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比"],"optionsEn":["Coding slight and prolonged severe exceedances identically can make very different plans appear equally risky.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"把輕微超限與長時間嚴重超限都記成一，可能讓不同方案看似同風險。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Coding slight and prolonged severe exceedances identically can make very different plans appear equally risky. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b280-v15-37","title":"預報改善與獨立驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Forecast improvement and independent validation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「預報改善與獨立驗證」如何影響洪水預報與水庫聯合操作的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Forecast improvement and independent validation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Flood forecasting and coordinated reservoir operation”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"平均絕對誤差描述流量預報偏離觀測的平均幅度，與參考預報比較可形成相對改善尺度。不同事件、提前時間及流量大小必須公平配對，否則看似改善可能只是測試樣本更容易。校準與驗證要按時間或事件分開，避免同一場洪水的相鄰資料同時進入訓練與測試。平均指標還可能掩蓋洪峰時間或極端事件表現，因此應搭配事件分層與操作後果回放，才能判斷改善是否對聯合調度有用。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「預報改善與獨立驗證」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mean absolute error describes average discharge discrepancy, and comparison with a reference forecast gives a relative improvement scale. Match events, lead times and flow regimes fairly; an easier test sample can mimic improvement. Separate calibration and validation by time or event so neighbouring records from one flood do not leak across sets. Average scores may hide peak-timing or extreme-event errors, requiring stratified evaluation and operational replays before claiming that better forecasting improves coordinated reservoir decisions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Forecast improvement and independent validation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「預報改善與獨立驗證」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Forecast improvement and independent validation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-37-k1","title":"預報改善與獨立驗證","titleEn":"Forecast improvement and independent validation","text":"平均絕對誤差描述流量預報偏離觀測的平均幅度，與參考預報比較可形成相對改善尺度。不同事件、提前時間及流量大小必須公平配對，否則看似改善可能只是測試樣本更容易。","textEn":"Mean absolute error describes average discharge discrepancy, and comparison with a reference forecast gives a relative improvement scale. Match events, lead times and flow regimes fairly; an easier test sample can mimic improvement.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「預報改善與獨立驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Forecast improvement and independent validation\" is correct?","options":["預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比","平均絕對誤差描述流量預報偏離觀測的平均幅度，與參考預報比較可形成相對改善尺度。","集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成"],"optionsEn":["The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction","Mean absolute error describes average discharge discrepancy, and comparison with a reference forecast gives a relative improvement scale.","Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent"],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均絕對誤差描述流量預報偏離觀測的平均幅度，與參考預報比較可形成相對改善尺度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mean absolute error describes average discharge discrepancy, and comparison with a reference forecast gives a relative improvement scale. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b280-v15-38","title":"預報改善與獨立驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Forecast improvement and independent validation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「預報改善與獨立驗證」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Forecast improvement and independent validation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless。適用邊界：同四筆保留樣本與正參考誤差，改善尺度不等於風險降低百分比。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Same four held-out cases with positive reference error; skill is not a percentage reduction in operational risk. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保存訓練截止日與所有預報發布版本，確認參考和新模型使用相同可取得資料。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Preserve training cutoffs and issued forecast versions, ensuring reference and new models use equally available information.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless。適用邊界：同四筆保留樣本與正參考誤差，改善尺度不等於風險降低百分比。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless. Applicable boundary: Same four held-out cases with positive reference error; skill is not a percentage reduction in operational risk.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「預報改善與獨立驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Forecast improvement and independent validation\", which statement holds?","options":["只用發生洪水的日期評分就能公平驗證所有機率預報","同一時刻兩座水庫的出流必然在下游同時到達","原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless。"],"optionsEn":["Scoring only flood dates fairly validates every probabilistic forecast system","Releases from two reservoirs at the same time necessarily arrive downstream together","Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教材輸入，不是現地設計值或操作指令：model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs, not field design values or operating instructions: model-errors=[12,8,20,4] m3/s; reference-errors=[20,15,25,12] m3/s; MAE=44/4=11 m3/s; MAEref=72/4=18 m3/s; skill=1-MAE/MAEref=0.388889 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b280-v15-39","title":"預報改善與獨立驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Forecast improvement and independent validation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「預報改善與獨立驗證」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Forecast improvement and independent validation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保存訓練截止日與所有預報發布版本，確認參考和新模型使用相同可取得資料。逐筆列絕對誤差，再按洪峰、低流與提前時間分層；最後用相同規則回放操作，檢查誤差改善是否真正改變庫容或下游結果。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Preserve training cutoffs and issued forecast versions, ensuring reference and new models use equally available information. List absolute errors and stratify by peaks, low flows and lead time. Replay identical operating rules to test whether better scores actually change storage or downstream outcomes. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將模型第三筆誤差降到十二立方公尺每秒重算改善尺度，其他資料不變。說明仍需哪些峰值時序及操作回放結果，才能判定對防洪決策有實際幫助。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reduce the third model error to twelve cubic metres per second and recompute skill with other values fixed. Identify peak-timing and operating-replay evidence still needed before judging whether the improvement benefits flood decisions.","failure":"注意干擾：用事後修正雨量驗證即時預報會造成資訊洩漏，誤差看似降低卻無法在發布時重現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Verifying a real-time forecast with later-corrected rainfall leaks future information and produces gains unavailable at issue time. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保存訓練截止日與所有預報發布版本，確認參考和新模型使用相同可取得資料。逐筆列絕對誤差，再按洪峰、低流與提前時間分層；最後用相同規則回放操作，檢查誤差改善是否真正改變庫容或下游結果。","textEn":"Preserve training cutoffs and issued forecast versions, ensuring reference and new models use equally available information. List absolute errors and stratify by peaks, low flows and lead time. Replay identical operating rules to test whether better scores actually change storage or downstream outcomes.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將模型第三筆誤差降到十二立方公尺每秒重算改善尺度，其他資料不變。說明仍需哪些峰值時序及操作回放結果，才能判定對防洪決策有實際幫助。","textEn":"Reduce the third model error to twelve cubic metres per second and recompute skill with other values fixed. Identify peak-timing and operating-replay evidence still needed before judging whether the improvement benefits flood decisions.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「預報改善與獨立驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Forecast improvement and independent validation\"?","options":["保存訓練截止日與所有預報發布版本，確認參考和新模型使用相同可取得資料。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","目標庫容除以最大閘流量就能保證預洩方案可執行"],"optionsEn":["Preserve training cutoffs and issued forecast versions, ensuring reference and new models use equally available information.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Target storage divided by maximum gate discharge guarantees an executable prerelease plan"],"answer":0,"explanation":"保存訓練截止日與所有預報發布版本，確認參考和新模型使用相同可取得資料。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Preserve training cutoffs and issued forecast versions, ensuring reference and new models use equally available information. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b280-v15-40","title":"預報改善與獨立驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Forecast improvement and independent validation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"prerequisiteIds":["b280-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「預報改善與獨立驗證」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Forecast improvement and independent validation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用事後修正雨量驗證即時預報會造成資訊洩漏，誤差看似降低卻無法在發布時重現。若模型只改善低流量，也可能未改善最關鍵洪峰操作。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Verifying a real-time forecast with later-corrected rainfall leaks future information and produces gains unavailable at issue time. Improvements concentrated in low flow may also leave the most consequential flood-peak decisions unchanged. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：平均指標還可能掩蓋洪峰時間或極端事件表現，因此應搭配事件分層與操作後果回放，才能判斷改善是否對聯合調度有用。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Average scores may hide peak-timing or extreme-event errors, requiring stratified evaluation and operational replays before claiming that better forecasting improves coordinated reservoir decisions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「預報平均誤差改善百分比必然等於下游洪災風險降低百分比」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The percentage improvement in mean forecast error necessarily equals downstream flood-risk reduction\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b280-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用事後修正雨量驗證即時預報會造成資訊洩漏，誤差看似降低卻無法在發布時重現。若模型只改善低流量，也可能未改善最關鍵洪峰操作。","textEn":"Verifying a real-time forecast with later-corrected rainfall leaks future information and produces gains unavailable at issue time. Improvements concentrated in low flow may also leave the most consequential flood-peak decisions unchanged.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]},{"id":"b280-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「預報改善與獨立驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Forecast improvement and independent validation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","用事後修正雨量驗證即時預報會造成資訊洩漏，誤差看似降低卻無法在發布時重現。","集合中四成成員超越就保證真實洪水機率恰為四成"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Verifying a real-time forecast with later-corrected rainfall leaks future information and produces gains unavailable at issue time.","Forty percent ensemble exceedance guarantees the true flood probability is exactly forty percent"],"answer":1,"explanation":"用事後修正雨量驗證即時預報會造成資訊洩漏，誤差看似降低卻無法在發布時重現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Verifying a real-time forecast with later-corrected rainfall leaks future information and produces gains unavailable at issue time. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-hec-network","v15s-nws-hefs","v15s-cw3e-firo"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b285","title":"海岸養灘工程","titleEn":"Beach nourishment","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以泥沙守恆與監測辨識養灘的短期重塑和長期功能。課程從邊界辨識與資料整理走到水理量化、構造介面及驗證紀錄；每一步把計算結果連回可量測的證據。十個不同單元分別處理關鍵機制，不以名義尺寸或單一通過率代替整體工程判斷，並明列合成算例與現地資料的差別。","summaryEn":"Distinguish nourishment reshaping and long-term function through sediment accounting and monitoring. The course moves from boundary identification and evidence to hydraulic quantification, structural interfaces and verification records. Ten distinct units connect each calculated quantity to measurable evidence. Nominal geometry or a single pass rate does not establish whole-system performance, and synthetic teaching examples remain separate from field observations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-coasts","subcategoryTitle":"海岸、港灣與水資源韌性","subcategoryTitleEn":"Coasts, ports and water-resource resilience","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-coasts","learningTags":["water","water-coasts","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-coast","architectureNodes":[["養灘幾何與方量","Nourishment geometry and volume"],["粒徑相容性","Grain-size compatibility"],["沿岸泥沙收支","Alongshore sediment budget"],["暴風後剖面恢復","Post-storm profile recovery"],["沉降與水平輸運","Settling and horizontal advection"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-coast","labels":["養灘幾何與方量","粒徑相容性","沿岸泥沙收支","暴風後剖面恢復","沉降與水平輸運"],"labelsEn":["Nourishment geometry and volume","Grain-size compatibility","Alongshore sediment budget","Post-storm profile recovery","Settling and horizontal advection"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為原創合成算例，不是地標工程的實測或推薦操作值。教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設長1000m、增寬20m、等厚1.5m，V=Lbt=30000m³；只作矩形填方示意，不是平衡剖面設計。假設增寬由20改為22m而長度、厚度不變，方量30000增至33000m³，增加10%；並不代表養灘維持時間增加10%。重新計算前先列固定條件、單位、適用尺度及可能失效的邊界。把模型敏感度與測量誤差分開，不能將單一參數變化直接當成工程風險或壽命比例。比較兩次結果後，記錄還需要哪些獨立證據，並由負責專業人員判斷適用性。","textEn":"This original synthetic example is neither a landmark measurement nor a recommended operating value. Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume length1000m, added width20m and uniform thickness1.5m. V=Lbt=30000m³ is rectangular accounting, not equilibrium-profile design. Increasing added width from20 to22m at fixed length and thickness raises volume from30000 to33000m³ by10%, without implying10% longer retention. Before recalculating, list fixed conditions, units, applicable scale and boundaries that could fail. Separate model sensitivity from measurement uncertainty: a parameter change does not directly give a proportional change in engineering risk or service life. Compare the results, record independent evidence still needed, and have the responsible specialist determine applicability.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b285-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「養灘幾何與方量」與「固體量與孔隙」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Nourishment geometry and volume\" and \"Solid quantity and porosity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b285-v15-01","title":"養灘幾何與方量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Nourishment geometry and volume: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「養灘幾何與方量」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Nourishment geometry and volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"養灘計量先界定施工面、斷面及高程基準，填入的鬆方與完成後剖面方量不必相等。矩形示意適合練習尺寸核對，真實海灘有斜坡與沿岸變化，需要逐剖面積分；初始灘寬也不保證風浪重塑後仍維持相同位置。 假設長1000m、增寬20m、等厚1.5m，V=Lbt=30000m³；只作矩形填方示意，不是平衡剖面設計。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「養灘幾何與方量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Nourishment accounting begins with placement limits, sections and a vertical datum. Delivered loose volume need not equal completed profile volume. A rectangular illustration helps check dimensions, but a real beach varies alongshore and across its slopes and requires section integration; initial width does not guarantee the same shoreline after wave-driven redistribution. Assume length1000m, added width20m and uniform thickness1.5m. V=Lbt=30000m³ is rectangular accounting, not equilibrium-profile design. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Nourishment geometry and volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「養灘幾何與方量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Nourishment geometry and volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-01-k1","title":"養灘幾何與方量","titleEn":"Nourishment geometry and volume","text":"養灘計量先界定施工面、斷面及高程基準，填入的鬆方與完成後剖面方量不必相等。矩形示意適合練習尺寸核對，真實海灘有斜坡與沿岸變化，需要逐剖面積分；初始灘寬也不保證風浪重塑後仍維持相同位置。","textEn":"Nourishment accounting begins with placement limits, sections and a vertical datum. Delivered loose volume need not equal completed profile volume.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「養灘幾何與方量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Nourishment geometry and volume\" is correct?","options":["施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。","養灘計量先界定施工面、斷面及高程基準，填入的鬆方與完成後剖面方量不必相等。","孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。"],"optionsEn":["The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season.","Nourishment accounting begins with placement limits, sections and a vertical datum.","Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains."],"answer":1,"explanation":"養灘計量先界定施工面、斷面及高程基準，填入的鬆方與完成後剖面方量不必相等。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Nourishment accounting begins with placement limits, sections and a vertical datum. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b285-v15-02","title":"養灘幾何與方量：定量估算","titleEn":"Nourishment geometry and volume: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「養灘幾何與方量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Nourishment geometry and volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設長1000m、增寬20m、等厚1.5m，V=Lbt=30000m³；只作矩形填方示意，不是平衡剖面設計。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume length1000m, added width20m and uniform thickness1.5m. V=Lbt=30000m³ is rectangular accounting, not equilibrium-profile design. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在同一基準上畫施工前後剖面，標出超出量測範圍的部分並逐區積分。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw before-and-after sections on one datum, identify unmeasured portions and integrate by area.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設長1000m、增寬20m、等厚1.5m，V=Lbt=30000m³；只作矩形填方示意，不是平衡剖面設計。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume length1000m, added width20m and uniform thickness1.5m. V=Lbt=30000m³ is rectangular accounting, not equilibrium-profile design.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「養灘幾何與方量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Nourishment geometry and volume\", which statement holds?","options":["新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。","乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement.","Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b285-v15-03","title":"養灘幾何與方量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Nourishment geometry and volume: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「養灘幾何與方量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Nourishment geometry and volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在同一基準上畫施工前後剖面，標出超出量測範圍的部分並逐區積分。核對計量採原狀、鬆方或完成方，與運輸票據比較差異時保留孔隙和含水定義。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw before-and-after sections on one datum, identify unmeasured portions and integrate by area. State whether quantities are in-situ, loose or completed volumes; retain porosity and moisture definitions when comparing survey totals with delivery records. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在同一基準上畫施工前後剖面，標出超出量測範圍的部分並逐區積分。核對計量採原狀、鬆方或完成方，與運輸票據比較差異時保留孔隙和含水定義。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw before-and-after sections on one datum, identify unmeasured portions and integrate by area. State whether quantities are in-situ, loose or completed volumes; retain porosity and moisture definitions when comparing survey totals with delivery records.","failure":"注意干擾：用車船鬆方直接代替完成灘體會把孔隙變化誤認為流失，缺少近岸水下剖面又會漏掉重分布砂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Substituting delivered loose volume for completed beach volume confuses porosity change with loss. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在同一基準上畫施工前後剖面，標出超出量測範圍的部分並逐區積分。核對計量採原狀、鬆方或完成方，與運輸票據比較差異時保留孔隙和含水定義。","textEn":"Draw before-and-after sections on one datum, identify unmeasured portions and integrate by area. State whether quantities are in-situ, loose or completed volumes; retain porosity and moisture definitions when comparing survey totals with delivery records.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在同一基準上畫施工前後剖面，標出超出量測範圍的部分並逐區積分。核對計量採原狀、鬆方或完成方，與運輸票據比較差異時保留孔隙和含水定義。","textEn":"Draw before-and-after sections on one datum, identify unmeasured portions and integrate by area. State whether quantities are in-situ, loose or completed volumes; retain porosity and moisture definitions when comparing survey totals with delivery records.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「養灘幾何與方量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Nourishment geometry and volume\"?","options":["在同一基準上畫施工前後剖面，標出超出量測範圍的部分並逐區積分。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。"],"optionsEn":["Draw before-and-after sections on one datum, identify unmeasured portions and integrate by area.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在同一基準上畫施工前後剖面，標出超出量測範圍的部分並逐區積分。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw before-and-after sections on one datum, identify unmeasured portions and integrate by area. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b285-v15-04","title":"養灘幾何與方量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Nourishment geometry and volume: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「養灘幾何與方量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Nourishment geometry and volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用車船鬆方直接代替完成灘體會把孔隙變化誤認為流失，缺少近岸水下剖面又會漏掉重分布砂。表面變寬不能單獨證明整個活動剖面已增加足夠儲砂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Substituting delivered loose volume for completed beach volume confuses porosity change with loss. Missing submerged sections conceal redistributed sand, and a wider dry beach alone does not establish added storage across the active profile. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設長1000m、增寬20m、等厚1.5m，V=Lbt=30000m³；只作矩形填方示意，不是平衡剖面設計。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: V=Lbt=30000m³ is rectangular accounting, not equilibrium-profile design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用車船鬆方直接代替完成灘體會把孔隙變化誤認為流失，缺少近岸水下剖面又會漏掉重分布砂。表面變寬不能單獨證明整個活動剖面已增加足夠儲砂。","textEn":"Substituting delivered loose volume for completed beach volume confuses porosity change with loss. Missing submerged sections conceal redistributed sand, and a wider dry beach alone does not establish added storage across the active profile.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「養灘幾何與方量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Nourishment geometry and volume\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","用車船鬆方直接代替完成灘體會把孔隙變化誤認為流失，缺少近岸水下剖面又會漏掉重分布砂。","孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Substituting delivered loose volume for completed beach volume confuses porosity change with loss.","Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用車船鬆方直接代替完成灘體會把孔隙變化誤認為流失，缺少近岸水下剖面又會漏掉重分布砂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Substituting delivered loose volume for completed beach volume confuses porosity change with loss. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b285-v15-05","title":"固體量與孔隙：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Solid quantity and porosity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「固體量與孔隙」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Solid quantity and porosity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"養灘材料以固體顆粒量追蹤比較穩定，因為排水及壓密會改變外觀體積。乾質量換算需用顆粒密度而非濕容重，孔隙率亦須對應相同材料狀態；黏土團塊或貝殼會使單一密度近似失準，不能只憑船艙刻度結算泥沙收支。 假設鬆方10000m³、孔隙率0.40、顆粒密度2650kg/m³，乾砂質量V(1−n)ρs=15900000kg；不含孔隙水。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「固體量與孔隙」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Tracking solid grains helps distinguish material movement from drainage and compaction. Dry-mass conversion requires grain density rather than wet bulk density, with porosity defined for the same condition. Clay aggregates or shells can invalidate a single-density approximation, so hopper readings alone cannot close the sediment balance. Assume bulk volume10000m³, porosity0.40 and grain density2650kg/m³. Dry mass V(1−n)ρs=15900000kg, excluding pore water. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Solid quantity and porosity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「固體量與孔隙」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Solid quantity and porosity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-05-k1","title":"固體量與孔隙","titleEn":"Solid quantity and porosity","text":"養灘材料以固體顆粒量追蹤比較穩定，因為排水及壓密會改變外觀體積。乾質量換算需用顆粒密度而非濕容重，孔隙率亦須對應相同材料狀態；黏土團塊或貝殼會使單一密度近似失準，不能只憑船艙刻度結算泥沙收支。","textEn":"Tracking solid grains helps distinguish material movement from drainage and compaction. Dry-mass conversion requires grain density rather than wet bulk density, with porosity defined for the same condition.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「固體量與孔隙」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Solid quantity and porosity\" is correct?","options":["孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。","借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。","養灘材料以固體顆粒量追蹤比較穩定，因為排水及壓密會改變外觀體積。"],"optionsEn":["Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains.","A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention.","Tracking solid grains helps distinguish material movement from drainage and compaction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"養灘材料以固體顆粒量追蹤比較穩定，因為排水及壓密會改變外觀體積。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Tracking solid grains helps distinguish material movement from drainage and compaction. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b285-v15-06","title":"固體量與孔隙：定量估算","titleEn":"Solid quantity and porosity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「固體量與孔隙」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Solid quantity and porosity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設鬆方10000m³、孔隙率0.40、顆粒密度2650kg/m³，乾砂質量V(1−n)ρs=15900000kg；不含孔隙水。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume bulk volume10000m³, porosity0.40 and grain density2650kg/m³. Dry mass V(1−n)ρs=15900000kg, excluding pore water. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：取具代表性的乾濕樣本，分別量含水、顆粒密度及堆積體積，保留採樣位置與重複試驗。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Collect representative wet and dry samples, measuring moisture, grain density and bulk volume with locations and replicates.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設鬆方10000m³、孔隙率0.40、顆粒密度2650kg/m³，乾砂質量V(1−n)ρs=15900000kg；不含孔隙水。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume bulk volume10000m³, porosity0.40 and grain density2650kg/m³. Dry mass V(1−n)ρs=15900000kg, excluding pore water.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「固體量與孔隙」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Solid quantity and porosity\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。","暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month.","All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b285-v15-07","title":"固體量與孔隙：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Solid quantity and porosity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「固體量與孔隙」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Solid quantity and porosity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"取具代表性的乾濕樣本，分別量含水、顆粒密度及堆積體積，保留採樣位置與重複試驗。把含水造成的重量變化和真正乾固體輸入分開，再檢查換算是否使用同一孔隙定義。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Collect representative wet and dry samples, measuring moisture, grain density and bulk volume with locations and replicates. Separate water-weight changes from dry-solid input, and verify that every conversion uses the same definition of void space. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：取具代表性的乾濕樣本，分別量含水、顆粒密度及堆積體積，保留採樣位置與重複試驗。把含水造成的重量變化和真正乾固體輸入分開，再檢查換算是否使用同一孔隙定義。","observationEn":"Site practice: Collect representative wet and dry samples, measuring moisture, grain density and bulk volume with locations and replicates. Separate water-weight changes from dry-solid input, and verify that every conversion uses the same definition of void space.","failure":"注意干擾：若濕砂質量被當成乾砂，輸入固體會被高估，排水後看似大量砂消失。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating wet mass as dry mass overstates solid input and makes drainage resemble major sand loss. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"取具代表性的乾濕樣本，分別量含水、顆粒密度及堆積體積，保留採樣位置與重複試驗。把含水造成的重量變化和真正乾固體輸入分開，再檢查換算是否使用同一孔隙定義。","textEn":"Collect representative wet and dry samples, measuring moisture, grain density and bulk volume with locations and replicates. Separate water-weight changes from dry-solid input, and verify that every conversion uses the same definition of void space.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"取具代表性的乾濕樣本，分別量含水、顆粒密度及堆積體積，保留採樣位置與重複試驗。把含水造成的重量變化和真正乾固體輸入分開，再檢查換算是否使用同一孔隙定義。","textEn":"Collect representative wet and dry samples, measuring moisture, grain density and bulk volume with locations and replicates. Separate water-weight changes from dry-solid input, and verify that every conversion uses the same definition of void space.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「固體量與孔隙」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Solid quantity and porosity\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","取具代表性的乾濕樣本，分別量含水、顆粒密度及堆積體積，保留採樣位置與重複試驗。","濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Collect representative wet and dry samples, measuring moisture, grain density and bulk volume with locations and replicates.","An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"取具代表性的乾濕樣本，分別量含水、顆粒密度及堆積體積，保留採樣位置與重複試驗。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Collect representative wet and dry samples, measuring moisture, grain density and bulk volume with locations and replicates. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b285-v15-08","title":"固體量與孔隙：失效診斷","titleEn":"Solid quantity and porosity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「固體量與孔隙」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Solid quantity and porosity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若濕砂質量被當成乾砂，輸入固體會被高估，排水後看似大量砂消失。不同批次含貝殼與細料時，沿用同一密度也可能製造不存在的收支缺口。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating wet mass as dry mass overstates solid input and makes drainage resemble major sand loss. Variable shell and fine content also makes a single borrowed density create an artificial deficit in the sediment budget. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設鬆方10000m³、孔隙率0.40、顆粒密度2650kg/m³，乾砂質量V(1−n)ρs=15900000kg；不含孔隙水。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Dry mass V(1−n)ρs=15900000kg, excluding pore water.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若濕砂質量被當成乾砂，輸入固體會被高估，排水後看似大量砂消失。不同批次含貝殼與細料時，沿用同一密度也可能製造不存在的收支缺口。","textEn":"Treating wet mass as dry mass overstates solid input and makes drainage resemble major sand loss. Variable shell and fine content also makes a single borrowed density create an artificial deficit in the sediment budget.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「固體量與孔隙」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Solid quantity and porosity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。","若濕砂質量被當成乾砂，輸入固體會被高估，排水後看似大量砂消失。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention.","Treating wet mass as dry mass overstates solid input and makes drainage resemble major sand loss."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若濕砂質量被當成乾砂，輸入固體會被高估，排水後看似大量砂消失。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating wet mass as dry mass overstates solid input and makes drainage resemble major sand loss. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b285-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「粒徑相容性」與「活動剖面平移」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Grain-size compatibility\" and \"Active-profile translation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b285-v15-09","title":"粒徑相容性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Grain-size compatibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「粒徑相容性」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Grain-size compatibility” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"借砂與原灘的中值粒徑可作第一層比較，但單一比值會隱藏級配、細料與顆粒形狀。不同粒群在波流中有不同沉降及搬運行為，較粗不必然在所有位置都更好；材料選擇還牽涉生態、灘坡和使用功能，需把各種證據並列。 假設借砂D50=0.45mm、原灘D50=0.30mm，比值1.50；不能據此單獨判定全級配相容或保留率。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「粒徑相容性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Median size offers an initial comparison between borrow material and native sand, but one ratio hides grading, fines and particle shape. Different fractions settle and move differently under waves and currents. Coarser is not universally better, and selection also involves ecology, beach slope and intended use, requiring several complementary observations. Assume borrow D50=0.45mm and native D50=0.30mm. Their ratio is1.50; this alone establishes neither grading compatibility nor retention. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Grain-size compatibility” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「粒徑相容性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Grain-size compatibility”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-09-k1","title":"粒徑相容性","titleEn":"Grain-size compatibility","text":"借砂與原灘的中值粒徑可作第一層比較，但單一比值會隱藏級配、細料與顆粒形狀。不同粒群在波流中有不同沉降及搬運行為，較粗不必然在所有位置都更好；材料選擇還牽涉生態、灘坡和使用功能，需把各種證據並列。","textEn":"Median size offers an initial comparison between borrow material and native sand, but one ratio hides grading, fines and particle shape. Different fractions settle and move differently under waves and currents.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「粒徑相容性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Grain-size compatibility\" is correct?","options":["借砂與原灘的中值粒徑可作第一層比較，但單一比值會隱藏級配、細料與顆粒形狀。","借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。","新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。"],"optionsEn":["Median size offers an initial comparison between borrow material and native sand, but one ratio hides grading, fines and particle shape.","A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention.","Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"借砂與原灘的中值粒徑可作第一層比較，但單一比值會隱藏級配、細料與顆粒形狀。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Median size offers an initial comparison between borrow material and native sand, but one ratio hides grading, fines and particle shape. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b285-v15-10","title":"粒徑相容性：定量估算","titleEn":"Grain-size compatibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「粒徑相容性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Grain-size compatibility” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設借砂D50=0.45mm、原灘D50=0.30mm，比值1.50；不能據此單獨判定全級配相容或保留率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume borrow D50=0.45mm and native D50=0.30mm. Their ratio is1.50; this alone establishes neither grading compatibility nor retention. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將完整累積粒徑曲線並排，核對細料比例及取樣深度，避免只比中值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare complete cumulative size curves, checking fines and sampling depth rather than only medians.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設借砂D50=0.45mm、原灘D50=0.30mm，比值1.50；不能據此單獨判定全級配相容或保留率。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume borrow D50=0.45mm and native D50=0.30mm. Their ratio is1.50; this alone establishes neither grading compatibility nor retention.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「粒徑相容性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Grain-size compatibility\", which statement holds?","options":["乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。"],"optionsEn":["Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b285-v15-11","title":"粒徑相容性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Grain-size compatibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「粒徑相容性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Grain-size compatibility” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將完整累積粒徑曲線並排，核對細料比例及取樣深度，避免只比中值。另記顆粒形狀、污染篩查與原灘季節變化，說明哪些物理或環境條件仍沒有代表性樣本。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare complete cumulative size curves, checking fines and sampling depth rather than only medians. Record particle shape, contaminant screening and seasonal native variability, identifying physical or environmental conditions for which representative field samples remain unavailable. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將完整累積粒徑曲線並排，核對細料比例及取樣深度，避免只比中值。另記顆粒形狀、污染篩查與原灘季節變化，說明哪些物理或環境條件仍沒有代表性樣本。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare complete cumulative size curves, checking fines and sampling depth rather than only medians. Record particle shape, contaminant screening and seasonal native variability, identifying physical or environmental conditions for which representative field samples remain unavailable.","failure":"注意干擾：中值相同的兩批材料可能有完全不同的細料尾端，入水後一批產生長距離濁羽、另一批迅速沉降。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Two materials with identical medians may have very different fine tails; one generates a long plume while another settles quickly. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將完整累積粒徑曲線並排，核對細料比例及取樣深度，避免只比中值。另記顆粒形狀、污染篩查與原灘季節變化，說明哪些物理或環境條件仍沒有代表性樣本。","textEn":"Compare complete cumulative size curves, checking fines and sampling depth rather than only medians. Record particle shape, contaminant screening and seasonal native variability, identifying physical or environmental conditions for which representative field samples remain unavailable.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將完整累積粒徑曲線並排，核對細料比例及取樣深度，避免只比中值。另記顆粒形狀、污染篩查與原灘季節變化，說明哪些物理或環境條件仍沒有代表性樣本。","textEn":"Compare complete cumulative size curves, checking fines and sampling depth rather than only medians. Record particle shape, contaminant screening and seasonal native variability, identifying physical or environmental conditions for which representative field samples remain unavailable.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「粒徑相容性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Grain-size compatibility\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。","將完整累積粒徑曲線並排，核對細料比例及取樣深度，避免只比中值。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again.","Compare complete cumulative size curves, checking fines and sampling depth rather than only medians."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將完整累積粒徑曲線並排，核對細料比例及取樣深度，避免只比中值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare complete cumulative size curves, checking fines and sampling depth rather than only medians. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b285-v15-12","title":"粒徑相容性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Grain-size compatibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「粒徑相容性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Grain-size compatibility” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"中值相同的兩批材料可能有完全不同的細料尾端，入水後一批產生長距離濁羽、另一批迅速沉降。只使用中值配比會錯估輸運與環境影響。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Two materials with identical medians may have very different fine tails; one generates a long plume while another settles quickly. Median-only matching therefore misrepresents both transport behavior and environmental consequences of placement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設借砂D50=0.45mm、原灘D50=0.30mm，比值1.50；不能據此單獨判定全級配相容或保留率。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Their ratio is1.50; this alone establishes neither grading compatibility nor retention.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"中值相同的兩批材料可能有完全不同的細料尾端，入水後一批產生長距離濁羽、另一批迅速沉降。只使用中值配比會錯估輸運與環境影響。","textEn":"Two materials with identical medians may have very different fine tails; one generates a long plume while another settles quickly. Median-only matching therefore misrepresents both transport behavior and environmental consequences of placement.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「粒徑相容性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Grain-size compatibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["中值相同的兩批材料可能有完全不同的細料尾端，入水後一批產生長距離濁羽、另一批迅速沉降。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。"],"optionsEn":["Two materials with identical medians may have very different fine tails; one generates a long plume while another settles quickly.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"中值相同的兩批材料可能有完全不同的細料尾端，入水後一批產生長距離濁羽、另一批迅速沉降。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Two materials with identical medians may have very different fine tails; one generates a long plume while another settles quickly. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b285-v15-13","title":"活動剖面平移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Active-profile translation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「活動剖面平移」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Active-profile translation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"把新增體積分配到假想活動剖面，可估計岸線平移的量級，但須先指定陸側高度與閉合水深。實際剖面會調整坡度並沿岸交換泥沙，閉合深度也受觀測期影響；平行平移只是一項幾何假設，不能將計算結果直接當成施工後岸線預測。 假設V=30000m³、沿岸長1000m、閉合深5m、陸側高2m，Δy=V/[L(hc+B)]=4.286m；只限平行平移。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「活動剖面平移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Distributing added volume across an assumed active profile gives a shoreline-displacement scale after specifying berm elevation and closure depth. Real profiles change slope and exchange sand alongshore, and closure depth depends on the observation period. Parallel translation is a geometric assumption, not a direct forecast of the actual post-construction beach shoreline. Assume V=30000m³, length1000m, closure depth5m and berm elevation2m. Parallel translation Δy=V/[L(hc+B)]=4.286m. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Active-profile translation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「活動剖面平移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Active-profile translation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-13-k1","title":"活動剖面平移","titleEn":"Active-profile translation","text":"把新增體積分配到假想活動剖面，可估計岸線平移的量級，但須先指定陸側高度與閉合水深。實際剖面會調整坡度並沿岸交換泥沙，閉合深度也受觀測期影響；平行平移只是一項幾何假設，不能將計算結果直接當成施工後岸線預測。","textEn":"Distributing added volume across an assumed active profile gives a shoreline-displacement scale after specifying berm elevation and closure depth. Real profiles change slope and exchange sand alongshore, and closure depth depends on the observation period.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「活動剖面平移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Active-profile translation\" is correct?","options":["新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。","把新增體積分配到假想活動剖面，可估計岸線平移的量級，但須先指定陸側高度與閉合水深。","年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。"],"optionsEn":["Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement.","Distributing added volume across an assumed active profile gives a shoreline-displacement scale after specifying berm elevation and closure depth.","An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把新增體積分配到假想活動剖面，可估計岸線平移的量級，但須先指定陸側高度與閉合水深。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Distributing added volume across an assumed active profile gives a shoreline-displacement scale after specifying berm elevation and closure depth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b285-v15-14","title":"活動剖面平移：定量估算","titleEn":"Active-profile translation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「活動剖面平移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Active-profile translation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設V=30000m³、沿岸長1000m、閉合深5m、陸側高2m，Δy=V/[L(hc+B)]=4.286m；只限平行平移。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume V=30000m³, length1000m, closure depth5m and berm elevation2m. Parallel translation Δy=V/[L(hc+B)]=4.286m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：清楚標出剖面上下界和零高程，測試閉合深度不同時結果如何改變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark profile limits and the vertical origin and test alternative closure depths.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設V=30000m³、沿岸長1000m、閉合深5m、陸側高2m，Δy=V/[L(hc+B)]=4.286m；只限平行平移。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume V=30000m³, length1000m, closure depth5m and berm elevation2m. Parallel translation Δy=V/[L(hc+B)]=4.286m.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「活動剖面平移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Active-profile translation\", which statement holds?","options":["暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。","濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast.","An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b285-v15-15","title":"活動剖面平移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Active-profile translation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「活動剖面平移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Active-profile translation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"清楚標出剖面上下界和零高程，測試閉合深度不同時結果如何改變。用多季節水陸聯測剖面比較實際重塑，將沿岸漏失、坡形變化及測量誤差另列，不強迫資料吻合平移。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark profile limits and the vertical origin and test alternative closure depths. Compare multiple seasonal land-and-water surveys with the translation estimate, listing alongshore exchange, slope adjustment and measurement error rather than forcing the measured observations to fit. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：清楚標出剖面上下界和零高程，測試閉合深度不同時結果如何改變。用多季節水陸聯測剖面比較實際重塑，將沿岸漏失、坡形變化及測量誤差另列，不強迫資料吻合平移。","observationEn":"Site practice: Mark profile limits and the vertical origin and test alternative closure depths. Compare multiple seasonal land-and-water surveys with the translation estimate, listing alongshore exchange, slope adjustment and measurement error rather than forcing the measured observations to fit.","failure":"注意干擾：把短期觀測不到變化的位置當成永久閉合深度，會高估岸線移動量；若近岸形成砂壩，材料仍在剖面內卻未出現在乾灘，使僅看岸線的判讀失真。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating a temporarily inactive depth as permanent closure can overstate shoreline movement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"清楚標出剖面上下界和零高程，測試閉合深度不同時結果如何改變。用多季節水陸聯測剖面比較實際重塑，將沿岸漏失、坡形變化及測量誤差另列，不強迫資料吻合平移。","textEn":"Mark profile limits and the vertical origin and test alternative closure depths. Compare multiple seasonal land-and-water surveys with the translation estimate, listing alongshore exchange, slope adjustment and measurement error rather than forcing the measured observations to fit.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"清楚標出剖面上下界和零高程，測試閉合深度不同時結果如何改變。用多季節水陸聯測剖面比較實際重塑，將沿岸漏失、坡形變化及測量誤差另列，不強迫資料吻合平移。","textEn":"Mark profile limits and the vertical origin and test alternative closure depths. Compare multiple seasonal land-and-water surveys with the translation estimate, listing alongshore exchange, slope adjustment and measurement error rather than forcing the measured observations to fit.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「活動剖面平移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Active-profile translation\"?","options":["清楚標出剖面上下界和零高程，測試閉合深度不同時結果如何改變。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。"],"optionsEn":["Mark profile limits and the vertical origin and test alternative closure depths.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season."],"answer":0,"explanation":"清楚標出剖面上下界和零高程，測試閉合深度不同時結果如何改變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark profile limits and the vertical origin and test alternative closure depths. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b285-v15-16","title":"活動剖面平移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Active-profile translation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「活動剖面平移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Active-profile translation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把短期觀測不到變化的位置當成永久閉合深度，會高估岸線移動量；若近岸形成砂壩，材料仍在剖面內卻未出現在乾灘，使僅看岸線的判讀失真。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating a temporarily inactive depth as permanent closure can overstate shoreline movement. A nearshore bar may retain sand within the profile without widening the dry beach, misleading interpretations based on shoreline position alone. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設V=30000m³、沿岸長1000m、閉合深5m、陸側高2m，Δy=V/[L(hc+B)]=4.286m；只限平行平移。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Parallel translation Δy=V/[L(hc+B)]=4.286m.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把短期觀測不到變化的位置當成永久閉合深度，會高估岸線移動量；若近岸形成砂壩，材料仍在剖面內卻未出現在乾灘，使僅看岸線的判讀失真。","textEn":"Treating a temporarily inactive depth as permanent closure can overstate shoreline movement. A nearshore bar may retain sand within the profile without widening the dry beach, misleading interpretations based on shoreline position alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「活動剖面平移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Active-profile translation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把短期觀測不到變化的位置當成永久閉合深度，會高估岸線移動量；若近岸形成砂壩，材料仍在剖面內卻未出現在乾灘，使僅看岸線的判讀失真。","年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Treating a temporarily inactive depth as permanent closure can overstate shoreline movement.","An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把短期觀測不到變化的位置當成永久閉合深度，會高估岸線移動量；若近岸形成砂壩，材料仍在剖面內卻未出現在乾灘，使僅看岸線的判讀失真。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating a temporarily inactive depth as permanent closure can overstate shoreline movement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b285-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「沿岸泥沙收支」與「壓密與體積變化」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Alongshore sediment budget\" and \"Compaction and apparent volume loss\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b285-v15-17","title":"沿岸泥沙收支：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Alongshore sediment budget: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「沿岸泥沙收支」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alongshore sediment budget” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"養灘區不是封閉容器，上下游輸砂差和跨岸交換共同改變儲砂。年度平均通量只適合所定義邊界與時段，暴風、港口阻砂及補砂事件可能打破平穩假設；應先確認輸入輸出各自的符號與單位，再討論需要維持的功能。 假設僅沿岸輸入30000、輸出45000m³/year，dV/dt=−15000m³/year；若通量固定5year，儲量減75000m³。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沿岸泥沙收支」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A nourishment reach is not a sealed container: alongshore flux differences and cross-shore exchange alter storage. Annual mean transport applies only to its specified boundaries and period. Storms, harbor interception and new placements can break stationarity, so signs and units must be established before discussing the intended coastal function to maintain. Assume only alongshore input30000 and output45000m³/year. dV/dt=−15000m³/year; fixed fluxes over5years reduce storage75000m³. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alongshore sediment budget” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沿岸泥沙收支」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alongshore sediment budget”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-17-k1","title":"沿岸泥沙收支","titleEn":"Alongshore sediment budget","text":"養灘區不是封閉容器，上下游輸砂差和跨岸交換共同改變儲砂。年度平均通量只適合所定義邊界與時段，暴風、港口阻砂及補砂事件可能打破平穩假設；應先確認輸入輸出各自的符號與單位，再討論需要維持的功能。","textEn":"A nourishment reach is not a sealed container: alongshore flux differences and cross-shore exchange alter storage. Annual mean transport applies only to its specified boundaries and period.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沿岸泥沙收支」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Alongshore sediment budget\" is correct?","options":["年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。","乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。","養灘區不是封閉容器，上下游輸砂差和跨岸交換共同改變儲砂。"],"optionsEn":["An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month.","Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume.","A nourishment reach is not a sealed container: alongshore flux differences and cross-shore exchange alter storage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"養灘區不是封閉容器，上下游輸砂差和跨岸交換共同改變儲砂。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A nourishment reach is not a sealed container: alongshore flux differences and cross-shore exchange alter storage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b285-v15-18","title":"沿岸泥沙收支：定量估算","titleEn":"Alongshore sediment budget: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沿岸泥沙收支」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alongshore sediment budget” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設僅沿岸輸入30000、輸出45000m³/year，dV/dt=−15000m³/year；若通量固定5year，儲量減75000m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume only alongshore input30000 and output45000m³/year. dV/dt=−15000m³/year; fixed fluxes over5years reduce storage75000m³. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在地圖上標示每個通量邊界、正方向及可觀測證據，檢查是否漏掉近岸或風成砂。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map each flux boundary, sign and observational evidence, checking nearshore and windblown pathways.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設僅沿岸輸入30000、輸出45000m³/year，dV/dt=−15000m³/year；若通量固定5year，儲量減75000m³。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume only alongshore input30000 and output45000m³/year. dV/dt=−15000m³/year; fixed fluxes over5years reduce storage75000m³.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沿岸泥沙收支」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Alongshore sediment budget\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。","粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero.","Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b285-v15-19","title":"沿岸泥沙收支：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Alongshore sediment budget: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沿岸泥沙收支」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alongshore sediment budget” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在地圖上標示每個通量邊界、正方向及可觀測證據，檢查是否漏掉近岸或風成砂。用獨立地形差量測試收支殘差，並把不同年份的風暴條件分開而不是只看長期平均。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map each flux boundary, sign and observational evidence, checking nearshore and windblown pathways. Test budget residuals against independent elevation change and distinguish storm conditions between years rather than relying exclusively on a single long-term average. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在地圖上標示每個通量邊界、正方向及可觀測證據，檢查是否漏掉近岸或風成砂。用獨立地形差量測試收支殘差，並把不同年份的風暴條件分開而不是只看長期平均。","observationEn":"Site practice: Map each flux boundary, sign and observational evidence, checking nearshore and windblown pathways. Test budget residuals against independent elevation change and distinguish storm conditions between years rather than relying exclusively on a single long-term average.","failure":"注意干擾：同一砂量在兩個相鄰邊界重複計入會製造假盈餘，忽略跨岸砂壩交換則容易將季節儲存誤認永久流失。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Double-counting sediment at adjacent boundaries creates an artificial surplus, while omitted cross-shore bar exchange makes seasonal storage resemble permanent loss. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在地圖上標示每個通量邊界、正方向及可觀測證據，檢查是否漏掉近岸或風成砂。用獨立地形差量測試收支殘差，並把不同年份的風暴條件分開而不是只看長期平均。","textEn":"Map each flux boundary, sign and observational evidence, checking nearshore and windblown pathways. Test budget residuals against independent elevation change and distinguish storm conditions between years rather than relying exclusively on a single long-term average.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在地圖上標示每個通量邊界、正方向及可觀測證據，檢查是否漏掉近岸或風成砂。用獨立地形差量測試收支殘差，並把不同年份的風暴條件分開而不是只看長期平均。","textEn":"Map each flux boundary, sign and observational evidence, checking nearshore and windblown pathways. Test budget residuals against independent elevation change and distinguish storm conditions between years rather than relying exclusively on a single long-term average.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沿岸泥沙收支」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Alongshore sediment budget\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在地圖上標示每個通量邊界、正方向及可觀測證據，檢查是否漏掉近岸或風成砂。","孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Map each flux boundary, sign and observational evidence, checking nearshore and windblown pathways.","Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在地圖上標示每個通量邊界、正方向及可觀測證據，檢查是否漏掉近岸或風成砂。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map each flux boundary, sign and observational evidence, checking nearshore and windblown pathways. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b285-v15-20","title":"沿岸泥沙收支：失效診斷","titleEn":"Alongshore sediment budget: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沿岸泥沙收支」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alongshore sediment budget” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"同一砂量在兩個相鄰邊界重複計入會製造假盈餘，忽略跨岸砂壩交換則容易將季節儲存誤認永久流失。平穩外推也可能低估一次大事件的主導作用。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Double-counting sediment at adjacent boundaries creates an artificial surplus, while omitted cross-shore bar exchange makes seasonal storage resemble permanent loss. Stationary extrapolation can also miss the dominant influence of one large event. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設僅沿岸輸入30000、輸出45000m³/year，dV/dt=−15000m³/year；若通量固定5year，儲量減75000m³。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume only alongshore input30000 and output45000m³/year. dV/dt=−15000m³/year; fixed fluxes over5years reduce storage75000m³.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"同一砂量在兩個相鄰邊界重複計入會製造假盈餘，忽略跨岸砂壩交換則容易將季節儲存誤認永久流失。平穩外推也可能低估一次大事件的主導作用。","textEn":"Double-counting sediment at adjacent boundaries creates an artificial surplus, while omitted cross-shore bar exchange makes seasonal storage resemble permanent loss. Stationary extrapolation can also miss the dominant influence of one large event.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沿岸泥沙收支」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Alongshore sediment budget\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。","同一砂量在兩個相鄰邊界重複計入會製造假盈餘，忽略跨岸砂壩交換則容易將季節儲存誤認永久流失。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume.","Double-counting sediment at adjacent boundaries creates an artificial surplus, while omitted cross-shore bar exchange makes seasonal storage resemble permanent loss."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同一砂量在兩個相鄰邊界重複計入會製造假盈餘，忽略跨岸砂壩交換則容易將季節儲存誤認永久流失。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Double-counting sediment at adjacent boundaries creates an artificial surplus, while omitted cross-shore bar exchange makes seasonal storage resemble permanent loss. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b285-v15-21","title":"壓密與體積變化：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Compaction and apparent volume loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「壓密與體積變化」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Compaction and apparent volume loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"同一乾固體量隨孔隙改變而呈現不同鬆方，養灘完工後地形下降不一定全是輸砂。需要把粒子輸出和孔隙水排除分開，同時注意級配分選會改變密實狀態；幾何測量提供外形，而固體收支才幫助辨認真正材料流失。 假設固體體積18000m³保持不變，孔隙率0.40時鬆方30000m³，降到0.35後V=18000/0.65=27692.3m³。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壓密與體積變化」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An unchanged quantity of solids occupies different bulk volumes as porosity changes, so post-placement lowering need not be entirely sediment transport. Separate particle export from drainage while recognizing that sorting changes packing. Geometry describes the exterior, whereas solid accounting helps identify actual offshore material loss. Assume unchanged solid volume18000m³. Bulk volume is30000m³ at porosity0.40 and27692.3m³ at porosity0.35, using V=Vs/(1−n). Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Compaction and apparent volume loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「壓密與體積變化」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Compaction and apparent volume loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-21-k1","title":"壓密與體積變化","titleEn":"Compaction and apparent volume loss","text":"同一乾固體量隨孔隙改變而呈現不同鬆方，養灘完工後地形下降不一定全是輸砂。需要把粒子輸出和孔隙水排除分開，同時注意級配分選會改變密實狀態；幾何測量提供外形，而固體收支才幫助辨認真正材料流失。","textEn":"An unchanged quantity of solids occupies different bulk volumes as porosity changes, so post-placement lowering need not be entirely sediment transport. Separate particle export from drainage while recognizing that sorting changes packing.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壓密與體積變化」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Compaction and apparent volume loss\" is correct?","options":["同一乾固體量隨孔隙改變而呈現不同鬆方，養灘完工後地形下降不一定全是輸砂。","乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。","暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。"],"optionsEn":["An unchanged quantity of solids occupies different bulk volumes as porosity changes, so post-placement lowering need not be entirely sediment transport.","Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume.","All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同一乾固體量隨孔隙改變而呈現不同鬆方，養灘完工後地形下降不一定全是輸砂。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An unchanged quantity of solids occupies different bulk volumes as porosity changes, so post-placement lowering need not be entirely sediment transport. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b285-v15-22","title":"壓密與體積變化：定量估算","titleEn":"Compaction and apparent volume loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「壓密與體積變化」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Compaction and apparent volume loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設固體體積18000m³保持不變，孔隙率0.40時鬆方30000m³，降到0.35後V=18000/0.65=27692.3m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume unchanged solid volume18000m³. Bulk volume is30000m³ at porosity0.40 and27692.3m³ at porosity0.35, using V=Vs/(1−n). Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在相同範圍重測剖面並取密度樣本，將沉降量與孔隙改變能解釋的部分比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Resurvey identical limits and sample density, comparing lowering with the portion explained by changing void space.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設固體體積18000m³保持不變，孔隙率0.40時鬆方30000m³，降到0.35後V=18000/0.65=27692.3m³。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume unchanged solid volume18000m³. Bulk volume is30000m³ at porosity0.40 and27692.3m³ at porosity0.35, using V=Vs/(1−n).","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「壓密與體積變化」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Compaction and apparent volume loss\", which statement holds?","options":["濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。"],"optionsEn":["An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b285-v15-23","title":"壓密與體積變化：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Compaction and apparent volume loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「壓密與體積變化」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Compaction and apparent volume loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在相同範圍重測剖面並取密度樣本，將沉降量與孔隙改變能解釋的部分比較。保持乾固體定義一致，另查波流輸出證據，避免以任意壓密係數吸收所有量測差異。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Resurvey identical limits and sample density, comparing lowering with the portion explained by changing void space. Maintain a consistent dry-solid definition and inspect transport evidence separately rather than automatically absorbing every discrepancy into an arbitrary compaction factor. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在相同範圍重測剖面並取密度樣本，將沉降量與孔隙改變能解釋的部分比較。保持乾固體定義一致，另查波流輸出證據，避免以任意壓密係數吸收所有量測差異。","observationEn":"Site practice: Resurvey identical limits and sample density, comparing lowering with the portion explained by changing void space. Maintain a consistent dry-solid definition and inspect transport evidence separately rather than automatically absorbing every discrepancy into an arbitrary compaction factor.","failure":"注意干擾：濕砂表面下降若全部記成侵蝕，會高估維護需求；反過來把真正沖失都稱為壓密，則隱藏砂源不足。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Calling all surface lowering erosion overstates maintenance needs, while labeling real export as compaction conceals inadequate supply. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在相同範圍重測剖面並取密度樣本，將沉降量與孔隙改變能解釋的部分比較。保持乾固體定義一致，另查波流輸出證據，避免以任意壓密係數吸收所有量測差異。","textEn":"Resurvey identical limits and sample density, comparing lowering with the portion explained by changing void space. Maintain a consistent dry-solid definition and inspect transport evidence separately rather than automatically absorbing every discrepancy into an arbitrary compaction factor.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在相同範圍重測剖面並取密度樣本，將沉降量與孔隙改變能解釋的部分比較。保持乾固體定義一致，另查波流輸出證據，避免以任意壓密係數吸收所有量測差異。","textEn":"Resurvey identical limits and sample density, comparing lowering with the portion explained by changing void space. Maintain a consistent dry-solid definition and inspect transport evidence separately rather than automatically absorbing every discrepancy into an arbitrary compaction factor.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「壓密與體積變化」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Compaction and apparent volume loss\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。","在相同範圍重測剖面並取密度樣本，將沉降量與孔隙改變能解釋的部分比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention.","Resurvey identical limits and sample density, comparing lowering with the portion explained by changing void space."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在相同範圍重測剖面並取密度樣本，將沉降量與孔隙改變能解釋的部分比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Resurvey identical limits and sample density, comparing lowering with the portion explained by changing void space. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b285-v15-24","title":"壓密與體積變化：失效診斷","titleEn":"Compaction and apparent volume loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「壓密與體積變化」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Compaction and apparent volume loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"濕砂表面下降若全部記成侵蝕，會高估維護需求；反過來把真正沖失都稱為壓密，則隱藏砂源不足。缺少密度與地形的共同證據無法區分兩種機制。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Calling all surface lowering erosion overstates maintenance needs, while labeling real export as compaction conceals inadequate supply. Without paired density and terrain evidence, the two mechanisms cannot reliably be distinguished in the completed beach. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設固體體積18000m³保持不變，孔隙率0.40時鬆方30000m³，降到0.35後V=18000/0.65=27692.3m³。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Bulk volume is30000m³ at porosity0.40 and27692.3m³ at porosity0.35, using V=Vs/(1−n).","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"濕砂表面下降若全部記成侵蝕，會高估維護需求；反過來把真正沖失都稱為壓密，則隱藏砂源不足。缺少密度與地形的共同證據無法區分兩種機制。","textEn":"Calling all surface lowering erosion overstates maintenance needs, while labeling real export as compaction conceals inadequate supply. Without paired density and terrain evidence, the two mechanisms cannot reliably be distinguished in the completed beach.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「壓密與體積變化」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Compaction and apparent volume loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["濕砂表面下降若全部記成侵蝕，會高估維護需求；反過來把真正沖失都稱為壓密，則隱藏砂源不足。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。"],"optionsEn":["Calling all surface lowering erosion overstates maintenance needs, while labeling real export as compaction conceals inadequate supply.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast."],"answer":0,"explanation":"濕砂表面下降若全部記成侵蝕，會高估維護需求；反過來把真正沖失都稱為壓密，則隱藏砂源不足。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Calling all surface lowering erosion overstates maintenance needs, while labeling real export as compaction conceals inadequate supply. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b285-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「暴風後剖面恢復」與「高程偏差與方量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Post-storm profile recovery\" and \"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b285-v15-25","title":"暴風後剖面恢復：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Post-storm profile recovery: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「暴風後剖面恢復」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Post-storm profile recovery” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"暴風可把上灘砂移到水下，後續較緩波況再將部分材料送回，因此恢復率需明示控制範圍與基準。相同乾灘體積恢復不代表粒群或灘形完全恢復，觀測期間亦會左右比例；應同時追蹤總量、位置與功能而非只追一個百分比。 假設固定調查範圍暴風減少20000m³，之後回增8000m³，仍缺12000m³、恢復率40%；未證明其餘砂永久外移。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「暴風後剖面恢復」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Storms can move upper-beach sand offshore and calmer waves return part of it. A recovery fraction therefore requires explicit survey limits and a reference state. Restored dry-beach volume does not imply identical grading or shape, and the observation interval affects the fraction; track quantity, geographical position and function together. Assume a fixed survey area loses20000m³ in a storm and later gains8000m³. Deficit remains12000m³ and recovery is40%, without proving permanent export. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Post-storm profile recovery” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「暴風後剖面恢復」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Post-storm profile recovery”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-25-k1","title":"暴風後剖面恢復","titleEn":"Post-storm profile recovery","text":"暴風可把上灘砂移到水下，後續較緩波況再將部分材料送回，因此恢復率需明示控制範圍與基準。相同乾灘體積恢復不代表粒群或灘形完全恢復，觀測期間亦會左右比例；應同時追蹤總量、位置與功能而非只追一個百分比。","textEn":"Storms can move upper-beach sand offshore and calmer waves return part of it. A recovery fraction therefore requires explicit survey limits and a reference state.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「暴風後剖面恢復」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Post-storm profile recovery\" is correct?","options":["暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。","暴風可把上灘砂移到水下，後續較緩波況再將部分材料送回，因此恢復率需明示控制範圍與基準。","增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。"],"optionsEn":["All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast.","Storms can move upper-beach sand offshore and calmer waves return part of it.","Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero."],"answer":1,"explanation":"暴風可把上灘砂移到水下，後續較緩波況再將部分材料送回，因此恢復率需明示控制範圍與基準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Storms can move upper-beach sand offshore and calmer waves return part of it. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b285-v15-26","title":"暴風後剖面恢復：定量估算","titleEn":"Post-storm profile recovery: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「暴風後剖面恢復」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Post-storm profile recovery” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設固定調查範圍暴風減少20000m³，之後回增8000m³，仍缺12000m³、恢復率40%；未證明其餘砂永久外移。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a fixed survey area loses20000m³ in a storm and later gains8000m³. Deficit remains12000m³ and recovery is40%, without proving permanent export. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保留暴風前、後及恢復期的同範圍剖面，分別記上灘與近岸砂壩的量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Retain matching pre-storm, post-storm and recovery surveys, separating upper-beach and nearshore-bar storage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設固定調查範圍暴風減少20000m³，之後回增8000m³，仍缺12000m³、恢復率40%；未證明其餘砂永久外移。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a fixed survey area loses20000m³ in a storm and later gains8000m³. Deficit remains12000m³ and recovery is40%, without proving permanent export.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「暴風後剖面恢復」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Post-storm profile recovery\", which statement holds?","options":["粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。","孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again.","Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b285-v15-27","title":"暴風後剖面恢復：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Post-storm profile recovery: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「暴風後剖面恢復」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Post-storm profile recovery” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保留暴風前、後及恢復期的同範圍剖面，分別記上灘與近岸砂壩的量。核對水位和季節條件，將未觀測水深列為未知，而不把那部分材料自動列為損失。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Retain matching pre-storm, post-storm and recovery surveys, separating upper-beach and nearshore-bar storage. Check water level and season, marking unobserved depths as unknown rather than automatically treating their material as lost from the system. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保留暴風前、後及恢復期的同範圍剖面，分別記上灘與近岸砂壩的量。核對水位和季節條件，將未觀測水深列為未知，而不把那部分材料自動列為損失。","observationEn":"Site practice: Retain matching pre-storm, post-storm and recovery surveys, separating upper-beach and nearshore-bar storage. Check water level and season, marking unobserved depths as unknown rather than automatically treating their material as lost from the system.","failure":"注意干擾：恢復期只量乾灘會忽略仍在近岸的庫存，調查邊界移動又可能創造假恢復。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Dry-beach-only monitoring misses nearshore storage, and moving survey boundaries can create artificial recovery. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保留暴風前、後及恢復期的同範圍剖面，分別記上灘與近岸砂壩的量。核對水位和季節條件，將未觀測水深列為未知，而不把那部分材料自動列為損失。","textEn":"Retain matching pre-storm, post-storm and recovery surveys, separating upper-beach and nearshore-bar storage. Check water level and season, marking unobserved depths as unknown rather than automatically treating their material as lost from the system.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保留暴風前、後及恢復期的同範圍剖面，分別記上灘與近岸砂壩的量。核對水位和季節條件，將未觀測水深列為未知，而不把那部分材料自動列為損失。","textEn":"Retain matching pre-storm, post-storm and recovery surveys, separating upper-beach and nearshore-bar storage. Check water level and season, marking unobserved depths as unknown rather than automatically treating their material as lost from the system.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「暴風後剖面恢復」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Post-storm profile recovery\"?","options":["保留暴風前、後及恢復期的同範圍剖面，分別記上灘與近岸砂壩的量。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。"],"optionsEn":["Retain matching pre-storm, post-storm and recovery surveys, separating upper-beach and nearshore-bar storage.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"保留暴風前、後及恢復期的同範圍剖面，分別記上灘與近岸砂壩的量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Retain matching pre-storm, post-storm and recovery surveys, separating upper-beach and nearshore-bar storage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b285-v15-28","title":"暴風後剖面恢復：失效診斷","titleEn":"Post-storm profile recovery: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「暴風後剖面恢復」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Post-storm profile recovery” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"恢復期只量乾灘會忽略仍在近岸的庫存，調查邊界移動又可能創造假恢復。若依單一百分比決定補砂，可能反覆搬入材料而沒有處理真正輸砂路徑。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Dry-beach-only monitoring misses nearshore storage, and moving survey boundaries can create artificial recovery. Basing replenishment on one percentage can repeatedly add material without addressing the actual sediment pathways responsible for observed change. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設固定調查範圍暴風減少20000m³，之後回增8000m³，仍缺12000m³、恢復率40%；未證明其餘砂永久外移。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Deficit remains12000m³ and recovery is40%, without proving permanent export.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"恢復期只量乾灘會忽略仍在近岸的庫存，調查邊界移動又可能創造假恢復。若依單一百分比決定補砂，可能反覆搬入材料而沒有處理真正輸砂路徑。","textEn":"Dry-beach-only monitoring misses nearshore storage, and moving survey boundaries can create artificial recovery. Basing replenishment on one percentage can repeatedly add material without addressing the actual sediment pathways responsible for observed change.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「暴風後剖面恢復」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Post-storm profile recovery\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","恢復期只量乾灘會忽略仍在近岸的庫存，調查邊界移動又可能創造假恢復。","增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Dry-beach-only monitoring misses nearshore storage, and moving survey boundaries can create artificial recovery.","Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero."],"answer":1,"explanation":"恢復期只量乾灘會忽略仍在近岸的庫存，調查邊界移動又可能創造假恢復。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Dry-beach-only monitoring misses nearshore storage, and moving survey boundaries can create artificial recovery. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b285-v15-29","title":"高程偏差與方量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「高程偏差與方量」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Elevation bias and volume uncertainty” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"大面積相減對共同高程偏差非常敏感，許多測點並不能消除同一基準造成的系統誤差。兩期獨立的整面偏差可用不確定度傳播估計量級，但不能與逐格獨立噪音混為一談；這項區別決定應改善控制點還是加密量測。 假設面積100000m²，兩期各有獨立整面高程標準不確定度0.03m，σV=A√2σz=4242.6m³；不是逐格獨立誤差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「高程偏差與方量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Large-area differencing is sensitive to coherent vertical bias, and many points do not remove an error shared by one datum. Independent whole-survey offsets can be propagated to estimate uncertainty, but they must not be confused with independent cell noise; that distinction determines whether better control or denser sampling is needed. Assume area100000m² and independent coherent survey offsets with standard uncertainty0.03m each. σV=A√2σz=4242.6m³, not independent cell error. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Elevation bias and volume uncertainty” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「高程偏差與方量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Elevation bias and volume uncertainty”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-29-k1","title":"高程偏差與方量","titleEn":"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty","text":"大面積相減對共同高程偏差非常敏感，許多測點並不能消除同一基準造成的系統誤差。兩期獨立的整面偏差可用不確定度傳播估計量級，但不能與逐格獨立噪音混為一談；這項區別決定應改善控制點還是加密量測。","textEn":"Large-area differencing is sensitive to coherent vertical bias, and many points do not remove an error shared by one datum. Independent whole-survey offsets can be propagated to estimate uncertainty, but they must not be confused with independent cell noise; that distinction determines whether better control or denser sampling is needed.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高程偏差與方量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty\" is correct?","options":["增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。","濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。","大面積相減對共同高程偏差非常敏感，許多測點並不能消除同一基準造成的系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero.","An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration.","Large-area differencing is sensitive to coherent vertical bias, and many points do not remove an error shared by one datum."],"answer":2,"explanation":"大面積相減對共同高程偏差非常敏感，許多測點並不能消除同一基準造成的系統誤差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Large-area differencing is sensitive to coherent vertical bias, and many points do not remove an error shared by one datum. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b285-v15-30","title":"高程偏差與方量：定量估算","titleEn":"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「高程偏差與方量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Elevation bias and volume uncertainty” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設面積100000m²，兩期各有獨立整面高程標準不確定度0.03m，σV=A√2σz=4242.6m³；不是逐格獨立誤差。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume area100000m² and independent coherent survey offsets with standard uncertainty0.03m each. σV=A√2σz=4242.6m³, not independent cell error. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用穩定地物及外部控制檢查每期共同偏差，分開報告隨機散布與高程系統分量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use stable features and external control to check common offsets, reporting random scatter separately from systematic elevation components.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設面積100000m²，兩期各有獨立整面高程標準不確定度0.03m，σV=A√2σz=4242.6m³；不是逐格獨立誤差。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume area100000m² and independent coherent survey offsets with standard uncertainty0.03m each. σV=A√2σz=4242.6m³, not independent cell error.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高程偏差與方量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。","借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season.","A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b285-v15-31","title":"高程偏差與方量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「高程偏差與方量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Elevation bias and volume uncertainty” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用穩定地物及外部控制檢查每期共同偏差，分開報告隨機散布與高程系統分量。重算方量差的不確定度時明列相關性，若兩期共用同一偏差則不可直接套獨立平方和。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use stable features and external control to check common offsets, reporting random scatter separately from systematic elevation components. State correlations when propagating volume uncertainty; shared bias across both epochs does not permit the same independent sum-of-squares calculation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用穩定地物及外部控制檢查每期共同偏差，分開報告隨機散布與高程系統分量。重算方量差的不確定度時明列相關性，若兩期共用同一偏差則不可直接套獨立平方和。","observationEn":"Site practice: Use stable features and external control to check common offsets, reporting random scatter separately from systematic elevation components. State correlations when propagating volume uncertainty; shared bias across both epochs does not permit the same independent sum-of-squares calculation.","failure":"注意干擾：把整面偏差除以測點數平方根會虛構極高精度，使很小的地形差被誤判為侵蝕。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Dividing coherent bias by the square root of point count invents precision and makes small elevation differences appear significant. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用穩定地物及外部控制檢查每期共同偏差，分開報告隨機散布與高程系統分量。重算方量差的不確定度時明列相關性，若兩期共用同一偏差則不可直接套獨立平方和。","textEn":"Use stable features and external control to check common offsets, reporting random scatter separately from systematic elevation components. State correlations when propagating volume uncertainty; shared bias across both epochs does not permit the same independent sum-of-squares calculation.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用穩定地物及外部控制檢查每期共同偏差，分開報告隨機散布與高程系統分量。重算方量差的不確定度時明列相關性，若兩期共用同一偏差則不可直接套獨立平方和。","textEn":"Use stable features and external control to check common offsets, reporting random scatter separately from systematic elevation components. State correlations when propagating volume uncertainty; shared bias across both epochs does not permit the same independent sum-of-squares calculation.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高程偏差與方量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","用穩定地物及外部控制檢查每期共同偏差，分開報告隨機散布與高程系統分量。","年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Use stable features and external control to check common offsets, reporting random scatter separately from systematic elevation components.","An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用穩定地物及外部控制檢查每期共同偏差，分開報告隨機散布與高程系統分量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use stable features and external control to check common offsets, reporting random scatter separately from systematic elevation components. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b285-v15-32","title":"高程偏差與方量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「高程偏差與方量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Elevation bias and volume uncertainty” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把整面偏差除以測點數平方根會虛構極高精度，使很小的地形差被誤判為侵蝕。共同控制點移動也可能讓兩次調查一起偏移而難以自行察覺。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Dividing coherent bias by the square root of point count invents precision and makes small elevation differences appear significant. Moving common control may also shift both surveys together, escaping detection within the survey network itself. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設面積100000m²，兩期各有獨立整面高程標準不確定度0.03m，σV=A√2σz=4242.6m³；不是逐格獨立誤差。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume area100000m² and independent coherent survey offsets with standard uncertainty0.03m each. σV=A√2σz=4242.6m³, not independent cell error.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「增加測點數一定能把共同高程基準偏差平均到零。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding more survey points always averages a common datum bias to zero.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把整面偏差除以測點數平方根會虛構極高精度，使很小的地形差被誤判為侵蝕。共同控制點移動也可能讓兩次調查一起偏移而難以自行察覺。","textEn":"Dividing coherent bias by the square root of point count invents precision and makes small elevation differences appear significant. Moving common control may also shift both surveys together, escaping detection within the survey network itself.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高程偏差與方量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Elevation bias and volume uncertainty\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。","把整面偏差除以測點數平方根會虛構極高精度，使很小的地形差被誤判為侵蝕。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration.","Dividing coherent bias by the square root of point count invents precision and makes small elevation differences appear significant."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把整面偏差除以測點數平方根會虛構極高精度，使很小的地形差被誤判為侵蝕。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Dividing coherent bias by the square root of point count invents precision and makes small elevation differences appear significant. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b285-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「背景扣除與濁羽通量」與「沉降與水平輸運」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Background correction and plume flux\" and \"Settling and horizontal advection\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b285-v15-33","title":"背景扣除與濁羽通量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Background correction and plume flux: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「背景扣除與濁羽通量」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Background correction and plume flux” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"濁度光學訊號不直接等於懸浮泥沙質量，需要採樣校正且區分自然背景。橫斷面通量取決於濃度與速度的共同分布，均勻完全混合只是示意；估算增量輸送量不能替代環境許可，粒徑、沉降與暴露時間仍須分別解釋。 假設均勻濃度150mg/L、背景20mg/L，增量130mg/L=0.13kg/m³，流量2m³/s，增量質量通量0.26kg/s。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「背景扣除與濁羽通量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An optical turbidity signal is not directly suspended-sediment mass; sampling calibration and background separation are required. Section flux depends jointly on concentration and velocity, with complete uniform mixing only an illustration. Estimated incremental transport does not establish environmental compliance; grading, settling and exposure duration remain separate questions. Assume uniform concentration150mg/L and background20mg/L. Increment130mg/L=0.13kg/m³; at2m³/s, incremental mass flux is0.26kg/s. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Background correction and plume flux” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「背景扣除與濁羽通量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Background correction and plume flux”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-33-k1","title":"背景扣除與濁羽通量","titleEn":"Background correction and plume flux","text":"濁度光學訊號不直接等於懸浮泥沙質量，需要採樣校正且區分自然背景。橫斷面通量取決於濃度與速度的共同分布，均勻完全混合只是示意；估算增量輸送量不能替代環境許可，粒徑、沉降與暴露時間仍須分別解釋。","textEn":"An optical turbidity signal is not directly suspended-sediment mass; sampling calibration and background separation are required. Section flux depends jointly on concentration and velocity, with complete uniform mixing only an illustration.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「背景扣除與濁羽通量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Background correction and plume flux\" is correct?","options":["濁度光學訊號不直接等於懸浮泥沙質量，需要採樣校正且區分自然背景。","濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。","粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。"],"optionsEn":["An optical turbidity signal is not directly suspended-sediment mass; sampling calibration and background separation are required.","An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration.","Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again."],"answer":0,"explanation":"濁度光學訊號不直接等於懸浮泥沙質量，需要採樣校正且區分自然背景。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An optical turbidity signal is not directly suspended-sediment mass; sampling calibration and background separation are required. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b285-v15-34","title":"背景扣除與濁羽通量：定量估算","titleEn":"Background correction and plume flux: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「背景扣除與濁羽通量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Background correction and plume flux” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設均勻濃度150mg/L、背景20mg/L，增量130mg/L=0.13kg/m³，流量2m³/s，增量質量通量0.26kg/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume uniform concentration150mg/L and background20mg/L. Increment130mg/L=0.13kg/m³; at2m³/s, incremental mass flux is0.26kg/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步取得背景、作業區濃度和流速，檢查背景點是否真的位於影響區外。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample background, working-area concentration and velocity together, verifying that the background station lies outside the affected plume.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設均勻濃度150mg/L、背景20mg/L，增量130mg/L=0.13kg/m³，流量2m³/s，增量質量通量0.26kg/s。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume uniform concentration150mg/L and background20mg/L. Increment130mg/L=0.13kg/m³; at2m³/s, incremental mass flux is0.26kg/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「背景扣除與濁羽通量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Background correction and plume flux\", which statement holds?","options":["孔隙水排出造成的重量下降全部代表養灘砂粒流失。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","新增砂量除以灘長就能得到岸線前進的長度。"],"optionsEn":["Every decrease in weight caused by drainage represents loss of nourishment grains.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Dividing added sand volume by beach length alone gives shoreline advancement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b285-v15-35","title":"背景扣除與濁羽通量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Background correction and plume flux: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「背景扣除與濁羽通量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Background correction and plume flux” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步取得背景、作業區濃度和流速，檢查背景點是否真的位於影響區外。以分層樣本辨識垂向差異，記錄光學校正式及適用粒群，將許可條件和質量計算分別比對。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample background, working-area concentration and velocity together, verifying that the background station lies outside the affected plume. Use depth-resolved samples to identify stratification, retain optical calibration and applicable grading, and assess permit conditions separately from mass accounting. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：同步取得背景、作業區濃度和流速，檢查背景點是否真的位於影響區外。以分層樣本辨識垂向差異，記錄光學校正式及適用粒群，將許可條件和質量計算分別比對。","observationEn":"Site practice: Sample background, working-area concentration and velocity together, verifying that the background station lies outside the affected plume. Use depth-resolved samples to identify stratification, retain optical calibration and applicable grading, and assess permit conditions separately from mass accounting.","failure":"注意干擾：選到已受影響的背景站會低估作業增量，速度和濃度不同時取樣也可能錯配通量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A contaminated background station understates the operational increment, and nonsynchronous concentration and velocity misstate flux. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步取得背景、作業區濃度和流速，檢查背景點是否真的位於影響區外。以分層樣本辨識垂向差異，記錄光學校正式及適用粒群，將許可條件和質量計算分別比對。","textEn":"Sample background, working-area concentration and velocity together, verifying that the background station lies outside the affected plume. Use depth-resolved samples to identify stratification, retain optical calibration and applicable grading, and assess permit conditions separately from mass accounting.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"同步取得背景、作業區濃度和流速，檢查背景點是否真的位於影響區外。以分層樣本辨識垂向差異，記錄光學校正式及適用粒群，將許可條件和質量計算分別比對。","textEn":"Sample background, working-area concentration and velocity together, verifying that the background station lies outside the affected plume. Use depth-resolved samples to identify stratification, retain optical calibration and applicable grading, and assess permit conditions separately from mass accounting.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「背景扣除與濁羽通量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Background correction and plume flux\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","乾固體總量不變時養灘外觀體積必定保持不變。","同步取得背景、作業區濃度和流速，檢查背景點是否真的位於影響區外。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Unchanged dry-solid quantity requires an unchanged visible bulk volume.","Sample background, working-area concentration and velocity together, verifying that the background station lies outside the affected plume."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步取得背景、作業區濃度和流速，檢查背景點是否真的位於影響區外。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample background, working-area concentration and velocity together, verifying that the background station lies outside the affected plume. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b285-v15-36","title":"背景扣除與濁羽通量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Background correction and plume flux: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「背景扣除與濁羽通量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Background correction and plume flux” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"選到已受影響的背景站會低估作業增量，速度和濃度不同時取樣也可能錯配通量。儀器讀值下降可能只是粒徑改變，不一定代表輸送質量減少。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A contaminated background station understates the operational increment, and nonsynchronous concentration and velocity misstate flux. Falling optical readings may reflect changed particle size rather than a reduction in the actual mass being transported. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設均勻濃度150mg/L、背景20mg/L，增量130mg/L=0.13kg/m³，流量2m³/s，增量質量通量0.26kg/s。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Increment130mg/L=0.13kg/m³; at2m³/s, incremental mass flux is0.26kg/s.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「濁度儀的光學讀值不經校正就等於泥沙質量濃度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An uncalibrated optical turbidity reading directly equals sediment mass concentration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"選到已受影響的背景站會低估作業增量，速度和濃度不同時取樣也可能錯配通量。儀器讀值下降可能只是粒徑改變，不一定代表輸送質量減少。","textEn":"A contaminated background station understates the operational increment, and nonsynchronous concentration and velocity misstate flux. Falling optical readings may reflect changed particle size rather than a reduction in the actual mass being transported.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「背景扣除與濁羽通量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Background correction and plume flux\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["選到已受影響的背景站會低估作業增量，速度和濃度不同時取樣也可能錯配通量。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。"],"optionsEn":["A contaminated background station understates the operational increment, and nonsynchronous concentration and velocity misstate flux.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again."],"answer":0,"explanation":"選到已受影響的背景站會低估作業增量，速度和濃度不同時取樣也可能錯配通量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A contaminated background station understates the operational increment, and nonsynchronous concentration and velocity misstate flux. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b285-v15-37","title":"沉降與水平輸運：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Settling and horizontal advection: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「沉降與水平輸運」如何影響海岸養灘工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Settling and horizontal advection” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beach nourishment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"粒子沉降與水流搬運的競爭影響落砂區，但真實濁羽還有紊流、絮凝和再懸浮。固定沉速及水平流速模型能建立時間與距離量級，不能將單一結果當成影響邊界；初始釋放深度和海床起伏也需與模型坐標一致。 假設距床3m、沉速0.02m/s、水平流0.30m/s，t=h/ws=150s，x=Ut=45m；忽略紊流與再懸浮。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沉降與水平輸運」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Competition between settling and advection influences deposition, but real plumes also experience turbulence, flocculation and resuspension. Constant settling and current velocities provide time and distance scales, not a definitive impact boundary. Release depth and bed relief must also be consistent with the coordinates used by the simplified model. Assume height above bed3m, settling speed0.02m/s and horizontal current0.30m/s. t=150s and x=45m, excluding turbulence and resuspension. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Settling and horizontal advection” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沉降與水平輸運」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Settling and horizontal advection”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-37-k1","title":"沉降與水平輸運","titleEn":"Settling and horizontal advection","text":"粒子沉降與水流搬運的競爭影響落砂區，但真實濁羽還有紊流、絮凝和再懸浮。固定沉速及水平流速模型能建立時間與距離量級，不能將單一結果當成影響邊界；初始釋放深度和海床起伏也需與模型坐標一致。","textEn":"Competition between settling and advection influences deposition, but real plumes also experience turbulence, flocculation and resuspension. Constant settling and current velocities provide time and distance scales, not a definitive impact boundary.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沉降與水平輸運」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Settling and horizontal advection\" is correct?","options":["粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。","粒子沉降與水流搬運的競爭影響落砂區，但真實濁羽還有紊流、絮凝和再懸浮。","施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。"],"optionsEn":["Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again.","Competition between settling and advection influences deposition, but real plumes also experience turbulence, flocculation and resuspension.","The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season."],"answer":1,"explanation":"粒子沉降與水流搬運的競爭影響落砂區，但真實濁羽還有紊流、絮凝和再懸浮。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Competition between settling and advection influences deposition, but real plumes also experience turbulence, flocculation and resuspension. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b285-v15-38","title":"沉降與水平輸運：定量估算","titleEn":"Settling and horizontal advection: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沉降與水平輸運」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Settling and horizontal advection” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設距床3m、沉速0.02m/s、水平流0.30m/s，t=h/ws=150s，x=Ut=45m；忽略紊流與再懸浮。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume height above bed3m, settling speed0.02m/s and horizontal current0.30m/s. t=150s and x=45m, excluding turbulence and resuspension. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以沉降柱試驗辨識不同粒群的速度範圍，核對現地潮流轉向及釋放深度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use settling-column tests to identify velocity ranges for different fractions and check current reversals and release depth.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設距床3m、沉速0.02m/s、水平流0.30m/s，t=h/ws=150s，x=Ut=45m；忽略紊流與再懸浮。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume height above bed3m, settling speed0.02m/s and horizontal current0.30m/s. t=150s and x=45m, excluding turbulence and resuspension.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沉降與水平輸運」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Settling and horizontal advection\", which statement holds?","options":["借砂中值粒徑較大即可證明材料全面相容且永不流失。","年平均泥沙赤字能保證每個月份都按同一速度退縮。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["A larger borrow-sand median proves complete compatibility and permanent retention.","An annual sediment deficit guarantees an identical retreat rate every month.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b285-v15-39","title":"沉降與水平輸運：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Settling and horizontal advection: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沉降與水平輸運」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Settling and horizontal advection” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以沉降柱試驗辨識不同粒群的速度範圍，核對現地潮流轉向及釋放深度。將最簡單軌跡與實測沉積分布比較，保留偏離方向作為混合或再懸浮的證據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use settling-column tests to identify velocity ranges for different fractions and check current reversals and release depth. Compare the simplest trajectory with observed deposition, retaining the direction of mismatch as evidence of mixing or resuspension. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以沉降柱試驗辨識不同粒群的速度範圍，核對現地潮流轉向及釋放深度。將最簡單軌跡與實測沉積分布比較，保留偏離方向作為混合或再懸浮的證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Use settling-column tests to identify velocity ranges for different fractions and check current reversals and release depth. Compare the simplest trajectory with observed deposition, retaining the direction of mismatch as evidence of mixing or resuspension.","failure":"注意干擾：用中值砂粒沉速代表細料會把擴散範圍算得過短，忽略潮流反轉又會放錯沉積方向。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using median-sand settling speed for fines understates plume extent, while ignoring tidal reversal misplaces deposition. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以沉降柱試驗辨識不同粒群的速度範圍，核對現地潮流轉向及釋放深度。將最簡單軌跡與實測沉積分布比較，保留偏離方向作為混合或再懸浮的證據。","textEn":"Use settling-column tests to identify velocity ranges for different fractions and check current reversals and release depth. Compare the simplest trajectory with observed deposition, retaining the direction of mismatch as evidence of mixing or resuspension.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以沉降柱試驗辨識不同粒群的速度範圍，核對現地潮流轉向及釋放深度。將最簡單軌跡與實測沉積分布比較，保留偏離方向作為混合或再懸浮的證據。","textEn":"Use settling-column tests to identify velocity ranges for different fractions and check current reversals and release depth. Compare the simplest trajectory with observed deposition, retaining the direction of mismatch as evidence of mixing or resuspension.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沉降與水平輸運」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Settling and horizontal advection\"?","options":["以沉降柱試驗辨識不同粒群的速度範圍，核對現地潮流轉向及釋放深度。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","暴風後尚未回到乾灘的砂都已永久離開海岸系統。"],"optionsEn":["Use settling-column tests to identify velocity ranges for different fractions and check current reversals and release depth.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","All sand not yet returned to the dry beach has permanently left the coast."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以沉降柱試驗辨識不同粒群的速度範圍，核對現地潮流轉向及釋放深度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use settling-column tests to identify velocity ranges for different fractions and check current reversals and release depth. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b285-v15-40","title":"沉降與水平輸運：失效診斷","titleEn":"Settling and horizontal advection: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"prerequisiteIds":["b285-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沉降與水平輸運」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Settling and horizontal advection” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用中值砂粒沉速代表細料會把擴散範圍算得過短，忽略潮流反轉又會放錯沉積方向。沉到床面也不保證永久固定，後續波浪可能重新輸送。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using median-sand settling speed for fines understates plume extent, while ignoring tidal reversal misplaces deposition. Reaching the bed does not establish permanent retention because later waves can mobilize and transport the same material again. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設距床3m、沉速0.02m/s、水平流0.30m/s，t=h/ws=150s，x=Ut=45m；忽略紊流與再懸浮。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume height above bed3m, settling speed0.02m/s and horizontal current0.30m/s. t=150s and x=45m, excluding turbulence and resuspension.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「粒子第一次碰到海床後就永遠不會再進入水體輸運。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once a particle first reaches the bed, it can never be transported again.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b285-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用中值砂粒沉速代表細料會把擴散範圍算得過短，忽略潮流反轉又會放錯沉積方向。沉到床面也不保證永久固定，後續波浪可能重新輸送。","textEn":"Using median-sand settling speed for fines understates plume extent, while ignoring tidal reversal misplaces deposition. Reaching the bed does not establish permanent retention because later waves can mobilize and transport the same material again.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]},{"id":"b285-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沉降與水平輸運」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Settling and horizontal advection\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","用中值砂粒沉速代表細料會把擴散範圍算得過短，忽略潮流反轉又會放錯沉積方向。","施工完成灘寬可以直接當成未來每個季節都固定的岸線。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using median-sand settling speed for fines understates plume extent, while ignoring tidal reversal misplaces deposition.","The completed beach width guarantees an unchanged shoreline in every future season."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用中值砂粒沉速代表細料會把擴散範圍算得過短，忽略潮流反轉又會放錯沉積方向。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using median-sand settling speed for fines understates plume extent, while ignoring tidal reversal misplaces deposition. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-beachmanual","v15s-pwdm","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin","v15s-borth-report"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b286","title":"離岸潛堤地形整合","titleEn":"Submerged-breakwater coastal integration","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"連結潛堤越頂透射缺口流與海岸地形的相互作用。課程從邊界辨識與資料整理走到水理量化、構造介面及驗證紀錄；每一步把計算結果連回可量測的證據。十個不同單元分別處理關鍵機制，不以名義尺寸或單一通過率代替整體工程判斷，並明列合成算例與現地資料的差別。","summaryEn":"Connect submerged-breakwater transmission, gap currents and evolving coastal morphology. The course moves from boundary identification and evidence to hydraulic quantification, structural interfaces and verification records. Ten distinct units connect each calculated quantity to measurable evidence. Nominal geometry or a single pass rate does not establish whole-system performance, and synthetic teaching examples remain separate from field observations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-coasts","subcategoryTitle":"海岸、港灣與水資源韌性","subcategoryTitleEn":"Coasts, ports and water-resource resilience","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-coasts","learningTags":["water","water-coasts","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-coast","architectureNodes":[["淹水深與共同基準","Submergence and shared datum"],["破波水深尺度","Depth-limited breaking scale"],["規則波能通量","Regular-wave energy flux"],["淺水傳播時間","Shallow-water propagation time"],["數值步長與收斂","Numerical timestep and convergence"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-coast","labels":["淹水深與共同基準","破波水深尺度","規則波能通量","淺水傳播時間","數值步長與收斂"],"labelsEn":["Submergence and shared datum","Depth-limited breaking scale","Regular-wave energy flux","Shallow-water propagation time","Numerical timestep and convergence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為原創合成算例，不是地標工程的實測或推薦操作值。教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水位2.0m、堤頂1.2m，淹水深0.8m；入射波高1.6m時相對淹水深0.50，非透射係數。假設水位由2.0升至2.2m、堤頂仍1.2m，覆水0.8增至1.0m，增加25%；相同1.6m入射波的相對覆水由0.50變0.625，仍不能推出新的透射量。重新計算前先列固定條件、單位、適用尺度及可能失效的邊界。把模型敏感度與測量誤差分開，不能將單一參數變化直接當成工程風險或壽命比例。比較兩次結果後，記錄還需要哪些獨立證據，並由負責專業人員判斷適用性。","textEn":"This original synthetic example is neither a landmark measurement nor a recommended operating value. Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume water level2.0m and crest1.2m. Cover is0.8m; relative to incident height1.6m the ratio is0.50, not transmission. Raising level from2.0 to2.2m at fixed crest1.2m increases cover from0.8 to1.0m by25%. Relative cover at unchanged1.6m incident height changes from0.50 to0.625, without determining a new transmission coefficient. Before recalculating, list fixed conditions, units, applicable scale and boundaries that could fail. Separate model sensitivity from measurement uncertainty: a parameter change does not directly give a proportional change in engineering risk or service life. Compare the results, record independent evidence still needed, and have the responsible specialist determine applicability.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b286-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「淹水深與共同基準」與「波高與能量透射」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Submergence and shared datum\" and \"Wave-height and energy transmission\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b286-v15-01","title":"淹水深與共同基準：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Submergence and shared datum: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「淹水深與共同基準」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Submergence and shared datum” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"潛堤是否淹水取決於堤頂與水位共同高程，不是海圖水深單獨決定。潮汐、增水與沉陷會改變相對淹水深，使同一結構在不同時段呈現不同透流狀態；越頂自由面和波浪運動仍須另行解析，不能把水下高度直接視為減波量。 假設水位2.0m、堤頂1.2m，淹水深0.8m；入射波高1.6m時相對淹水深0.50，非透射係數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「淹水深與共同基準」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Submergence depends on crest and water elevations on one datum, not chart depth alone. Tide, surge and settlement change relative cover, so the same structure experiences different transmission states. The overtopping free surface and wave motion still need separate analysis; water cover cannot directly represent the amount of wave reduction or the resulting shoreline response. Assume water level2.0m and crest1.2m. Cover is0.8m; relative to incident height1.6m the ratio is0.50, not transmission. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Submergence and shared datum” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「淹水深與共同基準」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Submergence and shared datum”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-01-k1","title":"淹水深與共同基準","titleEn":"Submergence and shared datum","text":"潛堤是否淹水取決於堤頂與水位共同高程，不是海圖水深單獨決定。潮汐、增水與沉陷會改變相對淹水深，使同一結構在不同時段呈現不同透流狀態；越頂自由面和波浪運動仍須另行解析，不能把水下高度直接視為減波量。","textEn":"Submergence depends on crest and water elevations on one datum, not chart depth alone. Tide, surge and settlement change relative cover, so the same structure experiences different transmission states.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「淹水深與共同基準」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Submergence and shared datum\" is correct?","options":["相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。","潛堤是否淹水取決於堤頂與水位共同高程，不是海圖水深單獨決定。","波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。"],"optionsEn":["Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width.","Submergence depends on crest and water elevations on one datum, not chart depth alone.","A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux."],"answer":1,"explanation":"潛堤是否淹水取決於堤頂與水位共同高程，不是海圖水深單獨決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Submergence depends on crest and water elevations on one datum, not chart depth alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b286-v15-02","title":"淹水深與共同基準：定量估算","titleEn":"Submergence and shared datum: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「淹水深與共同基準」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Submergence and shared datum” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水位2.0m、堤頂1.2m，淹水深0.8m；入射波高1.6m時相對淹水深0.50，非透射係數。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume water level2.0m and crest1.2m. Cover is0.8m; relative to incident height1.6m the ratio is0.50, not transmission. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將潮位、堤頂測量及海床資料轉到同一高程基準，保留每筆測量時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Convert tide, crest and seabed observations to one vertical datum and retain timestamps.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水位2.0m、堤頂1.2m，淹水深0.8m；入射波高1.6m時相對淹水深0.50，非透射係數。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume water level2.0m and crest1.2m. Cover is0.8m; relative to incident height1.6m the ratio is0.50, not transmission.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「淹水深與共同基準」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Submergence and shared datum\", which statement holds?","options":["缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。","希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point.","The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b286-v15-03","title":"淹水深與共同基準：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Submergence and shared datum: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「淹水深與共同基準」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Submergence and shared datum” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將潮位、堤頂測量及海床資料轉到同一高程基準，保留每筆測量時間。分別列出高低水位時的覆水範圍，並檢查堤頂起伏，避免以平均值掩蓋局部深缺口。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Convert tide, crest and seabed observations to one vertical datum and retain timestamps. List cover at different levels and inspect crest irregularities, ensuring an average elevation does not conceal a locally deep notch or missing section. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將潮位、堤頂測量及海床資料轉到同一高程基準，保留每筆測量時間。分別列出高低水位時的覆水範圍，並檢查堤頂起伏，避免以平均值掩蓋局部深缺口。","observationEn":"Site practice: Convert tide, crest and seabed observations to one vertical datum and retain timestamps. List cover at different levels and inspect crest irregularities, ensuring an average elevation does not conceal a locally deep notch or missing section.","failure":"注意干擾：不同高程基準相混可能把實際淹沒堤頂算成出水，直接改變選用的水理機制。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mixed elevation datums can turn a submerged crest into an apparently emerged one and select the wrong hydraulic mechanism. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將潮位、堤頂測量及海床資料轉到同一高程基準，保留每筆測量時間。分別列出高低水位時的覆水範圍，並檢查堤頂起伏，避免以平均值掩蓋局部深缺口。","textEn":"Convert tide, crest and seabed observations to one vertical datum and retain timestamps. List cover at different levels and inspect crest irregularities, ensuring an average elevation does not conceal a locally deep notch or missing section.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將潮位、堤頂測量及海床資料轉到同一高程基準，保留每筆測量時間。分別列出高低水位時的覆水範圍，並檢查堤頂起伏，避免以平均值掩蓋局部深缺口。","textEn":"Convert tide, crest and seabed observations to one vertical datum and retain timestamps. List cover at different levels and inspect crest irregularities, ensuring an average elevation does not conceal a locally deep notch or missing section.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「淹水深與共同基準」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Submergence and shared datum\"?","options":["將潮位、堤頂測量及海床資料轉到同一高程基準，保留每筆測量時間。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。"],"optionsEn":["Convert tide, crest and seabed observations to one vertical datum and retain timestamps.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將潮位、堤頂測量及海床資料轉到同一高程基準，保留每筆測量時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Convert tide, crest and seabed observations to one vertical datum and retain timestamps. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b286-v15-04","title":"淹水深與共同基準：失效診斷","titleEn":"Submergence and shared datum: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「淹水深與共同基準」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Submergence and shared datum” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不同高程基準相混可能把實際淹沒堤頂算成出水，直接改變選用的水理機制。局部低點若未量到，也可能集中越頂流而造成後側沖刷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mixed elevation datums can turn a submerged crest into an apparently emerged one and select the wrong hydraulic mechanism. An unmeasured low point may also concentrate overtopping flow and cause localized scour behind the structure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設水位2.0m、堤頂1.2m，淹水深0.8m；入射波高1.6m時相對淹水深0.50，非透射係數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Cover is0.8m; relative to incident height1.6m the ratio is0.50, not transmission.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不同高程基準相混可能把實際淹沒堤頂算成出水，直接改變選用的水理機制。局部低點若未量到，也可能集中越頂流而造成後側沖刷。","textEn":"Mixed elevation datums can turn a submerged crest into an apparently emerged one and select the wrong hydraulic mechanism. An unmeasured low point may also concentrate overtopping flow and cause localized scour behind the structure.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「淹水深與共同基準」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Submergence and shared datum\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","不同高程基準相混可能把實際淹沒堤頂算成出水，直接改變選用的水理機制。","波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Mixed elevation datums can turn a submerged crest into an apparently emerged one and select the wrong hydraulic mechanism.","A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同高程基準相混可能把實際淹沒堤頂算成出水，直接改變選用的水理機制。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mixed elevation datums can turn a submerged crest into an apparently emerged one and select the wrong hydraulic mechanism. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b286-v15-05","title":"波高與能量透射：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Wave-height and energy transmission: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「波高與能量透射」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wave-height and energy transmission” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"透射波高比描述振幅變化，能量通量還涉及群速度與水深，不能直接以相同百分比換算。量測必須分離入射反射及透射成分，兩側頻譜也可能因破波而改變；只有明定波型與能量定義後，才可比較堤前與堤後的水理量。 假設Hi=2m、Ht=0.8m，Kt=0.40；相同密度且群速比Cgt/Cgi=0.80時，能量通量比Kt²×0.80=0.128。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「波高與能量透射」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Wave-height transmission describes amplitude, whereas energy flux also depends on group velocity and depth. Measurements must separate incident, reflected and transmitted components, and breaking can change the spectrum. Only after defining wave type and energy consistently can measurements on either side be compared; an amplitude percentage is not automatically an energy percentage. Assume Hi=2m and Ht=0.8m, giving Kt=0.40. Equal density and group-speed ratio0.80 give energy-flux ratio Kt²×0.80=0.128. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wave-height and energy transmission” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「波高與能量透射」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wave-height and energy transmission”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-05-k1","title":"波高與能量透射","titleEn":"Wave-height and energy transmission","text":"透射波高比描述振幅變化，能量通量還涉及群速度與水深，不能直接以相同百分比換算。量測必須分離入射反射及透射成分，兩側頻譜也可能因破波而改變；只有明定波型與能量定義後，才可比較堤前與堤後的水理量。","textEn":"Wave-height transmission describes amplitude, whereas energy flux also depends on group velocity and depth. Measurements must separate incident, reflected and transmitted components, and breaking can change the spectrum.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「波高與能量透射」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wave-height and energy transmission\" is correct?","options":["波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。","只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。","透射波高比描述振幅變化，能量通量還涉及群速度與水深，不能直接以相同百分比換算。"],"optionsEn":["A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux.","At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height.","Wave-height transmission describes amplitude, whereas energy flux also depends on group velocity and depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"透射波高比描述振幅變化，能量通量還涉及群速度與水深，不能直接以相同百分比換算。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Wave-height transmission describes amplitude, whereas energy flux also depends on group velocity and depth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b286-v15-06","title":"波高與能量透射：定量估算","titleEn":"Wave-height and energy transmission: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「波高與能量透射」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wave-height and energy transmission” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設Hi=2m、Ht=0.8m，Kt=0.40；相同密度且群速比Cgt/Cgi=0.80時，能量通量比Kt²×0.80=0.128。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume Hi=2m and Ht=0.8m, giving Kt=0.40. Equal density and group-speed ratio0.80 give energy-flux ratio Kt²×0.80=0.128. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：配置可區分反射的多點波面量測，使用一致的分析時窗與頻譜定義。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use multiple wave gauges to separate reflection with consistent windows and spectral definitions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設Hi=2m、Ht=0.8m，Kt=0.40；相同密度且群速比Cgt/Cgi=0.80時，能量通量比Kt²×0.80=0.128。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume Hi=2m and Ht=0.8m, giving Kt=0.40. Equal density and group-speed ratio0.80 give energy-flux ratio Kt²×0.80=0.128.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「波高與能量透射」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wave-height and energy transmission\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。","所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change.","Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b286-v15-07","title":"波高與能量透射：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wave-height and energy transmission: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「波高與能量透射」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wave-height and energy transmission” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"配置可區分反射的多點波面量測，使用一致的分析時窗與頻譜定義。另求兩側群速度並說明水深假設，檢查高頻重分配，不能只比較兩支儀器顯示的最大峰值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use multiple wave gauges to separate reflection with consistent windows and spectral definitions. Determine group velocities on both sides and state depth assumptions, checking redistributed high-frequency energy rather than comparing only the maximum displayed by two sensors. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：配置可區分反射的多點波面量測，使用一致的分析時窗與頻譜定義。另求兩側群速度並說明水深假設，檢查高頻重分配，不能只比較兩支儀器顯示的最大峰值。","observationEn":"Site practice: Use multiple wave gauges to separate reflection with consistent windows and spectral definitions. Determine group velocities on both sides and state depth assumptions, checking redistributed high-frequency energy rather than comparing only the maximum displayed by two sensors.","failure":"注意干擾：把堤前駐波腹當成入射波高會低估透射係數，兩側群速差若被忽略則錯估能量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mistaking a standing-wave antinode for incident height understates transmission, and neglected group-speed differences distort energy estimates. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"配置可區分反射的多點波面量測，使用一致的分析時窗與頻譜定義。另求兩側群速度並說明水深假設，檢查高頻重分配，不能只比較兩支儀器顯示的最大峰值。","textEn":"Use multiple wave gauges to separate reflection with consistent windows and spectral definitions. Determine group velocities on both sides and state depth assumptions, checking redistributed high-frequency energy rather than comparing only the maximum displayed by two sensors.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"配置可區分反射的多點波面量測，使用一致的分析時窗與頻譜定義。另求兩側群速度並說明水深假設，檢查高頻重分配，不能只比較兩支儀器顯示的最大峰值。","textEn":"Use multiple wave gauges to separate reflection with consistent windows and spectral definitions. Determine group velocities on both sides and state depth assumptions, checking redistributed high-frequency energy rather than comparing only the maximum displayed by two sensors.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「波高與能量透射」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wave-height and energy transmission\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","配置可區分反射的多點波面量測，使用一致的分析時窗與頻譜定義。","覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Use multiple wave gauges to separate reflection with consistent windows and spectral definitions.","The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height."],"answer":1,"explanation":"配置可區分反射的多點波面量測，使用一致的分析時窗與頻譜定義。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use multiple wave gauges to separate reflection with consistent windows and spectral definitions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b286-v15-08","title":"波高與能量透射：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wave-height and energy transmission: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「波高與能量透射」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wave-height and energy transmission” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把堤前駐波腹當成入射波高會低估透射係數，兩側群速差若被忽略則錯估能量。即使整體透射降低，缺口附近仍可能有局部高波。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mistaking a standing-wave antinode for incident height understates transmission, and neglected group-speed differences distort energy estimates. Lower overall transmission can still coexist with locally high waves near a gap in the breakwater. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設Hi=2m、Ht=0.8m，Kt=0.40；相同密度且群速比Cgt/Cgi=0.80時，能量通量比Kt²×0.80=0.128。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Equal density and group-speed ratio0.80 give energy-flux ratio Kt²×0.80=0.128.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把堤前駐波腹當成入射波高會低估透射係數，兩側群速差若被忽略則錯估能量。即使整體透射降低，缺口附近仍可能有局部高波。","textEn":"Mistaking a standing-wave antinode for incident height understates transmission, and neglected group-speed differences distort energy estimates. Lower overall transmission can still coexist with locally high waves near a gap in the breakwater.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「波高與能量透射」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wave-height and energy transmission\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。","把堤前駐波腹當成入射波高會低估透射係數，兩側群速差若被忽略則錯估能量。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height.","Mistaking a standing-wave antinode for incident height understates transmission, and neglected group-speed differences distort energy estimates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把堤前駐波腹當成入射波高會低估透射係數，兩側群速差若被忽略則錯估能量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mistaking a standing-wave antinode for incident height understates transmission, and neglected group-speed differences distort energy estimates. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b286-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「破波水深尺度」與「缺口連續流量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Depth-limited breaking scale\" and \"Gap-flow continuity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b286-v15-09","title":"破波水深尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Depth-limited breaking scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「破波水深尺度」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Depth-limited breaking scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"淺水破波受波陡、坡度與水深限制，常見破波指標只是特定資料範圍下的近似。潛堤頂部流速和波形會改變，短堤頂也未必達到平衡破波；教學比例應用於辨識量級，不能被當成任何不規則波條件下的固定上限。 假設選用破波指標γb=0.78、水深h=2m，Hb=γbh=1.56m；此係數非所有潛堤的通用設計值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「破波水深尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shallow breaking depends on steepness, bed slope and depth, and a breaker index approximates a limited range of observations. Crest currents and wave shape change over a submerged structure, and a short crest may not develop equilibrium breaking. A teaching ratio establishes scale rather than a universal ceiling for every irregular-wave condition. Assume a selected breaker indexγb=0.78 at depth2m. Hb=γbh=1.56m; the index is not a universal submerged-breakwater design value. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Depth-limited breaking scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「破波水深尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Depth-limited breaking scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-09-k1","title":"破波水深尺度","titleEn":"Depth-limited breaking scale","text":"淺水破波受波陡、坡度與水深限制，常見破波指標只是特定資料範圍下的近似。潛堤頂部流速和波形會改變，短堤頂也未必達到平衡破波；教學比例應用於辨識量級，不能被當成任何不規則波條件下的固定上限。","textEn":"Shallow breaking depends on steepness, bed slope and depth, and a breaker index approximates a limited range of observations. Crest currents and wave shape change over a submerged structure, and a short crest may not develop equilibrium breaking.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「破波水深尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Depth-limited breaking scale\" is correct?","options":["淺水破波受波陡、坡度與水深限制，常見破波指標只是特定資料範圍下的近似。","只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。","缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。"],"optionsEn":["Shallow breaking depends on steepness, bed slope and depth, and a breaker index approximates a limited range of observations.","At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height.","The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point."],"answer":0,"explanation":"淺水破波受波陡、坡度與水深限制，常見破波指標只是特定資料範圍下的近似。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shallow breaking depends on steepness, bed slope and depth, and a breaker index approximates a limited range of observations. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b286-v15-10","title":"破波水深尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Depth-limited breaking scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「破波水深尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Depth-limited breaking scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設選用破波指標γb=0.78、水深h=2m，Hb=γbh=1.56m；此係數非所有潛堤的通用設計值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a selected breaker indexγb=0.78 at depth2m. Hb=γbh=1.56m; the index is not a universal submerged-breakwater design value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在示意剖面上標出實際水深定義，對比不同水位和波週期下的破波位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark the depth definition on a section and compare breaking positions for different levels and periods.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設選用破波指標γb=0.78、水深h=2m，Hb=γbh=1.56m；此係數非所有潛堤的通用設計值。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a selected breaker indexγb=0.78 at depth2m. Hb=γbh=1.56m; the index is not a universal submerged-breakwater design value.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「破波水深尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Depth-limited breaking scale\", which statement holds?","options":["希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。"],"optionsEn":["The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b286-v15-11","title":"破波水深尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Depth-limited breaking scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「破波水深尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Depth-limited breaking scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在示意剖面上標出實際水深定義，對比不同水位和波週期下的破波位置。保留試驗中未破波與碎波資料，說明所選指標的來源範圍，不把觀察外的海況直接外推。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark the depth definition on a section and compare breaking positions for different levels and periods. Retain both broken and unbroken observations, state the evidence range for the chosen index, and avoid extrapolating it directly to untested seas. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在示意剖面上標出實際水深定義，對比不同水位和波週期下的破波位置。保留試驗中未破波與碎波資料，說明所選指標的來源範圍，不把觀察外的海況直接外推。","observationEn":"Site practice: Mark the depth definition on a section and compare breaking positions for different levels and periods. Retain both broken and unbroken observations, state the evidence range for the chosen index, and avoid extrapolating it directly to untested seas.","failure":"注意干擾：水位升高可能使原先碎波的位置消失，波能穿過堤頂後才耗散。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Rising water can remove a former breaking location so that energy dissipates only after crossing the crest. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在示意剖面上標出實際水深定義，對比不同水位和波週期下的破波位置。保留試驗中未破波與碎波資料，說明所選指標的來源範圍，不把觀察外的海況直接外推。","textEn":"Mark the depth definition on a section and compare breaking positions for different levels and periods. Retain both broken and unbroken observations, state the evidence range for the chosen index, and avoid extrapolating it directly to untested seas.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在示意剖面上標出實際水深定義，對比不同水位和波週期下的破波位置。保留試驗中未破波與碎波資料，說明所選指標的來源範圍，不把觀察外的海況直接外推。","textEn":"Mark the depth definition on a section and compare breaking positions for different levels and periods. Retain both broken and unbroken observations, state the evidence range for the chosen index, and avoid extrapolating it directly to untested seas.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「破波水深尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Depth-limited breaking scale\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。","在示意剖面上標出實際水深定義，對比不同水位和波週期下的破波位置。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete.","Mark the depth definition on a section and compare breaking positions for different levels and periods."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在示意剖面上標出實際水深定義，對比不同水位和波週期下的破波位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark the depth definition on a section and compare breaking positions for different levels and periods. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b286-v15-12","title":"破波水深尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Depth-limited breaking scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「破波水深尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Depth-limited breaking scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"水位升高可能使原先碎波的位置消失，波能穿過堤頂後才耗散。若一直使用同一破波位置和係數，後側波況與岸灘受力可能被系統性低估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Rising water can remove a former breaking location so that energy dissipates only after crossing the crest. Keeping the same breaking point and coefficient can systematically understate lee-side waves and beach exposure during higher water. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設選用破波指標γb=0.78、水深h=2m，Hb=γbh=1.56m；此係數非所有潛堤的通用設計值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Hb=γbh=1.56m; the index is not a universal submerged-breakwater design value.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"水位升高可能使原先碎波的位置消失，波能穿過堤頂後才耗散。若一直使用同一破波位置和係數，後側波況與岸灘受力可能被系統性低估。","textEn":"Rising water can remove a former breaking location so that energy dissipates only after crossing the crest. Keeping the same breaking point and coefficient can systematically understate lee-side waves and beach exposure during higher water.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「破波水深尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Depth-limited breaking scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["水位升高可能使原先碎波的位置消失，波能穿過堤頂後才耗散。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。"],"optionsEn":["Rising water can remove a former breaking location so that energy dissipates only after crossing the crest.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水位升高可能使原先碎波的位置消失，波能穿過堤頂後才耗散。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Rising water can remove a former breaking location so that energy dissipates only after crossing the crest. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b286-v15-13","title":"缺口連續流量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Gap-flow continuity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「缺口連續流量」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gap-flow continuity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"堤後水位抬升產生回流，缺口可能集中流量並形成局部沖刷或游泳風險。面積平均流速只能滿足連續方程，不代表最大紊流或近床速度；流向會隨潮波改變，分析需要把堤段越頂輸入與缺口排出放在同一收支框架。 假設穩定缺口流量30m³/s、有效過水面積20m²，平均v=Q/A=1.50m/s；不等於局部最大流速。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「缺口連續流量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Setup behind a structure can drive return flow through gaps and concentrate scour or exposure. Section-mean velocity satisfies continuity but is not the maximum turbulent or near-bed velocity. Direction changes with tides and waves, so crest inflow and gap outflow must be evaluated within one water budget rather than as unrelated local observations. Assume steady gap discharge30m³/s through effective area20m². Mean v=Q/A=1.50m/s, not the local maximum velocity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gap-flow continuity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「缺口連續流量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gap-flow continuity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-13-k1","title":"缺口連續流量","titleEn":"Gap-flow continuity","text":"堤後水位抬升產生回流，缺口可能集中流量並形成局部沖刷或游泳風險。面積平均流速只能滿足連續方程，不代表最大紊流或近床速度；流向會隨潮波改變，分析需要把堤段越頂輸入與缺口排出放在同一收支框架。","textEn":"Setup behind a structure can drive return flow through gaps and concentrate scour or exposure. Section-mean velocity satisfies continuity but is not the maximum turbulent or near-bed velocity.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「缺口連續流量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gap-flow continuity\" is correct?","options":["缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。","堤後水位抬升產生回流，缺口可能集中流量並形成局部沖刷或游泳風險。","規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。"],"optionsEn":["The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point.","Setup behind a structure can drive return flow through gaps and concentrate scour or exposure.","Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change."],"answer":1,"explanation":"堤後水位抬升產生回流，缺口可能集中流量並形成局部沖刷或游泳風險。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Setup behind a structure can drive return flow through gaps and concentrate scour or exposure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b286-v15-14","title":"缺口連續流量：定量估算","titleEn":"Gap-flow continuity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「缺口連續流量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gap-flow continuity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設穩定缺口流量30m³/s、有效過水面積20m²，平均v=Q/A=1.50m/s；不等於局部最大流速。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume steady gap discharge30m³/s through effective area20m². Mean v=Q/A=1.50m/s, not the local maximum velocity. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿缺口橫斷面量測速度與水深，積分流量並核對堤後水位變化。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure velocity and depth across the gap, integrating discharge and comparing it with lee-side level change.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設穩定缺口流量30m³/s、有效過水面積20m²，平均v=Q/A=1.50m/s；不等於局部最大流速。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume steady gap discharge30m³/s through effective area20m². Mean v=Q/A=1.50m/s, not the local maximum velocity.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「缺口連續流量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gap-flow continuity\", which statement holds?","options":["所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。","覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength.","The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b286-v15-15","title":"缺口連續流量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gap-flow continuity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「缺口連續流量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gap-flow continuity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿缺口橫斷面量測速度與水深，積分流量並核對堤後水位變化。分別報告平均、近床和瞬時峰值，保存潮向與波況，避免把單點尖峰直接當成整斷面流量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure velocity and depth across the gap, integrating discharge and comparing it with lee-side level change. Report means, near-bed values and peaks separately with tide and waves; one-point spikes cannot represent discharge over the entire section. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：沿缺口橫斷面量測速度與水深，積分流量並核對堤後水位變化。分別報告平均、近床和瞬時峰值，保存潮向與波況，避免把單點尖峰直接當成整斷面流量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Measure velocity and depth across the gap, integrating discharge and comparing it with lee-side level change. Report means, near-bed values and peaks separately with tide and waves; one-point spikes cannot represent discharge over the entire section.","failure":"注意干擾：斷面局部被砂堆堵塞時平均面積假設失效，剩餘通道流速可能增加。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Partial blockage by sediment invalidates the assumed area and can accelerate flow through the remaining opening. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿缺口橫斷面量測速度與水深，積分流量並核對堤後水位變化。分別報告平均、近床和瞬時峰值，保存潮向與波況，避免把單點尖峰直接當成整斷面流量。","textEn":"Measure velocity and depth across the gap, integrating discharge and comparing it with lee-side level change. Report means, near-bed values and peaks separately with tide and waves; one-point spikes cannot represent discharge over the entire section.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"沿缺口橫斷面量測速度與水深，積分流量並核對堤後水位變化。分別報告平均、近床和瞬時峰值，保存潮向與波況，避免把單點尖峰直接當成整斷面流量。","textEn":"Measure velocity and depth across the gap, integrating discharge and comparing it with lee-side level change. Report means, near-bed values and peaks separately with tide and waves; one-point spikes cannot represent discharge over the entire section.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「缺口連續流量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gap-flow continuity\"?","options":["沿缺口橫斷面量測速度與水深，積分流量並核對堤後水位變化。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。"],"optionsEn":["Measure velocity and depth across the gap, integrating discharge and comparing it with lee-side level change.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沿缺口橫斷面量測速度與水深，積分流量並核對堤後水位變化。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure velocity and depth across the gap, integrating discharge and comparing it with lee-side level change. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b286-v15-16","title":"缺口連續流量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gap-flow continuity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「缺口連續流量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gap-flow continuity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"斷面局部被砂堆堵塞時平均面積假設失效，剩餘通道流速可能增加。若儀器只放在緩流區，收支殘差會掩蓋真正的集中流和沖刷熱點。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Partial blockage by sediment invalidates the assumed area and can accelerate flow through the remaining opening. Instruments placed only in slow water conceal concentrated currents and scour hotspots behind apparently modest mean-flow observations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設穩定缺口流量30m³/s、有效過水面積20m²，平均v=Q/A=1.50m/s；不等於局部最大流速。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mean v=Q/A=1.50m/s, not the local maximum velocity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"斷面局部被砂堆堵塞時平均面積假設失效，剩餘通道流速可能增加。若儀器只放在緩流區，收支殘差會掩蓋真正的集中流和沖刷熱點。","textEn":"Partial blockage by sediment invalidates the assumed area and can accelerate flow through the remaining opening. Instruments placed only in slow water conceal concentrated currents and scour hotspots behind apparently modest mean-flow observations.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「缺口連續流量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gap-flow continuity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","斷面局部被砂堆堵塞時平均面積假設失效，剩餘通道流速可能增加。","規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Partial blockage by sediment invalidates the assumed area and can accelerate flow through the remaining opening.","Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change."],"answer":1,"explanation":"斷面局部被砂堆堵塞時平均面積假設失效，剩餘通道流速可能增加。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Partial blockage by sediment invalidates the assumed area and can accelerate flow through the remaining opening. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b286-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「規則波能通量」與「床面剪力無因次化」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Regular-wave energy flux\" and \"Dimensionless bed shear\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b286-v15-17","title":"規則波能通量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Regular-wave energy flux: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「規則波能通量」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Regular-wave energy flux” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"波能公式必須說明波高代表規則波還是頻譜顯著波高，兩者係數不同。群速度傳遞能量而相速度描述波峰移動，混用會改變功率；入射角、反射和耗散也影響垂直結構方向的能流，單位寬度結果不能直接當成整座結構承受的總負荷。 假設規則線性波ρ=1025kg/m³、H=2m、Cg=5m/s，E=ρgH²/8=5027.6J/m²，P=ECg=25.138kW/m。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「規則波能通量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Wave-energy formulas must identify whether height is regular-wave height or spectral significant height because their coefficients differ. Group velocity transports energy while phase velocity follows crests. Incidence, reflection and dissipation also affect the normal energy flux, so a result per unit crest width does not directly describe total structural loading or impact pressure. Assume a regular linear wave:ρ=1025kg/m³, H=2m, Cg=5m/s. E=ρgH²/8=5027.6J/m² and P=25.138kW/m. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Regular-wave energy flux” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「規則波能通量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Regular-wave energy flux”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-17-k1","title":"規則波能通量","titleEn":"Regular-wave energy flux","text":"波能公式必須說明波高代表規則波還是頻譜顯著波高，兩者係數不同。群速度傳遞能量而相速度描述波峰移動，混用會改變功率；入射角、反射和耗散也影響垂直結構方向的能流，單位寬度結果不能直接當成整座結構承受的總負荷。","textEn":"Wave-energy formulas must identify whether height is regular-wave height or spectral significant height because their coefficients differ. Group velocity transports energy while phase velocity follows crests.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「規則波能通量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Regular-wave energy flux\" is correct?","options":["規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。","希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。","波能公式必須說明波高代表規則波還是頻譜顯著波高，兩者係數不同。"],"optionsEn":["Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change.","The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth.","Wave-energy formulas must identify whether height is regular-wave height or spectral significant height because their coefficients differ."],"answer":2,"explanation":"波能公式必須說明波高代表規則波還是頻譜顯著波高，兩者係數不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Wave-energy formulas must identify whether height is regular-wave height or spectral significant height because their coefficients differ. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b286-v15-18","title":"規則波能通量：定量估算","titleEn":"Regular-wave energy flux: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「規則波能通量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Regular-wave energy flux” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設規則線性波ρ=1025kg/m³、H=2m、Cg=5m/s，E=ρgH²/8=5027.6J/m²，P=ECg=25.138kW/m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a regular linear wave:ρ=1025kg/m³, H=2m, Cg=5m/s. E=ρgH²/8=5027.6J/m² and P=25.138kW/m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在計算表明列波高統計定義、密度及群速來源，確認每米寬度的方向。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record height convention, density and group-velocity derivation and define the direction of unit width.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設規則線性波ρ=1025kg/m³、H=2m、Cg=5m/s，E=ρgH²/8=5027.6J/m²，P=ECg=25.138kW/m。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a regular linear wave:ρ=1025kg/m³, H=2m, Cg=5m/s. E=ρgH²/8=5027.6J/m² and P=25.138kW/m.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「規則波能通量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Regular-wave energy flux\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。","模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape.","Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b286-v15-19","title":"規則波能通量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Regular-wave energy flux: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「規則波能通量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Regular-wave energy flux” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在計算表明列波高統計定義、密度及群速來源，確認每米寬度的方向。用能量收支比較反射透射與耗散；若改用顯著波高，重新選頻譜能量公式而不是保留原係數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record height convention, density and group-velocity derivation and define the direction of unit width. Compare reflected, transmitted and dissipated fluxes; when switching to significant height, select the corresponding spectral-energy formula instead of retaining the regular-wave coefficient. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在計算表明列波高統計定義、密度及群速來源，確認每米寬度的方向。用能量收支比較反射透射與耗散；若改用顯著波高，重新選頻譜能量公式而不是保留原係數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Record height convention, density and group-velocity derivation and define the direction of unit width. Compare reflected, transmitted and dissipated fluxes; when switching to significant height, select the corresponding spectral-energy formula instead of retaining the regular-wave coefficient.","failure":"注意干擾：使用顯著波高卻套規則波係數會使能量差一倍，拿相速度代群速度又增加另一偏差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using significant height in the regular-wave formula doubles the energy estimate, and substituting phase velocity adds another bias. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在計算表明列波高統計定義、密度及群速來源，確認每米寬度的方向。用能量收支比較反射透射與耗散；若改用顯著波高，重新選頻譜能量公式而不是保留原係數。","textEn":"Record height convention, density and group-velocity derivation and define the direction of unit width. Compare reflected, transmitted and dissipated fluxes; when switching to significant height, select the corresponding spectral-energy formula instead of retaining the regular-wave coefficient.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在計算表明列波高統計定義、密度及群速來源，確認每米寬度的方向。用能量收支比較反射透射與耗散；若改用顯著波高，重新選頻譜能量公式而不是保留原係數。","textEn":"Record height convention, density and group-velocity derivation and define the direction of unit width. Compare reflected, transmitted and dissipated fluxes; when switching to significant height, select the corresponding spectral-energy formula instead of retaining the regular-wave coefficient.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「規則波能通量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Regular-wave energy flux\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","在計算表明列波高統計定義、密度及群速來源，確認每米寬度的方向。","波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Record height convention, density and group-velocity derivation and define the direction of unit width.","A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在計算表明列波高統計定義、密度及群速來源，確認每米寬度的方向。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record height convention, density and group-velocity derivation and define the direction of unit width. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b286-v15-20","title":"規則波能通量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Regular-wave energy flux: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「規則波能通量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Regular-wave energy flux” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"使用顯著波高卻套規則波係數會使能量差一倍，拿相速度代群速度又增加另一偏差。數值即使量綱正確，仍可能因統計定義不同而不可比較。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using significant height in the regular-wave formula doubles the energy estimate, and substituting phase velocity adds another bias. Dimensionally correct numbers may still be incomparable because the underlying statistical definition is different. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設規則線性波ρ=1025kg/m³、H=2m、Cg=5m/s，E=ρgH²/8=5027.6J/m²，P=ECg=25.138kW/m。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: E=ρgH²/8=5027.6J/m² and P=25.138kW/m.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"使用顯著波高卻套規則波係數會使能量差一倍，拿相速度代群速度又增加另一偏差。數值即使量綱正確，仍可能因統計定義不同而不可比較。","textEn":"Using significant height in the regular-wave formula doubles the energy estimate, and substituting phase velocity adds another bias. Dimensionally correct numbers may still be incomparable because the underlying statistical definition is different.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「規則波能通量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Regular-wave energy flux\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。","使用顯著波高卻套規則波係數會使能量差一倍，拿相速度代群速度又增加另一偏差。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth.","Using significant height in the regular-wave formula doubles the energy estimate, and substituting phase velocity adds another bias."],"answer":2,"explanation":"使用顯著波高卻套規則波係數會使能量差一倍，拿相速度代群速度又增加另一偏差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using significant height in the regular-wave formula doubles the energy estimate, and substituting phase velocity adds another bias. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b286-v15-21","title":"床面剪力無因次化：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Dimensionless bed shear: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「床面剪力無因次化」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dimensionless bed shear” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"潛堤改變波流剪力後可能引發近床輸砂，粒徑與相對密度決定顆粒重量尺度。希爾茲參數只把作用力無因次化，起動條件還受級配、床面形態與振盪流影響；不能由單一參數宣告侵蝕深度，亦不能跳過黏性細料與非黏性砂的不同機制。 假設τ=2Pa、ρs=2650、ρ=1025kg/m³、D=0.0005m，θ=τ/[(ρs−ρ)gD]=0.2509；未指定起動門檻。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「床面剪力無因次化」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Modified wave-current shear can mobilize sediment, with grain size and relative density setting the gravitational scale. The Shields parameter nondimensionalizes forcing; onset also depends on grading, bed form and oscillatory motion. One parameter does not give scour depth, and cohesive fines require a different treatment from the noncohesive grains assumed here. Assumeτ=2Pa,ρs=2650,ρ=1025kg/m³ and D=0.0005m. θ=τ/[(ρs−ρ)gD]=0.2509, without prescribing a motion threshold. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Dimensionless bed shear” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「床面剪力無因次化」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Dimensionless bed shear”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-21-k1","title":"床面剪力無因次化","titleEn":"Dimensionless bed shear","text":"潛堤改變波流剪力後可能引發近床輸砂，粒徑與相對密度決定顆粒重量尺度。希爾茲參數只把作用力無因次化，起動條件還受級配、床面形態與振盪流影響；不能由單一參數宣告侵蝕深度，亦不能跳過黏性細料與非黏性砂的不同機制。","textEn":"Modified wave-current shear can mobilize sediment, with grain size and relative density setting the gravitational scale. The Shields parameter nondimensionalizes forcing; onset also depends on grading, bed form and oscillatory motion.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「床面剪力無因次化」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Dimensionless bed shear\" is correct?","options":["潛堤改變波流剪力後可能引發近床輸砂，粒徑與相對密度決定顆粒重量尺度。","希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。","所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。"],"optionsEn":["Modified wave-current shear can mobilize sediment, with grain size and relative density setting the gravitational scale.","The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth.","Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength."],"answer":0,"explanation":"潛堤改變波流剪力後可能引發近床輸砂，粒徑與相對密度決定顆粒重量尺度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Modified wave-current shear can mobilize sediment, with grain size and relative density setting the gravitational scale. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b286-v15-22","title":"床面剪力無因次化：定量估算","titleEn":"Dimensionless bed shear: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「床面剪力無因次化」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dimensionless bed shear” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設τ=2Pa、ρs=2650、ρ=1025kg/m³、D=0.0005m，θ=τ/[(ρs−ρ)gD]=0.2509；未指定起動門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assumeτ=2Pa,ρs=2650,ρ=1025kg/m³ and D=0.0005m. θ=τ/[(ρs−ρ)gD]=0.2509, without prescribing a motion threshold. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對剪力是瞬時或週期平均以及粒徑代表值，對照原床級配與黏性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check whether shear is instantaneous or cycle-averaged and identify representative size, grading and cohesion.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設τ=2Pa、ρs=2650、ρ=1025kg/m³、D=0.0005m，θ=τ/[(ρs−ρ)gD]=0.2509；未指定起動門檻。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assumeτ=2Pa,ρs=2650,ρ=1025kg/m³ and D=0.0005m. θ=τ/[(ρs−ρ)gD]=0.2509, without prescribing a motion threshold.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「床面剪力無因次化」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Dimensionless bed shear\", which statement holds?","options":["覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。"],"optionsEn":["The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b286-v15-23","title":"床面剪力無因次化：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Dimensionless bed shear: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「床面剪力無因次化」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dimensionless bed shear” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對剪力是瞬時或週期平均以及粒徑代表值，對照原床級配與黏性。以床形和起動觀察檢驗假設，另做沖刷深度分析，不能把一個無因次比值直接換成挖深。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check whether shear is instantaneous or cycle-averaged and identify representative size, grading and cohesion. Test assumptions against observed motion and bed form; analyze scour depth separately rather than converting one dimensionless ratio directly into an excavation depth. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：核對剪力是瞬時或週期平均以及粒徑代表值，對照原床級配與黏性。以床形和起動觀察檢驗假設，另做沖刷深度分析，不能把一個無因次比值直接換成挖深。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check whether shear is instantaneous or cycle-averaged and identify representative size, grading and cohesion. Test assumptions against observed motion and bed form; analyze scour depth separately rather than converting one dimensionless ratio directly into an excavation depth.","failure":"注意干擾：將黏土當成同粒徑砂會忽略顆粒間作用，僅取平均剪力又漏掉波峰短暫起動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating clay as sand of equal size omits interparticle forces, while mean shear can miss brief wave-driven motion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對剪力是瞬時或週期平均以及粒徑代表值，對照原床級配與黏性。以床形和起動觀察檢驗假設，另做沖刷深度分析，不能把一個無因次比值直接換成挖深。","textEn":"Check whether shear is instantaneous or cycle-averaged and identify representative size, grading and cohesion. Test assumptions against observed motion and bed form; analyze scour depth separately rather than converting one dimensionless ratio directly into an excavation depth.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"核對剪力是瞬時或週期平均以及粒徑代表值，對照原床級配與黏性。以床形和起動觀察檢驗假設，另做沖刷深度分析，不能把一個無因次比值直接換成挖深。","textEn":"Check whether shear is instantaneous or cycle-averaged and identify representative size, grading and cohesion. Test assumptions against observed motion and bed form; analyze scour depth separately rather than converting one dimensionless ratio directly into an excavation depth.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「床面剪力無因次化」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Dimensionless bed shear\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。","核對剪力是瞬時或週期平均以及粒徑代表值，對照原床級配與黏性。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height.","Check whether shear is instantaneous or cycle-averaged and identify representative size, grading and cohesion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對剪力是瞬時或週期平均以及粒徑代表值，對照原床級配與黏性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check whether shear is instantaneous or cycle-averaged and identify representative size, grading and cohesion. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b286-v15-24","title":"床面剪力無因次化：失效診斷","titleEn":"Dimensionless bed shear: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「床面剪力無因次化」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dimensionless bed shear” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將黏土當成同粒徑砂會忽略顆粒間作用，僅取平均剪力又漏掉波峰短暫起動。錯誤起動判斷可能使原本穩定的基床保護假設突然失效。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating clay as sand of equal size omits interparticle forces, while mean shear can miss brief wave-driven motion. Incorrect onset interpretation may invalidate the assumed stability of the bed supporting or protecting the structure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設τ=2Pa、ρs=2650、ρ=1025kg/m³、D=0.0005m，θ=τ/[(ρs−ρ)gD]=0.2509；未指定起動門檻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assumeτ=2Pa,ρs=2650,ρ=1025kg/m³ and D=0.0005m. θ=τ/[(ρs−ρ)gD]=0.2509, without prescribing a motion threshold.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將黏土當成同粒徑砂會忽略顆粒間作用，僅取平均剪力又漏掉波峰短暫起動。錯誤起動判斷可能使原本穩定的基床保護假設突然失效。","textEn":"Treating clay as sand of equal size omits interparticle forces, while mean shear can miss brief wave-driven motion. Incorrect onset interpretation may invalidate the assumed stability of the bed supporting or protecting the structure.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「床面剪力無因次化」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Dimensionless bed shear\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["將黏土當成同粒徑砂會忽略顆粒間作用，僅取平均剪力又漏掉波峰短暫起動。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。"],"optionsEn":["Treating clay as sand of equal size omits interparticle forces, while mean shear can miss brief wave-driven motion.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將黏土當成同粒徑砂會忽略顆粒間作用，僅取平均剪力又漏掉波峰短暫起動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating clay as sand of equal size omits interparticle forces, while mean shear can miss brief wave-driven motion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b286-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「淺水傳播時間」與「離岸幾何與岸線」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Shallow-water propagation time\" and \"Offshore geometry and shoreline response\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b286-v15-25","title":"淺水傳播時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shallow-water propagation time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「淺水傳播時間」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Shallow-water propagation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"長波相對水深很淺時，重力與水深控制傳播速度，可用來估計堤後區域的響應時間。這個近似不適用任意短波，亦未計底摩擦或水流影響；地形改變既影響速度也可能造成反射，因此傳播時間只是辨識訊號因果的一項線索。 假設線性淺水長波h=2m，c=√(gh)=4.429m/s；傳播100m約22.58s，需滿足水深遠小於波長。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「淺水傳播時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For sufficiently long waves relative to depth, gravity and depth control propagation speed and give a response-time scale behind the structure. The approximation does not apply to arbitrary short waves and excludes friction and currents. Bathymetric changes affect speed and reflections, so travel time is only one clue for interpreting cause and effect in observations. Assume a linear shallow-water long wave at depth2m. c=√(gh)=4.429m/s;100m takes22.58s, requiring depth much smaller than wavelength. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Shallow-water propagation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「淺水傳播時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Shallow-water propagation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-25-k1","title":"淺水傳播時間","titleEn":"Shallow-water propagation time","text":"長波相對水深很淺時，重力與水深控制傳播速度，可用來估計堤後區域的響應時間。這個近似不適用任意短波，亦未計底摩擦或水流影響；地形改變既影響速度也可能造成反射，因此傳播時間只是辨識訊號因果的一項線索。","textEn":"For sufficiently long waves relative to depth, gravity and depth control propagation speed and give a response-time scale behind the structure. The approximation does not apply to arbitrary short waves and excludes friction and currents.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「淺水傳播時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shallow-water propagation time\" is correct?","options":["所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。","長波相對水深很淺時，重力與水深控制傳播速度，可用來估計堤後區域的響應時間。","堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。"],"optionsEn":["Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength.","For sufficiently long waves relative to depth, gravity and depth control propagation speed and give a response-time scale behind the structure.","The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape."],"answer":1,"explanation":"長波相對水深很淺時，重力與水深控制傳播速度，可用來估計堤後區域的響應時間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For sufficiently long waves relative to depth, gravity and depth control propagation speed and give a response-time scale behind the structure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b286-v15-26","title":"淺水傳播時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Shallow-water propagation time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「淺水傳播時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Shallow-water propagation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設線性淺水長波h=2m，c=√(gh)=4.429m/s；傳播100m約22.58s，需滿足水深遠小於波長。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a linear shallow-water long wave at depth2m. c=√(gh)=4.429m/s;100m takes22.58s, requiring depth much smaller than wavelength. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：使用觀測週期檢查淺水條件，再比較兩站訊號延遲與估算傳播時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check the shallow-water condition using observed periods, then compare interstation delay with the estimate.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設線性淺水長波h=2m，c=√(gh)=4.429m/s；傳播100m約22.58s，需滿足水深遠小於波長。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a linear shallow-water long wave at depth2m. c=√(gh)=4.429m/s;100m takes22.58s, requiring depth much smaller than wavelength.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「淺水傳播時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shallow-water propagation time\", which statement holds?","options":["模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。","波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete.","A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b286-v15-27","title":"淺水傳播時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shallow-water propagation time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「淺水傳播時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Shallow-water propagation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"使用觀測週期檢查淺水條件，再比較兩站訊號延遲與估算傳播時間。同步校正儀器時鐘並檢查流向，若延遲不符，先查反射與群波影響而非直接調整水深湊合。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check the shallow-water condition using observed periods, then compare interstation delay with the estimate. Synchronize clocks and inspect current direction; investigate reflection and wave groups before changing assumed depth merely to force agreement with the recorded lag. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：使用觀測週期檢查淺水條件，再比較兩站訊號延遲與估算傳播時間。同步校正儀器時鐘並檢查流向，若延遲不符，先查反射與群波影響而非直接調整水深湊合。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check the shallow-water condition using observed periods, then compare interstation delay with the estimate. Synchronize clocks and inspect current direction; investigate reflection and wave groups before changing assumed depth merely to force agreement with the recorded lag.","failure":"注意干擾：儀器時間不同步會製造假的傳播速度，短波套長波公式則錯估延遲。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unsynchronized instruments create false travel speeds, and short waves modeled as long waves produce incorrect delays. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"使用觀測週期檢查淺水條件，再比較兩站訊號延遲與估算傳播時間。同步校正儀器時鐘並檢查流向，若延遲不符，先查反射與群波影響而非直接調整水深湊合。","textEn":"Check the shallow-water condition using observed periods, then compare interstation delay with the estimate. Synchronize clocks and inspect current direction; investigate reflection and wave groups before changing assumed depth merely to force agreement with the recorded lag.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"使用觀測週期檢查淺水條件，再比較兩站訊號延遲與估算傳播時間。同步校正儀器時鐘並檢查流向，若延遲不符，先查反射與群波影響而非直接調整水深湊合。","textEn":"Check the shallow-water condition using observed periods, then compare interstation delay with the estimate. Synchronize clocks and inspect current direction; investigate reflection and wave groups before changing assumed depth merely to force agreement with the recorded lag.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「淺水傳播時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shallow-water propagation time\"?","options":["使用觀測週期檢查淺水條件，再比較兩站訊號延遲與估算傳播時間。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。"],"optionsEn":["Check the shallow-water condition using observed periods, then compare interstation delay with the estimate.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point."],"answer":0,"explanation":"使用觀測週期檢查淺水條件，再比較兩站訊號延遲與估算傳播時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check the shallow-water condition using observed periods, then compare interstation delay with the estimate. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b286-v15-28","title":"淺水傳播時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shallow-water propagation time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「淺水傳播時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Shallow-water propagation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"儀器時間不同步會製造假的傳播速度，短波套長波公式則錯估延遲。把相關性峰值自動解釋為同一波列，還可能忽略反射訊號的替代來源。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unsynchronized instruments create false travel speeds, and short waves modeled as long waves produce incorrect delays. Automatically interpreting a correlation peak as one traveling wave can also overlook reflections as an alternative signal source. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設線性淺水長波h=2m，c=√(gh)=4.429m/s；傳播100m約22.58s，需滿足水深遠小於波長。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume a linear shallow-water long wave at depth2m. c=√(gh)=4.429m/s;100m takes22.58s, requiring depth much smaller than wavelength.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"儀器時間不同步會製造假的傳播速度，短波套長波公式則錯估延遲。把相關性峰值自動解釋為同一波列，還可能忽略反射訊號的替代來源。","textEn":"Unsynchronized instruments create false travel speeds, and short waves modeled as long waves produce incorrect delays. Automatically interpreting a correlation peak as one traveling wave can also overlook reflections as an alternative signal source.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「淺水傳播時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shallow-water propagation time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","儀器時間不同步會製造假的傳播速度，短波套長波公式則錯估延遲。","堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Unsynchronized instruments create false travel speeds, and short waves modeled as long waves produce incorrect delays.","The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape."],"answer":1,"explanation":"儀器時間不同步會製造假的傳播速度，短波套長波公式則錯估延遲。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unsynchronized instruments create false travel speeds, and short waves modeled as long waves produce incorrect delays. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b286-v15-29","title":"離岸幾何與岸線：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Offshore geometry and shoreline response: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「離岸幾何與岸線」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Offshore geometry and shoreline response” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"堤長與離岸距離影響遮蔽區形狀，但岸線反應同時受波向、輸砂供應及缺口控制。幾何比例可以整理案例，不能直接預報連島砂洲或突出灘形成；功能比較還需確認結構淹水狀態及尺度，避免將出水防波堤經驗直接移植到潛堤。 假設堤長L=100m、離岸距X=200m，L/X=0.50；僅為幾何描述，不是連島砂洲必然形成的門檻。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「離岸幾何與岸線」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Length and offshore distance influence the sheltered footprint, but wave direction, sediment supply and gaps also govern shoreline response. A geometric ratio organizes comparisons; it does not directly predict a salient or tombolo. Comparisons must account for submergence and scale rather than transferring emerged-breakwater experience directly to a submerged structure in a different sediment regime. Assume length100m and offshore distance200m. L/X=0.50 describes geometry only and is not a threshold guaranteeing tombolo formation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Offshore geometry and shoreline response” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「離岸幾何與岸線」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Offshore geometry and shoreline response”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-29-k1","title":"離岸幾何與岸線","titleEn":"Offshore geometry and shoreline response","text":"堤長與離岸距離影響遮蔽區形狀，但岸線反應同時受波向、輸砂供應及缺口控制。幾何比例可以整理案例，不能直接預報連島砂洲或突出灘形成；功能比較還需確認結構淹水狀態及尺度，避免將出水防波堤經驗直接移植到潛堤。","textEn":"Length and offshore distance influence the sheltered footprint, but wave direction, sediment supply and gaps also govern shoreline response. A geometric ratio organizes comparisons; it does not directly predict a salient or tombolo.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「離岸幾何與岸線」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Offshore geometry and shoreline response\" is correct?","options":["堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。","覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。","堤長與離岸距離影響遮蔽區形狀，但岸線反應同時受波向、輸砂供應及缺口控制。"],"optionsEn":["The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape.","The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height.","Length and offshore distance influence the sheltered footprint, but wave direction, sediment supply and gaps also govern shoreline response."],"answer":2,"explanation":"堤長與離岸距離影響遮蔽區形狀，但岸線反應同時受波向、輸砂供應及缺口控制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Length and offshore distance influence the sheltered footprint, but wave direction, sediment supply and gaps also govern shoreline response. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b286-v15-30","title":"離岸幾何與岸線：定量估算","titleEn":"Offshore geometry and shoreline response: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「離岸幾何與岸線」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Offshore geometry and shoreline response” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設堤長L=100m、離岸距X=200m，L/X=0.50；僅為幾何描述，不是連島砂洲必然形成的門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume length100m and offshore distance200m. L/X=0.50 describes geometry only and is not a threshold guaranteeing tombolo formation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在同一岸線基準下量堤長與距離，記錄波向分布、沿岸砂源和缺口位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure length and distance against a consistent shoreline reference and record directional waves, sediment supply and gaps.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設堤長L=100m、離岸距X=200m，L/X=0.50；僅為幾何描述，不是連島砂洲必然形成的門檻。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume length100m and offshore distance200m. L/X=0.50 describes geometry only and is not a threshold guaranteeing tombolo formation.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「離岸幾何與岸線」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Offshore geometry and shoreline response\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。","只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width.","At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b286-v15-31","title":"離岸幾何與岸線：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Offshore geometry and shoreline response: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「離岸幾何與岸線」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Offshore geometry and shoreline response” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在同一岸線基準下量堤長與距離，記錄波向分布、沿岸砂源和缺口位置。比較不同季節地形及鄰岸變化，將相似幾何但不同淹水條件的案例分開解讀。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure length and distance against a consistent shoreline reference and record directional waves, sediment supply and gaps. Compare seasonal and neighboring terrain, distinguishing geometrically similar cases whose submergence and transport conditions differ substantially from the site under study. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在同一岸線基準下量堤長與距離，記錄波向分布、沿岸砂源和缺口位置。比較不同季節地形及鄰岸變化，將相似幾何但不同淹水條件的案例分開解讀。","observationEn":"Site practice: Measure length and distance against a consistent shoreline reference and record directional waves, sediment supply and gaps. Compare seasonal and neighboring terrain, distinguishing geometrically similar cases whose submergence and transport conditions differ substantially from the site under study.","failure":"注意干擾：某一波向下的堆砂可能在季風轉向後消失，上游攔砂也可能讓遮蔽區缺乏材料。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Accumulation under one wave direction may disappear after seasonal reversal, while updrift interception leaves little sand for the shelter. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在同一岸線基準下量堤長與距離，記錄波向分布、沿岸砂源和缺口位置。比較不同季節地形及鄰岸變化，將相似幾何但不同淹水條件的案例分開解讀。","textEn":"Measure length and distance against a consistent shoreline reference and record directional waves, sediment supply and gaps. Compare seasonal and neighboring terrain, distinguishing geometrically similar cases whose submergence and transport conditions differ substantially from the site under study.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在同一岸線基準下量堤長與距離，記錄波向分布、沿岸砂源和缺口位置。比較不同季節地形及鄰岸變化，將相似幾何但不同淹水條件的案例分開解讀。","textEn":"Measure length and distance against a consistent shoreline reference and record directional waves, sediment supply and gaps. Compare seasonal and neighboring terrain, distinguishing geometrically similar cases whose submergence and transport conditions differ substantially from the site under study.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「離岸幾何與岸線」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Offshore geometry and shoreline response\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在同一岸線基準下量堤長與距離，記錄波向分布、沿岸砂源和缺口位置。","規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Measure length and distance against a consistent shoreline reference and record directional waves, sediment supply and gaps.","Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在同一岸線基準下量堤長與距離，記錄波向分布、沿岸砂源和缺口位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure length and distance against a consistent shoreline reference and record directional waves, sediment supply and gaps. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b286-v15-32","title":"離岸幾何與岸線：失效診斷","titleEn":"Offshore geometry and shoreline response: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「離岸幾何與岸線」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Offshore geometry and shoreline response” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"某一波向下的堆砂可能在季風轉向後消失，上游攔砂也可能讓遮蔽區缺乏材料。只憑幾何比例許諾岸線效果，會忽略整段海岸的收支限制。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Accumulation under one wave direction may disappear after seasonal reversal, while updrift interception leaves little sand for the shelter. Geometry-only promises therefore ignore sediment-budget limitations across the wider coast and its changing wave climate. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設堤長L=100m、離岸距X=200m，L/X=0.50；僅為幾何描述，不是連島砂洲必然形成的門檻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: L/X=0.50 describes geometry only and is not a threshold guaranteeing tombolo formation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「堤長與離岸距的比值足以唯一決定未來岸線形狀。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The length-to-offshore-distance ratio uniquely determines the future shoreline shape.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"某一波向下的堆砂可能在季風轉向後消失，上游攔砂也可能讓遮蔽區缺乏材料。只憑幾何比例許諾岸線效果，會忽略整段海岸的收支限制。","textEn":"Accumulation under one wave direction may disappear after seasonal reversal, while updrift interception leaves little sand for the shelter. Geometry-only promises therefore ignore sediment-budget limitations across the wider coast and its changing wave climate.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「離岸幾何與岸線」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Offshore geometry and shoreline response\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。","某一波向下的堆砂可能在季風轉向後消失，上游攔砂也可能讓遮蔽區缺乏材料。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height.","Accumulation under one wave direction may disappear after seasonal reversal, while updrift interception leaves little sand for the shelter."],"answer":2,"explanation":"某一波向下的堆砂可能在季風轉向後消失，上游攔砂也可能讓遮蔽區缺乏材料。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Accumulation under one wave direction may disappear after seasonal reversal, while updrift interception leaves little sand for the shelter. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b286-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「堤頂沉陷與覆水」與「數值步長與收斂」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Crest settlement and water cover\" and \"Numerical timestep and convergence\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b286-v15-33","title":"堤頂沉陷與覆水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Crest settlement and water cover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「堤頂沉陷與覆水」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Crest settlement and water cover” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"潛堤長期沉陷會增加覆水並改變波浪互動，不能只把沉陷看成材料方量問題。局部差異沉陷還形成優先過流通道，而透射對幾何的反應通常非線性；需要把結構監測、水位歷程與水理測試放在同一狀態描述中追蹤。 假設水位固定、原覆水0.8m，堤頂沉陷0.2m後覆水1.0m，增加25%；不能推論透射波高也增25%。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「堤頂沉陷與覆水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Settlement increases water cover and changes wave interaction rather than merely reducing material volume. Differential movement also creates preferred flow paths, while transmission often responds nonlinearly to geometry. Structural surveys, water-level history and hydraulic observations therefore need to describe the same evolving state; a percentage change in cover cannot determine an equal change in transmission. Assume fixed water level and original cover0.8m. Crest settlement0.2m raises cover to1.0m, a25% increase, not necessarily25% higher transmission. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Crest settlement and water cover” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「堤頂沉陷與覆水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Crest settlement and water cover”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-33-k1","title":"堤頂沉陷與覆水","titleEn":"Crest settlement and water cover","text":"潛堤長期沉陷會增加覆水並改變波浪互動，不能只把沉陷看成材料方量問題。局部差異沉陷還形成優先過流通道，而透射對幾何的反應通常非線性；需要把結構監測、水位歷程與水理測試放在同一狀態描述中追蹤。","textEn":"Settlement increases water cover and changes wave interaction rather than merely reducing material volume. Differential movement also creates preferred flow paths, while transmission often responds nonlinearly to geometry.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「堤頂沉陷與覆水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Crest settlement and water cover\" is correct?","options":["潛堤長期沉陷會增加覆水並改變波浪互動，不能只把沉陷看成材料方量問題。","覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。","模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。"],"optionsEn":["Settlement increases water cover and changes wave interaction rather than merely reducing material volume.","The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height.","Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete."],"answer":0,"explanation":"潛堤長期沉陷會增加覆水並改變波浪互動，不能只把沉陷看成材料方量問題。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Settlement increases water cover and changes wave interaction rather than merely reducing material volume. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b286-v15-34","title":"堤頂沉陷與覆水：定量估算","titleEn":"Crest settlement and water cover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「堤頂沉陷與覆水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Crest settlement and water cover” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水位固定、原覆水0.8m，堤頂沉陷0.2m後覆水1.0m，增加25%；不能推論透射波高也增25%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume fixed water level and original cover0.8m. Crest settlement0.2m raises cover to1.0m, a25% increase, not necessarily25% higher transmission. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：重測堤頂縱剖面並連結共同水位，分離均勻沉陷與局部凹槽。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Resurvey the crest against a shared water datum, separating uniform settlement from local troughs.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水位固定、原覆水0.8m，堤頂沉陷0.2m後覆水1.0m，增加25%；不能推論透射波高也增25%。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume fixed water level and original cover0.8m. Crest settlement0.2m raises cover to1.0m, a25% increase, not necessarily25% higher transmission.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「堤頂沉陷與覆水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Crest settlement and water cover\", which statement holds?","options":["波高減少六成就必然表示能量通量也只減少六成。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","缺口平均流速可以直接當成每一個位置的瞬時最大流速。"],"optionsEn":["A sixty-percent reduction in wave height always means exactly sixty-percent less energy flux.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The gap-average velocity directly gives the instantaneous maximum at every point."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b286-v15-35","title":"堤頂沉陷與覆水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Crest settlement and water cover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「堤頂沉陷與覆水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Crest settlement and water cover” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"重測堤頂縱剖面並連結共同水位，分離均勻沉陷與局部凹槽。以相近波況比較前後透射，保留地基與構件位移紀錄，確認變化是否來自沉陷而非潮位差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Resurvey the crest against a shared water datum, separating uniform settlement from local troughs. Compare transmission under similar waves and retain foundation and unit-movement records, checking whether the observed change results from settlement rather than different tidal levels. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重測堤頂縱剖面並連結共同水位，分離均勻沉陷與局部凹槽。以相近波況比較前後透射，保留地基與構件位移紀錄，確認變化是否來自沉陷而非潮位差。","observationEn":"Site practice: Resurvey the crest against a shared water datum, separating uniform settlement from local troughs. Compare transmission under similar waves and retain foundation and unit-movement records, checking whether the observed change results from settlement rather than different tidal levels.","failure":"注意干擾：量測只追最高點會漏掉主要低槽，平均沉陷很小仍可能有集中水流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Tracking only crest high points misses controlling troughs, allowing concentrated flow despite small mean settlement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"重測堤頂縱剖面並連結共同水位，分離均勻沉陷與局部凹槽。以相近波況比較前後透射，保留地基與構件位移紀錄，確認變化是否來自沉陷而非潮位差。","textEn":"Resurvey the crest against a shared water datum, separating uniform settlement from local troughs. Compare transmission under similar waves and retain foundation and unit-movement records, checking whether the observed change results from settlement rather than different tidal levels.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重測堤頂縱剖面並連結共同水位，分離均勻沉陷與局部凹槽。以相近波況比較前後透射，保留地基與構件位移紀錄，確認變化是否來自沉陷而非潮位差。","textEn":"Resurvey the crest against a shared water datum, separating uniform settlement from local troughs. Compare transmission under similar waves and retain foundation and unit-movement records, checking whether the observed change results from settlement rather than different tidal levels.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「堤頂沉陷與覆水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Crest settlement and water cover\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","希爾茲參數的數值本身就是預期海床沖刷深度。","重測堤頂縱剖面並連結共同水位，分離均勻沉陷與局部凹槽。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The numerical Shields parameter directly equals the expected seabed scour depth.","Resurvey the crest against a shared water datum, separating uniform settlement from local troughs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重測堤頂縱剖面並連結共同水位，分離均勻沉陷與局部凹槽。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Resurvey the crest against a shared water datum, separating uniform settlement from local troughs. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b286-v15-36","title":"堤頂沉陷與覆水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Crest settlement and water cover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「堤頂沉陷與覆水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Crest settlement and water cover” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"量測只追最高點會漏掉主要低槽，平均沉陷很小仍可能有集中水流。不同潮位的透射資料若直接比較，則可能把水位造成的差別誤認為結構損壞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Tracking only crest high points misses controlling troughs, allowing concentrated flow despite small mean settlement. Comparing transmission at different tides can instead mistake a water-level effect for deterioration of the physical structure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設水位固定、原覆水0.8m，堤頂沉陷0.2m後覆水1.0m，增加25%；不能推論透射波高也增25%。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Crest settlement0.2m raises cover to1.0m, a25% increase, not necessarily25% higher transmission.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「覆水深度增加百分比必定等於透射波高增加百分比。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The percentage increase in water cover must equal the percentage increase in transmitted height.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"量測只追最高點會漏掉主要低槽，平均沉陷很小仍可能有集中水流。不同潮位的透射資料若直接比較，則可能把水位造成的差別誤認為結構損壞。","textEn":"Tracking only crest high points misses controlling troughs, allowing concentrated flow despite small mean settlement. Comparing transmission at different tides can instead mistake a water-level effect for deterioration of the physical structure.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「堤頂沉陷與覆水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Crest settlement and water cover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["量測只追最高點會漏掉主要低槽，平均沉陷很小仍可能有集中水流。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。"],"optionsEn":["Tracking only crest high points misses controlling troughs, allowing concentrated flow despite small mean settlement.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete."],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測只追最高點會漏掉主要低槽，平均沉陷很小仍可能有集中水流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Tracking only crest high points misses controlling troughs, allowing concentrated flow despite small mean settlement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b286-v15-37","title":"數值步長與收斂：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Numerical timestep and convergence: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「數值步長與收斂」如何影響離岸潛堤地形整合的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Numerical timestep and convergence” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Submerged-breakwater coastal integration”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"地形整合模型需要同時考慮波流與泥沙的數值尺度，計算能運行不代表已收斂。特徵速度限制顯式步長，但邊界、乾濕轉換及所用格式可能更嚴；網格與步長應分別細化，並保持物理邊界一致，才能分辨數值擴散與真實地形平滑。 假設一維顯式淺水示意U=2m/s、h=2m、Δt=0.5s、Δx=5m，C=(U+√gh)Δt/Δx=0.6429；非穩定保證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「數值步長與收斂」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A morphology model must resolve wave-current and sediment scales, and successful execution does not establish convergence. Characteristic speed constrains an explicit timestep, while boundaries, wetting and drying or the selected scheme may be more restrictive. Refine space and time separately under unchanged physical boundaries to distinguish numerical diffusion from genuine smoothing of coastal terrain. Assume a one-dimensional explicit shallow-water illustration: U=2m/s,h=2m,Δt=0.5s,Δx=5m. C=(U+√gh)Δt/Δx=0.6429, not guaranteed stability. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Numerical timestep and convergence” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「數值步長與收斂」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Numerical timestep and convergence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-37-k1","title":"數值步長與收斂","titleEn":"Numerical timestep and convergence","text":"地形整合模型需要同時考慮波流與泥沙的數值尺度，計算能運行不代表已收斂。特徵速度限制顯式步長，但邊界、乾濕轉換及所用格式可能更嚴；網格與步長應分別細化，並保持物理邊界一致，才能分辨數值擴散與真實地形平滑。","textEn":"A morphology model must resolve wave-current and sediment scales, and successful execution does not establish convergence. Characteristic speed constrains an explicit timestep, while boundaries, wetting and drying or the selected scheme may be more restrictive.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「數值步長與收斂」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Numerical timestep and convergence\" is correct?","options":["模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。","地形整合模型需要同時考慮波流與泥沙的數值尺度，計算能運行不代表已收斂。","相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。"],"optionsEn":["Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete.","A morphology model must resolve wave-current and sediment scales, and successful execution does not establish convergence.","Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width."],"answer":1,"explanation":"地形整合模型需要同時考慮波流與泥沙的數值尺度，計算能運行不代表已收斂。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A morphology model must resolve wave-current and sediment scales, and successful execution does not establish convergence. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b286-v15-38","title":"數值步長與收斂：定量估算","titleEn":"Numerical timestep and convergence: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「數值步長與收斂」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Numerical timestep and convergence” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設一維顯式淺水示意U=2m/s、h=2m、Δt=0.5s、Δx=5m，C=(U+√gh)Δt/Δx=0.6429；非穩定保證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a one-dimensional explicit shallow-water illustration: U=2m/s,h=2m,Δt=0.5s,Δx=5m. C=(U+√gh)Δt/Δx=0.6429, not guaranteed stability. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐區檢查最小網格、最大特徵速度與時間步長，確認採用格式的條件。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check local minimum spacing, maximum characteristic speed and timestep against the actual scheme.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設一維顯式淺水示意U=2m/s、h=2m、Δt=0.5s、Δx=5m，C=(U+√gh)Δt/Δx=0.6429；非穩定保證。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a one-dimensional explicit shallow-water illustration: U=2m/s,h=2m,Δt=0.5s,Δx=5m. C=(U+√gh)Δt/Δx=0.6429, not guaranteed stability.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「數值步長與收斂」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Numerical timestep and convergence\", which statement holds?","options":["只要堤頂水深固定所有週期和波形都在同一高度破波。","規則波高和顯著波高可直接代入同一能量係數而無差別。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["At fixed crest depth every period and waveform breaks at exactly the same height.","Regular height and significant height can use the same energy coefficient without change.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b286-v15-39","title":"數值步長與收斂：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Numerical timestep and convergence: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「數值步長與收斂」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Numerical timestep and convergence” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐區檢查最小網格、最大特徵速度與時間步長，確認採用格式的條件。另做網格和步長細化，核對水量與泥沙守恆殘差，保存未收斂區域而不只展示平滑的彩色圖。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check local minimum spacing, maximum characteristic speed and timestep against the actual scheme. Refine grid and time separately, audit water and sediment residuals, and retain unconverged regions rather than displaying only smooth and visually persuasive contour maps. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：逐區檢查最小網格、最大特徵速度與時間步長，確認採用格式的條件。另做網格和步長細化，核對水量與泥沙守恆殘差，保存未收斂區域而不只展示平滑的彩色圖。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check local minimum spacing, maximum characteristic speed and timestep against the actual scheme. Refine grid and time separately, audit water and sediment residuals, and retain unconverged regions rather than displaying only smooth and visually persuasive contour maps.","failure":"注意干擾：平均網格符合條件仍可能在小網格區失穩，過度數值擴散則可能掩蓋缺口流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A satisfactory average grid hides instability in smaller cells, while excessive diffusion conceals gap currents. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐區檢查最小網格、最大特徵速度與時間步長，確認採用格式的條件。另做網格和步長細化，核對水量與泥沙守恆殘差，保存未收斂區域而不只展示平滑的彩色圖。","textEn":"Check local minimum spacing, maximum characteristic speed and timestep against the actual scheme. Refine grid and time separately, audit water and sediment residuals, and retain unconverged regions rather than displaying only smooth and visually persuasive contour maps.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"逐區檢查最小網格、最大特徵速度與時間步長，確認採用格式的條件。另做網格和步長細化，核對水量與泥沙守恆殘差，保存未收斂區域而不只展示平滑的彩色圖。","textEn":"Check local minimum spacing, maximum characteristic speed and timestep against the actual scheme. Refine grid and time separately, audit water and sediment residuals, and retain unconverged regions rather than displaying only smooth and visually persuasive contour maps.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「數值步長與收斂」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Numerical timestep and convergence\"?","options":["逐區檢查最小網格、最大特徵速度與時間步長，確認採用格式的條件。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","所有海浪的傳播速度都只由水深決定而與波長無關。"],"optionsEn":["Check local minimum spacing, maximum characteristic speed and timestep against the actual scheme.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Every ocean wave travels at a speed determined only by depth, regardless of wavelength."],"answer":0,"explanation":"逐區檢查最小網格、最大特徵速度與時間步長，確認採用格式的條件。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check local minimum spacing, maximum characteristic speed and timestep against the actual scheme. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b286-v15-40","title":"數值步長與收斂：失效診斷","titleEn":"Numerical timestep and convergence: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"prerequisiteIds":["b286-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「數值步長與收斂」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Numerical timestep and convergence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"平均網格符合條件仍可能在小網格區失穩，過度數值擴散則可能掩蓋缺口流。圖像平滑不代表守恆正確，錯誤地形趨勢甚至可能看起來很合理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A satisfactory average grid hides instability in smaller cells, while excessive diffusion conceals gap currents. Smooth graphics do not establish conservation, and an incorrect morphological trend can still appear visually plausible to an uncritical observer. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設一維顯式淺水示意U=2m/s、h=2m、Δt=0.5s、Δx=5m，C=(U+√gh)Δt/Δx=0.6429；非穩定保證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: C=(U+√gh)Δt/Δx=0.6429, not guaranteed stability.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模型圖形平滑且沒有報錯就代表網格與時間步長已收斂。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Smooth output without error messages proves that grid and timestep convergence is complete.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b286-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"平均網格符合條件仍可能在小網格區失穩，過度數值擴散則可能掩蓋缺口流。圖像平滑不代表守恆正確，錯誤地形趨勢甚至可能看起來很合理。","textEn":"A satisfactory average grid hides instability in smaller cells, while excessive diffusion conceals gap currents. Smooth graphics do not establish conservation, and an incorrect morphological trend can still appear visually plausible to an uncritical observer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]},{"id":"b286-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「數值步長與收斂」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Numerical timestep and convergence\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","平均網格符合條件仍可能在小網格區失穩，過度數值擴散則可能掩蓋缺口流。","相對淹水深等於波高透射係數且不受堤寬影響。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A satisfactory average grid hides instability in smaller cells, while excessive diffusion conceals gap currents.","Relative submergence equals the wave-height transmission coefficient regardless of crest width."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均網格符合條件仍可能在小網格區失穩，過度數值擴散則可能掩蓋缺口流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A satisfactory average grid hides instability in smaller cells, while excessive diffusion conceals gap currents. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-cem","v15s-borth-report","v15s-sandmotor","v15s-newbiggin"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b287","title":"港池航道疏浚","titleEn":"Harbor-basin and navigation-channel dredging","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以測深方量泥漿輸送與環境收支管理港池航道疏浚。課程從邊界辨識與資料整理走到水理量化、構造介面及驗證紀錄；每一步把計算結果連回可量測的證據。十個不同單元分別處理關鍵機制，不以名義尺寸或單一通過率代替整體工程判斷，並明列合成算例與現地資料的差別。","summaryEn":"Manage harbor dredging through sounding, volume, slurry transport and environmental accounting. The course moves from boundary identification and evidence to hydraulic quantification, structural interfaces and verification records. Ten distinct units connect each calculated quantity to measurable evidence. Nominal geometry or a single pass rate does not establish whole-system performance, and synthetic teaching examples remain separate from field observations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-coasts","subcategoryTitle":"海岸、港灣與水資源韌性","subcategoryTitleEn":"Coasts, ports and water-resource resilience","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-coasts","learningTags":["water","water-coasts","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-coast","architectureNodes":[["疏浚稜體與斷面","Dredging prism and sections"],["乾固體生產率","Dry-solid production rate"],["泵送能量收支","Pumping energy balance"],["測深不確定度預算","Sounding uncertainty budget"],["回流水固體平衡","Return-water solids balance"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-coast","labels":["疏浚稜體與斷面","乾固體生產率","泵送能量收支","測深不確定度預算","回流水固體平衡"],"labelsEn":["Dredging prism and sections","Dry-solid production rate","Pumping energy balance","Sounding uncertainty budget","Return-water solids balance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為原創合成算例，不是地標工程的實測或推薦操作值。教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設相鄰斷面挖方面積120與180m²、間距50m，V=(120+180)×50/2=7500m³；限線性面積變化。假設第二斷面面積由180增10%至198m²，其餘不變，方量由7500增至7950m³，只增加6%；不是任何航道加深都按同一百分比變化。重新計算前先列固定條件、單位、適用尺度及可能失效的邊界。把模型敏感度與測量誤差分開，不能將單一參數變化直接當成工程風險或壽命比例。比較兩次結果後，記錄還需要哪些獨立證據，並由負責專業人員判斷適用性。","textEn":"This original synthetic example is neither a landmark measurement nor a recommended operating value. Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume excavation areas120 and180m² separated by50m. V=(120+180)×50/2=7500m³, assuming linear area variation. Increasing the second section area from180 to198m² by10% with everything else fixed raises volume from7500 to7950m³, only6%; this is not a universal channel-deepening response. Before recalculating, list fixed conditions, units, applicable scale and boundaries that could fail. Separate model sensitivity from measurement uncertainty: a parameter change does not directly give a proportional change in engineering risk or service life. Compare the results, record independent evidence still needed, and have the responsible specialist determine applicability.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b287-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「疏浚稜體與斷面」與「泥漿密度與濃度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Dredging prism and sections\" and \"Slurry density and concentration\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b287-v15-01","title":"疏浚稜體與斷面：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Dredging prism and sections: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「疏浚稜體與斷面」如何影響港池航道疏浚的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dredging prism and sections” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Harbor-basin and navigation-channel dredging”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"航道挖方由既有海床和目標稜體之差形成，邊坡與局部淺點不能用單一平均深度取代。相鄰斷面梯形積分只在面積沿程近似線性時合理，曲率大時應加密；計量還須區分設計挖方、允許超挖及實際移除量，避免讓合約分類混入物理收支。 假設相鄰斷面挖方面積120與180m²、間距50m，V=(120+180)×50/2=7500m³；限線性面積變化。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「疏浚稜體與斷面」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Excavation is the difference between surveyed bed and a defined dredging prism; side slopes and local shoals cannot be replaced by one mean depth. Trapezoidal integration assumes approximately linear area variation between sections and needs refinement where curvature is large. Design volume, permitted overdepth and actual removal remain distinct quantities in the physical balance. Assume excavation areas120 and180m² separated by50m. V=(120+180)×50/2=7500m³, assuming linear area variation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Dredging prism and sections” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「航道平均深度達標就代表每個局部淺點都已移除。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Meeting average channel depth proves that every local controlling shoal has been removed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「疏浚稜體與斷面」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Dredging prism and sections”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-01-k1","title":"疏浚稜體與斷面","titleEn":"Dredging prism and sections","text":"航道挖方由既有海床和目標稜體之差形成，邊坡與局部淺點不能用單一平均深度取代。相鄰斷面梯形積分只在面積沿程近似線性時合理，曲率大時應加密；計量還須區分設計挖方、允許超挖及實際移除量，避免讓合約分類混入物理收支。","textEn":"Excavation is the difference between surveyed bed and a defined dredging prism; side slopes and local shoals cannot be replaced by one mean depth. Trapezoidal integration assumes approximately linear area variation between sections and needs refinement where curvature is large.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：航道平均深度達標就代表每個局部淺點都已移除。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Meeting average channel depth proves that every local controlling shoal has been removed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疏浚稜體與斷面」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Dredging prism and sections\" is correct?","options":["航道平均深度達標就代表每個局部淺點都已移除。","航道挖方由既有海床和目標稜體之差形成，邊坡與局部淺點不能用單一平均深度取代。","固體質量百分比和固體體積百分比可以不加換算直接互用。"],"optionsEn":["Meeting average channel depth proves that every local controlling shoal has been removed.","Excavation is the difference between surveyed bed and a defined dredging prism; side slopes and local shoals cannot be replaced by one mean depth.","Solid mass percentage and solid volume percentage are interchangeable without conversion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"航道挖方由既有海床和目標稜體之差形成，邊坡與局部淺點不能用單一平均深度取代。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Excavation is the difference between surveyed bed and a defined dredging prism; side slopes and local shoals cannot be replaced by one mean depth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b287-v15-02","title":"疏浚稜體與斷面：定量估算","titleEn":"Dredging prism and sections: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「疏浚稜體與斷面」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dredging prism and sections” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設相鄰斷面挖方面積120與180m²、間距50m，V=(120+180)×50/2=7500m³；限線性面積變化。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume excavation areas120 and180m² separated by50m. V=(120+180)×50/2=7500m³, assuming linear area variation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：繪出原床、設計底與邊坡交線，核對各斷面是否使用同一高程。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot original bed, design bottom and side-slope intersections on a shared datum.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設相鄰斷面挖方面積120與180m²、間距50m，V=(120+180)×50/2=7500m³；限線性面積變化。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume excavation areas120 and180m² separated by50m. V=(120+180)×50/2=7500m³, assuming linear area variation.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「疏浚稜體與斷面」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Dredging prism and sections\", which statement holds?","options":["清水管損公式無需任何修正就能保證高濃度泥漿可輸送。","測得聲波往返距離後不必考慮探頭吃水與潮位修正。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["An uncorrected clear-water friction formula guarantees transport of concentrated dredging slurry.","Acoustic range alone gives charted bed elevation without draft or tide correction.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b287-v15-03","title":"疏浚稜體與斷面：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Dredging prism and sections: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「疏浚稜體與斷面」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dredging prism and sections” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"繪出原床、設計底與邊坡交線，核對各斷面是否使用同一高程。加入中間剖面測試線性假設，並將超挖和不可測區獨立列帳，讓方量差能追溯到具體幾何。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot original bed, design bottom and side-slope intersections on a shared datum. Add an intermediate section to test linearity, and account for overdepth and unmeasured areas separately so volume differences remain traceable to explicit geometry. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：繪出原床、設計底與邊坡交線，核對各斷面是否使用同一高程。加入中間剖面測試線性假設，並將超挖和不可測區獨立列帳，讓方量差能追溯到具體幾何。","observationEn":"Site practice: Plot original bed, design bottom and side-slope intersections on a shared datum. Add an intermediate section to test linearity, and account for overdepth and unmeasured areas separately so volume differences remain traceable to explicit geometry.","failure":"注意干擾：斷面間藏有淺脊時梯形法會低估挖方，若把合約允許超挖全算成已挖則高估完成量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A hidden ridge between sections understates excavation, while treating all permitted overdepth as completed removal overstates progress. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"繪出原床、設計底與邊坡交線，核對各斷面是否使用同一高程。加入中間剖面測試線性假設，並將超挖和不可測區獨立列帳，讓方量差能追溯到具體幾何。","textEn":"Plot original bed, design bottom and side-slope intersections on a shared datum. Add an intermediate section to test linearity, and account for overdepth and unmeasured areas separately so volume differences remain traceable to explicit geometry.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"繪出原床、設計底與邊坡交線，核對各斷面是否使用同一高程。加入中間剖面測試線性假設，並將超挖和不可測區獨立列帳，讓方量差能追溯到具體幾何。","textEn":"Plot original bed, design bottom and side-slope intersections on a shared datum. Add an intermediate section to test linearity, and account for overdepth and unmeasured areas separately so volume differences remain traceable to explicit geometry.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「疏浚稜體與斷面」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Dredging prism and sections\"?","options":["繪出原床、設計底與邊坡交線，核對各斷面是否使用同一高程。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","靜態水深大於吃水就代表任何航速與波況都可以通航。"],"optionsEn":["Plot original bed, design bottom and side-slope intersections on a shared datum.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Water depth exceeding draft permits navigation at every speed and wave condition."],"answer":0,"explanation":"繪出原床、設計底與邊坡交線，核對各斷面是否使用同一高程。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot original bed, design bottom and side-slope intersections on a shared datum. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b287-v15-04","title":"疏浚稜體與斷面：失效診斷","titleEn":"Dredging prism and sections: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「疏浚稜體與斷面」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dredging prism and sections” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"斷面間藏有淺脊時梯形法會低估挖方，若把合約允許超挖全算成已挖則高估完成量。平均深度達到目標，也不能證明船舶通過路徑無淺點。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A hidden ridge between sections understates excavation, while treating all permitted overdepth as completed removal overstates progress. Adequate mean depth does not establish that the vessel route is free from controlling shallow features. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設相鄰斷面挖方面積120與180m²、間距50m，V=(120+180)×50/2=7500m³；限線性面積變化。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: V=(120+180)×50/2=7500m³, assuming linear area variation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「航道平均深度達標就代表每個局部淺點都已移除。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Meeting average channel depth proves that every local controlling shoal has been removed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"斷面間藏有淺脊時梯形法會低估挖方，若把合約允許超挖全算成已挖則高估完成量。平均深度達到目標，也不能證明船舶通過路徑無淺點。","textEn":"A hidden ridge between sections understates excavation, while treating all permitted overdepth as completed removal overstates progress. Adequate mean depth does not establish that the vessel route is free from controlling shallow features.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「疏浚稜體與斷面」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Dredging prism and sections\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","斷面間藏有淺脊時梯形法會低估挖方，若把合約允許超挖全算成已挖則高估完成量。","固體質量百分比和固體體積百分比可以不加換算直接互用。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A hidden ridge between sections understates excavation, while treating all permitted overdepth as completed removal overstates progress.","Solid mass percentage and solid volume percentage are interchangeable without conversion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"斷面間藏有淺脊時梯形法會低估挖方，若把合約允許超挖全算成已挖則高估完成量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A hidden ridge between sections understates excavation, while treating all permitted overdepth as completed removal overstates progress. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b287-v15-05","title":"泥漿密度與濃度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Slurry density and concentration: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「泥漿密度與濃度」如何影響港池航道疏浚的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Slurry density and concentration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Harbor-basin and navigation-channel dredging”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"泥漿混合密度可在兩相體積相加假設下推回固體體積濃度，但氣泡、鹽度與粒子密度變化會破壞簡單換算。質量濃度與體積濃度不是同一比例，需先定義量測對象；濃度提高也會改變流變和輸送阻力，不能只以濃泥漿代表高效作業。 假設泥漿1300、清水1000、顆粒2650kg/m³，Cv=(1300−1000)/(2650−1000)=0.1818；忽略含氣與體積非加成。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「泥漿密度與濃度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Under additive two-phase volumes, mixture density estimates solid volume concentration. Bubbles, salinity and varying grain density violate the simple conversion. Mass and volume concentration are different fractions and require explicit definitions. Higher concentration also changes rheology and resistance, so denser slurry does not by itself demonstrate efficient or sustainable pumping performance along the entire line. Assume mixture1300, water1000 and grains2650kg/m³. Cv=(1300−1000)/(2650−1000)=0.1818, excluding air and nonadditive volume effects. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Slurry density and concentration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「固體質量百分比和固體體積百分比可以不加換算直接互用。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Solid mass percentage and solid volume percentage are interchangeable without conversion.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「泥漿密度與濃度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Slurry density and concentration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-05-k1","title":"泥漿密度與濃度","titleEn":"Slurry density and concentration","text":"泥漿混合密度可在兩相體積相加假設下推回固體體積濃度，但氣泡、鹽度與粒子密度變化會破壞簡單換算。質量濃度與體積濃度不是同一比例，需先定義量測對象；濃度提高也會改變流變和輸送阻力，不能只以濃泥漿代表高效作業。","textEn":"Under additive two-phase volumes, mixture density estimates solid volume concentration. Bubbles, salinity and varying grain density violate the simple conversion.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：固體質量百分比和固體體積百分比可以不加換算直接互用。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Solid mass percentage and solid volume percentage are interchangeable without conversion. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「泥漿密度與濃度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Slurry density and concentration\" is correct?","options":["固體質量百分比和固體體積百分比可以不加換算直接互用。","泥漿流量全部等於真正挖出的乾固體體積流量。","泥漿混合密度可在兩相體積相加假設下推回固體體積濃度，但氣泡、鹽度與粒子密度變化會破壞簡單換算。"],"optionsEn":["Solid mass percentage and solid volume percentage are interchangeable without conversion.","The entire slurry discharge equals the actual excavated dry-solid volume flow.","Under additive two-phase volumes, mixture density estimates solid volume concentration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"泥漿混合密度可在兩相體積相加假設下推回固體體積濃度，但氣泡、鹽度與粒子密度變化會破壞簡單換算。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Under additive two-phase volumes, mixture density estimates solid volume concentration. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b287-v15-06","title":"泥漿密度與濃度：定量估算","titleEn":"Slurry density and concentration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「泥漿密度與濃度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Slurry density and concentration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設泥漿1300、清水1000、顆粒2650kg/m³，Cv=(1300−1000)/(2650−1000)=0.1818；忽略含氣與體積非加成。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume mixture1300, water1000 and grains2650kg/m³. Cv=(1300−1000)/(2650−1000)=0.1818, excluding air and nonadditive volume effects. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較線上密度計與乾固體採樣，核對水體鹽度和代表粒子密度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare inline density with dry-solid samples, checking salinity and representative grain density.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設泥漿1300、清水1000、顆粒2650kg/m³，Cv=(1300−1000)/(2650−1000)=0.1818；忽略含氣與體積非加成。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume mixture1300, water1000 and grains2650kg/m³. Cv=(1300−1000)/(2650−1000)=0.1818, excluding air and nonadditive volume effects.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「泥漿密度與濃度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Slurry density and concentration\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","泵的電力消耗增加就一定代表乾固體疏浚產量增加。","測深標準不確定度很小就表示所有航道障礙物都被找到。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Increased pump electricity consumption always means increased dry-solid dredging production.","Small sounding uncertainty proves that every channel obstruction has been detected."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b287-v15-07","title":"泥漿密度與濃度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Slurry density and concentration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「泥漿密度與濃度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Slurry density and concentration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較線上密度計與乾固體採樣，核對水體鹽度和代表粒子密度。標明每份報表用質量或體積濃度，追蹤氣泡與分層造成的偏差，不用單點讀值代表整段輸送狀態。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare inline density with dry-solid samples, checking salinity and representative grain density. Label each report by mass or volume concentration and track air or stratification biases instead of treating a single reading as the state of the full pipeline. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較線上密度計與乾固體採樣，核對水體鹽度和代表粒子密度。標明每份報表用質量或體積濃度，追蹤氣泡與分層造成的偏差，不用單點讀值代表整段輸送狀態。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare inline density with dry-solid samples, checking salinity and representative grain density. Label each report by mass or volume concentration and track air or stratification biases instead of treating a single reading as the state of the full pipeline.","failure":"注意干擾：吸入空氣會降低密度卻不等於固體供應下降，分層採樣則可能錯失底部高濃度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Entrained air lowers density without necessarily reducing solid feed, and stratified samples miss concentrated bed material. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較線上密度計與乾固體採樣，核對水體鹽度和代表粒子密度。標明每份報表用質量或體積濃度，追蹤氣泡與分層造成的偏差，不用單點讀值代表整段輸送狀態。","textEn":"Compare inline density with dry-solid samples, checking salinity and representative grain density. Label each report by mass or volume concentration and track air or stratification biases instead of treating a single reading as the state of the full pipeline.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較線上密度計與乾固體採樣，核對水體鹽度和代表粒子密度。標明每份報表用質量或體積濃度，追蹤氣泡與分層造成的偏差，不用單點讀值代表整段輸送狀態。","textEn":"Compare inline density with dry-solid samples, checking salinity and representative grain density. Label each report by mass or volume concentration and track air or stratification biases instead of treating a single reading as the state of the full pipeline.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「泥漿密度與濃度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Slurry density and concentration\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較線上密度計與乾固體採樣，核對水體鹽度和代表粒子密度。","每次滿艙容量乘理論班次就是已驗收的航道完成方量。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare inline density with dry-solid samples, checking salinity and representative grain density.","Full hopper capacity times theoretical cycles equals accepted completed channel excavation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較線上密度計與乾固體採樣，核對水體鹽度和代表粒子密度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare inline density with dry-solid samples, checking salinity and representative grain density. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b287-v15-08","title":"泥漿密度與濃度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Slurry density and concentration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「泥漿密度與濃度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Slurry density and concentration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"吸入空氣會降低密度卻不等於固體供應下降，分層採樣則可能錯失底部高濃度。將兩種濃度百分比互換會使固體產量與負荷計算同時偏離實際。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Entrained air lowers density without necessarily reducing solid feed, and stratified samples miss concentrated bed material. Interchanging mass and volume percentages simultaneously corrupts estimates of solid production and the hydraulic burden on the system. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設泥漿1300、清水1000、顆粒2650kg/m³，Cv=(1300−1000)/(2650−1000)=0.1818；忽略含氣與體積非加成。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Cv=(1300−1000)/(2650−1000)=0.1818, excluding air and nonadditive volume effects.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「固體質量百分比和固體體積百分比可以不加換算直接互用。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Solid mass percentage and solid volume percentage are interchangeable without conversion.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"吸入空氣會降低密度卻不等於固體供應下降，分層採樣則可能錯失底部高濃度。將兩種濃度百分比互換會使固體產量與負荷計算同時偏離實際。","textEn":"Entrained air lowers density without necessarily reducing solid feed, and stratified samples miss concentrated bed material. Interchanging mass and volume percentages simultaneously corrupts estimates of solid production and the hydraulic burden on the system.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「泥漿密度與濃度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Slurry density and concentration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","泥漿流量全部等於真正挖出的乾固體體積流量。","吸入空氣會降低密度卻不等於固體供應下降，分層採樣則可能錯失底部高濃度。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The entire slurry discharge equals the actual excavated dry-solid volume flow.","Entrained air lowers density without necessarily reducing solid feed, and stratified samples miss concentrated bed material."],"answer":2,"explanation":"吸入空氣會降低密度卻不等於固體供應下降，分層採樣則可能錯失底部高濃度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Entrained air lowers density without necessarily reducing solid feed, and stratified samples miss concentrated bed material. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b287-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「乾固體生產率」與「管路摩擦水頭」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Dry-solid production rate\" and \"Pipeline friction head\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b287-v15-09","title":"乾固體生產率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Dry-solid production rate: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「乾固體生產率」如何影響港池航道疏浚的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dry-solid production rate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Harbor-basin and navigation-channel dredging”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"吸泥泵的總體積流量包含大量水，疏浚產量必須說明是泥漿、固體或原狀土量。沿管路濃度和流速需同步量測，平均值相乘在兩者相關變動時未必等於平均固體通量；生產紀錄也要分出停機與工作時間，不能把瞬時峰值當日產量。 假設泥漿Q=2m³/s、均勻Cv=0.15、顆粒2650kg/m³，乾固體通量ρsCvQ=795kg/s，1h為2862000kg。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「乾固體生產率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pump volume includes carrier water, so production must distinguish slurry, solids and in-situ sediment. Concentration and velocity require synchronized observations; multiplying separate means need not equal mean solid flux when they covary. Records must also separate downtime from pumping duration, since an instantaneous peak cannot be interpreted as achieved daily production or retained placement volume. Assume slurry Q=2m³/s,Cv=0.15 and grain density2650kg/m³. Dry-solid flux is795kg/s, giving2862000kg over1h of unchanged operation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Dry-solid production rate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「泥漿流量全部等於真正挖出的乾固體體積流量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The entire slurry discharge equals the actual excavated dry-solid volume flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「乾固體生產率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Dry-solid production rate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-09-k1","title":"乾固體生產率","titleEn":"Dry-solid production rate","text":"吸泥泵的總體積流量包含大量水，疏浚產量必須說明是泥漿、固體或原狀土量。沿管路濃度和流速需同步量測，平均值相乘在兩者相關變動時未必等於平均固體通量；生產紀錄也要分出停機與工作時間，不能把瞬時峰值當日產量。","textEn":"Pump volume includes carrier water, so production must distinguish slurry, solids and in-situ sediment. Concentration and velocity require synchronized observations; multiplying separate means need not equal mean solid flux when they covary.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：泥漿流量全部等於真正挖出的乾固體體積流量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The entire slurry discharge equals the actual excavated dry-solid volume flow. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「乾固體生產率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Dry-solid production rate\" is correct?","options":["吸泥泵的總體積流量包含大量水，疏浚產量必須說明是泥漿、固體或原狀土量。","泥漿流量全部等於真正挖出的乾固體體積流量。","清水管損公式無需任何修正就能保證高濃度泥漿可輸送。"],"optionsEn":["Pump volume includes carrier water, so production must distinguish slurry, solids and in-situ sediment.","The entire slurry discharge equals the actual excavated dry-solid volume flow.","An uncorrected clear-water friction formula guarantees transport of concentrated dredging slurry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"吸泥泵的總體積流量包含大量水，疏浚產量必須說明是泥漿、固體或原狀土量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pump volume includes carrier water, so production must distinguish slurry, solids and in-situ sediment. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b287-v15-10","title":"乾固體生產率：定量估算","titleEn":"Dry-solid production rate: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「乾固體生產率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dry-solid production rate” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設泥漿Q=2m³/s、均勻Cv=0.15、顆粒2650kg/m³，乾固體通量ρsCvQ=795kg/s，1h為2862000kg。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume slurry Q=2m³/s,Cv=0.15 and grain density2650kg/m³. Dry-solid flux is795kg/s, giving2862000kg over1h of unchanged operation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：使用同步的流量和濃度時間序列積分固體量，將停機資料明確保留為零產量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Integrate synchronized discharge and concentration records, retaining downtime as zero production.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設泥漿Q=2m³/s、均勻Cv=0.15、顆粒2650kg/m³，乾固體通量ρsCvQ=795kg/s，1h為2862000kg。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume slurry Q=2m³/s,Cv=0.15 and grain density2650kg/m³. Dry-solid flux is795kg/s, giving2862000kg over1h of unchanged operation.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「乾固體生產率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Dry-solid production rate\", which statement holds?","options":["測得聲波往返距離後不必考慮探頭吃水與潮位修正。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","靜態水深大於吃水就代表任何航速與波況都可以通航。"],"optionsEn":["Acoustic range alone gives charted bed elevation without draft or tide correction.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Water depth exceeding draft permits navigation at every speed and wave condition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b287-v15-11","title":"乾固體生產率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Dry-solid production rate: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「乾固體生產率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dry-solid production rate” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"使用同步的流量和濃度時間序列積分固體量，將停機資料明確保留為零產量。以接收端乾固體抽樣作交叉檢查，說明管內暫存和輸送延遲，避免混淆兩端同時讀值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Integrate synchronized discharge and concentration records, retaining downtime as zero production. Cross-check receiver dry-solid samples and describe pipe storage and transit delay so readings at the two ends are not incorrectly compared at identical timestamps. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：使用同步的流量和濃度時間序列積分固體量，將停機資料明確保留為零產量。以接收端乾固體抽樣作交叉檢查，說明管內暫存和輸送延遲，避免混淆兩端同時讀值。","observationEn":"Site practice: Integrate synchronized discharge and concentration records, retaining downtime as zero production. Cross-check receiver dry-solid samples and describe pipe storage and transit delay so readings at the two ends are not incorrectly compared at identical timestamps.","failure":"注意干擾：只保留運轉時高濃度片段會高估整班產量，流量計與密度計時鐘偏移也會錯配脈動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Selecting only high-concentration operating periods overstates shift production, and clock offsets mispair pulses. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"使用同步的流量和濃度時間序列積分固體量，將停機資料明確保留為零產量。以接收端乾固體抽樣作交叉檢查，說明管內暫存和輸送延遲，避免混淆兩端同時讀值。","textEn":"Integrate synchronized discharge and concentration records, retaining downtime as zero production. Cross-check receiver dry-solid samples and describe pipe storage and transit delay so readings at the two ends are not incorrectly compared at identical timestamps.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"使用同步的流量和濃度時間序列積分固體量，將停機資料明確保留為零產量。以接收端乾固體抽樣作交叉檢查，說明管內暫存和輸送延遲，避免混淆兩端同時讀值。","textEn":"Integrate synchronized discharge and concentration records, retaining downtime as zero production. Cross-check receiver dry-solid samples and describe pipe storage and transit delay so readings at the two ends are not incorrectly compared at identical timestamps.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「乾固體生產率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Dry-solid production rate\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","九成九固體截留率可以自動證明回流水符合所有環境要求。","使用同步的流量和濃度時間序列積分固體量，將停機資料明確保留為零產量。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Ninety-nine-percent solid retention automatically proves that return water meets every environmental requirement.","Integrate synchronized discharge and concentration records, retaining downtime as zero production."],"answer":2,"explanation":"使用同步的流量和濃度時間序列積分固體量，將停機資料明確保留為零產量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Integrate synchronized discharge and concentration records, retaining downtime as zero production. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b287-v15-12","title":"乾固體生產率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Dry-solid production rate: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「乾固體生產率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dry-solid production rate” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只保留運轉時高濃度片段會高估整班產量，流量計與密度計時鐘偏移也會錯配脈動。到達填區的固體量不符時，需查暫存和洩漏而非修改帳面密度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Selecting only high-concentration operating periods overstates shift production, and clock offsets mispair pulses. A receiver discrepancy requires investigation of storage and leakage rather than arbitrary adjustment of the density used in the accounting. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設泥漿Q=2m³/s、均勻Cv=0.15、顆粒2650kg/m³，乾固體通量ρsCvQ=795kg/s，1h為2862000kg。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Dry-solid flux is795kg/s, giving2862000kg over1h of unchanged operation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「泥漿流量全部等於真正挖出的乾固體體積流量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The entire slurry discharge equals the actual excavated dry-solid volume flow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只保留運轉時高濃度片段會高估整班產量，流量計與密度計時鐘偏移也會錯配脈動。到達填區的固體量不符時，需查暫存和洩漏而非修改帳面密度。","textEn":"Selecting only high-concentration operating periods overstates shift production, and clock offsets mispair pulses. A receiver discrepancy requires investigation of storage and leakage rather than arbitrary adjustment of the density used in the accounting.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「乾固體生產率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Dry-solid production rate\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只保留運轉時高濃度片段會高估整班產量，流量計與密度計時鐘偏移也會錯配脈動。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","清水管損公式無需任何修正就能保證高濃度泥漿可輸送。"],"optionsEn":["Selecting only high-concentration operating periods overstates shift production, and clock offsets mispair pulses.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","An uncorrected clear-water friction formula guarantees transport of concentrated dredging slurry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只保留運轉時高濃度片段會高估整班產量，流量計與密度計時鐘偏移也會錯配脈動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Selecting only high-concentration operating periods overstates shift production, and clock offsets mispair pulses. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b287-v15-13","title":"管路摩擦水頭：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pipeline friction head: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「管路摩擦水頭」如何影響港池航道疏浚的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pipeline friction head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Harbor-basin and navigation-channel dredging”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"管路阻力消耗輸送能量，長度、直徑和速度影響不同，彎頭與高程則另有貢獻。清水達西式只作基準，含砂漿體可能沉積或表現非牛頓流變，不能沿用同一摩擦係數就宣稱可輸送；要把壓力觀測和材料狀態一起比較。 假設清水基準f=0.02、L=500m、D=0.50m、v=3m/s，hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g)=9.174m；不含彎頭與漿體修正。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「管路摩擦水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pipeline resistance consumes energy, with distinct effects from length, diameter and speed; fittings and elevation add separate terms. A clear-water Darcy relation is only a baseline. Slurry can deposit or develop non-Newtonian behavior, so retaining one friction factor does not establish transportability. Pressure observations need interpretation together with concentration, grading and material condition. Assume a clear-water baseline f=0.02,L=500m,D=0.50m,v=3m/s. hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g)=9.174m, excluding fittings and slurry corrections. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pipeline friction head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「清水管損公式無需任何修正就能保證高濃度泥漿可輸送。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An uncorrected clear-water friction formula guarantees transport of concentrated dredging slurry.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「管路摩擦水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pipeline friction head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-13-k1","title":"管路摩擦水頭","titleEn":"Pipeline friction head","text":"管路阻力消耗輸送能量，長度、直徑和速度影響不同，彎頭與高程則另有貢獻。清水達西式只作基準，含砂漿體可能沉積或表現非牛頓流變，不能沿用同一摩擦係數就宣稱可輸送；要把壓力觀測和材料狀態一起比較。","textEn":"Pipeline resistance consumes energy, with distinct effects from length, diameter and speed; fittings and elevation add separate terms. A clear-water Darcy relation is only a baseline.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：清水管損公式無需任何修正就能保證高濃度泥漿可輸送。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An uncorrected clear-water friction formula guarantees transport of concentrated dredging slurry. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「管路摩擦水頭」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pipeline friction head\" is correct?","options":["清水管損公式無需任何修正就能保證高濃度泥漿可輸送。","管路阻力消耗輸送能量，長度、直徑和速度影響不同，彎頭與高程則另有貢獻。","泵的電力消耗增加就一定代表乾固體疏浚產量增加。"],"optionsEn":["An uncorrected clear-water friction formula guarantees transport of concentrated dredging slurry.","Pipeline resistance consumes energy, with distinct effects from length, diameter and speed; fittings and elevation add separate terms.","Increased pump electricity consumption always means increased dry-solid dredging production."],"answer":1,"explanation":"管路阻力消耗輸送能量，長度、直徑和速度影響不同，彎頭與高程則另有貢獻。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pipeline resistance consumes energy, with distinct effects from length, diameter and speed; fittings and elevation add separate terms. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b287-v15-14","title":"管路摩擦水頭：定量估算","titleEn":"Pipeline friction head: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「管路摩擦水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pipeline friction head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設清水基準f=0.02、L=500m、D=0.50m、v=3m/s，hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g)=9.174m；不含彎頭與漿體修正。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a clear-water baseline f=0.02,L=500m,D=0.50m,v=3m/s. hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g)=9.174m, excluding fittings and slurry corrections. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以相同高度基準畫沿管壓力線，核對壓力計位置、流速和內徑。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot the pressure line on a common elevation datum, checking gauge positions, velocity and internal diameter.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設清水基準f=0.02、L=500m、D=0.50m、v=3m/s，hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g)=9.174m；不含彎頭與漿體修正。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a clear-water baseline f=0.02,L=500m,D=0.50m,v=3m/s. hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g)=9.174m, excluding fittings and slurry corrections.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「管路摩擦水頭」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pipeline friction head\", which statement holds?","options":["測深標準不確定度很小就表示所有航道障礙物都被找到。","每次滿艙容量乘理論班次就是已驗收的航道完成方量。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Small sounding uncertainty proves that every channel obstruction has been detected.","Full hopper capacity times theoretical cycles equals accepted completed channel excavation.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b287-v15-15","title":"管路摩擦水頭：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pipeline friction head: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「管路摩擦水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pipeline friction head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以相同高度基準畫沿管壓力線，核對壓力計位置、流速和內徑。比較清水試運與不同濃度資料，單獨列出局部損失及升高段，找出不能由基準摩擦解釋的壓降。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot the pressure line on a common elevation datum, checking gauge positions, velocity and internal diameter. Compare clear-water trials with different concentrations, listing fitting losses and rising sections separately to locate pressure drops unexplained by baseline friction. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以相同高度基準畫沿管壓力線，核對壓力計位置、流速和內徑。比較清水試運與不同濃度資料，單獨列出局部損失及升高段，找出不能由基準摩擦解釋的壓降。","observationEn":"Site practice: Plot the pressure line on a common elevation datum, checking gauge positions, velocity and internal diameter. Compare clear-water trials with different concentrations, listing fitting losses and rising sections separately to locate pressure drops unexplained by baseline friction.","failure":"注意干擾：管底沉積會縮小有效截面並增大阻力，壓力升高若只被當成流量增加可能延誤堵塞辨識。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Bed deposition reduces effective area and increases resistance; interpreting rising pressure solely as increased flow can delay blockage detection. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以相同高度基準畫沿管壓力線，核對壓力計位置、流速和內徑。比較清水試運與不同濃度資料，單獨列出局部損失及升高段，找出不能由基準摩擦解釋的壓降。","textEn":"Plot the pressure line on a common elevation datum, checking gauge positions, velocity and internal diameter. Compare clear-water trials with different concentrations, listing fitting losses and rising sections separately to locate pressure drops unexplained by baseline friction.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以相同高度基準畫沿管壓力線，核對壓力計位置、流速和內徑。比較清水試運與不同濃度資料，單獨列出局部損失及升高段，找出不能由基準摩擦解釋的壓降。","textEn":"Plot the pressure line on a common elevation datum, checking gauge positions, velocity and internal diameter. Compare clear-water trials with different concentrations, listing fitting losses and rising sections separately to locate pressure drops unexplained by baseline friction.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「管路摩擦水頭」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pipeline friction head\"?","options":["以相同高度基準畫沿管壓力線，核對壓力計位置、流速和內徑。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","航道平均深度達標就代表每個局部淺點都已移除。"],"optionsEn":["Plot the pressure line on a common elevation datum, checking gauge positions, velocity and internal diameter.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Meeting average channel depth proves that every local controlling shoal has been removed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以相同高度基準畫沿管壓力線，核對壓力計位置、流速和內徑。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot the pressure line on a common elevation datum, checking gauge positions, velocity and internal diameter. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b287-v15-16","title":"管路摩擦水頭：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pipeline friction head: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「管路摩擦水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pipeline friction head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"管底沉積會縮小有效截面並增大阻力，壓力升高若只被當成流量增加可能延誤堵塞辨識。老化管徑和磨耗也會使原先水力曲線不再代表實際系統。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Bed deposition reduces effective area and increases resistance; interpreting rising pressure solely as increased flow can delay blockage detection. Aging geometry and wear also make the original hydraulic curve unrepresentative of the operating pipeline. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設清水基準f=0.02、L=500m、D=0.50m、v=3m/s，hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g)=9.174m；不含彎頭與漿體修正。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume a clear-water baseline f=0.02,L=500m,D=0.50m,v=3m/s. hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g)=9.174m, excluding fittings and slurry corrections.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「清水管損公式無需任何修正就能保證高濃度泥漿可輸送。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An uncorrected clear-water friction formula guarantees transport of concentrated dredging slurry.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"管底沉積會縮小有效截面並增大阻力，壓力升高若只被當成流量增加可能延誤堵塞辨識。老化管徑和磨耗也會使原先水力曲線不再代表實際系統。","textEn":"Bed deposition reduces effective area and increases resistance; interpreting rising pressure solely as increased flow can delay blockage detection. Aging geometry and wear also make the original hydraulic curve unrepresentative of the operating pipeline.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「管路摩擦水頭」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pipeline friction head\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","管底沉積會縮小有效截面並增大阻力，壓力升高若只被當成流量增加可能延誤堵塞辨識。","泵的電力消耗增加就一定代表乾固體疏浚產量增加。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Bed deposition reduces effective area and increases resistance; interpreting rising pressure solely as increased flow can delay blockage detection.","Increased pump electricity consumption always means increased dry-solid dredging production."],"answer":1,"explanation":"管底沉積會縮小有效截面並增大阻力，壓力升高若只被當成流量增加可能延誤堵塞辨識。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Bed deposition reduces effective area and increases resistance; interpreting rising pressure solely as increased flow can delay blockage detection. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b287-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「泵送能量收支」與「聲波測深與基準」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pumping energy balance\" and \"Acoustic depth and datum\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b287-v15-17","title":"泵送能量收支：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pumping energy balance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「泵送能量收支」如何影響港池航道疏浚的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pumping energy balance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Harbor-basin and navigation-channel dredging”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水力功率代表流體得到的機械能，電功率還需除以泵與驅動效率，不能拿銘牌最大值代替工況。漿體密度、總水頭和流量必須來自同一時段，效率又隨運轉點改變；這項收支可診斷異常，但無法獨立決定設備選型或允許負載。 假設泥漿ρ=1300kg/m³、Q=2m³/s、總水頭20m、總效率0.70，Pin=ρgQH/η=728.7kW；效率固定示意。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「泵送能量收支」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Hydraulic power is mechanical energy delivered to the fluid, while input power additionally reflects pump and drive efficiency. Nameplate maximum is not an operating measurement. Density, total head and flow must describe the same period, and efficiency varies with operating point. This balance helps diagnose discrepancies but does not independently select machinery or establish its permissible load. Assume slurry1300kg/m³,Q=2m³/s,total head20m and total efficiency0.70. Pin=ρgQH/η=728.7kW with fixed illustrative efficiency. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pumping energy balance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「泵的電力消耗增加就一定代表乾固體疏浚產量增加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Increased pump electricity consumption always means increased dry-solid dredging production.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「泵送能量收支」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pumping energy balance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-17-k1","title":"泵送能量收支","titleEn":"Pumping energy balance","text":"水力功率代表流體得到的機械能，電功率還需除以泵與驅動效率，不能拿銘牌最大值代替工況。漿體密度、總水頭和流量必須來自同一時段，效率又隨運轉點改變；這項收支可診斷異常，但無法獨立決定設備選型或允許負載。","textEn":"Hydraulic power is mechanical energy delivered to the fluid, while input power additionally reflects pump and drive efficiency. Nameplate maximum is not an operating measurement.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：泵的電力消耗增加就一定代表乾固體疏浚產量增加。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Increased pump electricity consumption always means increased dry-solid dredging production. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「泵送能量收支」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pumping energy balance\" is correct?","options":["泵的電力消耗增加就一定代表乾固體疏浚產量增加。","測得聲波往返距離後不必考慮探頭吃水與潮位修正。","水力功率代表流體得到的機械能，電功率還需除以泵與驅動效率，不能拿銘牌最大值代替工況。"],"optionsEn":["Increased pump electricity consumption always means increased dry-solid dredging production.","Acoustic range alone gives charted bed elevation without draft or tide correction.","Hydraulic power is mechanical energy delivered to the fluid, while input power additionally reflects pump and drive efficiency."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水力功率代表流體得到的機械能，電功率還需除以泵與驅動效率，不能拿銘牌最大值代替工況。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Hydraulic power is mechanical energy delivered to the fluid, while input power additionally reflects pump and drive efficiency. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b287-v15-18","title":"泵送能量收支：定量估算","titleEn":"Pumping energy balance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「泵送能量收支」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pumping energy balance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設泥漿ρ=1300kg/m³、Q=2m³/s、總水頭20m、總效率0.70，Pin=ρgQH/η=728.7kW；效率固定示意。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume slurry1300kg/m³,Q=2m³/s,total head20m and total efficiency0.70. Pin=ρgQH/η=728.7kW with fixed illustrative efficiency. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步記電力、流量、進出口總水頭和密度，區分瞬時與平均資料。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record power, flow, inlet-outlet total head and density synchronously, distinguishing instantaneous and average records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設泥漿ρ=1300kg/m³、Q=2m³/s、總水頭20m、總效率0.70，Pin=ρgQH/η=728.7kW；效率固定示意。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume slurry1300kg/m³,Q=2m³/s,total head20m and total efficiency0.70. Pin=ρgQH/η=728.7kW with fixed illustrative efficiency.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「泵送能量收支」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pumping energy balance\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","靜態水深大於吃水就代表任何航速與波況都可以通航。","九成九固體截留率可以自動證明回流水符合所有環境要求。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Water depth exceeding draft permits navigation at every speed and wave condition.","Ninety-nine-percent solid retention automatically proves that return water meets every environmental requirement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b287-v15-19","title":"泵送能量收支：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pumping energy balance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「泵送能量收支」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pumping energy balance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步記電力、流量、進出口總水頭和密度，區分瞬時與平均資料。用實測工況核對效率範圍，查找水頭漏項與機械損失，不能因公式吻合就忽略振動或材料輸送異常。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record power, flow, inlet-outlet total head and density synchronously, distinguishing instantaneous and average records. Check efficiency at the measured operating point and investigate missing head terms or mechanical losses without overlooking vibration or transport abnormalities merely because arithmetic agrees. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：同步記電力、流量、進出口總水頭和密度，區分瞬時與平均資料。用實測工況核對效率範圍，查找水頭漏項與機械損失，不能因公式吻合就忽略振動或材料輸送異常。","observationEn":"Site practice: Record power, flow, inlet-outlet total head and density synchronously, distinguishing instantaneous and average records. Check efficiency at the measured operating point and investigate missing head terms or mechanical losses without overlooking vibration or transport abnormalities merely because arithmetic agrees.","failure":"注意干擾：用清水密度計算高濃度泥漿會低估功率，忽略吸入端速度和高程也會漏掉水頭。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using clear-water density for concentrated slurry understates power, while omitted suction velocity and elevation miss head terms. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步記電力、流量、進出口總水頭和密度，區分瞬時與平均資料。用實測工況核對效率範圍，查找水頭漏項與機械損失，不能因公式吻合就忽略振動或材料輸送異常。","textEn":"Record power, flow, inlet-outlet total head and density synchronously, distinguishing instantaneous and average records. Check efficiency at the measured operating point and investigate missing head terms or mechanical losses without overlooking vibration or transport abnormalities merely because arithmetic agrees.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"同步記電力、流量、進出口總水頭和密度，區分瞬時與平均資料。用實測工況核對效率範圍，查找水頭漏項與機械損失，不能因公式吻合就忽略振動或材料輸送異常。","textEn":"Record power, flow, inlet-outlet total head and density synchronously, distinguishing instantaneous and average records. Check efficiency at the measured operating point and investigate missing head terms or mechanical losses without overlooking vibration or transport abnormalities merely because arithmetic agrees.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「泵送能量收支」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pumping energy balance\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","同步記電力、流量、進出口總水頭和密度，區分瞬時與平均資料。","固體質量百分比和固體體積百分比可以不加換算直接互用。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Record power, flow, inlet-outlet total head and density synchronously, distinguishing instantaneous and average records.","Solid mass percentage and solid volume percentage are interchangeable without conversion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同步記電力、流量、進出口總水頭和密度，區分瞬時與平均資料。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record power, flow, inlet-outlet total head and density synchronously, distinguishing instantaneous and average records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b287-v15-20","title":"泵送能量收支：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pumping energy balance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「泵送能量收支」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pumping energy balance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用清水密度計算高濃度泥漿會低估功率，忽略吸入端速度和高程也會漏掉水頭。設備電力增加可能來自效率下降，並不一定代表固體生產增加。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using clear-water density for concentrated slurry understates power, while omitted suction velocity and elevation miss head terms. Higher electrical consumption can result from declining efficiency rather than increased production of useful dry solids. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設泥漿ρ=1300kg/m³、Q=2m³/s、總水頭20m、總效率0.70，Pin=ρgQH/η=728.7kW；效率固定示意。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Pin=ρgQH/η=728.7kW with fixed illustrative efficiency.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「泵的電力消耗增加就一定代表乾固體疏浚產量增加。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Increased pump electricity consumption always means increased dry-solid dredging production.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用清水密度計算高濃度泥漿會低估功率，忽略吸入端速度和高程也會漏掉水頭。設備電力增加可能來自效率下降，並不一定代表固體生產增加。","textEn":"Using clear-water density for concentrated slurry understates power, while omitted suction velocity and elevation miss head terms. Higher electrical consumption can result from declining efficiency rather than increased production of useful dry solids.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「泵送能量收支」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pumping energy balance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","測得聲波往返距離後不必考慮探頭吃水與潮位修正。","用清水密度計算高濃度泥漿會低估功率，忽略吸入端速度和高程也會漏掉水頭。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Acoustic range alone gives charted bed elevation without draft or tide correction.","Using clear-water density for concentrated slurry understates power, while omitted suction velocity and elevation miss head terms."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用清水密度計算高濃度泥漿會低估功率，忽略吸入端速度和高程也會漏掉水頭。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using clear-water density for concentrated slurry understates power, while omitted suction velocity and elevation miss head terms. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b287-v15-21","title":"聲波測深與基準：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Acoustic depth and datum: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「聲波測深與基準」如何影響港池航道疏浚的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Acoustic depth and datum” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Harbor-basin and navigation-channel dredging”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"測深由聲波往返時間轉成距離，探頭吃水、船體升沉和潮位又把距離轉成海床高程。聲速剖面隨溫鹽改變，斜波束更容易出現折射偏差；只校正一個表面聲速不足以代表整個水柱，且各項修正必須保持相同符號約定。 假設垂直聲束、均勻聲速1500m/s、往返0.020s，探頭至床距15m；探頭在瞬時水面下1m時水深16m。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「聲波測深與基準」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Sounding converts two-way travel time into range, then transducer draft, vessel motion and tide convert range into bed elevation. Temperature and salinity alter the sound-speed profile, particularly affecting oblique beams through refraction. A surface-only correction does not describe the whole water column, and every correction requires a consistent sign convention and reference frame. Assume a vertical beam, uniform sound speed1500m/s and two-way time0.020s. Transducer-bed range is15m;1m transducer draft gives water depth16m. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Acoustic depth and datum” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「測得聲波往返距離後不必考慮探頭吃水與潮位修正。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Acoustic range alone gives charted bed elevation without draft or tide correction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「聲波測深與基準」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Acoustic depth and datum”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-21-k1","title":"聲波測深與基準","titleEn":"Acoustic depth and datum","text":"測深由聲波往返時間轉成距離，探頭吃水、船體升沉和潮位又把距離轉成海床高程。聲速剖面隨溫鹽改變，斜波束更容易出現折射偏差；只校正一個表面聲速不足以代表整個水柱，且各項修正必須保持相同符號約定。","textEn":"Sounding converts two-way travel time into range, then transducer draft, vessel motion and tide convert range into bed elevation. Temperature and salinity alter the sound-speed profile, particularly affecting oblique beams through refraction.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：測得聲波往返距離後不必考慮探頭吃水與潮位修正。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Acoustic range alone gives charted bed elevation without draft or tide correction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「聲波測深與基準」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Acoustic depth and datum\" is correct?","options":["測深由聲波往返時間轉成距離，探頭吃水、船體升沉和潮位又把距離轉成海床高程。","測得聲波往返距離後不必考慮探頭吃水與潮位修正。","測深標準不確定度很小就表示所有航道障礙物都被找到。"],"optionsEn":["Sounding converts two-way travel time into range, then transducer draft, vessel motion and tide convert range into bed elevation.","Acoustic range alone gives charted bed elevation without draft or tide correction.","Small sounding uncertainty proves that every channel obstruction has been detected."],"answer":0,"explanation":"測深由聲波往返時間轉成距離，探頭吃水、船體升沉和潮位又把距離轉成海床高程。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Sounding converts two-way travel time into range, then transducer draft, vessel motion and tide convert range into bed elevation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b287-v15-22","title":"聲波測深與基準：定量估算","titleEn":"Acoustic depth and datum: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「聲波測深與基準」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Acoustic depth and datum” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設垂直聲束、均勻聲速1500m/s、往返0.020s，探頭至床距15m；探頭在瞬時水面下1m時水深16m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a vertical beam, uniform sound speed1500m/s and two-way time0.020s. Transducer-bed range is15m;1m transducer draft gives water depth16m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：畫水面、探頭和海床的高程關係，逐項核對吃水、升沉與潮位符號。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw elevations of water surface, transducer and bed and verify draft, heave and tide signs.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設垂直聲束、均勻聲速1500m/s、往返0.020s，探頭至床距15m；探頭在瞬時水面下1m時水深16m。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a vertical beam, uniform sound speed1500m/s and two-way time0.020s. Transducer-bed range is15m;1m transducer draft gives water depth16m.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「聲波測深與基準」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Acoustic depth and datum\", which statement holds?","options":["每次滿艙容量乘理論班次就是已驗收的航道完成方量。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","航道平均深度達標就代表每個局部淺點都已移除。"],"optionsEn":["Full hopper capacity times theoretical cycles equals accepted completed channel excavation.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Meeting average channel depth proves that every local controlling shoal has been removed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b287-v15-23","title":"聲波測深與基準：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Acoustic depth and datum: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「聲波測深與基準」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Acoustic depth and datum” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"畫水面、探頭和海床的高程關係，逐項核對吃水、升沉與潮位符號。用獨立檢核線和聲速剖面測試折射，保留時鐘及姿態校準紀錄，避免只看點雲外觀平順。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw elevations of water surface, transducer and bed and verify draft, heave and tide signs. Test refraction with independent check lines and sound-speed profiles, retaining timing and attitude calibration instead of relying solely on smooth point-cloud appearance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫水面、探頭和海床的高程關係，逐項核對吃水、升沉與潮位符號。用獨立檢核線和聲速剖面測試折射，保留時鐘及姿態校準紀錄，避免只看點雲外觀平順。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw elevations of water surface, transducer and bed and verify draft, heave and tide signs. Test refraction with independent check lines and sound-speed profiles, retaining timing and attitude calibration instead of relying solely on smooth point-cloud appearance.","failure":"注意干擾：聲速設錯會造成整條測線深度偏差，吃水符號反轉又能讓誤差加倍。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Incorrect sound speed biases the entire line, while reversed draft signs can amplify the error. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"畫水面、探頭和海床的高程關係，逐項核對吃水、升沉與潮位符號。用獨立檢核線和聲速剖面測試折射，保留時鐘及姿態校準紀錄，避免只看點雲外觀平順。","textEn":"Draw elevations of water surface, transducer and bed and verify draft, heave and tide signs. Test refraction with independent check lines and sound-speed profiles, retaining timing and attitude calibration instead of relying solely on smooth point-cloud appearance.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫水面、探頭和海床的高程關係，逐項核對吃水、升沉與潮位符號。用獨立檢核線和聲速剖面測試折射，保留時鐘及姿態校準紀錄，避免只看點雲外觀平順。","textEn":"Draw elevations of water surface, transducer and bed and verify draft, heave and tide signs. Test refraction with independent check lines and sound-speed profiles, retaining timing and attitude calibration instead of relying solely on smooth point-cloud appearance.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「聲波測深與基準」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Acoustic depth and datum\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","泥漿流量全部等於真正挖出的乾固體體積流量。","畫水面、探頭和海床的高程關係，逐項核對吃水、升沉與潮位符號。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The entire slurry discharge equals the actual excavated dry-solid volume flow.","Draw elevations of water surface, transducer and bed and verify draft, heave and tide signs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"畫水面、探頭和海床的高程關係，逐項核對吃水、升沉與潮位符號。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw elevations of water surface, transducer and bed and verify draft, heave and tide signs. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b287-v15-24","title":"聲波測深與基準：失效診斷","titleEn":"Acoustic depth and datum: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「聲波測深與基準」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Acoustic depth and datum” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"聲速設錯會造成整條測線深度偏差，吃水符號反轉又能讓誤差加倍。不同方向測線看似吻合時，仍可能共同受錯誤高程基準影響而一起偏移。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Incorrect sound speed biases the entire line, while reversed draft signs can amplify the error. Agreement between opposite survey directions can still conceal a shared incorrect vertical datum that shifts both sets of depths together. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設垂直聲束、均勻聲速1500m/s、往返0.020s，探頭至床距15m；探頭在瞬時水面下1m時水深16m。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Transducer-bed range is15m;1m transducer draft gives water depth16m.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「測得聲波往返距離後不必考慮探頭吃水與潮位修正。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Acoustic range alone gives charted bed elevation without draft or tide correction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"聲速設錯會造成整條測線深度偏差，吃水符號反轉又能讓誤差加倍。不同方向測線看似吻合時，仍可能共同受錯誤高程基準影響而一起偏移。","textEn":"Incorrect sound speed biases the entire line, while reversed draft signs can amplify the error. Agreement between opposite survey directions can still conceal a shared incorrect vertical datum that shifts both sets of depths together.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「聲波測深與基準」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Acoustic depth and datum\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["聲速設錯會造成整條測線深度偏差，吃水符號反轉又能讓誤差加倍。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","測深標準不確定度很小就表示所有航道障礙物都被找到。"],"optionsEn":["Incorrect sound speed biases the entire line, while reversed draft signs can amplify the error.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Small sounding uncertainty proves that every channel obstruction has been detected."],"answer":0,"explanation":"聲速設錯會造成整條測線深度偏差，吃水符號反轉又能讓誤差加倍。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Incorrect sound speed biases the entire line, while reversed draft signs can amplify the error. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b287-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「測深不確定度預算」與「船底淨空分項」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Sounding uncertainty budget\" and \"Under-keel clearance components\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b287-v15-25","title":"測深不確定度預算：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Sounding uncertainty budget: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「測深不確定度預算」如何影響港池航道疏浚的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sounding uncertainty budget” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Harbor-basin and navigation-channel dredging”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"深度不確定度來自儀器、聲速、姿態和基準等分量，獨立隨機分量才能直接平方和。覆蓋率和小物體偵測又屬不同品質維度，精度高並不表示沒有漏測；合成預算用來理解誤差傳播，不是在未指定測量等級時自行宣告符合國際標準。 假設三個獨立零均值標準不確定度0.05、0.08、0.04m，合成σ=√(0.05²+0.08²+0.04²)=0.1025m。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測深不確定度預算」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Depth uncertainty combines instrument, sound-speed, attitude and reference contributions, with direct quadrature applying only to independent random components. Coverage and feature detection are separate quality dimensions: accurate points can still leave unseen obstructions. A synthetic budget illustrates propagation rather than claiming compliance with an international survey order that has not been specified and verified. Assume independent zero-mean standard uncertainties0.05,0.08 and0.04m. Combinedσ=√(0.05²+0.08²+0.04²)=0.1025m, excluding systematic bias. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sounding uncertainty budget” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「測深標準不確定度很小就表示所有航道障礙物都被找到。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Small sounding uncertainty proves that every channel obstruction has been detected.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測深不確定度預算」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sounding uncertainty budget”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-25-k1","title":"測深不確定度預算","titleEn":"Sounding uncertainty budget","text":"深度不確定度來自儀器、聲速、姿態和基準等分量，獨立隨機分量才能直接平方和。覆蓋率和小物體偵測又屬不同品質維度，精度高並不表示沒有漏測；合成預算用來理解誤差傳播，不是在未指定測量等級時自行宣告符合國際標準。","textEn":"Depth uncertainty combines instrument, sound-speed, attitude and reference contributions, with direct quadrature applying only to independent random components. Coverage and feature detection are separate quality dimensions: accurate points can still leave unseen obstructions.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：測深標準不確定度很小就表示所有航道障礙物都被找到。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Small sounding uncertainty proves that every channel obstruction has been detected. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測深不確定度預算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sounding uncertainty budget\" is correct?","options":["測深標準不確定度很小就表示所有航道障礙物都被找到。","深度不確定度來自儀器、聲速、姿態和基準等分量，獨立隨機分量才能直接平方和。","靜態水深大於吃水就代表任何航速與波況都可以通航。"],"optionsEn":["Small sounding uncertainty proves that every channel obstruction has been detected.","Depth uncertainty combines instrument, sound-speed, attitude and reference contributions, with direct quadrature applying only to independent random components.","Water depth exceeding draft permits navigation at every speed and wave condition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"深度不確定度來自儀器、聲速、姿態和基準等分量，獨立隨機分量才能直接平方和。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Depth uncertainty combines instrument, sound-speed, attitude and reference contributions, with direct quadrature applying only to independent random components. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b287-v15-26","title":"測深不確定度預算：定量估算","titleEn":"Sounding uncertainty budget: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測深不確定度預算」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sounding uncertainty budget” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設三個獨立零均值標準不確定度0.05、0.08、0.04m，合成σ=√(0.05²+0.08²+0.04²)=0.1025m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume independent zero-mean standard uncertainties0.05,0.08 and0.04m. Combinedσ=√(0.05²+0.08²+0.04²)=0.1025m, excluding systematic bias. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將標準不確定度、偏差及信賴界限分欄，說明每個分量是否相關。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Separate standard uncertainty, bias and confidence limits and identify correlations between components.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設三個獨立零均值標準不確定度0.05、0.08、0.04m，合成σ=√(0.05²+0.08²+0.04²)=0.1025m。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume independent zero-mean standard uncertainties0.05,0.08 and0.04m. Combinedσ=√(0.05²+0.08²+0.04²)=0.1025m, excluding systematic bias.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測深不確定度預算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sounding uncertainty budget\", which statement holds?","options":["九成九固體截留率可以自動證明回流水符合所有環境要求。","固體質量百分比和固體體積百分比可以不加換算直接互用。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Ninety-nine-percent solid retention automatically proves that return water meets every environmental requirement.","Solid mass percentage and solid volume percentage are interchangeable without conversion.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b287-v15-27","title":"測深不確定度預算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sounding uncertainty budget: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測深不確定度預算」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sounding uncertainty budget” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將標準不確定度、偏差及信賴界限分欄，說明每個分量是否相關。另查測線覆蓋與物體偵測證據，把品質要求連回調查用途，避免以單一平方和取代整體測量驗證。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Separate standard uncertainty, bias and confidence limits and identify correlations between components. Check coverage and feature-detection evidence independently, linking requirements to intended use rather than replacing complete survey verification with one combined quadrature value. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將標準不確定度、偏差及信賴界限分欄，說明每個分量是否相關。另查測線覆蓋與物體偵測證據，把品質要求連回調查用途，避免以單一平方和取代整體測量驗證。","observationEn":"Site practice: Separate standard uncertainty, bias and confidence limits and identify correlations between components. Check coverage and feature-detection evidence independently, linking requirements to intended use rather than replacing complete survey verification with one combined quadrature value.","failure":"注意干擾：相關的潮位和基準誤差被假設獨立會低估不確定度，未測間隙中的石塊更不在預算內。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assuming independence between correlated tide and datum errors understates uncertainty, while a rock in an unsurveyed gap is absent from the budget entirely. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將標準不確定度、偏差及信賴界限分欄，說明每個分量是否相關。另查測線覆蓋與物體偵測證據，把品質要求連回調查用途，避免以單一平方和取代整體測量驗證。","textEn":"Separate standard uncertainty, bias and confidence limits and identify correlations between components. Check coverage and feature-detection evidence independently, linking requirements to intended use rather than replacing complete survey verification with one combined quadrature value.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將標準不確定度、偏差及信賴界限分欄，說明每個分量是否相關。另查測線覆蓋與物體偵測證據，把品質要求連回調查用途，避免以單一平方和取代整體測量驗證。","textEn":"Separate standard uncertainty, bias and confidence limits and identify correlations between components. Check coverage and feature-detection evidence independently, linking requirements to intended use rather than replacing complete survey verification with one combined quadrature value.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測深不確定度預算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sounding uncertainty budget\"?","options":["將標準不確定度、偏差及信賴界限分欄，說明每個分量是否相關。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","清水管損公式無需任何修正就能保證高濃度泥漿可輸送。"],"optionsEn":["Separate standard uncertainty, bias and confidence limits and identify correlations between components.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","An uncorrected clear-water friction formula guarantees transport of concentrated dredging slurry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將標準不確定度、偏差及信賴界限分欄，說明每個分量是否相關。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Separate standard uncertainty, bias and confidence limits and identify correlations between components. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b287-v15-28","title":"測深不確定度預算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sounding uncertainty budget: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測深不確定度預算」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sounding uncertainty budget” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"相關的潮位和基準誤差被假設獨立會低估不確定度，未測間隙中的石塊更不在預算內。漂亮的精度數字無法補救航道關鍵區沒有資料的問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assuming independence between correlated tide and datum errors understates uncertainty, while a rock in an unsurveyed gap is absent from the budget entirely. Impressive precision cannot compensate for missing observations in controlling navigation areas. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設三個獨立零均值標準不確定度0.05、0.08、0.04m，合成σ=√(0.05²+0.08²+0.04²)=0.1025m。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Combinedσ=√(0.05²+0.08²+0.04²)=0.1025m, excluding systematic bias.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「測深標準不確定度很小就表示所有航道障礙物都被找到。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Small sounding uncertainty proves that every channel obstruction has been detected.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"相關的潮位和基準誤差被假設獨立會低估不確定度，未測間隙中的石塊更不在預算內。漂亮的精度數字無法補救航道關鍵區沒有資料的問題。","textEn":"Assuming independence between correlated tide and datum errors understates uncertainty, while a rock in an unsurveyed gap is absent from the budget entirely. Impressive precision cannot compensate for missing observations in controlling navigation areas.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測深不確定度預算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sounding uncertainty budget\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","相關的潮位和基準誤差被假設獨立會低估不確定度，未測間隙中的石塊更不在預算內。","靜態水深大於吃水就代表任何航速與波況都可以通航。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Assuming independence between correlated tide and datum errors understates uncertainty, while a rock in an unsurveyed gap is absent from the budget entirely.","Water depth exceeding draft permits navigation at every speed and wave condition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相關的潮位和基準誤差被假設獨立會低估不確定度，未測間隙中的石塊更不在預算內。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assuming independence between correlated tide and datum errors understates uncertainty, while a rock in an unsurveyed gap is absent from the budget entirely. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b287-v15-29","title":"船底淨空分項：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Under-keel clearance components: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「船底淨空分項」如何影響港池航道疏浚的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Under-keel clearance components” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Harbor-basin and navigation-channel dredging”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"航道水深與船舶吃水差只是靜態淨空，航行時還有船體動態下沉、波浪運動及量測餘量。各項需求可能相關且受場址限制，教學減法僅用來顯示預算組成；不能將結果當作船舶通行批准，真正操航需依權責單位規定和即時條件。 假設可用水深15m、吃水13m、動態下沉0.5m、波動需求0.4m、量測餘量0.2m，剩餘示意淨空0.9m。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「船底淨空分項」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Depth minus draft is only static clearance. Vessel squat, wave motion and measurement allowances affect the available margin during navigation. Demands may be correlated and site-dependent, so this arithmetic merely exposes budget components. It is not a transit approval; actual navigation depends on the responsible authority, vessel characteristics and contemporaneous conditions rather than this illustrative calculation. Assume depth15m,draft13m,squat0.5m,wave demand0.4m and survey allowance0.2m. Illustrative residual clearance is0.9m, not permission to transit. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Under-keel clearance components” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「靜態水深大於吃水就代表任何航速與波況都可以通航。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Water depth exceeding draft permits navigation at every speed and wave condition.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「船底淨空分項」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Under-keel clearance components”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-29-k1","title":"船底淨空分項","titleEn":"Under-keel clearance components","text":"航道水深與船舶吃水差只是靜態淨空，航行時還有船體動態下沉、波浪運動及量測餘量。各項需求可能相關且受場址限制，教學減法僅用來顯示預算組成；不能將結果當作船舶通行批准，真正操航需依權責單位規定和即時條件。","textEn":"Depth minus draft is only static clearance. Vessel squat, wave motion and measurement allowances affect the available margin during navigation.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：靜態水深大於吃水就代表任何航速與波況都可以通航。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Water depth exceeding draft permits navigation at every speed and wave condition. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「船底淨空分項」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Under-keel clearance components\" is correct?","options":["靜態水深大於吃水就代表任何航速與波況都可以通航。","每次滿艙容量乘理論班次就是已驗收的航道完成方量。","航道水深與船舶吃水差只是靜態淨空，航行時還有船體動態下沉、波浪運動及量測餘量。"],"optionsEn":["Water depth exceeding draft permits navigation at every speed and wave condition.","Full hopper capacity times theoretical cycles equals accepted completed channel excavation.","Depth minus draft is only static clearance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"航道水深與船舶吃水差只是靜態淨空，航行時還有船體動態下沉、波浪運動及量測餘量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Depth minus draft is only static clearance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b287-v15-30","title":"船底淨空分項：定量估算","titleEn":"Under-keel clearance components: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「船底淨空分項」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Under-keel clearance components” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設可用水深15m、吃水13m、動態下沉0.5m、波動需求0.4m、量測餘量0.2m，剩餘示意淨空0.9m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume depth15m,draft13m,squat0.5m,wave demand0.4m and survey allowance0.2m. Illustrative residual clearance is0.9m, not permission to transit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：明列水位時刻、吃水來源與各需求的定義，檢查是否有重複或漏計。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record water-level time, draft source and each demand definition, checking duplication and omission.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設可用水深15m、吃水13m、動態下沉0.5m、波動需求0.4m、量測餘量0.2m，剩餘示意淨空0.9m。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume depth15m,draft13m,squat0.5m,wave demand0.4m and survey allowance0.2m. Illustrative residual clearance is0.9m, not permission to transit.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「船底淨空分項」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Under-keel clearance components\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","航道平均深度達標就代表每個局部淺點都已移除。","泥漿流量全部等於真正挖出的乾固體體積流量。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Meeting average channel depth proves that every local controlling shoal has been removed.","The entire slurry discharge equals the actual excavated dry-solid volume flow."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b287-v15-31","title":"船底淨空分項：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Under-keel clearance components: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「船底淨空分項」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Under-keel clearance components” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"明列水位時刻、吃水來源與各需求的定義，檢查是否有重複或漏計。將示意預算與權責單位的場址方法分開保存，核對船型、航速及波向適用性，不以平均水深代替最淺點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record water-level time, draft source and each demand definition, checking duplication and omission. Keep this illustration separate from the authority’s site method, verify vessel, speed and wave-direction applicability, and use controlling shallows rather than average depth. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：明列水位時刻、吃水來源與各需求的定義，檢查是否有重複或漏計。將示意預算與權責單位的場址方法分開保存，核對船型、航速及波向適用性，不以平均水深代替最淺點。","observationEn":"Site practice: Record water-level time, draft source and each demand definition, checking duplication and omission. Keep this illustration separate from the authority’s site method, verify vessel, speed and wave-direction applicability, and use controlling shallows rather than average depth.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略動態下沉會在靜態淨空看似充裕時低估碰底可能，混用潮位時刻也會錯估可用水深。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring squat can understate bottom-contact exposure despite apparently adequate static clearance, and mismatched tide times misstate depth. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"明列水位時刻、吃水來源與各需求的定義，檢查是否有重複或漏計。將示意預算與權責單位的場址方法分開保存，核對船型、航速及波向適用性，不以平均水深代替最淺點。","textEn":"Record water-level time, draft source and each demand definition, checking duplication and omission. Keep this illustration separate from the authority’s site method, verify vessel, speed and wave-direction applicability, and use controlling shallows rather than average depth.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"明列水位時刻、吃水來源與各需求的定義，檢查是否有重複或漏計。將示意預算與權責單位的場址方法分開保存，核對船型、航速及波向適用性，不以平均水深代替最淺點。","textEn":"Record water-level time, draft source and each demand definition, checking duplication and omission. Keep this illustration separate from the authority’s site method, verify vessel, speed and wave-direction applicability, and use controlling shallows rather than average depth.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「船底淨空分項」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Under-keel clearance components\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","明列水位時刻、吃水來源與各需求的定義，檢查是否有重複或漏計。","泵的電力消耗增加就一定代表乾固體疏浚產量增加。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Record water-level time, draft source and each demand definition, checking duplication and omission.","Increased pump electricity consumption always means increased dry-solid dredging production."],"answer":1,"explanation":"明列水位時刻、吃水來源與各需求的定義，檢查是否有重複或漏計。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record water-level time, draft source and each demand definition, checking duplication and omission. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b287-v15-32","title":"船底淨空分項：失效診斷","titleEn":"Under-keel clearance components: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「船底淨空分項」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Under-keel clearance components” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略動態下沉會在靜態淨空看似充裕時低估碰底可能，混用潮位時刻也會錯估可用水深。多個保守餘量重複扣除則可能讓分析失去可追溯性。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring squat can understate bottom-contact exposure despite apparently adequate static clearance, and mismatched tide times misstate depth. Duplicating conservative allowances creates the opposite error and makes the resulting assessment difficult to audit or interpret. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設可用水深15m、吃水13m、動態下沉0.5m、波動需求0.4m、量測餘量0.2m，剩餘示意淨空0.9m。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Illustrative residual clearance is0.9m, not permission to transit.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「靜態水深大於吃水就代表任何航速與波況都可以通航。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Water depth exceeding draft permits navigation at every speed and wave condition.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略動態下沉會在靜態淨空看似充裕時低估碰底可能，混用潮位時刻也會錯估可用水深。多個保守餘量重複扣除則可能讓分析失去可追溯性。","textEn":"Ignoring squat can understate bottom-contact exposure despite apparently adequate static clearance, and mismatched tide times misstate depth. Duplicating conservative allowances creates the opposite error and makes the resulting assessment difficult to audit or interpret.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「船底淨空分項」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Under-keel clearance components\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","每次滿艙容量乘理論班次就是已驗收的航道完成方量。","忽略動態下沉會在靜態淨空看似充裕時低估碰底可能，混用潮位時刻也會錯估可用水深。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Full hopper capacity times theoretical cycles equals accepted completed channel excavation.","Ignoring squat can understate bottom-contact exposure despite apparently adequate static clearance, and mismatched tide times misstate depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"忽略動態下沉會在靜態淨空看似充裕時低估碰底可能，混用潮位時刻也會錯估可用水深。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring squat can understate bottom-contact exposure despite apparently adequate static clearance, and mismatched tide times misstate depth. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b287-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「循環時間與產量」與「回流水固體平衡」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cycle time and production\" and \"Return-water solids balance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b287-v15-33","title":"循環時間與產量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cycle time and production: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「循環時間與產量」如何影響港池航道疏浚的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cycle time and production” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Harbor-basin and navigation-channel dredging”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"耙吸船或抓斗作業有挖取、移動、卸料及等待階段，只有完整循環才能換算持續產量。有效利用率需明確說明是否已包含等待，避免重複扣除；料艙容量亦非原狀土方，材料膨鬆與含水會使不同產量報表無法直接比較。 假設每循環合格完成方600m³、循環時間40min且另計可用率0.75，平均600×60/40×0.75=675m³/h。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「循環時間與產量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A dredging cycle includes excavation, travel, unloading and waiting, so sustainable production requires the complete cycle. Utilization must state whether waiting is already included to avoid double deductions. Hopper capacity is also not in-situ soil volume; bulking and water content make reports with different volume definitions unsuitable for direct comparison across equipment or shifts. Assume completed acceptable volume600m³ per40min cycle and separately defined availability0.75. Mean production=600×60/40×0.75=675m³/h. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cycle time and production” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「每次滿艙容量乘理論班次就是已驗收的航道完成方量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Full hopper capacity times theoretical cycles equals accepted completed channel excavation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「循環時間與產量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cycle time and production”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-33-k1","title":"循環時間與產量","titleEn":"Cycle time and production","text":"耙吸船或抓斗作業有挖取、移動、卸料及等待階段，只有完整循環才能換算持續產量。有效利用率需明確說明是否已包含等待，避免重複扣除；料艙容量亦非原狀土方，材料膨鬆與含水會使不同產量報表無法直接比較。","textEn":"A dredging cycle includes excavation, travel, unloading and waiting, so sustainable production requires the complete cycle. Utilization must state whether waiting is already included to avoid double deductions.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每次滿艙容量乘理論班次就是已驗收的航道完成方量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Full hopper capacity times theoretical cycles equals accepted completed channel excavation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「循環時間與產量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cycle time and production\" is correct?","options":["耙吸船或抓斗作業有挖取、移動、卸料及等待階段，只有完整循環才能換算持續產量。","每次滿艙容量乘理論班次就是已驗收的航道完成方量。","九成九固體截留率可以自動證明回流水符合所有環境要求。"],"optionsEn":["A dredging cycle includes excavation, travel, unloading and waiting, so sustainable production requires the complete cycle.","Full hopper capacity times theoretical cycles equals accepted completed channel excavation.","Ninety-nine-percent solid retention automatically proves that return water meets every environmental requirement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"耙吸船或抓斗作業有挖取、移動、卸料及等待階段，只有完整循環才能換算持續產量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A dredging cycle includes excavation, travel, unloading and waiting, so sustainable production requires the complete cycle. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b287-v15-34","title":"循環時間與產量：定量估算","titleEn":"Cycle time and production: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「循環時間與產量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cycle time and production” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設每循環合格完成方600m³、循環時間40min且另計可用率0.75，平均600×60/40×0.75=675m³/h。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume completed acceptable volume600m³ per40min cycle and separately defined availability0.75. Mean production=600×60/40×0.75=675m³/h. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用原始時戳分解循環階段，標明可用率排除或納入的停機原因。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use raw timestamps to separate cycle phases and define included downtime in availability.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設每循環合格完成方600m³、循環時間40min且另計可用率0.75，平均600×60/40×0.75=675m³/h。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume completed acceptable volume600m³ per40min cycle and separately defined availability0.75. Mean production=600×60/40×0.75=675m³/h.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「循環時間與產量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cycle time and production\", which statement holds?","options":["固體質量百分比和固體體積百分比可以不加換算直接互用。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","清水管損公式無需任何修正就能保證高濃度泥漿可輸送。"],"optionsEn":["Solid mass percentage and solid volume percentage are interchangeable without conversion.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","An uncorrected clear-water friction formula guarantees transport of concentrated dredging slurry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b287-v15-35","title":"循環時間與產量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cycle time and production: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「循環時間與產量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cycle time and production” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用原始時戳分解循環階段，標明可用率排除或納入的停機原因。核對完成方是否已由測量確認，並比較多個班次的分布，不以最快一趟或料艙名義容量代表長期績效。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use raw timestamps to separate cycle phases and define included downtime in availability. Check whether completed volume is survey-confirmed and compare distributions across shifts rather than representing long-term performance by the fastest trip or nominal hopper capacity. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用原始時戳分解循環階段，標明可用率排除或納入的停機原因。核對完成方是否已由測量確認，並比較多個班次的分布，不以最快一趟或料艙名義容量代表長期績效。","observationEn":"Site practice: Use raw timestamps to separate cycle phases and define included downtime in availability. Check whether completed volume is survey-confirmed and compare distributions across shifts rather than representing long-term performance by the fastest trip or nominal hopper capacity.","failure":"注意干擾：將等待時間納入循環又乘含等待的可用率會重複扣減，反之漏記卸料與移航則過度樂觀。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Counting waiting in both cycle time and availability double-reduces output, while omitting travel and unloading inflates it. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用原始時戳分解循環階段，標明可用率排除或納入的停機原因。核對完成方是否已由測量確認，並比較多個班次的分布，不以最快一趟或料艙名義容量代表長期績效。","textEn":"Use raw timestamps to separate cycle phases and define included downtime in availability. Check whether completed volume is survey-confirmed and compare distributions across shifts rather than representing long-term performance by the fastest trip or nominal hopper capacity.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用原始時戳分解循環階段，標明可用率排除或納入的停機原因。核對完成方是否已由測量確認，並比較多個班次的分布，不以最快一趟或料艙名義容量代表長期績效。","textEn":"Use raw timestamps to separate cycle phases and define included downtime in availability. Check whether completed volume is survey-confirmed and compare distributions across shifts rather than representing long-term performance by the fastest trip or nominal hopper capacity.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「循環時間與產量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cycle time and production\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","測得聲波往返距離後不必考慮探頭吃水與潮位修正。","用原始時戳分解循環階段，標明可用率排除或納入的停機原因。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Acoustic range alone gives charted bed elevation without draft or tide correction.","Use raw timestamps to separate cycle phases and define included downtime in availability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用原始時戳分解循環階段，標明可用率排除或納入的停機原因。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use raw timestamps to separate cycle phases and define included downtime in availability. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b287-v15-36","title":"循環時間與產量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cycle time and production: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「循環時間與產量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cycle time and production” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將等待時間納入循環又乘含等待的可用率會重複扣減，反之漏記卸料與移航則過度樂觀。容量達標而底部仍留淺點，也不能視為合格完成方。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Counting waiting in both cycle time and availability double-reduces output, while omitting travel and unloading inflates it. A full hopper does not represent acceptable completed excavation if controlling shallow patches remain on the bed. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設每循環合格完成方600m³、循環時間40min且另計可用率0.75，平均600×60/40×0.75=675m³/h。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mean production=600×60/40×0.75=675m³/h.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每次滿艙容量乘理論班次就是已驗收的航道完成方量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Full hopper capacity times theoretical cycles equals accepted completed channel excavation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將等待時間納入循環又乘含等待的可用率會重複扣減，反之漏記卸料與移航則過度樂觀。容量達標而底部仍留淺點，也不能視為合格完成方。","textEn":"Counting waiting in both cycle time and availability double-reduces output, while omitting travel and unloading inflates it. A full hopper does not represent acceptable completed excavation if controlling shallow patches remain on the bed.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「循環時間與產量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cycle time and production\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["將等待時間納入循環又乘含等待的可用率會重複扣減，反之漏記卸料與移航則過度樂觀。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","九成九固體截留率可以自動證明回流水符合所有環境要求。"],"optionsEn":["Counting waiting in both cycle time and availability double-reduces output, while omitting travel and unloading inflates it.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Ninety-nine-percent solid retention automatically proves that return water meets every environmental requirement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將等待時間納入循環又乘含等待的可用率會重複扣減，反之漏記卸料與移航則過度樂觀。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Counting waiting in both cycle time and availability double-reduces output, while omitting travel and unloading inflates it. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b287-v15-37","title":"回流水固體平衡：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Return-water solids balance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「回流水固體平衡」如何影響港池航道疏浚的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Return-water solids balance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Harbor-basin and navigation-channel dredging”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"放置區回流水可能攜帶細料，輸入和排出通量需以同一時段及乾固體定義比較。截留比例只說明材料收支，不能替代水質與生態評估；沉積暫存和再懸浮也會改變短期結果，因此要避免把短時間高截留率解釋為長期永久固定。 假設乾固體輸入100kg/s、回流水2m³/s且固體0.5kg/m³，輸出1kg/s，當期截留率99%；不代表水質合格。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「回流水固體平衡」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Return water can carry fines out of a placement area, so input and output fluxes require matching periods and dry-solid definitions. Retention describes material accounting rather than water-quality or ecological acceptability. Temporary storage and resuspension alter short-term results, meaning a high measured fraction cannot demonstrate permanent confinement or the absence of downstream effects. Assume dry-solid input100kg/s and return water2m³/s at0.5kg/m³. Export is1kg/s and period retention99%, not water-quality compliance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Return-water solids balance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「九成九固體截留率可以自動證明回流水符合所有環境要求。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Ninety-nine-percent solid retention automatically proves that return water meets every environmental requirement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「回流水固體平衡」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Return-water solids balance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-37-k1","title":"回流水固體平衡","titleEn":"Return-water solids balance","text":"放置區回流水可能攜帶細料，輸入和排出通量需以同一時段及乾固體定義比較。截留比例只說明材料收支，不能替代水質與生態評估；沉積暫存和再懸浮也會改變短期結果，因此要避免把短時間高截留率解釋為長期永久固定。","textEn":"Return water can carry fines out of a placement area, so input and output fluxes require matching periods and dry-solid definitions. Retention describes material accounting rather than water-quality or ecological acceptability.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：九成九固體截留率可以自動證明回流水符合所有環境要求。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Ninety-nine-percent solid retention automatically proves that return water meets every environmental requirement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「回流水固體平衡」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Return-water solids balance\" is correct?","options":["九成九固體截留率可以自動證明回流水符合所有環境要求。","放置區回流水可能攜帶細料，輸入和排出通量需以同一時段及乾固體定義比較。","航道平均深度達標就代表每個局部淺點都已移除。"],"optionsEn":["Ninety-nine-percent solid retention automatically proves that return water meets every environmental requirement.","Return water can carry fines out of a placement area, so input and output fluxes require matching periods and dry-solid definitions.","Meeting average channel depth proves that every local controlling shoal has been removed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"放置區回流水可能攜帶細料，輸入和排出通量需以同一時段及乾固體定義比較。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Return water can carry fines out of a placement area, so input and output fluxes require matching periods and dry-solid definitions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b287-v15-38","title":"回流水固體平衡：定量估算","titleEn":"Return-water solids balance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「回流水固體平衡」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Return-water solids balance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設乾固體輸入100kg/s、回流水2m³/s且固體0.5kg/m³，輸出1kg/s，當期截留率99%；不代表水質合格。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume dry-solid input100kg/s and return water2m³/s at0.5kg/m³. Export is1kg/s and period retention99%, not water-quality compliance. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量入料與回流水濃度流量，確認排水口是否全部納入，並扣除可辨識的原床再懸浮。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure input and all return outlets synchronously and account for identifiable native-bed resuspension.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設乾固體輸入100kg/s、回流水2m³/s且固體0.5kg/m³，輸出1kg/s，當期截留率99%；不代表水質合格。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume dry-solid input100kg/s and return water2m³/s at0.5kg/m³. Export is1kg/s and period retention99%, not water-quality compliance.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「回流水固體平衡」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Return-water solids balance\", which statement holds?","options":["泥漿流量全部等於真正挖出的乾固體體積流量。","泵的電力消耗增加就一定代表乾固體疏浚產量增加。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["The entire slurry discharge equals the actual excavated dry-solid volume flow.","Increased pump electricity consumption always means increased dry-solid dredging production.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b287-v15-39","title":"回流水固體平衡：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Return-water solids balance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「回流水固體平衡」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Return-water solids balance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量入料與回流水濃度流量，確認排水口是否全部納入，並扣除可辨識的原床再懸浮。用分期地形和乾固體存量核對積分收支，將環境暴露與截留率分開呈現。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure input and all return outlets synchronously and account for identifiable native-bed resuspension. Check integrated fluxes against repeated terrain and dry-solid storage observations, presenting environmental exposure separately from the numerical fraction retained during the selected period. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：同步量入料與回流水濃度流量，確認排水口是否全部納入，並扣除可辨識的原床再懸浮。用分期地形和乾固體存量核對積分收支，將環境暴露與截留率分開呈現。","observationEn":"Site practice: Measure input and all return outlets synchronously and account for identifiable native-bed resuspension. Check integrated fluxes against repeated terrain and dry-solid storage observations, presenting environmental exposure separately from the numerical fraction retained during the selected period.","failure":"注意干擾：少量流失若集中在敏感時段仍可能重要，漏掉旁通排水會使截留率虛高。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A small exported fraction can matter during sensitive periods, and omitted bypass outlets inflate retention. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量入料與回流水濃度流量，確認排水口是否全部納入，並扣除可辨識的原床再懸浮。用分期地形和乾固體存量核對積分收支，將環境暴露與截留率分開呈現。","textEn":"Measure input and all return outlets synchronously and account for identifiable native-bed resuspension. Check integrated fluxes against repeated terrain and dry-solid storage observations, presenting environmental exposure separately from the numerical fraction retained during the selected period.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"同步量入料與回流水濃度流量，確認排水口是否全部納入，並扣除可辨識的原床再懸浮。用分期地形和乾固體存量核對積分收支，將環境暴露與截留率分開呈現。","textEn":"Measure input and all return outlets synchronously and account for identifiable native-bed resuspension. Check integrated fluxes against repeated terrain and dry-solid storage observations, presenting environmental exposure separately from the numerical fraction retained during the selected period.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「回流水固體平衡」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Return-water solids balance\"?","options":["同步量入料與回流水濃度流量，確認排水口是否全部納入，並扣除可辨識的原床再懸浮。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","測深標準不確定度很小就表示所有航道障礙物都被找到。"],"optionsEn":["Measure input and all return outlets synchronously and account for identifiable native-bed resuspension.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Small sounding uncertainty proves that every channel obstruction has been detected."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步量入料與回流水濃度流量，確認排水口是否全部納入，並扣除可辨識的原床再懸浮。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure input and all return outlets synchronously and account for identifiable native-bed resuspension. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b287-v15-40","title":"回流水固體平衡：失效診斷","titleEn":"Return-water solids balance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"prerequisiteIds":["b287-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「回流水固體平衡」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Return-water solids balance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"少量流失若集中在敏感時段仍可能重要，漏掉旁通排水會使截留率虛高。存量變化不符時只改濃度平均值，會掩蓋未量到的出口或暫存延遲。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A small exported fraction can matter during sensitive periods, and omitted bypass outlets inflate retention. Adjusting mean concentration to close a storage discrepancy conceals unmeasured paths or delays instead of explaining the actual material balance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設乾固體輸入100kg/s、回流水2m³/s且固體0.5kg/m³，輸出1kg/s，當期截留率99%；不代表水質合格。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Export is1kg/s and period retention99%, not water-quality compliance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「九成九固體截留率可以自動證明回流水符合所有環境要求。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Ninety-nine-percent solid retention automatically proves that return water meets every environmental requirement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b287-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"少量流失若集中在敏感時段仍可能重要，漏掉旁通排水會使截留率虛高。存量變化不符時只改濃度平均值，會掩蓋未量到的出口或暫存延遲。","textEn":"A small exported fraction can matter during sensitive periods, and omitted bypass outlets inflate retention. Adjusting mean concentration to close a storage discrepancy conceals unmeasured paths or delays instead of explaining the actual material balance.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]},{"id":"b287-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「回流水固體平衡」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Return-water solids balance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","少量流失若集中在敏感時段仍可能重要，漏掉旁通排水會使截留率虛高。","航道平均深度達標就代表每個局部淺點都已移除。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A small exported fraction can matter during sensitive periods, and omitted bypass outlets inflate retention.","Meeting average channel depth proves that every local controlling shoal has been removed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"少量流失若集中在敏感時段仍可能重要，漏掉旁通排水會使截留率虛高。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A small exported fraction can matter during sensitive periods, and omitted bypass outlets inflate retention. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-dredge","v15s-iho44","v15s-savannah","v15s-poplar","v15s-itm"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b288","title":"疏浚泥沙有益利用","titleEn":"Beneficial reuse of dredged sediment","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"用材料分流地形高程和生態追蹤判斷疏浚土的有益利用。課程從邊界辨識與資料整理走到水理量化、構造介面及驗證紀錄；每一步把計算結果連回可量測的證據。十個不同單元分別處理關鍵機制，不以名義尺寸或單一通過率代替整體工程判斷，並明列合成算例與現地資料的差別。","summaryEn":"Evaluate dredged-sediment reuse through material routing, elevation and ecological follow-up. The course moves from boundary identification and evidence to hydraulic quantification, structural interfaces and verification records. Ten distinct units connect each calculated quantity to measurable evidence. Nominal geometry or a single pass rate does not establish whole-system performance, and synthetic teaching examples remain separate from field observations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-coasts","subcategoryTitle":"海岸、港灣與水資源韌性","subcategoryTitleEn":"Coasts, ports and water-resource resilience","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-coasts","learningTags":["water","water-coasts","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-coast","architectureNodes":[["材料分流與去向","Material routing and destinations"],["壓密後高程餘量","Post-consolidation elevation reserve"],["篩分回收與產率","Screening recovery and yield"],["覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量","Cover thickness and erosion reserve"],["對照監測與歸因","Control monitoring and attribution"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-coast","labels":["材料分流與去向","壓密後高程餘量","篩分回收與產率","覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量","對照監測與歸因"],"labelsEn":["Material routing and destinations","Post-consolidation elevation reserve","Screening recovery and yield","Cover thickness and erosion reserve","Control monitoring and attribution"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為原創合成算例，不是地標工程的實測或推薦操作值。教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設乾固體10000t中砂6500t、細料3000t、雜物500t，質量守恆10000t；若僅砂獲適用驗證，確認再利用率65%。假設其他類別保持不變，已驗證砂量6500增10%至7150t，總料由10000增至10650t，確認利用率為67.14%，並非原65%加10百分點。重新計算前先列固定條件、單位、適用尺度及可能失效的邊界。把模型敏感度與測量誤差分開，不能將單一參數變化直接當成工程風險或壽命比例。比較兩次結果後，記錄還需要哪些獨立證據，並由負責專業人員判斷適用性。","textEn":"This original synthetic example is neither a landmark measurement nor a recommended operating value. Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume dry solids10000t comprise sand6500t,fines3000t and debris500t. Balance closes; if only sand is verified suitable, confirmed reuse is65%. If verified sand increases10% from6500 to7150t while other classes remain fixed, total feed becomes10650t and confirmed reuse is67.14%, not65% plus ten percentage points. Before recalculating, list fixed conditions, units, applicable scale and boundaries that could fail. Separate model sensitivity from measurement uncertainty: a parameter change does not directly give a proportional change in engineering risk or service life. Compare the results, record independent evidence still needed, and have the responsible specialist determine applicability.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b288-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「材料分流與去向」與「薄層放置與高程」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Material routing and destinations\" and \"Thin-layer placement and elevation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b288-v15-01","title":"材料分流與去向：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Material routing and destinations: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「材料分流與去向」如何影響疏浚泥沙有益利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Material routing and destinations” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beneficial reuse of dredged sediment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"有益利用先確認可用材料類別與接收目的，不能將全部挖出量直接算成成功利用。篩分、脫水和不合用材料各有去向，所有分類需用一致乾質量基準並避免重複計數；接收場適合性還有污染、鹽分與地工條件，帳面分流不能取代證據。 假設乾固體10000t中砂6500t、細料3000t、雜物500t，質量守恆10000t；若僅砂獲適用驗證，確認再利用率65%。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「材料分流與去向」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Beneficial reuse starts with material classification and receiving purpose rather than counting all excavation as successful use. Screening, dewatering and unsuitable fractions have distinct destinations that require one dry-mass basis and no duplicate counting. Suitability additionally depends on contaminants, salinity and geotechnical behavior, so an accounting split cannot substitute for evidence of fitness at the receiving site. Assume dry solids10000t comprise sand6500t,fines3000t and debris500t. Balance closes; if only sand is verified suitable, confirmed reuse is65%. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Material routing and destinations” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「疏浚材料只要有預定去向就全部算成已驗證成功再利用。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every dredged batch with a planned destination already counts as verified successful reuse.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「材料分流與去向」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Material routing and destinations”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-01-k1","title":"材料分流與去向","titleEn":"Material routing and destinations","text":"有益利用先確認可用材料類別與接收目的，不能將全部挖出量直接算成成功利用。篩分、脫水和不合用材料各有去向，所有分類需用一致乾質量基準並避免重複計數；接收場適合性還有污染、鹽分與地工條件，帳面分流不能取代證據。","textEn":"Beneficial reuse starts with material classification and receiving purpose rather than counting all excavation as successful use. Screening, dewatering and unsuitable fractions have distinct destinations that require one dry-mass basis and no duplicate counting.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：疏浚材料只要有預定去向就全部算成已驗證成功再利用。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every dredged batch with a planned destination already counts as verified successful reuse. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「材料分流與去向」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Material routing and destinations\" is correct?","options":["疏浚材料只要有預定去向就全部算成已驗證成功再利用。","有益利用先確認可用材料類別與接收目的，不能將全部挖出量直接算成成功利用。","平均放置厚度達標就能證明每個位置的淹水條件都合適。"],"optionsEn":["Every dredged batch with a planned destination already counts as verified successful reuse.","Beneficial reuse starts with material classification and receiving purpose rather than counting all excavation as successful use.","A satisfactory mean placement thickness proves suitable inundation at every location."],"answer":1,"explanation":"有益利用先確認可用材料類別與接收目的，不能將全部挖出量直接算成成功利用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Beneficial reuse starts with material classification and receiving purpose rather than counting all excavation as successful use. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b288-v15-02","title":"材料分流與去向：定量估算","titleEn":"Material routing and destinations: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「材料分流與去向」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Material routing and destinations” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設乾固體10000t中砂6500t、細料3000t、雜物500t，質量守恆10000t；若僅砂獲適用驗證，確認再利用率65%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume dry solids10000t comprise sand6500t,fines3000t and debris500t. Balance closes; if only sand is verified suitable, confirmed reuse is65%. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對每一批建立來源、檢測、處理與接收紀錄，核對三類材料是否同用乾質量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace each batch through source, testing, treatment and receipt, checking a common dry-mass basis.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設乾固體10000t中砂6500t、細料3000t、雜物500t，質量守恆10000t；若僅砂獲適用驗證，確認再利用率65%。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume dry solids10000t comprise sand6500t,fines3000t and debris500t. Balance closes; if only sand is verified suitable, confirmed reuse is65%.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「材料分流與去向」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Material routing and destinations\", which statement holds?","options":["潮位超過地面的時間比例直接等於植被的存活機率。","混合後平均濃度降低代表同百分比的污染物已被消除。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["The fraction of time tide exceeds ground directly equals plant survival probability.","A lower average concentration after mixing means the same fraction of contaminant was destroyed.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b288-v15-03","title":"材料分流與去向：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Material routing and destinations: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「材料分流與去向」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Material routing and destinations” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對每一批建立來源、檢測、處理與接收紀錄，核對三類材料是否同用乾質量。將待判定材料獨立保留，不以計畫去向當成已完成利用，並查證接收端實際數量和用途。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace each batch through source, testing, treatment and receipt, checking a common dry-mass basis. Keep unresolved material separate, distinguish planned destinations from completed reuse, and verify actual received quantity and purpose rather than relying only on dispatch records. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對每一批建立來源、檢測、處理與接收紀錄，核對三類材料是否同用乾質量。將待判定材料獨立保留，不以計畫去向當成已完成利用，並查證接收端實際數量和用途。","observationEn":"Site practice: Trace each batch through source, testing, treatment and receipt, checking a common dry-mass basis. Keep unresolved material separate, distinguish planned destinations from completed reuse, and verify actual received quantity and purpose rather than relying only on dispatch records.","failure":"注意干擾：把含水泥漿與乾砂噸數相加會造出虛假利用量，待檢材料提前算成功也會掩蓋不合用比例。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adding wet slurry tonnes to dry sand invents reuse quantities, and counting untested material as accepted hides unsuitable fractions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對每一批建立來源、檢測、處理與接收紀錄，核對三類材料是否同用乾質量。將待判定材料獨立保留，不以計畫去向當成已完成利用，並查證接收端實際數量和用途。","textEn":"Trace each batch through source, testing, treatment and receipt, checking a common dry-mass basis. Keep unresolved material separate, distinguish planned destinations from completed reuse, and verify actual received quantity and purpose rather than relying only on dispatch records.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對每一批建立來源、檢測、處理與接收紀錄，核對三類材料是否同用乾質量。將待判定材料獨立保留，不以計畫去向當成已完成利用，並查證接收端實際數量和用途。","textEn":"Trace each batch through source, testing, treatment and receipt, checking a common dry-mass basis. Keep unresolved material separate, distinguish planned destinations from completed reuse, and verify actual received quantity and purpose rather than relying only on dispatch records.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「材料分流與去向」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Material routing and destinations\"?","options":["對每一批建立來源、檢測、處理與接收紀錄，核對三類材料是否同用乾質量。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","表面變乾就代表全部填料已完全排水並取得最終強度。"],"optionsEn":["Trace each batch through source, testing, treatment and receipt, checking a common dry-mass basis.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A dry surface proves that the entire fill has drained and reached final strength."],"answer":0,"explanation":"對每一批建立來源、檢測、處理與接收紀錄，核對三類材料是否同用乾質量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace each batch through source, testing, treatment and receipt, checking a common dry-mass basis. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b288-v15-04","title":"材料分流與去向：失效診斷","titleEn":"Material routing and destinations: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「材料分流與去向」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Material routing and destinations” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把含水泥漿與乾砂噸數相加會造出虛假利用量，待檢材料提前算成功也會掩蓋不合用比例。不同接收場需要的性質不同，不能以一處通過代表全用途適用。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adding wet slurry tonnes to dry sand invents reuse quantities, and counting untested material as accepted hides unsuitable fractions. Different receiving sites need different properties; acceptance for one purpose does not qualify every other use. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設乾固體10000t中砂6500t、細料3000t、雜物500t，質量守恆10000t；若僅砂獲適用驗證，確認再利用率65%。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Balance closes; if only sand is verified suitable, confirmed reuse is65%.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「疏浚材料只要有預定去向就全部算成已驗證成功再利用。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every dredged batch with a planned destination already counts as verified successful reuse.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把含水泥漿與乾砂噸數相加會造出虛假利用量，待檢材料提前算成功也會掩蓋不合用比例。不同接收場需要的性質不同，不能以一處通過代表全用途適用。","textEn":"Adding wet slurry tonnes to dry sand invents reuse quantities, and counting untested material as accepted hides unsuitable fractions. Different receiving sites need different properties; acceptance for one purpose does not qualify every other use.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「材料分流與去向」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Material routing and destinations\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把含水泥漿與乾砂噸數相加會造出虛假利用量，待檢材料提前算成功也會掩蓋不合用比例。","平均放置厚度達標就能證明每個位置的淹水條件都合適。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Adding wet slurry tonnes to dry sand invents reuse quantities, and counting untested material as accepted hides unsuitable fractions.","A satisfactory mean placement thickness proves suitable inundation at every location."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把含水泥漿與乾砂噸數相加會造出虛假利用量，待檢材料提前算成功也會掩蓋不合用比例。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adding wet slurry tonnes to dry sand invents reuse quantities, and counting untested material as accepted hides unsuitable fractions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b288-v15-05","title":"薄層放置與高程：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Thin-layer placement and elevation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「薄層放置與高程」如何影響疏浚泥沙有益利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Thin-layer placement and elevation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beneficial reuse of dredged sediment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"濕地放置厚度決定表面相對潮位位置，但卸入泥漿體積尚含會排出的水。完成厚度需明確指排水後或長期壓密後的狀態，地面高程和植被耐受也有空間差異；一個平均厚度不能保證所有區域得到相同淹水時間或恢復條件。 假設排水後保留體積12000m³、面積60000m²且均勻，平均厚度t=V/A=0.20m；不含後續壓密沉陷。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「薄層放置與高程」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Placement thickness sets surface position relative to tides, but delivered slurry includes water that later drains. Completed thickness must identify whether it is after drainage or longer-term consolidation. Terrain and vegetation tolerance vary spatially, so a mean layer cannot establish equal inundation or recovery conditions throughout the entire restored area without additional elevation and ecological observations. Assume retained post-drainage volume12000m³ over60000m² uniformly. Mean thickness t=V/A=0.20m, excluding subsequent consolidation settlement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Thin-layer placement and elevation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均放置厚度達標就能證明每個位置的淹水條件都合適。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A satisfactory mean placement thickness proves suitable inundation at every location.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「薄層放置與高程」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Thin-layer placement and elevation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-05-k1","title":"薄層放置與高程","titleEn":"Thin-layer placement and elevation","text":"濕地放置厚度決定表面相對潮位位置，但卸入泥漿體積尚含會排出的水。完成厚度需明確指排水後或長期壓密後的狀態，地面高程和植被耐受也有空間差異；一個平均厚度不能保證所有區域得到相同淹水時間或恢復條件。","textEn":"Placement thickness sets surface position relative to tides, but delivered slurry includes water that later drains. Completed thickness must identify whether it is after drainage or longer-term consolidation.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均放置厚度達標就能證明每個位置的淹水條件都合適。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A satisfactory mean placement thickness proves suitable inundation at every location. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「薄層放置與高程」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thin-layer placement and elevation\" is correct?","options":["平均放置厚度達標就能證明每個位置的淹水條件都合適。","放置材料乾固體沒有流失就代表地表高程不會再下降。","濕地放置厚度決定表面相對潮位位置，但卸入泥漿體積尚含會排出的水。"],"optionsEn":["A satisfactory mean placement thickness proves suitable inundation at every location.","If placed dry solids are retained, surface elevation cannot subsequently decrease.","Placement thickness sets surface position relative to tides, but delivered slurry includes water that later drains."],"answer":2,"explanation":"濕地放置厚度決定表面相對潮位位置，但卸入泥漿體積尚含會排出的水。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Placement thickness sets surface position relative to tides, but delivered slurry includes water that later drains. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b288-v15-06","title":"薄層放置與高程：定量估算","titleEn":"Thin-layer placement and elevation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「薄層放置與高程」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Thin-layer placement and elevation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設排水後保留體積12000m³、面積60000m²且均勻，平均厚度t=V/A=0.20m；不含後續壓密沉陷。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume retained post-drainage volume12000m³ over60000m² uniformly. Mean thickness t=V/A=0.20m, excluding subsequent consolidation settlement. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較放置前後同基準高程面，標明體積對應的排水時點及施工邊界。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare pre- and post-placement surfaces on one datum, specifying drainage time and boundaries.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設排水後保留體積12000m³、面積60000m²且均勻，平均厚度t=V/A=0.20m；不含後續壓密沉陷。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume retained post-drainage volume12000m³ over60000m² uniformly. Mean thickness t=V/A=0.20m, excluding subsequent consolidation settlement.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「薄層放置與高程」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thin-layer placement and elevation\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","產品純度與原料回收率永遠具有相同分母而且相等。","覆蓋材料總方量足夠就能證明各處隔離厚度與化學功能足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Product purity and feed recovery always share the same denominator and value.","Enough total cover volume proves adequate thickness and chemical isolation everywhere."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b288-v15-07","title":"薄層放置與高程：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Thin-layer placement and elevation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「薄層放置與高程」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Thin-layer placement and elevation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較放置前後同基準高程面，標明體積對應的排水時點及施工邊界。按高低地分區檢查厚度與植被狀態，保留低窪及局部堆厚資料，而不讓全區平均取代空間分布。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare pre- and post-placement surfaces on one datum, specifying drainage time and boundaries. Inspect thickness and vegetation by elevation zone, retaining depressions and local mounds rather than substituting a whole-site average for the distribution that controls actual inundation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較放置前後同基準高程面，標明體積對應的排水時點及施工邊界。按高低地分區檢查厚度與植被狀態，保留低窪及局部堆厚資料，而不讓全區平均取代空間分布。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare pre- and post-placement surfaces on one datum, specifying drainage time and boundaries. Inspect thickness and vegetation by elevation zone, retaining depressions and local mounds rather than substituting a whole-site average for the distribution that controls actual inundation.","failure":"注意干擾：平均厚度符合計畫時局部深堆仍可能掩埋植株，低區又可能沒有足夠增高。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Local mounds can bury vegetation despite a matching mean thickness, while low areas remain insufficiently raised. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較放置前後同基準高程面，標明體積對應的排水時點及施工邊界。按高低地分區檢查厚度與植被狀態，保留低窪及局部堆厚資料，而不讓全區平均取代空間分布。","textEn":"Compare pre- and post-placement surfaces on one datum, specifying drainage time and boundaries. Inspect thickness and vegetation by elevation zone, retaining depressions and local mounds rather than substituting a whole-site average for the distribution that controls actual inundation.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較放置前後同基準高程面，標明體積對應的排水時點及施工邊界。按高低地分區檢查厚度與植被狀態，保留低窪及局部堆厚資料，而不讓全區平均取代空間分布。","textEn":"Compare pre- and post-placement surfaces on one datum, specifying drainage time and boundaries. Inspect thickness and vegetation by elevation zone, retaining depressions and local mounds rather than substituting a whole-site average for the distribution that controls actual inundation.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「薄層放置與高程」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thin-layer placement and elevation\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較放置前後同基準高程面，標明體積對應的排水時點及施工邊界。","運距縮短的排放差額就是再利用方案完整的生命週期淨減碳。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare pre- and post-placement surfaces on one datum, specifying drainage time and boundaries.","The emissions saved by shorter transport equal the reuse project's complete life-cycle benefit."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較放置前後同基準高程面，標明體積對應的排水時點及施工邊界。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare pre- and post-placement surfaces on one datum, specifying drainage time and boundaries. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b288-v15-08","title":"薄層放置與高程：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thin-layer placement and elevation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「薄層放置與高程」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Thin-layer placement and elevation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"平均厚度符合計畫時局部深堆仍可能掩埋植株，低區又可能沒有足夠增高。泥漿排水後高程下降若未預先分辨，會讓施工方量和生態目標失去對應。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Local mounds can bury vegetation despite a matching mean thickness, while low areas remain insufficiently raised. Unrecognized lowering during slurry drainage breaks the intended link between delivered quantity and the ecological elevation objective. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設排水後保留體積12000m³、面積60000m²且均勻，平均厚度t=V/A=0.20m；不含後續壓密沉陷。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mean thickness t=V/A=0.20m, excluding subsequent consolidation settlement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均放置厚度達標就能證明每個位置的淹水條件都合適。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A satisfactory mean placement thickness proves suitable inundation at every location.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"平均厚度符合計畫時局部深堆仍可能掩埋植株，低區又可能沒有足夠增高。泥漿排水後高程下降若未預先分辨，會讓施工方量和生態目標失去對應。","textEn":"Local mounds can bury vegetation despite a matching mean thickness, while low areas remain insufficiently raised. Unrecognized lowering during slurry drainage breaks the intended link between delivered quantity and the ecological elevation objective.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「薄層放置與高程」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thin-layer placement and elevation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","放置材料乾固體沒有流失就代表地表高程不會再下降。","平均厚度符合計畫時局部深堆仍可能掩埋植株，低區又可能沒有足夠增高。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","If placed dry solids are retained, surface elevation cannot subsequently decrease.","Local mounds can bury vegetation despite a matching mean thickness, while low areas remain insufficiently raised."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平均厚度符合計畫時局部深堆仍可能掩埋植株，低區又可能沒有足夠增高。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Local mounds can bury vegetation despite a matching mean thickness, while low areas remain insufficiently raised. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b288-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「壓密後高程餘量」與「潮汐淹水比例」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Post-consolidation elevation reserve\" and \"Tidal inundation fraction\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b288-v15-09","title":"壓密後高程餘量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Post-consolidation elevation reserve: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「壓密後高程餘量」如何影響疏浚泥沙有益利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Post-consolidation elevation reserve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beneficial reuse of dredged sediment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"細泥排水壓密會使放置面逐漸降低，固體體積保持時孔隙比變化可換算一維厚度縮減。真實地基也會沉陷、側向流動及有機質分解，因此這個模型只涵蓋單層材料本身；應將施工時點高程和長期目標分開，而非一次測量完成即結案。 假設初厚1m、初孔隙比e0=2、末孔隙比e1=1，末厚H1=H0(1+e1)/(1+e0)=0.667m，沉陷0.333m。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壓密後高程餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Fine sediment lowers as it drains and consolidates. At fixed solid volume, void-ratio change gives a one-dimensional thickness reduction. Foundation settlement, lateral spreading and organic decomposition add other mechanisms, so this model covers only the placed layer itself. Construction elevation and long-term target must remain distinct, and one completion survey cannot close the performance assessment. Assume initial thickness1m,e0=2 and final e1=1. H1=H0(1+e1)/(1+e0)=0.667m and settlement0.333m, with fixed solid volume. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Post-consolidation elevation reserve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「放置材料乾固體沒有流失就代表地表高程不會再下降。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If placed dry solids are retained, surface elevation cannot subsequently decrease.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「壓密後高程餘量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Post-consolidation elevation reserve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-09-k1","title":"壓密後高程餘量","titleEn":"Post-consolidation elevation reserve","text":"細泥排水壓密會使放置面逐漸降低，固體體積保持時孔隙比變化可換算一維厚度縮減。真實地基也會沉陷、側向流動及有機質分解，因此這個模型只涵蓋單層材料本身；應將施工時點高程和長期目標分開，而非一次測量完成即結案。","textEn":"Fine sediment lowers as it drains and consolidates. At fixed solid volume, void-ratio change gives a one-dimensional thickness reduction.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：放置材料乾固體沒有流失就代表地表高程不會再下降。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If placed dry solids are retained, surface elevation cannot subsequently decrease. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壓密後高程餘量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Post-consolidation elevation reserve\" is correct?","options":["細泥排水壓密會使放置面逐漸降低，固體體積保持時孔隙比變化可換算一維厚度縮減。","放置材料乾固體沒有流失就代表地表高程不會再下降。","潮位超過地面的時間比例直接等於植被的存活機率。"],"optionsEn":["Fine sediment lowers as it drains and consolidates.","If placed dry solids are retained, surface elevation cannot subsequently decrease.","The fraction of time tide exceeds ground directly equals plant survival probability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"細泥排水壓密會使放置面逐漸降低，固體體積保持時孔隙比變化可換算一維厚度縮減。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Fine sediment lowers as it drains and consolidates. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b288-v15-10","title":"壓密後高程餘量：定量估算","titleEn":"Post-consolidation elevation reserve: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「壓密後高程餘量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Post-consolidation elevation reserve” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設初厚1m、初孔隙比e0=2、末孔隙比e1=1，末厚H1=H0(1+e1)/(1+e0)=0.667m，沉陷0.333m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume initial thickness1m,e0=2 and final e1=1. H1=H0(1+e1)/(1+e0)=0.667m and settlement0.333m, with fixed solid volume. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用沉陷板和孔壓觀測區分材料壓密與原地基移動，核對孔隙比樣本的代表性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use settlement and pore-pressure observations to distinguish placed-layer consolidation from foundation movement, checking void-ratio sampling.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設初厚1m、初孔隙比e0=2、末孔隙比e1=1，末厚H1=H0(1+e1)/(1+e0)=0.667m，沉陷0.333m。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume initial thickness1m,e0=2 and final e1=1. H1=H0(1+e1)/(1+e0)=0.667m and settlement0.333m, with fixed solid volume.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「壓密後高程餘量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Post-consolidation elevation reserve\", which statement holds?","options":["混合後平均濃度降低代表同百分比的污染物已被消除。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","表面變乾就代表全部填料已完全排水並取得最終強度。"],"optionsEn":["A lower average concentration after mixing means the same fraction of contaminant was destroyed.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","A dry surface proves that the entire fill has drained and reached final strength."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b288-v15-11","title":"壓密後高程餘量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Post-consolidation elevation reserve: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「壓密後高程餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Post-consolidation elevation reserve” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用沉陷板和孔壓觀測區分材料壓密與原地基移動，核對孔隙比樣本的代表性。比較不同時間的高程及乾固體存量，將側向外移和有機質損失另列，不強迫所有變化符合一維式。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use settlement and pore-pressure observations to distinguish placed-layer consolidation from foundation movement, checking void-ratio sampling. Compare elevation and dry-solid storage through time, listing lateral export and organic loss separately instead of forcing all change into one-dimensional compression. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用沉陷板和孔壓觀測區分材料壓密與原地基移動，核對孔隙比樣本的代表性。比較不同時間的高程及乾固體存量，將側向外移和有機質損失另列，不強迫所有變化符合一維式。","observationEn":"Site practice: Use settlement and pore-pressure observations to distinguish placed-layer consolidation from foundation movement, checking void-ratio sampling. Compare elevation and dry-solid storage through time, listing lateral export and organic loss separately instead of forcing all change into one-dimensional compression.","failure":"注意干擾：把原地基沉陷也算成填料壓密會誤估所需材料，未考慮側向流動又可能低估低處擴散。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assigning foundation settlement entirely to fill consolidation misstates material demand, while omitted spreading understates movement into low areas. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用沉陷板和孔壓觀測區分材料壓密與原地基移動，核對孔隙比樣本的代表性。比較不同時間的高程及乾固體存量，將側向外移和有機質損失另列，不強迫所有變化符合一維式。","textEn":"Use settlement and pore-pressure observations to distinguish placed-layer consolidation from foundation movement, checking void-ratio sampling. Compare elevation and dry-solid storage through time, listing lateral export and organic loss separately instead of forcing all change into one-dimensional compression.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用沉陷板和孔壓觀測區分材料壓密與原地基移動，核對孔隙比樣本的代表性。比較不同時間的高程及乾固體存量，將側向外移和有機質損失另列，不強迫所有變化符合一維式。","textEn":"Use settlement and pore-pressure observations to distinguish placed-layer consolidation from foundation movement, checking void-ratio sampling. Compare elevation and dry-solid storage through time, listing lateral export and organic loss separately instead of forcing all change into one-dimensional compression.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「壓密後高程餘量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Post-consolidation elevation reserve\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","處理區施工後植被增加就足以證明增長完全由工程造成。","用沉陷板和孔壓觀測區分材料壓密與原地基移動，核對孔隙比樣本的代表性。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Any vegetation increase after treatment proves that the project caused the entire increase.","Use settlement and pore-pressure observations to distinguish placed-layer consolidation from foundation movement, checking void-ratio sampling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用沉陷板和孔壓觀測區分材料壓密與原地基移動，核對孔隙比樣本的代表性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use settlement and pore-pressure observations to distinguish placed-layer consolidation from foundation movement, checking void-ratio sampling. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b288-v15-12","title":"壓密後高程餘量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Post-consolidation elevation reserve: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「壓密後高程餘量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Post-consolidation elevation reserve” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把原地基沉陷也算成填料壓密會誤估所需材料，未考慮側向流動又可能低估低處擴散。高程達標後持續下降會改變植被帶與潮溝連通，影響復育功能。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assigning foundation settlement entirely to fill consolidation misstates material demand, while omitted spreading understates movement into low areas. Continued lowering after nominal completion alters vegetation zones and creek connectivity, changing the intended restoration function. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設初厚1m、初孔隙比e0=2、末孔隙比e1=1，末厚H1=H0(1+e1)/(1+e0)=0.667m，沉陷0.333m。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: H1=H0(1+e1)/(1+e0)=0.667m and settlement0.333m, with fixed solid volume.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「放置材料乾固體沒有流失就代表地表高程不會再下降。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If placed dry solids are retained, surface elevation cannot subsequently decrease.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把原地基沉陷也算成填料壓密會誤估所需材料，未考慮側向流動又可能低估低處擴散。高程達標後持續下降會改變植被帶與潮溝連通，影響復育功能。","textEn":"Assigning foundation settlement entirely to fill consolidation misstates material demand, while omitted spreading understates movement into low areas. Continued lowering after nominal completion alters vegetation zones and creek connectivity, changing the intended restoration function.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「壓密後高程餘量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Post-consolidation elevation reserve\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把原地基沉陷也算成填料壓密會誤估所需材料，未考慮側向流動又可能低估低處擴散。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","潮位超過地面的時間比例直接等於植被的存活機率。"],"optionsEn":["Assigning foundation settlement entirely to fill consolidation misstates material demand, while omitted spreading understates movement into low areas.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The fraction of time tide exceeds ground directly equals plant survival probability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把原地基沉陷也算成填料壓密會誤估所需材料，未考慮側向流動又可能低估低處擴散。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assigning foundation settlement entirely to fill consolidation misstates material demand, while omitted spreading understates movement into low areas. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b288-v15-13","title":"潮汐淹水比例：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tidal inundation fraction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「潮汐淹水比例」如何影響疏浚泥沙有益利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tidal inundation fraction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beneficial reuse of dredged sediment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"潮位與地面高程的相對關係決定浸水時間，對植被及水質交換都重要。單一正弦潮忽略不對稱、風增水與排水滯後，但能說明高程小變動如何改變淹水比例；時間比例不同於水深，也不能直接換成某物種存活率或生態成功機率。 假設潮位η=A sinωt、A=1m、地面z=0.5m且無滯水，淹水比例arccos(z/A)/π=1/3，非存活率。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「潮汐淹水比例」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Relative tide and ground elevation determine inundation duration, affecting vegetation and exchange. One sinusoid omits asymmetry, wind setup and drainage lag but illustrates how elevation changes alter the wet fraction. Duration fraction differs from water depth and cannot directly become a species-survival probability or a general measure of ecological success at the restoration site. Assume tideη=A sinωt,A=1m and ground z=0.5m without ponding. Inundation fraction arccos(z/A)/π=1/3, not survival probability. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tidal inundation fraction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「潮位超過地面的時間比例直接等於植被的存活機率。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The fraction of time tide exceeds ground directly equals plant survival probability.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「潮汐淹水比例」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tidal inundation fraction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-13-k1","title":"潮汐淹水比例","titleEn":"Tidal inundation fraction","text":"潮位與地面高程的相對關係決定浸水時間，對植被及水質交換都重要。單一正弦潮忽略不對稱、風增水與排水滯後，但能說明高程小變動如何改變淹水比例；時間比例不同於水深，也不能直接換成某物種存活率或生態成功機率。","textEn":"Relative tide and ground elevation determine inundation duration, affecting vegetation and exchange. One sinusoid omits asymmetry, wind setup and drainage lag but illustrates how elevation changes alter the wet fraction.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：潮位超過地面的時間比例直接等於植被的存活機率。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The fraction of time tide exceeds ground directly equals plant survival probability. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「潮汐淹水比例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tidal inundation fraction\" is correct?","options":["潮位超過地面的時間比例直接等於植被的存活機率。","潮位與地面高程的相對關係決定浸水時間，對植被及水質交換都重要。","產品純度與原料回收率永遠具有相同分母而且相等。"],"optionsEn":["The fraction of time tide exceeds ground directly equals plant survival probability.","Relative tide and ground elevation determine inundation duration, affecting vegetation and exchange.","Product purity and feed recovery always share the same denominator and value."],"answer":1,"explanation":"潮位與地面高程的相對關係決定浸水時間，對植被及水質交換都重要。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Relative tide and ground elevation determine inundation duration, affecting vegetation and exchange. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b288-v15-14","title":"潮汐淹水比例：定量估算","titleEn":"Tidal inundation fraction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「潮汐淹水比例」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tidal inundation fraction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設潮位η=A sinωt、A=1m、地面z=0.5m且無滯水，淹水比例arccos(z/A)/π=1/3，非存活率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume tideη=A sinωt,A=1m and ground z=0.5m without ponding. Inundation fraction arccos(z/A)/π=1/3, not survival probability. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同一高程基準記錄地面與潮位序列，實算超過地面時間並檢查退潮後積水。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record terrain and tide on one datum and count exceedance time while checking post-tide ponding.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設潮位η=A sinωt、A=1m、地面z=0.5m且無滯水，淹水比例arccos(z/A)/π=1/3，非存活率。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume tideη=A sinωt,A=1m and ground z=0.5m without ponding. Inundation fraction arccos(z/A)/π=1/3, not survival probability.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「潮汐淹水比例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tidal inundation fraction\", which statement holds?","options":["覆蓋材料總方量足夠就能證明各處隔離厚度與化學功能足夠。","運距縮短的排放差額就是再利用方案完整的生命週期淨減碳。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Enough total cover volume proves adequate thickness and chemical isolation everywhere.","The emissions saved by shorter transport equal the reuse project's complete life-cycle benefit.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b288-v15-15","title":"潮汐淹水比例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tidal inundation fraction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「潮汐淹水比例」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tidal inundation fraction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同一高程基準記錄地面與潮位序列，實算超過地面時間並檢查退潮後積水。按季節和植被區分組比較，說明正弦示意漏掉的長週期變化與降雨，不用單次高潮代表全年。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record terrain and tide on one datum and count exceedance time while checking post-tide ponding. Compare by season and vegetation zone, identifying long-period variation and rainfall omitted by the sinusoid rather than treating one high tide as representative of the year. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以同一高程基準記錄地面與潮位序列，實算超過地面時間並檢查退潮後積水。按季節和植被區分組比較，說明正弦示意漏掉的長週期變化與降雨，不用單次高潮代表全年。","observationEn":"Site practice: Record terrain and tide on one datum and count exceedance time while checking post-tide ponding. Compare by season and vegetation zone, identifying long-period variation and rainfall omitted by the sinusoid rather than treating one high tide as representative of the year.","failure":"注意干擾：排水溝阻塞會使實際浸水長於海潮超越時間，基準偏差又會把植被帶放錯高程。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Blocked drainage prolongs inundation beyond tidal exceedance, while datum errors misplace vegetation zones. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同一高程基準記錄地面與潮位序列，實算超過地面時間並檢查退潮後積水。按季節和植被區分組比較，說明正弦示意漏掉的長週期變化與降雨，不用單次高潮代表全年。","textEn":"Record terrain and tide on one datum and count exceedance time while checking post-tide ponding. Compare by season and vegetation zone, identifying long-period variation and rainfall omitted by the sinusoid rather than treating one high tide as representative of the year.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以同一高程基準記錄地面與潮位序列，實算超過地面時間並檢查退潮後積水。按季節和植被區分組比較，說明正弦示意漏掉的長週期變化與降雨，不用單次高潮代表全年。","textEn":"Record terrain and tide on one datum and count exceedance time while checking post-tide ponding. Compare by season and vegetation zone, identifying long-period variation and rainfall omitted by the sinusoid rather than treating one high tide as representative of the year.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「潮汐淹水比例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tidal inundation fraction\"?","options":["以同一高程基準記錄地面與潮位序列，實算超過地面時間並檢查退潮後積水。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","疏浚材料只要有預定去向就全部算成已驗證成功再利用。"],"optionsEn":["Record terrain and tide on one datum and count exceedance time while checking post-tide ponding.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Every dredged batch with a planned destination already counts as verified successful reuse."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以同一高程基準記錄地面與潮位序列，實算超過地面時間並檢查退潮後積水。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record terrain and tide on one datum and count exceedance time while checking post-tide ponding. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b288-v15-16","title":"潮汐淹水比例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tidal inundation fraction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「潮汐淹水比例」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tidal inundation fraction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"排水溝阻塞會使實際浸水長於海潮超越時間，基準偏差又會把植被帶放錯高程。只用平均潮差而不看長時間序列，可能漏掉持續積水的關鍵事件。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Blocked drainage prolongs inundation beyond tidal exceedance, while datum errors misplace vegetation zones. A mean tidal range without a long record can miss the sustained flooding events that govern the actual response of restored habitat. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設潮位η=A sinωt、A=1m、地面z=0.5m且無滯水，淹水比例arccos(z/A)/π=1/3，非存活率。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Inundation fraction arccos(z/A)/π=1/3, not survival probability.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「潮位超過地面的時間比例直接等於植被的存活機率。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The fraction of time tide exceeds ground directly equals plant survival probability.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"排水溝阻塞會使實際浸水長於海潮超越時間，基準偏差又會把植被帶放錯高程。只用平均潮差而不看長時間序列，可能漏掉持續積水的關鍵事件。","textEn":"Blocked drainage prolongs inundation beyond tidal exceedance, while datum errors misplace vegetation zones. A mean tidal range without a long record can miss the sustained flooding events that govern the actual response of restored habitat.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「潮汐淹水比例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tidal inundation fraction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","排水溝阻塞會使實際浸水長於海潮超越時間，基準偏差又會把植被帶放錯高程。","產品純度與原料回收率永遠具有相同分母而且相等。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Blocked drainage prolongs inundation beyond tidal exceedance, while datum errors misplace vegetation zones.","Product purity and feed recovery always share the same denominator and value."],"answer":1,"explanation":"排水溝阻塞會使實際浸水長於海潮超越時間，基準偏差又會把植被帶放錯高程。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Blocked drainage prolongs inundation beyond tidal exceedance, while datum errors misplace vegetation zones. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b288-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「篩分回收與產率」與「污染質量與濃度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Screening recovery and yield\" and \"Contaminant mass versus concentration\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b288-v15-17","title":"篩分回收與產率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Screening recovery and yield: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「篩分回收與產率」如何影響疏浚泥沙有益利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Screening recovery and yield” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beneficial reuse of dredged sediment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分離處理需同時看產品中目標粒群的純度和原料目標粒群的回收率，兩者分母不同。增加篩分強度可能提高純度卻流失可用砂，且濕篩和乾篩結果需統一基準；工程用途還要求其他性質，因此產品比例不能被當成最終可用性證明。 假設原料乾砂600t，產品含砂540t且產品總乾質量600t；砂回收率540/600=90%，產品純度也90%，分母巧合相同。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「篩分回收與產率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separation must distinguish product purity from recovery of the target fraction in the feed, because the denominators differ. More aggressive screening may increase purity while losing usable sand, and wet and dry results require one basis. Intended use imposes additional properties, so a high product fraction does not itself qualify the material for placement or structural performance. Assume feed contains600t dry sand; product contains540t sand in600t total dry mass. Recovery and purity are both90%, with coincidentally equal denominators. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Screening recovery and yield” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「產品純度與原料回收率永遠具有相同分母而且相等。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Product purity and feed recovery always share the same denominator and value.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「篩分回收與產率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Screening recovery and yield”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-17-k1","title":"篩分回收與產率","titleEn":"Screening recovery and yield","text":"分離處理需同時看產品中目標粒群的純度和原料目標粒群的回收率，兩者分母不同。增加篩分強度可能提高純度卻流失可用砂，且濕篩和乾篩結果需統一基準；工程用途還要求其他性質，因此產品比例不能被當成最終可用性證明。","textEn":"Separation must distinguish product purity from recovery of the target fraction in the feed, because the denominators differ. More aggressive screening may increase purity while losing usable sand, and wet and dry results require one basis.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：產品純度與原料回收率永遠具有相同分母而且相等。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Product purity and feed recovery always share the same denominator and value. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「篩分回收與產率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Screening recovery and yield\" is correct?","options":["產品純度與原料回收率永遠具有相同分母而且相等。","混合後平均濃度降低代表同百分比的污染物已被消除。","分離處理需同時看產品中目標粒群的純度和原料目標粒群的回收率，兩者分母不同。"],"optionsEn":["Product purity and feed recovery always share the same denominator and value.","A lower average concentration after mixing means the same fraction of contaminant was destroyed.","Separation must distinguish product purity from recovery of the target fraction in the feed, because the denominators differ."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分離處理需同時看產品中目標粒群的純度和原料目標粒群的回收率，兩者分母不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separation must distinguish product purity from recovery of the target fraction in the feed, because the denominators differ. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b288-v15-18","title":"篩分回收與產率：定量估算","titleEn":"Screening recovery and yield: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「篩分回收與產率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Screening recovery and yield” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設原料乾砂600t，產品含砂540t且產品總乾質量600t；砂回收率540/600=90%，產品純度也90%，分母巧合相同。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume feed contains600t dry sand; product contains540t sand in600t total dry mass. Recovery and purity are both90%, with coincidentally equal denominators. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分別採原料、產品和排除物樣本，建立目標粒群的完整乾質量平衡。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample feed, product and reject streams and close the target fraction’s dry-mass balance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設原料乾砂600t，產品含砂540t且產品總乾質量600t；砂回收率540/600=90%，產品純度也90%，分母巧合相同。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume feed contains600t dry sand; product contains540t sand in600t total dry mass. Recovery and purity are both90%, with coincidentally equal denominators.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「篩分回收與產率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Screening recovery and yield\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","表面變乾就代表全部填料已完全排水並取得最終強度。","處理區施工後植被增加就足以證明增長完全由工程造成。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","A dry surface proves that the entire fill has drained and reached final strength.","Any vegetation increase after treatment proves that the project caused the entire increase."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b288-v15-19","title":"篩分回收與產率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Screening recovery and yield: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「篩分回收與產率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Screening recovery and yield” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分別採原料、產品和排除物樣本，建立目標粒群的完整乾質量平衡。用兩個不同分母重新計算回收與純度，檢查細料附著和含水偏差，並記錄未被篩分指標代表的材料需求。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample feed, product and reject streams and close the target fraction’s dry-mass balance. Recalculate recovery and purity using their distinct denominators, checking attached fines and moisture bias, and list material requirements that screening metrics alone do not represent. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分別採原料、產品和排除物樣本，建立目標粒群的完整乾質量平衡。用兩個不同分母重新計算回收與純度，檢查細料附著和含水偏差，並記錄未被篩分指標代表的材料需求。","observationEn":"Site practice: Sample feed, product and reject streams and close the target fraction’s dry-mass balance. Recalculate recovery and purity using their distinct denominators, checking attached fines and moisture bias, and list material requirements that screening metrics alone do not represent.","failure":"注意干擾：把產品純度當回收率可能隱藏大量好砂被丟棄，反之回收率高也可能得到含細料過多的產品。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Substituting purity for recovery can conceal discarded good sand, while high recovery may produce an excessively fine-rich product. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分別採原料、產品和排除物樣本，建立目標粒群的完整乾質量平衡。用兩個不同分母重新計算回收與純度，檢查細料附著和含水偏差，並記錄未被篩分指標代表的材料需求。","textEn":"Sample feed, product and reject streams and close the target fraction’s dry-mass balance. Recalculate recovery and purity using their distinct denominators, checking attached fines and moisture bias, and list material requirements that screening metrics alone do not represent.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分別採原料、產品和排除物樣本，建立目標粒群的完整乾質量平衡。用兩個不同分母重新計算回收與純度，檢查細料附著和含水偏差，並記錄未被篩分指標代表的材料需求。","textEn":"Sample feed, product and reject streams and close the target fraction’s dry-mass balance. Recalculate recovery and purity using their distinct denominators, checking attached fines and moisture bias, and list material requirements that screening metrics alone do not represent.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「篩分回收與產率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Screening recovery and yield\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","分別採原料、產品和排除物樣本，建立目標粒群的完整乾質量平衡。","平均放置厚度達標就能證明每個位置的淹水條件都合適。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Sample feed, product and reject streams and close the target fraction’s dry-mass balance.","A satisfactory mean placement thickness proves suitable inundation at every location."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分別採原料、產品和排除物樣本，建立目標粒群的完整乾質量平衡。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample feed, product and reject streams and close the target fraction’s dry-mass balance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b288-v15-20","title":"篩分回收與產率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Screening recovery and yield: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「篩分回收與產率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Screening recovery and yield” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把產品純度當回收率可能隱藏大量好砂被丟棄，反之回收率高也可能得到含細料過多的產品。只有單一產品樣本，不能追查分離設備真正的物料去向。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Substituting purity for recovery can conceal discarded good sand, while high recovery may produce an excessively fine-rich product. A product-only sample cannot reveal the actual routing of material through the separation process. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設原料乾砂600t，產品含砂540t且產品總乾質量600t；砂回收率540/600=90%，產品純度也90%，分母巧合相同。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Recovery and purity are both90%, with coincidentally equal denominators.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「產品純度與原料回收率永遠具有相同分母而且相等。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Product purity and feed recovery always share the same denominator and value.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把產品純度當回收率可能隱藏大量好砂被丟棄，反之回收率高也可能得到含細料過多的產品。只有單一產品樣本，不能追查分離設備真正的物料去向。","textEn":"Substituting purity for recovery can conceal discarded good sand, while high recovery may produce an excessively fine-rich product. A product-only sample cannot reveal the actual routing of material through the separation process.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「篩分回收與產率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Screening recovery and yield\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","混合後平均濃度降低代表同百分比的污染物已被消除。","把產品純度當回收率可能隱藏大量好砂被丟棄，反之回收率高也可能得到含細料過多的產品。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A lower average concentration after mixing means the same fraction of contaminant was destroyed.","Substituting purity for recovery can conceal discarded good sand, while high recovery may produce an excessively fine-rich product."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把產品純度當回收率可能隱藏大量好砂被丟棄，反之回收率高也可能得到含細料過多的產品。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Substituting purity for recovery can conceal discarded good sand, while high recovery may produce an excessively fine-rich product. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b288-v15-21","title":"污染質量與濃度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Contaminant mass versus concentration: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「污染質量與濃度」如何影響疏浚泥沙有益利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Contaminant mass versus concentration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beneficial reuse of dredged sediment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"固體污染物濃度乘乾質量可得到總負荷，這與孔隙水溶出或生物可利用性不同。混合會改變平均濃度卻不讓污染物消失，因此守恆算例絕不能被當成稀釋達標方法；評估須依物質、暴露路徑和適用法域選用檢測，不能只憑平均數決定用途。 假設乾料1000t、某示蹤物20mg/kg，總量20kg；加入1000t不含該物材料後均濃度10mg/kg，但總量仍20kg。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「污染質量與濃度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Dry-basis concentration times sediment mass gives total burden, distinct from dissolved release or bioavailability. Mixing changes mean concentration without destroying contaminants, so this conservation example must never be treated as a dilution-to-compliance method. Evaluation requires substance-specific tests, exposure pathways and applicable jurisdiction, not a use decision based solely on a convenient bulk average. Assume1000t dry sediment at tracer concentration20mg/kg: total20kg. Adding1000t tracer-free material gives10mg/kg while total remains20kg; no compliance claim. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Contaminant mass versus concentration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「混合後平均濃度降低代表同百分比的污染物已被消除。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A lower average concentration after mixing means the same fraction of contaminant was destroyed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「污染質量與濃度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Contaminant mass versus concentration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-21-k1","title":"污染質量與濃度","titleEn":"Contaminant mass versus concentration","text":"固體污染物濃度乘乾質量可得到總負荷，這與孔隙水溶出或生物可利用性不同。混合會改變平均濃度卻不讓污染物消失，因此守恆算例絕不能被當成稀釋達標方法；評估須依物質、暴露路徑和適用法域選用檢測，不能只憑平均數決定用途。","textEn":"Dry-basis concentration times sediment mass gives total burden, distinct from dissolved release or bioavailability. Mixing changes mean concentration without destroying contaminants, so this conservation example must never be treated as a dilution-to-compliance method.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混合後平均濃度降低代表同百分比的污染物已被消除。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A lower average concentration after mixing means the same fraction of contaminant was destroyed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「污染質量與濃度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Contaminant mass versus concentration\" is correct?","options":["固體污染物濃度乘乾質量可得到總負荷，這與孔隙水溶出或生物可利用性不同。","混合後平均濃度降低代表同百分比的污染物已被消除。","覆蓋材料總方量足夠就能證明各處隔離厚度與化學功能足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Dry-basis concentration times sediment mass gives total burden, distinct from dissolved release or bioavailability.","A lower average concentration after mixing means the same fraction of contaminant was destroyed.","Enough total cover volume proves adequate thickness and chemical isolation everywhere."],"answer":0,"explanation":"固體污染物濃度乘乾質量可得到總負荷，這與孔隙水溶出或生物可利用性不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Dry-basis concentration times sediment mass gives total burden, distinct from dissolved release or bioavailability. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b288-v15-22","title":"污染質量與濃度：定量估算","titleEn":"Contaminant mass versus concentration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「污染質量與濃度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Contaminant mass versus concentration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設乾料1000t、某示蹤物20mg/kg，總量20kg；加入1000t不含該物材料後均濃度10mg/kg，但總量仍20kg。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume1000t dry sediment at tracer concentration20mg/kg: total20kg. Adding1000t tracer-free material gives10mg/kg while total remains20kg; no compliance claim. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保留乾基定義、採樣分區與分析品質資料，分別計算總質量與濃度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Retain dry-basis definition, sampling zones and analytical quality records, calculating burden separately from concentration.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設乾料1000t、某示蹤物20mg/kg，總量20kg；加入1000t不含該物材料後均濃度10mg/kg，但總量仍20kg。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume1000t dry sediment at tracer concentration20mg/kg: total20kg. Adding1000t tracer-free material gives10mg/kg while total remains20kg; no compliance claim.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「污染質量與濃度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Contaminant mass versus concentration\", which statement holds?","options":["運距縮短的排放差額就是再利用方案完整的生命週期淨減碳。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","疏浚材料只要有預定去向就全部算成已驗證成功再利用。"],"optionsEn":["The emissions saved by shorter transport equal the reuse project's complete life-cycle benefit.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Every dredged batch with a planned destination already counts as verified successful reuse."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b288-v15-23","title":"污染質量與濃度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Contaminant mass versus concentration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「污染質量與濃度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Contaminant mass versus concentration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保留乾基定義、採樣分區與分析品質資料，分別計算總質量與濃度。另查溶出、生物暴露及材料用途的必要試驗，將任何混合方案交由適用程序評估，不把降低平均值當成去除污染。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Retain dry-basis definition, sampling zones and analytical quality records, calculating burden separately from concentration. Evaluate required leaching, biological exposure and intended-use tests through the applicable process, without treating a lower mixed average as removal of the substance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保留乾基定義、採樣分區與分析品質資料，分別計算總質量與濃度。另查溶出、生物暴露及材料用途的必要試驗，將任何混合方案交由適用程序評估，不把降低平均值當成去除污染。","observationEn":"Site practice: Retain dry-basis definition, sampling zones and analytical quality records, calculating burden separately from concentration. Evaluate required leaching, biological exposure and intended-use tests through the applicable process, without treating a lower mixed average as removal of the substance.","failure":"注意干擾：熱點被大量低濃度樣本平均後可能消失在報表中，總負荷和局部接觸仍存在。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A hotspot can disappear statistically among low-concentration samples while burden and local exposure persist. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保留乾基定義、採樣分區與分析品質資料，分別計算總質量與濃度。另查溶出、生物暴露及材料用途的必要試驗，將任何混合方案交由適用程序評估，不把降低平均值當成去除污染。","textEn":"Retain dry-basis definition, sampling zones and analytical quality records, calculating burden separately from concentration. Evaluate required leaching, biological exposure and intended-use tests through the applicable process, without treating a lower mixed average as removal of the substance.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保留乾基定義、採樣分區與分析品質資料，分別計算總質量與濃度。另查溶出、生物暴露及材料用途的必要試驗，將任何混合方案交由適用程序評估，不把降低平均值當成去除污染。","textEn":"Retain dry-basis definition, sampling zones and analytical quality records, calculating burden separately from concentration. Evaluate required leaching, biological exposure and intended-use tests through the applicable process, without treating a lower mixed average as removal of the substance.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「污染質量與濃度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Contaminant mass versus concentration\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","放置材料乾固體沒有流失就代表地表高程不會再下降。","保留乾基定義、採樣分區與分析品質資料，分別計算總質量與濃度。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","If placed dry solids are retained, surface elevation cannot subsequently decrease.","Retain dry-basis definition, sampling zones and analytical quality records, calculating burden separately from concentration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"保留乾基定義、採樣分區與分析品質資料，分別計算總質量與濃度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Retain dry-basis definition, sampling zones and analytical quality records, calculating burden separately from concentration. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b288-v15-24","title":"污染質量與濃度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Contaminant mass versus concentration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「污染質量與濃度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Contaminant mass versus concentration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"熱點被大量低濃度樣本平均後可能消失在報表中，總負荷和局部接觸仍存在。以稀釋比例代替處理成效會漏掉溶出條件改變和生物累積的可能途徑。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A hotspot can disappear statistically among low-concentration samples while burden and local exposure persist. Replacing treatment evidence with a dilution ratio overlooks changes in leaching conditions and possible pathways for biological accumulation after placement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設乾料1000t、某示蹤物20mg/kg，總量20kg；加入1000t不含該物材料後均濃度10mg/kg，但總量仍20kg。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Adding1000t tracer-free material gives10mg/kg while total remains20kg; no compliance claim.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混合後平均濃度降低代表同百分比的污染物已被消除。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A lower average concentration after mixing means the same fraction of contaminant was destroyed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"熱點被大量低濃度樣本平均後可能消失在報表中，總負荷和局部接觸仍存在。以稀釋比例代替處理成效會漏掉溶出條件改變和生物累積的可能途徑。","textEn":"A hotspot can disappear statistically among low-concentration samples while burden and local exposure persist. Replacing treatment evidence with a dilution ratio overlooks changes in leaching conditions and possible pathways for biological accumulation after placement.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「污染質量與濃度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Contaminant mass versus concentration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["熱點被大量低濃度樣本平均後可能消失在報表中，總負荷和局部接觸仍存在。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","覆蓋材料總方量足夠就能證明各處隔離厚度與化學功能足夠。"],"optionsEn":["A hotspot can disappear statistically among low-concentration samples while burden and local exposure persist.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Enough total cover volume proves adequate thickness and chemical isolation everywhere."],"answer":0,"explanation":"熱點被大量低濃度樣本平均後可能消失在報表中，總負荷和局部接觸仍存在。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A hotspot can disappear statistically among low-concentration samples while burden and local exposure persist. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b288-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量」與「填料有效應力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cover thickness and erosion reserve\" and \"Effective stress in placed sediment\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b288-v15-25","title":"覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cover thickness and erosion reserve: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量」如何影響疏浚泥沙有益利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cover thickness and erosion reserve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beneficial reuse of dredged sediment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"隔離覆蓋層需維持連續厚度，平均放置量不能代表局部最薄處。侵蝕、壓密和底泥混入會消耗幾何餘量，而化學隔離還涉及擴散與生物擾動；本課只計厚度收支，不提供任何污染場址的建議覆蓋規格或長期隔離保證。 假設初始覆蓋0.50m、侵蝕0.08m、壓密0.04m且均勻，剩餘0.38m；未考慮混層、擴散與生物擾動。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A cover layer needs continuous thickness, and average placed quantity does not describe its thinnest location. Erosion, consolidation and mixing consume geometric reserve, while chemical isolation also involves diffusion and biological disturbance. This lesson only accounts for thickness; it supplies no recommended contaminated-site cap specification and cannot establish durable isolation from the remaining number alone. Assume initial cover0.50m,erosion0.08m and compression0.04m uniformly. Remaining thickness is0.38m, excluding mixing, diffusion and bioturbation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cover thickness and erosion reserve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「覆蓋材料總方量足夠就能證明各處隔離厚度與化學功能足夠。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Enough total cover volume proves adequate thickness and chemical isolation everywhere.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cover thickness and erosion reserve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-25-k1","title":"覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量","titleEn":"Cover thickness and erosion reserve","text":"隔離覆蓋層需維持連續厚度，平均放置量不能代表局部最薄處。侵蝕、壓密和底泥混入會消耗幾何餘量，而化學隔離還涉及擴散與生物擾動；本課只計厚度收支，不提供任何污染場址的建議覆蓋規格或長期隔離保證。","textEn":"A cover layer needs continuous thickness, and average placed quantity does not describe its thinnest location. Erosion, consolidation and mixing consume geometric reserve, while chemical isolation also involves diffusion and biological disturbance.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：覆蓋材料總方量足夠就能證明各處隔離厚度與化學功能足夠。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Enough total cover volume proves adequate thickness and chemical isolation everywhere. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cover thickness and erosion reserve\" is correct?","options":["覆蓋材料總方量足夠就能證明各處隔離厚度與化學功能足夠。","隔離覆蓋層需維持連續厚度，平均放置量不能代表局部最薄處。","表面變乾就代表全部填料已完全排水並取得最終強度。"],"optionsEn":["Enough total cover volume proves adequate thickness and chemical isolation everywhere.","A cover layer needs continuous thickness, and average placed quantity does not describe its thinnest location.","A dry surface proves that the entire fill has drained and reached final strength."],"answer":1,"explanation":"隔離覆蓋層需維持連續厚度，平均放置量不能代表局部最薄處。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A cover layer needs continuous thickness, and average placed quantity does not describe its thinnest location. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b288-v15-26","title":"覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量：定量估算","titleEn":"Cover thickness and erosion reserve: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cover thickness and erosion reserve” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設初始覆蓋0.50m、侵蝕0.08m、壓密0.04m且均勻，剩餘0.38m；未考慮混層、擴散與生物擾動。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume initial cover0.50m,erosion0.08m and compression0.04m uniformly. Remaining thickness is0.38m, excluding mixing, diffusion and bioturbation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用可辨識界面量測覆蓋層頂底，分區記錄最薄值和不確定度，核對侵蝕與壓密是否重複扣除。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure identifiable upper and lower interfaces, recording minimum thickness and uncertainty by zone and checking double-counted erosion or compression.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設初始覆蓋0.50m、侵蝕0.08m、壓密0.04m且均勻，剩餘0.38m；未考慮混層、擴散與生物擾動。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume initial cover0.50m,erosion0.08m and compression0.04m uniformly. Remaining thickness is0.38m, excluding mixing, diffusion and bioturbation.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cover thickness and erosion reserve\", which statement holds?","options":["處理區施工後植被增加就足以證明增長完全由工程造成。","平均放置厚度達標就能證明每個位置的淹水條件都合適。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Any vegetation increase after treatment proves that the project caused the entire increase.","A satisfactory mean placement thickness proves suitable inundation at every location.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b288-v15-27","title":"覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cover thickness and erosion reserve: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cover thickness and erosion reserve” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用可辨識界面量測覆蓋層頂底，分區記錄最薄值和不確定度，核對侵蝕與壓密是否重複扣除。另查材料相容、滲流和生物作用，不讓幾何驗證取代完整隔離績效評估。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure identifiable upper and lower interfaces, recording minimum thickness and uncertainty by zone and checking double-counted erosion or compression. Assess compatibility, seepage and biological processes separately so geometric verification does not replace a complete isolation-performance evaluation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用可辨識界面量測覆蓋層頂底，分區記錄最薄值和不確定度，核對侵蝕與壓密是否重複扣除。另查材料相容、滲流和生物作用，不讓幾何驗證取代完整隔離績效評估。","observationEn":"Site practice: Measure identifiable upper and lower interfaces, recording minimum thickness and uncertainty by zone and checking double-counted erosion or compression. Assess compatibility, seepage and biological processes separately so geometric verification does not replace a complete isolation-performance evaluation.","failure":"注意干擾：覆蓋料與原泥混合會使外觀厚度足夠但隔離距離不足，局部沖槽也可能穿透平均合格的區域。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mixing with native sediment can leave adequate apparent thickness but inadequate separation, while a local scour channel breaches an otherwise satisfactory average cover. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用可辨識界面量測覆蓋層頂底，分區記錄最薄值和不確定度，核對侵蝕與壓密是否重複扣除。另查材料相容、滲流和生物作用，不讓幾何驗證取代完整隔離績效評估。","textEn":"Measure identifiable upper and lower interfaces, recording minimum thickness and uncertainty by zone and checking double-counted erosion or compression. Assess compatibility, seepage and biological processes separately so geometric verification does not replace a complete isolation-performance evaluation.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用可辨識界面量測覆蓋層頂底，分區記錄最薄值和不確定度，核對侵蝕與壓密是否重複扣除。另查材料相容、滲流和生物作用，不讓幾何驗證取代完整隔離績效評估。","textEn":"Measure identifiable upper and lower interfaces, recording minimum thickness and uncertainty by zone and checking double-counted erosion or compression. Assess compatibility, seepage and biological processes separately so geometric verification does not replace a complete isolation-performance evaluation.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cover thickness and erosion reserve\"?","options":["用可辨識界面量測覆蓋層頂底，分區記錄最薄值和不確定度，核對侵蝕與壓密是否重複扣除。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","潮位超過地面的時間比例直接等於植被的存活機率。"],"optionsEn":["Measure identifiable upper and lower interfaces, recording minimum thickness and uncertainty by zone and checking double-counted erosion or compression.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The fraction of time tide exceeds ground directly equals plant survival probability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用可辨識界面量測覆蓋層頂底，分區記錄最薄值和不確定度，核對侵蝕與壓密是否重複扣除。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure identifiable upper and lower interfaces, recording minimum thickness and uncertainty by zone and checking double-counted erosion or compression. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b288-v15-28","title":"覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cover thickness and erosion reserve: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cover thickness and erosion reserve” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"覆蓋料與原泥混合會使外觀厚度足夠但隔離距離不足，局部沖槽也可能穿透平均合格的區域。只依材料總方量驗收，無法找到控制暴露的薄弱路徑。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mixing with native sediment can leave adequate apparent thickness but inadequate separation, while a local scour channel breaches an otherwise satisfactory average cover. Total material quantity cannot identify the thin pathways controlling actual exposure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設初始覆蓋0.50m、侵蝕0.08m、壓密0.04m且均勻，剩餘0.38m；未考慮混層、擴散與生物擾動。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Remaining thickness is0.38m, excluding mixing, diffusion and bioturbation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「覆蓋材料總方量足夠就能證明各處隔離厚度與化學功能足夠。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Enough total cover volume proves adequate thickness and chemical isolation everywhere.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"覆蓋料與原泥混合會使外觀厚度足夠但隔離距離不足，局部沖槽也可能穿透平均合格的區域。只依材料總方量驗收，無法找到控制暴露的薄弱路徑。","textEn":"Mixing with native sediment can leave adequate apparent thickness but inadequate separation, while a local scour channel breaches an otherwise satisfactory average cover. Total material quantity cannot identify the thin pathways controlling actual exposure.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「覆蓋厚度與侵蝕餘量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cover thickness and erosion reserve\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","覆蓋料與原泥混合會使外觀厚度足夠但隔離距離不足，局部沖槽也可能穿透平均合格的區域。","表面變乾就代表全部填料已完全排水並取得最終強度。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Mixing with native sediment can leave adequate apparent thickness but inadequate separation, while a local scour channel breaches an otherwise satisfactory average cover.","A dry surface proves that the entire fill has drained and reached final strength."],"answer":1,"explanation":"覆蓋料與原泥混合會使外觀厚度足夠但隔離距離不足，局部沖槽也可能穿透平均合格的區域。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mixing with native sediment can leave adequate apparent thickness but inadequate separation, while a local scour channel breaches an otherwise satisfactory average cover. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b288-v15-29","title":"填料有效應力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Effective stress in placed sediment: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「填料有效應力」如何影響疏浚泥沙有益利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective stress in placed sediment” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beneficial reuse of dredged sediment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"新放置細泥的自重部分由孔隙水承受，有效應力才與土骨架壓縮及強度形成相關。總應力增加不等於立即取得同樣骨架荷載，排水時間和地層連通性需要量測；一個有效應力數值也不能直接代替剪力強度或允許設備通行荷重。 假設某點總垂直應力50kPa、孔隙壓35kPa，有效應力σ′=σ−u=15kPa；若總應力不變而u降10kPa，σ′升至25kPa。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「填料有效應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pore water supports part of freshly placed sediment weight; effective stress governs skeleton loading, compression and strength development. Increased total stress does not immediately become equal skeleton load, and drainage timing and connectivity need observation. One effective-stress result cannot replace a shear-strength evaluation or establish allowable equipment loading on a soft placement surface in the field. Assume total vertical stress50kPa and pore pressure35kPa:σ′=15kPa. At fixed total stress, a10kPa pressure fall raisesσ′ to25kPa. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective stress in placed sediment” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「表面變乾就代表全部填料已完全排水並取得最終強度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A dry surface proves that the entire fill has drained and reached final strength.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「填料有效應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective stress in placed sediment”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-29-k1","title":"填料有效應力","titleEn":"Effective stress in placed sediment","text":"新放置細泥的自重部分由孔隙水承受，有效應力才與土骨架壓縮及強度形成相關。總應力增加不等於立即取得同樣骨架荷載，排水時間和地層連通性需要量測；一個有效應力數值也不能直接代替剪力強度或允許設備通行荷重。","textEn":"Pore water supports part of freshly placed sediment weight; effective stress governs skeleton loading, compression and strength development. Increased total stress does not immediately become equal skeleton load, and drainage timing and connectivity need observation.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：表面變乾就代表全部填料已完全排水並取得最終強度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A dry surface proves that the entire fill has drained and reached final strength. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「填料有效應力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Effective stress in placed sediment\" is correct?","options":["表面變乾就代表全部填料已完全排水並取得最終強度。","運距縮短的排放差額就是再利用方案完整的生命週期淨減碳。","新放置細泥的自重部分由孔隙水承受，有效應力才與土骨架壓縮及強度形成相關。"],"optionsEn":["A dry surface proves that the entire fill has drained and reached final strength.","The emissions saved by shorter transport equal the reuse project's complete life-cycle benefit.","Pore water supports part of freshly placed sediment weight; effective stress governs skeleton loading, compression and strength development."],"answer":2,"explanation":"新放置細泥的自重部分由孔隙水承受，有效應力才與土骨架壓縮及強度形成相關。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pore water supports part of freshly placed sediment weight; effective stress governs skeleton loading, compression and strength development. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b288-v15-30","title":"填料有效應力：定量估算","titleEn":"Effective stress in placed sediment: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「填料有效應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective stress in placed sediment” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設某點總垂直應力50kPa、孔隙壓35kPa，有效應力σ′=σ−u=15kPa；若總應力不變而u降10kPa，σ′升至25kPa。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume total vertical stress50kPa and pore pressure35kPa:σ′=15kPa. At fixed total stress, a10kPa pressure fall raisesσ′ to25kPa. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在同一高程與時刻比較孔壓和總荷載，檢查加載、潮位與排水的共同影響。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare pore pressure and total loading at matching elevations and times, checking loading, tide and drainage together.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設某點總垂直應力50kPa、孔隙壓35kPa，有效應力σ′=σ−u=15kPa；若總應力不變而u降10kPa，σ′升至25kPa。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume total vertical stress50kPa and pore pressure35kPa:σ′=15kPa. At fixed total stress, a10kPa pressure fall raisesσ′ to25kPa.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「填料有效應力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Effective stress in placed sediment\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","疏浚材料只要有預定去向就全部算成已驗證成功再利用。","放置材料乾固體沒有流失就代表地表高程不會再下降。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Every dredged batch with a planned destination already counts as verified successful reuse.","If placed dry solids are retained, surface elevation cannot subsequently decrease."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b288-v15-31","title":"填料有效應力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Effective stress in placed sediment: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「填料有效應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective stress in placed sediment” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在同一高程與時刻比較孔壓和總荷載，檢查加載、潮位與排水的共同影響。以獨立土樣或現地試驗追蹤強度演進，明列有效應力與承載判斷之間仍缺的材料關係。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare pore pressure and total loading at matching elevations and times, checking loading, tide and drainage together. Track strength with independent samples or field tests and state the constitutive relationships still needed between effective stress and a bearing assessment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在同一高程與時刻比較孔壓和總荷載，檢查加載、潮位與排水的共同影響。以獨立土樣或現地試驗追蹤強度演進，明列有效應力與承載判斷之間仍缺的材料關係。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare pore pressure and total loading at matching elevations and times, checking loading, tide and drainage together. Track strength with independent samples or field tests and state the constitutive relationships still needed between effective stress and a bearing assessment.","failure":"注意干擾：孔壓計零點漂移可能假造排水進展，忽略新增填土則錯判有效應力變化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Piezometer drift can mimic drainage, while omitted new fill misstates effective-stress change. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在同一高程與時刻比較孔壓和總荷載，檢查加載、潮位與排水的共同影響。以獨立土樣或現地試驗追蹤強度演進，明列有效應力與承載判斷之間仍缺的材料關係。","textEn":"Compare pore pressure and total loading at matching elevations and times, checking loading, tide and drainage together. Track strength with independent samples or field tests and state the constitutive relationships still needed between effective stress and a bearing assessment.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在同一高程與時刻比較孔壓和總荷載，檢查加載、潮位與排水的共同影響。以獨立土樣或現地試驗追蹤強度演進，明列有效應力與承載判斷之間仍缺的材料關係。","textEn":"Compare pore pressure and total loading at matching elevations and times, checking loading, tide and drainage together. Track strength with independent samples or field tests and state the constitutive relationships still needed between effective stress and a bearing assessment.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「填料有效應力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Effective stress in placed sediment\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在同一高程與時刻比較孔壓和總荷載，檢查加載、潮位與排水的共同影響。","產品純度與原料回收率永遠具有相同分母而且相等。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare pore pressure and total loading at matching elevations and times, checking loading, tide and drainage together.","Product purity and feed recovery always share the same denominator and value."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在同一高程與時刻比較孔壓和總荷載，檢查加載、潮位與排水的共同影響。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare pore pressure and total loading at matching elevations and times, checking loading, tide and drainage together. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b288-v15-32","title":"填料有效應力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Effective stress in placed sediment: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「填料有效應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective stress in placed sediment” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"孔壓計零點漂移可能假造排水進展，忽略新增填土則錯判有效應力變化。表面看似乾燥而深部仍高孔壓時，設備荷載可能造成局部變形或側向擠出。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Piezometer drift can mimic drainage, while omitted new fill misstates effective-stress change. A dry-looking surface over persistently high deep pore pressures can still deform locally or squeeze laterally under equipment loading. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設某點總垂直應力50kPa、孔隙壓35kPa，有效應力σ′=σ−u=15kPa；若總應力不變而u降10kPa，σ′升至25kPa。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: At fixed total stress, a10kPa pressure fall raisesσ′ to25kPa.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「表面變乾就代表全部填料已完全排水並取得最終強度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A dry surface proves that the entire fill has drained and reached final strength.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"孔壓計零點漂移可能假造排水進展，忽略新增填土則錯判有效應力變化。表面看似乾燥而深部仍高孔壓時，設備荷載可能造成局部變形或側向擠出。","textEn":"Piezometer drift can mimic drainage, while omitted new fill misstates effective-stress change. A dry-looking surface over persistently high deep pore pressures can still deform locally or squeeze laterally under equipment loading.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「填料有效應力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Effective stress in placed sediment\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","運距縮短的排放差額就是再利用方案完整的生命週期淨減碳。","孔壓計零點漂移可能假造排水進展，忽略新增填土則錯判有效應力變化。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The emissions saved by shorter transport equal the reuse project's complete life-cycle benefit.","Piezometer drift can mimic drainage, while omitted new fill misstates effective-stress change."],"answer":2,"explanation":"孔壓計零點漂移可能假造排水進展，忽略新增填土則錯判有效應力變化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Piezometer drift can mimic drainage, while omitted new fill misstates effective-stress change. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b288-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「運輸碳量比較」與「對照監測與歸因」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Transport emissions comparison\" and \"Control monitoring and attribution\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b288-v15-33","title":"運輸碳量比較：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Transport emissions comparison: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「運輸碳量比較」如何影響疏浚泥沙有益利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Transport emissions comparison” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beneficial reuse of dredged sediment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"有益利用可改變材料運距與新料需求，但環境比較必須採相同功能和系統邊界。運輸噸公里只是部分排放，處理、泵送、空車回程及未避免的新料也可能重要；合成係數只練習計量，不能把局部節省包裝成完整生命週期淨收益。 假設10000t材料運距由50降至20km、係數0.08kgCO₂e/(t·km)，運輸差額10000×30×0.08=24000kgCO₂e。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「運輸碳量比較」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Reuse changes transport distance and demand for virgin material, but environmental comparisons require equivalent function and system boundaries. Tonne-kilometres describe only part of emissions; treatment, pumping, empty return trips and any unavoided supply also matter. A synthetic factor illustrates accounting rather than establishing complete life-cycle savings from a limited change in transport distance alone. Assume10000t moves20km instead of50km at0.08kgCO₂e/(t·km). Transport difference is24000kgCO₂e, excluding treatment and return-trip changes. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Transport emissions comparison” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「運距縮短的排放差額就是再利用方案完整的生命週期淨減碳。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The emissions saved by shorter transport equal the reuse project's complete life-cycle benefit.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「運輸碳量比較」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Transport emissions comparison”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-33-k1","title":"運輸碳量比較","titleEn":"Transport emissions comparison","text":"有益利用可改變材料運距與新料需求，但環境比較必須採相同功能和系統邊界。運輸噸公里只是部分排放，處理、泵送、空車回程及未避免的新料也可能重要；合成係數只練習計量，不能把局部節省包裝成完整生命週期淨收益。","textEn":"Reuse changes transport distance and demand for virgin material, but environmental comparisons require equivalent function and system boundaries. Tonne-kilometres describe only part of emissions; treatment, pumping, empty return trips and any unavoided supply also matter.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：運距縮短的排放差額就是再利用方案完整的生命週期淨減碳。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The emissions saved by shorter transport equal the reuse project's complete life-cycle benefit. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「運輸碳量比較」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Transport emissions comparison\" is correct?","options":["有益利用可改變材料運距與新料需求，但環境比較必須採相同功能和系統邊界。","運距縮短的排放差額就是再利用方案完整的生命週期淨減碳。","處理區施工後植被增加就足以證明增長完全由工程造成。"],"optionsEn":["Reuse changes transport distance and demand for virgin material, but environmental comparisons require equivalent function and system boundaries.","The emissions saved by shorter transport equal the reuse project's complete life-cycle benefit.","Any vegetation increase after treatment proves that the project caused the entire increase."],"answer":0,"explanation":"有益利用可改變材料運距與新料需求，但環境比較必須採相同功能和系統邊界。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Reuse changes transport distance and demand for virgin material, but environmental comparisons require equivalent function and system boundaries. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b288-v15-34","title":"運輸碳量比較：定量估算","titleEn":"Transport emissions comparison: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「運輸碳量比較」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Transport emissions comparison” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設10000t材料運距由50降至20km、係數0.08kgCO₂e/(t·km)，運輸差額10000×30×0.08=24000kgCO₂e。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume10000t moves20km instead of50km at0.08kgCO₂e/(t·km). Transport difference is24000kgCO₂e, excluding treatment and return-trip changes. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：明列兩方案是否提供同樣材料功能與時間需求，記錄噸位、路程和排放係數來源。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: State whether alternatives deliver equivalent function and timing and document mass, distance and emission-factor provenance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設10000t材料運距由50降至20km、係數0.08kgCO₂e/(t·km)，運輸差額10000×30×0.08=24000kgCO₂e。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume10000t moves20km instead of50km at0.08kgCO₂e/(t·km). Transport difference is24000kgCO₂e, excluding treatment and return-trip changes.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「運輸碳量比較」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Transport emissions comparison\", which statement holds?","options":["平均放置厚度達標就能證明每個位置的淹水條件都合適。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","潮位超過地面的時間比例直接等於植被的存活機率。"],"optionsEn":["A satisfactory mean placement thickness proves suitable inundation at every location.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The fraction of time tide exceeds ground directly equals plant survival probability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b288-v15-35","title":"運輸碳量比較：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Transport emissions comparison: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「運輸碳量比較」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Transport emissions comparison” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"明列兩方案是否提供同樣材料功能與時間需求，記錄噸位、路程和排放係數來源。將處理、能耗和回程另列，對主要係數作敏感度比較，保留沒有證據可抵扣的項目。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"State whether alternatives deliver equivalent function and timing and document mass, distance and emission-factor provenance. List treatment, energy and return trips separately, test important factors for sensitivity, and retain items without evidence for any claimed avoided burden. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：明列兩方案是否提供同樣材料功能與時間需求，記錄噸位、路程和排放係數來源。將處理、能耗和回程另列，對主要係數作敏感度比較，保留沒有證據可抵扣的項目。","observationEn":"Site practice: State whether alternatives deliver equivalent function and timing and document mass, distance and emission-factor provenance. List treatment, energy and return trips separately, test important factors for sensitivity, and retain items without evidence for any claimed avoided burden.","failure":"注意干擾：若再利用料需要額外長時間脫水，運輸減碳可能被處理能耗抵銷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Extended dewatering may offset transport savings through treatment energy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"明列兩方案是否提供同樣材料功能與時間需求，記錄噸位、路程和排放係數來源。將處理、能耗和回程另列，對主要係數作敏感度比較，保留沒有證據可抵扣的項目。","textEn":"State whether alternatives deliver equivalent function and timing and document mass, distance and emission-factor provenance. List treatment, energy and return trips separately, test important factors for sensitivity, and retain items without evidence for any claimed avoided burden.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"明列兩方案是否提供同樣材料功能與時間需求，記錄噸位、路程和排放係數來源。將處理、能耗和回程另列，對主要係數作敏感度比較，保留沒有證據可抵扣的項目。","textEn":"State whether alternatives deliver equivalent function and timing and document mass, distance and emission-factor provenance. List treatment, energy and return trips separately, test important factors for sensitivity, and retain items without evidence for any claimed avoided burden.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「運輸碳量比較」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Transport emissions comparison\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","混合後平均濃度降低代表同百分比的污染物已被消除。","明列兩方案是否提供同樣材料功能與時間需求，記錄噸位、路程和排放係數來源。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A lower average concentration after mixing means the same fraction of contaminant was destroyed.","State whether alternatives deliver equivalent function and timing and document mass, distance and emission-factor provenance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"明列兩方案是否提供同樣材料功能與時間需求，記錄噸位、路程和排放係數來源。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"State whether alternatives deliver equivalent function and timing and document mass, distance and emission-factor provenance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b288-v15-36","title":"運輸碳量比較：失效診斷","titleEn":"Transport emissions comparison: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「運輸碳量比較」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Transport emissions comparison” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若再利用料需要額外長時間脫水，運輸減碳可能被處理能耗抵銷。把並未真正減少的新料生產扣除，或忽略空船回程，都會放大報表上的環境好處。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Extended dewatering may offset transport savings through treatment energy. Crediting virgin production that was not actually avoided, or ignoring an empty return voyage, further inflates the environmental benefit claimed for the reuse alternative. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設10000t材料運距由50降至20km、係數0.08kgCO₂e/(t·km)，運輸差額10000×30×0.08=24000kgCO₂e。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Transport difference is24000kgCO₂e, excluding treatment and return-trip changes.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「運距縮短的排放差額就是再利用方案完整的生命週期淨減碳。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The emissions saved by shorter transport equal the reuse project's complete life-cycle benefit.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若再利用料需要額外長時間脫水，運輸減碳可能被處理能耗抵銷。把並未真正減少的新料生產扣除，或忽略空船回程，都會放大報表上的環境好處。","textEn":"Extended dewatering may offset transport savings through treatment energy. Crediting virgin production that was not actually avoided, or ignoring an empty return voyage, further inflates the environmental benefit claimed for the reuse alternative.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「運輸碳量比較」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Transport emissions comparison\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若再利用料需要額外長時間脫水，運輸減碳可能被處理能耗抵銷。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","處理區施工後植被增加就足以證明增長完全由工程造成。"],"optionsEn":["Extended dewatering may offset transport savings through treatment energy.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Any vegetation increase after treatment proves that the project caused the entire increase."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若再利用料需要額外長時間脫水，運輸減碳可能被處理能耗抵銷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Extended dewatering may offset transport savings through treatment energy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b288-v15-37","title":"對照監測與歸因：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control monitoring and attribution: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「對照監測與歸因」如何影響疏浚泥沙有益利用的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Control monitoring and attribution” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Beneficial reuse of dredged sediment”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"放置後植被或生物數量改變可能同時受季節、氣候與其他工程影響，單一前後差不能直接歸因。處理區與參照區的變化差提供較好的辨識起點，但仍依賴可比性和共同趨勢；多期及重複樣區可檢查這些假設，而不是以漂亮百分比宣布復育成功。 假設處理區植被覆蓋30%升50%、參照區40%升50%，差中差=(50−30)−(50−40)=10百分點；不是因果已證實。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「對照監測與歸因」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Post-placement ecological change can reflect season, climate or other works, so a simple before-after difference does not establish causation. Comparing changes in treatment and reference areas provides a stronger starting point but still requires comparability and parallel trends. Repeated periods and plots test those assumptions rather than allowing an attractive percentage to establish restoration success by itself. Assume treatment cover rises30%to50% and reference40%to50%. Difference-in-differences is10percentage points, not established causation without supporting assumptions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Control monitoring and attribution” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「處理區施工後植被增加就足以證明增長完全由工程造成。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any vegetation increase after treatment proves that the project caused the entire increase.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「對照監測與歸因」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Control monitoring and attribution”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-37-k1","title":"對照監測與歸因","titleEn":"Control monitoring and attribution","text":"放置後植被或生物數量改變可能同時受季節、氣候與其他工程影響，單一前後差不能直接歸因。處理區與參照區的變化差提供較好的辨識起點，但仍依賴可比性和共同趨勢；多期及重複樣區可檢查這些假設，而不是以漂亮百分比宣布復育成功。","textEn":"Post-placement ecological change can reflect season, climate or other works, so a simple before-after difference does not establish causation. Comparing changes in treatment and reference areas provides a stronger starting point but still requires comparability and parallel trends.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：處理區施工後植被增加就足以證明增長完全由工程造成。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any vegetation increase after treatment proves that the project caused the entire increase. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「對照監測與歸因」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control monitoring and attribution\" is correct?","options":["處理區施工後植被增加就足以證明增長完全由工程造成。","放置後植被或生物數量改變可能同時受季節、氣候與其他工程影響，單一前後差不能直接歸因。","疏浚材料只要有預定去向就全部算成已驗證成功再利用。"],"optionsEn":["Any vegetation increase after treatment proves that the project caused the entire increase.","Post-placement ecological change can reflect season, climate or other works, so a simple before-after difference does not establish causation.","Every dredged batch with a planned destination already counts as verified successful reuse."],"answer":1,"explanation":"放置後植被或生物數量改變可能同時受季節、氣候與其他工程影響，單一前後差不能直接歸因。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Post-placement ecological change can reflect season, climate or other works, so a simple before-after difference does not establish causation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b288-v15-38","title":"對照監測與歸因：定量估算","titleEn":"Control monitoring and attribution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「對照監測與歸因」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Control monitoring and attribution” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設處理區植被覆蓋30%升50%、參照區40%升50%，差中差=(50−30)−(50−40)=10百分點；不是因果已證實。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume treatment cover rises30%to50% and reference40%to50%. Difference-in-differences is10percentage points, not established causation without supporting assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保留相同季節與方法的重複樣區，檢查施工前處理與參照區是否有近似趨勢。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Maintain repeated plots surveyed with the same seasonal method and examine pre-treatment trends in both areas.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設處理區植被覆蓋30%升50%、參照區40%升50%，差中差=(50−30)−(50−40)=10百分點；不是因果已證實。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume treatment cover rises30%to50% and reference40%to50%. Difference-in-differences is10percentage points, not established causation without supporting assumptions.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「對照監測與歸因」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control monitoring and attribution\", which statement holds?","options":["放置材料乾固體沒有流失就代表地表高程不會再下降。","產品純度與原料回收率永遠具有相同分母而且相等。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["If placed dry solids are retained, surface elevation cannot subsequently decrease.","Product purity and feed recovery always share the same denominator and value.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b288-v15-39","title":"對照監測與歸因：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control monitoring and attribution: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「對照監測與歸因」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Control monitoring and attribution” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保留相同季節與方法的重複樣區，檢查施工前處理與參照區是否有近似趨勢。分開報告百分點、相對增幅及不確定度，追蹤物種組成與高程，避免只選有利單一指標。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Maintain repeated plots surveyed with the same seasonal method and examine pre-treatment trends in both areas. Report percentage points, relative changes and uncertainty separately, tracking composition and elevation rather than selecting only a favorable single indicator. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保留相同季節與方法的重複樣區，檢查施工前處理與參照區是否有近似趨勢。分開報告百分點、相對增幅及不確定度，追蹤物種組成與高程，避免只選有利單一指標。","observationEn":"Site practice: Maintain repeated plots surveyed with the same seasonal method and examine pre-treatment trends in both areas. Report percentage points, relative changes and uncertainty separately, tracking composition and elevation rather than selecting only a favorable single indicator.","failure":"注意干擾：參照區若同時受到放置濁羽影響便不是獨立比較，前後季節不同也會造成假改善。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A reference affected by the placement plume is not an independent comparison, and different survey seasons create apparent improvement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保留相同季節與方法的重複樣區，檢查施工前處理與參照區是否有近似趨勢。分開報告百分點、相對增幅及不確定度，追蹤物種組成與高程，避免只選有利單一指標。","textEn":"Maintain repeated plots surveyed with the same seasonal method and examine pre-treatment trends in both areas. Report percentage points, relative changes and uncertainty separately, tracking composition and elevation rather than selecting only a favorable single indicator.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保留相同季節與方法的重複樣區，檢查施工前處理與參照區是否有近似趨勢。分開報告百分點、相對增幅及不確定度，追蹤物種組成與高程，避免只選有利單一指標。","textEn":"Maintain repeated plots surveyed with the same seasonal method and examine pre-treatment trends in both areas. Report percentage points, relative changes and uncertainty separately, tracking composition and elevation rather than selecting only a favorable single indicator.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「對照監測與歸因」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control monitoring and attribution\"?","options":["保留相同季節與方法的重複樣區，檢查施工前處理與參照區是否有近似趨勢。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","覆蓋材料總方量足夠就能證明各處隔離厚度與化學功能足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Maintain repeated plots surveyed with the same seasonal method and examine pre-treatment trends in both areas.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Enough total cover volume proves adequate thickness and chemical isolation everywhere."],"answer":0,"explanation":"保留相同季節與方法的重複樣區，檢查施工前處理與參照區是否有近似趨勢。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Maintain repeated plots surveyed with the same seasonal method and examine pre-treatment trends in both areas. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b288-v15-40","title":"對照監測與歸因：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control monitoring and attribution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"prerequisiteIds":["b288-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「對照監測與歸因」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Control monitoring and attribution” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"參照區若同時受到放置濁羽影響便不是獨立比較，前後季節不同也會造成假改善。總覆蓋增加可能來自非目標物種，不能自動解釋為恢復預期棲地。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A reference affected by the placement plume is not an independent comparison, and different survey seasons create apparent improvement. Greater total cover may arise from nontarget species rather than recovery of the intended habitat function. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設處理區植被覆蓋30%升50%、參照區40%升50%，差中差=(50−30)−(50−40)=10百分點；不是因果已證實。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Difference-in-differences is10percentage points, not established causation without supporting assumptions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「處理區施工後植被增加就足以證明增長完全由工程造成。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any vegetation increase after treatment proves that the project caused the entire increase.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b288-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"參照區若同時受到放置濁羽影響便不是獨立比較，前後季節不同也會造成假改善。總覆蓋增加可能來自非目標物種，不能自動解釋為恢復預期棲地。","textEn":"A reference affected by the placement plume is not an independent comparison, and different survey seasons create apparent improvement. Greater total cover may arise from nontarget species rather than recovery of the intended habitat function.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]},{"id":"b288-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「對照監測與歸因」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control monitoring and attribution\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","參照區若同時受到放置濁羽影響便不是獨立比較，前後季節不同也會造成假改善。","疏浚材料只要有預定去向就全部算成已驗證成功再利用。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A reference affected by the placement plume is not an independent comparison, and different survey seasons create apparent improvement.","Every dredged batch with a planned destination already counts as verified successful reuse."],"answer":1,"explanation":"參照區若同時受到放置濁羽影響便不是獨立比較，前後季節不同也會造成假改善。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A reference affected by the placement plume is not an independent comparison, and different survey seasons create apparent improvement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-itm","v15s-dredge","v15s-poplar","v15s-mordecai"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b289","title":"大型港口沉箱碼頭","titleEn":"Large-port caisson quay walls","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"將回填土水壓船舶作用與地基變形連成沉箱碼頭受力路徑。課程從邊界辨識與資料整理走到水理量化、構造介面及驗證紀錄；每一步把計算結果連回可量測的證據。十個不同單元分別處理關鍵機制，不以名義尺寸或單一通過率代替整體工程判斷，並明列合成算例與現地資料的差別。","summaryEn":"Trace caisson-quay load paths through backfill, water, vessels and foundation deformation. The course moves from boundary identification and evidence to hydraulic quantification, structural interfaces and verification records. Ten distinct units connect each calculated quantity to measurable evidence. Nominal geometry or a single pass rate does not establish whole-system performance, and synthetic teaching examples remain separate from field observations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-coasts","subcategoryTitle":"海岸、港灣與水資源韌性","subcategoryTitleEn":"Coasts, ports and water-resource resilience","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-coasts","learningTags":["water","water-coasts","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-port","architectureNodes":[["主動土壓假設","Active earth-pressure assumptions"],["碼頭堆載側壓","Quay surcharge lateral action"],["基底偏心壓力","Eccentric base pressure"],["護舷曲線積分","Integrating fender response"],["接縫位移與止水","Joint movement and sealing"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-port","labels":["主動土壓假設","碼頭堆載側壓","基底偏心壓力","護舷曲線積分","接縫位移與止水"],"labelsEn":["Active earth-pressure assumptions","Quay surcharge lateral action","Eccentric base pressure","Integrating fender response","Joint movement and sealing"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為原創合成算例，不是地標工程的實測或推薦操作值。教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水平無黏性回填、光滑直立牆且已達主動狀態，φ=30°，Ka=tan²(45°−φ/2)=0.3333；不適用靜止狀態。假設摩擦角由30增10%至33°，其他朗肯條件不變，Ka由0.3333降為0.2948，約減11.56%；不能推論整座碼頭風險同比下降。重新計算前先列固定條件、單位、適用尺度及可能失效的邊界。把模型敏感度與測量誤差分開，不能將單一參數變化直接當成工程風險或壽命比例。比較兩次結果後，記錄還需要哪些獨立證據，並由負責專業人員判斷適用性。","textEn":"This original synthetic example is neither a landmark measurement nor a recommended operating value. Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume level cohesionless fill, a smooth vertical wall and mobilized active conditions. Atφ=30°,Ka=tan²(45°−φ/2)=0.3333, not at-rest pressure. Increasing friction angle10% from30°to33° under unchanged Rankine assumptions reduces Ka from0.3333 to0.2948, approximately11.56%, without an equivalent reduction in whole-quay risk. Before recalculating, list fixed conditions, units, applicable scale and boundaries that could fail. Separate model sensitivity from measurement uncertainty: a parameter change does not directly give a proportional change in engineering risk or service life. Compare the results, record independent evidence still needed, and have the responsible specialist determine applicability.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b289-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「主動土壓假設」與「有效土壓積分」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Active earth-pressure assumptions\" and \"Effective earth-pressure integration\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b289-v15-01","title":"主動土壓假設：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Active earth-pressure assumptions: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「主動土壓假設」如何影響大型港口沉箱碼頭的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Active earth-pressure assumptions” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large-port caisson quay walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"碼頭背填土會把側向作用傳入沉箱，但是否達到主動狀態取決於牆體位移及土體條件。簡單朗肯係數假設水平無黏性回填與光滑直立牆，與靜止土壓不同；港區受限位移、分層或密實施工時，不能僅憑摩擦角選一個較小係數。 假設水平無黏性回填、光滑直立牆且已達主動狀態，φ=30°，Ka=tan²(45°−φ/2)=0.3333；不適用靜止狀態。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「主動土壓假設」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Backfill transfers lateral action into a caisson, but mobilizing an active state requires compatible wall movement and soil conditions. The simple Rankine coefficient assumes level cohesionless backfill and a smooth vertical wall, distinct from at-rest pressure. Restricted deformation, layering or compaction means friction angle alone cannot justify selecting the smaller coefficient for every quay-wall condition. Assume level cohesionless fill, a smooth vertical wall and mobilized active conditions. Atφ=30°,Ka=tan²(45°−φ/2)=0.3333, not at-rest pressure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Active earth-pressure assumptions” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有碼頭背填土都不需牆體變形就會自動達到主動土壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every quay backfill automatically reaches active pressure without any wall movement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「主動土壓假設」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Active earth-pressure assumptions”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-01-k1","title":"主動土壓假設","titleEn":"Active earth-pressure assumptions","text":"碼頭背填土會把側向作用傳入沉箱，但是否達到主動狀態取決於牆體位移及土體條件。簡單朗肯係數假設水平無黏性回填與光滑直立牆，與靜止土壓不同；港區受限位移、分層或密實施工時，不能僅憑摩擦角選一個較小係數。","textEn":"Backfill transfers lateral action into a caisson, but mobilizing an active state requires compatible wall movement and soil conditions. The simple Rankine coefficient assumes level cohesionless backfill and a smooth vertical wall, distinct from at-rest pressure.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有碼頭背填土都不需牆體變形就會自動達到主動土壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every quay backfill automatically reaches active pressure without any wall movement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「主動土壓假設」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Active earth-pressure assumptions\" is correct?","options":["所有碼頭背填土都不需牆體變形就會自動達到主動土壓。","碼頭背填土會把側向作用傳入沉箱，但是否達到主動狀態取決於牆體位移及土體條件。","使用浮重度算出的有效土壓已經包含全部靜水壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Every quay backfill automatically reaches active pressure without any wall movement.","Backfill transfers lateral action into a caisson, but mobilizing an active state requires compatible wall movement and soil conditions.","Effective earth pressure calculated with submerged unit weight already includes all hydrostatic pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"碼頭背填土會把側向作用傳入沉箱，但是否達到主動狀態取決於牆體位移及土體條件。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Backfill transfers lateral action into a caisson, but mobilizing an active state requires compatible wall movement and soil conditions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b289-v15-02","title":"主動土壓假設：定量估算","titleEn":"Active earth-pressure assumptions: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「主動土壓假設」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Active earth-pressure assumptions” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水平無黏性回填、光滑直立牆且已達主動狀態，φ=30°，Ka=tan²(45°−φ/2)=0.3333；不適用靜止狀態。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume level cohesionless fill, a smooth vertical wall and mobilized active conditions. Atφ=30°,Ka=tan²(45°−φ/2)=0.3333, not at-rest pressure. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：畫出背填坡面、牆背摩擦與可能位移方向，核對使用主動狀態是否有足夠變形依據。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw backfill geometry, wall interface and possible movement, checking evidence for mobilizing the active state.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水平無黏性回填、光滑直立牆且已達主動狀態，φ=30°，Ka=tan²(45°−φ/2)=0.3333；不適用靜止狀態。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume level cohesionless fill, a smooth vertical wall and mobilized active conditions. Atφ=30°,Ka=tan²(45°−φ/2)=0.3333, not at-rest pressure.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「主動土壓假設」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Active earth-pressure assumptions\", which statement holds?","options":["回填內水位總是與外海潮位同步所以不必量測孔壓。","靠泊能量增加一倍就表示護舷峰值反力一定增加一倍。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Backfill water always follows the harbor tide exactly, making pore-pressure measurements unnecessary.","Doubling berthing energy necessarily doubles the fender's peak reaction force.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b289-v15-03","title":"主動土壓假設：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Active earth-pressure assumptions: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「主動土壓假設」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Active earth-pressure assumptions” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"畫出背填坡面、牆背摩擦與可能位移方向，核對使用主動狀態是否有足夠變形依據。分開檢查施工壓密與服務期約束，用土樣與位移紀錄確認參數，不以單一公式取代狀態辨識。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw backfill geometry, wall interface and possible movement, checking evidence for mobilizing the active state. Review compaction and service constraints separately and use soil and displacement records to justify parameters rather than substituting one formula for identification of the stress state. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出背填坡面、牆背摩擦與可能位移方向，核對使用主動狀態是否有足夠變形依據。分開檢查施工壓密與服務期約束，用土樣與位移紀錄確認參數，不以單一公式取代狀態辨識。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw backfill geometry, wall interface and possible movement, checking evidence for mobilizing the active state. Review compaction and service constraints separately and use soil and displacement records to justify parameters rather than substituting one formula for identification of the stress state.","failure":"注意干擾：剛性受限牆體未達主動位移卻採主動係數會低估側壓，黏性回填或坡面改變也使假設失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using active pressure for a restrained wall understates lateral action, and cohesive fill or altered slopes violate the assumptions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"畫出背填坡面、牆背摩擦與可能位移方向，核對使用主動狀態是否有足夠變形依據。分開檢查施工壓密與服務期約束，用土樣與位移紀錄確認參數，不以單一公式取代狀態辨識。","textEn":"Draw backfill geometry, wall interface and possible movement, checking evidence for mobilizing the active state. Review compaction and service constraints separately and use soil and displacement records to justify parameters rather than substituting one formula for identification of the stress state.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出背填坡面、牆背摩擦與可能位移方向，核對使用主動狀態是否有足夠變形依據。分開檢查施工壓密與服務期約束，用土樣與位移紀錄確認參數，不以單一公式取代狀態辨識。","textEn":"Draw backfill geometry, wall interface and possible movement, checking evidence for mobilizing the active state. Review compaction and service constraints separately and use soil and displacement records to justify parameters rather than substituting one formula for identification of the stress state.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「主動土壓假設」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Active earth-pressure assumptions\"?","options":["畫出背填坡面、牆背摩擦與可能位移方向，核對使用主動狀態是否有足夠變形依據。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","加重沉箱只增加抵抗力而不會增加任何地震慣性需求。"],"optionsEn":["Draw backfill geometry, wall interface and possible movement, checking evidence for mobilizing the active state.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Increasing caisson mass raises resistance without increasing any seismic inertia demand."],"answer":0,"explanation":"畫出背填坡面、牆背摩擦與可能位移方向，核對使用主動狀態是否有足夠變形依據。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw backfill geometry, wall interface and possible movement, checking evidence for mobilizing the active state. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b289-v15-04","title":"主動土壓假設：失效診斷","titleEn":"Active earth-pressure assumptions: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「主動土壓假設」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Active earth-pressure assumptions” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"剛性受限牆體未達主動位移卻採主動係數會低估側壓，黏性回填或坡面改變也使假設失效。施工時壓密設備可能留下高於單純自重理論的壓力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using active pressure for a restrained wall understates lateral action, and cohesive fill or altered slopes violate the assumptions. Compaction equipment may also leave pressures greater than predicted by a simple self-weight active model. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設水平無黏性回填、光滑直立牆且已達主動狀態，φ=30°，Ka=tan²(45°−φ/2)=0.3333；不適用靜止狀態。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Atφ=30°,Ka=tan²(45°−φ/2)=0.3333, not at-rest pressure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有碼頭背填土都不需牆體變形就會自動達到主動土壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every quay backfill automatically reaches active pressure without any wall movement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"剛性受限牆體未達主動位移卻採主動係數會低估側壓，黏性回填或坡面改變也使假設失效。施工時壓密設備可能留下高於單純自重理論的壓力。","textEn":"Using active pressure for a restrained wall understates lateral action, and cohesive fill or altered slopes violate the assumptions. Compaction equipment may also leave pressures greater than predicted by a simple self-weight active model.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「主動土壓假設」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Active earth-pressure assumptions\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","剛性受限牆體未達主動位移卻採主動係數會低估側壓，黏性回填或坡面改變也使假設失效。","使用浮重度算出的有效土壓已經包含全部靜水壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using active pressure for a restrained wall understates lateral action, and cohesive fill or altered slopes violate the assumptions.","Effective earth pressure calculated with submerged unit weight already includes all hydrostatic pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"剛性受限牆體未達主動位移卻採主動係數會低估側壓，黏性回填或坡面改變也使假設失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using active pressure for a restrained wall understates lateral action, and cohesive fill or altered slopes violate the assumptions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b289-v15-05","title":"有效土壓積分：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Effective earth-pressure integration: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「有效土壓積分」如何影響大型港口沉箱碼頭的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective earth-pressure integration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large-port caisson quay walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水下回填的土骨架壓力與孔隙水壓必須分開，使用浮重度積分的是有效土壓而不是總側壓。深度線性分布只涵蓋均質填料自重，分層和地面堆載另列；將孔壓漏掉或重複計入都會破壞沉箱整體平衡與作用點判讀。 假設Ka=1/3、浮重度10kN/m³、高H=15m，Pa=Kaγ′H²/2=375kN/m，作用在底上5m；水壓另算。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「有效土壓積分」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Effective skeleton pressure in submerged fill must be separated from pore pressure. Integration with submerged unit weight gives effective soil action, not total lateral action. A linear distribution covers homogeneous self-weight only; layers and surcharges require separate terms. Omitting or double-counting water pressure corrupts both caisson equilibrium and interpretation of the resultant location along the wall. Assume Ka=1/3,submerged unit weight10kN/m³ and H=15m. Pa=375kN/m acts5m above base; pore-water pressure is separate. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective earth-pressure integration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「使用浮重度算出的有效土壓已經包含全部靜水壓力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Effective earth pressure calculated with submerged unit weight already includes all hydrostatic pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「有效土壓積分」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective earth-pressure integration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-05-k1","title":"有效土壓積分","titleEn":"Effective earth-pressure integration","text":"水下回填的土骨架壓力與孔隙水壓必須分開，使用浮重度積分的是有效土壓而不是總側壓。深度線性分布只涵蓋均質填料自重，分層和地面堆載另列；將孔壓漏掉或重複計入都會破壞沉箱整體平衡與作用點判讀。","textEn":"Effective skeleton pressure in submerged fill must be separated from pore pressure. Integration with submerged unit weight gives effective soil action, not total lateral action.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：使用浮重度算出的有效土壓已經包含全部靜水壓力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Effective earth pressure calculated with submerged unit weight already includes all hydrostatic pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「有效土壓積分」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Effective earth-pressure integration\" is correct?","options":["使用浮重度算出的有效土壓已經包含全部靜水壓力。","全場平均堆載可以直接代表貼近岸壁的所有局部輪壓。","水下回填的土骨架壓力與孔隙水壓必須分開，使用浮重度積分的是有效土壓而不是總側壓。"],"optionsEn":["Effective earth pressure calculated with submerged unit weight already includes all hydrostatic pressure.","The terminal-average surcharge directly represents every concentrated wheel load near the quay edge.","Effective skeleton pressure in submerged fill must be separated from pore pressure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水下回填的土骨架壓力與孔隙水壓必須分開，使用浮重度積分的是有效土壓而不是總側壓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Effective skeleton pressure in submerged fill must be separated from pore pressure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b289-v15-06","title":"有效土壓積分：定量估算","titleEn":"Effective earth-pressure integration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「有效土壓積分」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective earth-pressure integration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設Ka=1/3、浮重度10kN/m³、高H=15m，Pa=Kaγ′H²/2=375kN/m，作用在底上5m；水壓另算。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume Ka=1/3,submerged unit weight10kN/m³ and H=15m. Pa=375kN/m acts5m above base; pore-water pressure is separate. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐層畫有效土壓和水壓圖，標明水位及每個三角形的作用點，積分後重建合力與力矩。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot effective-soil and water-pressure diagrams with levels and resultant locations, then reconstruct total force and moment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設Ka=1/3、浮重度10kN/m³、高H=15m，Pa=Kaγ′H²/2=375kN/m，作用在底上5m；水壓另算。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume Ka=1/3,submerged unit weight10kN/m³ and H=15m. Pa=375kN/m acts5m above base; pore-water pressure is separate.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「有效土壓積分」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Effective earth-pressure integration\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","基底平均壓力不大就足以證明邊緣接觸與承載都沒有問題。","護舷載入曲線下面積全部等於不可恢復的永久耗散能量。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","A modest mean base pressure proves that edge contact and foundation capacity are satisfactory.","All work under the fender loading curve is irreversibly dissipated energy."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b289-v15-07","title":"有效土壓積分：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Effective earth-pressure integration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「有效土壓積分」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective earth-pressure integration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐層畫有效土壓和水壓圖，標明水位及每個三角形的作用點，積分後重建合力與力矩。核對浮重度來源，將船舶、堆載及地震作用分開，避免相同水壓被不同表格重複加入。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot effective-soil and water-pressure diagrams with levels and resultant locations, then reconstruct total force and moment. Verify submerged unit weight and keep vessel, surcharge and seismic terms separate so the same water action is not added twice in different tables. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：逐層畫有效土壓和水壓圖，標明水位及每個三角形的作用點，積分後重建合力與力矩。核對浮重度來源，將船舶、堆載及地震作用分開，避免相同水壓被不同表格重複加入。","observationEn":"Site practice: Plot effective-soil and water-pressure diagrams with levels and resultant locations, then reconstruct total force and moment. Verify submerged unit weight and keep vessel, surcharge and seismic terms separate so the same water action is not added twice in different tables.","failure":"注意干擾：以飽和重度積分後又加完整水壓可能高估作用，僅用浮重度卻不加水壓則低估。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using saturated unit weight and then adding full water pressure can overcount action, while submerged weight alone omits water. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐層畫有效土壓和水壓圖，標明水位及每個三角形的作用點，積分後重建合力與力矩。核對浮重度來源，將船舶、堆載及地震作用分開，避免相同水壓被不同表格重複加入。","textEn":"Plot effective-soil and water-pressure diagrams with levels and resultant locations, then reconstruct total force and moment. Verify submerged unit weight and keep vessel, surcharge and seismic terms separate so the same water action is not added twice in different tables.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"逐層畫有效土壓和水壓圖，標明水位及每個三角形的作用點，積分後重建合力與力矩。核對浮重度來源，將船舶、堆載及地震作用分開，避免相同水壓被不同表格重複加入。","textEn":"Plot effective-soil and water-pressure diagrams with levels and resultant locations, then reconstruct total force and moment. Verify submerged unit weight and keep vessel, surcharge and seismic terms separate so the same water action is not added twice in different tables.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「有效土壓積分」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Effective earth-pressure integration\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","逐層畫有效土壓和水壓圖，標明水位及每個三角形的作用點，積分後重建合力與力矩。","全碼頭平均沉陷不大即可保證起重機軌道不會扭曲。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Plot effective-soil and water-pressure diagrams with levels and resultant locations, then reconstruct total force and moment.","Small average quay settlement guarantees that crane rails cannot distort."],"answer":1,"explanation":"逐層畫有效土壓和水壓圖，標明水位及每個三角形的作用點，積分後重建合力與力矩。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot effective-soil and water-pressure diagrams with levels and resultant locations, then reconstruct total force and moment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b289-v15-08","title":"有效土壓積分：失效診斷","titleEn":"Effective earth-pressure integration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「有效土壓積分」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective earth-pressure integration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以飽和重度積分後又加完整水壓可能高估作用，僅用浮重度卻不加水壓則低估。合力數值碰巧相近時，錯誤作用點仍可能使傾覆力矩嚴重偏離。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using saturated unit weight and then adding full water pressure can overcount action, while submerged weight alone omits water. Even coincidentally similar total forces can have incorrect resultant locations and materially wrong overturning moments. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設Ka=1/3、浮重度10kN/m³、高H=15m，Pa=Kaγ′H²/2=375kN/m，作用在底上5m；水壓另算。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Pa=375kN/m acts5m above base; pore-water pressure is separate.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「使用浮重度算出的有效土壓已經包含全部靜水壓力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Effective earth pressure calculated with submerged unit weight already includes all hydrostatic pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以飽和重度積分後又加完整水壓可能高估作用，僅用浮重度卻不加水壓則低估。合力數值碰巧相近時，錯誤作用點仍可能使傾覆力矩嚴重偏離。","textEn":"Using saturated unit weight and then adding full water pressure can overcount action, while submerged weight alone omits water. Even coincidentally similar total forces can have incorrect resultant locations and materially wrong overturning moments.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「有效土壓積分」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Effective earth-pressure integration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","全場平均堆載可以直接代表貼近岸壁的所有局部輪壓。","以飽和重度積分後又加完整水壓可能高估作用，僅用浮重度卻不加水壓則低估。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The terminal-average surcharge directly represents every concentrated wheel load near the quay edge.","Using saturated unit weight and then adding full water pressure can overcount action, while submerged weight alone omits water."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以飽和重度積分後又加完整水壓可能高估作用，僅用浮重度卻不加水壓則低估。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using saturated unit weight and then adding full water pressure can overcount action, while submerged weight alone omits water. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b289-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「碼頭堆載側壓」與「潮差與殘留水壓」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Quay surcharge lateral action\" and \"Tidal difference and retained water\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b289-v15-09","title":"碼頭堆載側壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Quay surcharge lateral action: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「碼頭堆載側壓」如何影響大型港口沉箱碼頭的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Quay surcharge lateral action” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large-port caisson quay walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"港區堆載的位置與範圍影響牆背側壓，無限均布面載只是簡化情境。貨櫃堆、起重機輪壓及條形基礎不能直接視為同一面載，局部作用可能沿牆長擴散；需要將工況、荷載路徑及土體假設相連，不能把一項平均值永久套用所有作業。 假設無限均布q=30kPa、Ka=1/3、牆高15m，增量側壓Ka q=10kPa、合力150kN/m；不代表局部輪載。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「碼頭堆載側壓」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Position and extent of terminal loading govern lateral response, with an infinite uniform surcharge only one idealization. Container stacks, crane wheels and strip foundations are different actions and can spread differently along the wall. Load cases, transfer paths and soil assumptions must be connected rather than assigning one average surcharge permanently to every possible terminal operation. Assume infinite uniform surcharge30kPa,Ka=1/3 and wall height15m. Incremental pressure is10kPa and resultant150kN/m, not a local wheel-load model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Quay surcharge lateral action” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「全場平均堆載可以直接代表貼近岸壁的所有局部輪壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The terminal-average surcharge directly represents every concentrated wheel load near the quay edge.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「碼頭堆載側壓」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Quay surcharge lateral action”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-09-k1","title":"碼頭堆載側壓","titleEn":"Quay surcharge lateral action","text":"港區堆載的位置與範圍影響牆背側壓，無限均布面載只是簡化情境。貨櫃堆、起重機輪壓及條形基礎不能直接視為同一面載，局部作用可能沿牆長擴散；需要將工況、荷載路徑及土體假設相連，不能把一項平均值永久套用所有作業。","textEn":"Position and extent of terminal loading govern lateral response, with an infinite uniform surcharge only one idealization. Container stacks, crane wheels and strip foundations are different actions and can spread differently along the wall.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全場平均堆載可以直接代表貼近岸壁的所有局部輪壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The terminal-average surcharge directly represents every concentrated wheel load near the quay edge. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「碼頭堆載側壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Quay surcharge lateral action\" is correct?","options":["港區堆載的位置與範圍影響牆背側壓，無限均布面載只是簡化情境。","全場平均堆載可以直接代表貼近岸壁的所有局部輪壓。","回填內水位總是與外海潮位同步所以不必量測孔壓。"],"optionsEn":["Position and extent of terminal loading govern lateral response, with an infinite uniform surcharge only one idealization.","The terminal-average surcharge directly represents every concentrated wheel load near the quay edge.","Backfill water always follows the harbor tide exactly, making pore-pressure measurements unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"港區堆載的位置與範圍影響牆背側壓，無限均布面載只是簡化情境。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Position and extent of terminal loading govern lateral response, with an infinite uniform surcharge only one idealization. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b289-v15-10","title":"碼頭堆載側壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Quay surcharge lateral action: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「碼頭堆載側壓」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Quay surcharge lateral action” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設無限均布q=30kPa、Ka=1/3、牆高15m，增量側壓Ka q=10kPa、合力150kN/m；不代表局部輪載。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume infinite uniform surcharge30kPa,Ka=1/3 and wall height15m. Incremental pressure is10kPa and resultant150kN/m, not a local wheel-load model. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在平面圖標出堆載邊界及距牆距離，確認荷載是否可近似無限均布。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map loading limits and setback from the wall and test the infinite-uniform approximation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設無限均布q=30kPa、Ka=1/3、牆高15m，增量側壓Ka q=10kPa、合力150kN/m；不代表局部輪載。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume infinite uniform surcharge30kPa,Ka=1/3 and wall height15m. Incremental pressure is10kPa and resultant150kN/m, not a local wheel-load model.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「碼頭堆載側壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Quay surcharge lateral action\", which statement holds?","options":["靠泊能量增加一倍就表示護舷峰值反力一定增加一倍。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","加重沉箱只增加抵抗力而不會增加任何地震慣性需求。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling berthing energy necessarily doubles the fender's peak reaction force.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Increasing caisson mass raises resistance without increasing any seismic inertia demand."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b289-v15-11","title":"碼頭堆載側壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Quay surcharge lateral action: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「碼頭堆載側壓」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Quay surcharge lateral action” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在平面圖標出堆載邊界及距牆距離，確認荷載是否可近似無限均布。另畫集中與條形荷載的傳遞路徑，將實際作業組合連回允許配置，不以日平均貨量取代短期峰值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map loading limits and setback from the wall and test the infinite-uniform approximation. Trace concentrated and strip-load paths separately, linking operational combinations to reviewed layouts rather than substituting daily average cargo for short-duration peak loading conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在平面圖標出堆載邊界及距牆距離，確認荷載是否可近似無限均布。另畫集中與條形荷載的傳遞路徑，將實際作業組合連回允許配置，不以日平均貨量取代短期峰值。","observationEn":"Site practice: Map loading limits and setback from the wall and test the infinite-uniform approximation. Trace concentrated and strip-load paths separately, linking operational combinations to reviewed layouts rather than substituting daily average cargo for short-duration peak loading conditions.","failure":"注意干擾：起重機靠牆時局部應力可能高於全場平均，倉儲配置改變又會新增未評估的荷載組合。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A crane near the edge can create stresses above the terminal average, while changed storage layouts add unreviewed combinations. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在平面圖標出堆載邊界及距牆距離，確認荷載是否可近似無限均布。另畫集中與條形荷載的傳遞路徑，將實際作業組合連回允許配置，不以日平均貨量取代短期峰值。","textEn":"Map loading limits and setback from the wall and test the infinite-uniform approximation. Trace concentrated and strip-load paths separately, linking operational combinations to reviewed layouts rather than substituting daily average cargo for short-duration peak loading conditions.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在平面圖標出堆載邊界及距牆距離，確認荷載是否可近似無限均布。另畫集中與條形荷載的傳遞路徑，將實際作業組合連回允許配置，不以日平均貨量取代短期峰值。","textEn":"Map loading limits and setback from the wall and test the infinite-uniform approximation. Trace concentrated and strip-load paths separately, linking operational combinations to reviewed layouts rather than substituting daily average cargo for short-duration peak loading conditions.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「碼頭堆載側壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Quay surcharge lateral action\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","止水材料幾何應變不大就能證明所有水頭下都完全不漏水。","在平面圖標出堆載邊界及距牆距離，確認荷載是否可近似無限均布。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Small geometric seal strain proves complete watertightness under every water head.","Map loading limits and setback from the wall and test the infinite-uniform approximation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在平面圖標出堆載邊界及距牆距離，確認荷載是否可近似無限均布。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map loading limits and setback from the wall and test the infinite-uniform approximation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b289-v15-12","title":"碼頭堆載側壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Quay surcharge lateral action: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「碼頭堆載側壓」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Quay surcharge lateral action” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"起重機靠牆時局部應力可能高於全場平均，倉儲配置改變又會新增未評估的荷載組合。只沿用初始均布數值，容易漏掉沉箱接縫附近的集中需求。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A crane near the edge can create stresses above the terminal average, while changed storage layouts add unreviewed combinations. Retaining the original uniform value may miss concentrated demand near joints between adjacent quay caissons. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設無限均布q=30kPa、Ka=1/3、牆高15m，增量側壓Ka q=10kPa、合力150kN/m；不代表局部輪載。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Incremental pressure is10kPa and resultant150kN/m, not a local wheel-load model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全場平均堆載可以直接代表貼近岸壁的所有局部輪壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The terminal-average surcharge directly represents every concentrated wheel load near the quay edge.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"起重機靠牆時局部應力可能高於全場平均，倉儲配置改變又會新增未評估的荷載組合。只沿用初始均布數值，容易漏掉沉箱接縫附近的集中需求。","textEn":"A crane near the edge can create stresses above the terminal average, while changed storage layouts add unreviewed combinations. Retaining the original uniform value may miss concentrated demand near joints between adjacent quay caissons.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「碼頭堆載側壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Quay surcharge lateral action\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["起重機靠牆時局部應力可能高於全場平均，倉儲配置改變又會新增未評估的荷載組合。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","回填內水位總是與外海潮位同步所以不必量測孔壓。"],"optionsEn":["A crane near the edge can create stresses above the terminal average, while changed storage layouts add unreviewed combinations.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Backfill water always follows the harbor tide exactly, making pore-pressure measurements unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"起重機靠牆時局部應力可能高於全場平均，倉儲配置改變又會新增未評估的荷載組合。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A crane near the edge can create stresses above the terminal average, while changed storage layouts add unreviewed combinations. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b289-v15-13","title":"潮差與殘留水壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tidal difference and retained water: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「潮差與殘留水壓」如何影響大型港口沉箱碼頭的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tidal difference and retained water” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large-port caisson quay walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"退潮時回填內水位可能下降較慢，沉箱兩側水壓不同步，排水能力便成為整體受力的一部分。兩側同底面靜水三角形可以分別積分後相減，但滲流、波動和排水堵塞會改變實際分布；只用海面潮位不能確定回填孔壓。 假設同底面兩側靜水深5與3m、海水γ=10.05525kN/m³，淨水平力γ(5²−3²)/2=80.442kN/m；不含滲流動態。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「潮差與殘留水壓」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"During falling tide, backfill water may lag behind the harbor level, making drainage part of the overall load path. Hydrostatic triangles referenced to the same base can be integrated separately and subtracted, but seepage, waves and clogged drains alter the distribution. Sea level alone cannot establish the pore-pressure condition within the backfill during the same event. Assume hydrostatic depths5 and3m above one base and seawaterγ=10.05525kN/m³. Net horizontal force=80.442kN/m, excluding transient seepage. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tidal difference and retained water” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「回填內水位總是與外海潮位同步所以不必量測孔壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Backfill water always follows the harbor tide exactly, making pore-pressure measurements unnecessary.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「潮差與殘留水壓」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tidal difference and retained water”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-13-k1","title":"潮差與殘留水壓","titleEn":"Tidal difference and retained water","text":"退潮時回填內水位可能下降較慢，沉箱兩側水壓不同步，排水能力便成為整體受力的一部分。兩側同底面靜水三角形可以分別積分後相減，但滲流、波動和排水堵塞會改變實際分布；只用海面潮位不能確定回填孔壓。","textEn":"During falling tide, backfill water may lag behind the harbor level, making drainage part of the overall load path. Hydrostatic triangles referenced to the same base can be integrated separately and subtracted, but seepage, waves and clogged drains alter the distribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：回填內水位總是與外海潮位同步所以不必量測孔壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Backfill water always follows the harbor tide exactly, making pore-pressure measurements unnecessary. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「潮差與殘留水壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tidal difference and retained water\" is correct?","options":["回填內水位總是與外海潮位同步所以不必量測孔壓。","退潮時回填內水位可能下降較慢，沉箱兩側水壓不同步，排水能力便成為整體受力的一部分。","基底平均壓力不大就足以證明邊緣接觸與承載都沒有問題。"],"optionsEn":["Backfill water always follows the harbor tide exactly, making pore-pressure measurements unnecessary.","During falling tide, backfill water may lag behind the harbor level, making drainage part of the overall load path.","A modest mean base pressure proves that edge contact and foundation capacity are satisfactory."],"answer":1,"explanation":"退潮時回填內水位可能下降較慢，沉箱兩側水壓不同步，排水能力便成為整體受力的一部分。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"During falling tide, backfill water may lag behind the harbor level, making drainage part of the overall load path. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b289-v15-14","title":"潮差與殘留水壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Tidal difference and retained water: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「潮差與殘留水壓」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tidal difference and retained water” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設同底面兩側靜水深5與3m、海水γ=10.05525kN/m³，淨水平力γ(5²−3²)/2=80.442kN/m；不含滲流動態。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume hydrostatic depths5 and3m above one base and seawaterγ=10.05525kN/m³. Net horizontal force=80.442kN/m, excluding transient seepage. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步讀取海側潮位及回填孔壓，畫退潮時的水位差歷程，檢查排水出口是否暢通。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronize harbor tide and backfill pressure records, plotting falling-tide lag and checking outlets.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設同底面兩側靜水深5與3m、海水γ=10.05525kN/m³，淨水平力γ(5²−3²)/2=80.442kN/m；不含滲流動態。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume hydrostatic depths5 and3m above one base and seawaterγ=10.05525kN/m³. Net horizontal force=80.442kN/m, excluding transient seepage.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「潮差與殘留水壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tidal difference and retained water\", which statement holds?","options":["護舷載入曲線下面積全部等於不可恢復的永久耗散能量。","全碼頭平均沉陷不大即可保證起重機軌道不會扭曲。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["All work under the fender loading curve is irreversibly dissipated energy.","Small average quay settlement guarantees that crane rails cannot distort.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b289-v15-15","title":"潮差與殘留水壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tidal difference and retained water: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「潮差與殘留水壓」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tidal difference and retained water” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步讀取海側潮位及回填孔壓，畫退潮時的水位差歷程，檢查排水出口是否暢通。以共同底面計算兩側合力並核對相位，另列不能用靜水三角形表達的滲流分量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronize harbor tide and backfill pressure records, plotting falling-tide lag and checking outlets. Integrate both sides above a common base and compare timing, separately identifying seepage contributions that cannot be represented by the two static pressure triangles. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：同步讀取海側潮位及回填孔壓，畫退潮時的水位差歷程，檢查排水出口是否暢通。以共同底面計算兩側合力並核對相位，另列不能用靜水三角形表達的滲流分量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Synchronize harbor tide and backfill pressure records, plotting falling-tide lag and checking outlets. Integrate both sides above a common base and compare timing, separately identifying seepage contributions that cannot be represented by the two static pressure triangles.","failure":"注意干擾：排水堵塞會在外海退潮後保留較高側壓，僅取兩側各自最高水位又可能拼出不存在的工況。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Blocked drains retain lateral pressure after the sea falls, while combining separate maximum levels can create a nonexistent load case. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步讀取海側潮位及回填孔壓，畫退潮時的水位差歷程，檢查排水出口是否暢通。以共同底面計算兩側合力並核對相位，另列不能用靜水三角形表達的滲流分量。","textEn":"Synchronize harbor tide and backfill pressure records, plotting falling-tide lag and checking outlets. Integrate both sides above a common base and compare timing, separately identifying seepage contributions that cannot be represented by the two static pressure triangles.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"同步讀取海側潮位及回填孔壓，畫退潮時的水位差歷程，檢查排水出口是否暢通。以共同底面計算兩側合力並核對相位，另列不能用靜水三角形表達的滲流分量。","textEn":"Synchronize harbor tide and backfill pressure records, plotting falling-tide lag and checking outlets. Integrate both sides above a common base and compare timing, separately identifying seepage contributions that cannot be represented by the two static pressure triangles.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「潮差與殘留水壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tidal difference and retained water\"?","options":["同步讀取海側潮位及回填孔壓，畫退潮時的水位差歷程，檢查排水出口是否暢通。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","所有碼頭背填土都不需牆體變形就會自動達到主動土壓。"],"optionsEn":["Synchronize harbor tide and backfill pressure records, plotting falling-tide lag and checking outlets.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Every quay backfill automatically reaches active pressure without any wall movement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步讀取海側潮位及回填孔壓，畫退潮時的水位差歷程，檢查排水出口是否暢通。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronize harbor tide and backfill pressure records, plotting falling-tide lag and checking outlets. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b289-v15-16","title":"潮差與殘留水壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tidal difference and retained water: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「潮差與殘留水壓」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tidal difference and retained water” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"排水堵塞會在外海退潮後保留較高側壓，僅取兩側各自最高水位又可能拼出不存在的工況。忽略時間相位，會錯估最不利水平作用及其持續時間。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Blocked drains retain lateral pressure after the sea falls, while combining separate maximum levels can create a nonexistent load case. Ignoring phase misstates both the adverse horizontal action and how long it persists. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設同底面兩側靜水深5與3m、海水γ=10.05525kN/m³，淨水平力γ(5²−3²)/2=80.442kN/m；不含滲流動態。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Net horizontal force=80.442kN/m, excluding transient seepage.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「回填內水位總是與外海潮位同步所以不必量測孔壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Backfill water always follows the harbor tide exactly, making pore-pressure measurements unnecessary.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"排水堵塞會在外海退潮後保留較高側壓，僅取兩側各自最高水位又可能拼出不存在的工況。忽略時間相位，會錯估最不利水平作用及其持續時間。","textEn":"Blocked drains retain lateral pressure after the sea falls, while combining separate maximum levels can create a nonexistent load case. Ignoring phase misstates both the adverse horizontal action and how long it persists.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「潮差與殘留水壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tidal difference and retained water\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","排水堵塞會在外海退潮後保留較高側壓，僅取兩側各自最高水位又可能拼出不存在的工況。","基底平均壓力不大就足以證明邊緣接觸與承載都沒有問題。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Blocked drains retain lateral pressure after the sea falls, while combining separate maximum levels can create a nonexistent load case.","A modest mean base pressure proves that edge contact and foundation capacity are satisfactory."],"answer":1,"explanation":"排水堵塞會在外海退潮後保留較高側壓，僅取兩側各自最高水位又可能拼出不存在的工況。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Blocked drains retain lateral pressure after the sea falls, while combining separate maximum levels can create a nonexistent load case. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b289-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「基底偏心壓力」與「船舶靠泊動能」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Eccentric base pressure\" and \"Vessel berthing energy\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b289-v15-17","title":"基底偏心壓力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Eccentric base pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「基底偏心壓力」如何影響大型港口沉箱碼頭的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Eccentric base pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large-port caisson quay walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"沉箱基底反力同時由法向力與力矩決定，平均壓力不足以描述邊緣需求。矩形線彈性全接觸公式還要求地基不出現拉力，若有缺口或基床不平需改變接觸模型；幾何壓力分布也只是作用需求，不能單獨證明現地地基的極限承載力足夠。 假設每米N=3000kN、B=15m、e=1.5m，q=N/B(1±6e/B)，qmax=320kPa、qmin=80kPa，且e<B/6。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「基底偏心壓力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Normal force and moment jointly determine base reaction, so average pressure misses edge demand. The rectangular linear full-contact formula requires nonnegative contact; gaps or uneven bedding change the model. This geometric pressure distribution describes demand only, not adequate foundation capacity, and must be paired with independent information about ground behavior and actual contact conditions. Assume per-metre N=3000kN,B=15m and e=1.5m. q=N/B(1±6e/B) gives320 and80kPa, with e<B/6. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Eccentric base pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「基底平均壓力不大就足以證明邊緣接觸與承載都沒有問題。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A modest mean base pressure proves that edge contact and foundation capacity are satisfactory.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「基底偏心壓力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Eccentric base pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-17-k1","title":"基底偏心壓力","titleEn":"Eccentric base pressure","text":"沉箱基底反力同時由法向力與力矩決定，平均壓力不足以描述邊緣需求。矩形線彈性全接觸公式還要求地基不出現拉力，若有缺口或基床不平需改變接觸模型；幾何壓力分布也只是作用需求，不能單獨證明現地地基的極限承載力足夠。","textEn":"Normal force and moment jointly determine base reaction, so average pressure misses edge demand. The rectangular linear full-contact formula requires nonnegative contact; gaps or uneven bedding change the model.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：基底平均壓力不大就足以證明邊緣接觸與承載都沒有問題。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A modest mean base pressure proves that edge contact and foundation capacity are satisfactory. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基底偏心壓力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Eccentric base pressure\" is correct?","options":["基底平均壓力不大就足以證明邊緣接觸與承載都沒有問題。","靠泊能量增加一倍就表示護舷峰值反力一定增加一倍。","沉箱基底反力同時由法向力與力矩決定，平均壓力不足以描述邊緣需求。"],"optionsEn":["A modest mean base pressure proves that edge contact and foundation capacity are satisfactory.","Doubling berthing energy necessarily doubles the fender's peak reaction force.","Normal force and moment jointly determine base reaction, so average pressure misses edge demand."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沉箱基底反力同時由法向力與力矩決定，平均壓力不足以描述邊緣需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Normal force and moment jointly determine base reaction, so average pressure misses edge demand. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b289-v15-18","title":"基底偏心壓力：定量估算","titleEn":"Eccentric base pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「基底偏心壓力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Eccentric base pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設每米N=3000kN、B=15m、e=1.5m，q=N/B(1±6e/B)，qmax=320kPa、qmin=80kPa，且e<B/6。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume per-metre N=3000kN,B=15m and e=1.5m. q=N/B(1±6e/B) gives320 and80kPa, with e<B/6. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：標明法向力是否已扣除揚壓，核對力矩參考點與偏心正負號。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: State whether normal force already excludes uplift and check moment reference and eccentricity signs.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設每米N=3000kN、B=15m、e=1.5m，q=N/B(1±6e/B)，qmax=320kPa、qmin=80kPa，且e<B/6。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume per-metre N=3000kN,B=15m and e=1.5m. q=N/B(1±6e/B) gives320 and80kPa, with e<B/6.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基底偏心壓力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Eccentric base pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","加重沉箱只增加抵抗力而不會增加任何地震慣性需求。","止水材料幾何應變不大就能證明所有水頭下都完全不漏水。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Increasing caisson mass raises resistance without increasing any seismic inertia demand.","Small geometric seal strain proves complete watertightness under every water head."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b289-v15-19","title":"基底偏心壓力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Eccentric base pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「基底偏心壓力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Eccentric base pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"標明法向力是否已扣除揚壓，核對力矩參考點與偏心正負號。積分壓力圖回算原合力，再以基床平整、接觸與土體資料檢查全接觸假設，保留局部不適用區域。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"State whether normal force already excludes uplift and check moment reference and eccentricity signs. Integrate the diagram back to the original resultant, then test full contact against bedding, interface and soil evidence, retaining locations where the assumption is unsupported. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：標明法向力是否已扣除揚壓，核對力矩參考點與偏心正負號。積分壓力圖回算原合力，再以基床平整、接觸與土體資料檢查全接觸假設，保留局部不適用區域。","observationEn":"Site practice: State whether normal force already excludes uplift and check moment reference and eccentricity signs. Integrate the diagram back to the original resultant, then test full contact against bedding, interface and soil evidence, retaining locations where the assumption is unsupported.","failure":"注意干擾：基床局部空洞會集中實際壓力，公式仍畫出平順分布卻不代表真接觸。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A bedding void concentrates real pressure despite a smooth calculated diagram. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"標明法向力是否已扣除揚壓，核對力矩參考點與偏心正負號。積分壓力圖回算原合力，再以基床平整、接觸與土體資料檢查全接觸假設，保留局部不適用區域。","textEn":"State whether normal force already excludes uplift and check moment reference and eccentricity signs. Integrate the diagram back to the original resultant, then test full contact against bedding, interface and soil evidence, retaining locations where the assumption is unsupported.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"標明法向力是否已扣除揚壓，核對力矩參考點與偏心正負號。積分壓力圖回算原合力，再以基床平整、接觸與土體資料檢查全接觸假設，保留局部不適用區域。","textEn":"State whether normal force already excludes uplift and check moment reference and eccentricity signs. Integrate the diagram back to the original resultant, then test full contact against bedding, interface and soil evidence, retaining locations where the assumption is unsupported.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基底偏心壓力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Eccentric base pressure\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","標明法向力是否已扣除揚壓，核對力矩參考點與偏心正負號。","使用浮重度算出的有效土壓已經包含全部靜水壓力。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","State whether normal force already excludes uplift and check moment reference and eccentricity signs.","Effective earth pressure calculated with submerged unit weight already includes all hydrostatic pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"標明法向力是否已扣除揚壓，核對力矩參考點與偏心正負號。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"State whether normal force already excludes uplift and check moment reference and eccentricity signs. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b289-v15-20","title":"基底偏心壓力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Eccentric base pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「基底偏心壓力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Eccentric base pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"基床局部空洞會集中實際壓力，公式仍畫出平順分布卻不代表真接觸。若把尚未扣揚壓的重量當有效法向力，側壓與承載驗算會一起出現不一致。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A bedding void concentrates real pressure despite a smooth calculated diagram. Treating weight before uplift deduction as effective normal force also creates inconsistent contact and resistance calculations, even if each separate spreadsheet appears internally tidy. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設每米N=3000kN、B=15m、e=1.5m，q=N/B(1±6e/B)，qmax=320kPa、qmin=80kPa，且e<B/6。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume per-metre N=3000kN,B=15m and e=1.5m. q=N/B(1±6e/B) gives320 and80kPa, with e<B/6.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「基底平均壓力不大就足以證明邊緣接觸與承載都沒有問題。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A modest mean base pressure proves that edge contact and foundation capacity are satisfactory.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"基床局部空洞會集中實際壓力，公式仍畫出平順分布卻不代表真接觸。若把尚未扣揚壓的重量當有效法向力，側壓與承載驗算會一起出現不一致。","textEn":"A bedding void concentrates real pressure despite a smooth calculated diagram. Treating weight before uplift deduction as effective normal force also creates inconsistent contact and resistance calculations, even if each separate spreadsheet appears internally tidy.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基底偏心壓力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Eccentric base pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","靠泊能量增加一倍就表示護舷峰值反力一定增加一倍。","基床局部空洞會集中實際壓力，公式仍畫出平順分布卻不代表真接觸。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Doubling berthing energy necessarily doubles the fender's peak reaction force.","A bedding void concentrates real pressure despite a smooth calculated diagram."],"answer":2,"explanation":"基床局部空洞會集中實際壓力，公式仍畫出平順分布卻不代表真接觸。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A bedding void concentrates real pressure despite a smooth calculated diagram. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b289-v15-21","title":"船舶靠泊動能：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Vessel berthing energy: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「船舶靠泊動能」如何影響大型港口沉箱碼頭的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Vessel berthing energy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large-port caisson quay walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"靠泊作用從船舶法向運動能量傳至護舷與碼頭，速度對能量有平方影響。有效質量和偏心等係數需明確定義，不能將排水量直接當任意工況的質量；能量需求也不同於峰值力，必須透過護舷特性及接觸路徑連接兩者。 假設已含附加質量的有效質量20000000kg、法向速0.10m/s、選定合成係數0.80，E=0.5Mv²C=80kJ。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「船舶靠泊動能」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Normal vessel motion transfers energy to fenders and the quay, with velocity entering quadratically. Effective mass and correction factors need explicit definitions rather than treating displacement as the mass for every condition. Energy demand differs from peak force; the fender response and contact path connect them, so one kinetic-energy number cannot alone determine the resulting structural action. Assume effective mass20000000kg already includes added mass, normal speed0.10m/s and selected combined factor0.80. E=0.5Mv²C=80kJ, not an operating limit. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Vessel berthing energy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「靠泊能量增加一倍就表示護舷峰值反力一定增加一倍。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Doubling berthing energy necessarily doubles the fender's peak reaction force.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「船舶靠泊動能」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Vessel berthing energy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-21-k1","title":"船舶靠泊動能","titleEn":"Vessel berthing energy","text":"靠泊作用從船舶法向運動能量傳至護舷與碼頭，速度對能量有平方影響。有效質量和偏心等係數需明確定義，不能將排水量直接當任意工況的質量；能量需求也不同於峰值力，必須透過護舷特性及接觸路徑連接兩者。","textEn":"Normal vessel motion transfers energy to fenders and the quay, with velocity entering quadratically. Effective mass and correction factors need explicit definitions rather than treating displacement as the mass for every condition.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：靠泊能量增加一倍就表示護舷峰值反力一定增加一倍。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Doubling berthing energy necessarily doubles the fender's peak reaction force. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「船舶靠泊動能」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Vessel berthing energy\" is correct?","options":["靠泊作用從船舶法向運動能量傳至護舷與碼頭，速度對能量有平方影響。","靠泊能量增加一倍就表示護舷峰值反力一定增加一倍。","護舷載入曲線下面積全部等於不可恢復的永久耗散能量。"],"optionsEn":["Normal vessel motion transfers energy to fenders and the quay, with velocity entering quadratically.","Doubling berthing energy necessarily doubles the fender's peak reaction force.","All work under the fender loading curve is irreversibly dissipated energy."],"answer":0,"explanation":"靠泊作用從船舶法向運動能量傳至護舷與碼頭，速度對能量有平方影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Normal vessel motion transfers energy to fenders and the quay, with velocity entering quadratically. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b289-v15-22","title":"船舶靠泊動能：定量估算","titleEn":"Vessel berthing energy: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「船舶靠泊動能」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Vessel berthing energy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設已含附加質量的有效質量20000000kg、法向速0.10m/s、選定合成係數0.80，E=0.5Mv²C=80kJ。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume effective mass20000000kg already includes added mass, normal speed0.10m/s and selected combined factor0.80. E=0.5Mv²C=80kJ, not an operating limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：列出質量與各修正因子的定義，確定附加質量沒有重複加入，並核對速度是接觸法向分量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Define mass and correction factors, avoiding duplicate added mass, and confirm that velocity is normal to contact.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設已含附加質量的有效質量20000000kg、法向速0.10m/s、選定合成係數0.80，E=0.5Mv²C=80kJ。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume effective mass20000000kg already includes added mass, normal speed0.10m/s and selected combined factor0.80. E=0.5Mv²C=80kJ, not an operating limit.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「船舶靠泊動能」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Vessel berthing energy\", which statement holds?","options":["全碼頭平均沉陷不大即可保證起重機軌道不會扭曲。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","所有碼頭背填土都不需牆體變形就會自動達到主動土壓。"],"optionsEn":["Small average quay settlement guarantees that crane rails cannot distort.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Every quay backfill automatically reaches active pressure without any wall movement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b289-v15-23","title":"船舶靠泊動能：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Vessel berthing energy: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「船舶靠泊動能」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Vessel berthing energy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"列出質量與各修正因子的定義，確定附加質量沒有重複加入，並核對速度是接觸法向分量。用多接觸點和護舷曲線檢查分配，保留船型、潮位與偏心條件，不將算例當操船指令。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Define mass and correction factors, avoiding duplicate added mass, and confirm that velocity is normal to contact. Review distribution across contact points using fender curves, retaining vessel, tide and eccentricity assumptions without treating the example as vessel-handling instructions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：列出質量與各修正因子的定義，確定附加質量沒有重複加入，並核對速度是接觸法向分量。用多接觸點和護舷曲線檢查分配，保留船型、潮位與偏心條件，不將算例當操船指令。","observationEn":"Site practice: Define mass and correction factors, avoiding duplicate added mass, and confirm that velocity is normal to contact. Review distribution across contact points using fender curves, retaining vessel, tide and eccentricity assumptions without treating the example as vessel-handling instructions.","failure":"注意干擾：把總航速當成法向速度可能高估能量，忽略附加質量或偏心則可能低估特定工況。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using total speed instead of the normal component can overstate energy, while omitted added mass or eccentricity understates particular cases. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"列出質量與各修正因子的定義，確定附加質量沒有重複加入，並核對速度是接觸法向分量。用多接觸點和護舷曲線檢查分配，保留船型、潮位與偏心條件，不將算例當操船指令。","textEn":"Define mass and correction factors, avoiding duplicate added mass, and confirm that velocity is normal to contact. Review distribution across contact points using fender curves, retaining vessel, tide and eccentricity assumptions without treating the example as vessel-handling instructions.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"列出質量與各修正因子的定義，確定附加質量沒有重複加入，並核對速度是接觸法向分量。用多接觸點和護舷曲線檢查分配，保留船型、潮位與偏心條件，不將算例當操船指令。","textEn":"Define mass and correction factors, avoiding duplicate added mass, and confirm that velocity is normal to contact. Review distribution across contact points using fender curves, retaining vessel, tide and eccentricity assumptions without treating the example as vessel-handling instructions.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「船舶靠泊動能」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Vessel berthing energy\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","全場平均堆載可以直接代表貼近岸壁的所有局部輪壓。","列出質量與各修正因子的定義，確定附加質量沒有重複加入，並核對速度是接觸法向分量。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The terminal-average surcharge directly represents every concentrated wheel load near the quay edge.","Define mass and correction factors, avoiding duplicate added mass, and confirm that velocity is normal to contact."],"answer":2,"explanation":"列出質量與各修正因子的定義，確定附加質量沒有重複加入，並核對速度是接觸法向分量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Define mass and correction factors, avoiding duplicate added mass, and confirm that velocity is normal to contact. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b289-v15-24","title":"船舶靠泊動能：失效診斷","titleEn":"Vessel berthing energy: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「船舶靠泊動能」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Vessel berthing energy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把總航速當成法向速度可能高估能量，忽略附加質量或偏心則可能低估特定工況。能量相同的兩種接觸可產生不同峰值力，不能只靠一個數字選結構。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using total speed instead of the normal component can overstate energy, while omitted added mass or eccentricity understates particular cases. Equal-energy contacts can produce different peak forces, so one value does not determine structural demand. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設已含附加質量的有效質量20000000kg、法向速0.10m/s、選定合成係數0.80，E=0.5Mv²C=80kJ。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: E=0.5Mv²C=80kJ, not an operating limit.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「靠泊能量增加一倍就表示護舷峰值反力一定增加一倍。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Doubling berthing energy necessarily doubles the fender's peak reaction force.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把總航速當成法向速度可能高估能量，忽略附加質量或偏心則可能低估特定工況。能量相同的兩種接觸可產生不同峰值力，不能只靠一個數字選結構。","textEn":"Using total speed instead of the normal component can overstate energy, while omitted added mass or eccentricity understates particular cases. Equal-energy contacts can produce different peak forces, so one value does not determine structural demand.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「船舶靠泊動能」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Vessel berthing energy\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把總航速當成法向速度可能高估能量，忽略附加質量或偏心則可能低估特定工況。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","護舷載入曲線下面積全部等於不可恢復的永久耗散能量。"],"optionsEn":["Using total speed instead of the normal component can overstate energy, while omitted added mass or eccentricity understates particular cases.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","All work under the fender loading curve is irreversibly dissipated energy."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把總航速當成法向速度可能高估能量，忽略附加質量或偏心則可能低估特定工況。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using total speed instead of the normal component can overstate energy, while omitted added mass or eccentricity understates particular cases. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b289-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「護舷曲線積分」與「簡化地震慣性」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Integrating fender response\" and \"Simplified seismic inertia\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b289-v15-25","title":"護舷曲線積分：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Integrating fender response: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「護舷曲線積分」如何影響大型港口沉箱碼頭的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Integrating fender response” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large-port caisson quay walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"護舷吸能是力與變形曲線下面積，不是峰值力直接當能量，材料又可能受溫度、速度及老化影響。線性示意有三角形面積，但實際橡膠護舷曲線常非線性；卸載回彈與耗散也不同，不能把可恢復儲能全部稱為永久吸收。 假設護舷載入反力從0線性增至1000kN、壓縮0.30m，載入功W=Fmaxδ/2=150kJ；卸載耗散未給定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「護舷曲線積分」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Fender work is the area under force versus displacement, not the numerical peak force. Temperature, loading rate and aging affect material response. A linear illustration gives triangular area, but real rubber curves are often nonlinear. Recoverable energy and dissipated energy also differ, so the complete loading work cannot automatically be labeled permanently absorbed impact energy. Assume reaction rises linearly from0 to1000kN over0.30m compression. Loading work is150kJ; unloading dissipation is not specified. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Integrating fender response” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「護舷載入曲線下面積全部等於不可恢復的永久耗散能量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All work under the fender loading curve is irreversibly dissipated energy.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「護舷曲線積分」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Integrating fender response”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-25-k1","title":"護舷曲線積分","titleEn":"Integrating fender response","text":"護舷吸能是力與變形曲線下面積，不是峰值力直接當能量，材料又可能受溫度、速度及老化影響。線性示意有三角形面積，但實際橡膠護舷曲線常非線性；卸載回彈與耗散也不同，不能把可恢復儲能全部稱為永久吸收。","textEn":"Fender work is the area under force versus displacement, not the numerical peak force. Temperature, loading rate and aging affect material response.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：護舷載入曲線下面積全部等於不可恢復的永久耗散能量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All work under the fender loading curve is irreversibly dissipated energy. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「護舷曲線積分」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Integrating fender response\" is correct?","options":["護舷載入曲線下面積全部等於不可恢復的永久耗散能量。","護舷吸能是力與變形曲線下面積，不是峰值力直接當能量，材料又可能受溫度、速度及老化影響。","加重沉箱只增加抵抗力而不會增加任何地震慣性需求。"],"optionsEn":["All work under the fender loading curve is irreversibly dissipated energy.","Fender work is the area under force versus displacement, not the numerical peak force.","Increasing caisson mass raises resistance without increasing any seismic inertia demand."],"answer":1,"explanation":"護舷吸能是力與變形曲線下面積，不是峰值力直接當能量，材料又可能受溫度、速度及老化影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Fender work is the area under force versus displacement, not the numerical peak force. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b289-v15-26","title":"護舷曲線積分：定量估算","titleEn":"Integrating fender response: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「護舷曲線積分」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Integrating fender response” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設護舷載入反力從0線性增至1000kN、壓縮0.30m，載入功W=Fmaxδ/2=150kJ；卸載耗散未給定。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume reaction rises linearly from0 to1000kN over0.30m compression. Loading work is150kJ; unloading dissipation is not specified. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：取得適用溫度與速度下的力變形曲線，積分載入和卸載並檢查量測單位。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Obtain response curves for applicable temperature and rate, integrating loading and unloading with consistent units.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設護舷載入反力從0線性增至1000kN、壓縮0.30m，載入功W=Fmaxδ/2=150kJ；卸載耗散未給定。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume reaction rises linearly from0 to1000kN over0.30m compression. Loading work is150kJ; unloading dissipation is not specified.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「護舷曲線積分」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Integrating fender response\", which statement holds?","options":["止水材料幾何應變不大就能證明所有水頭下都完全不漏水。","使用浮重度算出的有效土壓已經包含全部靜水壓力。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Small geometric seal strain proves complete watertightness under every water head.","Effective earth pressure calculated with submerged unit weight already includes all hydrostatic pressure.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b289-v15-27","title":"護舷曲線積分：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Integrating fender response: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「護舷曲線積分」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Integrating fender response” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"取得適用溫度與速度下的力變形曲線，積分載入和卸載並檢查量測單位。將峰值反力另傳到錨栓和沉箱模型，核對接觸面積與多護舷分擔，避免用吸能值取代力路徑。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Obtain response curves for applicable temperature and rate, integrating loading and unloading with consistent units. Transfer peak reaction separately to anchors and caisson, checking contact area and sharing among fenders rather than replacing the force path with an energy rating. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：取得適用溫度與速度下的力變形曲線，積分載入和卸載並檢查量測單位。將峰值反力另傳到錨栓和沉箱模型，核對接觸面積與多護舷分擔，避免用吸能值取代力路徑。","observationEn":"Site practice: Obtain response curves for applicable temperature and rate, integrating loading and unloading with consistent units. Transfer peak reaction separately to anchors and caisson, checking contact area and sharing among fenders rather than replacing the force path with an energy rating.","failure":"注意干擾：護舷變硬可能在相同位移產生較大峰力，老化裂損也可能改變回彈。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A stiffer fender produces higher reaction at the same displacement, while aging cracks alter recovery. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"取得適用溫度與速度下的力變形曲線，積分載入和卸載並檢查量測單位。將峰值反力另傳到錨栓和沉箱模型，核對接觸面積與多護舷分擔，避免用吸能值取代力路徑。","textEn":"Obtain response curves for applicable temperature and rate, integrating loading and unloading with consistent units. Transfer peak reaction separately to anchors and caisson, checking contact area and sharing among fenders rather than replacing the force path with an energy rating.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"取得適用溫度與速度下的力變形曲線，積分載入和卸載並檢查量測單位。將峰值反力另傳到錨栓和沉箱模型，核對接觸面積與多護舷分擔，避免用吸能值取代力路徑。","textEn":"Obtain response curves for applicable temperature and rate, integrating loading and unloading with consistent units. Transfer peak reaction separately to anchors and caisson, checking contact area and sharing among fenders rather than replacing the force path with an energy rating.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「護舷曲線積分」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Integrating fender response\"?","options":["取得適用溫度與速度下的力變形曲線，積分載入和卸載並檢查量測單位。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","回填內水位總是與外海潮位同步所以不必量測孔壓。"],"optionsEn":["Obtain response curves for applicable temperature and rate, integrating loading and unloading with consistent units.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Backfill water always follows the harbor tide exactly, making pore-pressure measurements unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"取得適用溫度與速度下的力變形曲線，積分載入和卸載並檢查量測單位。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Obtain response curves for applicable temperature and rate, integrating loading and unloading with consistent units. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b289-v15-28","title":"護舷曲線積分：失效診斷","titleEn":"Integrating fender response: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「護舷曲線積分」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Integrating fender response” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"護舷變硬可能在相同位移產生較大峰力，老化裂損也可能改變回彈。若只核對標稱吸能而忽略反力曲線，碼頭局部構件可能承受未被納入的需求。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A stiffer fender produces higher reaction at the same displacement, while aging cracks alter recovery. Checking nominal energy alone and ignoring the reaction curve can leave local quay components exposed to unexamined structural demands. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設護舷載入反力從0線性增至1000kN、壓縮0.30m，載入功W=Fmaxδ/2=150kJ；卸載耗散未給定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Loading work is150kJ; unloading dissipation is not specified.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「護舷載入曲線下面積全部等於不可恢復的永久耗散能量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All work under the fender loading curve is irreversibly dissipated energy.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"護舷變硬可能在相同位移產生較大峰力，老化裂損也可能改變回彈。若只核對標稱吸能而忽略反力曲線，碼頭局部構件可能承受未被納入的需求。","textEn":"A stiffer fender produces higher reaction at the same displacement, while aging cracks alter recovery. Checking nominal energy alone and ignoring the reaction curve can leave local quay components exposed to unexamined structural demands.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「護舷曲線積分」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Integrating fender response\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","護舷變硬可能在相同位移產生較大峰力，老化裂損也可能改變回彈。","加重沉箱只增加抵抗力而不會增加任何地震慣性需求。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A stiffer fender produces higher reaction at the same displacement, while aging cracks alter recovery.","Increasing caisson mass raises resistance without increasing any seismic inertia demand."],"answer":1,"explanation":"護舷變硬可能在相同位移產生較大峰力，老化裂損也可能改變回彈。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A stiffer fender produces higher reaction at the same displacement, while aging cracks alter recovery. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b289-v15-29","title":"簡化地震慣性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Simplified seismic inertia: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「簡化地震慣性」如何影響大型港口沉箱碼頭的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Simplified seismic inertia” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large-port caisson quay walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"沉箱質量在地震中產生慣性作用，但實際反應還包括土水互制、接觸非線性及背填地震土壓。等效靜力示意只能追蹤一個質量的慣性量級，不可被當成完整地震設計；加速度係數必須說明用途，不能直接拿地表峰值代替所有構件反應。 假設每米參與質量300000kg、指定水平加速度0.20g，F=ma=588.6kN/m；僅此質量慣性，不含動水與土壓。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「簡化地震慣性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Caisson mass produces seismic inertia, but actual response includes soil-water interaction, nonlinear contact and dynamic backfill action. An equivalent-static illustration tracks one mass contribution only, not complete seismic design. The acceleration coefficient needs an explicit purpose rather than substituting peak ground acceleration directly for the response of every structural component and interacting material domain. Assume participating mass300000kg per metre and selected horizontal acceleration0.20g. F=ma=588.6kN/m includes only this mass inertia, not dynamic soil or water action. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Simplified seismic inertia” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「加重沉箱只增加抵抗力而不會增加任何地震慣性需求。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Increasing caisson mass raises resistance without increasing any seismic inertia demand.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「簡化地震慣性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Simplified seismic inertia”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-29-k1","title":"簡化地震慣性","titleEn":"Simplified seismic inertia","text":"沉箱質量在地震中產生慣性作用，但實際反應還包括土水互制、接觸非線性及背填地震土壓。等效靜力示意只能追蹤一個質量的慣性量級，不可被當成完整地震設計；加速度係數必須說明用途，不能直接拿地表峰值代替所有構件反應。","textEn":"Caisson mass produces seismic inertia, but actual response includes soil-water interaction, nonlinear contact and dynamic backfill action. An equivalent-static illustration tracks one mass contribution only, not complete seismic design.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：加重沉箱只增加抵抗力而不會增加任何地震慣性需求。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Increasing caisson mass raises resistance without increasing any seismic inertia demand. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「簡化地震慣性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Simplified seismic inertia\" is correct?","options":["加重沉箱只增加抵抗力而不會增加任何地震慣性需求。","全碼頭平均沉陷不大即可保證起重機軌道不會扭曲。","沉箱質量在地震中產生慣性作用，但實際反應還包括土水互制、接觸非線性及背填地震土壓。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing caisson mass raises resistance without increasing any seismic inertia demand.","Small average quay settlement guarantees that crane rails cannot distort.","Caisson mass produces seismic inertia, but actual response includes soil-water interaction, nonlinear contact and dynamic backfill action."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沉箱質量在地震中產生慣性作用，但實際反應還包括土水互制、接觸非線性及背填地震土壓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Caisson mass produces seismic inertia, but actual response includes soil-water interaction, nonlinear contact and dynamic backfill action. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b289-v15-30","title":"簡化地震慣性：定量估算","titleEn":"Simplified seismic inertia: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「簡化地震慣性」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Simplified seismic inertia” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設每米參與質量300000kg、指定水平加速度0.20g，F=ma=588.6kN/m；僅此質量慣性，不含動水與土壓。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume participating mass300000kg per metre and selected horizontal acceleration0.20g. F=ma=588.6kN/m includes only this mass inertia, not dynamic soil or water action. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在自由體圖標出參與質量與施力位置，說明加速度是合成分析輸入而非現地建議值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark participating mass and force location on the free-body diagram and identify acceleration as a synthetic input.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設每米參與質量300000kg、指定水平加速度0.20g，F=ma=588.6kN/m；僅此質量慣性，不含動水與土壓。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume participating mass300000kg per metre and selected horizontal acceleration0.20g. F=ma=588.6kN/m includes only this mass inertia, not dynamic soil or water action.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「簡化地震慣性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Simplified seismic inertia\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","所有碼頭背填土都不需牆體變形就會自動達到主動土壓。","全場平均堆載可以直接代表貼近岸壁的所有局部輪壓。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Every quay backfill automatically reaches active pressure without any wall movement.","The terminal-average surcharge directly represents every concentrated wheel load near the quay edge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b289-v15-31","title":"簡化地震慣性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Simplified seismic inertia: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「簡化地震慣性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Simplified seismic inertia” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在自由體圖標出參與質量與施力位置，說明加速度是合成分析輸入而非現地建議值。另列動水、地基與背填作用，核對相位與組合方式，不將各自峰值任意相加。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark participating mass and force location on the free-body diagram and identify acceleration as a synthetic input. List water, foundation and backfill dynamics separately, checking phases and combination assumptions instead of arbitrarily adding unrelated peak values into one load case. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在自由體圖標出參與質量與施力位置，說明加速度是合成分析輸入而非現地建議值。另列動水、地基與背填作用，核對相位與組合方式，不將各自峰值任意相加。","observationEn":"Site practice: Mark participating mass and force location on the free-body diagram and identify acceleration as a synthetic input. List water, foundation and backfill dynamics separately, checking phases and combination assumptions instead of arbitrarily adding unrelated peak values into one load case.","failure":"注意干擾：只增加沉箱重量可能同時增加慣性需求，不能只看到抗滑增益。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Adding caisson weight can increase inertia as well as sliding resistance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在自由體圖標出參與質量與施力位置，說明加速度是合成分析輸入而非現地建議值。另列動水、地基與背填作用，核對相位與組合方式，不將各自峰值任意相加。","textEn":"Mark participating mass and force location on the free-body diagram and identify acceleration as a synthetic input. List water, foundation and backfill dynamics separately, checking phases and combination assumptions instead of arbitrarily adding unrelated peak values into one load case.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在自由體圖標出參與質量與施力位置，說明加速度是合成分析輸入而非現地建議值。另列動水、地基與背填作用，核對相位與組合方式，不將各自峰值任意相加。","textEn":"Mark participating mass and force location on the free-body diagram and identify acceleration as a synthetic input. List water, foundation and backfill dynamics separately, checking phases and combination assumptions instead of arbitrarily adding unrelated peak values into one load case.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「簡化地震慣性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Simplified seismic inertia\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在自由體圖標出參與質量與施力位置，說明加速度是合成分析輸入而非現地建議值。","基底平均壓力不大就足以證明邊緣接觸與承載都沒有問題。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Mark participating mass and force location on the free-body diagram and identify acceleration as a synthetic input.","A modest mean base pressure proves that edge contact and foundation capacity are satisfactory."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在自由體圖標出參與質量與施力位置，說明加速度是合成分析輸入而非現地建議值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark participating mass and force location on the free-body diagram and identify acceleration as a synthetic input. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b289-v15-32","title":"簡化地震慣性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Simplified seismic inertia: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「簡化地震慣性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Simplified seismic inertia” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只增加沉箱重量可能同時增加慣性需求，不能只看到抗滑增益。把土水作用漏掉或重複放入參與質量，都可能令整體地震反應和接觸壓力判讀失真。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Adding caisson weight can increase inertia as well as sliding resistance. Omitting soil-water action or counting it twice within participating mass can distort the interpreted overall seismic response and the associated distribution of contact pressure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設每米參與質量300000kg、指定水平加速度0.20g，F=ma=588.6kN/m；僅此質量慣性，不含動水與土壓。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: F=ma=588.6kN/m includes only this mass inertia, not dynamic soil or water action.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「加重沉箱只增加抵抗力而不會增加任何地震慣性需求。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Increasing caisson mass raises resistance without increasing any seismic inertia demand.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只增加沉箱重量可能同時增加慣性需求，不能只看到抗滑增益。把土水作用漏掉或重複放入參與質量，都可能令整體地震反應和接觸壓力判讀失真。","textEn":"Adding caisson weight can increase inertia as well as sliding resistance. Omitting soil-water action or counting it twice within participating mass can distort the interpreted overall seismic response and the associated distribution of contact pressure.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「簡化地震慣性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Simplified seismic inertia\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","全碼頭平均沉陷不大即可保證起重機軌道不會扭曲。","只增加沉箱重量可能同時增加慣性需求，不能只看到抗滑增益。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Small average quay settlement guarantees that crane rails cannot distort.","Adding caisson weight can increase inertia as well as sliding resistance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只增加沉箱重量可能同時增加慣性需求，不能只看到抗滑增益。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Adding caisson weight can increase inertia as well as sliding resistance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b289-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「地基壓縮與軌道」與「接縫位移與止水」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Foundation compression and rails\" and \"Joint movement and sealing\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b289-v15-33","title":"地基壓縮與軌道：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Foundation compression and rails: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「地基壓縮與軌道」如何影響大型港口沉箱碼頭的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Foundation compression and rails” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large-port caisson quay walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"碼頭地基沉陷影響岸壁和起重機軌道相對高程，均勻層壓縮只提供總沉陷的一個分量。有效應力增量、受壓層厚與拘束模數需對應同一排水狀態，另有分層和長期固結；服務功能往往由差異沉陷控制，不能只核對平均下沉值。 假設均勻層H=5m、有效應力增量100kPa、拘束模數M=10000kPa，一維s=Δσ′H/M=0.050m；非完整場址預測。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「地基壓縮與軌道」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Foundation settlement changes quay and crane-rail elevations, while uniform layer compression gives only one contribution. Effective stress increment, thickness and constrained modulus must refer to compatible drainage conditions; layering and delayed consolidation add other effects. Serviceability is often controlled by differential movement, so an average settlement alone cannot establish the geometry required by the operational equipment. Assume uniform layer5m,effective stress increment100kPa and constrained modulus10000kPa. One-dimensional s=Δσ′H/M=0.050m, not a complete site prediction. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Foundation compression and rails” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「全碼頭平均沉陷不大即可保證起重機軌道不會扭曲。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Small average quay settlement guarantees that crane rails cannot distort.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「地基壓縮與軌道」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Foundation compression and rails”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-33-k1","title":"地基壓縮與軌道","titleEn":"Foundation compression and rails","text":"碼頭地基沉陷影響岸壁和起重機軌道相對高程，均勻層壓縮只提供總沉陷的一個分量。有效應力增量、受壓層厚與拘束模數需對應同一排水狀態，另有分層和長期固結；服務功能往往由差異沉陷控制，不能只核對平均下沉值。","textEn":"Foundation settlement changes quay and crane-rail elevations, while uniform layer compression gives only one contribution. Effective stress increment, thickness and constrained modulus must refer to compatible drainage conditions; layering and delayed consolidation add other effects.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全碼頭平均沉陷不大即可保證起重機軌道不會扭曲。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Small average quay settlement guarantees that crane rails cannot distort. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地基壓縮與軌道」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Foundation compression and rails\" is correct?","options":["碼頭地基沉陷影響岸壁和起重機軌道相對高程，均勻層壓縮只提供總沉陷的一個分量。","全碼頭平均沉陷不大即可保證起重機軌道不會扭曲。","止水材料幾何應變不大就能證明所有水頭下都完全不漏水。"],"optionsEn":["Foundation settlement changes quay and crane-rail elevations, while uniform layer compression gives only one contribution.","Small average quay settlement guarantees that crane rails cannot distort.","Small geometric seal strain proves complete watertightness under every water head."],"answer":0,"explanation":"碼頭地基沉陷影響岸壁和起重機軌道相對高程，均勻層壓縮只提供總沉陷的一個分量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Foundation settlement changes quay and crane-rail elevations, while uniform layer compression gives only one contribution. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b289-v15-34","title":"地基壓縮與軌道：定量估算","titleEn":"Foundation compression and rails: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「地基壓縮與軌道」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Foundation compression and rails” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設均勻層H=5m、有效應力增量100kPa、拘束模數M=10000kPa，一維s=Δσ′H/M=0.050m；非完整場址預測。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume uniform layer5m,effective stress increment100kPa and constrained modulus10000kPa. One-dimensional s=Δσ′H/M=0.050m, not a complete site prediction. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在剖面標出受壓層與排水邊界，用試驗說明模數對應應力範圍，核對是否適用線性近似。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Identify compressible layers and drainage boundaries, justifying modulus over the relevant stress range and checking linearity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設均勻層H=5m、有效應力增量100kPa、拘束模數M=10000kPa，一維s=Δσ′H/M=0.050m；非完整場址預測。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume uniform layer5m,effective stress increment100kPa and constrained modulus10000kPa. One-dimensional s=Δσ′H/M=0.050m, not a complete site prediction.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地基壓縮與軌道」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Foundation compression and rails\", which statement holds?","options":["使用浮重度算出的有效土壓已經包含全部靜水壓力。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","回填內水位總是與外海潮位同步所以不必量測孔壓。"],"optionsEn":["Effective earth pressure calculated with submerged unit weight already includes all hydrostatic pressure.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Backfill water always follows the harbor tide exactly, making pore-pressure measurements unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b289-v15-35","title":"地基壓縮與軌道：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Foundation compression and rails: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「地基壓縮與軌道」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Foundation compression and rails” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在剖面標出受壓層與排水邊界，用試驗說明模數對應應力範圍，核對是否適用線性近似。沿岸壁和軌道佈設共同基準觀測，分解整體沉陷與差異變形並記錄時間歷程。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Identify compressible layers and drainage boundaries, justifying modulus over the relevant stress range and checking linearity. Observe wall and rails against a common datum, separating overall settlement from differential deformation and retaining their evolution through time rather than only final readings. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在剖面標出受壓層與排水邊界，用試驗說明模數對應應力範圍，核對是否適用線性近似。沿岸壁和軌道佈設共同基準觀測，分解整體沉陷與差異變形並記錄時間歷程。","observationEn":"Site practice: Identify compressible layers and drainage boundaries, justifying modulus over the relevant stress range and checking linearity. Observe wall and rails against a common datum, separating overall settlement from differential deformation and retaining their evolution through time rather than only final readings.","failure":"注意干擾：同一平均沉陷可能對應完全不同的軌道扭曲，地層厚度沿岸改變會放大局部差異。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Identical mean settlement can accompany very different rail distortion, and varying layer thickness amplifies local differences. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在剖面標出受壓層與排水邊界，用試驗說明模數對應應力範圍，核對是否適用線性近似。沿岸壁和軌道佈設共同基準觀測，分解整體沉陷與差異變形並記錄時間歷程。","textEn":"Identify compressible layers and drainage boundaries, justifying modulus over the relevant stress range and checking linearity. Observe wall and rails against a common datum, separating overall settlement from differential deformation and retaining their evolution through time rather than only final readings.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在剖面標出受壓層與排水邊界，用試驗說明模數對應應力範圍，核對是否適用線性近似。沿岸壁和軌道佈設共同基準觀測，分解整體沉陷與差異變形並記錄時間歷程。","textEn":"Identify compressible layers and drainage boundaries, justifying modulus over the relevant stress range and checking linearity. Observe wall and rails against a common datum, separating overall settlement from differential deformation and retaining their evolution through time rather than only final readings.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地基壓縮與軌道」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Foundation compression and rails\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","靠泊能量增加一倍就表示護舷峰值反力一定增加一倍。","在剖面標出受壓層與排水邊界，用試驗說明模數對應應力範圍，核對是否適用線性近似。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Doubling berthing energy necessarily doubles the fender's peak reaction force.","Identify compressible layers and drainage boundaries, justifying modulus over the relevant stress range and checking linearity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在剖面標出受壓層與排水邊界，用試驗說明模數對應應力範圍，核對是否適用線性近似。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Identify compressible layers and drainage boundaries, justifying modulus over the relevant stress range and checking linearity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b289-v15-36","title":"地基壓縮與軌道：失效診斷","titleEn":"Foundation compression and rails: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「地基壓縮與軌道」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Foundation compression and rails” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"同一平均沉陷可能對應完全不同的軌道扭曲，地層厚度沿岸改變會放大局部差異。把短期量測當最終值，又可能漏掉仍在發展的排水固結。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Identical mean settlement can accompany very different rail distortion, and varying layer thickness amplifies local differences. Treating short-term observations as final movement can also miss consolidation still progressing as excess pore pressure dissipates. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設均勻層H=5m、有效應力增量100kPa、拘束模數M=10000kPa，一維s=Δσ′H/M=0.050m；非完整場址預測。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: One-dimensional s=Δσ′H/M=0.050m, not a complete site prediction.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全碼頭平均沉陷不大即可保證起重機軌道不會扭曲。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Small average quay settlement guarantees that crane rails cannot distort.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"同一平均沉陷可能對應完全不同的軌道扭曲，地層厚度沿岸改變會放大局部差異。把短期量測當最終值，又可能漏掉仍在發展的排水固結。","textEn":"Identical mean settlement can accompany very different rail distortion, and varying layer thickness amplifies local differences. Treating short-term observations as final movement can also miss consolidation still progressing as excess pore pressure dissipates.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地基壓縮與軌道」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Foundation compression and rails\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["同一平均沉陷可能對應完全不同的軌道扭曲，地層厚度沿岸改變會放大局部差異。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","止水材料幾何應變不大就能證明所有水頭下都完全不漏水。"],"optionsEn":["Identical mean settlement can accompany very different rail distortion, and varying layer thickness amplifies local differences.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Small geometric seal strain proves complete watertightness under every water head."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同一平均沉陷可能對應完全不同的軌道扭曲，地層厚度沿岸改變會放大局部差異。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Identical mean settlement can accompany very different rail distortion, and varying layer thickness amplifies local differences. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b289-v15-37","title":"接縫位移與止水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Joint movement and sealing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「接縫位移與止水」如何影響大型港口沉箱碼頭的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Joint movement and sealing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Large-port caisson quay walls”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"相鄰沉箱接縫需要容納溫度、沉陷及水平變位，名義縫寬並不直接代表止水材料可用變形。軸向伸長應變只是幾何量，材料壓縮、剪切和黏結還要靠適用試驗；水密功能亦受水頭和缺陷控制，不能將應變計算當成漏水性能預測。 假設止水材料有效標距500mm、單軸伸長15mm，工程應變ε=15/500=0.030即3%；不含剪切或水密評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「接縫位移與止水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Joints between caissons accommodate temperature, settlement and horizontal movement, but nominal gap width is not the permissible movement of a seal. Axial strain is geometric; compression, shear and adhesion require relevant material tests. Watertightness also depends on head and defects, so a strain calculation cannot predict leakage performance or qualify a joint for all displacement combinations. Assume effective seal gauge length500mm and uniaxial extension15mm. Engineering strainε=0.030=3%, excluding shear and watertightness evaluation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Joint movement and sealing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「止水材料幾何應變不大就能證明所有水頭下都完全不漏水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Small geometric seal strain proves complete watertightness under every water head.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「接縫位移與止水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Joint movement and sealing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-37-k1","title":"接縫位移與止水","titleEn":"Joint movement and sealing","text":"相鄰沉箱接縫需要容納溫度、沉陷及水平變位，名義縫寬並不直接代表止水材料可用變形。軸向伸長應變只是幾何量，材料壓縮、剪切和黏結還要靠適用試驗；水密功能亦受水頭和缺陷控制，不能將應變計算當成漏水性能預測。","textEn":"Joints between caissons accommodate temperature, settlement and horizontal movement, but nominal gap width is not the permissible movement of a seal. Axial strain is geometric; compression, shear and adhesion require relevant material tests.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：止水材料幾何應變不大就能證明所有水頭下都完全不漏水。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Small geometric seal strain proves complete watertightness under every water head. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接縫位移與止水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Joint movement and sealing\" is correct?","options":["止水材料幾何應變不大就能證明所有水頭下都完全不漏水。","相鄰沉箱接縫需要容納溫度、沉陷及水平變位，名義縫寬並不直接代表止水材料可用變形。","所有碼頭背填土都不需牆體變形就會自動達到主動土壓。"],"optionsEn":["Small geometric seal strain proves complete watertightness under every water head.","Joints between caissons accommodate temperature, settlement and horizontal movement, but nominal gap width is not the permissible movement of a seal.","Every quay backfill automatically reaches active pressure without any wall movement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相鄰沉箱接縫需要容納溫度、沉陷及水平變位，名義縫寬並不直接代表止水材料可用變形。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Joints between caissons accommodate temperature, settlement and horizontal movement, but nominal gap width is not the permissible movement of a seal. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b289-v15-38","title":"接縫位移與止水：定量估算","titleEn":"Joint movement and sealing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「接縫位移與止水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Joint movement and sealing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設止水材料有效標距500mm、單軸伸長15mm，工程應變ε=15/500=0.030即3%；不含剪切或水密評估。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume effective seal gauge length500mm and uniaxial extension15mm. Engineering strainε=0.030=3%, excluding shear and watertightness evaluation. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：標定止水有效變形段而非任意表面長度，同步量接縫開口、剪切及相對轉角。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Identify the actual deforming gauge length and measure opening, shear and relative rotation together.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設止水材料有效標距500mm、單軸伸長15mm，工程應變ε=15/500=0.030即3%；不含剪切或水密評估。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume effective seal gauge length500mm and uniaxial extension15mm. Engineering strainε=0.030=3%, excluding shear and watertightness evaluation.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接縫位移與止水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Joint movement and sealing\", which statement holds?","options":["全場平均堆載可以直接代表貼近岸壁的所有局部輪壓。","基底平均壓力不大就足以證明邊緣接觸與承載都沒有問題。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["The terminal-average surcharge directly represents every concentrated wheel load near the quay edge.","A modest mean base pressure proves that edge contact and foundation capacity are satisfactory.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b289-v15-39","title":"接縫位移與止水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Joint movement and sealing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「接縫位移與止水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Joint movement and sealing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"標定止水有效變形段而非任意表面長度，同步量接縫開口、剪切及相對轉角。將量測路徑與材料試驗包絡比較，記錄水頭和漏水位置，保留不能由單軸模型代表的組合。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Identify the actual deforming gauge length and measure opening, shear and relative rotation together. Compare the observed movement path with material test envelopes, recording head and leakage location and retaining combinations that the uniaxial illustration does not represent. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：標定止水有效變形段而非任意表面長度，同步量接縫開口、剪切及相對轉角。將量測路徑與材料試驗包絡比較，記錄水頭和漏水位置，保留不能由單軸模型代表的組合。","observationEn":"Site practice: Identify the actual deforming gauge length and measure opening, shear and relative rotation together. Compare the observed movement path with material test envelopes, recording head and leakage location and retaining combinations that the uniaxial illustration does not represent.","failure":"注意干擾：把整條埋入長度當成有效標距會低估局部應變，界面脫黏又可能在材料仍完整時形成水路。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using the entire embedded length as deforming gauge length understates local strain, while debonding creates a water path even with intact material. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"標定止水有效變形段而非任意表面長度，同步量接縫開口、剪切及相對轉角。將量測路徑與材料試驗包絡比較，記錄水頭和漏水位置，保留不能由單軸模型代表的組合。","textEn":"Identify the actual deforming gauge length and measure opening, shear and relative rotation together. Compare the observed movement path with material test envelopes, recording head and leakage location and retaining combinations that the uniaxial illustration does not represent.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"標定止水有效變形段而非任意表面長度，同步量接縫開口、剪切及相對轉角。將量測路徑與材料試驗包絡比較，記錄水頭和漏水位置，保留不能由單軸模型代表的組合。","textEn":"Identify the actual deforming gauge length and measure opening, shear and relative rotation together. Compare the observed movement path with material test envelopes, recording head and leakage location and retaining combinations that the uniaxial illustration does not represent.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接縫位移與止水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Joint movement and sealing\"?","options":["標定止水有效變形段而非任意表面長度，同步量接縫開口、剪切及相對轉角。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","護舷載入曲線下面積全部等於不可恢復的永久耗散能量。"],"optionsEn":["Identify the actual deforming gauge length and measure opening, shear and relative rotation together.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","All work under the fender loading curve is irreversibly dissipated energy."],"answer":0,"explanation":"標定止水有效變形段而非任意表面長度，同步量接縫開口、剪切及相對轉角。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Identify the actual deforming gauge length and measure opening, shear and relative rotation together. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b289-v15-40","title":"接縫位移與止水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Joint movement and sealing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"prerequisiteIds":["b289-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「接縫位移與止水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Joint movement and sealing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把整條埋入長度當成有效標距會低估局部應變，界面脫黏又可能在材料仍完整時形成水路。只有外觀縫寬資料，無法辨識隱藏的剪切和背面滲漏。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using the entire embedded length as deforming gauge length understates local strain, while debonding creates a water path even with intact material. Visible gap width alone cannot identify hidden shear or leakage behind the joint. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設止水材料有效標距500mm、單軸伸長15mm，工程應變ε=15/500=0.030即3%；不含剪切或水密評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Engineering strainε=0.030=3%, excluding shear and watertightness evaluation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「止水材料幾何應變不大就能證明所有水頭下都完全不漏水。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Small geometric seal strain proves complete watertightness under every water head.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b289-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把整條埋入長度當成有效標距會低估局部應變，界面脫黏又可能在材料仍完整時形成水路。只有外觀縫寬資料，無法辨識隱藏的剪切和背面滲漏。","textEn":"Using the entire embedded length as deforming gauge length understates local strain, while debonding creates a water path even with intact material. Visible gap width alone cannot identify hidden shear or leakage behind the joint.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]},{"id":"b289-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接縫位移與止水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Joint movement and sealing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把整條埋入長度當成有效標距會低估局部應變，界面脫黏又可能在材料仍完整時形成水路。","所有碼頭背填土都不需牆體變形就會自動達到主動土壓。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using the entire embedded length as deforming gauge length understates local strain, while debonding creates a water path even with intact material.","Every quay backfill automatically reaches active pressure without any wall movement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把整條埋入長度當成有效標距會低估局部應變，界面脫黏又可能在材料仍完整時形成水路。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using the entire embedded length as deforming gauge length understates local strain, while debonding creates a water path even with intact material. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-tuas-port","v15s-tuas","v15s-tuas-last","v15s-kamaishi"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b290","title":"棧橋式碼頭樁基","titleEn":"Pile-supported pier foundations","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"由海床調查到樁群變形與耐久追蹤棧橋碼頭荷載。課程從邊界辨識與資料整理走到水理量化、構造介面及驗證紀錄；每一步把計算結果連回可量測的證據。十個不同單元分別處理關鍵機制，不以名義尺寸或單一通過率代替整體工程判斷，並明列合成算例與現地資料的差別。","summaryEn":"Trace pile-supported pier loads from seabed investigation to group deformation and durability. The course moves from boundary identification and evidence to hydraulic quantification, structural interfaces and verification records. Ten distinct units connect each calculated quantity to measurable evidence. Nominal geometry or a single pass rate does not establish whole-system performance, and synthetic teaching examples remain separate from field observations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-coasts","subcategoryTitle":"海岸、港灣與水資源韌性","subcategoryTitleEn":"Coasts, ports and water-resource resilience","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-coasts","learningTags":["water","water-coasts","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-port","architectureNodes":[["鋼管截面與軸應力","Steel-pipe section and axial stress"],["樁側阻力積分","Integrating shaft resistance"],["樁身彈性縮短","Elastic pile shortening"],["沖刷與側向剛度","Scour and lateral stiffness"],["循環需求與疲勞","Cyclic demand and fatigue"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-port","labels":["鋼管截面與軸應力","樁側阻力積分","樁身彈性縮短","沖刷與側向剛度","循環需求與疲勞"],"labelsEn":["Steel-pipe section and axial stress","Integrating shaft resistance","Elastic pile shortening","Scour and lateral stiffness","Cyclic demand and fatigue"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為原創合成算例，不是地標工程的實測或推薦操作值。教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設外徑1m、內徑0.96m，A=π(Do²−Di²)/4=0.061575m²；軸力2000kN時平均σ=32.48MPa。假設外徑1m增10%至1.1m、壁厚固定20mm且軸力固定，面積由0.061575增至0.067858m²，平均應力由32.48降至29.47MPa；未代表地工承載同步增加。重新計算前先列固定條件、單位、適用尺度及可能失效的邊界。把模型敏感度與測量誤差分開，不能將單一參數變化直接當成工程風險或壽命比例。比較兩次結果後，記錄還需要哪些獨立證據，並由負責專業人員判斷適用性。","textEn":"This original synthetic example is neither a landmark measurement nor a recommended operating value. Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume outer diameter1m and inner0.96m. Annular A=0.061575m²; axial load2000kN gives mean stress32.48MPa, excluding bending and buckling. Increasing outer diameter10% from1to1.1m at fixed20mm thickness and load raises area from0.061575 to0.067858m² and lowers mean stress from32.48 to29.47MPa, without an equivalent geotechnical capacity claim. Before recalculating, list fixed conditions, units, applicable scale and boundaries that could fail. Separate model sensitivity from measurement uncertainty: a parameter change does not directly give a proportional change in engineering risk or service life. Compare the results, record independent evidence still needed, and have the responsible specialist determine applicability.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b290-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「鋼管截面與軸應力」與「樁端面積與土阻」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Steel-pipe section and axial stress\" and \"Toe area and soil resistance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b290-v15-01","title":"鋼管截面與軸應力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Steel-pipe section and axial stress: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「鋼管截面與軸應力」如何影響棧橋式碼頭樁基的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Steel-pipe section and axial stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pile-supported pier foundations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海上鋼管樁的空心截面不能用外包圓面積計材料應力，內外徑與腐蝕減薄都會改變承載面。平均軸應力只是彈性需求，局部屈曲、焊接細節和彎矩需另行處理；打設與服務狀態的作用也不同，不能以一個低平均值證明所有階段可靠。 假設外徑1m、內徑0.96m，A=π(Do²−Di²)/4=0.061575m²；軸力2000kN時平均σ=32.48MPa。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鋼管截面與軸應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A hollow steel pile requires annular material area rather than its outer circular footprint. Diameters and corrosion loss change that area. Mean axial stress is an elastic demand only; local buckling, weld details and bending remain separate. Installation and service actions also differ, so one low average stress cannot demonstrate reliability throughout every stage of the pile's use. Assume outer diameter1m and inner0.96m. Annular A=0.061575m²; axial load2000kN gives mean stress32.48MPa, excluding bending and buckling. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Steel-pipe section and axial stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「空心鋼管樁的材料受壓面積就是整個外徑圓面積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The steel material area of a hollow pile equals its entire outer circular footprint.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「鋼管截面與軸應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Steel-pipe section and axial stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-01-k1","title":"鋼管截面與軸應力","titleEn":"Steel-pipe section and axial stress","text":"海上鋼管樁的空心截面不能用外包圓面積計材料應力，內外徑與腐蝕減薄都會改變承載面。平均軸應力只是彈性需求，局部屈曲、焊接細節和彎矩需另行處理；打設與服務狀態的作用也不同，不能以一個低平均值證明所有階段可靠。","textEn":"A hollow steel pile requires annular material area rather than its outer circular footprint. Diameters and corrosion loss change that area.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：空心鋼管樁的材料受壓面積就是整個外徑圓面積。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The steel material area of a hollow pile equals its entire outer circular footprint. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋼管截面與軸應力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Steel-pipe section and axial stress\" is correct?","options":["空心鋼管樁的材料受壓面積就是整個外徑圓面積。","海上鋼管樁的空心截面不能用外包圓面積計材料應力，內外徑與腐蝕減薄都會改變承載面。","開口管樁無論土塞狀態都具有與封閉端相同的有效端面積。"],"optionsEn":["The steel material area of a hollow pile equals its entire outer circular footprint.","A hollow steel pile requires annular material area rather than its outer circular footprint.","Every open-ended pipe pile has the same effective toe area as a closed pile regardless of plugging."],"answer":1,"explanation":"海上鋼管樁的空心截面不能用外包圓面積計材料應力，內外徑與腐蝕減薄都會改變承載面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A hollow steel pile requires annular material area rather than its outer circular footprint. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b290-v15-02","title":"鋼管截面與軸應力：定量估算","titleEn":"Steel-pipe section and axial stress: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼管截面與軸應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Steel-pipe section and axial stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設外徑1m、內徑0.96m，A=π(Do²−Di²)/4=0.061575m²；軸力2000kN時平均σ=32.48MPa。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume outer diameter1m and inner0.96m. Annular A=0.061575m²; axial load2000kN gives mean stress32.48MPa, excluding bending and buckling. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對實際壁厚與內外徑，量測多方向以辨識橢圓度和局部減薄，保留焊縫位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check actual thickness and diameters in several directions for ovality and local loss, retaining weld locations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設外徑1m、內徑0.96m，A=π(Do²−Di²)/4=0.061575m²；軸力2000kN時平均σ=32.48MPa。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume outer diameter1m and inner0.96m. Annular A=0.061575m²; axial load2000kN gives mean stress32.48MPa, excluding bending and buckling.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋼管截面與軸應力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Steel-pipe section and axial stress\", which statement holds?","options":["只要樁數相同每支樁在任何偏心荷載下都承擔相同軸力。","海床泥面在所有情況下都可直接視為樁身完全固定端。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Equal pile count means every pile carries identical axial force under any eccentric loading.","The seabed mudline can always be treated as a perfectly fixed pile support.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b290-v15-03","title":"鋼管截面與軸應力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Steel-pipe section and axial stress: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼管截面與軸應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Steel-pipe section and axial stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對實際壁厚與內外徑，量測多方向以辨識橢圓度和局部減薄，保留焊縫位置。將軸力、彎矩與施工動載分開列示，確認材料截面和土端阻用的承壓面積沒有混用。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check actual thickness and diameters in several directions for ovality and local loss, retaining weld locations. List axial, bending and installation actions separately and confirm that steel material area is not confused with the area used for geotechnical toe resistance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：核對實際壁厚與內外徑，量測多方向以辨識橢圓度和局部減薄，保留焊縫位置。將軸力、彎矩與施工動載分開列示，確認材料截面和土端阻用的承壓面積沒有混用。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check actual thickness and diameters in several directions for ovality and local loss, retaining weld locations. List axial, bending and installation actions separately and confirm that steel material area is not confused with the area used for geotechnical toe resistance.","failure":"注意干擾：用外包面積除軸力會大幅低估空心鋼管應力，平均壁厚又可能掩蓋局部凹蝕。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Dividing by outer footprint grossly understates hollow-pile stress, while average thickness hides local pitting. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對實際壁厚與內外徑，量測多方向以辨識橢圓度和局部減薄，保留焊縫位置。將軸力、彎矩與施工動載分開列示，確認材料截面和土端阻用的承壓面積沒有混用。","textEn":"Check actual thickness and diameters in several directions for ovality and local loss, retaining weld locations. List axial, bending and installation actions separately and confirm that steel material area is not confused with the area used for geotechnical toe resistance.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"核對實際壁厚與內外徑，量測多方向以辨識橢圓度和局部減薄，保留焊縫位置。將軸力、彎矩與施工動載分開列示，確認材料截面和土端阻用的承壓面積沒有混用。","textEn":"Check actual thickness and diameters in several directions for ovality and local loss, retaining weld locations. List axial, bending and installation actions separately and confirm that steel material area is not confused with the area used for geotechnical toe resistance.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋼管截面與軸應力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Steel-pipe section and axial stress\"?","options":["核對實際壁厚與內外徑，量測多方向以辨識橢圓度和局部減薄，保留焊縫位置。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","穩定流拖曳算式已經自動包含波浪造成的全部慣性作用。"],"optionsEn":["Check actual thickness and diameters in several directions for ovality and local loss, retaining weld locations.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The steady-current drag formula automatically includes all wave-induced inertia effects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對實際壁厚與內外徑，量測多方向以辨識橢圓度和局部減薄，保留焊縫位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check actual thickness and diameters in several directions for ovality and local loss, retaining weld locations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b290-v15-04","title":"鋼管截面與軸應力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Steel-pipe section and axial stress: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼管截面與軸應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Steel-pipe section and axial stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用外包面積除軸力會大幅低估空心鋼管應力，平均壁厚又可能掩蓋局部凹蝕。材料仍未屈服時，細薄區已可能因局部穩定問題控制反應。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Dividing by outer footprint grossly understates hollow-pile stress, while average thickness hides local pitting. A thin damaged region can govern local stability even when the average material stress remains below a nominal yield level. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設外徑1m、內徑0.96m，A=π(Do²−Di²)/4=0.061575m²；軸力2000kN時平均σ=32.48MPa。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Annular A=0.061575m²; axial load2000kN gives mean stress32.48MPa, excluding bending and buckling.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「空心鋼管樁的材料受壓面積就是整個外徑圓面積。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The steel material area of a hollow pile equals its entire outer circular footprint.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用外包面積除軸力會大幅低估空心鋼管應力，平均壁厚又可能掩蓋局部凹蝕。材料仍未屈服時，細薄區已可能因局部穩定問題控制反應。","textEn":"Dividing by outer footprint grossly understates hollow-pile stress, while average thickness hides local pitting. A thin damaged region can govern local stability even when the average material stress remains below a nominal yield level.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋼管截面與軸應力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Steel-pipe section and axial stress\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","用外包面積除軸力會大幅低估空心鋼管應力，平均壁厚又可能掩蓋局部凹蝕。","開口管樁無論土塞狀態都具有與封閉端相同的有效端面積。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Dividing by outer footprint grossly understates hollow-pile stress, while average thickness hides local pitting.","Every open-ended pipe pile has the same effective toe area as a closed pile regardless of plugging."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用外包面積除軸力會大幅低估空心鋼管應力，平均壁厚又可能掩蓋局部凹蝕。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Dividing by outer footprint grossly understates hollow-pile stress, while average thickness hides local pitting. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b290-v15-05","title":"樁端面積與土阻：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Toe area and soil resistance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「樁端面積與土阻」如何影響棧橋式碼頭樁基的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Toe area and soil resistance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pile-supported pier foundations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"樁端土阻與材料截面不同，封閉端和開口管樁是否形成土塞會影響有效承壓面積。端阻單位值必須來自場址證據和相應變位，不是可任意套用的材料強度；計算名義端阻仍須考慮打設擾動、持力層厚度與下伏弱層。 假設封閉圓端D=1m且均勻端阻qb=5MPa，Qb=qbπD²/4=3927.0kN；不直接用於未證實土塞的開口樁。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「樁端面積與土阻」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Geotechnical toe area differs from steel area, and open-ended plugging determines whether an outer footprint is mobilized. Unit resistance requires site evidence at compatible displacement rather than a freely selected material strength. Even nominal toe resistance needs review of installation disturbance, bearing-layer thickness and weaker layers below, none of which is resolved by area multiplication alone. Assume a closed circular toe1m in diameter with uniform qb=5MPa. Qb=3927.0kN; this footprint is not assumed for an unverified open-pile plug. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Toe area and soil resistance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「開口管樁無論土塞狀態都具有與封閉端相同的有效端面積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every open-ended pipe pile has the same effective toe area as a closed pile regardless of plugging.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「樁端面積與土阻」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Toe area and soil resistance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-05-k1","title":"樁端面積與土阻","titleEn":"Toe area and soil resistance","text":"樁端土阻與材料截面不同，封閉端和開口管樁是否形成土塞會影響有效承壓面積。端阻單位值必須來自場址證據和相應變位，不是可任意套用的材料強度；計算名義端阻仍須考慮打設擾動、持力層厚度與下伏弱層。","textEn":"Geotechnical toe area differs from steel area, and open-ended plugging determines whether an outer footprint is mobilized. Unit resistance requires site evidence at compatible displacement rather than a freely selected material strength.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：開口管樁無論土塞狀態都具有與封閉端相同的有效端面積。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every open-ended pipe pile has the same effective toe area as a closed pile regardless of plugging. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「樁端面積與土阻」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Toe area and soil resistance\" is correct?","options":["開口管樁無論土塞狀態都具有與封閉端相同的有效端面積。","樁側所有摩擦力都必定向上提供抵抗而不會增加軸力。","樁端土阻與材料截面不同，封閉端和開口管樁是否形成土塞會影響有效承壓面積。"],"optionsEn":["Every open-ended pipe pile has the same effective toe area as a closed pile regardless of plugging.","Every shaft-friction force necessarily acts upward and can never increase pile compression.","Geotechnical toe area differs from steel area, and open-ended plugging determines whether an outer footprint is mobilized."],"answer":2,"explanation":"樁端土阻與材料截面不同，封閉端和開口管樁是否形成土塞會影響有效承壓面積。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Geotechnical toe area differs from steel area, and open-ended plugging determines whether an outer footprint is mobilized. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b290-v15-06","title":"樁端面積與土阻：定量估算","titleEn":"Toe area and soil resistance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「樁端面積與土阻」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Toe area and soil resistance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設封閉圓端D=1m且均勻端阻qb=5MPa，Qb=qbπD²/4=3927.0kN；不直接用於未證實土塞的開口樁。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a closed circular toe1m in diameter with uniform qb=5MPa. Qb=3927.0kN; this footprint is not assumed for an unverified open-pile plug. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在地質剖面標出樁端與持力層厚度，說明端部封閉或土塞證據，核對單位端阻對應的位移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark toe depth and bearing-layer thickness, documenting closure or plugging and the displacement associated with unit resistance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設封閉圓端D=1m且均勻端阻qb=5MPa，Qb=qbπD²/4=3927.0kN；不直接用於未證實土塞的開口樁。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a closed circular toe1m in diameter with uniform qb=5MPa. Qb=3927.0kN; this footprint is not assumed for an unverified open-pile plug.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「樁端面積與土阻」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Toe area and soil resistance\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","樁頂沉陷完全來自土壤所以樁身彈性縮短永遠可以忽略。","沖刷只影響外觀而不會改變樁基水平剛度和彎矩需求。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Pile-head settlement comes entirely from soil, so elastic pile shortening can always be ignored.","Scour affects appearance only and cannot change lateral pile stiffness or bending demand."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b290-v15-07","title":"樁端面積與土阻：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Toe area and soil resistance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「樁端面積與土阻」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Toe area and soil resistance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在地質剖面標出樁端與持力層厚度，說明端部封閉或土塞證據，核對單位端阻對應的位移。比較試樁與施工紀錄，將下伏弱層與端部沉渣列入評估，不以名義直徑取代條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark toe depth and bearing-layer thickness, documenting closure or plugging and the displacement associated with unit resistance. Compare test piles and installation records, accounting for weaker underlying layers or toe debris rather than treating nominal diameter as complete evidence. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在地質剖面標出樁端與持力層厚度，說明端部封閉或土塞證據，核對單位端阻對應的位移。比較試樁與施工紀錄，將下伏弱層與端部沉渣列入評估，不以名義直徑取代條件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Mark toe depth and bearing-layer thickness, documenting closure or plugging and the displacement associated with unit resistance. Compare test piles and installation records, accounting for weaker underlying layers or toe debris rather than treating nominal diameter as complete evidence.","failure":"注意干擾：未形成土塞卻採完整圓面積會高估端阻，薄硬層下有軟層也可能發生穿透。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using full footprint without a developed plug overstates resistance, and a thin hard layer over soft ground may punch through. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在地質剖面標出樁端與持力層厚度，說明端部封閉或土塞證據，核對單位端阻對應的位移。比較試樁與施工紀錄，將下伏弱層與端部沉渣列入評估，不以名義直徑取代條件。","textEn":"Mark toe depth and bearing-layer thickness, documenting closure or plugging and the displacement associated with unit resistance. Compare test piles and installation records, accounting for weaker underlying layers or toe debris rather than treating nominal diameter as complete evidence.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在地質剖面標出樁端與持力層厚度，說明端部封閉或土塞證據，核對單位端阻對應的位移。比較試樁與施工紀錄，將下伏弱層與端部沉渣列入評估，不以名義直徑取代條件。","textEn":"Mark toe depth and bearing-layer thickness, documenting closure or plugging and the displacement associated with unit resistance. Compare test piles and installation records, accounting for weaker underlying layers or toe debris rather than treating nominal diameter as complete evidence.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「樁端面積與土阻」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Toe area and soil resistance\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在地質剖面標出樁端與持力層厚度，說明端部封閉或土塞證據，核對單位端阻對應的位移。","剩餘截面百分比必定等於鋼樁剩餘使用年限的百分比。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Mark toe depth and bearing-layer thickness, documenting closure or plugging and the displacement associated with unit resistance.","The remaining cross-sectional percentage necessarily equals the percentage of service life remaining."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在地質剖面標出樁端與持力層厚度，說明端部封閉或土塞證據，核對單位端阻對應的位移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark toe depth and bearing-layer thickness, documenting closure or plugging and the displacement associated with unit resistance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b290-v15-08","title":"樁端面積與土阻：失效診斷","titleEn":"Toe area and soil resistance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「樁端面積與土阻」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Toe area and soil resistance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未形成土塞卻採完整圓面積會高估端阻，薄硬層下有軟層也可能發生穿透。施工紀錄只達到預定深度，不能單獨證明樁端已取得假設的力學行為。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using full footprint without a developed plug overstates resistance, and a thin hard layer over soft ground may punch through. Reaching a specified depth during installation alone does not establish the assumed toe behavior or load-transfer mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設封閉圓端D=1m且均勻端阻qb=5MPa，Qb=qbπD²/4=3927.0kN；不直接用於未證實土塞的開口樁。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Qb=3927.0kN; this footprint is not assumed for an unverified open-pile plug.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「開口管樁無論土塞狀態都具有與封閉端相同的有效端面積。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every open-ended pipe pile has the same effective toe area as a closed pile regardless of plugging.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未形成土塞卻採完整圓面積會高估端阻，薄硬層下有軟層也可能發生穿透。施工紀錄只達到預定深度，不能單獨證明樁端已取得假設的力學行為。","textEn":"Using full footprint without a developed plug overstates resistance, and a thin hard layer over soft ground may punch through. Reaching a specified depth during installation alone does not establish the assumed toe behavior or load-transfer mechanism.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「樁端面積與土阻」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Toe area and soil resistance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","樁側所有摩擦力都必定向上提供抵抗而不會增加軸力。","未形成土塞卻採完整圓面積會高估端阻，薄硬層下有軟層也可能發生穿透。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Every shaft-friction force necessarily acts upward and can never increase pile compression.","Using full footprint without a developed plug overstates resistance, and a thin hard layer over soft ground may punch through."],"answer":2,"explanation":"未形成土塞卻採完整圓面積會高估端阻，薄硬層下有軟層也可能發生穿透。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using full footprint without a developed plug overstates resistance, and a thin hard layer over soft ground may punch through. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b290-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「樁側阻力積分」與「樁群偏心分配」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Integrating shaft resistance\" and \"Eccentric pile-group distribution\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b290-v15-09","title":"樁側阻力積分：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Integrating shaft resistance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「樁側阻力積分」如何影響棧橋式碼頭樁基的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Integrating shaft resistance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pile-supported pier foundations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"樁側剪力沿土層分布，平均值乘周長和長度只適合所定義區段。土體位移相對樁體的方向決定正側阻或負摩擦，不能把所有剪力都列為抵抗；側阻與端阻動員位移也不同，直接加總極值未必符合相同變形狀態。 假設D=1m、有效段長20m、均勻正側阻τ=50kPa，Qs=πτDL=3141.6kN；不含負摩擦或端阻。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「樁側阻力積分」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shaft shear varies by soil layer, and mean resistance times perimeter and length applies only to a defined segment. Relative soil-pile movement determines positive resistance or downdrag, so not all shear is beneficial. Shaft and toe resistance mobilize at different displacements, meaning their individual maxima may not coexist in a compatible overall load-transfer state for the pile. Assume diameter1m,effective length20m and uniform positive shaft shear50kPa. Qs=πτDL=3141.6kN, excluding downdrag and toe resistance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Integrating shaft resistance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「樁側所有摩擦力都必定向上提供抵抗而不會增加軸力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every shaft-friction force necessarily acts upward and can never increase pile compression.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「樁側阻力積分」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Integrating shaft resistance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-09-k1","title":"樁側阻力積分","titleEn":"Integrating shaft resistance","text":"樁側剪力沿土層分布，平均值乘周長和長度只適合所定義區段。土體位移相對樁體的方向決定正側阻或負摩擦，不能把所有剪力都列為抵抗；側阻與端阻動員位移也不同，直接加總極值未必符合相同變形狀態。","textEn":"Shaft shear varies by soil layer, and mean resistance times perimeter and length applies only to a defined segment. Relative soil-pile movement determines positive resistance or downdrag, so not all shear is beneficial.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：樁側所有摩擦力都必定向上提供抵抗而不會增加軸力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every shaft-friction force necessarily acts upward and can never increase pile compression. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「樁側阻力積分」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Integrating shaft resistance\" is correct?","options":["樁側剪力沿土層分布，平均值乘周長和長度只適合所定義區段。","樁側所有摩擦力都必定向上提供抵抗而不會增加軸力。","只要樁數相同每支樁在任何偏心荷載下都承擔相同軸力。"],"optionsEn":["Shaft shear varies by soil layer, and mean resistance times perimeter and length applies only to a defined segment.","Every shaft-friction force necessarily acts upward and can never increase pile compression.","Equal pile count means every pile carries identical axial force under any eccentric loading."],"answer":0,"explanation":"樁側剪力沿土層分布，平均值乘周長和長度只適合所定義區段。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shaft shear varies by soil layer, and mean resistance times perimeter and length applies only to a defined segment. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b290-v15-10","title":"樁側阻力積分：定量估算","titleEn":"Integrating shaft resistance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「樁側阻力積分」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Integrating shaft resistance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設D=1m、有效段長20m、均勻正側阻τ=50kPa，Qs=πτDL=3141.6kN；不含負摩擦或端阻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume diameter1m,effective length20m and uniform positive shaft shear50kPa. Qs=πτDL=3141.6kN, excluding downdrag and toe resistance. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按地層分段列出周長、長度與剪力方向，核對地下水及回填沉陷對相對位移的影響。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Divide the shaft by layer, listing perimeter, length and shear direction, and examine groundwater or fill settlement effects on relative movement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設D=1m、有效段長20m、均勻正側阻τ=50kPa，Qs=πτDL=3141.6kN；不含負摩擦或端阻。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume diameter1m,effective length20m and uniform positive shaft shear50kPa. Qs=πτDL=3141.6kN, excluding downdrag and toe resistance.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「樁側阻力積分」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Integrating shaft resistance\", which statement holds?","options":["海床泥面在所有情況下都可直接視為樁身完全固定端。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","穩定流拖曳算式已經自動包含波浪造成的全部慣性作用。"],"optionsEn":["The seabed mudline can always be treated as a perfectly fixed pile support.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The steady-current drag formula automatically includes all wave-induced inertia effects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b290-v15-11","title":"樁側阻力積分：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Integrating shaft resistance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「樁側阻力積分」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Integrating shaft resistance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按地層分段列出周長、長度與剪力方向，核對地下水及回填沉陷對相對位移的影響。利用應變或載重試驗重建傳力，避免把未動員的側阻和不同位移下端阻直接疊加。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Divide the shaft by layer, listing perimeter, length and shear direction, and examine groundwater or fill settlement effects on relative movement. Reconstruct transfer from strain or load testing, avoiding sums of unmobilized shaft resistance and toe resistance at incompatible displacements. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：按地層分段列出周長、長度與剪力方向，核對地下水及回填沉陷對相對位移的影響。利用應變或載重試驗重建傳力，避免把未動員的側阻和不同位移下端阻直接疊加。","observationEn":"Site practice: Divide the shaft by layer, listing perimeter, length and shear direction, and examine groundwater or fill settlement effects on relative movement. Reconstruct transfer from strain or load testing, avoiding sums of unmobilized shaft resistance and toe resistance at incompatible displacements.","failure":"注意干擾：新填土沉降可能把原本預期的正摩擦變為下拉，樁側土受擾也使平均參數失準。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Settling new fill can turn expected positive friction into downdrag, while installation disturbance invalidates a mean parameter. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按地層分段列出周長、長度與剪力方向，核對地下水及回填沉陷對相對位移的影響。利用應變或載重試驗重建傳力，避免把未動員的側阻和不同位移下端阻直接疊加。","textEn":"Divide the shaft by layer, listing perimeter, length and shear direction, and examine groundwater or fill settlement effects on relative movement. Reconstruct transfer from strain or load testing, avoiding sums of unmobilized shaft resistance and toe resistance at incompatible displacements.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"按地層分段列出周長、長度與剪力方向，核對地下水及回填沉陷對相對位移的影響。利用應變或載重試驗重建傳力，避免把未動員的側阻和不同位移下端阻直接疊加。","textEn":"Divide the shaft by layer, listing perimeter, length and shear direction, and examine groundwater or fill settlement effects on relative movement. Reconstruct transfer from strain or load testing, avoiding sums of unmobilized shaft resistance and toe resistance at incompatible displacements.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「樁側阻力積分」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Integrating shaft resistance\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","Miner損傷比等於一半就保證還能再使用同樣長的時間。","按地層分段列出周長、長度與剪力方向，核對地下水及回填沉陷對相對位移的影響。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A Miner damage fraction of one half guarantees an equally long remaining service period.","Divide the shaft by layer, listing perimeter, length and shear direction, and examine groundwater or fill settlement effects on relative movement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"按地層分段列出周長、長度與剪力方向，核對地下水及回填沉陷對相對位移的影響。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Divide the shaft by layer, listing perimeter, length and shear direction, and examine groundwater or fill settlement effects on relative movement. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b290-v15-12","title":"樁側阻力積分：失效診斷","titleEn":"Integrating shaft resistance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「樁側阻力積分」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Integrating shaft resistance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"新填土沉降可能把原本預期的正摩擦變為下拉，樁側土受擾也使平均參數失準。若仍把整段剪力列成有利作用，樁內最大軸力可能被低估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Settling new fill can turn expected positive friction into downdrag, while installation disturbance invalidates a mean parameter. Continuing to count all shaft shear as favorable can understate the maximum axial force within the pile itself. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設D=1m、有效段長20m、均勻正側阻τ=50kPa，Qs=πτDL=3141.6kN；不含負摩擦或端阻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Qs=πτDL=3141.6kN, excluding downdrag and toe resistance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「樁側所有摩擦力都必定向上提供抵抗而不會增加軸力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every shaft-friction force necessarily acts upward and can never increase pile compression.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"新填土沉降可能把原本預期的正摩擦變為下拉，樁側土受擾也使平均參數失準。若仍把整段剪力列成有利作用，樁內最大軸力可能被低估。","textEn":"Settling new fill can turn expected positive friction into downdrag, while installation disturbance invalidates a mean parameter. Continuing to count all shaft shear as favorable can understate the maximum axial force within the pile itself.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「樁側阻力積分」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Integrating shaft resistance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["新填土沉降可能把原本預期的正摩擦變為下拉，樁側土受擾也使平均參數失準。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要樁數相同每支樁在任何偏心荷載下都承擔相同軸力。"],"optionsEn":["Settling new fill can turn expected positive friction into downdrag, while installation disturbance invalidates a mean parameter.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Equal pile count means every pile carries identical axial force under any eccentric loading."],"answer":0,"explanation":"新填土沉降可能把原本預期的正摩擦變為下拉，樁側土受擾也使平均參數失準。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Settling new fill can turn expected positive friction into downdrag, while installation disturbance invalidates a mean parameter. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b290-v15-13","title":"樁群偏心分配：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Eccentric pile-group distribution: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「樁群偏心分配」如何影響棧橋式碼頭樁基的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Eccentric pile-group distribution” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pile-supported pier foundations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"剛性承台在等軸向剛度假設下可用線性分配追蹤軸力與力矩，但土層差異、斜樁及承台柔性會改變分擔。各樁反力需要同時滿足總力及總矩，並檢查是否有拉拔；群樁效率和地盤整體破壞不能由單樁算式直接保證。 假設4支等剛度樁、兩支x=+3m兩支−3m，P=12000kN、M=12000kN·m，Ni=P/4+Mxi/Σx²，得4000與2000kN。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「樁群偏心分配」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A rigid cap over equal axial stiffnesses permits linear sharing of force and moment. Different soils, battered piles and cap flexibility alter that distribution. Reactions must satisfy both total force and moment and be checked for uplift. Neither group efficiency nor overall ground failure is established by a single-pile resistance equation or a convenient equal-load assumption alone. Assume four equal-stiffness piles, two each at x=±3m,P=12000kN,M=12000kN·m. Ni=P/4+Mxi/Σx² gives4000 and2000kN. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Eccentric pile-group distribution” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要樁數相同每支樁在任何偏心荷載下都承擔相同軸力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal pile count means every pile carries identical axial force under any eccentric loading.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「樁群偏心分配」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Eccentric pile-group distribution”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-13-k1","title":"樁群偏心分配","titleEn":"Eccentric pile-group distribution","text":"剛性承台在等軸向剛度假設下可用線性分配追蹤軸力與力矩，但土層差異、斜樁及承台柔性會改變分擔。各樁反力需要同時滿足總力及總矩，並檢查是否有拉拔；群樁效率和地盤整體破壞不能由單樁算式直接保證。","textEn":"A rigid cap over equal axial stiffnesses permits linear sharing of force and moment. Different soils, battered piles and cap flexibility alter that distribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要樁數相同每支樁在任何偏心荷載下都承擔相同軸力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal pile count means every pile carries identical axial force under any eccentric loading. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「樁群偏心分配」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Eccentric pile-group distribution\" is correct?","options":["只要樁數相同每支樁在任何偏心荷載下都承擔相同軸力。","剛性承台在等軸向剛度假設下可用線性分配追蹤軸力與力矩，但土層差異、斜樁及承台柔性會改變分擔。","樁頂沉陷完全來自土壤所以樁身彈性縮短永遠可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Equal pile count means every pile carries identical axial force under any eccentric loading.","A rigid cap over equal axial stiffnesses permits linear sharing of force and moment.","Pile-head settlement comes entirely from soil, so elastic pile shortening can always be ignored."],"answer":1,"explanation":"剛性承台在等軸向剛度假設下可用線性分配追蹤軸力與力矩，但土層差異、斜樁及承台柔性會改變分擔。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A rigid cap over equal axial stiffnesses permits linear sharing of force and moment. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b290-v15-14","title":"樁群偏心分配：定量估算","titleEn":"Eccentric pile-group distribution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「樁群偏心分配」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Eccentric pile-group distribution” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設4支等剛度樁、兩支x=+3m兩支−3m，P=12000kN、M=12000kN·m，Ni=P/4+Mxi/Σx²，得4000與2000kN。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume four equal-stiffness piles, two each at x=±3m,P=12000kN,M=12000kN·m. Ni=P/4+Mxi/Σx² gives4000 and2000kN. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：畫樁位坐標並核對力矩軸，逐樁求反力後重新加總力及力矩。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot pile coordinates and moment axis, then independently sum calculated reactions and moments.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設4支等剛度樁、兩支x=+3m兩支−3m，P=12000kN、M=12000kN·m，Ni=P/4+Mxi/Σx²，得4000與2000kN。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume four equal-stiffness piles, two each at x=±3m,P=12000kN,M=12000kN·m. Ni=P/4+Mxi/Σx² gives4000 and2000kN.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「樁群偏心分配」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Eccentric pile-group distribution\", which statement holds?","options":["沖刷只影響外觀而不會改變樁基水平剛度和彎矩需求。","剩餘截面百分比必定等於鋼樁剩餘使用年限的百分比。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Scour affects appearance only and cannot change lateral pile stiffness or bending demand.","The remaining cross-sectional percentage necessarily equals the percentage of service life remaining.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b290-v15-15","title":"樁群偏心分配：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Eccentric pile-group distribution: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「樁群偏心分配」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Eccentric pile-group distribution” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"畫樁位坐標並核對力矩軸，逐樁求反力後重新加總力及力矩。用地層和試驗證據檢查等剛度，另列承台柔性與樁群影響，不能只因平衡成立就接受全部反力分配。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot pile coordinates and moment axis, then independently sum calculated reactions and moments. Test equal stiffness against geology and pile evidence, reviewing cap flexibility and group effects separately because satisfying equilibrium does not prove that the assumed distribution is physically realistic. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫樁位坐標並核對力矩軸，逐樁求反力後重新加總力及力矩。用地層和試驗證據檢查等剛度，另列承台柔性與樁群影響，不能只因平衡成立就接受全部反力分配。","observationEn":"Site practice: Plot pile coordinates and moment axis, then independently sum calculated reactions and moments. Test equal stiffness against geology and pile evidence, reviewing cap flexibility and group effects separately because satisfying equilibrium does not prove that the assumed distribution is physically realistic.","failure":"注意干擾：某支樁剛度下降會把荷載移轉給其他樁，算術平均仍可能掩蓋局部超載。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A softened pile transfers load to neighbors while a simple average hides concentration. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"畫樁位坐標並核對力矩軸，逐樁求反力後重新加總力及力矩。用地層和試驗證據檢查等剛度，另列承台柔性與樁群影響，不能只因平衡成立就接受全部反力分配。","textEn":"Plot pile coordinates and moment axis, then independently sum calculated reactions and moments. Test equal stiffness against geology and pile evidence, reviewing cap flexibility and group effects separately because satisfying equilibrium does not prove that the assumed distribution is physically realistic.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫樁位坐標並核對力矩軸，逐樁求反力後重新加總力及力矩。用地層和試驗證據檢查等剛度，另列承台柔性與樁群影響，不能只因平衡成立就接受全部反力分配。","textEn":"Plot pile coordinates and moment axis, then independently sum calculated reactions and moments. Test equal stiffness against geology and pile evidence, reviewing cap flexibility and group effects separately because satisfying equilibrium does not prove that the assumed distribution is physically realistic.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「樁群偏心分配」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Eccentric pile-group distribution\"?","options":["畫樁位坐標並核對力矩軸，逐樁求反力後重新加總力及力矩。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","空心鋼管樁的材料受壓面積就是整個外徑圓面積。"],"optionsEn":["Plot pile coordinates and moment axis, then independently sum calculated reactions and moments.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The steel material area of a hollow pile equals its entire outer circular footprint."],"answer":0,"explanation":"畫樁位坐標並核對力矩軸，逐樁求反力後重新加總力及力矩。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot pile coordinates and moment axis, then independently sum calculated reactions and moments. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b290-v15-16","title":"樁群偏心分配：失效診斷","titleEn":"Eccentric pile-group distribution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「樁群偏心分配」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Eccentric pile-group distribution” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"某支樁剛度下降會把荷載移轉給其他樁，算術平均仍可能掩蓋局部超載。樁位偏移或力矩軸弄錯時，總力雖正確但反力高低側可能完全相反。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A softened pile transfers load to neighbors while a simple average hides concentration. Position errors or an incorrect moment axis can also preserve total force yet assign the largest reactions to the wrong side of the group. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設4支等剛度樁、兩支x=+3m兩支−3m，P=12000kN、M=12000kN·m，Ni=P/4+Mxi/Σx²，得4000與2000kN。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Ni=P/4+Mxi/Σx² gives4000 and2000kN.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要樁數相同每支樁在任何偏心荷載下都承擔相同軸力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal pile count means every pile carries identical axial force under any eccentric loading.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"某支樁剛度下降會把荷載移轉給其他樁，算術平均仍可能掩蓋局部超載。樁位偏移或力矩軸弄錯時，總力雖正確但反力高低側可能完全相反。","textEn":"A softened pile transfers load to neighbors while a simple average hides concentration. Position errors or an incorrect moment axis can also preserve total force yet assign the largest reactions to the wrong side of the group.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「樁群偏心分配」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Eccentric pile-group distribution\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","某支樁剛度下降會把荷載移轉給其他樁，算術平均仍可能掩蓋局部超載。","樁頂沉陷完全來自土壤所以樁身彈性縮短永遠可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A softened pile transfers load to neighbors while a simple average hides concentration.","Pile-head settlement comes entirely from soil, so elastic pile shortening can always be ignored."],"answer":1,"explanation":"某支樁剛度下降會把荷載移轉給其他樁，算術平均仍可能掩蓋局部超載。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A softened pile transfers load to neighbors while a simple average hides concentration. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b290-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「樁身彈性縮短」與「側向彎曲基準」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Elastic pile shortening\" and \"Lateral bending baseline\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b290-v15-17","title":"樁身彈性縮短：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Elastic pile shortening: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「樁身彈性縮短」如何影響棧橋式碼頭樁基的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Elastic pile shortening” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pile-supported pier foundations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"長樁在受壓時材料本身會縮短，樁頂沉陷因此不全來自地基。均勻軸力模型只適用一段不沿程卸載的杆件，實際樁因側阻傳力而軸力隨深度改變，應分段積分；混凝土齡期、徐變與鋼材截面損失也可能影響有效軸向剛度。 假設均勻P=2MN、L=30m、E=200GPa、A=0.060m²，δ=PL/(EA)=0.005m=5mm；未含土體沉陷。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「樁身彈性縮短」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A long pile shortens under compression, so head settlement is not entirely ground movement. A uniform-force rod represents a segment without load shedding; real shaft transfer changes force with depth and requires segmented integration. Concrete age, creep and steel-section loss additionally alter effective axial stiffness, and these contributions must be separated when interpreting observed pile-head displacement. Assume uniform P=2MN,L=30m,E=200GPa,A=0.060m². Elastic shorteningδ=PL/(EA)=0.005m=5mm, excluding ground settlement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Elastic pile shortening” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「樁頂沉陷完全來自土壤所以樁身彈性縮短永遠可以忽略。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Pile-head settlement comes entirely from soil, so elastic pile shortening can always be ignored.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「樁身彈性縮短」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Elastic pile shortening”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-17-k1","title":"樁身彈性縮短","titleEn":"Elastic pile shortening","text":"長樁在受壓時材料本身會縮短，樁頂沉陷因此不全來自地基。均勻軸力模型只適用一段不沿程卸載的杆件，實際樁因側阻傳力而軸力隨深度改變，應分段積分；混凝土齡期、徐變與鋼材截面損失也可能影響有效軸向剛度。","textEn":"A long pile shortens under compression, so head settlement is not entirely ground movement. A uniform-force rod represents a segment without load shedding; real shaft transfer changes force with depth and requires segmented integration.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：樁頂沉陷完全來自土壤所以樁身彈性縮短永遠可以忽略。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Pile-head settlement comes entirely from soil, so elastic pile shortening can always be ignored. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「樁身彈性縮短」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Elastic pile shortening\" is correct?","options":["樁頂沉陷完全來自土壤所以樁身彈性縮短永遠可以忽略。","海床泥面在所有情況下都可直接視為樁身完全固定端。","長樁在受壓時材料本身會縮短，樁頂沉陷因此不全來自地基。"],"optionsEn":["Pile-head settlement comes entirely from soil, so elastic pile shortening can always be ignored.","The seabed mudline can always be treated as a perfectly fixed pile support.","A long pile shortens under compression, so head settlement is not entirely ground movement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"長樁在受壓時材料本身會縮短，樁頂沉陷因此不全來自地基。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A long pile shortens under compression, so head settlement is not entirely ground movement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b290-v15-18","title":"樁身彈性縮短：定量估算","titleEn":"Elastic pile shortening: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「樁身彈性縮短」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Elastic pile shortening” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設均勻P=2MN、L=30m、E=200GPa、A=0.060m²，δ=PL/(EA)=0.005m=5mm；未含土體沉陷。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume uniform P=2MN,L=30m,E=200GPa,A=0.060m². Elastic shorteningδ=PL/(EA)=0.005m=5mm, excluding ground settlement. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從傳力量測建立沿深度軸力分布，用分段EA計算材料縮短，核對儀器標距和溫度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build the depthwise force profile from load-transfer evidence and integrate shortening with segmented EA, checking gauge length and temperature.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設均勻P=2MN、L=30m、E=200GPa、A=0.060m²，δ=PL/(EA)=0.005m=5mm；未含土體沉陷。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume uniform P=2MN,L=30m,E=200GPa,A=0.060m². Elastic shorteningδ=PL/(EA)=0.005m=5mm, excluding ground settlement.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「樁身彈性縮短」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Elastic pile shortening\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","穩定流拖曳算式已經自動包含波浪造成的全部慣性作用。","Miner損傷比等於一半就保證還能再使用同樣長的時間。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The steady-current drag formula automatically includes all wave-induced inertia effects.","A Miner damage fraction of one half guarantees an equally long remaining service period."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b290-v15-19","title":"樁身彈性縮短：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Elastic pile shortening: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「樁身彈性縮短」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Elastic pile shortening” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從傳力量測建立沿深度軸力分布，用分段EA計算材料縮短，核對儀器標距和溫度。再把樁頂與樁端位移比較，分開材料壓縮和地盤反應，避免用單一頂部位移反推全部端阻。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build the depthwise force profile from load-transfer evidence and integrate shortening with segmented EA, checking gauge length and temperature. Compare head and toe movements to separate material compression from ground response rather than inferring all toe behavior from one head displacement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：從傳力量測建立沿深度軸力分布，用分段EA計算材料縮短，核對儀器標距和溫度。再把樁頂與樁端位移比較，分開材料壓縮和地盤反應，避免用單一頂部位移反推全部端阻。","observationEn":"Site practice: Build the depthwise force profile from load-transfer evidence and integrate shortening with segmented EA, checking gauge length and temperature. Compare head and toe movements to separate material compression from ground response rather than inferring all toe behavior from one head displacement.","failure":"注意干擾：將樁頂全部位移當成土體沉陷會低估地基剛度，反之忽略土體位移則高估樁身壓縮。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assigning all head movement to soil understates ground stiffness, while omitting ground movement overstates material compression. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從傳力量測建立沿深度軸力分布，用分段EA計算材料縮短，核對儀器標距和溫度。再把樁頂與樁端位移比較，分開材料壓縮和地盤反應，避免用單一頂部位移反推全部端阻。","textEn":"Build the depthwise force profile from load-transfer evidence and integrate shortening with segmented EA, checking gauge length and temperature. Compare head and toe movements to separate material compression from ground response rather than inferring all toe behavior from one head displacement.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"從傳力量測建立沿深度軸力分布，用分段EA計算材料縮短，核對儀器標距和溫度。再把樁頂與樁端位移比較，分開材料壓縮和地盤反應，避免用單一頂部位移反推全部端阻。","textEn":"Build the depthwise force profile from load-transfer evidence and integrate shortening with segmented EA, checking gauge length and temperature. Compare head and toe movements to separate material compression from ground response rather than inferring all toe behavior from one head displacement.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「樁身彈性縮短」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Elastic pile shortening\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","從傳力量測建立沿深度軸力分布，用分段EA計算材料縮短，核對儀器標距和溫度。","開口管樁無論土塞狀態都具有與封閉端相同的有效端面積。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Build the depthwise force profile from load-transfer evidence and integrate shortening with segmented EA, checking gauge length and temperature.","Every open-ended pipe pile has the same effective toe area as a closed pile regardless of plugging."],"answer":1,"explanation":"從傳力量測建立沿深度軸力分布，用分段EA計算材料縮短，核對儀器標距和溫度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build the depthwise force profile from load-transfer evidence and integrate shortening with segmented EA, checking gauge length and temperature. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b290-v15-20","title":"樁身彈性縮短：失效診斷","titleEn":"Elastic pile shortening: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「樁身彈性縮短」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Elastic pile shortening” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將樁頂全部位移當成土體沉陷會低估地基剛度，反之忽略土體位移則高估樁身壓縮。側阻傳遞很強時，以頂部最大軸力套全長會過度預測縮短。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assigning all head movement to soil understates ground stiffness, while omitting ground movement overstates material compression. With strong shaft transfer, applying the maximum head force along the entire length exaggerates elastic shortening of the pile. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設均勻P=2MN、L=30m、E=200GPa、A=0.060m²，δ=PL/(EA)=0.005m=5mm；未含土體沉陷。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Elastic shorteningδ=PL/(EA)=0.005m=5mm, excluding ground settlement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「樁頂沉陷完全來自土壤所以樁身彈性縮短永遠可以忽略。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Pile-head settlement comes entirely from soil, so elastic pile shortening can always be ignored.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將樁頂全部位移當成土體沉陷會低估地基剛度，反之忽略土體位移則高估樁身壓縮。側阻傳遞很強時，以頂部最大軸力套全長會過度預測縮短。","textEn":"Assigning all head movement to soil understates ground stiffness, while omitting ground movement overstates material compression. With strong shaft transfer, applying the maximum head force along the entire length exaggerates elastic shortening of the pile.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「樁身彈性縮短」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Elastic pile shortening\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","海床泥面在所有情況下都可直接視為樁身完全固定端。","將樁頂全部位移當成土體沉陷會低估地基剛度，反之忽略土體位移則高估樁身壓縮。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","The seabed mudline can always be treated as a perfectly fixed pile support.","Assigning all head movement to soil understates ground stiffness, while omitting ground movement overstates material compression."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將樁頂全部位移當成土體沉陷會低估地基剛度，反之忽略土體位移則高估樁身壓縮。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assigning all head movement to soil understates ground stiffness, while omitting ground movement overstates material compression. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b290-v15-21","title":"側向彎曲基準：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Lateral bending baseline: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「側向彎曲基準」如何影響棧橋式碼頭樁基的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lateral bending baseline” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pile-supported pier foundations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海上樁承受水平荷載時，露出段與土中支承共同控制變形。理想懸臂固定端只提供一個結構基準，不代表真實泥面就是完全固接，土體非線性和群樁遮蔽需要另建模型；自由長度選錯會因三次方關係放大樁頭側向撓度的預測誤差。 假設理想懸臂P=100kN、L=10m、E=200GPa、I=0.0074m⁴，δ=PL³/(3EI)=22.52mm，根部矩1000kN·m。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「側向彎曲基準」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Lateral pile response combines the exposed segment with support from embedded soil. An ideal fixed cantilever supplies a structural baseline, not proof that the mudline is perfectly clamped. Nonlinear soil and group shadowing need additional modeling. An incorrectly selected free length magnifies deflection through its cubic dependence, even when material stiffness and load are otherwise correctly specified. Assume ideal cantilever P=100kN,L=10m,E=200GPa,I=0.0074m⁴. δ=PL³/(3EI)=22.52mm and root moment1000kN·m, excluding soil flexibility. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lateral bending baseline” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「海床泥面在所有情況下都可直接視為樁身完全固定端。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The seabed mudline can always be treated as a perfectly fixed pile support.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「側向彎曲基準」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lateral bending baseline”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-21-k1","title":"側向彎曲基準","titleEn":"Lateral bending baseline","text":"海上樁承受水平荷載時，露出段與土中支承共同控制變形。理想懸臂固定端只提供一個結構基準，不代表真實泥面就是完全固接，土體非線性和群樁遮蔽需要另建模型；自由長度選錯會因三次方關係放大樁頭側向撓度的預測誤差。","textEn":"Lateral pile response combines the exposed segment with support from embedded soil. An ideal fixed cantilever supplies a structural baseline, not proof that the mudline is perfectly clamped.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：海床泥面在所有情況下都可直接視為樁身完全固定端。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The seabed mudline can always be treated as a perfectly fixed pile support. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「側向彎曲基準」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Lateral bending baseline\" is correct?","options":["海上樁承受水平荷載時，露出段與土中支承共同控制變形。","海床泥面在所有情況下都可直接視為樁身完全固定端。","沖刷只影響外觀而不會改變樁基水平剛度和彎矩需求。"],"optionsEn":["Lateral pile response combines the exposed segment with support from embedded soil.","The seabed mudline can always be treated as a perfectly fixed pile support.","Scour affects appearance only and cannot change lateral pile stiffness or bending demand."],"answer":0,"explanation":"海上樁承受水平荷載時，露出段與土中支承共同控制變形。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Lateral pile response combines the exposed segment with support from embedded soil. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b290-v15-22","title":"側向彎曲基準：定量估算","titleEn":"Lateral bending baseline: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「側向彎曲基準」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lateral bending baseline” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設理想懸臂P=100kN、L=10m、E=200GPa、I=0.0074m⁴，δ=PL³/(3EI)=22.52mm，根部矩1000kN·m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume ideal cantilever P=100kN,L=10m,E=200GPa,I=0.0074m⁴. δ=PL³/(3EI)=22.52mm and root moment1000kN·m, excluding soil flexibility. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：標出固定端是假設位置並核對露出長度，用位移及應變量測檢查彎曲形狀。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark the assumed fixed point and exposed length and check bending shape against displacement and strain observations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設理想懸臂P=100kN、L=10m、E=200GPa、I=0.0074m⁴，δ=PL³/(3EI)=22.52mm，根部矩1000kN·m。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume ideal cantilever P=100kN,L=10m,E=200GPa,I=0.0074m⁴. δ=PL³/(3EI)=22.52mm and root moment1000kN·m, excluding soil flexibility.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「側向彎曲基準」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Lateral bending baseline\", which statement holds?","options":["剩餘截面百分比必定等於鋼樁剩餘使用年限的百分比。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","空心鋼管樁的材料受壓面積就是整個外徑圓面積。"],"optionsEn":["The remaining cross-sectional percentage necessarily equals the percentage of service life remaining.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The steel material area of a hollow pile equals its entire outer circular footprint."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b290-v15-23","title":"側向彎曲基準：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Lateral bending baseline: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「側向彎曲基準」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lateral bending baseline” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"標出固定端是假設位置並核對露出長度，用位移及應變量測檢查彎曲形狀。比較含土彈簧與懸臂基準的差異，另檢查循環荷載和群樁效應，不將示意固定端當成現地邊界。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark the assumed fixed point and exposed length and check bending shape against displacement and strain observations. Compare soil-supported and cantilever responses, reviewing cyclic and group effects separately rather than treating the illustrative clamp as an established site boundary. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：標出固定端是假設位置並核對露出長度，用位移及應變量測檢查彎曲形狀。比較含土彈簧與懸臂基準的差異，另檢查循環荷載和群樁效應，不將示意固定端當成現地邊界。","observationEn":"Site practice: Mark the assumed fixed point and exposed length and check bending shape against displacement and strain observations. Compare soil-supported and cantilever responses, reviewing cyclic and group effects separately rather than treating the illustrative clamp as an established site boundary.","failure":"注意干擾：把泥面誤當完全固定可能低估水平位移，沖刷加深後若仍用舊長度則再次低估需求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating the mudline as perfectly fixed can understate lateral movement, and retaining old length after scour adds further error. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"標出固定端是假設位置並核對露出長度，用位移及應變量測檢查彎曲形狀。比較含土彈簧與懸臂基準的差異，另檢查循環荷載和群樁效應，不將示意固定端當成現地邊界。","textEn":"Mark the assumed fixed point and exposed length and check bending shape against displacement and strain observations. Compare soil-supported and cantilever responses, reviewing cyclic and group effects separately rather than treating the illustrative clamp as an established site boundary.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"標出固定端是假設位置並核對露出長度，用位移及應變量測檢查彎曲形狀。比較含土彈簧與懸臂基準的差異，另檢查循環荷載和群樁效應，不將示意固定端當成現地邊界。","textEn":"Mark the assumed fixed point and exposed length and check bending shape against displacement and strain observations. Compare soil-supported and cantilever responses, reviewing cyclic and group effects separately rather than treating the illustrative clamp as an established site boundary.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「側向彎曲基準」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Lateral bending baseline\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","樁側所有摩擦力都必定向上提供抵抗而不會增加軸力。","標出固定端是假設位置並核對露出長度，用位移及應變量測檢查彎曲形狀。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Every shaft-friction force necessarily acts upward and can never increase pile compression.","Mark the assumed fixed point and exposed length and check bending shape against displacement and strain observations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"標出固定端是假設位置並核對露出長度，用位移及應變量測檢查彎曲形狀。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark the assumed fixed point and exposed length and check bending shape against displacement and strain observations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b290-v15-24","title":"側向彎曲基準：失效診斷","titleEn":"Lateral bending baseline: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「側向彎曲基準」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lateral bending baseline” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把泥面誤當完全固定可能低估水平位移，沖刷加深後若仍用舊長度則再次低估需求。樁頭接合轉動也會改變彎矩分布，不能只核對一個頂端位移。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating the mudline as perfectly fixed can understate lateral movement, and retaining old length after scour adds further error. Pile-head connection rotation also changes moment distribution, so checking one head displacement is insufficient. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設理想懸臂P=100kN、L=10m、E=200GPa、I=0.0074m⁴，δ=PL³/(3EI)=22.52mm，根部矩1000kN·m。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume ideal cantilever P=100kN,L=10m,E=200GPa,I=0.0074m⁴. δ=PL³/(3EI)=22.52mm and root moment1000kN·m, excluding soil flexibility.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「海床泥面在所有情況下都可直接視為樁身完全固定端。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The seabed mudline can always be treated as a perfectly fixed pile support.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把泥面誤當完全固定可能低估水平位移，沖刷加深後若仍用舊長度則再次低估需求。樁頭接合轉動也會改變彎矩分布，不能只核對一個頂端位移。","textEn":"Treating the mudline as perfectly fixed can understate lateral movement, and retaining old length after scour adds further error. Pile-head connection rotation also changes moment distribution, so checking one head displacement is insufficient.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「側向彎曲基準」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Lateral bending baseline\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把泥面誤當完全固定可能低估水平位移，沖刷加深後若仍用舊長度則再次低估需求。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","沖刷只影響外觀而不會改變樁基水平剛度和彎矩需求。"],"optionsEn":["Treating the mudline as perfectly fixed can understate lateral movement, and retaining old length after scour adds further error.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Scour affects appearance only and cannot change lateral pile stiffness or bending demand."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把泥面誤當完全固定可能低估水平位移，沖刷加深後若仍用舊長度則再次低估需求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating the mudline as perfectly fixed can understate lateral movement, and retaining old length after scour adds further error. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b290-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「沖刷與側向剛度」與「波流拖曳分量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Scour and lateral stiffness\" and \"Wave-current drag component\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b290-v15-25","title":"沖刷與側向剛度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Scour and lateral stiffness: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「沖刷與側向剛度」如何影響棧橋式碼頭樁基的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Scour and lateral stiffness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pile-supported pier foundations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"沖刷移除上部土支承，可能增加有效自由長度並改變樁的水平剛度，作用不只是少了一層保護石。以固定彎曲剛度懸臂比較可看三次方敏感度，但真實固定點會隨土體反應移動，海床回填也不必然立即恢復原支承，需持續觀測。 假設同EI懸臂有效長度由10增至12m，k=3EI/L³，剛度比(10/12)³=0.5787，減少42.13%；非完整樁土預測。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沖刷與側向剛度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Scour removes near-surface support and can increase effective free length, changing lateral stiffness rather than merely removing armor. A constant-EI cantilever illustrates cubic sensitivity, but the effective fixity also shifts with soil response. Sediment refill does not necessarily restore original support immediately, requiring continued observation instead of assuming that a visually recovered bed reinstates the previous behavior. Assume fixed-EI cantilever length increases10to12m. k=3EI/L³ gives stiffness ratio0.5787, a42.13% reduction, not a complete pile-soil prediction. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Scour and lateral stiffness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「沖刷只影響外觀而不會改變樁基水平剛度和彎矩需求。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Scour affects appearance only and cannot change lateral pile stiffness or bending demand.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沖刷與側向剛度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Scour and lateral stiffness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-25-k1","title":"沖刷與側向剛度","titleEn":"Scour and lateral stiffness","text":"沖刷移除上部土支承，可能增加有效自由長度並改變樁的水平剛度，作用不只是少了一層保護石。以固定彎曲剛度懸臂比較可看三次方敏感度，但真實固定點會隨土體反應移動，海床回填也不必然立即恢復原支承，需持續觀測。","textEn":"Scour removes near-surface support and can increase effective free length, changing lateral stiffness rather than merely removing armor. A constant-EI cantilever illustrates cubic sensitivity, but the effective fixity also shifts with soil response.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：沖刷只影響外觀而不會改變樁基水平剛度和彎矩需求。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Scour affects appearance only and cannot change lateral pile stiffness or bending demand. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沖刷與側向剛度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Scour and lateral stiffness\" is correct?","options":["沖刷只影響外觀而不會改變樁基水平剛度和彎矩需求。","沖刷移除上部土支承，可能增加有效自由長度並改變樁的水平剛度，作用不只是少了一層保護石。","穩定流拖曳算式已經自動包含波浪造成的全部慣性作用。"],"optionsEn":["Scour affects appearance only and cannot change lateral pile stiffness or bending demand.","Scour removes near-surface support and can increase effective free length, changing lateral stiffness rather than merely removing armor.","The steady-current drag formula automatically includes all wave-induced inertia effects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"沖刷移除上部土支承，可能增加有效自由長度並改變樁的水平剛度，作用不只是少了一層保護石。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Scour removes near-surface support and can increase effective free length, changing lateral stiffness rather than merely removing armor. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b290-v15-26","title":"沖刷與側向剛度：定量估算","titleEn":"Scour and lateral stiffness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沖刷與側向剛度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Scour and lateral stiffness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設同EI懸臂有效長度由10增至12m，k=3EI/L³，剛度比(10/12)³=0.5787，減少42.13%；非完整樁土預測。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume fixed-EI cantilever length increases10to12m. k=3EI/L³ gives stiffness ratio0.5787, a42.13% reduction, not a complete pile-soil prediction. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較樁周沖刷坑和遠處海床基準，記錄不同潮波後的三維地形。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map local scour relative to the surrounding bed after different tide-wave events.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設同EI懸臂有效長度由10增至12m，k=3EI/L³，剛度比(10/12)³=0.5787，減少42.13%；非完整樁土預測。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume fixed-EI cantilever length increases10to12m. k=3EI/L³ gives stiffness ratio0.5787, a42.13% reduction, not a complete pile-soil prediction.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沖刷與側向剛度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Scour and lateral stiffness\", which statement holds?","options":["Miner損傷比等於一半就保證還能再使用同樣長的時間。","開口管樁無論土塞狀態都具有與封閉端相同的有效端面積。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["A Miner damage fraction of one half guarantees an equally long remaining service period.","Every open-ended pipe pile has the same effective toe area as a closed pile regardless of plugging.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b290-v15-27","title":"沖刷與側向剛度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Scour and lateral stiffness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沖刷與側向剛度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Scour and lateral stiffness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較樁周沖刷坑和遠處海床基準，記錄不同潮波後的三維地形。用側向量測檢查支承變化，將回淤材料密度與原土區分，避免只因床面高程回復就宣告剛度恢復。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map local scour relative to the surrounding bed after different tide-wave events. Check support changes through lateral observations and distinguish refill density from original soil, avoiding a declaration of restored stiffness solely because the bed elevation has returned. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較樁周沖刷坑和遠處海床基準，記錄不同潮波後的三維地形。用側向量測檢查支承變化，將回淤材料密度與原土區分，避免只因床面高程回復就宣告剛度恢復。","observationEn":"Site practice: Map local scour relative to the surrounding bed after different tide-wave events. Check support changes through lateral observations and distinguish refill density from original soil, avoiding a declaration of restored stiffness solely because the bed elevation has returned.","failure":"注意干擾：冲刷坑局部最深處可能被稀疏測線漏掉，平均海床高程不變仍可有單樁失去支承。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sparse surveys may miss the deepest local hole, so unchanged average bed level can conceal support loss at one pile. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較樁周沖刷坑和遠處海床基準，記錄不同潮波後的三維地形。用側向量測檢查支承變化，將回淤材料密度與原土區分，避免只因床面高程回復就宣告剛度恢復。","textEn":"Map local scour relative to the surrounding bed after different tide-wave events. Check support changes through lateral observations and distinguish refill density from original soil, avoiding a declaration of restored stiffness solely because the bed elevation has returned.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較樁周沖刷坑和遠處海床基準，記錄不同潮波後的三維地形。用側向量測檢查支承變化，將回淤材料密度與原土區分，避免只因床面高程回復就宣告剛度恢復。","textEn":"Map local scour relative to the surrounding bed after different tide-wave events. Check support changes through lateral observations and distinguish refill density from original soil, avoiding a declaration of restored stiffness solely because the bed elevation has returned.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沖刷與側向剛度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Scour and lateral stiffness\"?","options":["比較樁周沖刷坑和遠處海床基準，記錄不同潮波後的三維地形。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要樁數相同每支樁在任何偏心荷載下都承擔相同軸力。"],"optionsEn":["Map local scour relative to the surrounding bed after different tide-wave events.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Equal pile count means every pile carries identical axial force under any eccentric loading."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較樁周沖刷坑和遠處海床基準，記錄不同潮波後的三維地形。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map local scour relative to the surrounding bed after different tide-wave events. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b290-v15-28","title":"沖刷與側向剛度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Scour and lateral stiffness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沖刷與側向剛度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Scour and lateral stiffness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"冲刷坑局部最深處可能被稀疏測線漏掉，平均海床高程不變仍可有單樁失去支承。鬆散回淤又可能在下次波流迅速移除，留下反覆剛度變化。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sparse surveys may miss the deepest local hole, so unchanged average bed level can conceal support loss at one pile. Loose refill may be removed quickly during the next event, repeatedly altering lateral stiffness. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設同EI懸臂有效長度由10增至12m，k=3EI/L³，剛度比(10/12)³=0.5787，減少42.13%；非完整樁土預測。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume fixed-EI cantilever length increases10to12m. k=3EI/L³ gives stiffness ratio0.5787, a42.13% reduction, not a complete pile-soil prediction.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「沖刷只影響外觀而不會改變樁基水平剛度和彎矩需求。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Scour affects appearance only and cannot change lateral pile stiffness or bending demand.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"冲刷坑局部最深處可能被稀疏測線漏掉，平均海床高程不變仍可有單樁失去支承。鬆散回淤又可能在下次波流迅速移除，留下反覆剛度變化。","textEn":"Sparse surveys may miss the deepest local hole, so unchanged average bed level can conceal support loss at one pile. Loose refill may be removed quickly during the next event, repeatedly altering lateral stiffness.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沖刷與側向剛度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Scour and lateral stiffness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","冲刷坑局部最深處可能被稀疏測線漏掉，平均海床高程不變仍可有單樁失去支承。","穩定流拖曳算式已經自動包含波浪造成的全部慣性作用。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Sparse surveys may miss the deepest local hole, so unchanged average bed level can conceal support loss at one pile.","The steady-current drag formula automatically includes all wave-induced inertia effects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"冲刷坑局部最深處可能被稀疏測線漏掉，平均海床高程不變仍可有單樁失去支承。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sparse surveys may miss the deepest local hole, so unchanged average bed level can conceal support loss at one pile. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b290-v15-29","title":"波流拖曳分量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Wave-current drag component: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「波流拖曳分量」如何影響棧橋式碼頭樁基的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wave-current drag component” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pile-supported pier foundations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"細長樁的水動力可分速度拖曳和加速度慣性，兩者在波浪中未必同時達峰。穩定流拖曳基準需要投影直徑與流速，海生物附著會改變粗糙與尺度；不能拿單一拖曳值代表完整波浪荷載，也不能忽略成群樁的遮蔽與局部加速。 假設海水1025kg/m³、Cd=1.2、D=1m、穩定流2m/s，每米拖曳f=ρCdDU²/2=2.460kN/m；不含慣性力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「波流拖曳分量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Hydrodynamic action on a slender pile includes velocity-dependent drag and acceleration-dependent inertia, whose peaks need not coincide. A steady-flow drag baseline requires projected diameter and speed, with marine growth altering roughness and dimensions. One drag value cannot represent complete wave loading, and pile-group shielding or local acceleration may modify the action around individual members. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,Cd=1.2,D=1m and steady speed2m/s. Drag per length f=ρCdDU²/2=2.460kN/m, excluding inertia. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wave-current drag component” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「穩定流拖曳算式已經自動包含波浪造成的全部慣性作用。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The steady-current drag formula automatically includes all wave-induced inertia effects.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「波流拖曳分量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wave-current drag component”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-29-k1","title":"波流拖曳分量","titleEn":"Wave-current drag component","text":"細長樁的水動力可分速度拖曳和加速度慣性，兩者在波浪中未必同時達峰。穩定流拖曳基準需要投影直徑與流速，海生物附著會改變粗糙與尺度；不能拿單一拖曳值代表完整波浪荷載，也不能忽略成群樁的遮蔽與局部加速。","textEn":"Hydrodynamic action on a slender pile includes velocity-dependent drag and acceleration-dependent inertia, whose peaks need not coincide. A steady-flow drag baseline requires projected diameter and speed, with marine growth altering roughness and dimensions.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：穩定流拖曳算式已經自動包含波浪造成的全部慣性作用。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The steady-current drag formula automatically includes all wave-induced inertia effects. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「波流拖曳分量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wave-current drag component\" is correct?","options":["穩定流拖曳算式已經自動包含波浪造成的全部慣性作用。","剩餘截面百分比必定等於鋼樁剩餘使用年限的百分比。","細長樁的水動力可分速度拖曳和加速度慣性，兩者在波浪中未必同時達峰。"],"optionsEn":["The steady-current drag formula automatically includes all wave-induced inertia effects.","The remaining cross-sectional percentage necessarily equals the percentage of service life remaining.","Hydrodynamic action on a slender pile includes velocity-dependent drag and acceleration-dependent inertia, whose peaks need not coincide."],"answer":2,"explanation":"細長樁的水動力可分速度拖曳和加速度慣性，兩者在波浪中未必同時達峰。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Hydrodynamic action on a slender pile includes velocity-dependent drag and acceleration-dependent inertia, whose peaks need not coincide. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b290-v15-30","title":"波流拖曳分量：定量估算","titleEn":"Wave-current drag component: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「波流拖曳分量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wave-current drag component” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設海水1025kg/m³、Cd=1.2、D=1m、穩定流2m/s，每米拖曳f=ρCdDU²/2=2.460kN/m；不含慣性力。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,Cd=1.2,D=1m and steady speed2m/s. Drag per length f=ρCdDU²/2=2.460kN/m, excluding inertia. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對流速方向和量測高度，記錄海生物附著、樁群間距與所用拖曳係數的範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check velocity direction and elevation, recording marine growth, group spacing and the drag coefficient's evidence range.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設海水1025kg/m³、Cd=1.2、D=1m、穩定流2m/s，每米拖曳f=ρCdDU²/2=2.460kN/m；不含慣性力。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,Cd=1.2,D=1m and steady speed2m/s. Drag per length f=ρCdDU²/2=2.460kN/m, excluding inertia.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「波流拖曳分量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wave-current drag component\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","空心鋼管樁的材料受壓面積就是整個外徑圓面積。","樁側所有摩擦力都必定向上提供抵抗而不會增加軸力。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The steel material area of a hollow pile equals its entire outer circular footprint.","Every shaft-friction force necessarily acts upward and can never increase pile compression."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b290-v15-31","title":"波流拖曳分量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wave-current drag component: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「波流拖曳分量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wave-current drag component” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對流速方向和量測高度，記錄海生物附著、樁群間距與所用拖曳係數的範圍。波浪情境另保存速度與加速度時序，分相位計算兩分量，不任意把不同時刻峰值直接相加。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check velocity direction and elevation, recording marine growth, group spacing and the drag coefficient's evidence range. For waves, retain velocity and acceleration histories and calculate phase-resolved components rather than summing peaks occurring at unrelated times in the cycle. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：核對流速方向和量測高度，記錄海生物附著、樁群間距與所用拖曳係數的範圍。波浪情境另保存速度與加速度時序，分相位計算兩分量，不任意把不同時刻峰值直接相加。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check velocity direction and elevation, recording marine growth, group spacing and the drag coefficient's evidence range. For waves, retain velocity and acceleration histories and calculate phase-resolved components rather than summing peaks occurring at unrelated times in the cycle.","failure":"注意干擾：使用未附著的直徑可能低估長期拖曳，忽略慣性則漏掉短週期作用。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using a clean diameter can understate long-term drag, while omitted inertia misses short-period action. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對流速方向和量測高度，記錄海生物附著、樁群間距與所用拖曳係數的範圍。波浪情境另保存速度與加速度時序，分相位計算兩分量，不任意把不同時刻峰值直接相加。","textEn":"Check velocity direction and elevation, recording marine growth, group spacing and the drag coefficient's evidence range. For waves, retain velocity and acceleration histories and calculate phase-resolved components rather than summing peaks occurring at unrelated times in the cycle.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"核對流速方向和量測高度，記錄海生物附著、樁群間距與所用拖曳係數的範圍。波浪情境另保存速度與加速度時序，分相位計算兩分量，不任意把不同時刻峰值直接相加。","textEn":"Check velocity direction and elevation, recording marine growth, group spacing and the drag coefficient's evidence range. For waves, retain velocity and acceleration histories and calculate phase-resolved components rather than summing peaks occurring at unrelated times in the cycle.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「波流拖曳分量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wave-current drag component\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對流速方向和量測高度，記錄海生物附著、樁群間距與所用拖曳係數的範圍。","樁頂沉陷完全來自土壤所以樁身彈性縮短永遠可以忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check velocity direction and elevation, recording marine growth, group spacing and the drag coefficient's evidence range.","Pile-head settlement comes entirely from soil, so elastic pile shortening can always be ignored."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對流速方向和量測高度，記錄海生物附著、樁群間距與所用拖曳係數的範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check velocity direction and elevation, recording marine growth, group spacing and the drag coefficient's evidence range. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b290-v15-32","title":"波流拖曳分量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wave-current drag component: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「波流拖曳分量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wave-current drag component” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"使用未附著的直徑可能低估長期拖曳，忽略慣性則漏掉短週期作用。將遮蔽係數套用所有流向也可能低估前排或局部通道中的高流速需求。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using a clean diameter can understate long-term drag, while omitted inertia misses short-period action. Applying one shielding factor to every direction may also understate loads on leading piles or in accelerated local flow passages. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設海水1025kg/m³、Cd=1.2、D=1m、穩定流2m/s，每米拖曳f=ρCdDU²/2=2.460kN/m；不含慣性力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Drag per length f=ρCdDU²/2=2.460kN/m, excluding inertia.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「穩定流拖曳算式已經自動包含波浪造成的全部慣性作用。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The steady-current drag formula automatically includes all wave-induced inertia effects.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"使用未附著的直徑可能低估長期拖曳，忽略慣性則漏掉短週期作用。將遮蔽係數套用所有流向也可能低估前排或局部通道中的高流速需求。","textEn":"Using a clean diameter can understate long-term drag, while omitted inertia misses short-period action. Applying one shielding factor to every direction may also understate loads on leading piles or in accelerated local flow passages.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「波流拖曳分量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wave-current drag component\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","剩餘截面百分比必定等於鋼樁剩餘使用年限的百分比。","使用未附著的直徑可能低估長期拖曳，忽略慣性則漏掉短週期作用。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The remaining cross-sectional percentage necessarily equals the percentage of service life remaining.","Using a clean diameter can understate long-term drag, while omitted inertia misses short-period action."],"answer":2,"explanation":"使用未附著的直徑可能低估長期拖曳，忽略慣性則漏掉短週期作用。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using a clean diameter can understate long-term drag, while omitted inertia misses short-period action. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b290-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「腐蝕減薄與剩餘截面」與「循環需求與疲勞」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Corrosion loss and remaining section\" and \"Cyclic demand and fatigue\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b290-v15-33","title":"腐蝕減薄與剩餘截面：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Corrosion loss and remaining section: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「腐蝕減薄與剩餘截面」如何影響棧橋式碼頭樁基的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Corrosion loss and remaining section” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pile-supported pier foundations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"海水區鋼樁腐蝕常隨高程和環境變化，平均減薄無法代表局部凹蝕或焊縫。假設外徑不變且內壁損失只是一種幾何情境，真實腐蝕可能雙面發生；剩餘面積比例也不是剩餘壽命或承載比例，還需檢查彎曲、局部穩定及疲勞。 假設外徑固定1m，壁厚由20降至17mm，內徑0.960變0.966m，剩餘面積比[1−0.966²]/[1−0.960²]=0.8526。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「腐蝕減薄與剩餘截面」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Marine corrosion varies with elevation and environment, and average loss does not describe pitting or weld zones. Fixed outer diameter with internal loss is only one geometry; actual attack may occur on both faces. Remaining area fraction is neither remaining life nor overall capacity, since bending, local stability and fatigue depend on additional features of the damaged member. Assume fixed outer diameter1m and wall thickness20to17mm, so inner diameter0.960to0.966m. Remaining annular-area ratio is0.8526, not remaining life. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Corrosion loss and remaining section” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「剩餘截面百分比必定等於鋼樁剩餘使用年限的百分比。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The remaining cross-sectional percentage necessarily equals the percentage of service life remaining.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「腐蝕減薄與剩餘截面」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Corrosion loss and remaining section”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-33-k1","title":"腐蝕減薄與剩餘截面","titleEn":"Corrosion loss and remaining section","text":"海水區鋼樁腐蝕常隨高程和環境變化，平均減薄無法代表局部凹蝕或焊縫。假設外徑不變且內壁損失只是一種幾何情境，真實腐蝕可能雙面發生；剩餘面積比例也不是剩餘壽命或承載比例，還需檢查彎曲、局部穩定及疲勞。","textEn":"Marine corrosion varies with elevation and environment, and average loss does not describe pitting or weld zones. Fixed outer diameter with internal loss is only one geometry; actual attack may occur on both faces.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：剩餘截面百分比必定等於鋼樁剩餘使用年限的百分比。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The remaining cross-sectional percentage necessarily equals the percentage of service life remaining. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「腐蝕減薄與剩餘截面」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Corrosion loss and remaining section\" is correct?","options":["海水區鋼樁腐蝕常隨高程和環境變化，平均減薄無法代表局部凹蝕或焊縫。","剩餘截面百分比必定等於鋼樁剩餘使用年限的百分比。","Miner損傷比等於一半就保證還能再使用同樣長的時間。"],"optionsEn":["Marine corrosion varies with elevation and environment, and average loss does not describe pitting or weld zones.","The remaining cross-sectional percentage necessarily equals the percentage of service life remaining.","A Miner damage fraction of one half guarantees an equally long remaining service period."],"answer":0,"explanation":"海水區鋼樁腐蝕常隨高程和環境變化，平均減薄無法代表局部凹蝕或焊縫。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Marine corrosion varies with elevation and environment, and average loss does not describe pitting or weld zones. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b290-v15-34","title":"腐蝕減薄與剩餘截面：定量估算","titleEn":"Corrosion loss and remaining section: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「腐蝕減薄與剩餘截面」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Corrosion loss and remaining section” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設外徑固定1m，壁厚由20降至17mm，內徑0.960變0.966m，剩餘面積比[1−0.966²]/[1−0.960²]=0.8526。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume fixed outer diameter1m and wall thickness20to17mm, so inner diameter0.960to0.966m. Remaining annular-area ratio is0.8526, not remaining life. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按高程和周向建立厚度地圖，保留最薄區與量測不確定度，說明損失是在內外哪一面。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map thickness by elevation and circumference, retaining thin spots and uncertainty and identifying the affected face.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設外徑固定1m，壁厚由20降至17mm，內徑0.960變0.966m，剩餘面積比[1−0.966²]/[1−0.960²]=0.8526。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume fixed outer diameter1m and wall thickness20to17mm, so inner diameter0.960to0.966m. Remaining annular-area ratio is0.8526, not remaining life.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「腐蝕減薄與剩餘截面」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Corrosion loss and remaining section\", which statement holds?","options":["開口管樁無論土塞狀態都具有與封閉端相同的有效端面積。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","只要樁數相同每支樁在任何偏心荷載下都承擔相同軸力。"],"optionsEn":["Every open-ended pipe pile has the same effective toe area as a closed pile regardless of plugging.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Equal pile count means every pile carries identical axial force under any eccentric loading."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b290-v15-35","title":"腐蝕減薄與剩餘截面：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Corrosion loss and remaining section: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「腐蝕減薄與剩餘截面」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Corrosion loss and remaining section” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按高程和周向建立厚度地圖，保留最薄區與量測不確定度，說明損失是在內外哪一面。將更新截面帶回軸力彎矩與穩定分析，另檢查塗層和陰極防蝕狀態而非只報平均減薄。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map thickness by elevation and circumference, retaining thin spots and uncertainty and identifying the affected face. Recompute axial, bending and stability demands using updated geometry, reviewing coating and cathodic-protection condition separately rather than reporting only mean thickness loss. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：按高程和周向建立厚度地圖，保留最薄區與量測不確定度，說明損失是在內外哪一面。將更新截面帶回軸力彎矩與穩定分析，另檢查塗層和陰極防蝕狀態而非只報平均減薄。","observationEn":"Site practice: Map thickness by elevation and circumference, retaining thin spots and uncertainty and identifying the affected face. Recompute axial, bending and stability demands using updated geometry, reviewing coating and cathodic-protection condition separately rather than reporting only mean thickness loss.","failure":"注意干擾：水線附近局部深蝕可在平均截面尚大時控制失效，內外面誤判又會改變慣性矩。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Deep localized attack near the waterline can govern despite a large average remaining area, and misidentified corrosion faces alter inertia. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按高程和周向建立厚度地圖，保留最薄區與量測不確定度，說明損失是在內外哪一面。將更新截面帶回軸力彎矩與穩定分析，另檢查塗層和陰極防蝕狀態而非只報平均減薄。","textEn":"Map thickness by elevation and circumference, retaining thin spots and uncertainty and identifying the affected face. Recompute axial, bending and stability demands using updated geometry, reviewing coating and cathodic-protection condition separately rather than reporting only mean thickness loss.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"按高程和周向建立厚度地圖，保留最薄區與量測不確定度，說明損失是在內外哪一面。將更新截面帶回軸力彎矩與穩定分析，另檢查塗層和陰極防蝕狀態而非只報平均減薄。","textEn":"Map thickness by elevation and circumference, retaining thin spots and uncertainty and identifying the affected face. Recompute axial, bending and stability demands using updated geometry, reviewing coating and cathodic-protection condition separately rather than reporting only mean thickness loss.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「腐蝕減薄與剩餘截面」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Corrosion loss and remaining section\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","海床泥面在所有情況下都可直接視為樁身完全固定端。","按高程和周向建立厚度地圖，保留最薄區與量測不確定度，說明損失是在內外哪一面。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The seabed mudline can always be treated as a perfectly fixed pile support.","Map thickness by elevation and circumference, retaining thin spots and uncertainty and identifying the affected face."],"answer":2,"explanation":"按高程和周向建立厚度地圖，保留最薄區與量測不確定度，說明損失是在內外哪一面。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map thickness by elevation and circumference, retaining thin spots and uncertainty and identifying the affected face. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b290-v15-36","title":"腐蝕減薄與剩餘截面：失效診斷","titleEn":"Corrosion loss and remaining section: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「腐蝕減薄與剩餘截面」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Corrosion loss and remaining section” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"水線附近局部深蝕可在平均截面尚大時控制失效，內外面誤判又會改變慣性矩。用平均腐蝕速率外推壽命，可能漏掉環境變化和保護系統失效後的加速。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Deep localized attack near the waterline can govern despite a large average remaining area, and misidentified corrosion faces alter inertia. Extrapolating mean corrosion rate misses environmental changes or acceleration following loss of protective-system performance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設外徑固定1m，壁厚由20降至17mm，內徑0.960變0.966m，剩餘面積比[1−0.966²]/[1−0.960²]=0.8526。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Remaining annular-area ratio is0.8526, not remaining life.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「剩餘截面百分比必定等於鋼樁剩餘使用年限的百分比。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The remaining cross-sectional percentage necessarily equals the percentage of service life remaining.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"水線附近局部深蝕可在平均截面尚大時控制失效，內外面誤判又會改變慣性矩。用平均腐蝕速率外推壽命，可能漏掉環境變化和保護系統失效後的加速。","textEn":"Deep localized attack near the waterline can govern despite a large average remaining area, and misidentified corrosion faces alter inertia. Extrapolating mean corrosion rate misses environmental changes or acceleration following loss of protective-system performance.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「腐蝕減薄與剩餘截面」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Corrosion loss and remaining section\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["水線附近局部深蝕可在平均截面尚大時控制失效，內外面誤判又會改變慣性矩。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","Miner損傷比等於一半就保證還能再使用同樣長的時間。"],"optionsEn":["Deep localized attack near the waterline can govern despite a large average remaining area, and misidentified corrosion faces alter inertia.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A Miner damage fraction of one half guarantees an equally long remaining service period."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水線附近局部深蝕可在平均截面尚大時控制失效，內外面誤判又會改變慣性矩。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Deep localized attack near the waterline can govern despite a large average remaining area, and misidentified corrosion faces alter inertia. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b290-v15-37","title":"循環需求與疲勞：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cyclic demand and fatigue: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「循環需求與疲勞」如何影響棧橋式碼頭樁基的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cyclic demand and fatigue” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Pile-supported pier foundations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"波流與靠泊反覆作用在焊縫及接頭形成疲勞需求，應力範圍和循環次數需共同描述。線性損傷累積假設忽略載入順序、腐蝕交互及裂縫成長細節，只適合有相應曲線的初步比較；損傷比未到某值也不能取代檢查或保證剩餘壽命。 假設兩級循環n1=100000、N1=1000000，n2=200000、N2=500000，Miner D=Σn/N=0.50；非剩餘壽命保證。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「循環需求與疲勞」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Repeated waves and berthing create fatigue demand at welds and connections, requiring stress ranges together with cycle counts. Linear cumulative damage ignores sequence, corrosion interaction and detailed crack growth, supporting only a preliminary comparison with appropriate fatigue curves. A calculated fraction does not replace inspection or guarantee remaining life, especially when local details differ from those represented by the selected curve. Assume cycle pairs n1=100000,N1=1000000 and n2=200000,N2=500000. Miner D=Σn/N=0.50, not a remaining-life guarantee. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cyclic demand and fatigue” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「Miner損傷比等於一半就保證還能再使用同樣長的時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A Miner damage fraction of one half guarantees an equally long remaining service period.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「循環需求與疲勞」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cyclic demand and fatigue”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-37-k1","title":"循環需求與疲勞","titleEn":"Cyclic demand and fatigue","text":"波流與靠泊反覆作用在焊縫及接頭形成疲勞需求，應力範圍和循環次數需共同描述。線性損傷累積假設忽略載入順序、腐蝕交互及裂縫成長細節，只適合有相應曲線的初步比較；損傷比未到某值也不能取代檢查或保證剩餘壽命。","textEn":"Repeated waves and berthing create fatigue demand at welds and connections, requiring stress ranges together with cycle counts. Linear cumulative damage ignores sequence, corrosion interaction and detailed crack growth, supporting only a preliminary comparison with appropriate fatigue curves.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：Miner損傷比等於一半就保證還能再使用同樣長的時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A Miner damage fraction of one half guarantees an equally long remaining service period. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「循環需求與疲勞」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cyclic demand and fatigue\" is correct?","options":["Miner損傷比等於一半就保證還能再使用同樣長的時間。","波流與靠泊反覆作用在焊縫及接頭形成疲勞需求，應力範圍和循環次數需共同描述。","空心鋼管樁的材料受壓面積就是整個外徑圓面積。"],"optionsEn":["A Miner damage fraction of one half guarantees an equally long remaining service period.","Repeated waves and berthing create fatigue demand at welds and connections, requiring stress ranges together with cycle counts.","The steel material area of a hollow pile equals its entire outer circular footprint."],"answer":1,"explanation":"波流與靠泊反覆作用在焊縫及接頭形成疲勞需求，應力範圍和循環次數需共同描述。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Repeated waves and berthing create fatigue demand at welds and connections, requiring stress ranges together with cycle counts. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b290-v15-38","title":"循環需求與疲勞：定量估算","titleEn":"Cyclic demand and fatigue: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「循環需求與疲勞」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cyclic demand and fatigue” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設兩級循環n1=100000、N1=1000000，n2=200000、N2=500000，Miner D=Σn/N=0.50；非剩餘壽命保證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume cycle pairs n1=100000,N1=1000000 and n2=200000,N2=500000. Miner D=Σn/N=0.50, not a remaining-life guarantee. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：追蹤應力範圍來源與循環計數方法，核對疲勞曲線是否適合實際焊縫和環境。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trace stress-range derivation and cycle counting, verifying curve applicability to the actual weld and environment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設兩級循環n1=100000、N1=1000000，n2=200000、N2=500000，Miner D=Σn/N=0.50；非剩餘壽命保證。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume cycle pairs n1=100000,N1=1000000 and n2=200000,N2=500000. Miner D=Σn/N=0.50, not a remaining-life guarantee.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「循環需求與疲勞」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cyclic demand and fatigue\", which statement holds?","options":["樁側所有摩擦力都必定向上提供抵抗而不會增加軸力。","樁頂沉陷完全來自土壤所以樁身彈性縮短永遠可以忽略。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Every shaft-friction force necessarily acts upward and can never increase pile compression.","Pile-head settlement comes entirely from soil, so elastic pile shortening can always be ignored.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b290-v15-39","title":"循環需求與疲勞：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cyclic demand and fatigue: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「循環需求與疲勞」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cyclic demand and fatigue” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"追蹤應力範圍來源與循環計數方法，核對疲勞曲線是否適合實際焊縫和環境。將裂縫檢查、腐蝕減薄與載入歷史一起比對，記錄缺測區段及可能漏算的高幅事件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trace stress-range derivation and cycle counting, verifying curve applicability to the actual weld and environment. Compare crack inspections, corrosion loss and load history together, documenting missing periods and high-amplitude events that may not be represented in the recorded data. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：追蹤應力範圍來源與循環計數方法，核對疲勞曲線是否適合實際焊縫和環境。將裂縫檢查、腐蝕減薄與載入歷史一起比對，記錄缺測區段及可能漏算的高幅事件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Trace stress-range derivation and cycle counting, verifying curve applicability to the actual weld and environment. Compare crack inspections, corrosion loss and load history together, documenting missing periods and high-amplitude events that may not be represented in the recorded data.","failure":"注意干擾：名義應力沒有反映焊趾集中時會低估疲勞，少數大波事件也可能主導損傷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Nominal stress can miss weld-toe concentration, and a few large-wave events may dominate damage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"追蹤應力範圍來源與循環計數方法，核對疲勞曲線是否適合實際焊縫和環境。將裂縫檢查、腐蝕減薄與載入歷史一起比對，記錄缺測區段及可能漏算的高幅事件。","textEn":"Trace stress-range derivation and cycle counting, verifying curve applicability to the actual weld and environment. Compare crack inspections, corrosion loss and load history together, documenting missing periods and high-amplitude events that may not be represented in the recorded data.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"追蹤應力範圍來源與循環計數方法，核對疲勞曲線是否適合實際焊縫和環境。將裂縫檢查、腐蝕減薄與載入歷史一起比對，記錄缺測區段及可能漏算的高幅事件。","textEn":"Trace stress-range derivation and cycle counting, verifying curve applicability to the actual weld and environment. Compare crack inspections, corrosion loss and load history together, documenting missing periods and high-amplitude events that may not be represented in the recorded data.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「循環需求與疲勞」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cyclic demand and fatigue\"?","options":["追蹤應力範圍來源與循環計數方法，核對疲勞曲線是否適合實際焊縫和環境。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","沖刷只影響外觀而不會改變樁基水平剛度和彎矩需求。"],"optionsEn":["Trace stress-range derivation and cycle counting, verifying curve applicability to the actual weld and environment.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Scour affects appearance only and cannot change lateral pile stiffness or bending demand."],"answer":0,"explanation":"追蹤應力範圍來源與循環計數方法，核對疲勞曲線是否適合實際焊縫和環境。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trace stress-range derivation and cycle counting, verifying curve applicability to the actual weld and environment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b290-v15-40","title":"循環需求與疲勞：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cyclic demand and fatigue: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"prerequisiteIds":["b290-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「循環需求與疲勞」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cyclic demand and fatigue” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"名義應力沒有反映焊趾集中時會低估疲勞，少數大波事件也可能主導損傷。累積比看似不高但既有裂縫已發展時，仍需獨立評估而不能依比例延後處理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Nominal stress can miss weld-toe concentration, and a few large-wave events may dominate damage. A modest cumulative fraction does not justify deferring assessment when an existing crack has already developed in the actual connection. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設兩級循環n1=100000、N1=1000000，n2=200000、N2=500000，Miner D=Σn/N=0.50；非剩餘壽命保證。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Miner D=Σn/N=0.50, not a remaining-life guarantee.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「Miner損傷比等於一半就保證還能再使用同樣長的時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A Miner damage fraction of one half guarantees an equally long remaining service period.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b290-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"名義應力沒有反映焊趾集中時會低估疲勞，少數大波事件也可能主導損傷。累積比看似不高但既有裂縫已發展時，仍需獨立評估而不能依比例延後處理。","textEn":"Nominal stress can miss weld-toe concentration, and a few large-wave events may dominate damage. A modest cumulative fraction does not justify deferring assessment when an existing crack has already developed in the actual connection.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]},{"id":"b290-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「循環需求與疲勞」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cyclic demand and fatigue\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","名義應力沒有反映焊趾集中時會低估疲勞，少數大波事件也可能主導損傷。","空心鋼管樁的材料受壓面積就是整個外徑圓面積。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Nominal stress can miss weld-toe concentration, and a few large-wave events may dominate damage.","The steel material area of a hollow pile equals its entire outer circular footprint."],"answer":1,"explanation":"名義應力沒有反映焊趾集中時會低估疲勞，少數大波事件也可能主導損傷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Nominal stress can miss weld-toe concentration, and a few large-wave events may dominate damage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-piles","v15s-la-wharf","v15s-pakkok"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b291","title":"浮動碼頭繫泊系統","titleEn":"Mooring systems for floating docks","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"辨識浮碼頭浮力纜繩幾何與岸上通道的耦合反應。課程從邊界辨識與資料整理走到水理量化、構造介面及驗證紀錄；每一步把計算結果連回可量測的證據。十個不同單元分別處理關鍵機制，不以名義尺寸或單一通過率代替整體工程判斷，並明列合成算例與現地資料的差別。","summaryEn":"Identify coupled buoyancy, mooring geometry and shore-access response of floating docks. The course moves from boundary identification and evidence to hydraulic quantification, structural interfaces and verification records. Ten distinct units connect each calculated quantity to measurable evidence. Nominal geometry or a single pass rate does not establish whole-system performance, and synthetic teaching examples remain separate from field observations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-coasts","subcategoryTitle":"海岸、港灣與水資源韌性","subcategoryTitleEn":"Coasts, ports and water-resource resilience","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-coasts","learningTags":["water","water-coasts","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-port","architectureNodes":[["浮台載重與吃水","Pontoon loading and draft"],["水下流阻尺度","Submerged-current drag scale"],["材料伸長與有效剛度","Material extension and effective stiffness"],["並聯恢復剛度","Parallel restoring stiffness"],["浮力儲備與損艙","Buoyant reserve and compartment loss"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-port","labels":["浮台載重與吃水","水下流阻尺度","材料伸長與有效剛度","並聯恢復剛度","浮力儲備與損艙"],"labelsEn":["Pontoon loading and draft","Submerged-current drag scale","Material extension and effective stiffness","Parallel restoring stiffness","Buoyant reserve and compartment loss"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為原創合成算例，不是地標工程的實測或推薦操作值。教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設海水1025kg/m³、水線面100m²、均勻增重10250kg，ΔT=Δm/(ρA)=0.10m；不含傾斜與波浪。假設增重由10250加10%至11275kg、水線面與密度不變，平均吃水增量由0.10變0.11m；並不保證各角點只增加同樣深度。重新計算前先列固定條件、單位、適用尺度及可能失效的邊界。把模型敏感度與測量誤差分開，不能將單一參數變化直接當成工程風險或壽命比例。比較兩次結果後，記錄還需要哪些獨立證據，並由負責專業人員判斷適用性。","textEn":"This original synthetic example is neither a landmark measurement nor a recommended operating value. Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,constant waterplane100m² and uniformly added10250kg. Mean draft increaseΔT=0.10m, excluding heel and waves. Increasing added mass10% from10250 to11275kg at fixed waterplane and density changes mean draft increment from0.10 to0.11m, without guaranteeing equal immersion changes at every corner. Before recalculating, list fixed conditions, units, applicable scale and boundaries that could fail. Separate model sensitivity from measurement uncertainty: a parameter change does not directly give a proportional change in engineering risk or service life. Compare the results, record independent evidence still needed, and have the responsible specialist determine applicability.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b291-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「浮台載重與吃水」與「迎風面與風作用」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pontoon loading and draft\" and \"Windage and wind action\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b291-v15-01","title":"浮台載重與吃水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pontoon loading and draft: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「浮台載重與吃水」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pontoon loading and draft” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"浮碼頭用排水體積平衡總重量，增加人員或設備會改變平均吃水與乾舷。矩形常水線面只是靜水近似，重量位置還影響傾斜，進水或浮筒形狀變化會改變面積；因此承載評估需把平均下沉、偏載與損壞狀態分開，不能只算總浮力。 假設海水1025kg/m³、水線面100m²、均勻增重10250kg，ΔT=Δm/(ρA)=0.10m；不含傾斜與波浪。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「浮台載重與吃水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A floating dock balances total weight through displaced water. Added people or equipment change mean draft and freeboard. A constant rectangular waterplane is only a calm-water approximation; weight location causes heel, while flooding or changing hull shape alters area. Assessment must separate mean immersion, eccentric loading and damage rather than relying on one total-buoyancy figure for every condition. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,constant waterplane100m² and uniformly added10250kg. Mean draft increaseΔT=0.10m, excluding heel and waves. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pontoon loading and draft” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「浮台載重與吃水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pontoon loading and draft”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-01-k1","title":"浮台載重與吃水","titleEn":"Pontoon loading and draft","text":"浮碼頭用排水體積平衡總重量，增加人員或設備會改變平均吃水與乾舷。矩形常水線面只是靜水近似，重量位置還影響傾斜，進水或浮筒形狀變化會改變面積；因此承載評估需把平均下沉、偏載與損壞狀態分開，不能只算總浮力。","textEn":"A floating dock balances total weight through displaced water. Added people or equipment change mean draft and freeboard.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「浮台載重與吃水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pontoon loading and draft\" is correct?","options":["只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。","浮碼頭用排水體積平衡總重量，增加人員或設備會改變平均吃水與乾舷。","浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。"],"optionsEn":["Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves.","A floating dock balances total weight through displaced water.","Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels."],"answer":1,"explanation":"浮碼頭用排水體積平衡總重量，增加人員或設備會改變平均吃水與乾舷。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A floating dock balances total weight through displaced water. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b291-v15-02","title":"浮台載重與吃水：定量估算","titleEn":"Pontoon loading and draft: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「浮台載重與吃水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pontoon loading and draft” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設海水1025kg/m³、水線面100m²、均勻增重10250kg，ΔT=Δm/(ρA)=0.10m；不含傾斜與波浪。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,constant waterplane100m² and uniformly added10250kg. Mean draft increaseΔT=0.10m, excluding heel and waves. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用多角點吃水與重量清單交叉核對，標出人員和設備可能集中區，檢查水線面是否隨吃水改變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare corner drafts with the weight schedule, marking potential concentrated occupancy and checking whether waterplane changes with immersion.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設海水1025kg/m³、水線面100m²、均勻增重10250kg，ΔT=Δm/(ρA)=0.10m；不含傾斜與波浪。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,constant waterplane100m² and uniformly added10250kg. Mean draft increaseΔT=0.10m, excluding heel and waves.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「浮台載重與吃水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pontoon loading and draft\", which statement holds?","options":["纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。","浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry.","If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b291-v15-03","title":"浮台載重與吃水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pontoon loading and draft: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「浮台載重與吃水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pontoon loading and draft” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用多角點吃水與重量清單交叉核對，標出人員和設備可能集中區，檢查水線面是否隨吃水改變。另記密閉艙狀態及最低乾舷，把靜水預算與實際使用限制分開保存。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare corner drafts with the weight schedule, marking potential concentrated occupancy and checking whether waterplane changes with immersion. Record compartment condition and minimum freeboard, keeping this static budget distinct from the actual restrictions governing use of the facility. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用多角點吃水與重量清單交叉核對，標出人員和設備可能集中區，檢查水線面是否隨吃水改變。另記密閉艙狀態及最低乾舷，把靜水預算與實際使用限制分開保存。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare corner drafts with the weight schedule, marking potential concentrated occupancy and checking whether waterplane changes with immersion. Record compartment condition and minimum freeboard, keeping this static budget distinct from the actual restrictions governing use of the facility.","failure":"注意干擾：偏載時平均吃水正常仍可能有一角進水，未察覺艙漏又使有效浮力持續減少。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Eccentric loading can flood a corner despite normal mean draft, and unnoticed leakage progressively reduces buoyant reserve. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用多角點吃水與重量清單交叉核對，標出人員和設備可能集中區，檢查水線面是否隨吃水改變。另記密閉艙狀態及最低乾舷，把靜水預算與實際使用限制分開保存。","textEn":"Compare corner drafts with the weight schedule, marking potential concentrated occupancy and checking whether waterplane changes with immersion. Record compartment condition and minimum freeboard, keeping this static budget distinct from the actual restrictions governing use of the facility.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用多角點吃水與重量清單交叉核對，標出人員和設備可能集中區，檢查水線面是否隨吃水改變。另記密閉艙狀態及最低乾舷，把靜水預算與實際使用限制分開保存。","textEn":"Compare corner drafts with the weight schedule, marking potential concentrated occupancy and checking whether waterplane changes with immersion. Record compartment condition and minimum freeboard, keeping this static budget distinct from the actual restrictions governing use of the facility.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「浮台載重與吃水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pontoon loading and draft\"?","options":["用多角點吃水與重量清單交叉核對，標出人員和設備可能集中區，檢查水線面是否隨吃水改變。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。"],"optionsEn":["Compare corner drafts with the weight schedule, marking potential concentrated occupancy and checking whether waterplane changes with immersion.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用多角點吃水與重量清單交叉核對，標出人員和設備可能集中區，檢查水線面是否隨吃水改變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare corner drafts with the weight schedule, marking potential concentrated occupancy and checking whether waterplane changes with immersion. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b291-v15-04","title":"浮台載重與吃水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pontoon loading and draft: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「浮台載重與吃水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pontoon loading and draft” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"偏載時平均吃水正常仍可能有一角進水，未察覺艙漏又使有效浮力持續減少。只核對設計總重量，無法辨識局部低乾舷與失去密閉性的共同影響。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Eccentric loading can flood a corner despite normal mean draft, and unnoticed leakage progressively reduces buoyant reserve. Checking design total weight alone cannot reveal the combined effect of local low freeboard and compromised compartment integrity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設海水1025kg/m³、水線面100m²、均勻增重10250kg，ΔT=Δm/(ρA)=0.10m；不含傾斜與波浪。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mean draft increaseΔT=0.10m, excluding heel and waves.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"偏載時平均吃水正常仍可能有一角進水，未察覺艙漏又使有效浮力持續減少。只核對設計總重量，無法辨識局部低乾舷與失去密閉性的共同影響。","textEn":"Eccentric loading can flood a corner despite normal mean draft, and unnoticed leakage progressively reduces buoyant reserve. Checking design total weight alone cannot reveal the combined effect of local low freeboard and compromised compartment integrity.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「浮台載重與吃水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pontoon loading and draft\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","偏載時平均吃水正常仍可能有一角進水，未察覺艙漏又使有效浮力持續減少。","浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Eccentric loading can flood a corner despite normal mean draft, and unnoticed leakage progressively reduces buoyant reserve.","Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels."],"answer":1,"explanation":"偏載時平均吃水正常仍可能有一角進水，未察覺艙漏又使有效浮力持續減少。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Eccentric loading can flood a corner despite normal mean draft, and unnoticed leakage progressively reduces buoyant reserve. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b291-v15-05","title":"迎風面與風作用：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Windage and wind action: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「迎風面與風作用」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Windage and wind action” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"浮碼頭與繫泊船舶的迎風面共同傳力，風向改變會讓受力位置與扭矩不同。平方風速式使用指定平均時間與高度，不能把瞬間陣風和長期平均混在同一係數下；遮蔽、上層設施及船舶配置也會改變受風面，需追蹤實際組合。 假設空氣ρ=1.225kg/m³、Cd=1.2、投影面積100m²、指定風速20m/s，F=ρCdAU²/2=29.40kN；非操作門檻。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「迎風面與風作用」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The dock and attached vessels contribute windage and transfer load together; direction changes force location and torque. A quadratic wind relation requires a specified averaging period and elevation, rather than mixing gusts and long-term means under one coefficient. Shelter, superstructures and vessel arrangements also change projected area, making the actual combined configuration part of the load case. Assume air1.225kg/m³,Cd=1.2,projected area100m² and selected speed20m/s. F=ρCdAU²/2=29.40kN, not an operating threshold. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Windage and wind action” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「迎風面與風作用」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Windage and wind action”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-05-k1","title":"迎風面與風作用","titleEn":"Windage and wind action","text":"浮碼頭與繫泊船舶的迎風面共同傳力，風向改變會讓受力位置與扭矩不同。平方風速式使用指定平均時間與高度，不能把瞬間陣風和長期平均混在同一係數下；遮蔽、上層設施及船舶配置也會改變受風面，需追蹤實際組合。","textEn":"The dock and attached vessels contribute windage and transfer load together; direction changes force location and torque. A quadratic wind relation requires a specified averaging period and elevation, rather than mixing gusts and long-term means under one coefficient.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「迎風面與風作用」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Windage and wind action\" is correct?","options":["浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。","遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。","浮碼頭與繫泊船舶的迎風面共同傳力，風向改變會讓受力位置與扭矩不同。"],"optionsEn":["Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels.","A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface.","The dock and attached vessels contribute windage and transfer load together; direction changes force location and torque."],"answer":2,"explanation":"浮碼頭與繫泊船舶的迎風面共同傳力，風向改變會讓受力位置與扭矩不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The dock and attached vessels contribute windage and transfer load together; direction changes force location and torque. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b291-v15-06","title":"迎風面與風作用：定量估算","titleEn":"Windage and wind action: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「迎風面與風作用」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Windage and wind action” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設空氣ρ=1.225kg/m³、Cd=1.2、投影面積100m²、指定風速20m/s，F=ρCdAU²/2=29.40kN；非操作門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume air1.225kg/m³,Cd=1.2,projected area100m² and selected speed20m/s. F=ρCdAU²/2=29.40kN, not an operating threshold. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在平面與立面標出迎風投影、合力高度及係纜點，核對風速定義與量測位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map projected area, force height and mooring points and check wind-speed definition and measurement location.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設空氣ρ=1.225kg/m³、Cd=1.2、投影面積100m²、指定風速20m/s，F=ρCdAU²/2=29.40kN；非操作門檻。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume air1.225kg/m³,Cd=1.2,projected area100m² and selected speed20m/s. F=ρCdAU²/2=29.40kN, not an operating threshold.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「迎風面與風作用」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Windage and wind action\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。","所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling.","Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b291-v15-07","title":"迎風面與風作用：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Windage and wind action: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「迎風面與風作用」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Windage and wind action” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在平面與立面標出迎風投影、合力高度及係纜點，核對風速定義與量測位置。比較不同船舶和風向配置，將遮蔽證據與未遮蔽情境分開，保留由偏心造成的扭矩需求。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map projected area, force height and mooring points and check wind-speed definition and measurement location. Compare vessel and directional configurations, separating evidenced shelter from exposed conditions and retaining torque demand created by an eccentric line of action. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在平面與立面標出迎風投影、合力高度及係纜點，核對風速定義與量測位置。比較不同船舶和風向配置，將遮蔽證據與未遮蔽情境分開，保留由偏心造成的扭矩需求。","observationEn":"Site practice: Map projected area, force height and mooring points and check wind-speed definition and measurement location. Compare vessel and directional configurations, separating evidenced shelter from exposed conditions and retaining torque demand created by an eccentric line of action.","failure":"注意干擾：新增遮棚或高船舶可增加迎風面及力矩，沿用空碼頭參數會低估系統需求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A canopy or taller vessel increases windage and torque, so empty-dock parameters understate demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在平面與立面標出迎風投影、合力高度及係纜點，核對風速定義與量測位置。比較不同船舶和風向配置，將遮蔽證據與未遮蔽情境分開，保留由偏心造成的扭矩需求。","textEn":"Map projected area, force height and mooring points and check wind-speed definition and measurement location. Compare vessel and directional configurations, separating evidenced shelter from exposed conditions and retaining torque demand created by an eccentric line of action.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在平面與立面標出迎風投影、合力高度及係纜點，核對風速定義與量測位置。比較不同船舶和風向配置，將遮蔽證據與未遮蔽情境分開，保留由偏心造成的扭矩需求。","textEn":"Map projected area, force height and mooring points and check wind-speed definition and measurement location. Compare vessel and directional configurations, separating evidenced shelter from exposed conditions and retaining torque demand created by an eccentric line of action.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「迎風面與風作用」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Windage and wind action\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在平面與立面標出迎風投影、合力高度及係纜點，核對風速定義與量測位置。","引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Map projected area, force height and mooring points and check wind-speed definition and measurement location.","Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在平面與立面標出迎風投影、合力高度及係纜點，核對風速定義與量測位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map projected area, force height and mooring points and check wind-speed definition and measurement location. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b291-v15-08","title":"迎風面與風作用：失效診斷","titleEn":"Windage and wind action: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「迎風面與風作用」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Windage and wind action” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"新增遮棚或高船舶可增加迎風面及力矩，沿用空碼頭參數會低估系統需求。平均風速與陣風混用則可能把不同時間尺度的作用錯誤相加或相互抵銷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A canopy or taller vessel increases windage and torque, so empty-dock parameters understate demand. Mixing mean wind and gust definitions can also incorrectly combine or cancel actions occurring on different response timescales in the system. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設空氣ρ=1.225kg/m³、Cd=1.2、投影面積100m²、指定風速20m/s，F=ρCdAU²/2=29.40kN；非操作門檻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: F=ρCdAU²/2=29.40kN, not an operating threshold.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"新增遮棚或高船舶可增加迎風面及力矩，沿用空碼頭參數會低估系統需求。平均風速與陣風混用則可能把不同時間尺度的作用錯誤相加或相互抵銷。","textEn":"A canopy or taller vessel increases windage and torque, so empty-dock parameters understate demand. Mixing mean wind and gust definitions can also incorrectly combine or cancel actions occurring on different response timescales in the system.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「迎風面與風作用」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Windage and wind action\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。","新增遮棚或高船舶可增加迎風面及力矩，沿用空碼頭參數會低估系統需求。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface.","A canopy or taller vessel increases windage and torque, so empty-dock parameters understate demand."],"answer":2,"explanation":"新增遮棚或高船舶可增加迎風面及力矩，沿用空碼頭參數會低估系統需求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A canopy or taller vessel increases windage and torque, so empty-dock parameters understate demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b291-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「水下流阻尺度」與「纜繩力向分解」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Submerged-current drag scale\" and \"Resolving mooring-line forces\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b291-v15-09","title":"水下流阻尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Submerged-current drag scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「水下流阻尺度」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Submerged-current drag scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水流作用在浮體水下投影及附掛設備，水位與吃水改變會更新受流面。均勻穩定流估算沒有涵蓋波浪加速度或渦激反應，狹窄通道與船間流場又會加速；分析應將力向、作用點及變動時間列明，避免把平均流速當成完整動態作用。 假設海水1025kg/m³、Cd=1.0、水下面積20m²、均勻流1.5m/s，F=ρCdAU²/2=23.0625kN；不含波浪慣性。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水下流阻尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Current acts on the submerged projection and attached equipment, which change with draft and water level. A uniform steady estimate excludes wave acceleration and vortex response, while narrow passages or vessel gaps can accelerate flow. Direction, force location and timescale therefore need explicit treatment; mean current speed does not by itself describe the complete dynamic action on the moored assembly. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,Cd=1.0,submerged area20m² and uniform current1.5m/s. Steady drag is23.0625kN, excluding wave inertia. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Submerged-current drag scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水下流阻尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Submerged-current drag scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-09-k1","title":"水下流阻尺度","titleEn":"Submerged-current drag scale","text":"水流作用在浮體水下投影及附掛設備，水位與吃水改變會更新受流面。均勻穩定流估算沒有涵蓋波浪加速度或渦激反應，狹窄通道與船間流場又會加速；分析應將力向、作用點及變動時間列明，避免把平均流速當成完整動態作用。","textEn":"Current acts on the submerged projection and attached equipment, which change with draft and water level. A uniform steady estimate excludes wave acceleration and vortex response, while narrow passages or vessel gaps can accelerate flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水下流阻尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Submerged-current drag scale\" is correct?","options":["水流作用在浮體水下投影及附掛設備，水位與吃水改變會更新受流面。","遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。","纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。"],"optionsEn":["Current acts on the submerged projection and attached equipment, which change with draft and water level.","A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface.","Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"水流作用在浮體水下投影及附掛設備，水位與吃水改變會更新受流面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Current acts on the submerged projection and attached equipment, which change with draft and water level. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b291-v15-10","title":"水下流阻尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Submerged-current drag scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水下流阻尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Submerged-current drag scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設海水1025kg/m³、Cd=1.0、水下面積20m²、均勻流1.5m/s，F=ρCdAU²/2=23.0625kN；不含波浪慣性。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,Cd=1.0,submerged area20m² and uniform current1.5m/s. Steady drag is23.0625kN, excluding wave inertia. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測不同深度與流向的速度並記錄吃水，核對水下突起和海生物附著是否納入投影。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure speed by depth and direction with draft, checking projections of appendages and marine growth.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設海水1025kg/m³、Cd=1.0、水下面積20m²、均勻流1.5m/s，F=ρCdAU²/2=23.0625kN；不含波浪慣性。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume seawater1025kg/m³,Cd=1.0,submerged area20m² and uniform current1.5m/s. Steady drag is23.0625kN, excluding wave inertia.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水下流阻尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Submerged-current drag scale\", which statement holds?","options":["浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。"],"optionsEn":["If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b291-v15-11","title":"水下流阻尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Submerged-current drag scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水下流阻尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Submerged-current drag scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測不同深度與流向的速度並記錄吃水，核對水下突起和海生物附著是否納入投影。將波浪與潮流資料同步，分開穩定拖曳和動態分量，避免用單點緩流區代表整個浮體。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure speed by depth and direction with draft, checking projections of appendages and marine growth. Synchronize wave and tide records and distinguish steady drag from dynamic components rather than representing the full submerged body with one sheltered measurement point. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：量測不同深度與流向的速度並記錄吃水，核對水下突起和海生物附著是否納入投影。將波浪與潮流資料同步，分開穩定拖曳和動態分量，避免用單點緩流區代表整個浮體。","observationEn":"Site practice: Measure speed by depth and direction with draft, checking projections of appendages and marine growth. Synchronize wave and tide records and distinguish steady drag from dynamic components rather than representing the full submerged body with one sheltered measurement point.","failure":"注意干擾：潮向反轉會讓不同纜繩承力，漏掉水下附掛物則低估面積。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Tidal reversal engages different lines, and omitted submerged attachments understate area. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測不同深度與流向的速度並記錄吃水，核對水下突起和海生物附著是否納入投影。將波浪與潮流資料同步，分開穩定拖曳和動態分量，避免用單點緩流區代表整個浮體。","textEn":"Measure speed by depth and direction with draft, checking projections of appendages and marine growth. Synchronize wave and tide records and distinguish steady drag from dynamic components rather than representing the full submerged body with one sheltered measurement point.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"量測不同深度與流向的速度並記錄吃水，核對水下突起和海生物附著是否納入投影。將波浪與潮流資料同步，分開穩定拖曳和動態分量，避免用單點緩流區代表整個浮體。","textEn":"Measure speed by depth and direction with draft, checking projections of appendages and marine growth. Synchronize wave and tide records and distinguish steady drag from dynamic components rather than representing the full submerged body with one sheltered measurement point.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水下流阻尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Submerged-current drag scale\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。","量測不同深度與流向的速度並記錄吃水，核對水下突起和海生物附著是否納入投影。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading.","Measure speed by depth and direction with draft, checking projections of appendages and marine growth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測不同深度與流向的速度並記錄吃水，核對水下突起和海生物附著是否納入投影。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure speed by depth and direction with draft, checking projections of appendages and marine growth. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b291-v15-12","title":"水下流阻尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Submerged-current drag scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水下流阻尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Submerged-current drag scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"潮向反轉會讓不同纜繩承力，漏掉水下附掛物則低估面積。若水流被船體間隙加速，遠處量到的背景速度可能無法代表真正控制局部連接的流場。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Tidal reversal engages different lines, and omitted submerged attachments understate area. Flow accelerated through vessel gaps means distant background measurements may not represent the conditions controlling a particular connection or part of the floating structure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設海水1025kg/m³、Cd=1.0、水下面積20m²、均勻流1.5m/s，F=ρCdAU²/2=23.0625kN；不含波浪慣性。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Steady drag is23.0625kN, excluding wave inertia.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"潮向反轉會讓不同纜繩承力，漏掉水下附掛物則低估面積。若水流被船體間隙加速，遠處量到的背景速度可能無法代表真正控制局部連接的流場。","textEn":"Tidal reversal engages different lines, and omitted submerged attachments understate area. Flow accelerated through vessel gaps means distant background measurements may not represent the conditions controlling a particular connection or part of the floating structure.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水下流阻尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Submerged-current drag scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["潮向反轉會讓不同纜繩承力，漏掉水下附掛物則低估面積。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。"],"optionsEn":["Tidal reversal engages different lines, and omitted submerged attachments understate area.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"潮向反轉會讓不同纜繩承力，漏掉水下附掛物則低估面積。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Tidal reversal engages different lines, and omitted submerged attachments understate area. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b291-v15-13","title":"纜繩力向分解：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Resolving mooring-line forces: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「纜繩力向分解」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Resolving mooring-line forces” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"係纜的軸向張力只有投影分量抵抗指定水平力，平面角與垂直角均會影響傳力。理想兩索對稱必須同時張緊才可平均分擔，預張力、鬆弛與彈性差異會破壞此條件；不能將幾何張力直接當成纜具額定能力或現場張緊設定。 假設水平力40kN由兩條水平對稱張緊纜承受，各與力向30°，T=40/(2cos30°)=23.094kN；未含預張與動載。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「纜繩力向分解」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Only a line's projected tension resists the selected horizontal action, with both plan and vertical angles affecting transfer. Two symmetric lines share equally only when simultaneously engaged. Pretension, slack and different elasticity invalidate this assumption, so geometric tension is not the rated capacity of the hardware or an instruction for setting line tension during actual mooring operations. Assume horizontal40kN resisted by two taut horizontal symmetric lines30°from the force direction. T=23.094kN each, excluding pretension and dynamics. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Resolving mooring-line forces” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「纜繩力向分解」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Resolving mooring-line forces”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-13-k1","title":"纜繩力向分解","titleEn":"Resolving mooring-line forces","text":"係纜的軸向張力只有投影分量抵抗指定水平力，平面角與垂直角均會影響傳力。理想兩索對稱必須同時張緊才可平均分擔，預張力、鬆弛與彈性差異會破壞此條件；不能將幾何張力直接當成纜具額定能力或現場張緊設定。","textEn":"Only a line's projected tension resists the selected horizontal action, with both plan and vertical angles affecting transfer. Two symmetric lines share equally only when simultaneously engaged.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「纜繩力向分解」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Resolving mooring-line forces\" is correct?","options":["纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。","係纜的軸向張力只有投影分量抵抗指定水平力，平面角與垂直角均會影響傳力。","所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry.","Only a line's projected tension resists the selected horizontal action, with both plan and vertical angles affecting transfer.","Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"係纜的軸向張力只有投影分量抵抗指定水平力，平面角與垂直角均會影響傳力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Only a line's projected tension resists the selected horizontal action, with both plan and vertical angles affecting transfer. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b291-v15-14","title":"纜繩力向分解：定量估算","titleEn":"Resolving mooring-line forces: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「纜繩力向分解」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Resolving mooring-line forces” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水平力40kN由兩條水平對稱張緊纜承受，各與力向30°，T=40/(2cos30°)=23.094kN；未含預張與動載。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume horizontal40kN resisted by two taut horizontal symmetric lines30°from the force direction. T=23.094kN each, excluding pretension and dynamics. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：畫每條纜的三維方向和自由體圖，確認角度參考軸及同時受力條件，分開預張與荷載增量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw each line in three dimensions and define angle reference and simultaneous engagement, separating pretension from load increment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水平力40kN由兩條水平對稱張緊纜承受，各與力向30°，T=40/(2cos30°)=23.094kN；未含預張與動載。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume horizontal40kN resisted by two taut horizontal symmetric lines30°from the force direction. T=23.094kN each, excluding pretension and dynamics.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「纜繩力向分解」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Resolving mooring-line forces\", which statement holds?","options":["所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。","引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction.","Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b291-v15-15","title":"纜繩力向分解：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Resolving mooring-line forces: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「纜繩力向分解」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Resolving mooring-line forces” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"畫每條纜的三維方向和自由體圖，確認角度參考軸及同時受力條件，分開預張與荷載增量。沿纜具、連接和岸上錨點追蹤力路徑，核對不均分時的替代情境。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw each line in three dimensions and define angle reference and simultaneous engagement, separating pretension from load increment. Trace force through rope, fittings and shore anchorage and evaluate alternative sharing when the symmetric assumption is not supported. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫每條纜的三維方向和自由體圖，確認角度參考軸及同時受力條件，分開預張與荷載增量。沿纜具、連接和岸上錨點追蹤力路徑，核對不均分時的替代情境。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw each line in three dimensions and define angle reference and simultaneous engagement, separating pretension from load increment. Trace force through rope, fittings and shore anchorage and evaluate alternative sharing when the symmetric assumption is not supported.","failure":"注意干擾：一條纜鬆弛時另一條可能承擔大部分需求，垂直角增加又減少水平分量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One slack line shifts much of the demand to another, and vertical inclination reduces horizontal resistance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"畫每條纜的三維方向和自由體圖，確認角度參考軸及同時受力條件，分開預張與荷載增量。沿纜具、連接和岸上錨點追蹤力路徑，核對不均分時的替代情境。","textEn":"Draw each line in three dimensions and define angle reference and simultaneous engagement, separating pretension from load increment. Trace force through rope, fittings and shore anchorage and evaluate alternative sharing when the symmetric assumption is not supported.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫每條纜的三維方向和自由體圖，確認角度參考軸及同時受力條件，分開預張與荷載增量。沿纜具、連接和岸上錨點追蹤力路徑，核對不均分時的替代情境。","textEn":"Draw each line in three dimensions and define angle reference and simultaneous engagement, separating pretension from load increment. Trace force through rope, fittings and shore anchorage and evaluate alternative sharing when the symmetric assumption is not supported.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「纜繩力向分解」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Resolving mooring-line forces\"?","options":["畫每條纜的三維方向和自由體圖，確認角度參考軸及同時受力條件，分開預張與荷載增量。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。"],"optionsEn":["Draw each line in three dimensions and define angle reference and simultaneous engagement, separating pretension from load increment.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves."],"answer":0,"explanation":"畫每條纜的三維方向和自由體圖，確認角度參考軸及同時受力條件，分開預張與荷載增量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw each line in three dimensions and define angle reference and simultaneous engagement, separating pretension from load increment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b291-v15-16","title":"纜繩力向分解：失效診斷","titleEn":"Resolving mooring-line forces: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「纜繩力向分解」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Resolving mooring-line forces” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"一條纜鬆弛時另一條可能承擔大部分需求，垂直角增加又減少水平分量。僅靠纜數平均分配，會漏掉不對稱姿態及突然繃緊造成的衝擊。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One slack line shifts much of the demand to another, and vertical inclination reduces horizontal resistance. Dividing load only by line count misses asymmetric geometry and impact when a previously slack line suddenly becomes taut. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設水平力40kN由兩條水平對稱張緊纜承受，各與力向30°，T=40/(2cos30°)=23.094kN；未含預張與動載。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: T=23.094kN each, excluding pretension and dynamics.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"一條纜鬆弛時另一條可能承擔大部分需求，垂直角增加又減少水平分量。僅靠纜數平均分配，會漏掉不對稱姿態及突然繃緊造成的衝擊。","textEn":"One slack line shifts much of the demand to another, and vertical inclination reduces horizontal resistance. Dividing load only by line count misses asymmetric geometry and impact when a previously slack line suddenly becomes taut.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「纜繩力向分解」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Resolving mooring-line forces\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","一條纜鬆弛時另一條可能承擔大部分需求，垂直角增加又減少水平分量。","所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","One slack line shifts much of the demand to another, and vertical inclination reduces horizontal resistance.","Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"一條纜鬆弛時另一條可能承擔大部分需求，垂直角增加又減少水平分量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One slack line shifts much of the demand to another, and vertical inclination reduces horizontal resistance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b291-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「材料伸長與有效剛度」與「潮位幾何與鬆弛」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Material extension and effective stiffness\" and \"Tidal geometry and slack\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b291-v15-17","title":"材料伸長與有效剛度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Material extension and effective stiffness: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「材料伸長與有效剛度」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Material extension and effective stiffness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"纜繩伸長包含材料應變與編織重排，許多材料在循環中有遲滯、徐變和不同切線剛度。直桿彈性式只是一個局部基準，不適合把所有纜索都當鋼杆；量測時還需分開初始鬆弛與幾何拉直，否則剛度估計會隨量測區間改變。 假設直線彈性纜有效EA=5000kN、長20m、張力增量25kN，伸長ΔL=ΔTL/(EA)=0.10m；不含鬆弛與徐變。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「材料伸長與有效剛度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Line extension combines material strain with constructional rearrangement, and many ropes show hysteresis, creep and changing tangent stiffness. A straight elastic rod is a local baseline rather than a universal steel-like representation. Initial slack and geometric straightening must be separated from material extension, otherwise the inferred stiffness depends on which portion of the load-displacement path was measured. Assume a straight elastic line with effective EA=5000kN,length20m and tension increment25kN. Extension is0.10m, excluding slack and creep. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Material extension and effective stiffness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「材料伸長與有效剛度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Material extension and effective stiffness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-17-k1","title":"材料伸長與有效剛度","titleEn":"Material extension and effective stiffness","text":"纜繩伸長包含材料應變與編織重排，許多材料在循環中有遲滯、徐變和不同切線剛度。直桿彈性式只是一個局部基準，不適合把所有纜索都當鋼杆；量測時還需分開初始鬆弛與幾何拉直，否則剛度估計會隨量測區間改變。","textEn":"Line extension combines material strain with constructional rearrangement, and many ropes show hysteresis, creep and changing tangent stiffness. A straight elastic rod is a local baseline rather than a universal steel-like representation.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「材料伸長與有效剛度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Material extension and effective stiffness\" is correct?","options":["所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。","浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。","纜繩伸長包含材料應變與編織重排，許多材料在循環中有遲滯、徐變和不同切線剛度。"],"optionsEn":["Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling.","If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension.","Line extension combines material strain with constructional rearrangement, and many ropes show hysteresis, creep and changing tangent stiffness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"纜繩伸長包含材料應變與編織重排，許多材料在循環中有遲滯、徐變和不同切線剛度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Line extension combines material strain with constructional rearrangement, and many ropes show hysteresis, creep and changing tangent stiffness. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b291-v15-18","title":"材料伸長與有效剛度：定量估算","titleEn":"Material extension and effective stiffness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「材料伸長與有效剛度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Material extension and effective stiffness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設直線彈性纜有效EA=5000kN、長20m、張力增量25kN，伸長ΔL=ΔTL/(EA)=0.10m；不含鬆弛與徐變。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a straight elastic line with effective EA=5000kN,length20m and tension increment25kN. Extension is0.10m, excluding slack and creep. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：使用相符含水與循環條件的試驗曲線，明列有效標距並分離預張階段。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use response curves under relevant moisture and cycling, defining gauge length and separating pretension.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設直線彈性纜有效EA=5000kN、長20m、張力增量25kN，伸長ΔL=ΔTL/(EA)=0.10m；不含鬆弛與徐變。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume a straight elastic line with effective EA=5000kN,length20m and tension increment25kN. Extension is0.10m, excluding slack and creep.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「材料伸長與有效剛度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Material extension and effective stiffness\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。","理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information.","All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b291-v15-19","title":"材料伸長與有效剛度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Material extension and effective stiffness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「材料伸長與有效剛度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Material extension and effective stiffness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"使用相符含水與循環條件的試驗曲線，明列有效標距並分離預張階段。比較載入卸載與長時間保持資料，確認計算用割線或切線剛度，避免以單次拉伸斜率代表全部壽期。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use response curves under relevant moisture and cycling, defining gauge length and separating pretension. Compare loading, unloading and hold periods, identify secant versus tangent stiffness, and avoid representing the entire service history by one slope from a single tensile test. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：使用相符含水與循環條件的試驗曲線，明列有效標距並分離預張階段。比較載入卸載與長時間保持資料，確認計算用割線或切線剛度，避免以單次拉伸斜率代表全部壽期。","observationEn":"Site practice: Use response curves under relevant moisture and cycling, defining gauge length and separating pretension. Compare loading, unloading and hold periods, identify secant versus tangent stiffness, and avoid representing the entire service history by one slope from a single tensile test.","failure":"注意干擾：將編織收緊當材料彈性會低估後續切線剛度，長時間徐變又可能增加鬆弛和位移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mistaking constructional tightening for elasticity understates later tangent stiffness, while creep adds slack and displacement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"使用相符含水與循環條件的試驗曲線，明列有效標距並分離預張階段。比較載入卸載與長時間保持資料，確認計算用割線或切線剛度，避免以單次拉伸斜率代表全部壽期。","textEn":"Use response curves under relevant moisture and cycling, defining gauge length and separating pretension. Compare loading, unloading and hold periods, identify secant versus tangent stiffness, and avoid representing the entire service history by one slope from a single tensile test.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"使用相符含水與循環條件的試驗曲線，明列有效標距並分離預張階段。比較載入卸載與長時間保持資料，確認計算用割線或切線剛度，避免以單次拉伸斜率代表全部壽期。","textEn":"Use response curves under relevant moisture and cycling, defining gauge length and separating pretension. Compare loading, unloading and hold periods, identify secant versus tangent stiffness, and avoid representing the entire service history by one slope from a single tensile test.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「材料伸長與有效剛度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Material extension and effective stiffness\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","使用相符含水與循環條件的試驗曲線，明列有效標距並分離預張階段。","浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use response curves under relevant moisture and cycling, defining gauge length and separating pretension.","Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels."],"answer":1,"explanation":"使用相符含水與循環條件的試驗曲線，明列有效標距並分離預張階段。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use response curves under relevant moisture and cycling, defining gauge length and separating pretension. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b291-v15-20","title":"材料伸長與有效剛度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Material extension and effective stiffness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「材料伸長與有效剛度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Material extension and effective stiffness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將編織收緊當材料彈性會低估後續切線剛度，長時間徐變又可能增加鬆弛和位移。相同最終伸長下，張力歷史與儲能可以不同，不能只讀總長度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mistaking constructional tightening for elasticity understates later tangent stiffness, while creep adds slack and displacement. Equal final extension can conceal different tension histories and stored energy, so total line length alone is insufficient for interpreting response. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設直線彈性纜有效EA=5000kN、長20m、張力增量25kN，伸長ΔL=ΔTL/(EA)=0.10m；不含鬆弛與徐變。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Extension is0.10m, excluding slack and creep.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將編織收緊當材料彈性會低估後續切線剛度，長時間徐變又可能增加鬆弛和位移。相同最終伸長下，張力歷史與儲能可以不同，不能只讀總長度。","textEn":"Mistaking constructional tightening for elasticity understates later tangent stiffness, while creep adds slack and displacement. Equal final extension can conceal different tension histories and stored energy, so total line length alone is insufficient for interpreting response.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「材料伸長與有效剛度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Material extension and effective stiffness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。","將編織收緊當材料彈性會低估後續切線剛度，長時間徐變又可能增加鬆弛和位移。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension.","Mistaking constructional tightening for elasticity understates later tangent stiffness, while creep adds slack and displacement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將編織收緊當材料彈性會低估後續切線剛度，長時間徐變又可能增加鬆弛和位移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mistaking constructional tightening for elasticity understates later tangent stiffness, while creep adds slack and displacement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b291-v15-21","title":"潮位幾何與鬆弛：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tidal geometry and slack: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「潮位幾何與鬆弛」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tidal geometry and slack” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"岸上固定點與浮台的高差隨潮位變化，連線長度及入射角因此改變，即使平面位置未動也可能拉緊纜繩。直線距離只是幾何下限，鏈條垂度和海床接觸另影響反力；不能把一段預留長度視為在所有水位都具有相同的鬆弛餘量。 假設水平距10m，高差由1變3m，直線距由√101=10.0499增至√109=10.4403m，增0.3904m；非鏈條張力模型。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「潮位幾何與鬆弛」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The height difference between a shore point and a pontoon varies with tide, changing chord length and angle even without horizontal motion. Straight-line distance is a geometric lower bound; chain sag and bed contact separately affect reaction. A reserved length therefore does not provide the same slack margin at every water level or imply unchanged horizontal restoring behavior. Assume horizontal distance10m and height difference1to3m. Chord length rises10.0499to10.4403m, an increase0.3904m; this is not a catenary-tension model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tidal geometry and slack” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「潮位幾何與鬆弛」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tidal geometry and slack”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-21-k1","title":"潮位幾何與鬆弛","titleEn":"Tidal geometry and slack","text":"岸上固定點與浮台的高差隨潮位變化，連線長度及入射角因此改變，即使平面位置未動也可能拉緊纜繩。直線距離只是幾何下限，鏈條垂度和海床接觸另影響反力；不能把一段預留長度視為在所有水位都具有相同的鬆弛餘量。","textEn":"The height difference between a shore point and a pontoon varies with tide, changing chord length and angle even without horizontal motion. Straight-line distance is a geometric lower bound; chain sag and bed contact separately affect reaction.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「潮位幾何與鬆弛」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tidal geometry and slack\" is correct?","options":["岸上固定點與浮台的高差隨潮位變化，連線長度及入射角因此改變，即使平面位置未動也可能拉緊纜繩。","浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。","所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。"],"optionsEn":["The height difference between a shore point and a pontoon varies with tide, changing chord length and angle even without horizontal motion.","If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension.","Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"岸上固定點與浮台的高差隨潮位變化，連線長度及入射角因此改變，即使平面位置未動也可能拉緊纜繩。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The height difference between a shore point and a pontoon varies with tide, changing chord length and angle even without horizontal motion. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b291-v15-22","title":"潮位幾何與鬆弛：定量估算","titleEn":"Tidal geometry and slack: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「潮位幾何與鬆弛」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tidal geometry and slack” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水平距10m，高差由1變3m，直線距由√101=10.0499增至√109=10.4403m，增0.3904m；非鏈條張力模型。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume horizontal distance10m and height difference1to3m. Chord length rises10.0499to10.4403m, an increase0.3904m; this is not a catenary-tension model. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同一基準畫高低水位的纜端位置，量測可用纜長、垂度和海床接觸，核對可能卡阻。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot line-end positions at different levels on one datum, measuring available length, sag and seabed contact and checking obstructions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設水平距10m，高差由1變3m，直線距由√101=10.0499增至√109=10.4403m，增0.3904m；非鏈條張力模型。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume horizontal distance10m and height difference1to3m. Chord length rises10.0499to10.4403m, an increase0.3904m; this is not a catenary-tension model.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「潮位幾何與鬆弛」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tidal geometry and slack\", which statement holds?","options":["引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。"],"optionsEn":["Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b291-v15-23","title":"潮位幾何與鬆弛：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tidal geometry and slack: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「潮位幾何與鬆弛」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tidal geometry and slack” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同一基準畫高低水位的纜端位置，量測可用纜長、垂度和海床接觸，核對可能卡阻。把幾何變化連回經驗證的力位移曲線，另查高水位時岸上構件的垂直反力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot line-end positions at different levels on one datum, measuring available length, sag and seabed contact and checking obstructions. Relate geometric changes to a verified force-displacement curve and separately examine vertical reactions on shore attachments during higher water. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以同一基準畫高低水位的纜端位置，量測可用纜長、垂度和海床接觸，核對可能卡阻。把幾何變化連回經驗證的力位移曲線，另查高水位時岸上構件的垂直反力。","observationEn":"Site practice: Plot line-end positions at different levels on one datum, measuring available length, sag and seabed contact and checking obstructions. Relate geometric changes to a verified force-displacement curve and separately examine vertical reactions on shore attachments during higher water.","failure":"注意干擾：高水位使纜線接近拉直時，剩餘伸長可能轉為很大的張力增量；低水位則可能增加海床磨耗。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: As a line straightens at high water, further extension can produce a large tension increment, while low water increases seabed abrasion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同一基準畫高低水位的纜端位置，量測可用纜長、垂度和海床接觸，核對可能卡阻。把幾何變化連回經驗證的力位移曲線，另查高水位時岸上構件的垂直反力。","textEn":"Plot line-end positions at different levels on one datum, measuring available length, sag and seabed contact and checking obstructions. Relate geometric changes to a verified force-displacement curve and separately examine vertical reactions on shore attachments during higher water.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以同一基準畫高低水位的纜端位置，量測可用纜長、垂度和海床接觸，核對可能卡阻。把幾何變化連回經驗證的力位移曲線，另查高水位時岸上構件的垂直反力。","textEn":"Plot line-end positions at different levels on one datum, measuring available length, sag and seabed contact and checking obstructions. Relate geometric changes to a verified force-displacement curve and separately examine vertical reactions on shore attachments during higher water.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「潮位幾何與鬆弛」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tidal geometry and slack\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。","以同一基準畫高低水位的纜端位置，量測可用纜長、垂度和海床接觸，核對可能卡阻。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface.","Plot line-end positions at different levels on one datum, measuring available length, sag and seabed contact and checking obstructions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以同一基準畫高低水位的纜端位置，量測可用纜長、垂度和海床接觸，核對可能卡阻。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot line-end positions at different levels on one datum, measuring available length, sag and seabed contact and checking obstructions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b291-v15-24","title":"潮位幾何與鬆弛：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tidal geometry and slack: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「潮位幾何與鬆弛」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tidal geometry and slack” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"高水位使纜線接近拉直時，剩餘伸長可能轉為很大的張力增量；低水位則可能增加海床磨耗。只檢查中潮幾何，無法涵蓋兩端的不同行為。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"As a line straightens at high water, further extension can produce a large tension increment, while low water increases seabed abrasion. Mid-tide geometry alone cannot cover these different behaviors at the ends of the tidal range. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設水平距10m，高差由1變3m，直線距由√101=10.0499增至√109=10.4403m，增0.3904m；非鏈條張力模型。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Chord length rises10.0499to10.4403m, an increase0.3904m; this is not a catenary-tension model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"高水位使纜線接近拉直時，剩餘伸長可能轉為很大的張力增量；低水位則可能增加海床磨耗。只檢查中潮幾何，無法涵蓋兩端的不同行為。","textEn":"As a line straightens at high water, further extension can produce a large tension increment, while low water increases seabed abrasion. Mid-tide geometry alone cannot cover these different behaviors at the ends of the tidal range.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「潮位幾何與鬆弛」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tidal geometry and slack\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["高水位使纜線接近拉直時，剩餘伸長可能轉為很大的張力增量；低水位則可能增加海床磨耗。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。"],"optionsEn":["As a line straightens at high water, further extension can produce a large tension increment, while low water increases seabed abrasion.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高水位使纜線接近拉直時，剩餘伸長可能轉為很大的張力增量；低水位則可能增加海床磨耗。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"As a line straightens at high water, further extension can produce a large tension increment, while low water increases seabed abrasion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b291-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「並聯恢復剛度」與「水平振盪時間尺度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Parallel restoring stiffness\" and \"Horizontal oscillation timescale\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b291-v15-25","title":"並聯恢復剛度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Parallel restoring stiffness: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「並聯恢復剛度」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Parallel restoring stiffness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"多條纜的水平恢復力可以在特定平衡點線性化，但只有同方向、同時受力的小位移增量才直接相加。幾何旋轉與單向受拉特性會改變參與線數，整個系統還有浮台轉動自由度；單一總剛度不代表所有位移方向和幅度都相同。 假設兩個同向並聯線性恢復分量k1=20、k2=30kN/m，受增量力10kN時x=10/(20+30)=0.20m；兩者均持續受力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「並聯恢復剛度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Horizontal restoring force can be linearized about one equilibrium, with direct addition applying only to simultaneously engaged, collinear small-displacement increments. Geometry and tension-only behavior change the active lines, and the dock also rotates. One total stiffness cannot describe every direction and amplitude, so its use must remain tied to the specified equilibrium state and local motion coordinate. Assume two collinear parallel restoring components20and30kN/m remain engaged. An incremental10kN gives x=10/50=0.20m near that equilibrium. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Parallel restoring stiffness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「並聯恢復剛度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Parallel restoring stiffness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-25-k1","title":"並聯恢復剛度","titleEn":"Parallel restoring stiffness","text":"多條纜的水平恢復力可以在特定平衡點線性化，但只有同方向、同時受力的小位移增量才直接相加。幾何旋轉與單向受拉特性會改變參與線數，整個系統還有浮台轉動自由度；單一總剛度不代表所有位移方向和幅度都相同。","textEn":"Horizontal restoring force can be linearized about one equilibrium, with direct addition applying only to simultaneously engaged, collinear small-displacement increments. Geometry and tension-only behavior change the active lines, and the dock also rotates.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「並聯恢復剛度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Parallel restoring stiffness\" is correct?","options":["所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。","多條纜的水平恢復力可以在特定平衡點線性化，但只有同方向、同時受力的小位移增量才直接相加。","自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。"],"optionsEn":["Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction.","Horizontal restoring force can be linearized about one equilibrium, with direct addition applying only to simultaneously engaged, collinear small-displacement increments.","A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information."],"answer":1,"explanation":"多條纜的水平恢復力可以在特定平衡點線性化，但只有同方向、同時受力的小位移增量才直接相加。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Horizontal restoring force can be linearized about one equilibrium, with direct addition applying only to simultaneously engaged, collinear small-displacement increments. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b291-v15-26","title":"並聯恢復剛度：定量估算","titleEn":"Parallel restoring stiffness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「並聯恢復剛度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Parallel restoring stiffness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設兩個同向並聯線性恢復分量k1=20、k2=30kN/m，受增量力10kN時x=10/(20+30)=0.20m；兩者均持續受力。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume two collinear parallel restoring components20and30kN/m remain engaged. An incremental10kN gives x=10/50=0.20m near that equilibrium. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將每條纜的力位移投影到相同水平座標，檢查小位移試驗期間是否有鬆弛或滑移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Project each force-displacement response onto the same horizontal coordinate and check slack or sliding during small-motion tests.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設兩個同向並聯線性恢復分量k1=20、k2=30kN/m，受增量力10kN時x=10/(20+30)=0.20m；兩者均持續受力。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume two collinear parallel restoring components20and30kN/m remain engaged. An incremental10kN gives x=10/50=0.20m near that equilibrium.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「並聯恢復剛度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Parallel restoring stiffness\", which statement holds?","options":["理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。","浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading.","Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b291-v15-27","title":"並聯恢復剛度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Parallel restoring stiffness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「並聯恢復剛度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Parallel restoring stiffness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將每條纜的力位移投影到相同水平座標，檢查小位移試驗期間是否有鬆弛或滑移。比較正反向剛度與轉動耦合，記錄適用平衡點，不能將局部斜率延伸到極端偏移。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Project each force-displacement response onto the same horizontal coordinate and check slack or sliding during small-motion tests. Compare opposite directions and rotational coupling, recording the equilibrium point instead of extending one local slope to extreme offsets of the dock. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將每條纜的力位移投影到相同水平座標，檢查小位移試驗期間是否有鬆弛或滑移。比較正反向剛度與轉動耦合，記錄適用平衡點，不能將局部斜率延伸到極端偏移。","observationEn":"Site practice: Project each force-displacement response onto the same horizontal coordinate and check slack or sliding during small-motion tests. Compare opposite directions and rotational coupling, recording the equilibrium point instead of extending one local slope to extreme offsets of the dock.","failure":"注意干擾：一條纜失去預張會讓原先並聯分擔消失，總位移可能突然增加。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Loss of pretension removes a previously active parallel contribution and can sharply increase displacement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將每條纜的力位移投影到相同水平座標，檢查小位移試驗期間是否有鬆弛或滑移。比較正反向剛度與轉動耦合，記錄適用平衡點，不能將局部斜率延伸到極端偏移。","textEn":"Project each force-displacement response onto the same horizontal coordinate and check slack or sliding during small-motion tests. Compare opposite directions and rotational coupling, recording the equilibrium point instead of extending one local slope to extreme offsets of the dock.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將每條纜的力位移投影到相同水平座標，檢查小位移試驗期間是否有鬆弛或滑移。比較正反向剛度與轉動耦合，記錄適用平衡點，不能將局部斜率延伸到極端偏移。","textEn":"Project each force-displacement response onto the same horizontal coordinate and check slack or sliding during small-motion tests. Compare opposite directions and rotational coupling, recording the equilibrium point instead of extending one local slope to extreme offsets of the dock.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「並聯恢復剛度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Parallel restoring stiffness\"?","options":["將每條纜的力位移投影到相同水平座標，檢查小位移試驗期間是否有鬆弛或滑移。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。"],"optionsEn":["Project each force-displacement response onto the same horizontal coordinate and check slack or sliding during small-motion tests.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將每條纜的力位移投影到相同水平座標，檢查小位移試驗期間是否有鬆弛或滑移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Project each force-displacement response onto the same horizontal coordinate and check slack or sliding during small-motion tests. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b291-v15-28","title":"並聯恢復剛度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Parallel restoring stiffness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「並聯恢復剛度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Parallel restoring stiffness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"一條纜失去預張會讓原先並聯分擔消失，總位移可能突然增加。若只用所有材料EA相加而未投影幾何，會高估真正提供的水平恢復剛度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Loss of pretension removes a previously active parallel contribution and can sharply increase displacement. Adding material EA values without geometric projection also overstates the horizontal restoring stiffness actually available to the floating structure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設兩個同向並聯線性恢復分量k1=20、k2=30kN/m，受增量力10kN時x=10/(20+30)=0.20m；兩者均持續受力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: An incremental10kN gives x=10/50=0.20m near that equilibrium.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"一條纜失去預張會讓原先並聯分擔消失，總位移可能突然增加。若只用所有材料EA相加而未投影幾何，會高估真正提供的水平恢復剛度。","textEn":"Loss of pretension removes a previously active parallel contribution and can sharply increase displacement. Adding material EA values without geometric projection also overstates the horizontal restoring stiffness actually available to the floating structure.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「並聯恢復剛度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Parallel restoring stiffness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","一條纜失去預張會讓原先並聯分擔消失，總位移可能突然增加。","自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Loss of pretension removes a previously active parallel contribution and can sharply increase displacement.","A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information."],"answer":1,"explanation":"一條纜失去預張會讓原先並聯分擔消失，總位移可能突然增加。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Loss of pretension removes a previously active parallel contribution and can sharply increase displacement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b291-v15-29","title":"水平振盪時間尺度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Horizontal oscillation timescale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「水平振盪時間尺度」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Horizontal oscillation timescale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"浮碼頭質量、附加水質量與恢復剛度共同決定自然振盪尺度，與波浪或船行波頻率接近時反應可能放大。單自由度無阻尼模型只能估計週期，不能預測峰值或共振幅度；實際纜繩非線性、摩擦及輻射阻尼必須另行識別並與觀測對照。 假設已含附加質量的有效m=100000kg、水平k=50000N/m，Tn=2π√(m/k)=8.886s；無阻尼線性示意。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水平振盪時間尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Dock mass, hydrodynamic added mass and restoring stiffness set a natural timescale, with possible amplification near wave or wake frequencies. An undamped single-degree model estimates period only, not peak response or resonance amplitude. Real line nonlinearity, friction and radiation damping require separate identification and observation before the simplified timing relation can support interpretation of actual motion. Assume effective mass100000kg already includes added mass and horizontal stiffness50000N/m. Tn=2π√(m/k)=8.886s for an undamped linear illustration. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Horizontal oscillation timescale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水平振盪時間尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Horizontal oscillation timescale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-29-k1","title":"水平振盪時間尺度","titleEn":"Horizontal oscillation timescale","text":"浮碼頭質量、附加水質量與恢復剛度共同決定自然振盪尺度，與波浪或船行波頻率接近時反應可能放大。單自由度無阻尼模型只能估計週期，不能預測峰值或共振幅度；實際纜繩非線性、摩擦及輻射阻尼必須另行識別並與觀測對照。","textEn":"Dock mass, hydrodynamic added mass and restoring stiffness set a natural timescale, with possible amplification near wave or wake frequencies. An undamped single-degree model estimates period only, not peak response or resonance amplitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水平振盪時間尺度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Horizontal oscillation timescale\" is correct?","options":["自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。","引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。","浮碼頭質量、附加水質量與恢復剛度共同決定自然振盪尺度，與波浪或船行波頻率接近時反應可能放大。"],"optionsEn":["A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information.","Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements.","Dock mass, hydrodynamic added mass and restoring stiffness set a natural timescale, with possible amplification near wave or wake frequencies."],"answer":2,"explanation":"浮碼頭質量、附加水質量與恢復剛度共同決定自然振盪尺度，與波浪或船行波頻率接近時反應可能放大。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Dock mass, hydrodynamic added mass and restoring stiffness set a natural timescale, with possible amplification near wave or wake frequencies. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b291-v15-30","title":"水平振盪時間尺度：定量估算","titleEn":"Horizontal oscillation timescale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水平振盪時間尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Horizontal oscillation timescale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設已含附加質量的有效m=100000kg、水平k=50000N/m，Tn=2π√(m/k)=8.886s；無阻尼線性示意。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume effective mass100000kg already includes added mass and horizontal stiffness50000N/m. Tn=2π√(m/k)=8.886s for an undamped linear illustration. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從小幅自由衰減或環境振動記錄辨識週期，核對質量、纜態與潮位是否與模型一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Identify period from small-amplitude decay or ambient motion with matching mass, line state and tide.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設已含附加質量的有效m=100000kg、水平k=50000N/m，Tn=2π√(m/k)=8.886s；無阻尼線性示意。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume effective mass100000kg already includes added mass and horizontal stiffness50000N/m. Tn=2π√(m/k)=8.886s for an undamped linear illustration.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水平振盪時間尺度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Horizontal oscillation timescale\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。","遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves.","A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b291-v15-31","title":"水平振盪時間尺度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Horizontal oscillation timescale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水平振盪時間尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Horizontal oscillation timescale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從小幅自由衰減或環境振動記錄辨識週期，核對質量、纜態與潮位是否與模型一致。比較外力頻譜並另估阻尼，保留大位移時非線性特徵，不用單一週期推定峰值張力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Identify period from small-amplitude decay or ambient motion with matching mass, line state and tide. Compare forcing spectra and estimate damping separately, retaining nonlinear behavior at larger offsets rather than using one period to infer maximum line tension. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：從小幅自由衰減或環境振動記錄辨識週期，核對質量、纜態與潮位是否與模型一致。比較外力頻譜並另估阻尼，保留大位移時非線性特徵，不用單一週期推定峰值張力。","observationEn":"Site practice: Identify period from small-amplitude decay or ambient motion with matching mass, line state and tide. Compare forcing spectra and estimate damping separately, retaining nonlinear behavior at larger offsets rather than using one period to infer maximum line tension.","failure":"注意干擾：附加質量重複計入會拉長預測週期，纜剛度隨潮位改變則移動共振區。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Double-counted added mass lengthens the predicted period, while tide-dependent line stiffness shifts the resonance range. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從小幅自由衰減或環境振動記錄辨識週期，核對質量、纜態與潮位是否與模型一致。比較外力頻譜並另估阻尼，保留大位移時非線性特徵，不用單一週期推定峰值張力。","textEn":"Identify period from small-amplitude decay or ambient motion with matching mass, line state and tide. Compare forcing spectra and estimate damping separately, retaining nonlinear behavior at larger offsets rather than using one period to infer maximum line tension.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"從小幅自由衰減或環境振動記錄辨識週期，核對質量、纜態與潮位是否與模型一致。比較外力頻譜並另估阻尼，保留大位移時非線性特徵，不用單一週期推定峰值張力。","textEn":"Identify period from small-amplitude decay or ambient motion with matching mass, line state and tide. Compare forcing spectra and estimate damping separately, retaining nonlinear behavior at larger offsets rather than using one period to infer maximum line tension.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水平振盪時間尺度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Horizontal oscillation timescale\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","從小幅自由衰減或環境振動記錄辨識週期，核對質量、纜態與潮位是否與模型一致。","所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Identify period from small-amplitude decay or ambient motion with matching mass, line state and tide.","Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"從小幅自由衰減或環境振動記錄辨識週期，核對質量、纜態與潮位是否與模型一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Identify period from small-amplitude decay or ambient motion with matching mass, line state and tide. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b291-v15-32","title":"水平振盪時間尺度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Horizontal oscillation timescale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水平振盪時間尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Horizontal oscillation timescale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"附加質量重複計入會拉長預測週期，纜剛度隨潮位改變則移動共振區。即使週期吻合，錯誤阻尼仍可能讓預測振幅與實測相差很大。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Double-counted added mass lengthens the predicted period, while tide-dependent line stiffness shifts the resonance range. Matching period alone does not establish correct amplitude because an incorrect damping estimate can still produce a large response discrepancy. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設已含附加質量的有效m=100000kg、水平k=50000N/m，Tn=2π√(m/k)=8.886s；無阻尼線性示意。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Tn=2π√(m/k)=8.886s for an undamped linear illustration.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「自然週期算對就可以不需阻尼資料直接預測最大纜繩張力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A correct natural period predicts maximum mooring tension without any damping information.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"附加質量重複計入會拉長預測週期，纜剛度隨潮位改變則移動共振區。即使週期吻合，錯誤阻尼仍可能讓預測振幅與實測相差很大。","textEn":"Double-counted added mass lengthens the predicted period, while tide-dependent line stiffness shifts the resonance range. Matching period alone does not establish correct amplitude because an incorrect damping estimate can still produce a large response discrepancy.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水平振盪時間尺度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Horizontal oscillation timescale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。","附加質量重複計入會拉長預測週期，纜剛度隨潮位改變則移動共振區。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements.","Double-counted added mass lengthens the predicted period, while tide-dependent line stiffness shifts the resonance range."],"answer":2,"explanation":"附加質量重複計入會拉長預測週期，纜剛度隨潮位改變則移動共振區。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Double-counted added mass lengthens the predicted period, while tide-dependent line stiffness shifts the resonance range. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b291-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「引橋坡度與行程」與「浮力儲備與損艙」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Gangway slope and travel\" and \"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b291-v15-33","title":"引橋坡度與行程：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Gangway slope and travel: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「引橋坡度與行程」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Gangway slope and travel” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"岸上平台固定而浮台升降，引橋坡度及端部滑移隨水位變化，與纜繩容許位移需要共同檢查。幾何斜率不是無障礙或使用合格證明，轉折、扶手、表面及動態運動亦有要求；在水平長度和實際橋長之間混用會導致角度與行程錯誤。 假設高差1.2m、水平投影12m，坡度10%、角度atan(1.2/12)=5.711°，斜長12.0599m；不是通行允收值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「引橋坡度與行程」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A fixed shore platform and moving pontoon change gangway slope and end travel, which must be compatible with mooring offsets. Geometric grade is not proof of accessibility or acceptable use; transitions, rails, surfaces and dynamic movement matter too. Confusing horizontal run with actual span length corrupts angle and travel calculations even when the height difference is measured correctly. Assume rise1.2m and horizontal run12m. Grade is10%,angle5.711° and sloping length12.0599m, not an access acceptance criterion. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gangway slope and travel” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「引橋坡度與行程」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gangway slope and travel”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-33-k1","title":"引橋坡度與行程","titleEn":"Gangway slope and travel","text":"岸上平台固定而浮台升降，引橋坡度及端部滑移隨水位變化，與纜繩容許位移需要共同檢查。幾何斜率不是無障礙或使用合格證明，轉折、扶手、表面及動態運動亦有要求；在水平長度和實際橋長之間混用會導致角度與行程錯誤。","textEn":"A fixed shore platform and moving pontoon change gangway slope and end travel, which must be compatible with mooring offsets. Geometric grade is not proof of accessibility or acceptable use; transitions, rails, surfaces and dynamic movement matter too.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「引橋坡度與行程」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gangway slope and travel\" is correct?","options":["岸上平台固定而浮台升降，引橋坡度及端部滑移隨水位變化，與纜繩容許位移需要共同檢查。","引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。","理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。"],"optionsEn":["A fixed shore platform and moving pontoon change gangway slope and end travel, which must be compatible with mooring offsets.","Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements.","All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading."],"answer":0,"explanation":"岸上平台固定而浮台升降，引橋坡度及端部滑移隨水位變化，與纜繩容許位移需要共同檢查。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A fixed shore platform and moving pontoon change gangway slope and end travel, which must be compatible with mooring offsets. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b291-v15-34","title":"引橋坡度與行程：定量估算","titleEn":"Gangway slope and travel: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「引橋坡度與行程」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Gangway slope and travel” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設高差1.2m、水平投影12m，坡度10%、角度atan(1.2/12)=5.711°，斜長12.0599m；不是通行允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume rise1.2m and horizontal run12m. Grade is10%,angle5.711° and sloping length12.0599m, not an access acceptance criterion. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分別標示水平投影、實際橋長及端部可滑行範圍，在高低潮與浮台偏移組合下重畫幾何。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Distinguish horizontal run, span length and available end travel, redrawing geometry for combined tide and dock offsets.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設高差1.2m、水平投影12m，坡度10%、角度atan(1.2/12)=5.711°，斜長12.0599m；不是通行允收值。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume rise1.2m and horizontal run12m. Grade is10%,angle5.711° and sloping length12.0599m, not an access acceptance criterion.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「引橋坡度與行程」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gangway slope and travel\", which statement holds?","options":["浮碼頭繫泊需求只由碼頭自身迎風面決定而不受靠船影響。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","纜繩總數增加一倍就保證每條纜在任何姿態都只受一半張力。"],"optionsEn":["Floating-dock mooring demand depends only on dock windage and is unaffected by attached vessels.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Doubling line count guarantees half the tension in every line under any geometry."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b291-v15-35","title":"引橋坡度與行程：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gangway slope and travel: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「引橋坡度與行程」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Gangway slope and travel” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分別標示水平投影、實際橋長及端部可滑行範圍，在高低潮與浮台偏移組合下重畫幾何。依適用無障礙及設施設計要求檢查全路徑，另記防滑、夾點與動態運動的驗證證據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Distinguish horizontal run, span length and available end travel, redrawing geometry for combined tide and dock offsets. Check the entire route against applicable accessibility and facility requirements, retaining evidence for slip resistance, pinch interfaces and dynamic movement separately. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分別標示水平投影、實際橋長及端部可滑行範圍，在高低潮與浮台偏移組合下重畫幾何。依適用無障礙及設施設計要求檢查全路徑，另記防滑、夾點與動態運動的驗證證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Distinguish horizontal run, span length and available end travel, redrawing geometry for combined tide and dock offsets. Check the entire route against applicable accessibility and facility requirements, retaining evidence for slip resistance, pinch interfaces and dynamic movement separately.","failure":"注意干擾：只看平均坡度會漏掉端部短折角，浮台水平偏移也可能耗盡滑座行程。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Average grade can hide a short end transition, and horizontal pontoon movement can exhaust sliding travel. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分別標示水平投影、實際橋長及端部可滑行範圍，在高低潮與浮台偏移組合下重畫幾何。依適用無障礙及設施設計要求檢查全路徑，另記防滑、夾點與動態運動的驗證證據。","textEn":"Distinguish horizontal run, span length and available end travel, redrawing geometry for combined tide and dock offsets. Check the entire route against applicable accessibility and facility requirements, retaining evidence for slip resistance, pinch interfaces and dynamic movement separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分別標示水平投影、實際橋長及端部可滑行範圍，在高低潮與浮台偏移組合下重畫幾何。依適用無障礙及設施設計要求檢查全路徑，另記防滑、夾點與動態運動的驗證證據。","textEn":"Distinguish horizontal run, span length and available end travel, redrawing geometry for combined tide and dock offsets. Check the entire route against applicable accessibility and facility requirements, retaining evidence for slip resistance, pinch interfaces and dynamic movement separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「引橋坡度與行程」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gangway slope and travel\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","浮台隨潮升降但平面位置不變時纜繩幾何與張力也一定不變。","分別標示水平投影、實際橋長及端部可滑行範圍，在高低潮與浮台偏移組合下重畫幾何。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","If pontoon plan position is unchanged, tidal rise cannot alter line geometry or tension.","Distinguish horizontal run, span length and available end travel, redrawing geometry for combined tide and dock offsets."],"answer":2,"explanation":"分別標示水平投影、實際橋長及端部可滑行範圍，在高低潮與浮台偏移組合下重畫幾何。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Distinguish horizontal run, span length and available end travel, redrawing geometry for combined tide and dock offsets. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b291-v15-36","title":"引橋坡度與行程：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gangway slope and travel: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「引橋坡度與行程」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gangway slope and travel” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只看平均坡度會漏掉端部短折角，浮台水平偏移也可能耗盡滑座行程。即使靜態幾何仍可通行，波動造成的相對運動仍需在使用情境中評估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Average grade can hide a short end transition, and horizontal pontoon movement can exhaust sliding travel. Even apparently passable static geometry requires assessment of relative wave-induced movement within the actual use context of the facility. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設高差1.2m、水平投影12m，坡度10%、角度atan(1.2/12)=5.711°，斜長12.0599m；不是通行允收值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Grade is10%,angle5.711° and sloping length12.0599m, not an access acceptance criterion.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「引橋坡度符合任意幾何計算值就自動代表完全符合無障礙要求。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any calculated gangway slope automatically establishes full compliance with accessibility requirements.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只看平均坡度會漏掉端部短折角，浮台水平偏移也可能耗盡滑座行程。即使靜態幾何仍可通行，波動造成的相對運動仍需在使用情境中評估。","textEn":"Average grade can hide a short end transition, and horizontal pontoon movement can exhaust sliding travel. Even apparently passable static geometry requires assessment of relative wave-induced movement within the actual use context of the facility.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「引橋坡度與行程」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gangway slope and travel\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只看平均坡度會漏掉端部短折角，浮台水平偏移也可能耗盡滑座行程。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。"],"optionsEn":["Average grade can hide a short end transition, and horizontal pontoon movement can exhaust sliding travel.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只看平均坡度會漏掉端部短折角，浮台水平偏移也可能耗盡滑座行程。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Average grade can hide a short end transition, and horizontal pontoon movement can exhaust sliding travel. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b291-v15-37","title":"浮力儲備與損艙：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「浮力儲備與損艙」如何影響浮動碼頭繫泊系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Buoyant reserve and compartment loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Mooring systems for floating docks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"浮筒損壞會改變可用排水體積及重量分布，分艙的目的之一是限制局部進水影響。完整密閉體的總容積不是損壞後可用浮力，且浸沒到頂的理論餘量不含動態乾舷需求；應分開完整和損艙狀態，追蹤何處先失去通達或穩定功能。 假設密閉可排水體積120m³、海水1025kg/m³、總質量100000kg，至全浸沒理論質量餘量23000kg；不是允許載重。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「浮力儲備與損艙」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Damage changes available buoyant volume and weight distribution, while compartments limit the extent of flooding. Total enclosed volume in the intact state is not available buoyancy after damage, and a theoretical reserve to deck immersion excludes dynamic freeboard needs. Intact and damaged states need separate treatment, identifying where access or stability is lost before relying on a total reserve number. Assume sealed displacement capacity120m³,seawater1025kg/m³ and mass100000kg. Theoretical reserve to full immersion is23000kg, not an allowable additional load. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Buoyant reserve and compartment loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「浮力儲備與損艙」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Buoyant reserve and compartment loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-37-k1","title":"浮力儲備與損艙","titleEn":"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss","text":"浮筒損壞會改變可用排水體積及重量分布，分艙的目的之一是限制局部進水影響。完整密閉體的總容積不是損壞後可用浮力，且浸沒到頂的理論餘量不含動態乾舷需求；應分開完整和損艙狀態，追蹤何處先失去通達或穩定功能。","textEn":"Damage changes available buoyant volume and weight distribution, while compartments limit the extent of flooding. Total enclosed volume in the intact state is not available buoyancy after damage, and a theoretical reserve to deck immersion excludes dynamic freeboard needs.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「浮力儲備與損艙」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss\" is correct?","options":["理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。","浮筒損壞會改變可用排水體積及重量分布，分艙的目的之一是限制局部進水影響。","只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。"],"optionsEn":["All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading.","Damage changes available buoyant volume and weight distribution, while compartments limit the extent of flooding.","Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves."],"answer":1,"explanation":"浮筒損壞會改變可用排水體積及重量分布，分艙的目的之一是限制局部進水影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Damage changes available buoyant volume and weight distribution, while compartments limit the extent of flooding. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b291-v15-38","title":"浮力儲備與損艙：定量估算","titleEn":"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「浮力儲備與損艙」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Buoyant reserve and compartment loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設密閉可排水體積120m³、海水1025kg/m³、總質量100000kg，至全浸沒理論質量餘量23000kg；不是允許載重。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume sealed displacement capacity120m³,seawater1025kg/m³ and mass100000kg. Theoretical reserve to full immersion is23000kg, not an allowable additional load. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立分艙體積和重量位置清單，核對水密檢查及進水警示，分別畫完整與指定損艙吃水姿態。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Inventory compartment volumes and weight locations, checking watertightness and flooding detection.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設密閉可排水體積120m³、海水1025kg/m³、總質量100000kg，至全浸沒理論質量餘量23000kg；不是允許載重。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume sealed displacement capacity120m³,seawater1025kg/m³ and mass100000kg. Theoretical reserve to full immersion is23000kg, not an allowable additional load.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「浮力儲備與損艙」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss\", which statement holds?","options":["遠處測到的平均潮流速度必定等於所有浮體表面的局部速度。","所有纜繩都具固定線性剛度且循環後不會有永久伸長。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["A distant mean tidal-current measurement necessarily equals local velocity at every pontoon surface.","Every mooring line has constant linear stiffness and no permanent extension after cycling.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b291-v15-39","title":"浮力儲備與損艙：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「浮力儲備與損艙」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Buoyant reserve and compartment loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立分艙體積和重量位置清單，核對水密檢查及進水警示，分別畫完整與指定損艙吃水姿態。將理論浮力餘量與最低乾舷、穩性及使用條件分開，不讓總容積掩蓋局部進水。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Inventory compartment volumes and weight locations, checking watertightness and flooding detection. Draw intact and specified damaged attitudes separately and distinguish theoretical buoyant reserve from freeboard, stability and use requirements so total volume does not hide localized flooding. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立分艙體積和重量位置清單，核對水密檢查及進水警示，分別畫完整與指定損艙吃水姿態。將理論浮力餘量與最低乾舷、穩性及使用條件分開，不讓總容積掩蓋局部進水。","observationEn":"Site practice: Inventory compartment volumes and weight locations, checking watertightness and flooding detection. Draw intact and specified damaged attitudes separately and distinguish theoretical buoyant reserve from freeboard, stability and use requirements so total volume does not hide localized flooding.","failure":"注意干擾：某一端進水可能先造成傾斜和引橋不對位，總剩餘浮力尚大也不表示功能完整。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Flooding at one end can first cause heel and gangway misalignment even with substantial remaining total buoyancy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立分艙體積和重量位置清單，核對水密檢查及進水警示，分別畫完整與指定損艙吃水姿態。將理論浮力餘量與最低乾舷、穩性及使用條件分開，不讓總容積掩蓋局部進水。","textEn":"Inventory compartment volumes and weight locations, checking watertightness and flooding detection. Draw intact and specified damaged attitudes separately and distinguish theoretical buoyant reserve from freeboard, stability and use requirements so total volume does not hide localized flooding.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立分艙體積和重量位置清單，核對水密檢查及進水警示，分別畫完整與指定損艙吃水姿態。將理論浮力餘量與最低乾舷、穩性及使用條件分開，不讓總容積掩蓋局部進水。","textEn":"Inventory compartment volumes and weight locations, checking watertightness and flooding detection. Draw intact and specified damaged attitudes separately and distinguish theoretical buoyant reserve from freeboard, stability and use requirements so total volume does not hide localized flooding.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「浮力儲備與損艙」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss\"?","options":["建立分艙體積和重量位置清單，核對水密檢查及進水警示，分別畫完整與指定損艙吃水姿態。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","所有纜的軸向剛度相加就是任何方向的浮台水平剛度。"],"optionsEn":["Inventory compartment volumes and weight locations, checking watertightness and flooding detection.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Adding all axial line stiffnesses gives the pontoon's horizontal stiffness in every direction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"建立分艙體積和重量位置清單，核對水密檢查及進水警示，分別畫完整與指定損艙吃水姿態。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Inventory compartment volumes and weight locations, checking watertightness and flooding detection. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b291-v15-40","title":"浮力儲備與損艙：失效診斷","titleEn":"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"prerequisiteIds":["b291-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「浮力儲備與損艙」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Buoyant reserve and compartment loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"某一端進水可能先造成傾斜和引橋不對位，總剩餘浮力尚大也不表示功能完整。把全浸沒餘量當可加載量，會忽略波浪、進水和人員偏載所需的空間。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Flooding at one end can first cause heel and gangway misalignment even with substantial remaining total buoyancy. Treating reserve to full immersion as permissible loading ignores the space needed for waves, flooding and eccentric occupancy. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設密閉可排水體積120m³、海水1025kg/m³、總質量100000kg，至全浸沒理論質量餘量23000kg；不是允許載重。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Theoretical reserve to full immersion is23000kg, not an allowable additional load.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「理論全浸沒前的浮力餘量可以全部當成額外允許載重。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All buoyant reserve up to full immersion can be used as permissible additional loading.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b291-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"某一端進水可能先造成傾斜和引橋不對位，總剩餘浮力尚大也不表示功能完整。把全浸沒餘量當可加載量，會忽略波浪、進水和人員偏載所需的空間。","textEn":"Flooding at one end can first cause heel and gangway misalignment even with substantial remaining total buoyancy. Treating reserve to full immersion as permissible loading ignores the space needed for waves, flooding and eccentric occupancy.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]},{"id":"b291-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「浮力儲備與損艙」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Buoyant reserve and compartment loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","某一端進水可能先造成傾斜和引橋不對位，總剩餘浮力尚大也不表示功能完整。","只要總浮力大於總重量就代表偏載和波浪下所有角點都安全。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Flooding at one end can first cause heel and gangway misalignment even with substantial remaining total buoyancy.","Total buoyancy exceeding weight guarantees every corner remains safe under eccentric loading and waves."],"answer":1,"explanation":"某一端進水可能先造成傾斜和引橋不對位，總剩餘浮力尚大也不表示功能完整。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Flooding at one end can first cause heel and gangway misalignment even with substantial remaining total buoyancy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-pwdm","v15s-smallcraft","v15s-maliushui","v15s-hkpontoons"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000},{"id":"b292","title":"大型船閘灌排水系統","titleEn":"Filling and emptying systems for navigation locks","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從水量平衡到瞬變與船舶受力理解大型船閘灌排系統。課程從邊界辨識與資料整理走到水理量化、構造介面及驗證紀錄；每一步把計算結果連回可量測的證據。十個不同單元分別處理關鍵機制，不以名義尺寸或單一通過率代替整體工程判斷，並明列合成算例與現地資料的差別。","summaryEn":"Understand large-lock filling through water balance, transients and vessel forces. The course moves from boundary identification and evidence to hydraulic quantification, structural interfaces and verification records. Ten distinct units connect each calculated quantity to measurable evidence. Nominal geometry or a single pass rate does not establish whole-system performance, and synthetic teaching examples remain separate from field observations.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-coasts","subcategoryTitle":"海岸、港灣與水資源韌性","subcategoryTitleEn":"Coasts, ports and water-resource resilience","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-coasts","learningTags":["water","water-coasts","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-lock","architectureNodes":[["閘室有效水量","Effective chamber water volume"],["水位上升與空間均勻","Level rise and spatial uniformity"],["平水末段時間","Late-stage equalization time"],["射流動量與導流","Jet momentum and redirection"],["水面坡度與繫泊需求","Surface gradient and mooring demand"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-lock","labels":["閘室有效水量","水位上升與空間均勻","平水末段時間","射流動量與導流","水面坡度與繫泊需求"],"labelsEn":["Effective chamber water volume","Level rise and spatial uniformity","Late-stage equalization time","Jet momentum and redirection","Surface gradient and mooring demand"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為原創合成算例，不是地標工程的實測或推薦操作值。教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設空閘長300m、寬30m且垂直壁，水位升10m，ΔV=LBΔh=90000m³；不含節水池或船舶幾何。假設升水高度由10加10%至11m、空閘平面固定，水量由90000增至99000m³；若另假設平均流量仍150m³/s，時間600增至660s，但實際流量時程需重算。重新計算前先列固定條件、單位、適用尺度及可能失效的邊界。把模型敏感度與測量誤差分開，不能將單一參數變化直接當成工程風險或壽命比例。比較兩次結果後，記錄還需要哪些獨立證據，並由負責專業人員判斷適用性。","textEn":"This original synthetic example is neither a landmark measurement nor a recommended operating value. Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume an empty vertical-sided chamber300m long and30m wide with a10m rise. ΔV=LBΔh=90000m³, excluding basins and vessel geometry. Increasing lift10% from10to11m at fixed empty-chamber plan increases volume90000to99000m³. If mean discharge is separately held at150m³/s, time rises600to660s; the actual hydrograph must be recalculated. Before recalculating, list fixed conditions, units, applicable scale and boundaries that could fail. Separate model sensitivity from measurement uncertainty: a parameter change does not directly give a proportional change in engineering risk or service life. Compare the results, record independent evidence still needed, and have the responsible specialist determine applicability.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b292-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「閘室有效水量」與「平均流量與灌水時間」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Effective chamber water volume\" and \"Mean discharge and filling time\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b292-v15-01","title":"閘室有效水量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Effective chamber water volume: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「閘室有效水量」如何影響大型船閘灌排水系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective chamber water volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filling and emptying systems for navigation locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"閘室水位變化所需水量由有效水平面積積分，船舶排水、局部台階與側室會影響實際幾何。矩形空閘示意只是基本量級，水量還要連到上游庫與下游河段收支；不能把一次升降量直接當成每日取水量，因為節水池與交通次序不同。 假設空閘長300m、寬30m且垂直壁，水位升10m，ΔV=LBΔh=90000m³；不含節水池或船舶幾何。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「閘室有效水量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Required water volume follows integration of effective horizontal area with level; vessel displacement, steps and side spaces modify geometry. An empty rectangular chamber supplies a basic scale only, which must connect to upstream and downstream balances. One level-change volume is not daily freshwater demand because water-saving basins, traffic direction and operating sequences alter the complete system accounting. Assume an empty vertical-sided chamber300m long and30m wide with a10m rise. ΔV=LBΔh=90000m³, excluding basins and vessel geometry. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective chamber water volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「閘室全部容積就是每次通航必須重新消耗的淡水量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The entire chamber volume is fresh water that must be consumed anew on every transit.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「閘室有效水量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective chamber water volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-01-k1","title":"閘室有效水量","titleEn":"Effective chamber water volume","text":"閘室水位變化所需水量由有效水平面積積分，船舶排水、局部台階與側室會影響實際幾何。矩形空閘示意只是基本量級，水量還要連到上游庫與下游河段收支；不能把一次升降量直接當成每日取水量，因為節水池與交通次序不同。","textEn":"Required water volume follows integration of effective horizontal area with level; vessel displacement, steps and side spaces modify geometry. An empty rectangular chamber supplies a basic scale only, which must connect to upstream and downstream balances.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：閘室全部容積就是每次通航必須重新消耗的淡水量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The entire chamber volume is fresh water that must be consumed anew on every transit. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「閘室有效水量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Effective chamber water volume\" is correct?","options":["閘室全部容積就是每次通航必須重新消耗的淡水量。","閘室水位變化所需水量由有效水平面積積分，船舶排水、局部台階與側室會影響實際幾何。","峰值流量除以總水量即可準確代表整個灌排所需時間。"],"optionsEn":["The entire chamber volume is fresh water that must be consumed anew on every transit.","Required water volume follows integration of effective horizontal area with level; vessel displacement, steps and side spaces modify geometry.","Peak discharge alone provides an accurate filling duration for the complete chamber volume."],"answer":1,"explanation":"閘室水位變化所需水量由有效水平面積積分，船舶排水、局部台階與側室會影響實際幾何。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Required water volume follows integration of effective horizontal area with level; vessel displacement, steps and side spaces modify geometry. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b292-v15-02","title":"閘室有效水量：定量估算","titleEn":"Effective chamber water volume: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「閘室有效水量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective chamber water volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設空閘長300m、寬30m且垂直壁，水位升10m，ΔV=LBΔh=90000m³；不含節水池或船舶幾何。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume an empty vertical-sided chamber300m long and30m wide with a10m rise. ΔV=LBΔh=90000m³, excluding basins and vessel geometry. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用閘室各高程平面面積核對容積曲線，標明是否含船舶及側廊道。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify the volume-elevation curve from sectional areas, identifying vessel and side-space treatment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設空閘長300m、寬30m且垂直壁，水位升10m，ΔV=LBΔh=90000m³；不含節水池或船舶幾何。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume an empty vertical-sided chamber300m long and30m wide with a10m rise. ΔV=LBΔh=90000m³, excluding basins and vessel geometry.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「閘室有效水量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Effective chamber water volume\", which statement holds?","options":["閥門開度固定時流量就不受兩側水頭差變化影響。","廊道總水頭損失較小就保證船閘內水流一定更均勻。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["A fixed valve opening makes flow independent of the changing head difference.","Lower total culvert head loss guarantees a more uniform flow field inside the lock.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b292-v15-03","title":"閘室有效水量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Effective chamber water volume: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「閘室有效水量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective chamber water volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用閘室各高程平面面積核對容積曲線，標明是否含船舶及側廊道。將每次灌排的來源去向畫成收支圖，核對節水交換是否重複計入，並保留不同交通方向的水量差異。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify the volume-elevation curve from sectional areas, identifying vessel and side-space treatment. Map source and destination for each filling step, checking duplicated saving-basin exchange and retaining water-budget differences between traffic directions instead of assuming all lockages are identical. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用閘室各高程平面面積核對容積曲線，標明是否含船舶及側廊道。將每次灌排的來源去向畫成收支圖，核對節水交換是否重複計入，並保留不同交通方向的水量差異。","observationEn":"Site practice: Verify the volume-elevation curve from sectional areas, identifying vessel and side-space treatment. Map source and destination for each filling step, checking duplicated saving-basin exchange and retaining water-budget differences between traffic directions instead of assuming all lockages are identical.","failure":"注意干擾：把總閘室容積當升降用水會高估單次需求，忽略船舶與連通空間又可能漏掉水位相關面積。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using total chamber volume as lift water overstates demand, while ignored vessels or connected spaces misstate level-dependent area. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用閘室各高程平面面積核對容積曲線，標明是否含船舶及側廊道。將每次灌排的來源去向畫成收支圖，核對節水交換是否重複計入，並保留不同交通方向的水量差異。","textEn":"Verify the volume-elevation curve from sectional areas, identifying vessel and side-space treatment. Map source and destination for each filling step, checking duplicated saving-basin exchange and retaining water-budget differences between traffic directions instead of assuming all lockages are identical.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用閘室各高程平面面積核對容積曲線，標明是否含船舶及側廊道。將每次灌排的來源去向畫成收支圖，核對節水交換是否重複計入，並保留不同交通方向的水量差異。","textEn":"Verify the volume-elevation curve from sectional areas, identifying vessel and side-space treatment. Map source and destination for each filling step, checking duplicated saving-basin exchange and retaining water-budget differences between traffic directions instead of assuming all lockages are identical.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「閘室有效水量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Effective chamber water volume\"?","options":["用閘室各高程平面面積核對容積曲線，標明是否含船舶及側廊道。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","任何速度變化無論多慢都會產生相同的焦可夫斯基峰值水錘。"],"optionsEn":["Verify the volume-elevation curve from sectional areas, identifying vessel and side-space treatment.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Every velocity change produces the same Joukowsky peak regardless of how slowly it occurs."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用閘室各高程平面面積核對容積曲線，標明是否含船舶及側廊道。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify the volume-elevation curve from sectional areas, identifying vessel and side-space treatment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b292-v15-04","title":"閘室有效水量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Effective chamber water volume: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「閘室有效水量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective chamber water volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把總閘室容積當升降用水會高估單次需求，忽略船舶與連通空間又可能漏掉水位相關面積。若把回收水當新取水，則會錯判整個水源系統的壓力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using total chamber volume as lift water overstates demand, while ignored vessels or connected spaces misstate level-dependent area. Counting recovered water as fresh withdrawal then distorts the load placed on the wider source-water system. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設空閘長300m、寬30m且垂直壁，水位升10m，ΔV=LBΔh=90000m³；不含節水池或船舶幾何。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume an empty vertical-sided chamber300m long and30m wide with a10m rise. ΔV=LBΔh=90000m³, excluding basins and vessel geometry.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「閘室全部容積就是每次通航必須重新消耗的淡水量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The entire chamber volume is fresh water that must be consumed anew on every transit.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把總閘室容積當升降用水會高估單次需求，忽略船舶與連通空間又可能漏掉水位相關面積。若把回收水當新取水，則會錯判整個水源系統的壓力。","textEn":"Using total chamber volume as lift water overstates demand, while ignored vessels or connected spaces misstate level-dependent area. Counting recovered water as fresh withdrawal then distorts the load placed on the wider source-water system.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「閘室有效水量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Effective chamber water volume\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把總閘室容積當升降用水會高估單次需求，忽略船舶與連通空間又可能漏掉水位相關面積。","峰值流量除以總水量即可準確代表整個灌排所需時間。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using total chamber volume as lift water overstates demand, while ignored vessels or connected spaces misstate level-dependent area.","Peak discharge alone provides an accurate filling duration for the complete chamber volume."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把總閘室容積當升降用水會高估單次需求，忽略船舶與連通空間又可能漏掉水位相關面積。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using total chamber volume as lift water overstates demand, while ignored vessels or connected spaces misstate level-dependent area. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b292-v15-05","title":"平均流量與灌水時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Mean discharge and filling time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「平均流量與灌水時間」如何影響大型船閘灌排水系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mean discharge and filling time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filling and emptying systems for navigation locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"灌水時間由流量時程積分決定，平均流量只是一項事後或假設摘要。水頭隨閘室上升而降低，閥門與廊道慣性又使流量不會立即達峰；因此恆流除法適合收支檢查，不能生成現場操作時程，更不能只以最短時間評估系統功能。 假設所需補水量90000m³、整段平均流量150m³/s，t=V/Qavg=600s=10min；不表示瞬時流量恆定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「平均流量與灌水時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Filling duration follows integration of the discharge history, with mean discharge merely a summary or assumption. Head decreases as the chamber rises, and valves plus culvert inertia prevent instantaneous peak flow. Constant-flow division checks accounting but cannot generate an operational schedule or establish performance merely by minimizing elapsed time without considering water-surface disturbance and vessel response. Assume required volume90000m³ and interval-mean discharge150m³/s. t=V/Qavg=600s=10min, without implying constant instantaneous flow. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Mean discharge and filling time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「峰值流量除以總水量即可準確代表整個灌排所需時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Peak discharge alone provides an accurate filling duration for the complete chamber volume.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「平均流量與灌水時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Mean discharge and filling time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-05-k1","title":"平均流量與灌水時間","titleEn":"Mean discharge and filling time","text":"灌水時間由流量時程積分決定，平均流量只是一項事後或假設摘要。水頭隨閘室上升而降低，閥門與廊道慣性又使流量不會立即達峰；因此恆流除法適合收支檢查，不能生成現場操作時程，更不能只以最短時間評估系統功能。","textEn":"Filling duration follows integration of the discharge history, with mean discharge merely a summary or assumption. Head decreases as the chamber rises, and valves plus culvert inertia prevent instantaneous peak flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：峰值流量除以總水量即可準確代表整個灌排所需時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Peak discharge alone provides an accurate filling duration for the complete chamber volume. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「平均流量與灌水時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mean discharge and filling time\" is correct?","options":["峰值流量除以總水量即可準確代表整個灌排所需時間。","平均水位上升率穩定就證明閘室所有位置都沒有水面振盪。","灌水時間由流量時程積分決定，平均流量只是一項事後或假設摘要。"],"optionsEn":["Peak discharge alone provides an accurate filling duration for the complete chamber volume.","A steady mean rise proves that no surface oscillation exists anywhere in the chamber.","Filling duration follows integration of the discharge history, with mean discharge merely a summary or assumption."],"answer":2,"explanation":"灌水時間由流量時程積分決定，平均流量只是一項事後或假設摘要。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Filling duration follows integration of the discharge history, with mean discharge merely a summary or assumption. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b292-v15-06","title":"平均流量與灌水時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Mean discharge and filling time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「平均流量與灌水時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mean discharge and filling time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設所需補水量90000m³、整段平均流量150m³/s，t=V/Qavg=600s=10min；不表示瞬時流量恆定。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume required volume90000m³ and interval-mean discharge150m³/s. t=V/Qavg=600s=10min, without implying constant instantaneous flow. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：積分實測流量曲線與水位容積變化交叉核對，明列開閥前後是否納入計時。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Cross-check the integrated hydrograph against level-derived volume and define the timing interval.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設所需補水量90000m³、整段平均流量150m³/s，t=V/Qavg=600s=10min；不表示瞬時流量恆定。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume required volume90000m³ and interval-mean discharge150m³/s. t=V/Qavg=600s=10min, without implying constant instantaneous flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「平均流量與灌水時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mean discharge and filling time\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","只要某一瞬間兩側水位相等就代表後續不會再有壓差。","灌水射流的全部動量反力都必定直接施加在閘內船舶上。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","One instant of equal levels proves that no pressure difference can develop afterward.","The entire filling-jet momentum reaction necessarily acts directly on the vessel in the chamber."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b292-v15-07","title":"平均流量與灌水時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Mean discharge and filling time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「平均流量與灌水時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mean discharge and filling time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"積分實測流量曲線與水位容積變化交叉核對，明列開閥前後是否納入計時。檢查末段水頭變小時的流量衰減，並把船舶運動與壓力資料對時，不以時間達標取代其他性能。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Cross-check the integrated hydrograph against level-derived volume and define the timing interval. Inspect declining flow near equalization and align vessel-motion and pressure records, ensuring a target duration does not substitute for verification of the other hydraulic performance measures. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：積分實測流量曲線與水位容積變化交叉核對，明列開閥前後是否納入計時。檢查末段水頭變小時的流量衰減，並把船舶運動與壓力資料對時，不以時間達標取代其他性能。","observationEn":"Site practice: Cross-check the integrated hydrograph against level-derived volume and define the timing interval. Inspect declining flow near equalization and align vessel-motion and pressure records, ensuring a target duration does not substitute for verification of the other hydraulic performance measures.","failure":"注意干擾：以峰值流量計算全程會低估灌水時間，未量到的漏流則讓容積核對不閉合。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using peak flow throughout understates filling time, while unmeasured leakage prevents volume closure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"積分實測流量曲線與水位容積變化交叉核對，明列開閥前後是否納入計時。檢查末段水頭變小時的流量衰減，並把船舶運動與壓力資料對時，不以時間達標取代其他性能。","textEn":"Cross-check the integrated hydrograph against level-derived volume and define the timing interval. Inspect declining flow near equalization and align vessel-motion and pressure records, ensuring a target duration does not substitute for verification of the other hydraulic performance measures.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"積分實測流量曲線與水位容積變化交叉核對，明列開閥前後是否納入計時。檢查末段水頭變小時的流量衰減，並把船舶運動與壓力資料對時，不以時間達標取代其他性能。","textEn":"Cross-check the integrated hydrograph against level-derived volume and define the timing interval. Inspect declining flow near equalization and align vessel-motion and pressure records, ensuring a target duration does not substitute for verification of the other hydraulic performance measures.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「平均流量與灌水時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mean discharge and filling time\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","積分實測流量曲線與水位容積變化交叉核對，明列開閥前後是否納入計時。","壓力計顯示正表壓就可以排除閥內所有局部空化現象。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Cross-check the integrated hydrograph against level-derived volume and define the timing interval.","Positive gauge pressure at one sensor rules out all local cavitation inside the valve."],"answer":1,"explanation":"積分實測流量曲線與水位容積變化交叉核對，明列開閥前後是否納入計時。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Cross-check the integrated hydrograph against level-derived volume and define the timing interval. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b292-v15-08","title":"平均流量與灌水時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mean discharge and filling time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「平均流量與灌水時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mean discharge and filling time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以峰值流量計算全程會低估灌水時間，未量到的漏流則讓容積核對不閉合。更快的平均灌水也可能伴隨更大水面坡度，不能直接解讀為整體品質提升。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using peak flow throughout understates filling time, while unmeasured leakage prevents volume closure. Faster average filling may accompany larger surface gradients, so speed alone cannot be interpreted as an improvement in complete system performance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設所需補水量90000m³、整段平均流量150m³/s，t=V/Qavg=600s=10min；不表示瞬時流量恆定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume required volume90000m³ and interval-mean discharge150m³/s. t=V/Qavg=600s=10min, without implying constant instantaneous flow.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「峰值流量除以總水量即可準確代表整個灌排所需時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Peak discharge alone provides an accurate filling duration for the complete chamber volume.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以峰值流量計算全程會低估灌水時間，未量到的漏流則讓容積核對不閉合。更快的平均灌水也可能伴隨更大水面坡度，不能直接解讀為整體品質提升。","textEn":"Using peak flow throughout understates filling time, while unmeasured leakage prevents volume closure. Faster average filling may accompany larger surface gradients, so speed alone cannot be interpreted as an improvement in complete system performance.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「平均流量與灌水時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mean discharge and filling time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","平均水位上升率穩定就證明閘室所有位置都沒有水面振盪。","以峰值流量計算全程會低估灌水時間，未量到的漏流則讓容積核對不閉合。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A steady mean rise proves that no surface oscillation exists anywhere in the chamber.","Using peak flow throughout understates filling time, while unmeasured leakage prevents volume closure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以峰值流量計算全程會低估灌水時間，未量到的漏流則讓容積核對不閉合。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using peak flow throughout understates filling time, while unmeasured leakage prevents volume closure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b292-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「水位上升與空間均勻」與「孔口水頭流量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Level rise and spatial uniformity\" and \"Orifice head-discharge relation\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b292-v15-09","title":"水位上升與空間均勻：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Level rise and spatial uniformity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「水位上升與空間均勻」如何影響大型船閘灌排水系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Level rise and spatial uniformity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filling and emptying systems for navigation locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"連續方程把淨入流轉成平均水位上升率，但長閘室內可能同時存在波動與局部射流。平均值不能顯示船首船尾水位差，也不能代表每個港池的瞬時變化；需以多點水位資料檢查空間均勻性，並把流量與幾何定義維持一致。 假設有效面積9000m²、淨入流150m³/s，dη/dt=Q/A=0.01667m/s=1m/min；僅是空間平均。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水位上升與空間均勻」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Continuity converts net inflow into mean level rise, but a long chamber can simultaneously contain waves and local jets. The average does not show the difference between bow and stern elevations or every local instantaneous change. Multiple gauges must test spatial uniformity, with flow and effective area consistently defined before interpreting an apparent match between average water level and discharge. Assume effective area9000m² and net inflow150m³/s. Mean rise Q/A=0.01667m/s=1m/min, not every local surface velocity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Level rise and spatial uniformity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均水位上升率穩定就證明閘室所有位置都沒有水面振盪。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A steady mean rise proves that no surface oscillation exists anywhere in the chamber.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水位上升與空間均勻」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Level rise and spatial uniformity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-09-k1","title":"水位上升與空間均勻","titleEn":"Level rise and spatial uniformity","text":"連續方程把淨入流轉成平均水位上升率，但長閘室內可能同時存在波動與局部射流。平均值不能顯示船首船尾水位差，也不能代表每個港池的瞬時變化；需以多點水位資料檢查空間均勻性，並把流量與幾何定義維持一致。","textEn":"Continuity converts net inflow into mean level rise, but a long chamber can simultaneously contain waves and local jets. The average does not show the difference between bow and stern elevations or every local instantaneous change.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均水位上升率穩定就證明閘室所有位置都沒有水面振盪。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A steady mean rise proves that no surface oscillation exists anywhere in the chamber. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水位上升與空間均勻」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Level rise and spatial uniformity\" is correct?","options":["連續方程把淨入流轉成平均水位上升率，但長閘室內可能同時存在波動與局部射流。","平均水位上升率穩定就證明閘室所有位置都沒有水面振盪。","閥門開度固定時流量就不受兩側水頭差變化影響。"],"optionsEn":["Continuity converts net inflow into mean level rise, but a long chamber can simultaneously contain waves and local jets.","A steady mean rise proves that no surface oscillation exists anywhere in the chamber.","A fixed valve opening makes flow independent of the changing head difference."],"answer":0,"explanation":"連續方程把淨入流轉成平均水位上升率，但長閘室內可能同時存在波動與局部射流。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Continuity converts net inflow into mean level rise, but a long chamber can simultaneously contain waves and local jets. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b292-v15-10","title":"水位上升與空間均勻：定量估算","titleEn":"Level rise and spatial uniformity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水位上升與空間均勻」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Level rise and spatial uniformity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設有效面積9000m²、淨入流150m³/s，dη/dt=Q/A=0.01667m/s=1m/min；僅是空間平均。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume effective area9000m² and net inflow150m³/s. Mean rise Q/A=0.01667m/s=1m/min, not every local surface velocity. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿閘室和船側同步量水位，先求平均再檢查各測點偏離與相位，核對淨流量是否已扣出流。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure levels synchronously along the chamber and vessel, comparing mean, deviations and phase and checking that net flow excludes outflow.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設有效面積9000m²、淨入流150m³/s，dη/dt=Q/A=0.01667m/s=1m/min；僅是空間平均。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume effective area9000m² and net inflow150m³/s. Mean rise Q/A=0.01667m/s=1m/min, not every local surface velocity.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水位上升與空間均勻」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Level rise and spatial uniformity\", which statement holds?","options":["廊道總水頭損失較小就保證船閘內水流一定更均勻。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","任何速度變化無論多慢都會產生相同的焦可夫斯基峰值水錘。"],"optionsEn":["Lower total culvert head loss guarantees a more uniform flow field inside the lock.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Every velocity change produces the same Joukowsky peak regardless of how slowly it occurs."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b292-v15-11","title":"水位上升與空間均勻：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Level rise and spatial uniformity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水位上升與空間均勻」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Level rise and spatial uniformity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿閘室和船側同步量水位，先求平均再檢查各測點偏離與相位，核對淨流量是否已扣出流。將局部高差與船舶運動連結，避免僅靠一支水位計宣告灌水均勻。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure levels synchronously along the chamber and vessel, comparing mean, deviations and phase and checking that net flow excludes outflow. Relate local gradients to vessel motion rather than declaring uniform filling from one level sensor that happens to follow the average. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：沿閘室和船側同步量水位，先求平均再檢查各測點偏離與相位，核對淨流量是否已扣出流。將局部高差與船舶運動連結，避免僅靠一支水位計宣告灌水均勻。","observationEn":"Site practice: Measure levels synchronously along the chamber and vessel, comparing mean, deviations and phase and checking that net flow excludes outflow. Relate local gradients to vessel motion rather than declaring uniform filling from one level sensor that happens to follow the average.","failure":"注意干擾：感測器位在節點可能看不到明顯振盪，平均上升率正確仍可能有船端受力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A sensor near a modal node may miss oscillation even when vessel-end forces are significant. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿閘室和船側同步量水位，先求平均再檢查各測點偏離與相位，核對淨流量是否已扣出流。將局部高差與船舶運動連結，避免僅靠一支水位計宣告灌水均勻。","textEn":"Measure levels synchronously along the chamber and vessel, comparing mean, deviations and phase and checking that net flow excludes outflow. Relate local gradients to vessel motion rather than declaring uniform filling from one level sensor that happens to follow the average.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"沿閘室和船側同步量水位，先求平均再檢查各測點偏離與相位，核對淨流量是否已扣出流。將局部高差與船舶運動連結，避免僅靠一支水位計宣告灌水均勻。","textEn":"Measure levels synchronously along the chamber and vessel, comparing mean, deviations and phase and checking that net flow excludes outflow. Relate local gradients to vessel motion rather than declaring uniform filling from one level sensor that happens to follow the average.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水位上升與空間均勻」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Level rise and spatial uniformity\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","船舶所有繫纜力都可由兩端水位差單獨精確決定。","沿閘室和船側同步量水位，先求平均再檢查各測點偏離與相位，核對淨流量是否已扣出流。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The complete vessel mooring force is exactly determined by end-to-end level difference alone.","Measure levels synchronously along the chamber and vessel, comparing mean, deviations and phase and checking that net flow excludes outflow."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沿閘室和船側同步量水位，先求平均再檢查各測點偏離與相位，核對淨流量是否已扣出流。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure levels synchronously along the chamber and vessel, comparing mean, deviations and phase and checking that net flow excludes outflow. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b292-v15-12","title":"水位上升與空間均勻：失效診斷","titleEn":"Level rise and spatial uniformity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水位上升與空間均勻」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Level rise and spatial uniformity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"感測器位在節點可能看不到明顯振盪，平均上升率正確仍可能有船端受力。漏掉排水支路也會讓入流量推算比實際水位變化快，造成假異常。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A sensor near a modal node may miss oscillation even when vessel-end forces are significant. An omitted outlet also makes inflow-derived rise exceed the measured rate, creating an apparent anomaly unrelated to the filling distribution itself. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設有效面積9000m²、淨入流150m³/s，dη/dt=Q/A=0.01667m/s=1m/min；僅是空間平均。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Mean rise Q/A=0.01667m/s=1m/min, not every local surface velocity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均水位上升率穩定就證明閘室所有位置都沒有水面振盪。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A steady mean rise proves that no surface oscillation exists anywhere in the chamber.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"感測器位在節點可能看不到明顯振盪，平均上升率正確仍可能有船端受力。漏掉排水支路也會讓入流量推算比實際水位變化快，造成假異常。","textEn":"A sensor near a modal node may miss oscillation even when vessel-end forces are significant. An omitted outlet also makes inflow-derived rise exceed the measured rate, creating an apparent anomaly unrelated to the filling distribution itself.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水位上升與空間均勻」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Level rise and spatial uniformity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["感測器位在節點可能看不到明顯振盪，平均上升率正確仍可能有船端受力。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","閥門開度固定時流量就不受兩側水頭差變化影響。"],"optionsEn":["A sensor near a modal node may miss oscillation even when vessel-end forces are significant.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A fixed valve opening makes flow independent of the changing head difference."],"answer":0,"explanation":"感測器位在節點可能看不到明顯振盪，平均上升率正確仍可能有船端受力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A sensor near a modal node may miss oscillation even when vessel-end forces are significant. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b292-v15-13","title":"孔口水頭流量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Orifice head-discharge relation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「孔口水頭流量」如何影響大型船閘灌排水系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orifice head-discharge relation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filling and emptying systems for navigation locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"閥口和孔口將水頭轉成流速，縮流及損失由流量係數近似。固定開口準定常公式忽略廊道加速度與水頭快速變化，局部係數又受開度和雷諾數影響；實際灌排需追蹤上游水位、閘內水位及開度歷程，不能只以初始最大水頭推全程。 假設固定孔口Cd=0.70、面積8m²、瞬時水頭差5m，Q=CdA√(2gH)=55.465m³/s；準定常示意。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「孔口水頭流量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An opening converts head into flow, with a discharge coefficient approximating contraction and losses. A fixed-opening quasi-steady relation omits culvert acceleration and rapid head variation, while coefficient depends on opening and flow regime. Actual filling must track upper level, chamber level and valve position through time rather than extending the maximum initial head over the whole cycle. Assume fixed opening Cd=0.70,area8m² and instantaneous head difference5m. Quasi-steady Q=CdA√(2gH)=55.465m³/s, excluding acceleration effects. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orifice head-discharge relation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「閥門開度固定時流量就不受兩側水頭差變化影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A fixed valve opening makes flow independent of the changing head difference.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「孔口水頭流量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orifice head-discharge relation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-13-k1","title":"孔口水頭流量","titleEn":"Orifice head-discharge relation","text":"閥口和孔口將水頭轉成流速，縮流及損失由流量係數近似。固定開口準定常公式忽略廊道加速度與水頭快速變化，局部係數又受開度和雷諾數影響；實際灌排需追蹤上游水位、閘內水位及開度歷程，不能只以初始最大水頭推全程。","textEn":"An opening converts head into flow, with a discharge coefficient approximating contraction and losses. A fixed-opening quasi-steady relation omits culvert acceleration and rapid head variation, while coefficient depends on opening and flow regime.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：閥門開度固定時流量就不受兩側水頭差變化影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A fixed valve opening makes flow independent of the changing head difference. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「孔口水頭流量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Orifice head-discharge relation\" is correct?","options":["閥門開度固定時流量就不受兩側水頭差變化影響。","閥口和孔口將水頭轉成流速，縮流及損失由流量係數近似。","只要某一瞬間兩側水位相等就代表後續不會再有壓差。"],"optionsEn":["A fixed valve opening makes flow independent of the changing head difference.","An opening converts head into flow, with a discharge coefficient approximating contraction and losses.","One instant of equal levels proves that no pressure difference can develop afterward."],"answer":1,"explanation":"閥口和孔口將水頭轉成流速，縮流及損失由流量係數近似。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An opening converts head into flow, with a discharge coefficient approximating contraction and losses. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b292-v15-14","title":"孔口水頭流量：定量估算","titleEn":"Orifice head-discharge relation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「孔口水頭流量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orifice head-discharge relation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設固定孔口Cd=0.70、面積8m²、瞬時水頭差5m，Q=CdA√(2gH)=55.465m³/s；準定常示意。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume fixed opening Cd=0.70,area8m² and instantaneous head difference5m. Quasi-steady Q=CdA√(2gH)=55.465m³/s, excluding acceleration effects. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對孔口面積是否對應實際開度，同步比較兩側總水頭與流量，辨識係數在不同階段是否改變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check that opening area matches actual position and compare simultaneous heads and discharge, identifying coefficient changes through the cycle.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設固定孔口Cd=0.70、面積8m²、瞬時水頭差5m，Q=CdA√(2gH)=55.465m³/s；準定常示意。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume fixed opening Cd=0.70,area8m² and instantaneous head difference5m. Quasi-steady Q=CdA√(2gH)=55.465m³/s, excluding acceleration effects.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「孔口水頭流量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Orifice head-discharge relation\", which statement holds?","options":["灌水射流的全部動量反力都必定直接施加在閘內船舶上。","壓力計顯示正表壓就可以排除閥內所有局部空化現象。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["The entire filling-jet momentum reaction necessarily acts directly on the vessel in the chamber.","Positive gauge pressure at one sensor rules out all local cavitation inside the valve.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b292-v15-15","title":"孔口水頭流量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Orifice head-discharge relation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「孔口水頭流量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orifice head-discharge relation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對孔口面積是否對應實際開度，同步比較兩側總水頭與流量，辨識係數在不同階段是否改變。將啟動和接近平水的區段分開驗證，不用單一校正點宣稱全時程適用。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check that opening area matches actual position and compare simultaneous heads and discharge, identifying coefficient changes through the cycle. Validate startup and near-equalization separately rather than claiming complete hydrograph applicability from one conveniently matched calibration point. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：核對孔口面積是否對應實際開度，同步比較兩側總水頭與流量，辨識係數在不同階段是否改變。將啟動和接近平水的區段分開驗證，不用單一校正點宣稱全時程適用。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check that opening area matches actual position and compare simultaneous heads and discharge, identifying coefficient changes through the cycle. Validate startup and near-equalization separately rather than claiming complete hydrograph applicability from one conveniently matched calibration point.","failure":"注意干擾：開度相同而上游水頭不同會產生不同流量，廊道慣性又可能讓流量落後於水頭。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Equal opening with different upstream head gives different discharge, and culvert inertia can delay the response. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對孔口面積是否對應實際開度，同步比較兩側總水頭與流量，辨識係數在不同階段是否改變。將啟動和接近平水的區段分開驗證，不用單一校正點宣稱全時程適用。","textEn":"Check that opening area matches actual position and compare simultaneous heads and discharge, identifying coefficient changes through the cycle. Validate startup and near-equalization separately rather than claiming complete hydrograph applicability from one conveniently matched calibration point.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"核對孔口面積是否對應實際開度，同步比較兩側總水頭與流量，辨識係數在不同階段是否改變。將啟動和接近平水的區段分開驗證，不用單一校正點宣稱全時程適用。","textEn":"Check that opening area matches actual position and compare simultaneous heads and discharge, identifying coefficient changes through the cycle. Validate startup and near-equalization separately rather than claiming complete hydrograph applicability from one conveniently matched calibration point.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「孔口水頭流量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Orifice head-discharge relation\"?","options":["核對孔口面積是否對應實際開度，同步比較兩側總水頭與流量，辨識係數在不同階段是否改變。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","閘室全部容積就是每次通航必須重新消耗的淡水量。"],"optionsEn":["Check that opening area matches actual position and compare simultaneous heads and discharge, identifying coefficient changes through the cycle.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The entire chamber volume is fresh water that must be consumed anew on every transit."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對孔口面積是否對應實際開度，同步比較兩側總水頭與流量，辨識係數在不同階段是否改變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check that opening area matches actual position and compare simultaneous heads and discharge, identifying coefficient changes through the cycle. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b292-v15-16","title":"孔口水頭流量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Orifice head-discharge relation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「孔口水頭流量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orifice head-discharge relation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"開度相同而上游水頭不同會產生不同流量，廊道慣性又可能讓流量落後於水頭。沿用固定係數湊合資料，可能掩蓋閥口損傷或旁通流路改變。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Equal opening with different upstream head gives different discharge, and culvert inertia can delay the response. Tuning one fixed coefficient to fit observations may conceal damaged openings or changes in bypass paths through the system. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設固定孔口Cd=0.70、面積8m²、瞬時水頭差5m，Q=CdA√(2gH)=55.465m³/s；準定常示意。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Quasi-steady Q=CdA√(2gH)=55.465m³/s, excluding acceleration effects.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「閥門開度固定時流量就不受兩側水頭差變化影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A fixed valve opening makes flow independent of the changing head difference.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"開度相同而上游水頭不同會產生不同流量，廊道慣性又可能讓流量落後於水頭。沿用固定係數湊合資料，可能掩蓋閥口損傷或旁通流路改變。","textEn":"Equal opening with different upstream head gives different discharge, and culvert inertia can delay the response. Tuning one fixed coefficient to fit observations may conceal damaged openings or changes in bypass paths through the system.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔口水頭流量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Orifice head-discharge relation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","開度相同而上游水頭不同會產生不同流量，廊道慣性又可能讓流量落後於水頭。","只要某一瞬間兩側水位相等就代表後續不會再有壓差。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Equal opening with different upstream head gives different discharge, and culvert inertia can delay the response.","One instant of equal levels proves that no pressure difference can develop afterward."],"answer":1,"explanation":"開度相同而上游水頭不同會產生不同流量，廊道慣性又可能讓流量落後於水頭。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Equal opening with different upstream head gives different discharge, and culvert inertia can delay the response. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b292-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「平水末段時間」與「廊道局部水頭損失」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Late-stage equalization time\" and \"Local culvert head losses\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b292-v15-17","title":"平水末段時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Late-stage equalization time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「平水末段時間」如何影響大型船閘灌排水系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Late-stage equalization time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filling and emptying systems for navigation locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"閘內水位接近上游時水頭衰減，最後一段升水通常比簡單線性外推慢。固定上游庫、固定孔口且無慣性的積分模型可以顯示平方根關係，真實末段還有振盪、漏水及控制判定；剩餘水頭門檻只是數學終點，不是開門或通航條件。 假設Ac=9000m²、Cd=0.70、孔口8m²、固定上游，水頭由10降0.1m，t=2Ac(√10−√0.1)/(CdA√2g)=2065.3s。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「平水末段時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"As the chamber approaches the upper level, declining head slows the final rise compared with a linear extrapolation. Integration for a fixed reservoir and opening without inertia reveals the square-root relation. Actual late-stage behavior includes oscillation, leakage and control decisions; a residual-head endpoint in this model is mathematical only, not a gate-opening or transit criterion. Assume chamber area9000m²,Cd=0.70,opening8m² and fixed upper level. Reducing head10to0.1m gives t=2Ac(√10−√0.1)/(CdA√2g)=2065.3s. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Late-stage equalization time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要某一瞬間兩側水位相等就代表後續不會再有壓差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One instant of equal levels proves that no pressure difference can develop afterward.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「平水末段時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Late-stage equalization time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-17-k1","title":"平水末段時間","titleEn":"Late-stage equalization time","text":"閘內水位接近上游時水頭衰減，最後一段升水通常比簡單線性外推慢。固定上游庫、固定孔口且無慣性的積分模型可以顯示平方根關係，真實末段還有振盪、漏水及控制判定；剩餘水頭門檻只是數學終點，不是開門或通航條件。","textEn":"As the chamber approaches the upper level, declining head slows the final rise compared with a linear extrapolation. Integration for a fixed reservoir and opening without inertia reveals the square-root relation.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要某一瞬間兩側水位相等就代表後續不會再有壓差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One instant of equal levels proves that no pressure difference can develop afterward. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「平水末段時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Late-stage equalization time\" is correct?","options":["只要某一瞬間兩側水位相等就代表後續不會再有壓差。","廊道總水頭損失較小就保證船閘內水流一定更均勻。","閘內水位接近上游時水頭衰減，最後一段升水通常比簡單線性外推慢。"],"optionsEn":["One instant of equal levels proves that no pressure difference can develop afterward.","Lower total culvert head loss guarantees a more uniform flow field inside the lock.","As the chamber approaches the upper level, declining head slows the final rise compared with a linear extrapolation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"閘內水位接近上游時水頭衰減，最後一段升水通常比簡單線性外推慢。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"As the chamber approaches the upper level, declining head slows the final rise compared with a linear extrapolation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b292-v15-18","title":"平水末段時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Late-stage equalization time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「平水末段時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Late-stage equalization time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設Ac=9000m²、Cd=0.70、孔口8m²、固定上游，水頭由10降0.1m，t=2Ac(√10−√0.1)/(CdA√2g)=2065.3s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume chamber area9000m²,Cd=0.70,opening8m² and fixed upper level. Reducing head10to0.1m gives t=2Ac(√10−√0.1)/(CdA√2g)=2065.3s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：明列上游是否可當固定水位及孔口是否全程不變，將水頭平方根對時間作圖檢查近似。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: State whether upper level and opening remain fixed and plot square-root head against time to test the approximation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設Ac=9000m²、Cd=0.70、孔口8m²、固定上游，水頭由10降0.1m，t=2Ac(√10−√0.1)/(CdA√2g)=2065.3s。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume chamber area9000m²,Cd=0.70,opening8m² and fixed upper level. Reducing head10to0.1m gives t=2Ac(√10−√0.1)/(CdA√2g)=2065.3s.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「平水末段時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Late-stage equalization time\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","任何速度變化無論多慢都會產生相同的焦可夫斯基峰值水錘。","船舶所有繫纜力都可由兩端水位差單獨精確決定。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","Every velocity change produces the same Joukowsky peak regardless of how slowly it occurs.","The complete vessel mooring force is exactly determined by end-to-end level difference alone."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b292-v15-19","title":"平水末段時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Late-stage equalization time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「平水末段時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Late-stage equalization time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"明列上游是否可當固定水位及孔口是否全程不變，將水頭平方根對時間作圖檢查近似。保存末段振盪和測量解析度，另由正式系統要求判定平水條件，不以本算例終點操作閘門。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"State whether upper level and opening remain fixed and plot square-root head against time to test the approximation. Retain late oscillation and measurement resolution, leaving equalization criteria to the approved system rather than using this illustrative endpoint to operate a gate. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：明列上游是否可當固定水位及孔口是否全程不變，將水頭平方根對時間作圖檢查近似。保存末段振盪和測量解析度，另由正式系統要求判定平水條件，不以本算例終點操作閘門。","observationEn":"Site practice: State whether upper level and opening remain fixed and plot square-root head against time to test the approximation. Retain late oscillation and measurement resolution, leaving equalization criteria to the approved system rather than using this illustrative endpoint to operate a gate.","failure":"注意干擾：上游庫面積有限時兩側都會變位，套固定庫模型會算錯時間；末段壓力振盪則可能使瞬間水位相等後再次分離。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: With finite upper storage, both levels move and the fixed-reservoir estimate becomes inaccurate. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"明列上游是否可當固定水位及孔口是否全程不變，將水頭平方根對時間作圖檢查近似。保存末段振盪和測量解析度，另由正式系統要求判定平水條件，不以本算例終點操作閘門。","textEn":"State whether upper level and opening remain fixed and plot square-root head against time to test the approximation. Retain late oscillation and measurement resolution, leaving equalization criteria to the approved system rather than using this illustrative endpoint to operate a gate.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"明列上游是否可當固定水位及孔口是否全程不變，將水頭平方根對時間作圖檢查近似。保存末段振盪和測量解析度，另由正式系統要求判定平水條件，不以本算例終點操作閘門。","textEn":"State whether upper level and opening remain fixed and plot square-root head against time to test the approximation. Retain late oscillation and measurement resolution, leaving equalization criteria to the approved system rather than using this illustrative endpoint to operate a gate.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「平水末段時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Late-stage equalization time\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","明列上游是否可當固定水位及孔口是否全程不變，將水頭平方根對時間作圖檢查近似。","峰值流量除以總水量即可準確代表整個灌排所需時間。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","State whether upper level and opening remain fixed and plot square-root head against time to test the approximation.","Peak discharge alone provides an accurate filling duration for the complete chamber volume."],"answer":1,"explanation":"明列上游是否可當固定水位及孔口是否全程不變，將水頭平方根對時間作圖檢查近似。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"State whether upper level and opening remain fixed and plot square-root head against time to test the approximation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b292-v15-20","title":"平水末段時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Late-stage equalization time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「平水末段時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Late-stage equalization time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"上游庫面積有限時兩側都會變位，套固定庫模型會算錯時間；末段壓力振盪則可能使瞬間水位相等後再次分離。只檢查一刻讀值，無法證明持續平衡。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"With finite upper storage, both levels move and the fixed-reservoir estimate becomes inaccurate. Late pressure oscillations can also separate levels again after a momentary match, so one equal reading does not establish sustained hydraulic balance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設Ac=9000m²、Cd=0.70、孔口8m²、固定上游，水頭由10降0.1m，t=2Ac(√10−√0.1)/(CdA√2g)=2065.3s。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Reducing head10to0.1m gives t=2Ac(√10−√0.1)/(CdA√2g)=2065.3s.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要某一瞬間兩側水位相等就代表後續不會再有壓差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One instant of equal levels proves that no pressure difference can develop afterward.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"上游庫面積有限時兩側都會變位，套固定庫模型會算錯時間；末段壓力振盪則可能使瞬間水位相等後再次分離。只檢查一刻讀值，無法證明持續平衡。","textEn":"With finite upper storage, both levels move and the fixed-reservoir estimate becomes inaccurate. Late pressure oscillations can also separate levels again after a momentary match, so one equal reading does not establish sustained hydraulic balance.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「平水末段時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Late-stage equalization time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","廊道總水頭損失較小就保證船閘內水流一定更均勻。","上游庫面積有限時兩側都會變位，套固定庫模型會算錯時間；末段壓力振盪則可能使瞬間水位相等後再次分離。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Lower total culvert head loss guarantees a more uniform flow field inside the lock.","With finite upper storage, both levels move and the fixed-reservoir estimate becomes inaccurate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"上游庫面積有限時兩側都會變位，套固定庫模型會算錯時間；末段壓力振盪則可能使瞬間水位相等後再次分離。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"With finite upper storage, both levels move and the fixed-reservoir estimate becomes inaccurate. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b292-v15-21","title":"廊道局部水頭損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Local culvert head losses: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「廊道局部水頭損失」如何影響大型船閘灌排水系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Local culvert head losses” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filling and emptying systems for navigation locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"彎道、分岔和閥件將能量耗散成紊流，局部損失係數需指定參考速度。把不同截面速度下的係數直接相加會失去一致性，且閥門位置隨時間改變；低損失不一定代表閘內流場較均勻，流量分配和射流方向仍要另行檢驗。 假設同一參考流速v=4m/s、局部總係數K=3，hL=Kv²/(2g)=2.446m；只合併同速度基準的損失。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「廊道局部水頭損失」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Bends, junctions and valves dissipate energy through turbulence, with each coefficient tied to a reference velocity. Adding coefficients based on different areas is inconsistent, and valve position changes through time. Low total loss does not necessarily produce more uniform chamber flow; distribution and jet direction require separate assessment rather than being inferred from an apparently efficient hydraulic path. Assume common reference velocity4m/s and total local coefficient K=3. hL=Kv²/(2g)=2.446m, combining only coefficients on that velocity basis. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Local culvert head losses” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「廊道總水頭損失較小就保證船閘內水流一定更均勻。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Lower total culvert head loss guarantees a more uniform flow field inside the lock.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「廊道局部水頭損失」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Local culvert head losses”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-21-k1","title":"廊道局部水頭損失","titleEn":"Local culvert head losses","text":"彎道、分岔和閥件將能量耗散成紊流，局部損失係數需指定參考速度。把不同截面速度下的係數直接相加會失去一致性，且閥門位置隨時間改變；低損失不一定代表閘內流場較均勻，流量分配和射流方向仍要另行檢驗。","textEn":"Bends, junctions and valves dissipate energy through turbulence, with each coefficient tied to a reference velocity. Adding coefficients based on different areas is inconsistent, and valve position changes through time.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：廊道總水頭損失較小就保證船閘內水流一定更均勻。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Lower total culvert head loss guarantees a more uniform flow field inside the lock. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「廊道局部水頭損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Local culvert head losses\" is correct?","options":["彎道、分岔和閥件將能量耗散成紊流，局部損失係數需指定參考速度。","廊道總水頭損失較小就保證船閘內水流一定更均勻。","灌水射流的全部動量反力都必定直接施加在閘內船舶上。"],"optionsEn":["Bends, junctions and valves dissipate energy through turbulence, with each coefficient tied to a reference velocity.","Lower total culvert head loss guarantees a more uniform flow field inside the lock.","The entire filling-jet momentum reaction necessarily acts directly on the vessel in the chamber."],"answer":0,"explanation":"彎道、分岔和閥件將能量耗散成紊流，局部損失係數需指定參考速度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Bends, junctions and valves dissipate energy through turbulence, with each coefficient tied to a reference velocity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b292-v15-22","title":"廊道局部水頭損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Local culvert head losses: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「廊道局部水頭損失」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Local culvert head losses” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設同一參考流速v=4m/s、局部總係數K=3，hL=Kv²/(2g)=2.446m；只合併同速度基準的損失。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume common reference velocity4m/s and total local coefficient K=3. hL=Kv²/(2g)=2.446m, combining only coefficients on that velocity basis. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對每個彎頭分岔標示截面與參考速度，將係數轉至共同基準後再合計，並核對壓力測點位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Label area and reference velocity at each fitting and convert coefficients to one basis before summing, checking pressure-tap positions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設同一參考流速v=4m/s、局部總係數K=3，hL=Kv²/(2g)=2.446m；只合併同速度基準的損失。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume common reference velocity4m/s and total local coefficient K=3. hL=Kv²/(2g)=2.446m, combining only coefficients on that velocity basis.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「廊道局部水頭損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Local culvert head losses\", which statement holds?","options":["壓力計顯示正表壓就可以排除閥內所有局部空化現象。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","閘室全部容積就是每次通航必須重新消耗的淡水量。"],"optionsEn":["Positive gauge pressure at one sensor rules out all local cavitation inside the valve.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The entire chamber volume is fresh water that must be consumed anew on every transit."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b292-v15-23","title":"廊道局部水頭損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Local culvert head losses: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「廊道局部水頭損失」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Local culvert head losses” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對每個彎頭分岔標示截面與參考速度，將係數轉至共同基準後再合計，並核對壓力測點位置。比較各支路流量和閘內水面，不把較小總壓降直接解讀為較小船舶受力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Label area and reference velocity at each fitting and convert coefficients to one basis before summing, checking pressure-tap positions. Compare branch flows and chamber surface response rather than interpreting lower total pressure loss directly as reduced vessel loading during filling. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對每個彎頭分岔標示截面與參考速度，將係數轉至共同基準後再合計，並核對壓力測點位置。比較各支路流量和閘內水面，不把較小總壓降直接解讀為較小船舶受力。","observationEn":"Site practice: Label area and reference velocity at each fitting and convert coefficients to one basis before summing, checking pressure-tap positions. Compare branch flows and chamber surface response rather than interpreting lower total pressure loss directly as reduced vessel loading during filling.","failure":"注意干擾：廊道局部縮頸會提高速度，原係數基準不改便低估損失。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A local constriction raises velocity, and retaining the wrong coefficient basis understates loss. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對每個彎頭分岔標示截面與參考速度，將係數轉至共同基準後再合計，並核對壓力測點位置。比較各支路流量和閘內水面，不把較小總壓降直接解讀為較小船舶受力。","textEn":"Label area and reference velocity at each fitting and convert coefficients to one basis before summing, checking pressure-tap positions. Compare branch flows and chamber surface response rather than interpreting lower total pressure loss directly as reduced vessel loading during filling.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對每個彎頭分岔標示截面與參考速度，將係數轉至共同基準後再合計，並核對壓力測點位置。比較各支路流量和閘內水面，不把較小總壓降直接解讀為較小船舶受力。","textEn":"Label area and reference velocity at each fitting and convert coefficients to one basis before summing, checking pressure-tap positions. Compare branch flows and chamber surface response rather than interpreting lower total pressure loss directly as reduced vessel loading during filling.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「廊道局部水頭損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Local culvert head losses\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","平均水位上升率穩定就證明閘室所有位置都沒有水面振盪。","對每個彎頭分岔標示截面與參考速度，將係數轉至共同基準後再合計，並核對壓力測點位置。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A steady mean rise proves that no surface oscillation exists anywhere in the chamber.","Label area and reference velocity at each fitting and convert coefficients to one basis before summing, checking pressure-tap positions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對每個彎頭分岔標示截面與參考速度，將係數轉至共同基準後再合計，並核對壓力測點位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Label area and reference velocity at each fitting and convert coefficients to one basis before summing, checking pressure-tap positions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b292-v15-24","title":"廊道局部水頭損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Local culvert head losses: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「廊道局部水頭損失」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Local culvert head losses” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"廊道局部縮頸會提高速度，原係數基準不改便低估損失。分岔左右阻力不均可能讓水流偏向一側，即使總流量合計正確仍會產生不均勻水面和繫纜需求。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A local constriction raises velocity, and retaining the wrong coefficient basis understates loss. Unequal branch resistance directs flow to one side, producing nonuniform surface response and mooring demand even when total discharge is correctly predicted. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設同一參考流速v=4m/s、局部總係數K=3，hL=Kv²/(2g)=2.446m；只合併同速度基準的損失。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Assume common reference velocity4m/s and total local coefficient K=3. hL=Kv²/(2g)=2.446m, combining only coefficients on that velocity basis.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「廊道總水頭損失較小就保證船閘內水流一定更均勻。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Lower total culvert head loss guarantees a more uniform flow field inside the lock.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"廊道局部縮頸會提高速度，原係數基準不改便低估損失。分岔左右阻力不均可能讓水流偏向一側，即使總流量合計正確仍會產生不均勻水面和繫纜需求。","textEn":"A local constriction raises velocity, and retaining the wrong coefficient basis understates loss. Unequal branch resistance directs flow to one side, producing nonuniform surface response and mooring demand even when total discharge is correctly predicted.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「廊道局部水頭損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Local culvert head losses\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["廊道局部縮頸會提高速度，原係數基準不改便低估損失。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","灌水射流的全部動量反力都必定直接施加在閘內船舶上。"],"optionsEn":["A local constriction raises velocity, and retaining the wrong coefficient basis understates loss.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","The entire filling-jet momentum reaction necessarily acts directly on the vessel in the chamber."],"answer":0,"explanation":"廊道局部縮頸會提高速度，原係數基準不改便低估損失。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A local constriction raises velocity, and retaining the wrong coefficient basis understates loss. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b292-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「射流動量與導流」與「快速變速與水錘」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Jet momentum and redirection\" and \"Rapid velocity change and water hammer\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b292-v15-25","title":"射流動量與導流：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Jet momentum and redirection: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「射流動量與導流」如何影響大型船閘灌排水系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Jet momentum and redirection” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filling and emptying systems for navigation locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"灌水射流的動量需要由導流板、周邊水體和結構共同改變，控制體收支可估合力尺度。完全停止指定方向速度只是一種邊界，實際射流會擴散及偏轉；這個反力不能直接當成船體承受的荷載，船位、湍流與水面坡度還有其他傳力路徑。 假設淡水ρ=1000kg/m³、Q=20m³/s、入口水平v=4m/s，出口該方向速度為0且忽略壓力差，反力ρQv=80kN。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「射流動量與導流」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Filling-jet momentum is redirected by diffusers, surrounding water and structure. A control-volume balance provides a resultant scale, with complete stopping in one direction only a chosen boundary. Real jets spread and turn, so this reaction is not automatically the vessel load; vessel location, turbulence and surface gradients introduce additional transfer paths that need their own observations and models. Assume freshwater1000kg/m³,Q=20m³/s,inlet horizontal speed4m/s and zero outlet component, neglecting pressure differences. Momentum reaction is80kN, not vessel force. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Jet momentum and redirection” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「灌水射流的全部動量反力都必定直接施加在閘內船舶上。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The entire filling-jet momentum reaction necessarily acts directly on the vessel in the chamber.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「射流動量與導流」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Jet momentum and redirection”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-25-k1","title":"射流動量與導流","titleEn":"Jet momentum and redirection","text":"灌水射流的動量需要由導流板、周邊水體和結構共同改變，控制體收支可估合力尺度。完全停止指定方向速度只是一種邊界，實際射流會擴散及偏轉；這個反力不能直接當成船體承受的荷載，船位、湍流與水面坡度還有其他傳力路徑。","textEn":"Filling-jet momentum is redirected by diffusers, surrounding water and structure. A control-volume balance provides a resultant scale, with complete stopping in one direction only a chosen boundary.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：灌水射流的全部動量反力都必定直接施加在閘內船舶上。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The entire filling-jet momentum reaction necessarily acts directly on the vessel in the chamber. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「射流動量與導流」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Jet momentum and redirection\" is correct?","options":["灌水射流的全部動量反力都必定直接施加在閘內船舶上。","灌水射流的動量需要由導流板、周邊水體和結構共同改變，控制體收支可估合力尺度。","任何速度變化無論多慢都會產生相同的焦可夫斯基峰值水錘。"],"optionsEn":["The entire filling-jet momentum reaction necessarily acts directly on the vessel in the chamber.","Filling-jet momentum is redirected by diffusers, surrounding water and structure.","Every velocity change produces the same Joukowsky peak regardless of how slowly it occurs."],"answer":1,"explanation":"灌水射流的動量需要由導流板、周邊水體和結構共同改變，控制體收支可估合力尺度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Filling-jet momentum is redirected by diffusers, surrounding water and structure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b292-v15-26","title":"射流動量與導流：定量估算","titleEn":"Jet momentum and redirection: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「射流動量與導流」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Jet momentum and redirection” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設淡水ρ=1000kg/m³、Q=20m³/s、入口水平v=4m/s，出口該方向速度為0且忽略壓力差，反力ρQv=80kN。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume freshwater1000kg/m³,Q=20m³/s,inlet horizontal speed4m/s and zero outlet component, neglecting pressure differences. Momentum reaction is80kN, not vessel force. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：畫控制體的入口出口和壓力面，核對速度向量而不只用速率，檢查有無其他支流。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw control-volume boundaries and pressure faces, using velocity vectors rather than speed alone and checking side flows.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設淡水ρ=1000kg/m³、Q=20m³/s、入口水平v=4m/s，出口該方向速度為0且忽略壓力差，反力ρQv=80kN。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assume freshwater1000kg/m³,Q=20m³/s,inlet horizontal speed4m/s and zero outlet component, neglecting pressure differences. Momentum reaction is80kN, not vessel force.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「射流動量與導流」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Jet momentum and redirection\", which statement holds?","options":["船舶所有繫纜力都可由兩端水位差單獨精確決定。","峰值流量除以總水量即可準確代表整個灌排所需時間。","教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。"],"optionsEn":["The complete vessel mooring force is exactly determined by end-to-end level difference alone.","Peak discharge alone provides an accurate filling duration for the complete chamber volume.","Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b292-v15-27","title":"射流動量與導流：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Jet momentum and redirection: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「射流動量與導流」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Jet momentum and redirection” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"畫控制體的入口出口和壓力面，核對速度向量而不只用速率，檢查有無其他支流。以導流區壓力與流速資料測試動量收支，另量船舶受力，避免把兩者視為同一量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw control-volume boundaries and pressure faces, using velocity vectors rather than speed alone and checking side flows. Test momentum balance with diffuser-area measurements and observe vessel force separately, avoiding the assumption that these two distinct resultants must coincide. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫控制體的入口出口和壓力面，核對速度向量而不只用速率，檢查有無其他支流。以導流區壓力與流速資料測試動量收支，另量船舶受力，避免把兩者視為同一量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw control-volume boundaries and pressure faces, using velocity vectors rather than speed alone and checking side flows. Test momentum balance with diffuser-area measurements and observe vessel force separately, avoiding the assumption that these two distinct resultants must coincide.","failure":"注意干擾：射流轉向卻被當成完全停止會算錯反力方向，漏掉出口壓力又使合力不閉合。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating a turned jet as fully stopped misstates reaction direction, while omitted outlet pressure breaks the force balance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"畫控制體的入口出口和壓力面，核對速度向量而不只用速率，檢查有無其他支流。以導流區壓力與流速資料測試動量收支，另量船舶受力，避免把兩者視為同一量。","textEn":"Draw control-volume boundaries and pressure faces, using velocity vectors rather than speed alone and checking side flows. Test momentum balance with diffuser-area measurements and observe vessel force separately, avoiding the assumption that these two distinct resultants must coincide.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫控制體的入口出口和壓力面，核對速度向量而不只用速率，檢查有無其他支流。以導流區壓力與流速資料測試動量收支，另量船舶受力，避免把兩者視為同一量。","textEn":"Draw control-volume boundaries and pressure faces, using velocity vectors rather than speed alone and checking side flows. Test momentum balance with diffuser-area measurements and observe vessel force separately, avoiding the assumption that these two distinct resultants must coincide.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「射流動量與導流」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Jet momentum and redirection\"?","options":["畫控制體的入口出口和壓力面，核對速度向量而不只用速率，檢查有無其他支流。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","閥門開度固定時流量就不受兩側水頭差變化影響。"],"optionsEn":["Draw control-volume boundaries and pressure faces, using velocity vectors rather than speed alone and checking side flows.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A fixed valve opening makes flow independent of the changing head difference."],"answer":0,"explanation":"畫控制體的入口出口和壓力面，核對速度向量而不只用速率，檢查有無其他支流。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw control-volume boundaries and pressure faces, using velocity vectors rather than speed alone and checking side flows. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b292-v15-28","title":"射流動量與導流：失效診斷","titleEn":"Jet momentum and redirection: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「射流動量與導流」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Jet momentum and redirection” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"射流轉向卻被當成完全停止會算錯反力方向，漏掉出口壓力又使合力不閉合。船體只截取部分流場時，直接套整股射流動量會錯估接觸作用。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating a turned jet as fully stopped misstates reaction direction, while omitted outlet pressure breaks the force balance. If a vessel intercepts only part of the flow, applying the entire jet momentum misrepresents its actual hydrodynamic demand. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設淡水ρ=1000kg/m³、Q=20m³/s、入口水平v=4m/s，出口該方向速度為0且忽略壓力差，反力ρQv=80kN。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Momentum reaction is80kN, not vessel force.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「灌水射流的全部動量反力都必定直接施加在閘內船舶上。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The entire filling-jet momentum reaction necessarily acts directly on the vessel in the chamber.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"射流轉向卻被當成完全停止會算錯反力方向，漏掉出口壓力又使合力不閉合。船體只截取部分流場時，直接套整股射流動量會錯估接觸作用。","textEn":"Treating a turned jet as fully stopped misstates reaction direction, while omitted outlet pressure breaks the force balance. If a vessel intercepts only part of the flow, applying the entire jet momentum misrepresents its actual hydrodynamic demand.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「射流動量與導流」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Jet momentum and redirection\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","射流轉向卻被當成完全停止會算錯反力方向，漏掉出口壓力又使合力不閉合。","任何速度變化無論多慢都會產生相同的焦可夫斯基峰值水錘。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating a turned jet as fully stopped misstates reaction direction, while omitted outlet pressure breaks the force balance.","Every velocity change produces the same Joukowsky peak regardless of how slowly it occurs."],"answer":1,"explanation":"射流轉向卻被當成完全停止會算錯反力方向，漏掉出口壓力又使合力不閉合。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating a turned jet as fully stopped misstates reaction direction, while omitted outlet pressure breaks the force balance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b292-v15-29","title":"快速變速與水錘：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rapid velocity change and water hammer: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「快速變速與水錘」如何影響大型船閘灌排水系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rapid velocity change and water hammer” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filling and emptying systems for navigation locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"廊道水柱快速變速會傳遞彈性壓力波，波速與管壁和含氣狀態相關。焦可夫斯基式適用相對往返波時間很快的速度改變，慢變化需考慮反射和水柱運動，不能將同一峰壓套所有啟閉時程；算式用來辨識機制，不提供實際閥門操作設定。 假設ρ=1000kg/m³、波速a=900m/s、Δv=1m/s，快速變速Δp=ρaΔv=900kPa；L=300m時須相對2L/a=0.667s很快。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「快速變速與水錘」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Rapid culvert-velocity changes propagate elastic pressure waves, with speed affected by wall flexibility and entrained air. The Joukowsky relation applies to changes rapid relative to wave round-trip time. Slower changes require reflections and water-column dynamics, so the same peak cannot be applied to every valve history; the example identifies a mechanism rather than prescribing actual valve operation. Assumeρ=1000kg/m³,a=900m/s,Δv=1m/s. Rapid-changeΔp=900kPa; for L=300m the change must be fast relative to2L/a=0.667s. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rapid velocity change and water hammer” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「任何速度變化無論多慢都會產生相同的焦可夫斯基峰值水錘。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every velocity change produces the same Joukowsky peak regardless of how slowly it occurs.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「快速變速與水錘」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rapid velocity change and water hammer”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-29-k1","title":"快速變速與水錘","titleEn":"Rapid velocity change and water hammer","text":"廊道水柱快速變速會傳遞彈性壓力波，波速與管壁和含氣狀態相關。焦可夫斯基式適用相對往返波時間很快的速度改變，慢變化需考慮反射和水柱運動，不能將同一峰壓套所有啟閉時程；算式用來辨識機制，不提供實際閥門操作設定。","textEn":"Rapid culvert-velocity changes propagate elastic pressure waves, with speed affected by wall flexibility and entrained air. The Joukowsky relation applies to changes rapid relative to wave round-trip time.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任何速度變化無論多慢都會產生相同的焦可夫斯基峰值水錘。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every velocity change produces the same Joukowsky peak regardless of how slowly it occurs. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「快速變速與水錘」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rapid velocity change and water hammer\" is correct?","options":["任何速度變化無論多慢都會產生相同的焦可夫斯基峰值水錘。","壓力計顯示正表壓就可以排除閥內所有局部空化現象。","廊道水柱快速變速會傳遞彈性壓力波，波速與管壁和含氣狀態相關。"],"optionsEn":["Every velocity change produces the same Joukowsky peak regardless of how slowly it occurs.","Positive gauge pressure at one sensor rules out all local cavitation inside the valve.","Rapid culvert-velocity changes propagate elastic pressure waves, with speed affected by wall flexibility and entrained air."],"answer":2,"explanation":"廊道水柱快速變速會傳遞彈性壓力波，波速與管壁和含氣狀態相關。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Rapid culvert-velocity changes propagate elastic pressure waves, with speed affected by wall flexibility and entrained air. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b292-v15-30","title":"快速變速與水錘：定量估算","titleEn":"Rapid velocity change and water hammer: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「快速變速與水錘」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rapid velocity change and water hammer” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設ρ=1000kg/m³、波速a=900m/s、Δv=1m/s，快速變速Δp=ρaΔv=900kPa；L=300m時須相對2L/a=0.667s很快。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assumeρ=1000kg/m³,a=900m/s,Δv=1m/s. Rapid-changeΔp=900kPa; for L=300m the change must be fast relative to2L/a=0.667s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對壓力感測頻寬和時間同步，將閥位、流速與壓力波到達時刻比較，明列有效波速來源。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check pressure-sensor bandwidth and synchronization, comparing valve position, velocity and wave-arrival times with a justified wave speed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。假設ρ=1000kg/m³、波速a=900m/s、Δv=1m/s，快速變速Δp=ρaΔv=900kPa；L=300m時須相對2L/a=0.667s很快。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Assumeρ=1000kg/m³,a=900m/s,Δv=1m/s. Rapid-changeΔp=900kPa; for L=300m the change must be fast relative to2L/a=0.667s.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「快速變速與水錘」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rapid velocity change and water hammer\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","閘室全部容積就是每次通航必須重新消耗的淡水量。","平均水位上升率穩定就證明閘室所有位置都沒有水面振盪。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","The entire chamber volume is fresh water that must be consumed anew on every transit.","A steady mean rise proves that no surface oscillation exists anywhere in the chamber."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b292-v15-31","title":"快速變速與水錘：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rapid velocity change and water hammer: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「快速變速與水錘」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rapid velocity change and water hammer” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對壓力感測頻寬和時間同步，將閥位、流速與壓力波到達時刻比較，明列有效波速來源。另檢查反射及低壓分離可能，不把單一理想增壓當成完整瞬變包絡。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check pressure-sensor bandwidth and synchronization, comparing valve position, velocity and wave-arrival times with a justified wave speed. Review reflections and possible low-pressure separation separately instead of treating one ideal pressure increase as a complete transient envelope for the system. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：核對壓力感測頻寬和時間同步，將閥位、流速與壓力波到達時刻比較，明列有效波速來源。另檢查反射及低壓分離可能，不把單一理想增壓當成完整瞬變包絡。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check pressure-sensor bandwidth and synchronization, comparing valve position, velocity and wave-arrival times with a justified wave speed. Review reflections and possible low-pressure separation separately instead of treating one ideal pressure increase as a complete transient envelope for the system.","failure":"注意干擾：感測器太慢會漏掉短壓力尖峰，含氣量改變又使波速偏離原假設。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Slow sensors miss brief pressure peaks, and changing air content alters assumed wave speed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對壓力感測頻寬和時間同步，將閥位、流速與壓力波到達時刻比較，明列有效波速來源。另檢查反射及低壓分離可能，不把單一理想增壓當成完整瞬變包絡。","textEn":"Check pressure-sensor bandwidth and synchronization, comparing valve position, velocity and wave-arrival times with a justified wave speed. Review reflections and possible low-pressure separation separately instead of treating one ideal pressure increase as a complete transient envelope for the system.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"核對壓力感測頻寬和時間同步，將閥位、流速與壓力波到達時刻比較，明列有效波速來源。另檢查反射及低壓分離可能，不把單一理想增壓當成完整瞬變包絡。","textEn":"Check pressure-sensor bandwidth and synchronization, comparing valve position, velocity and wave-arrival times with a justified wave speed. Review reflections and possible low-pressure separation separately instead of treating one ideal pressure increase as a complete transient envelope for the system.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「快速變速與水錘」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rapid velocity change and water hammer\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","核對壓力感測頻寬和時間同步，將閥位、流速與壓力波到達時刻比較，明列有效波速來源。","只要某一瞬間兩側水位相等就代表後續不會再有壓差。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check pressure-sensor bandwidth and synchronization, comparing valve position, velocity and wave-arrival times with a justified wave speed.","One instant of equal levels proves that no pressure difference can develop afterward."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對壓力感測頻寬和時間同步，將閥位、流速與壓力波到達時刻比較，明列有效波速來源。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check pressure-sensor bandwidth and synchronization, comparing valve position, velocity and wave-arrival times with a justified wave speed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b292-v15-32","title":"快速變速與水錘：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rapid velocity change and water hammer: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「快速變速與水錘」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rapid velocity change and water hammer” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"感測器太慢會漏掉短壓力尖峰，含氣量改變又使波速偏離原假設。只檢查最大正壓而忽略低壓區，可能漏掉分離後再接合造成的另一波衝擊。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Slow sensors miss brief pressure peaks, and changing air content alters assumed wave speed. Checking only positive maximum pressure overlooks separation at low pressure and another impact when the separated water column subsequently rejoins. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：假設ρ=1000kg/m³、波速a=900m/s、Δv=1m/s，快速變速Δp=ρaΔv=900kPa；L=300m時須相對2L/a=0.667s很快。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Rapid-changeΔp=900kPa; for L=300m the change must be fast relative to2L/a=0.667s.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任何速度變化無論多慢都會產生相同的焦可夫斯基峰值水錘。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every velocity change produces the same Joukowsky peak regardless of how slowly it occurs.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b292-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"感測器太慢會漏掉短壓力尖峰，含氣量改變又使波速偏離原假設。只檢查最大正壓而忽略低壓區，可能漏掉分離後再接合造成的另一波衝擊。","textEn":"Slow sensors miss brief pressure peaks, and changing air content alters assumed wave speed. Checking only positive maximum pressure overlooks separation at low pressure and another impact when the separated water column subsequently rejoins.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]},{"id":"b292-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「快速變速與水錘」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rapid velocity change and water hammer\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","壓力計顯示正表壓就可以排除閥內所有局部空化現象。","感測器太慢會漏掉短壓力尖峰，含氣量改變又使波速偏離原假設。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Positive gauge pressure at one sensor rules out all local cavitation inside the valve.","Slow sensors miss brief pressure peaks, and changing air content alters assumed wave speed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"感測器太慢會漏掉短壓力尖峰，含氣量改變又使波速偏離原假設。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Slow sensors miss brief pressure peaks, and changing air content alters assumed wave speed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b292-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「絕對壓力與空化」與「水面坡度與繫泊需求」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Absolute pressure and cavitation\" and \"Surface gradient and mooring demand\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b292-v15-33","title":"絕對壓力與空化：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Absolute pressure and cavitation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-lockhyd","v15s-panama-open","v15s-lockvalve","v15s-panama-trial","v15s-panama-location"],"prerequisiteIds":["b292-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「絕對壓力與空化」如何影響大型船閘灌排水系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Absolute pressure and cavitation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Filling and emptying systems for navigation locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"閥口高速區可能接近水的汽化壓力，空化指標需用絕對壓力而非表壓。指標是否低於危險門檻與形狀、粗糙及氣核有關，不能用通用數字自動判定；同樣平均壓力下局部低壓仍可不同，水溫也會改變汽化壓力。 假設絕對壓力80kPa、汽化壓2.3kPa、ρ=1000kg/m³、v=10m/s，σ=(p−pv)/(ρv²/2)=1.554；非通用允收界線。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「絕對壓力與空化」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"High-speed valve regions can approach vapor pressure, and cavitation indices require absolute rather than gauge pressure. A relevant onset threshold depends on geometry, roughness and nuclei, not a universal number. Identical mean pressures can conceal different local minima, while temperature changes vapor pressure; the index therefore supports comparison but does not alone establish absence of damaging cavitation. Assume absolute pressure80kPa,vapor pressure2.3kPa,ρ=1000kg/m³,v=10m/s. Cavitation indexσ=1.554, not a universal acceptance boundary. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Absolute pressure and cavitation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非操作設定或設計允收值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not operating settings or design acceptance limits.","failure":"常見誤解：「壓力計顯示正表壓就可以排除閥內所有局部空化現象。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Positive gaug